verse	1	7	19	@@And the waters prevailed exceedingly upon the earth; and all the high hills, that @9were@7 under the whole heaven, were covered.
verse	1	7	20	Fifteen cubits upward did the waters prevail; and the mountains were covered.
verse	1	7	21	And all flesh died that moved upon the earth, both of fowl, and of cattle, and of beast, and of every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth, and every man:
verse	1	7	22	@@All in whose nostrils @9was@7 the breath of life, of all that @9was@7 in the dry @9land,@7 died.
verse	1	7	23	@@And every living substance was destroyed which was upon the face of the ground, both man, and cattle, and the creeping things, and the fowl of the heaven; and they were destroyed from the earth: and Noah only remained @9alive,@7 and they that @9were@7 with him in the ark.
verse	1	7	24	And the waters prevailed upon the earth an hundred and fifty days.
verse	1	8	1	@@And God remembered Noah, and every living thing, and all the cattle that @9was@7 with him in the ark: and God made a wind to pass over the earth, and the waters asswaged;
verse	1	8	2	The fountains also of the deep and the windows of heaven were stopped, and the rain from heaven was restrained;
verse	1	8	3	And the waters returned from off the earth continually: and after the end of the hundred and fifty days the waters were abated.
verse	1	8	4	And the ark rested in the seventh month, on the seventeenth day of the month, upon the mountains of Ararat.
verse	1	8	5	@@And the waters decreased continually until the tenth month: in the tenth @9month,@7 on the first @9day@7 of the month, were the tops of the mountains seen.
verse	1	8	6	And it came to pass at the end of forty days, that Noah opened the window of the ark which he had made:
verse	1	8	7	And he sent forth a raven, which went forth to and fro, until the waters were dried up from off the earth.
verse	1	8	8	Also he sent forth a dove from him, to see if the waters were abated from off the face of the ground;
verse	1	8	9	@@But the dove found no rest for the sole of her foot, and she returned unto him into the ark, for the waters @9were@7 on the face of the whole earth: then he put forth his hand, and took her, and pulled her in unto him into the ark.
verse	1	8	10	And he stayed yet other seven days; and again he sent forth the dove out of the ark;
