verse	1	31	50	@@If thou shalt afflict my daughters, or if thou shalt take @9other@7 wives beside my daughters, no man @9is@7 with us; see, God @9is@7 witness betwixt me and thee.
verse	1	31	51	@@And Laban said to Jacob, Behold this heap, and behold @9this@7 pillar, which I have cast betwixt me and thee;
verse	1	31	52	@@This heap @9be@7 witness, and @9this@7 pillar @9be@7 witness, that I will not pass over this heap to thee, and that thou shalt not pass over this heap and this pillar unto me, for harm.
verse	1	31	53	The God of Abraham, and the God of Nahor, the God of their father, judge betwixt us. And Jacob sware by the fear of his father Isaac.
verse	1	31	54	Then Jacob offered sacrifice upon the mount, and called his brethren to eat bread: and they did eat bread, and tarried all night in the mount.
