verse	1	32	11	@@Deliver me, I pray thee, from the hand of my brother, from the hand of Esau: for I fear him, lest he will come and smite me, @9and@7 the mother with the children.
verse	1	32	12	And thou saidst, I will surely do thee good, and make thy seed as the sand of the sea, which cannot be numbered for multitude.
verse	1	32	13	And he lodged there that same night; and took of that which came to his hand a present for Esau his brother;
verse	1	32	14	Two hundred she goats, and twenty he goats, two hundred ewes, and twenty rams,
verse	1	32	15	Thirty milch camels with their colts, forty kine, and ten bulls, twenty she asses, and ten foals.
verse	1	32	16	@@And he delivered @9them@7 into the hand of his servants, every drove by themselves; and said unto his servants, Pass over before me, and put a space betwixt drove and drove.
verse	1	32	17	@@And he commanded the foremost, saying, When Esau my brother meeteth thee, and asketh thee, saying, Whose @9art@7 thou? and whither goest thou? and whose @9are@7 these before thee?
verse	1	32	18	@@Then thou shalt say, @9They be@7 thy servant Jacob's; it @9is@7 a present sent unto my lord Esau: and, behold, also he @9is@7 behind us.
verse	1	32	19	And so commanded he the second, and the third, and all that followed the droves, saying, On this manner shall ye speak unto Esau, when ye find him.
verse	1	32	20	@@And say ye moreover, Behold, thy servant Jacob @9is@7 behind us. For he said, I will appease him with the present that goeth before me, and afterward I will see his face; peradventure he will accept of me.
verse	1	32	21	So went the present over before him: and himself lodged that night in the company.
verse	1	32	22	And he rose up that night, and took his two wives, and his two womenservants, and his eleven sons, and passed over the ford Jabbok.
verse	1	32	23	And he took them, and sent them over the brook, and sent over that he had.
