verse	1	32	25	And when he saw that he prevailed not against him, he touched the hollow of his thigh; and the hollow of Jacob's thigh was out of joint, as he wrestled with him.
verse	1	32	26	And he said, Let me go, for the day breaketh. And he said, I will not let thee go, except thou bless me.
verse	1	32	27	@@And he said unto him, What @9is@7 thy name? And he said, Jacob.
verse	1	32	28	And he said, Thy name shall be called no more Jacob, but Israel: for as a prince hast thou power with God and with men, and hast prevailed.
verse	1	32	29	@@And Jacob asked @9him,@7 and said, Tell @9me,@7 I pray thee, thy name. And he said, Wherefore @9is@7 it @9that@7 thou dost ask after my name? And he blessed him there.
verse	1	32	30	And Jacob called the name of the place Peniel: for I have seen God face to face, and my life is preserved.
verse	1	32	31	And as he passed over Penuel the sun rose upon him, and he halted upon his thigh.
verse	1	32	32	@@Therefore the children of Israel eat not @9of@7 the sinew which shrank, which @9is@7 upon the hollow of the thigh, unto this day: because he touched the hollow of Jacob's thigh in the sinew that shrank.
verse	1	33	1	And Jacob lifted up his eyes, and looked, and, behold, Esau came, and with him four hundred men. And he divided the children unto Leah, and unto Rachel, and unto the two handmaids.
verse	1	33	2	And he put the handmaids and their children foremost, and Leah and her children after, and Rachel and Joseph hindermost.
