verse	1	40	14	But think on me when it shall be well with thee, and shew kindness, I pray thee, unto me, and make mention of me unto Pharaoh, and bring me out of this house:
verse	1	40	15	For indeed I was stolen away out of the land of the Hebrews: and here also have I done nothing that they should put me into the dungeon.
verse	1	40	16	@@When the chief baker saw that the interpretation was good, he said unto Joseph, I also @9was@7 in my dream, and, behold, @9I had@7 three white baskets on my head:
verse	1	40	17	@@And in the uppermost basket @9there was@7 of all manner of bakemeats for Pharaoh; and the birds did eat them out of the basket upon my head.
verse	1	40	18	@@And Joseph answered and said, This @9is@7 the interpretation thereof: The three baskets @9are@7 three days:
verse	1	40	19	Yet within three days shall Pharaoh lift up thy head from off thee, and shall hang thee on a tree; and the birds shall eat thy flesh from off thee.
verse	1	40	20	@@And it came to pass the third day, @9which was@7 Pharaoh's birthday, that he made a feast unto all his servants: and he lifted up the head of the chief butler and of the chief baker among his servants.
verse	1	40	21	And he restored the chief butler unto his butlership again; and he gave the cup into Pharaoh's hand:
verse	1	40	22	But he hanged the chief baker: as Joseph had interpreted to them.
verse	1	40	23	Yet did not the chief butler remember Joseph, but forgat him.
verse	1	41	1	And it came to pass at the end of two full years, that Pharaoh dreamed: and, behold, he stood by the river.
verse	1	41	2	And, behold, there came up out of the river seven well favoured kine and fatfleshed; and they fed in a meadow.
verse	1	41	3	@@And, behold, seven other kine came up after them out of the river, ill favoured and leanfleshed; and stood by the @9other@7 kine upon the brink of the river.
verse	1	41	4	And the ill favoured and leanfleshed kine did eat up the seven well favoured and fat kine. So Pharaoh awoke.
verse	1	41	5	And he slept and dreamed the second time: and, behold, seven ears of corn came up upon one stalk, rank and good.
verse	1	41	6	And, behold, seven thin ears and blasted with the east wind sprung up after them.
verse	1	41	7	@@And the seven thin ears devoured the seven rank and full ears. And Pharaoh awoke, and, behold, @9it was@7 a dream.
verse	1	41	8	@@And it came to pass in the morning that his spirit was troubled; and he sent and called for all the magicians of Egypt, and all the wise men thereof: and Pharaoh told them his dream; but @9there was@7 none that could interpret them unto Pharaoh.
verse	1	41	9	Then spake the chief butler unto Pharaoh, saying, I do remember my faults this day:
verse	1	41	10	@@Pharaoh was wroth with his servants, and put me in ward in the captain of the guard's house, both @9me@7 and the chief baker:
verse	1	41	11	And we dreamed a dream in one night, I and he; we dreamed each man according to the interpretation of his dream.
verse	1	41	12	@@And @9there was@7 there with us a young man, an Hebrew, servant to the captain of the guard; and we told him, and he interpreted to us our dreams; to each man according to his dream he did interpret.
verse	1	41	13	And it came to pass, as he interpreted to us, so it was; me he restored unto mine office, and him he hanged.
verse	1	41	14	@@Then Pharaoh sent and called Joseph, and they brought him hastily out of the dungeon: and he shaved @9himself,@7 and changed his raiment, and came in unto Pharaoh.
verse	1	41	15	@@And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, I have dreamed a dream, and @9there is@7 none that can interpret it: and I have heard say of thee, @9that@7 thou canst understand a dream to interpret it.
verse	1	41	16	@@And Joseph answered Pharaoh, saying, @9It is@7 not in me: God shall give Pharaoh an answer of peace.
verse	1	41	17	And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, In my dream, behold, I stood upon the bank of the river:
verse	1	41	18	And, behold, there came up out of the river seven kine, fatfleshed and well favoured; and they fed in a meadow:
verse	1	41	19	And, behold, seven other kine came up after them, poor and very ill favoured and leanfleshed, such as I never saw in all the land of Egypt for badness:
verse	1	41	20	And the lean and the ill favoured kine did eat up the first seven fat kine:
verse	1	41	21	@@And when they had eaten them up, it could not be known that they had eaten them; but they @9were@7 still ill favoured, as at the beginning. So I awoke.
verse	1	41	22	And I saw in my dream, and, behold, seven ears came up in one stalk, full and good:
verse	1	41	23	@@And, behold, seven ears, withered, thin, @9and@7 blasted with the east wind, sprung up after them:
verse	1	41	24	@@And the thin ears devoured the seven good ears: and I told @9this@7 unto the magicians; but @9there was@7 none that could declare @9it@7 to me.
verse	1	41	25	@@And Joseph said unto Pharaoh, The dream of Pharaoh @9is@7 one: God hath shewed Pharaoh what he @9is@7 about to do.
verse	1	41	26	@@The seven good kine @9are@7 seven years; and the seven good ears @9are@7 seven years: the dream @9is@7 one.
verse	1	41	27	@@And the seven thin and ill favoured kine that came up after them @9are@7 seven years; and the seven empty ears blasted with the east wind shall be seven years of famine.
verse	1	41	28	@@This @9is@7 the thing which I have spoken unto Pharaoh: What God @9is@7 about to do he sheweth unto Pharaoh.
verse	1	41	29	Behold, there come seven years of great plenty throughout all the land of Egypt:
verse	1	41	30	And there shall arise after them seven years of famine; and all the plenty shall be forgotten in the land of Egypt; and the famine shall consume the land;
verse	1	41	31	@@And the plenty shall not be known in the land by reason of that famine following; for it @9shall be@7 very grievous.
verse	1	41	32	@@And for that the dream was doubled unto Pharaoh twice; @9it is@7 because the thing @9is@7 established by God, and God will shortly bring it to pass.
verse	1	41	33	Now therefore let Pharaoh look out a man discreet and wise, and set him over the land of Egypt.
verse	1	41	34	@@Let Pharaoh do @9this,@7 and let him appoint officers over the land, and take up the fifth part of the land of Egypt in the seven plenteous years.
verse	1	41	35	And let them gather all the food of those good years that come, and lay up corn under the hand of Pharaoh, and let them keep food in the cities.
