verse	1	41	47	And in the seven plenteous years the earth brought forth by handfuls.
verse	1	41	48	@@And he gathered up all the food of the seven years, which were in the land of Egypt, and laid up the food in the cities: the food of the field, which @9was@7 round about every city, laid he up in the same.
verse	1	41	49	@@And Joseph gathered corn as the sand of the sea, very much, until he left numbering; for @9it was@7 without number.
verse	1	41	50	And unto Joseph were born two sons before the years of famine came, which Asenath the daughter of Poti-pherah priest of On bare unto him.
verse	1	41	51	@@And Joseph called the name of the firstborn Manasseh: For God, @9said he,@7 hath made me forget all my toil, and all my father's house.
verse	1	41	52	And the name of the second called he Ephraim: For God hath caused me to be fruitful in the land of my affliction.
verse	1	41	53	And the seven years of plenteousness, that was in the land of Egypt, were ended.
verse	1	41	54	And the seven years of dearth began to come, according as Joseph had said: and the dearth was in all lands; but in all the land of Egypt there was bread.
verse	1	41	55	And when all the land of Egypt was famished, the people cried to Pharaoh for bread: and Pharaoh said unto all the Egyptians, Go unto Joseph; what he saith to you, do.
verse	1	41	56	And the famine was over all the face of the earth: And Joseph opened all the storehouses, and sold unto the Egyptians; and the famine waxed sore in the land of Egypt.
verse	1	41	57	@@And all countries came into Egypt to Joseph for to buy @9corn;@7 because that the famine was so sore in all lands.
verse	1	42	1	Now when Jacob saw that there was corn in Egypt, Jacob said unto his sons, Why do ye look one upon another?
verse	1	42	2	And he said, Behold, I have heard that there is corn in Egypt: get you down thither, and buy for us from thence; that we may live, and not die.
verse	1	42	3	And Joseph's ten brethren went down to buy corn in Egypt.
verse	1	42	4	But Benjamin, Joseph's brother, Jacob sent not with his brethren; for he said, Lest peradventure mischief befall him.
verse	1	42	5	@@And the sons of Israel came to buy @9corn@7 among those that came: for the famine was in the land of Canaan.
verse	1	42	6	@@And Joseph @9was@7 the governor over the land, @9and@7 he @9it was@7 that sold to all the people of the land: and Joseph's brethren came, and bowed down themselves before him @9with@7 their faces to the earth.
verse	1	42	7	And Joseph saw his brethren, and he knew them, but made himself strange unto them, and spake roughly unto them; and he said unto them, Whence come ye? And they said, From the land of Canaan to buy food.
verse	1	42	8	And Joseph knew his brethren, but they knew not him.
verse	1	42	9	@@And Joseph remembered the dreams which he dreamed of them, and said unto them, Ye @9are@7 spies; to see the nakedness of the land ye are come.
verse	1	42	10	And they said unto him, Nay, my lord, but to buy food are thy servants come.
verse	1	42	11	@@We @9are@7 all one man's sons; we @9are@7 true @9men,@7 thy servants are no spies.
verse	1	42	12	And he said unto them, Nay, but to see the nakedness of the land ye are come.
verse	1	42	13	@@And they said, Thy servants @9are@7 twelve brethren, the sons of one man in the land of Canaan; and, behold, the youngest @9is@7 this day with our father, and one @9is@7 not.
verse	1	42	14	@@And Joseph said unto them, That @9is it@7 that I spake unto you, saying, Ye @9are@7 spies:
verse	1	42	15	Hereby ye shall be proved: By the life of Pharaoh ye shall not go forth hence, except your youngest brother come hither.
verse	1	42	16	@@Send one of you, and let him fetch your brother, and ye shall be kept in prison, that your words may be proved, whether @9there be any@7 truth in you: or else by the life of Pharaoh surely ye @9are@7 spies.
verse	1	42	17	And he put them all together into ward three days.
verse	1	42	18	@@And Joseph said unto them the third day, This do, and live; @9for@7 I fear God:
verse	1	42	19	@@If ye @9be@7 true @9men,@7 let one of your brethren be bound in the house of your prison: go ye, carry corn for the famine of your houses:
verse	1	42	20	But bring your youngest brother unto me; so shall your words be verified, and ye shall not die. And they did so.
verse	1	42	21	@@And they said one to another, We @9are@7 verily guilty concerning our brother, in that we saw the anguish of his soul, when he besought us, and we would not hear; therefore is this distress come upon us.
verse	1	42	22	And Reuben answered them, saying, Spake I not unto you, saying, Do not sin against the child; and ye would not hear? therefore, behold, also his blood is required.
verse	1	42	23	@@And they knew not that Joseph understood @9them;@7 for he spake unto them by an interpreter.
verse	1	42	24	And he turned himself about from them, and wept; and returned to them again, and communed with them, and took from them Simeon, and bound him before their eyes.
verse	1	42	25	Then Joseph commanded to fill their sacks with corn, and to restore every man's money into his sack, and to give them provision for the way: and thus did he unto them.
verse	1	42	26	And they laded their asses with the corn, and departed thence.
verse	1	42	27	@@And as one of them opened his sack to give his ass provender in the inn, he espied his money; for, behold, it @9was@7 in his sack's mouth.
verse	1	42	28	@@And he said unto his brethren, My money is restored; and, lo, @9it is@7 even in my sack: and their heart failed @9them,@7 and they were afraid, saying one to another, What @9is@7 this @9that@7 God hath done unto us?
verse	1	42	29	And they came unto Jacob their father unto the land of Canaan, and told him all that befell unto them; saying,
verse	1	42	30	@@The man, @9who is@7 the lord of the land, spake roughly to us, and took us for spies of the country.
verse	1	42	31	@@And we said unto him, We @9are@7 true @9men;@7 we are no spies:
verse	1	42	32	@@We @9be@7 twelve brethren, sons of our father; one @9is@7 not, and the youngest @9is@7 this day with our father in the land of Canaan.
verse	1	42	33	@@And the man, the lord of the country, said unto us, Hereby shall I know that ye @9are@7 true @9men;@7 leave one of your brethren @9here@7 with me, and take @9food for@7 the famine of your households, and be gone:
verse	1	42	34	@@And bring your youngest brother unto me: then shall I know that ye @9are@7 no spies, but @9that@7 ye @9are@7 true @9men: so@7 will I deliver you your brother, and ye shall traffick in the land.
verse	1	42	35	@@And it came to pass as they emptied their sacks, that, behold, every man's bundle of money @9was@7 in his sack: and when @9both@7 they and their father saw the bundles of money, they were afraid.
verse	1	42	36	@@And Jacob their father said unto them, Me have ye bereaved @9of my children:@7 Joseph @9is@7 not, and Simeon @9is@7 not, and ye will take Benjamin @9away:@7 all these things are against me.
verse	1	42	37	And Reuben spake unto his father, saying, Slay my two sons, if I bring him not to thee: deliver him into my hand, and I will bring him to thee again.
verse	1	42	38	And he said, My son shall not go down with you; for his brother is dead, and he is left alone: if mischief befall him by the way in the which ye go, then shall ye bring down my gray hairs with sorrow to the grave.
verse	1	43	1	@@And the famine @9was@7 sore in the land.
verse	1	43	2	And it came to pass, when they had eaten up the corn which they had brought out of Egypt, their father said unto them, Go again, buy us a little food.
verse	1	43	3	@@And Judah spake unto him, saying, The man did solemnly protest unto us, saying, Ye shall not see my face, except your brother @9be@7 with you.
verse	1	43	4	If thou wilt send our brother with us, we will go down and buy thee food:
verse	1	43	5	@@But if thou wilt not send @9him,@7 we will not go down: for the man said unto us, Ye shall not see my face, except your brother @9be@7 with you.
verse	1	43	6	And Israel said, Wherefore dealt ye so ill with me, as to tell the man whether ye had yet a brother?
verse	1	43	7	@@And they said, The man asked us straitly of our state, and of our kindred, saying, @9Is@7 your father yet alive? have ye @9another@7 brother? and we told him according to the tenor of these words: could we certainly know that he would say, Bring your brother down?
verse	1	43	8	@@And Judah said unto Israel his father, Send the lad with me, and we will arise and go; that we may live, and not die, both we, and thou, @9and@7 also our little ones.
verse	1	43	9	I will be surety for him; of my hand shalt thou require him: if I bring him not unto thee, and set him before thee, then let me bear the blame for ever:
verse	1	43	10	For except we had lingered, surely now we had returned this second time.
verse	1	43	11	@@And their father Israel said unto them, If @9it must be@7 so now, do this; take of the best fruits in the land in your vessels, and carry down the man a present, a little balm, and a little honey, spices, and myrrh, nuts, and almonds:
verse	1	43	12	@@And take double money in your hand; and the money that was brought again in the mouth of your sacks, carry @9it@7 again in your hand; peradventure it @9was@7 an oversight:
verse	1	43	13	Take also your brother, and arise, go again unto the man:
verse	1	43	14	@@And God Almighty give you mercy before the man, that he may send away your other brother, and Benjamin. If I be bereaved @9of my children,@7 I am bereaved.
verse	1	43	15	And the men took that present, and they took double money in their hand, and Benjamin; and rose up, and went down to Egypt, and stood before Joseph.
verse	1	43	16	@@And when Joseph saw Benjamin with them, he said to the ruler of his house, Bring @9these@7 men home, and slay, and make ready; for @9these@7 men shall dine with me at noon.
verse	1	43	17	And the man did as Joseph bade; and the man brought the men into Joseph's house.
verse	1	43	18	And the men were afraid, because they were brought into Joseph's house; and they said, Because of the money that was returned in our sacks at the first time are we brought in; that he may seek occasion against us, and fall upon us, and take us for bondmen, and our asses.
verse	1	43	19	And they came near to the steward of Joseph's house, and they communed with him at the door of the house,
verse	1	43	20	And said, O sir, we came indeed down at the first time to buy food:
verse	1	43	21	@@And it came to pass, when we came to the inn, that we opened our sacks, and, behold, @9every@7 man's money @9was@7 in the mouth of his sack, our money in full weight: and we have brought it again in our hand.
verse	1	43	22	And other money have we brought down in our hands to buy food: we cannot tell who put our money in our sacks.
verse	1	43	23	@@And he said, Peace @9be@7 to you, fear not: your God, and the God of your father, hath given you treasure in your sacks: I had your money. And he brought Simeon out unto them.
verse	1	43	24	@@And the man brought the men into Joseph's house, and gave @9them@7 water, and they washed their feet; and he gave their asses provender.
verse	1	43	25	And they made ready the present against Joseph came at noon: for they heard that they should eat bread there.
verse	1	43	26	@@And when Joseph came home, they brought him the present which @9was@7 in their hand into the house, and bowed themselves to him to the earth.
verse	1	43	27	@@And he asked them of @9their@7 welfare, and said, @9Is@7 your father well, the old man of whom ye spake? @9Is@7 he yet alive?
verse	1	43	28	@@And they answered, Thy servant our father @9is@7 in good health, he @9is@7 yet alive. And they bowed down their heads, and made obeisance.
verse	1	43	29	@@And he lifted up his eyes, and saw his brother Benjamin, his mother's son, and said, @9Is@7 this your younger brother, of whom ye spake unto me? And he said, God be gracious unto thee, my son.
verse	1	43	30	@@And Joseph made haste; for his bowels did yearn upon his brother: and he sought @9where@7 to weep; and he entered into @9his@7 chamber, and wept there.
verse	1	43	31	And he washed his face, and went out, and refrained himself, and said, Set on bread.
verse	1	43	32	@@And they set on for him by himself, and for them by themselves, and for the Egyptians, which did eat with him, by themselves: because the Egyptians might not eat bread with the Hebrews; for that @9is@7 an abomination unto the Egyptians.
verse	1	43	33	And they sat before him, the firstborn according to his birthright, and the youngest according to his youth: and the men marvelled one at another.
verse	1	43	34	@@And he took @9and sent@7 messes unto them from before him: but Benjamin's mess was five times so much as any of theirs. And they drank, and were merry with him.
verse	1	44	1	@@And he commanded the steward of his house, saying, Fill the men's sacks @9with@7 food, as much as they can carry, and put every man's money in his sack's mouth.
verse	1	44	2	And put my cup, the silver cup, in the sack's mouth of the youngest, and his corn money. And he did according to the word that Joseph had spoken.
verse	1	44	3	As soon as the morning was light, the men were sent away, they and their asses.
verse	1	44	4	@@@9And@7 when they were gone out of the city, @9and@7 not @9yet@7 far off, Joseph said unto his steward, Up, follow after the men; and when thou dost overtake them, say unto them, Wherefore have ye rewarded evil for good?
verse	1	44	5	@@@9Is@7 not this @9it@7 in which my lord drinketh, and whereby indeed he divineth? ye have done evil in so doing.
verse	1	44	6	And he overtook them, and he spake unto them these same words.
verse	1	44	7	And they said unto him, Wherefore saith my lord these words? God forbid that thy servants should do according to this thing:
verse	1	44	8	Behold, the money, which we found in our sacks' mouths, we brought again unto thee out of the land of Canaan: how then should we steal out of thy lord's house silver or gold?
verse	1	44	9	With whomsoever of thy servants it be found, both let him die, and we also will be my lord's bondmen.
verse	1	44	10	@@And he said, Now also @9let@7 it @9be@7 according unto your words: he with whom it is found shall be my servant; and ye shall be blameless.
verse	1	44	11	Then they speedily took down every man his sack to the ground, and opened every man his sack.
verse	1	44	12	@@And he searched, @9and@7 began at the eldest, and left at the youngest: and the cup was found in Benjamin's sack.
verse	1	44	13	Then they rent their clothes, and laded every man his ass, and returned to the city.
verse	1	44	14	@@And Judah and his brethren came to Joseph's house; for he @9was@7 yet there: and they fell before him on the ground.
verse	1	44	15	@@And Joseph said unto them, What deed @9is@7 this that ye have done? wot ye not that such a man as I can certainly divine?
verse	1	44	16	@@And Judah said, What shall we say unto my lord? what shall we speak? or how shall we clear ourselves? God hath found out the iniquity of thy servants: behold, we @9are@7 my lord's servants, both we, and @9he@7 also with whom the cup is found.
verse	1	44	17	@@And he said, God forbid that I should do so: @9but@7 the man in whose hand the cup is found, he shall be my servant; and as for you, get you up in peace unto your father.
verse	1	44	18	@@Then Judah came near unto him, and said, Oh my lord, let thy servant, I pray thee, speak a word in my lord's ears, and let not thine anger burn against thy servant: for thou @9art@7 even as Pharaoh.
verse	1	44	19	My lord asked his servants, saying, Have ye a father, or a brother?
verse	1	44	20	And we said unto my lord, We have a father, an old man, and a child of his old age, a little one; and his brother is dead, and he alone is left of his mother, and his father loveth him.
verse	1	44	21	And thou saidst unto thy servants, Bring him down unto me, that I may set mine eyes upon him.
verse	1	44	22	@@And we said unto my lord, The lad cannot leave his father: for @9if@7 he should leave his father, @9his father@7 would die.
verse	1	44	23	And thou saidst unto thy servants, Except your youngest brother come down with you, ye shall see my face no more.
verse	1	44	24	And it came to pass when we came up unto thy servant my father, we told him the words of my lord.
verse	1	44	25	@@And our father said, Go again, @9and@7 buy us a little food.
verse	1	44	26	@@And we said, We cannot go down: if our youngest brother be with us, then will we go down: for we may not see the man's face, except our youngest brother @9be@7 with us.
verse	1	44	27	@@And thy servant my father said unto us, Ye know that my wife bare me two @9sons: @7
verse	1	44	28	And the one went out from me, and I said, Surely he is torn in pieces; and I saw him not since:
verse	1	44	29	And if ye take this also from me, and mischief befall him, ye shall bring down my gray hairs with sorrow to the grave.
verse	1	44	30	@@Now therefore when I come to thy servant my father, and the lad @9be@7 not with us; seeing that his life is bound up in the lad's life;
verse	1	44	31	@@It shall come to pass, when he seeth that the lad @9is@7 not @9with us,@7 that he will die: and thy servants shall bring down the gray hairs of thy servant our father with sorrow to the grave.
verse	1	44	32	For thy servant became surety for the lad unto my father, saying, If I bring him not unto thee, then I shall bear the blame to my father for ever.
verse	1	44	33	Now therefore, I pray thee, let thy servant abide instead of the lad a bondman to my lord; and let the lad go up with his brethren.
verse	1	44	34	@@For how shall I go up to my father, and the lad @9be@7 not with me? lest peradventure I see the evil that shall come on my father.
verse	1	45	1	Then Joseph could not refrain himself before all them that stood by him; and he cried, Cause every man to go out from me. And there stood no man with him, while Joseph made himself known unto his brethren.
verse	1	45	2	And he wept aloud: and the Egyptians and the house of Pharaoh heard.
verse	1	45	3	@@And Joseph said unto his brethren, I @9am@7 Joseph; doth my father yet live? And his brethren could not answer him; for they were troubled at his presence.
verse	1	45	4	@@And Joseph said unto his brethren, Come near to me, I pray you. And they came near. And he said, I @9am@7 Joseph your brother, whom ye sold into Egypt.
verse	1	45	5	Now therefore be not grieved, nor angry with yourselves, that ye sold me hither: for God did send me before you to preserve life.
verse	1	45	6	@@For these two years @9hath@7 the famine @9been@7 in the land: and yet @9there are@7 five years, in the which @9there shall@7 neither @9be@7 earing nor harvest.
verse	1	45	7	And God sent me before you to preserve you a posterity in the earth, and to save your lives by a great deliverance.
verse	1	45	8	@@So now @9it was@7 not you @9that@7 sent me hither, but God: and he hath made me a father to Pharaoh, and lord of all his house, and a ruler throughout all the land of Egypt.
verse	1	45	9	Haste ye, and go up to my father, and say unto him, Thus saith thy son Joseph, God hath made me lord of all Egypt: come down unto me, tarry not:
verse	1	45	10	And thou shalt dwell in the land of Goshen, and thou shalt be near unto me, thou, and thy children, and thy children's children, and thy flocks, and thy herds, and all that thou hast:
verse	1	45	11	@@And there will I nourish thee; for yet @9there are@7 five years of famine; lest thou, and thy household, and all that thou hast, come to poverty.
verse	1	45	12	@@And, behold, your eyes see, and the eyes of my brother Benjamin, that @9it is@7 my mouth that speaketh unto you.
verse	1	45	13	And ye shall tell my father of all my glory in Egypt, and of all that ye have seen; and ye shall haste and bring down my father hither.
verse	1	45	14	And he fell upon his brother Benjamin's neck, and wept; and Benjamin wept upon his neck.
verse	1	45	15	Moreover he kissed all his brethren, and wept upon them: and after that his brethren talked with him.
verse	1	45	16	And the fame thereof was heard in Pharaoh's house, saying, Joseph's brethren are come: and it pleased Pharaoh well, and his servants.
verse	1	45	17	And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, Say unto thy brethren, This do ye; lade your beasts, and go, get you unto the land of Canaan;
verse	1	45	18	And take your father and your households, and come unto me: and I will give you the good of the land of Egypt, and ye shall eat the fat of the land.
