verse	1	49	21	@@Naphtali @9is@7 a hind let loose: he giveth goodly words.
verse	1	49	22	@@Joseph @9is@7 a fruitful bough, @9even@7 a fruitful bough by a well; @9whose@7 branches run over the wall:
verse	1	49	23	@@The archers have sorely grieved him, and shot @9at him,@7 and hated him:
verse	1	49	24	@@But his bow abode in strength, and the arms of his hands were made strong by the hands of the mighty @9God@7 of Jacob; (from thence @9is@7 the shepherd, the stone of Israel:)
verse	1	49	25	@@@9Even@7 by the God of thy father, who shall help thee; and by the Almighty, who shall bless thee with blessings of heaven above, blessings of the deep that lieth under, blessings of the breasts, and of the womb:
verse	1	49	26	The blessings of thy father have prevailed above the blessings of my progenitors unto the utmost bound of the everlasting hills: they shall be on the head of Joseph, and on the crown of the head of him that was separate from his brethren.
