verse	2	2	1	@@And there went a man of the house of Levi, and took @9to wife@7 a daughter of Levi.
verse	2	2	2	@@And the woman conceived, and bare a son: and when she saw him that he @9was a@7 goodly @9child,@7 she hid him three months.
verse	2	2	3	@@And when she could not longer hide him, she took for him an ark of bulrushes, and daubed it with slime and with pitch, and put the child therein; and she laid @9it@7 in the flags by the river's brink.
verse	2	2	4	And his sister stood afar off, to wit what would be done to him.
verse	2	2	5	@@And the daughter of Pharaoh came down to wash @9herself@7 at the river; and her maidens walked along by the river's side; and when she saw the ark among the flags, she sent her maid to fetch it.
verse	2	2	6	@@And when she had opened @9it,@7 she saw the child: and, behold, the babe wept. And she had compassion on him, and said, This @9is one@7 of the Hebrews' children.
verse	2	2	7	Then said his sister to Pharaoh's daughter, Shall I go and call to thee a nurse of the Hebrew women, that she may nurse the child for thee?
verse	2	2	8	And Pharaoh's daughter said to her, Go. And the maid went and called the child's mother.
verse	2	2	9	@@And Pharaoh's daughter said unto her, Take this child away, and nurse it for me, and I will give @9thee@7 thy wages. And the woman took the child, and nursed it.
verse	2	2	10	And the child grew, and she brought him unto Pharaoh's daughter, and he became her son. And she called his name Moses: and she said, Because I drew him out of the water.
verse	2	2	11	And it came to pass in those days, when Moses was grown, that he went out unto his brethren, and looked on their burdens: and he spied an Egyptian smiting an Hebrew, one of his brethren.
verse	2	2	12	@@And he looked this way and that way, and when he saw that @9there was@7 no man, he slew the Egyptian, and hid him in the sand.
verse	2	2	13	And when he went out the second day, behold, two men of the Hebrews strove together: and he said to him that did the wrong, Wherefore smitest thou thy fellow?
verse	2	2	14	And he said, Who made thee a prince and a judge over us? intendest thou to kill me, as thou killedst the Egyptian? And Moses feared, and said, Surely this thing is known.
verse	2	2	15	Now when Pharaoh heard this thing, he sought to slay Moses. But Moses fled from the face of Pharaoh, and dwelt in the land of Midian: and he sat down by a well.
verse	2	2	16	@@Now the priest of Midian had seven daughters: and they came and drew @9water,@7 and filled the troughs to water their father's flock.
verse	2	2	17	And the shepherds came and drove them away: but Moses stood up and helped them, and watered their flock.
verse	2	2	18	@@And when they came to Reuel their father, he said, How @9is it that@7 ye are come so soon to day?
verse	2	2	19	@@And they said, An Egyptian delivered us out of the hand of the shepherds, and also drew @9water@7 enough for us, and watered the flock.
verse	2	2	20	@@And he said unto his daughters, And where @9is@7 he? why @9is@7 it @9that@7 ye have left the man? call him, that he may eat bread.
verse	2	2	21	And Moses was content to dwell with the man: and he gave Moses Zipporah his daughter.
