verse	2	14	9	@@But the Egyptians pursued after them, all the horses @9and@7 chariots of Pharaoh, and his horsemen, and his army, and overtook them encamping by the sea, beside Pihahiroth, before Baalzephon.
verse	2	14	10	And when Pharaoh drew nigh, the children of Israel lifted up their eyes, and, behold, the Egyptians marched after them; and they were sore afraid: and the children of Israel cried out unto the LORD.
verse	2	14	11	@@And they said unto Moses, Because @9there were@7 no graves in Egypt, hast thou taken us away to die in the wilderness? wherefore hast thou dealt thus with us, to carry us forth out of Egypt?
verse	2	14	12	@@@9Is@7 not this the word that we did tell thee in Egypt, saying, Let us alone, that we may serve the Egyptians? For @9it had been@7 better for us to serve the Egyptians, than that we should die in the wilderness.
verse	2	14	13	And Moses said unto the people, Fear ye not, stand still, and see the salvation of the LORD, which he will shew to you to day: for the Egyptians whom ye have seen to day, ye shall see them again no more for ever.
