verse	2	15	5	The depths have covered them: they sank into the bottom as a stone.
verse	2	15	6	Thy right hand, O LORD, is become glorious in power: thy right hand, O LORD, hath dashed in pieces the enemy.
verse	2	15	7	@@And in the greatness of thine excellency thou hast overthrown them that rose up against thee: thou sentest forth thy wrath, @9which@7 consumed them as stubble.
verse	2	15	8	@@And with the blast of thy nostrils the waters were gathered together, the floods stood upright as an heap, @9and@7 the depths were congealed in the heart of the sea.
verse	2	15	9	The enemy said, I will pursue, I will overtake, I will divide the spoil; my lust shall be satisfied upon them; I will draw my sword, my hand shall destroy them.
verse	2	15	10	Thou didst blow with thy wind, the sea covered them: they sank as lead in the mighty waters.
verse	2	15	11	@@Who @9is@7 like unto thee, O LORD, among the gods? who @9is@7 like thee, glorious in holiness, fearful @9in@7 praises, doing wonders?
verse	2	15	12	Thou stretchedst out thy right hand, the earth swallowed them.
verse	2	15	13	@@Thou in thy mercy hast led forth the people @9which@7 thou hast redeemed: thou hast guided @9them@7 in thy strength unto thy holy habitation.
verse	2	15	14	@@The people shall hear, @9and@7 be afraid: sorrow shall take hold on the inhabitants of Palestina.
verse	2	15	15	Then the dukes of Edom shall be amazed; the mighty men of Moab, trembling shall take hold upon them; all the inhabitants of Canaan shall melt away.
verse	2	15	16	@@Fear and dread shall fall upon them; by the greatness of thine arm they shall be @9as@7 still as a stone; till thy people pass over, O LORD, till the people pass over, @9which@7 thou hast purchased.
verse	2	15	17	@@Thou shalt bring them in, and plant them in the mountain of thine inheritance, @9in@7 the place, O LORD, @9which@7 thou hast made for thee to dwell in, in the Sanctuary, O Lord, @9which@7 thy hands have established.
verse	2	15	18	The LORD shall reign for ever and ever.
verse	2	15	19	@@For the horse of Pharaoh went in with his chariots and with his horsemen into the sea, and the LORD brought again the waters of the sea upon them; but the children of Israel went on dry @9land@7 in the midst of the sea.
verse	2	15	20	And Miriam the prophetess, the sister of Aaron, took a timbrel in her hand; and all the women went out after her with timbrels and with dances.
verse	2	15	21	And Miriam answered them, Sing ye to the LORD, for he hath triumphed gloriously; the horse and his rider hath he thrown into the sea.
verse	2	15	22	So Moses brought Israel from the Red sea, and they went out into the wilderness of Shur; and they went three days in the wilderness, and found no water.
verse	2	15	23	@@And when they came to Marah, they could not drink of the waters of Marah, for they @9were@7 bitter: therefore the name of it was called Marah.
verse	2	15	24	And the people murmured against Moses, saying, What shall we drink?
verse	2	15	25	@@And he cried unto the LORD; and the LORD shewed him a tree, @9which@7 when he had cast into the waters, the waters were made sweet: there he made for them a statute and an ordinance, and there he proved them,
verse	2	15	26	@@And said, If thou wilt diligently hearken to the voice of the LORD thy God, and wilt do that which is right in his sight, and wilt give ear to his commandments, and keep all his statutes, I will put none of these diseases upon thee, which I have brought upon the Egyptians: for I @9am@7 the LORD that healeth thee.
verse	2	15	27	@@And they came to Elim, where @9were@7 twelve wells of water, and threescore and ten palm trees: and they encamped there by the waters.
verse	2	16	1	@@And they took their journey from Elim, and all the congregation of the children of Israel came unto the wilderness of Sin, which @9is@7 between Elim and Sinai, on the fifteenth day of the second month after their departing out of the land of Egypt.
verse	2	16	2	And the whole congregation of the children of Israel murmured against Moses and Aaron in the wilderness:
verse	2	16	3	@@And the children of Israel said unto them, Would to God we had died by the hand of the LORD in the land of Egypt, when we sat by the flesh pots, @9and@7 when we did eat bread to the full; for ye have brought us forth into this wilderness, to kill this whole assembly with hunger.
verse	2	16	4	Then said the LORD unto Moses, Behold, I will rain bread from heaven for you; and the people shall go out and gather a certain rate every day, that I may prove them, whether they will walk in my law, or no.
verse	2	16	5	@@And it shall come to pass, that on the sixth day they shall prepare @9that@7 which they bring in; and it shall be twice as much as they gather daily.
verse	2	16	6	And Moses and Aaron said unto all the children of Israel, At even, then ye shall know that the LORD hath brought you out from the land of Egypt:
verse	2	16	7	@@And in the morning, then ye shall see the glory of the LORD; for that he heareth your murmurings against the LORD: and what @9are@7 we, that ye murmur against us?
verse	2	16	8	@@And Moses said, @9This shall be,@7 when the LORD shall give you in the evening flesh to eat, and in the morning bread to the full; for that the LORD heareth your murmurings which ye murmur against him: and what @9are@7 we? your murmurings @9are@7 not against us, but against the LORD.
verse	2	16	9	And Moses spake unto Aaron, Say unto all the congregation of the children of Israel, Come near before the LORD: for he hath heard your murmurings.
verse	2	16	10	And it came to pass, as Aaron spake unto the whole congregation of the children of Israel, that they looked toward the wilderness, and, behold, the glory of the LORD appeared in the cloud.
verse	2	16	11	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	2	16	12	@@I have heard the murmurings of the children of Israel: speak unto them, saying, At even ye shall eat flesh, and in the morning ye shall be filled with bread; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	2	16	13	And it came to pass, that at even the quails came up, and covered the camp: and in the morning the dew lay round about the host.
verse	2	16	14	@@And when the dew that lay was gone up, behold, upon the face of the wilderness @9there lay@7 a small round thing, @9as@7 small as the hoar frost on the ground.
verse	2	16	15	@@And when the children of Israel saw @9it,@7 they said one to another, It @9is@7 manna: for they wist not what it @9was.@7 And Moses said unto them, This @9is@7 the bread which the LORD hath given you to eat.
verse	2	16	16	@@This @9is@7 the thing which the LORD hath commanded, Gather of it every man @9according to@7 his eating, an omer for every man, according to the number of your persons; take ye every man for @9them@7 which @9are@7 in his tents.
verse	2	16	17	And the children of Israel did so, and gathered, some more, some less.
verse	2	16	18	@@And when they did mete @9it@7 with an omer, he that gathered much had nothing over, and he that gathered little had no lack; they gathered every man according to his eating.
verse	2	16	19	And Moses said, Let no man leave of it till the morning.
verse	2	16	20	Notwithstanding they hearkened not unto Moses; but some of them left of it until the morning, and it bred worms, and stank: and Moses was wroth with them.
verse	2	16	21	And they gathered it every morning, every man according to his eating: and when the sun waxed hot, it melted.
verse	2	16	22	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 on the sixth day they gathered twice as much bread, two omers for one @9man:@7 and all the rulers of the congregation came and told Moses.
verse	2	16	23	@@And he said unto them, This @9is that@7 which the LORD hath said, To morrow @9is@7 the rest of the holy sabbath unto the LORD: bake @9that@7 which ye will bake @9to day,@7 and seethe that ye will seethe; and that which remaineth over lay up for you to be kept until the morning.
verse	2	16	24	And they laid it up till the morning, as Moses bade: and it did not stink, neither was there any worm therein.
verse	2	16	25	@@And Moses said, Eat that to day; for to day @9is@7 a sabbath unto the LORD: to day ye shall not find it in the field.
verse	2	16	26	@@Six days ye shall gather it; but on the seventh day, @9which is@7 the sabbath, in it there shall be none.
verse	2	16	27	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 there went out @9some@7 of the people on the seventh day for to gather, and they found none.
verse	2	16	28	And the LORD said unto Moses, How long refuse ye to keep my commandments and my laws?
verse	2	16	29	See, for that the LORD hath given you the sabbath, therefore he giveth you on the sixth day the bread of two days; abide ye every man in his place, let no man go out of his place on the seventh day.
verse	2	16	30	So the people rested on the seventh day.
verse	2	16	31	@@And the house of Israel called the name thereof Manna: and it @9was@7 like coriander seed, white; and the taste of it @9was@7 like wafers @9made@7 with honey.
verse	2	16	32	@@And Moses said, This @9is@7 the thing which the LORD commandeth, Fill an omer of it to be kept for your generations; that they may see the bread wherewith I have fed you in the wilderness, when I brought you forth from the land of Egypt.
verse	2	16	33	And Moses said unto Aaron, Take a pot, and put an omer full of manna therein, and lay it up before the LORD, to be kept for your generations.
verse	2	16	34	As the LORD commanded Moses, so Aaron laid it up before the Testimony, to be kept.
verse	2	16	35	And the children of Israel did eat manna forty years, until they came to a land inhabited; they did eat manna, until they came unto the borders of the land of Canaan.
verse	2	16	36	@@Now an omer @9is@7 the tenth @9part@7 of an ephah.
verse	2	17	1	@@And all the congregation of the children of Israel journeyed from the wilderness of Sin, after their journeys, according to the commandment of the LORD, and pitched in Rephidim: and @9there was@7 no water for the people to drink.
verse	2	17	2	Wherefore the people did chide with Moses, and said, Give us water that we may drink. And Moses said unto them, Why chide ye with me? wherefore do ye tempt the LORD?
verse	2	17	3	@@And the people thirsted there for water; and the people murmured against Moses, and said, Wherefore @9is@7 this @9that@7 thou hast brought us up out of Egypt, to kill us and our children and our cattle with thirst?
verse	2	17	4	And Moses cried unto the LORD, saying, What shall I do unto this people? they be almost ready to stone me.
verse	2	17	5	And the LORD said unto Moses, Go on before the people, and take with thee of the elders of Israel; and thy rod, wherewith thou smotest the river, take in thine hand, and go.
verse	2	17	6	Behold, I will stand before thee there upon the rock in Horeb; and thou shalt smite the rock, and there shall come water out of it, that the people may drink. And Moses did so in the sight of the elders of Israel.
verse	2	17	7	And he called the name of the place Massah, and Meribah, because of the chiding of the children of Israel, and because they tempted the LORD, saying, Is the LORD among us, or not?
