verse	2	31	9	And the altar of burnt offering with all his furniture, and the laver and his foot,
verse	2	31	10	And the cloths of service, and the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest's office,
verse	2	31	11	@@And the anointing oil, and sweet incense for the holy @9place:@7 according to all that I have commanded thee shall they do.
verse	2	31	12	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	2	31	13	@@Speak thou also unto the children of Israel, saying, Verily my sabbaths ye shall keep: for it is a sign between me and you throughout your generations; that ye may know that I @9am@7 the LORD that doth sanctify you.
verse	2	31	14	@@Ye shall keep the sabbath therefore; for it @9is@7 holy unto you: every one that defileth it shall surely be put to death: for whosoever doeth @9any@7 work therein, that soul shall be cut off from among his people.
verse	2	31	15	@@Six days may work be done; but in the seventh is the sabbath of rest, holy to the LORD: whosoever doeth @9any@7 work in the sabbath day, he shall surely be put to death.
verse	2	31	16	@@Wherefore the children of Israel shall keep the sabbath, to observe the sabbath throughout their generations, @9for@7 a perpetual covenant.
