verse	2	32	4	@@And he received @9them@7 at their hand, and fashioned it with a graving tool, after he had made it a molten calf: and they said, These @9be@7 thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.
verse	2	32	5	@@And when Aaron saw @9it,@7 he built an altar before it; and Aaron made proclamation, and said, To morrow @9is@7 a feast to the LORD.
verse	2	32	6	And they rose up early on the morrow, and offered burnt offerings, and brought peace offerings; and the people sat down to eat and to drink, and rose up to play.
verse	2	32	7	@@And the LORD said unto Moses, Go, get thee down; for thy people, which thou broughtest out of the land of Egypt, have corrupted @9themselves: @7
verse	2	32	8	@@They have turned aside quickly out of the way which I commanded them: they have made them a molten calf, and have worshipped it, and have sacrificed thereunto, and said, These @9be@7 thy gods, O Israel, which have brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.
verse	2	32	9	@@And the LORD said unto Moses, I have seen this people, and, behold, it @9is@7 a stiffnecked people:
verse	2	32	10	Now therefore let me alone, that my wrath may wax hot against them, and that I may consume them: and I will make of thee a great nation.
verse	2	32	11	And Moses besought the LORD his God, and said, LORD, why doth thy wrath wax hot against thy people, which thou hast brought forth out of the land of Egypt with great power, and with a mighty hand?
verse	2	32	12	Wherefore should the Egyptians speak, and say, For mischief did he bring them out, to slay them in the mountains, and to consume them from the face of the earth? Turn from thy fierce wrath, and repent of this evil against thy people.
verse	2	32	13	@@Remember Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, thy servants, to whom thou swarest by thine own self, and saidst unto them, I will multiply your seed as the stars of heaven, and all this land that I have spoken of will I give unto your seed, and they shall inherit @9it@7 for ever.
verse	2	32	14	And the LORD repented of the evil which he thought to do unto his people.
verse	2	32	15	@@And Moses turned, and went down from the mount, and the two tables of the testimony @9were@7 in his hand: the tables @9were@7 written on both their sides; on the one side and on the other @9were@7 they written.
verse	2	32	16	@@And the tables @9were@7 the work of God, and the writing @9was@7 the writing of God, graven upon the tables.
verse	2	32	17	@@And when Joshua heard the noise of the people as they shouted, he said unto Moses, @9There is@7 a noise of war in the camp.
verse	2	32	18	@@And he said, @9It is@7 not the voice of @9them that@7 shout for mastery, neither @9is it@7 the voice of @9them that@7 cry for being overcome: @9but@7 the noise of @9them that@7 sing do I hear.
verse	2	32	19	And it came to pass, as soon as he came nigh unto the camp, that he saw the calf, and the dancing: and Moses' anger waxed hot, and he cast the tables out of his hands, and brake them beneath the mount.
verse	2	32	20	@@And he took the calf which they had made, and burnt @9it@7 in the fire, and ground @9it@7 to powder, and strawed @9it@7 upon the water, and made the children of Israel drink @9of it. @7
verse	2	32	21	And Moses said unto Aaron, What did this people unto thee, that thou hast brought so great a sin upon them?
verse	2	32	22	@@And Aaron said, Let not the anger of my lord wax hot: thou knowest the people, that they are @9set@7 on mischief.
verse	2	32	23	@@For they said unto me, Make us gods, which shall go before us: for @9as for@7 this Moses, the man that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we wot not what is become of him.
verse	2	32	24	@@And I said unto them, Whosoever hath any gold, let them break @9it@7 off. So they gave @9it@7 me: then I cast it into the fire, and there came out this calf.
verse	2	32	25	@@And when Moses saw that the people @9were@7 naked; (for Aaron had made them naked unto @9their@7 shame among their enemies:)
verse	2	32	26	@@Then Moses stood in the gate of the camp, and said, Who @9is@7 on the LORD'S side? @9let him come@7 unto me. And all the sons of Levi gathered themselves together unto him.
verse	2	32	27	@@And he said unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Put every man his sword by his side, @9and@7 go in and out from gate to gate throughout the camp, and slay every man his brother, and every man his companion, and every man his neighbour.
verse	2	32	28	And the children of Levi did according to the word of Moses: and there fell of the people that day about three thousand men.
