verse	2	33	1	@@And the LORD said unto Moses, Depart, @9and@7 go up hence, thou and the people which thou hast brought up out of the land of Egypt, unto the land which I sware unto Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, saying, Unto thy seed will I give it:
verse	2	33	2	And I will send an angel before thee; and I will drive out the Canaanite, the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite:
verse	2	33	3	@@Unto a land flowing with milk and honey: for I will not go up in the midst of thee; for thou @9art@7 a stiffnecked people: lest I consume thee in the way.
verse	2	33	4	And when the people heard these evil tidings, they mourned: and no man did put on him his ornaments.
verse	2	33	5	@@For the LORD had said unto Moses, Say unto the children of Israel, Ye @9are@7 a stiffnecked people: I will come up into the midst of thee in a moment, and consume thee: therefore now put off thy ornaments from thee, that I may know what to do unto thee.
verse	2	33	6	And the children of Israel stripped themselves of their ornaments by the mount Horeb.
verse	2	33	7	@@And Moses took the tabernacle, and pitched it without the camp, afar off from the camp, and called it the Tabernacle of the congregation. And it came to pass, @9that@7 every one which sought the LORD went out unto the tabernacle of the congregation, which @9was@7 without the camp.
verse	2	33	8	@@And it came to pass, when Moses went out unto the tabernacle, @9that@7 all the people rose up, and stood every man @9at@7 his tent door, and looked after Moses, until he was gone into the tabernacle.
verse	2	33	9	@@And it came to pass, as Moses entered into the tabernacle, the cloudy pillar descended, and stood @9at@7 the door of the tabernacle, and @9the@7 LORD talked with Moses.
verse	2	33	10	@@And all the people saw the cloudy pillar stand @9at@7 the tabernacle door: and all the people rose up and worshipped, every man @9in@7 his tent door.
verse	2	33	11	And the LORD spake unto Moses face to face, as a man speaketh unto his friend. And he turned again into the camp: but his servant Joshua, the son of Nun, a young man, departed not out of the tabernacle.
verse	2	33	12	And Moses said unto the LORD, See, thou sayest unto me, Bring up this people: and thou hast not let me know whom thou wilt send with me. Yet thou hast said, I know thee by name, and thou hast also found grace in my sight.
verse	2	33	13	@@Now therefore, I pray thee, if I have found grace in thy sight, shew me now thy way, that I may know thee, that I may find grace in thy sight: and consider that this nation @9is@7 thy people.
verse	2	33	14	@@And he said, My presence shall go @9with thee,@7 and I will give thee rest.
verse	2	33	15	@@And he said unto him, If thy presence go not @9with me,@7 carry us not up hence.
verse	2	33	16	@@For wherein shall it be known here that I and thy people have found grace in thy sight? @9is it@7 not in that thou goest with us? so shall we be separated, I and thy people, from all the people that @9are@7 upon the face of the earth.
verse	2	33	17	And the LORD said unto Moses, I will do this thing also that thou hast spoken: for thou hast found grace in my sight, and I know thee by name.
verse	2	33	18	And he said, I beseech thee, shew me thy glory.
verse	2	33	19	And he said, I will make all my goodness pass before thee, and I will proclaim the name of the LORD before thee; and will be gracious to whom I will be gracious, and will shew mercy on whom I will shew mercy.
verse	2	33	20	And he said, Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.
verse	2	33	21	@@And the LORD said, Behold, @9there is@7 a place by me, and thou shalt stand upon a rock:
