verse	2	39	41	@@The cloths of service to do service in the holy @9place,@7 and the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and his sons' garments, to minister in the priest's office.
verse	2	39	42	According to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so the children of Israel made all the work.
verse	2	39	43	And Moses did look upon all the work, and, behold, they had done it as the LORD had commanded, even so had they done it: and Moses blessed them.
verse	2	40	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	2	40	2	On the first day of the first month shalt thou set up the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation.
verse	2	40	3	And thou shalt put therein the ark of the testimony, and cover the ark with the vail.
verse	2	40	4	And thou shalt bring in the table, and set in order the things that are to be set in order upon it; and thou shalt bring in the candlestick, and light the lamps thereof.
verse	2	40	5	And thou shalt set the altar of gold for the incense before the ark of the testimony, and put the hanging of the door to the tabernacle.
verse	2	40	6	And thou shalt set the altar of the burnt offering before the door of the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation.
verse	2	40	7	And thou shalt set the laver between the tent of the congregation and the altar, and shalt put water therein.
verse	2	40	8	And thou shalt set up the court round about, and hang up the hanging at the court gate.
verse	2	40	9	@@And thou shalt take the anointing oil, and anoint the tabernacle, and all that @9is@7 therein, and shalt hallow it, and all the vessels thereof: and it shall be holy.
verse	2	40	10	And thou shalt anoint the altar of the burnt offering, and all his vessels, and sanctify the altar: and it shall be an altar most holy.
verse	2	40	11	And thou shalt anoint the laver and his foot, and sanctify it.
verse	2	40	12	And thou shalt bring Aaron and his sons unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and wash them with water.
verse	2	40	13	And thou shalt put upon Aaron the holy garments, and anoint him, and sanctify him; that he may minister unto me in the priest's office.
verse	2	40	14	And thou shalt bring his sons, and clothe them with coats:
verse	2	40	15	And thou shalt anoint them, as thou didst anoint their father, that they may minister unto me in the priest's office: for their anointing shall surely be an everlasting priesthood throughout their generations.
verse	2	40	16	Thus did Moses: according to all that the LORD commanded him, so did he.
verse	2	40	17	@@And it came to pass in the first month in the second year, on the first @9day@7 of the month, @9that@7 the tabernacle was reared up.
verse	2	40	18	And Moses reared up the tabernacle, and fastened his sockets, and set up the boards thereof, and put in the bars thereof, and reared up his pillars.
verse	2	40	19	And he spread abroad the tent over the tabernacle, and put the covering of the tent above upon it; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	2	40	20	And he took and put the testimony into the ark, and set the staves on the ark, and put the mercy seat above upon the ark:
verse	2	40	21	And he brought the ark into the tabernacle, and set up the vail of the covering, and covered the ark of the testimony; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	2	40	22	And he put the table in the tent of the congregation, upon the side of the tabernacle northward, without the vail.
verse	2	40	23	And he set the bread in order upon it before the LORD; as the LORD had commanded Moses.
verse	2	40	24	And he put the candlestick in the tent of the congregation, over against the table, on the side of the tabernacle southward.
verse	2	40	25	And he lighted the lamps before the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	2	40	26	And he put the golden altar in the tent of the congregation before the vail:
verse	2	40	27	And he burnt sweet incense thereon; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	2	40	28	@@And he set up the hanging @9at@7 the door of the tabernacle.
verse	2	40	29	@@And he put the altar of burnt offering @9by@7 the door of the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation, and offered upon it the burnt offering and the meat offering; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	2	40	30	@@And he set the laver between the tent of the congregation and the altar, and put water there, to wash @9withal. @7
verse	2	40	31	And Moses and Aaron and his sons washed their hands and their feet thereat:
verse	2	40	32	When they went into the tent of the congregation, and when they came near unto the altar, they washed; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	2	40	33	And he reared up the court round about the tabernacle and the altar, and set up the hanging of the court gate. So Moses finished the work.
verse	2	40	34	Then a cloud covered the tent of the congregation, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.
verse	2	40	35	And Moses was not able to enter into the tent of the congregation, because the cloud abode thereon, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.
verse	2	40	36	And when the cloud was taken up from over the tabernacle, the children of Israel went onward in all their journeys:
verse	2	40	37	But if the cloud were not taken up, then they journeyed not till the day that it was taken up.
verse	2	40	38	@@For the cloud of the LORD @9was@7 upon the tabernacle by day, and fire was on it by night, in the sight of all the house of Israel, throughout all their journeys.
verse	3	1	1	And the LORD called unto Moses, and spake unto him out of the tabernacle of the congregation, saying,
verse	3	1	2	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, If any man of you bring an offering unto the LORD, ye shall bring your offering of the cattle, @9even@7 of the herd, and of the flock.
verse	3	1	3	@@If his offering @9be@7 a burnt sacrifice of the herd, let him offer a male without blemish: he shall offer it of his own voluntary will at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD.
verse	3	1	4	And he shall put his hand upon the head of the burnt offering; and it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him.
verse	3	1	5	@@And he shall kill the bullock before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron's sons, shall bring the blood, and sprinkle the blood round about upon the altar that @9is by@7 the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	1	6	And he shall flay the burnt offering, and cut it into his pieces.
verse	3	1	7	And the sons of Aaron the priest shall put fire upon the altar, and lay the wood in order upon the fire:
verse	3	1	8	@@And the priests, Aaron's sons, shall lay the parts, the head, and the fat, in order upon the wood that @9is@7 on the fire which @9is@7 upon the altar:
verse	3	1	9	@@But his inwards and his legs shall he wash in water: and the priest shall burn all on the altar, @9to be@7 a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	3	1	10	@@And if his offering @9be@7 of the flocks, @9namely,@7 of the sheep, or of the goats, for a burnt sacrifice; he shall bring it a male without blemish.
verse	3	1	11	And he shall kill it on the side of the altar northward before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron's sons, shall sprinkle his blood round about upon the altar.
verse	3	1	12	@@And he shall cut it into his pieces, with his head and his fat: and the priest shall lay them in order on the wood that @9is@7 on the fire which @9is@7 upon the altar:
verse	3	1	13	@@But he shall wash the inwards and the legs with water: and the priest shall bring @9it@7 all, and burn @9it@7 upon the altar: it @9is@7 a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	3	1	14	@@And if the burnt sacrifice for his offering to the LORD @9be@7 of fowls, then he shall bring his offering of turtledoves, or of young pigeons.
verse	3	1	15	@@And the priest shall bring it unto the altar, and wring off his head, and burn @9it@7 on the altar; and the blood thereof shall be wrung out at the side of the altar:
verse	3	1	16	And he shall pluck away his crop with his feathers, and cast it beside the altar on the east part, by the place of the ashes:
verse	3	1	17	@@And he shall cleave it with the wings thereof, @9but@7 shall not divide @9it@7 asunder: and the priest shall burn it upon the altar, upon the wood that @9is@7 upon the fire: it @9is@7 a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	3	2	1	@@And when any will offer a meat offering unto the LORD, his offering shall be @9of@7 fine flour; and he shall pour oil upon it, and put frankincense thereon:
verse	3	2	2	@@And he shall bring it to Aaron's sons the priests: and he shall take thereout his handful of the flour thereof, and of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof; and the priest shall burn the memorial of it upon the altar, @9to be@7 an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD:
verse	3	2	3	@@And the remnant of the meat offering @9shall be@7 Aaron's and his sons': @9it is@7 a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.
verse	3	2	4	@@And if thou bring an oblation of a meat offering baken in the oven, @9it shall be@7 unleavened cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, or unleavened wafers anointed with oil.
verse	3	2	5	@@And if thy oblation @9be@7 a meat offering @9baken@7 in a pan, it shall be @9of@7 fine flour unleavened, mingled with oil.
verse	3	2	6	@@Thou shalt part it in pieces, and pour oil thereon: it @9is@7 a meat offering.
verse	3	2	7	@@And if thy oblation @9be@7 a meat offering @9baken@7 in the fryingpan, it shall be made @9of@7 fine flour with oil.
verse	3	2	8	And thou shalt bring the meat offering that is made of these things unto the LORD: and when it is presented unto the priest, he shall bring it unto the altar.
verse	3	2	9	@@And the priest shall take from the meat offering a memorial thereof, and shall burn @9it@7 upon the altar: @9it is@7 an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	3	2	10	@@And that which is left of the meat offering @9shall be@7 Aaron's and his sons': @9it is@7 a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.
verse	3	2	11	No meat offering, which ye shall bring unto the LORD, shall be made with leaven: for ye shall burn no leaven, nor any honey, in any offering of the LORD made by fire.
verse	3	2	12	As for the oblation of the firstfruits, ye shall offer them unto the LORD: but they shall not be burnt on the altar for a sweet savour.
verse	3	2	13	And every oblation of thy meat offering shalt thou season with salt; neither shalt thou suffer the salt of the covenant of thy God to be lacking from thy meat offering: with all thine offerings thou shalt offer salt.
verse	3	2	14	@@And if thou offer a meat offering of thy firstfruits unto the LORD, thou shalt offer for the meat offering of thy firstfruits green ears of corn dried by the fire, @9even@7 corn beaten out of full ears.
verse	3	2	15	@@And thou shalt put oil upon it, and lay frankincense thereon: it @9is@7 a meat offering.
verse	3	2	16	@@And the priest shall burn the memorial of it, @9part@7 of the beaten corn thereof, and @9part@7 of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof: @9it is@7 an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
verse	3	3	1	@@And if his oblation @9be@7 a sacrifice of peace offering, if he offer @9it@7 of the herd; whether @9it be@7 a male or female, he shall offer it without blemish before the LORD.
verse	3	3	2	@@And he shall lay his hand upon the head of his offering, and kill it @9at@7 the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron's sons the priests shall sprinkle the blood upon the altar round about.
verse	3	3	3	@@And he shall offer of the sacrifice of the peace offering an offering made by fire unto the LORD; the fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that @9is@7 upon the inwards,
verse	3	3	4	@@And the two kidneys, and the fat that @9is@7 on them, which @9is@7 by the flanks, and the caul above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away.
verse	3	3	5	@@And Aaron's sons shall burn it on the altar upon the burnt sacrifice, which @9is@7 upon the wood that @9is@7 on the fire: @9it is@7 an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	3	3	6	@@And if his offering for a sacrifice of peace offering unto the LORD @9be@7 of the flock; male or female, he shall offer it without blemish.
verse	3	3	7	If he offer a lamb for his offering, then shall he offer it before the LORD.
verse	3	3	8	And he shall lay his hand upon the head of his offering, and kill it before the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron's sons shall sprinkle the blood thereof round about upon the altar.
verse	3	3	9	@@And he shall offer of the sacrifice of the peace offering an offering made by fire unto the LORD; the fat thereof, @9and@7 the whole rump, it shall he take off hard by the backbone; and the fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that @9is@7 upon the inwards,
verse	3	3	10	@@And the two kidneys, and the fat that @9is@7 upon them, which @9is@7 by the flanks, and the caul above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away.
verse	3	3	11	@@And the priest shall burn it upon the altar: @9it is@7 the food of the offering made by fire unto the LORD.
verse	3	3	12	@@And if his offering @9be@7 a goat, then he shall offer it before the LORD.
verse	3	3	13	And he shall lay his hand upon the head of it, and kill it before the tabernacle of the congregation: and the sons of Aaron shall sprinkle the blood thereof upon the altar round about.
verse	3	3	14	@@And he shall offer thereof his offering, @9even@7 an offering made by fire unto the LORD; the fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that @9is@7 upon the inwards,
verse	3	3	15	@@And the two kidneys, and the fat that @9is@7 upon them, which @9is@7 by the flanks, and the caul above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away.
verse	3	3	16	@@And the priest shall burn them upon the altar: @9it is@7 the food of the offering made by fire for a sweet savour: all the fat @9is@7 the LORD'S.
verse	3	3	17	@@@9It shall be@7 a perpetual statute for your generations throughout all your dwellings, that ye eat neither fat nor blood.
verse	3	4	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	4	2	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, If a soul shall sin through ignorance against any of the commandments of the LORD @9concerning things@7 which ought not to be done, and shall do against any of them:
verse	3	4	3	If the priest that is anointed do sin according to the sin of the people; then let him bring for his sin, which he hath sinned, a young bullock without blemish unto the LORD for a sin offering.
verse	3	4	4	And he shall bring the bullock unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD; and shall lay his hand upon the bullock's head, and kill the bullock before the LORD.
verse	3	4	5	And the priest that is anointed shall take of the bullock's blood, and bring it to the tabernacle of the congregation:
verse	3	4	6	And the priest shall dip his finger in the blood, and sprinkle of the blood seven times before the LORD, before the vail of the sanctuary.
verse	3	4	7	@@And the priest shall put @9some@7 of the blood upon the horns of the altar of sweet incense before the LORD, which @9is@7 in the tabernacle of the congregation; and shall pour all the blood of the bullock at the bottom of the altar of the burnt offering, which @9is at@7 the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	4	8	@@And he shall take off from it all the fat of the bullock for the sin offering; the fat that covereth the inwards, and all the fat that @9is@7 upon the inwards,
verse	3	4	9	@@And the two kidneys, and the fat that @9is@7 upon them, which @9is@7 by the flanks, and the caul above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away,
verse	3	4	10	As it was taken off from the bullock of the sacrifice of peace offerings: and the priest shall burn them upon the altar of the burnt offering.
verse	3	4	11	And the skin of the bullock, and all his flesh, with his head, and with his legs, and his inwards, and his dung,
verse	3	4	12	Even the whole bullock shall he carry forth without the camp unto a clean place, where the ashes are poured out, and burn him on the wood with fire: where the ashes are poured out shall he be burnt.
verse	3	4	13	@@And if the whole congregation of Israel sin through ignorance, and the thing be hid from the eyes of the assembly, and they have done @9somewhat against@7 any of the commandments of the LORD @9concerning things@7 which should not be done, and are guilty;
verse	3	4	14	When the sin, which they have sinned against it, is known, then the congregation shall offer a young bullock for the sin, and bring him before the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	4	15	And the elders of the congregation shall lay their hands upon the head of the bullock before the LORD: and the bullock shall be killed before the LORD.
verse	3	4	16	And the priest that is anointed shall bring of the bullock's blood to the tabernacle of the congregation:
verse	3	4	17	@@And the priest shall dip his finger @9in some@7 of the blood, and sprinkle @9it@7 seven times before the LORD, @9even@7 before the vail.
verse	3	4	18	@@And he shall put @9some@7 of the blood upon the horns of the altar which @9is@7 before the LORD, that @9is@7 in the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall pour out all the blood at the bottom of the altar of the burnt offering, which @9is at@7 the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	4	19	@@And he shall take all his fat from him, and burn @9it@7 upon the altar.
verse	3	4	20	And he shall do with the bullock as he did with the bullock for a sin offering, so shall he do with this: and the priest shall make an atonement for them, and it shall be forgiven them.
verse	3	4	21	@@And he shall carry forth the bullock without the camp, and burn him as he burned the first bullock: it @9is@7 a sin offering for the congregation.
verse	3	4	22	@@When a ruler hath sinned, and done @9somewhat@7 through ignorance @9against@7 any of the commandments of the LORD his God @9concerning things@7 which should not be done, and is guilty;
verse	3	4	23	Or if his sin, wherein he hath sinned, come to his knowledge; he shall bring his offering, a kid of the goats, a male without blemish:
verse	3	4	24	@@And he shall lay his hand upon the head of the goat, and kill it in the place where they kill the burnt offering before the LORD: it @9is@7 a sin offering.
verse	3	4	25	@@And the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put @9it@7 upon the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out his blood at the bottom of the altar of burnt offering.
verse	3	4	26	And he shall burn all his fat upon the altar, as the fat of the sacrifice of peace offerings: and the priest shall make an atonement for him as concerning his sin, and it shall be forgiven him.
verse	3	4	27	@@And if any one of the common people sin through ignorance, while he doeth @9somewhat against@7 any of the commandments of the LORD @9concerning things@7 which ought not to be done, and be guilty;
verse	3	4	28	Or if his sin, which he hath sinned, come to his knowledge: then he shall bring his offering, a kid of the goats, a female without blemish, for his sin which he hath sinned.
verse	3	4	29	And he shall lay his hand upon the head of the sin offering, and slay the sin offering in the place of the burnt offering.
verse	3	4	30	@@And the priest shall take of the blood thereof with his finger, and put @9it@7 upon the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out all the blood thereof at the bottom of the altar.
verse	3	4	31	@@And he shall take away all the fat thereof, as the fat is taken away from off the sacrifice of peace offerings; and the priest shall burn @9it@7 upon the altar for a sweet savour unto the LORD; and the priest shall make an atonement for him, and it shall be forgiven him.
verse	3	4	32	And if he bring a lamb for a sin offering, he shall bring it a female without blemish.
verse	3	4	33	And he shall lay his hand upon the head of the sin offering, and slay it for a sin offering in the place where they kill the burnt offering.
verse	3	4	34	@@And the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put @9it@7 upon the horns of the altar of burnt offering, and shall pour out all the blood thereof at the bottom of the altar:
verse	3	4	35	And he shall take away all the fat thereof, as the fat of the lamb is taken away from the sacrifice of the peace offerings; and the priest shall burn them upon the altar, according to the offerings made by fire unto the LORD: and the priest shall make an atonement for his sin that he hath committed, and it shall be forgiven him.
verse	3	5	1	@@And if a soul sin, and hear the voice of swearing, and @9is@7 a witness, whether he hath seen or known @9of it;@7 if he do not utter @9it,@7 then he shall bear his iniquity.
verse	3	5	2	@@Or if a soul touch any unclean thing, whether @9it be@7 a carcase of an unclean beast, or a carcase of unclean cattle, or the carcase of unclean creeping things, and @9if@7 it be hidden from him; he also shall be unclean, and guilty.
verse	3	5	3	@@Or if he touch the uncleanness of man, whatsoever uncleanness @9it be@7 that a man shall be defiled withal, and it be hid from him; when he knoweth @9of it,@7 then he shall be guilty.
verse	3	5	4	@@Or if a soul swear, pronouncing with @9his@7 lips to do evil, or to do good, whatsoever @9it be@7 that a man shall pronounce with an oath, and it be hid from him; when he knoweth @9of it,@7 then he shall be guilty in one of these.
verse	3	5	5	@@And it shall be, when he shall be guilty in one of these @9things,@7 that he shall confess that he hath sinned in that @9thing: @7
verse	3	5	6	And he shall bring his trespass offering unto the LORD for his sin which he hath sinned, a female from the flock, a lamb or a kid of the goats, for a sin offering; and the priest shall make an atonement for him concerning his sin.
verse	3	5	7	And if he be not able to bring a lamb, then he shall bring for his trespass, which he hath committed, two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, unto the LORD; one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering.
verse	3	5	8	@@And he shall bring them unto the priest, who shall offer @9that@7 which @9is@7 for the sin offering first, and wring off his head from his neck, but shall not divide @9it@7 asunder:
verse	3	5	9	@@And he shall sprinkle of the blood of the sin offering upon the side of the altar; and the rest of the blood shall be wrung out at the bottom of the altar: it @9is@7 a sin offering.
verse	3	5	10	@@And he shall offer the second @9for@7 a burnt offering, according to the manner: and the priest shall make an atonement for him for his sin which he hath sinned, and it shall be forgiven him.
verse	3	5	11	@@But if he be not able to bring two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, then he that sinned shall bring for his offering the tenth part of an ephah of fine flour for a sin offering; he shall put no oil upon it, neither shall he put @9any@7 frankincense thereon: for it @9is@7 a sin offering.
verse	3	5	12	@@Then shall he bring it to the priest, and the priest shall take his handful of it, @9even@7 a memorial thereof, and burn @9it@7 on the altar, according to the offerings made by fire unto the LORD: it @9is@7 a sin offering.
verse	3	5	13	@@And the priest shall make an atonement for him as touching his sin that he hath sinned in one of these, and it shall be forgiven him: and @9the remnant@7 shall be the priest's, as a meat offering.
verse	3	5	14	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	5	15	If a soul commit a trespass, and sin through ignorance, in the holy things of the LORD; then he shall bring for his trespass unto the LORD a ram without blemish out of the flocks, with thy estimation by shekels of silver, after the shekel of the sanctuary, for a trespass offering:
verse	3	5	16	And he shall make amends for the harm that he hath done in the holy thing, and shall add the fifth part thereto, and give it unto the priest: and the priest shall make an atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering, and it shall be forgiven him.
verse	3	5	17	@@And if a soul sin, and commit any of these things which are forbidden to be done by the commandments of the LORD; though he wist @9it@7 not, yet is he guilty, and shall bear his iniquity.
verse	3	5	18	@@And he shall bring a ram without blemish out of the flock, with thy estimation, for a trespass offering, unto the priest: and the priest shall make an atonement for him concerning his ignorance wherein he erred and wist @9it@7 not, and it shall be forgiven him.
verse	3	5	19	@@It @9is@7 a trespass offering: he hath certainly trespassed against the LORD.
verse	3	6	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	6	2	If a soul sin, and commit a trespass against the LORD, and lie unto his neighbour in that which was delivered him to keep, or in fellowship, or in a thing taken away by violence, or hath deceived his neighbour;
verse	3	6	3	Or have found that which was lost, and lieth concerning it, and sweareth falsely; in any of all these that a man doeth, sinning therein:
verse	3	6	4	Then it shall be, because he hath sinned, and is guilty, that he shall restore that which he took violently away, or the thing which he hath deceitfully gotten, or that which was delivered him to keep, or the lost thing which he found,
verse	3	6	5	@@Or all that about which he hath sworn falsely; he shall even restore it in the principal, and shall add the fifth part more thereto, @9and@7 give it unto him to whom it appertaineth, in the day of his trespass offering.
verse	3	6	6	And he shall bring his trespass offering unto the LORD, a ram without blemish out of the flock, with thy estimation, for a trespass offering, unto the priest:
verse	3	6	7	And the priest shall make an atonement for him before the LORD: and it shall be forgiven him for any thing of all that he hath done in trespassing therein.
verse	3	6	8	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	6	9	@@Command Aaron and his sons, saying, This @9is@7 the law of the burnt offering: It @9is@7 the burnt offering, because of the burning upon the altar all night unto the morning, and the fire of the altar shall be burning in it.
verse	3	6	10	And the priest shall put on his linen garment, and his linen breeches shall he put upon his flesh, and take up the ashes which the fire hath consumed with the burnt offering on the altar, and he shall put them beside the altar.
verse	3	6	11	And he shall put off his garments, and put on other garments, and carry forth the ashes without the camp unto a clean place.
verse	3	6	12	And the fire upon the altar shall be burning in it; it shall not be put out: and the priest shall burn wood on it every morning, and lay the burnt offering in order upon it; and he shall burn thereon the fat of the peace offerings.
verse	3	6	13	The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out.
verse	3	6	14	@@And this @9is@7 the law of the meat offering: the sons of Aaron shall offer it before the LORD, before the altar.
verse	3	6	15	@@And he shall take of it his handful, of the flour of the meat offering, and of the oil thereof, and all the frankincense which @9is@7 upon the meat offering, and shall burn @9it@7 upon the altar @9for@7 a sweet savour, @9even@7 the memorial of it, unto the LORD.
verse	3	6	16	And the remainder thereof shall Aaron and his sons eat: with unleavened bread shall it be eaten in the holy place; in the court of the tabernacle of the congregation they shall eat it.
verse	3	6	17	@@It shall not be baken with leaven. I have given it @9unto them for@7 their portion of my offerings made by fire; it @9is@7 most holy, as @9is@7 the sin offering, and as the trespass offering.
verse	3	6	18	@@All the males among the children of Aaron shall eat of it. @9It shall be@7 a statute for ever in your generations concerning the offerings of the LORD made by fire: every one that toucheth them shall be holy.
verse	3	6	19	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	6	20	@@This @9is@7 the offering of Aaron and of his sons, which they shall offer unto the LORD in the day when he is anointed; the tenth part of an ephah of fine flour for a meat offering perpetual, half of it in the morning, and half thereof at night.
verse	3	6	21	@@In a pan it shall be made with oil; @9and when it is@7 baken, thou shalt bring it in: @9and@7 the baken pieces of the meat offering shalt thou offer @9for@7 a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	3	6	22	@@And the priest of his sons that is anointed in his stead shall offer it: @9it is@7 a statute for ever unto the LORD; it shall be wholly burnt.
verse	3	6	23	For every meat offering for the priest shall be wholly burnt: it shall not be eaten.
verse	3	6	24	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	6	25	@@Speak unto Aaron and to his sons, saying, This @9is@7 the law of the sin offering: In the place where the burnt offering is killed shall the sin offering be killed before the LORD: it @9is@7 most holy.
verse	3	6	26	The priest that offereth it for sin shall eat it: in the holy place shall it be eaten, in the court of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	6	27	Whatsoever shall touch the flesh thereof shall be holy: and when there is sprinkled of the blood thereof upon any garment, thou shalt wash that whereon it was sprinkled in the holy place.
verse	3	6	28	But the earthen vessel wherein it is sodden shall be broken: and if it be sodden in a brasen pot, it shall be both scoured, and rinsed in water.
verse	3	6	29	@@All the males among the priests shall eat thereof: it @9is@7 most holy.
verse	3	6	30	@@And no sin offering, whereof @9any@7 of the blood is brought into the tabernacle of the congregation to reconcile @9withal@7 in the holy @9place,@7 shall be eaten: it shall be burnt in the fire.
verse	3	7	1	@@Likewise this @9is@7 the law of the trespass offering: it @9is@7 most holy.
verse	3	7	2	In the place where they kill the burnt offering shall they kill the trespass offering: and the blood thereof shall he sprinkle round about upon the altar.
verse	3	7	3	And he shall offer of it all the fat thereof; the rump, and the fat that covereth the inwards,
verse	3	7	4	@@And the two kidneys, and the fat that @9is@7 on them, which @9is@7 by the flanks, and the caul @9that is@7 above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away:
verse	3	7	5	@@And the priest shall burn them upon the altar @9for@7 an offering made by fire unto the LORD: it @9is@7 a trespass offering.
verse	3	7	6	@@Every male among the priests shall eat thereof: it shall be eaten in the holy place: it @9is@7 most holy.
verse	3	7	7	@@As the sin offering @9is,@7 so @9is@7 the trespass offering: @9there is@7 one law for them: the priest that maketh atonement therewith shall have @9it. @7
verse	3	7	8	@@And the priest that offereth any man's burnt offering, @9even@7 the priest shall have to himself the skin of the burnt offering which he hath offered.
verse	3	7	9	And all the meat offering that is baken in the oven, and all that is dressed in the fryingpan, and in the pan, shall be the priest's that offereth it.
verse	3	7	10	@@And every meat offering, mingled with oil, and dry, shall all the sons of Aaron have, one @9as much@7 as another.
verse	3	7	11	@@And this @9is@7 the law of the sacrifice of peace offerings, which he shall offer unto the LORD.
verse	3	7	12	If he offer it for a thanksgiving, then he shall offer with the sacrifice of thanksgiving unleavened cakes mingled with oil, and unleavened wafers anointed with oil, and cakes mingled with oil, of fine flour, fried.
verse	3	7	13	@@Besides the cakes, he shall offer @9for@7 his offering leavened bread with the sacrifice of thanksgiving of his peace offerings.
verse	3	7	14	@@And of it he shall offer one out of the whole oblation @9for@7 an heave offering unto the LORD, @9and@7 it shall be the priest's that sprinkleth the blood of the peace offerings.
verse	3	7	15	And the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings for thanksgiving shall be eaten the same day that it is offered; he shall not leave any of it until the morning.
verse	3	7	16	@@But if the sacrifice of his offering @9be@7 a vow, or a voluntary offering, it shall be eaten the same day that he offereth his sacrifice: and on the morrow also the remainder of it shall be eaten:
verse	3	7	17	But the remainder of the flesh of the sacrifice on the third day shall be burnt with fire.
verse	3	7	18	@@And if @9any@7 of the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings be eaten at all on the third day, it shall not be accepted, neither shall it be imputed unto him that offereth it: it shall be an abomination, and the soul that eateth of it shall bear his iniquity.
verse	3	7	19	@@And the flesh that toucheth any unclean @9thing@7 shall not be eaten; it shall be burnt with fire: and as for the flesh, all that be clean shall eat thereof.
verse	3	7	20	@@But the soul that eateth @9of@7 the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings, that @9pertain@7 unto the LORD, having his uncleanness upon him, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.
verse	3	7	21	@@Moreover the soul that shall touch any unclean @9thing, as@7 the uncleanness of man, or @9any@7 unclean beast, or any abominable unclean @9thing,@7 and eat of the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings, which @9pertain@7 unto the LORD, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.
verse	3	7	22	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	7	23	Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, Ye shall eat no manner of fat, of ox, or of sheep, or of goat.
verse	3	7	24	And the fat of the beast that dieth of itself, and the fat of that which is torn with beasts, may be used in any other use: but ye shall in no wise eat of it.
verse	3	7	25	@@For whosoever eateth the fat of the beast, of which men offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD, even the soul that eateth @9it@7 shall be cut off from his people.
verse	3	7	26	@@Moreover ye shall eat no manner of blood, @9whether it be@7 of fowl or of beast, in any of your dwellings.
verse	3	7	27	@@Whatsoever soul @9it be@7 that eateth any manner of blood, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.
verse	3	7	28	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	7	29	Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, He that offereth the sacrifice of his peace offerings unto the LORD shall bring his oblation unto the LORD of the sacrifice of his peace offerings.
verse	3	7	30	@@His own hands shall bring the offerings of the LORD made by fire, the fat with the breast, it shall he bring, that the breast may be waved @9for@7 a wave offering before the LORD.
verse	3	7	31	And the priest shall burn the fat upon the altar: but the breast shall be Aaron's and his sons'.
verse	3	7	32	@@And the right shoulder shall ye give unto the priest @9for@7 an heave offering of the sacrifices of your peace offerings.
verse	3	7	33	@@He among the sons of Aaron, that offereth the blood of the peace offerings, and the fat, shall have the right shoulder for @9his@7 part.
verse	3	7	34	For the wave breast and the heave shoulder have I taken of the children of Israel from off the sacrifices of their peace offerings, and have given them unto Aaron the priest and unto his sons by a statute for ever from among the children of Israel.
verse	3	7	35	@@This @9is the portion@7 of the anointing of Aaron, and of the anointing of his sons, out of the offerings of the LORD made by fire, in the day @9when@7 he presented them to minister unto the LORD in the priest's office;
verse	3	7	36	@@Which the LORD commanded to be given them of the children of Israel, in the day that he anointed them, @9by@7 a statute for ever throughout their generations.
verse	3	7	37	@@This @9is@7 the law of the burnt offering, of the meat offering, and of the sin offering, and of the trespass offering, and of the consecrations, and of the sacrifice of the peace offerings;
verse	3	7	38	Which the LORD commanded Moses in mount Sinai, in the day that he commanded the children of Israel to offer their oblations unto the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai.
verse	3	8	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	8	2	Take Aaron and his sons with him, and the garments, and the anointing oil, and a bullock for the sin offering, and two rams, and a basket of unleavened bread;
verse	3	8	3	And gather thou all the congregation together unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	8	4	And Moses did as the LORD commanded him; and the assembly was gathered together unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	8	5	@@And Moses said unto the congregation, This @9is@7 the thing which the LORD commanded to be done.
verse	3	8	6	And Moses brought Aaron and his sons, and washed them with water.
verse	3	8	7	@@And he put upon him the coat, and girded him with the girdle, and clothed him with the robe, and put the ephod upon him, and he girded him with the curious girdle of the ephod, and bound @9it@7 unto him therewith.
verse	3	8	8	And he put the breastplate upon him: also he put in the breastplate the Urim and the Thummim.
verse	3	8	9	@@And he put the mitre upon his head; also upon the mitre, @9even@7 upon his forefront, did he put the golden plate, the holy crown; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	3	8	10	@@And Moses took the anointing oil, and anointed the tabernacle and all that @9was@7 therein, and sanctified them.
verse	3	8	11	And he sprinkled thereof upon the altar seven times, and anointed the altar and all his vessels, both the laver and his foot, to sanctify them.
verse	3	8	12	And he poured of the anointing oil upon Aaron's head, and anointed him, to sanctify him.
verse	3	8	13	And Moses brought Aaron's sons, and put coats upon them, and girded them with girdles, and put bonnets upon them; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	3	8	14	And he brought the bullock for the sin offering: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the bullock for the sin offering.
verse	3	8	15	@@And he slew @9it;@7 and Moses took the blood, and put @9it@7 upon the horns of the altar round about with his finger, and purified the altar, and poured the blood at the bottom of the altar, and sanctified it, to make reconciliation upon it.
verse	3	8	16	@@And he took all the fat that @9was@7 upon the inwards, and the caul @9above@7 the liver, and the two kidneys, and their fat, and Moses burned @9it@7 upon the altar.
verse	3	8	17	But the bullock, and his hide, his flesh, and his dung, he burnt with fire without the camp; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	3	8	18	And he brought the ram for the burnt offering: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the ram.
verse	3	8	19	@@And he killed @9it;@7 and Moses sprinkled the blood upon the altar round about.
verse	3	8	20	And he cut the ram into pieces; and Moses burnt the head, and the pieces, and the fat.
verse	3	8	21	@@And he washed the inwards and the legs in water; and Moses burnt the whole ram upon the altar: it @9was@7 a burnt sacrifice for a sweet savour, @9and@7 an offering made by fire unto the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	3	8	22	And he brought the other ram, the ram of consecration: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the ram.
verse	3	8	23	@@And he slew @9it;@7 and Moses took of the blood of it, and put @9it@7 upon the tip of Aaron's right ear, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot.
verse	3	8	24	And he brought Aaron's sons, and Moses put of the blood upon the tip of their right ear, and upon the thumbs of their right hands, and upon the great toes of their right feet: and Moses sprinkled the blood upon the altar round about.
verse	3	8	25	@@And he took the fat, and the rump, and all the fat that @9was@7 upon the inwards, and the caul @9above@7 the liver, and the two kidneys, and their fat, and the right shoulder:
verse	3	8	26	@@And out of the basket of unleavened bread, that @9was@7 before the LORD, he took one unleavened cake, and a cake of oiled bread, and one wafer, and put @9them@7 on the fat, and upon the right shoulder:
verse	3	8	27	@@And he put all upon Aaron's hands, and upon his sons' hands, and waved them @9for@7 a wave offering before the LORD.
verse	3	8	28	@@And Moses took them from off their hands, and burnt @9them@7 on the altar upon the burnt offering: they @9were@7 consecrations for a sweet savour: it @9is@7 an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
verse	3	8	29	@@And Moses took the breast, and waved it @9for@7 a wave offering before the LORD: @9for@7 of the ram of consecration it was Moses' part; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	3	8	30	@@And Moses took of the anointing oil, and of the blood which @9was@7 upon the altar, and sprinkled @9it@7 upon Aaron, @9and@7 upon his garments, and upon his sons, and upon his sons' garments with him; and sanctified Aaron, @9and@7 his garments, and his sons, and his sons' garments with him.
verse	3	8	31	@@And Moses said unto Aaron and to his sons, Boil the flesh at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and there eat it with the bread that @9is@7 in the basket of consecrations, as I commanded, saying, Aaron and his sons shall eat it.
