verse	3	11	23	@@But all @9other@7 flying creeping things, which have four feet, @9shall be@7 an abomination unto you.
verse	3	11	24	And for these ye shall be unclean: whosoever toucheth the carcase of them shall be unclean until the even.
verse	3	11	25	@@And whosoever beareth @9ought@7 of the carcase of them shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	11	26	@@@9The carcases@7 of every beast which divideth the hoof, and @9is@7 not clovenfooted, nor cheweth the cud, @9are@7 unclean unto you: every one that toucheth them shall be unclean.
verse	3	11	27	@@And whatsoever goeth upon his paws, among all manner of beasts that go on @9all@7 four, those @9are@7 unclean unto you: whoso toucheth their carcase shall be unclean until the even.
verse	3	11	28	@@And he that beareth the carcase of them shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even: they @9are@7 unclean unto you.
verse	3	11	29	@@These also @9shall be@7 unclean unto you among the creeping things that creep upon the earth; the weasel, and the mouse, and the tortoise after his kind,
verse	3	11	30	And the ferret, and the chameleon, and the lizard, and the snail, and the mole.
verse	3	11	31	@@These @9are@7 unclean to you among all that creep: whosoever doth touch them, when they be dead, shall be unclean until the even.
verse	3	11	32	@@And upon whatsoever @9any@7 of them, when they are dead, doth fall, it shall be unclean; whether @9it be@7 any vessel of wood, or raiment, or skin, or sack, whatsoever vessel @9it be,@7 wherein @9any@7 work is done, it must be put into water, and it shall be unclean until the even; so it shall be cleansed.
verse	3	11	33	@@And every earthen vessel, whereinto @9any@7 of them falleth, whatsoever is in it shall be unclean; and ye shall break it.
verse	3	11	34	@@Of all meat which may be eaten, @9that@7 on which @9such@7 water cometh shall be unclean: and all drink that may be drunk in every @9such@7 vessel shall be unclean.
verse	3	11	35	@@And every @9thing@7 whereupon @9any part@7 of their carcase falleth shall be unclean; @9whether it be@7 oven, or ranges for pots, they shall be broken down: @9for@7 they @9are@7 unclean, and shall be unclean unto you.
verse	3	11	36	@@Nevertheless a fountain or pit, @9wherein there is@7 plenty of water, shall be clean: but that which toucheth their carcase shall be unclean.
verse	3	11	37	@@And if @9any part@7 of their carcase fall upon any sowing seed which is to be sown, it @9shall be@7 clean.
verse	3	11	38	@@But if @9any@7 water be put upon the seed, and @9any part@7 of their carcase fall thereon, it @9shall be@7 unclean unto you.
verse	3	11	39	And if any beast, of which ye may eat, die; he that toucheth the carcase thereof shall be unclean until the even.
verse	3	11	40	And he that eateth of the carcase of it shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even: he also that beareth the carcase of it shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	11	41	@@And every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth @9shall be@7 an abomination; it shall not be eaten.
verse	3	11	42	@@Whatsoever goeth upon the belly, and whatsoever goeth upon @9all@7 four, or whatsoever hath more feet among all creeping things that creep upon the earth, them ye shall not eat; for they @9are@7 an abomination.
verse	3	11	43	Ye shall not make yourselves abominable with any creeping thing that creepeth, neither shall ye make yourselves unclean with them, that ye should be defiled thereby.
verse	3	11	44	@@For I @9am@7 the LORD your God: ye shall therefore sanctify yourselves, and ye shall be holy; for I @9am@7 holy: neither shall ye defile yourselves with any manner of creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth.
verse	3	11	45	@@For I @9am@7 the LORD that bringeth you up out of the land of Egypt, to be your God: ye shall therefore be holy, for I @9am@7 holy.
verse	3	11	46	@@This @9is@7 the law of the beasts, and of the fowl, and of every living creature that moveth in the waters, and of every creature that creepeth upon the earth:
