verse	3	12	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	12	2	Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, If a woman have conceived seed, and born a man child: then she shall be unclean seven days; according to the days of the separation for her infirmity shall she be unclean.
verse	3	12	3	And in the eighth day the flesh of his foreskin shall be circumcised.
verse	3	12	4	And she shall then continue in the blood of her purifying three and thirty days; she shall touch no hallowed thing, nor come into the sanctuary, until the days of her purifying be fulfilled.
verse	3	12	5	But if she bear a maid child, then she shall be unclean two weeks, as in her separation: and she shall continue in the blood of her purifying threescore and six days.
verse	3	12	6	And when the days of her purifying are fulfilled, for a son, or for a daughter, she shall bring a lamb of the first year for a burnt offering, and a young pigeon, or a turtledove, for a sin offering, unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, unto the priest:
verse	3	12	7	@@Who shall offer it before the LORD, and make an atonement for her; and she shall be cleansed from the issue of her blood. This @9is@7 the law for her that hath born a male or a female.
verse	3	12	8	And if she be not able to bring a lamb, then she shall bring two turtles, or two young pigeons; the one for the burnt offering, and the other for a sin offering: and the priest shall make an atonement for her, and she shall be clean.
verse	3	13	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses and Aaron, saying,
verse	3	13	2	@@When a man shall have in the skin of his flesh a rising, a scab, or bright spot, and it be in the skin of his flesh @9like@7 the plague of leprosy; then he shall be brought unto Aaron the priest, or unto one of his sons the priests:
verse	3	13	3	@@And the priest shall look on the plague in the skin of the flesh: and @9when@7 the hair in the plague is turned white, and the plague in sight @9be@7 deeper than the skin of his flesh, it @9is@7 a plague of leprosy: and the priest shall look on him, and pronounce him unclean.
verse	3	13	4	@@If the bright spot @9be@7 white in the skin of his flesh, and in sight @9be@7 not deeper than the skin, and the hair thereof be not turned white; then the priest shall shut up @9him that hath@7 the plague seven days:
verse	3	13	5	@@And the priest shall look on him the seventh day: and, behold, @9if@7 the plague in his sight be at a stay, @9and@7 the plague spread not in the skin; then the priest shall shut him up seven days more:
verse	3	13	6	@@And the priest shall look on him again the seventh day: and, behold, @9if@7 the plague @9be@7 somewhat dark, @9and@7 the plague spread not in the skin, the priest shall pronounce him clean: it @9is but@7 a scab: and he shall wash his clothes, and be clean.
verse	3	13	7	But if the scab spread much abroad in the skin, after that he hath been seen of the priest for his cleansing, he shall be seen of the priest again:
verse	3	13	8	@@And @9if@7 the priest see that, behold, the scab spreadeth in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it @9is@7 a leprosy.
verse	3	13	9	When the plague of leprosy is in a man, then he shall be brought unto the priest;
verse	3	13	10	@@And the priest shall see @9him:@7 and, behold, @9if@7 the rising @9be@7 white in the skin, and it have turned the hair white, and @9there be@7 quick raw flesh in the rising;
verse	3	13	11	@@It @9is@7 an old leprosy in the skin of his flesh, and the priest shall pronounce him unclean, and shall not shut him up: for he @9is@7 unclean.
verse	3	13	12	@@And if a leprosy break out abroad in the skin, and the leprosy cover all the skin of @9him that hath@7 the plague from his head even to his foot, wheresoever the priest looketh;
verse	3	13	13	@@Then the priest shall consider: and, behold, @9if@7 the leprosy have covered all his flesh, he shall pronounce @9him@7 clean @9that hath@7 the plague: it is all turned white: he @9is@7 clean.
verse	3	13	14	But when raw flesh appeareth in him, he shall be unclean.
verse	3	13	15	@@And the priest shall see the raw flesh, and pronounce him to be unclean: @9for@7 the raw flesh @9is@7 unclean: it @9is@7 a leprosy.
verse	3	13	16	Or if the raw flesh turn again, and be changed unto white, he shall come unto the priest;
verse	3	13	17	@@And the priest shall see him: and, behold, @9if@7 the plague be turned into white; then the priest shall pronounce @9him@7 clean @9that hath@7 the plague: he @9is@7 clean.
verse	3	13	18	@@The flesh also, in which, @9even@7 in the skin thereof, was a boil, and is healed,
verse	3	13	19	And in the place of the boil there be a white rising, or a bright spot, white, and somewhat reddish, and it be shewed to the priest;
verse	3	13	20	@@And if, when the priest seeth it, behold, it @9be@7 in sight lower than the skin, and the hair thereof be turned white; the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it @9is@7 a plague of leprosy broken out of the boil.
verse	3	13	21	@@But if the priest look on it, and, behold, @9there be@7 no white hairs therein, and @9if@7 it @9be@7 not lower than the skin, but @9be@7 somewhat dark; then the priest shall shut him up seven days:
verse	3	13	22	@@And if it spread much abroad in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it @9is@7 a plague.
verse	3	13	23	@@But if the bright spot stay in his place, @9and@7 spread not, it @9is@7 a burning boil; and the priest shall pronounce him clean.
verse	3	13	24	@@Or if there be @9any@7 flesh, in the skin whereof @9there is@7 a hot burning, and the quick @9flesh@7 that burneth have a white bright spot, somewhat reddish, or white;
verse	3	13	25	@@Then the priest shall look upon it: and, behold, @9if@7 the hair in the bright spot be turned white, and it @9be in@7 sight deeper than the skin; it @9is@7 a leprosy broken out of the burning: wherefore the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it @9is@7 the plague of leprosy.
verse	3	13	26	@@But if the priest look on it, and, behold, @9there be@7 no white hair in the bright spot, and it @9be@7 no lower than the @9other@7 skin, but @9be@7 somewhat dark; then the priest shall shut him up seven days:
verse	3	13	27	@@And the priest shall look upon him the seventh day: @9and@7 if it be spread much abroad in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it @9is@7 the plague of leprosy.
verse	3	13	28	@@And if the bright spot stay in his place, @9and@7 spread not in the skin, but it @9be@7 somewhat dark; it @9is@7 a rising of the burning, and the priest shall pronounce him clean: for it @9is@7 an inflammation of the burning.
verse	3	13	29	If a man or woman have a plague upon the head or the beard;
verse	3	13	30	@@Then the priest shall see the plague: and, behold, if it @9be@7 in sight deeper than the skin; @9and there be@7 in it a yellow thin hair; then the priest shall pronounce him unclean: it @9is@7 a dry scall, @9even@7 a leprosy upon the head or beard.
verse	3	13	31	@@And if the priest look on the plague of the scall, and, behold, it @9be@7 not in sight deeper than the skin, and @9that there is@7 no black hair in it; then the priest shall shut up @9him that hath@7 the plague of the scall seven days:
verse	3	13	32	@@And in the seventh day the priest shall look on the plague: and, behold, @9if@7 the scall spread not, and there be in it no yellow hair, and the scall @9be@7 not in sight deeper than the skin;
verse	3	13	33	@@He shall be shaven, but the scall shall he not shave; and the priest shall shut up @9him that hath@7 the scall seven days more:
verse	3	13	34	@@And in the seventh day the priest shall look on the scall: and, behold, @9if@7 the scall be not spread in the skin, nor @9be@7 in sight deeper than the skin; then the priest shall pronounce him clean: and he shall wash his clothes, and be clean.
verse	3	13	35	But if the scall spread much in the skin after his cleansing;
verse	3	13	36	@@Then the priest shall look on him: and, behold, if the scall be spread in the skin, the priest shall not seek for yellow hair; he @9is@7 unclean.
verse	3	13	37	@@But if the scall be in his sight at a stay, and @9that@7 there is black hair grown up therein; the scall is healed, he @9is@7 clean: and the priest shall pronounce him clean.
verse	3	13	38	@@If a man also or a woman have in the skin of their flesh bright spots, @9even@7 white bright spots;
verse	3	13	39	@@Then the priest shall look: and, behold, @9if@7 the bright spots in the skin of their flesh @9be@7 darkish white; it @9is@7 a freckled spot @9that@7 groweth in the skin; he @9is@7 clean.
verse	3	13	40	@@And the man whose hair is fallen off his head, he @9is@7 bald; @9yet is@7 he clean.
verse	3	13	41	@@And he that hath his hair fallen off from the part of his head toward his face, he @9is@7 forehead bald: @9yet is@7 he clean.
verse	3	13	42	@@And if there be in the bald head, or bald forehead, a white reddish sore; it @9is@7 a leprosy sprung up in his bald head, or his bald forehead.
