verse	3	13	44	@@He is a leprous man, he @9is@7 unclean: the priest shall pronounce him utterly unclean; his plague @9is@7 in his head.
verse	3	13	45	@@And the leper in whom the plague @9is,@7 his clothes shall be rent, and his head bare, and he shall put a covering upon his upper lip, and shall cry, Unclean, unclean.
verse	3	13	46	@@All the days wherein the plague @9shall be@7 in him he shall be defiled; he @9is@7 unclean: he shall dwell alone; without the camp @9shall@7 his habitation @9be.@7
verse	3	13	47	@@The garment also that the plague of leprosy is in, @9whether it be@7 a woollen garment, or a linen garment;
verse	3	13	48	@@Whether @9it be@7 in the warp, or woof; of linen, or of woollen; whether in a skin, or in any thing made of skin;
verse	3	13	49	@@And if the plague be greenish or reddish in the garment, or in the skin, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in any thing of skin; it @9is@7 a plague of leprosy, and shall be shewed unto the priest:
verse	3	13	50	@@And the priest shall look upon the plague, and shut up @9it that hath@7 the plague seven days:
verse	3	13	51	@@And he shall look on the plague on the seventh day: if the plague be spread in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in a skin, @9or@7 in any work that is made of skin; the plague @9is@7 a fretting leprosy; it @9is@7 unclean.
verse	3	13	52	@@He shall therefore burn that garment, whether warp or woof, in woollen or in linen, or any thing of skin, wherein the plague is: for it @9is@7 a fretting leprosy; it shall be burnt in the fire.
verse	3	13	53	And if the priest shall look, and, behold, the plague be not spread in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in any thing of skin;
verse	3	13	54	@@Then the priest shall command that they wash @9the thing@7 wherein the plague @9is,@7 and he shall shut it up seven days more:
verse	3	13	55	@@And the priest shall look on the plague, after that it is washed: and, behold, @9if@7 the plague have not changed his colour, and the plague be not spread; it @9is@7 unclean; thou shalt burn it in the fire; it @9is@7 fret inward, @9whether@7 it @9be@7 bare within or without.
verse	3	13	56	@@And if the priest look, and, behold, the plague @9be@7 somewhat dark after the washing of it; then he shall rend it out of the garment, or out of the skin, or out of the warp, or out of the woof:
verse	3	13	57	@@And if it appear still in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in any thing of skin; it @9is@7 a spreading @9plague:@7 thou shalt burn that wherein the plague @9is@7 with fire.
verse	3	13	58	@@And the garment, either warp, or woof, or whatsoever thing of skin @9it be,@7 which thou shalt wash, if the plague be departed from them, then it shall be washed the second time, and shall be clean.
verse	3	13	59	@@This @9is@7 the law of the plague of leprosy in a garment of woollen or linen, either in the warp, or woof, or any thing of skins, to pronounce it clean, or to pronounce it unclean.
verse	3	14	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	14	2	This shall be the law of the leper in the day of his cleansing: He shall be brought unto the priest:
verse	3	14	3	@@And the priest shall go forth out of the camp; and the priest shall look, and, behold, @9if@7 the plague of leprosy be healed in the leper;
verse	3	14	4	@@Then shall the priest command to take for him that is to be cleansed two birds alive @9and@7 clean, and cedar wood, and scarlet, and hyssop:
verse	3	14	5	And the priest shall command that one of the birds be killed in an earthen vessel over running water:
verse	3	14	6	@@As for the living bird, he shall take it, and the cedar wood, and the scarlet, and the hyssop, and shall dip them and the living bird in the blood of the bird @9that was@7 killed over the running water:
verse	3	14	7	And he shall sprinkle upon him that is to be cleansed from the leprosy seven times, and shall pronounce him clean, and shall let the living bird loose into the open field.
verse	3	14	8	And he that is to be cleansed shall wash his clothes, and shave off all his hair, and wash himself in water, that he may be clean: and after that he shall come into the camp, and shall tarry abroad out of his tent seven days.
verse	3	14	9	But it shall be on the seventh day, that he shall shave all his hair off his head and his beard and his eyebrows, even all his hair he shall shave off: and he shall wash his clothes, also he shall wash his flesh in water, and he shall be clean.
verse	3	14	10	@@And on the eighth day he shall take two he lambs without blemish, and one ewe lamb of the first year without blemish, and three tenth deals of fine flour @9for@7 a meat offering, mingled with oil, and one log of oil.
verse	3	14	11	@@And the priest that maketh @9him@7 clean shall present the man that is to be made clean, and those things, before the LORD, @9at@7 the door of the tabernacle of the congregation:
verse	3	14	12	@@And the priest shall take one he lamb, and offer him for a trespass offering, and the log of oil, and wave them @9for@7 a wave offering before the LORD:
verse	3	14	13	@@And he shall slay the lamb in the place where he shall kill the sin offering and the burnt offering, in the holy place: for as the sin offering @9is@7 the priest's, @9so is@7 the trespass offering: it @9is@7 most holy:
verse	3	14	14	@@And the priest shall take @9some@7 of the blood of the trespass offering, and the priest shall put @9it@7 upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot:
verse	3	14	15	@@And the priest shall take @9some@7 of the log of oil, and pour @9it@7 into the palm of his own left hand:
verse	3	14	16	@@And the priest shall dip his right finger in the oil that @9is@7 in his left hand, and shall sprinkle of the oil with his finger seven times before the LORD:
verse	3	14	17	@@And of the rest of the oil that @9is@7 in his hand shall the priest put upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot, upon the blood of the trespass offering:
verse	3	14	18	@@And the remnant of the oil that @9is@7 in the priest's hand he shall pour upon the head of him that is to be cleansed: and the priest shall make an atonement for him before the LORD.
verse	3	14	19	And the priest shall offer the sin offering, and make an atonement for him that is to be cleansed from his uncleanness; and afterward he shall kill the burnt offering:
verse	3	14	20	And the priest shall offer the burnt offering and the meat offering upon the altar: and the priest shall make an atonement for him, and he shall be clean.
verse	3	14	21	@@And if he @9be@7 poor, and cannot get so much; then he shall take one lamb @9for@7 a trespass offering to be waved, to make an atonement for him, and one tenth deal of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat offering, and a log of oil;
verse	3	14	22	And two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, such as he is able to get; and the one shall be a sin offering, and the other a burnt offering.
verse	3	14	23	And he shall bring them on the eighth day for his cleansing unto the priest, unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, before the LORD.
verse	3	14	24	@@And the priest shall take the lamb of the trespass offering, and the log of oil, and the priest shall wave them @9for@7 a wave offering before the LORD:
verse	3	14	25	@@And he shall kill the lamb of the trespass offering, and the priest shall take @9some@7 of the blood of the trespass offering, and put @9it@7 upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot:
verse	3	14	26	And the priest shall pour of the oil into the palm of his own left hand:
verse	3	14	27	@@And the priest shall sprinkle with his right finger @9some@7 of the oil that @9is@7 in his left hand seven times before the LORD:
verse	3	14	28	@@And the priest shall put of the oil that @9is@7 in his hand upon the tip of the right ear of him that is to be cleansed, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot, upon the place of the blood of the trespass offering:
verse	3	14	29	@@And the rest of the oil that @9is@7 in the priest's hand he shall put upon the head of him that is to be cleansed, to make an atonement for him before the LORD.
verse	3	14	30	And he shall offer the one of the turtledoves, or of the young pigeons, such as he can get;
verse	3	14	31	@@@9Even@7 such as he is able to get, the one @9for@7 a sin offering, and the other @9for@7 a burnt offering, with the meat offering: and the priest shall make an atonement for him that is to be cleansed before the LORD.
verse	3	14	32	@@This @9is@7 the law @9of him@7 in whom @9is@7 the plague of leprosy, whose hand is not able to get @9that which pertaineth@7 to his cleansing.
verse	3	14	33	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
verse	3	14	34	When ye be come into the land of Canaan, which I give to you for a possession, and I put the plague of leprosy in a house of the land of your possession;
verse	3	14	35	@@And he that owneth the house shall come and tell the priest, saying, It seemeth to me @9there is@7 as it were a plague in the house:
verse	3	14	36	@@Then the priest shall command that they empty the house, before the priest go @9into it@7 to see the plague, that all that @9is@7 in the house be not made unclean: and afterward the priest shall go in to see the house:
verse	3	14	37	@@And he shall look on the plague, and, behold, @9if@7 the plague @9be@7 in the walls of the house with hollow strakes, greenish or reddish, which in sight @9are@7 lower than the wall;
verse	3	14	38	Then the priest shall go out of the house to the door of the house, and shut up the house seven days:
verse	3	14	39	@@And the priest shall come again the seventh day, and shall look: and, behold, @9if@7 the plague be spread in the walls of the house;
verse	3	14	40	@@Then the priest shall command that they take away the stones in which the plague @9is,@7 and they shall cast them into an unclean place without the city:
verse	3	14	41	And he shall cause the house to be scraped within round about, and they shall pour out the dust that they scrape off without the city into an unclean place:
verse	3	14	42	@@And they shall take other stones, and put @9them@7 in the place of those stones; and he shall take other morter, and shall plaister the house.
verse	3	14	43	And if the plague come again, and break out in the house, after that he hath taken away the stones, and after he hath scraped the house, and after it is plaistered;
verse	3	14	44	@@Then the priest shall come and look, and, behold, @9if@7 the plague be spread in the house, it @9is@7 a fretting leprosy in the house: it is unclean.
verse	3	14	45	@@And he shall break down the house, the stones of it, and the timber thereof, and all the morter of the house; and he shall carry @9them@7 forth out of the city into an unclean place.
verse	3	14	46	Moreover he that goeth into the house all the while that it is shut up shall be unclean until the even.
verse	3	14	47	And he that lieth in the house shall wash his clothes; and he that eateth in the house shall wash his clothes.
verse	3	14	48	@@And if the priest shall come in, and look @9upon it,@7 and, behold, the plague hath not spread in the house, after the house was plaistered: then the priest shall pronounce the house clean, because the plague is healed.
verse	3	14	49	And he shall take to cleanse the house two birds, and cedar wood, and scarlet, and hyssop:
verse	3	14	50	And he shall kill the one of the birds in an earthen vessel over running water:
verse	3	14	51	And he shall take the cedar wood, and the hyssop, and the scarlet, and the living bird, and dip them in the blood of the slain bird, and in the running water, and sprinkle the house seven times:
verse	3	14	52	And he shall cleanse the house with the blood of the bird, and with the running water, and with the living bird, and with the cedar wood, and with the hyssop, and with the scarlet:
verse	3	14	53	But he shall let go the living bird out of the city into the open fields, and make an atonement for the house: and it shall be clean.
verse	3	14	54	@@This @9is@7 the law for all manner of plague of leprosy, and scall,
verse	3	14	55	And for the leprosy of a garment, and of a house,
verse	3	14	56	And for a rising, and for a scab, and for a bright spot:
verse	3	14	57	@@To teach when @9it is@7 unclean, and when @9it is@7 clean: this @9is@7 the law of leprosy.
verse	3	15	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses and to Aaron, saying,
verse	3	15	2	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When any man hath a running issue out of his flesh, @9because of@7 his issue he @9is@7 unclean.
verse	3	15	3	@@And this shall be his uncleanness in his issue: whether his flesh run with his issue, or his flesh be stopped from his issue, it @9is@7 his uncleanness.
verse	3	15	4	Every bed, whereon he lieth that hath the issue, is unclean: and every thing, whereon he sitteth, shall be unclean.
verse	3	15	5	@@And whosoever toucheth his bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	6	@@And he that sitteth on @9any@7 thing whereon he sat that hath the issue shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	7	@@And he that toucheth the flesh of him that hath the issue shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	8	@@And if he that hath the issue spit upon him that is clean; then he shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	9	And what saddle soever he rideth upon that hath the issue shall be unclean.
verse	3	15	10	@@And whosoever toucheth any thing that was under him shall be unclean until the even: and he that beareth @9any of@7 those things shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	11	@@And whomsoever he toucheth that hath the issue, and hath not rinsed his hands in water, he shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	12	And the vessel of earth, that he toucheth which hath the issue, shall be broken: and every vessel of wood shall be rinsed in water.
verse	3	15	13	And when he that hath an issue is cleansed of his issue; then he shall number to himself seven days for his cleansing, and wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in running water, and shall be clean.
verse	3	15	14	And on the eighth day he shall take to him two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, and come before the LORD unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and give them unto the priest:
verse	3	15	15	@@And the priest shall offer them, the one @9for@7 a sin offering, and the other @9for@7 a burnt offering; and the priest shall make an atonement for him before the LORD for his issue.
verse	3	15	16	And if any man's seed of copulation go out from him, then he shall wash all his flesh in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	17	And every garment, and every skin, whereon is the seed of copulation, shall be washed with water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	18	@@The woman also with whom man shall lie @9with@7 seed of copulation, they shall @9both@7 bathe @9themselves@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	19	@@And if a woman have an issue, @9and@7 her issue in her flesh be blood, she shall be put apart seven days: and whosoever toucheth her shall be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	20	And every thing that she lieth upon in her separation shall be unclean: every thing also that she sitteth upon shall be unclean.
verse	3	15	21	@@And whosoever toucheth her bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	22	@@And whosoever toucheth any thing that she sat upon shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	23	@@And if it @9be@7 on @9her@7 bed, or on any thing whereon she sitteth, when he toucheth it, he shall be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	24	@@And if any man lie with her at all, and her flowers be upon him, he shall be unclean seven days; and all the bed whereon he lieth @9shall be@7 unclean.
verse	3	15	25	And if a woman have an issue of her blood many days out of the time of her separation, or if it run beyond the time of her separation; all the days of the issue of her uncleanness shall be as the days of her separation: she shall be unclean.
verse	3	15	26	Every bed whereon she lieth all the days of her issue shall be unto her as the bed of her separation: and whatsoever she sitteth upon shall be unclean, as the uncleanness of her separation.
verse	3	15	27	@@And whosoever toucheth those things shall be unclean, and shall wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even.
verse	3	15	28	But if she be cleansed of her issue, then she shall number to herself seven days, and after that she shall be clean.
verse	3	15	29	And on the eighth day she shall take unto her two turtles, or two young pigeons, and bring them unto the priest, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	15	30	@@And the priest shall offer the one @9for@7 a sin offering, and the other @9for@7 a burnt offering; and the priest shall make an atonement for her before the LORD for the issue of her uncleanness.
verse	3	15	31	@@Thus shall ye separate the children of Israel from their uncleanness; that they die not in their uncleanness, when they defile my tabernacle that @9is@7 among them.
verse	3	15	32	@@This @9is@7 the law of him that hath an issue, and @9of him@7 whose seed goeth from him, and is defiled therewith;
verse	3	15	33	And of her that is sick of her flowers, and of him that hath an issue, of the man, and of the woman, and of him that lieth with her that is unclean.
verse	3	16	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses after the death of the two sons of Aaron, when they offered before the LORD, and died;
verse	3	16	2	@@And the LORD said unto Moses, Speak unto Aaron thy brother, that he come not at all times into the holy @9place@7 within the vail before the mercy seat, which @9is@7 upon the ark; that he die not: for I will appear in the cloud upon the mercy seat.
verse	3	16	3	@@Thus shall Aaron come into the holy @9place:@7 with a young bullock for a sin offering, and a ram for a burnt offering.
verse	3	16	4	@@He shall put on the holy linen coat, and he shall have the linen breeches upon his flesh, and shall be girded with a linen girdle, and with the linen mitre shall he be attired: these @9are@7 holy garments; therefore shall he wash his flesh in water, and @9so@7 put them on.
verse	3	16	5	And he shall take of the congregation of the children of Israel two kids of the goats for a sin offering, and one ram for a burnt offering.
verse	3	16	6	@@And Aaron shall offer his bullock of the sin offering, which @9is@7 for himself, and make an atonement for himself, and for his house.
verse	3	16	7	@@And he shall take the two goats, and present them before the LORD @9at@7 the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	3	16	8	And Aaron shall cast lots upon the two goats; one lot for the LORD, and the other lot for the scapegoat.
verse	3	16	9	@@And Aaron shall bring the goat upon which the LORD'S lot fell, and offer him @9for@7 a sin offering.
verse	3	16	10	@@But the goat, on which the lot fell to be the scapegoat, shall be presented alive before the LORD, to make an atonement with him, @9and@7 to let him go for a scapegoat into the wilderness.
verse	3	16	11	@@And Aaron shall bring the bullock of the sin offering, which @9is@7 for himself, and shall make an atonement for himself, and for his house, and shall kill the bullock of the sin offering which @9is@7 for himself:
verse	3	16	12	@@And he shall take a censer full of burning coals of fire from off the altar before the LORD, and his hands full of sweet incense beaten small, and bring @9it@7 within the vail:
verse	3	16	13	@@And he shall put the incense upon the fire before the LORD, that the cloud of the incense may cover the mercy seat that @9is@7 upon the testimony, that he die not:
verse	3	16	14	@@And he shall take of the blood of the bullock, and sprinkle @9it@7 with his finger upon the mercy seat eastward; and before the mercy seat shall he sprinkle of the blood with his finger seven times.
verse	3	16	15	@@Then shall he kill the goat of the sin offering, that @9is@7 for the people, and bring his blood within the vail, and do with that blood as he did with the blood of the bullock, and sprinkle it upon the mercy seat, and before the mercy seat:
verse	3	16	16	@@And he shall make an atonement for the holy @9place,@7 because of the uncleanness of the children of Israel, and because of their transgressions in all their sins: and so shall he do for the tabernacle of the congregation, that remaineth among them in the midst of their uncleanness.
verse	3	16	17	@@And there shall be no man in the tabernacle of the congregation when he goeth in to make an atonement in the holy @9place,@7 until he come out, and have made an atonement for himself, and for his household, and for all the congregation of Israel.
verse	3	16	18	@@And he shall go out unto the altar that @9is@7 before the LORD, and make an atonement for it; and shall take of the blood of the bullock, and of the blood of the goat, and put @9it@7 upon the horns of the altar round about.
verse	3	16	19	And he shall sprinkle of the blood upon it with his finger seven times, and cleanse it, and hallow it from the uncleanness of the children of Israel.
verse	3	16	20	@@And when he hath made an end of reconciling the holy @9place,@7 and the tabernacle of the congregation, and the altar, he shall bring the live goat:
verse	3	16	21	@@And Aaron shall lay both his hands upon the head of the live goat, and confess over him all the iniquities of the children of Israel, and all their transgressions in all their sins, putting them upon the head of the goat, and shall send @9him@7 away by the hand of a fit man into the wilderness:
verse	3	16	22	And the goat shall bear upon him all their iniquities unto a land not inhabited: and he shall let go the goat in the wilderness.
verse	3	16	23	@@And Aaron shall come into the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall put off the linen garments, which he put on when he went into the holy @9place,@7 and shall leave them there:
verse	3	16	24	And he shall wash his flesh with water in the holy place, and put on his garments, and come forth, and offer his burnt offering, and the burnt offering of the people, and make an atonement for himself, and for the people.
verse	3	16	25	And the fat of the sin offering shall he burn upon the altar.
verse	3	16	26	And he that let go the goat for the scapegoat shall wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in water, and afterward come into the camp.
verse	3	16	27	@@And the bullock @9for@7 the sin offering, and the goat @9for@7 the sin offering, whose blood was brought in to make atonement in the holy @9place,@7 shall @9one@7 carry forth without the camp; and they shall burn in the fire their skins, and their flesh, and their dung.
verse	3	16	28	And he that burneth them shall wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in water, and afterward he shall come into the camp.
verse	3	16	29	@@And @9this@7 shall be a statute for ever unto you: @9that@7 in the seventh month, on the tenth @9day@7 of the month, ye shall afflict your souls, and do no work at all, @9whether it be@7 one of your own country, or a stranger that sojourneth among you:
verse	3	16	30	@@For on that day shall @9the priest@7 make an atonement for you, to cleanse you, @9that@7 ye may be clean from all your sins before the LORD.
verse	3	16	31	@@It @9shall be@7 a sabbath of rest unto you, and ye shall afflict your souls, by a statute for ever.
verse	3	16	32	@@And the priest, whom he shall anoint, and whom he shall consecrate to minister in the priest's office in his father's stead, shall make the atonement, and shall put on the linen clothes, @9even@7 the holy garments:
verse	3	16	33	And he shall make an atonement for the holy sanctuary, and he shall make an atonement for the tabernacle of the congregation, and for the altar, and he shall make an atonement for the priests, and for all the people of the congregation.
verse	3	16	34	And this shall be an everlasting statute unto you, to make an atonement for the children of Israel for all their sins once a year. And he did as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	3	17	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	17	2	@@Speak unto Aaron, and unto his sons, and unto all the children of Israel, and say unto them; This @9is@7 the thing which the LORD hath commanded, saying,
verse	3	17	3	@@What man soever @9there be@7 of the house of Israel, that killeth an ox, or lamb, or goat, in the camp, or that killeth @9it@7 out of the camp,
verse	3	17	4	And bringeth it not unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, to offer an offering unto the LORD before the tabernacle of the LORD; blood shall be imputed unto that man; he hath shed blood; and that man shall be cut off from among his people:
verse	3	17	5	@@To the end that the children of Israel may bring their sacrifices, which they offer in the open field, even that they may bring them unto the LORD, unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, unto the priest, and offer them @9for@7 peace offerings unto the LORD.
verse	3	17	6	@@And the priest shall sprinkle the blood upon the altar of the LORD @9at@7 the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and burn the fat for a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	3	17	7	And they shall no more offer their sacrifices unto devils, after whom they have gone a whoring. This shall be a statute for ever unto them throughout their generations.
verse	3	17	8	@@And thou shalt say unto them, Whatsoever man @9there be@7 of the house of Israel, or of the strangers which sojourn among you, that offereth a burnt offering or sacrifice,
verse	3	17	9	And bringeth it not unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, to offer it unto the LORD; even that man shall be cut off from among his people.
verse	3	17	10	@@And whatsoever man @9there be@7 of the house of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn among you, that eateth any manner of blood; I will even set my face against that soul that eateth blood, and will cut him off from among his people.
verse	3	17	11	@@For the life of the flesh @9is@7 in the blood: and I have given it to you upon the altar to make an atonement for your souls: for it @9is@7 the blood @9that@7 maketh an atonement for the soul.
verse	3	17	12	Therefore I said unto the children of Israel, No soul of you shall eat blood, neither shall any stranger that sojourneth among you eat blood.
verse	3	17	13	@@And whatsoever man @9there be@7 of the children of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn among you, which hunteth and catcheth any beast or fowl that may be eaten; he shall even pour out the blood thereof, and cover it with dust.
verse	3	17	14	@@For @9it is@7 the life of all flesh; the blood of it @9is@7 for the life thereof: therefore I said unto the children of Israel, Ye shall eat the blood of no manner of flesh: for the life of all flesh @9is@7 the blood thereof: whosoever eateth it shall be cut off.
verse	3	17	15	@@And every soul that eateth that which died @9of itself,@7 or that which was torn @9with beasts, whether it be@7 one of your own country, or a stranger, he shall both wash his clothes, and bathe @9himself@7 in water, and be unclean until the even: then shall he be clean.
verse	3	17	16	@@But if he wash @9them@7 not, nor bathe his flesh; then he shall bear his iniquity.
verse	3	18	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	18	2	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, I am the LORD your God.
verse	3	18	3	After the doings of the land of Egypt, wherein ye dwelt, shall ye not do: and after the doings of the land of Canaan, whither I bring you, shall ye not do: neither shall ye walk in their ordinances.
verse	3	18	4	@@Ye shall do my judgments, and keep mine ordinances, to walk therein: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	18	5	@@Ye shall therefore keep my statutes, and my judgments: which if a man do, he shall live in them: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	18	6	@@None of you shall approach to any that is near of kin to him, to uncover @9their@7 nakedness: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	18	7	The nakedness of thy father, or the nakedness of thy mother, shalt thou not uncover: she is thy mother; thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.
verse	3	18	8	The nakedness of thy father's wife shalt thou not uncover: it is thy father's nakedness.
verse	3	18	9	@@The nakedness of thy sister, the daughter of thy father, or daughter of thy mother, @9whether she be@7 born at home, or born abroad, @9even@7 their nakedness thou shalt not uncover.
verse	3	18	10	@@The nakedness of thy son's daughter, or of thy daughter's daughter, @9even@7 their nakedness thou shalt not uncover: for theirs @9is@7 thine own nakedness.
verse	3	18	11	@@The nakedness of thy father's wife's daughter, begotten of thy father, she @9is@7 thy sister, thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.
verse	3	18	12	@@Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy father's sister: she @9is@7 thy father's near kinswoman.
verse	3	18	13	@@Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy mother's sister: for she @9is@7 thy mother's near kinswoman.
verse	3	18	14	@@Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy father's brother, thou shalt not approach to his wife: she @9is@7 thine aunt.
verse	3	18	15	@@Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy daughter in law: she @9is@7 thy son's wife; thou shalt not uncover her nakedness.
verse	3	18	16	@@Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy brother's wife: it @9is@7 thy brother's nakedness.
verse	3	18	17	@@Thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of a woman and her daughter, neither shalt thou take her son's daughter, or her daughter's daughter, to uncover her nakedness; @9for@7 they @9are@7 her near kinswomen: it @9is@7 wickedness.
verse	3	18	18	@@Neither shalt thou take a wife to her sister, to vex @9her,@7 to uncover her nakedness, beside the other in her life @9time. @7
verse	3	18	19	Also thou shalt not approach unto a woman to uncover her nakedness, as long as she is put apart for her uncleanness.
verse	3	18	20	Moreover thou shalt not lie carnally with thy neighbour's wife, to defile thyself with her.
verse	3	18	21	@@And thou shalt not let any of thy seed pass through @9the fire@7 to Molech, neither shalt thou profane the name of thy God: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	18	22	@@Thou shalt not lie with mankind, as with womankind: it @9is@7 abomination.
verse	3	18	23	@@Neither shalt thou lie with any beast to defile thyself therewith: neither shall any woman stand before a beast to lie down thereto: it @9is@7 confusion.
verse	3	18	24	Defile not ye yourselves in any of these things: for in all these the nations are defiled which I cast out before you:
verse	3	18	25	And the land is defiled: therefore I do visit the iniquity thereof upon it, and the land itself vomiteth out her inhabitants.
verse	3	18	26	@@Ye shall therefore keep my statutes and my judgments, and shall not commit @9any@7 of these abominations; @9neither@7 any of your own nation, nor any stranger that sojourneth among you:
verse	3	18	27	@@(For all these abominations have the men of the land done, which @9were@7 before you, and the land is defiled;)
verse	3	18	28	@@That the land spue not you out also, when ye defile it, as it spued out the nations that @9were@7 before you.
verse	3	18	29	@@For whosoever shall commit any of these abominations, even the souls that commit @9them@7 shall be cut off from among their people.
verse	3	18	30	@@Therefore shall ye keep mine ordinance, that @9ye@7 commit not @9any one@7 of these abominable customs, which were committed before you, and that ye defile not yourselves therein: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	19	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	19	2	@@Speak unto all the congregation of the children of Israel, and say unto them, Ye shall be holy: for I the LORD your God @9am@7 holy.
verse	3	19	3	@@Ye shall fear every man his mother, and his father, and keep my sabbaths: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	19	4	@@Turn ye not unto idols, nor make to yourselves molten gods: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	19	5	And if ye offer a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the LORD, ye shall offer it at your own will.
verse	3	19	6	It shall be eaten the same day ye offer it, and on the morrow: and if ought remain until the third day, it shall be burnt in the fire.
verse	3	19	7	@@And if it be eaten at all on the third day, it @9is@7 abominable; it shall not be accepted.
verse	3	19	8	@@Therefore @9every one@7 that eateth it shall bear his iniquity, because he hath profaned the hallowed thing of the LORD: and that soul shall be cut off from among his people.
verse	3	19	9	And when ye reap the harvest of your land, thou shalt not wholly reap the corners of thy field, neither shalt thou gather the gleanings of thy harvest.
verse	3	19	10	@@And thou shalt not glean thy vineyard, neither shalt thou gather @9every@7 grape of thy vineyard; thou shalt leave them for the poor and stranger: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	19	11	Ye shall not steal, neither deal falsely, neither lie one to another.
verse	3	19	12	@@And ye shall not swear by my name falsely, neither shalt thou profane the name of thy God: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	19	13	@@Thou shalt not defraud thy neighbour, neither rob @9him:@7 the wages of him that is hired shall not abide with thee all night until the morning.
verse	3	19	14	@@Thou shalt not curse the deaf, nor put a stumblingblock before the blind, but shalt fear thy God: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	19	15	@@Ye shall do no unrighteousness in judgment: thou shalt not respect the person of the poor, nor honour the person of the mighty: @9but@7 in righteousness shalt thou judge thy neighbour.
verse	3	19	16	@@Thou shalt not go up and down @9as@7 a talebearer among thy people: neither shalt thou stand against the blood of thy neighbour: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	19	17	Thou shalt not hate thy brother in thine heart: thou shalt in any wise rebuke thy neighbour, and not suffer sin upon him.
verse	3	19	18	@@Thou shalt not avenge, nor bear any grudge against the children of thy people, but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	19	19	Ye shall keep my statutes. Thou shalt not let thy cattle gender with a diverse kind: thou shalt not sow thy field with mingled seed: neither shall a garment mingled of linen and woollen come upon thee.
verse	3	19	20	@@And whosoever lieth carnally with a woman, that @9is@7 a bondmaid, betrothed to an husband, and not at all redeemed, nor freedom given her; she shall be scourged; they shall not be put to death, because she was not free.
verse	3	19	21	@@And he shall bring his trespass offering unto the LORD, unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, @9even@7 a ram for a trespass offering.
verse	3	19	22	And the priest shall make an atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering before the LORD for his sin which he hath done: and the sin which he hath done shall be forgiven him.
verse	3	19	23	And when ye shall come into the land, and shall have planted all manner of trees for food, then ye shall count the fruit thereof as uncircumcised: three years shall it be as uncircumcised unto you: it shall not be eaten of.
verse	3	19	24	@@But in the fourth year all the fruit thereof shall be holy to praise the LORD @9withal. @7
verse	3	19	25	@@And in the fifth year shall ye eat of the fruit thereof, that it may yield unto you the increase thereof: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	19	26	@@Ye shall not eat @9any thing@7 with the blood: neither shall ye use enchantment, nor observe times.
verse	3	19	27	Ye shall not round the corners of your heads, neither shalt thou mar the corners of thy beard.
verse	3	19	28	@@Ye shall not make any cuttings in your flesh for the dead, nor print any marks upon you: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	19	29	Do not prostitute thy daughter, to cause her to be a whore; lest the land fall to whoredom, and the land become full of wickedness.
verse	3	19	30	@@Ye shall keep my sabbaths, and reverence my sanctuary: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	19	31	@@Regard not them that have familiar spirits, neither seek after wizards, to be defiled by them: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	19	32	@@Thou shalt rise up before the hoary head, and honour the face of the old man, and fear thy God: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	19	33	And if a stranger sojourn with thee in your land, ye shall not vex him.
verse	3	19	34	@@@9But@7 the stranger that dwelleth with you shall be unto you as one born among you, and thou shalt love him as thyself; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	19	35	Ye shall do no unrighteousness in judgment, in meteyard, in weight, or in measure.
verse	3	19	36	@@Just balances, just weights, a just ephah, and a just hin, shall ye have: I @9am@7 the LORD your God, which brought you out of the land of Egypt.
verse	3	19	37	@@Therefore shall ye observe all my statutes, and all my judgments, and do them: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	20	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	20	2	@@Again, thou shalt say to the children of Israel, Whosoever @9he be@7 of the children of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn in Israel, that giveth @9any@7 of his seed unto Molech; he shall surely be put to death: the people of the land shall stone him with stones.
verse	3	20	3	And I will set my face against that man, and will cut him off from among his people; because he hath given of his seed unto Molech, to defile my sanctuary, and to profane my holy name.
verse	3	20	4	And if the people of the land do any ways hide their eyes from the man, when he giveth of his seed unto Molech, and kill him not:
verse	3	20	5	Then I will set my face against that man, and against his family, and will cut him off, and all that go a whoring after him, to commit whoredom with Molech, from among their people.
verse	3	20	6	And the soul that turneth after such as have familiar spirits, and after wizards, to go a whoring after them, I will even set my face against that soul, and will cut him off from among his people.
verse	3	20	7	@@Sanctify yourselves therefore, and be ye holy: for I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	20	8	@@And ye shall keep my statutes, and do them: I @9am@7 the LORD which sanctify you.
verse	3	20	9	@@For every one that curseth his father or his mother shall be surely put to death: he hath cursed his father or his mother; his blood @9shall be@7 upon him.
verse	3	20	10	@@And the man that committeth adultery with @9another@7 man's wife, @9even he@7 that committeth adultery with his neighbour's wife, the adulterer and the adulteress shall surely be put to death.
verse	3	20	11	@@And the man that lieth with his father's wife hath uncovered his father's nakedness: both of them shall surely be put to death; their blood @9shall be@7 upon them.
verse	3	20	12	@@And if a man lie with his daughter in law, both of them shall surely be put to death: they have wrought confusion; their blood @9shall be@7 upon them.
verse	3	20	13	@@If a man also lie with mankind, as he lieth with a woman, both of them have committed an abomination: they shall surely be put to death; their blood @9shall be@7 upon them.
verse	3	20	14	@@And if a man take a wife and her mother, it @9is@7 wickedness: they shall be burnt with fire, both he and they; that there be no wickedness among you.
verse	3	20	15	And if a man lie with a beast, he shall surely be put to death: and ye shall slay the beast.
verse	3	20	16	@@And if a woman approach unto any beast, and lie down thereto, thou shalt kill the woman, and the beast: they shall surely be put to death; their blood @9shall be@7 upon them.
verse	3	20	17	@@And if a man shall take his sister, his father's daughter, or his mother's daughter, and see her nakedness, and she see his nakedness; it @9is@7 a wicked thing; and they shall be cut off in the sight of their people: he hath uncovered his sister's nakedness; he shall bear his iniquity.
verse	3	20	18	And if a man shall lie with a woman having her sickness, and shall uncover her nakedness; he hath discovered her fountain, and she hath uncovered the fountain of her blood: and both of them shall be cut off from among their people.
verse	3	20	19	And thou shalt not uncover the nakedness of thy mother's sister, nor of thy father's sister: for he uncovereth his near kin: they shall bear their iniquity.
verse	3	20	20	And if a man shall lie with his uncle's wife, he hath uncovered his uncle's nakedness: they shall bear their sin; they shall die childless.
verse	3	20	21	@@And if a man shall take his brother's wife, it @9is@7 an unclean thing: he hath uncovered his brother's nakedness; they shall be childless.
verse	3	20	22	Ye shall therefore keep all my statutes, and all my judgments, and do them: that the land, whither I bring you to dwell therein, spue you not out.
verse	3	20	23	And ye shall not walk in the manners of the nation, which I cast out before you: for they committed all these things, and therefore I abhorred them.
verse	3	20	24	@@But I have said unto you, Ye shall inherit their land, and I will give it unto you to possess it, a land that floweth with milk and honey: I @9am@7 the LORD your God, which have separated you from @9other@7 people.
verse	3	20	25	Ye shall therefore put difference between clean beasts and unclean, and between unclean fowls and clean: and ye shall not make your souls abominable by beast, or by fowl, or by any manner of living thing that creepeth on the ground, which I have separated from you as unclean.
verse	3	20	26	@@And ye shall be holy unto me: for I the LORD @9am@7 holy, and have severed you from @9other@7 people, that ye should be mine.
verse	3	20	27	@@A man also or woman that hath a familiar spirit, or that is a wizard, shall surely be put to death: they shall stone them with stones: their blood @9shall be@7 upon them.
verse	3	21	1	And the LORD said unto Moses, Speak unto the priests the sons of Aaron, and say unto them, There shall none be defiled for the dead among his people:
verse	3	21	2	@@But for his kin, that is near unto him, @9that is,@7 for his mother, and for his father, and for his son, and for his daughter, and for his brother,
verse	3	21	3	And for his sister a virgin, that is nigh unto him, which hath had no husband; for her may he be defiled.
verse	3	21	4	@@@9But@7 he shall not defile himself, @9being@7 a chief man among his people, to profane himself.
verse	3	21	5	They shall not make baldness upon their head, neither shall they shave off the corner of their beard, nor make any cuttings in their flesh.
verse	3	21	6	@@They shall be holy unto their God, and not profane the name of their God: for the offerings of the LORD made by fire, @9and@7 the bread of their God, they do offer: therefore they shall be holy.
verse	3	21	7	@@They shall not take a wife @9that is@7 a whore, or profane; neither shall they take a woman put away from her husband: for he @9is@7 holy unto his God.
verse	3	21	8	@@Thou shalt sanctify him therefore; for he offereth the bread of thy God: he shall be holy unto thee: for I the LORD, which sanctify you, @9am@7 holy.
verse	3	21	9	And the daughter of any priest, if she profane herself by playing the whore, she profaneth her father: she shall be burnt with fire.
verse	3	21	10	@@And @9he that is@7 the high priest among his brethren, upon whose head the anointing oil was poured, and that is consecrated to put on the garments, shall not uncover his head, nor rend his clothes;
verse	3	21	11	Neither shall he go in to any dead body, nor defile himself for his father, or for his mother;
verse	3	21	12	@@Neither shall he go out of the sanctuary, nor profane the sanctuary of his God; for the crown of the anointing oil of his God @9is@7 upon him: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	21	13	And he shall take a wife in her virginity.
verse	3	21	14	@@A widow, or a divorced woman, or profane, @9or@7 an harlot, these shall he not take: but he shall take a virgin of his own people to wife.
verse	3	21	15	Neither shall he profane his seed among his people: for I the LORD do sanctify him.
verse	3	21	16	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	21	17	@@Speak unto Aaron, saying, Whosoever @9he be@7 of thy seed in their generations that hath @9any@7 blemish, let him not approach to offer the bread of his God.
verse	3	21	18	@@For whatsoever man @9he be@7 that hath a blemish, he shall not approach: a blind man, or a lame, or he that hath a flat nose, or any thing superfluous,
verse	3	21	19	Or a man that is brokenfooted, or brokenhanded,
verse	3	21	20	Or crookbackt, or a dwarf, or that hath a blemish in his eye, or be scurvy, or scabbed, or hath his stones broken;
verse	3	21	21	No man that hath a blemish of the seed of Aaron the priest shall come nigh to offer the offerings of the LORD made by fire: he hath a blemish; he shall not come nigh to offer the bread of his God.
verse	3	21	22	@@He shall eat the bread of his God, @9both@7 of the most holy, and of the holy.
verse	3	21	23	Only he shall not go in unto the vail, nor come nigh unto the altar, because he hath a blemish; that he profane not my sanctuaries: for I the LORD do sanctify them.
verse	3	21	24	@@And Moses told @9it@7 unto Aaron, and to his sons, and unto all the children of Israel.
verse	3	22	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	22	2	@@Speak unto Aaron and to his sons, that they separate themselves from the holy things of the children of Israel, and that they profane not my holy name @9in those things@7 which they hallow unto me: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	22	3	@@Say unto them, Whosoever @9he be@7 of all your seed among your generations, that goeth unto the holy things, which the children of Israel hallow unto the LORD, having his uncleanness upon him, that soul shall be cut off from my presence: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	22	4	@@What man soever of the seed of Aaron @9is@7 a leper, or hath a running issue; he shall not eat of the holy things, until he be clean. And whoso toucheth any thing @9that is@7 unclean @9by@7 the dead, or a man whose seed goeth from him;
verse	3	22	5	Or whosoever toucheth any creeping thing, whereby he may be made unclean, or a man of whom he may take uncleanness, whatsoever uncleanness he hath;
verse	3	22	6	The soul which hath touched any such shall be unclean until even, and shall not eat of the holy things, unless he wash his flesh with water.
verse	3	22	7	@@And when the sun is down, he shall be clean, and shall afterward eat of the holy things; because it @9is@7 his food.
verse	3	22	8	@@That which dieth of itself, or is torn @9with beasts,@7 he shall not eat to defile himself therewith: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	22	9	They shall therefore keep mine ordinance, lest they bear sin for it, and die therefore, if they profane it: I the LORD do sanctify them.
verse	3	22	10	@@There shall no stranger eat @9of@7 the holy thing: a sojourner of the priest, or an hired servant, shall not eat @9of@7 the holy thing.
verse	3	22	11	@@But if the priest buy @9any@7 soul with his money, he shall eat of it, and he that is born in his house: they shall eat of his meat.
verse	3	22	12	@@If the priest's daughter also be @9married@7 unto a stranger, she may not eat of an offering of the holy things.
verse	3	22	13	But if the priest's daughter be a widow, or divorced, and have no child, and is returned unto her father's house, as in her youth, she shall eat of her father's meat: but there shall no stranger eat thereof.
verse	3	22	14	@@And if a man eat @9of@7 the holy thing unwittingly, then he shall put the fifth @9part@7 thereof unto it, and shall give @9it@7 unto the priest with the holy thing.
verse	3	22	15	And they shall not profane the holy things of the children of Israel, which they offer unto the LORD;
verse	3	22	16	Or suffer them to bear the iniquity of trespass, when they eat their holy things: for I the LORD do sanctify them.
verse	3	22	17	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	22	18	@@Speak unto Aaron, and to his sons, and unto all the children of Israel, and say unto them, Whatsoever @9he be@7 of the house of Israel, or of the strangers in Israel, that will offer his oblation for all his vows, and for all his freewill offerings, which they will offer unto the LORD for a burnt offering;
verse	3	22	19	@@@9Ye shall offer@7 at your own will a male without blemish, of the beeves, of the sheep, or of the goats.
verse	3	22	20	@@@9But@7 whatsoever hath a blemish, @9that@7 shall ye not offer: for it shall not be acceptable for you.
verse	3	22	21	@@And whosoever offereth a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the LORD to accomplish @9his@7 vow, or a freewill offering in beeves or sheep, it shall be perfect to be accepted; there shall be no blemish therein.
verse	3	22	22	Blind, or broken, or maimed, or having a wen, or scurvy, or scabbed, ye shall not offer these unto the LORD, nor make an offering by fire of them upon the altar unto the LORD.
verse	3	22	23	@@Either a bullock or a lamb that hath any thing superfluous or lacking in his parts, that mayest thou offer @9for@7 a freewill offering; but for a vow it shall not be accepted.
verse	3	22	24	@@Ye shall not offer unto the LORD that which is bruised, or crushed, or broken, or cut; neither shall ye make @9any offering thereof@7 in your land.
verse	3	22	25	@@Neither from a stranger's hand shall ye offer the bread of your God of any of these; because their corruption @9is@7 in them, @9and@7 blemishes @9be@7 in them: they shall not be accepted for you.
verse	3	22	26	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	22	27	When a bullock, or a sheep, or a goat, is brought forth, then it shall be seven days under the dam; and from the eighth day and thenceforth it shall be accepted for an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
verse	3	22	28	@@And @9whether it be@7 cow or ewe, ye shall not kill it and her young both in one day.
verse	3	22	29	@@And when ye will offer a sacrifice of thanksgiving unto the LORD, offer @9it@7 at your own will.
verse	3	22	30	@@On the same day it shall be eaten up; ye shall leave none of it until the morrow: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	22	31	@@Therefore shall ye keep my commandments, and do them: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	22	32	@@Neither shall ye profane my holy name; but I will be hallowed among the children of Israel: I @9am@7 the LORD which hallow you,
verse	3	22	33	@@That brought you out of the land of Egypt, to be your God: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	23	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	23	2	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, @9Concerning@7 the feasts of the LORD, which ye shall proclaim @9to be@7 holy convocations, @9even@7 these @9are@7 my feasts.
verse	3	23	3	@@Six days shall work be done: but the seventh day @9is@7 the sabbath of rest, an holy convocation; ye shall do no work @9therein:@7 it @9is@7 the sabbath of the LORD in all your dwellings.
verse	3	23	4	@@These @9are@7 the feasts of the LORD, @9even@7 holy convocations, which ye shall proclaim in their seasons.
verse	3	23	5	@@In the fourteenth @9day@7 of the first month at even @9is@7 the LORD'S passover.
verse	3	23	6	@@And on the fifteenth day of the same month @9is@7 the feast of unleavened bread unto the LORD: seven days ye must eat unleavened bread.
verse	3	23	7	In the first day ye shall have an holy convocation: ye shall do no servile work therein.
verse	3	23	8	@@But ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD seven days: in the seventh day @9is@7 an holy convocation: ye shall do no servile work @9therein.@7
verse	3	23	9	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	23	10	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When ye be come into the land which I give unto you, and shall reap the harvest thereof, then ye shall bring a sheaf of the firstfruits of your harvest unto the priest:
verse	3	23	11	And he shall wave the sheaf before the LORD, to be accepted for you: on the morrow after the sabbath the priest shall wave it.
verse	3	23	12	And ye shall offer that day when ye wave the sheaf an he lamb without blemish of the first year for a burnt offering unto the LORD.
verse	3	23	13	@@And the meat offering thereof @9shall be@7 two tenth deals of fine flour mingled with oil, an offering made by fire unto the LORD @9for@7 a sweet savour: and the drink offering thereof @9shall be@7 of wine, the fourth @9part@7 of an hin.
verse	3	23	14	@@And ye shall eat neither bread, nor parched corn, nor green ears, until the selfsame day that ye have brought an offering unto your God: @9it shall be@7 a statute for ever throughout your generations in all your dwellings.
verse	3	23	15	And ye shall count unto you from the morrow after the sabbath, from the day that ye brought the sheaf of the wave offering; seven sabbaths shall be complete:
verse	3	23	16	Even unto the morrow after the seventh sabbath shall ye number fifty days; and ye shall offer a new meat offering unto the LORD.
verse	3	23	17	@@Ye shall bring out of your habitations two wave loaves of two tenth deals: they shall be of fine flour; they shall be baken with leaven; @9they are@7 the firstfruits unto the LORD.
verse	3	23	18	@@And ye shall offer with the bread seven lambs without blemish of the first year, and one young bullock, and two rams: they shall be @9for@7 a burnt offering unto the LORD, with their meat offering, and their drink offerings, @9even@7 an offering made by fire, of sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	3	23	19	Then ye shall sacrifice one kid of the goats for a sin offering, and two lambs of the first year for a sacrifice of peace offerings.
verse	3	23	20	@@And the priest shall wave them with the bread of the firstfruits @9for@7 a wave offering before the LORD, with the two lambs: they shall be holy to the LORD for the priest.
verse	3	23	21	@@And ye shall proclaim on the selfsame day, @9that@7 it may be an holy convocation unto you: ye shall do no servile work @9therein: it shall be@7 a statute for ever in all your dwellings throughout your generations.
verse	3	23	22	@@And when ye reap the harvest of your land, thou shalt not make clean riddance of the corners of thy field when thou reapest, neither shalt thou gather any gleaning of thy harvest: thou shalt leave them unto the poor, and to the stranger: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	23	23	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	23	24	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, In the seventh month, in the first @9day@7 of the month, shall ye have a sabbath, a memorial of blowing of trumpets, an holy convocation.
verse	3	23	25	@@Ye shall do no servile work @9therein:@7 but ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
verse	3	23	26	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	23	27	@@Also on the tenth @9day@7 of this seventh month @9there shall be@7 a day of atonement: it shall be an holy convocation unto you; and ye shall afflict your souls, and offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
verse	3	23	28	@@And ye shall do no work in that same day: for it @9is@7 a day of atonement, to make an atonement for you before the LORD your God.
verse	3	23	29	@@For whatsoever soul @9it be@7 that shall not be afflicted in that same day, he shall be cut off from among his people.
verse	3	23	30	@@And whatsoever soul @9it be@7 that doeth any work in that same day, the same soul will I destroy from among his people.
verse	3	23	31	@@Ye shall do no manner of work: @9it shall be@7 a statute for ever throughout your generations in all your dwellings.
verse	3	23	32	@@It @9shall be@7 unto you a sabbath of rest, and ye shall afflict your souls: in the ninth @9day@7 of the month at even, from even unto even, shall ye celebrate your sabbath.
verse	3	23	33	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	23	34	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, The fifteenth day of this seventh month @9shall be@7 the feast of tabernacles @9for@7 seven days unto the LORD.
verse	3	23	35	@@On the first day @9shall be@7 an holy convocation: ye shall do no servile work @9therein. @7
verse	3	23	36	@@Seven days ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD: on the eighth day shall be an holy convocation unto you; and ye shall offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD: it @9is@7 a solemn assembly; @9and@7 ye shall do no servile work @9therein. @7
verse	3	23	37	@@These @9are@7 the feasts of the LORD, which ye shall proclaim @9to be@7 holy convocations, to offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD, a burnt offering, and a meat offering, a sacrifice, and drink offerings, every thing upon his day:
verse	3	23	38	Beside the sabbaths of the LORD, and beside your gifts, and beside all your vows, and beside all your freewill offerings, which ye give unto the LORD.
verse	3	23	39	@@Also in the fifteenth day of the seventh month, when ye have gathered in the fruit of the land, ye shall keep a feast unto the LORD seven days: on the first day @9shall be@7 a sabbath, and on the eighth day @9shall be@7 a sabbath.
verse	3	23	40	And ye shall take you on the first day the boughs of goodly trees, branches of palm trees, and the boughs of thick trees, and willows of the brook; and ye shall rejoice before the LORD your God seven days.
verse	3	23	41	@@And ye shall keep it a feast unto the LORD seven days in the year. @9It shall be@7 a statute for ever in your generations: ye shall celebrate it in the seventh month.
verse	3	23	42	Ye shall dwell in booths seven days; all that are Israelites born shall dwell in booths:
verse	3	23	43	@@That your generations may know that I made the children of Israel to dwell in booths, when I brought them out of the land of Egypt: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	23	44	And Moses declared unto the children of Israel the feasts of the LORD.
verse	3	24	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	24	2	Command the children of Israel, that they bring unto thee pure oil olive beaten for the light, to cause the lamps to burn continually.
verse	3	24	3	@@Without the vail of the testimony, in the tabernacle of the congregation, shall Aaron order it from the evening unto the morning before the LORD continually: @9it shall be@7 a statute for ever in your generations.
verse	3	24	4	He shall order the lamps upon the pure candlestick before the LORD continually.
verse	3	24	5	And thou shalt take fine flour, and bake twelve cakes thereof: two tenth deals shall be in one cake.
verse	3	24	6	And thou shalt set them in two rows, six on a row, upon the pure table before the LORD.
verse	3	24	7	@@And thou shalt put pure frankincense upon @9each@7 row, that it may be on the bread for a memorial, @9even@7 an offering made by fire unto the LORD.
verse	3	24	8	@@Every sabbath he shall set it in order before the LORD continually, @9being taken@7 from the children of Israel by an everlasting covenant.
verse	3	24	9	@@And it shall be Aaron's and his sons'; and they shall eat it in the holy place: for it @9is@7 most holy unto him of the offerings of the LORD made by fire by a perpetual statute.
verse	3	24	10	@@And the son of an Israelitish woman, whose father @9was@7 an Egyptian, went out among the children of Israel: and this son of the Israelitish @9woman@7 and a man of Israel strove together in the camp;
verse	3	24	11	@@And the Israelitish woman's son blasphemed the name @9of the LORD,@7 and cursed. And they brought him unto Moses: (and his mother's name @9was@7 Shelomith, the daughter of Dibri, of the tribe of Dan:)
verse	3	24	12	And they put him in ward, that the mind of the LORD might be shewed them.
verse	3	24	13	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	24	14	@@Bring forth him that hath cursed without the camp; and let all that heard @9him@7 lay their hands upon his head, and let all the congregation stone him.
verse	3	24	15	And thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel, saying, Whosoever curseth his God shall bear his sin.
verse	3	24	16	@@And he that blasphemeth the name of the LORD, he shall surely be put to death, @9and@7 all the congregation shall certainly stone him: as well the stranger, as he that is born in the land, when he blasphemeth the name @9of the LORD,@7 shall be put to death.
verse	3	24	17	And he that killeth any man shall surely be put to death.
verse	3	24	18	And he that killeth a beast shall make it good; beast for beast.
verse	3	24	19	And if a man cause a blemish in his neighbour; as he hath done, so shall it be done to him;
verse	3	24	20	@@Breach for breach, eye for eye, tooth for tooth: as he hath caused a blemish in a man, so shall it be done to him @9again. @7
verse	3	24	21	And he that killeth a beast, he shall restore it: and he that killeth a man, he shall be put to death.
verse	3	24	22	@@Ye shall have one manner of law, as well for the stranger, as for one of your own country: for I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	24	23	And Moses spake to the children of Israel, that they should bring forth him that had cursed out of the camp, and stone him with stones. And the children of Israel did as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	3	25	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses in mount Sinai, saying,
verse	3	25	2	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When ye come into the land which I give you, then shall the land keep a sabbath unto the LORD.
verse	3	25	3	Six years thou shalt sow thy field, and six years thou shalt prune thy vineyard, and gather in the fruit thereof;
verse	3	25	4	But in the seventh year shall be a sabbath of rest unto the land, a sabbath for the LORD: thou shalt neither sow thy field, nor prune thy vineyard.
verse	3	25	5	@@That which groweth of its own accord of thy harvest thou shalt not reap, neither gather the grapes of thy vine undressed: @9for@7 it is a year of rest unto the land.
verse	3	25	6	And the sabbath of the land shall be meat for you; for thee, and for thy servant, and for thy maid, and for thy hired servant, and for thy stranger that sojourneth with thee,
verse	3	25	7	@@And for thy cattle, and for the beast that @9are@7 in thy land, shall all the increase thereof be meat.
verse	3	25	8	And thou shalt number seven sabbaths of years unto thee, seven times seven years; and the space of the seven sabbaths of years shall be unto thee forty and nine years.
verse	3	25	9	@@Then shalt thou cause the trumpet of the jubile to sound on the tenth @9day@7 of the seventh month, in the day of atonement shall ye make the trumpet sound throughout all your land.
verse	3	25	10	@@And ye shall hallow the fiftieth year, and proclaim liberty throughout @9all@7 the land unto all the inhabitants thereof: it shall be a jubile unto you; and ye shall return every man unto his possession, and ye shall return every man unto his family.
verse	3	25	11	@@A jubile shall that fiftieth year be unto you: ye shall not sow, neither reap that which groweth of itself in it, nor gather @9the grapes@7 in it of thy vine undressed.
verse	3	25	12	@@For it @9is@7 the jubile; it shall be holy unto you: ye shall eat the increase thereof out of the field.
verse	3	25	13	In the year of this jubile ye shall return every man unto his possession.
verse	3	25	14	@@And if thou sell @9ought@7 unto thy neighbour, or buyest ought of thy neighbour's hand, ye shall not oppress one another:
verse	3	25	15	@@According to the number of years after the jubile thou shalt buy of thy neighbour, @9and@7 according unto the number of years of the fruits he shall sell unto thee:
verse	3	25	16	@@According to the multitude of years thou shalt increase the price thereof, and according to the fewness of years thou shalt diminish the price of it: for @9according@7 to the number @9of the years@7 of the fruits doth he sell unto thee.
verse	3	25	17	@@Ye shall not therefore oppress one another; but thou shalt fear thy God: for I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	25	18	Wherefore ye shall do my statutes, and keep my judgments, and do them; and ye shall dwell in the land in safety.
verse	3	25	19	And the land shall yield her fruit, and ye shall eat your fill, and dwell therein in safety.
verse	3	25	20	And if ye shall say, What shall we eat the seventh year? behold, we shall not sow, nor gather in our increase:
verse	3	25	21	Then I will command my blessing upon you in the sixth year, and it shall bring forth fruit for three years.
verse	3	25	22	@@And ye shall sow the eighth year, and eat @9yet@7 of old fruit until the ninth year; until her fruits come in ye shall eat @9of@7 the old @9store.@7
verse	3	25	23	@@The land shall not be sold for ever: for the land @9is@7 mine; for ye @9are@7 strangers and sojourners with me.
verse	3	25	24	And in all the land of your possession ye shall grant a redemption for the land.
verse	3	25	25	@@If thy brother be waxen poor, and hath sold away @9some@7 of his possession, and if any of his kin come to redeem it, then shall he redeem that which his brother sold.
verse	3	25	26	And if the man have none to redeem it, and himself be able to redeem it;
verse	3	25	27	Then let him count the years of the sale thereof, and restore the overplus unto the man to whom he sold it; that he may return unto his possession.
verse	3	25	28	@@But if he be not able to restore @9it@7 to him, then that which is sold shall remain in the hand of him that hath bought it until the year of jubile: and in the jubile it shall go out, and he shall return unto his possession.
verse	3	25	29	@@And if a man sell a dwelling house in a walled city, then he may redeem it within a whole year after it is sold; @9within@7 a full year may he redeem it.
verse	3	25	30	@@And if it be not redeemed within the space of a full year, then the house that @9is@7 in the walled city shall be established for ever to him that bought it throughout his generations: it shall not go out in the jubile.
verse	3	25	31	But the houses of the villages which have no wall round about them shall be counted as the fields of the country: they may be redeemed, and they shall go out in the jubile.
verse	3	25	32	@@Notwithstanding the cities of the Levites, @9and@7 the houses of the cities of their possession, may the Levites redeem at any time.
verse	3	25	33	@@And if a man purchase of the Levites, then the house that was sold, and the city of his possession, shall go out in @9the year of@7 jubile: for the houses of the cities of the Levites @9are@7 their possession among the children of Israel.
verse	3	25	34	But the field of the suburbs of their cities may not be sold; for it is their perpetual possession.
verse	3	25	35	@@And if thy brother be waxen poor, and fallen in decay with thee; then thou shalt relieve him: @9yea, though he be@7 a stranger, or a sojourner; that he may live with thee.
verse	3	25	36	Take thou no usury of him, or increase: but fear thy God; that thy brother may live with thee.
verse	3	25	37	Thou shalt not give him thy money upon usury, nor lend him thy victuals for increase.
verse	3	25	38	@@I @9am@7 the LORD your God, which brought you forth out of the land of Egypt, to give you the land of Canaan, @9and@7 to be your God.
verse	3	25	39	@@And if thy brother @9that dwelleth@7 by thee be waxen poor, and be sold unto thee; thou shalt not compel him to serve as a bondservant:
verse	3	25	40	@@@9But@7 as an hired servant, @9and@7 as a sojourner, he shall be with thee, @9and@7 shall serve thee unto the year of jubile:
verse	3	25	41	@@And @9then@7 shall he depart from thee, @9both@7 he and his children with him, and shall return unto his own family, and unto the possession of his fathers shall he return.
verse	3	25	42	@@For they @9are@7 my servants, which I brought forth out of the land of Egypt: they shall not be sold as bondmen.
verse	3	25	43	Thou shalt not rule over him with rigour; but shalt fear thy God.
verse	3	25	44	@@Both thy bondmen, and thy bondmaids, which thou shalt have, @9shall be@7 of the heathen that are round about you; of them shall ye buy bondmen and bondmaids.
verse	3	25	45	@@Moreover of the children of the strangers that do sojourn among you, of them shall ye buy, and of their families that @9are@7 with you, which they begat in your land: and they shall be your possession.
verse	3	25	46	@@And ye shall take them as an inheritance for your children after you, to inherit @9them for@7 a possession; they shall be your bondmen for ever: but over your brethren the children of Israel, ye shall not rule one over another with rigour.
verse	3	25	47	@@And if a sojourner or stranger wax rich by thee, and thy brother @9that dwelleth@7 by him wax poor, and sell himself unto the stranger @9or@7 sojourner by thee, or to the stock of the stranger's family:
verse	3	25	48	After that he is sold he may be redeemed again; one of his brethren may redeem him:
verse	3	25	49	@@Either his uncle, or his uncle's son, may redeem him, or @9any@7 that is nigh of kin unto him of his family may redeem him; or if he be able, he may redeem himself.
verse	3	25	50	And he shall reckon with him that bought him from the year that he was sold to him unto the year of jubile: and the price of his sale shall be according unto the number of years, according to the time of an hired servant shall it be with him.
verse	3	25	51	@@If @9there be@7 yet many years @9behind,@7 according unto them he shall give again the price of his redemption out of the money that he was bought for.
verse	3	25	52	@@And if there remain but few years unto the year of jubile, then he shall count with him, @9and@7 according unto his years shall he give him again the price of his redemption.
verse	3	25	53	@@@9And@7 as a yearly hired servant shall he be with him: @9and the other@7 shall not rule with rigour over him in thy sight.
verse	3	25	54	@@And if he be not redeemed in these @9years,@7 then he shall go out in the year of jubile, @9both@7 he, and his children with him.
verse	3	25	55	@@For unto me the children of Israel @9are@7 servants; they @9are@7 my servants whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	26	1	@@Ye shall make you no idols nor graven image, neither rear you up a standing image, neither shall ye set up @9any@7 image of stone in your land, to bow down unto it: for I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	3	26	2	@@Ye shall keep my sabbaths, and reverence my sanctuary: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	26	3	If ye walk in my statutes, and keep my commandments, and do them;
verse	3	26	4	Then I will give you rain in due season, and the land shall yield her increase, and the trees of the field shall yield their fruit.
verse	3	26	5	And your threshing shall reach unto the vintage, and the vintage shall reach unto the sowing time: and ye shall eat your bread to the full, and dwell in your land safely.
verse	3	26	6	@@And I will give peace in the land, and ye shall lie down, and none shall make @9you@7 afraid: and I will rid evil beasts out of the land, neither shall the sword go through your land.
verse	3	26	7	And ye shall chase your enemies, and they shall fall before you by the sword.
verse	3	26	8	And five of you shall chase an hundred, and an hundred of you shall put ten thousand to flight: and your enemies shall fall before you by the sword.
verse	3	26	9	For I will have respect unto you, and make you fruitful, and multiply you, and establish my covenant with you.
verse	3	26	10	And ye shall eat old store, and bring forth the old because of the new.
verse	3	26	11	And I will set my tabernacle among you: and my soul shall not abhor you.
verse	3	26	12	And I will walk among you, and will be your God, and ye shall be my people.
verse	3	26	13	@@I @9am@7 the LORD your God, which brought you forth out of the land of Egypt, that ye should not be their bondmen; and I have broken the bands of your yoke, and made you go upright.
verse	3	26	14	But if ye will not hearken unto me, and will not do all these commandments;
verse	3	26	15	@@And if ye shall despise my statutes, or if your soul abhor my judgments, so that ye will not do all my commandments, @9but@7 that ye break my covenant:
verse	3	26	16	I also will do this unto you; I will even appoint over you terror, consumption, and the burning ague, that shall consume the eyes, and cause sorrow of heart: and ye shall sow your seed in vain, for your enemies shall eat it.
verse	3	26	17	And I will set my face against you, and ye shall be slain before your enemies: they that hate you shall reign over you; and ye shall flee when none pursueth you.
verse	3	26	18	And if ye will not yet for all this hearken unto me, then I will punish you seven times more for your sins.
verse	3	26	19	And I will break the pride of your power; and I will make your heaven as iron, and your earth as brass:
verse	3	26	20	And your strength shall be spent in vain: for your land shall not yield her increase, neither shall the trees of the land yield their fruits.
verse	3	26	21	And if ye walk contrary unto me, and will not hearken unto me; I will bring seven times more plagues upon you according to your sins.
verse	3	26	22	@@I will also send wild beasts among you, which shall rob you of your children, and destroy your cattle, and make you few in number; and your @9high@7 ways shall be desolate.
verse	3	26	23	And if ye will not be reformed by me by these things, but will walk contrary unto me;
verse	3	26	24	Then will I also walk contrary unto you, and will punish you yet seven times for your sins.
verse	3	26	25	@@And I will bring a sword upon you, that shall avenge the quarrel of @9my@7 covenant: and when ye are gathered together within your cities, I will send the pestilence among you; and ye shall be delivered into the hand of the enemy.
verse	3	26	26	@@@9And@7 when I have broken the staff of your bread, ten women shall bake your bread in one oven, and they shall deliver @9you@7 your bread again by weight: and ye shall eat, and not be satisfied.
verse	3	26	27	And if ye will not for all this hearken unto me, but walk contrary unto me;
verse	3	26	28	Then I will walk contrary unto you also in fury; and I, even I, will chastise you seven times for your sins.
verse	3	26	29	And ye shall eat the flesh of your sons, and the flesh of your daughters shall ye eat.
verse	3	26	30	And I will destroy your high places, and cut down your images, and cast your carcases upon the carcases of your idols, and my soul shall abhor you.
verse	3	26	31	And I will make your cities waste, and bring your sanctuaries unto desolation, and I will not smell the savour of your sweet odours.
verse	3	26	32	And I will bring the land into desolation: and your enemies which dwell therein shall be astonished at it.
verse	3	26	33	And I will scatter you among the heathen, and will draw out a sword after you: and your land shall be desolate, and your cities waste.
verse	3	26	34	@@Then shall the land enjoy her sabbaths, as long as it lieth desolate, and ye be in your enemies' land; @9even@7 then shall the land rest, and enjoy her sabbaths.
verse	3	26	35	As long as it lieth desolate it shall rest; because it did not rest in your sabbaths, when ye dwelt upon it.
verse	3	26	36	@@And upon them that are left @9alive@7 of you I will send a faintness into their hearts in the lands of their enemies; and the sound of a shaken leaf shall chase them; and they shall flee, as fleeing from a sword; and they shall fall when none pursueth.
verse	3	26	37	And they shall fall one upon another, as it were before a sword, when none pursueth: and ye shall have no power to stand before your enemies.
verse	3	26	38	And ye shall perish among the heathen, and the land of your enemies shall eat you up.
verse	3	26	39	And they that are left of you shall pine away in their iniquity in your enemies' lands; and also in the iniquities of their fathers shall they pine away with them.
verse	3	26	40	If they shall confess their iniquity, and the iniquity of their fathers, with their trespass which they trespassed against me, and that also they have walked contrary unto me;
verse	3	26	41	@@And @9that@7 I also have walked contrary unto them, and have brought them into the land of their enemies; if then their uncircumcised hearts be humbled, and they then accept of the punishment of their iniquity:
verse	3	26	42	Then will I remember my covenant with Jacob, and also my covenant with Isaac, and also my covenant with Abraham will I remember; and I will remember the land.
verse	3	26	43	The land also shall be left of them, and shall enjoy her sabbaths, while she lieth desolate without them: and they shall accept of the punishment of their iniquity: because, even because they despised my judgments, and because their soul abhorred my statutes.
verse	3	26	44	@@And yet for all that, when they be in the land of their enemies, I will not cast them away, neither will I abhor them, to destroy them utterly, and to break my covenant with them: for I @9am@7 the LORD their God.
verse	3	26	45	@@But I will for their sakes remember the covenant of their ancestors, whom I brought forth out of the land of Egypt in the sight of the heathen, that I might be their God: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	3	26	46	@@These @9are@7 the statutes and judgments and laws, which the LORD made between him and the children of Israel in mount Sinai by the hand of Moses.
verse	3	27	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	3	27	2	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When a man shall make a singular vow, the persons @9shall be@7 for the LORD by thy estimation.
verse	3	27	3	And thy estimation shall be of the male from twenty years old even unto sixty years old, even thy estimation shall be fifty shekels of silver, after the shekel of the sanctuary.
verse	3	27	4	@@And if it @9be@7 a female, then thy estimation shall be thirty shekels.
verse	3	27	5	@@And if @9it be@7 from five years old even unto twenty years old, then thy estimation shall be of the male twenty shekels, and for the female ten shekels.
verse	3	27	6	@@And if @9it be@7 from a month old even unto five years old, then thy estimation shall be of the male five shekels of silver, and for the female thy estimation @9shall be@7 three shekels of silver.
verse	3	27	7	@@And if @9it be@7 from sixty years old and above; if @9it be@7 a male, then thy estimation shall be fifteen shekels, and for the female ten shekels.
verse	3	27	8	But if he be poorer than thy estimation, then he shall present himself before the priest, and the priest shall value him; according to his ability that vowed shall the priest value him.
verse	3	27	9	@@And if @9it be@7 a beast, whereof men bring an offering unto the LORD, all that @9any man@7 giveth of such unto the LORD shall be holy.
verse	3	27	10	He shall not alter it, nor change it, a good for a bad, or a bad for a good: and if he shall at all change beast for beast, then it and the exchange thereof shall be holy.
verse	3	27	11	@@And if @9it be@7 any unclean beast, of which they do not offer a sacrifice unto the LORD, then he shall present the beast before the priest:
verse	3	27	12	@@And the priest shall value it, whether it be good or bad: as thou valuest it, @9who art@7 the priest, so shall it be.
verse	3	27	13	@@But if he will at all redeem it, then he shall add a fifth @9part@7 thereof unto thy estimation.
verse	3	27	14	@@And when a man shall sanctify his house @9to be@7 holy unto the LORD, then the priest shall estimate it, whether it be good or bad: as the priest shall estimate it, so shall it stand.
verse	3	27	15	@@And if he that sanctified it will redeem his house, then he shall add the fifth @9part@7 of the money of thy estimation unto it, and it shall be his.
verse	3	27	16	@@And if a man shall sanctify unto the LORD @9some part@7 of a field of his possession, then thy estimation shall be according to the seed thereof: an homer of barley seed @9shall be valued@7 at fifty shekels of silver.
verse	3	27	17	If he sanctify his field from the year of jubile, according to thy estimation it shall stand.
verse	3	27	18	But if he sanctify his field after the jubile, then the priest shall reckon unto him the money according to the years that remain, even unto the year of the jubile, and it shall be abated from thy estimation.
verse	3	27	19	@@And if he that sanctified the field will in any wise redeem it, then he shall add the fifth @9part@7 of the money of thy estimation unto it, and it shall be assured to him.
verse	3	27	20	And if he will not redeem the field, or if he have sold the field to another man, it shall not be redeemed any more.
verse	3	27	21	But the field, when it goeth out in the jubile, shall be holy unto the LORD, as a field devoted; the possession thereof shall be the priest's.
verse	3	27	22	@@And if @9a man@7 sanctify unto the LORD a field which he hath bought, which @9is@7 not of the fields of his possession;
verse	3	27	23	@@Then the priest shall reckon unto him the worth of thy estimation, @9even@7 unto the year of the jubile: and he shall give thine estimation in that day, @9as@7 a holy thing unto the LORD.
verse	3	27	24	@@In the year of the jubile the field shall return unto him of whom it was bought, @9even@7 to him to whom the possession of the land @9did belong. @7
verse	3	27	25	And all thy estimations shall be according to the shekel of the sanctuary: twenty gerahs shall be the shekel.
verse	3	27	26	@@Only the firstling of the beasts, which should be the LORD'S firstling, no man shall sanctify it; whether @9it be@7 ox, or sheep: it @9is@7 the LORD'S.
verse	3	27	27	@@And if @9it be@7 of an unclean beast, then he shall redeem it according to thine estimation, and shall add a fifth @9part@7 of it thereto: or if it be not redeemed, then it shall be sold according to thy estimation.
verse	3	27	28	@@Notwithstanding no devoted thing, that a man shall devote unto the LORD of all that he hath, @9both@7 of man and beast, and of the field of his possession, shall be sold or redeemed: every devoted thing @9is@7 most holy unto the LORD.
verse	3	27	29	@@None devoted, which shall be devoted of men, shall be redeemed; @9but@7 shall surely be put to death.
verse	3	27	30	@@And all the tithe of the land, @9whether@7 of the seed of the land, @9or@7 of the fruit of the tree, @9is@7 the LORD'S: @9it is@7 holy unto the LORD.
verse	3	27	31	@@And if a man will at all redeem @9ought@7 of his tithes, he shall add thereto the fifth @9part@7 thereof.
verse	3	27	32	@@And concerning the tithe of the herd, or of the flock, @9even@7 of whatsoever passeth under the rod, the tenth shall be holy unto the LORD.
verse	3	27	33	He shall not search whether it be good or bad, neither shall he change it: and if he change it at all, then both it and the change thereof shall be holy; it shall not be redeemed.
verse	3	27	34	@@These @9are@7 the commandments, which the LORD commanded Moses for the children of Israel in mount Sinai.
verse	4	1	1	@@And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the tabernacle of the congregation, on the first @9day@7 of the second month, in the second year after they were come out of the land of Egypt, saying,
verse	4	1	2	@@Take ye the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel, after their families, by the house of their fathers, with the number of @9their@7 names, every male by their polls;
verse	4	1	3	From twenty years old and upward, all that are able to go forth to war in Israel: thou and Aaron shall number them by their armies.
verse	4	1	4	And with you there shall be a man of every tribe; every one head of the house of his fathers.
verse	4	1	5	@@And these @9are@7 the names of the men that shall stand with you: of @9the tribe of@7 Reuben; Elizur the son of Shedeur.
verse	4	1	6	Of Simeon; Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai.
verse	4	1	7	Of Judah; Nahshon the son of Amminadab.
verse	4	1	8	Of Issachar; Nethaneel the son of Zuar.
verse	4	1	9	Of Zebulun; Eliab the son of Helon.
verse	4	1	10	Of the children of Joseph: of Ephraim; Elishama the son of Ammihud: of Manasseh; Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.
verse	4	1	11	Of Benjamin; Abidan the son of Gideoni.
verse	4	1	12	Of Dan; Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.
verse	4	1	13	Of Asher; Pagiel the son of Ocran.
verse	4	1	14	Of Gad; Eliasaph the son of Deuel.
verse	4	1	15	Of Naphtali; Ahira the son of Enan.
verse	4	1	16	@@These @9were@7 the renowned of the congregation, princes of the tribes of their fathers, heads of thousands in Israel.
verse	4	1	17	@@And Moses and Aaron took these men which are expressed by @9their@7 names:
verse	4	1	18	@@And they assembled all the congregation together on the first @9day@7 of the second month, and they declared their pedigrees after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, by their polls.
verse	4	1	19	As the LORD commanded Moses, so he numbered them in the wilderness of Sinai.
verse	4	1	20	And the children of Reuben, Israel's eldest son, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, by their polls, every male from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	21	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Reuben, @9were@7 forty and six thousand and five hundred.
verse	4	1	22	Of the children of Simeon, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, those that were numbered of them, according to the number of the names, by their polls, every male from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	23	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Simeon, @9were@7 fifty and nine thousand and three hundred.
verse	4	1	24	Of the children of Gad, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	25	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Gad, @9were@7 forty and five thousand six hundred and fifty.
verse	4	1	26	Of the children of Judah, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	27	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Judah, @9were@7 threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred.
verse	4	1	28	Of the children of Issachar, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	29	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Issachar, @9were@7 fifty and four thousand and four hundred.
verse	4	1	30	Of the children of Zebulun, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	31	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Zebulun, @9were@7 fifty and seven thousand and four hundred.
verse	4	1	32	@@Of the children of Joseph, @9namely,@7 of the children of Ephraim, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	33	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Ephraim, @9were@7 forty thousand and five hundred.
verse	4	1	34	Of the children of Manasseh, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	35	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Manasseh, @9were@7 thirty and two thousand and two hundred.
verse	4	1	36	Of the children of Benjamin, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	37	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Benjamin, @9were@7 thirty and five thousand and four hundred.
verse	4	1	38	Of the children of Dan, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	39	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Dan, @9were@7 threescore and two thousand and seven hundred.
verse	4	1	40	Of the children of Asher, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	41	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Asher, @9were@7 forty and one thousand and five hundred.
verse	4	1	42	Of the children of Naphtali, throughout their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;
verse	4	1	43	@@Those that were numbered of them, @9even@7 of the tribe of Naphtali, @9were@7 fifty and three thousand and four hundred.
verse	4	1	44	@@These @9are@7 those that were numbered, which Moses and Aaron numbered, and the princes of Israel, @9being@7 twelve men: each one was for the house of his fathers.
verse	4	1	45	So were all those that were numbered of the children of Israel, by the house of their fathers, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war in Israel;
verse	4	1	46	Even all they that were numbered were six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.
verse	4	1	47	But the Levites after the tribe of their fathers were not numbered among them.
verse	4	1	48	For the LORD had spoken unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	1	49	Only thou shalt not number the tribe of Levi, neither take the sum of them among the children of Israel:
verse	4	1	50	@@But thou shalt appoint the Levites over the tabernacle of testimony, and over all the vessels thereof, and over all things that @9belong@7 to it: they shall bear the tabernacle, and all the vessels thereof; and they shall minister unto it, and shall encamp round about the tabernacle.
verse	4	1	51	And when the tabernacle setteth forward, the Levites shall take it down: and when the tabernacle is to be pitched, the Levites shall set it up: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.
verse	4	1	52	And the children of Israel shall pitch their tents, every man by his own camp, and every man by his own standard, throughout their hosts.
verse	4	1	53	But the Levites shall pitch round about the tabernacle of testimony, that there be no wrath upon the congregation of the children of Israel: and the Levites shall keep the charge of the tabernacle of testimony.
verse	4	1	54	And the children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so did they.
verse	4	2	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
verse	4	2	2	Every man of the children of Israel shall pitch by his own standard, with the ensign of their father's house: far off about the tabernacle of the congregation shall they pitch.
verse	4	2	3	@@And on the east side toward the rising of the sun shall they of the standard of the camp of Judah pitch throughout their armies: and Nahshon the son of Amminadab @9shall be@7 captain of the children of Judah.
verse	4	2	4	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred.
verse	4	2	5	@@And those that do pitch next unto him @9shall be@7 the tribe of Issachar: and Nethaneel the son of Zuar @9shall be@7 captain of the children of Issachar.
verse	4	2	6	@@And his host, and those that were numbered thereof, @9were@7 fifty and four thousand and four hundred.
verse	4	2	7	@@@9Then@7 the tribe of Zebulun: and Eliab the son of Helon @9shall be@7 captain of the children of Zebulun.
verse	4	2	8	@@And his host, and those that were numbered thereof, @9were@7 fifty and seven thousand and four hundred.
verse	4	2	9	@@All that were numbered in the camp of Judah @9were@7 an hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred, throughout their armies. These shall first set forth.
verse	4	2	10	@@On the south side @9shall be@7 the standard of the camp of Reuben according to their armies: and the captain of the children of Reuben @9shall be@7 Elizur the son of Shedeur.
verse	4	2	11	@@And his host, and those that were numbered thereof, @9were@7 forty and six thousand and five hundred.
verse	4	2	12	@@And those which pitch by him @9shall be@7 the tribe of Simeon: and the captain of the children of Simeon @9shall be@7 Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai.
verse	4	2	13	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 fifty and nine thousand and three hundred.
verse	4	2	14	@@Then the tribe of Gad: and the captain of the sons of Gad @9shall be@7 Eliasaph the son of Reuel.
verse	4	2	15	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 forty and five thousand and six hundred and fifty.
verse	4	2	16	@@All that were numbered in the camp of Reuben @9were@7 an hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty, throughout their armies. And they shall set forth in the second rank.
verse	4	2	17	Then the tabernacle of the congregation shall set forward with the camp of the Levites in the midst of the camp: as they encamp, so shall they set forward, every man in his place by their standards.
verse	4	2	18	@@On the west side @9shall be@7 the standard of the camp of Ephraim according to their armies: and the captain of the sons of Ephraim @9shall be@7 Elishama the son of Ammihud.
verse	4	2	19	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 forty thousand and five hundred.
verse	4	2	20	@@And by him @9shall be@7 the tribe of Manasseh: and the captain of the children of Manasseh @9shall be@7 Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.
verse	4	2	21	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 thirty and two thousand and two hundred.
verse	4	2	22	@@Then the tribe of Benjamin: and the captain of the sons of Benjamin @9shall be@7 Abidan the son of Gideoni.
verse	4	2	23	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 thirty and five thousand and four hundred.
verse	4	2	24	@@All that were numbered of the camp of Ephraim @9were@7 an hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred, throughout their armies. And they shall go forward in the third rank.
verse	4	2	25	@@The standard of the camp of Dan @9shall be@7 on the north side by their armies: and the captain of the children of Dan @9shall be@7 Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.
verse	4	2	26	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 threescore and two thousand and seven hundred.
verse	4	2	27	@@And those that encamp by him @9shall be@7 the tribe of Asher: and the captain of the children of Asher @9shall be@7 Pagiel the son of Ocran.
verse	4	2	28	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 forty and one thousand and five hundred.
verse	4	2	29	@@Then the tribe of Naphtali: and the captain of the children of Naphtali @9shall be@7 Ahira the son of Enan.
verse	4	2	30	@@And his host, and those that were numbered of them, @9were@7 fifty and three thousand and four hundred.
verse	4	2	31	@@All they that were numbered in the camp of Dan @9were@7 an hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred. They shall go hindmost with their standards.
verse	4	2	32	@@These @9are@7 those which were numbered of the children of Israel by the house of their fathers: all those that were numbered of the camps throughout their hosts @9were@7 six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.
verse	4	2	33	But the Levites were not numbered among the children of Israel; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	4	2	34	And the children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses: so they pitched by their standards, and so they set forward, every one after their families, according to the house of their fathers.
verse	4	3	1	@@These also @9are@7 the generations of Aaron and Moses in the day @9that@7 the LORD spake with Moses in mount Sinai.
verse	4	3	2	@@And these @9are@7 the names of the sons of Aaron; Nadab the firstborn, and Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.
verse	4	3	3	@@These @9are@7 the names of the sons of Aaron, the priests which were anointed, whom he consecrated to minister in the priest's office.
verse	4	3	4	And Nadab and Abihu died before the LORD, when they offered strange fire before the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai, and they had no children: and Eleazar and Ithamar ministered in the priest's office in the sight of Aaron their father.
verse	4	3	5	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	3	6	Bring the tribe of Levi near, and present them before Aaron the priest, that they may minister unto him.
verse	4	3	7	And they shall keep his charge, and the charge of the whole congregation before the tabernacle of the congregation, to do the service of the tabernacle.
verse	4	3	8	And they shall keep all the instruments of the tabernacle of the congregation, and the charge of the children of Israel, to do the service of the tabernacle.
verse	4	3	9	@@And thou shalt give the Levites unto Aaron and to his sons: they @9are@7 wholly given unto him out of the children of Israel.
verse	4	3	10	And thou shalt appoint Aaron and his sons, and they shall wait on their priest's office: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.
verse	4	3	11	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	3	12	And I, behold, I have taken the Levites from among the children of Israel instead of all the firstborn that openeth the matrix among the children of Israel: therefore the Levites shall be mine;
verse	4	3	13	@@Because all the firstborn @9are@7 mine; @9for@7 on the day that I smote all the firstborn in the land of Egypt I hallowed unto me all the firstborn in Israel, both man and beast: mine shall they be: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	4	3	14	And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, saying,
verse	4	3	15	Number the children of Levi after the house of their fathers, by their families: every male from a month old and upward shalt thou number them.
verse	4	3	16	And Moses numbered them according to the word of the LORD, as he was commanded.
verse	4	3	17	And these were the sons of Levi by their names; Gershon, and Kohath, and Merari.
verse	4	3	18	@@And these @9are@7 the names of the sons of Gershon by their families; Libni, and Shimei.
verse	4	3	19	And the sons of Kohath by their families; Amram, and Izehar, Hebron, and Uzziel.
verse	4	3	20	@@And the sons of Merari by their families; Mahli, and Mushi. These @9are@7 the families of the Levites according to the house of their fathers.
verse	4	3	21	@@Of Gershon @9was@7 the family of the Libnites, and the family of the Shimites: these @9are@7 the families of the Gershonites.
verse	4	3	22	@@Those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, @9even@7 those that were numbered of them @9were@7 seven thousand and five hundred.
verse	4	3	23	The families of the Gershonites shall pitch behind the tabernacle westward.
verse	4	3	24	@@And the chief of the house of the father of the Gershonites @9shall be@7 Eliasaph the son of Lael.
verse	4	3	25	@@And the charge of the sons of Gershon in the tabernacle of the congregation @9shall be@7 the tabernacle, and the tent, the covering thereof, and the hanging for the door of the tabernacle of the congregation,
verse	4	3	26	@@And the hangings of the court, and the curtain for the door of the court, which @9is@7 by the tabernacle, and by the altar round about, and the cords of it for all the service thereof.
verse	4	3	27	@@And of Kohath @9was@7 the family of the Amramites, and the family of the Izeharites, and the family of the Hebronites, and the family of the Uzzielites: these @9are@7 the families of the Kohathites.
verse	4	3	28	@@In the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, @9were@7 eight thousand and six hundred, keeping the charge of the sanctuary.
verse	4	3	29	The families of the sons of Kohath shall pitch on the side of the tabernacle southward.
verse	4	3	30	@@And the chief of the house of the father of the families of the Kohathites @9shall be@7 Elizaphan the son of Uzziel.
verse	4	3	31	@@And their charge @9shall be@7 the ark, and the table, and the candlestick, and the altars, and the vessels of the sanctuary wherewith they minister, and the hanging, and all the service thereof.
verse	4	3	32	@@And Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest @9shall be@7 chief over the chief of the Levites, @9and have@7 the oversight of them that keep the charge of the sanctuary.
verse	4	3	33	@@Of Merari @9was@7 the family of the Mahlites, and the family of the Mushites: these @9are@7 the families of Merari.
verse	4	3	34	@@And those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, @9were@7 six thousand and two hundred.
verse	4	3	35	@@And the chief of the house of the father of the families of Merari @9was@7 Zuriel the son of Abihail: @9these@7 shall pitch on the side of the tabernacle northward.
verse	4	3	36	@@And @9under@7 the custody and charge of the sons of Merari @9shall be@7 the boards of the tabernacle, and the bars thereof, and the pillars thereof, and the sockets thereof, and all the vessels thereof, and all that serveth thereto,
verse	4	3	37	And the pillars of the court round about, and their sockets, and their pins, and their cords.
verse	4	3	38	@@But those that encamp before the tabernacle toward the east, @9even@7 before the tabernacle of the congregation eastward, @9shall be@7 Moses, and Aaron and his sons, keeping the charge of the sanctuary for the charge of the children of Israel; and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.
verse	4	3	39	@@All that were numbered of the Levites, which Moses and Aaron numbered at the commandment of the LORD, throughout their families, all the males from a month old and upward, @9were@7 twenty and two thousand.
verse	4	3	40	And the LORD said unto Moses, Number all the firstborn of the males of the children of Israel from a month old and upward, and take the number of their names.
verse	4	3	41	@@And thou shalt take the Levites for me (I @9am@7 the LORD) instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel; and the cattle of the Levites instead of all the firstlings among the cattle of the children of Israel.
verse	4	3	42	And Moses numbered, as the LORD commanded him, all the firstborn among the children of Israel.
verse	4	3	43	And all the firstborn males by the number of names, from a month old and upward, of those that were numbered of them, were twenty and two thousand two hundred and threescore and thirteen.
verse	4	3	44	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	3	45	@@Take the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel, and the cattle of the Levites instead of their cattle; and the Levites shall be mine: I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	4	3	46	And for those that are to be redeemed of the two hundred and threescore and thirteen of the firstborn of the children of Israel, which are more than the Levites;
verse	4	3	47	@@Thou shalt even take five shekels apiece by the poll, after the shekel of the sanctuary shalt thou take @9them:@7 (the shekel @9is@7 twenty gerahs:)
verse	4	3	48	And thou shalt give the money, wherewith the odd number of them is to be redeemed, unto Aaron and to his sons.
verse	4	3	49	And Moses took the redemption money of them that were over and above them that were redeemed by the Levites:
verse	4	3	50	@@Of the firstborn of the children of Israel took he the money; a thousand three hundred and threescore and five @9shekels,@7 after the shekel of the sanctuary:
verse	4	3	51	And Moses gave the money of them that were redeemed unto Aaron and to his sons, according to the word of the LORD, as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	4	4	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
verse	4	4	2	Take the sum of the sons of Kohath from among the sons of Levi, after their families, by the house of their fathers,
verse	4	4	3	From thirty years old and upward even until fifty years old, all that enter into the host, to do the work in the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	4	4	@@This @9shall be@7 the service of the sons of Kohath in the tabernacle of the congregation, @9about@7 the most holy things:
verse	4	4	5	And when the camp setteth forward, Aaron shall come, and his sons, and they shall take down the covering vail, and cover the ark of testimony with it:
verse	4	4	6	@@And shall put thereon the covering of badgers' skins, and shall spread over @9it@7 a cloth wholly of blue, and shall put in the staves thereof.
verse	4	4	7	And upon the table of shewbread they shall spread a cloth of blue, and put thereon the dishes, and the spoons, and the bowls, and covers to cover withal: and the continual bread shall be thereon:
verse	4	4	8	And they shall spread upon them a cloth of scarlet, and cover the same with a covering of badgers' skins, and shall put in the staves thereof.
verse	4	4	9	And they shall take a cloth of blue, and cover the candlestick of the light, and his lamps, and his tongs, and his snuffdishes, and all the oil vessels thereof, wherewith they minister unto it:
verse	4	4	10	@@And they shall put it and all the vessels thereof within a covering of badgers' skins, and shall put @9it@7 upon a bar.
verse	4	4	11	And upon the golden altar they shall spread a cloth of blue, and cover it with a covering of badgers' skins, and shall put to the staves thereof:
verse	4	4	12	@@And they shall take all the instruments of ministry, wherewith they minister in the sanctuary, and put @9them@7 in a cloth of blue, and cover them with a covering of badgers' skins, and shall put @9them@7 on a bar:
verse	4	4	13	And they shall take away the ashes from the altar, and spread a purple cloth thereon:
verse	4	4	14	@@And they shall put upon it all the vessels thereof, wherewith they minister about it, @9even@7 the censers, the fleshhooks, and the shovels, and the basons, all the vessels of the altar; and they shall spread upon it a covering of badgers' skins, and put to the staves of it.
verse	4	4	15	@@And when Aaron and his sons have made an end of covering the sanctuary, and all the vessels of the sanctuary, as the camp is to set forward; after that, the sons of Kohath shall come to bear @9it:@7 but they shall not touch @9any@7 holy thing, lest they die. These @9things are@7 the burden of the sons of Kohath in the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	4	16	@@And to the office of Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest @9pertaineth@7 the oil for the light, and the sweet incense, and the daily meat offering, and the anointing oil, @9and@7 the oversight of all the tabernacle, and of all that therein @9is,@7 in the sanctuary, and in the vessels thereof.
verse	4	4	17	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
verse	4	4	18	Cut ye not off the tribe of the families of the Kohathites from among the Levites:
verse	4	4	19	But thus do unto them, that they may live, and not die, when they approach unto the most holy things: Aaron and his sons shall go in, and appoint them every one to his service and to his burden:
verse	4	4	20	But they shall not go in to see when the holy things are covered, lest they die.
verse	4	4	21	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	4	22	Take also the sum of the sons of Gershon, throughout the houses of their fathers, by their families;
verse	4	4	23	From thirty years old and upward until fifty years old shalt thou number them; all that enter in to perform the service, to do the work in the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	4	24	@@This @9is@7 the service of the families of the Gershonites, to serve, and for burdens:
verse	4	4	25	@@And they shall bear the curtains of the tabernacle, and the tabernacle of the congregation, his covering, and the covering of the badgers' skins that @9is@7 above upon it, and the hanging for the door of the tabernacle of the congregation,
verse	4	4	26	@@And the hangings of the court, and the hanging for the door of the gate of the court, which @9is@7 by the tabernacle and by the altar round about, and their cords, and all the instruments of their service, and all that is made for them: so shall they serve.
verse	4	4	27	At the appointment of Aaron and his sons shall be all the service of the sons of the Gershonites, in all their burdens, and in all their service: and ye shall appoint unto them in charge all their burdens.
verse	4	4	28	@@This is the service of the families of the sons of Gershon in the tabernacle of the congregation: and their charge @9shall be@7 under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.
verse	4	4	29	As for the sons of Merari, thou shalt number them after their families, by the house of their fathers;
verse	4	4	30	From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old shalt thou number them, every one that entereth into the service, to do the work of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	4	31	@@And this @9is@7 the charge of their burden, according to all their service in the tabernacle of the congregation; the boards of the tabernacle, and the bars thereof, and the pillars thereof, and sockets thereof,
verse	4	4	32	And the pillars of the court round about, and their sockets, and their pins, and their cords, with all their instruments, and with all their service: and by name ye shall reckon the instruments of the charge of their burden.
verse	4	4	33	@@This @9is@7 the service of the families of the sons of Merari, according to all their service, in the tabernacle of the congregation, under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.
verse	4	4	34	And Moses and Aaron and the chief of the congregation numbered the sons of the Kohathites after their families, and after the house of their fathers,
verse	4	4	35	From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entereth into the service, for the work in the tabernacle of the congregation:
verse	4	4	36	And those that were numbered of them by their families were two thousand seven hundred and fifty.
verse	4	4	37	@@These @9were@7 they that were numbered of the families of the Kohathites, all that might do service in the tabernacle of the congregation, which Moses and Aaron did number according to the commandment of the LORD by the hand of Moses.
verse	4	4	38	And those that were numbered of the sons of Gershon, throughout their families, and by the house of their fathers,
verse	4	4	39	From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entereth into the service, for the work in the tabernacle of the congregation,
verse	4	4	40	Even those that were numbered of them, throughout their families, by the house of their fathers, were two thousand and six hundred and thirty.
verse	4	4	41	@@These @9are@7 they that were numbered of the families of the sons of Gershon, of all that might do service in the tabernacle of the congregation, whom Moses and Aaron did number according to the commandment of the LORD.
verse	4	4	42	And those that were numbered of the families of the sons of Merari, throughout their families, by the house of their fathers,
verse	4	4	43	From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entereth into the service, for the work in the tabernacle of the congregation,
verse	4	4	44	Even those that were numbered of them after their families, were three thousand and two hundred.
verse	4	4	45	@@These @9be@7 those that were numbered of the families of the sons of Merari, whom Moses and Aaron numbered according to the word of the LORD by the hand of Moses.
verse	4	4	46	All those that were numbered of the Levites, whom Moses and Aaron and the chief of Israel numbered, after their families, and after the house of their fathers,
verse	4	4	47	From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that came to do the service of the ministry, and the service of the burden in the tabernacle of the congregation,
verse	4	4	48	Even those that were numbered of them, were eight thousand and five hundred and fourscore.
verse	4	4	49	According to the commandment of the LORD they were numbered by the hand of Moses, every one according to his service, and according to his burden: thus were they numbered of him, as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	4	5	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	5	2	Command the children of Israel, that they put out of the camp every leper, and every one that hath an issue, and whosoever is defiled by the dead:
verse	4	5	3	Both male and female shall ye put out, without the camp shall ye put them; that they defile not their camps, in the midst whereof I dwell.
verse	4	5	4	And the children of Israel did so, and put them out without the camp: as the LORD spake unto Moses, so did the children of Israel.
verse	4	5	5	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	5	6	Speak unto the children of Israel, When a man or woman shall commit any sin that men commit, to do a trespass against the LORD, and that person be guilty;
verse	4	5	7	@@Then they shall confess their sin which they have done: and he shall recompense his trespass with the principal thereof, and add unto it the fifth @9part@7 thereof, and give @9it@7 unto @9him@7 against whom he hath trespassed.
verse	4	5	8	@@But if the man have no kinsman to recompense the trespass unto, let the trespass be recompensed unto the LORD, @9even@7 to the priest; beside the ram of the atonement, whereby an atonement shall be made for him.
verse	4	5	9	And every offering of all the holy things of the children of Israel, which they bring unto the priest, shall be his.
verse	4	5	10	And every man's hallowed things shall be his: whatsoever any man giveth the priest, it shall be his.
verse	4	5	11	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	5	12	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, If any man's wife go aside, and commit a trespass against him,
verse	4	5	13	@@And a man lie with her carnally, and it be hid from the eyes of her husband, and be kept close, and she be defiled, and @9there be@7 no witness against her, neither she be taken @9with the manner; @7
verse	4	5	14	And the spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, and she be defiled: or if the spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, and she be not defiled:
verse	4	5	15	@@Then shall the man bring his wife unto the priest, and he shall bring her offering for her, the tenth @9part@7 of an ephah of barley meal; he shall pour no oil upon it, nor put frankincense thereon; for it @9is@7 an offering of jealousy, an offering of memorial, bringing iniquity to remembrance.
verse	4	5	16	And the priest shall bring her near, and set her before the LORD:
verse	4	5	17	@@And the priest shall take holy water in an earthen vessel; and of the dust that is in the floor of the tabernacle the priest shall take, and put @9it@7 into the water:
verse	4	5	18	@@And the priest shall set the woman before the LORD, and uncover the woman's head, and put the offering of memorial in her hands, which @9is@7 the jealousy offering: and the priest shall have in his hand the bitter water that causeth the curse:
verse	4	5	19	@@And the priest shall charge her by an oath, and say unto the woman, If no man have lain with thee, and if thou hast not gone aside to uncleanness @9with another@7 instead of thy husband, be thou free from this bitter water that causeth the curse:
verse	4	5	20	@@But if thou hast gone aside @9to another@7 instead of thy husband, and if thou be defiled, and some man have lain with thee beside thine husband:
verse	4	5	21	Then the priest shall charge the woman with an oath of cursing, and the priest shall say unto the woman, The LORD make thee a curse and an oath among thy people, when the LORD doth make thy thigh to rot, and thy belly to swell;
verse	4	5	22	@@And this water that causeth the curse shall go into thy bowels, to make @9thy@7 belly to swell, and @9thy@7 thigh to rot: And the woman shall say, Amen, amen.
verse	4	5	23	@@And the priest shall write these curses in a book, and he shall blot @9them@7 out with the bitter water:
verse	4	5	24	@@And he shall cause the woman to drink the bitter water that causeth the curse: and the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her, @9and become@7 bitter.
verse	4	5	25	Then the priest shall take the jealousy offering out of the woman's hand, and shall wave the offering before the LORD, and offer it upon the altar:
verse	4	5	26	@@And the priest shall take an handful of the offering, @9even@7 the memorial thereof, and burn @9it@7 upon the altar, and afterward shall cause the woman to drink the water.
verse	4	5	27	@@And when he hath made her to drink the water, then it shall come to pass, @9that,@7 if she be defiled, and have done trespass against her husband, that the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her, @9and become@7 bitter, and her belly shall swell, and her thigh shall rot: and the woman shall be a curse among her people.
verse	4	5	28	And if the woman be not defiled, but be clean; then she shall be free, and shall conceive seed.
verse	4	5	29	@@This @9is@7 the law of jealousies, when a wife goeth aside @9to another@7 instead of her husband, and is defiled;
verse	4	5	30	Or when the spirit of jealousy cometh upon him, and he be jealous over his wife, and shall set the woman before the LORD, and the priest shall execute upon her all this law.
verse	4	5	31	Then shall the man be guiltless from iniquity, and this woman shall bear her iniquity.
verse	4	6	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	6	2	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When either man or woman shall separate @9themselves@7 to vow a vow of a Nazarite, to separate @9themselves@7 unto the LORD:
verse	4	6	3	@@He shall separate @9himself@7 from wine and strong drink, and shall drink no vinegar of wine, or vinegar of strong drink, neither shall he drink any liquor of grapes, nor eat moist grapes, or dried.
verse	4	6	4	All the days of his separation shall he eat nothing that is made of the vine tree, from the kernels even to the husk.
verse	4	6	5	@@All the days of the vow of his separation there shall no razor come upon his head: until the days be fulfilled, in the which he separateth @9himself@7 unto the LORD, he shall be holy, @9and@7 shall let the locks of the hair of his head grow.
verse	4	6	6	@@All the days that he separateth @9himself@7 unto the LORD he shall come at no dead body.
verse	4	6	7	@@He shall not make himself unclean for his father, or for his mother, for his brother, or for his sister, when they die: because the consecration of his God @9is@7 upon his head.
verse	4	6	8	@@All the days of his separation he @9is@7 holy unto the LORD.
verse	4	6	9	And if any man die very suddenly by him, and he hath defiled the head of his consecration; then he shall shave his head in the day of his cleansing, on the seventh day shall he shave it.
verse	4	6	10	And on the eighth day he shall bring two turtles, or two young pigeons, to the priest, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation:
verse	4	6	11	And the priest shall offer the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, and make an atonement for him, for that he sinned by the dead, and shall hallow his head that same day.
verse	4	6	12	And he shall consecrate unto the LORD the days of his separation, and shall bring a lamb of the first year for a trespass offering: but the days that were before shall be lost, because his separation was defiled.
verse	4	6	13	@@And this @9is@7 the law of the Nazarite, when the days of his separation are fulfilled: he shall be brought unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation:
verse	4	6	14	And he shall offer his offering unto the LORD, one he lamb of the first year without blemish for a burnt offering, and one ewe lamb of the first year without blemish for a sin offering, and one ram without blemish for peace offerings,
verse	4	6	15	And a basket of unleavened bread, cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, and wafers of unleavened bread anointed with oil, and their meat offering, and their drink offerings.
verse	4	6	16	@@And the priest shall bring @9them@7 before the LORD, and shall offer his sin offering, and his burnt offering:
verse	4	6	17	@@And he shall offer the ram @9for@7 a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the LORD, with the basket of unleavened bread: the priest shall offer also his meat offering, and his drink offering.
verse	4	6	18	@@And the Nazarite shall shave the head of his separation @9at@7 the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall take the hair of the head of his separation, and put @9it@7 in the fire which @9is@7 under the sacrifice of the peace offerings.
verse	4	6	19	@@And the priest shall take the sodden shoulder of the ram, and one unleavened cake out of the basket, and one unleavened wafer, and shall put @9them@7 upon the hands of the Nazarite, after @9the hair of@7 his separation is shaven:
verse	4	6	20	@@And the priest shall wave them @9for@7 a wave offering before the LORD: this @9is@7 holy for the priest, with the wave breast and heave shoulder: and after that the Nazarite may drink wine.
verse	4	6	21	@@This @9is@7 the law of the Nazarite who hath vowed, @9and of@7 his offering unto the LORD for his separation, beside that @9that@7 his hand shall get: according to the vow which he vowed, so he must do after the law of his separation.
verse	4	6	22	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	6	23	Speak unto Aaron and unto his sons, saying, On this wise ye shall bless the children of Israel, saying unto them,
verse	4	6	24	The LORD bless thee, and keep thee:
verse	4	6	25	The LORD make his face shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee:
verse	4	6	26	The LORD lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace.
verse	4	6	27	And they shall put my name upon the children of Israel; and I will bless them.
verse	4	7	1	And it came to pass on the day that Moses had fully set up the tabernacle, and had anointed it, and sanctified it, and all the instruments thereof, both the altar and all the vessels thereof, and had anointed them, and sanctified them;
verse	4	7	2	@@That the princes of Israel, heads of the house of their fathers, who @9were@7 the princes of the tribes, and were over them that were numbered, offered:
verse	4	7	3	And they brought their offering before the LORD, six covered wagons, and twelve oxen; a wagon for two of the princes, and for each one an ox: and they brought them before the tabernacle.
verse	4	7	4	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	7	5	@@Take @9it@7 of them, that they may be to do the service of the tabernacle of the congregation; and thou shalt give them unto the Levites, to every man according to his service.
verse	4	7	6	And Moses took the wagons and the oxen, and gave them unto the Levites.
verse	4	7	7	Two wagons and four oxen he gave unto the sons of Gershon, according to their service:
verse	4	7	8	And four wagons and eight oxen he gave unto the sons of Merari, according unto their service, under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.
verse	4	7	9	@@But unto the sons of Kohath he gave none: because the service of the sanctuary belonging unto them @9was that@7 they should bear upon their shoulders.
verse	4	7	10	And the princes offered for dedicating of the altar in the day that it was anointed, even the princes offered their offering before the altar.
verse	4	7	11	And the LORD said unto Moses, They shall offer their offering, each prince on his day, for the dedicating of the altar.
verse	4	7	12	And he that offered his offering the first day was Nahshon the son of Amminadab, of the tribe of Judah:
verse	4	7	13	@@And his offering @9was@7 one silver charger, the weight thereof @9was@7 an hundred and thirty @9shekels,@7 one silver bowl of seventy shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary; both of them @9were@7 full of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat offering:
