verse	4	8	5	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	8	6	Take the Levites from among the children of Israel, and cleanse them.
verse	4	8	7	@@And thus shalt thou do unto them, to cleanse them: Sprinkle water of purifying upon them, and let them shave all their flesh, and let them wash their clothes, and @9so@7 make themselves clean.
verse	4	8	8	@@Then let them take a young bullock with his meat offering, @9even@7 fine flour mingled with oil, and another young bullock shalt thou take for a sin offering.
verse	4	8	9	And thou shalt bring the Levites before the tabernacle of the congregation: and thou shalt gather the whole assembly of the children of Israel together:
verse	4	8	10	And thou shalt bring the Levites before the LORD: and the children of Israel shall put their hands upon the Levites:
verse	4	8	11	@@And Aaron shall offer the Levites before the LORD @9for@7 an offering of the children of Israel, that they may execute the service of the LORD.
verse	4	8	12	@@And the Levites shall lay their hands upon the heads of the bullocks: and thou shalt offer the one @9for@7 a sin offering, and the other @9for@7 a burnt offering, unto the LORD, to make an atonement for the Levites.
verse	4	8	13	@@And thou shalt set the Levites before Aaron, and before his sons, and offer them @9for@7 an offering unto the LORD.
verse	4	8	14	Thus shalt thou separate the Levites from among the children of Israel: and the Levites shall be mine.
verse	4	8	15	@@And after that shall the Levites go in to do the service of the tabernacle of the congregation: and thou shalt cleanse them, and offer them @9for@7 an offering.
verse	4	8	16	@@For they @9are@7 wholly given unto me from among the children of Israel; instead of such as open every womb, @9even instead of@7 the firstborn of all the children of Israel, have I taken them unto me.
verse	4	8	17	@@For all the firstborn of the children of Israel @9are@7 mine, @9both@7 man and beast: on the day that I smote every firstborn in the land of Egypt I sanctified them for myself.
verse	4	8	18	And I have taken the Levites for all the firstborn of the children of Israel.
verse	4	8	19	@@And I have given the Levites @9as@7 a gift to Aaron and to his sons from among the children of Israel, to do the service of the children of Israel in the tabernacle of the congregation, and to make an atonement for the children of Israel: that there be no plague among the children of Israel, when the children of Israel come nigh unto the sanctuary.
verse	4	8	20	And Moses, and Aaron, and all the congregation of the children of Israel, did to the Levites according unto all that the LORD commanded Moses concerning the Levites, so did the children of Israel unto them.
verse	4	8	21	@@And the Levites were purified, and they washed their clothes; and Aaron offered them @9as@7 an offering before the LORD; and Aaron made an atonement for them to cleanse them.
verse	4	8	22	And after that went the Levites in to do their service in the tabernacle of the congregation before Aaron, and before his sons: as the LORD had commanded Moses concerning the Levites, so did they unto them.
verse	4	8	23	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	8	24	@@This @9is it@7 that @9belongeth@7 unto the Levites: from twenty and five years old and upward they shall go in to wait upon the service of the tabernacle of the congregation:
verse	4	8	25	@@And from the age of fifty years they shall cease waiting upon the service @9thereof,@7 and shall serve no more:
verse	4	8	26	But shall minister with their brethren in the tabernacle of the congregation, to keep the charge, and shall do no service. Thus shalt thou do unto the Levites touching their charge.
verse	4	9	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the first month of the second year after they were come out of the land of Egypt, saying,
verse	4	9	2	Let the children of Israel also keep the passover at his appointed season.
verse	4	9	3	In the fourteenth day of this month, at even, ye shall keep it in his appointed season: according to all the rites of it, and according to all the ceremonies thereof, shall ye keep it.
verse	4	9	4	And Moses spake unto the children of Israel, that they should keep the passover.
verse	4	9	5	And they kept the passover on the fourteenth day of the first month at even in the wilderness of Sinai: according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so did the children of Israel.
verse	4	9	6	And there were certain men, who were defiled by the dead body of a man, that they could not keep the passover on that day: and they came before Moses and before Aaron on that day:
verse	4	9	7	@@And those men said unto him, We @9are@7 defiled by the dead body of a man: wherefore are we kept back, that we may not offer an offering of the LORD in his appointed season among the children of Israel?
verse	4	9	8	And Moses said unto them, Stand still, and I will hear what the LORD will command concerning you.
verse	4	9	9	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	9	10	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, If any man of you or of your posterity shall be unclean by reason of a dead body, or @9be@7 in a journey afar off, yet he shall keep the passover unto the LORD.
verse	4	9	11	@@The fourteenth day of the second month at even they shall keep it, @9and@7 eat it with unleavened bread and bitter @9herbs. @7
verse	4	9	12	They shall leave none of it unto the morning, nor break any bone of it: according to all the ordinances of the passover they shall keep it.
verse	4	9	13	@@But the man that @9is@7 clean, and is not in a journey, and forbeareth to keep the passover, even the same soul shall be cut off from among his people: because he brought not the offering of the LORD in his appointed season, that man shall bear his sin.
verse	4	9	14	And if a stranger shall sojourn among you, and will keep the passover unto the LORD; according to the ordinance of the passover, and according to the manner thereof, so shall he do: ye shall have one ordinance, both for the stranger, and for him that was born in the land.
verse	4	9	15	@@And on the day that the tabernacle was reared up the cloud covered the tabernacle, @9namely,@7 the tent of the testimony: and at even there was upon the tabernacle as it were the appearance of fire, until the morning.
verse	4	9	16	@@So it was alway: the cloud covered it @9by day,@7 and the appearance of fire by night.
verse	4	9	17	And when the cloud was taken up from the tabernacle, then after that the children of Israel journeyed: and in the place where the cloud abode, there the children of Israel pitched their tents.
verse	4	9	18	At the commandment of the LORD the children of Israel journeyed, and at the commandment of the LORD they pitched: as long as the cloud abode upon the tabernacle they rested in their tents.
verse	4	9	19	And when the cloud tarried long upon the tabernacle many days, then the children of Israel kept the charge of the LORD, and journeyed not.
verse	4	9	20	@@And @9so@7 it was, when the cloud was a few days upon the tabernacle; according to the commandment of the LORD they abode in their tents, and according to the commandment of the LORD they journeyed.
verse	4	9	21	@@And @9so@7 it was, when the cloud abode from even unto the morning, and @9that@7 the cloud was taken up in the morning, then they journeyed: whether @9it was@7 by day or by night that the cloud was taken up, they journeyed.
verse	4	9	22	@@Or @9whether it were@7 two days, or a month, or a year, that the cloud tarried upon the tabernacle, remaining thereon, the children of Israel abode in their tents, and journeyed not: but when it was taken up, they journeyed.
verse	4	9	23	At the commandment of the LORD they rested in the tents, and at the commandment of the LORD they journeyed: they kept the charge of the LORD, at the commandment of the LORD by the hand of Moses.
verse	4	10	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	10	2	Make thee two trumpets of silver; of a whole piece shalt thou make them: that thou mayest use them for the calling of the assembly, and for the journeying of the camps.
verse	4	10	3	And when they shall blow with them, all the assembly shall assemble themselves to thee at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	10	4	@@And if they blow @9but@7 with one @9trumpet,@7 then the princes, @9which are@7 heads of the thousands of Israel, shall gather themselves unto thee.
verse	4	10	5	When ye blow an alarm, then the camps that lie on the east parts shall go forward.
verse	4	10	6	When ye blow an alarm the second time, then the camps that lie on the south side shall take their journey: they shall blow an alarm for their journeys.
verse	4	10	7	But when the congregation is to be gathered together, ye shall blow, but ye shall not sound an alarm.
verse	4	10	8	And the sons of Aaron, the priests, shall blow with the trumpets; and they shall be to you for an ordinance for ever throughout your generations.
verse	4	10	9	And if ye go to war in your land against the enemy that oppresseth you, then ye shall blow an alarm with the trumpets; and ye shall be remembered before the LORD your God, and ye shall be saved from your enemies.
verse	4	10	10	@@Also in the day of your gladness, and in your solemn days, and in the beginnings of your months, ye shall blow with the trumpets over your burnt offerings, and over the sacrifices of your peace offerings; that they may be to you for a memorial before your God: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	4	10	11	@@And it came to pass on the twentieth @9day@7 of the second month, in the second year, that the cloud was taken up from off the tabernacle of the testimony.
verse	4	10	12	And the children of Israel took their journeys out of the wilderness of Sinai; and the cloud rested in the wilderness of Paran.
verse	4	10	13	And they first took their journey according to the commandment of the LORD by the hand of Moses.
verse	4	10	14	@@In the first @9place@7 went the standard of the camp of the children of Judah according to their armies: and over his host @9was@7 Nahshon the son of Amminadab.
verse	4	10	15	@@And over the host of the tribe of the children of Issachar @9was@7 Nethaneel the son of Zuar.
verse	4	10	16	@@And over the host of the tribe of the children of Zebulun @9was@7 Eliab the son of Helon.
verse	4	10	17	And the tabernacle was taken down; and the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari set forward, bearing the tabernacle.
verse	4	10	18	@@And the standard of the camp of Reuben set forward according to their armies: and over his host @9was@7 Elizur the son of Shedeur.
verse	4	10	19	And over the host of the tribe of the children of Simeon was Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai.
verse	4	10	20	And over the host of the tribe of the children of Gad was Eliasaph the son of Deuel.
verse	4	10	21	@@And the Kohathites set forward, bearing the sanctuary: and @9the other@7 did set up the tabernacle against they came.
verse	4	10	22	@@And the standard of the camp of the children of Ephraim set forward according to their armies: and over his host @9was@7 Elishama the son of Ammihud.
verse	4	10	23	@@And over the host of the tribe of the children of Manasseh @9was@7 Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.
verse	4	10	24	@@And over the host of the tribe of the children of Benjamin @9was@7 Abidan the son of Gideoni.
verse	4	10	25	@@And the standard of the camp of the children of Dan set forward, @9which was@7 the rereward of all the camps throughout their hosts: and over his host @9was@7 Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.
verse	4	10	26	@@And over the host of the tribe of the children of Asher @9was@7 Pagiel the son of Ocran.
verse	4	10	27	@@And over the host of the tribe of the children of Naphtali @9was@7 Ahira the son of Enan.
verse	4	10	28	@@Thus @9were@7 the journeyings of the children of Israel according to their armies, when they set forward.
verse	4	10	29	And Moses said unto Hobab, the son of Raguel the Midianite, Moses' father in law, We are journeying unto the place of which the LORD said, I will give it you: come thou with us, and we will do thee good: for the LORD hath spoken good concerning Israel.
verse	4	10	30	And he said unto him, I will not go; but I will depart to mine own land, and to my kindred.
verse	4	10	31	And he said, Leave us not, I pray thee; forasmuch as thou knowest how we are to encamp in the wilderness, and thou mayest be to us instead of eyes.
verse	4	10	32	And it shall be, if thou go with us, yea, it shall be, that what goodness the LORD shall do unto us, the same will we do unto thee.
verse	4	10	33	And they departed from the mount of the LORD three days' journey: and the ark of the covenant of the LORD went before them in the three days' journey, to search out a resting place for them.
verse	4	10	34	@@And the cloud of the LORD @9was@7 upon them by day, when they went out of the camp.
verse	4	10	35	And it came to pass, when the ark set forward, that Moses said, Rise up, LORD, and let thine enemies be scattered; and let them that hate thee flee before thee.
verse	4	10	36	And when it rested, he said, Return, O LORD, unto the many thousands of Israel.
verse	4	11	1	@@And @9when@7 the people complained, it displeased the LORD: and the LORD heard @9it;@7 and his anger was kindled; and the fire of the LORD burnt among them, and consumed @9them that were@7 in the uttermost parts of the camp.
verse	4	11	2	And the people cried unto Moses; and when Moses prayed unto the LORD, the fire was quenched.
verse	4	11	3	And he called the name of the place Taberah: because the fire of the LORD burnt among them.
verse	4	11	4	@@And the mixt multitude that @9was@7 among them fell a lusting: and the children of Israel also wept again, and said, Who shall give us flesh to eat?
verse	4	11	5	We remember the fish, which we did eat in Egypt freely; the cucumbers, and the melons, and the leeks, and the onions, and the garlick:
verse	4	11	6	@@But now our soul @9is@7 dried away: @9there is@7 nothing at all, beside this manna, @9before@7 our eyes.
verse	4	11	7	@@And the manna @9was@7 as coriander seed, and the colour thereof as the colour of bdellium.
verse	4	11	8	@@@9And@7 the people went about, and gathered @9it,@7 and ground @9it@7 in mills, or beat @9it@7 in a mortar, and baked @9it@7 in pans, and made cakes of it: and the taste of it was as the taste of fresh oil.
verse	4	11	9	And when the dew fell upon the camp in the night, the manna fell upon it.
