verse	4	14	9	@@Only rebel not ye against the LORD, neither fear ye the people of the land; for they @9are@7 bread for us: their defence is departed from them, and the LORD @9is@7 with us: fear them not.
verse	4	14	10	But all the congregation bade stone them with stones. And the glory of the LORD appeared in the tabernacle of the congregation before all the children of Israel.
verse	4	14	11	And the LORD said unto Moses, How long will this people provoke me? and how long will it be ere they believe me, for all the signs which I have shewed among them?
verse	4	14	12	I will smite them with the pestilence, and disinherit them, and will make of thee a greater nation and mightier than they.
verse	4	14	13	@@And Moses said unto the LORD, Then the Egyptians shall hear @9it,@7 (for thou broughtest up this people in thy might from among them;)
verse	4	14	14	@@And they will tell @9it@7 to the inhabitants of this land: @9for@7 they have heard that thou LORD @9art@7 among this people, that thou LORD art seen face to face, and @9that@7 thy cloud standeth over them, and @9that@7 thou goest before them, by day time in a pillar of a cloud, and in a pillar of fire by night.
verse	4	14	15	@@Now @9if@7 thou shalt kill @9all@7 this people as one man, then the nations which have heard the fame of thee will speak, saying,
verse	4	14	16	Because the LORD was not able to bring this people into the land which he sware unto them, therefore he hath slain them in the wilderness.
verse	4	14	17	And now, I beseech thee, let the power of my Lord be great, according as thou hast spoken, saying,
verse	4	14	18	@@The LORD @9is@7 longsuffering, and of great mercy, forgiving iniquity and transgression, and by no means clearing @9the guilty,@7 visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth @9generation. @7
verse	4	14	19	Pardon, I beseech thee, the iniquity of this people according unto the greatness of thy mercy, and as thou hast forgiven this people, from Egypt even until now.
verse	4	14	20	And the LORD said, I have pardoned according to thy word:
verse	4	14	21	@@But @9as@7 truly @9as@7 I live, all the earth shall be filled with the glory of the LORD.
verse	4	14	22	Because all those men which have seen my glory, and my miracles, which I did in Egypt and in the wilderness, and have tempted me now these ten times, and have not hearkened to my voice;
verse	4	14	23	Surely they shall not see the land which I sware unto their fathers, neither shall any of them that provoked me see it:
verse	4	14	24	But my servant Caleb, because he had another spirit with him, and hath followed me fully, him will I bring into the land whereinto he went; and his seed shall possess it.
verse	4	14	25	(Now the Amalekites and the Canaanites dwelt in the valley.) To morrow turn you, and get you into the wilderness by the way of the Red sea.
verse	4	14	26	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
verse	4	14	27	@@How long @9shall I bear with@7 this evil congregation, which murmur against me? I have heard the murmurings of the children of Israel, which they murmur against me.
verse	4	14	28	@@Say unto them, @9As truly as@7 I live, saith the LORD, as ye have spoken in mine ears, so will I do to you:
verse	4	14	29	Your carcases shall fall in this wilderness; and all that were numbered of you, according to your whole number, from twenty years old and upward, which have murmured against me,
verse	4	14	30	@@Doubtless ye shall not come into the land, @9concerning@7 which I sware to make you dwell therein, save Caleb the son of Jephunneh, and Joshua the son of Nun.
verse	4	14	31	But your little ones, which ye said should be a prey, them will I bring in, and they shall know the land which ye have despised.
verse	4	14	32	@@But @9as for@7 you, your carcases, they shall fall in this wilderness.
verse	4	14	33	And your children shall wander in the wilderness forty years, and bear your whoredoms, until your carcases be wasted in the wilderness.
verse	4	14	34	@@After the number of the days in which ye searched the land, @9even@7 forty days, each day for a year, shall ye bear your iniquities, @9even@7 forty years, and ye shall know my breach of promise.
verse	4	14	35	I the LORD have said, I will surely do it unto all this evil congregation, that are gathered together against me: in this wilderness they shall be consumed, and there they shall die.
verse	4	14	36	And the men, which Moses sent to search the land, who returned, and made all the congregation to murmur against him, by bringing up a slander upon the land,
verse	4	14	37	Even those men that did bring up the evil report upon the land, died by the plague before the LORD.
verse	4	14	38	@@But Joshua the son of Nun, and Caleb the son of Jephunneh, @9which were@7 of the men that went to search the land, lived @9still. @7
verse	4	14	39	And Moses told these sayings unto all the children of Israel: and the people mourned greatly.
verse	4	14	40	@@And they rose up early in the morning, and gat them up into the top of the mountain, saying, Lo, we @9be here,@7 and will go up unto the place which the LORD hath promised: for we have sinned.
verse	4	14	41	And Moses said, Wherefore now do ye transgress the commandment of the LORD? but it shall not prosper.
verse	4	14	42	@@Go not up, for the LORD @9is@7 not among you; that ye be not smitten before your enemies.
verse	4	14	43	@@For the Amalekites and the Canaanites @9are@7 there before you, and ye shall fall by the sword: because ye are turned away from the LORD, therefore the LORD will not be with you.
verse	4	14	44	But they presumed to go up unto the hill top: nevertheless the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and Moses, departed not out of the camp.
verse	4	14	45	@@Then the Amalekites came down, and the Canaanites which dwelt in that hill, and smote them, and discomfited them, @9even@7 unto Hormah.
verse	4	15	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	15	2	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When ye be come into the land of your habitations, which I give unto you,
verse	4	15	3	And will make an offering by fire unto the LORD, a burnt offering, or a sacrifice in performing a vow, or in a freewill offering, or in your solemn feasts, to make a sweet savour unto the LORD, of the herd, or of the flock:
verse	4	15	4	@@Then shall he that offereth his offering unto the LORD bring a meat offering of a tenth deal of flour mingled with the fourth @9part@7 of an hin of oil.
verse	4	15	5	@@And the fourth @9part@7 of an hin of wine for a drink offering shalt thou prepare with the burnt offering or sacrifice, for one lamb.
verse	4	15	6	@@Or for a ram, thou shalt prepare @9for@7 a meat offering two tenth deals of flour mingled with the third @9part@7 of an hin of oil.
verse	4	15	7	@@And for a drink offering thou shalt offer the third @9part@7 of an hin of wine, @9for@7 a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	4	15	8	@@And when thou preparest a bullock @9for@7 a burnt offering, or @9for@7 a sacrifice in performing a vow, or peace offerings unto the LORD:
verse	4	15	9	Then shall he bring with a bullock a meat offering of three tenth deals of flour mingled with half an hin of oil.
verse	4	15	10	And thou shalt bring for a drink offering half an hin of wine, for an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	4	15	11	Thus shall it be done for one bullock, or for one ram, or for a lamb, or a kid.
verse	4	15	12	According to the number that ye shall prepare, so shall ye do to every one according to their number.
verse	4	15	13	All that are born of the country shall do these things after this manner, in offering an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	4	15	14	@@And if a stranger sojourn with you, or whosoever @9be@7 among you in your generations, and will offer an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD; as ye do, so he shall do.
verse	4	15	15	@@One ordinance @9shall be both@7 for you of the congregation, and also for the stranger that sojourneth @9with you,@7 an ordinance for ever in your generations: as ye @9are,@7 so shall the stranger be before the LORD.
verse	4	15	16	One law and one manner shall be for you, and for the stranger that sojourneth with you.
verse	4	15	17	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	15	18	Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When ye come into the land whither I bring you,
verse	4	15	19	Then it shall be, that, when ye eat of the bread of the land, ye shall offer up an heave offering unto the LORD.
verse	4	15	20	@@Ye shall offer up a cake of the first of your dough @9for@7 an heave offering: as @9ye do@7 the heave offering of the threshingfloor, so shall ye heave it.
verse	4	15	21	Of the first of your dough ye shall give unto the LORD an heave offering in your generations.
verse	4	15	22	And if ye have erred, and not observed all these commandments, which the LORD hath spoken unto Moses,
verse	4	15	23	@@@9Even all@7 that the LORD hath commanded you by the hand of Moses, from the day that the LORD commanded @9Moses,@7 and henceforward among your generations;
verse	4	15	24	@@Then it shall be, if @9ought@7 be committed by ignorance without the knowledge of the congregation, that all the congregation shall offer one young bullock for a burnt offering, for a sweet savour unto the LORD, with his meat offering, and his drink offering, according to the manner, and one kid of the goats for a sin offering.
verse	4	15	25	And the priest shall make an atonement for all the congregation of the children of Israel, and it shall be forgiven them; for it is ignorance: and they shall bring their offering, a sacrifice made by fire unto the LORD, and their sin offering before the LORD, for their ignorance:
verse	4	15	26	@@And it shall be forgiven all the congregation of the children of Israel, and the stranger that sojourneth among them; seeing all the people @9were@7 in ignorance.
verse	4	15	27	And if any soul sin through ignorance, then he shall bring a she goat of the first year for a sin offering.
verse	4	15	28	And the priest shall make an atonement for the soul that sinneth ignorantly, when he sinneth by ignorance before the LORD, to make an atonement for him; and it shall be forgiven him.
verse	4	15	29	@@Ye shall have one law for him that sinneth through ignorance, @9both for@7 him that is born among the children of Israel, and for the stranger that sojourneth among them.
verse	4	15	30	@@But the soul that doeth @9ought@7 presumptuously, @9whether he be@7 born in the land, or a stranger, the same reproacheth the LORD; and that soul shall be cut off from among his people.
verse	4	15	31	@@Because he hath despised the word of the LORD, and hath broken his commandment, that soul shall utterly be cut off; his iniquity @9shall be@7 upon him.
verse	4	15	32	And while the children of Israel were in the wilderness, they found a man that gathered sticks upon the sabbath day.
verse	4	15	33	And they that found him gathering sticks brought him unto Moses and Aaron, and unto all the congregation.
verse	4	15	34	And they put him in ward, because it was not declared what should be done to him.
verse	4	15	35	And the LORD said unto Moses, The man shall be surely put to death: all the congregation shall stone him with stones without the camp.
verse	4	15	36	And all the congregation brought him without the camp, and stoned him with stones, and he died; as the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	4	15	37	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	15	38	Speak unto the children of Israel, and bid them that they make them fringes in the borders of their garments throughout their generations, and that they put upon the fringe of the borders a ribband of blue:
verse	4	15	39	And it shall be unto you for a fringe, that ye may look upon it, and remember all the commandments of the LORD, and do them; and that ye seek not after your own heart and your own eyes, after which ye use to go a whoring:
verse	4	15	40	That ye may remember, and do all my commandments, and be holy unto your God.
verse	4	15	41	@@I @9am@7 the LORD your God, which brought you out of the land of Egypt, to be your God: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	4	16	1	@@Now Korah, the son of Izhar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, and Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, and On, the son of Peleth, sons of Reuben, took @9men: @7
verse	4	16	2	And they rose up before Moses, with certain of the children of Israel, two hundred and fifty princes of the assembly, famous in the congregation, men of renown:
verse	4	16	3	@@And they gathered themselves together against Moses and against Aaron, and said unto them, @9Ye take@7 too much upon you, seeing all the congregation @9are@7 holy, every one of them, and the LORD @9is@7 among them: wherefore then lift ye up yourselves above the congregation of the LORD?
verse	4	16	4	@@And when Moses heard @9it,@7 he fell upon his face:
verse	4	16	5	@@And he spake unto Korah and unto all his company, saying, Even to morrow the LORD will shew who @9are@7 his, and @9who is@7 holy; and will cause @9him@7 to come near unto him: even @9him@7 whom he hath chosen will he cause to come near unto him.
verse	4	16	6	This do; Take you censers, Korah, and all his company;
verse	4	16	7	@@And put fire therein, and put incense in them before the LORD to morrow: and it shall be @9that@7 the man whom the LORD doth choose, he @9shall be@7 holy: @9ye take@7 too much upon you, ye sons of Levi.
verse	4	16	8	And Moses said unto Korah, Hear, I pray you, ye sons of Levi:
verse	4	16	9	@@@9Seemeth it but@7 a small thing unto you, that the God of Israel hath separated you from the congregation of Israel, to bring you near to himself to do the service of the tabernacle of the LORD, and to stand before the congregation to minister unto them?
verse	4	16	10	@@And he hath brought thee near @9to him,@7 and all thy brethren the sons of Levi with thee: and seek ye the priesthood also?
verse	4	16	11	@@For which cause @9both@7 thou and all thy company @9are@7 gathered together against the LORD: and what @9is@7 Aaron, that ye murmur against him?
verse	4	16	12	And Moses sent to call Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab: which said, We will not come up:
verse	4	16	13	@@@9Is it@7 a small thing that thou hast brought us up out of a land that floweth with milk and honey, to kill us in the wilderness, except thou make thyself altogether a prince over us?
verse	4	16	14	Moreover thou hast not brought us into a land that floweth with milk and honey, or given us inheritance of fields and vineyards: wilt thou put out the eyes of these men? we will not come up.
verse	4	16	15	And Moses was very wroth, and said unto the LORD, Respect not thou their offering: I have not taken one ass from them, neither have I hurt one of them.
verse	4	16	16	And Moses said unto Korah, Be thou and all thy company before the LORD, thou, and they, and Aaron, to morrow:
verse	4	16	17	@@And take every man his censer, and put incense in them, and bring ye before the LORD every man his censer, two hundred and fifty censers; thou also, and Aaron, each @9of you@7 his censer.
verse	4	16	18	And they took every man his censer, and put fire in them, and laid incense thereon, and stood in the door of the tabernacle of the congregation with Moses and Aaron.
verse	4	16	19	And Korah gathered all the congregation against them unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and the glory of the LORD appeared unto all the congregation.
verse	4	16	20	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
verse	4	16	21	Separate yourselves from among this congregation, that I may consume them in a moment.
verse	4	16	22	And they fell upon their faces, and said, O God, the God of the spirits of all flesh, shall one man sin, and wilt thou be wroth with all the congregation?
verse	4	16	23	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	16	24	Speak unto the congregation, saying, Get you up from about the tabernacle of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram.
verse	4	16	25	And Moses rose up and went unto Dathan and Abiram; and the elders of Israel followed him.
verse	4	16	26	And he spake unto the congregation, saying, Depart, I pray you, from the tents of these wicked men, and touch nothing of theirs, lest ye be consumed in all their sins.
verse	4	16	27	So they gat up from the tabernacle of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram, on every side: and Dathan and Abiram came out, and stood in the door of their tents, and their wives, and their sons, and their little children.
verse	4	16	28	@@And Moses said, Hereby ye shall know that the LORD hath sent me to do all these works; for @9I have@7 not @9done them@7 of mine own mind.
verse	4	16	29	@@If these men die the common death of all men, or if they be visited after the visitation of all men; @9then@7 the LORD hath not sent me.
verse	4	16	30	@@But if the LORD make a new thing, and the earth open her mouth, and swallow them up, with all that @9appertain@7 unto them, and they go down quick into the pit; then ye shall understand that these men have provoked the LORD.
verse	4	16	31	@@And it came to pass, as he had made an end of speaking all these words, that the ground clave asunder that @9was@7 under them:
verse	4	16	32	@@And the earth opened her mouth, and swallowed them up, and their houses, and all the men that @9appertained@7 unto Korah, and all @9their@7 goods.
verse	4	16	33	@@They, and all that @9appertained@7 to them, went down alive into the pit, and the earth closed upon them: and they perished from among the congregation.
verse	4	16	34	@@And all Israel that @9were@7 round about them fled at the cry of them: for they said, Lest the earth swallow us up @9also. @7
verse	4	16	35	And there came out a fire from the LORD, and consumed the two hundred and fifty men that offered incense.
verse	4	16	36	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	16	37	Speak unto Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest, that he take up the censers out of the burning, and scatter thou the fire yonder; for they are hallowed.
verse	4	16	38	@@The censers of these sinners against their own souls, let them make them broad plates @9for@7 a covering of the altar: for they offered them before the LORD, therefore they are hallowed: and they shall be a sign unto the children of Israel.
verse	4	16	39	@@And Eleazar the priest took the brasen censers, wherewith they that were burnt had offered; and they were made broad @9plates for@7 a covering of the altar:
verse	4	16	40	@@@9To be@7 a memorial unto the children of Israel, that no stranger, which is not of the seed of Aaron, come near to offer incense before the LORD; that he be not as Korah, and as his company: as the LORD said to him by the hand of Moses.
verse	4	16	41	But on the morrow all the congregation of the children of Israel murmured against Moses and against Aaron, saying, Ye have killed the people of the LORD.
verse	4	16	42	And it came to pass, when the congregation was gathered against Moses and against Aaron, that they looked toward the tabernacle of the congregation: and, behold, the cloud covered it, and the glory of the LORD appeared.
verse	4	16	43	And Moses and Aaron came before the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	16	44	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	16	45	Get you up from among this congregation, that I may consume them as in a moment. And they fell upon their faces.
verse	4	16	46	And Moses said unto Aaron, Take a censer, and put fire therein from off the altar, and put on incense, and go quickly unto the congregation, and make an atonement for them: for there is wrath gone out from the LORD; the plague is begun.
verse	4	16	47	And Aaron took as Moses commanded, and ran into the midst of the congregation; and, behold, the plague was begun among the people: and he put on incense, and made an atonement for the people.
verse	4	16	48	And he stood between the dead and the living; and the plague was stayed.
verse	4	16	49	Now they that died in the plague were fourteen thousand and seven hundred, beside them that died about the matter of Korah.
verse	4	16	50	And Aaron returned unto Moses unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and the plague was stayed.
verse	4	17	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	17	2	@@Speak unto the children of Israel, and take of every one of them a rod according to the house of @9their@7 fathers, of all their princes according to the house of their fathers twelve rods: write thou every man's name upon his rod.
verse	4	17	3	@@And thou shalt write Aaron's name upon the rod of Levi: for one rod @9shall be@7 for the head of the house of their fathers.
verse	4	17	4	And thou shalt lay them up in the tabernacle of the congregation before the testimony, where I will meet with you.
verse	4	17	5	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 the man's rod, whom I shall choose, shall blossom: and I will make to cease from me the murmurings of the children of Israel, whereby they murmur against you.
verse	4	17	6	@@And Moses spake unto the children of Israel, and every one of their princes gave him a rod apiece, for each prince one, according to their fathers' houses, @9even@7 twelve rods: and the rod of Aaron @9was@7 among their rods.
verse	4	17	7	And Moses laid up the rods before the LORD in the tabernacle of witness.
verse	4	17	8	And it came to pass, that on the morrow Moses went into the tabernacle of witness; and, behold, the rod of Aaron for the house of Levi was budded, and brought forth buds, and bloomed blossoms, and yielded almonds.
verse	4	17	9	And Moses brought out all the rods from before the LORD unto all the children of Israel: and they looked, and took every man his rod.
verse	4	17	10	And the LORD said unto Moses, Bring Aaron's rod again before the testimony, to be kept for a token against the rebels; and thou shalt quite take away their murmurings from me, that they die not.
verse	4	17	11	@@And Moses did @9so:@7 as the LORD commanded him, so did he.
verse	4	17	12	And the children of Israel spake unto Moses, saying, Behold, we die, we perish, we all perish.
verse	4	17	13	Whosoever cometh any thing near unto the tabernacle of the LORD shall die: shall we be consumed with dying?
verse	4	18	1	And the LORD said unto Aaron, Thou and thy sons and thy father's house with thee shall bear the iniquity of the sanctuary: and thou and thy sons with thee shall bear the iniquity of your priesthood.
verse	4	18	2	@@And thy brethren also of the tribe of Levi, the tribe of thy father, bring thou with thee, that they may be joined unto thee, and minister unto thee: but thou and thy sons with thee @9shall minister@7 before the tabernacle of witness.
verse	4	18	3	And they shall keep thy charge, and the charge of all the tabernacle: only they shall not come nigh the vessels of the sanctuary and the altar, that neither they, nor ye also, die.
verse	4	18	4	And they shall be joined unto thee, and keep the charge of the tabernacle of the congregation, for all the service of the tabernacle: and a stranger shall not come nigh unto you.
verse	4	18	5	And ye shall keep the charge of the sanctuary, and the charge of the altar: that there be no wrath any more upon the children of Israel.
verse	4	18	6	@@And I, behold, I have taken your brethren the Levites from among the children of Israel: to you @9they are@7 given @9as@7 a gift for the LORD, to do the service of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	18	7	@@Therefore thou and thy sons with thee shall keep your priest's office for every thing of the altar, and within the vail; and ye shall serve: I have given your priest's office @9unto you as@7 a service of gift: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.
verse	4	18	8	And the LORD spake unto Aaron, Behold, I also have given thee the charge of mine heave offerings of all the hallowed things of the children of Israel; unto thee have I given them by reason of the anointing, and to thy sons, by an ordinance for ever.
verse	4	18	9	@@This shall be thine of the most holy things, @9reserved@7 from the fire: every oblation of theirs, every meat offering of theirs, and every sin offering of theirs, and every trespass offering of theirs, which they shall render unto me, @9shall be@7 most holy for thee and for thy sons.
verse	4	18	10	@@In the most holy @9place@7 shalt thou eat it; every male shall eat it: it shall be holy unto thee.
verse	4	18	11	@@And this @9is@7 thine; the heave offering of their gift, with all the wave offerings of the children of Israel: I have given them unto thee, and to thy sons and to thy daughters with thee, by a statute for ever: every one that is clean in thy house shall eat of it.
verse	4	18	12	All the best of the oil, and all the best of the wine, and of the wheat, the firstfruits of them which they shall offer unto the LORD, them have I given thee.
verse	4	18	13	@@@9And@7 whatsoever is first ripe in the land, which they shall bring unto the LORD, shall be thine; every one that is clean in thine house shall eat @9of@7 it.
verse	4	18	14	Every thing devoted in Israel shall be thine.
verse	4	18	15	@@Every thing that openeth the matrix in all flesh, which they bring unto the LORD, @9whether it be@7 of men or beasts, shall be thine: nevertheless the firstborn of man shalt thou surely redeem, and the firstling of unclean beasts shalt thou redeem.
verse	4	18	16	@@And those that are to be redeemed from a month old shalt thou redeem, according to thine estimation, for the money of five shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary, which @9is@7 twenty gerahs.
verse	4	18	17	@@But the firstling of a cow, or the firstling of a sheep, or the firstling of a goat, thou shalt not redeem; they @9are@7 holy: thou shalt sprinkle their blood upon the altar, and shalt burn their fat @9for@7 an offering made by fire, for a sweet savour unto the LORD.
verse	4	18	18	And the flesh of them shall be thine, as the wave breast and as the right shoulder are thine.
verse	4	18	19	All the heave offerings of the holy things, which the children of Israel offer unto the LORD, have I given thee, and thy sons and thy daughters with thee, by a statute for ever: it is a covenant of salt for ever before the LORD unto thee and to thy seed with thee.
verse	4	18	20	@@And the LORD spake unto Aaron, Thou shalt have no inheritance in their land, neither shalt thou have any part among them: I @9am@7 thy part and thine inheritance among the children of Israel.
verse	4	18	21	@@And, behold, I have given the children of Levi all the tenth in Israel for an inheritance, for their service which they serve, @9even@7 the service of the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	18	22	Neither must the children of Israel henceforth come nigh the tabernacle of the congregation, lest they bear sin, and die.
verse	4	18	23	@@But the Levites shall do the service of the tabernacle of the congregation, and they shall bear their iniquity: @9it shall be@7 a statute for ever throughout your generations, that among the children of Israel they have no inheritance.
verse	4	18	24	@@But the tithes of the children of Israel, which they offer @9as@7 an heave offering unto the LORD, I have given to the Levites to inherit: therefore I have said unto them, Among the children of Israel they shall have no inheritance.
verse	4	18	25	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	18	26	@@Thus speak unto the Levites, and say unto them, When ye take of the children of Israel the tithes which I have given you from them for your inheritance, then ye shall offer up an heave offering of it for the LORD, @9even@7 a tenth @9part@7 of the tithe.
verse	4	18	27	@@And @9this@7 your heave offering shall be reckoned unto you, as though @9it were@7 the corn of the threshingfloor, and as the fulness of the winepress.
verse	4	18	28	Thus ye also shall offer an heave offering unto the LORD of all your tithes, which ye receive of the children of Israel; and ye shall give thereof the LORD'S heave offering to Aaron the priest.
verse	4	18	29	@@Out of all your gifts ye shall offer every heave offering of the LORD, of all the best thereof, @9even@7 the hallowed part thereof out of it.
verse	4	18	30	Therefore thou shalt say unto them, When ye have heaved the best thereof from it, then it shall be counted unto the Levites as the increase of the threshingfloor, and as the increase of the winepress.
verse	4	18	31	@@And ye shall eat it in every place, ye and your households: for it @9is@7 your reward for your service in the tabernacle of the congregation.
verse	4	18	32	And ye shall bear no sin by reason of it, when ye have heaved from it the best of it: neither shall ye pollute the holy things of the children of Israel, lest ye die.
verse	4	19	1	And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,
verse	4	19	2	@@This @9is@7 the ordinance of the law which the LORD hath commanded, saying, Speak unto the children of Israel, that they bring thee a red heifer without spot, wherein @9is@7 no blemish, @9and@7 upon which never came yoke:
verse	4	19	3	@@And ye shall give her unto Eleazar the priest, that he may bring her forth without the camp, and @9one@7 shall slay her before his face:
verse	4	19	4	And Eleazar the priest shall take of her blood with his finger, and sprinkle of her blood directly before the tabernacle of the congregation seven times:
verse	4	19	5	@@And @9one@7 shall burn the heifer in his sight; her skin, and her flesh, and her blood, with her dung, shall he burn:
verse	4	19	6	@@And the priest shall take cedar wood, and hyssop, and scarlet, and cast @9it@7 into the midst of the burning of the heifer.
verse	4	19	7	Then the priest shall wash his clothes, and he shall bathe his flesh in water, and afterward he shall come into the camp, and the priest shall be unclean until the even.
verse	4	19	8	And he that burneth her shall wash his clothes in water, and bathe his flesh in water, and shall be unclean until the even.
verse	4	19	9	@@And a man @9that is@7 clean shall gather up the ashes of the heifer, and lay @9them@7 up without the camp in a clean place, and it shall be kept for the congregation of the children of Israel for a water of separation: it @9is@7 a purification for sin.
verse	4	19	10	And he that gathereth the ashes of the heifer shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the even: and it shall be unto the children of Israel, and unto the stranger that sojourneth among them, for a statute for ever.
verse	4	19	11	He that toucheth the dead body of any man shall be unclean seven days.
verse	4	19	12	He shall purify himself with it on the third day, and on the seventh day he shall be clean: but if he purify not himself the third day, then the seventh day he shall not be clean.
verse	4	19	13	@@Whosoever toucheth the dead body of any man that is dead, and purifieth not himself, defileth the tabernacle of the LORD; and that soul shall be cut off from Israel: because the water of separation was not sprinkled upon him, he shall be unclean; his uncleanness @9is@7 yet upon him.
verse	4	19	14	@@This @9is@7 the law, when a man dieth in a tent: all that come into the tent, and all that @9is@7 in the tent, shall be unclean seven days.
verse	4	19	15	@@And every open vessel, which hath no covering bound upon it, @9is@7 unclean.
verse	4	19	16	And whosoever toucheth one that is slain with a sword in the open fields, or a dead body, or a bone of a man, or a grave, shall be unclean seven days.
verse	4	19	17	@@And for an unclean @9person@7 they shall take of the ashes of the burnt heifer of purification for sin, and running water shall be put thereto in a vessel:
verse	4	19	18	@@And a clean person shall take hyssop, and dip @9it@7 in the water, and sprinkle @9it@7 upon the tent, and upon all the vessels, and upon the persons that were there, and upon him that touched a bone, or one slain, or one dead, or a grave:
verse	4	19	19	@@And the clean @9person@7 shall sprinkle upon the unclean on the third day, and on the seventh day: and on the seventh day he shall purify himself, and wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and shall be clean at even.
verse	4	19	20	@@But the man that shall be unclean, and shall not purify himself, that soul shall be cut off from among the congregation, because he hath defiled the sanctuary of the LORD: the water of separation hath not been sprinkled upon him; he @9is@7 unclean.
verse	4	19	21	And it shall be a perpetual statute unto them, that he that sprinkleth the water of separation shall wash his clothes; and he that toucheth the water of separation shall be unclean until even.
verse	4	19	22	@@And whatsoever the unclean @9person@7 toucheth shall be unclean; and the soul that toucheth @9it@7 shall be unclean until even.
verse	4	20	1	@@Then came the children of Israel, @9even@7 the whole congregation, into the desert of Zin in the first month: and the people abode in Kadesh; and Miriam died there, and was buried there.
verse	4	20	2	And there was no water for the congregation: and they gathered themselves together against Moses and against Aaron.
verse	4	20	3	And the people chode with Moses, and spake, saying, Would God that we had died when our brethren died before the LORD!
verse	4	20	4	And why have ye brought up the congregation of the LORD into this wilderness, that we and our cattle should die there?
verse	4	20	5	@@And wherefore have ye made us to come up out of Egypt, to bring us in unto this evil place? it @9is@7 no place of seed, or of figs, or of vines, or of pomegranates; neither @9is@7 there any water to drink.
verse	4	20	6	And Moses and Aaron went from the presence of the assembly unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and they fell upon their faces: and the glory of the LORD appeared unto them.
verse	4	20	7	And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,
verse	4	20	8	Take the rod, and gather thou the assembly together, thou, and Aaron thy brother, and speak ye unto the rock before their eyes; and it shall give forth his water, and thou shalt bring forth to them water out of the rock: so thou shalt give the congregation and their beasts drink.
verse	4	20	9	And Moses took the rod from before the LORD, as he commanded him.
verse	4	20	10	And Moses and Aaron gathered the congregation together before the rock, and he said unto them, Hear now, ye rebels; must we fetch you water out of this rock?
verse	4	20	11	@@And Moses lifted up his hand, and with his rod he smote the rock twice: and the water came out abundantly, and the congregation drank, and their beasts @9also.@7
verse	4	20	12	And the LORD spake unto Moses and Aaron, Because ye believed me not, to sanctify me in the eyes of the children of Israel, therefore ye shall not bring this congregation into the land which I have given them.
verse	4	20	13	@@This @9is@7 the water of Meribah; because the children of Israel strove with the LORD, and he was sanctified in them.
verse	4	20	14	And Moses sent messengers from Kadesh unto the king of Edom, Thus saith thy brother Israel, Thou knowest all the travail that hath befallen us:
verse	4	20	15	How our fathers went down into Egypt, and we have dwelt in Egypt a long time; and the Egyptians vexed us, and our fathers:
verse	4	20	16	@@And when we cried unto the LORD, he heard our voice, and sent an angel, and hath brought us forth out of Egypt: and, behold, we @9are@7 in Kadesh, a city in the uttermost of thy border:
verse	4	20	17	@@Let us pass, I pray thee, through thy country: we will not pass through the fields, or through the vineyards, neither will we drink @9of@7 the water of the wells: we will go by the king's @9high@7 way, we will not turn to the right hand nor to the left, until we have passed thy borders.
verse	4	20	18	And Edom said unto him, Thou shalt not pass by me, lest I come out against thee with the sword.
verse	4	20	19	@@And the children of Israel said unto him, We will go by the high way: and if I and my cattle drink of thy water, then I will pay for it: I will only, without @9doing@7 any thing @9else,@7 go through on my feet.
verse	4	20	20	And he said, Thou shalt not go through. And Edom came out against him with much people, and with a strong hand.
verse	4	20	21	Thus Edom refused to give Israel passage through his border: wherefore Israel turned away from him.
verse	4	20	22	@@And the children of Israel, @9even@7 the whole congregation, journeyed from Kadesh, and came unto mount Hor.
verse	4	20	23	And the LORD spake unto Moses and Aaron in mount Hor, by the coast of the land of Edom, saying,
verse	4	20	24	Aaron shall be gathered unto his people: for he shall not enter into the land which I have given unto the children of Israel, because ye rebelled against my word at the water of Meribah.
verse	4	20	25	Take Aaron and Eleazar his son, and bring them up unto mount Hor:
verse	4	20	26	@@And strip Aaron of his garments, and put them upon Eleazar his son: and Aaron shall be gathered @9unto his people,@7 and shall die there.
verse	4	20	27	And Moses did as the LORD commanded: and they went up into mount Hor in the sight of all the congregation.
verse	4	20	28	And Moses stripped Aaron of his garments, and put them upon Eleazar his son; and Aaron died there in the top of the mount: and Moses and Eleazar came down from the mount.
verse	4	20	29	@@And when all the congregation saw that Aaron was dead, they mourned for Aaron thirty days, @9even@7 all the house of Israel.
verse	4	21	1	@@And @9when@7 king Arad the Canaanite, which dwelt in the south, heard tell that Israel came by the way of the spies; then he fought against Israel, and took @9some@7 of them prisoners.
verse	4	21	2	And Israel vowed a vow unto the LORD, and said, If thou wilt indeed deliver this people into my hand, then I will utterly destroy their cities.
verse	4	21	3	And the LORD hearkened to the voice of Israel, and delivered up the Canaanites; and they utterly destroyed them and their cities: and he called the name of the place Hormah.
verse	4	21	4	And they journeyed from mount Hor by the way of the Red sea, to compass the land of Edom: and the soul of the people was much discouraged because of the way.
verse	4	21	5	@@And the people spake against God, and against Moses, Wherefore have ye brought us up out of Egypt to die in the wilderness? for @9there is@7 no bread, neither @9is there any@7 water; and our soul loatheth this light bread.
verse	4	21	6	And the LORD sent fiery serpents among the people, and they bit the people; and much people of Israel died.
verse	4	21	7	Therefore the people came to Moses, and said, We have sinned, for we have spoken against the LORD, and against thee; pray unto the LORD, that he take away the serpents from us. And Moses prayed for the people.
verse	4	21	8	And the LORD said unto Moses, Make thee a fiery serpent, and set it upon a pole: and it shall come to pass, that every one that is bitten, when he looketh upon it, shall live.
verse	4	21	9	And Moses made a serpent of brass, and put it upon a pole, and it came to pass, that if a serpent had bitten any man, when he beheld the serpent of brass, he lived.
verse	4	21	10	And the children of Israel set forward, and pitched in Oboth.
verse	4	21	11	@@And they journeyed from Oboth, and pitched at Ijeabarim, in the wilderness which @9is@7 before Moab, toward the sunrising.
verse	4	21	12	From thence they removed, and pitched in the valley of Zared.
verse	4	21	13	@@From thence they removed, and pitched on the other side of Arnon, which @9is@7 in the wilderness that cometh out of the coasts of the Amorites: for Arnon @9is@7 the border of Moab, between Moab and the Amorites.
verse	4	21	14	Wherefore it is said in the book of the wars of the LORD, What he did in the Red sea, and in the brooks of Arnon,
verse	4	21	15	And at the stream of the brooks that goeth down to the dwelling of Ar, and lieth upon the border of Moab.
verse	4	21	16	@@And from thence @9they went@7 to Beer: that @9is@7 the well whereof the LORD spake unto Moses, Gather the people together, and I will give them water.
verse	4	21	17	Then Israel sang this song, Spring up, O well; sing ye unto it:
verse	4	21	18	@@The princes digged the well, the nobles of the people digged it, by @9the direction of@7 the lawgiver, with their staves. And from the wilderness @9they went@7 to Mattanah:
verse	4	21	19	And from Mattanah to Nahaliel: and from Nahaliel to Bamoth:
verse	4	21	20	@@And from Bamoth @9in@7 the valley, that @9is@7 in the country of Moab, to the top of Pisgah, which looketh toward Jeshimon.
verse	4	21	21	And Israel sent messengers unto Sihon king of the Amorites, saying,
verse	4	21	22	@@Let me pass through thy land: we will not turn into the fields, or into the vineyards; we will not drink @9of@7 the waters of the well: @9but@7 we will go along by the king's @9high@7 way, until we be past thy borders.
verse	4	21	23	And Sihon would not suffer Israel to pass through his border: but Sihon gathered all his people together, and went out against Israel into the wilderness: and he came to Jahaz, and fought against Israel.
verse	4	21	24	@@And Israel smote him with the edge of the sword, and possessed his land from Arnon unto Jabbok, even unto the children of Ammon: for the border of the children of Ammon @9was@7 strong.
verse	4	21	25	And Israel took all these cities: and Israel dwelt in all the cities of the Amorites, in Heshbon, and in all the villages thereof.
verse	4	21	26	@@For Heshbon @9was@7 the city of Sihon the king of the Amorites, who had fought against the former king of Moab, and taken all his land out of his hand, even unto Arnon.
verse	4	21	27	Wherefore they that speak in proverbs say, Come into Heshbon, let the city of Sihon be built and prepared:
verse	4	21	28	@@For there is a fire gone out of Heshbon, a flame from the city of Sihon: it hath consumed Ar of Moab, @9and@7 the lords of the high places of Arnon.
verse	4	21	29	Woe to thee, Moab! thou art undone, O people of Chemosh: he hath given his sons that escaped, and his daughters, into captivity unto Sihon king of the Amorites.
verse	4	21	30	@@We have shot at them; Heshbon is perished even unto Dibon, and we have laid them waste even unto Nophah, which @9reacheth@7 unto Medeba.
verse	4	21	31	Thus Israel dwelt in the land of the Amorites.
verse	4	21	32	@@And Moses sent to spy out Jaazer, and they took the villages thereof, and drove out the Amorites that @9were@7 there.
verse	4	21	33	And they turned and went up by the way of Bashan: and Og the king of Bashan went out against them, he, and all his people, to the battle at Edrei.
verse	4	21	34	And the LORD said unto Moses, Fear him not: for I have delivered him into thy hand, and all his people, and his land; and thou shalt do to him as thou didst unto Sihon king of the Amorites, which dwelt at Heshbon.
verse	4	21	35	So they smote him, and his sons, and all his people, until there was none left him alive: and they possessed his land.
verse	4	22	1	@@And the children of Israel set forward, and pitched in the plains of Moab on this side Jordan @9by@7 Jericho.
verse	4	22	2	And Balak the son of Zippor saw all that Israel had done to the Amorites.
verse	4	22	3	@@And Moab was sore afraid of the people, because they @9were@7 many: and Moab was distressed because of the children of Israel.
verse	4	22	4	@@And Moab said unto the elders of Midian, Now shall this company lick up all @9that are@7 round about us, as the ox licketh up the grass of the field. And Balak the son of Zippor @9was@7 king of the Moabites at that time.
verse	4	22	5	@@He sent messengers therefore unto Balaam the son of Beor to Pethor, which @9is@7 by the river of the land of the children of his people, to call him, saying, Behold, there is a people come out from Egypt: behold, they cover the face of the earth, and they abide over against me:
verse	4	22	6	@@Come now therefore, I pray thee, curse me this people; for they @9are@7 too mighty for me: peradventure I shall prevail, @9that@7 we may smite them, and @9that@7 I may drive them out of the land: for I wot that he whom thou blessest @9is@7 blessed, and he whom thou cursest is cursed.
verse	4	22	7	And the elders of Moab and the elders of Midian departed with the rewards of divination in their hand; and they came unto Balaam, and spake unto him the words of Balak.
verse	4	22	8	And he said unto them, Lodge here this night, and I will bring you word again, as the LORD shall speak unto me: and the princes of Moab abode with Balaam.
verse	4	22	9	@@And God came unto Balaam, and said, What men @9are@7 these with thee?
verse	4	22	10	@@And Balaam said unto God, Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab, hath sent unto me, @9saying, @7
verse	4	22	11	@@Behold, @9there is@7 a people come out of Egypt, which covereth the face of the earth: come now, curse me them; peradventure I shall be able to overcome them, and drive them out.
verse	4	22	12	@@And God said unto Balaam, Thou shalt not go with them; thou shalt not curse the people: for they @9are@7 blessed.
verse	4	22	13	And Balaam rose up in the morning, and said unto the princes of Balak, Get you into your land: for the LORD refuseth to give me leave to go with you.
verse	4	22	14	And the princes of Moab rose up, and they went unto Balak, and said, Balaam refuseth to come with us.
verse	4	22	15	And Balak sent yet again princes, more, and more honourable than they.
verse	4	22	16	And they came to Balaam, and said to him, Thus saith Balak the son of Zippor, Let nothing, I pray thee, hinder thee from coming unto me:
verse	4	22	17	For I will promote thee unto very great honour, and I will do whatsoever thou sayest unto me: come therefore, I pray thee, curse me this people.
verse	4	22	18	And Balaam answered and said unto the servants of Balak, If Balak would give me his house full of silver and gold, I cannot go beyond the word of the LORD my God, to do less or more.
verse	4	22	19	Now therefore, I pray you, tarry ye also here this night, that I may know what the LORD will say unto me more.
verse	4	22	20	@@And God came unto Balaam at night, and said unto him, If the men come to call thee, rise up, @9and@7 go with them; but yet the word which I shall say unto thee, that shalt thou do.
verse	4	22	21	And Balaam rose up in the morning, and saddled his ass, and went with the princes of Moab.
verse	4	22	22	@@And God's anger was kindled because he went: and the angel of the LORD stood in the way for an adversary against him. Now he was riding upon his ass, and his two servants @9were@7 with him.
verse	4	22	23	And the ass saw the angel of the LORD standing in the way, and his sword drawn in his hand: and the ass turned aside out of the way, and went into the field: and Balaam smote the ass, to turn her into the way.
verse	4	22	24	@@But the angel of the LORD stood in a path of the vineyards, a wall @9being@7 on this side, and a wall on that side.
verse	4	22	25	And when the ass saw the angel of the LORD, she thrust herself unto the wall, and crushed Balaam's foot against the wall: and he smote her again.
verse	4	22	26	@@And the angel of the LORD went further, and stood in a narrow place, where @9was@7 no way to turn either to the right hand or to the left.
verse	4	22	27	And when the ass saw the angel of the LORD, she fell down under Balaam: and Balaam's anger was kindled, and he smote the ass with a staff.
verse	4	22	28	And the LORD opened the mouth of the ass, and she said unto Balaam, What have I done unto thee, that thou hast smitten me these three times?
verse	4	22	29	And Balaam said unto the ass, Because thou hast mocked me: I would there were a sword in mine hand, for now would I kill thee.
verse	4	22	30	@@And the ass said unto Balaam, @9Am@7 not I thine ass, upon which thou hast ridden ever since @9I was@7 thine unto this day? was I ever wont to do so unto thee? And he said, Nay.
verse	4	22	31	Then the LORD opened the eyes of Balaam, and he saw the angel of the LORD standing in the way, and his sword drawn in his hand: and he bowed down his head, and fell flat on his face.
verse	4	22	32	@@And the angel of the LORD said unto him, Wherefore hast thou smitten thine ass these three times? behold, I went out to withstand thee, because @9thy@7 way is perverse before me:
verse	4	22	33	And the ass saw me, and turned from me these three times: unless she had turned from me, surely now also I had slain thee, and saved her alive.
verse	4	22	34	And Balaam said unto the angel of the LORD, I have sinned; for I knew not that thou stoodest in the way against me: now therefore, if it displease thee, I will get me back again.
verse	4	22	35	And the angel of the LORD said unto Balaam, Go with the men: but only the word that I shall speak unto thee, that thou shalt speak. So Balaam went with the princes of Balak.
verse	4	22	36	@@And when Balak heard that Balaam was come, he went out to meet him unto a city of Moab, which @9is@7 in the border of Arnon, which @9is@7 in the utmost coast.
verse	4	22	37	And Balak said unto Balaam, Did I not earnestly send unto thee to call thee? wherefore camest thou not unto me? am I not able indeed to promote thee to honour?
verse	4	22	38	And Balaam said unto Balak, Lo, I am come unto thee: have I now any power at all to say any thing? the word that God putteth in my mouth, that shall I speak.
verse	4	22	39	And Balaam went with Balak, and they came unto Kirjathhuzoth.
verse	4	22	40	@@And Balak offered oxen and sheep, and sent to Balaam, and to the princes that @9were@7 with him.
verse	4	22	41	@@And it came to pass on the morrow, that Balak took Balaam, and brought him up into the high places of Baal, that thence he might see the utmost @9part@7 of the people.
verse	4	23	1	And Balaam said unto Balak, Build me here seven altars, and prepare me here seven oxen and seven rams.
verse	4	23	2	@@And Balak did as Balaam had spoken; and Balak and Balaam offered on @9every@7 altar a bullock and a ram.
verse	4	23	3	And Balaam said unto Balak, Stand by thy burnt offering, and I will go: peradventure the LORD will come to meet me: and whatsoever he sheweth me I will tell thee. And he went to an high place.
verse	4	23	4	@@And God met Balaam: and he said unto him, I have prepared seven altars, and I have offered upon @9every@7 altar a bullock and a ram.
verse	4	23	5	And the LORD put a word in Balaam's mouth, and said, Return unto Balak, and thus thou shalt speak.
verse	4	23	6	And he returned unto him, and, lo, he stood by his burnt sacrifice, he, and all the princes of Moab.
verse	4	23	7	@@And he took up his parable, and said, Balak the king of Moab hath brought me from Aram, out of the mountains of the east, @9saying,@7 Come, curse me Jacob, and come, defy Israel.
verse	4	23	8	@@How shall I curse, whom God hath not cursed? or how shall I defy, @9whom@7 the LORD hath not defied?
verse	4	23	9	For from the top of the rocks I see him, and from the hills I behold him: lo, the people shall dwell alone, and shall not be reckoned among the nations.
verse	4	23	10	@@Who can count the dust of Jacob, and the number of the fourth @9part@7 of Israel? Let me die the death of the righteous, and let my last end be like his!
verse	4	23	11	@@And Balak said unto Balaam, What hast thou done unto me? I took thee to curse mine enemies, and, behold, thou hast blessed @9them@7 altogether.
verse	4	23	12	And he answered and said, Must I not take heed to speak that which the LORD hath put in my mouth?
verse	4	23	13	And Balak said unto him, Come, I pray thee, with me unto another place, from whence thou mayest see them: thou shalt see but the utmost part of them, and shalt not see them all: and curse me them from thence.
verse	4	23	14	@@And he brought him into the field of Zophim, to the top of Pisgah, and built seven altars, and offered a bullock and a ram on @9every@7 altar.
verse	4	23	15	@@And he said unto Balak, Stand here by thy burnt offering, while I meet @9the LORD@7 yonder.
verse	4	23	16	And the LORD met Balaam, and put a word in his mouth, and said, Go again unto Balak, and say thus.
verse	4	23	17	And when he came to him, behold, he stood by his burnt offering, and the princes of Moab with him. And Balak said unto him, What hath the LORD spoken?
verse	4	23	18	And he took up his parable, and said, Rise up, Balak, and hear; hearken unto me, thou son of Zippor:
verse	4	23	19	@@God @9is@7 not a man, that he should lie; neither the son of man, that he should repent: hath he said, and shall he not do @9it?@7 or hath he spoken, and shall he not make it good?
verse	4	23	20	@@Behold, I have received @9commandment@7 to bless: and he hath blessed; and I cannot reverse it.
verse	4	23	21	@@He hath not beheld iniquity in Jacob, neither hath he seen perverseness in Israel: the LORD his God @9is@7 with him, and the shout of a king @9is@7 among them.
verse	4	23	22	God brought them out of Egypt; he hath as it were the strength of an unicorn.
verse	4	23	23	@@Surely @9there is@7 no enchantment against Jacob, neither @9is there@7 any divination against Israel: according to this time it shall be said of Jacob and of Israel, What hath God wrought!
verse	4	23	24	@@Behold, the people shall rise up as a great lion, and lift up himself as a young lion: he shall not lie down until he eat @9of@7 the prey, and drink the blood of the slain.
verse	4	23	25	And Balak said unto Balaam, Neither curse them at all, nor bless them at all.
verse	4	23	26	But Balaam answered and said unto Balak, Told not I thee, saying, All that the LORD speaketh, that I must do?
verse	4	23	27	And Balak said unto Balaam, Come, I pray thee, I will bring thee unto another place; peradventure it will please God that thou mayest curse me them from thence.
