verse	5	32	39	@@See now that I, @9even@7 I, @9am@7 he, and @9there is@7 no god with me: I kill, and I make alive; I wound, and I heal: neither @9is there any@7 that can deliver out of my hand.
verse	5	32	40	For I lift up my hand to heaven, and say, I live for ever.
verse	5	32	41	If I whet my glittering sword, and mine hand take hold on judgment; I will render vengeance to mine enemies, and will reward them that hate me.
verse	5	32	42	@@I will make mine arrows drunk with blood, and my sword shall devour flesh; @9and that@7 with the blood of the slain and of the captives, from the beginning of revenges upon the enemy.
verse	5	32	43	@@Rejoice, O ye nations, @9with@7 his people: for he will avenge the blood of his servants, and will render vengeance to his adversaries, and will be merciful unto his land, @9and@7 to his people.
verse	5	32	44	And Moses came and spake all the words of this song in the ears of the people, he, and Hoshea the son of Nun.
verse	5	32	45	And Moses made an end of speaking all these words to all Israel:
verse	5	32	46	And he said unto them, Set your hearts unto all the words which I testify among you this day, which ye shall command your children to observe to do, all the words of this law.
verse	5	32	47	@@For it @9is@7 not a vain thing for you; because it @9is@7 your life: and through this thing ye shall prolong @9your@7 days in the land, whither ye go over Jordan to possess it.
verse	5	32	48	And the LORD spake unto Moses that selfsame day, saying,
verse	5	32	49	@@Get thee up into this mountain Abarim, @9unto@7 mount Nebo, which @9is@7 in the land of Moab, that @9is@7 over against Jericho; and behold the land of Canaan, which I give unto the children of Israel for a possession:
verse	5	32	50	And die in the mount whither thou goest up, and be gathered unto thy people; as Aaron thy brother died in mount Hor, and was gathered unto his people:
verse	5	32	51	Because ye trespassed against me among the children of Israel at the waters of Meribah-Kadesh, in the wilderness of Zin; because ye sanctified me not in the midst of the children of Israel.
verse	5	32	52	@@Yet thou shalt see the land before @9thee;@7 but thou shalt not go thither unto the land which I give the children of Israel.
verse	5	33	1	@@And this @9is@7 the blessing, wherewith Moses the man of God blessed the children of Israel before his death.
verse	5	33	2	@@And he said, The LORD came from Sinai, and rose up from Seir unto them; he shined forth from mount Paran, and he came with ten thousands of saints: from his right hand @9went@7 a fiery law for them.
verse	5	33	3	@@Yea, he loved the people; all his saints @9are@7 in thy hand: and they sat down at thy feet; @9every one@7 shall receive of thy words.
verse	5	33	4	@@Moses commanded us a law, @9even@7 the inheritance of the congregation of Jacob.
verse	5	33	5	@@And he was king in Jeshurun, when the heads of the people @9and@7 the tribes of Israel were gathered together.
verse	5	33	6	@@Let Reuben live, and not die; and let @9not@7 his men be few.
verse	5	33	7	@@And this @9is the blessing@7 of Judah: and he said, Hear, LORD, the voice of Judah, and bring him unto his people: let his hands be sufficient for him; and be thou an help @9to him@7 from his enemies.
verse	5	33	8	@@And of Levi he said, @9Let@7 thy Thummim and thy Urim @9be@7 with thy holy one, whom thou didst prove at Massah, @9and with@7 whom thou didst strive at the waters of Meribah;
verse	5	33	9	Who said unto his father and to his mother, I have not seen him; neither did he acknowledge his brethren, nor knew his own children: for they have observed thy word, and kept thy covenant.
verse	5	33	10	They shall teach Jacob thy judgments, and Israel thy law: they shall put incense before thee, and whole burnt sacrifice upon thine altar.
verse	5	33	11	Bless, LORD, his substance, and accept the work of his hands: smite through the loins of them that rise against him, and of them that hate him, that they rise not again.
verse	5	33	12	@@@9And@7 of Benjamin he said, The beloved of the LORD shall dwell in safety by him; @9and the LORD@7 shall cover him all the day long, and he shall dwell between his shoulders.
verse	5	33	13	@@And of Joseph he said, Blessed of the LORD @9be@7 his land, for the precious things of heaven, for the dew, and for the deep that coucheth beneath,
verse	5	33	14	@@And for the precious fruits @9brought forth@7 by the sun, and for the precious things put forth by the moon,
verse	5	33	15	And for the chief things of the ancient mountains, and for the precious things of the lasting hills,
verse	5	33	16	@@And for the precious things of the earth and fulness thereof, and @9for@7 the good will of him that dwelt in the bush: let @9the blessing@7 come upon the head of Joseph, and upon the top of the head of him @9that was@7 separated from his brethren.
verse	5	33	17	@@His glory @9is like@7 the firstling of his bullock, and his horns @9are like@7 the horns of unicorns: with them he shall push the people together to the ends of the earth: and they @9are@7 the ten thousands of Ephraim, and they @9are@7 the thousands of Manasseh.
verse	5	33	18	And of Zebulun he said, Rejoice, Zebulun, in thy going out; and, Issachar, in thy tents.
verse	5	33	19	@@They shall call the people unto the mountain; there they shall offer sacrifices of righteousness: for they shall suck @9of@7 the abundance of the seas, and @9of@7 treasures hid in the sand.
verse	5	33	20	@@And of Gad he said, Blessed @9be@7 he that enlargeth Gad: he dwelleth as a lion, and teareth the arm with the crown of the head.
verse	5	33	21	@@And he provided the first part for himself, because there, @9in@7 a portion of the lawgiver, @9was he@7 seated; and he came with the heads of the people, he executed the justice of the LORD, and his judgments with Israel.
verse	5	33	22	@@And of Dan he said, Dan @9is@7 a lion's whelp: he shall leap from Bashan.
verse	5	33	23	And of Naphtali he said, O Naphtali, satisfied with favour, and full with the blessing of the LORD: possess thou the west and the south.
verse	5	33	24	@@And of Asher he said, @9Let@7 Asher @9be@7 blessed with children; let him be acceptable to his brethren, and let him dip his foot in oil.
verse	5	33	25	@@Thy shoes @9shall be@7 iron and brass; and as thy days, @9so shall@7 thy strength @9be.@7
verse	5	33	26	@@@9There is@7 none like unto the God of Jeshurun, @9who@7 rideth upon the heaven in thy help, and in his excellency on the sky.
verse	5	33	27	@@The eternal God @9is thy@7 refuge, and underneath @9are@7 the everlasting arms: and he shall thrust out the enemy from before thee; and shall say, Destroy @9them. @7
verse	5	33	28	@@Israel then shall dwell in safety alone: the fountain of Jacob @9shall be@7 upon a land of corn and wine; also his heavens shall drop down dew.
verse	5	33	29	@@Happy @9art@7 thou, O Israel: who @9is@7 like unto thee, O people saved by the LORD, the shield of thy help, and who @9is@7 the sword of thy excellency! and thine enemies shall be found liars unto thee; and thou shalt tread upon their high places.
verse	5	34	1	@@And Moses went up from the plains of Moab unto the mountain of Nebo, to the top of Pisgah, that @9is@7 over against Jericho. And the LORD shewed him all the land of Gilead, unto Dan,
verse	5	34	2	And all Naphtali, and the land of Ephraim, and Manasseh, and all the land of Judah, unto the utmost sea,
verse	5	34	3	And the south, and the plain of the valley of Jericho, the city of palm trees, unto Zoar.
verse	5	34	4	@@And the LORD said unto him, This @9is@7 the land which I sware unto Abraham, unto Isaac, and unto Jacob, saying, I will give it unto thy seed: I have caused thee to see @9it@7 with thine eyes, but thou shalt not go over thither.
verse	5	34	5	So Moses the servant of the LORD died there in the land of Moab, according to the word of the LORD.
verse	5	34	6	And he buried him in a valley in the land of Moab, over against Bethpeor: but no man knoweth of his sepulchre unto this day.
verse	5	34	7	@@And Moses @9was@7 an hundred and twenty years old when he died: his eye was not dim, nor his natural force abated.
verse	5	34	8	@@And the children of Israel wept for Moses in the plains of Moab thirty days: so the days of weeping @9and@7 mourning for Moses were ended.
