verse	6	16	10	And they drave not out the Canaanites that dwelt in Gezer: but the Canaanites dwell among the Ephraimites unto this day, and serve under tribute.
verse	6	17	1	@@There was also a lot for the tribe of Manasseh; for he @9was@7 the firstborn of Joseph; @9to wit,@7 for Machir the firstborn of Manasseh, the father of Gilead: because he was a man of war, therefore he had Gilead and Bashan.
verse	6	17	2	@@There was also @9a lot@7 for the rest of the children of Manasseh by their families; for the children of Abiezer, and for the children of Helek, and for the children of Asriel, and for the children of Shechem, and for the children of Hepher, and for the children of Shemida: these @9were@7 the male children of Manasseh the son of Joseph by their families.
verse	6	17	3	@@But Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, had no sons, but daughters: and these @9are@7 the names of his daughters, Mahlah, and Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.
verse	6	17	4	And they came near before Eleazar the priest, and before Joshua the son of Nun, and before the princes, saying, The LORD commanded Moses to give us an inheritance among our brethren. Therefore according to the commandment of the LORD he gave them an inheritance among the brethren of their father.
verse	6	17	5	@@And there fell ten portions to Manasseh, beside the land of Gilead and Bashan, which @9were@7 on the other side Jordan;
verse	6	17	6	Because the daughters of Manasseh had an inheritance among his sons: and the rest of Manasseh's sons had the land of Gilead.
verse	6	17	7	@@And the coast of Manasseh was from Asher to Michmethah, that @9lieth@7 before Shechem; and the border went along on the right hand unto the inhabitants of Entappuah.
verse	6	17	8	@@@9Now@7 Manasseh had the land of Tappuah: but Tappuah on the border of Manasseh @9belonged@7 to the children of Ephraim;
verse	6	17	9	@@And the coast descended unto the river Kanah, southward of the river: these cities of Ephraim @9are@7 among the cities of Manasseh: the coast of Manasseh also @9was@7 on the north side of the river, and the outgoings of it were at the sea:
verse	6	17	10	@@Southward @9it was@7 Ephraim's, and northward @9it was@7 Manasseh's, and the sea is his border; and they met together in Asher on the north, and in Issachar on the east.
verse	6	17	11	@@And Manasseh had in Issachar and in Asher Bethshean and her towns, and Ibleam and her towns, and the inhabitants of Dor and her towns, and the inhabitants of Endor and her towns, and the inhabitants of Taanach and her towns, and the inhabitants of Megiddo and her towns, @9even@7 three countries.
verse	6	17	12	@@Yet the children of Manasseh could not drive out @9the inhabitants of@7 those cities; but the Canaanites would dwell in that land.
verse	6	17	13	Yet it came to pass, when the children of Israel were waxen strong, that they put the Canaanites to tribute; but did not utterly drive them out.
verse	6	17	14	@@And the children of Joseph spake unto Joshua, saying, Why hast thou given me @9but@7 one lot and one portion to inherit, seeing I @9am@7 a great people, forasmuch as the LORD hath blessed me hitherto?
verse	6	17	15	@@And Joshua answered them, If thou @9be@7 a great people, @9then@7 get thee up to the wood @9country,@7 and cut down for thyself there in the land of the Perizzites and of the giants, if mount Ephraim be too narrow for thee.
verse	6	17	16	@@And the children of Joseph said, The hill is not enough for us: and all the Canaanites that dwell in the land of the valley have chariots of iron, @9both they@7 who @9are@7 of Bethshean and her towns, and @9they@7 who @9are@7 of the valley of Jezreel.
verse	6	17	17	@@And Joshua spake unto the house of Joseph, @9even@7 to Ephraim and to Manasseh, saying, Thou @9art@7 a great people, and hast great power: thou shalt not have one lot @9only: @7
verse	6	17	18	@@But the mountain shall be thine; for it @9is@7 a wood, and thou shalt cut it down: and the outgoings of it shall be thine: for thou shalt drive out the Canaanites, though they have iron chariots, @9and@7 though they @9be@7 strong.
verse	6	18	1	And the whole congregation of the children of Israel assembled together at Shiloh, and set up the tabernacle of the congregation there. And the land was subdued before them.
verse	6	18	2	And there remained among the children of Israel seven tribes, which had not yet received their inheritance.
verse	6	18	3	@@And Joshua said unto the children of Israel, How long @9are@7 ye slack to go to possess the land, which the LORD God of your fathers hath given you?
verse	6	18	4	@@Give out from among you three men for @9each@7 tribe: and I will send them, and they shall rise, and go through the land, and describe it according to the inheritance of them; and they shall come @9again@7 to me.
verse	6	18	5	And they shall divide it into seven parts: Judah shall abide in their coast on the south, and the house of Joseph shall abide in their coasts on the north.
verse	6	18	6	@@Ye shall therefore describe the land @9into@7 seven parts, and bring @9the description@7 hither to me, that I may cast lots for you here before the LORD our God.
verse	6	18	7	But the Levites have no part among you; for the priesthood of the LORD is their inheritance: and Gad, and Reuben, and half the tribe of Manasseh, have received their inheritance beyond Jordan on the east, which Moses the servant of the LORD gave them.
verse	6	18	8	And the men arose, and went away: and Joshua charged them that went to describe the land, saying, Go and walk through the land, and describe it, and come again to me, that I may here cast lots for you before the LORD in Shiloh.
verse	6	18	9	@@And the men went and passed through the land, and described it by cities into seven parts in a book, and came @9again@7 to Joshua to the host at Shiloh.
