verse	6	20	1	The LORD also spake unto Joshua, saying,
verse	6	20	2	Speak to the children of Israel, saying, Appoint out for you cities of refuge, whereof I spake unto you by the hand of Moses:
verse	6	20	3	@@That the slayer that killeth @9any@7 person unawares @9and@7 unwittingly may flee thither: and they shall be your refuge from the avenger of blood.
verse	6	20	4	And when he that doth flee unto one of those cities shall stand at the entering of the gate of the city, and shall declare his cause in the ears of the elders of that city, they shall take him into the city unto them, and give him a place, that he may dwell among them.
verse	6	20	5	And if the avenger of blood pursue after him, then they shall not deliver the slayer up into his hand; because he smote his neighbour unwittingly, and hated him not beforetime.
verse	6	20	6	@@And he shall dwell in that city, until he stand before the congregation for judgment, @9and@7 until the death of the high priest that shall be in those days: then shall the slayer return, and come unto his own city, and unto his own house, unto the city from whence he fled.
verse	6	20	7	@@And they appointed Kedesh in Galilee in mount Naphtali, and Shechem in mount Ephraim, and Kirjatharba, which @9is@7 Hebron, in the mountain of Judah.
verse	6	20	8	And on the other side Jordan by Jericho eastward, they assigned Bezer in the wilderness upon the plain out of the tribe of Reuben, and Ramoth in Gilead out of the tribe of Gad, and Golan in Bashan out of the tribe of Manasseh.
verse	6	20	9	@@These were the cities appointed for all the children of Israel, and for the stranger that sojourneth among them, that whosoever killeth @9any@7 person at unawares might flee thither, and not die by the hand of the avenger of blood, until he stood before the congregation.
verse	6	21	1	Then came near the heads of the fathers of the Levites unto Eleazar the priest, and unto Joshua the son of Nun, and unto the heads of the fathers of the tribes of the children of Israel;
verse	6	21	2	And they spake unto them at Shiloh in the land of Canaan, saying, The LORD commanded by the hand of Moses to give us cities to dwell in, with the suburbs thereof for our cattle.
verse	6	21	3	And the children of Israel gave unto the Levites out of their inheritance, at the commandment of the LORD, these cities and their suburbs.
verse	6	21	4	@@And the lot came out for the families of the Kohathites: and the children of Aaron the priest, @9which were@7 of the Levites, had by lot out of the tribe of Judah, and out of the tribe of Simeon, and out of the tribe of Benjamin, thirteen cities.
verse	6	21	5	@@And the rest of the children of Kohath @9had@7 by lot out of the families of the tribe of Ephraim, and out of the tribe of Dan, and out of the half tribe of Manasseh, ten cities.
