verse	6	22	1	Then Joshua called the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh,
verse	6	22	2	And said unto them, Ye have kept all that Moses the servant of the LORD commanded you, and have obeyed my voice in all that I commanded you:
verse	6	22	3	Ye have not left your brethren these many days unto this day, but have kept the charge of the commandment of the LORD your God.
verse	6	22	4	@@And now the LORD your God hath given rest unto your brethren, as he promised them: therefore now return ye, and get you unto your tents, @9and@7 unto the land of your possession, which Moses the servant of the LORD gave you on the other side Jordan.
verse	6	22	5	But take diligent heed to do the commandment and the law, which Moses the servant of the LORD charged you, to love the LORD your God, and to walk in all his ways, and to keep his commandments, and to cleave unto him, and to serve him with all your heart and with all your soul.
verse	6	22	6	So Joshua blessed them, and sent them away: and they went unto their tents.
verse	6	22	7	@@Now to the @9one@7 half of the tribe of Manasseh Moses had given @9possession@7 in Bashan: but unto the @9other@7 half thereof gave Joshua among their brethren on this side Jordan westward. And when Joshua sent them away also unto their tents, then he blessed them,
verse	6	22	8	And he spake unto them, saying, Return with much riches unto your tents, and with very much cattle, with silver, and with gold, and with brass, and with iron, and with very much raiment: divide the spoil of your enemies with your brethren.
verse	6	22	9	@@And the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half tribe of Manasseh returned, and departed from the children of Israel out of Shiloh, which @9is@7 in the land of Canaan, to go unto the country of Gilead, to the land of their possession, whereof they were possessed, according to the word of the LORD by the hand of Moses.
verse	6	22	10	@@And when they came unto the borders of Jordan, that @9are@7 in the land of Canaan, the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half tribe of Manasseh built there an altar by Jordan, a great altar to see to.
verse	6	22	11	And the children of Israel heard say, Behold, the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half tribe of Manasseh have built an altar over against the land of Canaan, in the borders of Jordan, at the passage of the children of Israel.
verse	6	22	12	@@And when the children of Israel heard @9of it,@7 the whole congregation of the children of Israel gathered themselves together at Shiloh, to go up to war against them.
verse	6	22	13	And the children of Israel sent unto the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the half tribe of Manasseh, into the land of Gilead, Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest,
verse	6	22	14	@@And with him ten princes, of each chief house a prince throughout all the tribes of Israel; and each one @9was@7 an head of the house of their fathers among the thousands of Israel.
verse	6	22	15	And they came unto the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the half tribe of Manasseh, unto the land of Gilead, and they spake with them, saying,
verse	6	22	16	@@Thus saith the whole congregation of the LORD, What trespass @9is@7 this that ye have committed against the God of Israel, to turn away this day from following the LORD, in that ye have builded you an altar, that ye might rebel this day against the LORD?
verse	6	22	17	@@@9Is@7 the iniquity of Peor too little for us, from which we are not cleansed until this day, although there was a plague in the congregation of the LORD,
verse	6	22	18	@@But that ye must turn away this day from following the LORD? and it will be, @9seeing@7 ye rebel to day against the LORD, that to morrow he will be wroth with the whole congregation of Israel.
verse	6	22	19	@@Notwithstanding, if the land of your possession @9be@7 unclean, @9then@7 pass ye over unto the land of the possession of the LORD, wherein the LORD'S tabernacle dwelleth, and take possession among us: but rebel not against the LORD, nor rebel against us, in building you an altar beside the altar of the LORD our God.
verse	6	22	20	Did not Achan the son of Zerah commit a trespass in the accursed thing, and wrath fell on all the congregation of Israel? and that man perished not alone in his iniquity.
verse	6	22	21	Then the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half tribe of Manasseh answered, and said unto the heads of the thousands of Israel,
verse	6	22	22	@@The LORD God of gods, the LORD God of gods, he knoweth, and Israel he shall know; if @9it be@7 in rebellion, or if in transgression against the LORD, (save us not this day,)
verse	6	22	23	That we have built us an altar to turn from following the LORD, or if to offer thereon burnt offering or meat offering, or if to offer peace offerings thereon, let the LORD himself require it;
verse	6	22	24	@@And if we have not @9rather@7 done it for fear of @9this@7 thing, saying, In time to come your children might speak unto our children, saying, What have ye to do with the LORD God of Israel?
verse	6	22	25	For the LORD hath made Jordan a border between us and you, ye children of Reuben and children of Gad; ye have no part in the LORD: so shall your children make our children cease from fearing the LORD.
verse	6	22	26	Therefore we said, Let us now prepare to build us an altar, not for burnt offering, nor for sacrifice:
verse	6	22	27	@@But @9that@7 it @9may be@7 a witness between us, and you, and our generations after us, that we might do the service of the LORD before him with our burnt offerings, and with our sacrifices, and with our peace offerings; that your children may not say to our children in time to come, Ye have no part in the LORD.
verse	6	22	28	@@Therefore said we, that it shall be, when they should so say to us or to our generations in time to come, that we may say @9again,@7 Behold the pattern of the altar of the LORD, which our fathers made, not for burnt offerings, nor for sacrifices; but it @9is@7 a witness between us and you.
verse	6	22	29	@@God forbid that we should rebel against the LORD, and turn this day from following the LORD, to build an altar for burnt offerings, for meat offerings, or for sacrifices, beside the altar of the LORD our God that @9is@7 before his tabernacle.
verse	6	22	30	@@And when Phinehas the priest, and the princes of the congregation and heads of the thousands of Israel which @9were@7 with him, heard the words that the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the children of Manasseh spake, it pleased them.
verse	6	22	31	@@And Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest said unto the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the children of Manasseh, This day we perceive that the LORD @9is@7 among us, because ye have not committed this trespass against the LORD: now ye have delivered the children of Israel out of the hand of the LORD.
verse	6	22	32	And Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest, and the princes, returned from the children of Reuben, and from the children of Gad, out of the land of Gilead, unto the land of Canaan, to the children of Israel, and brought them word again.
verse	6	22	33	And the thing pleased the children of Israel; and the children of Israel blessed God, and did not intend to go up against them in battle, to destroy the land wherein the children of Reuben and Gad dwelt.
verse	6	22	34	@@And the children of Reuben and the children of Gad called the altar @9Ed:@7 for it @9shall be@7 a witness between us that the LORD @9is@7 God.
verse	6	23	1	@@And it came to pass a long time after that the LORD had given rest unto Israel from all their enemies round about, that Joshua waxed old @9and@7 stricken in age.
verse	6	23	2	@@And Joshua called for all Israel, @9and@7 for their elders, and for their heads, and for their judges, and for their officers, and said unto them, I am old @9and@7 stricken in age:
verse	6	23	3	@@And ye have seen all that the LORD your God hath done unto all these nations because of you; for the LORD your God @9is@7 he that hath fought for you.
verse	6	23	4	Behold, I have divided unto you by lot these nations that remain, to be an inheritance for your tribes, from Jordan, with all the nations that I have cut off, even unto the great sea westward.
verse	6	23	5	And the LORD your God, he shall expel them from before you, and drive them from out of your sight; and ye shall possess their land, as the LORD your God hath promised unto you.
verse	6	23	6	@@Be ye therefore very courageous to keep and to do all that is written in the book of the law of Moses, that ye turn not aside therefrom @9to@7 the right hand or @9to@7 the left;
verse	6	23	7	@@That ye come not among these nations, these that remain among you; neither make mention of the name of their gods, nor cause to swear @9by them,@7 neither serve them, nor bow yourselves unto them:
verse	6	23	8	But cleave unto the LORD your God, as ye have done unto this day.
verse	6	23	9	@@For the LORD hath driven out from before you great nations and strong: but @9as for@7 you, no man hath been able to stand before you unto this day.
verse	6	23	10	@@One man of you shall chase a thousand: for the LORD your God, he @9it is@7 that fighteth for you, as he hath promised you.
verse	6	23	11	Take good heed therefore unto yourselves, that ye love the LORD your God.
verse	6	23	12	@@Else if ye do in any wise go back, and cleave unto the remnant of these nations, @9even@7 these that remain among you, and shall make marriages with them, and go in unto them, and they to you:
verse	6	23	13	@@Know for a certainty that the LORD your God will no more drive out @9any of@7 these nations from before you; but they shall be snares and traps unto you, and scourges in your sides, and thorns in your eyes, until ye perish from off this good land which the LORD your God hath given you.
verse	6	23	14	@@And, behold, this day I @9am@7 going the way of all the earth: and ye know in all your hearts and in all your souls, that not one thing hath failed of all the good things which the LORD your God spake concerning you; all are come to pass unto you, @9and@7 not one thing hath failed thereof.
verse	6	23	15	@@Therefore it shall come to pass, @9that@7 as all good things are come upon you, which the LORD your God promised you; so shall the LORD bring upon you all evil things, until he have destroyed you from off this good land which the LORD your God hath given you.
verse	6	23	16	When ye have transgressed the covenant of the LORD your God, which he commanded you, and have gone and served other gods, and bowed yourselves to them; then shall the anger of the LORD be kindled against you, and ye shall perish quickly from off the good land which he hath given unto you.
verse	6	24	1	And Joshua gathered all the tribes of Israel to Shechem, and called for the elders of Israel, and for their heads, and for their judges, and for their officers; and they presented themselves before God.
verse	6	24	2	@@And Joshua said unto all the people, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Your fathers dwelt on the other side of the flood in old time, @9even@7 Terah, the father of Abraham, and the father of Nachor: and they served other gods.
verse	6	24	3	And I took your father Abraham from the other side of the flood, and led him throughout all the land of Canaan, and multiplied his seed, and gave him Isaac.
verse	6	24	4	And I gave unto Isaac Jacob and Esau: and I gave unto Esau mount Seir, to possess it; but Jacob and his children went down into Egypt.
verse	6	24	5	I sent Moses also and Aaron, and I plagued Egypt, according to that which I did among them: and afterward I brought you out.
verse	6	24	6	And I brought your fathers out of Egypt: and ye came unto the sea; and the Egyptians pursued after your fathers with chariots and horsemen unto the Red sea.
verse	6	24	7	And when they cried unto the LORD, he put darkness between you and the Egyptians, and brought the sea upon them, and covered them; and your eyes have seen what I have done in Egypt: and ye dwelt in the wilderness a long season.
verse	6	24	8	And I brought you into the land of the Amorites, which dwelt on the other side Jordan; and they fought with you: and I gave them into your hand, that ye might possess their land; and I destroyed them from before you.
verse	6	24	9	Then Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab, arose and warred against Israel, and sent and called Balaam the son of Beor to curse you:
verse	6	24	10	But I would not hearken unto Balaam; therefore he blessed you still: so I delivered you out of his hand.
verse	6	24	11	And ye went over Jordan, and came unto Jericho: and the men of Jericho fought against you, the Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Girgashites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites; and I delivered them into your hand.
verse	6	24	12	@@And I sent the hornet before you, which drave them out from before you, @9even@7 the two kings of the Amorites; @9but@7 not with thy sword, nor with thy bow.
verse	6	24	13	And I have given you a land for which ye did not labour, and cities which ye built not, and ye dwell in them; of the vineyards and oliveyards which ye planted not do ye eat.
verse	6	24	14	Now therefore fear the LORD, and serve him in sincerity and in truth: and put away the gods which your fathers served on the other side of the flood, and in Egypt; and serve ye the LORD.
verse	6	24	15	@@And if it seem evil unto you to serve the LORD, choose you this day whom ye will serve; whether the gods which your fathers served that @9were@7 on the other side of the flood, or the gods of the Amorites, in whose land ye dwell: but as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD.
verse	6	24	16	And the people answered and said, God forbid that we should forsake the LORD, to serve other gods;
verse	6	24	17	@@For the LORD our God, he @9it is@7 that brought us up and our fathers out of the land of Egypt, from the house of bondage, and which did those great signs in our sight, and preserved us in all the way wherein we went, and among all the people through whom we passed:
verse	6	24	18	@@And the LORD drave out from before us all the people, even the Amorites which dwelt in the land: @9therefore@7 will we also serve the LORD; for he @9is@7 our God.
verse	6	24	19	@@And Joshua said unto the people, Ye cannot serve the LORD: for he @9is@7 an holy God; he @9is@7 a jealous God; he will not forgive your transgressions nor your sins.
verse	6	24	20	If ye forsake the LORD, and serve strange gods, then he will turn and do you hurt, and consume you, after that he hath done you good.
verse	6	24	21	And the people said unto Joshua, Nay; but we will serve the LORD.
verse	6	24	22	@@And Joshua said unto the people, Ye @9are@7 witnesses against yourselves that ye have chosen you the LORD, to serve him. And they said, @9We are@7 witnesses.
verse	6	24	23	@@Now therefore put away, @9said he,@7 the strange gods which @9are@7 among you, and incline your heart unto the LORD God of Israel.
verse	6	24	24	And the people said unto Joshua, The LORD our God will we serve, and his voice will we obey.
verse	6	24	25	So Joshua made a covenant with the people that day, and set them a statute and an ordinance in Shechem.
verse	6	24	26	@@And Joshua wrote these words in the book of the law of God, and took a great stone, and set it up there under an oak, that @9was@7 by the sanctuary of the LORD.
verse	6	24	27	And Joshua said unto all the people, Behold, this stone shall be a witness unto us; for it hath heard all the words of the LORD which he spake unto us: it shall be therefore a witness unto you, lest ye deny your God.
verse	6	24	28	So Joshua let the people depart, every man unto his inheritance.
verse	6	24	29	@@And it came to pass after these things, that Joshua the son of Nun, the servant of the LORD, died, @9being@7 an hundred and ten years old.
verse	6	24	30	@@And they buried him in the border of his inheritance in Timnathserah, which @9is@7 in mount Ephraim, on the north side of the hill of Gaash.
verse	6	24	31	And Israel served the LORD all the days of Joshua, and all the days of the elders that overlived Joshua, and which had known all the works of the LORD, that he had done for Israel.
verse	6	24	32	And the bones of Joseph, which the children of Israel brought up out of Egypt, buried they in Shechem, in a parcel of ground which Jacob bought of the sons of Hamor the father of Shechem for an hundred pieces of silver: and it became the inheritance of the children of Joseph.
verse	6	24	33	@@And Eleazar the son of Aaron died; and they buried him in a hill @9that pertained to@7 Phinehas his son, which was given him in mount Ephraim.
verse	7	1	1	Now after the death of Joshua it came to pass, that the children of Israel asked the LORD, saying, Who shall go up for us against the Canaanites first, to fight against them?
verse	7	1	2	And the LORD said, Judah shall go up: behold, I have delivered the land into his hand.
verse	7	1	3	And Judah said unto Simeon his brother, Come up with me into my lot, that we may fight against the Canaanites; and I likewise will go with thee into thy lot. So Simeon went with him.
verse	7	1	4	And Judah went up; and the LORD delivered the Canaanites and the Perizzites into their hand: and they slew of them in Bezek ten thousand men.
verse	7	1	5	And they found Adonibezek in Bezek: and they fought against him, and they slew the Canaanites and the Perizzites.
verse	7	1	6	But Adonibezek fled; and they pursued after him, and caught him, and cut off his thumbs and his great toes.
verse	7	1	7	@@And Adonibezek said, Threescore and ten kings, having their thumbs and their great toes cut off, gathered @9their meat@7 under my table: as I have done, so God hath requited me. And they brought him to Jerusalem, and there he died.
verse	7	1	8	Now the children of Judah had fought against Jerusalem, and had taken it, and smitten it with the edge of the sword, and set the city on fire.
verse	7	1	9	And afterward the children of Judah went down to fight against the Canaanites, that dwelt in the mountain, and in the south, and in the valley.
verse	7	1	10	@@And Judah went against the Canaanites that dwelt in Hebron: (now the name of Hebron before @9was@7 Kirjatharba:) and they slew Sheshai, and Ahiman, and Talmai.
verse	7	1	11	@@And from thence he went against the inhabitants of Debir: and the name of Debir before @9was@7 Kirjathsepher:
verse	7	1	12	And Caleb said, He that smiteth Kirjathsepher, and taketh it, to him will I give Achsah my daughter to wife.
verse	7	1	13	And Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb's younger brother, took it: and he gave him Achsah his daughter to wife.
verse	7	1	14	@@And it came to pass, when she came @9to him,@7 that she moved him to ask of her father a field: and she lighted from off @9her@7 ass; and Caleb said unto her, What wilt thou?
verse	7	1	15	And she said unto him, Give me a blessing: for thou hast given me a south land; give me also springs of water. And Caleb gave her the upper springs and the nether springs.
verse	7	1	16	@@And the children of the Kenite, Moses' father in law, went up out of the city of palm trees with the children of Judah into the wilderness of Judah, which @9lieth@7 in the south of Arad; and they went and dwelt among the people.
verse	7	1	17	And Judah went with Simeon his brother, and they slew the Canaanites that inhabited Zephath, and utterly destroyed it. And the name of the city was called Hormah.
verse	7	1	18	Also Judah took Gaza with the coast thereof, and Askelon with the coast thereof, and Ekron with the coast thereof.
verse	7	1	19	@@And the LORD was with Judah; and he drave out the inhabitants of the mountain; but could not drive out @9the inhabitants of@7 the valley, because they had chariots of iron.
verse	7	1	20	And they gave Hebron unto Caleb, as Moses said: and he expelled thence the three sons of Anak.
verse	7	1	21	And the children of Benjamin did not drive out the Jebusites that inhabited Jerusalem; but the Jebusites dwell with the children of Benjamin in Jerusalem unto this day.
verse	7	1	22	@@And the house of Joseph, they also went up against Bethel: and the LORD @9was@7 with them.
verse	7	1	23	@@And the house of Joseph sent to descry Bethel. (Now the name of the city before @9was@7 Luz.)
verse	7	1	24	And the spies saw a man come forth out of the city, and they said unto him, Shew us, we pray thee, the entrance into the city, and we will shew thee mercy.
verse	7	1	25	And when he shewed them the entrance into the city, they smote the city with the edge of the sword; but they let go the man and all his family.
verse	7	1	26	@@And the man went into the land of the Hittites, and built a city, and called the name thereof Luz: which @9is@7 the name thereof unto this day.
verse	7	1	27	@@Neither did Manasseh drive out @9the inhabitants of@7 Bethshean and her towns, nor Taanach and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Dor and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Ibleam and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Megiddo and her towns: but the Canaanites would dwell in that land.
verse	7	1	28	And it came to pass, when Israel was strong, that they put the Canaanites to tribute, and did not utterly drive them out.
verse	7	1	29	Neither did Ephraim drive out the Canaanites that dwelt in Gezer; but the Canaanites dwelt in Gezer among them.
verse	7	1	30	Neither did Zebulun drive out the inhabitants of Kitron, nor the inhabitants of Nahalol; but the Canaanites dwelt among them, and became tributaries.
verse	7	1	31	Neither did Asher drive out the inhabitants of Accho, nor the inhabitants of Zidon, nor of Ahlab, nor of Achzib, nor of Helbah, nor of Aphik, nor of Rehob:
verse	7	1	32	But the Asherites dwelt among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land: for they did not drive them out.
verse	7	1	33	Neither did Naphtali drive out the inhabitants of Bethshemesh, nor the inhabitants of Bethanath; but he dwelt among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land: nevertheless the inhabitants of Bethshemesh and of Bethanath became tributaries unto them.
verse	7	1	34	And the Amorites forced the children of Dan into the mountain: for they would not suffer them to come down to the valley:
verse	7	1	35	But the Amorites would dwell in mount Heres in Aijalon, and in Shaalbim: yet the hand of the house of Joseph prevailed, so that they became tributaries.
verse	7	1	36	@@And the coast of the Amorites @9was@7 from the going up to Akrabbim, from the rock, and upward.
verse	7	2	1	And an angel of the LORD came up from Gilgal to Bochim, and said, I made you to go up out of Egypt, and have brought you unto the land which I sware unto your fathers; and I said, I will never break my covenant with you.
verse	7	2	2	And ye shall make no league with the inhabitants of this land; ye shall throw down their altars: but ye have not obeyed my voice: why have ye done this?
verse	7	2	3	@@Wherefore I also said, I will not drive them out from before you; but they shall be @9as thorns@7 in your sides, and their gods shall be a snare unto you.
verse	7	2	4	And it came to pass, when the angel of the LORD spake these words unto all the children of Israel, that the people lifted up their voice, and wept.
verse	7	2	5	And they called the name of that place Bochim: and they sacrificed there unto the LORD.
verse	7	2	6	And when Joshua had let the people go, the children of Israel went every man unto his inheritance to possess the land.
verse	7	2	7	And the people served the LORD all the days of Joshua, and all the days of the elders that outlived Joshua, who had seen all the great works of the LORD, that he did for Israel.
verse	7	2	8	@@And Joshua the son of Nun, the servant of the LORD, died, @9being@7 an hundred and ten years old.
verse	7	2	9	And they buried him in the border of his inheritance in Timnathheres, in the mount of Ephraim, on the north side of the hill Gaash.
verse	7	2	10	And also all that generation were gathered unto their fathers: and there arose another generation after them, which knew not the LORD, nor yet the works which he had done for Israel.
verse	7	2	11	And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD, and served Baalim:
verse	7	2	12	@@And they forsook the LORD God of their fathers, which brought them out of the land of Egypt, and followed other gods, of the gods of the people that @9were@7 round about them, and bowed themselves unto them, and provoked the LORD to anger.
verse	7	2	13	And they forsook the LORD, and served Baal and Ashtaroth.
verse	7	2	14	And the anger of the LORD was hot against Israel, and he delivered them into the hands of spoilers that spoiled them, and he sold them into the hands of their enemies round about, so that they could not any longer stand before their enemies.
verse	7	2	15	Whithersoever they went out, the hand of the LORD was against them for evil, as the LORD had said, and as the LORD had sworn unto them: and they were greatly distressed.
verse	7	2	16	Nevertheless the LORD raised up judges, which delivered them out of the hand of those that spoiled them.
verse	7	2	17	@@And yet they would not hearken unto their judges, but they went a whoring after other gods, and bowed themselves unto them: they turned quickly out of the way which their fathers walked in, obeying the commandments of the LORD; @9but@7 they did not so.
verse	7	2	18	And when the LORD raised them up judges, then the LORD was with the judge, and delivered them out of the hand of their enemies all the days of the judge: for it repented the LORD because of their groanings by reason of them that oppressed them and vexed them.
verse	7	2	19	@@And it came to pass, when the judge was dead, @9that@7 they returned, and corrupted @9themselves@7 more than their fathers, in following other gods to serve them, and to bow down unto them; they ceased not from their own doings, nor from their stubborn way.
verse	7	2	20	And the anger of the LORD was hot against Israel; and he said, Because that this people hath transgressed my covenant which I commanded their fathers, and have not hearkened unto my voice;
verse	7	2	21	I also will not henceforth drive out any from before them of the nations which Joshua left when he died:
verse	7	2	22	@@That through them I may prove Israel, whether they will keep the way of the LORD to walk therein, as their fathers did keep @9it,@7 or not.
verse	7	2	23	Therefore the LORD left those nations, without driving them out hastily; neither delivered he them into the hand of Joshua.
verse	7	3	1	@@Now these @9are@7 the nations which the LORD left, to prove Israel by them, @9even@7 as many @9of Israel@7 as had not known all the wars of Canaan;
verse	7	3	2	Only that the generations of the children of Israel might know, to teach them war, at the least such as before knew nothing thereof;
verse	7	3	3	@@@9Namely,@7 five lords of the Philistines, and all the Canaanites, and the Sidonians, and the Hivites that dwelt in mount Lebanon, from mount Baalhermon unto the entering in of Hamath.
verse	7	3	4	And they were to prove Israel by them, to know whether they would hearken unto the commandments of the LORD, which he commanded their fathers by the hand of Moses.
verse	7	3	5	And the children of Israel dwelt among the Canaanites, Hittites, and Amorites, and Perizzites, and Hivites, and Jebusites:
verse	7	3	6	And they took their daughters to be their wives, and gave their daughters to their sons, and served their gods.
verse	7	3	7	And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD, and forgat the LORD their God, and served Baalim and the groves.
verse	7	3	8	Therefore the anger of the LORD was hot against Israel, and he sold them into the hand of Chushanrishathaim king of Mesopotamia: and the children of Israel served Chushanrishathaim eight years.
verse	7	3	9	@@And when the children of Israel cried unto the LORD, the LORD raised up a deliverer to the children of Israel, who delivered them, @9even@7 Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb's younger brother.
verse	7	3	10	And the Spirit of the LORD came upon him, and he judged Israel, and went out to war: and the LORD delivered Chushanrishathaim king of Mesopotamia into his hand; and his hand prevailed against Chushanrishathaim.
verse	7	3	11	And the land had rest forty years. And Othniel the son of Kenaz died.
verse	7	3	12	And the children of Israel did evil again in the sight of the LORD: and the LORD strengthened Eglon the king of Moab against Israel, because they had done evil in the sight of the LORD.
verse	7	3	13	And he gathered unto him the children of Ammon and Amalek, and went and smote Israel, and possessed the city of palm trees.
verse	7	3	14	So the children of Israel served Eglon the king of Moab eighteen years.
verse	7	3	15	But when the children of Israel cried unto the LORD, the LORD raised them up a deliverer, Ehud the son of Gera, a Benjamite, a man lefthanded: and by him the children of Israel sent a present unto Eglon the king of Moab.
verse	7	3	16	But Ehud made him a dagger which had two edges, of a cubit length; and he did gird it under his raiment upon his right thigh.
verse	7	3	17	@@And he brought the present unto Eglon king of Moab: and Eglon @9was@7 a very fat man.
verse	7	3	18	And when he had made an end to offer the present, he sent away the people that bare the present.
verse	7	3	19	@@But he himself turned again from the quarries that @9were@7 by Gilgal, and said, I have a secret errand unto thee, O king: who said, Keep silence. And all that stood by him went out from him.
verse	7	3	20	@@And Ehud came unto him; and he was sitting in a summer parlour, which he had for himself alone. And Ehud said, I have a message from God unto thee. And he arose out of @9his@7 seat.
verse	7	3	21	And Ehud put forth his left hand, and took the dagger from his right thigh, and thrust it into his belly:
verse	7	3	22	And the haft also went in after the blade; and the fat closed upon the blade, so that he could not draw the dagger out of his belly; and the dirt came out.
verse	7	3	23	Then Ehud went forth through the porch, and shut the doors of the parlour upon him, and locked them.
verse	7	3	24	@@When he was gone out, his servants came; and when they saw that, behold, the doors of the parlour @9were@7 locked, they said, Surely he covereth his feet in his summer chamber.
verse	7	3	25	@@And they tarried till they were ashamed: and, behold, he opened not the doors of the parlour; therefore they took a key, and opened @9them:@7 and, behold, their lord @9was@7 fallen down dead on the earth.
verse	7	3	26	And Ehud escaped while they tarried, and passed beyond the quarries, and escaped unto Seirath.
verse	7	3	27	And it came to pass, when he was come, that he blew a trumpet in the mountain of Ephraim, and the children of Israel went down with him from the mount, and he before them.
verse	7	3	28	And he said unto them, Follow after me: for the LORD hath delivered your enemies the Moabites into your hand. And they went down after him, and took the fords of Jordan toward Moab, and suffered not a man to pass over.
verse	7	3	29	And they slew of Moab at that time about ten thousand men, all lusty, and all men of valour; and there escaped not a man.
verse	7	3	30	So Moab was subdued that day under the hand of Israel. And the land had rest fourscore years.
verse	7	3	31	And after him was Shamgar the son of Anath, which slew of the Philistines six hundred men with an ox goad: and he also delivered Israel.
verse	7	4	1	And the children of Israel again did evil in the sight of the LORD, when Ehud was dead.
verse	7	4	2	@@And the LORD sold them into the hand of Jabin king of Canaan, that reigned in Hazor; the captain of whose host @9was@7 Sisera, which dwelt in Harosheth of the Gentiles.
verse	7	4	3	And the children of Israel cried unto the LORD: for he had nine hundred chariots of iron; and twenty years he mightily oppressed the children of Israel.
verse	7	4	4	And Deborah, a prophetess, the wife of Lapidoth, she judged Israel at that time.
verse	7	4	5	And she dwelt under the palm tree of Deborah between Ramah and Bethel in mount Ephraim: and the children of Israel came up to her for judgment.
verse	7	4	6	@@And she sent and called Barak the son of Abinoam out of Kedeshnaphtali, and said unto him, Hath not the LORD God of Israel commanded, @9saying,@7 Go and draw toward mount Tabor, and take with thee ten thousand men of the children of Naphtali and of the children of Zebulun?
verse	7	4	7	And I will draw unto thee to the river Kishon Sisera, the captain of Jabin's army, with his chariots and his multitude; and I will deliver him into thine hand.
verse	7	4	8	@@And Barak said unto her, If thou wilt go with me, then I will go: but if thou wilt not go with me, @9then@7 I will not go.
verse	7	4	9	And she said, I will surely go with thee: notwithstanding the journey that thou takest shall not be for thine honour; for the LORD shall sell Sisera into the hand of a woman. And Deborah arose, and went with Barak to Kedesh.
verse	7	4	10	And Barak called Zebulun and Naphtali to Kedesh; and he went up with ten thousand men at his feet: and Deborah went up with him.
verse	7	4	11	@@Now Heber the Kenite, @9which was@7 of the children of Hobab the father in law of Moses, had severed himself from the Kenites, and pitched his tent unto the plain of Zaanaim, which @9is@7 by Kedesh.
verse	7	4	12	And they shewed Sisera that Barak the son of Abinoam was gone up to mount Tabor.
verse	7	4	13	@@And Sisera gathered together all his chariots, @9even@7 nine hundred chariots of iron, and all the people that @9were@7 with him, from Harosheth of the Gentiles unto the river of Kishon.
verse	7	4	14	@@And Deborah said unto Barak, Up; for this @9is@7 the day in which the LORD hath delivered Sisera into thine hand: is not the LORD gone out before thee? So Barak went down from mount Tabor, and ten thousand men after him.
verse	7	4	15	@@And the LORD discomfited Sisera, and all @9his@7 chariots, and all @9his@7 host, with the edge of the sword before Barak; so that Sisera lighted down off @9his@7 chariot, and fled away on his feet.
verse	7	4	16	@@But Barak pursued after the chariots, and after the host, unto Harosheth of the Gentiles: and all the host of Sisera fell upon the edge of the sword; @9and@7 there was not a man left.
verse	7	4	17	@@Howbeit Sisera fled away on his feet to the tent of Jael the wife of Heber the Kenite: for @9there was@7 peace between Jabin the king of Hazor and the house of Heber the Kenite.
verse	7	4	18	And Jael went out to meet Sisera, and said unto him, Turn in, my lord, turn in to me; fear not. And when he had turned in unto her into the tent, she covered him with a mantle.
verse	7	4	19	And he said unto her, Give me, I pray thee, a little water to drink; for I am thirsty. And she opened a bottle of milk, and gave him drink, and covered him.
verse	7	4	20	Again he said unto her, Stand in the door of the tent, and it shall be, when any man doth come and enquire of thee, and say, Is there any man here? that thou shalt say, No.
verse	7	4	21	Then Jael Heber's wife took a nail of the tent, and took an hammer in her hand, and went softly unto him, and smote the nail into his temples, and fastened it into the ground: for he was fast asleep and weary. So he died.
verse	7	4	22	@@And, behold, as Barak pursued Sisera, Jael came out to meet him, and said unto him, Come, and I will shew thee the man whom thou seekest. And when he came into her @9tent,@7 behold, Sisera lay dead, and the nail @9was@7 in his temples.
verse	7	4	23	So God subdued on that day Jabin the king of Canaan before the children of Israel.
verse	7	4	24	And the hand of the children of Israel prospered, and prevailed against Jabin the king of Canaan, until they had destroyed Jabin king of Canaan.
verse	7	5	1	Then sang Deborah and Barak the son of Abinoam on that day, saying,
verse	7	5	2	Praise ye the LORD for the avenging of Israel, when the people willingly offered themselves.
verse	7	5	3	@@Hear, O ye kings; give ear, O ye princes; I, @9even@7 I, will sing unto the LORD; I will sing @9praise@7 to the LORD God of Israel.
verse	7	5	4	LORD, when thou wentest out of Seir, when thou marchedst out of the field of Edom, the earth trembled, and the heavens dropped, the clouds also dropped water.
verse	7	5	5	@@The mountains melted from before the LORD, @9even@7 that Sinai from before the LORD God of Israel.
verse	7	5	6	In the days of Shamgar the son of Anath, in the days of Jael, the highways were unoccupied, and the travellers walked through byways.
verse	7	5	7	@@@9The inhabitants of@7 the villages ceased, they ceased in Israel, until that I Deborah arose, that I arose a mother in Israel.
verse	7	5	8	@@They chose new gods; then @9was@7 war in the gates: was there a shield or spear seen among forty thousand in Israel?
verse	7	5	9	@@My heart @9is@7 toward the governors of Israel, that offered themselves willingly among the people. Bless ye the LORD.
verse	7	5	10	Speak, ye that ride on white asses, ye that sit in judgment, and walk by the way.
verse	7	5	11	@@@9They that are delivered@7 from the noise of archers in the places of drawing water, there shall they rehearse the righteous acts of the LORD, @9even@7 the righteous acts @9toward the inhabitants@7 of his villages in Israel: then shall the people of the LORD go down to the gates.
verse	7	5	12	Awake, awake, Deborah: awake, awake, utter a song: arise, Barak, and lead thy captivity captive, thou son of Abinoam.
verse	7	5	13	Then he made him that remaineth have dominion over the nobles among the people: the LORD made me have dominion over the mighty.
verse	7	5	14	@@Out of Ephraim @9was there@7 a root of them against Amalek; after thee, Benjamin, among thy people; out of Machir came down governors, and out of Zebulun they that handle the pen of the writer.
verse	7	5	15	@@And the princes of Issachar @9were@7 with Deborah; even Issachar, and also Barak: he was sent on foot into the valley. For the divisions of Reuben @9there were@7 great thoughts of heart.
verse	7	5	16	@@Why abodest thou among the sheepfolds, to hear the bleatings of the flocks? For the divisions of Reuben @9there were@7 great searchings of heart.
verse	7	5	17	Gilead abode beyond Jordan: and why did Dan remain in ships? Asher continued on the sea shore, and abode in his breaches.
verse	7	5	18	@@Zebulun and Naphtali @9were@7 a people @9that@7 jeoparded their lives unto the death in the high places of the field.
verse	7	5	19	@@The kings came @9and@7 fought, then fought the kings of Canaan in Taanach by the waters of Megiddo; they took no gain of money.
verse	7	5	20	They fought from heaven; the stars in their courses fought against Sisera.
verse	7	5	21	The river of Kishon swept them away, that ancient river, the river Kishon. O my soul, thou hast trodden down strength.
verse	7	5	22	Then were the horsehoofs broken by the means of the pransings, the pransings of their mighty ones.
verse	7	5	23	Curse ye Meroz, said the angel of the LORD, curse ye bitterly the inhabitants thereof; because they came not to the help of the LORD, to the help of the LORD against the mighty.
verse	7	5	24	Blessed above women shall Jael the wife of Heber the Kenite be, blessed shall she be above women in the tent.
verse	7	5	25	@@He asked water, @9and@7 she gave @9him@7 milk; she brought forth butter in a lordly dish.
verse	7	5	26	She put her hand to the nail, and her right hand to the workmen's hammer; and with the hammer she smote Sisera, she smote off his head, when she had pierced and stricken through his temples.
verse	7	5	27	At her feet he bowed, he fell, he lay down: at her feet he bowed, he fell: where he bowed, there he fell down dead.
verse	7	5	28	@@The mother of Sisera looked out at a window, and cried through the lattice, Why is his chariot @9so@7 long in coming? why tarry the wheels of his chariots?
verse	7	5	29	Her wise ladies answered her, yea, she returned answer to herself,
verse	7	5	30	@@Have they not sped? have they @9not@7 divided the prey; to every man a damsel @9or@7 two; to Sisera a prey of divers colours, a prey of divers colours of needlework, of divers colours of needlework on both sides, @9meet@7 for the necks of @9them that take@7 the spoil?
verse	7	5	31	@@So let all thine enemies perish, O LORD: but @9let@7 them that love him @9be@7 as the sun when he goeth forth in his might. And the land had rest forty years.
verse	7	6	1	And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD: and the LORD delivered them into the hand of Midian seven years.
verse	7	6	2	@@And the hand of Midian prevailed against Israel: @9and@7 because of the Midianites the children of Israel made them the dens which @9are@7 in the mountains, and caves, and strong holds.
verse	7	6	3	@@And @9so@7 it was, when Israel had sown, that the Midianites came up, and the Amalekites, and the children of the east, even they came up against them;
verse	7	6	4	And they encamped against them, and destroyed the increase of the earth, till thou come unto Gaza, and left no sustenance for Israel, neither sheep, nor ox, nor ass.
verse	7	6	5	@@For they came up with their cattle and their tents, and they came as grasshoppers for multitude; @9for@7 both they and their camels were without number: and they entered into the land to destroy it.
verse	7	6	6	And Israel was greatly impoverished because of the Midianites; and the children of Israel cried unto the LORD.
verse	7	6	7	And it came to pass, when the children of Israel cried unto the LORD because of the Midianites,
verse	7	6	8	That the LORD sent a prophet unto the children of Israel, which said unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, I brought you up from Egypt, and brought you forth out of the house of bondage;
verse	7	6	9	And I delivered you out of the hand of the Egyptians, and out of the hand of all that oppressed you, and drave them out from before you, and gave you their land;
verse	7	6	10	@@And I said unto you, I @9am@7 the LORD your God; fear not the gods of the Amorites, in whose land ye dwell: but ye have not obeyed my voice.
verse	7	6	11	@@And there came an angel of the LORD, and sat under an oak which @9was@7 in Ophrah, that @9pertained@7 unto Joash the Abiezrite: and his son Gideon threshed wheat by the winepress, to hide @9it@7 from the Midianites.
verse	7	6	12	@@And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him, and said unto him, The LORD @9is@7 with thee, thou mighty man of valour.
verse	7	6	13	@@And Gideon said unto him, Oh my Lord, if the LORD be with us, why then is all this befallen us? and where @9be@7 all his miracles which our fathers told us of, saying, Did not the LORD bring us up from Egypt? but now the LORD hath forsaken us, and delivered us into the hands of the Midianites.
verse	7	6	14	And the LORD looked upon him, and said, Go in this thy might, and thou shalt save Israel from the hand of the Midianites: have not I sent thee?
verse	7	6	15	@@And he said unto him, Oh my Lord, wherewith shall I save Israel? behold, my family is poor in Manasseh, and I @9am@7 the least in my father's house.
verse	7	6	16	And the LORD said unto him, Surely I will be with thee, and thou shalt smite the Midianites as one man.
verse	7	6	17	And he said unto him, If now I have found grace in thy sight, then shew me a sign that thou talkest with me.
verse	7	6	18	@@Depart not hence, I pray thee, until I come unto thee, and bring forth my present, and set @9it@7 before thee. And he said, I will tarry until thou come again.
verse	7	6	19	@@And Gideon went in, and made ready a kid, and unleavened cakes of an ephah of flour: the flesh he put in a basket, and he put the broth in a pot, and brought @9it@7 out unto him under the oak, and presented @9it. @7
verse	7	6	20	@@And the angel of God said unto him, Take the flesh and the unleavened cakes, and lay @9them@7 upon this rock, and pour out the broth. And he did so.
verse	7	6	21	@@Then the angel of the LORD put forth the end of the staff that @9was@7 in his hand, and touched the flesh and the unleavened cakes; and there rose up fire out of the rock, and consumed the flesh and the unleavened cakes. Then the angel of the LORD departed out of his sight.
verse	7	6	22	@@And when Gideon perceived that he @9was@7 an angel of the LORD, Gideon said, Alas, O Lord GOD! for because I have seen an angel of the LORD face to face.
verse	7	6	23	@@And the LORD said unto him, Peace @9be@7 unto thee; fear not: thou shalt not die.
verse	7	6	24	Then Gideon built an altar there unto the LORD, and called it Jehovahshalom: unto this day it is yet in Ophrah of the Abiezrites.
verse	7	6	25	@@And it came to pass the same night, that the LORD said unto him, Take thy father's young bullock, even the second bullock of seven years old, and throw down the altar of Baal that thy father hath, and cut down the grove that @9is@7 by it:
verse	7	6	26	And build an altar unto the LORD thy God upon the top of this rock, in the ordered place, and take the second bullock, and offer a burnt sacrifice with the wood of the grove which thou shalt cut down.
verse	7	6	27	@@Then Gideon took ten men of his servants, and did as the LORD had said unto him: and @9so@7 it was, because he feared his father's household, and the men of the city, that he could not do @9it@7 by day, that he did @9it@7 by night.
verse	7	6	28	@@And when the men of the city arose early in the morning, behold, the altar of Baal was cast down, and the grove was cut down that @9was@7 by it, and the second bullock was offered upon the altar @9that was@7 built.
verse	7	6	29	And they said one to another, Who hath done this thing? And when they enquired and asked, they said, Gideon the son of Joash hath done this thing.
verse	7	6	30	@@Then the men of the city said unto Joash, Bring out thy son, that he may die: because he hath cast down the altar of Baal, and because he hath cut down the grove that @9was@7 by it.
verse	7	6	31	@@And Joash said unto all that stood against him, Will ye plead for Baal? will ye save him? he that will plead for him, let him be put to death whilst @9it is yet@7 morning: if he @9be@7 a god, let him plead for himself, because @9one@7 hath cast down his altar.
verse	7	6	32	Therefore on that day he called him Jerubbaal, saying, Let Baal plead against him, because he hath thrown down his altar.
verse	7	6	33	Then all the Midianites and the Amalekites and the children of the east were gathered together, and went over, and pitched in the valley of Jezreel.
verse	7	6	34	But the Spirit of the LORD came upon Gideon, and he blew a trumpet; and Abiezer was gathered after him.
verse	7	6	35	And he sent messengers throughout all Manasseh; who also was gathered after him: and he sent messengers unto Asher, and unto Zebulun, and unto Naphtali; and they came up to meet them.
verse	7	6	36	And Gideon said unto God, If thou wilt save Israel by mine hand, as thou hast said,
verse	7	6	37	@@Behold, I will put a fleece of wool in the floor; @9and@7 if the dew be on the fleece only, and @9it be@7 dry upon all the earth @9beside,@7 then shall I know that thou wilt save Israel by mine hand, as thou hast said.
verse	7	6	38	And it was so: for he rose up early on the morrow, and thrust the fleece together, and wringed the dew out of the fleece, a bowl full of water.
verse	7	6	39	And Gideon said unto God, Let not thine anger be hot against me, and I will speak but this once: let me prove, I pray thee, but this once with the fleece; let it now be dry only upon the fleece, and upon all the ground let there be dew.
verse	7	6	40	And God did so that night: for it was dry upon the fleece only, and there was dew on all the ground.
verse	7	7	1	@@Then Jerubbaal, who @9is@7 Gideon, and all the people that @9were@7 with him, rose up early, and pitched beside the well of Harod: so that the host of the Midianites were on the north side of them, by the hill of Moreh, in the valley.
verse	7	7	2	@@And the LORD said unto Gideon, The people that @9are@7 with thee @9are@7 too many for me to give the Midianites into their hands, lest Israel vaunt themselves against me, saying, Mine own hand hath saved me.
verse	7	7	3	@@Now therefore go to, proclaim in the ears of the people, saying, Whosoever @9is@7 fearful and afraid, let him return and depart early from mount Gilead. And there returned of the people twenty and two thousand; and there remained ten thousand.
verse	7	7	4	@@And the LORD said unto Gideon, The people @9are@7 yet @9too@7 many; bring them down unto the water, and I will try them for thee there: and it shall be, @9that@7 of whom I say unto thee, This shall go with thee, the same shall go with thee; and of whomsoever I say unto thee, This shall not go with thee, the same shall not go.
verse	7	7	5	So he brought down the people unto the water: and the LORD said unto Gideon, Every one that lappeth of the water with his tongue, as a dog lappeth, him shalt thou set by himself; likewise every one that boweth down upon his knees to drink.
verse	7	7	6	@@And the number of them that lapped, @9putting@7 their hand to their mouth, were three hundred men: but all the rest of the people bowed down upon their knees to drink water.
verse	7	7	7	@@And the LORD said unto Gideon, By the three hundred men that lapped will I save you, and deliver the Midianites into thine hand: and let all the @9other@7 people go every man unto his place.
verse	7	7	8	@@So the people took victuals in their hand, and their trumpets: and he sent all @9the rest of@7 Israel every man unto his tent, and retained those three hundred men: and the host of Midian was beneath him in the valley.
verse	7	7	9	And it came to pass the same night, that the LORD said unto him, Arise, get thee down unto the host; for I have delivered it into thine hand.
verse	7	7	10	But if thou fear to go down, go thou with Phurah thy servant down to the host:
verse	7	7	11	@@And thou shalt hear what they say; and afterward shall thine hands be strengthened to go down unto the host. Then went he down with Phurah his servant unto the outside of the armed men that @9were@7 in the host.
verse	7	7	12	@@And the Midianites and the Amalekites and all the children of the east lay along in the valley like grasshoppers for multitude; and their camels @9were@7 without number, as the sand by the sea side for multitude.
verse	7	7	13	@@And when Gideon was come, behold, @9there was@7 a man that told a dream unto his fellow, and said, Behold, I dreamed a dream, and, lo, a cake of barley bread tumbled into the host of Midian, and came unto a tent, and smote it that it fell, and overturned it, that the tent lay along.
verse	7	7	14	@@And his fellow answered and said, This @9is@7 nothing else save the sword of Gideon the son of Joash, a man of Israel: @9for@7 into his hand hath God delivered Midian, and all the host.
verse	7	7	15	@@And it was @9so,@7 when Gideon heard the telling of the dream, and the interpretation thereof, that he worshipped, and returned into the host of Israel, and said, Arise; for the LORD hath delivered into your hand the host of Midian.
verse	7	7	16	@@And he divided the three hundred men @9into@7 three companies, and he put a trumpet in every man's hand, with empty pitchers, and lamps within the pitchers.
verse	7	7	17	@@And he said unto them, Look on me, and do likewise: and, behold, when I come to the outside of the camp, it shall be @9that,@7 as I do, so shall ye do.
verse	7	7	18	@@When I blow with a trumpet, I and all that @9are@7 with me, then blow ye the trumpets also on every side of all the camp, and say, @9The sword@7 of the LORD, and of Gideon.
verse	7	7	19	@@So Gideon, and the hundred men that @9were@7 with him, came unto the outside of the camp in the beginning of the middle watch; and they had but newly set the watch: and they blew the trumpets, and brake the pitchers that @9were@7 in their hands.
verse	7	7	20	@@And the three companies blew the trumpets, and brake the pitchers, and held the lamps in their left hands, and the trumpets in their right hands to blow @9withal:@7 and they cried, The sword of the LORD, and of Gideon.
verse	7	7	21	And they stood every man in his place round about the camp: and all the host ran, and cried, and fled.
verse	7	7	22	@@And the three hundred blew the trumpets, and the LORD set every man's sword against his fellow, even throughout all the host: and the host fled to Bethshittah in Zererath, @9and@7 to the border of Abelmeholah, unto Tabbath.
verse	7	7	23	And the men of Israel gathered themselves together out of Naphtali, and out of Asher, and out of all Manasseh, and pursued after the Midianites.
verse	7	7	24	And Gideon sent messengers throughout all mount Ephraim, saying, Come down against the Midianites, and take before them the waters unto Bethbarah and Jordan. Then all the men of Ephraim gathered themselves together, and took the waters unto Bethbarah and Jordan.
verse	7	7	25	And they took two princes of the Midianites, Oreb and Zeeb; and they slew Oreb upon the rock Oreb, and Zeeb they slew at the winepress of Zeeb, and pursued Midian, and brought the heads of Oreb and Zeeb to Gideon on the other side Jordan.
verse	7	8	1	And the men of Ephraim said unto him, Why hast thou served us thus, that thou calledst us not, when thou wentest to fight with the Midianites? And they did chide with him sharply.
verse	7	8	2	@@And he said unto them, What have I done now in comparison of you? @9Is@7 not the gleaning of the grapes of Ephraim better than the vintage of Abiezer?
verse	7	8	3	God hath delivered into your hands the princes of Midian, Oreb and Zeeb: and what was I able to do in comparison of you? Then their anger was abated toward him, when he had said that.
verse	7	8	4	@@And Gideon came to Jordan, @9and@7 passed over, he, and the three hundred men that @9were@7 with him, faint, yet pursuing @9them. @7
verse	7	8	5	@@And he said unto the men of Succoth, Give, I pray you, loaves of bread unto the people that follow me; for they @9be@7 faint, and I am pursuing after Zebah and Zalmunna, kings of Midian.
verse	7	8	6	@@And the princes of Succoth said, @9Are@7 the hands of Zebah and Zalmunna now in thine hand, that we should give bread unto thine army?
verse	7	8	7	And Gideon said, Therefore when the LORD hath delivered Zebah and Zalmunna into mine hand, then I will tear your flesh with the thorns of the wilderness and with briers.
verse	7	8	8	@@And he went up thence to Penuel, and spake unto them likewise: and the men of Penuel answered him as the men of Succoth had answered @9him. @7
verse	7	8	9	And he spake also unto the men of Penuel, saying, When I come again in peace, I will break down this tower.
verse	7	8	10	@@Now Zebah and Zalmunna @9were@7 in Karkor, and their hosts with them, about fifteen thousand @9men,@7 all that were left of all the hosts of the children of the east: for there fell an hundred and twenty thousand men that drew sword.
verse	7	8	11	And Gideon went up by the way of them that dwelt in tents on the east of Nobah and Jogbehah, and smote the host: for the host was secure.
verse	7	8	12	And when Zebah and Zalmunna fled, he pursued after them, and took the two kings of Midian, Zebah and Zalmunna, and discomfited all the host.
verse	7	8	13	@@And Gideon the son of Joash returned from battle before the sun @9was up, @7
verse	7	8	14	@@And caught a young man of the men of Succoth, and enquired of him: and he described unto him the princes of Succoth, and the elders thereof, @9even@7 threescore and seventeen men.
verse	7	8	15	@@And he came unto the men of Succoth, and said, Behold Zebah and Zalmunna, with whom ye did upbraid me, saying, @9Are@7 the hands of Zebah and Zalmunna now in thine hand, that we should give bread unto thy men @9that are@7 weary?
verse	7	8	16	And he took the elders of the city, and thorns of the wilderness and briers, and with them he taught the men of Succoth.
verse	7	8	17	And he beat down the tower of Penuel, and slew the men of the city.
verse	7	8	18	@@Then said he unto Zebah and Zalmunna, What manner of men @9were they@7 whom ye slew at Tabor? And they answered, As thou @9art,@7 so @9were@7 they; each one resembled the children of a king.
verse	7	8	19	@@And he said, They @9were@7 my brethren, @9even@7 the sons of my mother: @9as@7 the LORD liveth, if ye had saved them alive, I would not slay you.
verse	7	8	20	@@And he said unto Jether his firstborn, Up, @9and@7 slay them. But the youth drew not his sword: for he feared, because he @9was@7 yet a youth.
verse	7	8	21	@@Then Zebah and Zalmunna said, Rise thou, and fall upon us: for as the man @9is, so is@7 his strength. And Gideon arose, and slew Zebah and Zalmunna, and took away the ornaments that @9were@7 on their camels' necks.
verse	7	8	22	Then the men of Israel said unto Gideon, Rule thou over us, both thou, and thy son, and thy son's son also: for thou hast delivered us from the hand of Midian.
verse	7	8	23	And Gideon said unto them, I will not rule over you, neither shall my son rule over you: the LORD shall rule over you.
verse	7	8	24	@@And Gideon said unto them, I would desire a request of you, that ye would give me every man the earrings of his prey. (For they had golden earrings, because they @9were@7 Ishmaelites.)
verse	7	8	25	@@And they answered, We will willingly give @9them.@7 And they spread a garment, and did cast therein every man the earrings of his prey.
verse	7	8	26	@@And the weight of the golden earrings that he requested was a thousand and seven hundred @9shekels@7 of gold; beside ornaments, and collars, and purple raiment that @9was@7 on the kings of Midian, and beside the chains that @9were@7 about their camels' necks.
verse	7	8	27	@@And Gideon made an ephod thereof, and put it in his city, @9even@7 in Ophrah: and all Israel went thither a whoring after it: which thing became a snare unto Gideon, and to his house.
verse	7	8	28	Thus was Midian subdued before the children of Israel, so that they lifted up their heads no more. And the country was in quietness forty years in the days of Gideon.
verse	7	8	29	And Jerubbaal the son of Joash went and dwelt in his own house.
verse	7	8	30	And Gideon had threescore and ten sons of his body begotten: for he had many wives.
verse	7	8	31	@@And his concubine that @9was@7 in Shechem, she also bare him a son, whose name he called Abimelech.
verse	7	8	32	And Gideon the son of Joash died in a good old age, and was buried in the sepulchre of Joash his father, in Ophrah of the Abiezrites.
verse	7	8	33	And it came to pass, as soon as Gideon was dead, that the children of Israel turned again, and went a whoring after Baalim, and made Baalberith their god.
verse	7	8	34	And the children of Israel remembered not the LORD their God, who had delivered them out of the hands of all their enemies on every side:
verse	7	8	35	@@Neither shewed they kindness to the house of Jerubbaal, @9namely,@7 Gideon, according to all the goodness which he had shewed unto Israel.
verse	7	9	1	And Abimelech the son of Jerubbaal went to Shechem unto his mother's brethren, and communed with them, and with all the family of the house of his mother's father, saying,
verse	7	9	2	@@Speak, I pray you, in the ears of all the men of Shechem, Whether is better for you, either that all the sons of Jerubbaal, @9which are@7 threescore and ten persons, reign over you, or that one reign over you? remember also that I @9am@7 your bone and your flesh.
verse	7	9	3	@@And his mother's brethren spake of him in the ears of all the men of Shechem all these words: and their hearts inclined to follow Abimelech; for they said, He @9is@7 our brother.
verse	7	9	4	@@And they gave him threescore and ten @9pieces@7 of silver out of the house of Baalberith, wherewith Abimelech hired vain and light persons, which followed him.
verse	7	9	5	@@And he went unto his father's house at Ophrah, and slew his brethren the sons of Jerubbaal, @9being@7 threescore and ten persons, upon one stone: notwithstanding yet Jotham the youngest son of Jerubbaal was left; for he hid himself.
verse	7	9	6	@@And all the men of Shechem gathered together, and all the house of Millo, and went, and made Abimelech king, by the plain of the pillar that @9was@7 in Shechem.
verse	7	9	7	@@And when they told @9it@7 to Jotham, he went and stood in the top of mount Gerizim, and lifted up his voice, and cried, and said unto them, Hearken unto me, ye men of Shechem, that God may hearken unto you.
verse	7	9	8	@@The trees went forth @9on a time@7 to anoint a king over them; and they said unto the olive tree, Reign thou over us.
verse	7	9	9	But the olive tree said unto them, Should I leave my fatness, wherewith by me they honour God and man, and go to be promoted over the trees?
verse	7	9	10	@@And the trees said to the fig tree, Come thou, @9and@7 reign over us.
verse	7	9	11	But the fig tree said unto them, Should I forsake my sweetness, and my good fruit, and go to be promoted over the trees?
verse	7	9	12	@@Then said the trees unto the vine, Come thou, @9and@7 reign over us.
verse	7	9	13	And the vine said unto them, Should I leave my wine, which cheereth God and man, and go to be promoted over the trees?
verse	7	9	14	@@Then said all the trees unto the bramble, Come thou, @9and@7 reign over us.
verse	7	9	15	@@And the bramble said unto the trees, If in truth ye anoint me king over you, @9then@7 come @9and@7 put your trust in my shadow: and if not, let fire come out of the bramble, and devour the cedars of Lebanon.
verse	7	9	16	Now therefore, if ye have done truly and sincerely, in that ye have made Abimelech king, and if ye have dealt well with Jerubbaal and his house, and have done unto him according to the deserving of his hands;
verse	7	9	17	(For my father fought for you, and adventured his life far, and delivered you out of the hand of Midian:
verse	7	9	18	@@And ye are risen up against my father's house this day, and have slain his sons, threescore and ten persons, upon one stone, and have made Abimelech, the son of his maidservant, king over the men of Shechem, because he @9is@7 your brother;)
verse	7	9	19	@@If ye then have dealt truly and sincerely with Jerubbaal and with his house this day, @9then@7 rejoice ye in Abimelech, and let him also rejoice in you:
verse	7	9	20	But if not, let fire come out from Abimelech, and devour the men of Shechem, and the house of Millo; and let fire come out from the men of Shechem, and from the house of Millo, and devour Abimelech.
verse	7	9	21	And Jotham ran away, and fled, and went to Beer, and dwelt there, for fear of Abimelech his brother.
verse	7	9	22	When Abimelech had reigned three years over Israel,
verse	7	9	23	Then God sent an evil spirit between Abimelech and the men of Shechem; and the men of Shechem dealt treacherously with Abimelech:
verse	7	9	24	@@That the cruelty @9done@7 to the threescore and ten sons of Jerubbaal might come, and their blood be laid upon Abimelech their brother, which slew them; and upon the men of Shechem, which aided him in the killing of his brethren.
verse	7	9	25	And the men of Shechem set liers in wait for him in the top of the mountains, and they robbed all that came along that way by them: and it was told Abimelech.
verse	7	9	26	And Gaal the son of Ebed came with his brethren, and went over to Shechem: and the men of Shechem put their confidence in him.
verse	7	9	27	@@And they went out into the fields, and gathered their vineyards, and trode @9the grapes,@7 and made merry, and went into the house of their god, and did eat and drink, and cursed Abimelech.
verse	7	9	28	@@And Gaal the son of Ebed said, Who @9is@7 Abimelech, and who @9is@7 Shechem, that we should serve him? @9is@7 not @9he@7 the son of Jerubbaal? and Zebul his officer? serve the men of Hamor the father of Shechem: for why should we serve him?
verse	7	9	29	And would to God this people were under my hand! then would I remove Abimelech. And he said to Abimelech, Increase thine army, and come out.
verse	7	9	30	And when Zebul the ruler of the city heard the words of Gaal the son of Ebed, his anger was kindled.
verse	7	9	31	And he sent messengers unto Abimelech privily, saying, Behold, Gaal the son of Ebed and his brethren be come to Shechem; and, behold, they fortify the city against thee.
verse	7	9	32	@@Now therefore up by night, thou and the people that @9is@7 with thee, and lie in wait in the field:
verse	7	9	33	@@And it shall be, @9that@7 in the morning, as soon as the sun is up, thou shalt rise early, and set upon the city: and, behold, @9when@7 he and the people that @9is@7 with him come out against thee, then mayest thou do to them as thou shalt find occasion.
verse	7	9	34	@@And Abimelech rose up, and all the people that @9were@7 with him, by night, and they laid wait against Shechem in four companies.
verse	7	9	35	@@And Gaal the son of Ebed went out, and stood in the entering of the gate of the city: and Abimelech rose up, and the people that @9were@7 with him, from lying in wait.
verse	7	9	36	@@And when Gaal saw the people, he said to Zebul, Behold, there come people down from the top of the mountains. And Zebul said unto him, Thou seest the shadow of the mountains as @9if they were@7 men.
verse	7	9	37	And Gaal spake again and said, See there come people down by the middle of the land, and another company come along by the plain of Meonenim.
verse	7	9	38	@@Then said Zebul unto him, Where @9is@7 now thy mouth, wherewith thou saidst, Who @9is@7 Abimelech, that we should serve him? @9is@7 not this the people that thou hast despised? go out, I pray now, and fight with them.
verse	7	9	39	And Gaal went out before the men of Shechem, and fought with Abimelech.
verse	7	9	40	@@And Abimelech chased him, and he fled before him, and many were overthrown @9and@7 wounded, @9even@7 unto the entering of the gate.
verse	7	9	41	And Abimelech dwelt at Arumah: and Zebul thrust out Gaal and his brethren, that they should not dwell in Shechem.
verse	7	9	42	And it came to pass on the morrow, that the people went out into the field; and they told Abimelech.
verse	7	9	43	@@And he took the people, and divided them into three companies, and laid wait in the field, and looked, and, behold, the people @9were@7 come forth out of the city; and he rose up against them, and smote them.
verse	7	9	44	@@And Abimelech, and the company that @9was@7 with him, rushed forward, and stood in the entering of the gate of the city: and the two @9other@7 companies ran upon all @9the people@7 that @9were@7 in the fields, and slew them.
verse	7	9	45	@@And Abimelech fought against the city all that day; and he took the city, and slew the people that @9was@7 therein, and beat down the city, and sowed it with salt.
verse	7	9	46	@@And when all the men of the tower of Shechem heard @9that,@7 they entered into an hold of the house of the god Berith.
verse	7	9	47	And it was told Abimelech, that all the men of the tower of Shechem were gathered together.
verse	7	9	48	@@And Abimelech gat him up to mount Zalmon, he and all the people that @9were@7 with him; and Abimelech took an axe in his hand, and cut down a bough from the trees, and took it, and laid @9it@7 on his shoulder, and said unto the people that @9were@7 with him, What ye have seen me do, make haste, @9and@7 do as I @9have done. @7
verse	7	9	49	@@And all the people likewise cut down every man his bough, and followed Abimelech, and put @9them@7 to the hold, and set the hold on fire upon them; so that all the men of the tower of Shechem died also, about a thousand men and women.
verse	7	9	50	Then went Abimelech to Thebez, and encamped against Thebez, and took it.
verse	7	9	51	@@But there was a strong tower within the city, and thither fled all the men and women, and all they of the city, and shut @9it@7 to them, and gat them up to the top of the tower.
verse	7	9	52	And Abimelech came unto the tower, and fought against it, and went hard unto the door of the tower to burn it with fire.
verse	7	9	53	And a certain woman cast a piece of a millstone upon Abimelech's head, and all to brake his skull.
verse	7	9	54	Then he called hastily unto the young man his armourbearer, and said unto him, Draw thy sword, and slay me, that men say not of me, A woman slew him. And his young man thrust him through, and he died.
verse	7	9	55	And when the men of Israel saw that Abimelech was dead, they departed every man unto his place.
verse	7	9	56	Thus God rendered the wickedness of Abimelech, which he did unto his father, in slaying his seventy brethren:
verse	7	9	57	And all the evil of the men of Shechem did God render upon their heads: and upon them came the curse of Jotham the son of Jerubbaal.
verse	7	10	1	And after Abimelech there arose to defend Israel Tola the son of Puah, the son of Dodo, a man of Issachar; and he dwelt in Shamir in mount Ephraim.
verse	7	10	2	And he judged Israel twenty and three years, and died, and was buried in Shamir.
verse	7	10	3	And after him arose Jair, a Gileadite, and judged Israel twenty and two years.
verse	7	10	4	@@And he had thirty sons that rode on thirty ass colts, and they had thirty cities, which are called Havothjair unto this day, which @9are@7 in the land of Gilead.
verse	7	10	5	And Jair died, and was buried in Camon.
verse	7	10	6	And the children of Israel did evil again in the sight of the LORD, and served Baalim, and Ashtaroth, and the gods of Syria, and the gods of Zidon, and the gods of Moab, and the gods of the children of Ammon, and the gods of the Philistines, and forsook the LORD, and served not him.
verse	7	10	7	And the anger of the LORD was hot against Israel, and he sold them into the hands of the Philistines, and into the hands of the children of Ammon.
verse	7	10	8	@@And that year they vexed and oppressed the children of Israel: eighteen years, all the children of Israel that @9were@7 on the other side Jordan in the land of the Amorites, which @9is@7 in Gilead.
verse	7	10	9	Moreover the children of Ammon passed over Jordan to fight also against Judah, and against Benjamin, and against the house of Ephraim; so that Israel was sore distressed.
verse	7	10	10	And the children of Israel cried unto the LORD, saying, We have sinned against thee, both because we have forsaken our God, and also served Baalim.
verse	7	10	11	@@And the LORD said unto the children of Israel, @9Did@7 not @9I deliver you@7 from the Egyptians, and from the Amorites, from the children of Ammon, and from the Philistines?
verse	7	10	12	The Zidonians also, and the Amalekites, and the Maonites, did oppress you; and ye cried to me, and I delivered you out of their hand.
verse	7	10	13	Yet ye have forsaken me, and served other gods: wherefore I will deliver you no more.
verse	7	10	14	Go and cry unto the gods which ye have chosen; let them deliver you in the time of your tribulation.
verse	7	10	15	And the children of Israel said unto the LORD, We have sinned: do thou unto us whatsoever seemeth good unto thee; deliver us only, we pray thee, this day.
verse	7	10	16	And they put away the strange gods from among them, and served the LORD: and his soul was grieved for the misery of Israel.
verse	7	10	17	Then the children of Ammon were gathered together, and encamped in Gilead. And the children of Israel assembled themselves together, and encamped in Mizpeh.
verse	7	10	18	@@And the people @9and@7 princes of Gilead said one to another, What man @9is he@7 that will begin to fight against the children of Ammon? he shall be head over all the inhabitants of Gilead.
verse	7	11	1	@@Now Jephthah the Gileadite was a mighty man of valour, and he @9was@7 the son of an harlot: and Gilead begat Jephthah.
verse	7	11	2	@@And Gilead's wife bare him sons; and his wife's sons grew up, and they thrust out Jephthah, and said unto him, Thou shalt not inherit in our father's house; for thou @9art@7 the son of a strange woman.
verse	7	11	3	Then Jephthah fled from his brethren, and dwelt in the land of Tob: and there were gathered vain men to Jephthah, and went out with him.
verse	7	11	4	And it came to pass in process of time, that the children of Ammon made war against Israel.
verse	7	11	5	And it was so, that when the children of Ammon made war against Israel, the elders of Gilead went to fetch Jephthah out of the land of Tob:
verse	7	11	6	And they said unto Jephthah, Come, and be our captain, that we may fight with the children of Ammon.
verse	7	11	7	And Jephthah said unto the elders of Gilead, Did not ye hate me, and expel me out of my father's house? and why are ye come unto me now when ye are in distress?
verse	7	11	8	And the elders of Gilead said unto Jephthah, Therefore we turn again to thee now, that thou mayest go with us, and fight against the children of Ammon, and be our head over all the inhabitants of Gilead.
verse	7	11	9	And Jephthah said unto the elders of Gilead, If ye bring me home again to fight against the children of Ammon, and the LORD deliver them before me, shall I be your head?
verse	7	11	10	And the elders of Gilead said unto Jephthah, The LORD be witness between us, if we do not so according to thy words.
verse	7	11	11	Then Jephthah went with the elders of Gilead, and the people made him head and captain over them: and Jephthah uttered all his words before the LORD in Mizpeh.
verse	7	11	12	And Jephthah sent messengers unto the king of the children of Ammon, saying, What hast thou to do with me, that thou art come against me to fight in my land?
verse	7	11	13	@@And the king of the children of Ammon answered unto the messengers of Jephthah, Because Israel took away my land, when they came up out of Egypt, from Arnon even unto Jabbok, and unto Jordan: now therefore restore those @9lands@7 again peaceably.
verse	7	11	14	And Jephthah sent messengers again unto the king of the children of Ammon:
verse	7	11	15	And said unto him, Thus saith Jephthah, Israel took not away the land of Moab, nor the land of the children of Ammon:
verse	7	11	16	But when Israel came up from Egypt, and walked through the wilderness unto the Red sea, and came to Kadesh;
verse	7	11	17	@@Then Israel sent messengers unto the king of Edom, saying, Let me, I pray thee, pass through thy land: but the king of Edom would not hearken @9thereto.@7 And in like manner they sent unto the king of Moab: but he would not @9consent:@7 and Israel abode in Kadesh.
verse	7	11	18	@@Then they went along through the wilderness, and compassed the land of Edom, and the land of Moab, and came by the east side of the land of Moab, and pitched on the other side of Arnon, but came not within the border of Moab: for Arnon @9was@7 the border of Moab.
verse	7	11	19	And Israel sent messengers unto Sihon king of the Amorites, the king of Heshbon; and Israel said unto him, Let us pass, we pray thee, through thy land into my place.
verse	7	11	20	But Sihon trusted not Israel to pass through his coast: but Sihon gathered all his people together, and pitched in Jahaz, and fought against Israel.
verse	7	11	21	And the LORD God of Israel delivered Sihon and all his people into the hand of Israel, and they smote them: so Israel possessed all the land of the Amorites, the inhabitants of that country.
verse	7	11	22	And they possessed all the coasts of the Amorites, from Arnon even unto Jabbok, and from the wilderness even unto Jordan.
verse	7	11	23	So now the LORD God of Israel hath dispossessed the Amorites from before his people Israel, and shouldest thou possess it?
verse	7	11	24	Wilt not thou possess that which Chemosh thy god giveth thee to possess? So whomsoever the LORD our God shall drive out from before us, them will we possess.
verse	7	11	25	@@And now @9art@7 thou any thing better than Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab? did he ever strive against Israel, or did he ever fight against them,
verse	7	11	26	@@While Israel dwelt in Heshbon and her towns, and in Aroer and her towns, and in all the cities that @9be@7 along by the coasts of Arnon, three hundred years? why therefore did ye not recover @9them@7 within that time?
verse	7	11	27	Wherefore I have not sinned against thee, but thou doest me wrong to war against me: the LORD the Judge be judge this day between the children of Israel and the children of Ammon.
verse	7	11	28	Howbeit the king of the children of Ammon hearkened not unto the words of Jephthah which he sent him.
verse	7	11	29	@@Then the Spirit of the LORD came upon Jephthah, and he passed over Gilead, and Manasseh, and passed over Mizpeh of Gilead, and from Mizpeh of Gilead he passed over @9unto@7 the children of Ammon.
verse	7	11	30	And Jephthah vowed a vow unto the LORD, and said, If thou shalt without fail deliver the children of Ammon into mine hands,
verse	7	11	31	Then it shall be, that whatsoever cometh forth of the doors of my house to meet me, when I return in peace from the children of Ammon, shall surely be the LORD'S, and I will offer it up for a burnt offering.
verse	7	11	32	So Jephthah passed over unto the children of Ammon to fight against them; and the LORD delivered them into his hands.
verse	7	11	33	@@And he smote them from Aroer, even till thou come to Minnith, @9even@7 twenty cities, and unto the plain of the vineyards, with a very great slaughter. Thus the children of Ammon were subdued before the children of Israel.
verse	7	11	34	@@And Jephthah came to Mizpeh unto his house, and, behold, his daughter came out to meet him with timbrels and with dances: and she @9was his@7 only child; beside her he had neither son nor daughter.
verse	7	11	35	And it came to pass, when he saw her, that he rent his clothes, and said, Alas, my daughter! thou hast brought me very low, and thou art one of them that trouble me: for I have opened my mouth unto the LORD, and I cannot go back.
verse	7	11	36	@@And she said unto him, My father, @9if@7 thou hast opened thy mouth unto the LORD, do to me according to that which hath proceeded out of thy mouth; forasmuch as the LORD hath taken vengeance for thee of thine enemies, @9even@7 of the children of Ammon.
verse	7	11	37	And she said unto her father, Let this thing be done for me: let me alone two months, that I may go up and down upon the mountains, and bewail my virginity, I and my fellows.
verse	7	11	38	@@And he said, Go. And he sent her away @9for@7 two months: and she went with her companions, and bewailed her virginity upon the mountains.
verse	7	11	39	@@And it came to pass at the end of two months, that she returned unto her father, who did with her @9according@7 to his vow which he had vowed: and she knew no man. And it was a custom in Israel,
