verse	9	18	4	@@And Jonathan stripped himself of the robe that @9was@7 upon him, and gave it to David, and his garments, even to his sword, and to his bow, and to his girdle.
verse	9	18	5	@@And David went out whithersoever Saul sent him, @9and@7 behaved himself wisely: and Saul set him over the men of war, and he was accepted in the sight of all the people, and also in the sight of Saul's servants.
verse	9	18	6	And it came to pass as they came, when David was returned from the slaughter of the Philistine, that the women came out of all cities of Israel, singing and dancing, to meet king Saul, with tabrets, with joy, and with instruments of musick.
verse	9	18	7	@@And the women answered @9one another@7 as they played, and said, Saul hath slain his thousands, and David his ten thousands.
verse	9	18	8	@@And Saul was very wroth, and the saying displeased him; and he said, They have ascribed unto David ten thousands, and to me they have ascribed @9but@7 thousands: and @9what@7 can he have more but the kingdom?
verse	9	18	9	And Saul eyed David from that day and forward.
verse	9	18	10	@@And it came to pass on the morrow, that the evil spirit from God came upon Saul, and he prophesied in the midst of the house: and David played with his hand, as at other times: and @9there was@7 a javelin in Saul's hand.
verse	9	18	11	@@And Saul cast the javelin; for he said, I will smite David even to the wall @9with it.@7 And David avoided out of his presence twice.
