verse	9	21	7	@@Now a certain man of the servants of Saul @9was@7 there that day, detained before the LORD; and his name @9was@7 Doeg, an Edomite, the chiefest of the herdmen that @9belonged@7 to Saul.
verse	9	21	8	And David said unto Ahimelech, And is there not here under thine hand spear or sword? for I have neither brought my sword nor my weapons with me, because the king's business required haste.
verse	9	21	9	@@And the priest said, The sword of Goliath the Philistine, whom thou slewest in the valley of Elah, behold, it @9is here@7 wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod: if thou wilt take that, take @9it:@7 for @9there is@7 no other save that here. And David said, @9There is@7 none like that; give it me.
verse	9	21	10	And David arose, and fled that day for fear of Saul, and went to Achish the king of Gath.
