verse	9	23	5	So David and his men went to Keilah, and fought with the Philistines, and brought away their cattle, and smote them with a great slaughter. So David saved the inhabitants of Keilah.
verse	9	23	6	@@And it came to pass, when Abiathar the son of Ahimelech fled to David to Keilah, @9that@7 he came down @9with@7 an ephod in his hand.
verse	9	23	7	And it was told Saul that David was come to Keilah. And Saul said, God hath delivered him into mine hand; for he is shut in, by entering into a town that hath gates and bars.
verse	9	23	8	And Saul called all the people together to war, to go down to Keilah, to besiege David and his men.
verse	9	23	9	And David knew that Saul secretly practised mischief against him; and he said to Abiathar the priest, Bring hither the ephod.
verse	9	23	10	Then said David, O LORD God of Israel, thy servant hath certainly heard that Saul seeketh to come to Keilah, to destroy the city for my sake.
verse	9	23	11	Will the men of Keilah deliver me up into his hand? will Saul come down, as thy servant hath heard? O LORD God of Israel, I beseech thee, tell thy servant. And the LORD said, He will come down.
verse	9	23	12	@@Then said David, Will the men of Keilah deliver me and my men into the hand of Saul? And the LORD said, They will deliver @9thee@7 up.
verse	9	23	13	@@Then David and his men, @9which were@7 about six hundred, arose and departed out of Keilah, and went whithersoever they could go. And it was told Saul that David was escaped from Keilah; and he forbare to go forth.
verse	9	23	14	And David abode in the wilderness in strong holds, and remained in a mountain in the wilderness of Ziph. And Saul sought him every day, but God delivered him not into his hand.
verse	9	23	15	@@And David saw that Saul was come out to seek his life: and David @9was@7 in the wilderness of Ziph in a wood.
verse	9	23	16	And Jonathan Saul's son arose, and went to David into the wood, and strengthened his hand in God.
verse	9	23	17	And he said unto him, Fear not: for the hand of Saul my father shall not find thee; and thou shalt be king over Israel, and I shall be next unto thee; and that also Saul my father knoweth.
verse	9	23	18	And they two made a covenant before the LORD: and David abode in the wood, and Jonathan went to his house.
verse	9	23	19	@@Then came up the Ziphites to Saul to Gibeah, saying, Doth not David hide himself with us in strong holds in the wood, in the hill of Hachilah, which @9is@7 on the south of Jeshimon?
verse	9	23	20	@@Now therefore, O king, come down according to all the desire of thy soul to come down; and our part @9shall be@7 to deliver him into the king's hand.
verse	9	23	21	@@And Saul said, Blessed @9be@7 ye of the LORD; for ye have compassion on me.
verse	9	23	22	@@Go, I pray you, prepare yet, and know and see his place where his haunt is, @9and@7 who hath seen him there: for it is told me @9that@7 he dealeth very subtilly.
verse	9	23	23	See therefore, and take knowledge of all the lurking places where he hideth himself, and come ye again to me with the certainty, and I will go with you: and it shall come to pass, if he be in the land, that I will search him out throughout all the thousands of Judah.
verse	9	23	24	@@And they arose, and went to Ziph before Saul: but David and his men @9were@7 in the wilderness of Maon, in the plain on the south of Jeshimon.
verse	9	23	25	@@Saul also and his men went to seek @9him.@7 And they told David: wherefore he came down into a rock, and abode in the wilderness of Maon. And when Saul heard @9that,@7 he pursued after David in the wilderness of Maon.
verse	9	23	26	And Saul went on this side of the mountain, and David and his men on that side of the mountain: and David made haste to get away for fear of Saul; for Saul and his men compassed David and his men round about to take them.
verse	9	23	27	But there came a messenger unto Saul, saying, Haste thee, and come; for the Philistines have invaded the land.
