verse	9	25	12	So David's young men turned their way, and went again, and came and told him all those sayings.
verse	9	25	13	And David said unto his men, Gird ye on every man his sword. And they girded on every man his sword; and David also girded on his sword: and there went up after David about four hundred men; and two hundred abode by the stuff.
verse	9	25	14	But one of the young men told Abigail, Nabal's wife, saying, Behold, David sent messengers out of the wilderness to salute our master; and he railed on them.
verse	9	25	15	@@But the men @9were@7 very good unto us, and we were not hurt, neither missed we any thing, as long as we were conversant with them, when we were in the fields:
verse	9	25	16	They were a wall unto us both by night and day, all the while we were with them keeping the sheep.
verse	9	25	17	@@Now therefore know and consider what thou wilt do; for evil is determined against our master, and against all his household: for he @9is such@7 a son of Belial, that @9a man@7 cannot speak to him.
verse	9	25	18	@@Then Abigail made haste, and took two hundred loaves, and two bottles of wine, and five sheep ready dressed, and five measures of parched @9corn,@7 and an hundred clusters of raisins, and two hundred cakes of figs, and laid @9them@7 on asses.
verse	9	25	19	And she said unto her servants, Go on before me; behold, I come after you. But she told not her husband Nabal.
