verse	9	25	25	@@Let not my lord, I pray thee, regard this man of Belial, @9even@7 Nabal: for as his name @9is,@7 so @9is@7 he; Nabal @9is@7 his name, and folly @9is@7 with him: but I thine handmaid saw not the young men of my lord, whom thou didst send.
verse	9	25	26	@@Now therefore, my lord, @9as@7 the LORD liveth, and @9as@7 thy soul liveth, seeing the LORD hath withholden thee from coming to @9shed@7 blood, and from avenging thyself with thine own hand, now let thine enemies, and they that seek evil to my lord, be as Nabal.
