verse	9	25	31	That this shall be no grief unto thee, nor offence of heart unto my lord, either that thou hast shed blood causeless, or that my lord hath avenged himself: but when the LORD shall have dealt well with my lord, then remember thine handmaid.
verse	9	25	32	@@And David said to Abigail, Blessed @9be@7 the LORD God of Israel, which sent thee this day to meet me:
verse	9	25	33	@@And blessed @9be@7 thy advice, and blessed @9be@7 thou, which hast kept me this day from coming to @9shed@7 blood, and from avenging myself with mine own hand.
verse	9	25	34	@@For in very deed, @9as@7 the LORD God of Israel liveth, which hath kept me back from hurting thee, except thou hadst hasted and come to meet me, surely there had not been left unto Nabal by the morning light any that pisseth against the wall.
verse	9	25	35	@@So David received of her hand @9that@7 which she had brought him, and said unto her, Go up in peace to thine house; see, I have hearkened to thy voice, and have accepted thy person.
verse	9	25	36	@@And Abigail came to Nabal; and, behold, he held a feast in his house, like the feast of a king; and Nabal's heart @9was@7 merry within him, for he @9was@7 very drunken: wherefore she told him nothing, less or more, until the morning light.
verse	9	25	37	@@But it came to pass in the morning, when the wine was gone out of Nabal, and his wife had told him these things, that his heart died within him, and he became @9as@7 a stone.
