verse	9	26	11	@@The LORD forbid that I should stretch forth mine hand against the LORD'S anointed: but, I pray thee, take thou now the spear that @9is@7 at his bolster, and the cruse of water, and let us go.
verse	9	26	12	@@So David took the spear and the cruse of water from Saul's bolster; and they gat them away, and no man saw @9it,@7 nor knew @9it,@7 neither awaked: for they @9were@7 all asleep; because a deep sleep from the LORD was fallen upon them.
verse	9	26	13	@@Then David went over to the other side, and stood on the top of an hill afar off; a great space @9being@7 between them:
verse	9	26	14	@@And David cried to the people, and to Abner the son of Ner, saying, Answerest thou not, Abner? Then Abner answered and said, Who @9art@7 thou @9that@7 criest to the king?
verse	9	26	15	@@And David said to Abner, @9Art@7 not thou a @9valiant@7 man? and who @9is@7 like to thee in Israel? wherefore then hast thou not kept thy lord the king? for there came one of the people in to destroy the king thy lord.
verse	9	26	16	@@This thing @9is@7 not good that thou hast done. @9As@7 the LORD liveth, ye @9are@7 worthy to die, because ye have not kept your master, the LORD'S anointed. And now see where the king's spear is, and the cruse of water that @9was@7 at his bolster.
verse	9	26	17	@@And Saul knew David's voice, and said, @9Is@7 this thy voice, my son David? And David said, @9It is@7 my voice, my lord, O king.
verse	9	26	18	@@And he said, Wherefore doth my lord thus pursue after his servant? for what have I done? or what evil @9is@7 in mine hand?
verse	9	26	19	@@Now therefore, I pray thee, let my lord the king hear the words of his servant. If the LORD have stirred thee up against me, let him accept an offering: but if @9they be@7 the children of men, cursed @9be@7 they before the LORD; for they have driven me out this day from abiding in the inheritance of the LORD, saying, Go, serve other gods.
