verse	9	26	25	@@Then Saul said to David, Blessed @9be@7 thou, my son David: thou shalt both do great things, and also shalt still prevail. So David went on his way, and Saul returned to his place.
verse	9	27	1	@@And David said in his heart, I shall now perish one day by the hand of Saul: @9there is@7 nothing better for me than that I should speedily escape into the land of the Philistines; and Saul shall despair of me, to seek me any more in any coast of Israel: so shall I escape out of his hand.
verse	9	27	2	@@And David arose, and he passed over with the six hundred men that @9were@7 with him unto Achish, the son of Maoch, king of Gath.
