verse	9	30	30	@@And to @9them@7 which @9were@7 in Hormah, and to @9them@7 which @9were@7 in Chorashan, and to @9them@7 which @9were@7 in Athach,
verse	9	30	31	@@And to @9them@7 which @9were@7 in Hebron, and to all the places where David himself and his men were wont to haunt.
verse	9	31	1	Now the Philistines fought against Israel: and the men of Israel fled from before the Philistines, and fell down slain in mount Gilboa.
verse	9	31	2	And the Philistines followed hard upon Saul and upon his sons; and the Philistines slew Jonathan, and Abinadab, and Melchishua, Saul's sons.
verse	9	31	3	And the battle went sore against Saul, and the archers hit him; and he was sore wounded of the archers.
verse	9	31	4	Then said Saul unto his armourbearer, Draw thy sword, and thrust me through therewith; lest these uncircumcised come and thrust me through, and abuse me. But his armourbearer would not; for he was sore afraid. Therefore Saul took a sword, and fell upon it.
verse	9	31	5	And when his armourbearer saw that Saul was dead, he fell likewise upon his sword, and died with him.
