verse	10	1	9	@@He said unto me again, Stand, I pray thee, upon me, and slay me: for anguish is come upon me, because my life @9is@7 yet whole in me.
verse	10	1	10	@@So I stood upon him, and slew him, because I was sure that he could not live after that he was fallen: and I took the crown that @9was@7 upon his head, and the bracelet that @9was@7 on his arm, and have brought them hither unto my lord.
verse	10	1	11	@@Then David took hold on his clothes, and rent them; and likewise all the men that @9were@7 with him:
verse	10	1	12	And they mourned, and wept, and fasted until even, for Saul, and for Jonathan his son, and for the people of the LORD, and for the house of Israel; because they were fallen by the sword.
verse	10	1	13	@@And David said unto the young man that told him, Whence @9art@7 thou? And he answered, I @9am@7 the son of a stranger, an Amalekite.
verse	10	1	14	And David said unto him, How wast thou not afraid to stretch forth thine hand to destroy the LORD'S anointed?
verse	10	1	15	@@And David called one of the young men, and said, Go near, @9and@7 fall upon him. And he smote him that he died.
verse	10	1	16	@@And David said unto him, Thy blood @9be@7 upon thy head; for thy mouth hath testified against thee, saying, I have slain the LORD'S anointed.
verse	10	1	17	And David lamented with this lamentation over Saul and over Jonathan his son:
verse	10	1	18	@@(Also he bade them teach the children of Judah @9the use of@7 the bow: behold, it is written in the book of Jasher.)
verse	10	1	19	The beauty of Israel is slain upon thy high places: how are the mighty fallen!
verse	10	1	20	@@Tell @9it@7 not in Gath, publish @9it@7 not in the streets of Askelon; lest the daughters of the Philistines rejoice, lest the daughters of the uncircumcised triumph.
verse	10	1	21	@@Ye mountains of Gilboa, @9let there be@7 no dew, neither @9let there be@7 rain, upon you, nor fields of offerings: for there the shield of the mighty is vilely cast away, the shield of Saul, @9as though he had@7 not @9been@7 anointed with oil.
verse	10	1	22	From the blood of the slain, from the fat of the mighty, the bow of Jonathan turned not back, and the sword of Saul returned not empty.
verse	10	1	23	@@Saul and Jonathan @9were@7 lovely and pleasant in their lives, and in their death they were not divided: they were swifter than eagles, they were stronger than lions.
