verse	10	3	32	And they buried Abner in Hebron: and the king lifted up his voice, and wept at the grave of Abner; and all the people wept.
verse	10	3	33	And the king lamented over Abner, and said, Died Abner as a fool dieth?
verse	10	3	34	@@Thy hands @9were@7 not bound, nor thy feet put into fetters: as a man falleth before wicked men, @9so@7 fellest thou. And all the people wept again over him.
verse	10	3	35	And when all the people came to cause David to eat meat while it was yet day, David sware, saying, So do God to me, and more also, if I taste bread, or ought else, till the sun be down.
verse	10	3	36	@@And all the people took notice @9of it,@7 and it pleased them: as whatsoever the king did pleased all the people.
verse	10	3	37	For all the people and all Israel understood that day that it was not of the king to slay Abner the son of Ner.
verse	10	3	38	And the king said unto his servants, Know ye not that there is a prince and a great man fallen this day in Israel?
verse	10	3	39	@@And I @9am@7 this day weak, though anointed king; and these men the sons of Zeruiah @9be@7 too hard for me: the LORD shall reward the doer of evil according to his wickedness.
verse	10	4	1	And when Saul's son heard that Abner was dead in Hebron, his hands were feeble, and all the Israelites were troubled.
verse	10	4	2	@@And Saul's son had two men @9that were@7 captains of bands: the name of the one @9was@7 Baanah, and the name of the other Rechab, the sons of Rimmon a Beerothite, of the children of Benjamin: (for Beeroth also was reckoned to Benjamin:
verse	10	4	3	And the Beerothites fled to Gittaim, and were sojourners there until this day.)
verse	10	4	4	@@And Jonathan, Saul's son, had a son @9that was@7 lame of @9his@7 feet. He was five years old when the tidings came of Saul and Jonathan out of Jezreel, and his nurse took him up, and fled: and it came to pass, as she made haste to flee, that he fell, and became lame. And his name @9was@7 Mephibosheth.
verse	10	4	5	And the sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, Rechab and Baanah, went, and came about the heat of the day to the house of Ishbosheth, who lay on a bed at noon.
verse	10	4	6	@@And they came thither into the midst of the house, @9as though@7 they would have fetched wheat; and they smote him under the fifth @9rib:@7 and Rechab and Baanah his brother escaped.
verse	10	4	7	For when they came into the house, he lay on his bed in his bedchamber, and they smote him, and slew him, and beheaded him, and took his head, and gat them away through the plain all night.
verse	10	4	8	And they brought the head of Ishbosheth unto David to Hebron, and said to the king, Behold the head of Ishbosheth the son of Saul thine enemy, which sought thy life; and the LORD hath avenged my lord the king this day of Saul, and of his seed.
verse	10	4	9	And David answered Rechab and Baanah his brother, the sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, and said unto them, As the LORD liveth, who hath redeemed my soul out of all adversity,
verse	10	4	10	@@When one told me, saying, Behold, Saul is dead, thinking to have brought good tidings, I took hold of him, and slew him in Ziklag, who @9thought@7 that I would have given him a reward for his tidings:
verse	10	4	11	How much more, when wicked men have slain a righteous person in his own house upon his bed? shall I not therefore now require his blood of your hand, and take you away from the earth?
verse	10	4	12	@@And David commanded his young men, and they slew them, and cut off their hands and their feet, and hanged @9them@7 up over the pool in Hebron. But they took the head of Ishbosheth, and buried @9it@7 in the sepulchre of Abner in Hebron.
verse	10	5	1	@@Then came all the tribes of Israel to David unto Hebron, and spake, saying, Behold, we @9are@7 thy bone and thy flesh.
verse	10	5	2	Also in time past, when Saul was king over us, thou wast he that leddest out and broughtest in Israel: and the LORD said to thee, Thou shalt feed my people Israel, and thou shalt be a captain over Israel.
verse	10	5	3	So all the elders of Israel came to the king to Hebron; and king David made a league with them in Hebron before the LORD: and they anointed David king over Israel.
verse	10	5	4	@@David @9was@7 thirty years old when he began to reign, @9and@7 he reigned forty years.
verse	10	5	5	In Hebron he reigned over Judah seven years and six months: and in Jerusalem he reigned thirty and three years over all Israel and Judah.
verse	10	5	6	And the king and his men went to Jerusalem unto the Jebusites, the inhabitants of the land: which spake unto David, saying, Except thou take away the blind and the lame, thou shalt not come in hither: thinking, David cannot come in hither.
verse	10	5	7	@@Nevertheless David took the strong hold of Zion: the same @9is@7 the city of David.
verse	10	5	8	@@And David said on that day, Whosoever getteth up to the gutter, and smiteth the Jebusites, and the lame and the blind, @9that are@7 hated of David's soul, @9he shall be chief and captain.@7 Wherefore they said, The blind and the lame shall not come into the house.
verse	10	5	9	So David dwelt in the fort, and called it the city of David. And David built round about from Millo and inward.
verse	10	5	10	@@And David went on, and grew great, and the LORD God of hosts @9was@7 with him.
verse	10	5	11	And Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David, and cedar trees, and carpenters, and masons: and they built David an house.
verse	10	5	12	And David perceived that the LORD had established him king over Israel, and that he had exalted his kingdom for his people Israel's sake.
verse	10	5	13	@@And David took @9him@7 more concubines and wives out of Jerusalem, after he was come from Hebron: and there were yet sons and daughters born to David.
verse	10	5	14	@@And these @9be@7 the names of those that were born unto him in Jerusalem; Shammua, and Shobab, and Nathan, and Solomon,
verse	10	5	15	Ibhar also, and Elishua, and Nepheg, and Japhia,
verse	10	5	16	And Elishama, and Eliada, and Eliphalet.
verse	10	5	17	@@But when the Philistines heard that they had anointed David king over Israel, all the Philistines came up to seek David; and David heard @9of it,@7 and went down to the hold.
verse	10	5	18	The Philistines also came and spread themselves in the valley of Rephaim.
verse	10	5	19	And David enquired of the LORD, saying, Shall I go up to the Philistines? wilt thou deliver them into mine hand? And the LORD said unto David, Go up: for I will doubtless deliver the Philistines into thine hand.
verse	10	5	20	And David came to Baalperazim, and David smote them there, and said, The LORD hath broken forth upon mine enemies before me, as the breach of waters. Therefore he called the name of that place Baalperazim.
verse	10	5	21	And there they left their images, and David and his men burned them.
verse	10	5	22	And the Philistines came up yet again, and spread themselves in the valley of Rephaim.
verse	10	5	23	@@And when David enquired of the LORD, he said, Thou shalt not go up; @9but@7 fetch a compass behind them, and come upon them over against the mulberry trees.
verse	10	5	24	And let it be, when thou hearest the sound of a going in the tops of the mulberry trees, that then thou shalt bestir thyself: for then shall the LORD go out before thee, to smite the host of the Philistines.
verse	10	5	25	And David did so, as the LORD had commanded him; and smote the Philistines from Geba until thou come to Gazer.
verse	10	6	1	@@Again, David gathered together all @9the@7 chosen @9men@7 of Israel, thirty thousand.
verse	10	6	2	@@And David arose, and went with all the people that @9were@7 with him from Baale of Judah, to bring up from thence the ark of God, whose name is called by the name of the LORD of hosts that dwelleth @9between@7 the cherubims.
verse	10	6	3	@@And they set the ark of God upon a new cart, and brought it out of the house of Abinadab that @9was@7 in Gibeah: and Uzzah and Ahio, the sons of Abinadab, drave the new cart.
verse	10	6	4	@@And they brought it out of the house of Abinadab which @9was@7 at Gibeah, accompanying the ark of God: and Ahio went before the ark.
verse	10	6	5	@@And David and all the house of Israel played before the LORD on all manner of @9instruments made of@7 fir wood, even on harps, and on psalteries, and on timbrels, and on cornets, and on cymbals.
verse	10	6	6	@@And when they came to Nachon's threshingfloor, Uzzah put forth @9his hand@7 to the ark of God, and took hold of it; for the oxen shook @9it. @7
verse	10	6	7	@@And the anger of the LORD was kindled against Uzzah; and God smote him there for @9his@7 error; and there he died by the ark of God.
verse	10	6	8	And David was displeased, because the LORD had made a breach upon Uzzah: and he called the name of the place Perezuzzah to this day.
verse	10	6	9	And David was afraid of the LORD that day, and said, How shall the ark of the LORD come to me?
verse	10	6	10	So David would not remove the ark of the LORD unto him into the city of David: but David carried it aside into the house of Obededom the Gittite.
verse	10	6	11	And the ark of the LORD continued in the house of Obededom the Gittite three months: and the LORD blessed Obededom, and all his household.
verse	10	6	12	@@And it was told king David, saying, The LORD hath blessed the house of Obed-edom, and all that @9pertaineth@7 unto him, because of the ark of God. So David went and brought up the ark of God from the house of Obededom into the city of David with gladness.
verse	10	6	13	@@And it was @9so,@7 that when they that bare the ark of the LORD had gone six paces, he sacrificed oxen and fatlings.
verse	10	6	14	@@And David danced before the LORD with all @9his@7 might; and David @9was@7 girded with a linen ephod.
verse	10	6	15	So David and all the house of Israel brought up the ark of the LORD with shouting, and with the sound of the trumpet.
verse	10	6	16	And as the ark of the LORD came into the city of David, Michal Saul's daughter looked through a window, and saw king David leaping and dancing before the LORD; and she despised him in her heart.
verse	10	6	17	And they brought in the ark of the LORD, and set it in his place, in the midst of the tabernacle that David had pitched for it: and David offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before the LORD.
verse	10	6	18	And as soon as David had made an end of offering burnt offerings and peace offerings, he blessed the people in the name of the LORD of hosts.
verse	10	6	19	@@And he dealt among all the people, @9even@7 among the whole multitude of Israel, as well to the women as men, to every one a cake of bread, and a good piece @9of flesh,@7 and a flagon @9of wine.@7 So all the people departed every one to his house.
verse	10	6	20	Then David returned to bless his household. And Michal the daughter of Saul came out to meet David, and said, How glorious was the king of Israel to day, who uncovered himself to day in the eyes of the handmaids of his servants, as one of the vain fellows shamelessly uncovereth himself!
verse	10	6	21	@@And David said unto Michal, @9It was@7 before the LORD, which chose me before thy father, and before all his house, to appoint me ruler over the people of the LORD, over Israel: therefore will I play before the LORD.
verse	10	6	22	And I will yet be more vile than thus, and will be base in mine own sight: and of the maidservants which thou hast spoken of, of them shall I be had in honour.
verse	10	6	23	Therefore Michal the daughter of Saul had no child unto the day of her death.
verse	10	7	1	And it came to pass, when the king sat in his house, and the LORD had given him rest round about from all his enemies;
verse	10	7	2	That the king said unto Nathan the prophet, See now, I dwell in an house of cedar, but the ark of God dwelleth within curtains.
verse	10	7	3	@@And Nathan said to the king, Go, do all that @9is@7 in thine heart; for the LORD @9is@7 with thee.
verse	10	7	4	And it came to pass that night, that the word of the LORD came unto Nathan, saying,
verse	10	7	5	Go and tell my servant David, Thus saith the LORD, Shalt thou build me an house for me to dwell in?
verse	10	7	6	@@Whereas I have not dwelt in @9any@7 house since the time that I brought up the children of Israel out of Egypt, even to this day, but have walked in a tent and in a tabernacle.
verse	10	7	7	@@In all @9the places@7 wherein I have walked with all the children of Israel spake I a word with any of the tribes of Israel, whom I commanded to feed my people Israel, saying, Why build ye not me an house of cedar?
verse	10	7	8	Now therefore so shalt thou say unto my servant David, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, I took thee from the sheepcote, from following the sheep, to be ruler over my people, over Israel:
verse	10	7	9	@@And I was with thee whithersoever thou wentest, and have cut off all thine enemies out of thy sight, and have made thee a great name, like unto the name of the great @9men@7 that @9are@7 in the earth.
verse	10	7	10	Moreover I will appoint a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, that they may dwell in a place of their own, and move no more; neither shall the children of wickedness afflict them any more, as beforetime,
verse	10	7	11	@@And as since the time that I commanded judges @9to be@7 over my people Israel, and have caused thee to rest from all thine enemies. Also the LORD telleth thee that he will make thee an house.
verse	10	7	12	And when thy days be fulfilled, and thou shalt sleep with thy fathers, I will set up thy seed after thee, which shall proceed out of thy bowels, and I will establish his kingdom.
verse	10	7	13	He shall build an house for my name, and I will stablish the throne of his kingdom for ever.
verse	10	7	14	I will be his father, and he shall be my son. If he commit iniquity, I will chasten him with the rod of men, and with the stripes of the children of men:
verse	10	7	15	@@But my mercy shall not depart away from him, as I took @9it@7 from Saul, whom I put away before thee.
verse	10	7	16	And thine house and thy kingdom shall be established for ever before thee: thy throne shall be established for ever.
verse	10	7	17	According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so did Nathan speak unto David.
verse	10	7	18	@@Then went king David in, and sat before the LORD, and he said, Who @9am@7 I, O Lord GOD? and what @9is@7 my house, that thou hast brought me hitherto?
verse	10	7	19	@@And this was yet a small thing in thy sight, O Lord GOD; but thou hast spoken also of thy servant's house for a great while to come. And @9is@7 this the manner of man, O Lord GOD?
verse	10	7	20	And what can David say more unto thee? for thou, Lord GOD, knowest thy servant.
verse	10	7	21	@@For thy word's sake, and according to thine own heart, hast thou done all these great things, to make thy servant know @9them. @7
verse	10	7	22	@@Wherefore thou art great, O LORD God: for @9there is@7 none like thee, neither @9is there any@7 God beside thee, according to all that we have heard with our ears.
verse	10	7	23	@@And what one nation in the earth @9is@7 like thy people, @9even@7 like Israel, whom God went to redeem for a people to himself, and to make him a name, and to do for you great things and terrible, for thy land, before thy people, which thou redeemedst to thee from Egypt, @9from@7 the nations and their gods?
verse	10	7	24	@@For thou hast confirmed to thyself thy people Israel @9to be@7 a people unto thee for ever: and thou, LORD, art become their God.
verse	10	7	25	@@And now, O LORD God, the word that thou hast spoken concerning thy servant, and concerning his house, establish @9it@7 for ever, and do as thou hast said.
verse	10	7	26	@@And let thy name be magnified for ever, saying, The LORD of hosts @9is@7 the God over Israel: and let the house of thy servant David be established before thee.
verse	10	7	27	For thou, O LORD of hosts, God of Israel, hast revealed to thy servant, saying, I will build thee an house: therefore hath thy servant found in his heart to pray this prayer unto thee.
verse	10	7	28	@@And now, O Lord GOD, thou @9art@7 that God, and thy words be true, and thou hast promised this goodness unto thy servant:
verse	10	7	29	@@Therefore now let it please thee to bless the house of thy servant, that it may continue for ever before thee: for thou, O Lord GOD, hast spoken @9it:@7 and with thy blessing let the house of thy servant be blessed for ever.
verse	10	8	1	And after this it came to pass, that David smote the Philistines, and subdued them: and David took Methegammah out of the hand of the Philistines.
verse	10	8	2	@@And he smote Moab, and measured them with a line, casting them down to the ground; even with two lines measured he to put to death, and with one full line to keep alive. And so the Moabites became David's servants, @9and@7 brought gifts.
verse	10	8	3	David smote also Hadadezer, the son of Rehob, king of Zobah, as he went to recover his border at the river Euphrates.
verse	10	8	4	@@And David took from him a thousand @9chariots,@7 and seven hundred horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen: and David houghed all the chariot @9horses,@7 but reserved of them @9for@7 an hundred chariots.
verse	10	8	5	And when the Syrians of Damascus came to succour Hadadezer king of Zobah, David slew of the Syrians two and twenty thousand men.
verse	10	8	6	@@Then David put garrisons in Syria of Damascus: and the Syrians became servants to David, @9and@7 brought gifts. And the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.
verse	10	8	7	And David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadadezer, and brought them to Jerusalem.
verse	10	8	8	And from Betah, and from Berothai, cities of Hadadezer, king David took exceeding much brass.
verse	10	8	9	When Toi king of Hamath heard that David had smitten all the host of Hadadezer,
verse	10	8	10	@@Then Toi sent Joram his son unto king David, to salute him, and to bless him, because he had fought against Hadadezer, and smitten him: for Hadadezer had wars with Toi. And @9Joram@7 brought with him vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and vessels of brass:
verse	10	8	11	Which also king David did dedicate unto the LORD, with the silver and gold that he had dedicated of all nations which he subdued;
verse	10	8	12	Of Syria, and of Moab, and of the children of Ammon, and of the Philistines, and of Amalek, and of the spoil of Hadadezer, son of Rehob, king of Zobah.
verse	10	8	13	@@And David gat @9him@7 a name when he returned from smiting of the Syrians in the valley of salt, @9being@7 eighteen thousand @9men.@7
verse	10	8	14	And he put garrisons in Edom; throughout all Edom put he garrisons, and all they of Edom became David's servants. And the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.
verse	10	8	15	And David reigned over all Israel; and David executed judgment and justice unto all his people.
verse	10	8	16	@@And Joab the son of Zeruiah @9was@7 over the host; and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud @9was@7 recorder;
verse	10	8	17	@@And Zadok the son of Ahitub, and Ahimelech the son of Abiathar, @9were@7 the priests; and Seraiah @9was@7 the scribe;
verse	10	8	18	@@And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada @9was over@7 both the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and David's sons were chief rulers.
verse	10	9	1	And David said, Is there yet any that is left of the house of Saul, that I may shew him kindness for Jonathan's sake?
verse	10	9	2	@@And @9there was@7 of the house of Saul a servant whose name @9was@7 Ziba. And when they had called him unto David, the king said unto him, @9Art@7 thou Ziba? And he said, Thy servant @9is he. @7
verse	10	9	3	@@And the king said, @9Is@7 there not yet any of the house of Saul, that I may shew the kindness of God unto him? And Ziba said unto the king, Jonathan hath yet a son, @9which is@7 lame on @9his@7 feet.
verse	10	9	4	@@And the king said unto him, Where @9is@7 he? And Ziba said unto the king, Behold, he @9is@7 in the house of Machir, the son of Ammiel, in Lodebar.
verse	10	9	5	Then king David sent, and fetched him out of the house of Machir, the son of Ammiel, from Lodebar.
verse	10	9	6	Now when Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan, the son of Saul, was come unto David, he fell on his face, and did reverence. And David said, Mephibosheth. And he answered, Behold thy servant!
verse	10	9	7	And David said unto him, Fear not: for I will surely shew thee kindness for Jonathan thy father's sake, and will restore thee all the land of Saul thy father; and thou shalt eat bread at my table continually.
verse	10	9	8	@@And he bowed himself, and said, What is thy servant, that thou shouldest look upon such a dead dog as I @9am?@7
verse	10	9	9	Then the king called to Ziba, Saul's servant, and said unto him, I have given unto thy master's son all that pertained to Saul and to all his house.
verse	10	9	10	@@Thou therefore, and thy sons, and thy servants, shall till the land for him, and thou shalt bring in @9the fruits,@7 that thy master's son may have food to eat: but Mephibosheth thy master's son shall eat bread alway at my table. Now Ziba had fifteen sons and twenty servants.
verse	10	9	11	@@Then said Ziba unto the king, According to all that my lord the king hath commanded his servant, so shall thy servant do. As for Mephibosheth, @9said the king,@7 he shall eat at my table, as one of the king's sons.
verse	10	9	12	@@And Mephibosheth had a young son, whose name @9was@7 Micha. And all that dwelt in the house of Ziba @9were@7 servants unto Mephibosheth.
verse	10	9	13	So Mephibosheth dwelt in Jerusalem: for he did eat continually at the king's table; and was lame on both his feet.
verse	10	10	1	And it came to pass after this, that the king of the children of Ammon died, and Hanun his son reigned in his stead.
verse	10	10	2	Then said David, I will shew kindness unto Hanun the son of Nahash, as his father shewed kindness unto me. And David sent to comfort him by the hand of his servants for his father. And David's servants came into the land of the children of Ammon.
verse	10	10	3	@@And the princes of the children of Ammon said unto Hanun their lord, Thinkest thou that David doth honour thy father, that he hath sent comforters unto thee? hath not David @9rather@7 sent his servants unto thee, to search the city, and to spy it out, and to overthrow it?
verse	10	10	4	@@Wherefore Hanun took David's servants, and shaved off the one half of their beards, and cut off their garments in the middle, @9even@7 to their buttocks, and sent them away.
verse	10	10	5	@@When they told @9it@7 unto David, he sent to meet them, because the men were greatly ashamed: and the king said, Tarry at Jericho until your beards be grown, and @9then@7 return.
verse	10	10	6	And when the children of Ammon saw that they stank before David, the children of Ammon sent and hired the Syrians of Bethrehob, and the Syrians of Zoba, twenty thousand footmen, and of king Maacah a thousand men, and of Ishtob twelve thousand men.
verse	10	10	7	@@And when David heard of @9it,@7 he sent Joab, and all the host of the mighty men.
verse	10	10	8	@@And the children of Ammon came out, and put the battle in array at the entering in of the gate: and the Syrians of Zoba, and of Rehob, and Ishtob, and Maacah, @9were@7 by themselves in the field.
verse	10	10	9	@@When Joab saw that the front of the battle was against him before and behind, he chose of all the choice @9men@7 of Israel, and put @9them@7 in array against the Syrians:
verse	10	10	10	@@And the rest of the people he delivered into the hand of Abishai his brother, that he might put @9them@7 in array against the children of Ammon.
verse	10	10	11	And he said, If the Syrians be too strong for me, then thou shalt help me: but if the children of Ammon be too strong for thee, then I will come and help thee.
verse	10	10	12	Be of good courage, and let us play the men for our people, and for the cities of our God: and the LORD do that which seemeth him good.
verse	10	10	13	@@And Joab drew nigh, and the people that @9were@7 with him, unto the battle against the Syrians: and they fled before him.
verse	10	10	14	And when the children of Ammon saw that the Syrians were fled, then fled they also before Abishai, and entered into the city. So Joab returned from the children of Ammon, and came to Jerusalem.
verse	10	10	15	And when the Syrians saw that they were smitten before Israel, they gathered themselves together.
verse	10	10	16	@@And Hadarezer sent, and brought out the Syrians that @9were@7 beyond the river: and they came to Helam; and Shobach the captain of the host of Hadarezer @9went@7 before them.
verse	10	10	17	And when it was told David, he gathered all Israel together, and passed over Jordan, and came to Helam. And the Syrians set themselves in array against David, and fought with him.
verse	10	10	18	@@And the Syrians fled before Israel; and David slew @9the men of@7 seven hundred chariots of the Syrians, and forty thousand horsemen, and smote Shobach the captain of their host, who died there.
verse	10	10	19	@@And when all the kings @9that were@7 servants to Hadarezer saw that they were smitten before Israel, they made peace with Israel, and served them. So the Syrians feared to help the children of Ammon any more.
verse	10	11	1	@@And it came to pass, after the year was expired, at the time when kings go forth @9to battle,@7 that David sent Joab, and his servants with him, and all Israel; and they destroyed the children of Ammon, and besieged Rabbah. But David tarried still at Jerusalem.
verse	10	11	2	@@And it came to pass in an eveningtide, that David arose from off his bed, and walked upon the roof of the king's house: and from the roof he saw a woman washing herself; and the woman @9was@7 very beautiful to look upon.
verse	10	11	3	@@And David sent and enquired after the woman. And @9one@7 said, @9Is@7 not this Bathsheba, the daughter of Eliam, the wife of Uriah the Hittite?
verse	10	11	4	And David sent messengers, and took her; and she came in unto him, and he lay with her; for she was purified from her uncleanness: and she returned unto her house.
verse	10	11	5	@@And the woman conceived, and sent and told David, and said, I @9am@7 with child.
verse	10	11	6	@@And David sent to Joab, @9saying,@7 Send me Uriah the Hittite. And Joab sent Uriah to David.
verse	10	11	7	@@And when Uriah was come unto him, David demanded @9of him@7 how Joab did, and how the people did, and how the war prospered.
verse	10	11	8	@@And David said to Uriah, Go down to thy house, and wash thy feet. And Uriah departed out of the king's house, and there followed him a mess @9of meat@7 from the king.
verse	10	11	9	But Uriah slept at the door of the king's house with all the servants of his lord, and went not down to his house.
verse	10	11	10	@@And when they had told David, saying, Uriah went not down unto his house, David said unto Uriah, Camest thou not from @9thy@7 journey? why @9then@7 didst thou not go down unto thine house?
verse	10	11	11	@@And Uriah said unto David, The ark, and Israel, and Judah, abide in tents; and my lord Joab, and the servants of my lord, are encamped in the open fields; shall I then go into mine house, to eat and to drink, and to lie with my wife? @9as@7 thou livest, and @9as@7 thy soul liveth, I will not do this thing.
verse	10	11	12	And David said to Uriah, Tarry here to day also, and to morrow I will let thee depart. So Uriah abode in Jerusalem that day, and the morrow.
verse	10	11	13	And when David had called him, he did eat and drink before him; and he made him drunk: and at even he went out to lie on his bed with the servants of his lord, but went not down to his house.
verse	10	11	14	@@And it came to pass in the morning, that David wrote a letter to Joab, and sent @9it@7 by the hand of Uriah.
verse	10	11	15	And he wrote in the letter, saying, Set ye Uriah in the forefront of the hottest battle, and retire ye from him, that he may be smitten, and die.
verse	10	11	16	@@And it came to pass, when Joab observed the city, that he assigned Uriah unto a place where he knew that valiant men @9were. @7
verse	10	11	17	@@And the men of the city went out, and fought with Joab: and there fell @9some@7 of the people of the servants of David; and Uriah the Hittite died also.
verse	10	11	18	Then Joab sent and told David all the things concerning the war;
verse	10	11	19	And charged the messenger, saying, When thou hast made an end of telling the matters of the war unto the king,
verse	10	11	20	And if so be that the king's wrath arise, and he say unto thee, Wherefore approached ye so nigh unto the city when ye did fight? knew ye not that they would shoot from the wall?
verse	10	11	21	Who smote Abimelech the son of Jerubbesheth? did not a woman cast a piece of a millstone upon him from the wall, that he died in Thebez? why went ye nigh the wall? then say thou, Thy servant Uriah the Hittite is dead also.
verse	10	11	22	So the messenger went, and came and shewed David all that Joab had sent him for.
verse	10	11	23	And the messenger said unto David, Surely the men prevailed against us, and came out unto us into the field, and we were upon them even unto the entering of the gate.
verse	10	11	24	@@And the shooters shot from off the wall upon thy servants; and @9some@7 of the king's servants be dead, and thy servant Uriah the Hittite is dead also.
verse	10	11	25	Then David said unto the messenger, Thus shalt thou say unto Joab, Let not this thing displease thee, for the sword devoureth one as well as another: make thy battle more strong against the city, and overthrow it: and encourage thou him.
verse	10	11	26	And when the wife of Uriah heard that Uriah her husband was dead, she mourned for her husband.
verse	10	11	27	And when the mourning was past, David sent and fetched her to his house, and she became his wife, and bare him a son. But the thing that David had done displeased the LORD.
verse	10	12	1	And the LORD sent Nathan unto David. And he came unto him, and said unto him, There were two men in one city; the one rich, and the other poor.
verse	10	12	2	@@The rich @9man@7 had exceeding many flocks and herds:
verse	10	12	3	@@But the poor @9man@7 had nothing, save one little ewe lamb, which he had bought and nourished up: and it grew up together with him, and with his children; it did eat of his own meat, and drank of his own cup, and lay in his bosom, and was unto him as a daughter.
verse	10	12	4	And there came a traveller unto the rich man, and he spared to take of his own flock and of his own herd, to dress for the wayfaring man that was come unto him; but took the poor man's lamb, and dressed it for the man that was come to him.
verse	10	12	5	@@And David's anger was greatly kindled against the man; and he said to Nathan, As the LORD liveth, the man that hath done this @9thing@7 shall surely die:
verse	10	12	6	And he shall restore the lamb fourfold, because he did this thing, and because he had no pity.
verse	10	12	7	@@And Nathan said to David, Thou @9art@7 the man. Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, I anointed thee king over Israel, and I delivered thee out of the hand of Saul;
verse	10	12	8	@@And I gave thee thy master's house, and thy master's wives into thy bosom, and gave thee the house of Israel and of Judah; and if @9that had been@7 too little, I would moreover have given unto thee such and such things.
verse	10	12	9	@@Wherefore hast thou despised the commandment of the LORD, to do evil in his sight? thou hast killed Uriah the Hittite with the sword, and hast taken his wife @9to be@7 thy wife, and hast slain him with the sword of the children of Ammon.
verse	10	12	10	Now therefore the sword shall never depart from thine house; because thou hast despised me, and hast taken the wife of Uriah the Hittite to be thy wife.
verse	10	12	11	@@Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will raise up evil against thee out of thine own house, and I will take thy wives before thine eyes, and give @9them@7 unto thy neighbour, and he shall lie with thy wives in the sight of this sun.
verse	10	12	12	@@For thou didst @9it@7 secretly: but I will do this thing before all Israel, and before the sun.
verse	10	12	13	And David said unto Nathan, I have sinned against the LORD. And Nathan said unto David, The LORD also hath put away thy sin; thou shalt not die.
verse	10	12	14	@@Howbeit, because by this deed thou hast given great occasion to the enemies of the LORD to blaspheme, the child also @9that is@7 born unto thee shall surely die.
verse	10	12	15	And Nathan departed unto his house. And the LORD struck the child that Uriah's wife bare unto David, and it was very sick.
verse	10	12	16	David therefore besought God for the child; and David fasted, and went in, and lay all night upon the earth.
verse	10	12	17	@@And the elders of his house arose, @9and went@7 to him, to raise him up from the earth: but he would not, neither did he eat bread with them.
verse	10	12	18	And it came to pass on the seventh day, that the child died. And the servants of David feared to tell him that the child was dead: for they said, Behold, while the child was yet alive, we spake unto him, and he would not hearken unto our voice: how will he then vex himself, if we tell him that the child is dead?
verse	10	12	19	But when David saw that his servants whispered, David perceived that the child was dead: therefore David said unto his servants, Is the child dead? And they said, He is dead.
verse	10	12	20	@@Then David arose from the earth, and washed, and anointed @9himself,@7 and changed his apparel, and came into the house of the LORD, and worshipped: then he came to his own house; and when he required, they set bread before him, and he did eat.
verse	10	12	21	@@Then said his servants unto him, What thing @9is@7 this that thou hast done? thou didst fast and weep for the child, @9while it was@7 alive; but when the child was dead, thou didst rise and eat bread.
verse	10	12	22	@@And he said, While the child was yet alive, I fasted and wept: for I said, Who can tell @9whether@7 GOD will be gracious to me, that the child may live?
verse	10	12	23	But now he is dead, wherefore should I fast? can I bring him back again? I shall go to him, but he shall not return to me.
verse	10	12	24	And David comforted Bathsheba his wife, and went in unto her, and lay with her: and she bare a son, and he called his name Solomon: and the LORD loved him.
verse	10	12	25	And he sent by the hand of Nathan the prophet; and he called his name Jedidiah, because of the LORD.
verse	10	12	26	And Joab fought against Rabbah of the children of Ammon, and took the royal city.
verse	10	12	27	And Joab sent messengers to David, and said, I have fought against Rabbah, and have taken the city of waters.
verse	10	12	28	Now therefore gather the rest of the people together, and encamp against the city, and take it: lest I take the city, and it be called after my name.
verse	10	12	29	And David gathered all the people together, and went to Rabbah, and fought against it, and took it.
verse	10	12	30	@@And he took their king's crown from off his head, the weight whereof @9was@7 a talent of gold with the precious stones: and it was @9set@7 on David's head. And he brought forth the spoil of the city in great abundance.
verse	10	12	31	@@And he brought forth the people that @9were@7 therein, and put @9them@7 under saws, and under harrows of iron, and under axes of iron, and made them pass through the brickkiln: and thus did he unto all the cities of the children of Ammon. So David and all the people returned unto Jerusalem.
verse	10	13	1	@@And it came to pass after this, that Absalom the son of David had a fair sister, whose name @9was@7 Tamar; and Amnon the son of David loved her.
verse	10	13	2	@@And Amnon was so vexed, that he fell sick for his sister Tamar; for she @9was@7 a virgin; and Amnon thought it hard for him to do any thing to her.
verse	10	13	3	@@But Amnon had a friend, whose name @9was@7 Jonadab, the son of Shimeah David's brother: and Jonadab @9was@7 a very subtil man.
verse	10	13	4	@@And he said unto him, Why @9art@7 thou, @9being@7 the king's son, lean from day to day? wilt thou not tell me? And Amnon said unto him, I love Tamar, my brother Absalom's sister.
verse	10	13	5	@@And Jonadab said unto him, Lay thee down on thy bed, and make thyself sick: and when thy father cometh to see thee, say unto him, I pray thee, let my sister Tamar come, and give me meat, and dress the meat in my sight, that I may see @9it,@7 and eat @9it@7 at her hand.
verse	10	13	6	So Amnon lay down, and made himself sick: and when the king was come to see him, Amnon said unto the king, I pray thee, let Tamar my sister come, and make me a couple of cakes in my sight, that I may eat at her hand.
verse	10	13	7	Then David sent home to Tamar, saying, Go now to thy brother Amnon's house, and dress him meat.
verse	10	13	8	@@So Tamar went to her brother Amnon's house; and he was laid down. And she took flour, and kneaded @9it,@7 and made cakes in his sight, and did bake the cakes.
verse	10	13	9	@@And she took a pan, and poured @9them@7 out before him; but he refused to eat. And Amnon said, Have out all men from me. And they went out every man from him.
verse	10	13	10	@@And Amnon said unto Tamar, Bring the meat into the chamber, that I may eat of thine hand. And Tamar took the cakes which she had made, and brought @9them@7 into the chamber to Amnon her brother.
verse	10	13	11	@@And when she had brought @9them@7 unto him to eat, he took hold of her, and said unto her, Come lie with me, my sister.
verse	10	13	12	And she answered him, Nay, my brother, do not force me; for no such thing ought to be done in Israel: do not thou this folly.
