verse	10	13	14	Howbeit he would not hearken unto her voice: but, being stronger than she, forced her, and lay with her.
verse	10	13	15	@@Then Amnon hated her exceedingly; so that the hatred wherewith he hated her @9was@7 greater than the love wherewith he had loved her. And Amnon said unto her, Arise, be gone.
verse	10	13	16	@@And she said unto him, @9There is@7 no cause: this evil in sending me away @9is@7 greater than the other that thou didst unto me. But he would not hearken unto her.
verse	10	13	17	@@Then he called his servant that ministered unto him, and said, Put now this @9woman@7 out from me, and bolt the door after her.
verse	10	13	18	@@And @9she had@7 a garment of divers colours upon her: for with such robes were the king's daughters @9that were@7 virgins apparelled. Then his servant brought her out, and bolted the door after her.
verse	10	13	19	@@And Tamar put ashes on her head, and rent her garment of divers colours that @9was@7 on her, and laid her hand on her head, and went on crying.
verse	10	13	20	@@And Absalom her brother said unto her, Hath Amnon thy brother been with thee? but hold now thy peace, my sister: he @9is@7 thy brother; regard not this thing. So Tamar remained desolate in her brother Absalom's house.
verse	10	13	21	But when king David heard of all these things, he was very wroth.
verse	10	13	22	And Absalom spake unto his brother Amnon neither good nor bad: for Absalom hated Amnon, because he had forced his sister Tamar.
verse	10	13	23	@@And it came to pass after two full years, that Absalom had sheepshearers in Baalhazor, which @9is@7 beside Ephraim: and Absalom invited all the king's sons.
