verse	10	14	1	@@Now Joab the son of Zeruiah perceived that the king's heart @9was@7 toward Absalom.
verse	10	14	2	And Joab sent to Tekoah, and fetched thence a wise woman, and said unto her, I pray thee, feign thyself to be a mourner, and put on now mourning apparel, and anoint not thyself with oil, but be as a woman that had a long time mourned for the dead:
verse	10	14	3	And come to the king, and speak on this manner unto him. So Joab put the words in her mouth.
verse	10	14	4	And when the woman of Tekoah spake to the king, she fell on her face to the ground, and did obeisance, and said, Help, O king.
verse	10	14	5	@@And the king said unto her, What aileth thee? And she answered, I @9am@7 indeed a widow woman, and mine husband is dead.
verse	10	14	6	@@And thy handmaid had two sons, and they two strove together in the field, and @9there was@7 none to part them, but the one smote the other, and slew him.
verse	10	14	7	@@And, behold, the whole family is risen against thine handmaid, and they said, Deliver him that smote his brother, that we may kill him, for the life of his brother whom he slew; and we will destroy the heir also: and so they shall quench my coal which is left, and shall not leave to my husband @9neither@7 name nor remainder upon the earth.
verse	10	14	8	And the king said unto the woman, Go to thine house, and I will give charge concerning thee.
verse	10	14	9	@@And the woman of Tekoah said unto the king, My lord, O king, the iniquity @9be@7 on me, and on my father's house: and the king and his throne @9be@7 guiltless.
verse	10	14	10	@@And the king said, Whosoever saith @9ought@7 unto thee, bring him to me, and he shall not touch thee any more.
verse	10	14	11	Then said she, I pray thee, let the king remember the LORD thy God, that thou wouldest not suffer the revengers of blood to destroy any more, lest they destroy my son. And he said, As the LORD liveth, there shall not one hair of thy son fall to the earth.
verse	10	14	12	@@Then the woman said, Let thine handmaid, I pray thee, speak @9one@7 word unto my lord the king. And he said, Say on.
verse	10	14	13	And the woman said, Wherefore then hast thou thought such a thing against the people of God? for the king doth speak this thing as one which is faulty, in that the king doth not fetch home again his banished.
verse	10	14	14	@@For we must needs die, and @9are@7 as water spilt on the ground, which cannot be gathered up again; neither doth God respect @9any@7 person: yet doth he devise means, that his banished be not expelled from him.
verse	10	14	15	@@Now therefore that I am come to speak of this thing unto my lord the king, @9it is@7 because the people have made me afraid: and thy handmaid said, I will now speak unto the king; it may be that the king will perform the request of his handmaid.
verse	10	14	16	@@For the king will hear, to deliver his handmaid out of the hand of the man @9that would@7 destroy me and my son together out of the inheritance of God.
verse	10	14	17	@@Then thine handmaid said, The word of my lord the king shall now be comfortable: for as an angel of God, so @9is@7 my lord the king to discern good and bad: therefore the LORD thy God will be with thee.
verse	10	14	18	Then the king answered and said unto the woman, Hide not from me, I pray thee, the thing that I shall ask thee. And the woman said, Let my lord the king now speak.
verse	10	14	19	@@And the king said, @9Is not@7 the hand of Joab with thee in all this? And the woman answered and said, @9As@7 thy soul liveth, my lord the king, none can turn to the right hand or to the left from ought that my lord the king hath spoken: for thy servant Joab, he bade me, and he put all these words in the mouth of thine handmaid:
verse	10	14	20	@@To fetch about this form of speech hath thy servant Joab done this thing: and my lord @9is@7 wise, according to the wisdom of an angel of God, to know all @9things@7 that @9are@7 in the earth.
verse	10	14	21	And the king said unto Joab, Behold now, I have done this thing: go therefore, bring the young man Absalom again.
