verse	10	14	25	But in all Israel there was none to be so much praised as Absalom for his beauty: from the sole of his foot even to the crown of his head there was no blemish in him.
verse	10	14	26	@@And when he polled his head, (for it was at every year's end that he polled @9it:@7 because @9the hair@7 was heavy on him, therefore he polled it:) he weighed the hair of his head at two hundred shekels after the king's weight.
verse	10	14	27	@@And unto Absalom there were born three sons, and one daughter, whose name @9was@7 Tamar: she was a woman of a fair countenance.
