verse	10	16	1	@@And when David was a little past the top @9of the hill,@7 behold, Ziba the servant of Mephibosheth met him, with a couple of asses saddled, and upon them two hundred @9loaves@7 of bread, and an hundred bunches of raisins, and an hundred of summer fruits, and a bottle of wine.
verse	10	16	2	@@And the king said unto Ziba, What meanest thou by these? And Ziba said, The asses @9be@7 for the king's household to ride on; and the bread and summer fruit for the young men to eat; and the wine, that such as be faint in the wilderness may drink.
