verse	10	20	5	@@So Amasa went to assemble @9the men of@7 Judah: but he tarried longer than the set time which he had appointed him.
verse	10	20	6	@@And David said to Abishai, Now shall Sheba the son of Bichri do us more harm than @9did@7 Absalom: take thou thy lord's servants, and pursue after him, lest he get him fenced cities, and escape us.
verse	10	20	7	And there went out after him Joab's men, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, and all the mighty men: and they went out of Jerusalem, to pursue after Sheba the son of Bichri.
verse	10	20	8	@@When they @9were@7 at the great stone which @9is@7 in Gibeon, Amasa went before them. And Joab's garment that he had put on was girded unto him, and upon it a girdle @9with@7 a sword fastened upon his loins in the sheath thereof; and as he went forth it fell out.
verse	10	20	9	@@And Joab said to Amasa, @9Art@7 thou in health, my brother? And Joab took Amasa by the beard with the right hand to kiss him.
verse	10	20	10	@@But Amasa took no heed to the sword that @9was@7 in Joab's hand: so he smote him therewith in the fifth @9rib,@7 and shed out his bowels to the ground, and struck him not again; and he died. So Joab and Abishai his brother pursued after Sheba the son of Bichri.
verse	10	20	11	@@And one of Joab's men stood by him, and said, He that favoureth Joab, and he that @9is@7 for David, @9let him go@7 after Joab.
verse	10	20	12	And Amasa wallowed in blood in the midst of the highway. And when the man saw that all the people stood still, he removed Amasa out of the highway into the field, and cast a cloth upon him, when he saw that every one that came by him stood still.
verse	10	20	13	When he was removed out of the highway, all the people went on after Joab, to pursue after Sheba the son of Bichri.
verse	10	20	14	And he went through all the tribes of Israel unto Abel, and to Bethmaachah, and all the Berites: and they were gathered together, and went also after him.
verse	10	20	15	@@And they came and besieged him in Abel of Bethmaachah, and they cast up a bank against the city, and it stood in the trench: and all the people that @9were@7 with Joab battered the wall, to throw it down.
verse	10	20	16	Then cried a wise woman out of the city, Hear, hear; say, I pray you, unto Joab, Come near hither, that I may speak with thee.
verse	10	20	17	@@And when he was come near unto her, the woman said, @9Art@7 thou Joab? And he answered, I @9am he.@7 Then she said unto him, Hear the words of thine handmaid. And he answered, I do hear.
verse	10	20	18	@@Then she spake, saying, They were wont to speak in old time, saying, They shall surely ask @9counsel@7 at Abel: and so they ended @9the matter. @7
verse	10	20	19	@@I @9am one of them that are@7 peaceable @9and@7 faithful in Israel: thou seekest to destroy a city and a mother in Israel: why wilt thou swallow up the inheritance of the LORD?
verse	10	20	20	And Joab answered and said, Far be it, far be it from me, that I should swallow up or destroy.
verse	10	20	21	@@The matter @9is@7 not so: but a man of mount Ephraim, Sheba the son of Bichri by name, hath lifted up his hand against the king, @9even@7 against David: deliver him only, and I will depart from the city. And the woman said unto Joab, Behold, his head shall be thrown to thee over the wall.
verse	10	20	22	@@Then the woman went unto all the people in her wisdom. And they cut off the head of Sheba the son of Bichri, and cast @9it@7 out to Joab. And he blew a trumpet, and they retired from the city, every man to his tent. And Joab returned to Jerusalem unto the king.
verse	10	20	23	@@Now Joab @9was@7 over all the host of Israel: and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada @9was@7 over the Cherethites and over the Pelethites:
