verse	10	20	26	And Ira also the Jairite was a chief ruler about David.
verse	10	21	1	@@Then there was a famine in the days of David three years, year after year; and David enquired of the LORD. And the LORD answered, @9It is@7 for Saul, and for @9his@7 bloody house, because he slew the Gibeonites.
verse	10	21	2	@@And the king called the Gibeonites, and said unto them; (now the Gibeonites @9were@7 not of the children of Israel, but of the remnant of the Amorites; and the children of Israel had sworn unto them: and Saul sought to slay them in his zeal to the children of Israel and Judah.)
verse	10	21	3	Wherefore David said unto the Gibeonites, What shall I do for you? and wherewith shall I make the atonement, that ye may bless the inheritance of the LORD?
verse	10	21	4	@@And the Gibeonites said unto him, We will have no silver nor gold of Saul, nor of his house; neither for us shalt thou kill any man in Israel. And he said, What ye shall say, @9that@7 will I do for you.
verse	10	21	5	@@And they answered the king, The man that consumed us, and that devised against us @9that@7 we should be destroyed from remaining in any of the coasts of Israel,
verse	10	21	6	@@Let seven men of his sons be delivered unto us, and we will hang them up unto the LORD in Gibeah of Saul, @9whom@7 the LORD did choose. And the king said, I will give @9them. @7
verse	10	21	7	@@But the king spared Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan the son of Saul, because of the LORD'S oath that @9was@7 between them, between David and Jonathan the son of Saul.
verse	10	21	8	But the king took the two sons of Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, whom she bare unto Saul, Armoni and Mephibosheth; and the five sons of Michal the daughter of Saul, whom she brought up for Adriel the son of Barzillai the Meholathite:
verse	10	21	9	@@And he delivered them into the hands of the Gibeonites, and they hanged them in the hill before the LORD: and they fell @9all@7 seven together, and were put to death in the days of harvest, in the first @9days,@7 in the beginning of barley harvest.
verse	10	21	10	And Rizpah the daughter of Aiah took sackcloth, and spread it for her upon the rock, from the beginning of harvest until water dropped upon them out of heaven, and suffered neither the birds of the air to rest on them by day, nor the beasts of the field by night.
verse	10	21	11	And it was told David what Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, the concubine of Saul, had done.
verse	10	21	12	And David went and took the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son from the men of  Jabeshgilead, which had stolen them from the street of Bethshan, where the Philistines had hanged them, when the Philistines had slain Saul in Gilboa:
verse	10	21	13	And he brought up from thence the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son; and they gathered the bones of them that were hanged.
verse	10	21	14	And the bones of Saul and Jonathan his son buried they in the country of Benjamin in Zelah, in the sepulchre of Kish his father: and they performed all that the king commanded. And after that God was intreated for the land.
verse	10	21	15	Moreover the Philistines had yet war again with Israel; and David went down, and his servants with him, and fought against the Philistines: and David waxed faint.
verse	10	21	16	@@And Ishbibenob, which @9was@7 of the sons of the giant, the weight of whose spear @9weighed@7 three hundred @9shekels@7 of brass in weight, he being girded with a new @9sword,@7 thought to have slain David.
verse	10	21	17	But Abishai the son of Zeruiah succoured him, and smote the Philistine, and killed him. Then the men of David sware unto him, saying, Thou shalt go no more out with us to battle, that thou quench not the light of Israel.
verse	10	21	18	@@And it came to pass after this, that there was again a battle with the Philistines at Gob: then Sibbechai the Hushathite slew Saph, which @9was@7 of the sons of the giant.
verse	10	21	19	@@And there was again a battle in Gob with the Philistines, where Elhanan the son of Jaareoregim, a Bethlehemite, slew @9the brother of@7 Goliath the Gittite, the staff of whose spear @9was@7 like a weaver's beam.
verse	10	21	20	@@And there was yet a battle in Gath, where was a man of @9great@7 stature, that had on every hand six fingers, and on every foot six toes, four and twenty in number; and he also was born to the giant.
verse	10	21	21	And when he defied Israel, Jonathan the son of Shimea the brother of David slew him.
verse	10	21	22	These four were born to the giant in Gath, and fell by the hand of David, and by the hand of his servants.
verse	10	22	1	@@And David spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day @9that@7 the LORD had delivered him out of the hand of all his enemies, and out of the hand of Saul:
verse	10	22	2	@@And he said, The LORD @9is@7 my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer;
verse	10	22	3	@@The God of my rock; in him will I trust: @9he is@7 my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my high tower, and my refuge, my saviour; thou savest me from violence.
verse	10	22	4	@@I will call on the LORD, @9who is@7 worthy to be praised: so shall I be saved from mine enemies.
verse	10	22	5	When the waves of death compassed me, the floods of ungodly men made me afraid;
verse	10	22	6	The sorrows of hell compassed me about; the snares of death prevented me;
verse	10	22	7	@@In my distress I called upon the LORD, and cried to my God: and he did hear my voice out of his temple, and my cry @9did enter@7 into his ears.
verse	10	22	8	Then the earth shook and trembled; the foundations of heaven moved and shook, because he was wroth.
verse	10	22	9	There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.
verse	10	22	10	@@He bowed the heavens also, and came down; and darkness @9was@7 under his feet.
verse	10	22	11	And he rode upon a cherub, and did fly: and he was seen upon the wings of the wind.
verse	10	22	12	@@And he made darkness pavilions round about him, dark waters, @9and@7 thick clouds of the skies.
verse	10	22	13	Through the brightness before him were coals of fire kindled.
verse	10	22	14	The LORD thundered from heaven, and the most High uttered his voice.
verse	10	22	15	And he sent out arrows, and scattered them; lightning, and discomfited them.
verse	10	22	16	And the channels of the sea appeared, the foundations of the world were discovered, at the rebuking of the LORD, at the blast of the breath of his nostrils.
verse	10	22	17	He sent from above, he took me; he drew me out of many waters;
verse	10	22	18	@@He delivered me from my strong enemy, @9and@7 from them that hated me: for they were too strong for me.
verse	10	22	19	They prevented me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD was my stay.
verse	10	22	20	He brought me forth also into a large place: he delivered me, because he delighted in me.
verse	10	22	21	The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness: according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.
verse	10	22	22	For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.
verse	10	22	23	@@For all his judgments @9were@7 before me: and @9as for@7 his statutes, I did not depart from them.
verse	10	22	24	I was also upright before him, and have kept myself from mine iniquity.
verse	10	22	25	Therefore the LORD hath recompensed me according to my righteousness; according to my cleanness in his eye sight.
verse	10	22	26	@@With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful, @9and@7 with the upright man thou wilt shew thyself upright.
verse	10	22	27	With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure; and with the froward thou wilt shew thyself unsavoury.
verse	10	22	28	@@And the afflicted people thou wilt save: but thine eyes @9are@7 upon the haughty, @9that@7 thou mayest bring @9them@7 down.
verse	10	22	29	@@For thou @9art@7 my lamp, O LORD: and the LORD will lighten my darkness.
verse	10	22	30	For by thee I have run through a troop: by my God have I leaped over a wall.
verse	10	22	31	@@@9As for@7 God, his way @9is@7 perfect; the word of the LORD @9is@7 tried: he @9is@7 a buckler to all them that trust in him.
verse	10	22	32	@@For who @9is@7 God, save the LORD? and who @9is@7 a rock, save our God?
verse	10	22	33	@@God @9is@7 my strength @9and@7 power: and he maketh my way perfect.
verse	10	22	34	@@He maketh my feet like hinds' @9feet:@7 and setteth me upon my high places.
verse	10	22	35	He teacheth my hands to war; so that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.
verse	10	22	36	Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy gentleness hath made me great.
verse	10	22	37	Thou hast enlarged my steps under me; so that my feet did not slip.
verse	10	22	38	I have pursued mine enemies, and destroyed them; and turned not again until I had consumed them.
verse	10	22	39	And I have consumed them, and wounded them, that they could not arise: yea, they are fallen under my feet.
verse	10	22	40	For thou hast girded me with strength to battle: them that rose up against me hast thou subdued under me.
verse	10	22	41	Thou hast also given me the necks of mine enemies, that I might destroy them that hate me.
verse	10	22	42	@@They looked, but @9there was@7 none to save; @9even@7 unto the LORD, but he answered them not.
verse	10	22	43	@@Then did I beat them as small as the dust of the earth, I did stamp them as the mire of the street, @9and@7 did spread them abroad.
verse	10	22	44	@@Thou also hast delivered me from the strivings of my people, thou hast kept me @9to be@7 head of the heathen: a people @9which@7 I knew not shall serve me.
verse	10	22	45	Strangers shall submit themselves unto me: as soon as they hear, they shall be obedient unto me.
verse	10	22	46	Strangers shall fade away, and they shall be afraid out of their close places.
verse	10	22	47	@@The LORD liveth; and blessed @9be@7 my rock; and exalted be the God of the rock of my salvation.
verse	10	22	48	@@It @9is@7 God that avengeth me, and that bringeth down the people under me,
verse	10	22	49	And that bringeth me forth from mine enemies: thou also hast lifted me up on high above them that rose up against me: thou hast delivered me from the violent man.
verse	10	22	50	Therefore I will give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the heathen, and I will sing praises unto thy name.
verse	10	22	51	@@@9He is@7 the tower of salvation for his king: and sheweth mercy to his anointed, unto David, and to his seed for evermore.
verse	10	23	1	@@Now these @9be@7 the last words of David. David the son of Jesse said, and the man @9who was@7 raised up on high, the anointed of the God of Jacob, and the sweet psalmist of Israel, said,
verse	10	23	2	@@The Spirit of the LORD spake by me, and his word @9was@7 in my tongue.
verse	10	23	3	@@The God of Israel said, the Rock of Israel spake to me, He that ruleth over men @9must be@7 just, ruling in the fear of God.
verse	10	23	4	@@And @9he shall be@7 as the light of the morning, @9when@7 the sun riseth, @9even@7 a morning without clouds; @9as@7 the tender grass @9springing@7 out of the earth by clear shining after rain.
verse	10	23	5	@@Although my house @9be@7 not so with God; yet he hath made with me an everlasting covenant, ordered in all @9things,@7 and sure: for @9this is@7 all my salvation, and all @9my@7 desire, although he make @9it@7 not to grow.
verse	10	23	6	@@But @9the sons@7 of Belial @9shall be@7 all of them as thorns thrust away, because they cannot be taken with hands:
verse	10	23	7	@@But the man @9that@7 shall touch them must be fenced with iron and the staff of a spear; and they shall be utterly burned with fire in the @9same@7 place.
verse	10	23	8	@@These @9be@7 the names of the mighty men whom David had: The Tachmonite that sat in the seat, chief among the captains; the same @9was@7 Adino the Eznite: @9he lift up his spear@7 against eight hundred, whom he slew at one time.
verse	10	23	9	@@And after him @9was@7 Eleazar the son of Dodo the Ahohite, @9one@7 of the three mighty men with David, when they defied the Philistines @9that@7 were there gathered together to battle, and the men of Israel were gone away:
verse	10	23	10	He arose, and smote the Philistines until his hand was weary, and his hand clave unto the sword: and the LORD wrought a great victory that day; and the people returned after him only to spoil.
verse	10	23	11	@@And after him @9was@7 Shammah the son of Agee the Hararite. And the Philistines were gathered together into a troop, where was a piece of ground full of lentiles: and the people fled from the Philistines.
verse	10	23	12	But he stood in the midst of the ground, and defended it, and slew the Philistines: and the LORD wrought a great victory.
verse	10	23	13	And three of the thirty chief went down, and came to David in the harvest time unto the cave of Adullam: and the troop of the Philistines pitched in the valley of Rephaim.
verse	10	23	14	@@And David @9was@7 then in an hold, and the garrison of the Philistines @9was@7 then @9in@7 Bethlehem.
verse	10	23	15	@@And David longed, and said, Oh that one would give me drink of the water of the well of Bethlehem, which @9is@7 by the gate!
verse	10	23	16	@@And the three mighty men brake through the host of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Bethlehem, that @9was@7 by the gate, and took @9it,@7 and brought @9it@7 to David: nevertheless he would not drink thereof, but poured it out unto the LORD.
verse	10	23	17	@@And he said, Be it far from me, O LORD, that I should do this: @9is not this@7 the blood of the men that went in jeopardy of their lives? therefore he would not drink it. These things did these three mighty men.
verse	10	23	18	@@And Abishai, the brother of Joab, the son of Zeruiah, was chief among three. And he lifted up his spear against three hundred, @9and@7 slew @9them,@7 and had the name among three.
verse	10	23	19	@@Was he not most honourable of three? therefore he was their captain: howbeit he attained not unto the @9first@7 three.
verse	10	23	20	And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son of a valiant man, of Kabzeel, who had done many acts, he slew two lionlike men of Moab: he went down also and slew a lion in the midst of a pit in time of snow:
verse	10	23	21	And he slew an Egyptian, a goodly man: and the Egyptian had a spear in his hand; but he went down to him with a staff, and plucked the spear out of the Egyptian's hand, and slew him with his own spear.
verse	10	23	22	@@These @9things@7 did Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and had the name among three mighty men.
