verse	10	24	1	And again the anger of the LORD was kindled against Israel, and he moved David against them to say, Go, number Israel and Judah.
verse	10	24	2	@@For the king said to Joab the captain of the host, which @9was@7 with him, Go now through all the tribes of Israel, from Dan even to Beersheba, and number ye the people, that I may know the number of the people.
verse	10	24	3	@@And Joab said unto the king, Now the LORD thy God add unto the people, how many soever they be, an hundredfold, and that the eyes of my lord the king may see @9it:@7 but why doth my lord the king delight in this thing?
verse	10	24	4	Notwithstanding the king's word prevailed against Joab, and against the captains of the host. And Joab and the captains of the host went out from the presence of the king, to number the people of Israel.
verse	10	24	5	@@And they passed over Jordan, and pitched in Aroer, on the right side of the city that @9lieth@7 in the midst of the river of Gad, and toward Jazer:
verse	10	24	6	Then they came to Gilead, and to the land of Tahtimhodshi; and they came to Danjaan, and about to Zidon,
verse	10	24	7	@@And came to the strong hold of Tyre, and to all the cities of the Hivites, and of the Canaanites: and they went out to the south of Judah, @9even@7 to Beersheba.
verse	10	24	8	So when they had gone through all the land, they came to Jerusalem at the end of nine months and twenty days.
verse	10	24	9	@@And Joab gave up the sum of the number of the people unto the king: and there were in Israel eight hundred thousand valiant men that drew the sword; and the men of Judah @9were@7 five hundred thousand men.
verse	10	24	10	And David's heart smote him after that he had numbered the people. And David said unto the LORD, I have sinned greatly in that I have done: and now, I beseech thee, O LORD, take away the iniquity of thy servant; for I have done very foolishly.
verse	10	24	11	For when David was up in the morning, the word of the LORD came unto the prophet Gad, David's seer, saying,
verse	10	24	12	@@Go and say unto David, Thus saith the LORD, I offer thee three @9things;@7 choose thee one of them, that I may @9do it@7 unto thee.
verse	10	24	13	So Gad came to David, and told him, and said unto him, Shall seven years of famine come unto thee in thy land? or wilt thou flee three months before thine enemies, while they pursue thee? or that there be three days' pestilence in thy land? now advise, and see what answer I shall return to him that sent me.
verse	10	24	14	@@And David said unto Gad, I am in a great strait: let us fall now into the hand of the LORD; for his mercies @9are@7 great: and let me not fall into the hand of man.
verse	10	24	15	So the LORD sent a pestilence upon Israel from the morning even to the time appointed: and there died of the people from Dan even to Beersheba seventy thousand men.
verse	10	24	16	And when the angel stretched out his hand upon Jerusalem to destroy it, the LORD repented him of the evil, and said to the angel that destroyed the people, It is enough: stay now thine hand. And the angel of the LORD was by the threshingplace of Araunah the Jebusite.
verse	10	24	17	And David spake unto the LORD when he saw the angel that smote the people, and said, Lo, I have sinned, and I have done wickedly: but these sheep, what have they done? let thine hand, I pray thee, be against me, and against my father's house.
verse	10	24	18	And Gad came that day to David, and said unto him, Go up, rear an altar unto the LORD in the threshingfloor of Araunah the Jebusite.
verse	10	24	19	And David, according to the saying of Gad, went up as the LORD commanded.
verse	10	24	20	And Araunah looked, and saw the king and his servants coming on toward him: and Araunah went out, and bowed himself before the king on his face upon the ground.
verse	10	24	21	And Araunah said, Wherefore is my lord the king come to his servant? And David said, To buy the threshingfloor of thee, to build an altar unto the LORD, that the plague may be stayed from the people.
verse	10	24	22	@@And Araunah said unto David, Let my lord the king take and offer up what @9seemeth@7 good unto him: behold, @9here be@7 oxen for burnt sacrifice, and threshing instruments and @9other@7 instruments of the oxen for wood.
verse	10	24	23	@@All @9these@7 things did Araunah, @9as@7 a king, give unto the king. And Araunah said unto the king, The LORD thy God accept thee.
verse	10	24	24	@@And the king said unto Araunah, Nay; but I will surely buy @9it@7 of thee at a price: neither will I offer burnt offerings unto the LORD my God of that which doth cost me nothing. So David bought the threshingfloor and the oxen for fifty shekels of silver.
verse	10	24	25	And David built there an altar unto the LORD, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings. So the LORD was intreated for the land, and the plague was stayed from Israel.
verse	11	1	1	@@Now king David was old @9and@7 stricken in years; and they covered him with clothes, but he gat no heat.
verse	11	1	2	Wherefore his servants said unto him, Let there be sought for my lord the king a young virgin: and let her stand before the king, and let her cherish him, and let her lie in thy bosom, that my lord the king may get heat.
