verse	11	1	4	@@And the damsel @9was@7 very fair, and cherished the king, and ministered to him: but the king knew her not.
verse	11	1	5	Then Adonijah the son of Haggith exalted himself, saying, I will be king: and he prepared him chariots and horsemen, and fifty men to run before him.
verse	11	1	6	@@And his father had not displeased him at any time in saying, Why hast thou done so? and he also @9was a@7 very goodly @9man;@7 and @9his mother@7 bare him after Absalom.
verse	11	1	7	@@And he conferred with Joab the son of Zeruiah, and with Abiathar the priest: and they following Adonijah helped @9him. @7
verse	11	1	8	@@But Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and Nathan the prophet, and Shimei, and Rei, and the mighty men which @9belonged@7 to David, were not with Adonijah.
verse	11	1	9	@@And Adonijah slew sheep and oxen and fat cattle by the stone of Zoheleth, which @9is@7 by Enrogel, and called all his brethren the king's sons, and all the men of Judah the king's servants:
verse	11	1	10	But Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah, and the mighty men, and Solomon his brother, he called not.
verse	11	1	11	@@Wherefore Nathan spake unto Bathsheba the mother of Solomon, saying, Hast thou not heard that Adonijah the son of Haggith doth reign, and David our lord knoweth @9it@7 not?
verse	11	1	12	Now therefore come, let me, I pray thee, give thee counsel, that thou mayest save thine own life, and the life of thy son Solomon.
verse	11	1	13	Go and get thee in unto king David, and say unto him, Didst not thou, my lord, O king, swear unto thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne? why then doth Adonijah reign?
verse	11	1	14	Behold, while thou yet talkest there with the king, I also will come in after thee, and confirm thy words.
verse	11	1	15	And Bathsheba went in unto the king into the chamber: and the king was very old; and Abishag the Shunammite ministered unto the king.
verse	11	1	16	And Bathsheba bowed, and did obeisance unto the king. And the king said, What wouldest thou?
verse	11	1	17	@@And she said unto him, My lord, thou swarest by the LORD thy God unto thine handmaid, @9saying,@7 Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne.
verse	11	1	18	@@And now, behold, Adonijah reigneth; and now, my lord the king, thou knowest @9it@7 not:
verse	11	1	19	And he hath slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and hath called all the sons of the king, and Abiathar the priest, and Joab the captain of the host: but Solomon thy servant hath he not called.
verse	11	1	20	@@And thou, my lord, O king, the eyes of all Israel @9are@7 upon thee, that thou shouldest tell them who shall sit on the throne of my lord the king after him.
verse	11	1	21	Otherwise it shall come to pass, when my lord the king shall sleep with his fathers, that I and my son Solomon shall be counted offenders.
verse	11	1	22	And, lo, while she yet talked with the king, Nathan the prophet also came in.
verse	11	1	23	And they told the king, saying, Behold Nathan the prophet. And when he was come in before the king, he bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground.
verse	11	1	24	And Nathan said, My lord, O king, hast thou said, Adonijah shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne?
verse	11	1	25	For he is gone down this day, and hath slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and hath called all the king's sons, and the captains of the host, and Abiathar the priest; and, behold, they eat and drink before him, and say, God save king Adonijah.
verse	11	1	26	@@But me, @9even@7 me thy servant, and Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and thy servant Solomon, hath he not called.
verse	11	1	27	@@Is this thing done by my lord the king, and thou hast not shewed @9it@7 unto thy servant, who should sit on the throne of my lord the king after him?
verse	11	1	28	Then king David answered and said, Call me Bathsheba. And she came into the king's presence, and stood before the king.
verse	11	1	29	@@And the king sware, and said, @9As@7 the LORD liveth, that hath redeemed my soul out of all distress,
verse	11	1	30	Even as I sware unto thee by the LORD God of Israel, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne in my stead; even so will I certainly do this day.
verse	11	1	31	@@Then Bathsheba bowed with @9her@7 face to the earth, and did reverence to the king, and said, Let my lord king David live for ever.
verse	11	1	32	And king David said, Call me Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada. And they came before the king.
verse	11	1	33	The king also said unto them, Take with you the servants of your lord, and cause Solomon my son to ride upon mine own mule, and bring him down to Gihon:
verse	11	1	34	And let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him there king over Israel: and blow ye with the trumpet, and say, God save king Solomon.
verse	11	1	35	Then ye shall come up after him, that he may come and sit upon my throne; for he shall be king in my stead: and I have appointed him to be ruler over Israel and over Judah.
verse	11	1	36	@@And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada answered the king, and said, Amen: the LORD God of my lord the king say so @9too. @7
verse	11	1	37	As the LORD hath been with my lord the king, even so be he with Solomon, and make his throne greater than the throne of my lord king David.
verse	11	1	38	So Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, went down, and caused Solomon to ride upon king David's mule, and brought him to Gihon.
verse	11	1	39	And Zadok the priest took an horn of oil out of the tabernacle, and anointed Solomon. And they blew the trumpet; and all the people said, God save king Solomon.
verse	11	1	40	And all the people came up after him, and the people piped with pipes, and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth rent with the sound of them.
verse	11	1	41	@@And Adonijah and all the guests that @9were@7 with him heard @9it@7 as they had made an end of eating. And when Joab heard the sound of the trumpet, he said, Wherefore @9is this@7 noise of the city being in an uproar?
verse	11	1	42	@@And while he yet spake, behold, Jonathan the son of Abiathar the priest came: and Adonijah said unto him, Come in; for thou @9art@7 a valiant man, and bringest good tidings.
verse	11	1	43	And Jonathan answered and said to Adonijah, Verily our lord king David hath made Solomon king.
verse	11	1	44	And the king hath sent with him Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, and they have caused him to ride upon the king's mule:
verse	11	1	45	@@And Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet have anointed him king in Gihon: and they are come up from thence rejoicing, so that the city rang again. This @9is@7 the noise that ye have heard.
verse	11	1	46	And also Solomon sitteth on the throne of the kingdom.
verse	11	1	47	And moreover the king's servants came to bless our lord king David, saying, God make the name of Solomon better than thy name, and make his throne greater than thy throne. And the king bowed himself upon the bed.
verse	11	1	48	@@And also thus said the king, Blessed @9be@7 the LORD God of Israel, which hath given @9one@7 to sit on my throne this day, mine eyes even seeing @9it. @7
verse	11	1	49	@@And all the guests that @9were@7 with Adonijah were afraid, and rose up, and went every man his way.
verse	11	1	50	And Adonijah feared because of Solomon, and arose, and went, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.
verse	11	1	51	And it was told Solomon, saying, Behold, Adonijah feareth king Solomon: for, lo, he hath caught hold on the horns of the altar, saying, Let king Solomon swear unto me to day that he will not slay his servant with the sword.
verse	11	1	52	And Solomon said, If he will shew himself a worthy man, there shall not an hair of him fall to the earth: but if wickedness shall be found in him, he shall die.
verse	11	1	53	So king Solomon sent, and they brought him down from the altar. And he came and bowed himself to king Solomon: and Solomon said unto him, Go to thine house.
verse	11	2	1	Now the days of David drew nigh that he should die; and he charged Solomon his son, saying,
verse	11	2	2	I go the way of all the earth: be thou strong therefore, and shew thyself a man;
verse	11	2	3	And keep the charge of the LORD thy God, to walk in his ways, to keep his statutes, and his commandments, and his judgments, and his testimonies, as it is written in the law of Moses, that thou mayest prosper in all that thou doest, and whithersoever thou turnest thyself:
verse	11	2	4	That the LORD may continue his word which he spake concerning me, saying, If thy children take heed to their way, to walk before me in truth with all their heart and with all their soul, there shall not fail thee (said he) a man on the throne of Israel.
verse	11	2	5	@@Moreover thou knowest also what Joab the son of Zeruiah did to me, @9and@7 what he did to the two captains of the hosts of Israel, unto Abner the son of Ner, and unto Amasa the son of Jether, whom he slew, and shed the blood of war in peace, and put the blood of war upon his girdle that @9was@7 about his loins, and in his shoes that @9were@7 on his feet.
verse	11	2	6	Do therefore according to thy wisdom, and let not his hoar head go down to the grave in peace.
verse	11	2	7	But shew kindness unto the sons of Barzillai the Gileadite, and let them be of those that eat at thy table: for so they came to me when I fled because of Absalom thy brother.
verse	11	2	8	@@And, behold, @9thou hast@7 with thee Shimei the son of Gera, a Benjamite of Bahurim, which cursed me with a grievous curse in the day when I went to Mahanaim: but he came down to meet me at Jordan, and I sware to him by the LORD, saying, I will not put thee to death with the sword.
verse	11	2	9	@@Now therefore hold him not guiltless: for thou @9art@7 a wise man, and knowest what thou oughtest to do unto him; but his hoar head bring thou down to the grave with blood.
verse	11	2	10	So David slept with his fathers, and was buried in the city of David.
verse	11	2	11	@@And the days that David reigned over Israel @9were@7 forty years: seven years reigned he in Hebron, and thirty and three years reigned he in Jerusalem.
verse	11	2	12	Then sat Solomon upon the throne of David his father; and his kingdom was established greatly.
verse	11	2	13	And Adonijah the son of Haggith came to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon. And she said, Comest thou peaceably? And he said, Peaceably.
verse	11	2	14	He said moreover, I have somewhat to say unto thee. And she said, Say on.
verse	11	2	15	@@And he said, Thou knowest that the kingdom was mine, and @9that@7 all Israel set their faces on me, that I should reign: howbeit the kingdom is turned about, and is become my brother's: for it was his from the LORD.
verse	11	2	16	And now I ask one petition of thee, deny me not. And she said unto him, Say on.
verse	11	2	17	And he said, Speak, I pray thee, unto Solomon the king, (for he will not say thee nay,) that he give me Abishag the Shunammite to wife.
verse	11	2	18	And Bathsheba said, Well; I will speak for thee unto the king.
verse	11	2	19	Bathsheba therefore went unto king Solomon, to speak unto him for Adonijah. And the king rose up to meet her, and bowed himself unto her, and sat down on his throne, and caused a seat to be set for the king's mother; and she sat on his right hand.
verse	11	2	20	@@Then she said, I desire one small petition of thee; @9I pray thee,@7 say me not nay. And the king said unto her, Ask on, my mother: for I will not say thee nay.
verse	11	2	21	And she said, Let Abishag the Shunammite be given to Adonijah thy brother to wife.
verse	11	2	22	@@And king Solomon answered and said unto his mother, And why dost thou ask Abishag the Shunammite for Adonijah? ask for him the kingdom also; for he @9is@7 mine elder brother; even for him, and for Abiathar the priest, and for Joab the son of Zeruiah.
verse	11	2	23	Then king Solomon sware by the LORD, saying, God do so to me, and more also, if Adonijah have not spoken this word against his own life.
verse	11	2	24	@@Now therefore, @9as@7 the LORD liveth, which hath established me, and set me on the throne of David my father, and who hath made me an house, as he promised, Adonijah shall be put to death this day.
verse	11	2	25	And king Solomon sent by the hand of Benaiah the son of Jehoiada; and he fell upon him that he died.
verse	11	2	26	@@And unto Abiathar the priest said the king, Get thee to Anathoth, unto thine own fields; for thou @9art@7 worthy of death: but I will not at this time put thee to death, because thou barest the ark of the Lord GOD before David my father, and because thou hast been afflicted in all wherein my father was afflicted.
verse	11	2	27	So Solomon thrust out Abiathar from being priest unto the LORD; that he might fulfil the word of the LORD, which he spake concerning the house of Eli in Shiloh.
verse	11	2	28	Then tidings came to Joab: for Joab had turned after Adonijah, though he turned not after Absalom. And Joab fled unto the tabernacle of the LORD, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.
verse	11	2	29	@@And it was told king Solomon that Joab was fled unto the tabernacle of the LORD; and, behold, @9he is@7 by the altar. Then Solomon sent Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, saying, Go, fall upon him.
verse	11	2	30	And Benaiah came to the tabernacle of the LORD, and said unto him, Thus saith the king, Come forth. And he said, Nay; but I will die here. And Benaiah brought the king word again, saying, Thus said Joab, and thus he answered me.
verse	11	2	31	And the king said unto him, Do as he hath said, and fall upon him, and bury him; that thou mayest take away the innocent blood, which Joab shed, from me, and from the house of my father.
verse	11	2	32	@@And the LORD shall return his blood upon his own head, who fell upon two men more righteous and better than he, and slew them with the sword, my father David not knowing @9thereof, to wit,@7 Abner the son of Ner, captain of the host of Israel, and Amasa the son of Jether, captain of the host of Judah.
verse	11	2	33	Their blood shall therefore return upon the head of Joab, and upon the head of his seed for ever: but upon David, and upon his seed, and upon his house, and upon his throne, shall there be peace for ever from the LORD.
verse	11	2	34	So Benaiah the son of Jehoiada went up, and fell upon him, and slew him: and he was buried in his own house in the wilderness.
verse	11	2	35	And the king put Benaiah the son of Jehoiada in his room over the host: and Zadok the priest did the king put in the room of Abiathar.
verse	11	2	36	And the king sent and called for Shimei, and said unto him, Build thee an house in Jerusalem, and dwell there, and go not forth thence any whither.
verse	11	2	37	@@For it shall be, @9that@7 on the day thou goest out, and passest over the brook Kidron, thou shalt know for certain that thou shalt surely die: thy blood shall be upon thine own head.
verse	11	2	38	@@And Shimei said unto the king, The saying @9is@7 good: as my lord the king hath said, so will thy servant do. And Shimei dwelt in Jerusalem many days.
verse	11	2	39	@@And it came to pass at the end of three years, that two of the servants of Shimei ran away unto Achish son of Maachah king of Gath. And they told Shimei, saying, Behold, thy servants @9be@7 in Gath.
verse	11	2	40	And Shimei arose, and saddled his ass, and went to Gath to Achish to seek his servants: and Shimei went, and brought his servants from Gath.
verse	11	2	41	And it was told Solomon that Shimei had gone from Jerusalem to Gath, and was come again.
verse	11	2	42	@@And the king sent and called for Shimei, and said unto him, Did I not make thee to swear by the LORD, and protested unto thee, saying, Know for a certain, on the day thou goest out, and walkest abroad any whither, that thou shalt surely die? and thou saidst unto me, The word @9that@7 I have heard @9is@7 good.
verse	11	2	43	Why then hast thou not kept the oath of the LORD, and the commandment that I have charged thee with?
verse	11	2	44	The king said moreover to Shimei, Thou knowest all the wickedness which thine heart is privy to, that thou didst to David my father: therefore the LORD shall return thy wickedness upon thine own head;
verse	11	2	45	@@And king Solomon @9shall be@7 blessed, and the throne of David shall be established before the LORD for ever.
verse	11	2	46	So the king commanded Benaiah the son of Jehoiada; which went out, and fell upon him, that he died. And the kingdom was established in the hand of Solomon.
verse	11	3	1	And Solomon made affinity with Pharaoh king of Egypt, and took Pharaoh's daughter, and brought her into the city of David, until he had made an end of building his own house, and the house of the LORD, and the wall of Jerusalem round about.
verse	11	3	2	Only the people sacrificed in high places, because there was no house built unto the name of the LORD, until those days.
verse	11	3	3	And Solomon loved the LORD, walking in the statutes of David his father: only he sacrificed and burnt incense in high places.
verse	11	3	4	@@And the king went to Gibeon to sacrifice there; for that @9was@7 the great high place: a thousand burnt offerings did Solomon offer upon that altar.
verse	11	3	5	In Gibeon the LORD appeared to Solomon in a dream by night: and God said, Ask what I shall give thee.
verse	11	3	6	@@And Solomon said, Thou hast shewed unto thy servant David my father great mercy, according as he walked before thee in truth, and in righteousness, and in uprightness of heart with thee; and thou hast kept for him this great kindness, that thou hast given him a son to sit on his throne, as @9it is@7 this day.
verse	11	3	7	@@And now, O LORD my God, thou hast made thy servant king instead of David my father: and I @9am but@7 a little child: I know not @9how@7 to go out or come in.
verse	11	3	8	@@And thy servant @9is@7 in the midst of thy people which thou hast chosen, a great people, that cannot be numbered nor counted for multitude.
verse	11	3	9	Give therefore thy servant an understanding heart to judge thy people, that I may discern between good and bad: for who is able to judge this thy so great a people?
verse	11	3	10	And the speech pleased the Lord, that Solomon had asked this thing.
verse	11	3	11	And God said unto him, Because thou hast asked this thing, and hast not asked for thyself long life; neither hast asked riches for thyself, nor hast asked the life of thine enemies; but hast asked for thyself understanding to discern judgment;
verse	11	3	12	Behold, I have done according to thy words: lo, I have given thee a wise and an understanding heart; so that there was none like thee before thee, neither after thee shall any arise like unto thee.
verse	11	3	13	And I have also given thee that which thou hast not asked, both riches, and honour: so that there shall not be any among the kings like unto thee all thy days.
verse	11	3	14	And if thou wilt walk in my ways, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as thy father David did walk, then I will lengthen thy days.
verse	11	3	15	@@And Solomon awoke; and, behold, @9it was@7 a dream. And he came to Jerusalem, and stood before the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and offered up burnt offerings, and offered peace offerings, and made a feast to all his servants.
verse	11	3	16	@@Then came there two women, @9that were@7 harlots, unto the king, and stood before him.
verse	11	3	17	And the one woman said, O my lord, I and this woman dwell in one house; and I was delivered of a child with her in the house.
verse	11	3	18	@@And it came to pass the third day after that I was delivered, that this woman was delivered also: and we @9were@7 together; @9there was@7 no stranger with us in the house, save we two in the house.
verse	11	3	19	And this woman's child died in the night; because she overlaid it.
verse	11	3	20	And she arose at midnight, and took my son from beside me, while thine handmaid slept, and laid it in her bosom, and laid her dead child in my bosom.
verse	11	3	21	And when I rose in the morning to give my child suck, behold, it was dead: but when I had considered it in the morning, behold, it was not my son, which I did bear.
verse	11	3	22	@@And the other woman said, Nay; but the living @9is@7 my son, and the dead @9is@7 thy son. And this said, No; but the dead @9is@7 thy son, and the living @9is@7 my son. Thus they spake before the king.
verse	11	3	23	@@Then said the king, The one saith, This @9is@7 my son that liveth, and thy son @9is@7 the dead: and the other saith, Nay; but thy son @9is@7 the dead, and my son @9is@7 the living.
verse	11	3	24	And the king said, Bring me a sword. And they brought a sword before the king.
verse	11	3	25	And the king said, Divide the living child in two, and give half to the one, and half to the other.
verse	11	3	26	@@Then spake the woman whose the living child @9was@7 unto the king, for her bowels yearned upon her son, and she said, O my lord, give her the living child, and in no wise slay it. But the other said, Let it be neither mine nor thine, @9but@7 divide @9it. @7
verse	11	3	27	@@Then the king answered and said, Give her the living child, and in no wise slay it: she @9is@7 the mother thereof.
verse	11	3	28	@@And all Israel heard of the judgment which the king had judged; and they feared the king: for they saw that the wisdom of God @9was@7 in him, to do judgment.
verse	11	4	1	So king Solomon was king over all Israel.
verse	11	4	2	@@And these @9were@7 the princes which he had; Azariah the son of Zadok the priest,
verse	11	4	3	Elihoreph and Ahiah, the sons of Shisha, scribes; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud, the recorder.
verse	11	4	4	@@And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada @9was@7 over the host: and Zadok and Abiathar @9were@7 the priests:
verse	11	4	5	@@And Azariah the son of Nathan @9was@7 over the officers: and Zabud the son of Nathan @9was@7 principal officer, @9and@7 the king's friend:
verse	11	4	6	@@And Ahishar @9was@7 over the household: and Adoniram the son of Abda @9was@7 over the tribute.
verse	11	4	7	And Solomon had twelve officers over all Israel, which provided victuals for the king and his household: each man his month in a year made provision.
verse	11	4	8	@@And these @9are@7 their names: The son of Hur, in mount Ephraim:
verse	11	4	9	The son of Dekar, in Makaz, and in Shaalbim, and Bethshemesh, and Elonbethhanan:
verse	11	4	10	@@The son of Hesed, in Aruboth; to him @9pertained@7 Sochoh, and all the land of Hepher:
verse	11	4	11	The son of Abinadab, in all the region of Dor; which had Taphath the daughter of Solomon to wife:
verse	11	4	12	@@Baana the son of Ahilud; @9to him pertained@7 Taanach and Megiddo, and all Bethshean, which is by Zartanah beneath Jezreel, from Bethshean to Abelmeholah, @9even@7 unto @9the place that is@7 beyond Jokneam:
verse	11	4	13	@@The son of Geber, in Ramothgilead; to him @9pertained@7 the towns of Jair the son of Manasseh, which @9are@7 in Gilead; to him @9also pertained@7 the region of Argob, which is in Bashan, threescore great cities with walls and brasen bars:
verse	11	4	14	@@Ahinadab the son of Iddo @9had@7 Mahanaim:
verse	11	4	15	@@Ahimaaz @9was@7 in Naphtali; he also took Basmath the daughter of Solomon to wife:
verse	11	4	16	@@Baanah the son of Hushai @9was@7 in Asher and in Aloth:
verse	11	4	17	Jehoshaphat the son of Paruah, in Issachar:
verse	11	4	18	Shimei the son of Elah, in Benjamin:
verse	11	4	19	@@Geber the son of Uri @9was@7 in the country of Gilead, @9in@7 the country of Sihon king of the Amorites, and of Og king of Bashan; and @9he was@7 the only officer which @9was@7 in the land.
verse	11	4	20	@@Judah and Israel @9were@7 many, as the sand which @9is@7 by the sea in multitude, eating and drinking, and making merry.
verse	11	4	21	And Solomon reigned over all kingdoms from the river unto the land of the Philistines, and unto the border of Egypt: they brought presents, and served Solomon all the days of his life.
verse	11	4	22	And Solomon's provision for one day was thirty measures of fine flour, and threescore measures of meal,
verse	11	4	23	Ten fat oxen, and twenty oxen out of the pastures, and an hundred sheep, beside harts, and roebucks, and fallowdeer, and fatted fowl.
verse	11	4	24	@@For he had dominion over all @9the region@7 on this side the river, from Tiphsah even to Azzah, over all the kings on this side the river: and he had peace on all sides round about him.
verse	11	4	25	And Judah and Israel dwelt safely, every man under his vine and under his fig tree, from Dan even to Beersheba, all the days of Solomon.
verse	11	4	26	And Solomon had forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen.
verse	11	4	27	And those officers provided victual for king Solomon, and for all that came unto king Solomon's table, every man in his month: they lacked nothing.
verse	11	4	28	@@Barley also and straw for the horses and dromedaries brought they unto the place where @9the officers@7 were, every man according to his charge.
verse	11	4	29	@@And God gave Solomon wisdom and understanding exceeding much, and largeness of heart, even as the sand that @9is@7 on the sea shore.
verse	11	4	30	And Solomon's wisdom excelled the wisdom of all the children of the east country, and all the wisdom of Egypt.
verse	11	4	31	For he was wiser than all men; than Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol: and his fame was in all nations round about.
verse	11	4	32	And he spake three thousand proverbs: and his songs were a thousand and five.
verse	11	4	33	@@And he spake of trees, from the cedar tree that @9is@7 in Lebanon even unto the hyssop that springeth out of the wall: he spake also of beasts, and of fowl, and of creeping things, and of fishes.
verse	11	4	34	And there came of all people to hear the wisdom of Solomon, from all kings of the earth, which had heard of his wisdom.
verse	11	5	1	And Hiram king of Tyre sent his servants unto Solomon; for he had heard that they had anointed him king in the room of his father: for Hiram was ever a lover of David.
verse	11	5	2	And Solomon sent to Hiram, saying,
verse	11	5	3	Thou knowest how that David my father could not build an house unto the name of the LORD his God for the wars which were about him on every side, until the LORD put them under the soles of his feet.
verse	11	5	4	@@But now the LORD my God hath given me rest on every side, @9so that there is@7 neither adversary nor evil occurrent.
verse	11	5	5	And, behold, I purpose to build an house unto the name of the LORD my God, as the LORD spake unto David my father, saying, Thy son, whom I will set upon thy throne in thy room, he shall build an house unto my name.
verse	11	5	6	@@Now therefore command thou that they hew me cedar trees out of Lebanon; and my servants shall be with thy servants: and unto thee will I give hire for thy servants according to all that thou shalt appoint: for thou knowest that @9there is@7 not among us any that can skill to hew timber like unto the Sidonians.
verse	11	5	7	@@And it came to pass, when Hiram heard the words of Solomon, that he rejoiced greatly, and said, Blessed @9be@7 the LORD this day, which hath given unto David a wise son over this great people.
verse	11	5	8	@@And Hiram sent to Solomon, saying, I have considered the things which thou sentest to me for: @9and@7 I will do all thy desire concerning timber of cedar, and concerning timber of fir.
verse	11	5	9	@@My servants shall bring @9them@7 down from Lebanon unto the sea: and I will convey them by sea in floats unto the place that thou shalt appoint me, and will cause them to be discharged there, and thou shalt receive @9them:@7 and thou shalt accomplish my desire, in giving food for my household.
verse	11	5	10	@@So Hiram gave Solomon cedar trees and fir trees @9according to@7 all his desire.
verse	11	5	11	@@And Solomon gave Hiram twenty thousand measures of wheat @9for@7 food to his household, and twenty measures of pure oil: thus gave Solomon to Hiram year by year.
verse	11	5	12	And the LORD gave Solomon wisdom, as he promised him: and there was peace between Hiram and Solomon; and they two made a league together.
verse	11	5	13	And king Solomon raised a levy out of all Israel; and the levy was thirty thousand men.
verse	11	5	14	@@And he sent them to Lebanon, ten thousand a month by courses: a month they were in Lebanon, @9and@7 two months at home: and Adoniram @9was@7 over the levy.
verse	11	5	15	And Solomon had threescore and ten thousand that bare burdens, and fourscore thousand hewers in the mountains;
verse	11	5	16	@@Beside the chief of Solomon's officers which @9were@7 over the work, three thousand and three hundred, which ruled over the people that wrought in the work.
verse	11	5	17	@@And the king commanded, and they brought great stones, costly stones, @9and@7 hewed stones, to lay the foundation of the house.
verse	11	5	18	@@And Solomon's builders and Hiram's builders did hew @9them,@7 and the stonesquarers: so they prepared timber and stones to build the house.
verse	11	6	1	@@And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Israel were come out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon's reign over Israel, in the month Zif, which @9is@7 the second month, that he began to build the house of the LORD.
verse	11	6	2	@@And the house which king Solomon built for the LORD, the length thereof @9was@7 threescore cubits, and the breadth thereof twenty @9cubits,@7 and the height thereof thirty cubits.
verse	11	6	3	@@And the porch before the temple of the house, twenty cubits @9was@7 the length thereof, according to the breadth of the house; @9and@7 ten cubits @9was@7 the breadth thereof before the house.
verse	11	6	4	And for the house he made windows of narrow lights.
verse	11	6	5	@@And against the wall of the house he built chambers round about, @9against@7 the walls of the house round about, @9both@7 of the temple and of the oracle: and he made chambers round about:
verse	11	6	6	@@The nethermost chamber @9was@7 five cubits broad, and the middle @9was@7 six cubits broad, and the third @9was@7 seven cubits broad: for without @9in the wall@7 of the house he made narrowed rests round about, that @9the beams@7 should not be fastened in the walls of the house.
verse	11	6	7	@@And the house, when it was in building, was built of stone made ready before it was brought thither: so that there was neither hammer nor axe @9nor@7 any tool of iron heard in the house, while it was in building.
verse	11	6	8	@@The door for the middle chamber @9was@7 in the right side of the house: and they went up with winding stairs into the middle @9chamber,@7 and out of the middle into the third.
verse	11	6	9	So he built the house, and finished it; and covered the house with beams and boards of cedar.
verse	11	6	10	@@And @9then@7 he built chambers against all the house, five cubits high: and they rested on the house @9with@7 timber of cedar.
verse	11	6	11	And the word of the LORD came to Solomon, saying,
verse	11	6	12	@@@9Concerning@7 this house which thou art in building, if thou wilt walk in my statutes, and execute my judgments, and keep all my commandments to walk in them; then will I perform my word with thee, which I spake unto David thy father:
verse	11	6	13	And I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will not forsake my people Israel.
verse	11	6	14	So Solomon built the house, and finished it.
verse	11	6	15	@@And he built the walls of the house within with boards of cedar, both the floor of the house, and the walls of the cieling: @9and@7 he covered @9them@7 on the inside with wood, and covered the floor of the house with planks of fir.
verse	11	6	16	@@And he built twenty cubits on the sides of the house, both the floor and the walls with boards of cedar: he even built @9them@7 for it within, @9even@7 for the oracle, @9even@7 for the most holy @9place. @7
verse	11	6	17	@@And the house, that @9is,@7 the temple before it, was forty cubits @9long. @7
verse	11	6	18	@@And the cedar of the house within @9was@7 carved with knops and open flowers: all @9was@7 cedar; there was no stone seen.
verse	11	6	19	And the oracle he prepared in the house within, to set there the ark of the covenant of the LORD.
verse	11	6	20	@@And the oracle in the forepart @9was@7 twenty cubits in length, and twenty cubits in breadth, and twenty cubits in the height thereof: and he overlaid it with pure gold; and so covered the altar @9which was of@7 cedar.
verse	11	6	21	So Solomon overlaid the house within with pure gold: and he made a partition by the chains of gold before the oracle; and he overlaid it with gold.
verse	11	6	22	@@And the whole house he overlaid with gold, until he had finished all the house: also the whole altar that @9was@7 by the oracle he overlaid with gold.
verse	11	6	23	@@And within the oracle he made two cherubims @9of@7 olive tree, @9each@7 ten cubits high.
verse	11	6	24	@@And five cubits @9was@7 the one wing of the cherub, and five cubits the other wing of the cherub: from the uttermost part of the one wing unto the uttermost part of the other @9were@7 ten cubits.
verse	11	6	25	@@And the other cherub @9was@7 ten cubits: both the cherubims @9were@7 of one measure and one size.
verse	11	6	26	@@The height of the one cherub @9was@7 ten cubits, and so @9was it@7 of the other cherub.
verse	11	6	27	@@And he set the cherubims within the inner house: and they stretched forth the wings of the cherubims, so that the wing of the one touched the @9one@7 wall, and the wing of the other cherub touched the other wall; and their wings touched one another in the midst of the house.
verse	11	6	28	And he overlaid the cherubims with gold.
verse	11	6	29	And he carved all the walls of the house round about with carved figures of cherubims and palm trees and open flowers, within and without.
verse	11	6	30	And the floor of the house he overlaid with gold, within and without.
verse	11	6	31	@@And for the entering of the oracle he made doors @9of@7 olive tree: the lintel @9and@7 side posts @9were@7 a fifth part @9of the wall. @7
verse	11	6	32	@@The two doors also @9were of@7 olive tree; and he carved upon them carvings of cherubims and palm trees and open flowers, and overlaid @9them@7 with gold, and spread gold upon the cherubims, and upon the palm trees.
verse	11	6	33	@@So also made he for the door of the temple posts of olive tree, a fourth part @9of the wall. @7
verse	11	6	34	@@And the two doors @9were of@7 fir tree: the two leaves of the one door @9were@7 folding, and the two leaves of the other door @9were@7 folding.
verse	11	6	35	@@And he carved @9thereon@7 cherubims and palm trees and open flowers: and covered @9them@7 with gold fitted upon the carved work.
verse	11	6	36	And he built the inner court with three rows of hewed stone, and a row of cedar beams.
verse	11	6	37	In the fourth year was the foundation of the house of the LORD laid, in the month Zif:
verse	11	6	38	@@And in the eleventh year, in the month Bul, which @9is@7 the eighth month, was the house finished throughout all the parts thereof, and according to all the fashion of it. So was he seven years in building it.
verse	11	7	1	But Solomon was building his own house thirteen years, and he finished all his house.
verse	11	7	2	@@He built also the house of the forest of Lebanon; the length thereof @9was@7 an hundred cubits, and the breadth thereof fifty cubits, and the height thereof thirty cubits, upon four rows of cedar pillars, with cedar beams upon the pillars.
verse	11	7	3	@@And @9it was@7 covered with cedar above upon the beams, that @9lay@7 on forty five pillars, fifteen @9in@7 a row.
verse	11	7	4	@@And @9there were@7 windows @9in@7 three rows, and light @9was@7 against light @9in@7 three ranks.
verse	11	7	5	@@And all the doors and posts @9were@7 square, with the windows: and light @9was@7 against light @9in@7 three ranks.
verse	11	7	6	@@And he made a porch of pillars; the length thereof @9was@7 fifty cubits, and the breadth thereof thirty cubits: and the porch was before them: and the @9other@7 pillars and the thick beam @9were@7 before them.
verse	11	7	7	@@Then he made a porch for the throne where he might judge, @9even@7 the porch of judgment: and @9it was@7 covered with cedar from one side of the floor to the other.
verse	11	7	8	@@And his house where he dwelt @9had@7 another court within the porch, @9which@7 was of the like work. Solomon made also an house for Pharaoh's daughter, whom he had taken @9to wife,@7 like unto this porch.
verse	11	7	9	@@All these @9were of@7 costly stones, according to the measures of hewed stones, sawed with saws, within and without, even from the foundation unto the coping, and so on the outside toward the great court.
verse	11	7	10	@@And the foundation @9was of@7 costly stones, even great stones, stones of ten cubits, and stones of eight cubits.
verse	11	7	11	@@And above @9were@7 costly stones, after the measures of hewed stones, and cedars.
verse	11	7	12	@@And the great court round about @9was@7 with three rows of hewed stones, and a row of cedar beams, both for the inner court of the house of the LORD, and for the porch of the house.
verse	11	7	13	And king Solomon sent and fetched Hiram out of Tyre.
verse	11	7	14	@@He @9was@7 a widow's son of the tribe of Naphtali, and his father @9was@7 a man of Tyre, a worker in brass: and he was filled with wisdom, and understanding, and cunning to work all works in brass. And he came to king Solomon, and wrought all his work.
verse	11	7	15	For he cast two pillars of brass, of eighteen cubits high apiece: and a line of twelve cubits did compass either of them about.
verse	11	7	16	@@And he made two chapiters @9of@7 molten brass, to set upon the tops of the pillars: the height of the one chapiter @9was@7 five cubits, and the height of the other chapiter @9was@7 five cubits:
verse	11	7	17	@@@9And@7 nets of checker work, and wreaths of chain work, for the chapiters which @9were@7 upon the top of the pillars; seven for the one chapiter, and seven for the other chapiter.
verse	11	7	18	@@And he made the pillars, and two rows round about upon the one network, to cover the chapiters that @9were@7 upon the top, with pomegranates: and so did he for the other chapiter.
verse	11	7	19	@@And the chapiters that @9were@7 upon the top of the pillars @9were@7 of lily work in the porch, four cubits.
verse	11	7	20	@@And the chapiters upon the two pillars @9had pomegranates@7 also above, over against the belly which @9was@7 by the network: and the pomegranates @9were@7 two hundred in rows round about upon the other chapiter.
verse	11	7	21	And he set up the pillars in the porch of the temple: and he set up the right pillar, and called the name thereof Jachin: and he set up the left pillar, and called the name thereof Boaz.
verse	11	7	22	@@And upon the top of the pillars @9was@7 lily work: so was the work of the pillars finished.
verse	11	7	23	@@And he made a molten sea, ten cubits from the one brim to the other: @9it was@7 round all about, and his height @9was@7 five cubits: and a line of thirty cubits did compass it round about.
verse	11	7	24	@@And under the brim of it round about @9there were@7 knops compassing it, ten in a cubit, compassing the sea round about: the knops @9were@7 cast in two rows, when it was cast.
verse	11	7	25	@@It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east: and the sea @9was set@7 above upon them, and all their hinder parts @9were@7 inward.
verse	11	7	26	@@And it @9was@7 an hand breadth thick, and the brim thereof was wrought like the brim of a cup, with flowers of lilies: it contained two thousand baths.
verse	11	7	27	@@And he made ten bases of brass; four cubits @9was@7 the length of one base, and four cubits the breadth thereof, and three cubits the height of it.
verse	11	7	28	@@And the work of the bases @9was@7 on this @9manner:@7 they had borders, and the borders @9were@7 between the ledges:
verse	11	7	29	@@And on the borders that @9were@7 between the ledges @9were@7 lions, oxen, and cherubims: and upon the ledges @9there was@7 a base above: and beneath the lions and oxen @9were@7 certain additions made of thin work.
verse	11	7	30	@@And every base had four brasen wheels, and plates of brass: and the four corners thereof had undersetters: under the laver @9were@7 undersetters molten, at the side of every addition.
verse	11	7	31	@@And the mouth of it within the chapiter and above @9was@7 a cubit: but the mouth thereof @9was@7 round @9after@7 the work of the base, a cubit and an half: and also upon the mouth of it @9were@7 gravings with their borders, foursquare, not round.
verse	11	7	32	@@And under the borders @9were@7 four wheels; and the axletrees of the wheels @9were joined@7 to the base: and the height of a wheel @9was@7 a cubit and half a cubit.
verse	11	7	33	@@And the work of the wheels was like the work of a chariot wheel: their axletrees, and their naves, and their felloes, and their spokes, @9were@7 all molten.
verse	11	7	34	@@And @9there were@7 four undersetters to the four corners of one base: @9and@7 the undersetters @9were@7 of the very base itself.
verse	11	7	35	@@And in the top of the base @9was there@7 a round compass of half a cubit high: and on the top of the base the ledges thereof and the borders thereof @9were@7 of the same.
verse	11	7	36	For on the plates of the ledges thereof, and on the borders thereof, he graved cherubims, lions, and palm trees, according to the proportion of every one, and additions round about.
verse	11	7	37	@@After this @9manner@7 he made the ten bases: all of them had one casting, one measure, @9and@7 one size.
verse	11	7	38	@@Then made he ten lavers of brass: one laver contained forty baths: @9and@7 every laver was four cubits: @9and@7 upon every one of the ten bases one laver.
verse	11	7	39	And he put five bases on the right side of the house, and five on the left side of the house: and he set the sea on the right side of the house eastward over against the south.
verse	11	7	40	And Hiram made the lavers, and the shovels, and the basons. So Hiram made an end of doing all the work that he made king Solomon for the house of the LORD:
verse	11	7	41	@@The two pillars, and the @9two@7 bowls of the chapiters that @9were@7 on the top of the two pillars; and the two networks, to cover the two bowls of the chapiters which @9were@7 upon the top of the pillars;
verse	11	7	42	@@And four hundred pomegranates for the two networks, @9even@7 two rows of pomegranates for one network, to cover the two bowls of the chapiters that @9were@7 upon the pillars;
verse	11	7	43	And the ten bases, and ten lavers on the bases;
verse	11	7	44	And one sea, and twelve oxen under the sea;
verse	11	7	45	@@And the pots, and the shovels, and the basons: and all these vessels, which Hiram made to king Solomon for the house of the LORD, @9were of@7 bright brass.
verse	11	7	46	In the plain of Jordan did the king cast them, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zarthan.
verse	11	7	47	@@And Solomon left all the vessels @9unweighed,@7 because they were exceeding many: neither was the weight of the brass found out.
verse	11	7	48	@@And Solomon made all the vessels that @9pertained@7 unto the house of the LORD: the altar of gold, and the table of gold, whereupon the shewbread @9was, @7
verse	11	7	49	@@And the candlesticks of pure gold, five on the right @9side,@7 and five on the left, before the oracle, with the flowers, and the lamps, and the tongs @9of@7 gold,
verse	11	7	50	@@And the bowls, and the snuffers, and the basons, and the spoons, and the censers @9of@7 pure gold; and the hinges @9of@7 gold, @9both@7 for the doors of the inner house, the most holy @9place, and@7 for the doors of the house, @9to wit,@7 of the temple.
verse	11	7	51	@@So was ended all the work that king Solomon made for the house of the LORD. And Solomon brought in the things which David his father had dedicated; @9even@7 the silver, and the gold, and the vessels, did he put among the treasures of the house of the LORD.
verse	11	8	1	@@Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel, and all the heads of the tribes, the chief of the fathers of the children of Israel, unto king Solomon in Jerusalem, that they might bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the city of David, which @9is@7 Zion.
verse	11	8	2	@@And all the men of Israel assembled themselves unto king Solomon at the feast in the month Ethanim, which @9is@7 the seventh month.
verse	11	8	3	And all the elders of Israel came, and the priests took up the ark.
verse	11	8	4	@@And they brought up the ark of the LORD, and the tabernacle of the congregation, and all the holy vessels that @9were@7 in the tabernacle, even those did the priests and the Levites bring up.
verse	11	8	5	@@And king Solomon, and all the congregation of Israel, that @9were@7 assembled unto him, were with him before the ark, sacrificing sheep and oxen, that could not be told nor numbered for multitude.
verse	11	8	6	@@And the priests brought in the ark of the covenant of the LORD unto his place, into the oracle of the house, to the most holy @9place, even@7 under the wings of the cherubims.
verse	11	8	7	@@For the cherubims spread forth @9their@7 two wings over the place of the ark, and the cherubims covered the ark and the staves thereof above.
verse	11	8	8	@@And they drew out the staves, that the ends of the staves were seen out in the holy @9place@7 before the oracle, and they were not seen without: and there they are unto this day.
verse	11	8	9	@@@9There was@7 nothing in the ark save the two tables of stone, which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made @9a covenant@7 with the children of Israel, when they came out of the land of Egypt.
verse	11	8	10	@@And it came to pass, when the priests were come out of the holy @9place,@7 that the cloud filled the house of the LORD,
verse	11	8	11	So that the priests could not stand to minister because of the cloud: for the glory of the LORD had filled the house of the LORD.
verse	11	8	12	Then spake Solomon, The LORD said that he would dwell in the thick darkness.
verse	11	8	13	I have surely built thee an house to dwell in, a settled place for thee to abide in for ever.
verse	11	8	14	And the king turned his face about, and blessed all the congregation of Israel: (and all the congregation of Israel stood;)
verse	11	8	15	@@And he said, Blessed @9be@7 the LORD God of Israel, which spake with his mouth unto David my father, and hath with his hand fulfilled @9it,@7 saying,
verse	11	8	16	Since the day that I brought forth my people Israel out of Egypt, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Israel to build an house, that my name might be therein; but I chose David to be over my people Israel.
verse	11	8	17	And it was in the heart of David my father to build an house for the name of the LORD God of Israel.
verse	11	8	18	And the LORD said unto David my father, Whereas it was in thine heart to build an house unto my name, thou didst well that it was in thine heart.
verse	11	8	19	Nevertheless thou shalt not build the house; but thy son that shall come forth out of thy loins, he shall build the house unto my name.
verse	11	8	20	And the LORD hath performed his word that he spake, and I am risen up in the room of David my father, and sit on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised, and have built an house for the name of the LORD God of Israel.
verse	11	8	21	@@And I have set there a place for the ark, wherein @9is@7 the covenant of the LORD, which he made with our fathers, when he brought them out of the land of Egypt.
verse	11	8	22	And Solomon stood before the altar of the LORD in the presence of all the congregation of Israel, and spread forth his hands toward heaven:
verse	11	8	23	@@And he said, LORD God of Israel, @9there is@7 no God like thee, in heaven above, or on earth beneath, who keepest covenant and mercy with thy servants that walk before thee with all their heart:
verse	11	8	24	@@Who hast kept with thy servant David my father that thou promisedst him: thou spakest also with thy mouth, and hast fulfilled @9it@7 with thine hand, as @9it is@7 this day.
verse	11	8	25	Therefore now, LORD God of Israel, keep with thy servant David my father that thou promisedst him, saying, There shall not fail thee a man in my sight to sit on the throne of Israel; so that thy children take heed to their way, that they walk before me as thou hast walked before me.
verse	11	8	26	And now, O God of Israel, let thy word, I pray thee, be verified, which thou spakest unto thy servant David my father.
verse	11	8	27	But will God indeed dwell on the earth? behold, the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain thee; how much less this house that I have builded?
verse	11	8	28	Yet have thou respect unto the prayer of thy servant, and to his supplication, O LORD my God, to hearken unto the cry and to the prayer, which thy servant prayeth before thee to day:
verse	11	8	29	@@That thine eyes may be open toward this house night and day, @9even@7 toward the place of which thou hast said, My name shall be there: that thou mayest hearken unto the prayer which thy servant shall make toward this place.
verse	11	8	30	And hearken thou to the supplication of thy servant, and of thy people Israel, when they shall pray toward this place: and hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place: and when thou hearest, forgive.
verse	11	8	31	If any man trespass against his neighbour, and an oath be laid upon him to cause him to swear, and the oath come before thine altar in this house:
verse	11	8	32	Then hear thou in heaven, and do, and judge thy servants, condemning the wicked, to bring his way upon his head; and justifying the righteous, to give him according to his righteousness.
verse	11	8	33	When thy people Israel be smitten down before the enemy, because they have sinned against thee, and shall turn again to thee, and confess thy name, and pray, and make supplication unto thee in this house:
verse	11	8	34	Then hear thou in heaven, and forgive the sin of thy people Israel, and bring them again unto the land which thou gavest unto their fathers.
verse	11	8	35	When heaven is shut up, and there is no rain, because they have sinned against thee; if they pray toward this place, and confess thy name, and turn from their sin, when thou afflictest them:
verse	11	8	36	Then hear thou in heaven, and forgive the sin of thy servants, and of thy people Israel, that thou teach them the good way wherein they should walk, and give rain upon thy land, which thou hast given to thy people for an inheritance.
verse	11	8	37	@@If there be in the land famine, if there be pestilence, blasting, mildew, locust, @9or@7 if there be caterpiller; if their enemy besiege them in the land of their cities; whatsoever plague, whatsoever sickness @9there be; @7
verse	11	8	38	@@What prayer and supplication soever be @9made@7 by any man, @9or@7 by all thy people Israel, which shall know every man the plague of his own heart, and spread forth his hands toward this house:
verse	11	8	39	@@Then hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place, and forgive, and do, and give to every man according to his ways, whose heart thou knowest; (for thou, @9even@7 thou only, knowest the hearts of all the children of men;)
verse	11	8	40	That they may fear thee all the days that they live in the land which thou gavest unto our fathers.
verse	11	8	41	@@Moreover concerning a stranger, that @9is@7 not of thy people Israel, but cometh out of a far country for thy name's sake;
verse	11	8	42	(For they shall hear of thy great name, and of thy strong hand, and of thy stretched out arm;) when he shall come and pray toward this house;
verse	11	8	43	@@Hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place, and do according to all that the stranger calleth to thee for: that all people of the earth may know thy name, to fear thee, as @9do@7 thy people Israel; and that they may know that this house, which I have builded, is called by thy name.
verse	11	8	44	@@If thy people go out to battle against their enemy, whithersoever thou shalt send them, and shall pray unto the LORD toward the city which thou hast chosen, and @9toward@7 the house that I have built for thy name:
verse	11	8	45	Then hear thou in heaven their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.
verse	11	8	46	@@If they sin against thee, (for @9there is@7 no man that sinneth not,) and thou be angry with them, and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captives unto the land of the enemy, far or near;
verse	11	8	47	@@@9Yet@7 if they shall bethink themselves in the land whither they were carried captives, and repent, and make supplication unto thee in the land of them that carried them captives, saying, We have sinned, and have done perversely, we have committed wickedness;
verse	11	8	48	@@And @9so@7 return unto thee with all their heart, and with all their soul, in the land of their enemies, which led them away captive, and pray unto thee toward their land, which thou gavest unto their fathers, the city which thou hast chosen, and the house which I have built for thy name:
verse	11	8	49	Then hear thou their prayer and their supplication in heaven thy dwelling place, and maintain their cause,
verse	11	8	50	And forgive thy people that have sinned against thee, and all their transgressions wherein they have transgressed against thee, and give them compassion before them who carried them captive, that they may have compassion on them:
verse	11	8	51	@@For they @9be@7 thy people, and thine inheritance, which thou broughtest forth out of Egypt, from the midst of the furnace of iron:
verse	11	8	52	That thine eyes may be open unto the supplication of thy servant, and unto the supplication of thy people Israel, to hearken unto them in all that they call for unto thee.
verse	11	8	53	@@For thou didst separate them from among all the people of the earth, @9to be@7 thine inheritance, as thou spakest by the hand of Moses thy servant, when thou broughtest our fathers out of Egypt, O Lord GOD.
verse	11	8	54	@@And it was @9so,@7 that when Solomon had made an end of praying all this prayer and supplication unto the LORD, he arose from before the altar of the LORD, from kneeling on his knees with his hands spread up to heaven.
verse	11	8	55	And he stood, and blessed all the congregation of Israel with a loud voice, saying,
verse	11	8	56	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD, that hath given rest unto his people Israel, according to all that he promised: there hath not failed one word of all his good promise, which he promised by the hand of Moses his servant.
verse	11	8	57	The LORD our God be with us, as he was with our fathers: let him not leave us, nor forsake us:
verse	11	8	58	That he may incline our hearts unto him, to walk in all his ways, and to keep his commandments, and his statutes, and his judgments, which he commanded our fathers.
verse	11	8	59	And let these my words, wherewith I have made supplication before the LORD, be nigh unto the LORD our God day and night, that he maintain the cause of his servant, and the cause of his people Israel at all times, as the matter shall require:
verse	11	8	60	@@That all the people of the earth may know that the LORD @9is@7 God, @9and that there is@7 none else.
verse	11	8	61	Let your heart therefore be perfect with the LORD our God, to walk in his statutes, and to keep his commandments, as at this day.
verse	11	8	62	And the king, and all Israel with him, offered sacrifice before the LORD.
verse	11	8	63	And Solomon offered a sacrifice of peace offerings, which he offered unto the LORD, two and twenty thousand oxen, and an hundred and twenty thousand sheep. So the king and all the children of Israel dedicated the house of the LORD.
verse	11	8	64	@@The same day did the king hallow the middle of the court that @9was@7 before the house of the LORD: for there he offered burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings: because the brasen altar that @9was@7 before the LORD @9was@7 too little to receive the burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings.
verse	11	8	65	@@And at that time Solomon held a feast, and all Israel with him, a great congregation, from the entering in of Hamath unto the river of Egypt, before the LORD our God, seven days and seven days, @9even@7 fourteen days.
verse	11	8	66	On the eighth day he sent the people away: and they blessed the king, and went unto their tents joyful and glad of heart for all the goodness that the LORD had done for David his servant, and for Israel his people.
verse	11	9	1	And it came to pass, when Solomon had finished the building of the house of the LORD, and the king's house, and all Solomon's desire which he was pleased to do,
verse	11	9	2	That the LORD appeared to Solomon the second time, as he had appeared unto him at Gibeon.
verse	11	9	3	And the LORD said unto him, I have heard thy prayer and thy supplication, that thou hast made before me: I have hallowed this house, which thou hast built, to put my name there for ever; and mine eyes and mine heart shall be there perpetually.
verse	11	9	4	@@And if thou wilt walk before me, as David thy father walked, in integrity of heart, and in uprightness, to do according to all that I have commanded thee, @9and@7 wilt keep my statutes and my judgments:
verse	11	9	5	Then I will establish the throne of thy kingdom upon Israel for ever, as I promised to David thy father, saying, There shall not fail thee a man upon the throne of Israel.
verse	11	9	6	@@@9But@7 if ye shall at all turn from following me, ye or your children, and will not keep my commandments @9and@7 my statutes which I have set before you, but go and serve other gods, and worship them:
verse	11	9	7	Then will I cut off Israel out of the land which I have given them; and this house, which I have hallowed for my name, will I cast out of my sight; and Israel shall be a proverb and a byword among all people:
verse	11	9	8	@@And at this house, @9which@7 is high, every one that passeth by it shall be astonished, and shall hiss; and they shall say, Why hath the LORD done thus unto this land, and to this house?
verse	11	9	9	And they shall answer, Because they forsook the LORD their God, who brought forth their fathers out of the land of Egypt, and have taken hold upon other gods, and have worshipped them, and served them: therefore hath the LORD brought upon them all this evil.
verse	11	9	10	And it came to pass at the end of twenty years, when Solomon had built the two houses, the house of the LORD, and the king's house,
verse	11	9	11	@@(@9Now@7 Hiram the king of Tyre had furnished Solomon with cedar trees and fir trees, and with gold, according to all his desire,) that then king Solomon gave Hiram twenty cities in the land of Galilee.
verse	11	9	12	And Hiram came out from Tyre to see the cities which Solomon had given him; and they pleased him not.
verse	11	9	13	@@And he said, What cities @9are@7 these which thou hast given me, my brother? And he called them the land of Cabul unto this day.
verse	11	9	14	And Hiram sent to the king sixscore talents of gold.
verse	11	9	15	@@And this @9is@7 the reason of the levy which king Solomon raised; for to build the house of the LORD, and his own house, and Millo, and the wall of Jerusalem, and Hazor, and Megiddo, and Gezer.
verse	11	9	16	@@@9For@7 Pharaoh king of Egypt had gone up, and taken Gezer, and burnt it with fire, and slain the Canaanites that dwelt in the city, and given it @9for@7 a present unto his daughter, Solomon's wife.
verse	11	9	17	And Solomon built Gezer, and Bethhoron the nether,
verse	11	9	18	And Baalath, and Tadmor in the wilderness, in the land,
verse	11	9	19	And all the cities of store that Solomon had, and cities for his chariots, and cities for his horsemen, and that which Solomon desired to build in Jerusalem, and in Lebanon, and in all the land of his dominion.
verse	11	9	20	@@@9And@7 all the people @9that were@7 left of the Amorites, Hittites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites, which @9were@7 not of the children of Israel,
verse	11	9	21	Their children that were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel also were not able utterly to destroy, upon those did Solomon levy a tribute of bondservice unto this day.
verse	11	9	22	@@But of the children of Israel did Solomon make no bondmen: but they @9were@7 men of war, and his servants, and his princes, and his captains, and rulers of his chariots, and his horsemen.
verse	11	9	23	@@These @9were@7 the chief of the officers that @9were@7 over Solomon's work, five hundred and fifty, which bare rule over the people that wrought in the work.
verse	11	9	24	@@But Pharaoh's daughter came up out of the city of David unto her house which @9Solomon@7 had built for her: then did he build Millo.
verse	11	9	25	@@And three times in a year did Solomon offer burnt offerings and peace offerings upon the altar which he built unto the LORD, and he burnt incense upon the altar that @9was@7 before the LORD. So he finished the house.
verse	11	9	26	And king Solomon made a navy of ships in Eziongeber, which is beside Eloth, on the shore of the Red sea, in the land of Edom.
verse	11	9	27	And Hiram sent in the navy his servants, shipmen that had knowledge of the sea, with the servants of Solomon.
verse	11	9	28	@@And they came to Ophir, and fetched from thence gold, four hundred and twenty talents, and brought @9it@7 to king Solomon.
verse	11	10	1	And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon concerning the name of the LORD, she came to prove him with hard questions.
verse	11	10	2	And she came to Jerusalem with a very great train, with camels that bare spices, and very much gold, and precious stones: and when she was come to Solomon, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.
verse	11	10	3	@@And Solomon told her all her questions: there was not @9any@7 thing hid from the king, which he told her not.
verse	11	10	4	And when the queen of Sheba had seen all Solomon's wisdom, and the house that he had built,
verse	11	10	5	And the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel, and his cupbearers, and his ascent by which he went up unto the house of the LORD; there was no more spirit in her.
verse	11	10	6	And she said to the king, It was a true report that I heard in mine own land of thy acts and of thy wisdom.
verse	11	10	7	@@Howbeit I believed not the words, until I came, and mine eyes had seen @9it:@7 and, behold, the half was not told me: thy wisdom and prosperity exceedeth the fame which I heard.
verse	11	10	8	@@Happy @9are@7 thy men, happy @9are@7 these thy servants, which stand continually before thee, @9and@7 that hear thy wisdom.
verse	11	10	9	Blessed be the LORD thy God, which delighted in thee, to set thee on the throne of Israel: because the LORD loved Israel for ever, therefore made he thee king, to do judgment and justice.
verse	11	10	10	And she gave the king an hundred and twenty talents of gold, and of spices very great store, and precious stones: there came no more such abundance of spices as these which the queen of Sheba gave to king Solomon.
verse	11	10	11	And the navy also of Hiram, that brought gold from Ophir, brought in from Ophir great plenty of almug trees, and precious stones.
verse	11	10	12	And the king made of the almug trees pillars for the house of the LORD, and for the king's house, harps also and psalteries for singers: there came no such almug trees, nor were seen unto this day.
verse	11	10	13	@@And king Solomon gave unto the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatsoever she asked, beside @9that@7 which Solomon gave her of his royal bounty. So she turned and went to her own country, she and her servants.
verse	11	10	14	Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred threescore and six talents of gold,
verse	11	10	15	@@Beside @9that he had@7 of the merchantmen, and of the traffick of the spice merchants, and of all the kings of Arabia, and of the governors of the country.
verse	11	10	16	@@And king Solomon made two hundred targets of beaten gold: six hundred @9shekels@7 of gold went to one target.
verse	11	10	17	And he made three hundred shields of beaten gold; three pound of gold went to one shield: and the king put them in the house of the forest of Lebanon.
verse	11	10	18	Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with the best gold.
verse	11	10	19	@@The throne had six steps, and the top of the throne @9was@7 round behind: and @9there were@7 stays on either side on the place of the seat, and two lions stood beside the stays.
verse	11	10	20	And twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other upon the six steps: there was not the like made in any kingdom.
verse	11	10	21	@@And all king Solomon's drinking vessels @9were of@7 gold, and all the vessels of the house of the forest of Lebanon @9were of@7 pure gold; none @9were of@7 silver: it was nothing accounted of in the days of Solomon.
verse	11	10	22	For the king had at sea a navy of Tharshish with the navy of Hiram: once in three years came the navy of Tharshish, bringing gold, and silver, ivory, and apes, and peacocks.
verse	11	10	23	So king Solomon exceeded all the kings of the earth for riches and for wisdom.
verse	11	10	24	And all the earth sought to Solomon, to hear his wisdom, which God had put in his heart.
verse	11	10	25	And they brought every man his present, vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and garments, and armour, and spices, horses, and mules, a rate year by year.
verse	11	10	26	And Solomon gathered together chariots and horsemen: and he had a thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen, whom he bestowed in the cities for chariots, and with the king at Jerusalem.
verse	11	10	27	@@And the king made silver @9to be@7 in Jerusalem as stones, and cedars made he @9to be@7 as the sycomore trees that @9are@7 in the vale, for abundance.
verse	11	10	28	And Solomon had horses brought out of Egypt, and linen yarn: the king's merchants received the linen yarn at a price.
verse	11	10	29	@@And a chariot came up and went out of Egypt for six hundred @9shekels@7 of silver, and an horse for an hundred and fifty: and so for all the kings of the Hittites, and for the kings of Syria, did they bring @9them@7 out by their means.
verse	11	11	1	@@But king Solomon loved many strange women, together with the daughter of Pharaoh, women of the Moabites, Ammonites, Edomites, Zidonians, @9and@7 Hittites;
verse	11	11	2	@@Of the nations @9concerning@7 which the LORD said unto the children of Israel, Ye shall not go in to them, neither shall they come in unto you: @9for@7 surely they will turn away your heart after their gods: Solomon clave unto these in love.
verse	11	11	3	And he had seven hundred wives, princesses, and three hundred concubines: and his wives turned away his heart.
verse	11	11	4	@@For it came to pass, when Solomon was old, @9that@7 his wives turned away his heart after other gods: and his heart was not perfect with the LORD his God, as @9was@7 the heart of David his father.
verse	11	11	5	For Solomon went after Ashtoreth the goddess of the Zidonians, and after Milcom the abomination of the Ammonites.
verse	11	11	6	@@And Solomon did evil in the sight of the LORD, and went not fully after the LORD, as @9did@7 David his father.
verse	11	11	7	@@Then did Solomon build an high place for Chemosh, the abomination of Moab, in the hill that @9is@7 before Jerusalem, and for Molech, the abomination of the children of Ammon.
verse	11	11	8	And likewise did he for all his strange wives, which burnt incense and sacrificed unto their gods.
verse	11	11	9	And the LORD was angry with Solomon, because his heart was turned from the LORD God of Israel, which had appeared unto him twice,
verse	11	11	10	And had commanded him concerning this thing, that he should not go after other gods: but he kept not that which the LORD commanded.
verse	11	11	11	Wherefore the LORD said unto Solomon, Forasmuch as this is done of thee, and thou hast not kept my covenant and my statutes, which I have commanded thee, I will surely rend the kingdom from thee, and will give it to thy servant.
verse	11	11	12	@@Notwithstanding in thy days I will not do it for David thy father's sake: @9but@7 I will rend it out of the hand of thy son.
verse	11	11	13	@@Howbeit I will not rend away all the kingdom; @9but@7 will give one tribe to thy son for David my servant's sake, and for Jerusalem's sake which I have chosen.
verse	11	11	14	@@And the LORD stirred up an adversary unto Solomon, Hadad the Edomite: he @9was@7 of the king's seed in Edom.
verse	11	11	15	For it came to pass, when David was in Edom, and Joab the captain of the host was gone up to bury the slain, after he had smitten every male in Edom;
verse	11	11	16	(For six months did Joab remain there with all Israel, until he had cut off every male in Edom:)
verse	11	11	17	@@That Hadad fled, he and certain Edomites of his father's servants with him, to go into Egypt; Hadad @9being@7 yet a little child.
verse	11	11	18	And they arose out of Midian, and came to Paran: and they took men with them out of Paran, and they came to Egypt, unto Pharaoh king of Egypt; which gave him an house, and appointed him victuals, and gave him land.
verse	11	11	19	And Hadad found great favour in the sight of Pharaoh, so that he gave him to wife the sister of his own wife, the sister of Tahpenes the queen.
verse	11	11	20	And the sister of Tahpenes bare him Genubath his son, whom Tahpenes weaned in Pharaoh's house: and Genubath was in Pharaoh's household among the sons of Pharaoh.
verse	11	11	21	And when Hadad heard in Egypt that David slept with his fathers, and that Joab the captain of the host was dead, Hadad said to Pharaoh, Let me depart, that I may go to mine own country.
verse	11	11	22	Then Pharaoh said unto him, But what hast thou lacked with me, that, behold, thou seekest to go to thine own country? And he answered, Nothing: howbeit let me go in any wise.
verse	11	11	23	@@And God stirred him up @9another@7 adversary, Rezon the son of Eliadah, which fled from his lord Hadadezer king of Zobah:
verse	11	11	24	@@And he gathered men unto him, and became captain over a band, when David slew them @9of Zobah:@7 and they went to Damascus, and dwelt therein, and reigned in Damascus.
verse	11	11	25	@@And he was an adversary to Israel all the days of Solomon, beside the mischief that Hadad @9did:@7 and he abhorred Israel, and reigned over Syria.
verse	11	11	26	@@And Jeroboam the son of Nebat, an Ephrathite of Zereda, Solomon's servant, whose mother's name @9was@7 Zeruah, a widow woman, even he lifted up @9his@7 hand against the king.
verse	11	11	27	@@And this @9was@7 the cause that he lifted up @9his@7 hand against the king: Solomon built Millo, @9and@7 repaired the breaches of the city of David his father.
verse	11	11	28	@@And the man Jeroboam @9was@7 a mighty man of valour: and Solomon seeing the young man that he was industrious, he made him ruler over all the charge of the house of Joseph.
verse	11	11	29	@@And it came to pass at that time when Jeroboam went out of Jerusalem, that the prophet Ahijah the Shilonite found him in the way; and he had clad himself with a new garment; and they two @9were@7 alone in the field:
verse	11	11	30	@@And Ahijah caught the new garment that @9was@7 on him, and rent it @9in@7 twelve pieces:
verse	11	11	31	And he said to Jeroboam, Take thee ten pieces: for thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, Behold, I will rend the kingdom out of the hand of Solomon, and will give ten tribes to thee:
verse	11	11	32	(But he shall have one tribe for my servant David's sake, and for Jerusalem's sake, the city which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel:)
verse	11	11	33	@@Because that they have forsaken me, and have worshipped Ashtoreth the goddess of the Zidonians, Chemosh the god of the Moabites, and Milcom the god of the children of Ammon, and have not walked in my ways, to do @9that which is@7 right in mine eyes, and @9to keep@7 my statutes and my judgments, as @9did@7 David his father.
verse	11	11	34	Howbeit I will not take the whole kingdom out of his hand: but I will make him prince all the days of his life for David my servant's sake, whom I chose, because he kept my commandments and my statutes:
verse	11	11	35	@@But I will take the kingdom out of his son's hand, and will give it unto thee, @9even@7 ten tribes.
verse	11	11	36	And unto his son will I give one tribe, that David my servant may have a light alway before me in Jerusalem, the city which I have chosen me to put my name there.
verse	11	11	37	And I will take thee, and thou shalt reign according to all that thy soul desireth, and shalt be king over Israel.
verse	11	11	38	@@And it shall be, if thou wilt hearken unto all that I command thee, and wilt walk in my ways, and do @9that is@7 right in my sight, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as David my servant did; that I will be with thee, and build thee a sure house, as I built for David, and will give Israel unto thee.
verse	11	11	39	And I will for this afflict the seed of David, but not for ever.
verse	11	11	40	Solomon sought therefore to kill Jeroboam. And Jeroboam arose, and fled into Egypt, unto Shishak king of Egypt, and was in Egypt until the death of Solomon.
verse	11	11	41	@@And the rest of the acts of Solomon, and all that he did, and his wisdom, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the acts of Solomon?
verse	11	11	42	@@And the time that Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel @9was@7 forty years.
verse	11	11	43	And Solomon slept with his fathers, and was buried in the city of David his father: and Rehoboam his son reigned in his stead.
verse	11	12	1	And Rehoboam went to Shechem: for all Israel were come to Shechem to make him king.
verse	11	12	2	@@And it came to pass, when Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who was yet in Egypt, heard @9of it,@7 (for he was fled from the presence of king Solomon, and Jeroboam dwelt in Egypt;)
verse	11	12	3	That they sent and called him. And Jeroboam and all the congregation of Israel came, and spake unto Rehoboam, saying,
verse	11	12	4	Thy father made our yoke grievous: now therefore make thou the grievous service of thy father, and his heavy yoke which he put upon us, lighter, and we will serve thee.
verse	11	12	5	@@And he said unto them, Depart yet @9for@7 three days, then come again to me. And the people departed.
verse	11	12	6	And king Rehoboam consulted with the old men, that stood before Solomon his father while he yet lived, and said, How do ye advise that I may answer this people?
verse	11	12	7	And they spake unto him, saying, If thou wilt be a servant unto this people this day, and wilt serve them, and answer them, and speak good words to them, then they will be thy servants for ever.
verse	11	12	8	@@But he forsook the counsel of the old men, which they had given him, and consulted with the young men that were grown up with him, @9and@7 which stood before him:
verse	11	12	9	And he said unto them, What counsel give ye that we may answer this people, who have spoken to me, saying, Make the yoke which thy father did put upon us lighter?
verse	11	12	10	@@And the young men that were grown up with him spake unto him, saying, Thus shalt thou speak unto this people that spake unto thee, saying, Thy father made our yoke heavy, but make thou @9it@7 lighter unto us; thus shalt thou say unto them, My little @9finger@7 shall be thicker than my father's loins.
verse	11	12	11	And now whereas my father did lade you with a heavy yoke, I will add to your yoke: my father hath chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.
verse	11	12	12	So Jeroboam and all the people came to Rehoboam the third day, as the king had appointed, saying, Come to me again the third day.
verse	11	12	13	And the king answered the people roughly, and forsook the old men's counsel that they gave him;
verse	11	12	14	@@And spake to them after the counsel of the young men, saying, My father made your yoke heavy, and I will add to your yoke: my father @9also@7 chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.
verse	11	12	15	Wherefore the king hearkened not unto the people; for the cause was from the LORD, that he might perform his saying, which the LORD spake by Ahijah the Shilonite unto Jeroboam the son of Nebat.
verse	11	12	16	@@So when all Israel saw that the king hearkened not unto them, the people answered the king, saying, What portion have we in David? neither @9have we@7 inheritance in the son of Jesse: to your tents, O Israel: now see to thine own house, David. So Israel departed unto their tents.
verse	11	12	17	@@But @9as for@7 the children of Israel which dwelt in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them.
verse	11	12	18	@@Then king Rehoboam sent Adoram, who @9was@7 over the tribute; and all Israel stoned him with stones, that he died. Therefore king Rehoboam made speed to get him up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem.
verse	11	12	19	So Israel rebelled against the house of David unto this day.
verse	11	12	20	And it came to pass, when all Israel heard that Jeroboam was come again, that they sent and called him unto the congregation, and made him king over all Israel: there was none that followed the house of David, but the tribe of Judah only.
verse	11	12	21	And when Rehoboam was come to Jerusalem, he assembled all the house of Judah, with the tribe of Benjamin, an hundred and fourscore thousand chosen men, which were warriors, to fight against the house of Israel, to bring the kingdom again to Rehoboam the son of Solomon.
verse	11	12	22	But the word of God came unto Shemaiah the man of God, saying,
verse	11	12	23	Speak unto Rehoboam, the son of Solomon, king of Judah, and unto all the house of Judah and Benjamin, and to the remnant of the people, saying,
verse	11	12	24	Thus saith the LORD, Ye shall not go up, nor fight against your brethren the children of Israel: return every man to his house; for this thing is from me. They hearkened therefore to the word of the LORD, and returned to depart, according to the word of the LORD.
verse	11	12	25	Then Jeroboam built Shechem in mount Ephraim, and dwelt therein; and went out from thence, and built Penuel.
verse	11	12	26	And Jeroboam said in his heart, Now shall the kingdom return to the house of David:
verse	11	12	27	@@If this people go up to do sacrifice in the house of the LORD at Jerusalem, then shall the heart of this people turn again unto their lord, @9even@7 unto Rehoboam king of Judah, and they shall kill me, and go again to Rehoboam king of Judah.
verse	11	12	28	@@Whereupon the king took counsel, and made two calves @9of@7 gold, and said unto them, It is too much for you to go up to Jerusalem: behold thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.
verse	11	12	29	And he set the one in Bethel, and the other put he in Dan.
verse	11	12	30	@@And this thing became a sin: for the people went @9to worship@7 before the one, @9even@7 unto Dan.
verse	11	12	31	And he made an house of high places, and made priests of the lowest of the people, which were not of the sons of Levi.
verse	11	12	32	@@And Jeroboam ordained a feast in the eighth month, on the fifteenth day of the month, like unto the feast that @9is@7 in Judah, and he offered upon the altar. So did he in Bethel, sacrificing unto the calves that he had made: and he placed in Bethel the priests of the high places which he had made.
verse	11	12	33	@@So he offered upon the altar which he had made in Bethel the fifteenth day of the eighth month, @9even@7 in the month which he had devised of his own heart; and ordained a feast unto the children of Israel: and he offered upon the altar, and burnt incense.
verse	11	13	1	And, behold, there came a man of God out of Judah by the word of the LORD unto Bethel: and Jeroboam stood by the altar to burn incense.
verse	11	13	2	And he cried against the altar in the word of the LORD, and said, O altar, altar, thus saith the LORD; Behold, a child shall be born unto the house of David, Josiah by name; and upon thee shall he offer the priests of the high places that burn incense upon thee, and men's bones shall be burnt upon thee.
verse	11	13	3	@@And he gave a sign the same day, saying, This @9is@7 the sign which the LORD hath spoken; Behold, the altar shall be rent, and the ashes that @9are@7 upon it shall be poured out.
verse	11	13	4	And it came to pass, when king Jeroboam heard the saying of the man of God, which had cried against the altar in Bethel, that he put forth his hand from the altar, saying, Lay hold on him. And his hand, which he put forth against him, dried up, so that he could not pull it in again to him.
verse	11	13	5	The altar also was rent, and the ashes poured out from the altar, according to the sign which the man of God had given by the word of the LORD.
verse	11	13	6	@@And the king answered and said unto the man of God, Intreat now the face of the LORD thy God, and pray for me, that my hand may be restored me again. And the man of God besought the LORD, and the king's hand was restored him again, and became as @9it was@7 before.
verse	11	13	7	And the king said unto the man of God, Come home with me, and refresh thyself, and I will give thee a reward.
verse	11	13	8	And the man of God said unto the king, If thou wilt give me half thine house, I will not go in with thee, neither will I eat bread nor drink water in this place:
verse	11	13	9	For so was it charged me by the word of the LORD, saying, Eat no bread, nor drink water, nor turn again by the same way that thou camest.
verse	11	13	10	So he went another way, and returned not by the way that he came to Bethel.
verse	11	13	11	Now there dwelt an old prophet in Bethel; and his sons came and told him all the works that the man of God had done that day in Bethel: the words which he had spoken unto the king, them they told also to their father.
verse	11	13	12	And their father said unto them, What way went he? For his sons had seen what way the man of God went, which came from Judah.
verse	11	13	13	And he said unto his sons, Saddle me the ass. So they saddled him the ass: and he rode thereon,
verse	11	13	14	@@And went after the man of God, and found him sitting under an oak: and he said unto him, @9Art@7 thou the man of God that camest from Judah? And he said, I @9am. @7
verse	11	13	15	Then he said unto him, Come home with me, and eat bread.
verse	11	13	16	And he said, I may not return with thee, nor go in with thee: neither will I eat bread nor drink water with thee in this place:
verse	11	13	17	For it was said to me by the word of the LORD, Thou shalt eat no bread nor drink water there, nor turn again to go by the way that thou camest.
verse	11	13	18	@@He said unto him, I @9am@7 a prophet also as thou @9art;@7 and an angel spake unto me by the word of the LORD, saying, Bring him back with thee into thine house, that he may eat bread and drink water. @9But@7 he lied unto him.
verse	11	13	19	So he went back with him, and did eat bread in his house, and drank water.
verse	11	13	20	And it came to pass, as they sat at the table, that the word of the LORD came unto the prophet that brought him back:
verse	11	13	21	And he cried unto the man of God that came from Judah, saying, Thus saith the LORD, Forasmuch as thou hast disobeyed the mouth of the LORD, and hast not kept the commandment which the LORD thy God commanded thee,
verse	11	13	22	@@But camest back, and hast eaten bread and drunk water in the place, of the which @9the LORD@7 did say to thee, Eat no bread, and drink no water; thy carcase shall not come unto the sepulchre of thy fathers.
verse	11	13	23	@@And it came to pass, after he had eaten bread, and after he had drunk, that he saddled for him the ass, @9to wit,@7 for the prophet whom he had brought back.
verse	11	13	24	And when he was gone, a lion met him by the way, and slew him: and his carcase was cast in the way, and the ass stood by it, the lion also stood by the carcase.
verse	11	13	25	And, behold, men passed by, and saw the carcase cast in the way, and the lion standing by the carcase: and they came and told it in the city where the old prophet dwelt.
verse	11	13	26	@@And when the prophet that brought him back from the way heard @9thereof,@7 he said, It @9is@7 the man of God, who was disobedient unto the word of the LORD: therefore the LORD hath delivered him unto the lion, which hath torn him, and slain him, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake unto him.
verse	11	13	27	@@And he spake to his sons, saying, Saddle me the ass. And they saddled @9him. @7
verse	11	13	28	And he went and found his carcase cast in the way, and the ass and the lion standing by the carcase: the lion had not eaten the carcase, nor torn the ass.
verse	11	13	29	And the prophet took up the carcase of the man of God, and laid it upon the ass, and brought it back: and the old prophet came to the city, to mourn and to bury him.
verse	11	13	30	@@And he laid his carcase in his own grave; and they mourned over him, @9saying,@7 Alas, my brother!
verse	11	13	31	@@And it came to pass, after he had buried him, that he spake to his sons, saying, When I am dead, then bury me in the sepulchre wherein the man of God @9is@7 buried; lay my bones beside his bones:
