verse	11	16	3	Behold, I will take away the posterity of Baasha, and the posterity of his house; and will make thy house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat.
verse	11	16	4	Him that dieth of Baasha in the city shall the dogs eat; and him that dieth of his in the fields shall the fowls of the air eat.
verse	11	16	5	@@Now the rest of the acts of Baasha, and what he did, and his might, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?
verse	11	16	6	So Baasha slept with his fathers, and was buried in Tirzah: and Elah his son reigned in his stead.
verse	11	16	7	And also by the hand of the prophet Jehu the son of Hanani came the word of the LORD against Baasha, and against his house, even for all the evil that he did in the sight of the LORD, in provoking him to anger with the work of his hands, in being like the house of Jeroboam; and because he killed him.
