verse	11	16	13	For all the sins of Baasha, and the sins of Elah his son, by which they sinned, and by which they made Israel to sin, in provoking the LORD God of Israel to anger with their vanities.
verse	11	16	14	@@Now the rest of the acts of Elah, and all that he did, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?
verse	11	16	15	@@In the twenty and seventh year of Asa king of Judah did Zimri reign seven days in Tirzah. And the people @9were@7 encamped against Gibbethon, which @9belonged@7 to the Philistines.
verse	11	16	16	@@And the people @9that were@7 encamped heard say, Zimri hath conspired, and hath also slain the king: wherefore all Israel made Omri, the captain of the host, king over Israel that day in the camp.
verse	11	16	17	And Omri went up from Gibbethon, and all Israel with him, and they besieged Tirzah.
