verse	11	16	28	So Omri slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria: and Ahab his son reigned in his stead.
verse	11	16	29	And in the thirty and eighth year of Asa king of Judah began Ahab the son of Omri to reign over Israel: and Ahab the son of Omri reigned over Israel in Samaria twenty and two years.
verse	11	16	30	@@And Ahab the son of Omri did evil in the sight of the LORD above all that @9were@7 before him.
verse	11	16	31	And it came to pass, as if it had been a light thing for him to walk in the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, that he took to wife Jezebel the daughter of Ethbaal king of the Zidonians, and went and served Baal, and worshipped him.
verse	11	16	32	And he reared up an altar for Baal in the house of Baal, which he had built in Samaria.
verse	11	16	33	And Ahab made a grove; and Ahab did more to provoke the LORD God of Israel to anger than all the kings of Israel that were before him.
verse	11	16	34	@@In his days did Hiel the Bethelite build Jericho: he laid the foundation thereof in Abiram his firstborn, and set up the gates thereof in his youngest @9son@7 Segub, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake by Joshua the son of Nun.
verse	11	17	1	@@And Elijah the Tishbite, @9who was@7 of the inhabitants of Gilead, said unto Ahab, @9As@7 the LORD God of Israel liveth, before whom I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word.
verse	11	17	2	And the word of the LORD came unto him, saying,
