verse	11	17	4	@@And it shall be, @9that@7 thou shalt drink of the brook; and I have commanded the ravens to feed thee there.
verse	11	17	5	@@So he went and did according unto the word of the LORD: for he went and dwelt by the brook Cherith, that @9is@7 before Jordan.
verse	11	17	6	And the ravens brought him bread and flesh in the morning, and bread and flesh in the evening; and he drank of the brook.
verse	11	17	7	And it came to pass after a while, that the brook dried up, because there had been no rain in the land.
verse	11	17	8	And the word of the LORD came unto him, saying,
verse	11	17	9	@@Arise, get thee to Zarephath, which @9belongeth@7 to Zidon, and dwell there: behold, I have commanded a widow woman there to sustain thee.
verse	11	17	10	@@So he arose and went to Zarephath. And when he came to the gate of the city, behold, the widow woman @9was@7 there gathering of sticks: and he called to her, and said, Fetch me, I pray thee, a little water in a vessel, that I may drink.
verse	11	17	11	@@And as she was going to fetch @9it,@7 he called to her, and said, Bring me, I pray thee, a morsel of bread in thine hand.
verse	11	17	12	@@And she said, @9As@7 the LORD thy God liveth, I have not a cake, but an handful of meal in a barrel, and a little oil in a cruse: and, behold, I @9am@7 gathering two sticks, that I may go in and dress it for me and my son, that we may eat it, and die.
verse	11	17	13	@@And Elijah said unto her, Fear not; go @9and@7 do as thou hast said: but make me thereof a little cake first, and bring @9it@7 unto me, and after make for thee and for thy son.
verse	11	17	14	@@For thus saith the LORD God of Israel, The barrel of meal shall not waste, neither shall the cruse of oil fail, until the day @9that@7 the LORD sendeth rain upon the earth.
verse	11	17	15	@@And she went and did according to the saying of Elijah: and she, and he, and her house, did eat @9many@7 days.
verse	11	17	16	@@@9And@7 the barrel of meal wasted not, neither did the cruse of oil fail, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake by Elijah.
verse	11	17	17	@@And it came to pass after these things, @9that@7 the son of the woman, the mistress of the house, fell sick; and his sickness was so sore, that there was no breath left in him.
verse	11	17	18	And she said unto Elijah, What have I to do with thee, O thou man of God? art thou come unto me to call my sin to remembrance, and to slay my son?
verse	11	17	19	And he said unto her, Give me thy son. And he took him out of her bosom, and carried him up into a loft, where he abode, and laid him upon his own bed.
verse	11	17	20	And he cried unto the LORD, and said, O LORD my God, hast thou also brought evil upon the widow with whom I sojourn, by slaying her son?
verse	11	17	21	And he stretched himself upon the child three times, and cried unto the LORD, and said, O LORD my God, I pray thee, let this child's soul come into him again.
