verse	11	18	21	@@And Elijah came unto all the people, and said, How long halt ye between two opinions? if the LORD @9be@7 God, follow him: but if Baal, @9then@7 follow him. And the people answered him not a word.
verse	11	18	22	@@Then said Elijah unto the people, I, @9even@7 I only, remain a prophet of the LORD; but Baal's prophets @9are@7 four hundred and fifty men.
verse	11	18	23	@@Let them therefore give us two bullocks; and let them choose one bullock for themselves, and cut it in pieces, and lay @9it@7 on wood, and put no fire @9under:@7 and I will dress the other bullock, and lay @9it@7 on wood, and put no fire @9under: @7
verse	11	18	24	And call ye on the name of your gods, and I will call on the name of the LORD: and the God that answereth by fire, let him be God. And all the people answered and said, It is well spoken.
verse	11	18	25	@@And Elijah said unto the prophets of Baal, Choose you one bullock for yourselves, and dress @9it@7 first; for ye @9are@7 many; and call on the name of your gods, but put no fire @9under. @7
verse	11	18	26	@@And they took the bullock which was given them, and they dressed @9it,@7 and called on the name of Baal from morning even until noon, saying, O Baal, hear us. But @9there was@7 no voice, nor any that answered. And they leaped upon the altar which was made.
verse	11	18	27	@@And it came to pass at noon, that Elijah mocked them, and said, Cry aloud: for he @9is@7 a god; either he is talking, or he is pursuing, or he is in a journey, @9or@7 peradventure he sleepeth, and must be awaked.
