verse	11	22	17	And he said, I saw all Israel scattered upon the hills, as sheep that have not a shepherd: and the LORD said, These have no master: let them return every man to his house in peace.
verse	11	22	18	And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, Did I not tell thee that he would prophesy no good concerning me, but evil?
verse	11	22	19	And he said, Hear thou therefore the word of the LORD: I saw the LORD sitting on his throne, and all the host of heaven standing by him on his right hand and on his left.
verse	11	22	20	And the LORD said, Who shall persuade Ahab, that he may go up and fall at Ramothgilead? And one said on this manner, and another said on that manner.
verse	11	22	21	And there came forth a spirit, and stood before the LORD, and said, I will persuade him.
verse	11	22	22	@@And the LORD said unto him, Wherewith? And he said, I will go forth, and I will be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets. And he said, Thou shalt persuade @9him,@7 and prevail also: go forth, and do so.
verse	11	22	23	Now therefore, behold, the LORD hath put a lying spirit in the mouth of all these thy prophets, and the LORD hath spoken evil concerning thee.
verse	11	22	24	But Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah went near, and smote Micaiah on the cheek, and said, Which way went the Spirit of the LORD from me to speak unto thee?
verse	11	22	25	And Micaiah said, Behold, thou shalt see in that day, when thou shalt go into an inner chamber to hide thyself.
verse	11	22	26	And the king of Israel said, Take Micaiah, and carry him back unto Amon the governor of the city, and to Joash the king's son;
verse	11	22	27	@@And say, Thus saith the king, Put this @9fellow@7 in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I come in peace.
verse	11	22	28	And Micaiah said, If thou return at all in peace, the LORD hath not spoken by me. And he said, Hearken, O people, every one of you.
verse	11	22	29	So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went up to Ramothgilead.
verse	11	22	30	And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, I will disguise myself, and enter into the battle; but put thou on thy robes. And the king of Israel disguised himself, and went into the battle.
verse	11	22	31	But the king of Syria commanded his thirty and two captains that had rule over his chariots, saying, Fight neither with small nor great, save only with the king of Israel.
verse	11	22	32	@@And it came to pass, when the captains of the chariots saw Jehoshaphat, that they said, Surely it @9is@7 the king of Israel. And they turned aside to fight against him: and Jehoshaphat cried out.
verse	11	22	33	@@And it came to pass, when the captains of the chariots perceived that it @9was@7 not the king of Israel, that they turned back from pursuing him.
verse	11	22	34	@@And a @9certain@7 man drew a bow at a venture, and smote the king of Israel between the joints of the harness: wherefore he said unto the driver of his chariot, Turn thine hand, and carry me out of the host; for I am wounded.
verse	11	22	35	And the battle increased that day: and the king was stayed up in his chariot against the Syrians, and died at even: and the blood ran out of the wound into the midst of the chariot.
verse	11	22	36	And there went a proclamation throughout the host about the going down of the sun, saying, Every man to his city, and every man to his own country.
verse	11	22	37	So the king died, and was brought to Samaria; and they buried the king in Samaria.
verse	11	22	38	@@And @9one@7 washed the chariot in the pool of Samaria; and the dogs licked up his blood; and they washed his armour; according unto the word of the LORD which he spake.
verse	11	22	39	@@Now the rest of the acts of Ahab, and all that he did, and the ivory house which he made, and all the cities that he built, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?
verse	11	22	40	So Ahab slept with his fathers; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his stead.
verse	11	22	41	And Jehoshaphat the son of Asa began to reign over Judah in the fourth year of Ahab king of Israel.
verse	11	22	42	@@Jehoshaphat @9was@7 thirty and five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty and five years in Jerusalem. And his mother's name @9was@7 Azubah the daughter of Shilhi.
verse	11	22	43	@@And he walked in all the ways of Asa his father; he turned not aside from it, doing @9that which was@7 right in the eyes of the LORD: nevertheless the high places were not taken away; @9for@7 the people offered and burnt incense yet in the high places.
verse	11	22	44	And Jehoshaphat made peace with the king of Israel.
verse	11	22	45	@@Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, and his might that he shewed, and how he warred, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?
verse	11	22	46	And the remnant of the sodomites, which remained in the days of his father Asa, he took out of the land.
verse	11	22	47	@@@9There was@7 then no king in Edom: a deputy @9was@7 king.
verse	11	22	48	Jehoshaphat made ships of Tharshish to go to Ophir for gold: but they went not; for the ships were broken at Eziongeber.
verse	11	22	49	Then said Ahaziah the son of Ahab unto Jehoshaphat, Let my servants go with thy servants in the ships. But Jehoshaphat would not.
verse	11	22	50	And Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David his father: and Jehoram his son reigned in his stead.
verse	11	22	51	Ahaziah the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria the seventeenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and reigned two years over Israel.
verse	11	22	52	And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, and walked in the way of his father, and in the way of his mother, and in the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin:
verse	11	22	53	For he served Baal, and worshipped him, and provoked to anger the LORD God of Israel, according to all that his father had done.
verse	12	1	1	Then Moab rebelled against Israel after the death of Ahab.
verse	12	1	2	@@And Ahaziah fell down through a lattice in his upper chamber that @9was@7 in Samaria, and was sick: and he sent messengers, and said unto them, Go, enquire of Baalzebub the god of Ekron whether I shall recover of this disease.
verse	12	1	3	@@But the angel of the LORD said to Elijah the Tishbite, Arise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria, and say unto them, @9Is it@7 not because @9there is@7 not a God in Israel, @9that@7 ye go to enquire of Baalzebub the god of Ekron?
verse	12	1	4	Now therefore thus saith the LORD, Thou shalt not come down from that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die. And Elijah departed.
verse	12	1	5	And when the messengers turned back unto him, he said unto them, Why are ye now turned back?
verse	12	1	6	@@And they said unto him, There came a man up to meet us, and said unto us, Go, turn again unto the king that sent you, and say unto him, Thus saith the LORD, @9Is it@7 not because @9there is@7 not a God in Israel, @9that@7 thou sendest to enquire of Baalzebub the god of Ekron? therefore thou shalt not come down from that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die.
verse	12	1	7	@@And he said unto them, What manner of man @9was he@7 which came up to meet you, and told you these words?
verse	12	1	8	@@And they answered him, @9He was@7 an hairy man, and girt with a girdle of leather about his loins. And he said, It @9is@7 Elijah the Tishbite.
verse	12	1	9	Then the king sent unto him a captain of fifty with his fifty. And he went up to him: and, behold, he sat on the top of an hill. And he spake unto him, Thou man of God, the king hath said, Come down.
verse	12	1	10	@@And Elijah answered and said to the captain of fifty, If I @9be@7 a man of God, then let fire come down from heaven, and consume thee and thy fifty. And there came down fire from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.
verse	12	1	11	Again also he sent unto him another captain of fifty with his fifty. And he answered and said unto him, O man of God, thus hath the king said, Come down quickly.
verse	12	1	12	@@And Elijah answered and said unto them, If I @9be@7 a man of God, let fire come down from heaven, and consume thee and thy fifty. And the fire of God came down from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.
verse	12	1	13	And he sent again a captain of the third fifty with his fifty. And the third captain of fifty went up, and came and fell on his knees before Elijah, and besought him, and said unto him, O man of God, I pray thee, let my life, and the life of these fifty thy servants, be precious in thy sight.
verse	12	1	14	Behold, there came fire down from heaven, and burnt up the two captains of the former fifties with their fifties: therefore let my life now be precious in thy sight.
verse	12	1	15	And the angel of the LORD said unto Elijah, Go down with him: be not afraid of him. And he arose, and went down with him unto the king.
verse	12	1	16	@@And he said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Forasmuch as thou hast sent messengers to enquire of Baalzebub the god of Ekron, @9is it@7 not because @9there is@7 no God in Israel to enquire of his word? therefore thou shalt not come down off that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die.
verse	12	1	17	So he died according to the word of the LORD which Elijah had spoken. And Jehoram reigned in his stead in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah; because he had no son.
verse	12	1	18	@@Now the rest of the acts of Ahaziah which he did, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?
verse	12	2	1	And it came to pass, when the LORD would take up Elijah into heaven by a whirlwind, that Elijah went with Elisha from Gilgal.
verse	12	2	2	@@And Elijah said unto Elisha, Tarry here, I pray thee; for the LORD hath sent me to Bethel. And Elisha said @9unto him, As@7 the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. So they went down to Bethel.
verse	12	2	3	@@And the sons of the prophets that @9were@7 at Bethel came forth to Elisha, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the LORD will take away thy master from thy head to day? And he said, Yea, I know @9it;@7 hold ye your peace.
verse	12	2	4	@@And Elijah said unto him, Elisha, tarry here, I pray thee; for the LORD hath sent me to Jericho. And he said, @9As@7 the LORD liveth, and @9as@7 thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. So they came to Jericho.
verse	12	2	5	@@And the sons of the prophets that @9were@7 at Jericho came to Elisha, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the LORD will take away thy master from thy head to day? And he answered, Yea, I know @9it;@7 hold ye your peace.
verse	12	2	6	@@And Elijah said unto him, Tarry, I pray thee, here; for the LORD hath sent me to Jordan. And he said, @9As@7 the LORD liveth, and @9as@7 thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. And they two went on.
verse	12	2	7	And fifty men of the sons of the prophets went, and stood to view afar off: and they two stood by Jordan.
verse	12	2	8	@@And Elijah took his mantle, and wrapped @9it@7 together, and smote the waters, and they were divided hither and thither, so that they two went over on dry ground.
verse	12	2	9	And it came to pass, when they were gone over, that Elijah said unto Elisha, Ask what I shall do for thee, before I be taken away from thee. And Elisha said, I pray thee, let a double portion of thy spirit be upon me.
verse	12	2	10	@@And he said, Thou hast asked a hard thing: @9nevertheless,@7 if thou see me @9when I am@7 taken from thee, it shall be so unto thee; but if not, it shall not be so.
verse	12	2	11	@@And it came to pass, as they still went on, and talked, that, behold, @9there appeared@7 a chariot of fire, and horses of fire, and parted them both asunder; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven.
verse	12	2	12	@@And Elisha saw @9it,@7 and he cried, My father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof. And he saw him no more: and he took hold of his own clothes, and rent them in two pieces.
verse	12	2	13	He took up also the mantle of Elijah that fell from him, and went back, and stood by the bank of Jordan;
verse	12	2	14	@@And he took the mantle of Elijah that fell from him, and smote the waters, and said, Where @9is@7 the LORD God of Elijah? and when he also had smitten the waters, they parted hither and thither: and Elisha went over.
verse	12	2	15	@@And when the sons of the prophets which @9were@7 to view at Jericho saw him, they said, The spirit of Elijah doth rest on Elisha. And they came to meet him, and bowed themselves to the ground before him.
verse	12	2	16	And they said unto him, Behold now, there be with thy servants fifty strong men; let them go, we pray thee, and seek thy master: lest peradventure the Spirit of the LORD hath taken him up, and cast him upon some mountain, or into some valley. And he said, Ye shall not send.
verse	12	2	17	And when they urged him till he was ashamed, he said, Send. They sent therefore fifty men; and they sought three days, but found him not.
verse	12	2	18	And when they came again to him, (for he tarried at Jericho,) he said unto them, Did I not say unto you, Go not?
verse	12	2	19	@@And the men of the city said unto Elisha, Behold, I pray thee, the situation of this city @9is@7 pleasant, as my lord seeth: but the water @9is@7 naught, and the ground barren.
verse	12	2	20	@@And he said, Bring me a new cruse, and put salt therein. And they brought @9it@7 to him.
verse	12	2	21	@@And he went forth unto the spring of the waters, and cast the salt in there, and said, Thus saith the LORD, I have healed these waters; there shall not be from thence any more death or barren @9land. @7
verse	12	2	22	So the waters were healed unto this day, according to the saying of Elisha which he spake.
verse	12	2	23	And he went up from thence unto Bethel: and as he was going up by the way, there came forth little children out of the city, and mocked him, and said unto him, Go up, thou bald head; go up, thou bald head.
verse	12	2	24	And he turned back, and looked on them, and cursed them in the name of the LORD. And there came forth two she bears out of the wood, and tare forty and two children of them.
verse	12	2	25	And he went from thence to mount Carmel, and from thence he returned to Samaria.
verse	12	3	1	Now Jehoram the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria the eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and reigned twelve years.
verse	12	3	2	And he wrought evil in the sight of the LORD; but not like his father, and like his mother: for he put away the image of Baal that his father had made.
verse	12	3	3	Nevertheless he cleaved unto the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, which made Israel to sin; he departed not therefrom.
verse	12	3	4	And Mesha king of Moab was a sheepmaster, and rendered unto the king of Israel an hundred thousand lambs, and an hundred thousand rams, with the wool.
verse	12	3	5	But it came to pass, when Ahab was dead, that the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel.
verse	12	3	6	And king Jehoram went out of Samaria the same time, and numbered all Israel.
verse	12	3	7	@@And he went and sent to Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, saying, The king of Moab hath rebelled against me: wilt thou go with me against Moab to battle? And he said, I will go up: I @9am@7 as thou @9art,@7 my people as thy people, @9and@7 my horses as thy horses.
verse	12	3	8	And he said, Which way shall we go up? And he answered, The way through the wilderness of Edom.
verse	12	3	9	So the king of Israel went, and the king of Judah, and the king of Edom: and they fetched a compass of seven days' journey: and there was no water for the host, and for the cattle that followed them.
verse	12	3	10	And the king of Israel said, Alas! that the LORD hath called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Moab!
verse	12	3	11	@@But Jehoshaphat said, @9Is there@7 not here a prophet of the LORD, that we may enquire of the LORD by him? And one of the king of Israel's servants answered and said, Here @9is@7 Elisha the son of Shaphat, which poured water on the hands of Elijah.
verse	12	3	12	And Jehoshaphat said, The word of the LORD is with him. So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him.
verse	12	3	13	And Elisha said unto the king of Israel, What have I to do with thee? get thee to the prophets of thy father, and to the prophets of thy mother. And the king of Israel said unto him, Nay: for the LORD hath called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Moab.
verse	12	3	14	@@And Elisha said, @9As@7 the LORD of hosts liveth, before whom I stand, surely, were it not that I regard the presence of Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, I would not look toward thee, nor see thee.
verse	12	3	15	But now bring me a minstrel. And it came to pass, when the minstrel played, that the hand of the LORD came upon him.
verse	12	3	16	And he said, Thus saith the LORD, Make this valley full of ditches.
verse	12	3	17	For thus saith the LORD, Ye shall not see wind, neither shall ye see rain; yet that valley shall be filled with water, that ye may drink, both ye, and your cattle, and your beasts.
verse	12	3	18	@@And this is @9but@7 a light thing in the sight of the LORD: he will deliver the Moabites also into your hand.
verse	12	3	19	And ye shall smite every fenced city, and every choice city, and shall fell every good tree, and stop all wells of water, and mar every good piece of land with stones.
verse	12	3	20	And it came to pass in the morning, when the meat offering was offered, that, behold, there came water by the way of Edom, and the country was filled with water.
verse	12	3	21	And when all the Moabites heard that the kings were come up to fight against them, they gathered all that were able to put on armour, and upward, and stood in the border.
verse	12	3	22	@@And they rose up early in the morning, and the sun shone upon the water, and the Moabites saw the water on the other side @9as@7 red as blood:
verse	12	3	23	@@And they said, This @9is@7 blood: the kings are surely slain, and they have smitten one another: now therefore, Moab, to the spoil.
verse	12	3	24	@@And when they came to the camp of Israel, the Israelites rose up and smote the Moabites, so that they fled before them: but they went forward smiting the Moabites, even in @9their@7 country.
verse	12	3	25	@@And they beat down the cities, and on every good piece of land cast every man his stone, and filled it; and they stopped all the wells of water, and felled all the good trees: only in Kirharaseth left they the stones thereof; howbeit the slingers went about @9it,@7 and smote it.
verse	12	3	26	@@And when the king of Moab saw that the battle was too sore for him, he took with him seven hundred men that drew swords, to break through @9even@7 unto the king of Edom: but they could not.
verse	12	3	27	@@Then he took his eldest son that should have reigned in his stead, and offered him @9for@7 a burnt offering upon the wall. And there was great indignation against Israel: and they departed from him, and returned to @9their own@7 land.
verse	12	4	1	Now there cried a certain woman of the wives of the sons of the prophets unto Elisha, saying, Thy servant my husband is dead; and thou knowest that thy servant did fear the LORD: and the creditor is come to take unto him my two sons to be bondmen.
verse	12	4	2	And Elisha said unto her, What shall I do for thee? tell me, what hast thou in the house? And she said, Thine handmaid hath not any thing in the house, save a pot of oil.
verse	12	4	3	@@Then he said, Go, borrow thee vessels abroad of all thy neighbours, @9even@7 empty vessels; borrow not a few.
verse	12	4	4	And when thou art come in, thou shalt shut the door upon thee and upon thy sons, and shalt pour out into all those vessels, and thou shalt set aside that which is full.
verse	12	4	5	@@So she went from him, and shut the door upon her and upon her sons, who brought @9the vessels@7 to her; and she poured out.
verse	12	4	6	@@And it came to pass, when the vessels were full, that she said unto her son, Bring me yet a vessel. And he said unto her, @9There is@7 not a vessel more. And the oil stayed.
verse	12	4	7	Then she came and told the man of God. And he said, Go, sell the oil, and pay thy debt, and live thou and thy children of the rest.
verse	12	4	8	@@And it fell on a day, that Elisha passed to Shunem, where @9was@7 a great woman; and she constrained him to eat bread. And so it was, @9that@7 as oft as he passed by, he turned in thither to eat bread.
verse	12	4	9	@@And she said unto her husband, Behold now, I perceive that this @9is@7 an holy man of God, which passeth by us continually.
verse	12	4	10	Let us make a little chamber, I pray thee, on the wall; and let us set for him there a bed, and a table, and a stool, and a candlestick: and it shall be, when he cometh to us, that he shall turn in thither.
verse	12	4	11	And it fell on a day, that he came thither, and he turned into the chamber, and lay there.
verse	12	4	12	And he said to Gehazi his servant, Call this Shunammite. And when he had called her, she stood before him.
verse	12	4	13	@@And he said unto him, Say now unto her, Behold, thou hast been careful for us with all this care; what @9is@7 to be done for thee? wouldest thou be spoken for to the king, or to the captain of the host? And she answered, I dwell among mine own people.
verse	12	4	14	@@And he said, What then @9is@7 to be done for her? And Gehazi answered, Verily she hath no child, and her husband is old.
verse	12	4	15	And he said, Call her. And when he had called her, she stood in the door.
verse	12	4	16	@@And he said, About this season, according to the time of life, thou shalt embrace a son. And she said, Nay, my lord, @9thou@7 man of God, do not lie unto thine handmaid.
verse	12	4	17	And the woman conceived, and bare a son at that season that Elisha had said unto her, according to the time of life.
verse	12	4	18	And when the child was grown, it fell on a day, that he went out to his father to the reapers.
