verse	12	4	20	@@And when he had taken him, and brought him to his mother, he sat on her knees till noon, and @9then@7 died.
verse	12	4	21	@@And she went up, and laid him on the bed of the man of God, and shut @9the door@7 upon him, and went out.
verse	12	4	22	And she called unto her husband, and said, Send me, I pray thee, one of the young men, and one of the asses, that I may run to the man of God, and come again.
verse	12	4	23	@@And he said, Wherefore wilt thou go to him to day? @9it is@7 neither new moon, nor sabbath. And she said, @9It shall be@7 well.
verse	12	4	24	@@Then she saddled an ass, and said to her servant, Drive, and go forward; slack not @9thy@7 riding for me, except I bid thee.
verse	12	4	25	@@So she went and came unto the man of God to mount Carmel. And it came to pass, when the man of God saw her afar off, that he said to Gehazi his servant, Behold, @9yonder is@7 that Shunammite:
verse	12	4	26	@@Run now, I pray thee, to meet her, and say unto her, @9Is it@7 well with thee? @9is it@7 well with thy husband? @9is it@7 well with the child? And she answered, @9It is@7 well.
verse	12	4	27	@@And when she came to the man of God to the hill, she caught him by the feet: but Gehazi came near to thrust her away. And the man of God said, Let her alone; for her soul @9is@7 vexed within her: and the LORD hath hid @9it@7 from me, and hath not told me.
verse	12	4	28	Then she said, Did I desire a son of my lord? did I not say, Do not deceive me?
verse	12	4	29	Then he said to Gehazi, Gird up thy loins, and take my staff in thine hand, and go thy way: if thou meet any man, salute him not; and if any salute thee, answer him not again: and lay my staff upon the face of the child.
verse	12	4	30	@@And the mother of the child said, @9As@7 the LORD liveth, and @9as@7 thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. And he arose, and followed her.
