verse	12	8	5	@@And it came to pass, as he was telling the king how he had restored a dead body to life, that, behold, the woman, whose son he had restored to life, cried to the king for her house and for her land. And Gehazi said, My lord, O king, this @9is@7 the woman, and this @9is@7 her son, whom Elisha restored to life.
verse	12	8	6	@@And when the king asked the woman, she told him. So the king appointed unto her a certain officer, saying, Restore all that @9was@7 hers, and all the fruits of the field since the day that she left the land, even until now.
verse	12	8	7	And Elisha came to Damascus; and Benhadad the king of Syria was sick; and it was told him, saying, The man of God is come hither.
verse	12	8	8	And the king said unto Hazael, Take a present in thine hand, and go, meet the man of God, and enquire of the LORD by him, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?
verse	12	8	9	So Hazael went to meet him, and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Damascus, forty camels' burden, and came and stood before him, and said, Thy son Benhadad king of Syria hath sent me to thee, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?
verse	12	8	10	And Elisha said unto him, Go, say unto him, Thou mayest certainly recover: howbeit the LORD hath shewed me that he shall surely die.
verse	12	8	11	And he settled his countenance stedfastly, until he was ashamed: and the man of God wept.
verse	12	8	12	And Hazael said, Why weepeth my lord? And he answered, Because I know the evil that thou wilt do unto the children of Israel: their strong holds wilt thou set on fire, and their young men wilt thou slay with the sword, and wilt dash their children, and rip up their women with child.
verse	12	8	13	@@And Hazael said, But what, @9is@7 thy servant a dog, that he should do this great thing? And Elisha answered, The LORD hath shewed me that thou @9shalt be@7 king over Syria.
