verse	12	15	9	@@And he did @9that which was@7 evil in the sight of the LORD, as his fathers had done: he departed not from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.
verse	12	15	10	And Shallum the son of Jabesh conspired against him, and smote him before the people, and slew him, and reigned in his stead.
verse	12	15	11	@@And the rest of the acts of Zachariah, behold, they @9are@7 written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.
verse	12	15	12	@@This @9was@7 the word of the LORD which he spake unto Jehu, saying, Thy sons shall sit on the throne of Israel unto the fourth @9generation.@7 And so it came to pass.
verse	12	15	13	Shallum the son of Jabesh began to reign in the nine and thirtieth year of Uzziah king of Judah; and he reigned a full month in Samaria.
verse	12	15	14	For Menahem the son of Gadi went up from Tirzah, and came to Samaria, and smote Shallum the son of Jabesh in Samaria, and slew him, and reigned in his stead.
verse	12	15	15	@@And the rest of the acts of Shallum, and his conspiracy which he made, behold, they @9are@7 written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.
verse	12	15	16	@@Then Menahem smote Tiphsah, and all that @9were@7 therein, and the coasts thereof from Tirzah: because they opened not @9to him,@7 therefore he smote @9it; and@7 all the women therein that were with child he ripped up.
verse	12	15	17	@@In the nine and thirtieth year of Azariah king of Judah began Menahem the son of Gadi to reign over Israel, @9and reigned@7 ten years in Samaria.
verse	12	15	18	@@And he did @9that which was@7 evil in the sight of the LORD: he departed not all his days from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.
verse	12	15	19	@@@9And@7 Pul the king of Assyria came against the land: and Menahem gave Pul a thousand talents of silver, that his hand might be with him to confirm the kingdom in his hand.
verse	12	15	20	@@And Menahem exacted the money of Israel, @9even@7 of all the mighty men of wealth, of each man fifty shekels of silver, to give to the king of Assyria. So the king of Assyria turned back, and stayed not there in the land.
verse	12	15	21	@@And the rest of the acts of Menahem, and all that he did, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?
verse	12	15	22	And Menahem slept with his fathers; and Pekahiah his son reigned in his stead.
verse	12	15	23	@@In the fiftieth year of Azariah king of Judah Pekahiah the son of Menahem began to reign over Israel in Samaria, @9and reigned@7 two years.
verse	12	15	24	@@And he did @9that which was@7 evil in the sight of the LORD: he departed not from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.
verse	12	15	25	But Pekah the son of Remaliah, a captain of his, conspired against him, and smote him in Samaria, in the palace of the king's house, with Argob and Arieh, and with him fifty men of the Gileadites: and he killed him, and reigned in his room.
verse	12	15	26	@@And the rest of the acts of Pekahiah, and all that he did, behold, they @9are@7 written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.
verse	12	15	27	@@In the two and fiftieth year of Azariah king of Judah Pekah the son of Remaliah began to reign over Israel in Samaria, @9and reigned@7 twenty years.
verse	12	15	28	@@And he did @9that which was@7 evil in the sight of the LORD: he departed not from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.
verse	12	15	29	In the days of Pekah king of Israel came Tiglathpileser king of Assyria, and took Ijon, and Abel-Bethmaachah, and Janoah, and Kedesh, and Hazor, and Gilead, and Galilee, all the land of Naphtali, and carried them captive to Assyria.
verse	12	15	30	And Hoshea the son of Elah made a conspiracy against Pekah the son of Remaliah, and smote him, and slew him, and reigned in his stead, in the twentieth year of Jotham the son of Uzziah.
verse	12	15	31	@@And the rest of the acts of Pekah, and all that he did, behold, they @9are@7 written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.
verse	12	15	32	In the second year of Pekah the son of Remaliah king of Israel began Jotham the son of Uzziah king of Judah to reign.
verse	12	15	33	@@Five and twenty years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. And his mother's name @9was@7 Jerusha, the daughter of Zadok.
verse	12	15	34	@@And he did @9that which was@7 right in the sight of the LORD: he did according to all that his father Uzziah had done.
verse	12	15	35	Howbeit the high places were not removed: the people sacrificed and burned incense still in the high places. He built the higher gate of the house of the LORD.
verse	12	15	36	@@Now the rest of the acts of Jotham, and all that he did, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?
verse	12	15	37	In those days the LORD began to send against Judah Rezin the king of Syria, and Pekah the son of Remaliah.
verse	12	15	38	And Jotham slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David his father: and Ahaz his son reigned in his stead.
verse	12	16	1	In the seventeenth year of Pekah the son of Remaliah Ahaz the son of Jotham king of Judah began to reign.
verse	12	16	2	@@Twenty years old @9was@7 Ahaz when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem, and did not @9that which was@7 right in the sight of the LORD his God, like David his father.
verse	12	16	3	But he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, yea, and made his son to pass through the fire, according to the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel.
verse	12	16	4	And he sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places, and on the hills, and under every green tree.
verse	12	16	5	@@Then Rezin king of Syria and Pekah son of Remaliah king of Israel came up to Jerusalem to war: and they besieged Ahaz, but could not overcome @9him. @7
verse	12	16	6	At that time Rezin king of Syria recovered Elath to Syria, and drave the Jews from Elath: and the Syrians came to Elath, and dwelt there unto this day.
verse	12	16	7	@@So Ahaz sent messengers to Tiglathpileser king of Assyria, saying, I @9am@7 thy servant and thy son: come up, and save me out of the hand of the king of Syria, and out of the hand of the king of Israel, which rise up against me.
verse	12	16	8	@@And Ahaz took the silver and gold that was found in the house of the LORD, and in the treasures of the king's house, and sent @9it for@7 a present to the king of Assyria.
verse	12	16	9	@@And the king of Assyria hearkened unto him: for the king of Assyria went up against Damascus, and took it, and carried @9the people of@7 it captive to Kir, and slew Rezin.
verse	12	16	10	@@And king Ahaz went to Damascus to meet Tiglathpileser king of Assyria, and saw an altar that @9was@7 at Damascus: and king Ahaz sent to Urijah the priest the fashion of the altar, and the pattern of it, according to all the workmanship thereof.
verse	12	16	11	@@And Urijah the priest built an altar according to all that king Ahaz had sent from Damascus: so Urijah the priest made @9it@7 against king Ahaz came from Damascus.
verse	12	16	12	And when the king was come from Damascus, the king saw the altar: and the king approached to the altar, and offered thereon.
verse	12	16	13	And he burnt his burnt offering and his meat offering, and poured his drink offering, and sprinkled the blood of his peace offerings, upon the altar.
verse	12	16	14	@@And he brought also the brasen altar, which @9was@7 before the LORD, from the forefront of the house, from between the altar and the house of the LORD, and put it on the north side of the altar.
verse	12	16	15	@@And king Ahaz commanded Urijah the priest, saying, Upon the great altar burn the morning burnt offering, and the evening meat offering, and the king's burnt sacrifice, and his meat offering, with the burnt offering of all the people of the land, and their meat offering, and their drink offerings; and sprinkle upon it all the blood of the burnt offering, and all the blood of the sacrifice: and the brasen altar shall be for me to enquire @9by. @7
verse	12	16	16	Thus did Urijah the priest, according to all that king Ahaz commanded.
verse	12	16	17	@@And king Ahaz cut off the borders of the bases, and removed the laver from off them; and took down the sea from off the brasen oxen that @9were@7 under it, and put it upon a pavement of stones.
verse	12	16	18	And the covert for the sabbath that they had built in the house, and the king's entry without, turned he from the house of the LORD for the king of Assyria.
verse	12	16	19	@@Now the rest of the acts of Ahaz which he did, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?
verse	12	16	20	And Ahaz slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David: and Hezekiah his son reigned in his stead.
verse	12	17	1	In the twelfth year of Ahaz king of Judah began Hoshea the son of Elah to reign in Samaria over Israel nine years.
verse	12	17	2	@@And he did @9that which was@7 evil in the sight of the LORD, but not as the kings of Israel that were before him.
verse	12	17	3	Against him came up Shalmaneser king of Assyria; and Hoshea became his servant, and gave him presents.
verse	12	17	4	@@And the king of Assyria found conspiracy in Hoshea: for he had sent messengers to So king of Egypt, and brought no present to the king of Assyria, as @9he had done@7 year by year: therefore the king of Assyria shut him up, and bound him in prison.
verse	12	17	5	Then the king of Assyria came up throughout all the land, and went up to Samaria, and besieged it three years.
verse	12	17	6	@@In the ninth year of Hoshea the king of Assyria took Samaria, and carried Israel away into Assyria, and placed them in Halah and in Habor @9by@7 the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes.
verse	12	17	7	@@For @9so@7 it was, that the children of Israel had sinned against the LORD their God, which had brought them up out of the land of Egypt, from under the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt, and had feared other gods,
verse	12	17	8	And walked in the statutes of the heathen, whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel, and of the kings of Israel, which they had made.
verse	12	17	9	@@And the children of Israel did secretly @9those@7 things that @9were@7 not right against the LORD their God, and they built them high places in all their cities, from the tower of the watchmen to the fenced city.
verse	12	17	10	And they set them up images and groves in every high hill, and under every green tree:
verse	12	17	11	@@And there they burnt incense in all the high places, as @9did@7 the heathen whom the LORD carried away before them; and wrought wicked things to provoke the LORD to anger:
verse	12	17	12	For they served idols, whereof the LORD had said unto them, Ye shall not do this thing.
verse	12	17	13	@@Yet the LORD testified against Israel, and against Judah, by all the prophets, @9and by@7 all the seers, saying, Turn ye from your evil ways, and keep my commandments @9and@7 my statutes, according to all the law which I commanded your fathers, and which I sent to you by my servants the prophets.
verse	12	17	14	Notwithstanding they would not hear, but hardened their necks, like to the neck of their fathers, that did not believe in the LORD their God.
verse	12	17	15	@@And they rejected his statutes, and his covenant that he made with their fathers, and his testimonies which he testified against them; and they followed vanity, and became vain, and went after the heathen that @9were@7 round about them, @9concerning@7 whom the LORD had charged them, that they should not do like them.
verse	12	17	16	@@And they left all the commandments of the LORD their God, and made them molten images, @9even@7 two calves, and made a grove, and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served Baal.
verse	12	17	17	And they caused their sons and their daughters to pass through the fire, and used divination and enchantments, and sold themselves to do evil in the sight of the LORD, to provoke him to anger.
verse	12	17	18	Therefore the LORD was very angry with Israel, and removed them out of his sight: there was none left but the tribe of Judah only.
verse	12	17	19	Also Judah kept not the commandments of the LORD their God, but walked in the statutes of Israel which they made.
verse	12	17	20	And the LORD rejected all the seed of Israel, and afflicted them, and delivered them into the hand of spoilers, until he had cast them out of his sight.
verse	12	17	21	For he rent Israel from the house of David; and they made Jeroboam the son of Nebat king: and Jeroboam drave Israel from following the LORD, and made them sin a great sin.
verse	12	17	22	For the children of Israel walked in all the sins of Jeroboam which he did; they departed not from them;
verse	12	17	23	Until the LORD removed Israel out of his sight, as he had said by all his servants the prophets. So was Israel carried away out of their own land to Assyria unto this day.
verse	12	17	24	@@And the king of Assyria brought @9men@7 from Babylon, and from Cuthah, and from Ava, and from Hamath, and from Sepharvaim, and placed @9them@7 in the cities of Samaria instead of the children of Israel: and they possessed Samaria, and dwelt in the cities thereof.
verse	12	17	25	@@And @9so@7 it was at the beginning of their dwelling there, @9that@7 they feared not the LORD: therefore the LORD sent lions among them, which slew @9some@7 of them.
verse	12	17	26	Wherefore they spake to the king of Assyria, saying, The nations which thou hast removed, and placed in the cities of Samaria, know not the manner of the God of the land: therefore he hath sent lions among them, and, behold, they slay them, because they know not the manner of the God of the land.
verse	12	17	27	Then the king of Assyria commanded, saying, Carry thither one of the priests whom ye brought from thence; and let them go and dwell there, and let him teach them the manner of the God of the land.
verse	12	17	28	Then one of the priests whom they had carried away from Samaria came and dwelt in Bethel, and taught them how they should fear the LORD.
verse	12	17	29	@@Howbeit every nation made gods of their own, and put @9them@7 in the houses of the high places which the Samaritans had made, every nation in their cities wherein they dwelt.
verse	12	17	30	And the men of Babylon made Succothbenoth, and the men of Cuth made Nergal, and the men of Hamath made Ashima,
verse	12	17	31	And the Avites made Nibhaz and Tartak, and the Sepharvites burnt their children in fire to Adrammelech and Anammelech, the gods of Sepharvaim.
verse	12	17	32	So they feared the LORD, and made unto themselves of the lowest of them priests of the high places, which sacrificed for them in the houses of the high places.
verse	12	17	33	They feared the LORD, and served their own gods, after the manner of the nations whom they carried away from thence.
verse	12	17	34	Unto this day they do after the former manners: they fear not the LORD, neither do they after their statutes, or after their ordinances, or after the law and commandment which the LORD commanded the children of Jacob, whom he named Israel;
verse	12	17	35	With whom the LORD had made a covenant, and charged them, saying, Ye shall not fear other gods, nor bow yourselves to them, nor serve them, nor sacrifice to them:
verse	12	17	36	But the LORD, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt with great power and a stretched out arm, him shall ye fear, and him shall ye worship, and to him shall ye do sacrifice.
verse	12	17	37	And the statutes, and the ordinances, and the law, and the commandment, which he wrote for you, ye shall observe to do for evermore; and ye shall not fear other gods.
verse	12	17	38	And the covenant that I have made with you ye shall not forget; neither shall ye fear other gods.
verse	12	17	39	But the LORD your God ye shall fear; and he shall deliver you out of the hand of all your enemies.
verse	12	17	40	Howbeit they did not hearken, but they did after their former manner.
verse	12	17	41	So these nations feared the LORD, and served their graven images, both their children, and their children's children: as did their fathers, so do they unto this day.
verse	12	18	1	@@Now it came to pass in the third year of Hoshea son of Elah king of Israel, @9that@7 Hezekiah the son of Ahaz king of Judah began to reign.
verse	12	18	2	@@Twenty and five years old was he when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty and nine years in Jerusalem. His mother's name also @9was@7 Abi, the daughter of Zachariah.
verse	12	18	3	@@And he did @9that which was@7 right in the sight of the LORD, according to all that David his father did.
verse	12	18	4	He removed the high places, and brake the images, and cut down the groves, and brake in pieces the brasen serpent that Moses had made: for unto those days the children of Israel did burn incense to it: and he called it Nehushtan.
verse	12	18	5	@@He trusted in the LORD God of Israel; so that after him was none like him among all the kings of Judah, nor @9any@7 that were before him.
verse	12	18	6	@@For he clave to the LORD, @9and@7 departed not from following him, but kept his commandments, which the LORD commanded Moses.
verse	12	18	7	@@And the LORD was with him; @9and@7 he prospered whithersoever he went forth: and he rebelled against the king of Assyria, and served him not.
verse	12	18	8	@@He smote the Philistines, @9even@7 unto Gaza, and the borders thereof, from the tower of the watchmen to the fenced city.
verse	12	18	9	@@And it came to pass in the fourth year of king Hezekiah, which @9was@7 the seventh year of Hoshea son of Elah king of Israel, @9that@7 Shalmaneser king of Assyria came up against Samaria, and besieged it.
verse	12	18	10	@@And at the end of three years they took it: @9even@7 in the sixth year of Hezekiah, that @9is@7 the ninth year of Hoshea king of Israel, Samaria was taken.
verse	12	18	11	@@And the king of Assyria did carry away Israel unto Assyria, and put them in Halah and in Habor @9by@7 the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes:
verse	12	18	12	@@Because they obeyed not the voice of the LORD their God, but transgressed his covenant, @9and@7 all that Moses the servant of the LORD commanded, and would not hear @9them,@7 nor do @9them. @7
verse	12	18	13	Now in the fourteenth year of king Hezekiah did Sennacherib king of Assyria come up against all the fenced cities of Judah, and took them.
verse	12	18	14	And Hezekiah king of Judah sent to the king of Assyria to Lachish, saying, I have offended; return from me: that which thou puttest on me will I bear. And the king of Assyria appointed unto Hezekiah king of Judah three hundred talents of silver and thirty talents of gold.
verse	12	18	15	@@And Hezekiah gave @9him@7 all the silver that was found in the house of the LORD, and in the treasures of the king's house.
verse	12	18	16	@@At that time did Hezekiah cut off @9the gold from@7 the doors of the temple of the LORD, and @9from@7 the pillars which Hezekiah king of Judah had overlaid, and gave it to the king of Assyria.
verse	12	18	17	And the king of Assyria sent Tartan and Rabsaris and Rabshakeh from Lachish to king Hezekiah with a great host against Jerusalem. And they went up and came to Jerusalem. And when they were come up, they came and stood by the conduit of the upper pool, which is in the highway of the fuller's field.
verse	12	18	18	@@And when they had called to the king, there came out to them Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, which @9was@7 over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder.
verse	12	18	19	And Rab-shakeh said unto them, Speak ye now to Hezekiah, Thus saith the great king, the king of Assyria, What confidence is this wherein thou trustest?
verse	12	18	20	@@Thou sayest, (but @9they are but@7 vain words,) @9I have@7 counsel and strength for the war. Now on whom dost thou trust, that thou rebellest against me?
verse	12	18	21	@@Now, behold, thou trustest upon the staff of this bruised reed, @9even@7 upon Egypt, on which if a man lean, it will go into his hand, and pierce it: so is Pharaoh king of Egypt unto all that trust on him.
verse	12	18	22	@@But if ye say unto me, We trust in the LORD our God: @9is@7 not that he, whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah hath taken away, and hath said to Judah and Jerusalem, Ye shall worship before this altar in Jerusalem?
verse	12	18	23	Now therefore, I pray thee, give pledges to my lord the king of Assyria, and I will deliver thee two thousand horses, if thou be able on thy part to set riders upon them.
verse	12	18	24	How then wilt thou turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master's servants, and put thy trust on Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?
verse	12	18	25	Am I now come up without the LORD against this place to destroy it? The LORD said to me, Go up against this land, and destroy it.
verse	12	18	26	@@Then said Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, and Shebna, and Joah, unto Rabshakeh, Speak, I pray thee, to thy servants in the Syrian language; for we understand @9it:@7 and talk not with us in the Jews' language in the ears of the people that @9are@7 on the wall.
verse	12	18	27	@@But Rabshakeh said unto them, Hath my master sent me to thy master, and to thee, to speak these words? @9hath he@7 not @9sent me@7 to the men which sit on the wall, that they may eat their own dung, and drink their own piss with you?
verse	12	18	28	Then Rabshakeh stood and cried with a loud voice in the Jews' language, and spake, saying, Hear the word of the great king, the king of Assyria:
verse	12	18	29	Thus saith the king, Let not Hezekiah deceive you: for he shall not be able to deliver you out of his hand:
verse	12	18	30	Neither let Hezekiah make you trust in the LORD, saying, The LORD will surely deliver us, and this city shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.
verse	12	18	31	@@Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus saith the king of Assyria, Make @9an agreement@7 with me by a present, and come out to me, and @9then@7 eat ye every man of his own vine, and every one of his fig tree, and drink ye every one the waters of his cistern:
verse	12	18	32	Until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of corn and wine, a land of bread and vineyards, a land of oil olive and of honey, that ye may live, and not die: and hearken not unto Hezekiah, when he persuadeth you, saying, The LORD will deliver us.
verse	12	18	33	Hath any of the gods of the nations delivered at all his land out of the hand of the king of Assyria?
verse	12	18	34	@@Where @9are@7 the gods of Hamath, and of Arpad? where @9are@7 the gods of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivah? have they delivered Samaria out of mine hand?
verse	12	18	35	@@Who @9are@7 they among all the gods of the countries, that have delivered their country out of mine hand, that the LORD should deliver Jerusalem out of mine hand?
verse	12	18	36	But the people held their peace, and answered him not a word: for the king's commandment was, saying, Answer him not.
verse	12	18	37	@@Then came Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, which @9was@7 over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder, to Hezekiah with @9their@7 clothes rent, and told him the words of Rabshakeh.
verse	12	19	1	@@And it came to pass, when king Hezekiah heard @9it,@7 that he rent his clothes, and covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the house of the LORD.
verse	12	19	2	@@And he sent Eliakim, which @9was@7 over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.
verse	12	19	3	@@And they said unto him, Thus saith Hezekiah, This day @9is@7 a day of trouble, and of rebuke, and blasphemy: for the children are come to the birth, and @9there is@7 not strength to bring forth.
verse	12	19	4	@@It may be the LORD thy God will hear all the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master hath sent to reproach the living God; and will reprove the words which the LORD thy God hath heard: wherefore lift up @9thy@7 prayer for the remnant that are left.
verse	12	19	5	So the servants of king Hezekiah came to Isaiah.
verse	12	19	6	And Isaiah said unto them, Thus shall ye say to your master, Thus saith the LORD, Be not afraid of the words which thou hast heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me.
verse	12	19	7	Behold, I will send a blast upon him, and he shall hear a rumour, and shall return to his own land; and I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.
verse	12	19	8	So Rabshakeh returned, and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah: for he had heard that he was departed from Lachish.
verse	12	19	9	And when he heard say of Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, Behold, he is come out to fight against thee: he sent messengers again unto Hezekiah, saying,
verse	12	19	10	Thus shall ye speak to Hezekiah king of Judah, saying, Let not thy God in whom thou trustest deceive thee, saying, Jerusalem shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.
verse	12	19	11	Behold, thou hast heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands, by destroying them utterly: and shalt thou be delivered?
verse	12	19	12	@@Have the gods of the nations delivered them which my fathers have destroyed; @9as@7 Gozan, and Haran, and Rezeph, and the children of Eden which @9were@7 in Thelasar?
verse	12	19	13	@@Where @9is@7 the king of Hamath, and the king of Arpad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and Ivah?
verse	12	19	14	And Hezekiah received the letter of the hand of the messengers, and read it: and Hezekiah went up into the house of the LORD, and spread it before the LORD.
verse	12	19	15	@@And Hezekiah prayed before the LORD, and said, O LORD God of Israel, which dwellest @9between@7 the cherubims, thou art the God, @9even@7 thou alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth; thou hast made heaven and earth.
verse	12	19	16	LORD, bow down thine ear, and hear: open, LORD, thine eyes, and see: and hear the words of Sennacherib, which hath sent him to reproach the living God.
verse	12	19	17	Of a truth, LORD, the kings of Assyria have destroyed the nations and their lands,
verse	12	19	18	@@And have cast their gods into the fire: for they @9were@7 no gods, but the work of men's hands, wood and stone: therefore they have destroyed them.
verse	12	19	19	@@Now therefore, O LORD our God, I beseech thee, save thou us out of his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that thou @9art@7 the LORD God, @9even@7 thou only.
verse	12	19	20	@@Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent to Hezekiah, saying, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, @9That@7 which thou hast prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria I have heard.
verse	12	19	21	@@This @9is@7 the word that the LORD hath spoken concerning him; The virgin the daughter of Zion hath despised thee, @9and@7 laughed thee to scorn; the daughter of Jerusalem hath shaken her head at thee.
verse	12	19	22	@@Whom hast thou reproached and blasphemed? and against whom hast thou exalted @9thy@7 voice, and lifted up thine eyes on high? @9even@7 against the Holy @9One@7 of Israel.
verse	12	19	23	@@By thy messengers thou hast reproached the Lord, and hast said, With the multitude of my chariots I am come up to the height of the mountains, to the sides of Lebanon, and will cut down the tall cedar trees thereof, @9and@7 the choice fir trees thereof: and I will enter into the lodgings of his borders, @9and into@7 the forest of his Carmel.
verse	12	19	24	I have digged and drunk strange waters, and with the sole of my feet have I dried up all the rivers of besieged places.
verse	12	19	25	@@Hast thou not heard long ago @9how@7 I have done it, @9and@7 of ancient times that I have formed it? now have I brought it to pass, that thou shouldest be to lay waste fenced cities @9into@7 ruinous heaps.
verse	12	19	26	@@Therefore their inhabitants were of small power, they were dismayed and confounded; they were @9as@7 the grass of the field, and @9as@7 the green herb, @9as@7 the grass on the housetops, and @9as corn@7 blasted before it be grown up.
verse	12	19	27	But I know thy abode, and thy going out, and thy coming in, and thy rage against me.
verse	12	19	28	Because thy rage against me and thy tumult is come up into mine ears, therefore I will put my hook in thy nose, and my bridle in thy lips, and I will turn thee back by the way by which thou camest.
verse	12	19	29	@@And this @9shall be@7 a sign unto thee, Ye shall eat this year such things as grow of themselves, and in the second year that which springeth of the same; and in the third year sow ye, and reap, and plant vineyards, and eat the fruits thereof.
verse	12	19	30	And the remnant that is escaped of the house of Judah shall yet again take root downward, and bear fruit upward.
verse	12	19	31	@@For out of Jerusalem shall go forth a remnant, and they that escape out of mount Zion: the zeal of the LORD @9of hosts@7 shall do this.
verse	12	19	32	Therefore thus saith the LORD concerning the king of Assyria, He shall not come into this city, nor shoot an arrow there, nor come before it with shield, nor cast a bank against it.
verse	12	19	33	By the way that he came, by the same shall he return, and shall not come into this city, saith the LORD.
verse	12	19	34	For I will defend this city, to save it, for mine own sake, and for my servant David's sake.
verse	12	19	35	@@And it came to pass that night, that the angel of the LORD went out, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians an hundred fourscore and five thousand: and when they arose early in the morning, behold, they @9were@7 all dead corpses.
verse	12	19	36	So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, and went and returned, and dwelt at Nineveh.
verse	12	19	37	And it came to pass, as he was worshipping in the house of Nisroch his god, that Adrammelech and Sharezer his sons smote him with the sword: and they escaped into the land of Armenia. And Esar-haddon his son reigned in his stead.
verse	12	20	1	In those days was Hezekiah sick unto death. And the prophet Isaiah the son of Amoz came to him, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Set thine house in order; for thou shalt die, and not live.
verse	12	20	2	Then he turned his face to the wall, and prayed unto the LORD, saying,
verse	12	20	3	@@I beseech thee, O LORD, remember now how I have walked before thee in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done @9that which is@7 good in thy sight. And Hezekiah wept sore.
verse	12	20	4	And it came to pass, afore Isaiah was gone out into the middle court, that the word of the LORD came to him, saying,
verse	12	20	5	Turn again, and tell Hezekiah the captain of my people, Thus saith the LORD, the God of David thy father, I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears: behold, I will heal thee: on the third day thou shalt go up unto the house of the LORD.
verse	12	20	6	And I will add unto thy days fifteen years; and I will deliver thee and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria; and I will defend this city for mine own sake, and for my servant David's sake.
verse	12	20	7	@@And Isaiah said, Take a lump of figs. And they took and laid @9it@7 on the boil, and he recovered.
verse	12	20	8	@@And Hezekiah said unto Isaiah, What @9shall be@7 the sign that the LORD will heal me, and that I shall go up into the house of the LORD the third day?
verse	12	20	9	And Isaiah said, This sign shalt thou have of the LORD, that the LORD will do the thing that he hath spoken: shall the shadow go forward ten degrees, or go back ten degrees?
verse	12	20	10	And Hezekiah answered, It is a light thing for the shadow to go down ten degrees: nay, but let the shadow return backward ten degrees.
verse	12	20	11	And Isaiah the prophet cried unto the LORD: and he brought the shadow ten degrees backward, by which it had gone down in the dial of Ahaz.
verse	12	20	12	At that time Berodachbaladan, the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present unto Hezekiah: for he had heard that Hezekiah had been sick.
verse	12	20	13	@@And Hezekiah hearkened unto them, and shewed them all the house of his precious things, the silver, and the gold, and the spices, and the precious ointment, and @9all@7 the house of his armour, and all that was found in his treasures: there was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them not.
verse	12	20	14	@@Then came Isaiah the prophet unto king Hezekiah, and said unto him, What said these men? and from whence came they unto thee? And Hezekiah said, They are come from a far country, @9even@7 from Babylon.
verse	12	20	15	@@And he said, What have they seen in thine house? And Hezekiah answered, All @9the things@7 that @9are@7 in mine house have they seen: there is nothing among my treasures that I have not shewed them.
verse	12	20	16	And Isaiah said unto Hezekiah, Hear the word of the LORD.
verse	12	20	17	@@Behold, the days come, that all that @9is@7 in thine house,and that which thy fathers have laid up in store unto this day, shall be carried into Babylon: nothing shall be left, saith the LORD.
verse	12	20	18	And of thy sons that shall issue from thee, which thou shalt beget, shall they take away; and they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.
verse	12	20	19	@@Then said Hezekiah unto Isaiah, Good is the word of the LORD which thou hast spoken. And he said, @9Is it@7 not @9good,@7 if peace and truth be in my days?
verse	12	20	20	@@And the rest of the acts of Hezekiah, and all his might, and how he made a pool, and a conduit, and brought water into the city, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?
verse	12	20	21	And Hezekiah slept with his fathers: and Manasseh his son reigned in his stead.
verse	12	21	1	@@Manasseh @9was@7 twelve years old when he began to reign, and reigned fifty and five years in Jerusalem. And his mother's name @9was@7 Hephzibah.
verse	12	21	2	@@And he did @9that which was@7 evil in the sight of the LORD, after the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.
verse	12	21	3	For he built up again the high places which Hezekiah his father had destroyed; and he reared up altars for Baal, and made a grove, as did Ahab king of Israel; and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served them.
verse	12	21	4	And he built altars in the house of the LORD, of which the LORD said, In Jerusalem will I put my name.
verse	12	21	5	And he built altars for all the host of heaven in the two courts of the house of the LORD.
verse	12	21	6	@@And he made his son pass through the fire, and observed times, and used enchantments, and dealt with familiar spirits and wizards: he wrought much wickedness in the sight of the LORD, to provoke @9him@7 to anger.
verse	12	21	7	And he set a graven image of the grove that he had made in the house, of which the LORD said to David, and to Solomon his son, In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all tribes of Israel, will I put my name for ever:
verse	12	21	8	Neither will I make the feet of Israel move any more out of the land which I gave their fathers; only if they will observe to do according to all that I have commanded them, and according to all the law that my servant Moses commanded them.
verse	12	21	9	But they hearkened not: and Manasseh seduced them to do more evil than did the nations whom the LORD destroyed before the children of Israel.
verse	12	21	10	And the LORD spake by his servants the prophets, saying,
verse	12	21	11	@@Because Manasseh king of Judah hath done these abominations, @9and@7 hath done wickedly above all that the Amorites did, which @9were@7 before him, and hath made Judah also to sin with his idols:
verse	12	21	12	@@Therefore thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Behold, I @9am@7 bringing @9such@7 evil upon Jerusalem and Judah, that whosoever heareth of it, both his ears shall tingle.
verse	12	21	13	@@And I will stretch over Jerusalem the line of Samaria, and the plummet of the house of Ahab: and I will wipe Jerusalem as @9a man@7 wipeth a dish, wiping @9it,@7 and turning @9it@7 upside down.
verse	12	21	14	And I will forsake the remnant of mine inheritance, and deliver them into the hand of their enemies; and they shall become a prey and a spoil to all their enemies;
verse	12	21	15	@@Because they have done @9that which was@7 evil in my sight,and have provoked me to anger, since the day their fathers came forth out of Egypt, even unto this day.
verse	12	21	16	@@Moreover Manasseh shed innocent blood very much, till he had filled Jerusalem from one end to another; beside his sin wherewith he made Judah to sin, in doing @9that which was@7 evil in the sight of the LORD.
verse	12	21	17	@@Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and all that he did, and his sin that he sinned, @9are@7 they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?
verse	12	21	18	And Manasseh slept with his fathers, and was buried in the garden of his own house, in the garden of Uzza: and Amon his son reigned in his stead.
verse	12	21	19	@@Amon @9was@7 twenty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned two years in Jerusalem. And his mother's name @9was@7 Meshullemeth, the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah.
verse	12	21	20	@@And he did @9that which was@7 evil in the sight of the LORD, as his father Manasseh did.
