verse	12	25	4	@@And the city was broken up, and all the men of war @9fled@7 by night by the way of the gate between two walls, which @9is@7 by the king's garden: (now the Chaldees @9were@7 against the city round about:) and @9the king@7 went the way toward the plain.
verse	12	25	5	And the army of the Chaldees pursued after the king, and overtook him in the plains of Jericho: and all his army were scattered from him.
verse	12	25	6	So they took the king, and brought him up to the king of Babylon to Riblah; and they gave judgment upon him.
verse	12	25	7	And they slew the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes, and put out the eyes of Zedekiah, and bound him with fetters of brass, and carried him to Babylon.
verse	12	25	8	@@And in the fifth month, on the seventh @9day@7 of the month, which @9is@7 the nineteenth year of king Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, came Nebuzaradan, captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon, unto Jerusalem:
verse	12	25	9	@@And he burnt the house of the LORD, and the king's house, and all the houses of Jerusalem, and every great @9man's@7 house burnt he with fire.
verse	12	25	10	@@And all the army of the Chaldees, that @9were with@7 the captain of the guard, brake down the walls of Jerusalem round about.
verse	12	25	11	@@Now the rest of the people @9that were@7 left in the city, and the fugitives that fell away to the king of Babylon, with the remnant of the multitude, did Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carry away.
verse	12	25	12	@@But the captain of the guard left of the poor of the land @9to be@7 vinedressers and husbandmen.
verse	12	25	13	@@And the pillars of brass that @9were@7 in the house of the LORD, and the bases, and the brasen sea that @9was@7 in the house of the LORD, did the Chaldees break in pieces, and carried the brass of them to Babylon.
verse	12	25	14	And the pots, and the shovels, and the snuffers, and the spoons, and all the vessels of brass wherewith they ministered, took they away.
verse	12	25	15	@@And the firepans, and the bowls, @9and@7 such things as @9were@7 of gold, @9in@7 gold, and of silver, @9in@7 silver, the captain of the guard took away.
verse	12	25	16	The two pillars, one sea, and the bases which Solomon had made for the house of the LORD; the brass of all these vessels was without weight.
verse	12	25	17	@@The height of the one pillar @9was@7 eighteen cubits, and the chapiter upon it @9was@7 brass: and the height of the chapiter three cubits; and the wreathen work, and pomegranates upon the chapiter round about, all of brass: and like unto these had the second pillar with wreathen work.
verse	12	25	18	And the captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, and Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the door:
verse	12	25	19	@@And out of the city he took an officer that was set over the men of war, and five men of them that were in the king's presence, which were found in the city, and the principal scribe of the host, which mustered the people of the land, and threescore men of the people of the land @9that were@7 found in the city:
verse	12	25	20	And Nebuzaradan captain of the guard took these, and brought them to the king of Babylon to Riblah:
verse	12	25	21	And the king of Babylon smote them, and slew them at Riblah in the land of Hamath. So Judah was carried away out of their land.
verse	12	25	22	@@And @9as for@7 the people that remained in the land of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had left, even over them he made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, ruler.
verse	12	25	23	And when all the captains of the armies, they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah governor, there came to Gedaliah to Mizpah, even Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and Johanan the son of Careah, and Seraiah the son of Tanhumeth the Netophathite, and Jaazaniah the son of a Maachathite, they and their men.
verse	12	25	24	And Gedaliah sware to them, and to their men, and said unto them, Fear not to be the servants of the Chaldees: dwell in the land, and serve the king of Babylon; and it shall be well with you.
verse	12	25	25	But it came to pass in the seventh month, that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, the son of Elishama, of the seed royal, came, and ten men with him, and smote Gedaliah, that he died, and the Jews and the Chaldees that were with him at Mizpah.
verse	12	25	26	And all the people, both small and great, and the captains of the armies, arose, and came to Egypt: for they were afraid of the Chaldees.
verse	12	25	27	@@And it came to pass in the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, on the seven and twentieth @9day@7 of the month, @9that@7 Evilmerodach king of Babylon in the year that he began to reign did lift up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah out of prison;
verse	12	25	28	@@And he spake kindly to him, and set his throne above the throne of the kings that @9were@7 with him in Babylon;
verse	12	25	29	And changed his prison garments: and he did eat bread continually before him all the days of his life.
verse	12	25	30	@@And his allowance @9was@7 a continual allowance given him of the king, a daily rate for every day, all the days of his life.
verse	13	1	1	Adam, Sheth, Enosh,
verse	13	1	2	Kenan, Mahalaleel, Jered,
verse	13	1	3	Henoch, Methuselah, Lamech,
verse	13	1	4	Noah, Shem, Ham, and Japheth.
verse	13	1	5	The sons of Japheth; Gomer, and Magog, and Madai, and Javan, and Tubal, and Meshech, and Tiras.
verse	13	1	6	And the sons of Gomer; Ashchenaz, and Riphath, and Togarmah.
verse	13	1	7	And the sons of Javan; Elishah, and Tarshish, Kittim, and Dodanim.
verse	13	1	8	The sons of Ham; Cush, and Mizraim, Put, and Canaan.
verse	13	1	9	And the sons of Cush; Seba, and Havilah, and Sabta, and Raamah, and Sabtecha. And the sons of Raamah; Sheba, and Dedan.
verse	13	1	10	And Cush begat Nimrod: he began to be mighty upon the earth.
verse	13	1	11	And Mizraim begat Ludim, and Anamim, and Lehabim, and Napthtuhim,
verse	13	1	12	And Pathrusim, and Casluhim, (of whom came the Philistines,) and Caphthorim.
verse	13	1	13	And Canaan begat Zidon his firstborn, and Heth,
verse	13	1	14	The Jebusite also, and the Amorite, and the Girgashite,
verse	13	1	15	And the Hivite, and the Arkite, and the Sinite,
verse	13	1	16	And the Arvadite, and the Zemarite, and the Hamathite.
verse	13	1	17	The sons of Shem; Elam, and Asshur, and Arphaxad, and Lud, and Aram, and Uz, and Hul, and Gether, and Meshech.
verse	13	1	18	And Arphaxad begat Shelah, and Shelah begat Eber.
verse	13	1	19	@@And unto Eber were born two sons: the name of the one @9was@7 Peleg; because in his days the earth was divided: and his brother's name @9was@7 Joktan.
verse	13	1	20	And Joktan begat Almodad, and Sheleph, and Hazarmaveth, and Jerah,
verse	13	1	21	Hadoram also, and Uzal, and Diklah,
verse	13	1	22	And Ebal, and Abimael, and Sheba,
verse	13	1	23	@@And Ophir, and Havilah, and Jobab. All these @9were@7 the sons of Joktan.
verse	13	1	24	Shem, Arphaxad, Shelah,
verse	13	1	25	Eber, Peleg, Reu,
verse	13	1	26	Serug, Nahor, Terah,
verse	13	1	27	@@Abram; the same @9is@7 Abraham.
verse	13	1	28	The sons of Abraham; Isaac, and Ishmael.
verse	13	1	29	@@These @9are@7 their generations: The firstborn of Ishmael, Nebaioth; then Kedar, and Adbeel, and Mibsam,
verse	13	1	30	Mishma and Dumah, Massa, Hadad, and Tema,
verse	13	1	31	Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah. These are the sons of Ishmael.
verse	13	1	32	Now the sons of Keturah, Abraham's concubine: she bare Zimran, and Jokshan, and Medan, and Midian, and Ishbak, and Shuah. And the sons of Jokshan; Sheba, and Dedan.
verse	13	1	33	@@And the sons of Midian; Ephah, and Epher, and Henoch, and Abida, and Eldaah. All these @9are@7 the sons of Keturah.
verse	13	1	34	And Abraham begat Isaac. The sons of Isaac; Esau and Israel.
verse	13	1	35	The sons of Esau; Eliphaz, Reuel, and Jeush, and Jaalam, and Korah.
verse	13	1	36	The sons of Eliphaz; Teman, and Omar, Zephi, and Gatam, Kenaz, and Timna, and Amalek.
verse	13	1	37	The sons of Reuel; Nahath, Zerah, Shammah, and Mizzah.
verse	13	1	38	And the sons of Seir; Lotan, and Shobal, and Zibeon, and Anah, and Dishon, and Ezar, and Dishan.
verse	13	1	39	@@And the sons of Lotan; Hori, and Homam: and Timna @9was@7 Lotan's sister.
verse	13	1	40	The sons of Shobal; Alian, and Manahath, and Ebal, Shephi, and Onam. And the sons of Zibeon; Aiah, and Anah.
verse	13	1	41	The sons of Anah; Dishon. And the sons of Dishon; Amram, and Eshban, and Ithran, and Cheran.
verse	13	1	42	@@The sons of Ezer; Bilhan, and Zavan, @9and@7 Jakan. The sons of Dishan; Uz, and Aran.
verse	13	1	43	@@Now these @9are@7 the kings that reigned in the land of Edom before @9any@7 king reigned over the children of Israel; Bela the son of Beor: and the name of his city @9was@7 Dinhabah.
verse	13	1	44	And when Bela was dead, Jobab the son of Zerah of Bozrah reigned in his stead.
verse	13	1	45	And when Jobab was dead, Husham of the land of the Temanites reigned in his stead.
verse	13	1	46	@@And when Husham was dead, Hadad the son of Bedad, which smote Midian in the field of Moab, reigned in his stead: and the name of his city @9was@7 Avith.
verse	13	1	47	And when Hadad was dead, Samlah of Masrekah reigned in his stead.
verse	13	1	48	And when Samlah was dead, Shaul of Rehoboth by the river reigned in his stead.
verse	13	1	49	And when Shaul was dead, Baalhanan the son of Achbor reigned in his stead.
verse	13	1	50	@@And when Baalhanan was dead, Hadad reigned in his stead: and the name of his city @9was@7 Pai; and his wife's name @9was@7 Mehetabel, the daughter of Matred, the daughter of Mezahab.
verse	13	1	51	Hadad died also. And the dukes of Edom were; duke Timnah, duke Aliah, duke Jetheth,
verse	13	1	52	Duke Aholibamah, duke Elah, duke Pinon,
verse	13	1	53	Duke Kenaz, duke Teman, duke Mibzar,
verse	13	1	54	@@Duke Magdiel, duke Iram. These @9are@7 the dukes of Edom.
verse	13	2	1	@@These @9are@7 the sons of Israel; Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah, Issachar, and Zebulun,
verse	13	2	2	Dan, Joseph, and Benjamin, Naphtali, Gad, and Asher.
verse	13	2	3	@@The sons of Judah; Er, and Onan, and Shelah: @9which@7 three were born unto him of the daughter of Shua the Canaanitess. And Er, the firstborn of Judah, was evil in the sight of the LORD; and he slew him.
verse	13	2	4	@@And Tamar his daughter in law bare him Pharez and Zerah. All the sons of Judah @9were@7 five.
verse	13	2	5	The sons of Pharez; Hezron, and Hamul.
verse	13	2	6	And the sons of Zerah; Zimri, and Ethan, and Heman, and Calcol, and Dara: five of them in all.
verse	13	2	7	And the sons of Carmi; Achar, the troubler of Israel, who transgressed in the thing accursed.
verse	13	2	8	And the sons of Ethan; Azariah.
verse	13	2	9	The sons also of Hezron, that were born unto him; Jerahmeel, and Ram, and Chelubai.
verse	13	2	10	And Ram begat Amminadab; and Amminadab begat Nahshon, prince of the children of Judah;
verse	13	2	11	And Nahshon begat Salma, and Salma begat Boaz,
verse	13	2	12	And Boaz begat Obed, and Obed begat Jesse,
verse	13	2	13	And Jesse begat his firstborn Eliab, and Abinadab the second, and Shimma the third,
verse	13	2	14	Nethaneel the fourth, Raddai the fifth,
verse	13	2	15	Ozem the sixth, David the seventh:
verse	13	2	16	@@Whose sisters @9were@7 Zeruiah, and Abigail. And the sons of Zeruiah; Abishai, and Joab, and Asahel, three.
verse	13	2	17	@@And Abigail bare Amasa: and the father of Amasa @9was@7 Jether the Ishmeelite.
verse	13	2	18	@@And Caleb the son of Hezron begat @9children@7 of Azubah @9his@7 wife, and of Jerioth: her sons @9are@7 these; Jesher, and Shobab, and Ardon.
verse	13	2	19	And when Azubah was dead, Caleb took unto him Ephrath, which bare him Hur.
verse	13	2	20	And Hur begat Uri, and Uri begat Bezaleel.
verse	13	2	21	@@And afterward Hezron went in to the daughter of Machir the father of Gilead, whom he married when he @9was@7 threescore years old; and she bare him Segub.
verse	13	2	22	And Segub begat Jair, who had three and twenty cities in the land of Gilead.
verse	13	2	23	@@And he took Geshur, and Aram, with the towns of Jair, from them, with Kenath, and the towns thereof, @9even@7 threescore cities. All these @9belonged to@7 the sons of Machir the father of Gilead.
verse	13	2	24	And after that Hezron was dead in Caleb-ephratah, then Abiah Hezron's wife bare him Ashur the father of Tekoa.
verse	13	2	25	@@And the sons of Jerahmeel the firstborn of Hezron were, Ram the firstborn, and Bunah, and Oren, and Ozem, @9and@7 Ahijah.
verse	13	2	26	@@Jerahmeel had also another wife, whose name @9was@7 Atarah; she @9was@7 the mother of Onam.
verse	13	2	27	And the sons of Ram the firstborn of Jerahmeel were, Maaz, and Jamin, and Eker.
verse	13	2	28	And the sons of Onam were, Shammai, and Jada. And the sons of Shammai; Nadab, and Abishur.
verse	13	2	29	@@And the name of the wife of Abishur @9was@7 Abihail, and she bare him Ahban, and Molid.
verse	13	2	30	And the sons of Nadab; Seled, and Appaim: but Seled died without children.
verse	13	2	31	And the sons of Appaim; Ishi. And the sons of Ishi; Sheshan. And the children of Sheshan; Ahlai.
verse	13	2	32	And the sons of Jada the brother of Shammai; Jether and Jonathan: and Jether died without children.
verse	13	2	33	And the sons of Jonathan; Peleth, and Zaza. These were the sons of Jerahmeel.
verse	13	2	34	@@Now Sheshan had no sons, but daughters. And Sheshan had a servant, an Egyptian, whose name @9was@7 Jarha.
verse	13	2	35	And Sheshan gave his daughter to Jarha his servant to wife; and she bare him Attai.
verse	13	2	36	And Attai begat Nathan, and Nathan begat Zabad,
verse	13	2	37	And Zabad begat Ephlal, and Ephlal begat Obed,
verse	13	2	38	And Obed begat Jehu, and Jehu begat Azariah,
verse	13	2	39	And Azariah begat Helez, and Helez begat Eleasah,
verse	13	2	40	And Eleasah begat Sisamai, and Sisamai begat Shallum,
verse	13	2	41	And Shallum begat Jekamiah, and Jekamiah begat Elishama.
verse	13	2	42	@@Now the sons of Caleb the brother of Jerahmeel @9were,@7 Mesha his firstborn, which was the father of Ziph; and the sons of Mareshah the father of Hebron.
verse	13	2	43	And the sons of Hebron; Korah, and Tappuah, and Rekem, and Shema.
verse	13	2	44	And Shema begat Raham, the father of Jorkoam: and Rekem begat Shammai.
verse	13	2	45	@@And the son of Shammai @9was@7 Maon: and Maon @9was@7 the father of Bethzur.
verse	13	2	46	And Ephah, Caleb's concubine, bare Haran, and Moza, and Gazez: and Haran begat Gazez.
verse	13	2	47	And the sons of Jahdai; Regem, and Jotham, and Gesham, and Pelet, and Ephah, and Shaaph.
verse	13	2	48	Maachah, Caleb's concubine, bare Sheber, and Tirhanah.
verse	13	2	49	@@She bare also Shaaph the father of Madmannah, Sheva the father of Machbenah, and the father of Gibea: and the daughter of Caleb @9was@7 Achsa.
verse	13	2	50	These were the sons of Caleb the son of Hur, the firstborn of Ephratah; Shobal the father of Kirjathjearim,
verse	13	2	51	Salma the father of Bethlehem, Hareph the father of Beth-gader.
verse	13	2	52	@@And Shobal the father of Kirjathjearim had sons; Haroeh, @9and@7 half of the Manahethites.
verse	13	2	53	And the families of Kirjathjearim; the Ithrites, and the Puhites, and the Shumathites, and the Mishraites; of them came the Zareathites, and the Eshtaulites.
verse	13	2	54	The sons of Salma; Bethlehem, and the Netophathites, Ataroth, the house of Joab, and half of the Manahethites, the Zorites.
verse	13	2	55	@@And the families of the scribes which dwelt at Jabez; the Tirathites, the Shimeathites, @9and@7 Suchathites. These @9are@7 the Kenites that came of Hemath, the father of the house of Rechab.
verse	13	3	1	Now these were the sons of David, which were born unto him in Hebron; the firstborn Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess; the second Daniel, of Abigail the Carmelitess:
verse	13	3	2	The third, Absalom the son of Maachah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur: the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith:
verse	13	3	3	The fifth, Shephatiah of Abital: the sixth, Ithream by Eglah his wife.
verse	13	3	4	@@@9These@7 six were born unto him in Hebron; and there he reigned seven years and six months: and in Jerusalem he reigned thirty and three years.
verse	13	3	5	And these were born unto him in Jerusalem; Shimea, and Shobab, and Nathan, and Solomon, four, of Bath-shua the daughter of Ammiel:
verse	13	3	6	Ibhar also, and Elishama, and Eliphelet,
verse	13	3	7	And Nogah, and Nepheg, and Japhia,
verse	13	3	8	And Elishama, and Eliada, and Eliphelet, nine.
verse	13	3	9	@@@9These were@7 all the sons of David, beside the sons of the concubines, and Tamar their sister.
verse	13	3	10	@@And Solomon's son @9was@7 Rehoboam, Abia his son, Asa his son, Jehoshaphat his son,
verse	13	3	11	Joram his son, Ahaziah his son, Joash his son,
verse	13	3	12	Amaziah his son, Azariah his son, Jotham his son,
verse	13	3	13	Ahaz his son, Hezekiah his son, Manasseh his son,
verse	13	3	14	Amon his son, Josiah his son.
verse	13	3	15	@@And the sons of Josiah @9were,@7 the firstborn Johanan, the second Jehoiakim, the third Zedekiah, the fourth Shallum.
verse	13	3	16	And the sons of Jehoiakim: Jeconiah his son, Zedekiah his son.
verse	13	3	17	And the sons of Jeconiah; Assir, Salathiel his son,
verse	13	3	18	Malchiram also, and Pedaiah, and Shenazar, Jecamiah, Hoshama, and Nedabiah.
verse	13	3	19	@@And the sons of Pedaiah @9were,@7 Zerubbabel, and Shimei: and the sons of Zerubbabel; Meshullam, and Hananiah, and Shelomith their sister:
verse	13	3	20	And Hashubah, and Ohel, and Berechiah, and Hasadiah, Jushab-hesed, five.
verse	13	3	21	And the sons of Hananiah; Pelatiah, and Jesaiah: the sons of Rephaiah, the sons of Arnan, the sons of Obadiah, the sons of Shechaniah.
verse	13	3	22	And the sons of Shechaniah; Shemaiah; and the sons of Shemaiah; Hattush, and Igeal, and Bariah, and Neariah, and Shaphat, six.
verse	13	3	23	And the sons of Neariah; Elioenai, and Hezekiah, and Azrikam, three.
verse	13	3	24	@@And the sons of Elioenai @9were,@7 Hodaiah, and Eliashib, and Pelaiah, and Akkub, and Johanan, and Dalaiah, and Anani, seven.
verse	13	4	1	The sons of Judah; Pharez, Hezron, and Carmi, and Hur, and Shobal.
verse	13	4	2	@@And Reaiah the son of Shobal begat Jahath; and Jahath begat Ahumai and Lahad. These @9are@7 the families of the Zorathites.
verse	13	4	3	@@And these @9were of@7 the father of Etam; Jezreel, and Ishma, and Idbash: and the name of their sister @9was@7 Hazelelponi:
verse	13	4	4	@@And Penuel the father of Gedor and Ezer the father of Hushah. These @9are@7 the sons of Hur, the firstborn of Ephratah, the father of Bethlehem.
verse	13	4	5	And Ashur the father of Tekoa had two wives, Helah and Naarah.
verse	13	4	6	@@And Naarah bare him Ahuzam, and Hepher, and Temeni, and Haahashtari. These @9were@7 the sons of Naarah.
verse	13	4	7	@@And the sons of Helah @9were,@7 Zereth, and Jezoar, and Ethnan.
verse	13	4	8	And Coz begat Anub, and Zobebah, and the families of Aharhel the son of Harum.
verse	13	4	9	And Jabez was more honourable than his brethren: and his mother called his name Jabez, saying, Because I bare him with sorrow.
verse	13	4	10	@@And Jabez called on the God of Israel, saying, Oh that thou wouldest bless me indeed, and enlarge my coast, and that thine hand might be with me, and that thou wouldest keep @9me@7 from evil, that it may not grieve me! And God granted him that which he requested.
verse	13	4	11	@@And Chelub the brother of Shuah begat Mehir, which @9was@7 the father of Eshton.
verse	13	4	12	@@And Eshton begat Beth-rapha, and Paseah, and Tehinnah the father of Ir-nahash. These @9are@7 the men of Rechah.
verse	13	4	13	And the sons of Kenaz; Othniel, and Seraiah: and the sons of Othniel; Hathath.
verse	13	4	14	And Meonothai begat Ophrah: and Seraiah begat Joab, the father of the valley of Charashim; for they were craftsmen.
verse	13	4	15	And the sons of Caleb the son of Jephunneh; Iru, Elah, and Naam: and the sons of Elah, even Kenaz.
verse	13	4	16	And the sons of Jehaleleel; Ziph, and Ziphah, Tiria, and Asareel.
verse	13	4	17	@@And the sons of Ezra @9were,@7 Jether, and Mered, and Epher, and Jalon: and she bare Miriam, and Shammai, and Ishbah the father of Eshtemoa.
verse	13	4	18	@@And his wife Jehudijah bare Jered the father of Gedor, and Heber the father of Socho, and Jekuthiel the father of Zanoah. And these @9are@7 the sons of Bithiah the daughter of Pharaoh, which Mered took.
verse	13	4	19	@@And the sons of @9his@7 wife Hodiah the sister of Naham, the father of Keilah the Garmite, and Eshtemoa the Maachathite.
verse	13	4	20	@@And the sons of Shimon @9were,@7 Amnon, and Rinnah, Ben-hanan, and Tilon. And the sons of Ishi @9were,@7 Zoheth, and Ben-zoheth.
verse	13	4	21	@@The sons of Shelah the son of Judah @9were,@7 Er the father of Lecah, and Laadah the father of Mareshah, and the families of the house of them that wrought fine linen, of the house of Ashbea,
verse	13	4	22	@@And Jokim, and the men of Chozeba, and Joash, and Saraph, who had the dominion in Moab, and Jashubi-lehem. And @9these are@7 ancient things.
verse	13	4	23	@@These @9were@7 the potters, and those that dwelt among plants and hedges: there they dwelt with the king for his work.
verse	13	4	24	@@The sons of Simeon @9were,@7 Nemuel, and Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, @9and@7 Shaul:
verse	13	4	25	Shallum his son, Mibsam his son, Mishma his son.
verse	13	4	26	And the sons of Mishma; Hamuel his son, Zacchur his son, Shimei his son.
verse	13	4	27	And Shimei had sixteen sons and six daughters; but his brethren had not many children, neither did all their family multiply, like to the children of Judah.
verse	13	4	28	And they dwelt at Beersheba, and Moladah, and Hazarshual,
verse	13	4	29	And at Bilhah, and at Ezem, and at Tolad,
verse	13	4	30	And at Bethuel, and at Hormah, and at Ziklag,
verse	13	4	31	@@And at Bethmarcaboth, and Hazar-susim, and at Beth-birei, and at Shaaraim. These @9were@7 their cities unto the reign of David.
verse	13	4	32	@@And their villages @9were,@7 Etam, and Ain, Rimmon, and Tochen, and Ashan, five cities:
verse	13	4	33	@@And all their villages that @9were@7 round about the same cities, unto Baal. These @9were@7 their habitations, and their genealogy.
verse	13	4	34	And Meshobab, and Jamlech, and Joshah the son of Amaziah,
verse	13	4	35	And Joel, and Jehu the son of Josibiah, the son of Seraiah, the son of Asiel,
verse	13	4	36	And Elioenai, and Jaakobah, and Jeshohaiah, and Asaiah, and Adiel, and Jesimiel, and Benaiah,
verse	13	4	37	And Ziza the son of Shiphi, the son of Allon, the son of Jedaiah, the son of Shimri, the son of Shemaiah;
verse	13	4	38	@@These mentioned by @9their@7 names @9were@7 princes in their families: and the house of their fathers increased greatly.
verse	13	4	39	@@And they went to the entrance of Gedor, @9even@7 unto the east side of the valley, to seek pasture for their flocks.
verse	13	4	40	@@And they found fat pasture and good, and the land @9was@7 wide, and quiet, and peaceable; for @9they@7 of Ham had dwelt there of old.
verse	13	4	41	@@And these written by name came in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah, and smote their tents, and the habitations that were found there, and destroyed them utterly unto this day, and dwelt in their rooms: because @9there was@7 pasture there for their flocks.
verse	13	4	42	@@And @9some@7 of them, @9even@7 of the sons of Simeon, five hundred men, went to mount Seir, having for their captains Pelatiah, and Neariah, and Rephaiah, and Uzziel, the sons of Ishi.
verse	13	4	43	And they smote the rest of the Amalekites that were escaped, and dwelt there unto this day.
verse	13	5	1	@@Now the sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel, (for he @9was@7 the firstborn; but, forasmuch as he defiled his father's bed, his birthright was given unto the sons of Joseph the son of Israel: and the genealogy is not to be reckoned after the birthright.
verse	13	5	2	@@For Judah prevailed above his brethren, and of him @9came@7 the chief ruler; but the birthright @9was@7 Joseph's:)
verse	13	5	3	@@The sons, @9I say,@7 of Reuben the firstborn of Israel @9were,@7 Hanoch, and Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi.
verse	13	5	4	The sons of Joel; Shemaiah his son, Gog his son, Shimei his son,
verse	13	5	5	Micah his son, Reaia his son, Baal his son,
verse	13	5	6	@@Beerah his son, whom Tilgath-pilneser king of Assyria carried away @9captive:@7 he @9was@7 prince of the Reubenites.
verse	13	5	7	@@And his brethren by their families, when the genealogy of their generations was reckoned, @9were@7 the chief, Jeiel, and Zechariah,
verse	13	5	8	And Bela the son of Azaz, the son of Shema, the son of Joel, who dwelt in Aroer, even unto Nebo and Baalmeon:
verse	13	5	9	@@And eastward he inhabited unto the entering in of the wilderness from the river Euphrates: because their cattle were multiplied in the @9land@7 of Gilead.
verse	13	5	10	And in the days of Saul they made war with the Hagarites, who fell by their hand: and they dwelt in their tents throughout all the east land of Gilead.
verse	13	5	11	And the children of Gad dwelt over against them, in the land of Bashan unto Salchah:
verse	13	5	12	Joel the chief, and Shapham the next, and Jaanai, and Shaphat in Bashan.
verse	13	5	13	@@And their brethren of the house of their fathers @9were,@7 Michael, and Meshullam, and Sheba, and Jorai, and Jachan, and Zia, and Heber, seven.
verse	13	5	14	@@These @9are@7 the children of Abihail the son of Huri, the son of Jaroah, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz;
verse	13	5	15	Ahi the son of Abdiel, the son of Guni, chief of the house of their fathers.
verse	13	5	16	And they dwelt in Gilead in Bashan, and in her towns, and in all the suburbs of Sharon, upon their borders.
verse	13	5	17	All these were reckoned by genealogies in the days of Jotham king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam king of Israel.
verse	13	5	18	@@The sons of Reuben, and the Gadites, and half the tribe of Manasseh, of valiant men, men able to bear buckler and sword, and to shoot with bow, and skilful in war, @9were@7 four and forty thousand seven hundred and threescore, that went out to the war.
verse	13	5	19	And they made war with the Hagarites, with Jetur, and Nephish, and Nodab.
verse	13	5	20	@@And they were helped against them, and the Hagarites were delivered into their hand, and all that @9were@7 with them: for they cried to God in the battle, and he was intreated of them; because they put their trust in him.
verse	13	5	21	And they took away their cattle; of their camels fifty thousand, and of sheep two hundred and fifty thousand, and of asses two thousand, and of men an hundred thousand.
verse	13	5	22	@@For there fell down many slain, because the war @9was@7 of God. And they dwelt in their steads until the captivity.
verse	13	5	23	And the children of the half tribe of Manasseh dwelt in the land: they increased from Bashan unto Baalhermon and Senir, and unto mount Hermon.
verse	13	5	24	@@And these @9were@7 the heads of the house of their fathers, even Epher, and Ishi, and Eliel, and Azriel, and Jeremiah, and Hodaviah, and Jahdiel, mighty men of valour, famous men, @9and@7 heads of the house of their fathers.
verse	13	5	25	And they transgressed against the God of their fathers, and went a whoring after the gods of the people of the land, whom God destroyed before them.
verse	13	5	26	And the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul king of Assyria, and the spirit of Tilgath-pilneser king of Assyria, and he carried them away, even the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh, and brought them unto Halah, and Habor, and Hara, and to the river Gozan, unto this day.
verse	13	6	1	The sons of Levi; Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.
verse	13	6	2	And the sons of Kohath; Amram, Izhar, and Hebron, and Uzziel.
verse	13	6	3	And the children of Amram; Aaron, and Moses, and Miriam. The sons also of Aaron; Nadab, and Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.
verse	13	6	4	Eleazar begat Phinehas, Phinehas begat Abishua,
verse	13	6	5	And Abishua begat Bukki, and Bukki begat Uzzi,
verse	13	6	6	And Uzzi begat Zerahiah, and Zerahiah begat Meraioth,
verse	13	6	7	Meraioth begat Amariah, and Amariah begat Ahitub,
verse	13	6	8	And Ahitub begat Zadok, and Zadok begat Ahimaaz,
verse	13	6	9	And Ahimaaz begat Azariah, and Azariah begat Johanan,
