verse	13	11	11	@@And this @9is@7 the number of the mighty men whom David had; Jashobeam, and Hachmonite, the chief of the captains: he lifted up his spear against three hundred slain @9by him@7 at one time.
verse	13	11	12	@@And after him @9was@7 Eleazar the son of Dodo, the Ahohite, who @9was one@7 of the three mighties.
verse	13	11	13	He was with David at Pas-dammim, and there the Philistines were gathered together to battle, where was a parcel of ground full of barley; and the people fled from before the Philistines.
verse	13	11	14	@@And they set themselves in the midst of @9that@7 parcel, and delivered it, and slew the Philistines; and the LORD saved @9them@7 by a great deliverance.
verse	13	11	15	Now three of the thirty captains went down to the rock to David, into the cave of Adullam; and the host of the Philistines encamped in the valley of Rephaim.
verse	13	11	16	@@And David @9was@7 then in the hold, and the Philistines' garrison @9was@7 then at Bethlehem.
verse	13	11	17	@@And David longed, and said, Oh that one would give me drink of the water of the well of Bethlehem, that @9is@7 at the gate!
verse	13	11	18	@@And the three brake through the host of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Bethlehem, that @9was@7 by the gate, and took @9it,@7 and brought @9it@7 to David: but David would not drink @9of@7 it, but poured it out to the LORD,
verse	13	11	19	@@And said, My God forbid it me, that I should do this thing: shall I drink the blood of these men that have put their lives in jeopardy? for with @9the jeopardy of@7 their lives they brought it. Therefore he would not drink it. These things did these three mightiest.
verse	13	11	20	@@And Abishai the brother of Joab, he was chief of the three: for lifting up his spear against three hundred, he slew @9them,@7 and had a name among the three.
