verse	13	15	9	Of the sons of Hebron; Eliel the chief, and his brethren fourscore:
verse	13	15	10	Of the sons of Uzziel; Amminadab the chief, and his brethren an hundred and twelve.
verse	13	15	11	And David called for Zadok and Abiathar the priests, and for the Levites, for Uriel, Asaiah, and Joel, Shemaiah, and Eliel, and Amminadab,
verse	13	15	12	@@And said unto them, Ye @9are@7 the chief of the fathers of the Levites: sanctify yourselves, @9both@7 ye and your brethren, that ye may bring up the ark of the LORD God of Israel unto @9the place that@7 I have prepared for it.
verse	13	15	13	@@For because ye @9did it@7 not at the first, the LORD our God made a breach upon us, for that we sought him not after the due order.
verse	13	15	14	So the priests and the Levites sanctified themselves to bring up the ark of the LORD God of Israel.
verse	13	15	15	And the children of the Levites bare the ark of God upon their shoulders with the staves thereon, as Moses commanded according to the word of the LORD.
verse	13	15	16	@@And David spake to the chief of the Levites to appoint their brethren @9to be@7 the singers with instruments of musick, psalteries and harps and cymbals, sounding, by lifting up the voice with joy.
verse	13	15	17	So the Levites appointed Heman the son of Joel; and of his brethren, Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of the sons of Merari their brethren, Ethan the son of Kushaiah;
verse	13	15	18	@@And with them their brethren of the second @9degree,@7 Zechariah, Ben, and Jaaziel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Unni, Eliab, and Benaiah, and Maaseiah, and Mattithiah, and Elipheleh, and Mikneiah, and Obededom, and Jeiel, the porters.
verse	13	15	19	@@So the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, @9were appointed@7 to sound with cymbals of brass;
