verse	13	16	5	Asaph the chief, and next to him Zechariah, Jeiel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Mattithiah, and Eliab, and Benaiah, and Obededom: and Jeiel with psalteries and with harps; but Asaph made a sound with cymbals;
verse	13	16	6	Benaiah also and Jahaziel the priests with trumpets continually before the ark of the covenant of God.
verse	13	16	7	@@Then on that day David delivered first @9this psalm@7 to thank the LORD into the hand of Asaph and his brethren.
verse	13	16	8	Give thanks unto the LORD, call upon his name, make known his deeds among the people.
verse	13	16	9	Sing unto him, sing psalms unto him, talk ye of all his wondrous works.
verse	13	16	10	Glory ye in his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice that seek the LORD.
verse	13	16	11	Seek the LORD and his strength, seek his face continually.
verse	13	16	12	Remember his marvellous works that he hath done, his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;
verse	13	16	13	O ye seed of Israel his servant, ye children of Jacob, his chosen ones.
verse	13	16	14	@@He @9is@7 the LORD our God; his judgments @9are@7 in all the earth.
verse	13	16	15	@@Be ye mindful always of his covenant; the word @9which@7 he commanded to a thousand generations;
verse	13	16	16	@@@9Even of the covenant@7 which he made with Abraham, and of his oath unto Isaac;
verse	13	16	17	@@And hath confirmed the same to Jacob for a law, @9and@7 to Israel @9for@7 an everlasting covenant,
verse	13	16	18	Saying, Unto thee will I give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance;
