verse	13	16	43	And all the people departed every man to his house: and David returned to bless his house.
verse	13	17	1	@@Now it came to pass, as David sat in his house, that David said to Nathan the prophet, Lo, I dwell in an house of cedars, but the ark of the covenant of the LORD @9remaineth@7 under curtains.
verse	13	17	2	@@Then Nathan said unto David, Do all that is in thine heart; for God @9is@7 with thee.
verse	13	17	3	And it came to pass the same night, that the word of God came to Nathan, saying,
verse	13	17	4	Go and tell David my servant, Thus saith the LORD, Thou shalt not build me an house to dwell in:
verse	13	17	5	@@For I have not dwelt in an house since the day that I brought up Israel unto this day; but have gone from tent to tent, and from @9one@7 tabernacle @9to another. @7
verse	13	17	6	Wheresoever I have walked with all Israel, spake I a word to any of the judges of Israel, whom I commanded to feed my people, saying, Why have ye not built me an house of cedars?
verse	13	17	7	@@Now therefore thus shalt thou say unto my servant David, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, I took thee from the sheepcote, @9even@7 from following the sheep, that thou shouldest be ruler over my people Israel:
verse	13	17	8	@@And I have been with thee whithersoever thou hast walked, and have cut off all thine enemies from before thee, and have made thee a name like the name of the great men that @9are@7 in the earth.
verse	13	17	9	Also I will ordain a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, and they shall dwell in their place, and shall be moved no more; neither shall the children of wickedness waste them any more, as at the beginning,
verse	13	17	10	@@And since the time that I commanded judges @9to be@7 over my people Israel. Moreover I will subdue all thine enemies. Furthermore I tell thee that the LORD will build thee an house.
verse	13	17	11	@@And it shall come to pass, when thy days be expired that thou must go @9to be@7 with thy fathers, that I will raise up thy seed after thee, which shall be of thy sons; and I will establish his kingdom.
verse	13	17	12	He shall build me an house, and I will stablish his throne for ever.
verse	13	17	13	@@I will be his father, and he shall be my son: and I will not take my mercy away from him, as I took @9it@7 from @9him@7 that was before thee:
verse	13	17	14	But I will settle him in mine house and in my kingdom for ever: and his throne shall be established for evermore.
verse	13	17	15	According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so did Nathan speak unto David.
verse	13	17	16	@@And David the king came and sat before the LORD, and said, Who @9am@7 I, O LORD God, and what @9is@7 mine house, that thou hast brought me hitherto?
verse	13	17	17	@@And @9yet@7 this was a small thing in thine eyes, O God; for thou hast @9also@7 spoken of thy servant's house for a great while to come, and hast regarded me according to the estate of a man of high degree, O LORD God.
verse	13	17	18	@@What can David @9speak@7 more to thee for the honour of thy servant? for thou knowest thy servant.
verse	13	17	19	O LORD, for thy servant's sake, and according to thine own heart, hast thou done all this greatness, in making known all these great things.
verse	13	17	20	@@O LORD, @9there is@7 none like thee, neither @9is there any@7 God beside thee, according to all that we have heard with our ears.
verse	13	17	21	@@And what one nation in the earth @9is@7 like thy people Israel, whom God went to redeem @9to be@7 his own people, to make thee a name of greatness and terribleness, by driving out nations from before thy people, whom thou hast redeemed out of Egypt?
verse	13	17	22	For thy people Israel didst thou make thine own people for ever; and thou, LORD, becamest their God.
verse	13	17	23	Therefore now, LORD, let the thing that thou hast spoken concerning thy servant and concerning his house be established for ever, and do as thou hast said.
verse	13	17	24	@@Let it even be established, that thy name may be magnified for ever, saying, The LORD of hosts @9is@7 the God of Israel, @9even@7 a God to Israel: and @9let@7 the house of David thy servant @9be@7 established before thee.
verse	13	17	25	@@For thou, O my God, hast told thy servant that thou wilt build him an house: therefore thy servant hath found @9in his heart@7 to pray before thee.
verse	13	17	26	And now, LORD, thou art God, and hast promised this goodness unto thy servant:
verse	13	17	27	@@Now therefore let it please thee to bless the house of thy servant, that it may be before thee for ever: for thou blessest, O LORD, and @9it shall be@7 blessed for ever.
verse	13	18	1	Now after this it came to pass, that David smote the Philistines, and subdued them, and took Gath and her towns out of the hand of the Philistines.
verse	13	18	2	@@And he smote Moab; and the Moabites became David's servants, @9and@7 brought gifts.
