verse	13	21	20	And Ornan turned back, and saw the angel; and his four sons with him hid themselves. Now Ornan was threshing wheat.
verse	13	21	21	@@And as David came to Ornan, Ornan looked and saw David, and went out of the threshingfloor, and bowed himself to David with @9his@7 face to the ground.
verse	13	21	22	@@Then David said to Ornan, Grant me the place of @9this@7 threshingfloor, that I may build an altar therein unto the LORD: thou shalt grant it me for the full price: that the plague may be stayed from the people.
verse	13	21	23	@@And Ornan said unto David, Take @9it@7 to thee, and let my lord the king do @9that which is@7 good in his eyes: lo,I give @9thee@7 the oxen @9also@7 for burnt offerings, and the threshing instruments for wood, and the wheat for the meat offering; I give it all.
verse	13	21	24	@@And king David said to Ornan, Nay; but I will verily buy it for the full price: for I will not take @9that@7 which @9is@7 thine for the LORD, nor offer burnt offerings without cost.
verse	13	21	25	So David gave to Ornan for the place six hundred shekels of gold by weight.
verse	13	21	26	And David built there an altar unto the LORD, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings, and called upon the LORD; and he answered him from heaven by fire upon the altar of burnt offering.
verse	13	21	27	And the LORD commanded the angel; and he put up his sword again into the sheath thereof.
verse	13	21	28	At that time when David saw that the LORD had answered him in the threshingfloor of Ornan the Jebusite, then he sacrificed there.
verse	13	21	29	@@For the tabernacle of the LORD, which Moses made in the wilderness, and the altar of the burnt offering, @9were@7 at that season in the high place at Gibeon.
verse	13	21	30	But David could not go before it to enquire of God: for he was afraid because of the sword of the angel of the LORD.
verse	13	22	1	@@Then David said, This @9is@7 the house of the LORD God, and this @9is@7 the altar of the burnt offering for Israel.
verse	13	22	2	@@And David commanded to gather together the strangers that @9were@7 in the land of Israel; and he set masons to hew wrought stones to build the house of God.
verse	13	22	3	And David prepared iron in abundance for the nails for the doors of the gates, and for the joinings; and brass in abundance without weight;
verse	13	22	4	Also cedar trees in abundance: for the Zidonians and they of Tyre brought much cedar wood to David.
verse	13	22	5	@@And David said, Solomon my son @9is@7 young and tender, and the house @9that is@7 to be builded for the LORD @9must be@7 exceeding magnifical, of fame and of glory throughout all countries: I will @9therefore@7 now make preparation for it. So David prepared abundantly before his death.
verse	13	22	6	Then he called for Solomon his son, and charged him to build an house for the LORD God of Israel.
verse	13	22	7	And David said to Solomon, My son, as for me, it was in my mind to build an house unto the name of the LORD my God:
verse	13	22	8	But the word of the LORD came to me, saying, Thou hast shed blood abundantly, and hast made great wars: thou shalt not build an house unto my name, because thou hast shed much blood upon the earth in my sight.
verse	13	22	9	Behold, a son shall be born to thee, who shall be a man of rest; and I will give him rest from all his enemies round about: for his name shall be Solomon, and I will give peace and quietness unto Israel in his days.
verse	13	22	10	@@He shall build an house for my name; and he shall be my son, and I @9will be@7 his father; and I will establish the throne of his kingdom over Israel for ever.
verse	13	22	11	Now, my son, the LORD be with thee; and prosper thou, and build the house of the LORD thy God, as he hath said of thee.
verse	13	22	12	Only the LORD give thee wisdom and understanding, and give thee charge concerning Israel, that thou mayest keep the law of the LORD thy God.
verse	13	22	13	Then shalt thou prosper, if thou takest heed to fulfil the statutes and judgments which the LORD charged Moses with concerning Israel: be strong, and of good courage; dread not, nor be dismayed.
verse	13	22	14	Now, behold, in my trouble I have prepared for the house of the LORD an hundred thousand talents of gold, and a thousand thousand talents of silver; and of brass and iron without weight; for it is in abundance: timber also and stone have I prepared; and thou mayest add thereto.
verse	13	22	15	@@Moreover @9there are@7 workmen with thee in abundance, hewers and workers of stone and timber, and all manner of cunning men for every manner of work.
verse	13	22	16	@@Of the gold, the silver, and the brass, and the iron, @9there is@7 no number. Arise @9therefore,@7 and be doing, and the LORD be with thee.
verse	13	22	17	@@David also commanded all the princes of Israel to help Solomon his son, @9saying, @7
verse	13	22	18	@@@9Is@7 not the LORD your God with you? and hath he @9not@7 given you rest on every side? for he hath given the inhabitants of the land into mine hand; and the land is subdued before the LORD, and before his people.
verse	13	22	19	Now set your heart and your soul to seek the LORD your God; arise therefore, and build ye the sanctuary of the LORD God, to bring the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and the holy vessels of God, into the house that is to be built to the name of the LORD.
verse	13	23	1	So when David was old and full of days, he made Solomon his son king over Israel.
verse	13	23	2	And he gathered together all the princes of Israel, with the priests and the Levites.
verse	13	23	3	Now the Levites were numbered from the age of thirty years and upward: and their number by their polls, man by man, was thirty and eight thousand.
verse	13	23	4	@@Of which, twenty and four thousand @9were@7 to set forward the work of the house of the LORD; and six thousand @9were@7 officers and judges:
verse	13	23	5	@@Moreover four thousand @9were@7 porters; and four thousand praised the LORD with the instruments which I made, @9said David,@7 to praise @9therewith. @7
verse	13	23	6	@@And David divided them into courses among the sons of Levi, @9namely,@7 Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.
verse	13	23	7	@@Of the Gershonites @9were,@7 Laadan, and Shimei.
verse	13	23	8	@@The sons of Laadan; the chief @9was@7 Jehiel, and Zetham, and Joel, three.
verse	13	23	9	@@The sons of Shimei; Shelomith, and Haziel, and Haran, three. These @9were@7 the chief of the fathers of Laadan.
verse	13	23	10	@@And the sons of Shimei @9were,@7 Jahath, Zina, and Jeush, and Beriah. These four @9were@7 the sons of Shimei.
verse	13	23	11	@@And Jahath was the chief, and Zizah the second: but Jeush and Beriah had not many sons; therefore they were in one reckoning, according to @9their@7 father's house.
verse	13	23	12	The sons of Kohath; Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel, four.
verse	13	23	13	The sons of Amram; Aaron and Moses: and Aaron was separated, that he should sanctify the most holy things, he and his sons for ever, to burn incense before the LORD, to minister unto him, and to bless in his name for ever.
verse	13	23	14	@@Now @9concerning@7 Moses the man of God, his sons were named of the tribe of Levi.
verse	13	23	15	@@The sons of Moses @9were,@7 Gershom, and Eliezer.
verse	13	23	16	@@Of the sons of Gershom, Shebuel @9was@7 the chief.
verse	13	23	17	@@And the sons of Eliezer @9were,@7 Rehabiah the chief. And Eliezer had none other sons; but the sons of Rehabiah were very many.
verse	13	23	18	Of the sons of Izhar; Shelomith the chief.
verse	13	23	19	Of the sons of Hebron; Jeriah the first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth.
verse	13	23	20	Of the sons of Uzziel; Micah the first, and Jesiah the second.
verse	13	23	21	The sons of Merari; Mahli, and Mushi. The sons of Mahli; Eleazar, and Kish.
verse	13	23	22	And Eleazar died, and had no sons, but daughters: and their brethren the sons of Kish took them.
verse	13	23	23	The sons of Mushi; Mahli, and Eder, and Jeremoth, three.
verse	13	23	24	@@These @9were@7 the sons of Levi after the house of their fathers; @9even@7 the chief of the fathers, as they were counted by number of names by their polls, that did the work for the service of the house of the LORD, from the age of twenty years and upward.
verse	13	23	25	For David said, The LORD God of Israel hath given rest unto his people, that they may dwell in Jerusalem for ever:
verse	13	23	26	@@And also unto the Levites; they shall no @9more@7 carry the tabernacle, nor any vessels of it for the service thereof.
verse	13	23	27	@@For by the last words of David the Levites @9were@7 numbered from twenty years old and above:
verse	13	23	28	@@Because their office @9was@7 to wait on the sons of Aaron for the service of the house of the LORD, in the courts, and in the chambers, and in the purifying of all holy things, and the work of the service of the house of God;
verse	13	23	29	@@Both for the shewbread, and for the fine flour for meat offering, and for the unleavened cakes, and for @9that which is baked in@7 the pan, and for that which is fried, and for all manner of measure and size;
verse	13	23	30	And to stand every morning to thank and praise the LORD, and likewise at even;
verse	13	23	31	And to offer all burnt sacrifices unto the LORD in the sabbaths, in the new moons, and on the set feasts, by number, according to the order commanded unto them, continually before the LORD:
verse	13	23	32	@@And that they should keep the charge of the tabernacle of the congregation, and the charge of the holy @9place,@7 and the charge of the sons of Aaron their brethren, in the service of the house of the LORD.
verse	13	24	1	@@Now @9these are@7 the divisions of the sons of Aaron. The sons of Aaron; Nadab, and Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.
verse	13	24	2	But Nadab and Abihu died before their father, and had no children: therefore Eleazar and Ithamar executed the priest's office.
verse	13	24	3	And David distributed them, both Zadok of the sons of Eleazar, and Ahimelech of the sons of Ithamar, according to their offices in their service.
verse	13	24	4	@@And there were more chief men found of the sons of Eleazar than of the sons of Ithamar; and @9thus@7 were they divided. Among the sons of Eleazar @9there were@7 sixteen chief men of the house of @9their@7 fathers, and eight among the sons of Ithamar according to the house of their fathers.
verse	13	24	5	@@Thus were they divided by lot, one sort with another; for the governors of the sanctuary, and governors @9of the house@7 of God, were of the sons of Eleazar, and of the sons of Ithamar.
verse	13	24	6	@@And Shemaiah the son of Nethaneel the scribe, @9one@7 of the Levites, wrote them before the king, and the princes, and Zadok the priest, and Ahimelech the son of Abiathar, and @9before@7 the chief of the fathers of the priests and Levites: one principal household being taken for Eleazar, and @9one@7 taken for Ithamar.
verse	13	24	7	Now the first lot came forth to Jehoiarib, the second to Jedaiah,
verse	13	24	8	The third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim,
verse	13	24	9	The fifth to Malchijah, the sixth to Mijamin,
verse	13	24	10	The seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to Abijah,
verse	13	24	11	The ninth to Jeshua, the tenth to Shecaniah,
verse	13	24	12	The eleventh to Eliashib, the twelfth to Jakim,
verse	13	24	13	The thirteenth to Huppah, the fourteenth to Jeshebeab,
verse	13	24	14	The fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,
verse	13	24	15	The seventeenth to Hezir, the eighteenth to Aphses,
verse	13	24	16	The nineteenth to Pethahiah, the twentieth to Jehezekel,
verse	13	24	17	The one and twentieth to Jachin, the two and twentieth to Gamul,
verse	13	24	18	The three and twentieth to Delaiah, the four and twentieth to Maaziah.
verse	13	24	19	@@These @9were@7 the orderings of them in their service to come into the house of the LORD, according to their manner, under Aaron their father, as the LORD God of Israel had commanded him.
verse	13	24	20	@@And the rest of the sons of Levi @9were these:@7 Of the sons of Amram; Shubael: of the sons of Shubael; Jehdeiah.
verse	13	24	21	@@Concerning Rehabiah: of the sons of Rehabiah, the first @9was@7 Isshiah.
verse	13	24	22	Of the Izharites; Shelomoth: of the sons of Shelomoth; Jahath.
verse	13	24	23	@@And the sons @9of Hebron;@7 Jeriah @9the first,@7 Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, Jekameam the fourth.
verse	13	24	24	@@@9Of@7 the sons of Uzziel; Michah: of the sons of Michah; Shamir.
verse	13	24	25	@@The brother of Michah @9was@7 Isshiah: of the sons of Isshiah; Zechariah.
verse	13	24	26	@@The sons of Merari @9were@7 Mahli and Mushi: the sons of Jaaziah; Beno.
verse	13	24	27	The sons of Merari by Jaaziah; Beno, and Shoham, and Zaccur, and Ibri.
