verse	13	26	22	@@The sons of Jehieli; Zetham, and Joel his brother, @9which were@7 over the treasures of the house of the LORD.
verse	13	26	23	@@Of the Amramites, @9and@7 the Izharites, the Hebronites, @9and@7 the Uzzielites:
verse	13	26	24	@@And Shebuel the son of Gershom, the son of Moses, @9was@7 ruler of the treasures.
verse	13	26	25	And his brethren by Eliezer; Rehabiah his son, and Jeshaiah his son, and Joram his son, and Zichri his son, and Shelomith his son.
verse	13	26	26	@@Which Shelomith and his brethren @9were@7 over all the treasures of the dedicated things, which David the king, and the chief fathers, the captains over thousands and hundreds, and the captains of the host, had dedicated.
verse	13	26	27	Out of the spoils won in battles did they dedicate to maintain the house of the LORD.
verse	13	26	28	@@And all that Samuel the seer, and Saul the son of Kish, and Abner the son of Ner, and Joab the son of Zeruiah, had dedicated; @9and@7 whosoever had dedicated @9any thing, it was@7 under the hand of Shelomith, and of his brethren.
verse	13	26	29	@@Of the Izharites, Chenaniah and his sons @9were@7 for the outward business over Israel, for officers and judges.
verse	13	26	30	@@@9And@7 of the Hebronites, Hashabiah and his brethren, men of valour, a thousand and seven hundred, @9were@7 officers among them of Israel on this side Jordan westward in all the business of the LORD, and in the service of the king.
verse	13	26	31	@@Among the Hebronites @9was@7 Jerijah the chief, @9even@7 among the Hebronites, according to the generations of his fathers. In the fortieth year of the reign of David they were sought for, and there were found among them mighty men of valour at Jazer of Gilead.
verse	13	26	32	@@And his brethren, men of valour, @9were@7 two thousand and seven hundred chief fathers, whom king David made rulers over the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh, for every matter pertaining to God, and affairs of the king.
verse	13	27	1	@@Now the children of Israel after their number, @9to wit,@7 the chief fathers and captains of thousands and hundreds, and their officers that served the king in any matter of the courses, which came in and went out month by month throughout all the months of the year, of every course @9were@7 twenty and four thousand.
verse	13	27	2	@@Over the first course for the first month @9was@7 Jashobeam the son of Zabdiel: and in his course @9were@7 twenty and four thousand.
verse	13	27	3	@@Of the children of Perez @9was@7 the chief of all the captains of the host for the first month.
verse	13	27	4	@@And over the course of the second month @9was@7 Dodai an Ahohite, and of his course @9was@7 Mikloth also the ruler: in his course likewise @9were@7 twenty and four thousand.
verse	13	27	5	@@The third captain of the host for the third month @9was@7 Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, a chief priest: and in his course @9were@7 twenty and four thousand.
verse	13	27	6	@@This @9is that@7 Benaiah, @9who was@7 mighty @9among@7 the thirty, and above the thirty: and in his course @9was@7 Ammizabad his son.
verse	13	27	7	@@The fourth @9captain@7 for the fourth month @9was@7 Asahel the brother of Joab, and Zebadiah his son after him: and in his course @9were@7 twenty and four thousand.
