verse	14	25	11	And Amaziah strengthened himself, and led forth his people, and went to the valley of salt, and smote of the children of Seir ten thousand.
verse	14	25	12	@@And @9other@7 ten thousand @9left@7 alive did the children of Judah carry away captive, and brought them unto the top of the rock, and cast them down from the top of the rock, that they all were broken in pieces.
verse	14	25	13	But the soldiers of the army which Amaziah sent back, that they should not go with him to battle, fell upon the cities of Judah, from Samaria even unto Bethhoron, and smote three thousand of them, and took much spoil.
verse	14	25	14	@@Now it came to pass, after that Amaziah was come from the slaughter of the Edomites, that he brought the gods of the children of Seir, and set them up @9to be@7 his gods, and bowed down himself before them, and burned incense unto them.
verse	14	25	15	Wherefore the anger of the LORD was kindled against Amaziah, and he sent unto him a prophet, which said unto him, Why hast thou sought after the gods of the people, which could not deliver their own people out of thine hand?
verse	14	25	16	@@And it came to pass, as he talked with him, that @9the king@7 said unto him, Art thou made of the king's counsel? forbear; why shouldest thou be smitten? Then the prophet forbare, and said, I know that God hath determined to destroy thee, because thou hast done this, and hast not hearkened unto my counsel.
verse	14	25	17	Then Amaziah king of Judah took advice, and sent to Joash, the son of Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, Come, let us see one another in the face.
verse	14	25	18	@@And Joash king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The thistle that @9was@7 in Lebanon sent to the cedar that @9was@7 in Lebanon, saying, Give thy daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that @9was@7 in Lebanon, and trode down the thistle.
verse	14	25	19	@@Thou sayest, Lo, thou hast smitten the Edomites; and thine heart lifteth thee up to boast: abide now at home; why shouldest thou meddle to @9thine@7 hurt, that thou shouldest fall, @9even@7 thou, and Judah with thee?
verse	14	25	20	@@But Amaziah would not hear; for it @9came@7 of God, that he might deliver them into the hand @9of their enemies,@7 because they sought after the gods of Edom.
