verse	14	26	2	He built Eloth, and restored it to Judah, after that the king slept with his fathers.
verse	14	26	3	@@Sixteen years old @9was@7 Uzziah when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty and two years in Jerusalem. His mother's name also was Jecoliah of Jerusalem.
verse	14	26	4	@@And he did @9that which was@7 right in the sight of the LORD, according to all that his father Amaziah did.
verse	14	26	5	And he sought God in the days of Zechariah, who had understanding in the visions of God: and as long as he sought the LORD, God made him to prosper.
verse	14	26	6	And he went forth and warred against the Philistines, and brake down the wall of Gath, and the wall of Jabneh, and the wall of Ashdod, and built cities about Ashdod, and among the Philistines.
verse	14	26	7	And God helped him against the Philistines, and against the Arabians that dwelt in Gur-baal, and the Mehunims.
verse	14	26	8	@@And the Ammonites gave gifts to Uzziah: and his name spread abroad @9even@7 to the entering in of Egypt; for he strengthened @9himself@7 exceedingly.
verse	14	26	9	@@Moreover Uzziah built towers in Jerusalem at the corner gate, and at the valley gate, and at the turning @9of the wall,@7 and fortified them.
verse	14	26	10	@@Also he built towers in the desert, and digged many wells: for he had much cattle, both in the low country, and in the plains: husbandmen @9also,@7 and vine dressers in the mountains, and in Carmel: for he loved husbandry.
verse	14	26	11	@@Moreover Uzziah had an host of fighting men, that went out to war by bands, according to the number of their account by the hand of Jeiel the scribe and Maaseiah the ruler, under the hand of Hananiah, @9one@7 of the king's captains.
verse	14	26	12	@@The whole number of the chief of the fathers of the mighty men of valour @9were@7 two thousand and six hundred.
verse	14	26	13	@@And under their hand @9was@7 an army, three hundred thousand and seven thousand and five hundred, that made war with mighty power, to help the king against the enemy.
verse	14	26	14	@@And Uzziah prepared for them throughout all the host shields, and spears, and helmets, and habergeons, and bows, and slings @9to cast@7 stones.
verse	14	26	15	And he made in Jerusalem engines, invented by cunning men, to be on the towers and upon the bulwarks, to shoot arrows and great stones withal. And his name spread far abroad; for he was marvellously helped, till he was strong.
verse	14	26	16	@@But when he was strong, his heart was lifted up to @9his@7 destruction: for he transgressed against the LORD his God, and went into the temple of the LORD to burn incense upon the altar of incense.
verse	14	26	17	@@And Azariah the priest went in after him, and with him fourscore priests of the LORD, @9that were@7 valiant men:
verse	14	26	18	@@And they withstood Uzziah the king, and said unto him, @9It appertaineth@7 not unto thee, Uzziah, to burn incense unto the LORD, but to the priests the sons of Aaron, that are consecrated to burn incense: go out of the sanctuary; for thou hast trespassed; neither @9shall it be@7 for thine honour from the LORD God.
verse	14	26	19	@@Then Uzziah was wroth, and @9had@7 a censer in his hand to burn incense: and while he was wroth with the priests, the leprosy even rose up in his forehead before the priests in the house of the LORD, from beside the incense altar.
verse	14	26	20	@@And Azariah the chief priest, and all the priests, looked upon him, and, behold, he @9was@7 leprous in his forehead, and they thrust him out from thence; yea, himself hasted also to go out, because the LORD had smitten him.
verse	14	26	21	@@And Uzziah the king was a leper unto the day of his death, and dwelt in a several house, @9being@7 a leper; for he was cut off from the house of the LORD: and Jotham his son @9was@7 over the king's house, judging the people of the land.
verse	14	26	22	Now the rest of the acts of Uzziah, first and last, did Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, write.
verse	14	26	23	@@So Uzziah slept with his fathers, and they buried him with his fathers in the field of the burial which @9belonged@7 to the kings; for they said, He @9is@7 a leper: and Jotham his son reigned in his stead.
verse	14	27	1	@@Jotham @9was@7 twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. His mother's name also @9was@7 Jerushah, the daughter of Zadok.
verse	14	27	2	@@And he did @9that which was@7 right in the sight of the LORD, according to all that his father Uzziah did: howbeit he entered not into the temple of the LORD. And the people did yet corruptly.
