verse	14	30	4	And the thing pleased the king and all the congregation.
verse	14	30	5	@@So they established a decree to make proclamation throughout all Israel, from Beersheba even to Dan, that they should come to keep the passover unto the LORD God of Israel at Jerusalem: for they had not done @9it@7 of a long @9time in such sort@7 as it was written.
verse	14	30	6	So the posts went with the letters from the king and his princes throughout all Israel and Judah, and according to the commandment of the king, saying, Ye children of Israel, turn again unto the LORD God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, and he will return to the remnant of you, that are escaped out of the hand of the kings of Assyria.
verse	14	30	7	@@And be not ye like your fathers, and like your brethren, which trespassed against the LORD God of their fathers, @9who@7 therefore gave them up to desolation, as ye see.
verse	14	30	8	@@Now be ye not stiffnecked, as your fathers @9were, but@7 yield yourselves unto the LORD, and enter into his sanctuary, which he hath sanctified for ever: and serve the LORD your God, that the fierceness of his wrath may turn away from you.
verse	14	30	9	@@For if ye turn again unto the LORD, your brethren and your children @9shall find@7 compassion before them that lead them captive, so that they shall come again into this land: for the LORD your God @9is@7 gracious and merciful, and will not turn away @9his@7 face from you, if ye return unto him.
