verse	14	32	5	@@Also he strengthened himself, and built up all the wall that was broken, and raised @9it@7 up to the towers, and another wall without, and repaired Millo @9in@7 the city of David, and made darts and shields in abundance.
verse	14	32	6	And he set captains of war over the people, and gathered them together to him in the street of the gate of the city, and spake comfortably to them, saying,
verse	14	32	7	@@Be strong and courageous, be not afraid nor dismayed for the king of Assyria, nor for all the multitude that @9is@7 with him: for @9there be@7 more with us than with him:
verse	14	32	8	@@With him @9is@7 an arm of flesh; but with us @9is@7 the LORD our God to help us, and to fight our battles. And the people rested themselves upon the words of Hezekiah king of Judah.
verse	14	32	9	@@After this did Sennacherib king of Assyria send his servants to Jerusalem, (but he @9himself laid siege@7 against Lachish, and all his power with him,) unto Hezekiah king of Judah, and unto all Judah that @9were@7 at Jerusalem, saying,
verse	14	32	10	Thus saith Sennacherib king of Assyria, Whereon do ye trust, that ye abide in the siege in Jerusalem?
verse	14	32	11	Doth not Hezekiah persuade you to give over yourselves to die by famine and by thirst, saying, The LORD our God shall deliver us out of the hand of the king of Assyria?
verse	14	32	12	Hath not the same Hezekiah taken away his high places and his altars, and commanded Judah and Jerusalem, saying, Ye shall worship before one altar, and burn incense upon it?
verse	14	32	13	@@Know ye not what I and my fathers have done unto all the people of @9other@7 lands? were the gods of the nations of those lands any ways able to deliver their lands out of mine hand?
verse	14	32	14	@@Who @9was there@7 among all the gods of those nations that my fathers utterly destroyed, that could deliver his people out of mine hand, that your God should be able to deliver you out of mine hand?
verse	14	32	15	Now therefore let not Hezekiah deceive you, nor persuade you on this manner, neither yet believe him: for no god of any nation or kingdom was able to deliver his people out of mine hand, and out of the hand of my fathers: how much less shall your God deliver you out of mine hand?
verse	14	32	16	@@And his servants spake yet @9more@7 against the LORD God, and against his servant Hezekiah.
verse	14	32	17	@@He wrote also letters to rail on the LORD God of Israel, and to speak against him, saying, As the gods of the nations of @9other@7 lands have not delivered their people out of mine hand, so shall not the God of Hezekiah deliver his people out of mine hand.
verse	14	32	18	@@Then they cried with a loud voice in the Jews' speech unto the people of Jerusalem that @9were@7 on the wall, to affright them, and to trouble them; that they might take the city.
verse	14	32	19	@@And they spake against the God of Jerusalem, as against the gods of the people of the earth, @9which were@7 the work of the hands of man.
verse	14	32	20	@@And for this @9cause@7 Hezekiah the king, and the prophet Isaiah the son of Amoz, prayed and cried to heaven.
verse	14	32	21	And the LORD sent an angel, which cut off all the mighty men of valour, and the leaders and captains in the camp of the king of Assyria. So he returned with shame of face to his own land. And when he was come into the house of his god, they that came forth of his own bowels slew him there with the sword.
verse	14	32	22	@@Thus the LORD saved Hezekiah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem from the hand of Sennacherib the king of Assyria, and from the hand of all @9other,@7 and guided them on every side.
verse	14	32	23	And many brought gifts unto the LORD to Jerusalem, and presents to Hezekiah king of Judah: so that he was magnified in the sight of all nations from thenceforth.
