verse	14	32	25	@@But Hezekiah rendered not again according to the benefit @9done@7 unto him; for his heart was lifted up: therefore there was wrath upon him, and upon Judah and Jerusalem.
verse	14	32	26	@@Notwithstanding Hezekiah humbled himself for the pride of his heart, @9both@7 he and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so that the wrath of the LORD came not upon them in the days of Hezekiah.
verse	14	32	27	And Hezekiah had exceeding much riches and honour: and he made himself treasuries for silver, and for gold, and for precious stones, and for spices, and for shields, and for all manner of pleasant jewels;
verse	14	32	28	Storehouses also for the increase of corn, and wine, and oil; and stalls for all manner of beasts, and cotes for flocks.
