verse	14	34	2	@@And he did @9that which was@7 right in the sight of the LORD, and walked in the ways of David his father, and declined @9neither@7 to the right hand, nor to the left.
verse	14	34	3	For in the eighth year of his reign, while he was yet young, he began to seek after the God of David his father: and in the twelfth year he began to purge Judah and Jerusalem from the high places, and the groves, and the carved images, and the molten images.
verse	14	34	4	@@And they brake down the altars of Baalim in his presence; and the images, that @9were@7 on high above them, he cut down; and the groves, and the carved images, and the molten images, he brake in pieces, and made dust @9of them,@7 and strowed @9it@7 upon the graves of them that had sacrificed unto them.
verse	14	34	5	And he burnt the bones of the priests upon their altars, and cleansed Judah and Jerusalem.
