verse	15	2	55	The children of Solomon's servants: the children of Sotai, the children of Sophereth, the children of Peruda,
verse	15	2	56	The children of Jaalah, the children of Darkon, the children of Giddel,
verse	15	2	57	The children of Shephatiah, the children of Hattil, the children of Pochereth of Zebaim, the children of Ami.
verse	15	2	58	@@All the Nethinims, and the children of Solomon's servants, @9were@7 three hundred ninety and two.
verse	15	2	59	@@And these @9were@7 they which went up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsa, Cherub, Addan, @9and@7 Immer: but they could not shew their father's house, and their seed, whether they @9were@7 of Israel:
verse	15	2	60	The children of Delaiah, the children of Tobiah, the children of Nekoda, six hundred fifty and two.
verse	15	2	61	And of the children of the priests: the children of Habaiah, the children of Koz, the children of Barzillai; which took a wife of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite, and was called after their name:
verse	15	2	62	@@These sought their register @9among@7 those that were reckoned by genealogy, but they were not found: therefore were they, as polluted, put from the priesthood.
verse	15	2	63	And the Tirshatha said unto them, that they should not eat of the most holy things, till there stood up a priest with Urim and with Thummim.
verse	15	2	64	@@The whole congregation together @9was@7 forty and two thousand three hundred @9and@7 threescore,
verse	15	2	65	@@Beside their servants and their maids, of whom @9there were@7 seven thousand three hundred thirty and seven: and @9there were@7 among them two hundred singing men and singing women.
verse	15	2	66	@@Their horses @9were@7 seven hundred thirty and six; their mules, two hundred forty and five;
verse	15	2	67	@@Their camels, four hundred thirty and five; @9their@7 asses, six thousand seven hundred and twenty.
verse	15	2	68	@@And @9some@7 of the chief of the fathers, when they came to the house of the LORD which @9is@7 at Jerusalem, offered freely for the house of God to set it up in his place:
verse	15	2	69	They gave after their ability unto the treasure of the work threescore and one thousand drams of gold, and five thousand pound of silver, and one hundred priests garments.
verse	15	2	70	@@So the priests, and the Levites, and @9some@7 of the people, and the singers, and the porters, and the Nethinims, dwelt in their cities, and all Israel in their cities.
verse	15	3	1	@@And when the seventh month was come, and the children of Israel @9were@7 in the cities, the people gathered themselves together as one man to Jerusalem.
verse	15	3	2	@@Then stood up Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and his brethren the priests, and Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and his brethren, and builded the altar of the God of Israel, to offer burnt offerings thereon, as @9it is@7 written in the law of Moses the man of God.
verse	15	3	3	@@And they set the altar upon his bases; for fear @9was@7 upon them because of the people of those countries: and they offered burnt offerings thereon unto the LORD, @9even@7 burnt offerings morning and evening.
verse	15	3	4	@@They kept also the feast of tabernacles, as @9it is@7 written, and @9offered@7 the daily burnt offerings by number, according to the custom, as the duty of every day required;
verse	15	3	5	@@And afterward @9offered@7 the continual burnt offering, both of the new moons, and of all the set feasts of the LORD that were consecrated, and of every one that willingly offered a freewill offering unto the LORD.
verse	15	3	6	@@From the first day of the seventh month began they to offer burnt offerings unto the LORD. But the foundation of the temple of the LORD was not @9yet@7 laid.
verse	15	3	7	They gave money also unto the masons, and to the carpenters; and meat, and drink, and oil, unto them of Zidon, and to them of Tyre, to bring cedar trees from Lebanon to the sea of Joppa, according to the grant that they had of Cyrus king of Persia.
verse	15	3	8	Now in the second year of their coming unto the house of God at Jerusalem, in the second month, began Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and the remnant of their brethren the priests and the Levites, and all they that were come out of the captivity unto Jerusalem; and appointed the Levites, from twenty years old and upward, to set forward the work of the house of the LORD.
verse	15	3	9	@@Then stood Jeshua @9with@7 his sons and his brethren, Kadmiel and his sons, the sons of Judah, together, to set forward the workmen in the house of God: the sons of Henadad, @9with@7 their sons and their brethren the Levites.
verse	15	3	10	And when the builders laid the foundation of the temple of the LORD, they set the priests in their apparel with trumpets, and the Levites the sons of Asaph with cymbals, to praise the LORD, after the ordinance of David king of Israel.
verse	15	3	11	@@And they sang together by course in praising and giving thanks unto the LORD; because @9he is@7 good, for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever toward Israel. And all the people shouted with a great shout, when they praised the LORD, because the foundation of the house of the LORD was laid.
verse	15	3	12	@@But many of the priests and Levites and chief of the fathers, @9who were@7 ancient men, that had seen the first house, when the foundation of this house was laid before their eyes, wept with a loud voice; and many shouted aloud for joy:
verse	15	3	13	So that the people could not discern the noise of the shout of joy from the noise of the weeping of the people: for the people shouted with a loud shout, and the noise was heard afar off.
verse	15	4	1	Now when the adversaries of Judah and Benjamin heard that the children of the captivity builded the temple unto the LORD God of Israel;
verse	15	4	2	@@Then they came to Zerubbabel, and to the chief of the fathers, and said unto them, Let us build with you: for we seek your God, as ye @9do;@7 and we do sacrifice unto him since the days of Esar-haddon king of Assur, which brought us up hither.
verse	15	4	3	But Zerubbabel, and Jeshua, and the rest of the chief of the fathers of Israel, said unto them, Ye have nothing to do with us to build an house unto our God; but we ourselves together will build unto the LORD God of Israel, as king Cyrus the king of Persia hath commanded us.
verse	15	4	4	Then the people of the land weakened the hands of the people of Judah, and troubled them in building,
verse	15	4	5	And hired counsellors against them, to frustrate their purpose, all the days of Cyrus king of Persia, even until the reign of Darius king of Persia.
verse	15	4	6	@@And in the reign of Ahasuerus, in the beginning of his reign, wrote they @9unto him@7 an accusation against the inhabitants of Judah and Jerusalem.
verse	15	4	7	@@And in the days of Artaxerxes wrote Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of their companions, unto Artaxerxes king of Persia; and the writing of the letter @9was@7 written in the Syrian tongue, and interpreted in the Syrian tongue.
verse	15	4	8	Rehum the chancellor and Shimshai the scribe wrote a letter against Jerusalem to Artaxerxes the king in this sort:
verse	15	4	9	@@Then @9wrote@7 Rehum the chancellor, and Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of their companions; the Dinaites, the Apharsathchites, the Tarpelites, the Apharsites, the Archevites, the Babylonians, the Susanchites, the Dehavites, @9and@7 the Elamites,
verse	15	4	10	@@And the rest of the nations whom the great and noble Asnapper brought over, and set in the cities of Samaria, and the rest @9that are@7 on this side the river, and at such a time.
verse	15	4	11	@@This @9is@7 the copy of the letter that they sent unto him, @9even@7 unto Artaxerxes the king; Thy servants the men on this side the river, and at such a time.
verse	15	4	12	@@Be it known unto the king, that the Jews which came up from thee to us are come unto Jerusalem, building the rebellious and the bad city, and have set up the walls @9thereof,@7 and joined the foundations.
verse	15	4	13	@@Be it known now unto the king, that, if this city be builded, and the walls set up @9again, then@7 will they not pay toll, tribute, and custom, and @9so@7 thou shalt endamage the revenue of the kings.
verse	15	4	14	@@Now because we have maintenance from @9the king's@7 palace, and it was not meet for us to see the king's dishonour, therefore have we sent and certified the king;
verse	15	4	15	@@That search may be made in the book of the records of thy fathers: so shalt thou find in the book of the records, and know that this city @9is@7 a rebellious city, and hurtful unto kings and provinces, and that they have moved sedition within the same of old time: for which cause was this city destroyed.
verse	15	4	16	@@We certify the king that, if this city be builded @9again,@7 and the walls thereof set up, by this means thou shalt have no portion on this side the river.
verse	15	4	17	@@@9Then@7 sent the king an answer unto Rehum the chancellor, and @9to@7 Shimshai the scribe, and @9to@7 the rest of their companions that dwell in Samaria, and @9unto@7 the rest beyond the river, Peace, and at such a time.
verse	15	4	18	The letter which ye sent unto us hath been plainly read before me.
verse	15	4	19	@@And I commanded, and search hath been made, and it is found that this city of old time hath made insurrection against kings, and @9that@7 rebellion and sedition have been made therein.
verse	15	4	20	@@There have been mighty kings also over Jerusalem, which have ruled over all @9countries@7 beyond the river; and toll, tribute, and custom, was paid unto them.
verse	15	4	21	@@Give ye now commandment to cause these men to cease, and that this city be not builded, until @9another@7 commandment shall be given from me.
verse	15	4	22	Take heed now that ye fail not to do this: why should damage grow to the hurt of the kings?
verse	15	4	23	@@Now when the copy of king Artaxerxes' letter @9was@7 read before Rehum, and Shimshai the scribe, and their companions, they went up in haste to Jerusalem unto the Jews, and made them to cease by force and power.
verse	15	4	24	@@Then ceased the work of the house of God which @9is@7 at Jerusalem. So it ceased unto the second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia.
verse	15	5	1	@@Then the prophets, Haggai the prophet, and Zechariah the son of Iddo, prophesied unto the Jews that @9were@7 in Judah and Jerusalem in the name of the God of Israel, @9even@7 unto them.
verse	15	5	2	@@Then rose up Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and began to build the house of God which @9is@7 at Jerusalem: and with them @9were@7 the prophets of God helping them.
verse	15	5	3	At the same time came to them Tatnai, governor on this side the river, and Shethar-boznai, and their companions, and said thus unto them, Who hath commanded you to build this house, and to make up this wall?
verse	15	5	4	Then said we unto them after this manner, What are the names of the men that make this building?
verse	15	5	5	@@But the eye of their God was upon the elders of the Jews, that they could not cause them to cease, till the matter came to Darius: and then they returned answer by letter concerning this @9matter.@7
verse	15	5	6	@@The copy of the letter that Tatnai, governor on this side the river, and Shethar-boznai, and his companions the Apharsachites, which @9were@7 on this side the river, sent unto Darius the king:
verse	15	5	7	They sent a letter unto him, wherein was written thus; Unto Darius the king, all peace.
verse	15	5	8	Be it known unto the king, that we went into the province of Judea, to the house of the great God, which is builded with great stones, and timber is laid in the walls, and this work goeth fast on, and prospereth in their hands.
verse	15	5	9	@@Then asked we those elders, @9and@7 said unto them thus, Who commanded you to build this house, and to make up these walls?
verse	15	5	10	@@We asked their names also, to certify thee, that we might write the names of the men that @9were@7 the chief of them.
verse	15	5	11	And thus they returned us answer, saying, We are the servants of the God of heaven and earth, and build the house that was builded these many years ago, which a great king of Israel builded and set up.
verse	15	5	12	But after that our fathers had provoked the God of heaven unto wrath, he gave them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, the Chaldean, who destroyed this house, and carried the people away into Babylon.
verse	15	5	13	@@But in the first year of Cyrus the king of Babylon @9the same@7 king Cyrus made a decree to build this house of God.
verse	15	5	14	@@And the vessels also of gold and silver of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took out of the temple that @9was@7 in Jerusalem, and brought them into the temple of Babylon, those did Cyrus the king take out of the temple of Babylon, and they were delivered unto @9one,@7 whose name @9was@7 Sheshbazzar, whom he had made governor;
verse	15	5	15	@@And said unto him, Take these vessels, go, carry them into the temple that @9is@7 in Jerusalem, and let the house of God be builded in his place.
verse	15	5	16	@@Then came the same Sheshbazzar, @9and@7 laid the foundation of the house of God which @9is@7 in Jerusalem: and since that time even until now hath it been in building, and @9yet@7 it is not finished.
verse	15	5	17	@@Now therefore, if @9it seem@7 good to the king, let there be search made in the king's treasure house, which @9is@7 there at Babylon, whether it be @9so,@7 that a decree was made of Cyrus the king to build this house of God at Jerusalem, and let the king send his pleasure to us concerning this matter.
verse	15	6	1	Then Darius the king made a decree, and search was made in the house of the rolls, where the treasures were laid up in Babylon.
verse	15	6	2	@@And there was found at Achmetha, in the palace that is in the province of the Medes, a roll, and therein @9was@7 a record thus written:
verse	15	6	3	@@In the first year of Cyrus the king @9the same@7 Cyrus the king made a decree @9concerning@7 the house of God at Jerusalem, Let the house be builded, the place where they offered sacrifices, and let the foundations thereof be strongly laid; the height thereof threescore cubits, @9and@7 the breadth thereof threescore cubits;
verse	15	6	4	@@@9With@7 three rows of great stones, and a row of new timber: and let the expences be given out of the king's house:
verse	15	6	5	@@And also let the golden and silver vessels of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took forth out of the temple which is at Jerusalem, and brought unto Babylon, be restored, and brought again unto the temple which is at Jerusalem, @9every one@7 to his place, and place @9them@7 in the house of God.
verse	15	6	6	@@Now @9therefore,@7 Tatnai, governor beyond the river, Shethar-boznai, and your companions the Apharsachites, which @9are@7 beyond the river, be ye far from thence:
verse	15	6	7	Let the work of this house of God alone; let the governor of the Jews and the elders of the Jews build this house of God in his place.
verse	15	6	8	@@Moreover I make a decree what ye shall do to the elders of these Jews for the building of this house of God: that of the king's goods, @9even@7 of the tribute beyond the river, forthwith expences be given unto these men, that they be not hindered.
verse	15	6	9	@@And that which they have need of, both young bullocks, and rams, and lambs, for the burnt offerings of the God of heaven, wheat, salt, wine, and oil, according to the appointment of the priests which @9are@7 at Jerusalem, let it be given them day by day without fail:
verse	15	6	10	That they may offer sacrifices of sweet savours unto the God of heaven, and pray for the life of the king, and of his sons.
verse	15	6	11	Also I have made a decree, that whosoever shall alter this word, let timber be pulled down from his house, and being set up, let him be hanged thereon; and let his house be made a dunghill for this.
verse	15	6	12	@@And the God that hath caused his name to dwell there destroy all kings and people, that shall put to their hand to alter @9and@7 to destroy this house of God which is at Jerusalem. I Darius have made a decree; let it be done with speed.
verse	15	6	13	Then Tatnai, governor on this side the river, Shethar-boznai, and their companions, according to that which Darius the king had sent, so they did speedily.
verse	15	6	14	@@And the elders of the Jews builded, and they prospered through the prophesying of Haggai the prophet and Zechariah the son of Iddo. And they builded, and finished @9it,@7 according to the commandment of the God of Israel, and according to the commandment of Cyrus, and Darius, and Artaxerxes king of Persia.
verse	15	6	15	And this house was finished on the third day of the month Adar, which was in the sixth year of the reign of Darius the king.
verse	15	6	16	And the children of Israel, the priests, and the Levites, and the rest of the children of the captivity, kept the dedication of this house of God with joy,
verse	15	6	17	And offered at the dedication of this house of God an hundred bullocks, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs; and for a sin offering for all Israel, twelve he goats, according to the number of the tribes of Israel.
verse	15	6	18	@@And they set the priests in their divisions, and the Levites in their courses, for the service of God, which @9is@7 at Jerusalem; as it is written in the book of Moses.
verse	15	6	19	@@And the children of the captivity kept the passover upon the fourteenth @9day@7 of the first month.
verse	15	6	20	@@For the priests and the Levites were purified together, all of them @9were@7 pure, and killed the passover for all the children of the captivity, and for their brethren the priests, and for themselves.
verse	15	6	21	And the children of Israel, which were come again out of captivity, and all such as had separated themselves unto them from the filthiness of the heathen of the land, to seek the LORD God of Israel, did eat,
verse	15	6	22	And kept the feast of unleavened bread seven days with joy: for the LORD had made them joyful, and turned the heart of the king of Assyria unto them, to strengthen their hands in the work of the house of God, the God of Israel.
verse	15	7	1	Now after these things, in the reign of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Ezra the son of Seraiah, the son of Azariah, the son of Hilkiah,
verse	15	7	2	The son of Shallum, the son of Zadok, the son of Ahitub,
verse	15	7	3	The son of Amariah, the son of Azariah, the son of Meraioth,
verse	15	7	4	The son of Zerahiah, the son of Uzzi, the son of Bukki,
verse	15	7	5	The son of Abishua, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the chief priest:
verse	15	7	6	@@This Ezra went up from Babylon; and he @9was@7 a ready scribe in the law of Moses, which the LORD God of Israel had given: and the king granted him all his request, according to the hand of the LORD his God upon him.
verse	15	7	7	@@And there went up @9some@7 of the children of Israel, and of the priests, and the Levites, and the singers, and the porters, and the Nethinims, unto Jerusalem, in the seventh year of Artaxerxes the king.
verse	15	7	8	@@And he came to Jerusalem in the fifth month, which @9was@7 in the seventh year of the king.
verse	15	7	9	@@For upon the first @9day@7 of the first month began he to go up from Babylon, and on the first @9day@7 of the fifth month came he to Jerusalem, according to the good hand of his God upon him.
verse	15	7	10	@@For Ezra had prepared his heart to seek the law of the LORD, and to do @9it,@7 and to teach in Israel statutes and judgments.
verse	15	7	11	@@Now this @9is@7 the copy of the letter that the king Artaxerxes gave unto Ezra the priest, the scribe, @9even@7 a scribe of the words of the commandments of the LORD, and of his statutes to Israel.
verse	15	7	12	@@Artaxerxes, king of kings, unto Ezra the priest, a scribe of the law of the God of heaven, perfect @9peace,@7 and at such a time.
verse	15	7	13	@@I make a decree, that all they of the people of Israel, and @9of@7 his priests and Levites, in my realm, which are minded of their own freewill to go up to Jerusalem, go with thee.
verse	15	7	14	@@Forasmuch as thou art sent of the king, and of his seven counsellors, to enquire concerning Judah and Jerusalem, according to the law of thy God which @9is@7 in thine hand;
verse	15	7	15	@@And to carry the silver and gold, which the king and his counsellors have freely offered unto the God of Israel, whose habitation @9is@7 in Jerusalem,
verse	15	7	16	@@And all the silver and gold that thou canst find in all the province of Babylon, with the freewill offering of the people, and of the priests, offering willingly for the house of their God which @9is@7 in Jerusalem:
verse	15	7	17	@@That thou mayest buy speedily with this money bullocks, rams, lambs, with their meat offerings and their drink offerings, and offer them upon the altar of the house of your God which @9is@7 in Jerusalem.
verse	15	7	18	And whatsoever shall seem good to thee, and to thy brethren, to do with the rest of the silver and the gold, that do after the will of your God.
verse	15	7	19	@@The vessels also that are given thee for the service of the house of thy God, @9those@7 deliver thou before the God of Jerusalem.
verse	15	7	20	@@And whatsoever more shall be needful for the house of thy God, which thou shalt have occasion to bestow, bestow @9it@7 out of the king's treasure house.
verse	15	7	21	@@And I, @9even@7 I Artaxerxes the king, do make a decree to all the treasurers which @9are@7 beyond the river, that whatsoever Ezra the priest, the scribe of the law of the God of heaven, shall require of you, it be done speedily,
verse	15	7	22	@@Unto an hundred talents of silver, and to an hundred measures of wheat, and to an hundred baths of wine, and to an hundred baths of oil, and salt without prescribing @9how much. @7
verse	15	7	23	Whatsoever is commanded by the God of heaven, let it be diligently done for the house of the God of heaven: for why should there be wrath against the realm of the king and his sons?
verse	15	7	24	Also we certify you, that touching any of the priests and Levites, singers, porters, Nethinims, or ministers of this house of God, it shall not be lawful to impose toll, tribute, or custom, upon them.
verse	15	7	25	@@And thou, Ezra, after the wisdom of thy God, that @9is@7 in thine hand, set magistrates and judges, which may judge all the people that @9are@7 beyond the river, all such as know the laws of thy God; and teach ye them that know @9them@7 not.
verse	15	7	26	@@And whosoever will not do the law of thy God, and the law of the king, let judgment be executed speedily upon him, whether @9it be@7 unto death, or to banishment, or to confiscation of goods, or to imprisonment.
verse	15	7	27	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD God of our fathers, which hath put @9such a thing@7 as this in the king's heart, to beautify the house of the LORD which @9is@7 in Jerusalem:
verse	15	7	28	@@And hath extended mercy unto me before the king, and his counsellors, and before all the king's mighty princes. And I was strengthened as the hand of the LORD my God @9was@7 upon me, and I gathered together out of Israel chief men to go up with me.
verse	15	8	1	@@These @9are@7 now the chief of their fathers, and @9this is@7 the genealogy of them that went up with me from Babylon, in the reign of Artaxerxes the king.
verse	15	8	2	Of the sons of Phinehas; Gershom: of the sons of Ithamar; Daniel: of the sons of David; Hattush.
verse	15	8	3	Of the sons of Shechaniah, of the sons of Pharosh; Zechariah: and with him were reckoned by genealogy of the males an hundred and fifty.
verse	15	8	4	Of the sons of Pahath-moab; Elihoenai the son of Zerahiah, and with him two hundred males.
verse	15	8	5	Of the sons of Shechaniah; the son of Jahaziel, and with him three hundred males.
verse	15	8	6	Of the sons also of Adin; Ebed the son of Jonathan, and with him fifty males.
verse	15	8	7	And of the sons of Elam; Jeshaiah the son of Athaliah, and with him seventy males.
verse	15	8	8	And of the sons of Shephatiah; Zebadiah the son of Michael, and with him fourscore males.
verse	15	8	9	Of the sons of Joab; Obadiah the son of Jehiel, and with him two hundred and eighteen males.
verse	15	8	10	And of the sons of Shelomith; the son of Josiphiah, and with him an hundred and threescore males.
verse	15	8	11	And of the sons of Bebai; Zechariah the son of Bebai, and with him twenty and eight males.
verse	15	8	12	And of the sons of Azgad; Johanan the son of Hakkatan, and with him an hundred and ten males.
verse	15	8	13	@@And of the last sons of Adonikam, whose names @9are@7 these, Eliphelet, Jeiel, and Shemaiah, and with them threescore males.
verse	15	8	14	Of the sons also of Bigvai; Uthai, and Zabbud, and with them seventy males.
verse	15	8	15	And I gathered them together to the river that runneth to Ahava; and there abode we in tents three days: and I viewed the people, and the priests, and found there none of the sons of Levi.
verse	15	8	16	Then sent I for Eliezer, for Ariel, for Shemaiah, and for Elnathan, and for Jarib, and for Elnathan, and for Nathan, and for Zechariah, and for Meshullam, chief men; also for Joiarib, and for Elnathan, men of understanding.
verse	15	8	17	@@And I sent them with commandment unto Iddo the chief at the place Casiphia, and I told them what they should say unto Iddo, @9and@7 to his brethren the Nethinims, at the place Casiphia, that they should bring unto us ministers for the house of our God.
verse	15	8	18	And by the good hand of our God upon us they brought us a man of understanding, of the sons of Mahli, the son of Levi, the son of Israel; and Sherebiah, with his sons and his brethren, eighteen;
verse	15	8	19	And Hashabiah, and with him Jeshaiah of the sons of Merari, his brethren and their sons, twenty;
verse	15	8	20	Also of the Nethinims, whom David and the princes had appointed for the service of the Levites, two hundred and twenty Nethinims: all of them were expressed by name.
verse	15	8	21	Then I proclaimed a fast there, at the river of Ahava, that we might afflict ourselves before our God, to seek of him a right way for us, and for our little ones, and for all our substance.
verse	15	8	22	@@For I was ashamed to require of the king a band of soldiers and horsemen to help us against the enemy in the way: because we had spoken unto the king, saying, The hand of our God @9is@7 upon all them for good that seek him; but his power and his wrath @9is@7 against all them that forsake him.
verse	15	8	23	So we fasted and besought our God for this: and he was intreated of us.
verse	15	8	24	Then I separated twelve of the chief of the priests, Sherebiah, Hashabiah, and ten of their brethren with them,
verse	15	8	25	@@And weighed unto them the silver, and the gold, and the vessels, @9even@7 the offering of the house of our God, which the king, and his counsellors, and his lords, and all Israel @9there@7 present, had offered:
verse	15	8	26	@@I even weighed unto their hand six hundred and fifty talents of silver, and silver vessels an hundred talents, @9and@7 of gold an hundred talents;
verse	15	8	27	Also twenty basons of gold, of a thousand drams; and two vessels of fine copper, precious as gold.
verse	15	8	28	@@And I said unto them, Ye @9are@7 holy unto the LORD; the vessels @9are@7 holy also; and the silver and the gold @9are@7 a freewill offering unto the LORD God of your fathers.
verse	15	8	29	@@Watch ye, and keep @9them,@7 until ye weigh @9them@7 before the chief of the priests and the Levites, and chief of the fathers of Israel, at Jerusalem, in the chambers of the house of the LORD.
verse	15	8	30	@@So took the priests and the Levites the weight of the silver, and the gold, and the vessels, to bring @9them@7 to Jerusalem unto the house of our God.
verse	15	8	31	@@Then we departed from the river of Ahava on the twelfth @9day@7 of the first month, to go unto Jerusalem: and the hand of our God was upon us, and he delivered us from the hand of the enemy, and of such as lay in wait by the way.
verse	15	8	32	And we came to Jerusalem, and abode there three days.
verse	15	8	33	@@Now on the fourth day was the silver and the gold and the vessels weighed in the house of our God by the hand of Meremoth the son of Uriah the priest; and with him @9was@7 Eleazar the son of Phinehas; and with them @9was@7 Jozabad the son of Jeshua, and Noadiah the son of Binnui, Levites;
verse	15	8	34	@@By number @9and@7 by weight of every one: and all the weight was written at that time.
verse	15	8	35	@@@9Also@7 the children of those that had been carried away, which were come out of the captivity, offered burnt offerings unto the God of Israel, twelve bullocks for all Israel, ninety and six rams, seventy and seven lambs, twelve he goats @9for@7 a sin offering: all @9this was@7 a burnt offering unto the LORD.
verse	15	8	36	And they delivered the king's commissions unto the king's lieutenants, and to the governors on this side the river: and they furthered the people, and the house of God.
verse	15	9	1	@@Now when these things were done, the princes came to me, saying, The people of Israel, and the priests, and the Levites, have not separated themselves from the people of the lands, @9doing@7 according to their abominations, @9even@7 of the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Perizzites, the Jebusites, the Ammonites, the Moabites, the Egyptians, and the Amorites.
verse	15	9	2	@@For they have taken of their daughters for themselves, and for their sons: so that the holy seed have mingled themselves with the people of @9those@7 lands: yea, the hand of the princes and rulers hath been chief in this trespass.
verse	15	9	3	And when I heard this thing, I rent my garment and my mantle, and plucked off the hair of my head and of my beard, and sat down astonied.
verse	15	9	4	Then were assembled unto me every one that trembled at the words of the God of Israel, because of the transgression of those that had been carried away; and I sat astonied until the evening sacrifice.
verse	15	9	5	And at the evening sacrifice I arose up from my heaviness; and having rent my garment and my mantle, I fell upon my knees, and spread out my hands unto the LORD my God.
verse	15	9	6	@@And said, O my God, I am ashamed and blush to lift up my face to thee, my God: for our iniquities are increased over @9our@7 head, and our trespass is grown up unto the heavens.
verse	15	9	7	@@Since the days of our fathers @9have@7 we @9been@7 in a great trespass unto this day; and for our iniquities have we, our kings, and @9our@7 priests, been delivered into the hand of the kings of the lands, to the sword, to captivity, and to a spoil, and to confusion of face, as @9it is@7 this day.
verse	15	9	8	@@And now for a little space grace hath been @9shewed@7 from the LORD our God, to leave us a remnant to escape, and to give us a nail in his holy place, that our God may lighten our eyes, and give us a little reviving in our bondage.
verse	15	9	9	@@For we @9were@7 bondmen; yet our God hath not forsaken us in our bondage, but hath extended mercy unto us in the sight of the kings of Persia, to give us a reviving, to set up the house of our God, and to repair the desolations thereof, and to give us a wall in Judah and in Jerusalem.
verse	15	9	10	And now, O our God, what shall we say after this? for we have forsaken thy commandments,
verse	15	9	11	Which thou hast commanded by thy servants the prophets, saying, The land, unto which ye go to possess it, is an unclean land with the filthiness of the people of the lands, with their abominations, which have filled it from one end to another with their uncleanness.
verse	15	9	12	@@Now therefore give not your daughters unto their sons, neither take their daughters unto your sons, nor seek their peace or their wealth for ever: that ye may be strong, and eat the good of the land, and leave @9it@7 for an inheritance to your children for ever.
verse	15	9	13	@@And after all that is come upon us for our evil deeds, and for our great trespass, seeing that thou our God hast punished us less than our iniquities @9deserve,@7 and hast given us @9such@7 deliverance as this;
verse	15	9	14	@@Should we again break thy commandments, and join in affinity with the people of these abominations? wouldest not thou be angry with us till thou hadst consumed @9us,@7 so that @9there should be@7 no remnant nor escaping?
verse	15	9	15	@@O LORD God of Israel, thou @9art@7 righteous: for we remain yet escaped, as @9it is@7 this day: behold, we @9are@7 before thee in our trespasses: for we cannot stand before thee because of this.
verse	15	10	1	Now when Ezra had prayed, and when he had confessed, weeping and casting himself down before the house of God, there assembled unto him out of Israel a very great congregation of men and women and children: for the people wept very sore.
verse	15	10	2	@@And Shechaniah the son of Jehiel, @9one@7 of the sons of Elam, answered and said unto Ezra, We have trespassed against our God, and have taken strange wives of the people of the land: yet now there is hope in Israel concerning this thing.
verse	15	10	3	Now therefore let us make a covenant with our God to put away all the wives, and such as are born of them, according to the counsel of my lord, and of those that tremble at the commandment of our God; and let it be done according to the law.
verse	15	10	4	@@Arise; for @9this@7 matter @9belongeth@7 unto thee: we also @9will be@7 with thee: be of good courage, and do @9it. @7
verse	15	10	5	Then arose Ezra, and made the chief priests, the Levites, and all Israel, to swear that they should do according to this word. And they sware.
verse	15	10	6	@@Then Ezra rose up from before the house of God, and went into the chamber of Johanan the son of Eliashib: and @9when@7 he came thither, he did eat no bread, nor drink water: for he mourned because of the transgression of them that had been carried away.
verse	15	10	7	And they made proclamation throughout Judah and Jerusalem unto all the children of the captivity, that they should gather themselves together unto Jerusalem;
verse	15	10	8	And that whosoever would not come within three days, according to the counsel of the princes and the elders, all his substance should be forfeited, and himself separated from the congregation of those that had been carried away.
verse	15	10	9	@@Then all the men of Judah and Benjamin gathered themselves together unto Jerusalem within three days. It @9was@7 the ninth month, on the twentieth @9day@7 of the month; and all the people sat in the street of the house of God, trembling because of @9this@7 matter, and for the great rain.
verse	15	10	10	And Ezra the priest stood up, and said unto them, Ye have transgressed, and have taken strange wives, to increase the trespass of Israel.
verse	15	10	11	Now therefore make confession unto the LORD God of your fathers, and do his pleasure: and separate yourselves from the people of the land, and from the strange wives.
verse	15	10	12	Then all the congregation answered and said with a loud voice, As thou hast said, so must we do.
verse	15	10	13	@@But the people @9are@7 many, and @9it is@7 a time of much rain, and we are not able to stand without, neither @9is this@7 a work of one day or two: for we are many that have transgressed in this thing.
verse	15	10	14	Let now our rulers of all the congregation stand, and let all them which have taken strange wives in our cities come at appointed times, and with them the elders of every city, and the judges thereof, until the fierce wrath of our God for this matter be turned from us.
verse	15	10	15	@@Only Jonathan the son of Asahel and Jahaziah the son of Tikvah were employed about this @9matter:@7 and Meshullam and Shabbethai the Levite helped them.
verse	15	10	16	@@And the children of the captivity did so. And Ezra the priest, @9with@7 certain chief of the fathers, after the house of their fathers, and all of them by @9their@7 names, were separated, and sat down in the first day of the tenth month to examine the matter.
verse	15	10	17	And they made an end with all the men that had taken strange wives by the first day of the first month.
verse	15	10	18	@@And among the sons of the priests there were found that had taken strange wives: @9namely,@7 of the sons of Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and his brethren; Maaseiah, and Eliezer, and Jarib, and Gedaliah.
verse	15	10	19	@@And they gave their hands that they would put away their wives; and @9being@7 guilty, @9they offered@7 a ram of the flock for their trespass.
verse	15	10	20	And of the sons of Immer; Hanani, and Zebadiah.
verse	15	10	21	And of the sons of Harim; Maaseiah, and Elijah, and Shemaiah, and Jehiel, and Uzziah.
verse	15	10	22	And of the sons of Pashur; Elioenai, Maaseiah, Ishmael, Nethaneel, Jozabad, and Elasah.
verse	15	10	23	@@Also of the Levites; Jozabad, and Shimei, and Kelaiah, (the same @9is@7 Kelita,) Pethahiah, Judah, and Eliezer.
verse	15	10	24	Of the singers also; Eliashib: and of the porters; Shallum, and Telem, and Uri.
verse	15	10	25	Moreover of Israel: of the sons of Parosh; Ramiah, and Jeziah, and Malchiah, and Miamin, and Eleazar, and Malchijah, and Benaiah.
verse	15	10	26	And of the sons of Elam; Mattaniah, Zechariah, and Jehiel, and Abdi, and Jeremoth, and Eliah.
verse	15	10	27	And of the sons of Zattu; Elioenai, Eliashib, Mattaniah, and Jeremoth, and Zabad, and Aziza.
verse	15	10	28	@@Of the sons also of Bebai; Jehohanan, Hananiah, Zabbai, @9and@7 Athlai.
verse	15	10	29	And of the sons of Bani; Meshullam, Malluch, and Adaiah, Jashub, and Sheal, and Ramoth.
verse	15	10	30	And of the sons of Pahath-moab; Adna, and Chelal, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattaniah, Bezaleel, and Binnui, and Manasseh.
verse	15	10	31	@@And @9of@7 the sons of Harim; Eliezer, Ishijah, Malchiah, Shemaiah, Shimeon,
verse	15	10	32	@@Benjamin, Malluch, @9and@7 Shemariah.
verse	15	10	33	@@Of the sons of Hashum; Mattenai, Mattathah, Zabad, Eliphelet, Jeremai, Manasseh, @9and@7 Shimei.
verse	15	10	34	Of the sons of Bani; Maadai, Amram, and Uel,
verse	15	10	35	Benaiah, Bedeiah, Chelluh,
verse	15	10	36	Vaniah, Meremoth, Eliashib,
verse	15	10	37	Mattaniah, Mattenai, and Jaasau,
verse	15	10	38	And Bani, and Binnui, Shimei,
verse	15	10	39	And Shelemiah, and Nathan, and Adaiah,
verse	15	10	40	Machnadebai, Shashai, Sharai,
verse	15	10	41	PrAzareel, and Shelemiah, Shemariah,
verse	15	10	42	@@Shallum, Amariah, @9and@7 Joseph.
verse	15	10	43	Of the sons of Nebo; Jeiel, Mattithiah, Zabad, Zebina, Jadau, and Joel, Benaiah.
verse	15	10	44	@@All these had taken strange wives: and @9some@7 of them had wives by whom they had children.
verse	16	1	1	The words of Nehemiah the son of Hachaliah. And it came to pass in the month Chisleu, in the twentieth year, as I was in Shushan the palace,
verse	16	1	2	@@That Hanani, one of my brethren, came, he and @9certain@7 men of Judah; and I asked them concerning the Jews that had escaped, which were left of the captivity, and concerning Jerusalem.
verse	16	1	3	@@And they said unto me, The remnant that are left of the captivity there in the province @9are@7 in great affliction and reproach: the wall of Jerusalem also @9is@7 broken down, and the gates thereof are burned with fire.
verse	16	1	4	@@And it came to pass, when I heard these words, that I sat down and wept, and mourned @9certain@7 days, and fasted, and prayed before the God of heaven,
verse	16	1	5	And said, I beseech thee, O LORD God of heaven, the great and terrible God, that keepeth covenant and mercy for them that love him and observe his commandments:
verse	16	1	6	Let thine ear now be attentive, and thine eyes open, that thou mayest hear the prayer of thy servant, which I pray before thee now, day and night, for the children of Israel thy servants, and confess the sins of the children of Israel, which we have sinned against thee: both I and my father's house have sinned.
verse	16	1	7	We have dealt very corruptly against thee, and have not kept the commandments, nor the statutes, nor the judgments, which thou commandedst thy servant Moses.
verse	16	1	8	@@Remember, I beseech thee, the word that thou commandedst thy servant Moses, saying, @9If@7 ye transgress, I will scatter you abroad among the nations:
verse	16	1	9	@@But @9if@7 ye turn unto me, and keep my commandments, and do them; though there were of you cast out unto the uttermost part of the heaven, @9yet@7 will I gather them from thence, and will bring them unto the place that I have chosen to set my name there.
verse	16	1	10	@@Now these @9are@7 thy servants and thy people, whom thou hast redeemed by thy great power, and by thy strong hand.
verse	16	1	11	O Lord, I beseech thee, let now thine ear be attentive to the prayer of thy servant, and to the prayer of thy servants, who desire to fear thy name: and prosper, I pray thee, thy servant this day, and grant him mercy in the sight of this man. For I was the king's cupbearer.
verse	16	2	1	@@And it came to pass in the month Nisan, in the twentieth year of Artaxerxes the king, @9that@7 wine @9was@7 before him: and I took up the wine, and gave @9it@7 unto the king. Now I had not been @9beforetime@7 sad in his presence.
verse	16	2	2	@@Wherefore the king said unto me, Why @9is@7 thy countenance sad, seeing thou @9art@7 not sick? this @9is@7 nothing @9else@7 but sorrow of heart. Then I was very sore afraid,
verse	16	2	3	@@And said unto the king, Let the king live for ever: why should not my countenance be sad, when the city, the place of my fathers' sepulchres, @9lieth@7 waste, and the gates thereof are consumed with fire?
verse	16	2	4	Then the king said unto me, For what dost thou make request? So I prayed to the God of heaven.
verse	16	2	5	And I said unto the king, If it please the king, and if thy servant have found favour in thy sight, that thou wouldest send me unto Judah, unto the city of my fathers' sepulchres, that I may build it.
verse	16	2	6	And the king said unto me, (the queen also sitting by him,) For how long shall thy journey be? and when wilt thou return? So it pleased the king to send me; and I set him a time.
verse	16	2	7	Moreover I said unto the king, If it please the king, let letters be given me to the governors beyond the river, that they may convey me over till I come into Judah;
verse	16	2	8	@@And a letter unto Asaph the keeper of the king's forest, that he may give me timber to make beams for the gates of the palace which @9appertained@7 to the house, and for the wall of the city, and for the house that I shall enter into. And the king granted me, according to the good hand of my God upon me.
verse	16	2	9	Then I came to the governors beyond the river, and gave them the king's letters. Now the king had sent captains of the army and horsemen with me.
verse	16	2	10	@@When Sanballat the Horonite, and Tobiah the servant, the Ammonite, heard @9of it,@7 it grieved them exceedingly that there was come a man to seek the welfare of the children of Israel.
verse	16	2	11	So I came to Jerusalem, and was there three days.
verse	16	2	12	@@And I arose in the night, I and some few men with me; neither told I @9any@7 man what my God had put in my heart to do at Jerusalem: neither @9was there any@7 beast with me, save the beast that I rode upon.
verse	16	2	13	And I went out by night by the gate of the valley, even before the dragon well, and to the dung port, and viewed the walls of Jerusalem, which were broken down, and the gates thereof were consumed with fire.
verse	16	2	14	@@Then I went on to the gate of the fountain, and to the king's pool: but @9there was@7 no place for the beast @9that was@7 under me to pass.
verse	16	2	15	@@Then went I up in the night by the brook, and viewed the wall, and turned back, and entered by the gate of the valley, and @9so@7 returned.
verse	16	2	16	@@And the rulers knew not whither I went, or what I did; neither had I as yet told @9it@7 to the Jews, nor to the priests, nor to the nobles, nor to the rulers, nor to the rest that did the work.
verse	16	2	17	@@Then said I unto them, Ye see the distress that we @9are@7 in, how Jerusalem @9lieth@7 waste, and the gates thereof are burned with fire: come, and let us build up the wall of Jerusalem, that we be no more a reproach.
verse	16	2	18	@@Then I told them of the hand of my God which was good upon me; as also the king's words that he had spoken unto me. And they said, Let us rise up and build. So they strengthened their hands for @9this@7 good @9work. @7
verse	16	2	19	@@But when Sanballat the Horonite, and Tobiah the servant, the Ammonite, and Geshem the Arabian, heard @9it,@7 they laughed us to scorn, and despised us, and said, What @9is@7 this thing that ye do? will ye rebel against the king?
verse	16	2	20	Then answered I them, and said unto them, The God of heaven, he will prosper us; therefore we his servants will arise and build: but ye have no portion, nor right, nor memorial, in Jerusalem.
verse	16	3	1	Then Eliashib the high priest rose up with his brethren the priests, and they builded the sheep gate; they sanctified it, and set up the doors of it; even unto the tower of Meah they sanctified it, unto the tower of Hananeel.
verse	16	3	2	And next unto him builded the men of Jericho. And next to them builded Zaccur the son of Imri.
verse	16	3	3	@@But the fish gate did the sons of Hassenaah build, who @9also@7 laid the beams thereof, and set up the doors thereof, the locks thereof, and the bars thereof.
verse	16	3	4	And next unto them repaired Meremoth the son of Urijah, the son of Koz. And next unto them repaired Meshullam the son of Berechiah, the son of Meshezabeel. And next unto them repaired Zadok the son of Baana.
verse	16	3	5	And next unto them the Tekoites repaired; but their nobles put not their necks to the work of their Lord.
verse	16	3	6	Moreover the old gate repaired Jehoiada the son of Paseah, and Meshullam the son of Besodeiah; they laid the beams thereof, and set up the doors thereof, and the locks thereof, and the bars thereof.
verse	16	3	7	And next unto them repaired Melatiah the Gibeonite, and Jadon the Meronothite, the men of Gibeon, and of Mizpah, unto the throne of the governor on this side the river.
verse	16	3	8	@@Next unto him repaired Uzziel the son of Harhaiah, of the goldsmiths. Next unto him also repaired Hananiah the son of @9one of@7 the apothecaries, and they fortified Jerusalem unto the broad wall.
verse	16	3	9	And next unto them repaired Rephaiah the son of Hur, the ruler of the half part of Jerusalem.
verse	16	3	10	And next unto them repaired Jedaiah the son of Harumaph, even over against his house. And next unto him repaired Hattush the son of Hashabniah.
verse	16	3	11	Malchijah the son of Harim, and Hashub the son of Pahath-moab, repaired the other piece, and the tower of the furnaces.
verse	16	3	12	And next unto him repaired Shallum the son of Halohesh, the ruler of the half part of Jerusalem, he and his daughters.
verse	16	3	13	The valley gate repaired Hanun, and the inhabitants of Zanoah; they built it, and set up the doors thereof, the locks thereof, and the bars thereof, and a thousand cubits on the wall unto the dung gate.
verse	16	3	14	But the dung gate repaired Malchiah the son of Rechab, the ruler of part of Beth-haccerem; he build it, and set up the doors thereof, the locks thereof, and the bars thereof.
verse	16	3	15	But the gate of the fountain repaired Shallun the son of Col-hozeh, the ruler of part of Mizpah; he built it, and covered it, and set up the doors thereof, the locks thereof, and the bars thereof, and the wall of the pool of Siloah by the king's garden, and unto the stairs that go down from the city of David.
verse	16	3	16	@@After him repaired Nehemiah the son of Azbuk, the ruler of the half part of Bethzur, unto @9the place@7 over against the sepulchres of David, and to the pool that was made, and unto the house of the mighty.
verse	16	3	17	After him repaired the Levites, Rehum the son of Bani. Next unto him repaired Hashabiah, the ruler of the half part of Keilah, in his part.
verse	16	3	18	After him repaired their brethren, Bavai the son of Henadad, the ruler of the half part of Keilah.
verse	16	3	19	@@And next to him repaired Ezer the son of Jeshua, the ruler of Mizpah, another piece over against the going up to the armoury at the turning @9of the wall. @7
verse	16	3	20	@@After him Baruch the son of Zabbai earnestly repaired the other piece, from the turning @9of the wall@7 unto the door of the house of Eliashib the high priest.
verse	16	3	21	After him repaired Meremoth the son of Urijah the son of Koz another piece, from the door of the house of Eliashib even to the end of the house of Eliashib.
verse	16	3	22	And after him repaired the priests, the men of the plain.
verse	16	3	23	After him repaired Benjamin and Hashub over against their house. After him repaired Azariah the son of Maaseiah the son of Ananiah by his house.
verse	16	3	24	@@After him repaired Binnui the son of Henadad another piece, from the house of Azariah unto the turning @9of the wall,@7 even unto the corner.
verse	16	3	25	@@Palal the son of Uzai, over against the turning @9of the wall,@7 and the tower which lieth out from the king's high house, that @9was@7 by the court of the prison. After him Pedaiah the son of Parosh.
verse	16	3	26	@@Moreover the Nethinims dwelt in Ophel, unto @9the place@7 over against the water gate toward the east, and the tower that lieth out.
verse	16	3	27	After them the Tekoites repaired another piece, over against the great tower that lieth out, even unto the wall of Ophel.
verse	16	3	28	From above the horse gate repaired the priests, every one over against his house.
verse	16	3	29	After them repaired Zadok the son of Immer over against his house. After him repaired also Shemaiah the son of Shechaniah, the keeper of the east gate.
verse	16	3	30	After him repaired Hananiah the son of Shelemiah, and Hanun the sixth son of Zalaph, another piece. After him repaired Meshullam the son of Berechiah over against his chamber.
verse	16	3	31	After him repaired Malchiah the goldsmith's son unto the place of the Nethinims, and of the merchants, over against the gate Miphkad, and to the going up of the corner.
verse	16	3	32	And between the going up of the corner unto the sheep gate repaired the goldsmiths and the merchants.
verse	16	4	1	But it came to pass, that when Sanballat heard that we builded the wall, he was wroth, and took great indignation, and mocked the Jews.
verse	16	4	2	And he spake before his brethren and the army of Samaria, and said, What do these feeble Jews? will they fortify themselves? will they sacrifice? will they make an end in a day? will they revive the stones out of the heaps of the rubbish which are burned?
verse	16	4	3	@@Now Tobiah the Ammonite @9was@7 by him, and he said, Even that which they build, if a fox go up, he shall even break down their stone wall.
verse	16	4	4	Hear, O our God; for we are despised: and turn their reproach upon their own head, and give them for a prey in the land of captivity:
verse	16	4	5	@@And cover not their iniquity, and let not their sin be blotted out from before thee: for they have provoked @9thee@7 to anger before the builders.
verse	16	4	6	So built we the wall; and all the wall was joined together unto the half thereof: for the people had a mind to work.
verse	16	4	7	@@But it came to pass, @9that@7 when Sanballat, and Tobiah, and the Arabians, and the Ammonites, and the Ashdodites, heard that the walls of Jerusalem were made up, @9and@7 that the breaches began to be stopped, then they were very wroth,
verse	16	4	8	@@And conspired all of them together to come @9and@7 to fight against Jerusalem, and to hinder it.
verse	16	4	9	Nevertheless we made our prayer unto our God, and set a watch against them day and night, because of them.
verse	16	4	10	@@And Judah said, The strength of the bearers of burdens is decayed, and @9there is@7 much rubbish; so that we are not able to build the wall.
verse	16	4	11	And our adversaries said, They shall not know, neither see, till we come in the midst among them, and slay them, and cause the work to cease.
verse	16	4	12	@@And it came to pass, that when the Jews which dwelt by them came, they said unto us ten times, From all places whence ye shall return unto us @9they will be upon you.@7
verse	16	4	13	@@Therefore set I in the lower places behind the wall, @9and@7 on the higher places, I even set the people after their families with their swords, their spears, and their bows.
verse	16	4	14	@@And I looked, and rose up, and said unto the nobles, and to the rulers, and to the rest of the people, Be not ye afraid of them: remember the Lord, @9which is@7 great and terrible, and fight for your brethren, your sons, and your daughters, your wives, and your houses.
verse	16	4	15	And it came to pass, when our enemies heard that it was known unto us, and God had brought their counsel to nought, that we returned all of us to the wall, every one unto his work.
verse	16	4	16	@@And it came to pass from that time forth, @9that@7 the half of my servants wrought in the work, and the other half of them held both the spears, the shields, and the bows, and the habergeons; and the rulers @9were@7 behind all the house of Judah.
verse	16	4	17	@@They which builded on the wall, and they that bare burdens, with those that laded, @9every one@7 with one of his hands wrought in the work, and with the other @9hand@7 held a weapon.
verse	16	4	18	@@For the builders, every one had his sword girded by his side, and @9so@7 builded. And he that sounded the trumpet @9was@7 by me.
verse	16	4	19	@@And I said unto the nobles, and to the rulers, and to the rest of the people, The work @9is@7 great and large, and we are separated upon the wall, one far from another.
verse	16	4	20	@@In what place @9therefore@7 ye hear the sound of the trumpet, resort ye thither unto us: our God shall fight for us.
verse	16	4	21	So we laboured in the work: and half of them held the spears from the rising of the morning till the stars appeared.
verse	16	4	22	Likewise at the same time said I unto the people, Let every one with his servant lodge within Jerusalem, that in the night they may be a guard to us, and labour on the day.
verse	16	4	23	@@So neither I, nor my brethren, nor my servants, nor the men of the guard which followed me, none of us put off our clothes, @9saving that@7 every one put them off for washing.
verse	16	5	1	And there was a great cry of the people and of their wives against their brethren the Jews.
verse	16	5	2	@@For there were that said, We, our sons, and our daughters, @9are@7 many: therefore we take up corn @9for them,@7 that we may eat, and live.
verse	16	5	3	@@@9Some@7 also there were that said, We have mortgaged our lands, vineyards, and houses, that we might buy corn, because of the dearth.
verse	16	5	4	@@There were also that said, We have borrowed money for the king's tribute, @9and that upon@7 our lands and vineyards.
verse	16	5	5	@@Yet now our flesh @9is@7 as the flesh of our brethren, our children as their children: and, lo, we bring into bondage our sons and our daughters to be servants, and @9some@7 of our daughters are brought unto bondage @9already:@7 neither @9is it@7 in our power @9to redeem them;@7 for other men have our lands and vineyards.
verse	16	5	6	And I was very angry when I heard their cry and these words.
verse	16	5	7	Then I consulted with myself, and I rebuked the nobles, and the rulers, and said unto them, Ye exact usury, every one of his brother. And I set a great assembly against them.
verse	16	5	8	@@And I said unto them, We after our ability have redeemed our brethren the Jews, which were sold unto the heathen; and will ye even sell your brethren? or shall they be sold unto us? Then held they their peace, and found nothing @9to answer. @7
verse	16	5	9	@@Also I said, It @9is@7 not good that ye do: ought ye not to walk in the fear of our God because of the reproach of the heathen our enemies?
verse	16	5	10	@@I likewise, @9and@7 my brethren, and my servants, might exact of them money and corn: I pray you, let us leave off this usury.
verse	16	5	11	@@Restore, I pray you, to them, even this day, their lands, their vineyards, their oliveyards, and their houses, also the the hundredth @9part@7 of the money, and of the corn, the wine, and the oil, that ye exact of them.
verse	16	5	12	@@Then said they, We will restore @9them,@7 and will require nothing of them; so will we do as thou sayest. Then I called the priests, and took an oath of them, that they should do according to this promise.
verse	16	5	13	Also I shook my lap, and said, So God shake out every man from his house, and from his labour, that performeth not this promise, even thus be he shaken out, and emptied. And all the congregation said, Amen, and praised the LORD. And the people did according to this promise.
verse	16	5	14	@@Moreover from the time that I was appointed to be their governor in the land of Judah, from the twentieth year even unto the two and thirtieth year of Artaxerxes the king, @9that is,@7 twelve years, I and my brethren have not eaten the bread of the governor.
verse	16	5	15	@@But the former governors that @9had been@7 before me were chargeable unto the people, and had taken of them bread and wine, beside forty shekels of silver; yea, even their servants bare rule over the people: but so did not I, because of the fear of God.
verse	16	5	16	@@Yea, also I continued in the work of this wall, neither bought we any land: and all my servants @9were@7 gathered thither unto the work.
verse	16	5	17	@@Moreover @9there were@7 at my table an hundred and fifty of the Jews and rulers, beside those that came unto us from among the heathen that @9are@7 about us.
verse	16	5	18	@@Now @9that@7 which was prepared @9for me@7 daily @9was@7 one ox @9and@7 six choice sheep; also fowls were prepared for me, and once in ten days store of all sorts of wine: yet for all this required not I the bread of the governor, because the bondage was heavy upon this people.
verse	16	5	19	@@Think upon me, my God, for good, @9according@7 to all that I have done for this people.
verse	16	6	1	@@Now it came to pass, when Sanballat, and Tobiah, and Geshem the Arabian, and the rest of our enemies, heard that I had builded the wall, and @9that@7 there was no breach left therein; (though at that time I had not set up the doors upon the gates;)
verse	16	6	2	@@That Sanballat and Geshem sent unto me, saying, Come, let us meet together in @9some one of@7 the villages in the plain of Ono. But they thought to do me mischief.
verse	16	6	3	@@And I sent messengers unto them, saying, I @9am@7 doing a great work, so that I cannot come down: why should the work cease, whilst I leave it, and come down to you?
verse	16	6	4	Yet they sent unto me four times after this sort; and I answered them after the same manner.
verse	16	6	5	Then sent Sanballat his servant unto me in like manner the fifth time with an open letter in his hand;
verse	16	6	6	@@Wherein @9was@7 written, It is reported among the heathen, and Gashmu saith @9it, that@7 thou and the Jews think to rebel: for which cause thou buildest the wall, that thou mayest be their king, according to these words.
verse	16	6	7	@@And thou hast also appointed prophets to preach of thee at Jerusalem, saying, @9There is@7 a king in Judah: and now shall it be reported to the king according to these words. Come now therefore, and let us take counsel together.
verse	16	6	8	Then I sent unto him, saying, There are no such things done as thou sayest, but thou feignest them out of thine own heart.
verse	16	6	9	@@For they all made us afraid, saying, Their hands shall be weakened from the work, that it be not done. Now therefore, @9O God,@7 strengthen my hands.
verse	16	6	10	@@Afterward I came unto the house of Shemaiah the son of Delaiah the son of Mehetabeel, who @9was@7 shut up; and he said, Let us meet together in the house of God, within the temple, and let us shut the doors of the temple: for they will come to slay thee; yea, in the night will they come to slay thee.
verse	16	6	11	@@And I said, Should such a man as I flee? and who @9is there,@7 that, @9being@7 as I @9am,@7 would go into the temple to save his life? I will not go in.
verse	16	6	12	And, lo, I perceived that God had not sent him; but that he pronounced this prophecy against me: for Tobiah and Sanballat had hired him.
verse	16	6	13	@@Therefore @9was@7 he hired, that I should be afraid, and do so, and sin, and @9that@7 they might have @9matter@7 for an evil report, that they might reproach me.
verse	16	6	14	My God, think thou upon Tobiah and Sanballat according to these their works, and on the prophetess Noadiah, and the rest of the prophets, that would have put me in fear.
verse	16	6	15	@@So the wall was finished in the twenty and fifth @9day@7 of @9the month@7 Elul, in fifty and two days.
verse	16	6	16	@@And it came to pass, that when all our enemies heard @9thereof,@7 and all the heathen that @9were@7 about us saw @9these things,@7 they were much cast down in their own eyes: for they perceived that this work was wrought of our God.
verse	16	6	17	@@Moreover in those days the nobles of Judah sent many letters unto Tobiah, and @9the letters@7 of Tobiah came unto them.
verse	16	6	18	@@For @9there were@7 many in Judah sworn unto him, because he @9was@7 the son in law of Shechaniah the son of Arah; and his son Johanan had taken the daughter of Meshullam the son of Berechiah.
verse	16	6	19	@@Also they reported his good deeds before me, and uttered my words to him. @9And@7 Tobiah sent letters to put me in fear.
verse	16	7	1	Now it came to pass, when the wall was built, and I had set up the doors, and the porters and the singers and the Levites were appointed,
verse	16	7	2	@@That I gave my brother Hanani, and Hananiah the ruler of the palace, charge over Jerusalem: for he @9was@7 a faithful man, and feared God above many.
verse	16	7	3	@@And I said unto them, Let not the gates of Jerusalem be opened until the sun be hot; and while they stand by, let them shut the doors, and bar @9them:@7 and appoint watches of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, every one in his watch, and every one @9to be@7 over against his house.
verse	16	7	4	@@Now the city @9was@7 large and great: but the people @9were@7 few therein, and the houses @9were@7 not builded.
verse	16	7	5	And my God put into mine heart to gather together the nobles, and the rulers, and the people, that they might be reckoned by genealogy. And I found a register of the genealogy of them which came up at the first, and found written therein,
verse	16	7	6	@@These @9are@7 the children of the province, that went up out of the captivity, of those that had been carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away, and came again to Jerusalem and to Judah, every one unto his city;
verse	16	7	7	@@Who came with Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Azariah, Raamiah, Nahamani, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispereth, Bigvai, Nehum, Baanah. The number, @9I say,@7 of the men of the people of Israel @9was this; @7
