verse	16	7	60	@@All the Nethinims, and the children of Solomon's servants, @9were@7 three hundred ninety and two.
verse	16	7	61	@@And these @9were@7 they which went up @9also@7 from Telmelah, Telharesha, Cherub, Addon, and Immer: but they could not shew their father's house, nor their seed, whether they @9were@7 of Israel.
verse	16	7	62	The children of Delaiah, the children of Tobiah, the children of Nekoda, six hundred forty and two.
verse	16	7	63	@@And of the priests: the children of Habaiah, the children of Koz, the children of Barzillai, which took @9one@7 of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite to wife, and was called after their name.
verse	16	7	64	@@These sought their register @9among@7 those that were reckoned by genealogy, but it was not found: therefore were they, as polluted, put from the priesthood.
verse	16	7	65	@@And the Tirshatha said unto them, that they should not eat of the most holy things, till there stood @9up@7 a priest with Urim and Thummim.
verse	16	7	66	@@The whole congregation together @9was@7 forty and two thousand three hundred and threescore,
verse	16	7	67	@@Beside their manservants and their maidservants, of whom @9there were@7 seven thousand three hundred thirty and seven: and they had two hundred forty and five singing men and singing women.
verse	16	7	68	Their horses, seven hundred thirty and six: their mules, two hundred forty and five:
verse	16	7	69	@@@9Their@7 camels, four hundred thirty and five: six thousand seven hundred and twenty asses.
verse	16	7	70	And some of the chief of the fathers gave unto the work. The Tirshatha gave to the treasure a thousand drams of gold, fifty basons, five hundred and thirty priests' garments.
verse	16	7	71	@@And @9some@7 of the chief of the fathers gave to the treasure of the work twenty thousand drams of gold, and two thousand and two hundred pounds of silver.
verse	16	7	72	@@And @9that@7 which the rest of the people gave @9was@7 twenty thousand drams of gold, and two thousand pounds of silver, and threescore and seven priests' garments.
verse	16	7	73	@@So the priests, and the Levites, and the porters, and the singers, and @9some@7 of the people, and the Nethinims, and all Israel, dwelt in their cities; and when the seventh month came, the children of Israel @9were@7 in their cities.
verse	16	8	1	@@And all the people gathered themselves together as one man into the street that @9was@7 before the water gate; and they spake unto Ezra the scribe to bring the book of the law of Moses, which the LORD had commanded to Israel.
verse	16	8	2	And Ezra the priest brought the law before the congregation both of men and women, and all that could hear with understanding, upon the first day of the seventh month.
verse	16	8	3	@@And he read therein before the street that @9was@7 before the water gate from the morning until midday, before the men and the women, and those that could understand; and the ears of all the people @9were attentive@7 unto the book of the law.
verse	16	8	4	@@And Ezra the scribe stood upon a pulpit of wood, which they had made for the purpose; and beside him stood Mattithiah, and Shema, and Anaiah, and Urijah, and Hilkiah, and Maaseiah, on his right hand; and on his left hand, Pedaiah, and Mishael, and Malchiah, and Hashum, and Hashbadana, Zechariah, @9and@7 Meshullam.
verse	16	8	5	And Ezra opened the book in the sight of all the people; (for he was above all the people;) and when he opened it, all the people stood up:
verse	16	8	6	@@And Ezra blessed the LORD, the great God. And all the people answered, Amen, Amen, with lifting up their hands: and they bowed their heads, and worshipped the LORD with @9their@7 faces to the ground.
verse	16	8	7	@@Also Jeshua, and Bani, and Sherebiah, Jamin, Akkub, Shabbethai, Hodijah, Maaseiah, Kelita, Azariah, Jozabad, Hanan, Pelaiah, and the Levites, caused the people to understand the law: and the people @9stood@7 in their place.
verse	16	8	8	@@So they read in the book in the law of God distinctly, and gave the sense, and caused @9them@7 to understand the reading.
verse	16	8	9	@@And Nehemiah, which @9is@7 the Tirshatha, and Ezra the priest the scribe, and the Levites that taught the people, said unto all the people, This day @9is@7 holy unto the LORD your God; mourn not, nor weep. For all the people wept, when they heard the words of the law.
verse	16	8	10	@@Then he said unto them, Go your way, eat the fat, and drink the sweet, and send portions unto them for whom nothing is prepared: for @9this@7 day @9is@7 holy unto our Lord: neither be ye sorry; for the joy of the LORD is your strength.
verse	16	8	11	@@So the Levites stilled all the people, saying, Hold your peace, for the day @9is@7 holy; neither be ye grieved.
verse	16	8	12	And all the people went their way to eat, and to drink, and to send portions, and to make great mirth, because they had understood the words that were declared unto them.
verse	16	8	13	And on the second day were gathered together the chief of the fathers of all the people, the priests, and the Levites, unto Ezra the scribe, even to understand the words of the law.
verse	16	8	14	And they found written in the law which the LORD had commanded by Moses, that the children of Israel should dwell in booths in the feast of the seventh month:
verse	16	8	15	@@And that they should publish and proclaim in all their cities, and in Jerusalem, saying, Go forth unto the mount, and fetch olive branches, and pine branches, and myrtle branches, and palm branches, and branches of thick trees, to make booths, as @9it is@7 written.
verse	16	8	16	@@So the people went forth, and brought @9them,@7 and made themselves booths, every one upon the roof of his house, and in their courts, and in the courts of the house of God, and in the street of the water gate, and in the street of the gate of Ephraim.
verse	16	8	17	And all the congregation of them that were come again out of the captivity made booths, and sat under the booths: for since the days of Jeshua the son of Nun unto that day had not the children of Israel done so. And there was very great gladness.
verse	16	8	18	@@Also day by day, from the first day unto the last day, he read in the book of the law of God. And they kept the feast seven days; and on the eighth day @9was@7 a solemn assembly, according unto the manner.
verse	16	9	1	Now in the twenty and fourth day of this month the children of Israel were assembled with fasting, and with sackclothes, and earth upon them.
verse	16	9	2	And the seed of Israel separated themselves from all strangers, and stood and confessed their sins, and the iniquities of their fathers.
verse	16	9	3	@@And they stood up in their place, and read in the book of the law of the LORD their God @9one@7 fourth part of the day; and @9another@7 fourth part they confessed, and worshipped the LORD their God.
verse	16	9	4	@@Then stood up upon the stairs, of the Levites, Jeshua, and Bani, Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni, Sherebiah, Bani, @9and@7 Chenani, and cried with a loud voice unto the LORD their God.
verse	16	9	5	@@Then the Levites, Jeshua, and Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabniah, Sherebiah, Hodijah, Shebaniah, @9and@7 Pethahiah, said, Stand up @9and@7 bless the LORD your God for ever and ever: and blessed be thy glorious name, which is exalted above all blessing and praise.
verse	16	9	6	@@Thou, @9even@7 thou, @9art@7 LORD alone; thou hast made heaven, the heaven of heavens, with all their host, the earth, and all @9things@7 that @9are@7 therein, the seas, and all that @9is@7 therein, and thou preservest them all; and the host of heaven worshippeth thee.
verse	16	9	7	@@Thou @9art@7 the LORD the God, who didst choose Abram, and broughtest him forth out of Ur of the Chaldees, and gavest him the name of Abraham;
verse	16	9	8	@@And foundest his heart faithful before thee, and madest a covenant with him to give the land of the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the Jebusites, and the Girgashites, to give @9it, I say,@7 to his seed, and hast performed thy words; for thou @9art@7 righteous:
verse	16	9	9	And didst see the affliction of our fathers in Egypt, and heardest their cry by the Red sea;
verse	16	9	10	@@And shewedst signs and wonders upon Pharaoh, and on all his servants, and on all the people of his land: for thou knewest that they dealt proudly against them. So didst thou get thee a name, as @9it is@7 this day.
verse	16	9	11	And thou didst divide the sea before them, so that they went through the midst of the sea on the dry land; and their persecutors thou threwest into the deeps, as a stone into the mighty waters.
verse	16	9	12	Moreover thou leddest them in the day by a cloudy pillar; and in the night by a pillar of fire, to give them light in the way wherein they should go.
verse	16	9	13	Thou camest down also upon mount Sinai, and spakest with them from heaven, and gavest them right judgments, and true laws, good statutes and commandments:
verse	16	9	14	And madest known unto them thy holy sabbath, and commandedst them precepts, statutes, and laws, by the hand of Moses thy servant:
verse	16	9	15	And gavest them bread from heaven for their hunger, and broughtest forth water for them out of the rock for their thirst, and promisedst them that they should go in to possess the land which thou hadst sworn to give them.
verse	16	9	16	But they and our fathers dealt proudly, and hardened their necks, and hearkened not to thy commandments,
verse	16	9	17	@@And refused to obey, neither were mindful of thy wonders that thou didst among them; but hardened their necks, and in their rebellion appointed a captain to return to their bondage: but thou @9art@7 a God ready to pardon, gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and forsookest them not.
verse	16	9	18	@@Yea, when they had made them a molten calf, and said, This @9is@7 thy God that brought thee up out of Egypt, and had wrought great provocations;
verse	16	9	19	Yet thou in thy manifold mercies forsookest them not in the wilderness: the pillar of the cloud departed not from them by day, to lead them in the way; neither the pillar of fire by night, to shew them light, and the way wherein they should go.
verse	16	9	20	Thou gavest also thy good spirit to instruct them, and withheldest not thy manna from their mouth, and gavest them water for their thirst.
verse	16	9	21	@@Yea, forty years didst thou sustain them in the wilderness, @9so that@7 they lacked nothing; their clothes waxed not old, and their feet swelled not.
verse	16	9	22	Moreover thou gavest them kingdoms and nations, and didst divide them into corners: so they possessed the land of Sihon, and the land of the king of Heshbon, and the land of Og king of Bashan.
verse	16	9	23	@@Their children also multipliedst thou as the stars of heaven, and broughtest them into the land, concerning which thou hadst promised to their fathers, that they should go in to possess @9it. @7
verse	16	9	24	So the children went in and possessed the land, and thou subduedst before them the inhabitants of the land, the Canaanites, and gavest them into their hands, with their kings, and the people of the land, that they might do with them as they would.
verse	16	9	25	And they took strong cities, and a fat land, and possessed houses full of all goods, wells digged, vineyards, and oliveyards, and fruit trees in abundance: so they did eat, and were filled, and became fat, and delighted themselves in thy great goodness.
verse	16	9	26	Nevertheless they were disobedient, and rebelled against thee, and cast thy law behind their backs, and slew thy prophets which testified against them to turn them to thee, and they wrought great provocations.
verse	16	9	27	@@Therefore thou deliveredst them into the hand of their enemies, who vexed them: and in the time of their trouble, when they cried unto thee, thou heardest @9them@7 from heaven; and according to thy manifold mercies thou gavest them saviours, who saved them out of the hand of their enemies.
verse	16	9	28	@@But after they had rest, they did evil again before thee: therefore leftest thou them in the hand of their enemies, so that they had the dominion over them: yet when they returned, and cried unto thee, thou heardest @9them@7 from heaven; and many times didst thou deliver them according to thy mercies;
verse	16	9	29	And testifiedst against them, that thou mightest bring them again unto thy law: yet they dealt proudly, and hearkened not unto thy commandments, but sinned against thy judgments, (which if a man do, he shall live in them;) and withdrew the shoulder, and hardened their neck, and would not hear.
verse	16	9	30	Yet many years didst thou forbear them, and testifiedst against them by thy spirit in thy prophets: yet would they not give ear: therefore gavest thou them into the hand of the people of the lands.
verse	16	9	31	@@Nevertheless for thy great mercies' sake thou didst not utterly consume them, nor forsake them; for thou @9art@7 a gracious and merciful God.
verse	16	9	32	Now therefore, our God, the great, the mighty, and the terrible God, who keepest covenant and mercy, let not all the trouble seem little before thee, that hath come upon us, on our kings, on our princes, and on our priests, and on our prophets, and on our fathers, and on all thy people, since the time of the kings of Assyria unto this day.
verse	16	9	33	@@Howbeit thou @9art@7 just in all that is brought upon us; for thou hast done right, but we have done wickedly:
verse	16	9	34	Neither have our kings, our princes, our priests, nor our fathers, kept thy law, nor hearkened unto thy commandments and thy testimonies, wherewith thou didst testify against them.
verse	16	9	35	For they have not served thee in their kingdom, and in thy great goodness that thou gavest them, and in the large and fat land which thou gavest before them, neither turned they from their wicked works.
verse	16	9	36	@@Behold, we @9are@7 servants this day, and @9for@7 the land that thou gavest unto our fathers to eat the fruit thereof and the good thereof, behold, we @9are@7 servants in it:
verse	16	9	37	@@And it yieldeth much increase unto the kings whom thou hast set over us because of our sins: also they have dominion over our bodies, and over our cattle, at their pleasure, and we @9are@7 in great distress.
verse	16	9	38	@@And because of all this we make a sure @9covenant,@7 and write @9it;@7 and our princes, Levites, @9and@7 priests, seal @9unto it.@7
verse	16	10	1	@@Now those that sealed @9were,@7 Nehemiah, the Tirshatha, the son of Hachaliah, and Zidkijah,
verse	16	10	2	Seraiah, Azariah, Jeremiah,
verse	16	10	3	Pashur, Amariah, Malchijah,
