verse	16	10	14	The chief of the people; Parosh, Pahath-moab, Elam, Zatthu, Bani,
verse	16	10	15	Bunni, Azgad, Bebai,
verse	16	10	16	Adonijah, Bigvai, Adin,
verse	16	10	17	Ater, Hizkijah, Azzur,
verse	16	10	18	Hodijah, Hashum, Bezai,
verse	16	10	19	Hariph, Anathoth, Nebai,
verse	16	10	20	Magpiash, Meshullam, Hezir,
verse	16	10	21	Meshezabeel, Zadok, Jaddua,
verse	16	10	22	Pelatiah, Hanan, Anaiah,
verse	16	10	23	Hoshea, Hananiah, Hashub,
verse	16	10	24	Hallohesh, Pileha, Shobek,
verse	16	10	25	Rehum, Hashabnah, Maaseiah,
verse	16	10	26	And Ahijah, Hanan, Anan,
verse	16	10	27	Malluch, Harim, Baanah.
verse	16	10	28	And the rest of the people, the priests, the Levites, the porters, the singers, the Nethinims, and all they that had separated themselves from the people of the lands unto the law of God, their wives, their sons, and their daughters, every one having knowledge, and having understanding;
verse	16	10	29	They clave to their brethren, their nobles, and entered into a curse, and into an oath, to walk in God's law, which was given by Moses the servant of God, and to observe and do all the commandments of the LORD our Lord, and his judgments and his statutes;
verse	16	10	30	And that we would not give our daughters unto the people of the land, nor take their daughters for our sons:
verse	16	10	31	@@And @9if@7 the people of the land bring ware or any victuals on the sabbath day to sell, @9that@7 we would not buy it of them on the sabbath, or on the holy day: and @9that@7 we would leave the seventh year, and the exaction of every debt.
verse	16	10	32	Also we made ordinances for us, to charge ourselves yearly with the third part of a shekel for the service of the house of our God;
verse	16	10	33	@@For the shewbread, and for the continual meat offering, and for the continual burnt offering, of the sabbaths, of the new moons, for the set feasts, and for the holy @9things,@7 and for the sin offerings to make an atonement for Israel, and @9for@7 all the work of the house of our God.
verse	16	10	34	@@And we cast the lots among the priests, the Levites, and the people, for the wood offering, to bring @9it@7 into the house of our God, after the houses of our fathers, at times appointed year by year, to burn upon the altar of the LORD our God, as @9it is@7 written in the law:
verse	16	10	35	And to bring the firstfruits of our ground, and the firstfruits of all fruit of all trees, year by year, unto the house of the LORD:
verse	16	10	36	@@Also the firstborn of our sons, and of our cattle, as @9it is@7 written in the law, and the firstlings of our herds and of our flocks, to bring to the house of our God, unto the priests that minister in the house of our God:
verse	16	10	37	@@And @9that@7 we should bring the firstfruits of our dough, and our offerings, and the fruit of all manner of trees, of wine and of oil, unto the priests, to the chambers of the house of our God; and the tithes of our ground unto the Levites, that the same Levites might have the tithes in all the cities of our tillage.
verse	16	10	38	And the priest the son of Aaron shall be with the Levites, when the Levites take tithes: and the Levites shall bring up the tithe of the tithes unto the house of our God, to the chambers, into the treasure house.
verse	16	10	39	@@For the children of Israel and the children of Levi shall bring the offering of the corn, of the new wine, and the oil, unto the chambers, where @9are@7 the vessels of the sanctuary, and the priests that minister, and the porters, and the singers: and we will not forsake the house of our God.
verse	16	11	1	@@And the rulers of the people dwelt at Jerusalem: the rest of the people also cast lots, to bring one of ten to dwell in Jerusalem the holy city, and nine parts @9to dwell@7 in @9other@7 cities.
verse	16	11	2	And the people blessed all the men, that willingly offered themselves to dwell at Jerusalem.
verse	16	11	3	@@Now these @9are@7 the chief of the province that dwelt in Jerusalem: but in the cities of Judah dwelt every one in his possession in their cities, @9to wit,@7 Israel, the priests, and the Levites, and the Nethinims, and the children of Solomon's servants.
verse	16	11	4	@@And at Jerusalem dwelt @9certain@7 of the children of Judah, and of the children of Benjamin. Of the children of Judah; Athaiah the son of Uzziah, the son of Zechariah, the son of Amariah, the son of Shephatiah, the son of Mahalaleel, of the children of Perez;
verse	16	11	5	And Maaseiah the son of Baruch, the son of Col-hozeh, the son of Hazaiah, the son of Adaiah, the son of Joiarib, the son of Zechariah, the son of Shiloni.
verse	16	11	6	@@All the sons of Perez that dwelt at Jerusalem @9were@7 four hundred threescore and eight valiant men.
verse	16	11	7	@@And these @9are@7 the sons of Benjamin; Sallu the son of Meshullam, the son of Joed, the son of Pedaiah, the son of Kolaiah, the son of Maaseiah, the son of Ithiel, the son of Jesaiah.
verse	16	11	8	And after him Gabbai, Sallai, nine hundred twenty and eight.
verse	16	11	9	@@And Joel the son of Zichri @9was@7 their overseer: and Judah the son of Senuah @9was@7 second over the city.
verse	16	11	10	Of the priests: Jedaiah the son of Joiarib, Jachin.
verse	16	11	11	@@Seraiah the son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, @9was@7 the ruler of the house of God.
verse	16	11	12	@@And their brethren that did the work of the house @9were@7 eight hundred twenty and two: and Adaiah the son of Jeroham, the son of Pelaliah, the son of Amzi, the son of Zechariah, the son of Pashur, the son of Malchiah,
verse	16	11	13	And his brethren, chief of the fathers, two hundred forty and two: and Amashai the son of PrAzareel, the son of Ahasai, the son of Meshillemoth, the son of Immer,
verse	16	11	14	@@And their brethren, mighty men of valour, an hundred twenty and eight: and their overseer @9was@7 Zabdiel, the son of @9one of@7 the great men.
verse	16	11	15	Also of the Levites: Shemaiah the son of Hashub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Bunni;
verse	16	11	16	@@And Shabbethai and Jozabad, of the chief of the Levites, @9had@7 the oversight of the outward business of the house of God.
verse	16	11	17	@@And Mattaniah the son of Micha, the son of Zabdi, the son of Asaph, @9was@7 the principal to begin the thanksgiving in prayer: and Bakbukiah the second among his brethren, and Abda the son of Shammua, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun.
verse	16	11	18	@@All the Levites in the holy city @9were@7 two hundred fourscore and four.
verse	16	11	19	@@Moreover the porters, Akkub, Talmon, and their brethren that kept the gates, @9were@7 an hundred seventy and two.
verse	16	11	20	@@And the residue of Israel, of the priests, @9and@7 the Levites, @9were@7 in all the cities of Judah, every one in his inheritance.
verse	16	11	21	@@But the Nethinims dwelt in Ophel: and Ziha and Gispa @9were@7 over the Nethinims.
verse	16	11	22	@@The overseer also of the Levites at Jerusalem @9was@7 Uzzi the son of Bani, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Micha. Of the sons of Asaph, the singers @9were@7 over the business of the house of God.
verse	16	11	23	@@For @9it was@7 the king's commandment concerning them, that a certain portion should be for the singers, due for every day.
verse	16	11	24	@@And Pethahiah the son of Meshezabeel, of the children of Zerah the son of Judah, @9was@7 at the king's hand in all matters concerning the people.
verse	16	11	25	@@And for the villages, with their fields, @9some@7 of the children of Judah dwelt at Kirjatharba, and @9in@7 the villages thereof, and at Dibon, and in the villages thereof, and at Jekabzeel, and @9in@7 the villages thereof,
verse	16	11	26	And at Jeshua, and at Moladah, and at Beth-phelet,
verse	16	11	27	@@And at Hazarshual, and at Beersheba, and @9in@7 the villages thereof,
verse	16	11	28	And at Ziklag, and at Mekonah, and in the villages thereof,
verse	16	11	29	And at En-rimmon, and at Zareah, and at Jarmuth,
verse	16	11	30	@@Zanoah, Adullam, and @9in@7 their villages, at Lachish, and the fields thereof, at Azekah, and @9in@7 the villages thereof. And they dwelt from Beersheba unto the valley of Hinnom.
verse	16	11	31	@@The children also of Benjamin from Geba @9dwelt@7 at Michmash, and Aija, and Bethel, and @9in@7 their villages,
verse	16	11	32	@@@9And@7 at Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah,
verse	16	11	33	Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim,
verse	16	11	34	Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat,
verse	16	11	35	Lod, and Ono, the valley of craftsmen.
verse	16	11	36	@@And of the Levites @9were@7 divisions @9in@7 Judah, @9and@7 in Benjamin.
verse	16	12	1	@@Now these @9are@7 the priests and the Levites that went up with Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua: Seraiah, Jeremiah, Ezra,
verse	16	12	2	Amariah, Malluch, Hattush,
verse	16	12	3	Shechaniah, Rehum, Meremoth,
verse	16	12	4	Iddo, Ginnetho, Abijah,
verse	16	12	5	Miamin, Maadiah, Bilgah,
verse	16	12	6	Shemaiah, and Joiarib, Jedaiah,
verse	16	12	7	@@Sallu, Amok, Hilkiah, Jedaiah. These @9were@7 the chief of the priests and of their brethren in the days of Jeshua.
verse	16	12	8	@@Moreover the Levites: Jeshua, Binnui, Kadmiel, Sherebiah, Judah, @9and@7 Mattaniah, @9which was@7 over the thanksgiving, he and his brethren.
verse	16	12	9	@@Also Bakbukiah and Unni, their brethren, @9were@7 over against them in the watches.
verse	16	12	10	And Jeshua begat Joiakim, Joiakim also begat Eliashib, and Eliashib begat Joiada,
verse	16	12	11	And Joiada begat Jonathan, and Jonathan begat Jaddua.
verse	16	12	12	And in the days of Joiakim were priests, the chief of the fathers: of Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah, Hananiah;
verse	16	12	13	Of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah, Jehohanan;
verse	16	12	14	Of Melicu, Jonathan; of Shebaniah, Joseph;
verse	16	12	15	Of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth, Helkai;
verse	16	12	16	Of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon, Meshullam;
verse	16	12	17	Of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin, of Moadiah, Piltai;
verse	16	12	18	Of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah, Jehonathan;
verse	16	12	19	And of Joiarib, Mattenai; of Jedaiah, Uzzi;
verse	16	12	20	Of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;
verse	16	12	21	Of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; of Jedaiah, Nethaneel.
verse	16	12	22	@@The Levites in the days of Eliashib, Joiada, and Johanan, and Jaddua, @9were@7 recorded chief of the fathers: also the priests, to the reign of Darius the Persian.
verse	16	12	23	@@The sons of Levi, the chief of the fathers, @9were@7 written in the book of the chronicles, even until the days of Johanan the son of Eliashib.
verse	16	12	24	@@And the chief of the Levites: Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua the son of Kadmiel, with their brethren over against them, to praise @9and@7 to give thanks, according to the commandment of David the man of God, ward over against ward.
verse	16	12	25	@@Mattaniah, and Bakbukiah, Obadiah, Meshullam, Talmon, Akkub, @9were@7 porters keeping the ward at the thresholds of the gates.
verse	16	12	26	@@These @9were@7 in the days of Joiakim the son of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah the governor, and of Ezra the priest, the scribe.
verse	16	12	27	@@And at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem they sought the Levites out of all their places, to bring them to Jerusalem, to keep the dedication with gladness, both with thanksgivings, and with singing, @9with@7 cymbals, psalteries, and with harps.
verse	16	12	28	And the sons of the singers gathered themselves together, both out of the plain country round about Jerusalem, and from the villages of Netophathi;
verse	16	12	29	Also from the house of Gilgal, and out of the fields of Geba and Azmaveth: for the singers had builded them villages round about Jerusalem.
verse	16	12	30	And the priests and the Levites purified themselves, and purified the people, and the gates, and the wall.
verse	16	12	31	@@Then I brought up the princes of Judah upon the wall, and appointed two great @9companies of them that gave@7 thanks, @9whereof one@7 went on the right hand upon the wall toward the dung gate:
verse	16	12	32	And after them went Hoshaiah, and half of the princes of Judah,
verse	16	12	33	And Azariah, Ezra, and Meshullam,
verse	16	12	34	Judah, and Benjamin, and Shemaiah, and Jeremiah,
verse	16	12	35	@@And @9certain@7 of the priests' sons with trumpets; @9namely,@7 Zechariah the son of Jonathan, the son of Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Michaiah, the son of Zaccur, the son of Asaph:
verse	16	12	36	And his brethren, Shemaiah, and PrAzarael, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai, Nethaneel, and Judah, Hanani, with the musical instruments of David the man of God, and Ezra the scribe before them.
verse	16	12	37	And at the fountain gate, which was over against them, they went up by the stairs of the city of David, at the going up of the wall, above the house of David, even unto the water gate eastward.
verse	16	12	38	@@And the other @9company of them that gave@7 thanks went over against @9them,@7 and I after them, and the half of the people upon the wall, from beyond the tower of the furnaces even unto the broad wall;
verse	16	12	39	And from above the gate of Ephraim, and above the old gate, and above the fish gate, and the tower of Hananeel, and the tower of Meah, even unto the sheep gate: and they stood still in the prison gate.
verse	16	12	40	@@So stood the two @9companies of them that gave@7 thanks in the house of God, and I, and the half of the rulers with me:
verse	16	12	41	@@And the priests; Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Michaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah, @9and@7 Hananiah, with trumpets;
verse	16	12	42	@@And Maaseiah, and Shemaiah, and Eleazar, and Uzzi, and Jehohanan, and Malchijah, and Elam, and Ezer. And the singers sang loud, with Jezrahiah @9their@7 overseer.
verse	16	12	43	Also that day they offered great sacrifices, and rejoiced: for God had made them rejoice with great joy: the wives also and the children rejoiced: so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard even afar off.
verse	16	12	44	And at that time were some appointed over the chambers for the treasures, for the offerings, for the firstfruits, and for the tithes, to gather into them out of the fields of the cities the portions of the law for the priests and Levites: for Judah rejoiced for the priests and for the Levites that waited.
verse	16	12	45	@@And both the singers and the porters kept the ward of their God, and the ward of the purification, according to the commandment of David, @9and@7 of Solomon his son.
verse	16	12	46	@@For in the days of David and Asaph of old @9there were@7 chief of the singers, and songs of praise and thanksgiving unto God.
verse	16	12	47	@@And all Israel in the days of Zerubbabel, and in the days of Nehemiah, gave the portions of the singers and the porters, every day his portion: and they sanctified @9holy things@7 unto the Levites; and the Levites sanctified @9them@7 unto the children of Aaron.
verse	16	13	1	On that day they read in the book of Moses in the audience of the people; and therein was found written, that the Ammonite and the Moabite should not come into the congregation of God for ever;
verse	16	13	2	Because they met not the children of Israel with bread and with water, but hired Balaam against them, that he should curse them: howbeit our God turned the curse into a blessing.
verse	16	13	3	Now it came to pass, when they had heard the law, that they separated from Israel all the mixed multitude.
verse	16	13	4	@@And before this, Eliashib the priest, having the oversight of the chamber of the house of our God, @9was@7 allied unto Tobiah:
verse	16	13	5	@@And he had prepared for him a great chamber, where aforetime they laid the meat offerings, the frankincense, and the vessels, and the tithes of the corn, the new wine, and the oil, which was commanded @9to be given@7 to the Levites, and the singers, and the porters; and the offerings of the priests.
verse	16	13	6	@@But in all this @9time@7 was not I at Jerusalem: for in the two and thirtieth year of Artaxerxes king of Babylon came I unto the king, and after certain days obtained I leave of the king:
verse	16	13	7	And I came to Jerusalem, and understood of the evil that Eliashib did for Tobiah, in preparing him a chamber in the courts of the house of God.
verse	16	13	8	And it grieved me sore: therefore I cast forth all the household stuff of Tobiah out of the chamber.
verse	16	13	9	Then I commanded, and they cleansed the chambers: and thither brought I again the vessels of the house of God, with the meat offering and the frankincense.
verse	16	13	10	@@And I perceived that the portions of the Levites had not been given @9them:@7 for the Levites and the singers, that did the work, were fled every one to his field.
verse	16	13	11	Then contended I with the rulers, and said, Why is the house of God forsaken? And I gathered them together, and set them in their place.
verse	16	13	12	Then brought all Judah the tithe of the corn and the new wine and the oil unto the treasuries.
verse	16	13	13	@@And I made treasurers over the treasuries, Shelemiah the priest, and Zadok the scribe, and of the Levites, Pedaiah: and next to them @9was@7 Hanan the son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah: for they were counted faithful, and their office @9was@7 to distribute unto their brethren.
verse	16	13	14	Remember me, O my God, concerning this, and wipe not out my good deeds that I have done for the house of my God, and for the offices thereof.
verse	16	13	15	@@In those days saw I in Judah @9some@7 treading winepresses on the sabbath, and bringing in sheaves, and lading asses; as also wine, grapes, and figs, and all @9manner of@7 burdens, which they brought into Jerusalem on the sabbath day: and I testified @9against them@7 in the day wherein they sold victuals.
verse	16	13	16	There dwelt men of Tyre also therein, which brought fish, and all manner of ware, and sold on the sabbath unto the children of Judah, and in Jerusalem.
verse	16	13	17	@@Then I contended with the nobles of Judah, and said unto them, What evil thing @9is@7 this that ye do, and profane the sabbath day?
verse	16	13	18	Did not your fathers thus, and did not our God bring all this evil upon us, and upon this city? yet ye bring more wrath upon Israel by profaning the sabbath.
verse	16	13	19	@@And it came to pass, that when the gates of Jerusalem began to be dark before the sabbath, I commanded that the gates should be shut, and charged that they should not be opened till after the sabbath: and @9some@7 of my servants set I at the gates, @9that@7 there should no burden be brought in on the sabbath day.
verse	16	13	20	So the merchants and sellers of all kind of ware lodged without Jerusalem once or twice.
verse	16	13	21	@@Then I testified against them, and said unto them, Why lodge ye about the wall? if ye do so again, I will lay hands on you. From that time forth came they no @9more@7 on the sabbath.
verse	16	13	22	@@And I commanded the Levites that they should cleanse themselves, and @9that@7 they should come @9and@7 keep the gates, to sanctify the sabbath day. Remember me, O my God, @9concerning@7 this also, and spare me according to the greatness of thy mercy.
verse	16	13	23	@@In those days also saw I Jews @9that@7 had married wives of Ashdod, of Ammon, @9and@7 of Moab:
verse	16	13	24	And their children spake half in the speech of Ashdod, and could not speak in the Jews' language, but according to the language of each people.
verse	16	13	25	@@And I contended with them, and cursed them, and smote certain of them, and plucked off their hair, and made them swear by God, @9saying,@7 Ye shall not give your daughters unto their sons, nor take their daughters unto your sons, or for yourselves.
verse	16	13	26	Did not Solomon king of Israel sin by these things? yet among many nations was there no king like him, who was beloved of his God, and God made him king over all Israel: nevertheless even him did outlandish women cause to sin.
verse	16	13	27	Shall we then hearken unto you to do all this great evil, to transgress against our God in marrying strange wives?
verse	16	13	28	@@And @9one@7 of the sons of Joiada, the son of Eliashib the high priest, @9was@7 son in law to Sanballat the Horonite: therefore I chased him from me.
verse	16	13	29	Remember them, O my God, because they have defiled the priesthood, and the covenant of the priesthood, and of the Levites.
verse	16	13	30	Thus cleansed I them from all strangers, and appointed the wards of the priests and the Levites, every one in his business;
verse	16	13	31	And for the wood offering, at times appointed, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God, for good.
verse	17	1	1	@@Now it came to pass in the days of Ahasuerus, (this @9is@7 Ahasuerus which reigned, from India even unto Ethiopia, @9over@7 an hundred and seven and twenty provinces:)
verse	17	1	2	@@@9That@7 in those days, when the king Ahasuerus sat on the throne of his kingdom, which @9was@7 in Shushan the palace,
verse	17	1	3	@@In the third year of his reign, he made a feast unto all his princes and his servants; the power of Persia and Media, the nobles and princes of the provinces, @9being@7 before him:
verse	17	1	4	@@When he shewed the riches of his glorious kingdom and the honour of his excellent majesty many days, @9even@7 an hundred and fourscore days.
verse	17	1	5	And when these days were expired, the king made a feast unto all the people that were present in Shushan the palace, both unto great and small, seven days, in the court of the garden of the king's palace;
verse	17	1	6	@@@9Where were@7 white, green, and blue, @9hangings,@7 fastened with cords of fine linen and purple to silver rings and pillars of marble: the beds @9were of@7 gold and silver, upon a pavement of red, and blue, and white, and black, marble.
verse	17	1	7	@@And they gave @9them@7 drink in vessels of gold, (the vessels being diverse one from another,) and royal wine in abundance, according to the state of the king.
verse	17	1	8	@@And the drinking @9was@7 according to the law; none did compel: for so the king had appointed to all the officers of his house, that they should do according to every man's pleasure.
verse	17	1	9	@@Also Vashti the queen made a feast for the women @9in@7 the royal house which @9belonged@7 to king Ahasuerus.
verse	17	1	10	On the seventh day, when the heart of the king was merry with wine, he commanded Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, and Abagtha, Zethar, and Carcas, the seven chamberlains that served in the presence of Ahasuerus the king,
verse	17	1	11	@@To bring Vashti the queen before the king with the crown royal, to shew the people and the princes her beauty: for she @9was@7 fair to look on.
verse	17	1	12	@@But the queen Vashti refused to come at the king's commandment by @9his@7 chamberlains: therefore was the king very wroth, and his anger burned in him.
verse	17	1	13	@@Then the king said to the wise men, which knew the times, (for so @9was@7 the king's manner toward all that knew law and judgment:
verse	17	1	14	@@And the next unto him @9was@7 Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, @9and@7 Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media, which saw the king's face, @9and@7 which sat the first in the kingdom;)
verse	17	1	15	What shall we do unto the queen Vashti according to law, because she hath not performed the commandment of the king Ahasuerus by the chamberlains?
verse	17	1	16	@@And Memucan answered before the king and the princes, Vashti the queen hath not done wrong to the king only, but also to all the princes, and to all the people that @9are@7 in all the provinces of the king Ahasuerus.
verse	17	1	17	@@For @9this@7 deed of the queen shall come abroad unto all women, so that they shall despise their husbands in their eyes, when it shall be reported, The king Ahasuerus commanded Vashti the queen to be brought in before him, but she came not.
verse	17	1	18	@@@9Likewise@7 shall the ladies of Persia and Media say this day unto all the king's princes, which have heard of the deed of the queen. Thus @9shall there arise@7 too much contempt and wrath.
verse	17	1	19	If it please the king, let there go a royal commandment from him, and let it be written among the laws of the Persians and the Medes, that it be not altered, That Vashti come no more before king Ahasuerus; and let the king give her royal estate unto another that is better than she.
verse	17	1	20	And when the king's decree which he shall make shall be published throughout all his empire, (for it is great,) all the wives shall give to their husbands honour, both to great and small.
verse	17	1	21	And the saying pleased the king and the princes; and the king did according to the word of Memucan:
verse	17	1	22	@@For he sent letters into all the king's provinces, into every province according to the writing thereof, and to every people after their language, that every man should bear rule in his own house, and that @9it@7 should be published according to the language of every people.
verse	17	2	1	After these things, when the wrath of king Ahasuerus was appeased, he remembered Vashti, and what she had done, and what was decreed against her.
verse	17	2	2	Then said the king's servants that ministered unto him, Let there be fair young virgins sought for the king:
verse	17	2	3	@@And let the king appoint officers in all the provinces of his kingdom, that they may gather together all the fair young virgins unto Shushan the palace, to the house of the women unto the custody of Hege the king's chamberlain, keeper of the women; and let their things for purification be given @9them: @7
verse	17	2	4	And let the maiden which pleaseth the king be queen instead of Vashti. And the thing pleased the king; and he did so.
verse	17	2	5	@@@9Now@7 in Shushan the palace there was a certain Jew, whose name @9was@7 Mordecai, the son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish, a Benjamite;
verse	17	2	6	Who had been carried away from Jerusalem with the captivity which had been carried away with Jeconiah king of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away.
verse	17	2	7	@@And he brought up Hadassah, that @9is,@7 Esther, his uncle's daughter: for she had neither father nor mother, and the maid @9was@7 fair and beautiful; whom Mordecai, when her father and mother were dead, took for his own daughter.
verse	17	2	8	So it came to pass, when the king's commandment and his decree was heard, and when many maidens were gathered together unto Shushan the palace, to the custody of Hegai, that Esther was brought also unto the king's house, to the custody of Hegai, keeper of the women.
verse	17	2	9	@@And the maiden pleased him, and she obtained kindness of him; and he speedily gave her her things for purification, with such things as belonged to her, and seven maidens, @9which were@7 meet to be given her, out of the king's house: and he preferred her and her maids unto the best @9place@7 of the house of the women.
verse	17	2	10	@@Esther had not shewed her people nor her kindred: for Mordecai had charged her that she should not shew @9it. @7
verse	17	2	11	And Mordecai walked every day before the court of the women's house, to know how Esther did, and what should become of her.
verse	17	2	12	@@Now when every maid's turn was come to go in to king Ahasuerus, after that she had been twelve months, according to the manner of the women, (for so were the days of their purifications accomplished, @9to wit,@7 six months with oil of myrrh, and six months with sweet odours, and with @9other@7 things for the purifying of the women;)
verse	17	2	13	@@Then thus came @9every@7 maiden unto the king; whatsoever she desired was given her to go with her out of the house of the women unto the king's house.
verse	17	2	14	In the evening she went, and on the morrow she returned into the second house of the women, to the custody of Shaashgaz, the king's chamberlain, which kept the concubines: she came in unto the king no more, except the king delighted in her, and that she were called by name.
verse	17	2	15	Now when the turn of Esther, the daughter of Abihail the uncle of Mordecai, who had taken her for his daughter, was come to go in unto the king, she required nothing but what Hegai the king's chamberlain, the keeper of the women, appointed. And Esther obtained favour in the sight of all them that looked upon her.
verse	17	2	16	@@So Esther was taken unto king Ahasuerus into his house royal in the tenth month, which @9is@7 the month Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign.
verse	17	2	17	And the king loved Esther above all the women, and she obtained grace and favour in his sight more than all the virgins; so that he set the royal crown upon her head, and made her queen instead of Vashti.
verse	17	2	18	@@Then the king made a great feast unto all his princes and his servants, @9even@7 Esther's feast; and he made a release to the provinces, and gave gifts, according to the state of the king.
verse	17	2	19	And when the virgins were gathered together the second time, then Mordecai sat in the king's gate.
verse	17	2	20	@@Esther had not @9yet@7 shewed her kindred nor her people; as Mordecai had charged her: for Esther did the commandment of Mordecai, like as when she was brought up with him.
verse	17	2	21	In those days, while Mordecai sat in the king's gate, two of the king's chamberlains, Bigthan and Teresh, of those which kept the door, were wroth, and sought to lay hand on the king Ahasuerus.
verse	17	2	22	@@And the thing was known to Mordecai, who told it unto Esther the queen; and Esther certified the king @9thereof@7 in Mordecai's name.
verse	17	2	23	And when inquisition was made of the matter, it was found out; therefore they were both hanged on a tree: and it was written in the book of the chronicles before the king.
verse	17	3	1	@@After these things did king Ahasuerus promote Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, and advanced him, and set his seat above all the princes that @9were@7 with him.
verse	17	3	2	@@And all the king's servants, that @9were@7 in the king's gate, bowed, and reverenced Haman: for the king had so commanded concerning him. But Mordecai bowed not, nor did @9him@7 reverence.
verse	17	3	3	@@Then the king's servants, which @9were@7 in the king's gate, said unto Mordecai, Why transgressest thou the king's commandment?
verse	17	3	4	@@Now it came to pass, when they spake daily unto him, and he hearkened not unto them, that they told Haman, to see whether Mordecai's matters would stand: for he had told them that he @9was@7 a Jew.
verse	17	3	5	And when Haman saw that Mordecai bowed not, nor did him reverence, then was Haman full of wrath.
verse	17	3	6	@@And he thought scorn to lay hands on Mordecai alone; for they had shewed him the people of Mordecai: wherefore Haman sought to destroy all the Jews that @9were@7 throughout the whole kingdom of Ahasuerus, @9even@7 the people of Mordecai.
verse	17	3	7	@@In the first month, that @9is,@7 the month Nisan, in the twelfth year of king Ahasuerus, they cast Pur, that @9is,@7 the lot, before Haman from day to day, and from month to month, @9to@7 the twelfth @9month,@7 that @9is,@7 the month Adar.
verse	17	3	8	@@And Haman said unto king Ahasuerus, There is a certain people scattered abroad and dispersed among the people in all the provinces of thy kingdom; and their laws @9are@7 diverse from all people; neither keep they the king's laws: therefore it @9is@7 not for the king's profit to suffer them.
verse	17	3	9	@@If it please the king, let it be written that they may be destroyed: and I will pay ten thousand talents of silver to the hands of those that have the charge of the business, to bring @9it@7 into the king's treasuries.
verse	17	3	10	And the king took his ring from his hand, and gave it unto Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, the Jews' enemy.
verse	17	3	11	@@And the king said unto Haman, The silver @9is@7 given to thee, the people also, to do with them as it seemeth good to thee.
verse	17	3	12	@@Then were the king's scribes called on the thirteenth day of the first month, and there was written according to all that Haman had commanded unto the king's lieutenants, and to the governors that @9were@7 over every province, and to the rulers of every people of every province according to the writing thereof, and @9to@7 every people after their language; in the name of king Ahasuerus was it written, and sealed with the king's ring.
verse	17	3	13	@@And the letters were sent by posts into all the king's provinces, to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish, all Jews, both young and old, little children and women, in one day, @9even@7 upon the thirteenth @9day@7 of the twelfth month, which @9is@7 the month Adar, and @9to take@7 the spoil of them for a prey.
verse	17	3	14	The copy of the writing for a commandment to be given in every province was published unto all people, that they should be ready against that day.
verse	17	3	15	The posts went out, being hastened by the king's commandment, and the decree was given in Shushan the palace. And the king and Haman sat down to drink; but the city Shushan was perplexed.
verse	17	4	1	When Mordecai perceived all that was done, Mordecai rent his clothes, and put on sackcloth with ashes, and went out into the midst of the city, and cried with a loud and a bitter cry;
verse	17	4	2	@@And came even before the king's gate: for none @9might@7 enter into the king's gate clothed with sackcloth.
verse	17	4	3	@@And in every province, whithersoever the king's commandment and his decree came, @9there was@7 great mourning among the Jews, and fasting, and weeping, and wailing; and many lay in sackcloth and ashes.
verse	17	4	4	@@So Esther's maids and her chamberlains came and told @9it@7 her. Then was the queen exceedingly grieved; and she sent raiment to clothe Mordecai, and to take away his sackcloth from him: but he received @9it@7 not.
verse	17	4	5	@@Then called Esther for Hatach, @9one@7 of the king's chamberlains, whom he had appointed to attend upon her, and gave him a commandment to Mordecai, to know what it @9was,@7 and why it @9was. @7
