verse	17	4	11	@@All the king's servants, and the people of the king's provinces, do know, that whosoever, whether man or woman, shall come unto the king into the inner court, who is not called, @9there is@7 one law of his to put @9him@7 to death, except such to whom the king shall hold out the golden sceptre, that he may live: but I have not been called to come in unto the king these thirty days.
verse	17	4	12	And they told to Mordecai Esther's words.
verse	17	4	13	Then Mordecai commanded to answer Esther, Think not with thyself that thou shalt escape in the king's house, more than all the Jews.
verse	17	4	14	@@For if thou altogether holdest thy peace at this time, @9then@7 shall there enlargement and deliverance arise to the Jews from another place; but thou and thy father's house shall be destroyed: and who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for @9such@7 a time as this?
