verse	17	8	8	@@Write ye also for the Jews, as it liketh you, in the king's name, and seal @9it@7 with the king's ring: for the writing which is written in the king's name, and sealed with the king's ring, may no man reverse.
verse	17	8	9	@@Then were the king's scribes called at that time in the third month, that @9is,@7 the month Sivan, on the three and twentieth @9day@7 thereof; and it was written according to all that Mordecai commanded unto the Jews, and to the lieutenants, and the deputies and rulers of the provinces which @9are@7 from India unto Ethiopia, an hundred twenty and seven provinces, unto every province according to the writing thereof, and unto every people after their language, and to the Jews according to their writing, and according to their language.
verse	17	8	10	@@And he wrote in the king Ahasuerus' name, and sealed it with the king's ring, and sent letters by posts on horseback, @9and@7 riders on mules, camels, @9and@7 young dromedaries:
verse	17	8	11	@@Wherein the king granted the Jews which @9were@7 in every city to gather themselves together, and to stand for their life, to destroy, to slay, and to cause to perish, all the power of the people and province that would assault them, @9both@7 little ones and women, and @9to take@7 the spoil of them for a prey,
verse	17	8	12	@@Upon one day in all the provinces of king Ahasuerus, @9namely,@7 upon the thirteenth @9day@7 of the twelfth month, which @9is@7 the month Adar.
verse	17	8	13	@@The copy of the writing for a commandment to be given in every province @9was@7 published unto all people, and that the Jews should be ready against that day to avenge themselves on their enemies.
verse	17	8	14	@@@9So@7 the posts that rode upon mules @9and@7 camels went out, being hastened and pressed on by the king's commandment. And the decree was given at Shushan the palace.
