verse	17	9	28	@@And @9that@7 these days @9should be@7 remembered and kept throughout every generation, every family, every province, and every city; and @9that@7 these days of Purim should not fail from among the Jews, nor the memorial of them perish from their seed.
verse	17	9	29	Then Esther the queen, the daughter of Abihail, and Mordecai the Jew, wrote with all authority, to confirm this second letter of Purim.
verse	17	9	30	@@And he sent the letters unto all the Jews, to the hundred twenty and seven provinces of the kingdom of Ahasuerus, @9with@7 words of peace and truth,
verse	17	9	31	@@To confirm these days of Purim in their times @9appointed,@7 according as Mordecai the Jew and Esther the queen had enjoined them, and as they had decreed for themselves and for their seed, the matters of the fastings and their cry.
