verse	18	1	4	@@And his sons went and feasted @9in their@7 houses, every one his day; and sent and called for their three sisters to eat and to drink with them.
verse	18	1	5	@@And it was so, when the days of @9their@7 feasting were gone about, that Job sent and sanctified them, and rose up early in the morning, and offered burnt offerings @9according@7 to the number of them all: for Job said, It may be that my sons have sinned, and cursed God in their hearts. Thus did Job continually.
verse	18	1	6	Now there was a day when the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan came also among them.
verse	18	1	7	And the LORD said unto Satan, Whence comest thou? Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, From going to and fro in the earth, and from walking up and down in it.
verse	18	1	8	@@And the LORD said unto Satan, Hast thou considered my servant Job, that @9there is@7 none like him in the earth, a perfect and an upright man, one that feareth God, and escheweth evil?
