verse	18	3	7	Lo, let that night be solitary, let no joyful voice come therein.
verse	18	3	8	Let them curse it that curse the day, who are ready to raise up their mourning.
verse	18	3	9	@@Let the stars of the twilight thereof be dark; let it look for light, but @9have@7 none; neither let it see the dawning of the day:
verse	18	3	10	@@Because it shut not up the doors of my @9mother's@7 womb, nor hid sorrow from mine eyes.
verse	18	3	11	@@Why died I not from the womb? @9why@7 did I @9not@7 give up the ghost when I came out of the belly?
verse	18	3	12	Why did the knees prevent me? or why the breasts that I should suck?
verse	18	3	13	For now should I have lain still and been quiet, I should have slept: then had I been at rest,
verse	18	3	14	With kings and counsellors of the earth, which built desolate places for themselves;
verse	18	3	15	Or with princes that had gold, who filled their houses with silver:
verse	18	3	16	@@Or as an hidden untimely birth I had not been; as infants @9which@7 never saw light.
verse	18	3	17	@@There the wicked cease @9from@7 troubling; and there the weary be at rest.
