verse	18	4	9	By the blast of God they perish, and by the breath of his nostrils are they consumed.
verse	18	4	10	The roaring of the lion, and the voice of the fierce lion, and the teeth of the young lions, are broken.
verse	18	4	11	The old lion perisheth for lack of prey, and the stout lion's whelps are scattered abroad.
verse	18	4	12	Now a thing was secretly brought to me, and mine ear received a little thereof.
verse	18	4	13	In thoughts from the visions of the night, when deep sleep falleth on men,
