verse	18	4	15	Then a spirit passed before my face; the hair of my flesh stood up:
verse	18	4	16	@@It stood still, but I could not discern the form thereof: an image @9was@7 before mine eyes, @9there was@7 silence, and I heard a voice, @9saying, @7
verse	18	4	17	Shall mortal man be more just than God? shall a man be more pure than his maker?
verse	18	4	18	Behold, he put no trust in his servants; and his angels he charged with folly:
verse	18	4	19	@@How much less @9in@7 them that dwell in houses of clay, whose foundation @9is@7 in the dust, @9which@7 are crushed before the moth?
verse	18	4	20	@@They are destroyed from morning to evening: they perish for ever without any regarding @9it. @7
verse	18	4	21	@@Doth not their excellency @9which is@7 in them go away? they die, even without wisdom.
verse	18	5	1	Call now, if there be any that will answer thee; and to which of the saints wilt thou turn?
verse	18	5	2	For wrath killeth the foolish man, and envy slayeth the silly one.
verse	18	5	3	I have seen the foolish taking root: but suddenly I cursed his habitation.
verse	18	5	4	@@His children are far from safety, and they are crushed in the gate, neither @9is there@7 any to deliver @9them. @7
verse	18	5	5	Whose harvest the hungry eateth up, and taketh it even out of the thorns, and the robber swalloweth up their substance.
verse	18	5	6	Although affliction cometh not forth of the dust, neither doth trouble spring out of the ground;
verse	18	5	7	Yet man is born unto trouble, as the sparks fly upward.
verse	18	5	8	I would seek unto God, and unto God would I commit my cause:
verse	18	5	9	Which doeth great things and unsearchable; marvellous things without number:
verse	18	5	10	Who giveth rain upon the earth, and sendeth waters upon the fields:
verse	18	5	11	To set up on high those that be low; that those which mourn may be exalted to safety.
verse	18	5	12	@@He disappointeth the devices of the crafty, so that their hands cannot perform @9their@7 enterprise.
verse	18	5	13	He taketh the wise in their own craftiness: and the counsel of the froward is carried headlong.
verse	18	5	14	They meet with darkness in the daytime, and grope in the noonday as in the night.
verse	18	5	15	But he saveth the poor from the sword, from their mouth, and from the hand of the mighty.
verse	18	5	16	So the poor hath hope, and iniquity stoppeth her mouth.
verse	18	5	17	@@Behold, happy @9is@7 the man whom God correcteth: therefore despise not thou the chastening of the Almighty:
verse	18	5	18	For he maketh sore, and bindeth up: he woundeth, and his hands make whole.
verse	18	5	19	He shall deliver thee in six troubles: yea, in seven there shall no evil touch thee.
verse	18	5	20	In famine he shall redeem thee from death: and in war from the power of the sword.
verse	18	5	21	Thou shalt be hid from the scourge of the tongue: neither shalt thou be afraid of destruction when it cometh.
verse	18	5	22	At destruction and famine thou shalt laugh: neither shalt thou be afraid of the beasts of the earth.
verse	18	5	23	For thou shalt be in league with the stones of the field: and the beasts of the field shall be at peace with thee.
verse	18	5	24	@@And thou shalt know that thy tabernacle @9shall be@7 in peace; and thou shalt visit thy habitation, and shalt not sin.
verse	18	5	25	@@Thou shalt know also that thy seed @9shall be@7 great, and thine offspring as the grass of the earth.
verse	18	5	26	@@Thou shalt come to @9thy@7 grave in a full age, like as a shock of corn cometh in in his season.
