verse	18	6	1	But Job answered and said,
verse	18	6	2	O that my grief were throughly weighed, and my calamity laid in the balances together!
verse	18	6	3	For now it would be heavier than the sand of the sea: therefore my words are swallowed up.
verse	18	6	4	@@For the arrows of the Almighty @9are@7 within me, the poison whereof drinketh up my spirit: the terrors of God do set themselves in array against me.
verse	18	6	5	Doth the wild ass bray when he hath grass? or loweth the ox over his fodder?
verse	18	6	6	@@Can that which is unsavoury be eaten without salt? or is there @9any@7 taste in the white of an egg?
verse	18	6	7	@@The things @9that@7 my soul refused to touch @9are@7 as my sorrowful meat.
verse	18	6	8	@@Oh that I might have my request; and that God would grant @9me@7 the thing that I long for!
verse	18	6	9	Even that it would please God to destroy me; that he would let loose his hand, and cut me off!
verse	18	6	10	Then should I yet have comfort; yea, I would harden myself in sorrow: let him not spare; for I have not concealed the words of the Holy One.
verse	18	6	11	@@What @9is@7 my strength, that I should hope? and what @9is@7 mine end, that I should prolong my life?
