verse	18	14	22	But his flesh upon him shall have pain, and his soul within him shall mourn.
verse	18	15	1	Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,
verse	18	15	2	Should a wise man utter vain knowledge, and fill his belly with the east wind?
verse	18	15	3	Should he reason with unprofitable talk? or with speeches wherewith he can do no good?
verse	18	15	4	Yea, thou castest off fear, and restrainest prayer before God.
verse	18	15	5	For thy mouth uttereth thine iniquity, and thou choosest the tongue of the crafty.
verse	18	15	6	Thine own mouth condemneth thee, and not I: yea, thine own lips testify against thee.
verse	18	15	7	@@@9Art@7 thou the first man @9that@7 was born? or wast thou made before the hills?
verse	18	15	8	Hast thou heard the secret of God? and dost thou restrain wisdom to thyself?
verse	18	15	9	@@What knowest thou, that we know not? @9what@7 understandest thou, which @9is@7 not in us?
verse	18	15	10	@@With us @9are@7 both the grayheaded and very aged men, much elder than thy father.
verse	18	15	11	@@@9Are@7 the consolations of God small with thee? is there any secret thing with thee?
verse	18	15	12	Why doth thine heart carry thee away? and what do thy eyes wink at,
verse	18	15	13	@@That thou turnest thy spirit against God, and lettest @9such@7 words go out of thy mouth?
verse	18	15	14	@@What @9is@7 man, that he should be clean? and @9he which is@7 born of a woman, that he should be righteous?
verse	18	15	15	Behold, he putteth no trust in his saints; yea, the heavens are not clean in his sight.
verse	18	15	16	@@How much more abominable and filthy @9is@7 man, which drinketh iniquity like water?
verse	18	15	17	@@I will shew thee, hear me; and that @9which@7 I have seen I will declare;
verse	18	15	18	@@Which wise men have told from their fathers, and have not hid @9it: @7
verse	18	15	19	Unto whom alone the earth was given, and no stranger passed among them.
verse	18	15	20	@@The wicked man travaileth with pain all @9his@7 days, and the number of years is hidden to the oppressor.
verse	18	15	21	@@A dreadful sound @9is@7 in his ears: in prosperity the destroyer shall come upon him.
verse	18	15	22	He believeth not that he shall return out of darkness, and he is waited for of the sword.
verse	18	15	23	@@He wandereth abroad for bread, @9saying,@7 Where @9is it?@7 he knoweth that the day of darkness is ready at his hand.
verse	18	15	24	Trouble and anguish shall make him afraid; they shall prevail against him, as a king ready to the battle.
verse	18	15	25	For he stretcheth out his hand against God, and strengtheneth himself against the Almighty.
verse	18	15	26	@@He runneth upon him, @9even@7 on @9his@7 neck, upon the thick bosses of his bucklers:
verse	18	15	27	@@Because he covereth his face with his fatness, and maketh collops of fat on @9his@7 flanks.
verse	18	15	28	@@And he dwelleth in desolate cities, @9and@7 in houses which no man inhabiteth, which are ready to become heaps.
verse	18	15	29	He shall not be rich, neither shall his substance continue, neither shall he prolong the perfection thereof upon the earth.
verse	18	15	30	He shall not depart out of darkness; the flame shall dry up his branches, and by the breath of his mouth shall he go away.
verse	18	15	31	Let not him that is deceived trust in vanity: for vanity shall be his recompence.
verse	18	15	32	It shall be accomplished before his time, and his branch shall not be green.
verse	18	15	33	He shall shake off his unripe grape as the vine, and shall cast off his flower as the olive.
verse	18	15	34	@@For the congregation of hypocrites @9shall be@7 desolate, and fire shall consume the tabernacles of bribery.
verse	18	15	35	They conceive mischief, and bring forth vanity, and their belly prepareth deceit.
verse	18	16	1	Then Job answered and said,
verse	18	16	2	@@I have heard many such things: miserable comforters @9are@7 ye all.
verse	18	16	3	Shall vain words have an end? or what emboldeneth thee that thou answerest?
verse	18	16	4	@@I also could speak as ye @9do:@7 if your soul were in my soul's stead, I could heap up words against you, and shake mine head at you.
verse	18	16	5	@@@9But@7 I would strengthen you with my mouth, and the moving of my lips should asswage @9your grief. @7
verse	18	16	6	@@Though I speak, my grief is not asswaged: and @9though@7 I forbear, what am I eased?
verse	18	16	7	But now he hath made me weary: thou hast made desolate all my company.
verse	18	16	8	@@And thou hast filled me with wrinkles, @9which@7 is a witness @9against me:@7 and my leanness rising up in me beareth witness to my face.
verse	18	16	9	@@He teareth @9me@7 in his wrath, who hateth me: he gnasheth upon me with his teeth; mine enemy sharpeneth his eyes upon me.
verse	18	16	10	They have gaped upon me with their mouth; they have smitten me upon the cheek reproachfully; they have gathered themselves together against me.
verse	18	16	11	God hath delivered me to the ungodly, and turned me over into the hands of the wicked.
verse	18	16	12	@@I was at ease, but he hath broken me asunder: he hath also taken @9me@7 by my neck, and shaken me to pieces, and set me up for his mark.
verse	18	16	13	His archers compass me round about, he cleaveth my reins asunder, and doth not spare; he poureth out my gall upon the ground.
verse	18	16	14	He breaketh me with breach upon breach, he runneth upon me like a giant.
verse	18	16	15	I have sewed sackcloth upon my skin, and defiled my horn in the dust.
verse	18	16	16	My face is foul with weeping, and my eyelids is the shadow of death;
verse	18	16	17	@@Not for @9any@7 injustice in mine hands: also my prayer @9is@7 pure.
verse	18	16	18	O earth, cover not thou my blood, and let my cry have no place.
verse	18	16	19	@@Also now, behold, my witness @9is@7 in heaven, and my record @9is@7 on high.
verse	18	16	20	@@My friends scorn me: @9but@7 mine eye poureth out @9tears@7 unto God.
verse	18	16	21	@@Oh that one might plead for a man with God, as a man @9pleadeth@7 for his neighbour!
verse	18	16	22	@@When a few years are come, then I shall go the way @9whence@7 I shall not return.
verse	18	17	1	@@My breath is corrupt, my days are extinct, the graves @9are ready@7 for me.
verse	18	17	2	@@@9Are there@7 not mockers with me? and doth not mine eye continue in their provocation?
verse	18	17	3	@@Lay down now, put me in a surety with thee; who @9is@7 he @9that@7 will strike hands with me?
verse	18	17	4	@@For thou hast hid their heart from understanding: therefore shalt thou not exalt @9them. @7
verse	18	17	5	@@He that speaketh flattery to @9his@7 friends, even the eyes of his children shall fail.
verse	18	17	6	He hath made me also a byword of the people; and aforetime I was as a tabret.
verse	18	17	7	@@Mine eye also is dim by reason of sorrow, and all my members @9are@7 as a shadow.
verse	18	17	8	@@Upright @9men@7 shall be astonied at this, and the innocent shall stir up himself against the hypocrite.
verse	18	17	9	The righteous also shall hold on his way, and he that hath clean hands shall be stronger and stronger.
verse	18	17	10	@@But as for you all, do ye return, and come now: for I cannot find @9one@7 wise @9man@7 among you.
verse	18	17	11	@@My days are past, my purposes are broken off, @9even@7 the thoughts of my heart.
verse	18	17	12	@@They change the night into day: the light @9is@7 short because of darkness.
verse	18	17	13	@@If I wait, the grave @9is@7 mine house: I have made my bed in the darkness.
verse	18	17	14	@@I have said to corruption, Thou @9art@7 my father: to the worm, @9Thou art@7 my mother, and my sister.
verse	18	17	15	@@And where @9is@7 now my hope? as for my hope, who shall see it?
verse	18	17	16	@@They shall go down to the bars of the pit, when @9our@7 rest together @9is@7 in the dust.
verse	18	18	1	Then answered Bildad the Shuhite, and said,
verse	18	18	2	@@How long @9will it be ere@7 ye make an end of words? mark, and afterwards we will speak.
verse	18	18	3	@@Wherefore are we counted as beasts, @9and@7 reputed vile in your sight?
verse	18	18	4	He teareth himself in his anger: shall the earth be forsaken for thee? and shall the rock be removed out of his place?
verse	18	18	5	Yea, the light of the wicked shall be put out, and the spark of his fire shall not shine.
verse	18	18	6	The light shall be dark in his tabernacle, and his candle shall be put out with him.
verse	18	18	7	The steps of his strength shall be straitened, and his own counsel shall cast him down.
verse	18	18	8	For he is cast into a net by his own feet, and he walketh upon a snare.
verse	18	18	9	@@The gin shall take @9him@7 by the heel, @9and@7 the robber shall prevail against him.
verse	18	18	10	@@The snare @9is@7 laid for him in the ground, and a trap for him in the way.
verse	18	18	11	Terrors shall make him afraid on every side, and shall drive him to his feet.
verse	18	18	12	@@His strength shall be hungerbitten, and destruction @9shall be@7 ready at his side.
verse	18	18	13	@@It shall devour the strength of his skin: @9even@7 the firstborn of death shall devour his strength.
verse	18	18	14	His confidence shall be rooted out of his tabernacle, and it shall bring him to the king of terrors.
verse	18	18	15	@@It shall dwell in his tabernacle, because @9it is@7 none of his: brimstone shall be scattered upon his habitation.
verse	18	18	16	His roots shall be dried up beneath, and above shall his branch be cut off.
verse	18	18	17	His remembrance shall perish from the earth, and he shall have no name in the street.
verse	18	18	18	He shall be driven from light into darkness, and chased out of the world.
verse	18	18	19	He shall neither have son nor nephew among his people, nor any remaining in his dwellings.
verse	18	18	20	@@They that come after @9him@7 shall be astonied at his day, as they that went before were affrighted.
verse	18	18	21	@@Surely such @9are@7 the dwellings of the wicked, and this @9is@7 the place @9of him that@7 knoweth not God.
verse	18	19	1	Then Job answered and said,
verse	18	19	2	How long will ye vex my soul, and break me in pieces with words?
verse	18	19	3	@@These ten times have ye reproached me: ye are not ashamed @9that@7 ye make yourselves strange to me.
verse	18	19	4	@@And be it indeed @9that@7 I have erred, mine error remaineth with myself.
verse	18	19	5	@@If indeed ye will magnify @9yourselves@7 against me, and plead against me my reproach:
verse	18	19	6	Know now that God hath overthrown me, and hath compassed me with his net.
verse	18	19	7	@@Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard: I cry aloud, but @9there is@7 no judgment.
verse	18	19	8	He hath fenced up my way that I cannot pass, and he hath set darkness in my paths.
verse	18	19	9	@@He hath stripped me of my glory, and taken the crown @9from@7 my head.
verse	18	19	10	He hath destroyed me on every side, and I am gone: and mine hope hath he removed like a tree.
verse	18	19	11	@@He hath also kindled his wrath against me, and he counteth me unto him as @9one of@7 his enemies.
verse	18	19	12	His troops come together, and raise up their way against me, and encamp round about my tabernacle.
verse	18	19	13	He hath put my brethren far from me, and mine acquaintance are verily estranged from me.
verse	18	19	14	My kinsfolk have failed, and my familiar friends have forgotten me.
verse	18	19	15	They that dwell in mine house, and my maids, count me for a stranger: I am an alien in their sight.
verse	18	19	16	@@I called my servant, and he gave @9me@7 no answer; I intreated him with my mouth.
verse	18	19	17	@@My breath is strange to my wife, though I intreated for the children's @9sake@7 of mine own body.
verse	18	19	18	Yea, young children despised me; I arose, and they spake against me.
verse	18	19	19	All my inward friends abhorred me: and they whom I loved are turned against me.
verse	18	19	20	My bone cleaveth to my skin and to my flesh, and I am escaped with the skin of my teeth.
verse	18	19	21	Have pity upon me, have pity upon me, O ye my friends; for the hand of God hath touched me.
verse	18	19	22	Why do ye persecute me as God, and are not satisfied with my flesh?
verse	18	19	23	Oh that my words were now written! oh that they were printed in a book!
verse	18	19	24	That they were graven with an iron pen and lead in the rock for ever!
verse	18	19	25	@@For I know @9that@7 my redeemer liveth, and @9that@7 he shall stand at the latter @9day@7 upon the earth:
verse	18	19	26	@@And @9though@7 after my skin @9worms@7 destroy this @9body,@7 yet in my flesh shall I see God:
verse	18	19	27	@@Whom I shall see for myself, and mine eyes shall behold, and not another; @9though@7 my reins be consumed within me.
verse	18	19	28	But ye should say, Why persecute we him, seeing the root of the matter is found in me?
verse	18	19	29	@@Be ye afraid of the sword: for wrath @9bringeth@7 the punishments of the sword, that ye may know @9there is@7 a judgment.
verse	18	20	1	Then answered Zophar the Naamathite, and said,
verse	18	20	2	@@Therefore do my thoughts cause me to answer, and for @9this@7 I make haste.
verse	18	20	3	I have heard the check of my reproach, and the spirit of my understanding causeth me to answer.
verse	18	20	4	@@Knowest thou @9not@7 this of old, since man was placed upon earth,
verse	18	20	5	@@That the triumphing of the wicked @9is@7 short, and the joy of the hypocrite @9but@7 for a moment?
verse	18	20	6	Though his excellency mount up to the heavens, and his head reach unto the clouds;
verse	18	20	7	@@@9Yet@7 he shall perish for ever like his own dung: they which have seen him shall say, Where @9is@7 he?
verse	18	20	8	He shall fly away as a dream, and shall not be found: yea, he shall be chased away as a vision of the night.
verse	18	20	9	@@The eye also @9which@7 saw him shall @9see him@7 no more; neither shall his place any more behold him.
verse	18	20	10	His children shall seek to please the poor, and his hands shall restore their goods.
verse	18	20	11	@@His bones are full @9of the sin@7 of his youth, which shall lie down with him in the dust.
verse	18	20	12	@@Though wickedness be sweet in his mouth, @9though@7 he hide it under his tongue;
verse	18	20	13	@@@9Though@7 he spare it, and forsake it not; but keep it still within his mouth:
verse	18	20	14	@@@9Yet@7 his meat in his bowels is turned, @9it is@7 the gall of asps within him.
verse	18	20	15	He hath swallowed down riches, and he shall vomit them up again: God shall cast them out of his belly.
verse	18	20	16	He shall suck the poison of asps: the viper's tongue shall slay him.
verse	18	20	17	He shall not see the rivers, the floods, the brooks of honey and butter.
verse	18	20	18	@@That which he laboured for shall he restore, and shall not swallow @9it@7 down: according to @9his@7 substance @9shall@7 the restitution @9be,@7 and he shall not rejoice @9therein. @7
verse	18	20	19	@@Because he hath oppressed @9and@7 hath forsaken the poor; @9because@7 he hath violently taken away an house which he builded not;
verse	18	20	20	Surely he shall not feel quietness in his belly, he shall not save of that which he desired.
verse	18	20	21	There shall none of his meat be left; therefore shall no man look for his goods.
verse	18	20	22	In the fulness of his sufficiency he shall be in straits: every hand of the wicked shall come upon him.
verse	18	20	23	@@@9When@7 he is about to fill his belly, @9God@7 shall cast the fury of his wrath upon him, and shall rain @9it@7 upon him while he is eating.
verse	18	20	24	@@He shall flee from the iron weapon, @9and@7 the bow of steel shall strike him through.
verse	18	20	25	@@It is drawn, and cometh out of the body; yea, the glittering sword cometh out of his gall: terrors @9are@7 upon him.
verse	18	20	26	@@All darkness @9shall be@7 hid in his secret places: a fire not blown shall consume him; it shall go ill with him that is left in his tabernacle.
verse	18	20	27	The heaven shall reveal his iniquity; and the earth shall rise up against him.
verse	18	20	28	@@The increase of his house shall depart, @9and his goods@7 shall flow away in the day of his wrath.
verse	18	20	29	@@This @9is@7 the portion of a wicked man from God, and the heritage appointed unto him by God.
verse	18	21	1	But Job answered and said,
verse	18	21	2	Hear diligently my speech, and let this be your consolations.
verse	18	21	3	Suffer me that I may speak; and after that I have spoken, mock on.
verse	18	21	4	@@As for me, @9is@7 my complaint to man? and if @9it were so,@7 why should not my spirit be troubled?
verse	18	21	5	@@Mark me, and be astonished, and lay @9your@7 hand upon @9your@7 mouth.
verse	18	21	6	Even when I remember I am afraid, and trembling taketh hold on my flesh.
verse	18	21	7	Wherefore do the wicked live, become old, yea, are mighty in power?
verse	18	21	8	Their seed is established in their sight with them, and their offspring before their eyes.
verse	18	21	9	@@Their houses @9are@7 safe from fear, neither @9is@7 the rod of God upon them.
verse	18	21	10	Their bull gendereth, and faileth not; their cow calveth, and casteth not her calf.
verse	18	21	11	They send forth their little ones like a flock, and their children dance.
verse	18	21	12	They take the timbrel and harp, and rejoice at the sound of the organ.
verse	18	21	13	They spend their days in wealth, and in a moment go down to the grave.
verse	18	21	14	Therefore they say unto God, Depart from us; for we desire not the knowledge of thy ways.
verse	18	21	15	@@What @9is@7 the Almighty, that we should serve him? and what profit should we have, if we pray unto him?
verse	18	21	16	@@Lo, their good @9is@7 not in their hand: the counsel of the wicked is far from me.
verse	18	21	17	@@How oft is the candle of the wicked put out! and @9how oft@7 cometh their destruction upon them! @9God@7 distributeth sorrows in his anger.
verse	18	21	18	They are as stubble before the wind, and as chaff that the storm carrieth away.
verse	18	21	19	@@God layeth up his iniquity for his children: he rewardeth him, and he shall know @9it. @7
verse	18	21	20	His eyes shall see his destruction, and he shall drink of the wrath of the Almighty.
verse	18	21	21	@@For what pleasure @9hath@7 he in his house after him, when the number of his months is cut off in the midst?
verse	18	21	22	@@Shall @9any@7 teach God knowledge? seeing he judgeth those that are high.
verse	18	21	23	One dieth in his full strength, being wholly at ease and quiet.
verse	18	21	24	His breasts are full of milk, and his bones are moistened with marrow.
verse	18	21	25	And another dieth in the bitterness of his soul, and never eateth with pleasure.
verse	18	21	26	They shall lie down alike in the dust, and the worms shall cover them.
verse	18	21	27	@@Behold, I know your thoughts, and the devices @9which@7 ye wrongfully imagine against me.
verse	18	21	28	@@For ye say, Where @9is@7 the house of the prince? and where @9are@7 the dwelling places of the wicked?
verse	18	21	29	Have ye not asked them that go by the way? and do ye not know their tokens,
verse	18	21	30	That the wicked is reserved to the day of destruction? they shall be brought forth to the day of wrath.
verse	18	21	31	@@Who shall declare his way to his face? and who shall repay him @9what@7 he hath done?
verse	18	21	32	Yet shall he be brought to the grave, and shall remain in the tomb.
verse	18	21	33	@@The clods of the valley shall be sweet unto him, and every man shall draw after him, as @9there are@7 innumerable before him.
verse	18	21	34	How then comfort ye me in vain, seeing in your answers there remaineth falsehood?
verse	18	22	1	Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said,
verse	18	22	2	Can a man be profitable unto God, as he that is wise may be profitable unto himself?
verse	18	22	3	@@@9Is it@7 any pleasure to the Almighty, that thou art righteous? or @9is it@7 gain @9to him@7 that thou makest thy ways perfect?
verse	18	22	4	Will he reprove thee for fear of thee? will he enter with thee into judgment?
verse	18	22	5	@@@9Is@7 not thy wickedness great? and thine iniquities infinite?
verse	18	22	6	For thou hast taken a pledge from thy brother for nought, and stripped the naked of their clothing.
verse	18	22	7	Thou hast not given water to the weary to drink, and thou hast withholden bread from the hungry.
verse	18	22	8	@@But @9as for@7 the mighty man, he had the earth; and the honourable man dwelt in it.
verse	18	22	9	Thou hast sent widows away empty, and the arms of the fatherless have been broken.
verse	18	22	10	@@Therefore snares @9are@7 round about thee, and sudden fear troubleth thee;
verse	18	22	11	@@Or darkness, @9that@7 thou canst not see; and abundance of waters cover thee.
verse	18	22	12	@@@9Is@7 not God in the height of heaven? and behold the height of the stars, how high they are!
verse	18	22	13	And thou sayest, How doth God know? can he judge through the dark cloud?
verse	18	22	14	@@Thick clouds @9are@7 a covering to him, that he seeth not; and he walketh in the circuit of heaven.
verse	18	22	15	Hast thou marked the old way which wicked men have trodden?
verse	18	22	16	Which were cut down out of time, whose foundation was overflown with a flood:
verse	18	22	17	Which said unto God, Depart from us: and what can the Almighty do for them?
verse	18	22	18	@@Yet he filled their houses with good @9things:@7 but the counsel of the wicked is far from me.
verse	18	22	19	@@The righteous see @9it,@7 and are glad: and the innocent laugh them to scorn.
verse	18	22	20	Whereas our substance is not cut down, but the remnant of them the fire consumeth.
verse	18	22	21	Acquaint now thyself with him, and be at peace: thereby good shall come unto thee.
verse	18	22	22	Receive, I pray thee, the law from his mouth, and lay up his words in thine heart.
verse	18	22	23	If thou return to the Almighty, thou shalt be built up, thou shalt put away iniquity far from thy tabernacles.
verse	18	22	24	@@Then shalt thou lay up gold as dust, and the @9gold@7 of Ophir as the stones of the brooks.
verse	18	22	25	Yea, the Almighty shall be thy defence, and thou shalt have plenty of silver.
verse	18	22	26	For then shalt thou have thy delight in the Almighty, and shalt lift up thy face unto God.
verse	18	22	27	Thou shalt make thy prayer unto him, and he shall hear thee, and thou shalt pay thy vows.
verse	18	22	28	Thou shalt also decree a thing, and it shall be established unto thee: and the light shall shine upon thy ways.
verse	18	22	29	@@When @9men@7 are cast down, then thou shalt say, @9There is@7 lifting up; and he shall save the humble person.
verse	18	22	30	He shall deliver the island of the innocent: and it is delivered by the pureness of thine hands.
verse	18	23	1	Then Job answered and said,
verse	18	23	2	@@Even to day @9is@7 my complaint bitter: my stroke is heavier than my groaning.
verse	18	23	3	@@Oh that I knew where I might find him! @9that@7 I might come @9even@7 to his seat!
verse	18	23	4	@@I would order @9my@7 cause before him, and fill my mouth with arguments.
verse	18	23	5	@@I would know the words @9which@7 he would answer me, and understand what he would say unto me.
verse	18	23	6	@@Will he plead against me with @9his@7 great power? No; but he would put @9strength@7 in me.
verse	18	23	7	There the righteous might dispute with him; so should I be delivered for ever from my judge.
verse	18	23	8	@@Behold, I go forward, but he @9is@7 not @9there;@7 and backward, but I cannot perceive him:
verse	18	23	9	@@On the left hand, where he doth work, but I cannot behold @9him:@7 he hideth himself on the right hand, that I cannot see @9him: @7
verse	18	23	10	@@But he knoweth the way that I take: @9when@7 he hath tried me, I shall come forth as gold.
verse	18	23	11	My foot hath held his steps, his way have I kept, and not declined.
verse	18	23	12	@@Neither have I gone back from the commandment of his lips; I have esteemed the words of his mouth more than my necessary @9food. @7
verse	18	23	13	@@But he @9is@7 in one @9mind,@7 and who can turn him? and @9what@7 his soul desireth, even @9that@7 he doeth.
verse	18	23	14	@@For he performeth @9the thing that is@7 appointed for me: and many such @9things are@7 with him.
verse	18	23	15	Therefore am I troubled at his presence: when I consider, I am afraid of him.
verse	18	23	16	For God maketh my heart soft, and the Almighty troubleth me:
verse	18	23	17	@@Because I was not cut off before the darkness, @9neither@7 hath he covered the darkness from my face.
verse	18	24	1	Why, seeing times are not hidden from the Almighty, do they that know him not see his days?
verse	18	24	2	@@@9Some@7 remove the landmarks; they violently take away flocks, and feed @9thereof. @7
verse	18	24	3	They drive away the ass of the fatherless, they take the widow's ox for a pledge.
verse	18	24	4	They turn the needy out of the way: the poor of the earth hide themselves together.
verse	18	24	5	@@Behold, @9as@7 wild asses in the desert, go they forth to their work; rising betimes for a prey: the wilderness @9yieldeth@7 food for them @9and@7 for @9their@7 children.
verse	18	24	6	@@They reap @9every one@7 his corn in the field: and they gather the vintage of the wicked.
verse	18	24	7	@@They cause the naked to lodge without clothing, that @9they have@7 no covering in the cold.
verse	18	24	8	They are wet with the showers of the mountains, and embrace the rock for want of a shelter.
verse	18	24	9	They pluck the fatherless from the breast, and take a pledge of the poor.
verse	18	24	10	@@They cause @9him@7 to go naked without clothing, and they take away the sheaf @9from@7 the hungry;
verse	18	24	11	@@@9Which@7 make oil within their walls, @9and@7 tread @9their@7 winepresses, and suffer thirst.
verse	18	24	12	@@Men groan from out of the city, and the soul of the wounded crieth out: yet God layeth not folly @9to them. @7
verse	18	24	13	They are of those that rebel against the light; they know not the ways thereof, nor abide in the paths thereof.
verse	18	24	14	The murderer rising with the light killeth the poor and needy, and in the night is as a thief.
verse	18	24	15	@@The eye also of the adulterer waiteth for the twilight, saying, No eye shall see me: and disguiseth @9his@7 face.
verse	18	24	16	@@In the dark they dig through houses, @9which@7 they had marked for themselves in the daytime: they know not the light.
verse	18	24	17	@@For the morning @9is@7 to them even as the shadow of death: if @9one@7 know @9them, they are in@7 the terrors of the shadow of death.
verse	18	24	18	@@He @9is@7 swift as the waters; their portion is cursed in the earth: he beholdeth not the way of the vineyards.
verse	18	24	19	@@Drought and heat consume the snow waters: @9so doth@7 the grave @9those which@7 have sinned.
verse	18	24	20	The womb shall forget him; the worm shall feed sweetly on him; he shall be no more remembered; and wickedness shall be broken as a tree.
verse	18	24	21	@@He evil entreateth the barren that @9beareth@7 not: and doeth not good to the widow.
verse	18	24	22	@@He draweth also the mighty with his power: he riseth up, and no @9man@7 is sure of life.
verse	18	24	23	@@@9Though@7 it be given him @9to be@7 in safety, whereon he resteth; yet his eyes @9are@7 upon their ways.
verse	18	24	24	@@They are exalted for a little while, but are gone and brought low; they are taken out of the way as all @9other,@7 and cut off as the tops of the ears of corn.
verse	18	24	25	@@And if @9it be@7 not @9so@7 now, who will make me a liar, and make my speech nothing worth?
verse	18	25	1	Then answered Bildad the Shuhite, and said,
verse	18	25	2	@@Dominion and fear @9are@7 with him, he maketh peace in his high places.
verse	18	25	3	Is there any number of his armies? and upon whom doth not his light arise?
verse	18	25	4	@@How then can man be justified with God? or how can he be clean @9that is@7 born of a woman?
verse	18	25	5	Behold even to the moon, and it shineth not; yea, the stars are not pure in his sight.
verse	18	25	6	@@How much less man, @9that is@7 a worm? and the son of man, @9which is@7 a worm?
verse	18	26	1	But Job answered and said,
verse	18	26	2	@@How hast thou helped @9him that is@7 without power? @9how@7 savest thou the arm @9that hath@7 no strength?
verse	18	26	3	@@How hast thou counseled @9him that hath@7 no wisdom? and @9how@7 hast thou plentifully declared the thing as it is?
verse	18	26	4	To whom hast thou uttered words? and whose spirit came from thee?
verse	18	26	5	@@Dead @9things@7 are formed from under the waters, and the inhabitants thereof.
verse	18	26	6	@@Hell @9is@7 naked before him, and destruction hath no covering.
verse	18	26	7	@@He stretcheth out the north over the empty place, @9and@7 hangeth the earth upon nothing.
verse	18	26	8	He bindeth up the waters in his thick clouds; and the cloud is not rent under them.
verse	18	26	9	@@He holdeth back the face of his throne, @9and@7 spreadeth his cloud upon it.
verse	18	26	10	He hath compassed the waters with bounds, until the day and night come to an end.
verse	18	26	11	The pillars of heaven tremble and are astonished at his reproof.
verse	18	26	12	He divideth the sea with his power, and by his understanding he smiteth through the proud.
verse	18	26	13	By his spirit he hath garnished the heavens; his hand hath formed the crooked serpent.
verse	18	26	14	@@Lo, these @9are@7 parts of his ways: but how little a portion is heard of him? but the thunder of his power who can understand?
verse	18	27	1	Moreover Job continued his parable, and said,
verse	18	27	2	@@@9As@7 God liveth, @9who@7 hath taken away my judgment; and the Almighty, @9who@7 hath vexed my soul;
verse	18	27	3	@@All the while my breath @9is@7 in me, and the spirit of God @9is@7 in my nostrils;
verse	18	27	4	My lips shall not speak wickedness, nor my tongue utter deceit.
verse	18	27	5	God forbid that I should justify you: till I die I will not remove mine integrity from me.
verse	18	27	6	@@My righteousness I hold fast, and will not let it go: my heart shall not reproach @9me@7 so long as I live.
verse	18	27	7	Let mine enemy be as the wicked, and he that riseth up against me as the unrighteous.
verse	18	27	8	@@For what @9is@7 the hope of the hypocrite, though he hath gained, when God taketh away his soul?
verse	18	27	9	Will God hear his cry when trouble cometh upon him?
verse	18	27	10	Will he delight himself in the Almighty? will he always call upon God?
verse	18	27	11	@@I will teach you by the hand of God: @9that@7 which @9is@7 with the Almighty will I not conceal.
verse	18	27	12	@@Behold, all ye yourselves have seen @9it;@7 why then are ye thus altogether vain?
verse	18	27	13	@@This @9is@7 the portion of a wicked man with God, and the heritage of oppressors, @9which@7 they shall receive of the Almighty.
verse	18	27	14	@@If his children be multiplied, @9it is@7 for the sword: and his offspring shall not be satisfied with bread.
