verse	18	35	9	@@By reason of the multitude of oppressions they make @9the oppressed@7 to cry: they cry out by reason of the arm of the mighty.
verse	18	35	10	@@But none saith, Where @9is@7 God my maker, who giveth songs in the night;
verse	18	35	11	Who teacheth us more than the beasts of the earth, and maketh us wiser than the fowls of heaven?
verse	18	35	12	There they cry, but none giveth answer, because of the pride of evil men.
verse	18	35	13	Surely God will not hear vanity, neither will the Almighty regard it.
verse	18	35	14	@@Although thou sayest thou shalt not see him, @9yet@7 judgment @9is@7 before him; therefore trust thou in him.
verse	18	35	15	@@But now, because @9it is@7 not @9so,@7 he hath visited in his anger; yet he knoweth @9it@7 not in great extremity:
verse	18	35	16	Therefore doth Job open his mouth in vain; he multiplieth words without knowledge.
verse	18	36	1	Elihu also proceeded, and said,
verse	18	36	2	@@Suffer me a little, and I will shew thee that @9I have@7 yet to speak on God's behalf.
verse	18	36	3	I will fetch my knowledge from afar, and will ascribe righteousness to my Maker.
verse	18	36	4	@@For truly my words @9shall@7 not @9be@7 false: he that is perfect in knowledge @9is@7 with thee.
verse	18	36	5	@@Behold, God @9is@7 mighty, and despiseth not @9any: he is@7 mighty in strength @9and@7 wisdom.
verse	18	36	6	He preserveth not the life of the wicked: but giveth right to the poor.
verse	18	36	7	@@He withdraweth not his eyes from the righteous: but with kings @9are they@7 on the throne; yea, he doth establish them for ever, and they are exalted.
verse	18	36	8	@@And if @9they be@7 bound in fetters, @9and@7 be holden in cords of affliction;
verse	18	36	9	Then he sheweth them their work, and their transgressions that they have exceeded.
verse	18	36	10	He openeth also their ear to discipline, and commandeth that they return from iniquity.
verse	18	36	11	@@If they obey and serve @9him,@7 they shall spend their days in prosperity, and their years in pleasures.
verse	18	36	12	But if they obey not, they shall perish by the sword, and they shall die without knowledge.
verse	18	36	13	But the hypocrites in heart heap up wrath: they cry not when he bindeth them.
verse	18	36	14	@@They die in youth, and their life @9is@7 among the unclean.
verse	18	36	15	He delivereth the poor in his affliction, and openeth their ears in oppression.
verse	18	36	16	@@Even so would he have removed thee out of the strait @9into@7 a broad place, where @9there is@7 no straitness; and that which @9should be@7 set on thy table should be full of fatness.
verse	18	36	17	@@But thou hast fulfilled the judgment of the wicked: judgment and justice take hold @9on thee. @7
verse	18	36	18	@@Because @9there is@7 wrath, @9beware@7 lest he take thee away with @9his@7 stroke: then a great ransom cannot deliver thee.
verse	18	36	19	@@Will he esteem thy riches? @9no,@7 not gold, nor all the forces of strength.
verse	18	36	20	Desire not the night, when people are cut off in their place.
verse	18	36	21	Take heed, regard not iniquity: for this hast thou chosen rather than affliction.
verse	18	36	22	Behold, God exalteth by his power: who teacheth like him?
verse	18	36	23	Who hath enjoined him his way? or who can say, Thou hast wrought iniquity?
verse	18	36	24	Remember that thou magnify his work, which men behold.
verse	18	36	25	@@Every man may see it; man may behold @9it@7 afar off.
verse	18	36	26	@@Behold, God @9is@7 great, and we know @9him@7 not, neither can the number of his years be searched out.
verse	18	36	27	For he maketh small the drops of water: they pour down rain according to the vapour thereof:
verse	18	36	28	@@Which the clouds do drop @9and@7 distil upon man abundantly.
verse	18	36	29	@@Also can @9any@7 understand the spreadings of the clouds, @9or@7 the noise of his tabernacle?
verse	18	36	30	Behold, he spreadeth his light upon it, and covereth the bottom of the sea.
verse	18	36	31	For by them judgeth he the people; he giveth meat in abundance.
verse	18	36	32	@@With clouds he covereth the light; and commandeth it @9not to shine@7 by @9the cloud@7 that cometh betwixt.
verse	18	36	33	The noise thereof sheweth concerning it, the cattle also concerning the vapour.
verse	18	37	1	At this also my heart trembleth, and is moved out of his place.
verse	18	37	2	@@Hear attentively the noise of his voice, and the sound @9that@7 goeth out of his mouth.
verse	18	37	3	He directeth it under the whole heaven, and his lightning unto the ends of the earth.
verse	18	37	4	After it a voice roareth: he thundereth with the voice of his excellency; and he will not stay them when his voice is heard.
verse	18	37	5	God thundereth marvellously with his voice; great things doeth he, which we cannot comprehend.
verse	18	37	6	@@For he saith to the snow, Be thou @9on@7 the earth; likewise to the small rain, and to the great rain of his strength.
verse	18	37	7	He sealeth up the hand of every man; that all men may know his work.
verse	18	37	8	Then the beasts go into dens, and remain in their places.
verse	18	37	9	Out of the south cometh the whirlwind: and cold out of the north.
verse	18	37	10	By the breath of God frost is given: and the breadth of the waters is straitened.
verse	18	37	11	Also by watering he wearieth the thick cloud: he scattereth his bright cloud:
verse	18	37	12	And it is turned round about by his counsels: that they may do whatsoever he commandeth them upon the face of the world in the earth.
verse	18	37	13	He causeth it to come, whether for correction, or for his land, or for mercy.
verse	18	37	14	Hearken unto this, O Job: stand still, and consider the wondrous works of God.
verse	18	37	15	Dost thou know when God disposed them, and caused the light of his cloud to shine?
verse	18	37	16	Dost thou know the balancings of the clouds, the wondrous works of him which is perfect in knowledge?
verse	18	37	17	@@How thy garments @9are@7 warm, when he quieteth the earth by the south @9wind? @7
verse	18	37	18	@@Hast thou with him spread out the sky, @9which is@7 strong, @9and@7 as a molten looking glass?
verse	18	37	19	@@Teach us what we shall say unto him; @9for@7 we cannot order @9our speech@7 by reason of darkness.
verse	18	37	20	Shall it be told him that I speak? if a man speak, surely he shall be swallowed up.
verse	18	37	21	@@And now @9men@7 see not the bright light which is in the clouds: but the wind passeth, and cleanseth them.
verse	18	37	22	Fair weather cometh out of the north: with God is terrible majesty.
verse	18	37	23	@@@9Touching@7 the Almighty, we cannot find him out: @9he is@7 excellent in power, and in judgment, and in plenty of justice: he will not afflict.
verse	18	37	24	@@Men do therefore fear him: he respecteth not any @9that are@7 wise of heart.
verse	18	38	1	Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind, and said,
verse	18	38	2	@@Who @9is@7 this that darkeneth counsel by words without knowledge?
verse	18	38	3	Gird up now thy loins like a man; for I will demand of thee, and answer thou me.
verse	18	38	4	Where wast thou when I laid the foundations of the earth? declare, if thou hast understanding.
verse	18	38	5	Who hath laid the measures thereof, if thou knowest? or who hath stretched the line upon it?
verse	18	38	6	Whereupon are the foundations thereof fastened? or who laid the corner stone thereof;
verse	18	38	7	When the morning stars sang together, and all the sons of God shouted for joy?
verse	18	38	8	@@Or @9who@7 shut up the sea with doors, when it brake forth, @9as if@7 it had issued out of the womb?
verse	18	38	9	When I made the cloud the garment thereof, and thick darkness a swaddlingband for it,
verse	18	38	10	@@And brake up for it my decreed @9place,@7 and set bars and doors,
verse	18	38	11	And said, Hitherto shalt thou come, but no further: and here shall thy proud waves be stayed?
verse	18	38	12	@@Hast thou commanded the morning since thy days; @9and@7 caused the dayspring to know his place;
verse	18	38	13	That it might take hold of the ends of the earth, that the wicked might be shaken out of it?
verse	18	38	14	@@It is turned as clay @9to@7 the seal; and they stand as a garment.
verse	18	38	15	And from the wicked their light is withholden, and the high arm shall be broken.
verse	18	38	16	Hast thou entered into the springs of the sea? or hast thou walked in the search of the depth?
verse	18	38	17	Have the gates of death been opened unto thee? or hast thou seen the doors of the shadow of death?
verse	18	38	18	Hast thou perceived the breadth of the earth? declare if thou knowest it all.
verse	18	38	19	@@Where @9is@7 the way @9where@7 light dwelleth? and @9as for@7 darkness, where @9is@7 the place thereof,
verse	18	38	20	@@That thou shouldest take it to the bound thereof, and that thou shouldest know the paths @9to@7 the house thereof?
verse	18	38	21	@@Knowest thou @9it,@7 because thou wast then born? or @9because@7 the number of thy days @9is@7 great?
verse	18	38	22	Hast thou entered into the treasures of the snow? or hast thou seen the treasures of the hail,
verse	18	38	23	Which I have reserved against the time of trouble, against the day of battle and war?
verse	18	38	24	@@By what way is the light parted, @9which@7 scattereth the east wind upon the earth?
verse	18	38	25	Who hath divided a watercourse for the overflowing of waters, or a way for the lightning of thunder;
verse	18	38	26	@@To cause it to rain on the earth, @9where@7 no man @9is; on@7 the wilderness, wherein @9there is@7 no man;
verse	18	38	27	@@To satisfy the desolate and waste @9ground;@7 and to cause the bud of the tender herb to spring forth?
verse	18	38	28	Hath the rain a father? or who hath begotten the drops of dew?
verse	18	38	29	Out of whose womb came the ice? and the hoary frost of heaven, who hath gendered it?
verse	18	38	30	@@The waters are hid as @9with@7 a stone, and the face of the deep is frozen.
verse	18	38	31	Canst thou bind the sweet influences of Pleiades, or loose the bands of Orion?
verse	18	38	32	Canst thou bring forth Mazzaroth in his season? or canst thou guide Arcturus with his sons?
verse	18	38	33	Knowest thou the ordinances of heaven? canst thou set the dominion thereof in the earth?
verse	18	38	34	Canst thou lift up thy voice to the clouds, that abundance of waters may cover thee?
verse	18	38	35	@@Canst thou send lightnings, that they may go, and say unto thee, Here we @9are? @7
verse	18	38	36	Who hath put wisdom in the inward parts? or who hath given understanding to the heart?
verse	18	38	37	Who can number the clouds in wisdom? or who can stay the bottles of heaven,
verse	18	38	38	When the dust groweth into hardness, and the clods cleave fast together?
verse	18	38	39	Wilt thou hunt the prey for the lion? or fill the appetite of the young lions,
verse	18	38	40	@@When they couch in @9their@7 dens, @9and@7 abide in the covert to lie in wait?
verse	18	38	41	Who provideth for the raven his food? when his young ones cry unto God, they wander for lack of meat.
verse	18	39	1	@@Knowest thou the time when the wild goats of the rock bring forth? @9or@7 canst thou mark when the hinds do calve?
verse	18	39	2	@@Canst thou number the months @9that@7 they fulfil? or knowest thou the time when they bring forth?
verse	18	39	3	They bow themselves, they bring forth their young ones, they cast out their sorrows.
verse	18	39	4	Their young ones are in good liking, they grow up with corn; they go forth, and return not unto them.
verse	18	39	5	Who hath sent out the wild ass free? or who hath loosed the bands of the wild ass?
verse	18	39	6	Whose house I have made the wilderness, and the barren land his dwellings.
verse	18	39	7	He scorneth the multitude of the city, neither regardeth he the crying of the driver.
verse	18	39	8	@@The range of the mountains @9is@7 his pasture, and he searcheth after every green thing.
verse	18	39	9	Will the unicorn be willing to serve thee, or abide by thy crib?
verse	18	39	10	Canst thou bind the unicorn with his band in the furrow? or will he harrow the valleys after thee?
verse	18	39	11	@@Wilt thou trust him, because his strength @9is@7 great? or wilt thou leave thy labour to him?
verse	18	39	12	@@Wilt thou believe him, that he will bring home thy seed, and gather @9it into@7 thy barn?
verse	18	39	13	@@@9Gavest thou@7 the goodly wings unto the peacocks? or wings and feathers unto the ostrich?
verse	18	39	14	Which leaveth her eggs in the earth, and warmeth them in dust,
verse	18	39	15	And forgetteth that the foot may crush them, or that the wild beast may break them.
verse	18	39	16	@@She is hardened against her young ones, as though @9they were@7 not hers: her labour is in vain without fear;
verse	18	39	17	Because God hath deprived her of wisdom, neither hath he imparted to her understanding.
verse	18	39	18	What time she lifteth up herself on high, she scorneth the horse and his rider.
verse	18	39	19	Hath thou given the horse strength? hast thou clothed his neck with thunder?
verse	18	39	20	@@Canst thou make him afraid as a grasshopper? the glory of his nostrils @9is@7 terrible.
verse	18	39	21	@@He paweth in the valley, and rejoiceth in @9his@7 strength: he goeth on to meet the armed men.
verse	18	39	22	He mocketh at fear, and is not affrighted; neither turneth he back from the sword.
verse	18	39	23	The quiver rattleth against him, the glittering spear and the shield.
verse	18	39	24	@@He swalloweth the ground with fierceness and rage: neither believeth he that @9it is@7 the sound of the trumpet.
verse	18	39	25	He saith among the trumpets, Ha, ha; and he smelleth the battle afar off, the thunder of the captains, and the shouting.
verse	18	39	26	@@Doth the hawk fly by thy wisdom, @9and@7 stretch her wings toward the south?
verse	18	39	27	Doth the eagle mount up at thy command, and make her nest on high?
verse	18	39	28	She dwelleth and abideth on the rock, upon the crag of the rock, and the strong place.
verse	18	39	29	@@From thence she seeketh the prey, @9and@7 her eyes behold afar off.
verse	18	39	30	@@Her young ones also suck up blood: and where the slain @9are,@7 there @9is@7 she.
verse	18	40	1	Moreover the LORD answered Job, and said,
verse	18	40	2	@@Shall he that contendeth with the Almighty instruct @9him?@7 he that reproveth God, let him answer it.
verse	18	40	3	Then Job answered the LORD, and said,
verse	18	40	4	Behold, I am vile; what shall I answer thee? I will lay mine hand upon my mouth.
verse	18	40	5	Once have I spoken; but I will not answer: yea, twice; but I will proceed no further.
verse	18	40	6	Then answered the LORD unto Job out of the whirlwind, and said,
verse	18	40	7	Gird up thy loins now like a man: I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.
verse	18	40	8	Wilt thou also disannul my judgment? wilt thou condemn me, that thou mayest be righteous?
verse	18	40	9	Hast thou an arm like God? or canst thou thunder with a voice like him?
verse	18	40	10	@@Deck thyself now @9with@7 majesty and excellency; and array thyself with glory and beauty.
verse	18	40	11	@@Cast abroad the rage of thy wrath: and behold every one @9that is@7 proud, and abase him.
verse	18	40	12	@@Look on every one @9that is@7 proud, @9and@7 bring him low; and tread down the wicked in their place.
verse	18	40	13	@@Hide them in the dust together; @9and@7 bind their faces in secret.
verse	18	40	14	Then will I also confess unto thee that thine own right hand can save thee.
verse	18	40	15	Behold now behemoth, which I made with thee; he eateth grass as an ox.
verse	18	40	16	@@Lo now, his strength @9is@7 in his loins, and his force @9is@7 in the navel of his belly.
verse	18	40	17	He moveth his tail like a cedar: the sinews of his stones are wrapped together.
verse	18	40	18	@@His bones @9are as@7 strong pieces of brass; his bones @9are@7 like bars of iron.
verse	18	40	19	@@He @9is@7 the chief of the ways of God: he that made him can make his sword to approach @9unto him. @7
verse	18	40	20	Surely the mountains bring him forth food, where all the beasts of the field play.
verse	18	40	21	He lieth under the shady trees, in the covert of the reed, and fens.
verse	18	40	22	@@The shady trees cover him @9with@7 their shadow; the willows of the brook compass him about.
verse	18	40	23	@@Behold, he drinketh up a river, @9and@7 hasteth not: he trusteth that he can draw up Jordan into his mouth.
verse	18	40	24	@@He taketh it with his eyes: @9his@7 nose pierceth through snares.
verse	18	41	1	@@Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook? or his tongue with a cord @9which@7 thou lettest down?
verse	18	41	2	Canst thou put an hook into his nose? or bore his jaw through with a thorn?
verse	18	41	3	@@Will he make many supplications unto thee? will he speak soft @9words@7 unto thee?
verse	18	41	4	Will he make a covenant with thee? wilt thou take him for a servant for ever?
verse	18	41	5	@@Wilt thou play with him as @9with@7 a bird? or wilt thou bind him for thy maidens?
verse	18	41	6	Shall the companions make a banquet of him? shall they part him among the merchants?
verse	18	41	7	Canst thou fill his skin with barbed irons? or his head with fish spears?
verse	18	41	8	Lay thine hand upon him, remember the battle, do no more.
verse	18	41	9	@@Behold, the hope of him is in vain: shall not @9one@7 be cast down even at the sight of him?
verse	18	41	10	@@None @9is so@7 fierce that dare stir him up: who then is able to stand before me?
verse	18	41	11	@@Who hath prevented me, that I should repay @9him? whatsoever is@7 under the whole heaven is mine.
verse	18	41	12	I will not conceal his parts, nor his power, nor his comely proportion.
verse	18	41	13	@@Who can discover the face of his garment? @9or@7 who can come @9to him@7 with his double bridle?
verse	18	41	14	@@Who can open the doors of his face? his teeth @9are@7 terrible round about.
verse	18	41	15	@@@9His@7 scales @9are his@7 pride, shut up together @9as with@7 a close seal.
verse	18	41	16	One is so near to another, that no air can come between them.
verse	18	41	17	They are joined one to another, they stick together, that they cannot be sundered.
verse	18	41	18	@@By his neesings a light doth shine, and his eyes @9are@7 like the eyelids of the morning.
verse	18	41	19	@@Out of his mouth go burning lamps, @9and@7 sparks of fire leap out.
verse	18	41	20	@@Out of his nostrils goeth smoke, as @9out@7 of a seething pot or caldron.
verse	18	41	21	His breath kindleth coals, and a flame goeth out of his mouth.
verse	18	41	22	In his neck remaineth strength, and sorrow is turned into joy before him.
verse	18	41	23	The flakes of his flesh are joined together: they are firm in themselves; they cannot be moved.
verse	18	41	24	@@His heart is as firm as a stone; yea, as hard as a piece of the nether @9millstone. @7
verse	18	41	25	When he raiseth up himself, the mighty are afraid: by reason of breakings they purify themselves.
verse	18	41	26	The sword of him that layeth at him cannot hold: the spear, the dart, nor the habergeon.
verse	18	41	27	@@He esteemeth iron as straw, @9and@7 brass as rotten wood.
verse	18	41	28	The arrow cannot make him flee: slingstones are turned with him into stubble.
verse	18	41	29	Darts are counted as stubble: he laugheth at the shaking of a spear.
verse	18	41	30	@@Sharp stones @9are@7 under him: he spreadeth sharp pointed things upon the mire.
verse	18	41	31	He maketh the deep to boil like a pot: he maketh the sea like a pot of ointment.
verse	18	41	32	@@He maketh a path to shine after him; @9one@7 would think the deep @9to be@7 hoary.
verse	18	41	33	Upon earth there is not his like, who is made without fear.
verse	18	41	34	@@He beholdeth all high @9things:@7 he @9is@7 a king over all the children of pride.
verse	18	42	1	Then Job answered the LORD, and said,
verse	18	42	2	@@I know that thou canst do every @9thing,@7 and @9that@7 no thought can be withholden from thee.
verse	18	42	3	@@Who @9is@7 he that hideth counsel without knowledge? therefore have I uttered that I understood not; things too wonderful for me, which I knew not.
verse	18	42	4	Hear, I beseech thee, and I will speak: I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.
verse	18	42	5	I have heard of thee by the hearing of the ear: but now mine eye seeth thee.
verse	18	42	6	@@Wherefore I abhor @9myself,@7 and repent in dust and ashes.
verse	18	42	7	@@And it was @9so,@7 that after the LORD had spoken these words unto Job, the LORD said to Eliphaz the Temanite, My wrath is kindled against thee, and against thy two friends: for ye have not spoken of me @9the thing that is@7 right, as my servant Job @9hath. @7
verse	18	42	8	@@Therefore take unto you now seven bullocks and seven rams, and go to my servant Job, and offer up for yourselves a burnt offering; and my servant Job shall pray for you: for him will I accept: lest I deal with you @9after your@7 folly, in that ye have not spoken of me @9the thing which is@7 right, like my servant Job.
verse	18	42	9	@@So Eliphaz the Temanite and Bildad the Shuhite @9and@7 Zophar the Naamathite went, and did according as the LORD commanded them: the LORD also accepted Job.
verse	18	42	10	And the LORD turned the captivity of Job, when he prayed for his friends: also the LORD gave Job twice as much as he had before.
verse	18	42	11	Then came there unto him all his brethren, and all his sisters, and all they that had been of his acquaintance before, and did eat bread with him in his house: and they bemoaned him, and comforted him over all the evil that the LORD had brought upon him: every man also gave him a piece of money, and every one an earring of gold.
verse	18	42	12	So the LORD blessed the latter end of Job more than his beginning: for he had fourteen thousand sheep, and six thousand camels, and a thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand she asses.
verse	18	42	13	He had also seven sons and three daughters.
verse	18	42	14	And he called the name of the first, Jemima; and the name of the second, Kezia; and the name of the third, Keren-happuch.
verse	18	42	15	@@And in all the land were no women found @9so@7 fair as the daughters of Job: and their father gave them inheritance among their brethren.
verse	18	42	16	@@After this lived Job an hundred and forty years, and saw his sons, and his sons' sons, @9even@7 four generations.
verse	18	42	17	@@So Job died, @9being@7 old and full of days.
verse	19	1	1	@@Blessed @9is@7 the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.
verse	19	1	2	@@But his delight @9is@7 in the law of the LORD; and in his law doth he meditate day and night.
verse	19	1	3	And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.
verse	19	1	4	@@The ungodly @9are@7 not so: but @9are@7 like the chaff which the wind driveth away.
verse	19	1	5	Therefore the ungodly shall not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous.
verse	19	1	6	For the LORD knoweth the way of the righteous: but the way of the ungodly shall perish.
verse	19	2	1	Why do the heathen rage, and the people imagine a vain thing?
verse	19	2	2	@@The kings of the earth set themselves, and the rulers take counsel together, against the LORD, and against his anointed, @9saying,@7
verse	19	2	3	Let us break their bands asunder, and cast away their cords from us.
verse	19	2	4	He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh: the Lord shall have them in derision.
verse	19	2	5	Then shall he speak unto them in his wrath, and vex them in his sore displeasure.
verse	19	2	6	Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion.
verse	19	2	7	@@I will declare the decree: the LORD hath said unto me, Thou @9art@7 my Son; this day have I begotten thee.
verse	19	2	8	@@Ask of me, and I shall give @9thee@7 the heathen @9for@7 thine inheritance, and the uttermost parts of the earth @9for@7 thy possession.
verse	19	2	9	Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter's vessel.
verse	19	2	10	Be wise now therefore, O ye kings: be instructed, ye judges of the earth.
verse	19	2	11	Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling.
verse	19	2	12	@@Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and ye perish @9from@7 the way, when his wrath is kindled but a little. Blessed @9are@7 all they that put their trust in him.
pericope	19	3	1	A Psalm of David, when he fled from Absalom his son.
verse	19	3	1	@@LORD, how are they increased that trouble me! many @9are@7 they that rise up against me.
verse	19	3	2	@@Many @9there be@7 which say of my soul, @9There is@7 no help for him in God. Selah.
verse	19	3	3	@@But thou, O LORD, @9art@7 a shield for me; my glory, and the lifter up of mine head.
verse	19	3	4	I cried unto the LORD with my voice, and he heard me out of his holy hill. Selah.
verse	19	3	5	I laid me down and slept; I awaked; for the LORD sustained me.
verse	19	3	6	@@I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, that have set @9themselves@7 against me round about.
verse	19	3	7	@@Arise, O LORD; save me, O my God: for thou hast smitten all mine enemies @9upon@7 the cheek bone; thou hast broken the teeth of the ungodly.
verse	19	3	8	@@Salvation @9belongeth@7 unto the LORD: thy blessing @9is@7 upon thy people. Selah.
pericope	19	4	1	To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	4	1	@@Hear me when I call, O God of my righteousness: thou hast enlarged me @9when I was@7 in distress; have mercy upon me, and hear my prayer.
verse	19	4	2	@@O ye sons of men, how long @9will ye turn@7 my glory into shame? @9how long@7 will ye love vanity, @9and@7 seek after leasing? Selah.
verse	19	4	3	But know that the LORD hath set apart him that is godly for himself: the LORD will hear when I call unto him.
verse	19	4	4	Stand in awe, and sin not: commune with your own heart upon your bed, and be still. Selah.
verse	19	4	5	Offer the sacrifices of righteousness, and put your trust in the LORD.
verse	19	4	6	@@@9There be@7 many that say, Who will shew us @9any@7 good? LORD, lift thou up the light of thy countenance upon us.
verse	19	4	7	@@Thou hast put gladness in my heart, more than in the time @9that@7 their corn and their wine increased.
verse	19	4	8	I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, LORD, only makest me dwell in safety.
pericope	19	5	1	To the chief Musician upon Nehiloth, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	5	1	Give ear to my words, O LORD, consider my meditation.
verse	19	5	2	Hearken unto the voice of my cry, my King, and my God: for unto thee will I pray.
verse	19	5	3	@@My voice shalt thou hear in the morning, O LORD; in the morning will I direct @9my prayer@7 unto thee, and will look up.
verse	19	5	4	@@For thou @9art@7 not a God that hath pleasure in wickedness: neither shall evil dwell with thee.
verse	19	5	5	The foolish shall not stand in thy sight: thou hatest all workers of iniquity.
verse	19	5	6	Thou shalt destroy them that speak leasing: the LORD will abhor the bloody and deceitful man.
verse	19	5	7	@@But as for me, I will come @9into@7 thy house in the multitude of thy mercy: @9and@7 in thy fear will I worship toward thy holy temple.
verse	19	5	8	Lead me, O LORD, in thy righteousness because of mine enemies; make thy way straight before my face.
verse	19	5	9	@@For @9there is@7 no faithfulness in their mouth; their inward part @9is@7 very wickedness; their throat @9is@7 an open sepulchre; they flatter with their tongue.
verse	19	5	10	Destroy thou them, O God; let them fall by their own counsels; cast them out in the multitude of their transgressions; for they have rebelled against thee.
verse	19	5	11	But let all those that put their trust in thee rejoice: let them ever shout for joy, because thou defendest them: let them also that love thy name be joyful in thee.
verse	19	5	12	@@For thou, LORD, wilt bless the righteous; with favour wilt thou compass him as @9with@7 a shield.
pericope	19	6	1	To the chief Musician on Neginoth upon Sheminith, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	6	1	O LORD, rebuke me not in thine anger, neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.
verse	19	6	2	@@Have mercy upon me, O LORD; for I @9am@7 weak: O LORD, heal me; for my bones are vexed.
verse	19	6	3	My soul is also sore vexed: but thou, O LORD, how long?
verse	19	6	4	Return, O LORD, deliver my soul: oh save me for thy mercies' sake.
verse	19	6	5	@@For in death @9there is@7 no remembrance of thee: in the grave who shall give thee thanks?
verse	19	6	6	I am weary with my groaning; all the night make I my bed to swim; I water my couch with my tears.
verse	19	6	7	Mine eye is consumed because of grief; it waxeth old because of all mine enemies.
verse	19	6	8	Depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity; for the LORD hath heard the voice of my weeping.
verse	19	6	9	The LORD hath heard my supplication; the LORD will receive my prayer.
verse	19	6	10	@@Let all mine enemies be ashamed and sore vexed: let them return @9and@7 be ashamed suddenly.
pericope	19	7	1	Shiggaion of David, which he sang unto the LORD, concerning the words of Cush the Benjamite.
verse	19	7	1	O Lord my God, in thee do I put my trust: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me:
verse	19	7	2	@@Lest he tear my soul like a lion, rending @9it@7 in pieces, while @9there is@7 none to deliver.
verse	19	7	3	O LORD my God, if I have done this; if there be iniquity in my hands;
verse	19	7	4	If I have rewarded evil unto him that was at peace with me; (yea, I have delivered him that without cause is mine enemy:)
verse	19	7	5	@@Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take @9it;@7 yea, let him tread down my life upon the earth, and lay mine honour in the dust. Selah.
verse	19	7	6	@@Arise, O LORD, in thine anger, lift up thyself because of the rage of mine enemies: and awake for me @9to@7 the judgment @9that@7 thou hast commanded.
verse	19	7	7	So shall the congregation of the people compass thee about: for their sakes therefore return thou on high.
verse	19	7	8	@@The LORD shall judge the people: judge me, O LORD, according to my righteousness, and according to mine integrity @9that is@7 in me.
verse	19	7	9	Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end; but establish the just: for the righteous God trieth the hearts and reins.
verse	19	7	10	@@My defence @9is@7 of God, which saveth the upright in heart.
verse	19	7	11	@@God judgeth the righteous, and God is angry @9with the wicked@7 every day.
verse	19	7	12	If he turn not, he will whet his sword; he hath bent his bow, and made it ready.
verse	19	7	13	He hath also prepared for him the instruments of death; he ordaineth his arrows against the persecutors.
verse	19	7	14	Behold, he travaileth with iniquity, and hath conceived mischief, and brought forth falsehood.
verse	19	7	15	@@He made a pit, and digged it, and is fallen into the ditch @9which@7 he made.
verse	19	7	16	His mischief shall return upon his own head, and his violent dealing shall come down upon his own pate.
verse	19	7	17	I will praise the LORD according to his righteousness: and will sing praise to the name of the LORD most high.
pericope	19	8	1	To the chief Musician upon Gittith, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	8	1	@@O LORD our Lord, how excellent @9is@7 thy name in all the earth! who hast set thy glory above the heavens.
verse	19	8	2	Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings hast thou ordained strength because of thine enemies, that thou mightest still the enemy and the avenger.
verse	19	8	3	When I consider thy heavens, the work of thy fingers, the moon and the stars, which thou hast ordained;
verse	19	8	4	What is man, that thou art mindful of him? and the son of man, that thou visitest him?
verse	19	8	5	For thou hast made him a little lower than the angels, and hast crowned him with glory and honour.
verse	19	8	6	@@Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands; thou hast put all @9things@7 under his feet:
verse	19	8	7	All sheep and oxen, yea, and the beasts of the field;
verse	19	8	8	@@The fowl of the air, and the fish of the sea, @9and whatsoever@7 passeth through the paths of the seas.
verse	19	8	9	O LORD our Lord, how excellent is thy name in all the earth!
pericope	19	9	1	To the chief Musician upon Muth-labben, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	9	1	@@I will praise @9thee,@7 O LORD, with my whole heart; I will shew forth all thy marvellous works.
verse	19	9	2	I will be glad and rejoice in thee: I will sing praise to thy name, O thou most High.
verse	19	9	3	When mine enemies are turned back, they shall fall and perish at thy presence.
verse	19	9	4	For thou hast maintained my right and my cause; thou satest in the throne judging right.
verse	19	9	5	Thou hast rebuked the heathen, thou hast destroyed the wicked, thou hast put out their name for ever and ever.
verse	19	9	6	O thou enemy, destructions are come to a perpetual end: and thou hast destroyed cities; their memorial is perished with them.
verse	19	9	7	But the LORD shall endure for ever: he hath prepared his throne for judgment.
verse	19	9	8	And he shall judge the world in righteousness, he shall minister judgment to the people in uprightness.
verse	19	9	9	The LORD also will be a refuge for the oppressed, a refuge in times of trouble.
verse	19	9	10	And they that know thy name will put their trust in thee: for thou, LORD, hast not forsaken them that seek thee.
verse	19	9	11	Sing praises to the LORD, which dwelleth in Zion: declare among the people his doings.
verse	19	9	12	When he maketh inquisition for blood, he remembereth them: he forgetteth not the cry of the humble.
verse	19	9	13	@@Have mercy upon me, O LORD; consider my trouble @9which I suffer@7 of them that hate me, thou that liftest me up from the gates of death:
verse	19	9	14	That I may shew forth all thy praise in the gates of the daughter of Zion: I will rejoice in thy salvation.
verse	19	9	15	@@The heathen are sunk down in the pit @9that@7 they made: in the net which they hid is their own foot taken.
verse	19	9	16	@@The LORD is known @9by@7 the judgment @9which@7 he executeth: the wicked is snared in the work of his own hands. Higgaion. Selah.
verse	19	9	17	@@The wicked shall be turned into hell, @9and@7 all the nations that forget God.
verse	19	9	18	@@For the needy shall not alway be forgotten: the expectation of the poor shall @9not@7 perish for ever.
verse	19	9	19	Arise, O LORD; let not man prevail: let the heathen be judged in thy sight.
verse	19	9	20	@@Put them in fear, O LORD: @9that@7 the nations may know themselves @9to be but@7 men. Selah.
verse	19	10	1	@@Why standest thou afar off, O LORD? @9why@7 hidest thou @9thyself@7 in times of trouble?
verse	19	10	2	@@The wicked in @9his@7 pride doth persecute the poor: let them be taken in the devices that they have imagined.
verse	19	10	3	@@For the wicked boasteth of his heart's desire, and blesseth the covetous, @9whom@7 the LORD abhorreth.
verse	19	10	4	@@The wicked, through the pride of his countenance, will not seek @9after God:@7 God @9is@7 not in all his thoughts.
verse	19	10	5	@@His ways are always grievous; thy judgments @9are@7 far above out of his sight: @9as for@7 all his enemies, he puffeth at them.
verse	19	10	6	@@He hath said in his heart, I shall not be moved: for @9I shall@7 never @9be@7 in adversity.
verse	19	10	7	@@His mouth is full of cursing and deceit and fraud: under his tongue @9is@7 mischief and vanity.
verse	19	10	8	He sitteth in the lurking places of the villages: in the secret places doth he murder the innocent: his eyes are privily set against the poor.
verse	19	10	9	He lieth in wait secretly as a lion in his den: he lieth in wait to catch the poor: he doth catch the poor, when he draweth him into his net.
verse	19	10	10	@@He croucheth, @9and@7 humbleth himself, that the poor may fall by his strong ones.
verse	19	10	11	@@He hath said in his heart, God hath forgotten: he hideth his face; he will never see @9it.@7
verse	19	10	12	Arise, O LORD; O God, lift up thine hand: forget not the humble.
verse	19	10	13	@@Wherefore doth the wicked contemn God? he hath said in his heart, Thou wilt not require @9it.@7
verse	19	10	14	@@Thou hast seen @9it;@7 for thou beholdest mischief and spite, to requite @9it@7 with thy hand: the poor committeth himself unto thee; thou art the helper of the fatherless.
verse	19	10	15	@@Break thou the arm of the wicked and the evil @9man:@7 seek out his wickedness @9till@7 thou find none.
verse	19	10	16	@@The LORD @9is@7 King for ever and ever: the heathen are perished out of his land.
verse	19	10	17	LORD, thou hast heard the desire of the humble: thou wilt prepare their heart, thou wilt cause thine ear to hear:
verse	19	10	18	To judge the fatherless and the oppressed, that the man of the earth may no more oppress.
pericope	19	11	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	11	1	@@In the LORD put I my trust: How say ye to my soul, Flee @9as@7 a bird to your mountain?
verse	19	11	2	@@For, lo, the wicked bend @9their@7 bow, they make ready their arrow upon the string, that they may privily shoot at the upright in heart.
verse	19	11	3	If the foundations be destroyed, what can the righteous do?
verse	19	11	4	@@The LORD @9is@7 in his holy temple, the LORD'S throne @9is@7 in heaven: his eyes behold, his eyelids try, the children of men.
verse	19	11	5	The LORD trieth the righteous: but the wicked and him that loveth violence his soul hateth.
verse	19	11	6	@@Upon the wicked he shall rain snares, fire and brimstone, and an horrible tempest: @9this shall be@7 the portion of their cup.
verse	19	11	7	For the righteous LORD loveth righteousness; his countenance doth behold the upright.
pericope	19	12	1	To the chief Musician upon Sheminith, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	12	1	Help, LORD; for the godly man ceaseth; for the faithful fail from among the children of men.
verse	19	12	2	@@They speak vanity every one with his neighbour: @9with@7 flattering lips @9and@7 with a double heart do they speak.
verse	19	12	3	@@The LORD shall cut off all flattering lips, @9and@7 the tongue that speaketh proud things:
verse	19	12	4	@@Who have said, With our tongue will we prevail; our lips @9are@7 our own: who @9is@7 lord over us?
verse	19	12	5	@@For the oppression of the poor, for the sighing of the needy, now will I arise, saith the LORD; I will set @9him@7 in safety @9from him that@7 puffeth at him.
verse	19	12	6	@@The words of the LORD @9are@7 pure words: @9as@7 silver tried in a furnace of earth, purified seven times.
verse	19	12	7	Thou shalt keep them, O LORD, thou shalt preserve them from this generation for ever.
verse	19	12	8	The wicked walk on every side, when the vilest men are exalted.
pericope	19	13	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	13	1	How long wilt thou forget me, O LORD? for ever? how long wilt thou hide thy face from me?
verse	19	13	2	@@How long shall I take counsel in my soul, @9having@7 sorrow in my heart daily? how long shall mine enemy be exalted over me?
verse	19	13	3	@@Consider @9and@7 hear me, O LORD my God: lighten mine eyes, lest I sleep the @9sleep of@7 death;
verse	19	13	4	@@Lest mine enemy say, I have prevailed against him; @9and@7 those that trouble me rejoice when I am moved.
verse	19	13	5	But I have trusted in thy mercy; my heart shall rejoice in thy salvation.
verse	19	13	6	I will sing unto the LORD, because he hath dealt bountifully with me.
pericope	19	14	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	14	1	@@The fool hath said in his heart, @9There is@7 no God. They are corrupt, they have done abominable works, @9there is@7 none that doeth good.
verse	19	14	2	@@The LORD looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were any that did understand, @9and@7 seek God.
verse	19	14	3	@@They are all gone aside, they are @9all@7 together become filthy: @9there is@7 none that doeth good, no, not one.
verse	19	14	4	@@Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people @9as@7 they eat bread, and call not upon the LORD.
verse	19	14	5	@@There were they in great fear: for God @9is@7 in the generation of the righteous.
verse	19	14	6	@@Ye have shamed the counsel of the poor, because the LORD @9is@7 his refuge.
verse	19	14	7	@@Oh that the salvation of Israel @9were come@7 out of Zion! when the LORD bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, @9and@7 Israel shall be glad.
pericope	19	15	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	15	1	LORD, who shall abide in thy tabernacle? who shall dwell in thy holy hill?
verse	19	15	2	He that walketh uprightly, and worketh righteousness, and speaketh the truth in his heart.
verse	19	15	3	@@@9He that@7 backbiteth not with his tongue, nor doeth evil to his neighbour, nor taketh up a reproach against his neighbour.
verse	19	15	4	@@In whose eyes a vile person is contemned; but he honoureth them that fear the LORD. @9He that@7 sweareth to @9his own@7 hurt, and changeth not.
verse	19	15	5	@@@9He that@7 putteth not out his money to usury, nor taketh reward against the innocent. He that doeth these @9things@7 shall never be moved.
pericope	19	16	1	Michtam of David.
verse	19	16	1	Preserve me, O God: for in thee do I put my trust.
verse	19	16	2	@@@9O my soul,@7 thou hast said unto the LORD, Thou @9art@7 my Lord: my goodness @9extendeth@7 not to thee;
verse	19	16	3	@@@9But@7 to the saints that @9are@7 in the earth, and @9to@7 the excellent, in whom @9is@7 all my delight.
verse	19	16	4	@@Their sorrows shall be multiplied @9that@7 hasten @9after@7 another @9god:@7 their drink offerings of blood will I not offer, nor take up their names into my lips.
verse	19	16	5	@@The LORD @9is@7 the portion of mine inheritance and of my cup: thou maintainest my lot.
verse	19	16	6	@@The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant @9places;@7 yea, I have a goodly heritage.
verse	19	16	7	I will bless the LORD, who hath given me counsel: my reins also instruct me in the night seasons.
verse	19	16	8	@@I have set the LORD always before me: because @9he is@7 at my right hand, I shall not be moved.
verse	19	16	9	Therefore my heart is glad, and my glory rejoiceth: my flesh also shall rest in hope.
verse	19	16	10	For thou wilt not leave my soul in hell; neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption.
verse	19	16	11	@@Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence @9is@7 fulness of joy; at thy right hand @9there are@7 pleasures for evermore.
pericope	19	17	1	A Prayer of David.
verse	19	17	1	@@Hear the right, O LORD, attend unto my cry, give ear unto my prayer, @9that goeth@7 not out of feigned lips.
verse	19	17	2	Let my sentence come forth from thy presence; let thine eyes behold the things that are equal.
verse	19	17	3	@@Thou hast proved mine heart; thou hast visited @9me@7 in the night; thou hast tried me, @9and@7 shalt find nothing; I am purposed @9that@7 my mouth shall not transgress.
verse	19	17	4	@@Concerning the words of men, by the word of thy lips I have kept @9me from@7 the paths of the destroyer.
verse	19	17	5	@@Hold up my goings in thy paths, @9that@7 my footsteps slip not.
verse	19	17	6	@@I have called upon thee, for thou wilt hear me, O God: incline thine ear unto me, @9and hear@7 my speech.
verse	19	17	7	@@Shew thy marvellous lovingkindness, O thou that savest by thy right hand them which put their trust @9in thee@7 from those that rise up @9against them.@7
verse	19	17	8	Keep me as the apple of the eye, hide me under the shadow of thy wings,
verse	19	17	9	@@From the wicked that oppress me, @9from@7 my deadly enemies, @9who@7 compass me about.
verse	19	17	10	They are inclosed in their own fat: with their mouth they speak proudly.
verse	19	17	11	They have now compassed us in our steps: they have set their eyes bowing down to the earth;
verse	19	17	12	@@Like as a lion @9that@7 is greedy of his prey, and as it were a young lion lurking in secret places.
verse	19	17	13	@@Arise, O LORD, disappoint him, cast him down: deliver my soul from the wicked, @9which is@7 thy sword:
verse	19	17	14	@@From men @9which are@7 thy hand, O LORD, from men of the world, @9which have@7 their portion in @9this@7 life, and whose belly thou fillest with thy hid @9treasure:@7 they are full of children, and leave the rest of their @9substance@7 to their babes.
verse	19	17	15	As for me, I will behold thy face in righteousness: I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with thy likeness.
pericope	19	18	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day that the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,
verse	19	18	1	I will love thee, O LORD, my strength.
verse	19	18	2	@@The LORD @9is@7 my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, @9and@7 my high tower.
verse	19	18	3	@@I will call upon the LORD, @9who is worthy@7 to be praised: so shall I be saved from mine enemies.
verse	19	18	4	The sorrows of death compassed me, and the floods of ungodly men made me afraid.
verse	19	18	5	The sorrows of hell compassed me about: the snares of death prevented me.
verse	19	18	6	@@In my distress I called upon the LORD, and cried unto my God: he heard my voice out of his temple, and my cry came before him, @9even@7 into his ears.
verse	19	18	7	Then the earth shook and trembled; the foundations also of the hills moved and were shaken, because he was wroth.
verse	19	18	8	There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.
verse	19	18	9	@@He bowed the heavens also, and came down: and darkness @9was@7 under his feet.
verse	19	18	10	And he rode upon a cherub, and did fly: yea, he did fly upon the wings of the wind.
verse	19	18	11	@@He made darkness his secret place; his pavilion round about him @9were@7 dark waters @9and@7 thick clouds of the skies.
verse	19	18	12	@@At the brightness @9that was@7 before him his thick clouds passed, hail @9stones@7 and coals of fire.
verse	19	18	13	@@The LORD also thundered in the heavens, and the Highest gave his voice; hail @9stones@7 and coals of fire.
verse	19	18	14	Yea, he sent out his arrows, and scattered them; and he shot out lightnings, and discomfited them.
verse	19	18	15	Then the channels of waters were seen, and the foundations of the world were discovered at thy rebuke, O LORD, at the blast of the breath of thy nostrils.
verse	19	18	16	He sent from above, he took me, he drew me out of many waters.
verse	19	18	17	He delivered me from my strong enemy, and from them which hated me: for they were too strong for me.
verse	19	18	18	They prevented me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD was my stay.
verse	19	18	19	He brought me forth also into a large place; he delivered me, because he delighted in me.
verse	19	18	20	The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness; according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.
verse	19	18	21	For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.
verse	19	18	22	@@For all his judgments @9were@7 before me, and I did not put away his statutes from me.
verse	19	18	23	I was also upright before him, and I kept myself from mine iniquity.
verse	19	18	24	Therefore hath the LORD recompensed me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight.
verse	19	18	25	With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful; with an upright man thou wilt shew thyself upright;
verse	19	18	26	With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure; and with the froward thou wilt shew thyself froward.
verse	19	18	27	For thou wilt save the afflicted people; but wilt bring down high looks.
verse	19	18	28	For thou wilt light my candle: the LORD my God will enlighten my darkness.
verse	19	18	29	For by thee I have run through a troop; and by my God have I leaped over a wall.
verse	19	18	30	@@@9As for@7 God, his way @9is@7 perfect: the word of the LORD is tried: he @9is@7 a buckler to all those that trust in him.
verse	19	18	31	@@For who @9is@7 God save the LORD? or who @9is@7 a rock save our God?
verse	19	18	32	@@@9It is@7 God that girdeth me with strength, and maketh my way perfect.
verse	19	18	33	@@He maketh my feet like hinds' @9feet,@7 and setteth me upon my high places.
verse	19	18	34	He teacheth my hands to war, so that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.
verse	19	18	35	Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy right hand hath holden me up, and thy gentleness hath made me great.
verse	19	18	36	Thou hast enlarged my steps under me, that my feet did not slip.
verse	19	18	37	I have pursued mine enemies, and overtaken them: neither did I turn again till they were consumed.
verse	19	18	38	I have wounded them that they were not able to rise: they are fallen under my feet.
verse	19	18	39	For thou hast girded me with strength unto the battle: thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me.
verse	19	18	40	Thou hast also given me the necks of mine enemies; that I might destroy them that hate me.
verse	19	18	41	@@They cried, but @9there was@7 none to save @9them: even@7 unto the LORD, but he answered them not.
verse	19	18	42	Then did I beat them small as the dust before the wind: I did cast them out as the dirt in the streets.
verse	19	18	43	@@Thou hast delivered me from the strivings of the people; @9and@7 thou hast made me the head of the heathen: a people @9whom@7 I have not known shall serve me.
verse	19	18	44	As soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me: the strangers shall submit themselves unto me.
verse	19	18	45	The strangers shall fade away, and be afraid out of their close places.
verse	19	18	46	@@The LORD liveth; and blessed @9be@7 my rock; and let the God of my salvation be exalted.
verse	19	18	47	@@@9It is@7 God that avengeth me, and subdueth the people under me.
verse	19	18	48	He delivereth me from mine enemies: yea, thou liftest me up above those that rise up against me: thou hast delivered me from the violent man.
verse	19	18	49	Therefore will I give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the heathen, and sing praises unto thy name.
verse	19	18	50	Great deliverance giveth he to his king; and sheweth mercy to his anointed, to David, and to his seed for evermore.
pericope	19	19	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	19	1	The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.
verse	19	19	2	Day unto day uttereth speech, and night unto night sheweth knowledge.
verse	19	19	3	@@@9There is@7 no speech nor language, @9where@7 their voice is not heard.
verse	19	19	4	Their line is gone out through all the earth, and their words to the end of the world. In them hath he set a tabernacle for the sun,
verse	19	19	5	@@Which @9is@7 as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber, @9and@7 rejoiceth as a strong man to run a race.
verse	19	19	6	@@His going forth @9is@7 from the end of the heaven, and his circuit unto the ends of it: and there is nothing hid from the heat thereof.
verse	19	19	7	@@The law of the LORD @9is@7 perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of the LORD @9is@7 sure, making wise the simple.
verse	19	19	8	@@The statutes of the LORD @9are@7 right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the LORD @9is@7 pure, enlightening the eyes.
verse	19	19	9	@@The fear of the LORD @9is@7 clean, enduring for ever: the judgments of the LORD @9are@7 true @9and@7 righteous altogether.
verse	19	19	10	@@More to be desired @9are they@7 than gold, yea, than much fine gold: sweeter also than honey and the honeycomb.
verse	19	19	11	@@Moreover by them is thy servant warned: @9and@7 in keeping of them @9there is@7 great reward.
verse	19	19	12	@@Who can understand @9his@7 errors? cleanse thou me from secret @9faults.@7
verse	19	19	13	@@Keep back thy servant also from presumptuous @9sins;@7 let them not have dominion over me: then shall I be upright, and I shall be innocent from the great transgression.
verse	19	19	14	Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my strength, and my redeemer.
pericope	19	20	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	20	1	The LORD hear thee in the day of trouble; the name of the God of Jacob defend thee;
verse	19	20	2	Send thee help from the sanctuary, and strengthen thee out of Zion;
verse	19	20	3	Remember all thy offerings, and accept thy burnt sacrifice; Selah.
verse	19	20	4	Grant thee according to thine own heart, and fulfil all thy counsel.
verse	19	20	5	@@We will rejoice in thy salvation, and in the name of our God we will set up @9our@7 banners: the LORD fulfil all thy petitions.
verse	19	20	6	Now know I that the LORD saveth his anointed; he will hear him from his holy heaven with the saving strength of his right hand.
verse	19	20	7	@@Some @9trust@7 in chariots, and some in horses: but we will remember the name of the LORD our God.
verse	19	20	8	They are brought down and fallen: but we are risen, and stand upright.
verse	19	20	9	Save, LORD: let the king hear us when we call.
pericope	19	21	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	21	1	The king shall joy in thy strength, O LORD; and in thy salvation how greatly shall he rejoice!
verse	19	21	2	Thou hast given him his heart's desire, and hast not withholden the request of his lips. Selah.
verse	19	21	3	For thou preventest him with the blessings of goodness: thou settest a crown of pure gold on his head.
verse	19	21	4	@@He asked life of thee, @9and@7 thou gavest @9it@7 him, @9even@7 length of days for ever and ever.
verse	19	21	5	@@His glory @9is@7 great in thy salvation: honour and majesty hast thou laid upon him.
verse	19	21	6	For thou hast made him most blessed for ever: thou hast made him exceeding glad with thy countenance.
verse	19	21	7	For the king trusteth in the LORD, and through the mercy of the most High he shall not be moved.
verse	19	21	8	Thine hand shall find out all thine enemies: thy right hand shall find out those that hate thee.
verse	19	21	9	Thou shalt make them as a fiery oven in the time of thine anger: the LORD shall swallow them up in his wrath, and the fire shall devour them.
verse	19	21	10	Their fruit shalt thou destroy from the earth, and their seed from among the children of men.
verse	19	21	11	@@For they intended evil against thee: they imagined a mischievous device, @9which@7 they are not able @9to perform.@7
verse	19	21	12	@@Therefore shalt thou make them turn their back, @9when@7 thou shalt make ready @9thine arrows@7 upon thy strings against the face of them.
verse	19	21	13	@@Be thou exalted, LORD, in thine own strength: @9so@7 will we sing and praise thy power.
pericope	19	22	1	To the chief Musician upon Aijeleth Shahar, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	22	1	@@My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me? @9why art thou so@7 far from helping me, @9and from@7 the words of my roaring?
verse	19	22	2	O my God, I cry in the daytime, but thou hearest not; and in the night season, and am not silent.
verse	19	22	3	@@But thou @9art@7 holy, @9O thou@7 that inhabitest the praises of Israel.
verse	19	22	4	Our fathers trusted in thee: they trusted, and thou didst deliver them.
verse	19	22	5	They cried unto thee, and were delivered: they trusted in thee, and were not confounded.
verse	19	22	6	@@But I @9am@7 a worm, and no man; a reproach of men, and despised of the people.
verse	19	22	7	@@All they that see me laugh me to scorn: they shoot out the lip, they shake the head @9saying,@7
verse	19	22	8	@@He trusted on the LORD @9that@7 he would deliver him: let him deliver him, seeing he delighted in him.
verse	19	22	9	@@But thou @9art@7 he that took me out of the womb: thou didst make me hope @9when I was@7 upon my mother's breasts.
verse	19	22	10	@@I was cast upon thee from the womb: thou @9art@7 my God from my mother's belly.
verse	19	22	11	@@Be not far from me; for trouble @9is@7 near; for @9there is@7 none to help.
verse	19	22	12	@@Many bulls have compassed me: strong @9bulls@7 of Bashan have beset me round.
verse	19	22	13	@@They gaped upon me @9with@7 their mouths, @9as@7 a ravening and a roaring lion.
verse	19	22	14	I am poured out like water, and all my bones are out of joint: my heart is like wax; it is melted in the midst of my bowels.
verse	19	22	15	My strength is dried up like a potsherd; and my tongue cleaveth to my jaws; and thou hast brought me into the dust of death.
verse	19	22	16	For dogs have compassed me: the assembly of the wicked have inclosed me: they pierced my hands and my feet.
verse	19	22	17	@@I may tell all my bones: they look @9and@7 stare upon me.
verse	19	22	18	They part my garments among them, and cast lots upon my vesture.
verse	19	22	19	But be not thou far from me, O LORD: O my strength, haste thee to help me.
verse	19	22	20	Deliver my soul from the sword; my darling from the power of the dog.
verse	19	22	21	Save me from the lion's mouth: for thou hast heard me from the horns of the unicorns.
verse	19	22	22	I will declare thy name unto my brethren: in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee.
verse	19	22	23	Ye that fear the LORD, praise him; all ye the seed of Jacob, glorify him; and fear him, all ye the seed of Israel.
verse	19	22	24	For he hath not despised nor abhorred the affliction of the afflicted; neither hath he hid his face from him; but when he cried unto him, he heard.
verse	19	22	25	@@My praise @9shall be@7 of thee in the great congregation: I will pay my vows before them that fear him.
verse	19	22	26	The meek shall eat and be satisfied: they shall praise the LORD that seek him: your heart shall live for ever.
verse	19	22	27	All the ends of the world shall remember and turn unto the LORD: and all the kindreds of the nations shall worship before thee.
verse	19	22	28	@@For the kingdom @9is@7 the LORD'S: and he @9is@7 the governor among the nations.
verse	19	22	29	@@All @9they that be@7 fat upon earth shall eat and worship: all they that go down to the dust shall bow before him: and none can keep alive his own soul.
verse	19	22	30	A seed shall serve him; it shall be accounted to the Lord for a generation.
verse	19	22	31	@@They shall come, and shall declare his righteousness unto a people that shall be born, that he hath done @9this.@7
pericope	19	23	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	23	1	@@The LORD @9is@7 my shepherd; I shall not want.
verse	19	23	2	He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters.
verse	19	23	3	He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name's sake.
verse	19	23	4	@@Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou @9art@7 with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.
verse	19	23	5	Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over.
verse	19	23	6	Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the LORD for ever.
pericope	19	24	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	24	1	@@The earth @9is@7 the LORD'S, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein.
verse	19	24	2	For he hath founded it upon the seas, and established it upon the floods.
verse	19	24	3	Who shall ascend into the hill of the LORD? or who shall stand in his holy place?
verse	19	24	4	He that hath clean hands, and a pure heart; who hath not lifted up his soul unto vanity, nor sworn deceitfully.
verse	19	24	5	He shall receive the blessing from the LORD, and righteousness from the God of his salvation.
verse	19	24	6	@@This @9is@7 the generation of them that seek him, that seek thy face, O Jacob. Selah.
verse	19	24	7	Lift up your heads, O ye gates; and be ye lift up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.
verse	19	24	8	@@Who @9is@7 this King of glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.
verse	19	24	9	@@Lift up your heads, O ye gates; even lift @9them@7 up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.
verse	19	24	10	@@Who is this King of glory? The LORD of hosts, he @9is@7 the King of glory. Selah.
pericope	19	25	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	25	1	Unto thee, O LORD, do I lift up my soul.
verse	19	25	2	O my God, I trust in thee: let me not be ashamed, let not mine enemies triumph over me.
verse	19	25	3	Yea, let none that wait on thee be ashamed: let them be ashamed which transgress without cause.
verse	19	25	4	Shew me thy ways, O LORD; teach me thy paths.
verse	19	25	5	@@Lead me in thy truth, and teach me: for thou @9art@7 the God of my salvation; on thee do I wait all the day.
verse	19	25	6	@@Remember, O LORD, thy tender mercies and thy lovingkindnesses; for they @9have been@7 ever of old.
verse	19	25	7	Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions: according to thy mercy remember thou me for thy goodness' sake, O LORD.
verse	19	25	8	@@Good and upright @9is@7 the LORD: therefore will he teach sinners in the way.
verse	19	25	9	The meek will he guide in judgment: and the meek will he teach his way.
verse	19	25	10	@@All the paths of the LORD @9are@7 mercy and truth unto such as keep his covenant and his testimonies.
verse	19	25	11	@@For thy name's sake, O LORD, pardon mine iniquity; for it @9is@7 great.
verse	19	25	12	@@What man @9is@7 he that feareth the LORD? him shall he teach in the way @9that@7 he shall choose.
verse	19	25	13	His soul shall dwell at ease; and his seed shall inherit the earth.
verse	19	25	14	@@The secret of the LORD @9is@7 with them that fear him; and he will shew them his covenant.
verse	19	25	15	@@Mine eyes @9are@7 ever toward the LORD; for he shall pluck my feet out of the net.
verse	19	25	16	@@Turn thee unto me, and have mercy upon me; for I @9am@7 desolate and afflicted.
verse	19	25	17	@@The troubles of my heart are enlarged: @9O@7 bring thou me out of my distresses.
verse	19	25	18	Look upon mine affliction and my pain; and forgive all my sins.
verse	19	25	19	Consider mine enemies; for they are many; and they hate me with cruel hatred.
verse	19	25	20	O keep my soul, and deliver me: let me not be ashamed; for I put my trust in thee.
verse	19	25	21	Let integrity and uprightness preserve me; for I wait on thee.
verse	19	25	22	Redeem Israel, O God, out of all his troubles.
pericope	19	26	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	26	1	@@Judge me, O LORD; for I have walked in mine integrity: I have trusted also in the LORD; @9therefore@7 I shall not slide.
verse	19	26	2	Examine me, O LORD, and prove me; try my reins and my heart.
verse	19	26	3	@@For thy lovingkindness @9is@7 before mine eyes: and I have walked in thy truth.
verse	19	26	4	I have not sat with vain persons, neither will I go in with dissemblers.
verse	19	26	5	I have hated the congregation of evildoers; and will not sit with the wicked.
verse	19	26	6	I will wash mine hands in innocency: so will I compass thine altar, O LORD:
verse	19	26	7	That I may publish with the voice of thanksgiving, and tell of all thy wondrous works.
verse	19	26	8	LORD, I have loved the habitation of thy house, and the place where thine honour dwelleth.
verse	19	26	9	Gather not my soul with sinners, nor my life with bloody men:
verse	19	26	10	@@In whose hands @9is@7 mischief, and their right hand is full of bribes.
verse	19	26	11	But as for me, I will walk in mine integrity: redeem me, and be merciful unto me.
verse	19	26	12	My foot standeth in an even place: in the congregations will I bless the LORD.
pericope	19	27	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	27	1	@@The LORD @9is@7 my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the LORD @9is@7 the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?
verse	19	27	2	@@When the wicked, @9even@7 mine enemies and my foes, came upon me to eat up my flesh, they stumbled and fell.
verse	19	27	3	@@Though an host should encamp against me, my heart shall not fear: though war should rise against me, in this @9will@7 I @9be@7 confident.
verse	19	27	4	@@One @9thing@7 have I desired of the LORD, that will I seek after; that I may dwell in the house of the LORD all the days of my life, to behold the beauty of the LORD, and to enquire in his temple.
verse	19	27	5	For in the time of trouble he shall hide me in his pavilion: in the secret of his tabernacle shall he hide me; he shall set me up upon a rock.
verse	19	27	6	And now shall mine head be lifted up above mine enemies round about me: therefore will I offer in his tabernacle sacrifices of joy; I will sing, yea, I will sing praises unto the LORD.
verse	19	27	7	@@Hear, O LORD, @9when@7 I cry with my voice: have mercy also upon me, and answer me.
verse	19	27	8	@@@9When thou saidst,@7 Seek ye my face; my heart said unto thee, Thy face, LORD, will I seek.
verse	19	27	9	@@Hide not thy face @9far@7 from me; put not thy servant away in anger: thou hast been my help; leave me not, neither forsake me, O God of my salvation.
verse	19	27	10	When my father and my mother forsake me, then the LORD will take me up.
verse	19	27	11	Teach me thy way, O LORD, and lead me in a plain path, because of mine enemies.
verse	19	27	12	Deliver me not over unto the will of mine enemies: for false witnesses are risen up against me, and such as breathe out cruelty.
verse	19	27	13	@@@9I had fainted,@7 unless I had believed to see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living.
verse	19	27	14	Wait on the LORD: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the LORD.
pericope	19	28	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	28	1	@@Unto thee will I cry, O LORD my rock; be not silent to me: lest, @9if@7 thou be silent to me, I become like them that go down into the pit.
verse	19	28	2	Hear the voice of my supplications, when I cry unto thee, when I lift up my hands toward thy holy oracle.
verse	19	28	3	@@Draw me not away with the wicked, and with the workers of iniquity, which speak peace to their neighbours, but mischief @9is@7 in their hearts.
verse	19	28	4	Give them according to their deeds, and according to the wickedness of their endeavours: give them after the work of their hands; render to them their desert.
verse	19	28	5	Because they regard not the works of the LORD, nor the operation of his hands, he shall destroy them, and not build them up.
verse	19	28	6	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD, because he hath heard the voice of my supplications.
verse	19	28	7	@@The LORD @9is@7 my strength and my shield; my heart trusted in him, and I am helped: therefore my heart greatly rejoiceth; and with my song will I praise him.
verse	19	28	8	@@The LORD @9is@7 their strength, and he @9is@7 the saving strength of his anointed.
verse	19	28	9	Save thy people, and bless thine inheritance: feed them also, and lift them up for ever.
pericope	19	29	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	29	1	Give unto the LORD, O ye mighty, give unto the LORD glory and strength.
verse	19	29	2	Give unto the LORD the glory due unto his name; worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness.
verse	19	29	3	@@The voice of the LORD @9is@7 upon the waters: the God of glory thundereth: the LORD @9is@7 upon many waters.
verse	19	29	4	@@The voice of the LORD @9is@7 powerful; the voice of the LORD @9is@7 full of majesty.
verse	19	29	5	The voice of the LORD breaketh the cedars; yea, the LORD breaketh the cedars of Lebanon.
verse	19	29	6	He maketh them also to skip like a calf; Lebanon and Sirion like a young unicorn.
verse	19	29	7	The voice of the LORD divideth the flames of fire.
verse	19	29	8	The voice of the LORD shaketh the wilderness; the LORD shaketh the wilderness of Kadesh.
verse	19	29	9	@@The voice of the LORD maketh the hinds to calve, and discovereth the forests: and in his temple doth every one speak of @9his@7 glory.
verse	19	29	10	The LORD sitteth upon the flood; yea, the LORD sitteth King for ever.
verse	19	29	11	The LORD will give strength unto his people; the LORD will bless his people with peace.
pericope	19	30	1	A Psalm and Song at the dedication of the house of David.
verse	19	30	1	I will extol thee, O LORD; for thou hast lifted me up, and hast not made my foes to rejoice over me.
verse	19	30	2	O LORD my God, I cried unto thee, and thou hast healed me.
verse	19	30	3	O LORD, thou hast brought up my soul from the grave: thou hast kept me alive, that I should not go down to the pit.
verse	19	30	4	Sing unto the LORD, O ye saints of his, and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness.
verse	19	30	5	@@For his anger @9endureth but@7 a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy @9cometh@7 in the morning.
verse	19	30	6	And in my prosperity I said, I shall never be moved.
verse	19	30	7	@@LORD, by thy favour thou hast made my mountain to stand strong: thou didst hide thy face, @9and@7 I was troubled.
verse	19	30	8	I cried to thee, O LORD; and unto the LORD I made supplication.
verse	19	30	9	@@What profit @9is there@7 in my blood, when I go down to the pit? Shall the dust praise thee? shall it declare thy truth?
verse	19	30	10	Hear, O LORD, and have mercy upon me: LORD, be thou my helper.
verse	19	30	11	Thou hast turned for me my mourning into dancing: thou hast put off my sackcloth, and girded me with gladness;
verse	19	30	12	@@To the end that @9my@7 glory may sing praise to thee, and not be silent. O LORD my God, I will give thanks unto thee for ever.
pericope	19	31	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	31	1	In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust; let me never be ashamed: deliver me in thy righteousness.
verse	19	31	2	Bow down thine ear to me; deliver me speedily: be thou my strong rock, for an house of defence to save me.
verse	19	31	3	@@For thou @9art@7 my rock and my fortress; therefore for thy name's sake lead me, and guide me.
verse	19	31	4	@@Pull me out of the net that they have laid privily for me: for thou @9art@7 my strength.
verse	19	31	5	Into thine hand I commit my spirit: thou hast redeemed me, O LORD God of truth.
verse	19	31	6	I have hated them that regard lying vanities: but I trust in the LORD.
verse	19	31	7	I will be glad and rejoice in thy mercy: for thou hast considered my trouble; thou hast known my soul in adversities;
verse	19	31	8	And hast not shut me up into the hand of the enemy: thou hast set my feet in a large room.
verse	19	31	9	@@Have mercy upon me, O LORD, for I am in trouble: mine eye is consumed with grief, @9yea,@7 my soul and my belly.
verse	19	31	10	For my life is spent with grief, and my years with sighing: my strength faileth because of mine iniquity, and my bones are consumed.
verse	19	31	11	I was a reproach among all mine enemies, but especially among my neighbours, and a fear to mine acquaintance: they that did see me without fled from me.
verse	19	31	12	I am forgotten as a dead man out of mind: I am like a broken vessel.
verse	19	31	13	@@For I have heard the slander of many: fear @9was@7 on every side: while they took counsel together against me, they devised to take away my life.
verse	19	31	14	@@But I trusted in thee, O LORD: I said, Thou @9art@7 my God.
verse	19	31	15	@@My times @9are@7 in thy hand: deliver me from the hand of mine enemies, and from them that persecute me.
verse	19	31	16	Make thy face to shine upon thy servant: save me for thy mercies' sake.
verse	19	31	17	@@Let me not be ashamed, O LORD; for I have called upon thee: let the wicked be ashamed, @9and@7 let them be silent in the grave.
verse	19	31	18	Let the lying lips be put to silence; which speak grievous things proudly and contemptuously against the righteous.
verse	19	31	19	@@@9Oh@7 how great @9is@7 thy goodness, which thou hast laid up for them that fear thee; @9which@7 thou hast wrought for them that trust in thee before the sons of men!
verse	19	31	20	Thou shalt hide them in the secret of thy presence from the pride of man: thou shalt keep them secretly in a pavilion from the strife of tongues.
verse	19	31	21	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD: for he hath shewed me his marvellous kindness in a strong city.
verse	19	31	22	For I said in my haste, I am cut off from before thine eyes: nevertheless thou heardest the voice of my supplications when I cried unto thee.
verse	19	31	23	@@O love the LORD, all ye his saints: @9for@7 the LORD preserveth the faithful, and plentifully rewardeth the proud doer.
verse	19	31	24	Be of good courage, and he shall strengthen your heart, all ye that hope in the LORD.
pericope	19	32	1	A Psalm of David, Maschil.
verse	19	32	1	@@Blessed @9is he whose@7 transgression @9is@7 forgiven, @9whose@7 sin @9is@7 covered.
verse	19	32	2	@@Blessed @9is@7 the man unto whom the LORD imputeth not iniquity, and in whose spirit @9there is@7 no guile.
verse	19	32	3	When I kept silence, my bones waxed old through my roaring all the day long.
verse	19	32	4	For day and night thy hand was heavy upon me: my moisture is turned into the drought of summer. Selah.
verse	19	32	5	I acknowledged my sin unto thee, and mine iniquity have I not hid. I said, I will confess my transgressions unto the LORD; and thou forgavest the iniquity of my sin. Selah.
verse	19	32	6	For this shall every one that is godly pray unto thee in a time when thou mayest be found: surely in the floods of great waters they shall not come nigh unto him.
verse	19	32	7	@@Thou @9art@7 my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble; thou shalt compass me about with songs of deliverance. Selah.
verse	19	32	8	I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye.
verse	19	32	9	@@Be ye not as the horse, @9or@7 as the mule, @9which@7 have no understanding: whose mouth must be held in with bit and bridle, lest they come near unto thee.
verse	19	32	10	@@Many sorrows @9shall be@7 to the wicked: but he that trusteth in the LORD, mercy shall compass him about.
verse	19	32	11	@@Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, ye righteous: and shout for joy, all @9ye that are@7 upright in heart.
verse	19	33	1	@@Rejoice in the LORD, O ye righteous: @9for@7 praise is comely for the upright.
verse	19	33	2	@@Praise the LORD with harp: sing unto him with the psaltery @9and@7 an instrument of ten strings.
verse	19	33	3	Sing unto him a new song; play skilfully with a loud noise.
verse	19	33	4	@@For the word of the LORD @9is@7 right; and all his works @9are done@7 in truth.
verse	19	33	5	He loveth righteousness and judgment: the earth is full of the goodness of the LORD.
verse	19	33	6	By the word of the LORD were the heavens made; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.
verse	19	33	7	He gathereth the waters of the sea together as an heap: he layeth up the depth in storehouses.
verse	19	33	8	Let all the earth fear the LORD: let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of him.
verse	19	33	9	@@For he spake, and it was @9done;@7 he commanded, and it stood fast.
verse	19	33	10	The LORD bringeth the counsel of the heathen to nought: he maketh the devices of the people of none effect.
verse	19	33	11	The counsel of the LORD standeth for ever, the thoughts of his heart to all generations.
verse	19	33	12	@@Blessed @9is@7 the nation whose God @9is@7 the LORD: @9and@7 the people @9whom@7 he hath chosen for his own inheritance.
verse	19	33	13	The LORD looketh from heaven; he beholdeth all the sons of men.
verse	19	33	14	From the place of his habitation he looketh upon all the inhabitants of the earth.
verse	19	33	15	He fashioneth their hearts alike; he considereth all their works.
verse	19	33	16	There is no king saved by the multitude of an host: a mighty man is not delivered by much strength.
verse	19	33	17	@@An horse @9is@7 a vain thing for safety: neither shall he deliver @9any@7 by his great strength.
verse	19	33	18	@@Behold, the eye of the LORD @9is@7 upon them that fear him, upon them that hope in his mercy;
verse	19	33	19	To deliver their soul from death, and to keep them alive in famine.
verse	19	33	20	@@Our soul waiteth for the LORD: he @9is@7 our help and our shield.
verse	19	33	21	For our heart shall rejoice in him, because we have trusted in his holy name.
verse	19	33	22	Let thy mercy, O LORD, be upon us, according as we hope in thee.
pericope	19	34	1	A Psalm of David, when he changed his behaviour before Abimelech; who drove him away, and he departed.
verse	19	34	1	@@I will bless the LORD at all times: his praise @9shall@7 continually @9be@7 in my mouth.
verse	19	34	2	@@My soul shall make her boast in the LORD: the humble shall hear @9thereof,@7 and be glad.
verse	19	34	3	O magnify the LORD with me, and let us exalt his name together.
verse	19	34	4	I sought the LORD, and he heard me, and delivered me from all my fears.
verse	19	34	5	They looked unto him, and were lightened: and their faces were not ashamed.
verse	19	34	6	@@This poor man cried, and the LORD heard @9him,@7 and saved him out of all his troubles.
verse	19	34	7	The angel of the LORD encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.
verse	19	34	8	@@O taste and see that the LORD @9is@7 good: blessed @9is@7 the man @9that@7 trusteth in him.
verse	19	34	9	@@O fear the LORD, ye his saints: for @9there is@7 no want to them that fear him.
verse	19	34	10	@@The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the LORD shall not want any good @9thing.@7
verse	19	34	11	Come, ye children, hearken unto me: I will teach you the fear of the LORD.
verse	19	34	12	@@What man @9is he that@7 desireth life, @9and@7 loveth @9many@7 days, that he may see good?
verse	19	34	13	Keep thy tongue from evil, and thy lips from speaking guile.
verse	19	34	14	Depart from evil, and do good; seek peace, and pursue it.
verse	19	34	15	@@The eyes of the LORD @9are@7 upon the righteous, and his ears @9are open@7 unto their cry.
verse	19	34	16	@@The face of the LORD @9is@7 against them that do evil, to cut off the remembrance of them from the earth.
verse	19	34	17	@@@9The righteous@7 cry, and the LORD heareth, and delivereth them out of all their troubles.
verse	19	34	18	@@The LORD @9is@7 nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.
verse	19	34	19	@@Many @9are@7 the afflictions of the righteous: but the LORD delivereth him out of them all.
verse	19	34	20	He keepeth all his bones: not one of them is broken.
verse	19	34	21	Evil shall slay the wicked: and they that hate the righteous shall be desolate.
verse	19	34	22	The LORD redeemeth the soul of his servants: and none of them that trust in him shall be desolate.
pericope	19	35	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	35	1	@@Plead @9my cause,@7 O LORD, with them that strive with me: fight against them that fight against me.
verse	19	35	2	Take hold of shield and buckler, and stand up for mine help.
verse	19	35	3	@@Draw out also the spear, and stop @9the way@7 against them that persecute me: say unto my soul, I @9am@7 thy salvation.
verse	19	35	4	Let them be confounded and put to shame that seek after my soul: let them be turned back and brought to confusion that devise my hurt.
verse	19	35	5	@@Let them be as chaff before the wind: and let the angel of the LORD chase @9them.@7
verse	19	35	6	Let their way be dark and slippery: and let the angel of the LORD persecute them.
verse	19	35	7	@@For without cause have they hid for me their net @9in@7 a pit, @9which@7 without cause they have digged for my soul.
verse	19	35	8	Let destruction come upon him at unawares; and let his net that he hath hid catch himself: into that very destruction let him fall.
verse	19	35	9	And my soul shall be joyful in the LORD: it shall rejoice in his salvation.
verse	19	35	10	@@All my bones shall say, LORD, who @9is@7 like unto thee, which deliverest the poor from him that is too strong for him, yea, the poor and the needy from him that spoileth him?
verse	19	35	11	@@False witnesses did rise up; they laid to my charge @9things@7 that I knew not.
verse	19	35	12	@@They rewarded me evil for good @9to@7 the spoiling of my soul.
verse	19	35	13	@@But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing @9was@7 sackcloth: I humbled my soul with fasting; and my prayer returned into mine own bosom.
verse	19	35	14	@@I behaved myself as though @9he had been@7 my friend @9or@7 brother: I bowed down heavily, as one that mourneth @9for his@7 mother.
verse	19	35	15	@@But in mine adversity they rejoiced, and gathered themselves together: @9yea,@7 the abjects gathered themselves together against me, and I knew @9it@7 not; they did tear @9me,@7 and ceased not:
verse	19	35	16	With hypocritical mockers in feasts, they gnashed upon me with their teeth.
verse	19	35	17	Lord, how long wilt thou look on? rescue my soul from their destructions, my darling from the lions.
verse	19	35	18	I will give thee thanks in the great congregation: I will praise thee among much people.
verse	19	35	19	@@Let not them that are mine enemies wrongfully rejoice over me: @9neither@7 let them wink with the eye that hate me without a cause.
verse	19	35	20	@@For they speak not peace: but they devise deceitful matters against @9them that are@7 quiet in the land.
verse	19	35	21	@@Yea, they opened their mouth wide against me, @9and@7 said, Aha, aha, our eye hath seen @9it.@7
verse	19	35	22	@@@9This@7 thou hast seen, O LORD: keep not silence: O Lord, be not far from me.
verse	19	35	23	@@Stir up thyself, and awake to my judgment, @9even@7 unto my cause, my God and my Lord.
verse	19	35	24	Judge me, O LORD my God, according to thy righteousness; and let them not rejoice over me.
verse	19	35	25	Let them not say in their hearts, Ah, so would we have it: let them not say, We have swallowed him up.
verse	19	35	26	@@Let them be ashamed and brought to confusion together that rejoice at mine hurt: let them be clothed with shame and dishonour that magnify @9themselves@7 against me.
verse	19	35	27	Let them shout for joy, and be glad, that favour my righteous cause: yea, let them say continually, Let the LORD be magnified, which hath pleasure in the prosperity of his servant.
verse	19	35	28	@@And my tongue shall speak of thy righteousness @9and@7 of thy praise all the day long.
pericope	19	36	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David the servant of the LORD.
verse	19	36	1	@@The transgression of the wicked saith within my heart, @9that there is@7 no fear of God before his eyes.
verse	19	36	2	For he flattereth himself in his own eyes, until his iniquity be found to be hateful.
verse	19	36	3	@@The words of his mouth @9are@7 iniquity and deceit: he hath left off to be wise, @9and@7 to do good.
verse	19	36	4	@@He deviseth mischief upon his bed; he setteth himself in a way @9that is@7 not good; he abhorreth not evil.
verse	19	36	5	@@Thy mercy, O LORD, @9is@7 in the heavens; @9and@7 thy faithfulness @9reacheth@7 unto the clouds.
verse	19	36	6	@@Thy righteousness @9is@7 like the great mountains; thy judgments @9are@7 a great deep: O LORD, thou preservest man and beast.
verse	19	36	7	@@How excellent @9is@7 thy lovingkindness, O God! therefore the children of men put their trust under the shadow of thy wings.
verse	19	36	8	They shall be abundantly satisfied with the fatness of thy house; and thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures.
verse	19	36	9	@@For with thee @9is@7 the fountain of life: in thy light shall we see light.
verse	19	36	10	O continue thy lovingkindness unto them that know thee; and thy righteousness to the upright in heart.
verse	19	36	11	Let not the foot of pride come against me, and let not the hand of the wicked remove me.
verse	19	36	12	There are the workers of iniquity fallen: they are cast down, and shall not be able to rise.
pericope	19	37	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	37	1	Fret not thyself because of evildoers, neither be thou envious against the workers of iniquity.
verse	19	37	2	For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb.
verse	19	37	3	@@Trust in the LORD, and do good; @9so@7 shalt thou dwell in the land, and verily thou shalt be fed.
verse	19	37	4	Delight thyself also in the LORD; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart.
verse	19	37	5	@@Commit thy way unto the LORD; trust also in him; and he shall bring @9it@7 to pass.
verse	19	37	6	And he shall bring forth thy righteousness as the light, and thy judgment as the noonday.
verse	19	37	7	Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself because of him who prospereth in his way, because of the man who bringeth wicked devices to pass.
verse	19	37	8	Cease from anger, and forsake wrath: fret not thyself in any wise to do evil.
verse	19	37	9	For evildoers shall be cut off: but those that wait upon the LORD, they shall inherit the earth.
verse	19	37	10	@@For yet a little while, and the wicked @9shall@7 not @9be:@7 yea, thou shalt diligently consider his place, and it @9shall@7 not @9be.@7
verse	19	37	11	But the meek shall inherit the earth; and shall delight themselves in the abundance of peace.
verse	19	37	12	The wicked plotteth against the just, and gnasheth upon him with his teeth.
verse	19	37	13	The Lord shall laugh at him: for he seeth that his day is coming.
verse	19	37	14	@@The wicked have drawn out the sword, and have bent their bow, to cast down the poor and needy, @9and@7 to slay such as be of upright conversation.
verse	19	37	15	Their sword shall enter into their own heart, and their bows shall be broken.
verse	19	37	16	@@A little that a righteous man hath @9is@7 better than the riches of many wicked.
verse	19	37	17	For the arms of the wicked shall be broken: but the LORD upholdeth the righteous.
verse	19	37	18	The LORD knoweth the days of the upright: and their inheritance shall be for ever.
verse	19	37	19	They shall not be ashamed in the evil time: and in the days of famine they shall be satisfied.
verse	19	37	20	@@But the wicked shall perish, and the enemies of the LORD @9shall be@7 as the fat of lambs: they shall consume; into smoke shall they consume away.
verse	19	37	21	The wicked borroweth, and payeth not again: but the righteous sheweth mercy, and giveth.
verse	19	37	22	@@For @9such as be@7 blessed of him shall inherit the earth; and @9they that be@7 cursed of him shall be cut off.
verse	19	37	23	@@The steps of a @9good@7 man are ordered by the LORD: and he delighteth in his way.
verse	19	37	24	@@Though he fall, he shall not be utterly cast down: for the LORD upholdeth @9him with@7 his hand.
verse	19	37	25	@@I have been young, and @9now@7 am old; yet have I not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed begging bread.
verse	19	37	26	@@@9He is@7 ever merciful, and lendeth; and his seed @9is@7 blessed.
verse	19	37	27	Depart from evil, and do good; and dwell for evermore.
verse	19	37	28	For the LORD loveth judgment, and forsaketh not his saints; they are preserved for ever: but the seed of the wicked shall be cut off.
verse	19	37	29	The righteous shall inherit the land, and dwell therein for ever.
verse	19	37	30	The mouth of the righteous speaketh wisdom, and his tongue talketh of judgment.
verse	19	37	31	@@The law of his God @9is@7 in his heart; none of his steps shall slide.
verse	19	37	32	The wicked watcheth the righteous, and seeketh to slay him.
verse	19	37	33	The LORD will not leave him in his hand, nor condemn him when he is judged.
verse	19	37	34	@@Wait on the LORD, and keep his way, and he shall exalt thee to inherit the land: when the wicked are cut off, thou shalt see @9it.@7
verse	19	37	35	I have seen the wicked in great power, and spreading himself like a green bay tree.
verse	19	37	36	@@Yet he passed away, and, lo, he @9was@7 not: yea, I sought him, but he could not be found.
verse	19	37	37	@@Mark the perfect @9man,@7 and behold the upright: for the end of @9that@7 man @9is@7 peace.
verse	19	37	38	But the transgressors shall be destroyed together: the end of the wicked shall be cut off.
verse	19	37	39	@@But the salvation of the righteous @9is@7 of the LORD: @9he is@7 their strength in the time of trouble.
verse	19	37	40	And the LORD shall help them and deliver them: he shall deliver them from the wicked, and save them, because they trust in him.
pericope	19	38	1	A Psalm of David, to bring to remembrance.
verse	19	38	1	O LORD, rebuke me not in thy wrath: neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.
verse	19	38	2	For thine arrows stick fast in me, and thy hand presseth me sore.
verse	19	38	3	@@@9There is@7 no soundness in my flesh because of thine anger; neither @9is there any@7 rest in my bones because of my sin.
verse	19	38	4	For mine iniquities are gone over mine head: as an heavy burden they are too heavy for me.
verse	19	38	5	@@My wounds stink @9and@7 are corrupt because of my foolishness.
verse	19	38	6	I am troubled; I am bowed down greatly; I go mourning all the day long.
verse	19	38	7	@@For my loins are filled with a loathsome @9disease:@7 and @9there is@7 no soundness in my flesh.
verse	19	38	8	I am feeble and sore broken: I have roared by reason of the disquietness of my heart.
verse	19	38	9	@@Lord, all my desire @9is@7 before thee; and my groaning is not hid from thee.
verse	19	38	10	My heart panteth, my strength faileth me: as for the light of mine eyes, it also is gone from me.
verse	19	38	11	My lovers and my friends stand aloof from my sore; and my kinsmen stand afar off.
verse	19	38	12	@@They also that seek after my life lay snares @9for me:@7 and they that seek my hurt speak mischievous things, and imagine deceits all the day long.
verse	19	38	13	@@But I, as a deaf @9man,@7 heard not; and @9I was@7 as a dumb man @9that@7 openeth not his mouth.
verse	19	38	14	@@Thus I was as a man that heareth not, and in whose mouth @9are@7 no reproofs.
verse	19	38	15	For in thee, O LORD, do I hope: thou wilt hear, O Lord my God.
verse	19	38	16	@@For I said, @9Hear me,@7 lest @9otherwise@7 they should rejoice over me: when my foot slippeth, they magnify @9themselves@7 against me.
verse	19	38	17	@@For I @9am@7 ready to halt, and my sorrow @9is@7 continually before me.
verse	19	38	18	For I will declare mine iniquity; I will be sorry for my sin.
verse	19	38	19	@@But mine enemies @9are@7 lively, @9and@7 they are strong: and they that hate me wrongfully are multiplied.
verse	19	38	20	@@They also that render evil for good are mine adversaries; because I follow @9the thing that@7 good @9is.@7
verse	19	38	21	Forsake me not, O LORD: O my God, be not far from me.
verse	19	38	22	Make haste to help me, O Lord my salvation.
pericope	19	39	1	To the chief Musician, even to Jeduthun, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	39	1	I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I will keep my mouth with a bridle, while the wicked is before me.
verse	19	39	2	@@I was dumb with silence, I held my peace, @9even@7 from good; and my sorrow was stirred.
verse	19	39	3	@@My heart was hot within me, while I was musing the fire burned: @9then@7 spake I with my tongue,
verse	19	39	4	@@LORD, make me to know mine end, and the measure of my days, what it @9is; that@7 I may know how frail I @9am.@7
verse	19	39	5	@@Behold, thou hast made my days @9as@7 an handbreadth; and mine age @9is@7 as nothing before thee: verily every man at his best state @9is@7 altogether vanity. Selah.
verse	19	39	6	@@Surely every man walketh in a vain shew: surely they are disquieted in vain: he heapeth up @9riches,@7 and knoweth not who shall gather them.
verse	19	39	7	@@And now, Lord, what wait I for? my hope @9is@7 in thee.
verse	19	39	8	Deliver me from all my transgressions: make me not the reproach of the foolish.
verse	19	39	9	@@I was dumb, I opened not my mouth; because thou didst @9it.@7
verse	19	39	10	Remove thy stroke away from me: I am consumed by the blow of thine hand.
verse	19	39	11	@@When thou with rebukes dost correct man for iniquity, thou makest his beauty to consume away like a moth: surely every man @9is@7 vanity. Selah.
verse	19	39	12	@@Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear unto my cry; hold not thy peace at my tears: for I @9am@7 a stranger with thee, @9and@7 a sojourner, as all my fathers @9were.@7
verse	19	39	13	O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more.
pericope	19	40	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	40	1	I waited patiently for the LORD; and he inclined unto me, and heard my cry.
verse	19	40	2	@@He brought me up also out of an horrible pit, out of the miry clay, and set my feet upon a rock, @9and@7 established my goings.
verse	19	40	3	@@And he hath put a new song in my mouth, @9even@7 praise unto our God: many shall see @9it,@7 and fear, and shall trust in the LORD.
verse	19	40	4	@@Blessed @9is@7 that man that maketh the LORD his trust, and respecteth not the proud, nor such as turn aside to lies.
verse	19	40	5	@@Many, O LORD my God, @9are@7 thy wonderful works @9which@7 thou hast done, and thy thoughts @9which are@7 to us-ward: they cannot be reckoned up in order unto thee: @9if@7 I would declare and speak @9of them,@7 they are more than can be numbered.
verse	19	40	6	Sacrifice and offering thou didst not desire; mine ears hast thou opened: burnt offering and sin offering hast thou not required.
verse	19	40	7	@@Then said I, Lo, I come: in the volume of the book @9it is@7 written of me,
verse	19	40	8	@@I delight to do thy will, O my God: yea, thy law @9is@7 within my heart.
verse	19	40	9	I have preached righteousness in the great congregation: lo, I have not refrained my lips, O LORD, thou knowest.
verse	19	40	10	I have not hid thy righteousness within my heart; I have declared thy faithfulness and thy salvation: I have not concealed thy lovingkindness and thy truth from the great congregation.
verse	19	40	11	Withhold not thou thy tender mercies from me, O LORD: let thy lovingkindness and thy truth continually preserve me.
verse	19	40	12	For innumerable evils have compassed me about: mine iniquities have taken hold upon me, so that I am not able to look up; they are more than the hairs of mine head: therefore my heart faileth me.
verse	19	40	13	Be pleased, O LORD, to deliver me: O LORD, make haste to help me.
verse	19	40	14	Let them be ashamed and confounded together that seek after my soul to destroy it; let them be driven backward and put to shame that wish me evil.
verse	19	40	15	Let them be desolate for a reward of their shame that say unto me, Aha, aha.
verse	19	40	16	Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: let such as love thy salvation say continually, The LORD be magnified.
verse	19	40	17	@@But I @9am@7 poor and needy; @9yet@7 the Lord thinketh upon me: thou @9art@7 my help and my deliverer; make no tarrying, O my God.
pericope	19	41	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	41	1	@@Blessed @9is@7 he that considereth the poor: the LORD will deliver him in time of trouble.
verse	19	41	2	@@The LORD will preserve him, and keep him alive; @9and@7 he shall be blessed upon the earth: and thou wilt not deliver him unto the will of his enemies.
verse	19	41	3	The LORD will strengthen him upon the bed of languishing: thou wilt make all his bed in his sickness.
verse	19	41	4	I said, LORD, be merciful unto me: heal my soul; for I have sinned against thee.
verse	19	41	5	Mine enemies speak evil of me, When shall he die, and his name perish?
verse	19	41	6	@@And if he come to see @9me,@7 he speaketh vanity: his heart gathereth iniquity to itself; @9when@7 he goeth abroad, he telleth @9it.@7
verse	19	41	7	All that hate me whisper together against me: against me do they devise my hurt.
verse	19	41	8	@@An evil disease, @9say they,@7 cleaveth fast unto him: and @9now@7 that he lieth he shall rise up no more.
verse	19	41	9	@@Yea, mine own familiar friend, in whom I trusted, which did eat of my bread, hath lifted up @9his@7 heel against me.
verse	19	41	10	But thou, O LORD, be merciful unto me, and raise me up, that I may requite them.
verse	19	41	11	By this I know that thou favourest me, because mine enemy doth not triumph over me.
verse	19	41	12	And as for me, thou upholdest me in mine integrity, and settest me before thy face for ever.
verse	19	41	13	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD God of Israel from everlasting, and to everlasting. Amen, and Amen.
pericope	19	42	1	To the chief Musician, Maschil, for the sons of Korah.
verse	19	42	1	As the hart panteth after the water brooks, so panteth my soul after thee, O God.
verse	19	42	2	My soul thirsteth for God, for the living God: when shall I come and appear before God?
verse	19	42	3	@@My tears have been my meat day and night, while they continually say unto me, Where @9is@7 thy God?
verse	19	42	4	@@When I remember these @9things,@7 I pour out my soul in me: for I had gone with the multitude, I went with them to the house of God, with the voice of joy and praise, with a multitude that kept holyday.
verse	19	42	5	@@Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why @9art@7 thou disquieted in me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him @9for@7 the help of his countenance.
verse	19	42	6	O my God, my soul is cast down within me: therefore will I remember thee from the land of Jordan, and of the Hermonites, from the hill Mizar.
verse	19	42	7	Deep calleth unto deep at the noise of thy waterspouts: all thy waves and thy billows are gone over me.
verse	19	42	8	@@@9Yet@7 the LORD will command his lovingkindness in the daytime, and in the night his song @9shall be@7 with me, @9and@7 my prayer unto the God of my life.
verse	19	42	9	I will say unto God my rock, Why hast thou forgotten me? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?
verse	19	42	10	@@@9As@7 with a sword in my bones, mine enemies reproach me; while they say daily unto me, Where @9is@7 thy God?
verse	19	42	11	@@Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, @9who is@7 the health of my countenance, and my God.
verse	19	43	1	Judge me, O God, and plead my cause against an ungodly nation: O deliver me from the deceitful and unjust man.
verse	19	43	2	@@For thou @9art@7 the God of my strength: why dost thou cast me off? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?
verse	19	43	3	O send out thy light and thy truth: let them lead me; let them bring me unto thy holy hill, and to thy tabernacles.
verse	19	43	4	Then will I go unto the altar of God, unto God my exceeding joy: yea, upon the harp will I praise thee, O God my God.
verse	19	43	5	@@Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope in God: for I shall yet praise him, @9who is@7 the health of my countenance, and my God.
pericope	19	44	1	To the chief Musician for the sons of Korah, Maschil.
verse	19	44	1	@@We have heard with our ears, O God, our fathers have told us, @9what@7 work thou didst in their days, in the times of old.
verse	19	44	2	@@@9How@7 thou didst drive out the heathen with thy hand, and plantedst them; @9how@7 thou didst afflict the people, and cast them out.
verse	19	44	3	For they got not the land in possession by their own sword, neither did their own arm save them: but thy right hand, and thine arm, and the light of thy countenance, because thou hadst a favour unto them.
verse	19	44	4	Thou art my King, O God: command deliverances for Jacob.
verse	19	44	5	Through thee will we push down our enemies: through thy name will we tread them under that rise up against us.
verse	19	44	6	For I will not trust in my bow, neither shall my sword save me.
verse	19	44	7	But thou hast saved us from our enemies, and hast put them to shame that hated us.
verse	19	44	8	In God we boast all the day long, and praise thy name for ever. Selah.
verse	19	44	9	But thou hast cast off, and put us to shame; and goest not forth with our armies.
verse	19	44	10	Thou makest us to turn back from the enemy: and they which hate us spoil for themselves.
verse	19	44	11	@@Thou hast given us like sheep @9appointed@7 for meat; and hast scattered us among the heathen.
verse	19	44	12	@@Thou sellest thy people for nought, and dost not increase @9thy wealth@7 by their price.
verse	19	44	13	Thou makest us a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and a derision to them that are round about us.
verse	19	44	14	Thou makest us a byword among the heathen, a shaking of the head among the people.
verse	19	44	15	@@My confusion @9is@7 continually before me, and the shame of my face hath covered me,
verse	19	44	16	For the voice of him that reproacheth and blasphemeth; by reason of the enemy and avenger.
verse	19	44	17	All this is come upon us; yet have we not forgotten thee, neither have we dealt falsely in thy covenant.
verse	19	44	18	Our heart is not turned back, neither have our steps declined from thy way;
verse	19	44	19	Though thou hast sore broken us in the place of dragons, and covered us with the shadow of death.
verse	19	44	20	If we have forgotten the name of our God, or stretched out our hands to a strange god;
verse	19	44	21	Shall not God search this out? for he knoweth the secrets of the heart.
verse	19	44	22	Yea, for thy sake are we killed all the day long; we are counted as sheep for the slaughter.
verse	19	44	23	@@Awake, why sleepest thou, O Lord? arise, cast @9us@7 not off for ever.
verse	19	44	24	@@Wherefore hidest thou thy face, @9and@7 forgettest our affliction and our oppression?
verse	19	44	25	For our soul is bowed down to the dust: our belly cleaveth unto the earth.
verse	19	44	26	Arise for our help, and redeem us for thy mercies' sake.
pericope	19	45	1	To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim, for the sons of Korah, Maschil, A Song of loves.
verse	19	45	1	@@My heart is inditing a good matter: I speak of the things which I have made touching the king: my tongue @9is@7 the pen of a ready writer.
verse	19	45	2	Thou art fairer than the children of men: grace is poured into thy lips: therefore God hath blessed thee for ever.
verse	19	45	3	@@Gird thy sword upon @9thy@7 thigh, O @9most@7 mighty, with thy glory and thy majesty.
verse	19	45	4	@@And in thy majesty ride prosperously because of truth and meekness @9and@7 righteousness; and thy right hand shall teach thee terrible things.
verse	19	45	5	@@Thine arrows @9are@7 sharp in the heart of the king's enemies; @9whereby@7 the people fall under thee.
verse	19	45	6	@@Thy throne, O God, @9is@7 for ever and ever: the sceptre of thy kingdom @9is@7 a right sceptre.
verse	19	45	7	Thou lovest righteousness, and hatest wickedness: therefore God, thy God, hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows.
verse	19	45	8	@@All thy garments @9smell@7 of myrrh, and aloes, @9and@7 cassia, out of the ivory palaces, whereby they have made thee glad.
verse	19	45	9	@@Kings' daughters @9were@7 among thy honourable women: upon thy right hand did stand the queen in gold of Ophir.
verse	19	45	10	Hearken, O daughter, and consider, and incline thine ear; forget also thine own people, and thy father's house;
verse	19	45	11	@@So shall the king greatly desire thy beauty: for he @9is@7 thy Lord; and worship thou him.
verse	19	45	12	@@And the daughter of Tyre @9shall be there@7 with a gift; @9even@7 the rich among the people shall intreat thy favour.
verse	19	45	13	@@The king's daughter @9is@7 all glorious within: her clothing @9is@7 of wrought gold.
verse	19	45	14	She shall be brought unto the king in raiment of needlework: the virgins her companions that follow her shall be brought unto thee.
verse	19	45	15	With gladness and rejoicing shall they be brought: they shall enter into the king's palace.
verse	19	45	16	Instead of thy fathers shall be thy children, whom thou mayest make princes in all the earth.
verse	19	45	17	I will make thy name to be remembered in all generations: therefore shall the people praise thee for ever and ever.
pericope	19	46	1	To the chief Musician for the sons of Korah, A Song upon Alamoth.
verse	19	46	1	@@God @9is@7 our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.
verse	19	46	2	Therefore will not we fear, though the earth be removed, and though the mountains be carried into the midst of the sea;
verse	19	46	3	@@@9Though@7 the waters thereof roar @9and@7 be troubled, @9though@7 the mountains shake with the swelling thereof. Selah.
verse	19	46	4	@@@9There is@7 a river, the streams whereof shall make glad the city of God, the holy @9place@7 of the tabernacles of the most High.
verse	19	46	5	@@God @9is@7 in the midst of her; she shall not be moved: God shall help her, @9and that@7 right early.
verse	19	46	6	The heathen raged, the kingdoms were moved: he uttered his voice, the earth melted.
verse	19	46	7	@@The LORD of hosts @9is@7 with us; the God of Jacob @9is@7 our refuge. Selah.
verse	19	46	8	Come, behold the works of the LORD, what desolations he hath made in the earth.
verse	19	46	9	He maketh wars to cease unto the end of the earth; he breaketh the bow, and cutteth the spear in sunder; he burneth the chariot in the fire.
verse	19	46	10	@@Be still, and know that I @9am@7 God: I will be exalted among the heathen, I will be exalted in the earth.
verse	19	46	11	@@The LORD of hosts @9is@7 with us; the God of Jacob @9is@7 our refuge. Selah.
pericope	19	47	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.
verse	19	47	1	O clap your hands, all ye people; shout unto God with the voice of triumph.
verse	19	47	2	@@For the LORD most high @9is@7 terrible; @9he is@7 a great King over all the earth.
verse	19	47	3	He shall subdue the people under us, and the nations under our feet.
verse	19	47	4	He shall choose our inheritance for us, the excellency of Jacob whom he loved. Selah.
verse	19	47	5	God is gone up with a shout, the LORD with the sound of a trumpet.
verse	19	47	6	Sing praises to God, sing praises: sing praises unto our King, sing praises.
verse	19	47	7	@@For God @9is@7 the King of all the earth: sing ye praises with understanding.
verse	19	47	8	God reigneth over the heathen: God sitteth upon the throne of his holiness.
verse	19	47	9	@@The princes of the people are gathered together, @9even@7 the people of the God of Abraham: for the shields of the earth @9belong@7 unto God: he is greatly exalted.
pericope	19	48	1	A Song and Psalm for the sons of Korah.
verse	19	48	1	@@Great @9is@7 the LORD, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, @9in@7 the mountain of his holiness.
verse	19	48	2	@@Beautiful for situation, the joy of the whole earth, @9is@7 mount Zion, @9on@7 the sides of the north, the city of the great King.
verse	19	48	3	God is known in her palaces for a refuge.
verse	19	48	4	For, lo, the kings were assembled, they passed by together.
verse	19	48	5	@@They saw @9it, and@7 so they marvelled; they were troubled, @9and@7 hasted away.
verse	19	48	6	@@Fear took hold upon them there, @9and@7 pain, as of a woman in travail.
verse	19	48	7	Thou breakest the ships of Tarshish with an east wind.
verse	19	48	8	As we have heard, so have we seen in the city of the LORD of hosts, in the city of our God: God will establish it for ever. Selah.
verse	19	48	9	We have thought of thy lovingkindness, O God, in the midst of thy temple.
verse	19	48	10	@@According to thy name, O God, so @9is@7 thy praise unto the ends of the earth: thy right hand is full of righteousness.
verse	19	48	11	Let mount Zion rejoice, let the daughters of Judah be glad, because of thy judgments.
verse	19	48	12	Walk about Zion, and go round about her: tell the towers thereof.
verse	19	48	13	@@Mark ye well her bulwarks, consider her palaces; that ye may tell @9it@7 to the generation following.
verse	19	48	14	@@For this God @9is@7 our God for ever and ever: he will be our guide @9even@7 unto death.
pericope	19	49	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.
verse	19	49	1	@@Hear this, all @9ye@7 people; give ear, all @9ye@7 inhabitants of the world:
verse	19	49	2	Both low and high, rich and poor, together.
verse	19	49	3	@@My mouth shall speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart @9shall be@7 of understanding.
verse	19	49	4	I will incline mine ear to a parable: I will open my dark saying upon the harp.
verse	19	49	5	@@Wherefore should I fear in the days of evil, @9when@7 the iniquity of my heels shall compass me about?
verse	19	49	6	They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;
verse	19	49	7	@@None @9of them@7 can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to God a ransom for him:
verse	19	49	8	@@(For the redemption of their soul @9is@7 precious, and it ceaseth for ever:)
verse	19	49	9	@@That he should still live for ever, @9and@7 not see corruption.
verse	19	49	10	@@For he seeth @9that@7 wise men die, likewise the fool and the brutish person perish, and leave their wealth to others.
verse	19	49	11	@@Their inward thought @9is, that@7 their houses @9shall continue@7 for ever, @9and@7 their dwelling places to all generations; they call @9their@7 lands after their own names.
verse	19	49	12	@@Nevertheless man @9being@7 in honour abideth not: he is like the beasts @9that@7 perish.
verse	19	49	13	@@This their way @9is@7 their folly: yet their posterity approve their sayings. Selah.
verse	19	49	14	Like sheep they are laid in the grave; death shall feed on them; and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their beauty shall consume in the grave from their dwelling.
verse	19	49	15	But God will redeem my soul from the power of the grave: for he shall receive me. Selah.
verse	19	49	16	Be not thou afraid when one is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased;
verse	19	49	17	For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him.
verse	19	49	18	@@Though while he lived he blessed his soul: and @9men@7 will praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself.
verse	19	49	19	He shall go to the generation of his fathers; they shall never see light.
verse	19	49	20	@@Man @9that is@7 in honour, and understandeth not, is like the beasts @9that@7 perish.
pericope	19	50	1	A Psalm of Asaph.
verse	19	50	1	@@The mighty God, @9even@7 the LORD, hath spoken, and called the earth from the rising of the sun unto the going down thereof.
verse	19	50	2	Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God hath shined.
verse	19	50	3	Our God shall come, and shall not keep silence: a fire shall devour before him, and it shall be very tempestuous round about him.
verse	19	50	4	He shall call to the heavens from above, and to the earth, that he may judge his people.
verse	19	50	5	Gather my saints together unto me; those that have made a covenant with me by sacrifice.
verse	19	50	6	@@And the heavens shall declare his righteousness: for God @9is@7 judge himself. Selah.
verse	19	50	7	@@Hear, O my people, and I will speak; O Israel, and I will testify against thee: I @9am@7 God, @9even@7 thy God.
verse	19	50	8	@@I will not reprove thee for thy sacrifices or thy burnt offerings, @9to have been@7 continually before me.
verse	19	50	9	@@I will take no bullock out of thy house, @9nor@7 he goats out of thy folds.
verse	19	50	10	@@For every beast of the forest @9is@7 mine, @9and@7 the cattle upon a thousand hills.
verse	19	50	11	@@I know all the fowls of the mountains: and the wild beasts of the field @9are@7 mine.
verse	19	50	12	@@If I were hungry, I would not tell thee: for the world @9is@7 mine, and the fulness thereof.
verse	19	50	13	Will I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?
verse	19	50	14	Offer unto God thanksgiving; and pay thy vows unto the most High:
verse	19	50	15	And call upon me in the day of trouble: I will deliver thee, and thou shalt glorify me.
verse	19	50	16	@@But unto the wicked God saith, What hast thou to do to declare my statutes, or @9that@7 thou shouldest take my covenant in thy mouth?
verse	19	50	17	Seeing thou hatest instruction, and castest my words behind thee.
verse	19	50	18	When thou sawest a thief, then thou consentedst with him, and hast been partaker with adulterers.
verse	19	50	19	Thou givest thy mouth to evil, and thy tongue frameth deceit.
verse	19	50	20	@@Thou sittest @9and@7 speakest against thy brother; thou slanderest thine own mother's son.
verse	19	50	21	@@These @9things@7 hast thou done, and I kept silence; thou thoughtest that I was altogether @9such an one@7 as thyself: @9but@7 I will reprove thee, and set @9them@7 in order before thine eyes.
verse	19	50	22	@@Now consider this, ye that forget God, lest I tear @9you@7 in pieces, and @9there be@7 none to deliver.
verse	19	50	23	@@Whoso offereth praise glorifieth me: and to him that ordereth @9his@7 conversation @9aright@7 will I shew the salvation of God.
pericope	19	51	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David, when Nathan the prophet came unto him, after he had gone in to Bath-sheba.
verse	19	51	1	Have mercy upon me, O God, according to thy lovingkindness: according unto the multitude of thy tender mercies blot out my transgressions.
verse	19	51	2	Wash me throughly from mine iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.
verse	19	51	3	@@For I acknowledge my transgressions: and my sin @9is@7 ever before me.
verse	19	51	4	@@Against thee, thee only, have I sinned, and done @9this@7 evil in thy sight: that thou mightest be justified when thou speakest, @9and@7 be clear when thou judgest.
verse	19	51	5	Behold, I was shapen in iniquity; and in sin did my mother conceive me.
verse	19	51	6	@@Behold, thou desirest truth in the inward parts: and in the hidden @9part@7 thou shalt make me to know wisdom.
verse	19	51	7	Purge me with hyssop, and I shall be clean: wash me, and I shall be whiter than snow.
verse	19	51	8	@@Make me to hear joy and gladness; @9that@7 the bones @9which@7 thou hast broken may rejoice.
verse	19	51	9	Hide thy face from my sins, and blot out all mine iniquities.
verse	19	51	10	Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.
verse	19	51	11	Cast me not away from thy presence; and take not thy holy spirit from me.
verse	19	51	12	@@Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation; and uphold me @9with thy@7 free spirit.
verse	19	51	13	@@@9Then@7 will I teach transgressors thy ways; and sinners shall be converted unto thee.
verse	19	51	14	@@Deliver me from bloodguiltiness, O God, thou God of my salvation: @9and@7 my tongue shall sing aloud of thy righteousness.
verse	19	51	15	O Lord, open thou my lips; and my mouth shall shew forth thy praise.
verse	19	51	16	@@For thou desirest not sacrifice; else would I give @9it:@7 thou delightest not in burnt offering.
verse	19	51	17	@@The sacrifices of God @9are@7 a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.
verse	19	51	18	Do good in thy good pleasure unto Zion: build thou the walls of Jerusalem.
verse	19	51	19	Then shalt thou be pleased with the sacrifices of righteousness, with burnt offering and whole burnt offering: then shall they offer bullocks upon thine altar.
pericope	19	52	1	To the chief Musician, Maschil, A Psalm of David, when Doeg the Edomite came and told Saul, and said unto him, David is come to the house of Ahimelech.
verse	19	52	1	@@Why boastest thou thyself in mischief, O mighty man? the goodness of God @9endureth @7continually.
verse	19	52	2	Thy tongue deviseth mischiefs; like a sharp rasor, working deceitfully.
verse	19	52	3	@@Thou lovest evil more than good; @9and@7 lying rather than to speak righteousness. Selah.
verse	19	52	4	@@Thou lovest all devouring words, O @9thou@7 deceitful tongue.
verse	19	52	5	@@God shall likewise destroy thee for ever, he shall take thee away, and pluck thee out of @9thy@7 dwelling place, and root thee out of the land of the living. Selah.
verse	19	52	6	The righteous also shall see, and fear, and shall laugh at him:
verse	19	52	7	@@Lo, @9this is@7 the man @9that@7 made not God his strength; but trusted in the abundance of his riches, @9and@7 strengthened himself in his wickedness.
verse	19	52	8	@@But I @9am@7 like a green olive tree in the house of God: I trust in the mercy of God for ever and ever.
verse	19	52	9	@@I will praise thee for ever, because thou hast done @9it:@7 and I will wait on thy name; for @9it is@7 good before thy saints.
pericope	19	53	1	To the chief Musician upon Mahalath, Maschil, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	53	1	@@The fool hath said in his heart, @9There is@7 no God. Corrupt are they, and have done abominable iniquity: @9there is@7 none that doeth good.
verse	19	53	2	@@God looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were @9any@7 that did understand, that did seek God.
verse	19	53	3	@@Every one of them is gone back: they are altogether become filthy; @9there is@7 none that doeth good, no, not one.
verse	19	53	4	@@Have the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people @9as@7 they eat bread: they have not called upon God.
verse	19	53	5	@@There were they in great fear, @9where@7 no fear was: for God hath scattered the bones of him that encampeth @9against@7 thee: thou hast put @9them@7 to shame, because God hath despised them.
verse	19	53	6	@@Oh that the salvation of Israel @9were come@7 out of Zion! When God bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, @9and@7 Israel shall be glad.
pericope	19	54	1	To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, A Psalm of David, when the Ziphims came and said to Saul, Doth not David hide himself with us?
verse	19	54	1	Save me, O God, by thy name, and judge me by thy strength.
verse	19	54	2	Hear my prayer, O God; give ear to the words of my mouth.
verse	19	54	3	For strangers are risen up against me, and oppressors seek after my soul: they have not set God before them. Selah.
verse	19	54	4	@@Behold, God @9is@7 mine helper: the Lord @9is@7 with them that uphold my soul.
verse	19	54	5	He shall reward evil unto mine enemies: cut them off in thy truth.
verse	19	54	6	@@I will freely sacrifice unto thee: I will praise thy name, O LORD; for @9it is@7 good.
verse	19	54	7	@@For he hath delivered me out of all trouble: and mine eye hath seen @9his desire@7 upon mine enemies.
pericope	19	55	1	To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	55	1	Give ear to my prayer, O God; and hide not thyself from my supplication.
verse	19	55	2	Attend unto me, and hear me: I mourn in my complaint, and make a noise;
verse	19	55	3	Because of the voice of the enemy, because of the oppression of the wicked: for they cast iniquity upon me, and in wrath they hate me.
verse	19	55	4	My heart is sore pained within me: and the terrors of death are fallen upon me.
verse	19	55	5	Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me, and horror hath overwhelmed me.
verse	19	55	6	@@And I said, Oh that I had wings like a dove! @9for then@7 would I fly away, and be at rest.
verse	19	55	7	@@Lo, @9then@7 would I wander far off, @9and@7 remain in the wilderness. Selah.
verse	19	55	8	@@I would hasten my escape from the windy storm @9and@7 tempest.
verse	19	55	9	@@Destroy, O Lord, @9and@7 divide their tongues: for I have seen violence and strife in the city.
verse	19	55	10	@@Day and night they go about it upon the walls thereof: mischief also and sorrow @9are@7 in the midst of it.
verse	19	55	11	@@Wickedness @9is@7 in the midst thereof: deceit and guile depart not from her streets.
verse	19	55	12	@@For @9it was@7 not an enemy @9that@7 reproached me; then I could have borne @9it:@7 neither @9was it@7 he that hated me @9that@7 did magnify @9himself@7 against me; then I would have hid myself from him:
verse	19	55	13	@@But @9it was@7 thou, a man mine equal, my guide, and mine acquaintance.
verse	19	55	14	@@We took sweet counsel together, @9and@7 walked unto the house of God in company.
verse	19	55	15	@@Let death seize upon them, @9and@7 let them go down quick into hell: for wickedness is in their dwellings, @9and@7 among them.
verse	19	55	16	As for me, I will call upon God; and the LORD shall save me.
verse	19	55	17	Evening, and morning, and at noon, will I pray, and cry aloud: and he shall hear my voice.
verse	19	55	18	@@He hath delivered my soul in peace from the battle @9that was@7 against me: for there were many with me.
verse	19	55	19	God shall hear, and afflict them, even he that abideth of old. Selah. Because they have no changes, therefore they fear not God.
verse	19	55	20	He hath put forth his hands against such as be at peace with him: he hath broken his covenant.
verse	19	55	21	@@@9The words@7 of his mouth were smoother than butter, but war @9was@7 in his heart: his words were softer than oil, yet @9were@7 they drawn swords.
verse	19	55	22	Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.
verse	19	55	23	But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction: bloody and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee.
pericope	19	56	1	To the chief Musician upon Jonath-elem-rechokim, Michtam of David, when the Philistines took him in Gath.
verse	19	56	1	Be merciful unto me, O God: for man would swallow me up; he fighting daily oppresseth me.
verse	19	56	2	@@Mine enemies would daily swallow @9me@7 up: for @9they be@7 many that fight against me, O thou most High.
verse	19	56	3	What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.
verse	19	56	4	In God I will praise his word, in God I have put my trust; I will not fear what flesh can do unto me.
verse	19	56	5	@@Every day they wrest my words: all their thoughts @9are@7 against me for evil.
verse	19	56	6	They gather themselves together, they hide themselves, they mark my steps, when they wait for my soul.
verse	19	56	7	@@Shall they escape by iniquity? in @9thine@7 anger cast down the people, O God.
verse	19	56	8	@@Thou tellest my wanderings: put thou my tears into thy bottle: @9are they@7 not in thy book?
verse	19	56	9	@@When I cry @9unto thee,@7 then shall mine enemies turn back: this I know; for God @9is@7 for me.
verse	19	56	10	@@In God will I praise @9his@7 word: in the LORD will I praise @9his@7 word.
verse	19	56	11	In God have I put my trust: I will not be afraid what man can do unto me.
verse	19	56	12	@@Thy vows @9are@7 upon me, O God: I will render praises unto thee.
verse	19	56	13	@@For thou hast delivered my soul from death: @9wilt@7 not @9thou deliver@7 my feet from falling, that I may walk before God in the light of the living?
pericope	19	57	1	To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, Michtam of David, when he fled from Saul in the cave.
verse	19	57	1	@@Be merciful unto me, O God, be merciful unto me: for my soul trusteth in thee: yea, in the shadow of thy wings will I make my refuge, until @9these@7 calamities be overpast.
verse	19	57	2	@@I will cry unto God most high; unto God that performeth @9all things@7 for me.
verse	19	57	3	@@He shall send from heaven, and save @9from@7 the reproach of him that would swallow me up. Selah. God shall send forth his mercy and his truth.
verse	19	57	4	@@My soul @9is@7 among lions: @9and@7 I lie @9even among@7 them that are set on fire, @9even@7 the sons of men, whose teeth @9are@7 spears and arrows, and their tongue a sharp sword.
verse	19	57	5	@@Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens; @9let@7 thy glory @9be@7 above all the earth.
verse	19	57	6	@@They have prepared a net for my steps; my soul is bowed down: they have digged a pit before me, into the midst whereof they are fallen @9themselves.@7 Selah.
verse	19	57	7	My heart is fixed, O God, my heart is fixed: I will sing and give praise.
verse	19	57	8	@@Awake up, my glory; awake, psaltery and harp: I @9myself@7 will awake early.
verse	19	57	9	I will praise thee, O Lord, among the people: I will sing unto thee among the nations.
verse	19	57	10	For thy mercy is great unto the heavens, and thy truth unto the clouds.
verse	19	57	11	@@Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: @9let@7 thy glory @9be@7 above all the earth.
pericope	19	58	1	To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, Michtam of David.
verse	19	58	1	Do ye indeed speak righteousness, O congregation? do ye judge uprightly, O ye sons of men?
verse	19	58	2	Yea, in heart ye work wickedness; ye weigh the violence of your hands in the earth.
verse	19	58	3	The wicked are estranged from the womb: they go astray as soon as they be born, speaking lies.
verse	19	58	4	@@Their poison @9is@7 like the poison of a serpent: @9they are@7 like the deaf adder @9that@7 stoppeth her ear;
verse	19	58	5	Which will not hearken to the voice of charmers, charming never so wisely.
verse	19	58	6	Break their teeth, O God, in their mouth: break out the great teeth of the young lions, O LORD.
verse	19	58	7	@@Let them melt away as waters @9which@7 run continually: @9when@7 he bendeth @9his bow to shoot@7 his arrows, let them be as cut in pieces.
verse	19	58	8	@@As a snail @9which@7 melteth, let @9every one of them@7 pass away: @9like@7 the untimely birth of a woman, @9that@7 they may not see the sun.
verse	19	58	9	@@Before your pots can feel the thorns, he shall take them away as with a whirlwind, both living, and in @9his@7 wrath.
verse	19	58	10	The righteous shall rejoice when he seeth the vengeance: he shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked.
verse	19	58	11	@@So that a man shall say, Verily @9there is@7 a reward for the righteous: verily he is a God that judgeth in the earth.
pericope	19	59	1	To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, Michtam of David; when Saul sent, and they watched the house to kill him.
verse	19	59	1	Deliver me from mine enemies, O my God: defend me from them that rise up against me.
verse	19	59	2	Deliver me from the workers of iniquity, and save me from bloody men.
verse	19	59	3	@@For, lo, they lie in wait for my soul: the mighty are gathered against me; not @9for@7 my transgression, nor @9for@7 my sin, O LORD.
verse	19	59	4	@@They run and prepare themselves without @9my@7 fault: awake to help me, and behold.
verse	19	59	5	Thou therefore, O LORD God of hosts, the God of Israel, awake to visit all the heathen: be not merciful to any wicked transgressors. Selah.
verse	19	59	6	They return at evening: they make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.
verse	19	59	7	@@Behold, they belch out with their mouth: swords @9are@7 in their lips: for who, @9say they,@7 doth hear?
verse	19	59	8	But thou, O LORD, shalt laugh at them; thou shalt have all the heathen in derision.
verse	19	59	9	@@@9Because of@7 his strength will I wait upon thee: for God @9is@7 my defence.
verse	19	59	10	@@The God of my mercy shall prevent me: God shall let me see @9my desire@7 upon mine enemies.
verse	19	59	11	Slay them not, lest my people forget: scatter them by thy power; and bring them down, O Lord our shield.
verse	19	59	12	@@@9For@7 the sin of their mouth @9and@7 the words of their lips let them even be taken in their pride: and for cursing and lying @9which@7 they speak.
verse	19	59	13	@@Consume @9them@7 in wrath, consume @9them,@7 that they @9may@7 not @9be:@7 and let them know that God ruleth in Jacob unto the ends of the earth. Selah.
verse	19	59	14	@@And at evening let them return; @9and@7 let them make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.
verse	19	59	15	Let them wander up and down for meat, and grudge if they be not satisfied.
verse	19	59	16	But I will sing of thy power; yea, I will sing aloud of thy mercy in the morning: for thou hast been my defence and refuge in the day of my trouble.
verse	19	59	17	@@Unto thee, O my strength, will I sing: for God @9is@7 my defence, @9and@7 the God of my mercy.
pericope	19	60	1	To the chief Musician upon Shushan-eduth, Michtam of David, to teach; when he strove with Aram-naharaim and with Aram-zobah, when Joab returned, and smote of Edom in the valley of salt twelve thousand.
verse	19	60	1	O God, thou hast cast us off, thou hast scattered us, thou hast been displeased; O turn thyself to us again.
verse	19	60	2	Thou hast made the earth to tremble; thou hast broken it: heal the breaches thereof; for it shaketh.
verse	19	60	3	Thou hast shewed thy people hard things: thou hast made us to drink the wine of astonishment.
verse	19	60	4	Thou hast given a banner to them that fear thee, that it may be displayed because of the truth. Selah.
verse	19	60	5	@@That thy beloved may be delivered; save @9with@7 thy right hand, and hear me.
verse	19	60	6	God hath spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.
verse	19	60	7	@@Gilead @9is@7 mine, and Manasseh @9is@7 mine; Ephraim also @9is@7 the strength of mine head; Judah @9is@7 my lawgiver;
verse	19	60	8	@@Moab @9is@7 my washpot; over Edom will I cast out my shoe: Philistia, triumph thou because of me.
verse	19	60	9	@@Who will bring me @9into@7 the strong city? who will lead me into Edom?
verse	19	60	10	@@@9Wilt@7 not thou, O God, @9which@7 hadst cast us off? and @9thou,@7 O God, @9which@7 didst not go out with our armies?
verse	19	60	11	@@Give us help from trouble: for vain @9is@7 the help of man.
verse	19	60	12	@@Through God we shall do valiantly: for he @9it is that@7 shall tread down our enemies.
pericope	19	61	1	To the chief Musician upon Neginah, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	61	1	Hear my cry, O God; attend unto my prayer.
verse	19	61	2	@@From the end of the earth will I cry unto thee, when my heart is overwhelmed: lead me to the rock @9that@7 is higher than I.
verse	19	61	3	@@For thou hast been a shelter for me, @9and@7 a strong tower from the enemy.
verse	19	61	4	I will abide in thy tabernacle for ever: I will trust in the covert of thy wings. Selah.
verse	19	61	5	@@For thou, O God, hast heard my vows: thou hast given @9me@7 the heritage of those that fear thy name.
verse	19	61	6	@@Thou wilt prolong the king's life: @9and@7 his years as many generations.
verse	19	61	7	@@He shall abide before God for ever: O prepare mercy and truth, @9which@7 may preserve him.
verse	19	61	8	So will I sing praise unto thy name for ever, that I may daily perform my vows.
pericope	19	62	1	To the chief Musician, to Jeduthun, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	62	1	@@Truly my soul waiteth upon God: from him @9cometh@7 my salvation.
verse	19	62	2	@@He only @9is@7 my rock and my salvation; @9he is@7 my defence; I shall not be greatly moved.
verse	19	62	3	@@How long will ye imagine mischief against a man? ye shall be slain all of you: as a bowing wall @9shall ye be, and as@7 a tottering fence.
verse	19	62	4	@@They only consult to cast @9him@7 down from his excellency: they delight in lies: they bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly. Selah.
verse	19	62	5	@@My soul, wait thou only upon God; for my expectation @9is@7 from him.
verse	19	62	6	@@He only @9is@7 my rock and my salvation: @9he is@7 my defence; I shall not be moved.
verse	19	62	7	@@In God @9is@7 my salvation and my glory: the rock of my strength, @9and@7 my refuge, @9is@7 in God.
verse	19	62	8	@@Trust in him at all times; @9ye@7 people, pour out your heart before him: God @9is@7 a refuge for us. Selah.
verse	19	62	9	@@Surely men of low degree @9are@7 vanity, @9and@7 men of high degree @9are@7 a lie: to be laid in the balance, they @9are@7 altogether @9lighter@7 than vanity.
verse	19	62	10	@@Trust not in oppression, and become not vain in robbery: if riches increase, set not your heart @9upon them.@7
verse	19	62	11	@@God hath spoken once; twice have I heard this; that power @9belongeth@7 unto God.
verse	19	62	12	@@Also unto thee, O Lord, @9belongeth@7 mercy: for thou renderest to every man according to his work.
pericope	19	63	1	A Psalm of David, when he was in the wilderness of Judah.
verse	19	63	1	@@O God, thou @9art@7 my God; early will I seek thee: my soul thirsteth for thee, my flesh longeth for thee in a dry and thirsty land, where no water is;
verse	19	63	2	@@To see thy power and thy glory, so @9as@7 I have seen thee in the sanctuary.
verse	19	63	3	@@Because thy lovingkindness @9is@7 better than life, my lips shall praise thee.
verse	19	63	4	Thus will I bless thee while I live: I will lift up my hands in thy name.
verse	19	63	5	@@My soul shall be satisfied as @9with@7 marrow and fatness; and my mouth shall praise @9thee@7 with joyful lips:
verse	19	63	6	@@When I remember thee upon my bed, @9and@7 meditate on thee in the @9night@7 watches.
verse	19	63	7	Because thou hast been my help, therefore in the shadow of thy wings will I rejoice.
verse	19	63	8	My soul followeth hard after thee: thy right hand upholdeth me.
verse	19	63	9	@@But those @9that@7 seek my soul, to destroy @9it,@7 shall go into the lower parts of the earth.
verse	19	63	10	They shall fall by the sword: they shall be a portion for foxes.
verse	19	63	11	But the king shall rejoice in God; every one that sweareth by him shall glory: but the mouth of them that speak lies shall be stopped.
pericope	19	64	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	64	1	Hear my voice, O God, in my prayer: preserve my life from fear of the enemy.
verse	19	64	2	Hide me from the secret counsel of the wicked; from the insurrection of the workers of iniquity:
verse	19	64	3	@@Who whet their tongue like a sword, @9and@7 bend @9their bows to shoot@7 their arrows, @9even@7 bitter words:
verse	19	64	4	That they may shoot in secret at the perfect: suddenly do they shoot at him, and fear not.
verse	19	64	5	@@They encourage themselves @9in@7 an evil matter: they commune of laying snares privily; they say, Who shall see them?
verse	19	64	6	@@They search out iniquities; they accomplish a diligent search: both the inward @9thought@7 of every one @9of them,@7 and the heart, @9is@7 deep.
verse	19	64	7	@@But God shall shoot at them @9with@7 an arrow; suddenly shall they be wounded.
verse	19	64	8	So they shall make their own tongue to fall upon themselves: all that see them shall flee away.
verse	19	64	9	And all men shall fear, and shall declare the work of God; for they shall wisely consider of his doing.
verse	19	64	10	The righteous shall be glad in the LORD, and shall trust in him; and all the upright in heart shall glory.
pericope	19	65	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm and Song of David.
verse	19	65	1	Praise waiteth for thee, O God, in Sion: and unto thee shall the vow be performed.
verse	19	65	2	O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come.
verse	19	65	3	@@Iniquities prevail against me: @9as for@7 our transgressions, thou shalt purge them away.
verse	19	65	4	@@Blessed @9is the man whom@7 thou choosest, and causest to approach @9unto thee, that@7 he may dwell in thy courts: we shall be satisfied with the goodness of thy house, @9even@7 of thy holy temple.
verse	19	65	5	@@By terrible things in righteousness wilt thou answer us, O God of our salvation; @9who art@7 the confidence of all the ends of the earth, and of them that are afar off @9upon@7 the sea:
verse	19	65	6	@@Which by his strength setteth fast the mountains; @9being@7 girded with power:
verse	19	65	7	Which stilleth the noise of the seas, the noise of their waves, and the tumult of the people.
verse	19	65	8	They also that dwell in the uttermost parts are afraid at thy tokens: thou makest the outgoings of the morning and evening to rejoice.
verse	19	65	9	@@Thou visitest the earth, and waterest it: thou greatly enrichest it with the river of God, @9which@7 is full of water: thou preparest them corn, when thou hast so provided for it.
verse	19	65	10	Thou waterest the ridges thereof abundantly: thou settlest the furrows thereof: thou makest it soft with showers: thou blessest the springing thereof.
verse	19	65	11	Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; and thy paths drop fatness.
verse	19	65	12	@@They drop @9upon@7 the pastures of the wilderness: and the little hills rejoice on every side.
verse	19	65	13	The pastures are clothed with flocks; the valleys also are covered over with corn; they shout for joy, they also sing.
pericope	19	66	1	To the chief Musician, A Song or Psalm.
verse	19	66	1	Make a joyful noise unto God, all ye lands:
verse	19	66	2	Sing forth the honour of his name: make his praise glorious.
verse	19	66	3	@@Say unto God, How terrible @9art thou in@7 thy works! through the greatness of thy power shall thine enemies submit themselves unto thee.
verse	19	66	4	@@All the earth shall worship thee, and shall sing unto thee; they shall sing @9to@7 thy name. Selah.
verse	19	66	5	@@Come and see the works of God: @9he is@7 terrible @9in his@7 doing toward the children of men.
verse	19	66	6	@@He turned the sea into dry @9land:@7 they went through the flood on foot: there did we rejoice in him.
verse	19	66	7	He ruleth by his power for ever; his eyes behold the nations: let not the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah.
verse	19	66	8	O bless our God, ye people, and make the voice of his praise to be heard:
verse	19	66	9	Which holdeth our soul in life, and suffereth not our feet to be moved.
verse	19	66	10	For thou, O God, hast proved us: thou hast tried us, as silver is tried.
verse	19	66	11	Thou broughtest us into the net; thou laidst affliction upon our loins.
verse	19	66	12	@@Thou hast caused men to ride over our heads; we went through fire and through water: but thou broughtest us out into a wealthy @9place.@7
verse	19	66	13	I will go into thy house with burnt offerings: I will pay thee my vows,
verse	19	66	14	Which my lips have uttered, and my mouth hath spoken, when I was in trouble.
verse	19	66	15	I will offer unto thee burnt sacrifices of fatlings, with the incense of rams; I will offer bullocks with goats. Selah.
verse	19	66	16	@@Come @9and@7 hear, all ye that fear God, and I will declare what he hath done for my soul.
verse	19	66	17	I cried unto him with my mouth, and he was extolled with my tongue.
verse	19	66	18	@@If I regard iniquity in my heart, the Lord will not hear @9me:@7
verse	19	66	19	@@@9But@7 verily God hath heard @9me;@7 he hath attended to the voice of my prayer.
verse	19	66	20	@@Blessed @9be@7 God, which hath not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me.
pericope	19	67	1	To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm or Song.
verse	19	67	1	@@God be merciful unto us, and bless us; @9and@7 cause his face to shine upon us; Selah.
verse	19	67	2	That thy way may be known upon earth, thy saving health among all nations.
verse	19	67	3	Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.
verse	19	67	4	O let the nations be glad and sing for joy: for thou shalt judge the people righteously, and govern the nations upon earth. Selah.
verse	19	67	5	Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.
verse	19	67	6	@@@9Then@7 shall the earth yield her increase; @9and@7 God, @9even@7 our own God, shall bless us.
verse	19	67	7	God shall bless us; and all the ends of the earth shall fear him.
pericope	19	68	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm or Song of David.
verse	19	68	1	Let God arise, let his enemies be scattered: let them also that hate him flee before him.
verse	19	68	2	@@As smoke is driven away, @9so@7 drive @9them@7 away: as wax melteth before the fire, @9so@7 let the wicked perish at the presence of God.
verse	19	68	3	But let the righteous be glad; let them rejoice before God: yea, let them exceedingly rejoice.
verse	19	68	4	Sing unto God, sing praises to his name: extol him that rideth upon the heavens by his name JAH, and rejoice before him.
verse	19	68	5	@@A father of the fatherless, and a judge of the widows, @9is@7 God in his holy habitation.
verse	19	68	6	@@God setteth the solitary in families: he bringeth out those which are bound with chains: but the rebellious dwell in a dry @9land.@7
verse	19	68	7	O God, when thou wentest forth before thy people, when thou didst march through the wilderness; Selah:
verse	19	68	8	@@The earth shook, the heavens also dropped at the presence of God: @9even@7 Sinai itself @9was moved@7 at the presence of God, the God of Israel.
verse	19	68	9	Thou, O God, didst send a plentiful rain, whereby thou didst confirm thine inheritance, when it was weary.
verse	19	68	10	Thy congregation hath dwelt therein: thou, O God, hast prepared of thy goodness for the poor.
verse	19	68	11	@@The Lord gave the word: great @9was@7 the company of those that published @9it.@7
verse	19	68	12	Kings of armies did flee apace: and she that tarried at home divided the spoil.
verse	19	68	13	@@Though ye have lien among the pots, @9yet shall ye be as@7 the wings of a dove covered with silver, and her feathers with yellow gold.
verse	19	68	14	@@When the Almighty scattered kings in it, it was @9white@7 as snow in Salmon.
verse	19	68	15	@@The hill of God @9is as@7 the hill of Bashan; an high hill @9as@7 the hill of Bashan.
verse	19	68	16	@@Why leap ye, ye high hills? @9this is@7 the hill @9which@7 God desireth to dwell in; yea, the LORD will dwell @9in it@7 for ever.
verse	19	68	17	@@The chariots of God @9are@7 twenty thousand, @9even@7 thousands of angels: the Lord @9is@7 among them, @9as in@7 Sinai, in the holy @9place.@7
verse	19	68	18	@@Thou hast ascended on high, thou hast led captivity captive: thou hast received gifts for men; yea, @9for@7 the rebellious also, that the LORD God might dwell @9among them.@7
verse	19	68	19	@@Blessed @9be@7 the Lord, @9who@7 daily loadeth us @9with benefits, even@7 the God of our salvation. Selah.
verse	19	68	20	@@@9He that is@7 our God @9is@7 the God of salvation; and unto God the Lord @9belong@7 the issues from death.
verse	19	68	21	@@But God shall wound the head of his enemies, @9and@7 the hairy scalp of such an one as goeth on still in his trespasses.
verse	19	68	22	@@The Lord said, I will bring again from Bashan, I will bring @9my people@7 again from the depths of the sea:
verse	19	68	23	@@That thy foot may be dipped in the blood of @9thine@7 enemies, @9and@7 the tongue of thy dogs in the same.
verse	19	68	24	@@They have seen thy goings, O God; @9even@7 the goings of my God, my King, in the sanctuary.
verse	19	68	25	@@The singers went before, the players on instruments @9followed@7 after; among @9them were@7 the damsels playing with timbrels.
verse	19	68	26	@@Bless ye God in the congregations, @9even@7 the Lord, from the fountain of Israel.
verse	19	68	27	@@There @9is@7 little Benjamin @9with@7 their ruler, the princes of Judah @9and@7 their council, the princes of Zebulun, @9and@7 the princes of Naphtali.
verse	19	68	28	Thy God hath commanded thy strength: strengthen, O God, that which thou hast wrought for us.
verse	19	68	29	Because of thy temple at Jerusalem shall kings bring presents unto thee.
verse	19	68	30	@@Rebuke the company of spearmen, the multitude of the bulls, with the calves of the people, @9till every one@7 submit himself with pieces of silver: scatter thou the people @9that@7 delight in war.
verse	19	68	31	Princes shall come out of Egypt; Ethiopia shall soon stretch out her hands unto God.
verse	19	68	32	Sing unto God, ye kingdoms of the earth; O sing praises unto the Lord; Selah:
verse	19	68	33	@@To him that rideth upon the heavens of heavens, @9which were@7 of old; lo, he doth send out his voice, @9and that@7 a mighty voice.
verse	19	68	34	@@Ascribe ye strength unto God: his excellency @9is@7 over Israel, and his strength @9is@7 in the clouds.
verse	19	68	35	@@O God, @9thou art@7 terrible out of thy holy places: the God of Israel @9is@7 he that giveth strength and power unto @9his@7 people. Blessed @9be@7 God.
pericope	19	69	1	To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	69	1	@@Save me, O God; for the waters are come in unto @9my@7 soul.
verse	19	69	2	@@I sink in deep mire, where @9there is@7 no standing: I am come into deep waters, where the floods overflow me.
verse	19	69	3	I am weary of my crying: my throat is dried: mine eyes fail while I wait for my God.
verse	19	69	4	@@They that hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of mine head: they that would destroy me, @9being@7 mine enemies wrongfully, are mighty: then I restored @9that@7 which I took not away.
verse	19	69	5	O God, thou knowest my foolishness; and my sins are not hid from thee.
verse	19	69	6	Let not them that wait on thee, O Lord GOD of hosts, be ashamed for my sake: let not those that seek thee be confounded for my sake, O God of Israel.
verse	19	69	7	Because for thy sake I have borne reproach; shame hath covered my face.
verse	19	69	8	I am become a stranger unto my brethren, and an alien unto my mother's children.
verse	19	69	9	For the zeal of thine house hath eaten me up; and the reproaches of them that reproached thee are fallen upon me.
verse	19	69	10	@@When I wept, @9and chastened@7 my soul with fasting, that was to my reproach.
verse	19	69	11	I made sackcloth also my garment; and I became a proverb to them.
verse	19	69	12	@@They that sit in the gate speak against me; and I @9was@7 the song of the drunkards.
verse	19	69	13	@@But as for me, my prayer @9is@7 unto thee, O LORD, @9in@7 an acceptable time: O God, in the multitude of thy mercy hear me, in the truth of thy salvation.
verse	19	69	14	Deliver me out of the mire, and let me not sink: let me be delivered from them that hate me, and out of the deep waters.
verse	19	69	15	Let not the waterflood overflow me, neither let the deep swallow me up, and let not the pit shut her mouth upon me.
verse	19	69	16	@@Hear me, O LORD; for thy lovingkindness @9is@7 good: turn unto me according to the multitude of thy tender mercies.
verse	19	69	17	And hide not thy face from thy servant; for I am in trouble: hear me speedily.
verse	19	69	18	@@Draw nigh unto my soul, @9and@7 redeem it: deliver me because of mine enemies.
verse	19	69	19	@@Thou hast known my reproach, and my shame, and my dishonour: mine adversaries @9are@7 all before thee.
verse	19	69	20	@@Reproach hath broken my heart; and I am full of heaviness: and I looked @9for some@7 to take pity, but @9there was@7 none; and for comforters, but I found none.
verse	19	69	21	They gave me also gall for my meat; and in my thirst they gave me vinegar to drink.
verse	19	69	22	@@Let their table become a snare before them: and @9that which should have been@7 for @9their@7 welfare, @9let it become@7 a trap.
verse	19	69	23	Let their eyes be darkened, that they see not; and make their loins continually to shake.
verse	19	69	24	Pour out thine indignation upon them, and let thy wrathful anger take hold of them.
verse	19	69	25	@@Let their habitation be desolate; @9and@7 let none dwell in their tents.
verse	19	69	26	@@For they persecute @9him@7 whom thou hast smitten; and they talk to the grief of those whom thou hast wounded.
verse	19	69	27	Add iniquity unto their iniquity: and let them not come into thy righteousness.
verse	19	69	28	Let them be blotted out of the book of the living, and not be written with the righteous.
verse	19	69	29	@@But I @9am@7 poor and sorrowful: let thy salvation, O God, set me up on high.
verse	19	69	30	I will praise the name of God with a song, and will magnify him with thanksgiving.
verse	19	69	31	@@@9This@7 also shall please the LORD better than an ox @9or@7 bullock that hath horns and hoofs.
verse	19	69	32	@@The humble shall see @9this, and@7 be glad: and your heart shall live that seek God.
verse	19	69	33	For the LORD heareth the poor, and despiseth not his prisoners.
verse	19	69	34	Let the heaven and earth praise him, the seas, and every thing that moveth therein.
verse	19	69	35	For God will save Zion, and will build the cities of Judah: that they may dwell there, and have it in possession.
verse	19	69	36	The seed also of his servants shall inherit it: and they that love his name shall dwell therein.
pericope	19	70	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David, to bring to remembrance.
verse	19	70	1	@@@9Make haste,@7 O God, to deliver me; make haste to help me, O LORD.
verse	19	70	2	Let them be ashamed and confounded that seek after my soul: let them be turned backward, and put to confusion, that desire my hurt.
verse	19	70	3	Let them be turned back for a reward of their shame that say, Aha, aha.
verse	19	70	4	Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: and let such as love thy salvation say continually, Let God be magnified.
verse	19	70	5	@@But I @9am@7 poor and needy: make haste unto me, O God: thou @9art@7 my help and my deliverer; O LORD, make no tarrying.
verse	19	71	1	In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust: let me never be put to confusion.
verse	19	71	2	Deliver me in thy righteousness, and cause me to escape: incline thine ear unto me, and save me.
verse	19	71	3	@@Be thou my strong habitation, whereunto I may continually resort: thou hast given commandment to save me; for thou @9art@7 my rock and my fortress.
verse	19	71	4	Deliver me, O my God, out of the hand of the wicked, out of the hand of the unrighteous and cruel man.
verse	19	71	5	@@For thou @9art@7 my hope, O Lord GOD: @9thou art@7 my trust from my youth.
verse	19	71	6	@@By thee have I been holden up from the womb: thou art he that took me out of my mother's bowels: my praise @9shall be@7 continually of thee.
verse	19	71	7	@@I am as a wonder unto many; but thou @9art@7 my strong refuge.
verse	19	71	8	@@Let my mouth be filled @9with@7 thy praise @9and with@7 thy honour all the day.
verse	19	71	9	Cast me not off in the time of old age; forsake me not when my strength faileth.
verse	19	71	10	For mine enemies speak against me; and they that lay wait for my soul take counsel together,
verse	19	71	11	@@Saying, God hath forsaken him: persecute and take him; for @9there is@7 none to deliver @9him.@7
verse	19	71	12	O God, be not far from me: O my God, make haste for my help.
verse	19	71	13	@@Let them be confounded @9and@7 consumed that are adversaries to my soul; let them be covered @9with@7 reproach and dishonour that seek my hurt.
verse	19	71	14	But I will hope continually, and will yet praise thee more and more.
verse	19	71	15	@@My mouth shall shew forth thy righteousness @9and@7 thy salvation all the day; for I know not the numbers @9thereof.@7
verse	19	71	16	@@I will go in the strength of the Lord GOD: I will make mention of thy righteousness, @9even@7 of thine only.
verse	19	71	17	O God, thou hast taught me from my youth: and hitherto have I declared thy wondrous works.
verse	19	71	18	@@Now also when I am old and greyheaded, O God, forsake me not; until I have shewed thy strength unto @9this@7 generation, @9and@7 thy power to every one @9that@7 is to come.
verse	19	71	19	@@Thy righteousness also, O God, @9is@7 very high, who hast done great things: O God, who @9is@7 like unto thee!
verse	19	71	20	@@@9Thou,@7 which hast shewed me great and sore troubles, shalt quicken me again, and shalt bring me up again from the depths of the earth.
verse	19	71	21	Thou shalt increase my greatness, and comfort me on every side.
verse	19	71	22	@@I will also praise thee with the psaltery, @9even@7 thy truth, O my God: unto thee will I sing with the harp, O thou Holy One of Israel.
verse	19	71	23	My lips shall greatly rejoice when I sing unto thee; and my soul, which thou hast redeemed.
verse	19	71	24	My tongue also shall talk of thy righteousness all the day long: for they are confounded, for they are brought unto shame, that seek my hurt.
pericope	19	72	1	A Psalm for Solomon.
verse	19	72	1	Give the king thy judgments, O God, and thy righteousness unto the king's son.
verse	19	72	2	He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment.
verse	19	72	3	The mountains shall bring peace to the people, and the little hills, by righteousness.
verse	19	72	4	He shall judge the poor of the people, he shall save the children of the needy, and shall break in pieces the oppressor.
verse	19	72	5	They shall fear thee as long as the sun and moon endure, throughout all generations.
verse	19	72	6	@@He shall come down like rain upon the mown grass: as showers @9that@7 water the earth.
verse	19	72	7	In his days shall the righteous flourish; and abundance of peace so long as the moon endureth.
verse	19	72	8	He shall have dominion also from sea to sea, and from the river unto the ends of the earth.
verse	19	72	9	They that dwell in the wilderness shall bow before him; and his enemies shall lick the dust.
verse	19	72	10	The kings of Tarshish and of the isles shall bring presents: the kings of Sheba and Seba shall offer gifts.
verse	19	72	11	Yea, all kings shall fall down before him: all nations shall serve him.
verse	19	72	12	@@For he shall deliver the needy when he crieth; the poor also, and @9him@7 that hath no helper.
verse	19	72	13	He shall spare the poor and needy, and shall save the souls of the needy.
verse	19	72	14	He shall redeem their soul from deceit and violence: and precious shall their blood be in his sight.
verse	19	72	15	@@And he shall live, and to him shall be given of the gold of Sheba: prayer also shall be made for him continually; @9and@7 daily shall he be praised.
verse	19	72	16	@@There shall be an handful of corn in the earth upon the top of the mountains; the fruit thereof shall shake like Lebanon: and @9they@7 of the city shall flourish like grass of the earth.
verse	19	72	17	@@His name shall endure for ever: his name shall be continued as long as the sun: and @9men@7 shall be blessed in him: all nations shall call him blessed.
verse	19	72	18	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD God, the God of Israel, who only doeth wondrous things.
verse	19	72	19	@@And blessed @9be@7 his glorious name for ever: and let the whole earth be filled @9with@7 his glory; Amen, and Amen.
verse	19	72	20	The prayers of David the son of Jesse are ended.
pericope	19	73	1	A Psalm of Asaph.
verse	19	73	1	@@Truly God @9is@7 good to Israel, @9even@7 to such as are of a clean heart.
verse	19	73	2	But as for me, my feet were almost gone; my steps had well nigh slipped.
verse	19	73	3	@@For I was envious at the foolish, @9when@7 I saw the prosperity of the wicked.
verse	19	73	4	@@For @9there are@7 no bands in their death: but their strength @9is@7 firm.
verse	19	73	5	@@They @9are@7 not in trouble @9as other@7 men; neither are they plagued like @9other@7 men.
verse	19	73	6	@@Therefore pride compasseth them about as a chain; violence covereth them @9as@7 a garment.
verse	19	73	7	Their eyes stand out with fatness: they have more than heart could wish.
verse	19	73	8	@@They are corrupt, and speak wickedly @9concerning@7 oppression: they speak loftily.
verse	19	73	9	They set their mouth against the heavens, and their tongue walketh through the earth.
verse	19	73	10	@@Therefore his people return hither: and waters of a full @9cup@7 are wrung out to them.
verse	19	73	11	And they say, How doth God know? and is there knowledge in the most High?
verse	19	73	12	@@Behold, these @9are@7 the ungodly, who prosper in the world; they increase @9in@7 riches.
verse	19	73	13	@@Verily I have cleansed my heart @9in@7 vain, and washed my hands in innocency.
verse	19	73	14	For all the day long have I been plagued, and chastened every morning.
verse	19	73	15	@@If I say, I will speak thus; behold, I should offend @9against@7 the generation of thy children.
verse	19	73	16	@@When I thought to know this, it @9was@7 too painful for me;
verse	19	73	17	@@Until I went into the sanctuary of God; @9then@7 understood I their end.
verse	19	73	18	Surely thou didst set them in slippery places: thou castedst them down into destruction.
verse	19	73	19	@@How are they @9brought@7 into desolation, as in a moment! they are utterly consumed with terrors.
verse	19	73	20	@@As a dream when @9one@7 awaketh; @9so,@7 O Lord, when thou awakest, thou shalt despise their image.
verse	19	73	21	Thus my heart was grieved, and I was pricked in my reins.
verse	19	73	22	@@So foolish @9was@7 I, and ignorant: I was @9as@7 a beast before thee.
verse	19	73	23	@@Nevertheless I @9am@7 continually with thee: thou hast holden @9me@7 by my right hand.
verse	19	73	24	@@Thou shalt guide me with thy counsel, and afterward receive me @9to@7 glory.
verse	19	73	25	@@Whom have I in heaven @9but thee?@7 and @9there is@7 none upon earth @9that@7 I desire beside thee.
verse	19	73	26	@@My flesh and my heart faileth: @9but@7 God @9is@7 the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.
verse	19	73	27	For, lo, they that are far from thee shall perish: thou hast destroyed all them that go a whoring from thee.
verse	19	73	28	@@But @9it is@7 good for me to draw near to God: I have put my trust in the Lord GOD, that I may declare all thy works.
pericope	19	74	1	Maschil of Asaph.
verse	19	74	1	@@O God, why hast thou cast us off for ever? @9why@7 doth thine anger smoke against the sheep of thy pasture?
verse	19	74	2	@@Remember thy congregation, @9which@7 thou hast purchased of old; the rod of thine inheritance, @9which@7 thou hast redeemed; this mount Zion, wherein thou hast dwelt.
verse	19	74	3	@@Lift up thy feet unto the perpetual desolations; @9even@7 all @9that@7 the enemy hath done wickedly in the sanctuary.
verse	19	74	4	@@Thine enemies roar in the midst of thy congregations; they set up their ensigns @9for@7 signs.
verse	19	74	5	@@@9A man@7 was famous according as he had lifted up axes upon the thick trees.
verse	19	74	6	But now they break down the carved work thereof at once with axes and hammers.
verse	19	74	7	@@They have cast fire into thy sanctuary, they have defiled @9by casting down@7 the dwelling place of thy name to the ground.
verse	19	74	8	They said in their hearts, Let us destroy them together: they have burned up all the synagogues of God in the land.
verse	19	74	9	@@We see not our signs: @9there is@7 no more any prophet: neither @9is there@7 among us any that knoweth how long.
verse	19	74	10	O God, how long shall the adversary reproach? shall the enemy blaspheme thy name for ever?
verse	19	74	11	@@Why withdrawest thou thy hand, even thy right hand? pluck @9it@7 out of thy bosom.
verse	19	74	12	@@For God @9is@7 my King of old, working salvation in the midst of the earth.
verse	19	74	13	Thou didst divide the sea by thy strength: thou brakest the heads of the dragons in the waters.
verse	19	74	14	@@Thou brakest the heads of leviathan in pieces, @9and@7 gavest him @9to be@7 meat to the people inhabiting the wilderness.
verse	19	74	15	Thou didst cleave the fountain and the flood: thou driedst up mighty rivers.
verse	19	74	16	@@The day @9is@7 thine, the night also @9is@7 thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun.
verse	19	74	17	Thou hast set all the borders of the earth: thou hast made summer and winter.
verse	19	74	18	@@Remember this, @9that@7 the enemy hath reproached, O LORD, and @9that@7 the foolish people have blasphemed thy name.
verse	19	74	19	@@O deliver not the soul of thy turtledove unto the multitude @9of the wicked:@7 forget not the congregation of thy poor for ever.
verse	19	74	20	Have respect unto the covenant: for the dark places of the earth are full of the habitations of cruelty.
verse	19	74	21	O let not the oppressed return ashamed: let the poor and needy praise thy name.
verse	19	74	22	Arise, O God, plead thine own cause: remember how the foolish man reproacheth thee daily.
verse	19	74	23	Forget not the voice of thine enemies: the tumult of those that rise up against thee increaseth continually.
pericope	19	75	1	To the chief Musician, Al-taschith, A Psalm or Song of Asaph.
verse	19	75	1	@@Unto thee, O God, do we give thanks, @9unto thee@7 do we give thanks: for @9that@7 thy name is near thy wondrous works declare.
verse	19	75	2	When I shall receive the congregation I will judge uprightly.
verse	19	75	3	The earth and all the inhabitants thereof are dissolved: I bear up the pillars of it. Selah.
verse	19	75	4	I said unto the fools, Deal not foolishly: and to the wicked, Lift not up the horn:
verse	19	75	5	@@Lift not up your horn on high: speak @9not with@7 a stiff neck.
verse	19	75	6	@@For promotion @9cometh@7 neither from the east, nor from the west, nor from the south.
verse	19	75	7	@@But God @9is@7 the judge: he putteth down one, and setteth up another.
verse	19	75	8	@@For in the hand of the LORD @9there is@7 a cup, and the wine is red; it is full of mixture; and he poureth out of the same: but the dregs thereof, all the wicked of the earth shall wring @9them@7 out, @9and@7 drink @9them.@7
verse	19	75	9	But I will declare for ever; I will sing praises to the God of Jacob.
verse	19	75	10	@@All the horns of the wicked also will I cut off; @9but@7 the horns of the righteous shall be exalted.
pericope	19	76	1	To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm or Song of Asaph.
verse	19	76	1	@@In Judah @9is@7 God known: his name @9is@7 great in Israel.
verse	19	76	2	In Salem also is his tabernacle, and his dwelling place in Zion.
verse	19	76	3	There brake he the arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the battle. Selah.
verse	19	76	4	@@Thou @9art@7 more glorious @9and@7 excellent than the mountains of prey.
verse	19	76	5	The stouthearted are spoiled, they have slept their sleep: and none of the men of might have found their hands.
verse	19	76	6	At thy rebuke, O God of Jacob, both the chariot and horse are cast into a dead sleep.
verse	19	76	7	@@Thou, @9even@7 thou, @9art@7 to be feared: and who may stand in thy sight when once thou art angry?
verse	19	76	8	Thou didst cause judgment to be heard from heaven; the earth feared, and was still,
verse	19	76	9	When God arose to judgment, to save all the meek of the earth. Selah.
verse	19	76	10	Surely the wrath of man shall praise thee: the remainder of wrath shalt thou restrain.
verse	19	76	11	Vow, and pay unto the LORD your God: let all that be round about him bring presents unto him that ought to be feared.
verse	19	76	12	@@He shall cut off the spirit of princes: @9he is@7 terrible to the kings of the earth.
pericope	19	77	1	To the chief Musician, to Jeduthun, A Psalm of Asaph.
verse	19	77	1	@@I cried unto God with my voice, @9even@7 unto God with my voice; and he gave ear unto me.
verse	19	77	2	In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord: my sore ran in the night, and ceased not: my soul refused to be comforted.
verse	19	77	3	I remembered God, and was troubled: I complained, and my spirit was overwhelmed. Selah.
verse	19	77	4	Thou holdest mine eyes waking: I am so troubled that I cannot speak.
verse	19	77	5	I have considered the days of old, the years of ancient times.
verse	19	77	6	I call to remembrance my song in the night: I commune with mine own heart: and my spirit made diligent search.
verse	19	77	7	Will the Lord cast off for ever? and will he be favourable no more?
verse	19	77	8	@@Is his mercy clean gone for ever? doth @9his@7 promise fail for evermore?
verse	19	77	9	Hath God forgotten to be gracious? hath he in anger shut up his tender mercies? Selah.
verse	19	77	10	@@And I said, This @9is@7 my infirmity: @9but I will remember@7 the years of the right hand of the most High.
verse	19	77	11	I will remember the works of the LORD: surely I will remember thy wonders of old.
verse	19	77	12	I will meditate also of all thy work, and talk of thy doings.
verse	19	77	13	@@Thy way, O God, @9is@7 in the sanctuary: who @9is so@7 great a God as @9our@7 God?
verse	19	77	14	@@Thou @9art@7 the God that doest wonders: thou hast declared thy strength among the people.
verse	19	77	15	@@Thou hast with @9thine@7 arm redeemed thy people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah.
verse	19	77	16	The waters saw thee, O God, the waters saw thee; they were afraid: the depths also were troubled.
verse	19	77	17	The clouds poured out water: the skies sent out a sound: thine arrows also went abroad.
verse	19	77	18	@@The voice of thy thunder @9was@7 in the heaven: the lightnings lightened the world: the earth trembled and shook.
verse	19	77	19	@@Thy way @9is@7 in the sea, and thy path in the great waters, and thy footsteps are not known.
verse	19	77	20	Thou leddest thy people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron.
pericope	19	78	1	Maschil of Asaph.
verse	19	78	1	@@Give ear, O my people, @9to@7 my law: incline your ears to the words of my mouth.
verse	19	78	2	I will open my mouth in a parable: I will utter dark sayings of old:
verse	19	78	3	Which we have heard and known, and our fathers have told us.
verse	19	78	4	@@We will not hide @9them@7 from their children, shewing to the generation to come the praises of the LORD, and his strength, and his wonderful works that he hath done.
verse	19	78	5	For he established a testimony in Jacob, and appointed a law in Israel, which he commanded our fathers, that they should make them known to their children:
verse	19	78	6	@@That the generation to come might know @9them, even@7 the children @9which@7 should be born; @9who@7 should arise and declare @9them@7 to their children:
verse	19	78	7	That they might set their hope in God, and not forget the works of God, but keep his commandments:
verse	19	78	8	@@And might not be as their fathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation; a generation @9that@7 set not their heart aright, and whose spirit was not stedfast with God.
verse	19	78	9	@@The children of Ephraim, @9being@7 armed, @9and@7 carrying bows, turned back in the day of battle.
verse	19	78	10	They kept not the covenant of God, and refused to walk in his law;
verse	19	78	11	And forgat his works, and his wonders that he had shewed them.
verse	19	78	12	@@Marvellous things did he in the sight of their fathers, in the land of Egypt, @9in@7 the field of Zoan.
verse	19	78	13	He divided the sea, and caused them to pass through; and he made the waters to stand as an heap.
verse	19	78	14	In the daytime also he led them with a cloud, and all the night with a light of fire.
verse	19	78	15	@@He clave the rocks in the wilderness, and gave @9them@7 drink as @9out of@7 the great depths.
verse	19	78	16	He brought streams also out of the rock, and caused waters to run down like rivers.
verse	19	78	17	And they sinned yet more against him by provoking the most High in the wilderness.
verse	19	78	18	And they tempted God in their heart by asking meat for their lust.
verse	19	78	19	Yea, they spake against God; they said, Can God furnish a table in the wilderness?
verse	19	78	20	Behold, he smote the rock, that the waters gushed out, and the streams overflowed; can he give bread also? can he provide flesh for his people?
verse	19	78	21	@@Therefore the LORD heard @9this,@7 and was wroth: so a fire was kindled against Jacob, and anger also came up against Israel;
verse	19	78	22	Because they believed not in God, and trusted not in his salvation:
verse	19	78	23	Though he had commanded the clouds from above, and opened the doors of heaven,
verse	19	78	24	And had rained down manna upon them to eat, and had given them of the corn of heaven.
verse	19	78	25	Man did eat angels' food: he sent them meat to the full.
verse	19	78	26	He caused an east wind to blow in the heaven: and by his power he brought in the south wind.
verse	19	78	27	He rained flesh also upon them as dust, and feathered fowls like as the sand of the sea:
verse	19	78	28	@@And he let @9it@7 fall in the midst of their camp, round about their habitations.
verse	19	78	29	So they did eat, and were well filled: for he gave them their own desire;
verse	19	78	30	@@They were not estranged from their lust. But while their meat @9was@7 yet in their mouths,
verse	19	78	31	@@The wrath of God came upon them, and slew the fattest of them, and smote down the chosen @9men@7 of Israel.
verse	19	78	32	For all this they sinned still, and believed not for his wondrous works.
verse	19	78	33	Therefore their days did he consume in vanity, and their years in trouble.
verse	19	78	34	When he slew them, then they sought him: and they returned and enquired early after God.
verse	19	78	35	@@And they remembered that God @9was@7 their rock, and the high God their redeemer.
verse	19	78	36	Nevertheless they did flatter him with their mouth, and they lied unto him with their tongues.
verse	19	78	37	For their heart was not right with him, neither were they stedfast in his covenant.
verse	19	78	38	@@But he, @9being@7 full of compassion, forgave @9their@7 iniquity, and destroyed @9them@7 not: yea, many a time turned he his anger away, and did not stir up all his wrath.
verse	19	78	39	@@For he remembered that they @9were but@7 flesh; a wind that passeth away, and cometh not again.
verse	19	78	40	@@How oft did they provoke him in the wilderness, @9and@7 grieve him in the desert!
verse	19	78	41	Yea, they turned back and tempted God, and limited the Holy One of Israel.
verse	19	78	42	@@They remembered not his hand, @9nor@7 the day when he delivered them from the enemy.
verse	19	78	43	How he had wrought his signs in Egypt, and his wonders in the field of Zoan:
verse	19	78	44	And had turned their rivers into blood; and their floods, that they could not drink.
verse	19	78	45	He sent divers sorts of flies among them, which devoured them; and frogs, which destroyed them.
verse	19	78	46	He gave also their increase unto the caterpiller, and their labour unto the locust.
verse	19	78	47	He destroyed their vines with hail, and their sycomore trees with frost.
verse	19	78	48	He gave up their cattle also to the hail, and their flocks to hot thunderbolts.
verse	19	78	49	@@He cast upon them the fierceness of his anger, wrath, and indignation, and trouble, by sending evil angels @9among them.@7
verse	19	78	50	He made a way to his anger; he spared not their soul from death, but gave their life over to the pestilence;
verse	19	78	51	@@And smote all the firstborn in Egypt; the chief of @9their@7 strength in the tabernacles of Ham:
verse	19	78	52	But made his own people to go forth like sheep, and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.
verse	19	78	53	And he led them on safely, so that they feared not: but the sea overwhelmed their enemies.
verse	19	78	54	@@And he brought them to the border of his sanctuary, @9even to@7 this mountain, @9which@7 his right hand had purchased.
verse	19	78	55	He cast out the heathen also before them, and divided them an inheritance by line, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.
verse	19	78	56	Yet they tempted and provoked the most high God, and kept not his testimonies:
verse	19	78	57	But turned back, and dealt unfaithfully like their fathers: they were turned aside like a deceitful bow.
verse	19	78	58	For they provoked him to anger with their high places, and moved him to jealousy with their graven images.
verse	19	78	59	@@When God heard @9this,@7 he was wroth, and greatly abhorred Israel:
verse	19	78	60	@@So that he forsook the tabernacle of Shiloh, the tent @9which@7 he placed among men;
verse	19	78	61	And delivered his strength into captivity, and his glory into the enemy's hand.
verse	19	78	62	He gave his people over also unto the sword; and was wroth with his inheritance.
verse	19	78	63	The fire consumed their young men; and their maidens were not given to marriage.
verse	19	78	64	Their priests fell by the sword; and their widows made no lamentation.
verse	19	78	65	@@Then the Lord awaked as one out of sleep, @9and@7 like a mighty man that shouteth by reason of wine.
verse	19	78	66	And he smote his enemies in the hinder parts: he put them to a perpetual reproach.
verse	19	78	67	Moreover he refused the tabernacle of Joseph, and chose not the tribe of Ephraim:
verse	19	78	68	But chose the tribe of Judah, the mount Zion which he loved.
verse	19	78	69	@@And he built his sanctuary like high @9palaces,@7 like the earth which he hath established for ever.
verse	19	78	70	He chose David also his servant, and took him from the sheepfolds:
verse	19	78	71	From following the ewes great with young he brought him to feed Jacob his people, and Israel his inheritance.
verse	19	78	72	So he fed them according to the integrity of his heart; and guided them by the skilfulness of his hands.
pericope	19	79	1	A Psalm of Asaph.
verse	19	79	1	O God, the heathen are come into thine inheritance; thy holy temple have they defiled; they have laid Jerusalem on heaps.
verse	19	79	2	@@The dead bodies of thy servants have they given @9to be@7 meat unto the fowls of the heaven, the flesh of thy saints unto the beasts of the earth.
verse	19	79	3	@@Their blood have they shed like water round about Jerusalem; and @9there was@7 none to bury @9them.@7
verse	19	79	4	We are become a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and derision to them that are round about us.
verse	19	79	5	How long, LORD? wilt thou be angry for ever? shall thy jealousy burn like fire?
verse	19	79	6	Pour out thy wrath upon the heathen that have not known thee, and upon the kingdoms that have not called upon thy name.
verse	19	79	7	For they have devoured Jacob, and laid waste his dwelling place.
verse	19	79	8	O remember not against us former iniquities: let thy tender mercies speedily prevent us: for we are brought very low.
verse	19	79	9	Help us, O God of our salvation, for the glory of thy name: and deliver us, and purge away our sins, for thy name's sake.
verse	19	79	10	@@Wherefore should the heathen say, Where @9is@7 their God? let him be known among the heathen in our sight @9by@7 the revenging of the blood of thy servants @9which is@7 shed.
verse	19	79	11	Let the sighing of the prisoner come before thee; according to the greatness of thy power preserve thou those that are appointed to die;
verse	19	79	12	And render unto our neighbours sevenfold into their bosom their reproach, wherewith they have reproached thee, O Lord.
verse	19	79	13	So we thy people and sheep of thy pasture will give thee thanks for ever: we will shew forth thy praise to all generations.
pericope	19	80	1	To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim-Eduth, A Psalm of Asaph.
verse	19	80	1	@@Give ear, O Shepherd of Israel, thou that leadest Joseph like a flock; thou that dwellest @9between@7 the cherubims, shine forth.
verse	19	80	2	@@Before Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasseh stir up thy strength, and come @9and@7 save us.
verse	19	80	3	Turn us again, O God, and cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.
verse	19	80	4	O LORD God of hosts, how long wilt thou be angry against the prayer of thy people?
verse	19	80	5	Thou feedest them with the bread of tears; and givest them tears to drink in great measure.
verse	19	80	6	Thou makest us a strife unto our neighbours: and our enemies laugh among themselves.
verse	19	80	7	Turn us again, O God of hosts, and cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.
verse	19	80	8	Thou hast brought a vine out of Egypt: thou hast cast out the heathen, and planted it.
verse	19	80	9	@@Thou preparedst @9room@7 before it, and didst cause it to take deep root, and it filled the land.
verse	19	80	10	@@The hills were covered with the shadow of it, and the boughs thereof @9were like@7 the goodly cedars.
verse	19	80	11	She sent out her boughs unto the sea, and her branches unto the river.
verse	19	80	12	@@Why hast thou @9then@7 broken down her hedges, so that all they which pass by the way do pluck her?
verse	19	80	13	The boar out of the wood doth waste it, and the wild beast of the field doth devour it.
verse	19	80	14	Return, we beseech thee, O God of hosts: look down from heaven, and behold, and visit this vine;
verse	19	80	15	@@And the vineyard which thy right hand hath planted, and the branch @9that@7 thou madest strong for thyself.
verse	19	80	16	@@@9It is@7 burned with fire, @9it is@7 cut down: they perish at the rebuke of thy countenance.
verse	19	80	17	@@Let thy hand be upon the man of thy right hand, upon the son of man @9whom@7 thou madest strong for thyself.
verse	19	80	18	So will not we go back from thee: quicken us, and we will call upon thy name.
verse	19	80	19	Turn us again, O LORD God of hosts, cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.
pericope	19	81	1	To the chief Musician upon Gittith, A Psalm of Asaph.
verse	19	81	1	Sing aloud unto God our strength: make a joyful noise unto the God of Jacob.
verse	19	81	2	Take a psalm, and bring hither the timbrel, the pleasant harp with the psaltery.
verse	19	81	3	Blow up the trumpet in the new moon, in the time appointed, on our solemn feast day.
verse	19	81	4	@@For this @9was@7 a statute for Israel, @9and@7 a law of the God of Jacob.
verse	19	81	5	@@This he ordained in Joseph @9for@7 a testimony, when he went out through the land of Egypt: @9where@7 I heard a language @9that@7 I understood not.
verse	19	81	6	I removed his shoulder from the burden: his hands were delivered from the pots.
verse	19	81	7	Thou calledst in trouble, and I delivered thee; I answered thee in the secret place of thunder: I proved thee at the waters of Meribah. Selah.
verse	19	81	8	Hear, O my people, and I will testify unto thee: O Israel, if thou wilt hearken unto me;
verse	19	81	9	There shall no strange god be in thee; neither shalt thou worship any strange god.
verse	19	81	10	@@I @9am@7 the LORD thy God, which brought thee out of the land of Egypt: open thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.
verse	19	81	11	But my people would not hearken to my voice; and Israel would none of me.
verse	19	81	12	@@So I gave them up unto their own hearts' lust: @9and@7 they walked in their own counsels.
verse	19	81	13	@@Oh that my people had hearkened unto me, @9and@7 Israel had walked in my ways!
verse	19	81	14	I should soon have subdued their enemies, and turned my hand against their adversaries.
verse	19	81	15	The haters of the LORD should have submitted themselves unto him: but their time should have endured for ever.
verse	19	81	16	He should have fed them also with the finest of the wheat: and with honey out of the rock should I have satisfied thee.
pericope	19	82	1	A Psalm of Asaph.
verse	19	82	1	God standeth in the congregation of the mighty; he judgeth among the gods.
verse	19	82	2	How long will ye judge unjustly, and accept the persons of the wicked? Selah.
verse	19	82	3	Defend the poor and fatherless: do justice to the afflicted and needy.
verse	19	82	4	@@Deliver the poor and needy: rid @9them@7 out of the hand of the wicked.
verse	19	82	5	They know not, neither will they understand; they walk on in darkness: all the foundations of the earth are out of course.
verse	19	82	6	@@I have said, Ye @9are@7 gods; and all of you @9are@7 children of the most High.
verse	19	82	7	But ye shall die like men, and fall like one of the princes.
verse	19	82	8	Arise, O God, judge the earth: for thou shalt inherit all nations.
pericope	19	83	1	A Song or Psalm of Asaph.
verse	19	83	1	Keep not thou silence, O God: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God.
verse	19	83	2	For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.
verse	19	83	3	They have taken crafty counsel against thy people, and consulted against thy hidden ones.
verse	19	83	4	@@They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from @9being@7 a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.
verse	19	83	5	For they have consulted together with one consent: they are confederate against thee:
verse	19	83	6	The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the Hagarenes;
verse	19	83	7	Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;
verse	19	83	8	Assur also is joined with them: they have holpen the children of Lot. Selah.
verse	19	83	9	@@Do unto them as @9unto@7 the Midianites; as @9to@7 Sisera, as @9to@7 Jabin, at the brook of Kison:
verse	19	83	10	@@@9Which@7 perished at Endor: they became @9as@7 dung for the earth.
verse	19	83	11	Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb: yea, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:
verse	19	83	12	Who said, Let us take to ourselves the houses of God in possession.
verse	19	83	13	O my God, make them like a wheel; as the stubble before the wind.
verse	19	83	14	As the fire burneth a wood, and as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;
verse	19	83	15	So persecute them with thy tempest, and make them afraid with thy storm.
verse	19	83	16	Fill their faces with shame; that they may seek thy name, O LORD.
verse	19	83	17	Let them be confounded and troubled for ever; yea, let them be put to shame, and perish:
verse	19	83	18	@@That @9men@7 may know that thou, whose name alone @9is@7 JEHOVAH, @9art@7 the most high over all the earth.
pericope	19	84	1	To the chief Musician upon Gittith, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.
verse	19	84	1	@@How amiable @9are@7 thy tabernacles, O LORD of hosts!
verse	19	84	2	My soul longeth, yea, even fainteth for the courts of the LORD: my heart and my flesh crieth out for the living God.
verse	19	84	3	@@Yea, the sparrow hath found an house, and the swallow a nest for herself, where she may lay her young, @9even@7 thine altars, O LORD of hosts, my King, and my God.
verse	19	84	4	@@Blessed @9are@7 they that dwell in thy house: they will be still praising thee. Selah.
verse	19	84	5	@@Blessed @9is@7 the man whose strength @9is@7 in thee; in whose heart @9are@7 the ways @9of them.@7
verse	19	84	6	@@@9Who@7 passing through the valley of Baca make it a well; the rain also filleth the pools.
verse	19	84	7	@@They go from strength to strength, @9every one of them@7 in Zion appeareth before God.
verse	19	84	8	O LORD God of hosts, hear my prayer: give ear, O God of Jacob. Selah.
verse	19	84	9	Behold, O God our shield, and look upon the face of thine anointed.
verse	19	84	10	@@For a day in thy courts @9is@7 better than a thousand. I had rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.
verse	19	84	11	@@For the LORD God @9is@7 a sun and shield: the LORD will give grace and glory: no good @9thing@7 will he withhold from them that walk uprightly.
verse	19	84	12	@@O LORD of hosts, blessed @9is@7 the man that trusteth in thee.
pericope	19	85	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.
verse	19	85	1	LORD, thou hast been favourable unto thy land: thou hast brought back the captivity of Jacob.
verse	19	85	2	Thou hast forgiven the iniquity of thy people, thou hast covered all their sin. Selah.
verse	19	85	3	@@Thou hast taken away all thy wrath: thou hast turned @9thyself@7 from the fierceness of thine anger.
verse	19	85	4	Turn us, O God of our salvation, and cause thine anger toward us to cease.
verse	19	85	5	Wilt thou be angry with us for ever? wilt thou draw out thine anger to all generations?
verse	19	85	6	Wilt thou not revive us again: that thy people may rejoice in thee?
verse	19	85	7	Shew us thy mercy, O LORD, and grant us thy salvation.
verse	19	85	8	I will hear what God the LORD will speak: for he will speak peace unto his people, and to his saints: but let them not turn again to folly.
verse	19	85	9	@@Surely his salvation @9is@7 nigh them that fear him; that glory may dwell in our land.
verse	19	85	10	@@Mercy and truth are met together; righteousness and peace have kissed @9each other.@7
verse	19	85	11	Truth shall spring out of the earth; and righteousness shall look down from heaven.
verse	19	85	12	@@Yea, the LORD shall give @9that which is@7 good; and our land shall yield her increase.
verse	19	85	13	@@Righteousness shall go before him; and shall set @9us@7 in the way of his steps.
pericope	19	86	1	A Prayer of David.
verse	19	86	1	@@Bow down thine ear, O LORD, hear me: for I @9am@7 poor and needy.
verse	19	86	2	@@Preserve my soul; for I @9am@7 holy: O thou my God, save thy servant that trusteth in thee.
verse	19	86	3	Be merciful unto me, O Lord: for I cry unto thee daily.
verse	19	86	4	Rejoice the soul of thy servant: for unto thee, O Lord, do I lift up my soul.
verse	19	86	5	@@For thou, Lord, @9art@7 good, and ready to forgive; and plenteous in mercy unto all them that call upon thee.
verse	19	86	6	Give ear, O LORD, unto my prayer; and attend to the voice of my supplications.
verse	19	86	7	In the day of my trouble I will call upon thee: for thou wilt answer me.
verse	19	86	8	@@Among the gods @9there is@7 none like unto thee, O Lord; neither @9are there any works@7 like unto thy works.
verse	19	86	9	All nations whom thou hast made shall come and worship before thee, O Lord; and shall glorify thy name.
verse	19	86	10	@@For thou @9art@7 great, and doest wondrous things: thou @9art@7 God alone.
verse	19	86	11	Teach me thy way, O LORD; I will walk in thy truth: unite my heart to fear thy name.
verse	19	86	12	I will praise thee, O Lord my God, with all my heart: and I will glorify thy name for evermore.
verse	19	86	13	@@For great @9is@7 thy mercy toward me: and thou hast delivered my soul from the lowest hell.
verse	19	86	14	@@O God, the proud are risen against me, and the assemblies of violent @9men@7 have sought after my soul; and have not set thee before them.
verse	19	86	15	@@But thou, O Lord, @9art@7 a God full of compassion, and gracious, longsuffering, and plenteous in mercy and truth.
verse	19	86	16	O turn unto me, and have mercy upon me; give thy strength unto thy servant, and save the son of thine handmaid.
verse	19	86	17	@@Shew me a token for good; that they which hate me may see @9it,@7 and be ashamed: because thou, LORD, hast holpen me, and comforted me.
pericope	19	87	1	A Psalm or Song for the sons of Korah.
verse	19	87	1	@@His foundation @9is@7 in the holy mountains.
verse	19	87	2	The LORD loveth the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob.
verse	19	87	3	Glorious things are spoken of thee, O city of God. Selah.
verse	19	87	4	@@I will make mention of Rahab and Babylon to them that know me: behold Philistia, and Tyre, with Ethiopia; this @9man@7 was born there.
verse	19	87	5	@@And of Zion it shall be said, This and @9that man@7 was born in her: and the highest himself shall establish her.
verse	19	87	6	The LORD shall count, when he writeth up the people, that this man was born there. Selah.
verse	19	87	7	@@As well the singers as the players on instruments @9shall be there:@7 all my springs @9are@7 in thee.
pericope	19	88	1	A Song or Psalm for the sons of Korah, to the chief Musician upon Mahalath Leannoth, Maschil of Heman the Ezrahite.
verse	19	88	1	@@O LORD God of my salvation, I have cried day @9and@7 night before thee:
verse	19	88	2	Let my prayer come before thee: incline thine ear unto my cry;
verse	19	88	3	For my soul is full of troubles: and my life draweth nigh unto the grave.
verse	19	88	4	@@I am counted with them that go down into the pit: I am as a man @9that hath@7 no strength:
verse	19	88	5	Free among the dead, like the slain that lie in the grave, whom thou rememberest no more: and they are cut off from thy hand.
verse	19	88	6	Thou hast laid me in the lowest pit, in darkness, in the deeps.
verse	19	88	7	@@Thy wrath lieth hard upon me, and thou hast afflicted @9me@7 with all thy waves. Selah.
verse	19	88	8	@@Thou hast put away mine acquaintance far from me; thou hast made me an abomination unto them: @9I am@7 shut up, and I cannot come forth.
verse	19	88	9	Mine eye mourneth by reason of affliction: LORD, I have called daily upon thee, I have stretched out my hands unto thee.
verse	19	88	10	@@Wilt thou shew wonders to the dead? shall the dead arise @9and@7 praise thee? Selah.
verse	19	88	11	@@Shall thy lovingkindness be declared in the grave? @9or@7 thy faithfulness in destruction?
verse	19	88	12	Shall thy wonders be known in the dark? and thy righteousness in the land of forgetfulness?
verse	19	88	13	But unto thee have I cried, O LORD; and in the morning shall my prayer prevent thee.
verse	19	88	14	@@LORD, why castest thou off my soul? @9why@7 hidest thou thy face from me?
verse	19	88	15	@@I @9am@7 afflicted and ready to die from @9my@7 youth up: @9while@7 I suffer thy terrors I am distracted.
verse	19	88	16	Thy fierce wrath goeth over me; thy terrors have cut me off.
verse	19	88	17	They came round about me daily like water; they compassed me about together.
verse	19	88	18	@@Lover and friend hast thou put far from me, @9and@7 mine acquaintance into darkness.
pericope	19	89	1	Maschil of Ethan the Ezrahite.
verse	19	89	1	I will sing of the mercies of the LORD for ever: with my mouth will I make known thy faithfulness to all generations.
verse	19	89	2	For I have said, Mercy shall be built up for ever: thy faithfulness shalt thou establish in the very heavens.
verse	19	89	3	I have made a covenant with my chosen, I have sworn unto David my servant,
verse	19	89	4	Thy seed will I establish for ever, and build up thy throne to all generations. Selah.
verse	19	89	5	And the heavens shall praise thy wonders, O LORD: thy faithfulness also in the congregation of the saints.
verse	19	89	6	@@For who in the heaven can be compared unto the LORD? @9who@7 among the sons of the mighty can be likened unto the LORD?
verse	19	89	7	@@God is greatly to be feared in the assembly of the saints, and to be had in reverence of all @9them that are@7 about him.
verse	19	89	8	@@O LORD God of hosts, who @9is@7 a strong LORD like unto thee? or to thy faithfulness round about thee?
verse	19	89	9	Thou rulest the raging of the sea: when the waves thereof arise, thou stillest them.
verse	19	89	10	Thou hast broken Rahab in pieces, as one that is slain; thou hast scattered thine enemies with thy strong arm.
verse	19	89	11	@@The heavens @9are@7 thine, the earth also @9is@7 thine: @9as for@7 the world and the fulness thereof, thou hast founded them.
verse	19	89	12	The north and the south thou hast created them: Tabor and Hermon shall rejoice in thy name.
verse	19	89	13	@@Thou hast a mighty arm: strong is thy hand, @9and@7 high is thy right hand.
verse	19	89	14	@@Justice and judgment @9are@7 the habitation of thy throne: mercy and truth shall go before thy face.
verse	19	89	15	@@Blessed @9is@7 the people that know the joyful sound: they shall walk, O LORD, in the light of thy countenance.
verse	19	89	16	In thy name shall they rejoice all the day: and in thy righteousness shall they be exalted.
verse	19	89	17	@@For thou @9art@7 the glory of their strength: and in thy favour our horn shall be exalted.
verse	19	89	18	@@For the LORD @9is@7 our defence; and the Holy One of Israel @9is@7 our king.
verse	19	89	19	@@Then thou spakest in vision to thy holy one, and saidst, I have laid help upon @9one that is@7 mighty; I have exalted @9one@7 chosen out of the people.
verse	19	89	20	I have found David my servant; with my holy oil have I anointed him:
verse	19	89	21	With whom my hand shall be established: mine arm also shall strengthen him.
verse	19	89	22	The enemy shall not exact upon him; nor the son of wickedness afflict him.
verse	19	89	23	And I will beat down his foes before his face, and plague them that hate him.
verse	19	89	24	@@But my faithfulness and my mercy @9shall be@7 with him: and in my name shall his horn be exalted.
verse	19	89	25	I will set his hand also in the sea, and his right hand in the rivers.
verse	19	89	26	@@He shall cry unto me, Thou @9art@7 my father, my God, and the rock of my salvation.
verse	19	89	27	@@Also I will make him @9my@7 firstborn, higher than the kings of the earth.
verse	19	89	28	My mercy will I keep for him for evermore, and my covenant shall stand fast with him.
verse	19	89	29	@@His seed also will I make @9to endure@7 for ever, and his throne as the days of heaven.
verse	19	89	30	If his children forsake my law, and walk not in my judgments;
verse	19	89	31	If they break my statutes, and keep not my commandments;
verse	19	89	32	Then will I visit their transgression with the rod, and their iniquity with stripes.
verse	19	89	33	Nevertheless my lovingkindness will I not utterly take from him, nor suffer my faithfulness to fail.
verse	19	89	34	My covenant will I not break, nor alter the thing that is gone out of my lips.
verse	19	89	35	Once have I sworn by my holiness that I will not lie unto David.
verse	19	89	36	His seed shall endure for ever, and his throne as the sun before me.
verse	19	89	37	@@It shall be established for ever as the moon, and @9as@7 a faithful witness in heaven. Selah.
verse	19	89	38	But thou hast cast off and abhorred, thou hast been wroth with thine anointed.
verse	19	89	39	@@Thou hast made void the covenant of thy servant: thou hast profaned his crown @9by casting it@7 to the ground.
verse	19	89	40	Thou hast broken down all his hedges; thou hast brought his strong holds to ruin.
verse	19	89	41	All that pass by the way spoil him: he is a reproach to his neighbours.
verse	19	89	42	Thou hast set up the right hand of his adversaries; thou hast made all his enemies to rejoice.
verse	19	89	43	Thou hast also turned the edge of his sword, and hast not made him to stand in the battle.
verse	19	89	44	Thou hast made his glory to cease, and cast his throne down to the ground.
verse	19	89	45	The days of his youth hast thou shortened: thou hast covered him with shame. Selah.
verse	19	89	46	How long, LORD? wilt thou hide thyself for ever? shall thy wrath burn like fire?
verse	19	89	47	Remember how short my time is: wherefore hast thou made all men in vain?
verse	19	89	48	@@What man @9is he that@7 liveth, and shall not see death? shall he deliver his soul from the hand of the grave? Selah.
verse	19	89	49	@@Lord, where @9are@7 thy former lovingkindnesses, @9which@7 thou swarest unto David in thy truth?
verse	19	89	50	@@Remember, Lord, the reproach of thy servants; @9how@7 I do bear in my bosom @9the reproach of@7 all the mighty people;
verse	19	89	51	Wherewith thine enemies have reproached, O LORD; wherewith they have reproached the footsteps of thine anointed.
verse	19	89	52	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD for evermore. Amen, and Amen.
pericope	19	90	1	A Prayer of Moses the man of God.
verse	19	90	1	LORD, thou hast been our dwelling place in all generations.
verse	19	90	2	@@Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou @9art@7 God.
verse	19	90	3	Thou turnest man to destruction; and sayest, Return, ye children of men.
verse	19	90	4	@@For a thousand years in thy sight @9are but@7 as yesterday when it is past, and @9as@7 a watch in the night.
verse	19	90	5	@@Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are @9as@7 a sleep: in the morning @9they are@7 like grass @9which@7 groweth up.
verse	19	90	6	In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth up; in the evening it is cut down, and withereth.
verse	19	90	7	For we are consumed by thine anger, and by thy wrath are we troubled.
verse	19	90	8	@@Thou hast set our iniquities before thee, our secret @9sins@7 in the light of thy countenance.
verse	19	90	9	@@For all our days are passed away in thy wrath: we spend our years as a tale @9that is told.@7
verse	19	90	10	@@The days of our years @9are@7 threescore years and ten; and if by reason of strength @9they be@7 fourscore years, yet @9is@7 their strength labour and sorrow; for it is soon cut off, and we fly away.
verse	19	90	11	@@Who knoweth the power of thine anger? even according to thy fear, @9so is@7 thy wrath.
verse	19	90	12	@@So teach @9us@7 to number our days, that we may apply @9our@7 hearts unto wisdom.
verse	19	90	13	Return, O LORD, how long? and let it repent thee concerning thy servants.
verse	19	90	14	O satisfy us early with thy mercy; that we may rejoice and be glad all our days.
verse	19	90	15	@@Make us glad according to the days @9wherein@7 thou hast afflicted us, @9and@7 the years @9wherein@7 we have seen evil.
verse	19	90	16	Let thy work appear unto thy servants, and thy glory unto their children.
verse	19	90	17	And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.
verse	19	91	1	He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty.
verse	19	91	2	@@I will say of the LORD, @9He is@7 my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.
verse	19	91	3	@@Surely he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler, @9and@7 from the noisome pestilence.
verse	19	91	4	@@He shall cover thee with his feathers, and under his wings shalt thou trust: his truth @9shall be thy@7 shield and buckler.
verse	19	91	5	@@Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night; @9nor@7 for the arrow @9that@7 flieth by day;
verse	19	91	6	@@@9Nor@7 for the pestilence @9that@7 walketh in darkness; @9nor@7 for the destruction @9that@7 wasteth at noonday.
verse	19	91	7	@@A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand; @9but@7 it shall not come nigh thee.
verse	19	91	8	Only with thine eyes shalt thou behold and see the reward of the wicked.
verse	19	91	9	@@Because thou hast made the LORD, @9which is@7 my refuge, @9even@7 the most High, thy habitation;
verse	19	91	10	There shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy dwelling.
verse	19	91	11	For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.
verse	19	91	12	@@They shall bear thee up in @9their@7 hands, lest thou dash thy foot against a stone.
verse	19	91	13	Thou shalt tread upon the lion and adder: the young lion and the dragon shalt thou trample under feet.
verse	19	91	14	Because he hath set his love upon me, therefore will I deliver him: I will set him on high, because he hath known my name.
verse	19	91	15	@@He shall call upon me, and I will answer him: I @9will be@7 with him in trouble; I will deliver him, and honour him.
verse	19	91	16	With long life will I satisfy him, and shew him my salvation.
pericope	19	92	1	A Psalm or Song for the sabbath day.
verse	19	92	1	@@@9It is a@7 good @9thing@7 to give thanks unto the LORD, and to sing praises unto thy name, O most High:
verse	19	92	2	To shew forth thy lovingkindness in the morning, and thy faithfulness every night,
verse	19	92	3	Upon an instrument of ten strings, and upon the psaltery; upon the harp with a solemn sound.
verse	19	92	4	For thou, LORD, hast made me glad through thy work: I will triumph in the works of thy hands.
verse	19	92	5	@@O LORD, how great are thy works! @9and@7 thy thoughts are very deep.
verse	19	92	6	A brutish man knoweth not; neither doth a fool understand this.
verse	19	92	7	@@When the wicked spring as the grass, and when all the workers of iniquity do flourish; @9it is@7 that they shall be destroyed for ever:
verse	19	92	8	@@But thou, LORD, @9art most@7 high for evermore.
verse	19	92	9	For, lo, thine enemies, O LORD, for, lo, thine enemies shall perish; all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.
verse	19	92	10	@@But my horn shalt thou exalt like @9the horn of@7 an unicorn: I shall be anointed with fresh oil.
verse	19	92	11	@@Mine eye also shall see @9my desire@7 on mine enemies, @9and@7 mine ears shall hear @9my desire@7 of the wicked that rise up against me.
verse	19	92	12	The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree: he shall grow like a cedar in Lebanon.
verse	19	92	13	Those that be planted in the house of the LORD shall flourish in the courts of our God.
verse	19	92	14	They shall still bring forth fruit in old age; they shall be fat and flourishing;
verse	19	92	15	@@To shew that the LORD @9is@7 upright: @9he is@7 my rock, and @9there is@7 no unrighteousness in him.
verse	19	93	1	@@The LORD reigneth, he is clothed with majesty; the LORD is clothed with strength, @9wherewith@7 he hath girded himself: the world also is stablished, that it cannot be moved.
verse	19	93	2	@@Thy throne @9is@7 established of old: thou @9art@7 from everlasting.
verse	19	93	3	The floods have lifted up, O LORD, the floods have lifted up their voice; the floods lift up their waves.
verse	19	93	4	@@The LORD on high @9is@7 mightier than the noise of many waters, @9yea, than@7 the mighty waves of the sea.
verse	19	93	5	Thy testimonies are very sure: holiness becometh thine house, O LORD, for ever.
verse	19	94	1	O LORD God, to whom vengeance belongeth; O God, to whom vengeance belongeth, shew thyself.
verse	19	94	2	Lift up thyself, thou judge of the earth: render a reward to the proud.
verse	19	94	3	LORD, how long shall the wicked, how long shall the wicked triumph?
verse	19	94	4	@@@9How long@7 shall they utter @9and@7 speak hard things? @9and@7 all the workers of iniquity boast themselves?
verse	19	94	5	They break in pieces thy people, O LORD, and afflict thine heritage.
verse	19	94	6	They slay the widow and the stranger, and murder the fatherless.
verse	19	94	7	@@Yet they say, The LORD shall not see, neither shall the God of Jacob regard @9it.@7
verse	19	94	8	@@Understand, ye brutish among the people: and @9ye@7 fools, when will ye be wise?
verse	19	94	9	He that planted the ear, shall he not hear? he that formed the eye, shall he not see?
verse	19	94	10	@@He that chastiseth the heathen, shall not he correct? he that teacheth man knowledge, @9shall not he know?@7
verse	19	94	11	@@The LORD knoweth the thoughts of man, that they @9are@7 vanity.
verse	19	94	12	@@Blessed @9is@7 the man whom thou chastenest, O LORD, and teachest him out of thy law;
verse	19	94	13	That thou mayest give him rest from the days of adversity, until the pit be digged for the wicked.
verse	19	94	14	For the LORD will not cast off his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance.
verse	19	94	15	But judgment shall return unto righteousness: and all the upright in heart shall follow it.
verse	19	94	16	@@Who will rise up for me against the evildoers? @9or@7 who will stand up for me against the workers of iniquity?
verse	19	94	17	@@Unless the LORD @9had been@7 my help, my soul had almost dwelt in silence.
verse	19	94	18	When I said, My foot slippeth; thy mercy, O LORD, held me up.
verse	19	94	19	In the multitude of my thoughts within me thy comforts delight my soul.
verse	19	94	20	Shall the throne of iniquity have fellowship with thee, which frameth mischief by a law?
verse	19	94	21	They gather themselves together against the soul of the righteous, and condemn the innocent blood.
verse	19	94	22	@@But the LORD is my defence; and my God @9is@7 the rock of my refuge.
verse	19	94	23	@@And he shall bring upon them their own iniquity, and shall cut them off in their own wickedness; @9yea,@7 the LORD our God shall cut them off.
verse	19	95	1	O come, let us sing unto the LORD: let us make a joyful noise to the rock of our salvation.
verse	19	95	2	Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, and make a joyful noise unto him with psalms.
verse	19	95	3	@@For the LORD @9is@7 a great God, and a great King above all gods.
verse	19	95	4	@@In his hand @9are@7 the deep places of the earth: the strength of the hills @9is@7 his also.
verse	19	95	5	@@The sea @9is@7 his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry @9land.@7
verse	19	95	6	O come, let us worship and bow down: let us kneel before the LORD our maker.
verse	19	95	7	@@For he @9is@7 our God; and we @9are@7 the people of his pasture, and the sheep of his hand. To day if ye will hear his voice,
verse	19	95	8	@@Harden not your heart, as in the provocation, @9and as in@7 the day of temptation in the wilderness:
verse	19	95	9	When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my work.
verse	19	95	10	@@Forty years long was I grieved with @9this@7 generation, and said, It @9is@7 a people that do err in their heart, and they have not known my ways:
verse	19	95	11	Unto whom I sware in my wrath that they should not enter into my rest.
verse	19	96	1	O sing unto the LORD a new song: sing unto the LORD, all the earth.
verse	19	96	2	Sing unto the LORD, bless his name; shew forth his salvation from day to day.
verse	19	96	3	Declare his glory among the heathen, his wonders among all people.
verse	19	96	4	@@For the LORD @9is@7 great, and greatly to be praised: he @9is@7 to be feared above all gods.
verse	19	96	5	@@For all the gods of the nations @9are@7 idols: but the LORD made the heavens.
verse	19	96	6	@@Honour and majesty @9are@7 before him: strength and beauty @9are@7 in his sanctuary.
verse	19	96	7	Give unto the LORD, O ye kindreds of the people, give unto the LORD glory and strength.
verse	19	96	8	@@Give unto the LORD the glory @9due unto@7 his name: bring an offering, and come into his courts.
verse	19	96	9	O worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness: fear before him, all the earth.
verse	19	96	10	@@Say among the heathen @9that@7 the LORD reigneth: the world also shall be established that it shall not be moved: he shall judge the people righteously.
verse	19	96	11	Let the heavens rejoice, and let the earth be glad; let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof.
verse	19	96	12	@@Let the field be joyful, and all that @9is@7 therein: then shall all the trees of the wood rejoice
verse	19	96	13	Before the LORD: for he cometh, for he cometh to judge the earth: he shall judge the world with righteousness, and the people with his truth.
verse	19	97	1	@@The LORD reigneth; let the earth rejoice; let the multitude of isles be glad @9thereof.@7
verse	19	97	2	@@Clouds and darkness @9are@7 round about him: righteousness and judgment @9are@7 the habitation of his throne.
verse	19	97	3	A fire goeth before him, and burneth up his enemies round about.
verse	19	97	4	His lightnings enlightened the world: the earth saw, and trembled.
verse	19	97	5	The hills melted like wax at the presence of the LORD, at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth.
verse	19	97	6	The heavens declare his righteousness, and all the people see his glory.
verse	19	97	7	@@Confounded be all they that serve graven images, that boast themselves of idols: worship him, all @9ye@7 gods.
verse	19	97	8	Zion heard, and was glad; and the daughters of Judah rejoiced because of thy judgments, O LORD.
verse	19	97	9	@@For thou, LORD, @9art@7 high above all the earth: thou art exalted far above all gods.
verse	19	97	10	Ye that love the LORD, hate evil: he preserveth the souls of his saints; he delivereth them out of the hand of the wicked.
verse	19	97	11	Light is sown for the righteous, and gladness for the upright in heart.
verse	19	97	12	Rejoice in the LORD, ye righteous; and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness.
pericope	19	98	1	A Psalm.
verse	19	98	1	O sing unto the LORD a new song; for he hath done marvellous things: his right hand, and his holy arm, hath gotten him the victory.
verse	19	98	2	The LORD hath made known his salvation: his righteousness hath he openly shewed in the sight of the heathen.
verse	19	98	3	He hath remembered his mercy and his truth toward the house of Israel: all the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.
verse	19	98	4	Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all the earth: make a loud noise, and rejoice, and sing praise.
verse	19	98	5	Sing unto the LORD with the harp; with the harp, and the voice of a psalm.
verse	19	98	6	With trumpets and sound of cornet make a joyful noise before the LORD, the King.
verse	19	98	7	Let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein.
verse	19	98	8	@@Let the floods clap @9their@7 hands: let the hills be joyful together
verse	19	98	9	Before the LORD; for he cometh to judge the earth: with righteousness shall he judge the world, and the people with equity.
verse	19	99	1	@@The LORD reigneth; let the people tremble: he sitteth @9between@7 the cherubims; let the earth be moved.
verse	19	99	2	@@The LORD @9is@7 great in Zion; and he @9is@7 high above all the people.
verse	19	99	3	@@Let them praise thy great and terrible name; @9for@7 it @9is@7 holy.
verse	19	99	4	The king's strength also loveth judgment; thou dost establish equity, thou executest judgment and righteousness in Jacob.
verse	19	99	5	@@Exalt ye the LORD our God, and worship at his footstool; @9for@7 he @9is@7 holy.
verse	19	99	6	Moses and Aaron among his priests, and Samuel among them that call upon his name; they called upon the LORD, and he answered them.
verse	19	99	7	@@He spake unto them in the cloudy pillar: they kept his testimonies, and the ordinance @9that@7 he gave them.
verse	19	99	8	Thou answeredst them, O LORD our God: thou wast a God that forgavest them, though thou tookest vengeance of their inventions.
verse	19	99	9	@@Exalt the LORD our God, and worship at his holy hill; for the LORD our God @9is@7 holy.
pericope	19	100	1	A Psalm of praise.
verse	19	100	1	Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all ye lands.
verse	19	100	2	Serve the LORD with gladness: come before his presence with singing.
verse	19	100	3	@@Know ye that the LORD he @9is@7 God: @9it is@7 he @9that@7 hath made us, and not we ourselves; @9we are@7 his people, and the sheep of his pasture.
verse	19	100	4	@@Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, @9and@7 into his courts with praise: be thankful unto him, @9and@7 bless his name.
verse	19	100	5	@@For the LORD @9is@7 good; his mercy @9is@7 everlasting; and his truth @9endureth@7 to all generations.
pericope	19	101	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	101	1	I will sing of mercy and judgment: unto thee, O LORD, will I sing.
verse	19	101	2	I will behave myself wisely in a perfect way. O when wilt thou come unto me? I will walk within my house with a perfect heart.
verse	19	101	3	@@I will set no wicked thing before mine eyes: I hate the work of them that turn aside; @9it@7 shall not cleave to me.
verse	19	101	4	@@A froward heart shall depart from me: I will not know a wicked @9person.@7
verse	19	101	5	Whoso privily slandereth his neighbour, him will I cut off: him that hath an high look and a proud heart will not I suffer.
verse	19	101	6	@@Mine eyes @9shall be@7 upon the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me: he that walketh in a perfect way, he shall serve me.
verse	19	101	7	He that worketh deceit shall not dwell within my house: he that telleth lies shall not tarry in my sight.
verse	19	101	8	I will early destroy all the wicked of the land; that I may cut off all wicked doers from the city of the LORD.
pericope	19	102	1	A Prayer of the afflicted, when he is overwhelmed, and poureth out his complaint before the LORD.
verse	19	102	1	Hear my prayer, O LORD, and let my cry come unto thee.
verse	19	102	2	@@Hide not thy face from me in the day @9when@7 I am in trouble; incline thine ear unto me: in the day @9when@7 I call answer me speedily.
verse	19	102	3	For my days are consumed like smoke, and my bones are burned as an hearth.
verse	19	102	4	My heart is smitten, and withered like grass; so that I forget to eat my bread.
verse	19	102	5	By reason of the voice of my groaning my bones cleave to my skin.
verse	19	102	6	I am like a pelican of the wilderness: I am like an owl of the desert.
verse	19	102	7	I watch, and am as a sparrow alone upon the house top.
verse	19	102	8	@@Mine enemies reproach me all the day; @9and@7 they that are mad against me are sworn against me.
verse	19	102	9	For I have eaten ashes like bread, and mingled my drink with weeping,
verse	19	102	10	Because of thine indignation and thy wrath: for thou hast lifted me up, and cast me down.
verse	19	102	11	@@My days @9are@7 like a shadow that declineth; and I am withered like grass.
verse	19	102	12	But thou, O LORD, shalt endure for ever; and thy remembrance unto all generations.
verse	19	102	13	@@Thou shalt arise, @9and@7 have mercy upon Zion: for the time to favour her, yea, the set time, is come.
verse	19	102	14	For thy servants take pleasure in her stones, and favour the dust thereof.
verse	19	102	15	So the heathen shall fear the name of the LORD, and all the kings of the earth thy glory.
verse	19	102	16	When the LORD shall build up Zion, he shall appear in his glory.
verse	19	102	17	He will regard the prayer of the destitute, and not despise their prayer.
verse	19	102	18	This shall be written for the generation to come: and the people which shall be created shall praise the LORD.
verse	19	102	19	For he hath looked down from the height of his sanctuary; from heaven did the LORD behold the earth;
verse	19	102	20	To hear the groaning of the prisoner; to loose those that are appointed to death;
verse	19	102	21	To declare the name of the LORD in Zion, and his praise in Jerusalem;
verse	19	102	22	When the people are gathered together, and the kingdoms, to serve the LORD.
verse	19	102	23	He weakened my strength in the way; he shortened my days.
verse	19	102	24	@@I said, O my God, take me not away in the midst of my days: thy years @9are@7 throughout all generations.
verse	19	102	25	@@Of old hast thou laid the foundation of the earth: and the heavens @9are@7 the work of thy hands.
verse	19	102	26	They shall perish, but thou shalt endure: yea, all of them shall wax old like a garment; as a vesture shalt thou change them, and they shall be changed:
verse	19	102	27	@@But thou @9art@7 the same, and thy years shall have no end.
verse	19	102	28	The children of thy servants shall continue, and their seed shall be established before thee.
pericope	19	103	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	103	1	@@Bless the LORD, O my soul: and all that is within me, @9bless@7 his holy name.
verse	19	103	2	Bless the LORD, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits:
verse	19	103	3	Who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases;
verse	19	103	4	Who redeemeth thy life from destruction; who crowneth thee with lovingkindness and tender mercies;
verse	19	103	5	@@Who satisfieth thy mouth with good @9things; so that@7 thy youth is renewed like the eagle's.
verse	19	103	6	The LORD executeth righteousness and judgment for all that are oppressed.
verse	19	103	7	He made known his ways unto Moses, his acts unto the children of Israel.
verse	19	103	8	@@The LORD @9is@7 merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy.
verse	19	103	9	@@He will not always chide: neither will he keep @9his anger@7 for ever.
verse	19	103	10	He hath not dealt with us after our sins; nor rewarded us according to our iniquities.
verse	19	103	11	@@For as the heaven is high above the earth, @9so@7 great is his mercy toward them that fear him.
verse	19	103	12	@@As far as the east is from the west, @9so@7 far hath he removed our transgressions from us.
verse	19	103	13	@@Like as a father pitieth @9his@7 children, @9so@7 the LORD pitieth them that fear him.
verse	19	103	14	@@For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we @9are@7 dust.
verse	19	103	15	@@@9As for@7 man, his days @9are@7 as grass: as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth.
verse	19	103	16	For the wind passeth over it, and it is gone; and the place thereof shall know it no more.
verse	19	103	17	@@But the mercy of the LORD @9is@7 from everlasting to everlasting upon them that fear him, and his righteousness unto children's children;
verse	19	103	18	To such as keep his covenant, and to those that remember his commandments to do them.
verse	19	103	19	The LORD hath prepared his throne in the heavens; and his kingdom ruleth over all.
verse	19	103	20	Bless the LORD, ye his angels, that excel in strength, that do his commandments, hearkening unto the voice of his word.
verse	19	103	21	@@Bless ye the LORD, all @9ye@7 his hosts; @9ye@7 ministers of his, that do his pleasure.
verse	19	103	22	Bless the LORD, all his works in all places of his dominion: bless the LORD, O my soul.
verse	19	104	1	Bless the LORD, O my soul. O LORD my God, thou art very great; thou art clothed with honour and majesty.
verse	19	104	2	@@Who coverest @9thyself@7 with light as @9with@7 a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:
verse	19	104	3	Who layeth the beams of his chambers in the waters: who maketh the clouds his chariot: who walketh upon the wings of the wind:
verse	19	104	4	Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:
verse	19	104	5	@@@9Who@7 laid the foundations of the earth, @9that@7 it should not be removed for ever.
verse	19	104	6	@@Thou coveredst it with the deep as @9with@7 a garment: the waters stood above the mountains.
verse	19	104	7	At thy rebuke they fled; at the voice of thy thunder they hasted away.
verse	19	104	8	They go up by the mountains; they go down by the valleys unto the place which thou hast founded for them.
verse	19	104	9	Thou hast set a bound that they may not pass over; that they turn not again to cover the earth.
verse	19	104	10	@@He sendeth the springs into the valleys, @9which@7 run among the hills.
verse	19	104	11	They give drink to every beast of the field: the wild asses quench their thirst.
verse	19	104	12	@@By them shall the fowls of the heaven have their habitation, @9which@7 sing among the branches.
verse	19	104	13	He watereth the hills from his chambers: the earth is satisfied with the fruit of thy works.
verse	19	104	14	He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle, and herb for the service of man: that he may bring forth food out of the earth;
verse	19	104	15	@@And wine @9that@7 maketh glad the heart of man, @9and@7 oil to make @9his@7 face to shine, and bread @9which@7 strengtheneth man's heart.
verse	19	104	16	@@The trees of the LORD are full @9of sap;@7 the cedars of Lebanon, which he hath planted;
verse	19	104	17	@@Where the birds make their nests: @9as for@7 the stork, the fir trees @9are@7 her house.
verse	19	104	18	@@The high hills @9are@7 a refuge for the wild goats; @9and@7 the rocks for the conies.
verse	19	104	19	He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.
verse	19	104	20	@@Thou makest darkness, and it is night: wherein all the beasts of the forest do creep @9forth.@7
verse	19	104	21	The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their meat from God.
verse	19	104	22	The sun ariseth, they gather themselves together, and lay them down in their dens.
verse	19	104	23	Man goeth forth unto his work and to his labour until the evening.
verse	19	104	24	O LORD, how manifold are thy works! in wisdom hast thou made them all: the earth is full of thy riches.
verse	19	104	25	@@@9So is@7 this great and wide sea, wherein @9are@7 things creeping innumerable, both small and great beasts.
verse	19	104	26	@@There go the ships: @9there is@7 that leviathan, @9whom@7 thou hast made to play therein.
verse	19	104	27	@@These wait all upon thee; that thou mayest give @9them@7 their meat in due season.
verse	19	104	28	@@@9That@7 thou givest them they gather: thou openest thine hand, they are filled with good.
verse	19	104	29	Thou hidest thy face, they are troubled: thou takest away their breath, they die, and return to their dust.
verse	19	104	30	Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created: and thou renewest the face of the earth.
verse	19	104	31	The glory of the LORD shall endure for ever: the LORD shall rejoice in his works.
verse	19	104	32	He looketh on the earth, and it trembleth: he toucheth the hills, and they smoke.
verse	19	104	33	I will sing unto the LORD as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.
verse	19	104	34	My meditation of him shall be sweet: I will be glad in the LORD.
verse	19	104	35	Let the sinners be consumed out of the earth, and let the wicked be no more. Bless thou the LORD, O my soul. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	105	1	O give thanks unto the LORD; call upon his name: make known his deeds among the people.
verse	19	105	2	Sing unto him, sing psalms unto him: talk ye of all his wondrous works.
verse	19	105	3	Glory ye in his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice that seek the LORD.
verse	19	105	4	Seek the LORD, and his strength: seek his face evermore.
verse	19	105	5	Remember his marvellous works that he hath done; his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;
verse	19	105	6	O ye seed of Abraham his servant, ye children of Jacob his chosen.
verse	19	105	7	@@He @9is@7 the LORD our God: his judgments @9are@7 in all the earth.
verse	19	105	8	@@He hath remembered his covenant for ever, the word @9which@7 he commanded to a thousand generations.
verse	19	105	9	@@Which @9covenant@7 he made with Abraham, and his oath unto Isaac;
verse	19	105	10	@@And confirmed the same unto Jacob for a law, @9and@7 to Israel @9for@7 an everlasting covenant:
verse	19	105	11	Saying, Unto thee will I give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance:
verse	19	105	12	@@When they were @9but@7 a few men in number; yea, very few, and strangers in it.
verse	19	105	13	@@When they went from one nation to another, from @9one@7 kingdom to another people;
verse	19	105	14	He suffered no man to do them wrong: yea, he reproved kings for their sakes;
verse	19	105	15	@@@9Saying,@7 Touch not mine anointed, and do my prophets no harm.
verse	19	105	16	Moreover he called for a famine upon the land: he brake the whole staff of bread.
verse	19	105	17	@@He sent a man before them, @9even@7 Joseph, @9who@7 was sold for a servant:
verse	19	105	18	Whose feet they hurt with fetters: he was laid in iron:
verse	19	105	19	Until the time that his word came: the word of the LORD tried him.
verse	19	105	20	@@The king sent and loosed him; @9even@7 the ruler of the people, and let him go free.
verse	19	105	21	He made him lord of his house, and ruler of all his substance:
verse	19	105	22	To bind his princes at his pleasure; and teach his senators wisdom.
verse	19	105	23	Israel also came into Egypt; and Jacob sojourned in the land of Ham.
verse	19	105	24	And he increased his people greatly; and made them stronger than their enemies.
verse	19	105	25	He turned their heart to hate his people, to deal subtilly with his servants.
verse	19	105	26	@@He sent Moses his servant; @9and@7 Aaron whom he had chosen.
verse	19	105	27	They shewed his signs among them, and wonders in the land of Ham.
verse	19	105	28	He sent darkness, and made it dark; and they rebelled not against his word.
verse	19	105	29	He turned their waters into blood, and slew their fish.
verse	19	105	30	Their land brought forth frogs in abundance, in the chambers of their kings.
verse	19	105	31	@@He spake, and there came divers sorts of flies, @9and@7 lice in all their coasts.
verse	19	105	32	@@He gave them hail for rain, @9and@7 flaming fire in their land.
verse	19	105	33	He smote their vines also and their fig trees; and brake the trees of their coasts.
verse	19	105	34	He spake, and the locusts came, and caterpillers, and that without number,
verse	19	105	35	And did eat up all the herbs in their land, and devoured the fruit of their ground.
verse	19	105	36	He smote also all the firstborn in their land, the chief of all their strength.
verse	19	105	37	@@He brought them forth also with silver and gold: and @9there was@7 not one feeble @9person@7 among their tribes.
verse	19	105	38	Egypt was glad when they departed: for the fear of them fell upon them.
verse	19	105	39	He spread a cloud for a covering; and fire to give light in the night.
verse	19	105	40	@@@9The people@7 asked, and he brought quails, and satisfied them with the bread of heaven.
verse	19	105	41	@@He opened the rock, and the waters gushed out; they ran in the dry places @9like@7 a river.
verse	19	105	42	@@For he remembered his holy promise, @9and@7 Abraham his servant.
verse	19	105	43	@@And he brought forth his people with joy, @9and@7 his chosen with gladness:
verse	19	105	44	And gave them the lands of the heathen: and they inherited the labour of the people;
verse	19	105	45	That they might observe his statutes, and keep his laws. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	106	1	@@Praise ye the LORD. O give thanks unto the LORD; for @9he is@7 good: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	106	2	@@Who can utter the mighty acts of the LORD? @9who@7 can shew forth all his praise?
verse	19	106	3	@@Blessed @9are@7 they that keep judgment, @9and@7 he that doeth righteousness at all times.
verse	19	106	4	@@Remember me, O LORD, with the favour @9that thou bearest unto@7 thy people: O visit me with thy salvation;
verse	19	106	5	That I may see the good of thy chosen, that I may rejoice in the gladness of thy nation, that I may glory with thine inheritance.
verse	19	106	6	We have sinned with our fathers, we have committed iniquity, we have done wickedly.
verse	19	106	7	@@Our fathers understood not thy wonders in Egypt; they remembered not the multitude of thy mercies; but provoked @9him@7 at the sea, @9even@7 at the Red sea.
verse	19	106	8	Nevertheless he saved them for his name's sake, that he might make his mighty power to be known.
verse	19	106	9	He rebuked the Red sea also, and it was dried up: so he led them through the depths, as through the wilderness.
verse	19	106	10	@@And he saved them from the hand of him that hated @9them,@7 and redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.
verse	19	106	11	And the waters covered their enemies: there was not one of them left.
verse	19	106	12	Then believed they his words; they sang his praise.
verse	19	106	13	They soon forgat his works; they waited not for his counsel:
verse	19	106	14	But lusted exceedingly in the wilderness, and tempted God in the desert.
verse	19	106	15	And he gave them their request; but sent leanness into their soul.
verse	19	106	16	@@They envied Moses also in the camp, @9and@7 Aaron the saint of the LORD.
verse	19	106	17	The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan, and covered the company of Abiram.
verse	19	106	18	And a fire was kindled in their company; the flame burned up the wicked.
verse	19	106	19	They made a calf in Horeb, and worshipped the molten image.
verse	19	106	20	Thus they changed their glory into the similitude of an ox that eateth grass.
verse	19	106	21	They forgat God their saviour, which had done great things in Egypt;
verse	19	106	22	@@Wondrous works in the land of Ham, @9and@7 terrible things by the Red sea.
verse	19	106	23	@@Therefore he said that he would destroy them, had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach, to turn away his wrath, lest he should destroy @9them.@7
verse	19	106	24	Yea, they despised the pleasant land, they believed not his word:
verse	19	106	25	@@But murmured in their tents, @9and@7 hearkened not unto the voice of the LORD.
verse	19	106	26	Therefore he lifted up his hand against them, to overthrow them in the wilderness:
verse	19	106	27	To overthrow their seed also among the nations, and to scatter them in the lands.
verse	19	106	28	They joined themselves also unto Baalpeor, and ate the sacrifices of the dead.
verse	19	106	29	@@Thus they provoked @9him@7 to anger with their inventions: and the plague brake in upon them.
verse	19	106	30	@@Then stood up Phinehas, and executed judgment: and @9so@7 the plague was stayed.
verse	19	106	31	And that was counted unto him for righteousness unto all generations for evermore.
verse	19	106	32	@@They angered @9him@7 also at the waters of strife, so that it went ill with Moses for their sakes:
verse	19	106	33	Because they provoked his spirit, so that he spake unadvisedly with his lips.
verse	19	106	34	They did not destroy the nations, concerning whom the LORD commanded them:
verse	19	106	35	But were mingled among the heathen, and learned their works.
verse	19	106	36	And they served their idols: which were a snare unto them.
verse	19	106	37	Yea, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters unto devils,
verse	19	106	38	@@And shed innocent blood, @9even@7 the blood of their sons and of their daughters, whom they sacrificed unto the idols of Canaan: and the land was polluted with blood.
verse	19	106	39	Thus were they defiled with their own works, and went a whoring with their own inventions.
verse	19	106	40	Therefore was the wrath of the LORD kindled against his people, insomuch that he abhorred his own inheritance.
verse	19	106	41	And he gave them into the hand of the heathen; and they that hated them ruled over them.
verse	19	106	42	Their enemies also oppressed them, and they were brought into subjection under their hand.
verse	19	106	43	@@Many times did he deliver them; but they provoked @9him@7 with their counsel, and were brought low for their iniquity.
verse	19	106	44	Nevertheless he regarded their affliction, when he heard their cry:
verse	19	106	45	And he remembered for them his covenant, and repented according to the multitude of his mercies.
verse	19	106	46	He made them also to be pitied of all those that carried them captives.
verse	19	106	47	@@Save us, O LORD our God, and gather us from among the heathen, to give thanks unto thy holy name, @9and@7 to triumph in thy praise.
verse	19	106	48	@@Blessed @9be@7 the Lord God of Israel from everlasting to everlasting: and let all the people say, Amen. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	107	1	@@O give thanks unto the LORD, for @9he is@7 good: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	107	2	Let the redeemed of the LORD say so, whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the enemy;
verse	19	107	3	And gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and from the west, from the north, and from the south.
verse	19	107	4	They wandered in the wilderness in a solitary way; they found no city to dwell in.
verse	19	107	5	Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them.
verse	19	107	6	@@Then they cried unto the LORD in their trouble, @9and@7 he delivered them out of their distresses.
verse	19	107	7	And he led them forth by the right way, that they might go to a city of habitation.
verse	19	107	8	@@Oh that @9men@7 would praise the LORD @9for@7 his goodness, and @9for@7 his wonderful works to the children of men!
verse	19	107	9	For he satisfieth the longing soul, and filleth the hungry soul with goodness.
verse	19	107	10	@@Such as sit in darkness and in the shadow of death, @9being@7 bound in affliction and iron;
verse	19	107	11	Because they rebelled against the words of God, and contemned the counsel of the most High:
verse	19	107	12	@@Therefore he brought down their heart with labour; they fell down, and @9there was@7 none to help.
verse	19	107	13	@@Then they cried unto the LORD in their trouble, @9and@7 he saved them out of their distresses.
verse	19	107	14	He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and brake their bands in sunder.
verse	19	107	15	@@Oh that @9men@7 would praise the LORD @9for@7 his goodness, and @9for@7 his wonderful works to the children of men!
verse	19	107	16	For he hath broken the gates of brass, and cut the bars of iron in sunder.
verse	19	107	17	Fools because of their transgression, and because of their iniquities, are afflicted.
verse	19	107	18	Their soul abhorreth all manner of meat; and they draw near unto the gates of death.
verse	19	107	19	@@Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, @9and@7 he saveth them out of their distresses.
verse	19	107	20	@@He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered @9them@7 from their destructions.
verse	19	107	21	@@Oh that @9men@7 would praise the LORD @9for@7 his goodness, and @9for@7 his wonderful works to the children of men!
verse	19	107	22	And let them sacrifice the sacrifices of thanksgiving, and declare his works with rejoicing.
verse	19	107	23	They that go down to the sea in ships, that do business in great waters;
verse	19	107	24	These see the works of the LORD, and his wonders in the deep.
verse	19	107	25	For he commandeth, and raiseth the stormy wind, which lifteth up the waves thereof.
verse	19	107	26	They mount up to the heaven, they go down again to the depths: their soul is melted because of trouble.
verse	19	107	27	They reel to and fro, and stagger like a drunken man, and are at their wit's end.
verse	19	107	28	Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, and he bringeth them out of their distresses.
verse	19	107	29	He maketh the storm a calm, so that the waves thereof are still.
verse	19	107	30	Then are they glad because they be quiet; so he bringeth them unto their desired haven.
verse	19	107	31	@@Oh that @9men@7 would praise the LORD @9for@7 his goodness, and @9for@7 his wonderful works to the children of men!
verse	19	107	32	Let them exalt him also in the congregation of the people, and praise him in the assembly of the elders.
verse	19	107	33	He turneth rivers into a wilderness, and the watersprings into dry ground;
verse	19	107	34	A fruitful land into barrenness, for the wickedness of them that dwell therein.
verse	19	107	35	He turneth the wilderness into a standing water, and dry ground into watersprings.
verse	19	107	36	And there he maketh the hungry to dwell, that they may prepare a city for habitation;
verse	19	107	37	And sow the fields, and plant vineyards, which may yield fruits of increase.
verse	19	107	38	He blesseth them also, so that they are multiplied greatly; and suffereth not their cattle to decrease.
verse	19	107	39	Again, they are minished and brought low through oppression, affliction, and sorrow.
verse	19	107	40	@@He poureth contempt upon princes, and causeth them to wander in the wilderness, @9where there is@7 no way.
verse	19	107	41	@@Yet setteth he the poor on high from affliction, and maketh @9him@7 families like a flock.
verse	19	107	42	@@The righteous shall see @9it,@7 and rejoice: and all iniquity shall stop her mouth.
verse	19	107	43	@@Whoso @9is@7 wise, and will observe these @9things,@7 even they shall understand the lovingkindness of the LORD.
pericope	19	108	1	A Song or Psalm of David.
verse	19	108	1	O God, my heart is fixed; I will sing and give praise, even with my glory.
verse	19	108	2	@@Awake, psaltery and harp: I @9myself@7 will awake early.
verse	19	108	3	I will praise thee, O LORD, among the people: and I will sing praises unto thee among the nations.
verse	19	108	4	@@For thy mercy @9is@7 great above the heavens: and thy truth @9reacheth@7 unto the clouds.
verse	19	108	5	Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: and thy glory above all the earth;
verse	19	108	6	@@That thy beloved may be delivered: save @9with@7 thy right hand, and answer me.
verse	19	108	7	God hath spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.
verse	19	108	8	@@Gilead @9is@7 mine; Manasseh @9is@7 mine; Ephraim also @9is@7 the strength of mine head; Judah @9is@7 my lawgiver;
verse	19	108	9	@@Moab @9is@7 my washpot; over Edom will I cast out my shoe; over Philistia will I triumph.
verse	19	108	10	Who will bring me into the strong city? who will lead me into Edom?
verse	19	108	11	@@@9Wilt@7 not @9thou,@7 O God, @9who@7 hast cast us off? and wilt not thou, O God, go forth with our hosts?
verse	19	108	12	@@Give us help from trouble: for vain @9is@7 the help of man.
verse	19	108	13	@@Through God we shall do valiantly: for he @9it is that@7 shall tread down our enemies.
pericope	19	109	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	109	1	Hold not thy peace, O God of my praise;
verse	19	109	2	For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful are opened against me: they have spoken against me with a lying tongue.
verse	19	109	3	They compassed me about also with words of hatred; and fought against me without a cause.
verse	19	109	4	@@For my love they are my adversaries: but I @9give myself unto@7 prayer.
verse	19	109	5	And they have rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.
verse	19	109	6	Set thou a wicked man over him: and let Satan stand at his right hand.
verse	19	109	7	When he shall be judged, let him be condemned: and let his prayer become sin.
verse	19	109	8	@@Let his days be few; @9and@7 let another take his office.
verse	19	109	9	Let his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.
verse	19	109	10	@@Let his children be continually vagabonds, and beg: let them seek @9their bread@7 also out of their desolate places.
verse	19	109	11	Let the extortioner catch all that he hath; and let the strangers spoil his labour.
verse	19	109	12	Let there be none to extend mercy unto him: neither let there be any to favour his fatherless children.
verse	19	109	13	@@Let his posterity be cut off; @9and@7 in the generation following let their name be blotted out.
verse	19	109	14	Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered with the LORD; and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.
verse	19	109	15	Let them be before the LORD continually, that he may cut off the memory of them from the earth.
verse	19	109	16	Because that he remembered not to shew mercy, but persecuted the poor and needy man, that he might even slay the broken in heart.
verse	19	109	17	As he loved cursing, so let it come unto him: as he delighted not in blessing, so let it be far from him.
verse	19	109	18	As he clothed himself with cursing like as with his garment, so let it come into his bowels like water, and like oil into his bones.
verse	19	109	19	@@Let it be unto him as the garment @9which@7 covereth him, and for a girdle wherewith he is girded continually.
verse	19	109	20	@@@9Let@7 this @9be@7 the reward of mine adversaries from the LORD, and of them that speak evil against my soul.
verse	19	109	21	@@But do thou for me, O GOD the Lord, for thy name's sake: because thy mercy @9is@7 good, deliver thou me.
verse	19	109	22	@@For I @9am@7 poor and needy, and my heart is wounded within me.
verse	19	109	23	I am gone like the shadow when it declineth: I am tossed up and down as the locust.
verse	19	109	24	My knees are weak through fasting; and my flesh faileth of fatness.
verse	19	109	25	@@I became also a reproach unto them: @9when@7 they looked upon me they shaked their heads.
verse	19	109	26	Help me, O LORD my God: O save me according to thy mercy:
verse	19	109	27	@@That they may know that this @9is@7 thy hand; @9that@7 thou, LORD, hast done it.
verse	19	109	28	Let them curse, but bless thou: when they arise, let them be ashamed; but let thy servant rejoice.
verse	19	109	29	Let mine adversaries be clothed with shame, and let them cover themselves with their own confusion, as with a mantle.
verse	19	109	30	I will greatly praise the LORD with my mouth; yea, I will praise him among the multitude.
verse	19	109	31	@@For he shall stand at the right hand of the poor, to save @9him@7 from those that condemn his soul.
pericope	19	110	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	110	1	The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou at my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool.
verse	19	110	2	The LORD shall send the rod of thy strength out of Zion: rule thou in the midst of thine enemies.
verse	19	110	3	@@Thy people @9shall be@7 willing in the day of thy power, in the beauties of holiness from the womb of the morning: thou hast the dew of thy youth.
verse	19	110	4	@@The LORD hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou @9art@7 a priest for ever after the order of Melchizedek.
verse	19	110	5	The Lord at thy right hand shall strike through kings in the day of his wrath.
verse	19	110	6	@@He shall judge among the heathen, he shall fill @9the places@7 with the dead bodies; he shall wound the heads over many countries.
verse	19	110	7	He shall drink of the brook in the way: therefore shall he lift up the head.
verse	19	111	1	@@Praise ye the LORD. I will praise the LORD with @9my@7 whole heart, in the assembly of the upright, and @9in@7 the congregation.
verse	19	111	2	@@The works of the LORD @9are@7 great, sought out of all them that have pleasure therein.
verse	19	111	3	@@His work @9is@7 honourable and glorious: and his righteousness endureth for ever.
verse	19	111	4	@@He hath made his wonderful works to be remembered: the LORD @9is@7 gracious and full of compassion.
verse	19	111	5	He hath given meat unto them that fear him: he will ever be mindful of his covenant.
verse	19	111	6	He hath shewed his people the power of his works, that he may give them the heritage of the heathen.
verse	19	111	7	@@The works of his hands @9are@7 verity and judgment; all his commandments @9are@7 sure.
verse	19	111	8	@@They stand fast for ever and ever, @9and are@7 done in truth and uprightness.
verse	19	111	9	@@He sent redemption unto his people: he hath commanded his covenant for ever: holy and reverend @9is@7 his name.
verse	19	111	10	@@The fear of the LORD @9is@7 the beginning of wisdom: a good understanding have all they that do @9his commandments:@7 his praise endureth for ever.
verse	19	112	1	@@Praise ye the LORD. Blessed @9is@7 the man @9that@7 feareth the LORD, @9that@7 delighteth greatly in his commandments.
verse	19	112	2	His seed shall be mighty upon earth: the generation of the upright shall be blessed.
verse	19	112	3	@@Wealth and riches @9shall be@7 in his house: and his righteousness endureth for ever.
verse	19	112	4	@@Unto the upright there ariseth light in the darkness: @9he is@7 gracious, and full of compassion, and righteous.
verse	19	112	5	A good man sheweth favour, and lendeth: he will guide his affairs with discretion.
verse	19	112	6	Surely he shall not be moved for ever: the righteous shall be in everlasting remembrance.
verse	19	112	7	He shall not be afraid of evil tidings: his heart is fixed, trusting in the LORD.
verse	19	112	8	@@His heart @9is@7 established, he shall not be afraid, until he see @9his desire@7 upon his enemies.
verse	19	112	9	He hath dispersed, he hath given to the poor; his righteousness endureth for ever; his horn shall be exalted with honour.
verse	19	112	10	@@The wicked shall see @9it,@7 and be grieved; he shall gnash with his teeth, and melt away: the desire of the wicked shall perish.
verse	19	113	1	Praise ye the LORD. Praise, O ye servants of the LORD, praise the name of the LORD.
verse	19	113	2	Blessed be the name of the LORD from this time forth and for evermore.
verse	19	113	3	@@From the rising of the sun unto the going down of the same the LORD'S name @9is@7 to be praised.
verse	19	113	4	@@The LORD @9is@7 high above all nations, @9and@7 his glory above the heavens.
verse	19	113	5	@@Who @9is@7 like unto the LORD our God, who dwelleth on high,
verse	19	113	6	@@Who humbleth @9himself@7 to behold @9the things that are@7 in heaven, and in the earth!
verse	19	113	7	@@He raiseth up the poor out of the dust, @9and@7 lifteth the needy out of the dunghill;
verse	19	113	8	@@That he may set @9him@7 with princes, @9even@7 with the princes of his people.
verse	19	113	9	@@He maketh the barren woman to keep house, @9and to be@7 a joyful mother of children. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	114	1	When Israel went out of Egypt, the house of Jacob from a people of strange language;
verse	19	114	2	@@Judah was his sanctuary, @9and@7 Israel his dominion.
verse	19	114	3	@@The sea saw @9it,@7 and fled: Jordan was driven back.
verse	19	114	4	@@The mountains skipped like rams, @9and@7 the little hills like lambs.
verse	19	114	5	@@What @9ailed@7 thee, O thou sea, that thou fleddest? thou Jordan, @9that@7 thou wast driven back?
verse	19	114	6	@@Ye mountains, @9that@7 ye skipped like rams; @9and@7 ye little hills, like lambs?
verse	19	114	7	Tremble, thou earth, at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob;
verse	19	114	8	@@Which turned the rock @9into@7 a standing water, the flint into a fountain of waters.
verse	19	115	1	@@Not unto us, O LORD, not unto us, but unto thy name give glory, for thy mercy, @9and@7 for thy truth's sake.
verse	19	115	2	@@Wherefore should the heathen say, Where @9is@7 now their God?
verse	19	115	3	@@But our God @9is@7 in the heavens: he hath done whatsoever he hath pleased.
verse	19	115	4	@@Their idols @9are@7 silver and gold, the work of men's hands.
verse	19	115	5	They have mouths, but they speak not: eyes have they, but they see not:
verse	19	115	6	They have ears, but they hear not: noses have they, but they smell not:
verse	19	115	7	They have hands, but they handle not: feet have they, but they walk not: neither speak they through their throat.
verse	19	115	8	@@They that make them are like unto them; @9so is@7 every one that trusteth in them.
verse	19	115	9	@@O Israel, trust thou in the LORD: he @9is@7 their help and their shield.
verse	19	115	10	@@O house of Aaron, trust in the LORD: he @9is@7 their help and their shield.
verse	19	115	11	@@Ye that fear the LORD, trust in the LORD: he @9is@7 their help and their shield.
verse	19	115	12	@@The LORD hath been mindful of us: he will bless @9us;@7 he will bless the house of Israel; he will bless the house of Aaron.
verse	19	115	13	@@He will bless them that fear the LORD, @9both@7 small and great.
verse	19	115	14	The LORD shall increase you more and more, you and your children.
verse	19	115	15	@@Ye @9are@7 blessed of the LORD which made heaven and earth.
verse	19	115	16	@@The heaven, @9even@7 the heavens, @9are@7 the LORD'S: but the earth hath he given to the children of men.
verse	19	115	17	The dead praise not the LORD, neither any that go down into silence.
verse	19	115	18	But we will bless the LORD from this time forth and for evermore. Praise the LORD.
verse	19	116	1	@@I love the LORD, because he hath heard my voice @9and@7 my supplications.
verse	19	116	2	@@Because he hath inclined his ear unto me, therefore will I call upon @9him@7 as long as I live.
verse	19	116	3	The sorrows of death compassed me, and the pains of hell gat hold upon me: I found trouble and sorrow.
verse	19	116	4	Then called I upon the name of the LORD; O LORD, I beseech thee, deliver my soul.
verse	19	116	5	@@Gracious @9is@7 the LORD, and righteous; yea, our God @9is@7 merciful.
verse	19	116	6	The LORD preserveth the simple: I was brought low, and he helped me.
verse	19	116	7	Return unto thy rest, O my soul; for the LORD hath dealt bountifully with thee.
verse	19	116	8	@@For thou hast delivered my soul from death, mine eyes from tears, @9and@7 my feet from falling.
verse	19	116	9	I will walk before the LORD in the land of the living.
verse	19	116	10	I believed, therefore have I spoken: I was greatly afflicted:
verse	19	116	11	@@I said in my haste, All men @9are@7 liars.
verse	19	116	12	@@What shall I render unto the LORD @9for@7 all his benefits toward me?
verse	19	116	13	I will take the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the LORD.
verse	19	116	14	I will pay my vows unto the LORD now in the presence of all his people.
verse	19	116	15	@@Precious in the sight of the LORD @9is@7 the death of his saints.
verse	19	116	16	@@O LORD, truly I @9am@7 thy servant; I @9am@7 thy servant, @9and@7 the son of thine handmaid: thou hast loosed my bonds.
verse	19	116	17	I will offer to thee the sacrifice of thanksgiving, and will call upon the name of the LORD.
verse	19	116	18	I will pay my vows unto the LORD now in the presence of all his people,
verse	19	116	19	In the courts of the LORD'S house, in the midst of thee, O Jerusalem. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	117	1	O praise the LORD, all ye nations: praise him, all ye people.
verse	19	117	2	@@For his merciful kindness is great toward us: and the truth of the LORD @9endureth@7 for ever. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	118	1	@@O give thanks unto the LORD; for @9he is@7 good: because his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	118	2	@@Let Israel now say, that his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	118	3	@@Let the house of Aaron now say, that his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	118	4	@@Let them now that fear the LORD say, that his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	118	5	@@I called upon the LORD in distress: the LORD answered me, @9and set me@7 in a large place.
verse	19	118	6	@@The LORD @9is@7 on my side; I will not fear: what can man do unto me?
verse	19	118	7	@@The LORD taketh my part with them that help me: therefore shall I see @9my desire@7 upon them that hate me.
verse	19	118	8	@@@9It is@7 better to trust in the LORD than to put confidence in man.
verse	19	118	9	@@@9It is@7 better to trust in the LORD than to put confidence in princes.
verse	19	118	10	All nations compassed me about: but in the name of the LORD will I destroy them.
verse	19	118	11	They compassed me about; yea, they compassed me about: but in the name of the LORD I will destroy them.
verse	19	118	12	They compassed me about like bees; they are quenched as the fire of thorns: for in the name of the LORD I will destroy them.
verse	19	118	13	Thou hast thrust sore at me that I might fall: but the LORD helped me.
verse	19	118	14	@@The LORD @9is@7 my strength and song, and is become my salvation.
verse	19	118	15	@@The voice of rejoicing and salvation @9is@7 in the tabernacles of the righteous: the right hand of the LORD doeth valiantly.
verse	19	118	16	The right hand of the LORD is exalted: the right hand of the LORD doeth valiantly.
verse	19	118	17	I shall not die, but live, and declare the works of the LORD.
verse	19	118	18	The LORD hath chastened me sore: but he hath not given me over unto death.
verse	19	118	19	@@Open to me the gates of righteousness: I will go into them, @9and@7 I will praise the LORD:
verse	19	118	20	This gate of the LORD, into which the righteous shall enter.
verse	19	118	21	I will praise thee: for thou hast heard me, and art become my salvation.
verse	19	118	22	@@The stone @9which@7 the builders refused is become the head @9stone@7 of the corner.
verse	19	118	23	@@This is the LORD'S doing; it @9is@7 marvellous in our eyes.
verse	19	118	24	@@This @9is@7 the day @9which@7 the LORD hath made; we will rejoice and be glad in it.
verse	19	118	25	Save now, I beseech thee, O LORD: O LORD, I beseech thee, send now prosperity.
verse	19	118	26	@@Blessed @9be@7 he that cometh in the name of the LORD: we have blessed you out of the house of the LORD.
verse	19	118	27	@@God @9is@7 the LORD, which hath shewed us light: bind the sacrifice with cords, @9even@7 unto the horns of the altar.
verse	19	118	28	@@Thou @9art@7 my God, and I will praise thee: @9thou art@7 my God, I will exalt thee.
verse	19	118	29	@@O give thanks unto the LORD; for @9he is@7 good: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
pericope	19	119	1	ALEPH.
verse	19	119	1	@@Blessed @9are@7 the undefiled in the way, who walk in the law of the LORD.
verse	19	119	2	@@Blessed @9are@7 they that keep his testimonies, @9and that@7 seek him with the whole heart.
verse	19	119	3	They also do no iniquity: they walk in his ways.
verse	19	119	4	@@Thou hast commanded @9us@7 to keep thy precepts diligently.
verse	19	119	5	O that my ways were directed to keep thy statutes!
verse	19	119	6	Then shall I not be ashamed, when I have respect unto all thy commandments.
verse	19	119	7	I will praise thee with uprightness of heart, when I shall have learned thy righteous judgments.
verse	19	119	8	I will keep thy statutes: O forsake me not utterly.
pericope	19	119	9	BETH.
verse	19	119	9	@@Wherewithal shall a young man cleanse his way? by taking heed @9thereto@7 according to thy word.
verse	19	119	10	With my whole heart have I sought thee: O let me not wander from thy commandments.
verse	19	119	11	Thy word have I hid in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee.
verse	19	119	12	@@Blessed @9art@7 thou, O LORD: teach me thy statutes.
verse	19	119	13	With my lips have I declared all the judgments of thy mouth.
verse	19	119	14	@@I have rejoiced in the way of thy testimonies, as @9much as@7 in all riches.
verse	19	119	15	I will meditate in thy precepts, and have respect unto thy ways.
verse	19	119	16	I will delight myself in thy statutes: I will not forget thy word.
pericope	19	119	17	GIMEL.
verse	19	119	17	@@Deal bountifully with thy servant, @9that@7 I may live, and keep thy word.
verse	19	119	18	Open thou mine eyes, that I may behold wondrous things out of thy law.
verse	19	119	19	@@I @9am@7 a stranger in the earth: hide not thy commandments from me.
verse	19	119	20	@@My soul breaketh for the longing @9that it hath@7 unto thy judgments at all times.
verse	19	119	21	@@Thou hast rebuked the proud @9that are@7 cursed, which do err from thy commandments.
verse	19	119	22	Remove from me reproach and contempt; for I have kept thy testimonies.
verse	19	119	23	@@Princes also did sit @9and@7 speak against me: @9but@7 thy servant did meditate in thy statutes.
verse	19	119	24	@@Thy testimonies also @9are@7 my delight @9and@7 my counsellors.
pericope	19	119	25	DALETH.
verse	19	119	25	My soul cleaveth unto the dust: quicken thou me according to thy word.
verse	19	119	26	I have declared my ways, and thou heardest me: teach me thy statutes.
verse	19	119	27	Make me to understand the way of thy precepts: so shall I talk of thy wondrous works.
verse	19	119	28	My soul melteth for heaviness: strengthen thou me according unto thy word.
verse	19	119	29	Remove from me the way of lying: and grant me thy law graciously.
verse	19	119	30	@@I have chosen the way of truth: thy judgments have I laid @9before me.@7
verse	19	119	31	I have stuck unto thy testimonies: O LORD, put me not to shame.
verse	19	119	32	I will run the way of thy commandments, when thou shalt enlarge my heart.
pericope	19	119	33	HE.
verse	19	119	33	@@Teach me, O LORD, the way of thy statutes; and I shall keep it @9unto@7 the end.
verse	19	119	34	@@Give me understanding, and I shall keep thy law; yea, I shall observe it with @9my@7 whole heart.
verse	19	119	35	Make me to go in the path of thy commandments; for therein do I delight.
verse	19	119	36	Incline my heart unto thy testimonies, and not to covetousness.
verse	19	119	37	@@Turn away mine eyes from beholding vanity; @9and@7 quicken thou me in thy way.
verse	19	119	38	@@Stablish thy word unto thy servant, who @9is devoted@7 to thy fear.
verse	19	119	39	@@Turn away my reproach which I fear: for thy judgments @9are@7 good.
verse	19	119	40	Behold, I have longed after thy precepts: quicken me in thy righteousness.
pericope	19	119	41	VAU.
verse	19	119	41	@@Let thy mercies come also unto me, O LORD, @9even@7 thy salvation, according to thy word.
verse	19	119	42	So shall I have wherewith to answer him that reproacheth me: for I trust in thy word.
verse	19	119	43	And take not the word of truth utterly out of my mouth; for I have hoped in thy judgments.
verse	19	119	44	So shall I keep thy law continually for ever and ever.
verse	19	119	45	And I will walk at liberty: for I seek thy precepts.
verse	19	119	46	I will speak of thy testimonies also before kings, and will not be ashamed.
verse	19	119	47	And I will delight myself in thy commandments, which I have loved.
verse	19	119	48	My hands also will I lift up unto thy commandments, which I have loved; and I will meditate in thy statutes.
pericope	19	119	49	ZAIN.
verse	19	119	49	Remember the word unto thy servant, upon which thou hast caused me to hope.
verse	19	119	50	@@This @9is@7 my comfort in my affliction: for thy word hath quickened me.
verse	19	119	51	@@The proud have had me greatly in derision: @9yet@7 have I not declined from thy law.
verse	19	119	52	I remembered thy judgments of old, O LORD; and have comforted myself.
verse	19	119	53	Horror hath taken hold upon me because of the wicked that forsake thy law.
verse	19	119	54	Thy statutes have been my songs in the house of my pilgrimage.
verse	19	119	55	I have remembered thy name, O LORD, in the night, and have kept thy law.
verse	19	119	56	This I had, because I kept thy precepts.
pericope	19	119	57	CHETH.
verse	19	119	57	@@@9Thou art@7 my portion, O LORD: I have said that I would keep thy words.
verse	19	119	58	@@I intreated thy favour with @9my@7 whole heart: be merciful unto me according to thy word.
verse	19	119	59	I thought on my ways, and turned my feet unto thy testimonies.
verse	19	119	60	I made haste, and delayed not to keep thy commandments.
verse	19	119	61	@@The bands of the wicked have robbed me: @9but@7 I have not forgotten thy law.
verse	19	119	62	At midnight I will rise to give thanks unto thee because of thy righteous judgments.
verse	19	119	63	@@I @9am@7 a companion of all @9them@7 that fear thee, and of them that keep thy precepts.
verse	19	119	64	The earth, O LORD, is full of thy mercy: teach me thy statutes.
pericope	19	119	65	TETH.
verse	19	119	65	Thou hast dealt well with thy servant, O LORD, according unto thy word.
verse	19	119	66	Teach me good judgment and knowledge: for I have believed thy commandments.
verse	19	119	67	Before I was afflicted I went astray: but now have I kept thy word.
verse	19	119	68	@@Thou @9art@7 good, and doest good; teach me thy statutes.
verse	19	119	69	@@The proud have forged a lie against me: @9but@7 I will keep thy precepts with @9my@7 whole heart.
verse	19	119	70	@@Their heart is as fat as grease; @9but@7 I delight in thy law.
verse	19	119	71	@@@9It is@7 good for me that I have been afflicted; that I might learn thy statutes.
verse	19	119	72	@@The law of thy mouth @9is@7 better unto me than thousands of gold and silver.
pericope	19	119	73	JOD.
verse	19	119	73	Thy hands have made me and fashioned me: give me understanding, that I may learn thy commandments.
verse	19	119	74	They that fear thee will be glad when they see me; because I have hoped in thy word.
verse	19	119	75	@@I know, O LORD, that thy judgments @9are@7 right, and that @9thou@7 in faithfulness hast afflicted me.
verse	19	119	76	Let, I pray thee, thy merciful kindness be for my comfort, according to thy word unto thy servant.
verse	19	119	77	@@Let thy tender mercies come unto me, that I may live: for thy law @9is@7 my delight.
verse	19	119	78	@@Let the proud be ashamed; for they dealt perversely with me without a cause: @9but@7 I will meditate in thy precepts.
verse	19	119	79	Let those that fear thee turn unto me, and those that have known thy testimonies.
verse	19	119	80	Let my heart be sound in thy statutes; that I be not ashamed.
pericope	19	119	81	CAPH.
verse	19	119	81	@@My soul fainteth for thy salvation: @9but@7 I hope in thy word.
verse	19	119	82	Mine eyes fail for thy word, saying, When wilt thou comfort me?
verse	19	119	83	@@For I am become like a bottle in the smoke; @9yet@7 do I not forget thy statutes.
verse	19	119	84	@@How many @9are@7 the days of thy servant? when wilt thou execute judgment on them that persecute me?
verse	19	119	85	@@The proud have digged pits for me, which @9are@7 not after thy law.
verse	19	119	86	@@All thy commandments @9are@7 faithful: they persecute me wrongfully; help thou me.
verse	19	119	87	They had almost consumed me upon earth; but I forsook not thy precepts.
verse	19	119	88	Quicken me after thy lovingkindness; so shall I keep the testimony of thy mouth.
pericope	19	119	89	LAMED.
verse	19	119	89	For ever, O LORD, thy word is settled in heaven.
verse	19	119	90	@@Thy faithfulness @9is@7 unto all generations: thou hast established the earth, and it abideth.
verse	19	119	91	@@They continue this day according to thine ordinances: for all @9are@7 thy servants.
verse	19	119	92	@@Unless thy law @9had been@7 my delights, I should then have perished in mine affliction.
verse	19	119	93	I will never forget thy precepts: for with them thou hast quickened me.
verse	19	119	94	@@I @9am@7 thine, save me; for I have sought thy precepts.
verse	19	119	95	@@The wicked have waited for me to destroy me: @9but@7 I will consider thy testimonies.
verse	19	119	96	@@I have seen an end of all perfection: @9but@7 thy commandment @9is@7 exceeding broad.
pericope	19	119	97	MEM.
verse	19	119	97	@@O how love I thy law! it @9is@7 my meditation all the day.
verse	19	119	98	@@Thou through thy commandments hast made me wiser than mine enemies: for they @9are@7 ever with me.
verse	19	119	99	@@I have more understanding than all my teachers: for thy testimonies @9are@7 my meditation.
verse	19	119	100	I understand more than the ancients, because I keep thy precepts.
verse	19	119	101	I have refrained my feet from every evil way, that I might keep thy word.
verse	19	119	102	I have not departed from thy judgments: for thou hast taught me.
verse	19	119	103	@@How sweet are thy words unto my taste! @9yea, sweeter@7 than honey to my mouth!
verse	19	119	104	Through thy precepts I get understanding: therefore I hate every false way.
pericope	19	119	105	NUN.
verse	19	119	105	@@Thy word @9is@7 a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path.
verse	19	119	106	@@I have sworn, and I will perform @9it,@7 that I will keep thy righteous judgments.
verse	19	119	107	I am afflicted very much: quicken me, O LORD, according unto thy word.
verse	19	119	108	Accept, I beseech thee, the freewill offerings of my mouth, O LORD, and teach me thy judgments.
verse	19	119	109	@@My soul @9is@7 continually in my hand: yet do I not forget thy law.
verse	19	119	110	The wicked have laid a snare for me: yet I erred not from thy precepts.
verse	19	119	111	@@Thy testimonies have I taken as an heritage for ever: for they @9are@7 the rejoicing of my heart.
verse	19	119	112	@@I have inclined mine heart to perform thy statutes alway, @9even unto@7 the end.
pericope	19	119	113	SAMECH.
verse	19	119	113	@@I hate @9vain@7 thoughts: but thy law do I love.
verse	19	119	114	@@Thou @9art@7 my hiding place and my shield: I hope in thy word.
verse	19	119	115	Depart from me, ye evildoers: for I will keep the commandments of my God.
verse	19	119	116	Uphold me according unto thy word, that I may live: and let me not be ashamed of my hope.
verse	19	119	117	Hold thou me up, and I shall be safe: and I will have respect unto thy statutes continually.
verse	19	119	118	@@Thou hast trodden down all them that err from thy statutes: for their deceit @9is@7 falsehood.
verse	19	119	119	@@Thou puttest away all the wicked of the earth @9like@7 dross: therefore I love thy testimonies.
verse	19	119	120	My flesh trembleth for fear of thee; and I am afraid of thy judgments.
pericope	19	119	121	AIN.
verse	19	119	121	I have done judgment and justice: leave me not to mine oppressors.
verse	19	119	122	Be surety for thy servant for good: let not the proud oppress me.
verse	19	119	123	Mine eyes fail for thy salvation, and for the word of thy righteousness.
verse	19	119	124	Deal with thy servant according unto thy mercy, and teach me thy statutes.
verse	19	119	125	@@I @9am@7 thy servant; give me understanding, that I may know thy testimonies.
verse	19	119	126	@@@9It is@7 time for @9thee,@7 LORD, to work: @9for@7 they have made void thy law.
verse	19	119	127	Therefore I love thy commandments above gold; yea, above fine gold.
verse	19	119	128	@@Therefore I esteem all @9thy@7 precepts @9concerning@7 all @9things to be@7 right; @9and@7 I hate every false way.
pericope	19	119	129	PE.
verse	19	119	129	@@Thy testimonies @9are@7 wonderful: therefore doth my soul keep them.
verse	19	119	130	The entrance of thy words giveth light; it giveth understanding unto the simple.
verse	19	119	131	I opened my mouth, and panted: for I longed for thy commandments.
verse	19	119	132	Look thou upon me, and be merciful unto me, as thou usest to do unto those that love thy name.
verse	19	119	133	Order my steps in thy word: and let not any iniquity have dominion over me.
verse	19	119	134	Deliver me from the oppression of man: so will I keep thy precepts.
verse	19	119	135	Make thy face to shine upon thy servant; and teach me thy statutes.
verse	19	119	136	Rivers of waters run down mine eyes, because they keep not thy law.
pericope	19	119	137	TZADDI.
verse	19	119	137	@@Righteous @9art@7 thou, O LORD, and upright @9are@7 thy judgments.
verse	19	119	138	@@Thy testimonies @9that@7 thou hast commanded @9are@7 righteous and very faithful.
verse	19	119	139	My zeal hath consumed me, because mine enemies have forgotten thy words.
verse	19	119	140	@@Thy word @9is@7 very pure: therefore thy servant loveth it.
verse	19	119	141	@@I @9am@7 small and despised: @9yet@7 do not I forget thy precepts.
verse	19	119	142	@@Thy righteousness @9is@7 an everlasting righteousness, and thy law @9is@7 the truth.
verse	19	119	143	@@Trouble and anguish have taken hold on me: @9yet@7 thy commandments @9are@7 my delights.
verse	19	119	144	@@The righteousness of thy testimonies @9is@7 everlasting: give me understanding, and I shall live.
pericope	19	119	145	KOPH.
verse	19	119	145	@@I cried with @9my@7 whole heart; hear me, O LORD: I will keep thy statutes.
verse	19	119	146	I cried unto thee; save me, and I shall keep thy testimonies.
verse	19	119	147	I prevented the dawning of the morning, and cried: I hoped in thy word.
verse	19	119	148	@@Mine eyes prevent the @9night@7 watches, that I might meditate in thy word.
verse	19	119	149	Hear my voice according unto thy lovingkindness: O LORD, quicken me according to thy judgment.
verse	19	119	150	They draw nigh that follow after mischief: they are far from thy law.
verse	19	119	151	@@Thou @9art@7 near, O LORD; and all thy commandments @9are@7 truth.
verse	19	119	152	Concerning thy testimonies, I have known of old that thou hast founded them for ever.
pericope	19	119	153	RESH.
verse	19	119	153	Consider mine affliction, and deliver me: for I do not forget thy law.
verse	19	119	154	Plead my cause, and deliver me: quicken me according to thy word.
verse	19	119	155	@@Salvation @9is@7 far from the wicked: for they seek not thy statutes.
verse	19	119	156	@@Great @9are@7 thy tender mercies, O LORD: quicken me according to thy judgments.
verse	19	119	157	@@Many @9are@7 my persecutors and mine enemies; @9yet@7 do I not decline from thy testimonies.
verse	19	119	158	I beheld the transgressors, and was grieved; because they kept not thy word.
verse	19	119	159	Consider how I love thy precepts: quicken me, O LORD, according to thy lovingkindness.
verse	19	119	160	@@Thy word @9is@7 true @9from@7 the beginning: and every one of thy righteous judgments @9endureth@7 for ever.
pericope	19	119	161	SCHIN.
verse	19	119	161	Princes have persecuted me without a cause: but my heart standeth in awe of thy word.
verse	19	119	162	I rejoice at thy word, as one that findeth great spoil.
verse	19	119	163	@@I hate and abhor lying: @9but@7 thy law do I love.
verse	19	119	164	Seven times a day do I praise thee because of thy righteous judgments.
verse	19	119	165	Great peace have they which love thy law: and nothing shall offend them.
verse	19	119	166	LORD, I have hoped for thy salvation, and done thy commandments.
verse	19	119	167	My soul hath kept thy testimonies; and I love them exceedingly.
verse	19	119	168	@@I have kept thy precepts and thy testimonies: for all my ways @9are@7 before thee.
pericope	19	119	169	TAU.
verse	19	119	169	Let my cry come near before thee, O LORD: give me understanding according to thy word.
verse	19	119	170	Let my supplication come before thee: deliver me according to thy word.
verse	19	119	171	My lips shall utter praise, when thou hast taught me thy statutes.
verse	19	119	172	@@My tongue shall speak of thy word: for all thy commandments @9are@7 righteousness.
verse	19	119	173	Let thine hand help me; for I have chosen thy precepts.
verse	19	119	174	@@I have longed for thy salvation, O LORD; and thy law @9is@7 my delight.
verse	19	119	175	Let my soul live, and it shall praise thee; and let thy judgments help me.
verse	19	119	176	I have gone astray like a lost sheep; seek thy servant; for I do not forget thy commandments.
pericope	19	120	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	120	1	In my distress I cried unto the LORD, and he heard me.
verse	19	120	2	@@Deliver my soul, O LORD, from lying lips, @9and@7 from a deceitful tongue.
verse	19	120	3	What shall be given unto thee? or what shall be done unto thee, thou false tongue?
verse	19	120	4	Sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals of juniper.
verse	19	120	5	@@Woe is me, that I sojourn in Mesech, @9that@7 I dwell in the tents of Kedar!
verse	19	120	6	My soul hath long dwelt with him that hateth peace.
verse	19	120	7	@@I @9am for@7 peace: but when I speak, they @9are@7 for war.
pericope	19	121	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	121	1	I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help.
verse	19	121	2	@@My help @9cometh@7 from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.
verse	19	121	3	He will not suffer thy foot to be moved: he that keepeth thee will not slumber.
verse	19	121	4	Behold, he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep.
verse	19	121	5	@@The LORD @9is@7 thy keeper: the LORD @9is@7 thy shade upon thy right hand.
verse	19	121	6	The sun shall not smite thee by day, nor the moon by night.
verse	19	121	7	The LORD shall preserve thee from all evil: he shall preserve thy soul.
verse	19	121	8	The LORD shall preserve thy going out and thy coming in from this time forth, and even for evermore.
pericope	19	122	1	A Song of degrees of David.
verse	19	122	1	I was glad when they said unto me, Let us go into the house of the LORD.
verse	19	122	2	Our feet shall stand within thy gates, O Jerusalem.
verse	19	122	3	Jerusalem is builded as a city that is compact together:
verse	19	122	4	Whither the tribes go up, the tribes of the LORD, unto the testimony of Israel, to give thanks unto the name of the LORD.
verse	19	122	5	For there are set thrones of judgment, the thrones of the house of David.
verse	19	122	6	Pray for the peace of Jerusalem: they shall prosper that love thee.
verse	19	122	7	@@Peace be within thy walls, @9and@7 prosperity within thy palaces.
verse	19	122	8	@@For my brethren and companions' sakes, I will now say, Peace @9be@7 within thee.
verse	19	122	9	Because of the house of the LORD our God I will seek thy good.
pericope	19	123	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	123	1	Unto thee lift I up mine eyes, O thou that dwellest in the heavens.
verse	19	123	2	@@Behold, as the eyes of servants @9look@7 unto the hand of their masters, @9and@7 as the eyes of a maiden unto the hand of her mistress; so our eyes @9wait@7 upon the LORD our God, until that he have mercy upon us.
verse	19	123	3	Have mercy upon us, O LORD, have mercy upon us: for we are exceedingly filled with contempt.
verse	19	123	4	@@Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scorning of those that are at ease, @9and@7 with the contempt of the proud.
pericope	19	124	1	A Song of degrees of David.
verse	19	124	1	@@If @9it had not been@7 the LORD who was on our side, now may Israel say;
verse	19	124	2	@@If @9it had not been@7 the LORD who was on our side, when men rose up against us:
verse	19	124	3	Then they had swallowed us up quick, when their wrath was kindled against us:
verse	19	124	4	Then the waters had overwhelmed us, the stream had gone over our soul:
verse	19	124	5	Then the proud waters had gone over our soul.
verse	19	124	6	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD, who hath not given us @9as@7 a prey to their teeth.
verse	19	124	7	Our soul is escaped as a bird out of the snare of the fowlers: the snare is broken, and we are escaped.
verse	19	124	8	@@Our help @9is@7 in the name of the LORD, who made heaven and earth.
pericope	19	125	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	125	1	@@They that trust in the LORD @9shall be@7 as mount Zion, @9which@7 cannot be removed, @9but@7 abideth for ever.
verse	19	125	2	@@As the mountains @9are@7 round about Jerusalem, so the LORD @9is@7 round about his people from henceforth even for ever.
verse	19	125	3	For the rod of the wicked shall not rest upon the lot of the righteous; lest the righteous put forth their hands unto iniquity.
verse	19	125	4	@@Do good, O LORD, unto @9those that be@7 good, and @9to them that are@7 upright in their hearts.
verse	19	125	5	@@As for such as turn aside unto their crooked ways, the LORD shall lead them forth with the workers of iniquity: @9but@7 peace @9shall be@7 upon Israel.
pericope	19	126	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	126	1	When the LORD turned again the captivity of Zion, we were like them that dream.
verse	19	126	2	Then was our mouth filled with laughter, and our tongue with singing: then said they among the heathen, The LORD hath done great things for them.
verse	19	126	3	@@The LORD hath done great things for us; @9whereof@7 we are glad.
verse	19	126	4	Turn again our captivity, O LORD, as the streams in the south.
verse	19	126	5	They that sow in tears shall reap in joy.
verse	19	126	6	@@He that goeth forth and weepeth, bearing precious seed, shall doubtless come again with rejoicing, bringing his sheaves @9with him.@7
pericope	19	127	1	A Song of degrees for Solomon.
verse	19	127	1	@@Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it: except the LORD keep the city, the watchman waketh @9but@7 in vain.
verse	19	127	2	@@@9It is@7 vain for you to rise up early, to sit up late, to eat the bread of sorrows: @9for@7 so he giveth his beloved sleep.
verse	19	127	3	@@Lo, children @9are@7 an heritage of the LORD: @9and@7 the fruit of the womb @9is his@7 reward.
verse	19	127	4	@@As arrows @9are@7 in the hand of a mighty man; so @9are@7 children of the youth.
verse	19	127	5	@@Happy @9is@7 the man that hath his quiver full of them: they shall not be ashamed, but they shall speak with the enemies in the gate.
pericope	19	128	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	128	1	@@Blessed @9is@7 every one that feareth the LORD; that walketh in his ways.
verse	19	128	2	@@For thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands: happy @9shalt@7 thou @9be,@7 and @9it shall be@7 well with thee.
verse	19	128	3	@@Thy wife @9shall be@7 as a fruitful vine by the sides of thine house: thy children like olive plants round about thy table.
verse	19	128	4	Behold, that thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the LORD.
verse	19	128	5	The LORD shall bless thee out of Zion: and thou shalt see the good of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.
verse	19	128	6	@@Yea, thou shalt see thy children's children, @9and@7 peace upon Israel.
pericope	19	129	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	129	1	Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth, may Israel now say:
verse	19	129	2	Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth: yet they have not prevailed against me.
verse	19	129	3	The plowers plowed upon my back: they made long their furrows.
verse	19	129	4	@@The LORD @9is@7 righteous: he hath cut asunder the cords of the wicked.
verse	19	129	5	Let them all be confounded and turned back that hate Zion.
verse	19	129	6	@@Let them be as the grass @9upon@7 the housetops, which withereth afore it groweth up:
verse	19	129	7	Wherewith the mower filleth not his hand; nor he that bindeth sheaves his bosom.
verse	19	129	8	@@Neither do they which go by say, The blessing of the LORD @9be@7 upon you: we bless you in the name of the LORD.
pericope	19	130	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	130	1	Out of the depths have I cried unto thee, O LORD.
verse	19	130	2	Lord, hear my voice: let thine ears be attentive to the voice of my supplications.
verse	19	130	3	If thou, LORD, shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, who shall stand?
verse	19	130	4	@@But @9there is@7 forgiveness with thee, that thou mayest be feared.
verse	19	130	5	I wait for the LORD, my soul doth wait, and in his word do I hope.
verse	19	130	6	@@My soul @9waiteth@7 for the Lord more than they that watch for the morning: @9I say, more than@7 they that watch for the morning.
verse	19	130	7	@@Let Israel hope in the LORD: for with the LORD @9there is@7 mercy, and with him @9is@7 plenteous redemption.
verse	19	130	8	And he shall redeem Israel from all his iniquities.
pericope	19	131	1	A Song of degrees of David.
verse	19	131	1	LORD, my heart is not haughty, nor mine eyes lofty: neither do I exercise myself in great matters, or in things too high for me.
verse	19	131	2	@@Surely I have behaved and quieted myself, as a child that is weaned of his mother: my soul @9is@7 even as a weaned child.
verse	19	131	3	Let Israel hope in the LORD from henceforth and for ever.
pericope	19	132	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	132	1	@@LORD, remember David, @9and@7 all his afflictions:
verse	19	132	2	@@How he sware unto the LORD, @9and@7 vowed unto the mighty @9God@7 of Jacob;
verse	19	132	3	Surely I will not come into the tabernacle of my house, nor go up into my bed;
verse	19	132	4	@@I will not give sleep to mine eyes, @9or@7 slumber to mine eyelids,
verse	19	132	5	@@Until I find out a place for the LORD, an habitation for the mighty @9God@7 of Jacob.
verse	19	132	6	Lo, we heard of it at Ephratah: we found it in the fields of the wood.
verse	19	132	7	We will go into his tabernacles: we will worship at his footstool.
verse	19	132	8	Arise, O LORD, into thy rest; thou, and the ark of thy strength.
verse	19	132	9	Let thy priests be clothed with righteousness; and let thy saints shout for joy.
verse	19	132	10	For thy servant David's sake turn not away the face of thine anointed.
verse	19	132	11	@@The LORD hath sworn @9in@7 truth unto David; he will not turn from it; Of the fruit of thy body will I set upon thy throne.
verse	19	132	12	If thy children will keep my covenant and my testimony that I shall teach them, their children shall also sit upon thy throne for evermore.
verse	19	132	13	@@For the LORD hath chosen Zion; he hath desired @9it@7 for his habitation.
verse	19	132	14	@@This @9is@7 my rest for ever: here will I dwell; for I have desired it.
verse	19	132	15	I will abundantly bless her provision: I will satisfy her poor with bread.
verse	19	132	16	I will also clothe her priests with salvation: and her saints shall shout aloud for joy.
verse	19	132	17	There will I make the horn of David to bud: I have ordained a lamp for mine anointed.
verse	19	132	18	His enemies will I clothe with shame: but upon himself shall his crown flourish.
pericope	19	133	1	A Song of degrees of David.
verse	19	133	1	@@Behold, how good and how pleasant @9it is@7 for brethren to dwell together in unity!
verse	19	133	2	@@@9It is@7 like the precious ointment upon the head, that ran down upon the beard, @9even@7 Aaron's beard: that went down to the skirts of his garments;
verse	19	133	3	@@As the dew of Hermon, @9and as the dew@7 that descended upon the mountains of Zion: for there the LORD commanded the blessing, @9even@7 life for evermore.
pericope	19	134	1	A Song of degrees.
verse	19	134	1	@@Behold, bless ye the LORD, all @9ye@7 servants of the LORD, which by night stand in the house of the LORD.
verse	19	134	2	@@Lift up your hands @9in@7 the sanctuary, and bless the LORD.
verse	19	134	3	The LORD that made heaven and earth bless thee out of Zion.
verse	19	135	1	@@Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the name of the LORD; praise @9him,@7 O ye servants of the LORD.
verse	19	135	2	Ye that stand in the house of the LORD, in the courts of the house of our God,
verse	19	135	3	@@Praise the LORD; for the LORD @9is@7 good: sing praises unto his name; for @9it is@7 pleasant.
verse	19	135	4	@@For the LORD hath chosen Jacob unto himself, @9and@7 Israel for his peculiar treasure.
verse	19	135	5	@@For I know that the LORD @9is@7 great, and @9that@7 our Lord @9is@7 above all gods.
verse	19	135	6	@@Whatsoever the LORD pleased, @9that@7 did he in heaven, and in earth, in the seas, and all deep places.
verse	19	135	7	He causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings for the rain; he bringeth the wind out of his treasuries.
verse	19	135	8	Who smote the firstborn of Egypt, both of man and beast.
verse	19	135	9	@@@9Who@7 sent tokens and wonders into the midst of thee, O Egypt, upon Pharaoh, and upon all his servants.
verse	19	135	10	Who smote great nations, and slew mighty kings;
verse	19	135	11	Sihon king of the Amorites, and Og king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms of Canaan:
verse	19	135	12	@@And gave their land @9for@7 an heritage, an heritage unto Israel his people.
verse	19	135	13	@@Thy name, O LORD, @9endureth@7 for ever; @9and@7 thy memorial, O LORD, throughout all generations.
verse	19	135	14	For the LORD will judge his people, and he will repent himself concerning his servants.
verse	19	135	15	@@The idols of the heathen @9are@7 silver and gold, the work of men's hands.
verse	19	135	16	They have mouths, but they speak not; eyes have they, but they see not;
verse	19	135	17	@@They have ears, but they hear not; neither is there @9any@7 breath in their mouths.
verse	19	135	18	@@They that make them are like unto them: @9so is@7 every one that trusteth in them.
verse	19	135	19	Bless the LORD, O house of Israel: bless the LORD, O house of Aaron:
verse	19	135	20	Bless the LORD, O house of Levi: ye that fear the LORD, bless the LORD.
verse	19	135	21	Blessed be the LORD out of Zion, which dwelleth at Jerusalem. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	136	1	@@O give thanks unto the LORD; for @9he is@7 good: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	2	@@O give thanks unto the God of gods: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	3	@@O give thanks to the Lord of lords: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	4	@@To him who alone doeth great wonders: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	5	@@To him that by wisdom made the heavens: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	6	@@To him that stretched out the earth above the waters: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	7	@@To him that made great lights: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	8	@@The sun to rule by day: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	9	@@The moon and stars to rule by night: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	10	@@To him that smote Egypt in their firstborn: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	11	@@And brought out Israel from among them: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	12	@@With a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	13	@@To him which divided the Red sea into parts: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	14	@@And made Israel to pass through the midst of it: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	15	@@But overthrew Pharaoh and his host in the Red sea: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	16	@@To him which led his people through the wilderness: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	17	@@To him which smote great kings: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	18	@@And slew famous kings: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	19	@@Sihon king of the Amorites: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	20	@@And Og the king of Bashan: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	21	@@And gave their land for an heritage: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	22	@@@9Even@7 an heritage unto Israel his servant: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	23	@@Who remembered us in our low estate: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever:
verse	19	136	24	@@And hath redeemed us from our enemies: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	25	@@Who giveth food to all flesh: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	136	26	@@O give thanks unto the God of heaven: for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever.
verse	19	137	1	By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion.
verse	19	137	2	We hanged our harps upon the willows in the midst thereof.
verse	19	137	3	@@For there they that carried us away captive required of us a song; and they that wasted us @9required of us@7 mirth, @9saying,@7 Sing us @9one@7 of the songs of Zion.
verse	19	137	4	How shall we sing the LORD'S song in a strange land?
verse	19	137	5	@@If I forget thee, O Jerusalem, let my right hand forget @9her cunning.@7
verse	19	137	6	If I do not remember thee, let my tongue cleave to the roof of my mouth; if I prefer not Jerusalem above my chief joy.
verse	19	137	7	@@Remember, O LORD, the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem; who said, Rase @9it,@7 rase @9it, even@7 to the foundation thereof.
verse	19	137	8	@@O daughter of Babylon, who art to be destroyed; happy @9shall he be,@7 that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us.
verse	19	137	9	@@Happy @9shall he be,@7 that taketh and dasheth thy little ones against the stones.
pericope	19	138	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	138	1	I will praise thee with my whole heart: before the gods will I sing praise unto thee.
verse	19	138	2	I will worship toward thy holy temple, and praise thy name for thy lovingkindness and for thy truth: for thou hast magnified thy word above all thy name.
verse	19	138	3	@@In the day when I cried thou answeredst me, @9and@7 strengthenedst me @9with@7 strength in my soul.
verse	19	138	4	All the kings of the earth shall praise thee, O LORD, when they hear the words of thy mouth.
verse	19	138	5	@@Yea, they shall sing in the ways of the LORD: for great @9is@7 the glory of the LORD.
verse	19	138	6	@@Though the LORD @9be@7 high, yet hath he respect unto the lowly: but the proud he knoweth afar off.
verse	19	138	7	Though I walk in the midst of trouble, thou wilt revive me: thou shalt stretch forth thine hand against the wrath of mine enemies, and thy right hand shall save me.
verse	19	138	8	@@The LORD will perfect @9that which@7 concerneth me: thy mercy, O LORD, @9endureth@7 for ever: forsake not the works of thine own hands.
pericope	19	139	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	139	1	@@O LORD, thou hast searched me, and known @9me.@7
verse	19	139	2	Thou knowest my downsitting and mine uprising, thou understandest my thought afar off.
verse	19	139	3	@@Thou compassest my path and my lying down, and art acquainted @9with@7 all my ways.
verse	19	139	4	@@For @9there is@7 not a word in my tongue, @9but,@7 lo, O LORD, thou knowest it altogether.
verse	19	139	5	Thou hast beset me behind and before, and laid thine hand upon me.
verse	19	139	6	@@@9Such@7 knowledge @9is@7 too wonderful for me; it is high, I cannot @9attain@7 unto it.
verse	19	139	7	Whither shall I go from thy spirit? or whither shall I flee from thy presence?
verse	19	139	8	@@If I ascend up into heaven, thou @9art@7 there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou @9art there.@7
verse	19	139	9	@@@9If@7 I take the wings of the morning, @9and@7 dwell in the uttermost parts of the sea;
verse	19	139	10	Even there shall thy hand lead me, and thy right hand shall hold me.
verse	19	139	11	If I say, Surely the darkness shall cover me; even the night shall be light about me.
verse	19	139	12	@@Yea, the darkness hideth not from thee; but the night shineth as the day: the darkness and the light @9are@7 both alike @9to thee.@7
verse	19	139	13	For thou hast possessed my reins: thou hast covered me in my mother's womb.
verse	19	139	14	@@I will praise thee; for I am fearfully @9and@7 wonderfully made: marvellous @9are@7 thy works; and @9that@7 my soul knoweth right well.
verse	19	139	15	@@My substance was not hid from thee, when I was made in secret, @9and@7 curiously wrought in the lowest parts of the earth.
verse	19	139	16	@@Thine eyes did see my substance, yet being unperfect; and in thy book all @9my members@7 were written, @9which@7 in continuance were fashioned, when @9as yet there was@7 none of them.
verse	19	139	17	How precious also are thy thoughts unto me, O God! how great is the sum of them!
verse	19	139	18	@@@9If@7 I should count them, they are more in number than the sand: when I awake, I am still with thee.
verse	19	139	19	Surely thou wilt slay the wicked, O God: depart from me therefore, ye bloody men.
verse	19	139	20	@@For they speak against thee wickedly, @9and@7 thine enemies take @9thy name@7 in vain.
verse	19	139	21	Do not I hate them, O LORD, that hate thee? and am not I grieved with those that rise up against thee?
verse	19	139	22	I hate them with perfect hatred: I count them mine enemies.
verse	19	139	23	Search me, O God, and know my heart: try me, and know my thoughts:
verse	19	139	24	@@And see if @9there be any@7 wicked way in me, and lead me in the way everlasting.
pericope	19	140	1	To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.
verse	19	140	1	Deliver me, O LORD, from the evil man: preserve me from the violent man;
verse	19	140	2	@@Which imagine mischiefs in @9their@7 heart; continually are they gathered together @9for@7 war.
verse	19	140	3	@@They have sharpened their tongues like a serpent; adders' poison @9is@7 under their lips. Selah.
verse	19	140	4	Keep me, O LORD, from the hands of the wicked; preserve me from the violent man; who have purposed to overthrow my goings.
verse	19	140	5	The proud have hid a snare for me, and cords; they have spread a net by the wayside; they have set gins for me. Selah.
verse	19	140	6	@@I said unto the LORD, Thou @9art@7 my God: hear the voice of my supplications, O LORD.
verse	19	140	7	O GOD the Lord, the strength of my salvation, thou hast covered my head in the day of battle.
verse	19	140	8	@@Grant not, O LORD, the desires of the wicked: further not his wicked device; @9lest@7 they exalt themselves. Selah.
verse	19	140	9	@@@9As for@7 the head of those that compass me about, let the mischief of their own lips cover them.
verse	19	140	10	Let burning coals fall upon them: let them be cast into the fire; into deep pits, that they rise not up again.
verse	19	140	11	@@Let not an evil speaker be established in the earth: evil shall hunt the violent man to overthrow @9him.@7
verse	19	140	12	@@I know that the LORD will maintain the cause of the afflicted, @9and@7 the right of the poor.
verse	19	140	13	Surely the righteous shall give thanks unto thy name: the upright shall dwell in thy presence.
pericope	19	141	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	141	1	LORD, I cry unto thee: make haste unto me; give ear unto my voice, when I cry unto thee.
verse	19	141	2	@@Let my prayer be set forth before thee @9as@7 incense; @9and@7 the lifting up of my hands @9as@7 the evening sacrifice.
verse	19	141	3	Set a watch, O LORD, before my mouth; keep the door of my lips.
verse	19	141	4	@@Incline not my heart to @9any@7 evil thing, to practise wicked works with men that work iniquity: and let me not eat of their dainties.
verse	19	141	5	@@Let the righteous smite me; @9it shall be@7 a kindness: and let him reprove me; @9it shall be@7 an excellent oil, @9which@7 shall not break my head: for yet my prayer also @9shall be@7 in their calamities.
verse	19	141	6	When their judges are overthrown in stony places, they shall hear my words; for they are sweet.
verse	19	141	7	@@Our bones are scattered at the grave's mouth, as when one cutteth and cleaveth @9wood@7 upon the earth.
verse	19	141	8	@@But mine eyes @9are@7 unto thee, O GOD the Lord: in thee is my trust; leave not my soul destitute.
verse	19	141	9	@@Keep me from the snares @9which@7 they have laid for me, and the gins of the workers of iniquity.
verse	19	141	10	Let the wicked fall into their own nets, whilst that I withal escape.
pericope	19	142	1	Maschil of David; A Prayer when he was in the cave.
verse	19	142	1	I cried unto the LORD with my voice; with my voice unto the LORD did I make my supplication.
verse	19	142	2	I poured out my complaint before him; I shewed before him my trouble.
verse	19	142	3	When my spirit was overwhelmed within me, then thou knewest my path. In the way wherein I walked have they privily laid a snare for me.
verse	19	142	4	@@I looked on @9my@7 right hand, and beheld, but @9there was@7 no man that would know me: refuge failed me; no man cared for my soul.
verse	19	142	5	@@I cried unto thee, O LORD: I said, Thou @9art@7 my refuge @9and@7 my portion in the land of the living.
verse	19	142	6	Attend unto my cry; for I am brought very low: deliver me from my persecutors; for they are stronger than I.
verse	19	142	7	Bring my soul out of prison, that I may praise thy name: the righteous shall compass me about; for thou shalt deal bountifully with me.
pericope	19	143	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	143	1	@@Hear my prayer, O LORD, give ear to my supplications: in thy faithfulness answer me, @9and@7 in thy righteousness.
verse	19	143	2	And enter not into judgment with thy servant: for in thy sight shall no man living be justified.
verse	19	143	3	For the enemy hath persecuted my soul; he hath smitten my life down to the ground; he hath made me to dwell in darkness, as those that have been long dead.
verse	19	143	4	Therefore is my spirit overwhelmed within me; my heart within me is desolate.
verse	19	143	5	I remember the days of old; I meditate on all thy works; I muse on the work of thy hands.
verse	19	143	6	@@I stretch forth my hands unto thee: my soul @9thirsteth@7 after thee, as a thirsty land. Selah.
verse	19	143	7	Hear me speedily, O LORD: my spirit faileth: hide not thy face from me, lest I be like unto them that go down into the pit.
verse	19	143	8	Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.
verse	19	143	9	Deliver me, O LORD, from mine enemies: I flee unto thee to hide me.
verse	19	143	10	@@Teach me to do thy will; for thou @9art@7 my God: thy spirit @9is@7 good; lead me into the land of uprightness.
verse	19	143	11	Quicken me, O LORD, for thy name's sake: for thy righteousness' sake bring my soul out of trouble.
verse	19	143	12	@@And of thy mercy cut off mine enemies, and destroy all them that afflict my soul: for I @9am@7 thy servant.
pericope	19	144	1	A Psalm of David.
verse	19	144	1	@@Blessed @9be@7 the LORD my strength, which teacheth my hands to war, @9and@7 my fingers to fight:
verse	19	144	2	@@My goodness, and my fortress; my high tower, and my deliverer; my shield, and @9he@7 in whom I trust; who subdueth my people under me.
verse	19	144	3	@@LORD, what @9is@7 man, that thou takest knowledge of him! @9or@7 the son of man, that thou makest account of him!
verse	19	144	4	@@Man is like to vanity: his days @9are@7 as a shadow that passeth away.
verse	19	144	5	Bow thy heavens, O LORD, and come down: touch the mountains, and they shall smoke.
verse	19	144	6	Cast forth lightning, and scatter them: shoot out thine arrows, and destroy them.
verse	19	144	7	Send thine hand from above; rid me, and deliver me out of great waters, from the hand of strange children;
verse	19	144	8	@@Whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand @9is@7 a right hand of falsehood.
verse	19	144	9	@@I will sing a new song unto thee, O God: upon a psaltery @9and@7 an instrument of ten strings will I sing praises unto thee.
verse	19	144	10	@@@9It is he@7 that giveth salvation unto kings: who delivereth David his servant from the hurtful sword.
verse	19	144	11	@@Rid me, and deliver me from the hand of strange children, whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand @9is@7 a right hand of falsehood:
verse	19	144	12	@@That our sons @9may be@7 as plants grown up in their youth; @9that@7 our daughters @9may be@7 as corner stones, polished @9after@7 the similitude of a palace:
verse	19	144	13	@@@9That@7 our garners @9may be@7 full, affording all manner of store: @9that@7 our sheep may bring forth thousands and ten thousands in our streets:
verse	19	144	14	@@@9That@7 our oxen @9may be@7 strong to labour; @9that there be@7 no breaking in, nor going out; that @9there be@7 no complaining in our streets.
verse	19	144	15	@@Happy @9is that@7 people, that is in such a case: @9yea,@7 happy @9is that@7 people, whose God @9is@7 the LORD.
pericope	19	145	1	David's Psalm of praise.
verse	19	145	1	I will extol thee, my God, O king; and I will bless thy name for ever and ever.
verse	19	145	2	Every day will I bless thee; and I will praise thy name for ever and ever.
verse	19	145	3	@@Great @9is@7 the LORD, and greatly to be praised; and his greatness @9is@7 unsearchable.
verse	19	145	4	One generation shall praise thy works to another, and shall declare thy mighty acts.
verse	19	145	5	I will speak of the glorious honour of thy majesty, and of thy wondrous works.
verse	19	145	6	@@And @9men@7 shall speak of the might of thy terrible acts: and I will declare thy greatness.
verse	19	145	7	They shall abundantly utter the memory of thy great goodness, and shall sing of thy righteousness.
verse	19	145	8	@@The LORD @9is@7 gracious, and full of compassion; slow to anger, and of great mercy.
verse	19	145	9	@@The LORD @9is@7 good to all: and his tender mercies @9are@7 over all his works.
verse	19	145	10	All thy works shall praise thee, O LORD; and thy saints shall bless thee.
verse	19	145	11	They shall speak of the glory of thy kingdom, and talk of thy power;
verse	19	145	12	To make known to the sons of men his mighty acts, and the glorious majesty of his kingdom.
verse	19	145	13	@@Thy kingdom @9is@7 an everlasting kingdom, and thy dominion @9endureth@7 throughout all generations.
verse	19	145	14	@@The LORD upholdeth all that fall, and raiseth up all @9those that be@7 bowed down.
verse	19	145	15	The eyes of all wait upon thee; and thou givest them their meat in due season.
verse	19	145	16	Thou openest thine hand, and satisfiest the desire of every living thing.
verse	19	145	17	@@The LORD @9is@7 righteous in all his ways, and holy in all his works.
verse	19	145	18	@@The LORD @9is@7 nigh unto all them that call upon him, to all that call upon him in truth.
verse	19	145	19	He will fulfil the desire of them that fear him: he also will hear their cry, and will save them.
verse	19	145	20	The LORD preserveth all them that love him: but all the wicked will he destroy.
verse	19	145	21	My mouth shall speak the praise of the LORD: and let all flesh bless his holy name for ever and ever.
verse	19	146	1	Praise ye the LORD. Praise the LORD, O my soul.
verse	19	146	2	While I live will I praise the LORD: I will sing praises unto my God while I have any being.
verse	19	146	3	@@Put not your trust in princes, @9nor@7 in the son of man, in whom @9there is@7 no help.
verse	19	146	4	His breath goeth forth, he returneth to his earth; in that very day his thoughts perish.
verse	19	146	5	@@Happy @9is he@7 that @9hath@7 the God of Jacob for his help, whose hope @9is@7 in the LORD his God:
verse	19	146	6	@@Which made heaven, and earth, the sea, and all that therein @9is:@7 which keepeth truth for ever:
verse	19	146	7	Which executeth judgment for the oppressed: which giveth food to the hungry. The LORD looseth the prisoners:
verse	19	146	8	@@The LORD openeth @9the eyes of@7 the blind: the LORD raiseth them that are bowed down: the LORD loveth the righteous:
verse	19	146	9	The LORD preserveth the strangers; he relieveth the fatherless and widow: but the way of the wicked he turneth upside down.
verse	19	146	10	@@The LORD shall reign for ever, @9even@7 thy God, O Zion, unto all generations. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	147	1	@@Praise ye the LORD: for @9it is@7 good to sing praises unto our God; for @9it is@7 pleasant; @9and@7 praise is comely.
verse	19	147	2	The LORD doth build up Jerusalem: he gathereth together the outcasts of Israel.
verse	19	147	3	He healeth the broken in heart, and bindeth up their wounds.
verse	19	147	4	@@He telleth the number of the stars; he calleth them all by @9their@7 names.
verse	19	147	5	@@Great @9is@7 our Lord, and of great power: his understanding @9is@7 infinite.
verse	19	147	6	The LORD lifteth up the meek: he casteth the wicked down to the ground.
verse	19	147	7	Sing unto the LORD with thanksgiving; sing praise upon the harp unto our God:
verse	19	147	8	Who covereth the heaven with clouds, who prepareth rain for the earth, who maketh grass to grow upon the mountains.
verse	19	147	9	@@He giveth to the beast his food, @9and@7 to the young ravens which cry.
verse	19	147	10	He delighteth not in the strength of the horse: he taketh not pleasure in the legs of a man.
verse	19	147	11	The LORD taketh pleasure in them that fear him, in those that hope in his mercy.
verse	19	147	12	Praise the LORD, O Jerusalem; praise thy God, O Zion.
verse	19	147	13	For he hath strengthened the bars of thy gates; he hath blessed thy children within thee.
verse	19	147	14	@@He maketh peace @9in@7 thy borders, @9and@7 filleth thee with the finest of the wheat.
verse	19	147	15	@@He sendeth forth his commandment @9upon@7 earth: his word runneth very swiftly.
verse	19	147	16	He giveth snow like wool: he scattereth the hoar frost like ashes.
verse	19	147	17	He casteth forth his ice like morsels: who can stand before his cold?
verse	19	147	18	@@He sendeth out his word, and melteth them: he causeth his wind to blow, @9and@7 the waters flow.
verse	19	147	19	He sheweth his word unto Jacob, his statutes and his judgments unto Israel.
verse	19	147	20	@@He hath not dealt so with any nation: and @9as for his@7 judgments, they have not known them. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	148	1	Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the LORD from the heavens: praise him in the heights.
verse	19	148	2	Praise ye him, all his angels: praise ye him, all his hosts.
verse	19	148	3	Praise ye him, sun and moon: praise him, all ye stars of light.
verse	19	148	4	@@Praise him, ye heavens of heavens, and ye waters that @9be@7 above the heavens.
verse	19	148	5	Let them praise the name of the LORD: for he commanded, and they were created.
verse	19	148	6	He hath also stablished them for ever and ever: he hath made a decree which shall not pass.
verse	19	148	7	Praise the LORD from the earth, ye dragons, and all deeps:
verse	19	148	8	Fire, and hail; snow, and vapours; stormy wind fulfilling his word:
verse	19	148	9	Mountains, and all hills; fruitful trees, and all cedars:
verse	19	148	10	Beasts, and all cattle; creeping things, and flying fowl:
verse	19	148	11	Kings of the earth, and all people; princes, and all judges of the earth:
verse	19	148	12	Both young men, and maidens; old men, and children:
verse	19	148	13	@@Let them praise the name of the LORD: for his name alone is excellent; his glory @9is@7 above the earth and heaven.
verse	19	148	14	@@He also exalteth the horn of his people, the praise of all his saints; @9even@7 of the children of Israel, a people near unto him. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	149	1	@@Praise ye the LORD. Sing unto the LORD a new song, @9and@7 his praise in the congregation of saints.
verse	19	149	2	Let Israel rejoice in him that made him: let the children of Zion be joyful in their King.
verse	19	149	3	Let them praise his name in the dance: let them sing praises unto him with the timbrel and harp.
verse	19	149	4	For the LORD taketh pleasure in his people: he will beautify the meek with salvation.
verse	19	149	5	Let the saints be joyful in glory: let them sing aloud upon their beds.
verse	19	149	6	@@@9Let@7 the high @9praises@7 of God @9be@7 in their mouth, and a twoedged sword in their hand;
verse	19	149	7	@@To execute vengeance upon the heathen, @9and@7 punishments upon the people;
verse	19	149	8	To bind their kings with chains, and their nobles with fetters of iron;
verse	19	149	9	To execute upon them the judgment written: this honour have all his saints. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	19	150	1	Praise ye the LORD. Praise God in his sanctuary: praise him in the firmament of his power.
verse	19	150	2	Praise him for his mighty acts: praise him according to his excellent greatness.
verse	19	150	3	Praise him with the sound of the trumpet: praise him with the psaltery and harp.
verse	19	150	4	Praise him with the timbrel and dance: praise him with stringed instruments and organs.
verse	19	150	5	Praise him upon the loud cymbals: praise him upon the high sounding cymbals.
verse	19	150	6	Let every thing that hath breath praise the LORD. Praise ye the LORD.
verse	20	1	1	The proverbs of Solomon the son of David, king of Israel;
verse	20	1	2	To know wisdom and instruction; to perceive the words of understanding;
verse	20	1	3	To receive the instruction of wisdom, justice, and judgment, and equity;
verse	20	1	4	To give subtilty to the simple, to the young man knowledge and discretion.
verse	20	1	5	@@A wise @9man@7 will hear, and will increase learning; and a man of understanding shall attain unto wise counsels:
verse	20	1	6	To understand a proverb, and the interpretation; the words of the wise, and their dark sayings.
verse	20	1	7	@@The fear of the LORD @9is@7 the beginning of knowledge: @9but@7 fools despise wisdom and instruction.
verse	20	1	8	My son, hear the instruction of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother:
verse	20	1	9	@@For they @9shall be@7 an ornament of grace unto thy head, and chains about thy neck.
verse	20	1	10	My son, if sinners entice thee, consent thou not.
verse	20	1	11	If they say, Come with us, let us lay wait for blood, let us lurk privily for the innocent without cause:
verse	20	1	12	Let us swallow them up alive as the grave; and whole, as those that go down into the pit:
verse	20	1	13	We shall find all precious substance, we shall fill our houses with spoil:
verse	20	1	14	Cast in thy lot among us; let us all have one purse:
verse	20	1	15	My son, walk not thou in the way with them; refrain thy foot from their path:
verse	20	1	16	For their feet run to evil, and make haste to shed blood.
verse	20	1	17	Surely in vain the net is spread in the sight of any bird.
verse	20	1	18	@@And they lay wait for their @9own@7 blood; they lurk privily for their @9own@7 lives.
verse	20	1	19	@@So @9are@7 the ways of every one that is greedy of gain; @9which@7 taketh away the life of the owners thereof.
verse	20	1	20	Wisdom crieth without; she uttereth her voice in the streets:
verse	20	1	21	@@She crieth in the chief place of concourse, in the openings of the gates: in the city she uttereth her words, @9saying, @7
verse	20	1	22	How long, ye simple ones, will ye love simplicity? and the scorners delight in their scorning, and fools hate knowledge?
verse	20	1	23	Turn you at my reproof: behold, I will pour out my spirit unto you, I will make known my words unto you.
verse	20	1	24	Because I have called, and ye refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no man regarded;
verse	20	1	25	But ye have set at nought all my counsel, and would none of my reproof:
verse	20	1	26	I also will laugh at your calamity; I will mock when your fear cometh;
verse	20	1	27	When your fear cometh as desolation, and your destruction cometh as a whirlwind; when distress and anguish cometh upon you.
verse	20	1	28	Then shall they call upon me, but I will not answer; they shall seek me early, but they shall not find me:
verse	20	1	29	For that they hated knowledge, and did not choose the fear of the LORD:
verse	20	1	30	They would none of my counsel: they despised all my reproof.
verse	20	1	31	Therefore shall they eat of the fruit of their own way, and be filled with their own devices.
verse	20	1	32	For the turning away of the simple shall slay them, and the prosperity of fools shall destroy them.
verse	20	1	33	But whoso hearkeneth unto me shall dwell safely, and shall be quiet from fear of evil.
verse	20	2	1	My son, if thou wilt receive my words, and hide my commandments with thee;
verse	20	2	2	@@So that thou incline thine ear unto wisdom, @9and@7 apply thine heart to understanding;
verse	20	2	3	@@Yea, if thou criest after knowledge, @9and@7 liftest up thy voice for understanding;
verse	20	2	4	@@If thou seekest her as silver, and searchest for her as @9for@7 hid treasures;
verse	20	2	5	Then shalt thou understand the fear of the LORD, and find the knowledge of God.
verse	20	2	6	@@For the LORD giveth wisdom: out of his mouth @9cometh@7 knowledge and understanding.
verse	20	2	7	@@He layeth up sound wisdom for the righteous: @9he is@7 a buckler to them that walk uprightly.
verse	20	2	8	He keepeth the paths of judgment, and preserveth the way of his saints.
verse	20	2	9	@@Then shalt thou understand righteousness, and judgment, and equity; @9yea,@7 every good path.
verse	20	2	10	When wisdom entereth into thine heart, and knowledge is pleasant unto thy soul;
verse	20	2	11	Discretion shall preserve thee, understanding shall keep thee:
verse	20	2	12	@@To deliver thee from the way of the evil @9man,@7 from the man that speaketh froward things;
verse	20	2	13	Who leave the paths of uprightness, to walk in the ways of darkness;
verse	20	2	14	@@Who rejoice to do evil, @9and@7 delight in the frowardness of the wicked;
verse	20	2	15	@@Whose ways @9are@7 crooked, and @9they@7 froward in their paths:
verse	20	2	16	@@To deliver thee from the strange woman, @9even@7 from the stranger @9which@7 flattereth with her words;
verse	20	2	17	Which forsaketh the guide of her youth, and forgetteth the covenant of her God.
verse	20	2	18	For her house inclineth unto death, and her paths unto the dead.
verse	20	2	19	None that go unto her return again, neither take they hold of the paths of life.
verse	20	2	20	@@That thou mayest walk in the way of good @9men,@7 and keep the paths of the righteous.
verse	20	2	21	For the upright shall dwell in the land, and the perfect shall remain in it.
verse	20	2	22	But the wicked shall be cut off from the earth, and the transgressors shall be rooted out of it.
verse	20	3	1	My son, forget not my law; but let thine heart keep my commandments:
verse	20	3	2	For length of days, and long life, and peace, shall they add to thee.
verse	20	3	3	Let not mercy and truth forsake thee: bind them about thy neck; write them upon the table of thine heart:
verse	20	3	4	So shalt thou find favour and good understanding in the sight of God and man.
verse	20	3	5	Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.
verse	20	3	6	In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.
verse	20	3	7	Be not wise in thine own eyes: fear the LORD, and depart from evil.
verse	20	3	8	It shall be health to thy navel, and marrow to thy bones.
verse	20	3	9	Honour the LORD with thy substance, and with the firstfruits of all thine increase:
verse	20	3	10	So shall thy barns be filled with plenty, and thy presses shall burst out with new wine.
verse	20	3	11	My son, despise not the chastening of the LORD; neither be weary of his correction:
verse	20	3	12	@@For whom the LORD loveth he correcteth; even as a father the son @9in whom@7 he delighteth.
verse	20	3	13	@@Happy @9is@7 the man @9that@7 findeth wisdom, and the man @9that@7 getteth understanding.
verse	20	3	14	@@For the merchandise of it @9is@7 better than the merchandise of silver, and the gain thereof than fine gold.
verse	20	3	15	@@She @9is@7 more precious than rubies: and all the things thou canst desire are not to be compared unto her.
verse	20	3	16	@@Length of days @9is@7 in her right hand; @9and@7 in her left hand riches and honour.
verse	20	3	17	@@Her ways @9are@7 ways of pleasantness, and all her paths @9are@7 peace.
verse	20	3	18	@@She @9is@7 a tree of life to them that lay hold upon her: and happy @9is every one@7 that retaineth her.
verse	20	3	19	The LORD by wisdom hath founded the earth; by understanding hath he established the heavens.
verse	20	3	20	By his knowledge the depths are broken up, and the clouds drop down the dew.
verse	20	3	21	My son, let not them depart from thine eyes: keep sound wisdom and discretion:
verse	20	3	22	So shall they be life unto thy soul, and grace to thy neck.
verse	20	3	23	Then shalt thou walk in thy way safely, and thy foot shall not stumble.
verse	20	3	24	When thou liest down, thou shalt not be afraid: yea, thou shalt lie down, and thy sleep shall be sweet.
verse	20	3	25	Be not afraid of sudden fear, neither of the desolation of the wicked, when it cometh.
verse	20	3	26	For the LORD shall be thy confidence, and shall keep thy foot from being taken.
verse	20	3	27	@@Withhold not good from them to whom it is due, when it is in the power of thine hand to do @9it. @7
verse	20	3	28	Say not unto thy neighbour, Go, and come again, and to morrow I will give; when thou hast it by thee.
verse	20	3	29	Devise not evil against thy neighbour, seeing he dwelleth securely by thee.
verse	20	3	30	Strive not with a man without cause, if he have done thee no harm.
verse	20	3	31	Envy thou not the oppressor, and choose none of his ways.
verse	20	3	32	@@For the froward @9is@7 abomination to the LORD: but his secret @9is@7 with the righteous.
verse	20	3	33	@@The curse of the LORD @9is@7 in the house of the wicked: but he blesseth the habitation of the just.
verse	20	3	34	Surely he scorneth the scorners: but he giveth grace unto the lowly.
verse	20	3	35	The wise shall inherit glory: but shame shall be the promotion of fools.
verse	20	4	1	Hear, ye children, the instruction of a father, and attend to know understanding.
verse	20	4	2	For I give you good doctrine, forsake ye not my law.
verse	20	4	3	@@For I was my father's son, tender and only @9beloved@7 in the sight of my mother.
verse	20	4	4	He taught me also, and said unto me, Let thine heart retain my words: keep my commandments, and live.
verse	20	4	5	@@Get wisdom, get understanding: forget @9it@7 not; neither decline from the words of my mouth.
verse	20	4	6	Forsake her not, and she shall preserve thee: love her, and she shall keep thee.
verse	20	4	7	@@Wisdom @9is@7 the principal thing; @9therefore@7 get wisdom: and with all thy getting get understanding.
verse	20	4	8	Exalt her, and she shall promote thee: she shall bring thee to honour, when thou dost embrace her.
verse	20	4	9	She shall give to thine head an ornament of grace: a crown of glory shall she deliver to thee.
verse	20	4	10	Hear, O my son, and receive my sayings; and the years of thy life shall be many.
verse	20	4	11	I have taught thee in the way of wisdom; I have led thee in right paths.
verse	20	4	12	When thou goest, thy steps shall not be straitened; and when thou runnest, thou shalt not stumble.
verse	20	4	13	@@Take fast hold of instruction; let @9her@7 not go: keep her; for she @9is@7 thy life.
verse	20	4	14	@@Enter not into the path of the wicked, and go not in the way of evil @9men. @7
verse	20	4	15	Avoid it, pass not by it, turn from it, and pass away.
verse	20	4	16	@@For they sleep not, except they have done mischief; and their sleep is taken away, unless they cause @9some@7 to fall.
verse	20	4	17	For they eat the bread of wickedness, and drink the wine of violence.
verse	20	4	18	@@But the path of the just @9is@7 as the shining light, that shineth more and more unto the perfect day.
verse	20	4	19	@@The way of the wicked @9is@7 as darkness: they know not at what they stumble.
verse	20	4	20	My son, attend to my words; incline thine ear unto my sayings.
verse	20	4	21	Let them not depart from thine eyes; keep them in the midst of thine heart.
verse	20	4	22	@@For they @9are@7 life unto those that find them, and health to all their flesh.
verse	20	4	23	@@Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it @9are@7 the issues of life.
verse	20	4	24	Put away from thee a froward mouth, and perverse lips put far from thee.
verse	20	4	25	Let thine eyes look right on, and let thine eyelids look straight before thee.
verse	20	4	26	Ponder the path of thy feet, and let all thy ways be established.
verse	20	4	27	Turn not to the right hand nor to the left: remove thy foot from evil.
verse	20	5	1	@@My son, attend unto my wisdom, @9and@7 bow thine ear to my understanding:
verse	20	5	2	@@That thou mayest regard discretion, and @9that@7 thy lips may keep knowledge.
verse	20	5	3	@@For the lips of a strange woman drop @9as@7 an honeycomb, and her mouth @9is@7 smoother than oil:
verse	20	5	4	But her end is bitter as wormwood, sharp as a twoedged sword.
verse	20	5	5	Her feet go down to death; her steps take hold on hell.
verse	20	5	6	@@Lest thou shouldest ponder the path of life, her ways are moveable, @9that@7 thou canst not know @9them. @7
verse	20	5	7	Hear me now therefore, O ye children, and depart not from the words of my mouth.
verse	20	5	8	Remove thy way far from her, and come not nigh the door of her house:
verse	20	5	9	Lest thou give thine honour unto others, and thy years unto the cruel:
verse	20	5	10	@@Lest strangers be filled with thy wealth; and thy labours @9be@7 in the house of a stranger;
verse	20	5	11	And thou mourn at the last, when thy flesh and thy body are consumed,
verse	20	5	12	And say, How have I hated instruction, and my heart despised reproof;
verse	20	5	13	And have not obeyed the voice of my teachers, nor inclined mine ear to them that instructed me!
verse	20	5	14	I was almost in all evil in the midst of the congregation and assembly.
verse	20	5	15	Drink waters out of thine own cistern, and running waters out of thine own well.
verse	20	5	16	@@Let thy fountains be dispersed abroad, @9and@7 rivers of waters in the streets.
verse	20	5	17	Let them be only thine own, and not strangers' with thee.
verse	20	5	18	Let thy fountain be blessed: and rejoice with the wife of thy youth.
verse	20	5	19	@@@9Let her be as@7 the loving hind and pleasant roe; let her breasts satisfy thee at all times; and be thou ravished always with her love.
verse	20	5	20	And why wilt thou, my son, be ravished with a strange woman, and embrace the bosom of a stranger?
verse	20	5	21	@@For the ways of man @9are@7 before the eyes of the LORD, and he pondereth all his goings.
verse	20	5	22	His own iniquities shall take the wicked himself, and he shall be holden with the cords of his sins.
verse	20	5	23	He shall die without instruction; and in the greatness of his folly he shall go astray.
verse	20	6	1	@@My son, if thou be surety for thy friend, @9if@7 thou hast stricken thy hand with a stranger,
verse	20	6	2	Thou art snared with the words of thy mouth, thou art taken with the words of thy mouth.
verse	20	6	3	Do this now, my son, deliver thyself, when thou art come into the hand of thy friend; go, humble thyself, and make sure thy friend.
verse	20	6	4	Give not sleep to thine eyes, nor slumber to thine eyelids.
verse	20	6	5	@@Deliver thyself as a roe from the hand @9of the hunter,@7 and as a bird from the hand of the fowler.
verse	20	6	6	Go to the ant, thou sluggard; consider her ways, and be wise:
verse	20	6	7	Which having no guide, overseer, or ruler,
verse	20	6	8	@@Provideth her meat in the summer, @9and@7 gathereth her food in the harvest.
verse	20	6	9	How long wilt thou sleep, O sluggard? when wilt thou arise out of thy sleep?
verse	20	6	10	@@@9Yet@7 a little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to sleep:
verse	20	6	11	So shall thy poverty come as one that travelleth, and thy want as an armed man.
verse	20	6	12	A naughty person, a wicked man, walketh with a froward mouth.
verse	20	6	13	He winketh with his eyes, he speaketh with his feet, he teacheth with his fingers;
verse	20	6	14	@@Frowardness @9is@7 in his heart, he deviseth mischief continually; he soweth discord.
verse	20	6	15	Therefore shall his calamity come suddenly; suddenly shall he be broken without remedy.
verse	20	6	16	@@These six @9things@7 doth the LORD hate: yea, seven @9are@7 an abomination unto him:
verse	20	6	17	A proud look, a lying tongue, and hands that shed innocent blood,
verse	20	6	18	An heart that deviseth wicked imaginations, feet that be swift in running to mischief,
verse	20	6	19	@@A false witness @9that@7 speaketh lies, and he that soweth discord among brethren.
verse	20	6	20	My son, keep thy father's commandment, and forsake not the law of thy mother:
verse	20	6	21	@@Bind them continually upon thine heart, @9and@7 tie them about thy neck.
verse	20	6	22	@@When thou goest, it shall lead thee; when thou sleepest, it shall keep thee; and @9when@7 thou awakest, it shall talk with thee.
verse	20	6	23	@@For the commandment @9is@7 a lamp; and the law @9is@7 light; and reproofs of instruction @9are@7 the way of life:
verse	20	6	24	To keep thee from the evil woman, from the flattery of the tongue of a strange woman.
verse	20	6	25	Lust not after her beauty in thine heart; neither let her take thee with her eyelids.
verse	20	6	26	@@For by means of a whorish woman @9a man is brought@7 to a piece of bread: and the adulteress will hunt for the precious life.
verse	20	6	27	Can a man take fire in his bosom, and his clothes not be burned?
verse	20	6	28	Can one go upon hot coals, and his feet not be burned?
verse	20	6	29	So he that goeth in to his neighbour's wife; whosoever toucheth her shall not be innocent.
verse	20	6	30	@@@9Men@7 do not despise a thief, if he steal to satisfy his soul when he is hungry;
verse	20	6	31	@@But @9if@7 he be found, he shall restore sevenfold; he shall give all the substance of his house.
verse	20	6	32	@@@9But@7 whoso committeth adultery with a woman lacketh understanding: he @9that@7 doeth it destroyeth his own soul.
verse	20	6	33	A wound and dishonour shall he get; and his reproach shall not be wiped away.
verse	20	6	34	@@For jealousy @9is@7 the rage of a man: therefore he will not spare in the day of vengeance.
verse	20	6	35	He will not regard any ransom; neither will he rest content, though thou givest many gifts.
verse	20	7	1	My son, keep my words, and lay up my commandments with thee.
verse	20	7	2	Keep my commandments, and live; and my law as the apple of thine eye.
verse	20	7	3	Bind them upon thy fingers, write them upon the table of thine heart.
verse	20	7	4	@@Say unto wisdom, Thou @9art@7 my sister; and call understanding @9thy@7 kinswoman:
verse	20	7	5	@@That they may keep thee from the strange woman, from the stranger @9which@7 flattereth with her words.
verse	20	7	6	For at the window of my house I looked through my casement,
verse	20	7	7	And beheld among the simple ones, I discerned among the youths, a young man void of understanding,
verse	20	7	8	Passing through the street near her corner; and he went the way to her house,
verse	20	7	9	In the twilight, in the evening, in the black and dark night:
verse	20	7	10	@@And, behold, there met him a woman @9with@7 the attire of an harlot, and subtil of heart.
verse	20	7	11	@@(She @9is@7 loud and stubborn; her feet abide not in her house:
verse	20	7	12	@@Now @9is she@7 without, now in the streets, and lieth in wait at every corner.)
verse	20	7	13	@@So she caught him, and kissed him, @9and@7 with an impudent face said unto him,
verse	20	7	14	@@@9I have@7 peace offerings with me; this day have I payed my vows.
verse	20	7	15	Therefore came I forth to meet thee, diligently to seek thy face, and I have found thee.
verse	20	7	16	@@I have decked my bed with coverings of tapestry, with carved @9works,@7 with fine linen of Egypt.
verse	20	7	17	I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.
verse	20	7	18	Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning: let us solace ourselves with loves.
verse	20	7	19	@@For the goodman @9is@7 not at home, he is gone a long journey:
verse	20	7	20	@@He hath taken a bag of money with him, @9and@7 will come home at the day appointed.
verse	20	7	21	With her much fair speech she caused him to yield, with the flattering of her lips she forced him.
verse	20	7	22	He goeth after her straightway, as an ox goeth to the slaughter, or as a fool to the correction of the stocks;
verse	20	7	23	@@Till a dart strike through his liver; as a bird hasteth to the snare, and knoweth not that it @9is@7 for his life.
verse	20	7	24	Hearken unto me now therefore, O ye children, and attend to the words of my mouth.
verse	20	7	25	Let not thine heart decline to her ways, go not astray in her paths.
verse	20	7	26	@@For she hath cast down many wounded: yea, many strong @9men@7 have been slain by her.
verse	20	7	27	@@Her house @9is@7 the way to hell, going down to the chambers of death.
verse	20	8	1	Doth not wisdom cry? and understanding put forth her voice?
verse	20	8	2	She standeth in the top of high places, by the way in the places of the paths.
verse	20	8	3	She crieth at the gates, at the entry of the city, at the coming in at the doors.
verse	20	8	4	@@Unto you, O men, I call; and my voice @9is@7 to the sons of man.
verse	20	8	5	O ye simple, understand wisdom: and, ye fools, be ye of an understanding heart.
verse	20	8	6	@@Hear; for I will speak of excellent things; and the opening of my lips @9shall be@7 right things.
verse	20	8	7	@@For my mouth shall speak truth; and wickedness @9is@7 an abomination to my lips.
verse	20	8	8	@@All the words of my mouth @9are@7 in righteousness; @9there is@7 nothing froward or perverse in them.
verse	20	8	9	@@They @9are@7 all plain to him that understandeth, and right to them that find knowledge.
verse	20	8	10	Receive my instruction, and not silver; and knowledge rather than choice gold.
verse	20	8	11	@@For wisdom @9is@7 better than rubies; and all the things that may be desired are not to be compared to it.
verse	20	8	12	I wisdom dwell with prudence, and find out knowledge of witty inventions.
verse	20	8	13	@@The fear of the LORD @9is@7 to hate evil: pride, and arrogancy, and the evil way, and the froward mouth, do I hate.
verse	20	8	14	@@Counsel @9is@7 mine, and sound wisdom: I @9am@7 understanding; I have strength.
verse	20	8	15	By me kings reign, and princes decree justice.
verse	20	8	16	@@By me princes rule, and nobles, @9even@7 all the judges of the earth.
verse	20	8	17	I love them that love me; and those that seek me early shall find me.
verse	20	8	18	@@Riches and honour @9are@7 with me; @9yea,@7 durable riches and righteousness.
verse	20	8	19	@@My fruit @9is@7 better than gold, yea, than fine gold; and my revenue than choice silver.
verse	20	8	20	I lead in the way of righteousness, in the midst of the paths of judgment:
verse	20	8	21	That I may cause those that love me to inherit substance; and I will fill their treasures.
verse	20	8	22	The LORD possessed me in the beginning of his way, before his works of old.
verse	20	8	23	I was set up from everlasting, from the beginning, or ever the earth was.
verse	20	8	24	@@When @9there were@7 no depths, I was brought forth; when @9there were@7 no fountains abounding with water.
verse	20	8	25	Before the mountains were settled, before the hills was I brought forth:
verse	20	8	26	While as yet he had not made the earth, nor the fields, nor the highest part of the dust of the world.
verse	20	8	27	@@When he prepared the heavens, I @9was@7 there: when he set a compass upon the face of the depth:
verse	20	8	28	When he established the clouds above: when he strengthened the fountains of the deep:
verse	20	8	29	When he gave to the sea his decree, that the waters should not pass his commandment: when he appointed the foundations of the earth:
verse	20	8	30	@@Then I was by him, @9as@7 one brought up @9with him:@7 and I was daily @9his@7 delight, rejoicing always before him;
verse	20	8	31	@@Rejoicing in the habitable part of his earth; and my delights @9were@7 with the sons of men.
verse	20	8	32	@@Now therefore hearken unto me, O ye children: for blessed @9are they that@7 keep my ways.
verse	20	8	33	Hear instruction, and be wise, and refuse it not.
verse	20	8	34	@@Blessed @9is@7 the man that heareth me, watching daily at my gates, waiting at the posts of my doors.
verse	20	8	35	For whoso findeth me findeth life, and shall obtain favour of the LORD.
verse	20	8	36	But he that sinneth against me wrongeth his own soul: all they that hate me love death.
verse	20	9	1	Wisdom hath builded her house, she hath hewn out her seven pillars:
verse	20	9	2	She hath killed her beasts; she hath mingled her wine; she hath also furnished her table.
verse	20	9	3	She hath sent forth her maidens: she crieth upon the highest places of the city,
verse	20	9	4	@@Whoso @9is@7 simple, let him turn in hither: @9as for@7 him that wanteth understanding, she saith to him,
verse	20	9	5	@@Come, eat of my bread, and drink of the wine @9which@7 I have mingled.
verse	20	9	6	Forsake the foolish, and live; and go in the way of understanding.
verse	20	9	7	@@He that reproveth a scorner getteth to himself shame: and he that rebuketh a wicked @9man getteth@7 himself a blot.
verse	20	9	8	Reprove not a scorner, lest he hate thee: rebuke a wise man, and he will love thee.
verse	20	9	9	@@Give @9instruction@7 to a wise @9man,@7 and he will be yet wiser: teach a just @9man,@7 and he will increase in learning.
verse	20	9	10	@@The fear of the LORD @9is@7 the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy @9is@7 understanding.
verse	20	9	11	For by me thy days shall be multiplied, and the years of thy life shall be increased.
verse	20	9	12	@@If thou be wise, thou shalt be wise for thyself: but @9if@7 thou scornest, thou alone shalt bear @9it.@7
verse	20	9	13	@@A foolish woman @9is@7 clamorous: @9she is@7 simple, and knoweth nothing.
verse	20	9	14	For she sitteth at the door of her house, on a seat in the high places of the city,
verse	20	9	15	To call passengers who go right on their ways:
verse	20	9	16	@@Whoso @9is@7 simple, let him turn in hither: and @9as for@7 him that wanteth understanding, she saith to him,
verse	20	9	17	@@Stolen waters are sweet, and bread @9eaten@7 in secret is pleasant.
verse	20	9	18	@@But he knoweth not that the dead @9are@7 there; @9and that@7 her guests @9are@7 in the depths of hell.
verse	20	10	1	@@The proverbs of Solomon. A wise son maketh a glad father: but a foolish son @9is@7 the heaviness of his mother.
verse	20	10	2	Treasures of wickedness profit nothing: but righteousness delivereth from death.
verse	20	10	3	The LORD will not suffer the soul of the righteous to famish: but he casteth away the substance of the wicked.
verse	20	10	4	@@He becometh poor that dealeth @9with@7 a slack hand: but the hand of the diligent maketh rich.
verse	20	10	5	@@He that gathereth in summer @9is@7 a wise son: @9but@7 he that sleepeth in harvest @9is@7 a son that causeth shame.
verse	20	10	6	@@Blessings @9are@7 upon the head of the just: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked.
verse	20	10	7	The memory of the just is blessed: but the name of the wicked shall rot.
verse	20	10	8	The wise in heart will receive commandments: but a prating fool shall fall.
verse	20	10	9	He that walketh uprightly walketh surely: but he that perverteth his ways shall be known.
verse	20	10	10	He that winketh with the eye causeth sorrow: but a prating fool shall fall.
verse	20	10	11	@@The mouth of a righteous @9man is@7 a well of life: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked.
verse	20	10	12	Hatred stirreth up strifes: but love covereth all sins.
verse	20	10	13	@@In the lips of him that hath understanding wisdom is found: but a rod @9is@7 for the back of him that is void of understanding.
verse	20	10	14	@@Wise @9men@7 lay up knowledge: but the mouth of the foolish @9is@7 near destruction.
verse	20	10	15	@@The rich man's wealth @9is@7 his strong city: the destruction of the poor @9is@7 their poverty.
verse	20	10	16	@@The labour of the righteous @9tendeth@7 to life: the fruit of the wicked to sin.
verse	20	10	17	@@He @9is in@7 the way of life that keepeth instruction: but he that refuseth reproof erreth.
verse	20	10	18	@@He that hideth hatred @9with@7 lying lips, and he that uttereth a slander, @9is@7 a fool.
verse	20	10	19	@@In the multitude of words there wanteth not sin: but he that refraineth his lips @9is@7 wise.
verse	20	10	20	@@The tongue of the just @9is as@7 choice silver: the heart of the wicked @9is@7 little worth.
verse	20	10	21	The lips of the righteous feed many: but fools die for want of wisdom.
verse	20	10	22	The blessing of the LORD, it maketh rich, and he addeth no sorrow with it.
verse	20	10	23	@@@9It is@7 as sport to a fool to do mischief: but a man of understanding hath wisdom.
verse	20	10	24	The fear of the wicked, it shall come upon him: but the desire of the righteous shall be granted.
verse	20	10	25	@@As the whirlwind passeth, so @9is@7 the wicked no @9more:@7 but the righteous @9is@7 an everlasting foundation.
verse	20	10	26	@@As vinegar to the teeth, and as smoke to the eyes, so @9is@7 the sluggard to them that send him.
verse	20	10	27	The fear of the LORD prolongeth days: but the years of the wicked shall be shortened.
verse	20	10	28	@@The hope of the righteous @9shall be@7 gladness: but the expectation of the wicked shall perish.
verse	20	10	29	@@The way of the LORD @9is@7 strength to the upright: but destruction @9shall be@7 to the workers of iniquity.
verse	20	10	30	The righteous shall never be removed: but the wicked shall not inhabit the earth.
verse	20	10	31	The mouth of the just bringeth forth wisdom: but the froward tongue shall be cut out.
verse	20	10	32	@@The lips of the righteous know what is acceptable: but the mouth of the wicked @9speaketh@7 frowardness.
verse	20	11	1	@@A false balance @9is@7 abomination to the LORD: but a just weight @9is@7 his delight.
verse	20	11	2	@@@9When@7 pride cometh, then cometh shame: but with the lowly @9is@7 wisdom.
verse	20	11	3	The integrity of the upright shall guide them: but the perverseness of transgressors shall destroy them.
verse	20	11	4	Riches profit not in the day of wrath: but righteousness delivereth from death.
verse	20	11	5	The righteousness of the perfect shall direct his way: but the wicked shall fall by his own wickedness.
verse	20	11	6	@@The righteousness of the upright shall deliver them: but transgressors shall be taken in @9their own@7 naughtiness.
verse	20	11	7	@@When a wicked man dieth, @9his@7 expectation shall perish: and the hope of unjust @9men@7 perisheth.
verse	20	11	8	The righteous is delivered out of trouble, and the wicked cometh in his stead.
verse	20	11	9	@@An hypocrite with @9his@7 mouth destroyeth his neighbour: but through knowledge shall the just be delivered.
verse	20	11	10	@@When it goeth well with the righteous, the city rejoiceth: and when the wicked perish, @9there is@7 shouting.
verse	20	11	11	By the blessing of the upright the city is exalted: but it is overthrown by the mouth of the wicked.
verse	20	11	12	He that is void of wisdom despiseth his neighbour: but a man of understanding holdeth his peace.
verse	20	11	13	A talebearer revealeth secrets: but he that is of a faithful spirit concealeth the matter.
verse	20	11	14	@@Where no counsel @9is,@7 the people fall: but in the multitude of counsellors @9there is@7 safety.
verse	20	11	15	@@He that is surety for a stranger shall smart @9for it:@7 and he that hateth suretiship is sure.
verse	20	11	16	@@A gracious woman retaineth honour: and strong @9men@7 retain riches.
verse	20	11	17	@@The merciful man doeth good to his own soul: but @9he that is@7 cruel troubleth his own flesh.
verse	20	11	18	@@The wicked worketh a deceitful work: but to him that soweth righteousness @9shall be@7 a sure reward.
verse	20	11	19	@@As righteousness @9tendeth@7 to life: so he that pursueth evil @9pursueth it@7 to his own death.
verse	20	11	20	@@They that are of a froward heart @9are@7 abomination to the LORD: but @9such as are@7 upright in @9their@7 way @9are@7 his delight.
verse	20	11	21	@@@9Though@7 hand @9join@7 in hand, the wicked shall not be unpunished: but the seed of the righteous shall be delivered.
verse	20	11	22	@@@9As@7 a jewel of gold in a swine's snout, @9so is@7 a fair woman which is without discretion.
verse	20	11	23	@@The desire of the righteous @9is@7 only good: @9but@7 the expectation of the wicked @9is@7 wrath.
verse	20	11	24	@@There is that scattereth, and yet increaseth; and @9there is@7 that withholdeth more than is meet, but @9it tendeth@7 to poverty.
verse	20	11	25	The liberal soul shall be made fat: and he that watereth shall be watered also himself.
verse	20	11	26	@@He that withholdeth corn, the people shall curse him: but blessing @9shall be@7 upon the head of him that selleth @9it. @7
verse	20	11	27	He that diligently seeketh good procureth favour: but he that seeketh mischief, it shall come unto him.
verse	20	11	28	He that trusteth in his riches shall fall: but the righteous shall flourish as a branch.
verse	20	11	29	@@He that troubleth his own house shall inherit the wind: and the fool @9shall be@7 servant to the wise of heart.
verse	20	11	30	@@The fruit of the righteous @9is@7 a tree of life; and he that winneth souls @9is@7 wise.
verse	20	11	31	Behold, the righteous shall be recompensed in the earth: much more the wicked and the sinner.
verse	20	12	1	@@Whoso loveth instruction loveth knowledge: but he that hateth reproof @9is@7 brutish.
verse	20	12	2	@@A good @9man@7 obtaineth favour of the LORD: but a man of wicked devices will he condemn.
verse	20	12	3	A man shall not be established by wickedness: but the root of the righteous shall not be moved.
verse	20	12	4	@@A virtuous woman @9is@7 a crown to her husband: but she that maketh ashamed @9is@7 as rottenness in his bones.
verse	20	12	5	@@The thoughts of the righteous @9are@7 right: @9but@7 the counsels of the wicked @9are@7 deceit.
verse	20	12	6	@@The words of the wicked @9are@7 to lie in wait for blood: but the mouth of the upright shall deliver them.
verse	20	12	7	@@The wicked are overthrown, and @9are@7 not: but the house of the righteous shall stand.
verse	20	12	8	A man shall be commended according to his wisdom: but he that is of a perverse heart shall be despised.
verse	20	12	9	@@@9He that is@7 despised, and hath a servant, @9is@7 better than he that honoureth himself, and lacketh bread.
verse	20	12	10	@@A righteous @9man@7 regardeth the life of his beast: but the tender mercies of the wicked @9are@7 cruel.
verse	20	12	11	@@He that tilleth his land shall be satisfied with bread: but he that followeth vain @9persons is@7 void of understanding.
verse	20	12	12	@@The wicked desireth the net of evil @9men:@7 but the root of the righteous yieldeth @9fruit. @7
verse	20	12	13	@@The wicked is snared by the transgression of @9his@7 lips: but the just shall come out of trouble.
verse	20	12	14	@@A man shall be satisfied with good by the fruit of @9his@7 mouth: and the recompense of a man's hands shall be rendered unto him.
verse	20	12	15	@@The way of a fool @9is@7 right in his own eyes: but he that hearkeneth unto counsel @9is@7 wise.
verse	20	12	16	@@A fool's wrath is presently known: but a prudent @9man@7 covereth shame.
verse	20	12	17	@@@9He that@7 speaketh truth sheweth forth righteousness: but a false witness deceit.
verse	20	12	18	@@There is that speaketh like the piercings of a sword: but the tongue of the wise @9is@7 health.
verse	20	12	19	@@The lip of truth shall be established for ever: but a lying tongue @9is@7 but for a moment.
verse	20	12	20	@@Deceit @9is@7 in the heart of them that imagine evil: but to the counsellors of peace @9is@7 joy.
verse	20	12	21	There shall no evil happen to the just: but the wicked shall be filled with mischief.
verse	20	12	22	@@Lying lips @9are@7 abomination to the LORD: but they that deal truly @9are@7 his delight.
verse	20	12	23	A prudent man concealeth knowledge: but the heart of fools proclaimeth foolishness.
verse	20	12	24	The hand of the diligent shall bear rule: but the slothful shall be under tribute.
verse	20	12	25	Heaviness in the heart of man maketh it stoop: but a good word maketh it glad.
verse	20	12	26	@@The righteous @9is@7 more excellent than his neighbour: but the way of the wicked seduceth them.
verse	20	12	27	@@The slothful @9man@7 roasteth not that which he took in hunting: but the substance of a diligent man @9is@7 precious.
verse	20	12	28	@@In the way of righteousness @9is@7 life; and @9in@7 the pathway @9thereof there is@7 no death.
verse	20	13	1	@@A wise son @9heareth@7 his father's instruction: but a scorner heareth not rebuke.
verse	20	13	2	@@A man shall eat good by the fruit of @9his@7 mouth: but the soul of the transgressors @9shall eat@7 violence.
verse	20	13	3	@@He that keepeth his mouth keepeth his life: @9but@7 he that openeth wide his lips shall have destruction.
verse	20	13	4	@@The soul of the sluggard desireth, and @9hath@7 nothing: but the soul of the diligent shall be made fat.
verse	20	13	5	@@A righteous @9man@7 hateth lying: but a wicked @9man@7 is loathsome, and cometh to shame.
verse	20	13	6	@@Righteousness keepeth @9him that is@7 upright in the way: but wickedness overthroweth the sinner.
verse	20	13	7	@@There is that maketh himself rich, yet @9hath@7 nothing: @9there is@7 that maketh himself poor, yet @9hath@7 great riches.
verse	20	13	8	@@The ransom of a man's life @9are@7 his riches: but the poor heareth not rebuke.
verse	20	13	9	The light of the righteous rejoiceth: but the lamp of the wicked shall be put out.
verse	20	13	10	@@Only by pride cometh contention: but with the well advised @9is@7 wisdom.
verse	20	13	11	@@Wealth @9gotten@7 by vanity shall be diminished: but he that gathereth by labour shall increase.
verse	20	13	12	@@Hope deferred maketh the heart sick: but @9when@7 the desire cometh, @9it is@7 a tree of life.
verse	20	13	13	Whoso despiseth the word shall be destroyed: but he that feareth the commandment shall be rewarded.
verse	20	13	14	@@The law of the wise @9is@7 a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.
verse	20	13	15	@@Good understanding giveth favour: but the way of transgressors @9is@7 hard.
verse	20	13	16	@@Every prudent @9man@7 dealeth with knowledge: but a fool layeth open @9his@7 folly.
verse	20	13	17	@@A wicked messenger falleth into mischief: but a faithful ambassador @9is@7 health.
verse	20	13	18	@@Poverty and shame @9shall be to@7 him that refuseth instruction: but he that regardeth reproof shall be honoured.
verse	20	13	19	@@The desire accomplished is sweet to the soul: but @9it is@7 abomination to fools to depart from evil.
verse	20	13	20	@@He that walketh with wise @9men@7 shall be wise: but a companion of fools shall be destroyed.
verse	20	13	21	Evil pursueth sinners: but to the righteous good shall be repaid.
verse	20	13	22	@@A good @9man@7 leaveth an inheritance to his children's children: and the wealth of the sinner is laid up for the just.
verse	20	13	23	@@Much food @9is in@7 the tillage of the poor: but there is @9that is@7 destroyed for want of judgment.
verse	20	13	24	He that spareth his rod hateth his son: but he that loveth him chasteneth him betimes.
verse	20	13	25	The righteous eateth to the satisfying of his soul: but the belly of the wicked shall want.
verse	20	14	1	Every wise woman buildeth her house: but the foolish plucketh it down with her hands.
verse	20	14	2	@@He that walketh in his uprightness feareth the LORD: but @9he that is@7 perverse in his ways despiseth him.
verse	20	14	3	In the mouth of the foolish is a rod of pride: but the lips of the wise shall preserve them.
verse	20	14	4	@@Where no oxen @9are,@7 the crib @9is@7 clean: but much increase @9is@7 by the strength of the ox.
verse	20	14	5	A faithful witness will not lie: but a false witness will utter lies.
verse	20	14	6	@@A scorner seeketh wisdom, and @9findeth it@7 not: but knowledge @9is@7 easy unto him that understandeth.
verse	20	14	7	@@Go from the presence of a foolish man, when thou perceivest not @9in him@7 the lips of knowledge.
verse	20	14	8	@@The wisdom of the prudent @9is@7 to understand his way: but the folly of fools @9is@7 deceit.
verse	20	14	9	@@Fools make a mock at sin: but among the righteous @9there is@7 favour.
verse	20	14	10	The heart knoweth his own bitterness; and a stranger doth not intermeddle with his joy.
verse	20	14	11	The house of the wicked shall be overthrown: but the tabernacle of the upright shall flourish.
verse	20	14	12	@@There is a way which seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof @9are@7 the ways of death.
verse	20	14	13	@@Even in laughter the heart is sorrowful; and the end of that mirth @9is@7 heaviness.
verse	20	14	14	@@The backslider in heart shall be filled with his own ways: and a good man @9shall be satisfied@7 from himself.
verse	20	14	15	@@The simple believeth every word: but the prudent @9man@7 looketh well to his going.
verse	20	14	16	@@A wise @9man@7 feareth, and departeth from evil: but the fool rageth, and is confident.
verse	20	14	17	@@@9He that is@7 soon angry dealeth foolishly: and a man of wicked devices is hated.
verse	20	14	18	The simple inherit folly: but the prudent are crowned with knowledge.
verse	20	14	19	The evil bow before the good; and the wicked at the gates of the righteous.
verse	20	14	20	@@The poor is hated even of his own neighbour: but the rich @9hath@7 many friends.
verse	20	14	21	@@He that despiseth his neighbour sinneth: but he that hath mercy on the poor, happy @9is@7 he.
verse	20	14	22	@@Do they not err that devise evil? but mercy and truth @9shall be@7 to them that devise good.
verse	20	14	23	@@In all labour there is profit: but the talk of the lips @9tendeth@7 only to penury.
verse	20	14	24	@@The crown of the wise is their riches: @9but@7 the foolishness of fools @9is@7 folly.
verse	20	14	25	@@A true witness delivereth souls: but a deceitful @9witness@7 speaketh lies.
verse	20	14	26	@@In the fear of the LORD @9is@7 strong confidence: and his children shall have a place of refuge.
verse	20	14	27	@@The fear of the LORD @9is@7 a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.
verse	20	14	28	@@In the multitude of people @9is@7 the king's honour: but in the want of people @9is@7 the destruction of the prince.
verse	20	14	29	@@@9He that is@7 slow to wrath @9is@7 of great understanding: but @9he that is@7 hasty of spirit exalteth folly.
verse	20	14	30	@@A sound heart @9is@7 the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.
verse	20	14	31	He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker: but he that honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.
verse	20	14	32	The wicked is driven away in his wickedness: but the righteous hath hope in his death.
verse	20	14	33	@@Wisdom resteth in the heart of him that hath understanding: but @9that which is@7 in the midst of fools is made known.
verse	20	14	34	@@Righteousness exalteth a nation: but sin @9is@7 a reproach to any people.
verse	20	14	35	@@The king's favour @9is@7 toward a wise servant: but his wrath is @9against@7 him that causeth shame.
verse	20	15	1	A soft answer turneth away wrath: but grievous words stir up anger.
verse	20	15	2	The tongue of the wise useth knowledge aright: but the mouth of fools poureth out foolishness.
verse	20	15	3	@@The eyes of the LORD @9are@7 in every place, beholding the evil and the good.
verse	20	15	4	@@A wholesome tongue @9is@7 a tree of life: but perverseness therein @9is@7 a breach in the spirit.
verse	20	15	5	A fool despiseth his father's instruction: but he that regardeth reproof is prudent.
verse	20	15	6	@@In the house of the righteous @9is@7 much treasure: but in the revenues of the wicked is trouble.
verse	20	15	7	@@The lips of the wise disperse knowledge: but the heart of the foolish @9doeth@7 not so.
verse	20	15	8	@@The sacrifice of the wicked @9is@7 an abomination to the LORD: but the prayer of the upright @9is@7 his delight.
verse	20	15	9	@@The way of the wicked @9is@7 an abomination unto the LORD: but he loveth him that followeth after righteousness.
verse	20	15	10	@@Correction @9is@7 grievous unto him that forsaketh the way: @9and@7 he that hateth reproof shall die.
verse	20	15	11	@@Hell and destruction @9are@7 before the LORD: how much more then the hearts of the children of men?
verse	20	15	12	A scorner loveth not one that reproveth him: neither will he go unto the wise.
verse	20	15	13	A merry heart maketh a cheerful countenance: but by sorrow of the heart the spirit is broken.
verse	20	15	14	The heart of him that hath understanding seeketh knowledge: but the mouth of fools feedeth on foolishness.
verse	20	15	15	@@All the days of the afflicted @9are@7 evil: but he that is of a merry heart @9hath@7 a continual feast.
verse	20	15	16	@@Better @9is@7 little with the fear of the LORD than great treasure and trouble therewith.
verse	20	15	17	@@Better @9is@7 a dinner of herbs where love is, than a stalled ox and hatred therewith.
verse	20	15	18	@@A wrathful man stirreth up strife: but @9he that is@7 slow to anger appeaseth strife.
verse	20	15	19	@@The way of the slothful @9man is@7 as an hedge of thorns: but the way of the righteous @9is@7 made plain.
verse	20	15	20	A wise son maketh a glad father: but a foolish man despiseth his mother.
verse	20	15	21	@@Folly @9is@7 joy to @9him that is@7 destitute of wisdom: but a man of understanding walketh uprightly.
verse	20	15	22	Without counsel purposes are disappointed: but in the multitude of counsellors they are established.
verse	20	15	23	@@A man hath joy by the answer of his mouth: and a word @9spoken@7 in due season, how good @9is it! @7
verse	20	15	24	@@The way of life @9is@7 above to the wise, that he may depart from hell beneath.
verse	20	15	25	The LORD will destroy the house of the proud: but he will establish the border of the widow.
verse	20	15	26	@@The thoughts of the wicked @9are@7 an abomination to the LORD: but @9the words@7 of the pure @9are@7 pleasant words.
verse	20	15	27	He that is greedy of gain troubleth his own house; but he that hateth gifts shall live.
verse	20	15	28	The heart of the righteous studieth to answer: but the mouth of the wicked poureth out evil things.
verse	20	15	29	@@The LORD @9is@7 far from the wicked: but he heareth the prayer of the righteous.
verse	20	15	30	@@The light of the eyes rejoiceth the heart: @9and@7 a good report maketh the bones fat.
verse	20	15	31	The ear that heareth the reproof of life abideth among the wise.
verse	20	15	32	He that refuseth instruction despiseth his own soul: but he that heareth reproof getteth understanding.
verse	20	15	33	@@The fear of the LORD @9is@7 the instruction of wisdom; and before honour @9is@7 humility.
verse	20	16	1	@@The preparations of the heart in man, and the answer of the tongue, @9is@7 from the LORD.
verse	20	16	2	@@All the ways of a man @9are@7 clean in his own eyes; but the LORD weigheth the spirits.
verse	20	16	3	Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.
verse	20	16	4	@@The LORD hath made all @9things@7 for himself: yea, even the wicked for the day of evil.
verse	20	16	5	@@Every one @9that is@7 proud in heart @9is@7 an abomination to the LORD: @9though@7 hand @9join@7 in hand, he shall not be unpunished.
verse	20	16	6	@@By mercy and truth iniquity is purged: and by the fear of the LORD @9men@7 depart from evil.
verse	20	16	7	When a man's ways please the LORD, he maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him.
verse	20	16	8	@@Better @9is@7 a little with righteousness than great revenues without right.
verse	20	16	9	A man's heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.
verse	20	16	10	@@A divine sentence @9is@7 in the lips of the king: his mouth transgresseth not in judgment.
verse	20	16	11	@@A just weight and balance @9are@7 the LORD'S: all the weights of the bag @9are@7 his work.
verse	20	16	12	@@@9It is@7 an abomination to kings to commit wickedness: for the throne is established by righteousness.
verse	20	16	13	@@Righteous lips @9are@7 the delight of kings; and they love him that speaketh right.
verse	20	16	14	@@The wrath of a king @9is as@7 messengers of death: but a wise man will pacify it.
verse	20	16	15	@@In the light of the king's countenance @9is@7 life; and his favour @9is@7 as a cloud of the latter rain.
verse	20	16	16	@@How much better @9is it@7 to get wisdom than gold! and to get understanding rather to be chosen than silver!
verse	20	16	17	@@The highway of the upright @9is@7 to depart from evil: he that keepeth his way preserveth his soul.
verse	20	16	18	@@Pride @9goeth@7 before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.
verse	20	16	19	@@Better @9it is to be@7 of an humble spirit with the lowly, than to divide the spoil with the proud.
verse	20	16	20	@@He that handleth a matter wisely shall find good: and whoso trusteth in the LORD, happy @9is@7 he.
verse	20	16	21	The wise in heart shall be called prudent: and the sweetness of the lips increaseth learning.
verse	20	16	22	@@Understanding @9is@7 a wellspring of life unto him that hath it: but the instruction of fools @9is@7 folly.
verse	20	16	23	The heart of the wise teacheth his mouth, and addeth learning to his lips.
verse	20	16	24	@@Pleasant words @9are as@7 an honeycomb, sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.
verse	20	16	25	@@There is a way that seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof @9are@7 the ways of death.
verse	20	16	26	He that laboureth laboureth for himself; for his mouth craveth it of him.
verse	20	16	27	@@An ungodly man diggeth up evil: and in his lips @9there is@7 as a burning fire.
verse	20	16	28	A froward man soweth strife: and a whisperer separateth chief friends.
verse	20	16	29	@@A violent man enticeth his neighbour, and leadeth him into the way @9that is@7 not good.
verse	20	16	30	He shutteth his eyes to devise froward things: moving his lips he bringeth evil to pass.
verse	20	16	31	@@The hoary head @9is@7 a crown of glory, @9if@7 it be found in the way of righteousness.
verse	20	16	32	@@@9He that is@7 slow to anger @9is@7 better than the mighty; and he that ruleth his spirit than he that taketh a city.
verse	20	16	33	@@The lot is cast into the lap; but the whole disposing thereof @9is@7 of the LORD.
verse	20	17	1	@@Better @9is@7 a dry morsel, and quietness therewith, than an house full of sacrifices @9with@7 strife.
verse	20	17	2	A wise servant shall have rule over a son that causeth shame, and shall have part of the inheritance among the brethren.
verse	20	17	3	@@The fining pot @9is@7 for silver, and the furnace for gold: but the LORD trieth the hearts.
verse	20	17	4	@@A wicked doer giveth heed to false lips; @9and@7 a liar giveth ear to a naughty tongue.
verse	20	17	5	@@Whoso mocketh the poor reproacheth his Maker: @9and@7 he that is glad at calamities shall not be unpunished.
verse	20	17	6	@@Children's children @9are@7 the crown of old men; and the glory of children @9are@7 their fathers.
verse	20	17	7	Excellent speech becometh not a fool: much less do lying lips a prince.
verse	20	17	8	@@A gift @9is as@7 a precious stone in the eyes of him that hath it: whithersoever it turneth, it prospereth.
verse	20	17	9	@@He that covereth a transgression seeketh love; but he that repeateth a matter separateth @9very@7 friends.
verse	20	17	10	A reproof entereth more into a wise man than an hundred stripes into a fool.
verse	20	17	11	@@An evil @9man@7 seeketh only rebellion: therefore a cruel messenger shall be sent against him.
verse	20	17	12	Let a bear robbed of her whelps meet a man, rather than a fool in his folly.
verse	20	17	13	Whoso rewardeth evil for good, evil shall not depart from his house.
verse	20	17	14	@@The beginning of strife @9is as@7 when one letteth out water: therefore leave off contention, before it be meddled with.
verse	20	17	15	@@He that justifieth the wicked, and he that condemneth the just, even they both @9are@7 abomination to the LORD.
verse	20	17	16	@@Wherefore @9is there@7 a price in the hand of a fool to get wisdom, seeing @9he hath@7 no heart @9to it? @7
verse	20	17	17	A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.
verse	20	17	18	@@A man void of understanding striketh hands, @9and@7 becometh surety in the presence of his friend.
verse	20	17	19	@@He loveth transgression that loveth strife: @9and@7 he that exalteth his gate seeketh destruction.
verse	20	17	20	He that hath a froward heart findeth no good: and he that hath a perverse tongue falleth into mischief.
verse	20	17	21	@@He that begetteth a fool @9doeth it@7 to his sorrow: and the father of a fool hath no joy.
verse	20	17	22	@@A merry heart doeth good @9like@7 a medicine: but a broken spirit drieth the bones.
verse	20	17	23	@@A wicked @9man@7 taketh a gift out of the bosom to pervert the ways of judgment.
verse	20	17	24	@@Wisdom @9is@7 before him that hath understanding; but the eyes of a fool @9are@7 in the ends of the earth.
verse	20	17	25	@@A foolish son @9is@7 a grief to his father, and bitterness to her that bare him.
verse	20	17	26	@@Also to punish the just @9is@7 not good, @9nor@7 to strike princes for equity.
verse	20	17	27	@@He that hath knowledge spareth his words: @9and@7 a man of understanding is of an excellent spirit.
verse	20	17	28	@@Even a fool, when he holdeth his peace, is counted wise: @9and@7 he that shutteth his lips @9is esteemed@7 a man of understanding.
verse	20	18	1	@@Through desire a man, having separated himself, seeketh @9and@7 intermeddleth with all wisdom.
verse	20	18	2	A fool hath no delight in understanding, but that his heart may discover itself.
verse	20	18	3	@@When the wicked cometh, @9then@7 cometh also contempt, and with ignominy reproach.
verse	20	18	4	@@The words of a man's mouth @9are as@7 deep waters, @9and@7 the wellspring of wisdom @9as@7 a flowing brook.
verse	20	18	5	@@@9It is@7 not good to accept the person of the wicked, to overthrow the righteous in judgment.
verse	20	18	6	A fool's lips enter into contention, and his mouth calleth for strokes.
verse	20	18	7	@@A fool's mouth @9is@7 his destruction, and his lips @9are@7 the snare of his soul.
verse	20	18	8	@@The words of a talebearer @9are@7 as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.
verse	20	18	9	He also that is slothful in his work is brother to him that is a great waster.
verse	20	18	10	@@The name of the LORD @9is@7 a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.
verse	20	18	11	@@The rich man's wealth @9is@7 his strong city, and as an high wall in his own conceit.
verse	20	18	12	@@Before destruction the heart of man is haughty, and before honour @9is@7 humility.
verse	20	18	13	@@He that answereth a matter before he heareth @9it,@7 it @9is@7 folly and shame unto him.
verse	20	18	14	The spirit of a man will sustain his infirmity; but a wounded spirit who can bear?
verse	20	18	15	The heart of the prudent getteth knowledge; and the ear of the wise seeketh knowledge.
verse	20	18	16	A man's gift maketh room for him, and bringeth him before great men.
verse	20	18	17	@@@9He that is@7 first in his own cause @9seemeth@7 just; but his neighbour cometh and searcheth him.
verse	20	18	18	The lot causeth contentions to cease, and parteth between the mighty.
verse	20	18	19	@@A brother offended @9is harder to be won@7 than a strong city: and @9their@7 contentions @9are@7 like the bars of a castle.
verse	20	18	20	@@A man's belly shall be satisfied with the fruit of his mouth; @9and@7 with the increase of his lips shall he be filled.
verse	20	18	21	@@Death and life @9are@7 in the power of the tongue: and they that love it shall eat the fruit thereof.
verse	20	18	22	@@@9Whoso@7 findeth a wife findeth a good @9thing,@7 and obtaineth favour of the LORD.
verse	20	18	23	The poor useth intreaties; but the rich answereth roughly.
verse	20	18	24	@@A man @9that hath@7 friends must shew himself friendly: and there is a friend @9that@7 sticketh closer than a brother.
verse	20	19	1	@@Better @9is@7 the poor that walketh in his integrity, than @9he that is@7 perverse in his lips, and is a fool.
verse	20	19	2	@@Also, @9that@7 the soul @9be@7 without knowledge, @9it is@7 not good; and he that hasteth with @9his@7 feet sinneth.
verse	20	19	3	The foolishness of man perverteth his way: and his heart fretteth against the LORD.
verse	20	19	4	Wealth maketh many friends; but the poor is separated from his neighbour.
verse	20	19	5	@@A false witness shall not be unpunished, and @9he that@7 speaketh lies shall not escape.
verse	20	19	6	@@Many will intreat the favour of the prince: and every man @9is@7 a friend to him that giveth gifts.
verse	20	19	7	@@All the brethren of the poor do hate him: how much more do his friends go far from him? he pursueth @9them with@7 words, @9yet@7 they @9are@7 wanting @9to him. @7
verse	20	19	8	@@He that getteth wisdom loveth his own soul: @9he that@7 keepeth understanding shall find good.
verse	20	19	9	A false witness shall not be unpunished, and he that speaketh lies shall perish.
verse	20	19	10	Delight is not seemly for a fool; much less for a servant to have rule over princes.
verse	20	19	11	@@The discretion of a man deferreth his anger; and @9it is@7 his glory to pass over a transgression.
verse	20	19	12	@@The king's wrath @9is@7 as the roaring of a lion; but his favour @9is@7 as dew upon the grass.
verse	20	19	13	@@A foolish son @9is@7 the calamity of his father: and the contentions of a wife @9are@7 a continual dropping.
verse	20	19	14	@@House and riches @9are@7 the inheritance of fathers and a prudent wife @9is@7 from the LORD.
verse	20	19	15	Slothfulness casteth into a deep sleep; and an idle soul shall suffer hunger.
verse	20	19	16	@@He that keepeth the commandment keepeth his own soul; @9but@7 he that despiseth his ways shall die.
verse	20	19	17	He that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto the LORD; and that which he hath given will he pay him again.
verse	20	19	18	Chasten thy son while there is hope, and let not thy soul spare for his crying.
verse	20	19	19	@@A man of great wrath shall suffer punishment: for if thou deliver @9him,@7 yet thou must do it again.
verse	20	19	20	Hear counsel, and receive instruction, that thou mayest be wise in thy latter end.
verse	20	19	21	@@@9There are@7 many devices in a man's heart; nevertheless the counsel of the LORD, that shall stand.
verse	20	19	22	@@The desire of a man @9is@7 his kindness: and a poor man @9is@7 better than a liar.
verse	20	19	23	@@The fear of the LORD @9tendeth@7 to life: and @9he that hath it@7 shall abide satisfied; he shall not be visited with evil.
verse	20	19	24	@@A slothful @9man@7 hideth his hand in @9his@7 bosom, and will not so much as bring it to his mouth again.
verse	20	19	25	@@Smite a scorner, and the simple will beware: and reprove one that hath understanding, @9and@7 he will understand knowledge.
verse	20	19	26	@@He that wasteth @9his@7 father, @9and@7 chaseth away @9his@7 mother, @9is@7 a son that causeth shame, and bringeth reproach.
verse	20	19	27	@@Cease, my son, to hear the instruction @9that causeth@7 to err from the words of knowledge.
verse	20	19	28	An ungodly witness scorneth judgment: and the mouth of the wicked devoureth iniquity.
verse	20	19	29	Judgments are prepared for scorners, and stripes for the back of fools.
verse	20	20	1	@@Wine @9is@7 a mocker, strong drink @9is@7 raging: and whosoever is deceived thereby is not wise.
verse	20	20	2	@@The fear of a king @9is@7 as the roaring of a lion: @9whoso@7 provoketh him to anger sinneth @9against@7 his own soul.
verse	20	20	3	@@@9It is@7 an honour for a man to cease from strife: but every fool will be meddling.
verse	20	20	4	@@The sluggard will not plow by reason of the cold; @9therefore@7 shall he beg in harvest, and @9have@7 nothing.
verse	20	20	5	@@Counsel in the heart of man @9is like@7 deep water; but a man of understanding will draw it out.
verse	20	20	6	Most men will proclaim every one his own goodness: but a faithful man who can find?
verse	20	20	7	@@The just @9man@7 walketh in his integrity: his children @9are@7 blessed after him.
verse	20	20	8	A king that sitteth in the throne of judgment scattereth away all evil with his eyes.
verse	20	20	9	Who can say, I have made my heart clean, I am pure from my sin?
verse	20	20	10	@@Divers weights, @9and@7 divers measures, both of them @9are@7 alike abomination to the LORD.
verse	20	20	11	@@Even a child is known by his doings, whether his work @9be@7 pure, and whether @9it be@7 right.
verse	20	20	12	The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, the LORD hath made even both of them.
verse	20	20	13	@@Love not sleep, lest thou come to poverty; open thine eyes, @9and@7 thou shalt be satisfied with bread.
verse	20	20	14	@@@9It is@7 naught, @9it is@7 naught, saith the buyer: but when he is gone his way, then he boasteth.
verse	20	20	15	@@There is gold, and a multitude of rubies: but the lips of knowledge @9are@7 a precious jewel.
verse	20	20	16	@@Take his garment that is surety @9for@7 a stranger: and take a pledge of him for a strange woman.
verse	20	20	17	@@Bread of deceit @9is@7 sweet to a man; but afterwards his mouth shall be filled with gravel.
verse	20	20	18	@@@9Every@7 purpose is established by counsel: and with good advice make war.
verse	20	20	19	@@He that goeth about @9as@7 a talebearer revealeth secrets: therefore meddle not with him that flattereth with his lips.
verse	20	20	20	Whoso curseth his father or his mother, his lamp shall be put out in obscure darkness.
verse	20	20	21	@@An inheritance @9may be@7 gotten hastily at the beginning; but the end thereof shall not be blessed.
verse	20	20	22	@@Say not thou, I will recompense evil; @9but@7 wait on the LORD, and he shall save thee.
verse	20	20	23	@@Divers weights @9are@7 an abomination unto the LORD; and a false balance @9is@7 not good.
verse	20	20	24	@@Man's goings @9are@7 of the LORD; how can a man then understand his own way?
verse	20	20	25	@@@9It is@7 a snare to the man @9who@7 devoureth @9that which is@7 holy, and after vows to make enquiry.
verse	20	20	26	A wise king scattereth the wicked, and bringeth the wheel over them.
verse	20	20	27	@@The spirit of man @9is@7 the candle of the LORD, searching all the inward parts of the belly.
verse	20	20	28	Mercy and truth preserve the king: and his throne is upholden by mercy.
verse	20	20	29	@@The glory of young men @9is@7 their strength: and the beauty of old men @9is@7 the grey head.
verse	20	20	30	@@The blueness of a wound cleanseth away evil: so @9do@7 stripes the inward parts of the belly.
verse	20	21	1	@@The king's heart @9is@7 in the hand of the LORD, @9as@7 the rivers of water: he turneth it whithersoever he will.
verse	20	21	2	@@Every way of a man @9is@7 right in his own eyes: but the LORD pondereth the hearts.
verse	20	21	3	@@To do justice and judgment @9is@7 more acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice.
verse	20	21	4	@@An high look, and a proud heart, @9and@7 the plowing of the wicked, @9is@7 sin.
verse	20	21	5	@@The thoughts of the diligent @9tend@7 only to plenteousness; but of every one @9that is@7 hasty only to want.
verse	20	21	6	@@The getting of treasures by a lying tongue @9is@7 a vanity tossed to and fro of them that seek death.
verse	20	21	7	The robbery of the wicked shall destroy them; because they refuse to do judgment.
verse	20	21	8	@@The way of man @9is@7 froward and strange: but @9as for@7 the pure, his work @9is@7 right.
verse	20	21	9	@@@9It is@7 better to dwell in a corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman in a wide house.
verse	20	21	10	The soul of the wicked desireth evil: his neighbour findeth no favour in his eyes.
verse	20	21	11	When the scorner is punished, the simple is made wise: and when the wise is instructed, he receiveth knowledge.
verse	20	21	12	@@The righteous @9man@7 wisely considereth the house of the wicked: @9but God@7 overthroweth the wicked for @9their@7 wickedness.
verse	20	21	13	Whoso stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor, he also shall cry himself, but shall not be heard.
verse	20	21	14	A gift in secret pacifieth anger: and a reward in the bosom strong wrath.
verse	20	21	15	@@@9It is@7 joy to the just to do judgment: but destruction @9shall be@7 to the workers of iniquity.
verse	20	21	16	The man that wandereth out of the way of understanding shall remain in the congregation of the dead.
verse	20	21	17	@@He that loveth pleasure @9shall be@7 a poor man: he that loveth wine and oil shall not be rich.
verse	20	21	18	@@The wicked @9shall be@7 a ransom for the righteous, and the transgressor for the upright.
verse	20	21	19	@@@9It is@7 better to dwell in the wilderness, than with a contentious and an angry woman.
verse	20	21	20	@@@9There is@7 treasure to be desired and oil in the dwelling of the wise; but a foolish man spendeth it up.
verse	20	21	21	He that followeth after righteousness and mercy findeth life, righteousness, and honour.
verse	20	21	22	@@A wise @9man@7 scaleth the city of the mighty, and casteth down the strength of the confidence thereof.
verse	20	21	23	Whoso keepeth his mouth and his tongue keepeth his soul from troubles.
verse	20	21	24	@@Proud @9and@7 haughty scorner @9is@7 his name, who dealeth in proud wrath.
verse	20	21	25	The desire of the slothful killeth him; for his hands refuse to labour.
verse	20	21	26	He coveteth greedily all the day long: but the righteous giveth and spareth not.
verse	20	21	27	@@The sacrifice of the wicked @9is@7 abomination: how much more, @9when@7 he bringeth it with a wicked mind?
verse	20	21	28	A false witness shall perish: but the man that heareth speaketh constantly.
verse	20	21	29	@@A wicked man hardeneth his face: but @9as for@7 the upright, he directeth his way.
verse	20	21	30	@@@9There is@7 no wisdom nor understanding nor counsel against the LORD.
verse	20	21	31	@@The horse @9is@7 prepared against the day of battle: but safety @9is@7 of the LORD.
verse	20	22	1	@@A @9good@7 name @9is@7 rather to be chosen than great riches, @9and@7 loving favour rather than silver and gold.
verse	20	22	2	@@The rich and poor meet together: the LORD @9is@7 the maker of them all.
verse	20	22	3	@@A prudent @9man@7 foreseeth the evil, and hideth himself: but the simple pass on, and are punished.
verse	20	22	4	@@By humility @9and@7 the fear of the LORD @9are@7 riches, and honour, and life.
verse	20	22	5	@@Thorns @9and@7 snares @9are@7 in the way of the froward: he that doth keep his soul shall be far from them.
verse	20	22	6	Train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it.
verse	20	22	7	@@The rich ruleth over the poor, and the borrower @9is@7 servant to the lender.
verse	20	22	8	He that soweth iniquity shall reap vanity: and the rod of his anger shall fail.
verse	20	22	9	He that hath a bountiful eye shall be blessed; for he giveth of his bread to the poor.
verse	20	22	10	Cast out the scorner, and contention shall go out; yea, strife and reproach shall cease.
verse	20	22	11	@@He that loveth pureness of heart, @9for@7 the grace of his lips the king @9shall be@7 his friend.
verse	20	22	12	The eyes of the LORD preserve knowledge, and he overthroweth the words of the transgressor.
verse	20	22	13	@@The slothful @9man@7 saith, @9There is@7 a lion without, I shall be slain in the streets.
verse	20	22	14	@@The mouth of strange women @9is@7 a deep pit: he that is abhorred of the LORD shall fall therein.
verse	20	22	15	@@Foolishness @9is@7 bound in the heart of a child; @9but@7 the rod of correction shall drive it far from him.
verse	20	22	16	@@He that oppresseth the poor to increase his @9riches, and@7 he that giveth to the rich, @9shall@7 surely @9come@7 to want.
verse	20	22	17	Bow down thine ear, and hear the words of the wise, and apply thine heart unto my knowledge.
verse	20	22	18	@@For @9it is@7 a pleasant thing if thou keep them within thee; they shall withal be fitted in thy lips.
verse	20	22	19	That thy trust may be in the LORD, I have made known to thee this day, even to thee.
verse	20	22	20	Have not I written to thee excellent things in counsels and knowledge,
verse	20	22	21	That I might make thee know the certainty of the words of truth; that thou mightest answer the words of truth to them that send unto thee?
verse	20	22	22	@@Rob not the poor, because he @9is@7 poor: neither oppress the afflicted in the gate:
verse	20	22	23	For the LORD will plead their cause, and spoil the soul of those that spoiled them.
verse	20	22	24	Make no friendship with an angry man; and with a furious man thou shalt not go:
verse	20	22	25	Lest thou learn his ways, and get a snare to thy soul.
verse	20	22	26	@@Be not thou @9one@7 of them that strike hands, @9or@7 of them that are sureties for debts.
verse	20	22	27	If thou hast nothing to pay, why should he take away thy bed from under thee?
verse	20	22	28	Remove not the ancient landmark, which thy fathers have set.
verse	20	22	29	@@Seest thou a man diligent in his business? he shall stand before kings; he shall not stand before mean @9men.@7
verse	20	23	1	@@When thou sittest to eat with a ruler, consider diligently what @9is@7 before thee:
verse	20	23	2	@@And put a knife to thy throat, if thou @9be@7 a man given to appetite.
verse	20	23	3	@@Be not desirous of his dainties: for they @9are@7 deceitful meat.
verse	20	23	4	Labour not to be rich: cease from thine own wisdom.
verse	20	23	5	@@Wilt thou set thine eyes upon that which is not? for @9riches@7 certainly make themselves wings; they fly away as an eagle toward heaven.
verse	20	23	6	@@Eat thou not the bread of @9him that hath@7 an evil eye, neither desire thou his dainty meats:
verse	20	23	7	@@For as he thinketh in his heart, so @9is@7 he: Eat and drink, saith he to thee; but his heart @9is@7 not with thee.
verse	20	23	8	@@The morsel @9which@7 thou hast eaten shalt thou vomit up, and lose thy sweet words.
verse	20	23	9	Speak not in the ears of a fool: for he will despise the wisdom of thy words.
verse	20	23	10	Remove not the old landmark; and enter not into the fields of the fatherless:
verse	20	23	11	@@For their redeemer @9is@7 mighty; he shall plead their cause with thee.
verse	20	23	12	Apply thine heart unto instruction, and thine ears to the words of knowledge.
verse	20	23	13	@@Withhold not correction from the child: for @9if@7 thou beatest him with the rod, he shall not die.
verse	20	23	14	Thou shalt beat him with the rod, and shalt deliver his soul from hell.
verse	20	23	15	My son, if thine heart be wise, my heart shall rejoice, even mine.
verse	20	23	16	Yea, my reins shall rejoice, when thy lips speak right things.
verse	20	23	17	@@Let not thine heart envy sinners: but @9be thou@7 in the fear of the LORD all the day long.
verse	20	23	18	For surely there is an end; and thine expectation shall not be cut off.
verse	20	23	19	Hear thou, my son, and be wise, and guide thine heart in the way.
verse	20	23	20	Be not among winebibbers; among riotous eaters of flesh:
verse	20	23	21	@@For the drunkard and the glutton shall come to poverty: and drowsiness shall clothe @9a man@7 with rags.
verse	20	23	22	Hearken unto thy father that begat thee, and despise not thy mother when she is old.
verse	20	23	23	@@Buy the truth, and sell @9it@7 not; @9also@7 wisdom, and instruction, and understanding.
verse	20	23	24	@@The father of the righteous shall greatly rejoice: and he that begetteth a wise @9child@7 shall have joy of him.
verse	20	23	25	Thy father and thy mother shall be glad, and she that bare thee shall rejoice.
verse	20	23	26	My son, give me thine heart, and let thine eyes observe my ways.
verse	20	23	27	@@For a whore @9is@7 a deep ditch; and a strange woman @9is@7 a narrow pit.
verse	20	23	28	@@She also lieth in wait as @9for@7 a prey, and increaseth the transgressors among men.
verse	20	23	29	Who hath woe? who hath sorrow? who hath contentions? who hath babbling? who hath wounds without cause? who hath redness of eyes?
verse	20	23	30	They that tarry long at the wine; they that go to seek mixed wine.
verse	20	23	31	@@Look not thou upon the wine when it is red, when it giveth his colour in the cup, @9when@7 it moveth itself aright.
verse	20	23	32	At the last it biteth like a serpent, and stingeth like an adder.
verse	20	23	33	Thine eyes shall behold strange women, and thine heart shall utter perverse things.
verse	20	23	34	Yea, thou shalt be as he that lieth down in the midst of the sea, or as he that lieth upon the top of a mast.
verse	20	23	35	@@They have stricken me, @9shalt thou say, and@7 I was not sick; they have beaten me, @9and@7 I felt @9it@7 not: when shall I awake? I will seek it yet again.
verse	20	24	1	Be not thou envious against evil men, neither desire to be with them.
verse	20	24	2	For their heart studieth destruction, and their lips talk of mischief.
verse	20	24	3	Through wisdom is an house builded; and by understanding it is established:
verse	20	24	4	And by knowledge shall the chambers be filled with all precious and pleasant riches.
verse	20	24	5	@@A wise man @9is@7 strong; yea, a man of knowledge increaseth strength.
verse	20	24	6	@@For by wise counsel thou shalt make thy war: and in multitude of counsellors @9there is@7 safety.
verse	20	24	7	@@Wisdom @9is@7 too high for a fool: he openeth not his mouth in the gate.
verse	20	24	8	He that deviseth to do evil shall be called a mischievous person.
verse	20	24	9	@@The thought of foolishness @9is@7 sin: and the scorner @9is@7 an abomination to men.
verse	20	24	10	@@@9If@7 thou faint in the day of adversity, thy strength @9is@7 small.
verse	20	24	11	@@If thou forbear to deliver @9them that are@7 drawn unto death, and @9those that are@7 ready to be slain;
verse	20	24	12	@@If thou sayest, Behold, we knew it not; doth not he that pondereth the heart consider @9it?@7 and he that keepeth thy soul, doth @9not@7 he know @9it?@7 and shall @9not@7 he render to @9every@7 man according to his works?
verse	20	24	13	@@My son, eat thou honey, because @9it is@7 good; and the honeycomb, @9which is@7 sweet to thy taste:
verse	20	24	14	@@So @9shall@7 the knowledge of wisdom @9be@7 unto thy soul: when thou hast found @9it,@7 then there shall be a reward, and thy expectation shall not be cut off.
verse	20	24	15	@@Lay not wait, O wicked @9man,@7 against the dwelling of the righteous; spoil not his resting place:
verse	20	24	16	@@For a just @9man@7 falleth seven times, and riseth up again: but the wicked shall fall into mischief.
verse	20	24	17	Rejoice not when thine enemy falleth, and let not thine heart be glad when he stumbleth:
verse	20	24	18	@@Lest the LORD see @9it,@7 and it displease him, and he turn away his wrath from him.
verse	20	24	19	@@Fret not thyself because of evil @9men,@7 neither be thou envious at the wicked;
verse	20	24	20	@@For there shall be no reward to the evil @9man;@7 the candle of the wicked shall be put out.
verse	20	24	21	@@My son, fear thou the LORD and the king: @9and@7 meddle not with them that are given to change:
verse	20	24	22	For their calamity shall rise suddenly; and who knoweth the ruin of them both?
verse	20	24	23	@@These @9things@7 also @9belong@7 to the wise. @9It is@7 not good to have respect of persons in judgment.
verse	20	24	24	@@He that saith unto the wicked, Thou @9art@7 righteous; him shall the people curse, nations shall abhor him:
verse	20	24	25	@@But to them that rebuke @9him@7 shall be delight, and a good blessing shall come upon them.
verse	20	24	26	@@@9Every man@7 shall kiss @9his@7 lips that giveth a right answer.
verse	20	24	27	Prepare thy work without, and make it fit for thyself in the field; and afterwards build thine house.
verse	20	24	28	@@Be not a witness against thy neighbour without cause; and deceive @9not@7 with thy lips.
verse	20	24	29	Say not, I will do so to him as he hath done to me: I will render to the man according to his work.
verse	20	24	30	I went by the field of the slothful, and by the vineyard of the man void of understanding;
verse	20	24	31	@@And, lo, it was all grown over with thorns, @9and@7 nettles had covered the face thereof, and the stone wall thereof was broken down.
verse	20	24	32	@@Then I saw, @9and@7 considered @9it@7 well: I looked upon @9it, and@7 received instruction.
verse	20	24	33	@@@9Yet@7 a little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to sleep:
verse	20	24	34	So shall thy poverty come as one that travelleth; and thy want as an armed man.
verse	20	25	1	@@These @9are@7 also proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out.
verse	20	25	2	@@@9It is@7 the glory of God to conceal a thing: but the honour of kings @9is@7 to search out a matter.
verse	20	25	3	@@The heaven for height, and the earth for depth, and the heart of kings @9is@7 unsearchable.
verse	20	25	4	Take away the dross from the silver, and there shall come forth a vessel for the finer.
verse	20	25	5	@@Take away the wicked @9from@7 before the king, and his throne shall be established in righteousness.
verse	20	25	6	@@Put not forth thyself in the presence of the king, and stand not in the place of great @9men: @7
verse	20	25	7	@@For better @9it is@7 that it be said unto thee, Come up hither; than that thou shouldest be put lower in the presence of the prince whom thine eyes have seen.
verse	20	25	8	@@Go not forth hastily to strive, lest @9thou know not@7 what to do in the end thereof, when thy neighbour hath put thee to shame.
verse	20	25	9	@@Debate thy cause with thy neighbour @9himself;@7 and discover not a secret to another:
verse	20	25	10	@@Lest he that heareth @9it@7 put thee to shame, and thine infamy turn not away.
verse	20	25	11	@@A word fitly spoken @9is like@7 apples of gold in pictures of silver.
verse	20	25	12	@@@9As@7 an earring of gold, and an ornament of fine gold, @9so is@7 a wise reprover upon an obedient ear.
verse	20	25	13	@@As the cold of snow in the time of harvest, @9so is@7 a faithful messenger to them that send him: for he refresheth the soul of his masters.
verse	20	25	14	@@Whoso boasteth himself of a false gift @9is like@7 clouds and wind without rain.
verse	20	25	15	By long forbearing is a prince persuaded, and a soft tongue breaketh the bone.
verse	20	25	16	Hast thou found honey? eat so much as is sufficient for thee, lest thou be filled therewith, and vomit it.
verse	20	25	17	@@Withdraw thy foot from thy neighbour's house; lest he be weary of thee, and @9so@7 hate thee.
verse	20	25	18	@@A man that beareth false witness against his neighbour @9is@7 a maul, and a sword, and a sharp arrow.
verse	20	25	19	@@Confidence in an unfaithful man in time of trouble @9is like@7 a broken tooth, and a foot out of joint.
verse	20	25	20	@@@9As@7 he that taketh away a garment in cold weather, @9and as@7 vinegar upon nitre, so @9is@7 he that singeth songs to an heavy heart.
verse	20	25	21	If thine enemy be hungry, give him bread to eat; and if he be thirsty, give him water to drink:
verse	20	25	22	For thou shalt heap coals of fire upon his head, and the LORD shall reward thee.
verse	20	25	23	@@The north wind driveth away rain: so @9doth@7 an angry countenance a backbiting tongue.
verse	20	25	24	@@@9It is@7 better to dwell in the corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman and in a wide house.
verse	20	25	25	@@@9As@7 cold waters to a thirsty soul, so @9is@7 good news from a far country.
verse	20	25	26	@@A righteous man falling down before the wicked @9is as@7 a troubled fountain, and a corrupt spring.
verse	20	25	27	@@@9It is @7not good to eat much honey: so @9for men @7to search their own glory @9is not @7glory.
verse	20	25	28	@@He that @9hath@7 no rule over his own spirit @9is like@7 a city @9that is@7 broken down, @9and@7 without walls.
verse	20	26	1	As snow in summer, and as rain in harvest, so honour is not seemly for a fool.
verse	20	26	2	As the bird by wandering, as the swallow by flying, so the curse causeless shall not come.
verse	20	26	3	A whip for the horse, a bridle for the ass, and a rod for the fool's back.
verse	20	26	4	Answer not a fool according to his folly, lest thou also be like unto him.
verse	20	26	5	Answer a fool according to his folly, lest he be wise in his own conceit.
verse	20	26	6	@@He that sendeth a message by the hand of a fool cutteth off the feet, @9and@7 drinketh damage.
verse	20	26	7	@@The legs of the lame are not equal: so @9is@7 a parable in the mouth of fools.
verse	20	26	8	@@As he that bindeth a stone in a sling, so @9is@7 he that giveth honour to a fool.
verse	20	26	9	@@@9As@7 a thorn goeth up into the hand of a drunkard, so @9is@7 a parable in the mouth of fools.
verse	20	26	10	@@The great @9God@7 that formed all @9things@7 both rewardeth the fool, and rewardeth transgressors.
verse	20	26	11	@@As a dog returneth to his vomit, @9so@7 a fool returneth to his folly.
verse	20	26	12	@@Seest thou a man wise in his own conceit? @9there is@7 more hope of a fool than of him.
verse	20	26	13	@@The slothful @9man@7 saith, @9There is@7 a lion in the way; a lion @9is@7 in the streets.
verse	20	26	14	@@@9As@7 the door turneth upon his hinges, so @9doth@7 the slothful upon his bed.
verse	20	26	15	@@The slothful hideth his hand in @9his@7 bosom; it grieveth him to bring it again to his mouth.
verse	20	26	16	@@The sluggard @9is@7 wiser in his own conceit than seven men that can render a reason.
verse	20	26	17	@@He that passeth by, @9and@7 meddleth with strife @9belonging@7 not to him, @9is like@7 one that taketh a dog by the ears.
verse	20	26	18	@@As a mad @9man@7 who casteth firebrands, arrows, and death,
verse	20	26	19	@@So @9is@7 the man @9that@7 deceiveth his neighbour, and saith, Am not I in sport?
verse	20	26	20	@@Where no wood is, @9there@7 the fire goeth out: so where @9there is@7 no talebearer, the strife ceaseth.
verse	20	26	21	@@@9As@7 coals @9are@7 to burning coals, and wood to fire; so @9is@7 a contentious man to kindle strife.
verse	20	26	22	@@The words of a talebearer @9are@7 as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.
verse	20	26	23	@@Burning lips and a wicked heart @9are like@7 a potsherd covered with silver dross.
verse	20	26	24	He that hateth dissembleth with his lips, and layeth up deceit within him;
verse	20	26	25	@@When he speaketh fair, believe him not: for @9there are@7 seven abominations in his heart.
verse	20	26	26	@@@9Whose@7 hatred is covered by deceit, his wickedness shall be shewed before the @9whole@7 congregation.
verse	20	26	27	Whoso diggeth a pit shall fall therein: and he that rolleth a stone, it will return upon him.
verse	20	26	28	@@A lying tongue hateth @9those that are@7 afflicted by it; and a flattering mouth worketh ruin.
verse	20	27	1	Boast not thyself of to morrow; for thou knowest not what a day may bring forth.
verse	20	27	2	Let another man praise thee, and not thine own mouth; a stranger, and not thine own lips.
verse	20	27	3	@@A stone @9is@7 heavy, and the sand weighty; but a fool's wrath @9is@7 heavier than them both.
verse	20	27	4	@@Wrath @9is@7 cruel, and anger @9is@7 outrageous; but who @9is@7 able to stand before envy?
verse	20	27	5	@@Open rebuke @9is@7 better than secret love.
verse	20	27	6	@@Faithful @9are@7 the wounds of a friend; but the kisses of an enemy @9are@7 deceitful.
verse	20	27	7	The full soul loatheth an honeycomb; but to the hungry soul every bitter thing is sweet.
verse	20	27	8	@@As a bird that wandereth from her nest, so @9is@7 a man that wandereth from his place.
verse	20	27	9	@@Ointment and perfume rejoice the heart: so @9doth@7 the sweetness of a man's friend by hearty counsel.
verse	20	27	10	@@Thine own friend, and thy father's friend, forsake not; neither go into thy brother's house in the day of thy calamity: @9for@7 better @9is@7 a neighbour @9that is@7 near than a brother far off.
verse	20	27	11	My son, be wise, and make my heart glad, that I may answer him that reproacheth me.
verse	20	27	12	@@A prudent @9man@7 foreseeth the evil, @9and@7 hideth himself; @9but@7 the simple pass on, @9and@7 are punished.
verse	20	27	13	Take his garment that is surety for a stranger, and take a pledge of him for a strange woman.
verse	20	27	14	He that blesseth his friend with a loud voice, rising early in the morning, it shall be counted a curse to him.
verse	20	27	15	A continual dropping in a very rainy day and a contentious woman are alike.
verse	20	27	16	@@Whosoever hideth her hideth the wind, and the ointment of his right hand, @9which@7 bewrayeth @9itself. @7
verse	20	27	17	Iron sharpeneth iron; so a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend.
verse	20	27	18	Whoso keepeth the fig tree shall eat the fruit thereof: so he that waiteth on his master shall be honoured.
verse	20	27	19	@@As in water face @9answereth@7 to face, so the heart of man to man.
verse	20	27	20	Hell and destruction are never full; so the eyes of man are never satisfied.
verse	20	27	21	@@@9As@7 the fining pot for silver, and the furnace for gold; so @9is@7 a man to his praise.
verse	20	27	22	@@Though thou shouldest bray a fool in a mortar among wheat with a pestle, @9yet@7 will not his foolishness depart from him.
verse	20	27	23	@@Be thou diligent to know the state of thy flocks, @9and@7 look well to thy herds.
verse	20	27	24	@@For riches @9are@7 not for ever: and doth the crown @9endure@7 to every generation?
verse	20	27	25	The hay appeareth, and the tender grass sheweth itself, and herbs of the mountains are gathered.
verse	20	27	26	@@The lambs @9are@7 for thy clothing, and the goats @9are@7 the price of the field.
verse	20	27	27	@@And @9thou shalt have@7 goats' milk enough for thy food, for the food of thy household, and @9for@7 the maintenance for thy maidens.
verse	20	28	1	The wicked flee when no man pursueth: but the righteous are bold as a lion.
verse	20	28	2	@@For the transgression of a land many @9are@7 the princes thereof: but by a man of understanding @9and@7 knowledge the state @9thereof@7 shall be prolonged.
verse	20	28	3	@@A poor man that oppresseth the poor @9is like@7 a sweeping rain which leaveth no food.
verse	20	28	4	They that forsake the law praise the wicked: but such as keep the law contend with them.
verse	20	28	5	@@Evil men understand not judgment: but they that seek the LORD understand all @9things. @7
verse	20	28	6	@@Better @9is@7 the poor that walketh in his uprightness, than @9he that is@7 perverse @9in his@7 ways, though he @9be@7 rich.
verse	20	28	7	@@Whoso keepeth the law @9is@7 a wise son: but he that is a companion of riotous @9men@7 shameth his father.
verse	20	28	8	He that by usury and unjust gain increaseth his substance, he shall gather it for him that will pity the poor.
verse	20	28	9	@@He that turneth away his ear from hearing the law, even his prayer @9shall be@7 abomination.
verse	20	28	10	@@Whoso causeth the righteous to go astray in an evil way, he shall fall himself into his own pit: but the upright shall have good @9things@7 in possession.
verse	20	28	11	@@The rich man @9is@7 wise in his own conceit; but the poor that hath understanding searcheth him out.
verse	20	28	12	@@When righteous @9men@7 do rejoice, @9there is@7 great glory: but when the wicked rise, a man is hidden.
verse	20	28	13	@@He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh @9them@7 shall have mercy.
verse	20	28	14	@@Happy @9is@7 the man that feareth alway: but he that hardeneth his heart shall fall into mischief.
verse	20	28	15	@@@9As@7 a roaring lion, and a ranging bear; @9so is@7 a wicked ruler over the poor people.
verse	20	28	16	@@The prince that wanteth understanding @9is@7 also a great oppressor: @9but@7 he that hateth covetousness shall prolong @9his@7 days.
verse	20	28	17	@@A man that doeth violence to the blood of @9any@7 person shall flee to the pit; let no man stay him.
verse	20	28	18	@@Whoso walketh uprightly shall be saved: but @9he that is@7 perverse @9in his@7 ways shall fall at once.
verse	20	28	19	@@He that tilleth his land shall have plenty of bread: but he that followeth after vain @9persons@7 shall have poverty enough.
verse	20	28	20	A faithful man shall abound with blessings: but he that maketh haste to be rich shall not be innocent.
verse	20	28	21	@@To have respect of persons @9is@7 not good: for for a piece of bread @9that@7 man will transgress.
verse	20	28	22	@@He that hasteth to be rich @9hath@7 an evil eye, and considereth not that poverty shall come upon him.
verse	20	28	23	He that rebuketh a man afterwards shall find more favour than he that flattereth with the tongue.
verse	20	28	24	@@Whoso robbeth his father or his mother, and saith, @9It is@7 no transgression; the same @9is@7 the companion of a destroyer.
verse	20	28	25	He that is of a proud heart stirreth up strife: but he that putteth his trust in the LORD shall be made fat.
verse	20	28	26	He that trusteth in his own heart is a fool: but whoso walketh wisely, he shall be delivered.
verse	20	28	27	He that giveth unto the poor shall not lack: but he that hideth his eyes shall have many a curse.
verse	20	28	28	When the wicked rise, men hide themselves: but when they perish, the righteous increase.
verse	20	29	1	@@He, that being often reproved hardeneth @9his@7 neck, shall suddenly be destroyed, and that without remedy.
verse	20	29	2	When the righteous are in authority, the people rejoice: but when the wicked beareth rule, the people mourn.
verse	20	29	3	@@Whoso loveth wisdom rejoiceth his father: but he that keepeth company with harlots spendeth @9his@7 substance.
verse	20	29	4	The king by judgment establisheth the land: but he that receiveth gifts overthroweth it.
verse	20	29	5	A man that flattereth his neighbour spreadeth a net for his feet.
verse	20	29	6	@@In the transgression of an evil man @9there is@7 a snare: but the righteous doth sing and rejoice.
verse	20	29	7	@@The righteous considereth the cause of the poor: @9but@7 the wicked regardeth not to know @9it. @7
verse	20	29	8	@@Scornful men bring a city into a snare: but wise @9men@7 turn away wrath.
verse	20	29	9	@@@9If@7 a wise man contendeth with a foolish man, whether he rage or laugh, @9there is@7 no rest.
verse	20	29	10	The bloodthirsty hate the upright: but the just seek his soul.
verse	20	29	11	@@A fool uttereth all his mind: but a wise @9man@7 keepeth it in till afterwards.
verse	20	29	12	@@If a ruler hearken to lies, all his servants @9are@7 wicked.
verse	20	29	13	The poor and the deceitful man meet together: the LORD lighteneth both their eyes.
verse	20	29	14	The king that faithfully judgeth the poor, his throne shall be established for ever.
verse	20	29	15	@@The rod and reproof give wisdom: but a child left @9to himself@7 bringeth his mother to shame.
verse	20	29	16	When the wicked are multiplied, transgression increaseth: but the righteous shall see their fall.
verse	20	29	17	Correct thy son, and he shall give thee rest; yea, he shall give delight unto thy soul.
verse	20	29	18	@@Where @9there is@7 no vision, the people perish: but he that keepeth the law, happy @9is@7 he.
verse	20	29	19	A servant will not be corrected by words: for though he understand he will not answer.
verse	20	29	20	@@Seest thou a man @9that is@7 hasty in his words? @9there is@7 more hope of a fool than of him.
verse	20	29	21	@@He that delicately bringeth up his servant from a child shall have him become @9his@7 son at the length.
verse	20	29	22	An angry man stirreth up strife, and a furious man aboundeth in transgression.
verse	20	29	23	A man's pride shall bring him low: but honour shall uphold the humble in spirit.
verse	20	29	24	@@Whoso is partner with a thief hateth his own soul: he heareth cursing, and bewrayeth @9it@7 not.
verse	20	29	25	The fear of man bringeth a snare: but whoso putteth his trust in the LORD shall be safe.
verse	20	29	26	@@Many seek the ruler's favour; but @9every@7 man's judgment @9cometh@7 from the LORD.
verse	20	29	27	@@An unjust man @9is@7 an abomination to the just: and @9he that is@7 upright in the way @9is@7 abomination to the wicked.
verse	20	30	1	@@The words of Agur the son of Jakeh, @9even@7 the prophecy: the man spake unto Ithiel, even unto Ithiel and Ucal,
verse	20	30	2	@@Surely I @9am@7 more brutish than @9any@7 man, and have not the understanding of a man.
verse	20	30	3	I neither learned wisdom, nor have the knowledge of the holy.
verse	20	30	4	@@Who hath ascended up into heaven, or descended? who hath gathered the wind in his fists? who hath bound the waters in a garment? who hath established all the ends of the earth? what @9is@7 his name, and what @9is@7 his son's name, if thou canst tell?
verse	20	30	5	@@Every word of God @9is@7 pure: he @9is@7 a shield unto them that put their trust in him.
verse	20	30	6	Add thou not unto his words, lest he reprove thee, and thou be found a liar.
verse	20	30	7	@@Two @9things@7 have I required of thee; deny me @9them@7 not before I die:
verse	20	30	8	Remove far from me vanity and lies: give me neither poverty nor riches; feed me with food convenient for me:
verse	20	30	9	@@Lest I be full, and deny @9thee,@7 and say, Who @9is@7 the LORD? or lest I be poor, and steal, and take the name of my God @9in vain. @7
verse	20	30	10	Accuse not a servant unto his master, lest he curse thee, and thou be found guilty.
verse	20	30	11	@@@9There is@7 a generation @9that@7 curseth their father, and doth not bless their mother.
verse	20	30	12	@@@9There is@7 a generation @9that are@7 pure in their own eyes, and @9yet@7 is not washed from their filthiness.
verse	20	30	13	@@@9There is@7 a generation, O how lofty are their eyes! and their eyelids are lifted up.
verse	20	30	14	@@@9There is@7 a generation, whose teeth @9are as@7 swords, and their jaw teeth @9as@7 knives, to devour the poor from off the earth, and the needy from @9among@7 men.
verse	20	30	15	@@The horseleach hath two daughters, @9crying,@7 Give, give. There are three @9things that are@7 never satisfied, @9yea,@7 four @9things@7 say not, @9It is@7 enough:
verse	20	30	16	@@The grave; and the barren womb; the earth @9that@7 is not filled with water; and the fire @9that@7 saith not, @9It is@7 enough.
verse	20	30	17	@@The eye @9that@7 mocketh at @9his@7 father, and despiseth to obey @9his@7 mother, the ravens of the valley shall pick it out, and the young eagles shall eat it.
verse	20	30	18	@@There be three @9things which@7 are too wonderful for me, yea, four which I know not:
verse	20	30	19	The way of an eagle in the air; the way of a serpent upon a rock; the way of a ship in the midst of the sea; and the way of a man with a maid.
verse	20	30	20	@@Such @9is@7 the way of an adulterous woman; she eateth, and wipeth her mouth, and saith, I have done no wickedness.
verse	20	30	21	@@For three @9things@7 the earth is disquieted, and for four @9which@7 it cannot bear:
verse	20	30	22	For a servant when he reigneth; and a fool when he is filled with meat;
verse	20	30	23	@@For an odious @9woman@7 when she is married; and an handmaid that is heir to her mistress.
verse	20	30	24	@@There be four @9things which are@7 little upon the earth, but they @9are@7 exceeding wise:
verse	20	30	25	@@The ants @9are@7 a people not strong, yet they prepare their meat in the summer;
verse	20	30	26	@@The conies @9are but@7 a feeble folk, yet make they their houses in the rocks;
verse	20	30	27	The locusts have no king, yet go they forth all of them by bands;
verse	20	30	28	The spider taketh hold with her hands, and is in kings' palaces.
verse	20	30	29	@@There be three @9things@7 which go well, yea, four are comely in going:
verse	20	30	30	@@A lion @9which is@7 strongest among beasts, and turneth not away for any;
verse	20	30	31	@@A greyhound; an he goat also; and a king, against whom @9there is@7 no rising up.
verse	20	30	32	@@If thou hast done foolishly in lifting up thyself, or if thou hast thought evil, @9lay@7 thine hand upon thy mouth.
verse	20	30	33	Surely the churning of milk bringeth forth butter, and the wringing of the nose bringeth forth blood: so the forcing of wrath bringeth forth strife.
verse	20	31	1	The words of king Lemuel, the prophecy that his mother taught him.
verse	20	31	2	What, my son? and what, the son of my womb? and what, the son of my vows?
verse	20	31	3	Give not thy strength unto women, nor thy ways to that which destroyeth kings.
verse	20	31	4	@@@9It is@7 not for kings, O Lemuel, @9it is@7 not for kings to drink wine; nor for princes strong drink:
verse	20	31	5	Lest they drink, and forget the law, and pervert the judgment of any of the afflicted.
verse	20	31	6	Give strong drink unto him that is ready to perish, and wine unto those that be of heavy hearts.
verse	20	31	7	Let him drink, and forget his poverty, and remember his misery no more.
verse	20	31	8	Open thy mouth for the dumb in the cause of all such as are appointed to destruction.
verse	20	31	9	Open thy mouth, judge righteously, and plead the cause of the poor and needy.
verse	20	31	10	@@Who can find a virtuous woman? for her price @9is@7 far above rubies.
verse	20	31	11	The heart of her husband doth safely trust in her, so that he shall have no need of spoil.
verse	20	31	12	She will do him good and not evil all the days of her life.
verse	20	31	13	She seeketh wool, and flax, and worketh willingly with her hands.
verse	20	31	14	She is like the merchants' ships; she bringeth her food from afar.
verse	20	31	15	She riseth also while it is yet night, and giveth meat to her household, and a portion to her maidens.
verse	20	31	16	She considereth a field, and buyeth it: with the fruit of her hands she planteth a vineyard.
verse	20	31	17	She girdeth her loins with strength, and strengtheneth her arms.
verse	20	31	18	@@She perceiveth that her merchandise @9is@7 good: her candle goeth not out by night.
verse	20	31	19	She layeth her hands to the spindle, and her hands hold the distaff.
verse	20	31	20	She stretcheth out her hand to the poor; yea, she reacheth forth her hands to the needy.
verse	20	31	21	@@She is not afraid of the snow for her household: for all her household @9are@7 clothed with scarlet.
verse	20	31	22	@@She maketh herself coverings of tapestry; her clothing @9is@7 silk and purple.
verse	20	31	23	Her husband is known in the gates, when he sitteth among the elders of the land.
verse	20	31	24	@@She maketh fine linen, and selleth @9it;@7 and delivereth girdles unto the merchant.
verse	20	31	25	@@Strength and honour @9are@7 her clothing; and she shall rejoice in time to come.
verse	20	31	26	@@She openeth her mouth with wisdom; and in her tongue @9is@7 the law of kindness.
verse	20	31	27	She looketh well to the ways of her household, and eateth not the bread of idleness.
verse	20	31	28	@@Her children arise up, and call her blessed; her husband @9also,@7 and he praiseth her.
verse	20	31	29	Many daughters have done virtuously, but thou excellest them all.
verse	20	31	30	@@Favour @9is@7 deceitful, and beauty @9is@7 vain: @9but@7 a woman @9that@7 feareth the LORD, she shall be praised.
verse	20	31	31	Give her of the fruit of her hands; and let her own works praise her in the gates.
verse	21	1	1	The words of the Preacher, the son of David, king in Jerusalem.
verse	21	1	2	@@Vanity of vanities, saith the Preacher, vanity of vanities; all @9is@7 vanity.
verse	21	1	3	What profit hath a man of all his labour which he taketh under the sun?
verse	21	1	4	@@@9One@7 generation passeth away, and @9another@7 generation cometh: but the earth abideth for ever.
verse	21	1	5	The sun also ariseth, and the sun goeth down, and hasteth to his place where he arose.
verse	21	1	6	The wind goeth toward the south, and turneth about unto the north; it whirleth about continually, and the wind returneth again according to his circuits.
verse	21	1	7	@@All the rivers run into the sea; yet the sea @9is@7 not full; unto the place from whence the rivers come, thither they return again.
verse	21	1	8	@@All things @9are@7 full of labour; man cannot utter @9it:@7 the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing.
verse	21	1	9	@@The thing that hath been, it @9is that@7 which shall be; and that which is done @9is@7 that which shall be done: and @9there is@7 no new @9thing@7 under the sun.
verse	21	1	10	@@Is there @9any@7 thing whereof it may be said, See, this @9is@7 new? it hath been already of old time, which was before us.
verse	21	1	11	@@@9There is@7 no remembrance of former @9things;@7 neither shall there be @9any@7 remembrance of @9things@7 that are to come with @9those@7 that shall come after.
verse	21	1	12	I the Preacher was king over Israel in Jerusalem.
verse	21	1	13	@@And I gave my heart to seek and search out by wisdom concerning all @9things@7 that are done under heaven: this sore travail hath God given to the sons of man to be exercised therewith.
verse	21	1	14	@@I have seen all the works that are done under the sun; and, behold, all @9is@7 vanity and vexation of spirit.
verse	21	1	15	@@@9That which is@7 crooked cannot be made straight: and that which is wanting cannot be numbered.
verse	21	1	16	@@I communed with mine own heart, saying, Lo, I am come to great estate, and have gotten more wisdom than all @9they@7 that have been before me in Jerusalem: yea, my heart had great experience of wisdom and knowledge.
verse	21	1	17	And I gave my heart to know wisdom, and to know madness and folly: I perceived that this also is vexation of spirit.
verse	21	1	18	@@For in much wisdom @9is@7 much grief: and he that increaseth knowledge increaseth sorrow.
verse	21	2	1	@@I said in mine heart, Go to now, I will prove thee with mirth, therefore enjoy pleasure: and, behold, this also @9is@7 vanity.
verse	21	2	2	@@I said of laughter, @9It is@7 mad: and of mirth, What doeth it?
verse	21	2	3	@@I sought in mine heart to give myself unto wine, yet acquainting mine heart with wisdom; and to lay hold on folly, till I might see what @9was@7 that good for the sons of men, which they should do under the heaven all the days of their life.
verse	21	2	4	I made me great works; I builded me houses; I planted me vineyards:
verse	21	2	5	@@I made me gardens and orchards, and I planted trees in them of all @9kind of@7 fruits:
verse	21	2	6	I made me pools of water, to water therewith the wood that bringeth forth trees:
verse	21	2	7	@@I got @9me@7 servants and maidens, and had servants born in my house; also I had great possessions of great and small cattle above all that were in Jerusalem before me:
verse	21	2	8	@@I gathered me also silver and gold, and the peculiar treasure of kings and of the provinces: I gat me men singers and women singers, and the delights of the sons of men, @9as@7 musical instruments, and that of all sorts.
verse	21	2	9	So I was great, and increased more than all that were before me in Jerusalem: also my wisdom remained with me.
verse	21	2	10	And whatsoever mine eyes desired I kept not from them, I withheld not my heart from any joy; for my heart rejoiced in all my labour: and this was my portion of all my labour.
verse	21	2	11	@@Then I looked on all the works that my hands had wrought, and on the labour that I had laboured to do: and, behold, all @9was@7 vanity and vexation of spirit, and @9there was@7 no profit under the sun.
verse	21	2	12	@@And I turned myself to behold wisdom, and madness, and folly: for what @9can@7 the man @9do@7 that cometh after the king? @9even@7 that which hath been already done.
verse	21	2	13	Then I saw that wisdom excelleth folly, as far as light excelleth darkness.
verse	21	2	14	@@The wise man's eyes @9are@7 in his head; but the fool walketh in darkness: and I myself perceived also that one event happeneth to them all.
verse	21	2	15	@@Then said I in my heart, As it happeneth to the fool, so it happeneth even to me; and why was I then more wise? Then I said in my heart, that this also @9is@7 vanity.
verse	21	2	16	@@For @9there is@7 no remembrance of the wise more than of the fool for ever; seeing that which now @9is@7 in the days to come shall all be forgotten. And how dieth the wise @9man?@7 as the fool.
verse	21	2	17	@@Therefore I hated life; because the work that is wrought under the sun is grievous unto me: for all @9is@7 vanity and vexation of spirit.
verse	21	2	18	Yea, I hated all my labour which I had taken under the sun: because I should leave it unto the man that shall be after me.
verse	21	2	19	@@And who knoweth whether he shall be a wise @9man@7 or a fool? yet shall he have rule over all my labour wherein I have laboured, and wherein I have shewed myself wise under the sun. This @9is@7 also vanity.
verse	21	2	20	Therefore I went about to cause my heart to despair of all the labour which I took under the sun.
verse	21	2	21	@@For there is a man whose labour @9is@7 in wisdom, and in knowledge, and in equity; yet to a man that hath not laboured therein shall he leave it @9for@7 his portion. This also @9is@7 vanity and a great evil.
verse	21	2	22	For what hath man of all his labour, and of the vexation of his heart, wherein he hath laboured under the sun?
verse	21	2	23	@@For all his days @9are@7 sorrows, and his travail grief; yea, his heart taketh not rest in the night. This is also vanity.
verse	21	2	24	@@@9There is@7 nothing better for a man, @9than@7 that he should eat and drink, and @9that@7 he should make his soul enjoy good in his labour. This also I saw, that it @9was@7 from the hand of God.
verse	21	2	25	@@For who can eat, or who else can hasten @9hereunto,@7 more than I?
verse	21	2	26	@@For @9God@7 giveth to a man that @9is@7 good in his sight wisdom, and knowledge, and joy: but to the sinner he giveth travail, to gather and to heap up, that he may give to @9him that is@7 good before God. This also @9is@7 vanity and vexation of spirit.
verse	21	3	1	@@To every @9thing there is@7 a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven:
verse	21	3	2	@@A time to be born, and a time to die; a time to plant, and a time to pluck up @9that which is@7 planted;
verse	21	3	3	A time to kill, and a time to heal; a time to break down, and a time to build up;
verse	21	3	4	A time to weep, and a time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to dance;
verse	21	3	5	A time to cast away stones, and a time to gather stones together; a time to embrace, and a time to refrain from embracing;
verse	21	3	6	A time to get, and a time to lose; a time to keep, and a time to cast away;
verse	21	3	7	A time to rend, and a time to sew; a time to keep silence, and a time to speak;
verse	21	3	8	A time to love, and a time to hate; a time of war, and a time of peace.
verse	21	3	9	What profit hath he that worketh in that wherein he laboureth?
verse	21	3	10	I have seen the travail, which God hath given to the sons of men to be exercised in it.
verse	21	3	11	@@He hath made every @9thing@7 beautiful in his time: also he hath set the world in their heart, so that no man can find out the work that God maketh from the beginning to the end.
verse	21	3	12	@@I know that @9there is@7 no good in them, but for @9a man@7 to rejoice, and to do good in his life.
verse	21	3	13	@@And also that every man should eat and drink, and enjoy the good of all his labour, it @9is@7 the gift of God.
verse	21	3	14	@@I know that, whatsoever God doeth, it shall be for ever: nothing can be put to it, nor any thing taken from it: and God doeth @9it,@7 that @9men@7 should fear before him.
verse	21	3	15	That which hath been is now; and that which is to be hath already been; and God requireth that which is past.
verse	21	3	16	@@And moreover I saw under the sun the place of judgment, @9that@7 wickedness @9was@7 there; and the place of righteousness, @9that@7 iniquity @9was@7 there.
verse	21	3	17	@@I said in mine heart, God shall judge the righteous and the wicked: for @9there is@7 a time there for every purpose and for every work.
verse	21	3	18	I said in mine heart concerning the estate of the sons of men, that God might manifest them, and that they might see that they themselves are beasts.
verse	21	3	19	@@For that which befalleth the sons of men befalleth beasts; even one thing befalleth them: as the one dieth, so dieth the other; yea, they have all one breath; so that a man hath no preeminence above a beast: for all @9is@7 vanity.
verse	21	3	20	All go unto one place; all are of the dust, and all turn to dust again.
verse	21	3	21	Who knoweth the spirit of man that goeth upward, and the spirit of the beast that goeth downward to the earth?
verse	21	3	22	@@Wherefore I perceive that @9there is@7 nothing better, than that a man should rejoice in his own works; for that @9is@7 his portion: for who shall bring him to see what shall be after him?
verse	21	4	1	@@So I returned, and considered all the oppressions that are done under the sun: and behold the tears of @9such as were@7 oppressed, and they had no comforter; and on the side of their oppressors @9there was@7 power; but they had no comforter.
verse	21	4	2	Wherefore I praised the dead which are already dead more than the living which are yet alive.
verse	21	4	3	@@Yea, better @9is he@7 than both they, which hath not yet been, who hath not seen the evil work that is done under the sun.
verse	21	4	4	@@Again, I considered all travail, and every right work, that for this a man is envied of his neighbour. This @9is@7 also vanity and vexation of spirit.
verse	21	4	5	The fool foldeth his hands together, and eateth his own flesh.
verse	21	4	6	@@Better @9is@7 an handful @9with@7 quietness, than both the hands full @9with@7 travail and vexation of spirit.
verse	21	4	7	Then I returned, and I saw vanity under the sun.
verse	21	4	8	@@There is one @9alone,@7 and @9there is@7 not a second; yea, he hath neither child nor brother: yet @9is there@7 no end of all his labour; neither is his eye satisfied with riches; neither @9saith he,@7 For whom do I labour, and bereave my soul of good? This @9is@7 also vanity, yea, it @9is@7 a sore travail.
verse	21	4	9	@@Two @9are@7 better than one; because they have a good reward for their labour.
verse	21	4	10	@@For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow: but woe to him @9that is@7 alone when he falleth; for @9he hath@7 not another to help him up.
verse	21	4	11	@@Again, if two lie together, then they have heat: but how can one be warm @9alone? @7
verse	21	4	12	And if one prevail against him, two shall withstand him; and a threefold cord is not quickly broken.
verse	21	4	13	@@Better @9is@7 a poor and a wise child than an old and foolish king, who will no more be admonished.
verse	21	4	14	@@For out of prison he cometh to reign; whereas also @9he that is@7 born in his kingdom becometh poor.
verse	21	4	15	I considered all the living which walk under the sun, with the second child that shall stand up in his stead.
verse	21	4	16	@@@9There is@7 no end of all the people, @9even@7 of all that have been before them: they also that come after shall not rejoice in him. Surely this also @9is@7 vanity and vexation of spirit.
verse	21	5	1	Keep thy foot when thou goest to the house of God, and be more ready to hear, than to give the sacrifice of fools: for they consider not that they do evil.
verse	21	5	2	@@Be not rash with thy mouth, and let not thine heart be hasty to utter @9any@7 thing before God: for God @9is@7 in heaven, and thou upon earth: therefore let thy words be few.
verse	21	5	3	@@For a dream cometh through the multitude of business; and a fool's voice @9is known@7 by multitude of words.
verse	21	5	4	@@When thou vowest a vow unto God, defer not to pay it; for @9he hath@7 no pleasure in fools: pay that which thou hast vowed.
verse	21	5	5	@@Better @9is it@7 that thou shouldest not vow, than that thou shouldest vow and not pay.
verse	21	5	6	@@Suffer not thy mouth to cause thy flesh to sin; neither say thou before the angel, that it @9was@7 an error: wherefore should God be angry at thy voice, and destroy the work of thine hands?
verse	21	5	7	@@For in the multitude of dreams and many words @9there are@7 also @9divers@7 vanities: but fear thou God.
verse	21	5	8	@@If thou seest the oppression of the poor, and violent perverting of judgment and justice in a province, marvel not at the matter: for @9he that is@7 higher than the highest regardeth; and @9there be@7 higher than they.
verse	21	5	9	@@Moreover the profit of the earth is for all: the king @9himself@7 is served by the field.
verse	21	5	10	@@He that loveth silver shall not be satisfied with silver; nor he that loveth abundance with increase: this @9is@7 also vanity.
verse	21	5	11	@@When goods increase, they are increased that eat them: and what good @9is there@7 to the owners thereof, saving the beholding @9of them@7 with their eyes?
verse	21	5	12	@@The sleep of a labouring man @9is@7 sweet, whether he eat little or much: but the abundance of the rich will not suffer him to sleep.
verse	21	5	13	@@There is a sore evil @9which@7 I have seen under the sun, @9namely,@7 riches kept for the owners thereof to their hurt.
verse	21	5	14	@@But those riches perish by evil travail: and he begetteth a son, and @9there is@7 nothing in his hand.
verse	21	5	15	As he came forth of his mother's womb, naked shall he return to go as he came, and shall take nothing of his labour, which he may carry away in his hand.
verse	21	5	16	@@And this also @9is@7 a sore evil, @9that@7 in all points as he came, so shall he go: and what profit hath he that hath laboured for the wind?
verse	21	5	17	@@All his days also he eateth in darkness, and @9he hath@7 much sorrow and wrath with his sickness.
verse	21	5	18	@@Behold @9that@7 which I have seen: @9it is@7 good and comely @9for one@7 to eat and to drink, and to enjoy the good of all his labour that he taketh under the sun all the days of his life, which God giveth him: for it @9is@7 his portion.
verse	21	5	19	@@Every man also to whom God hath given riches and wealth, and hath given him power to eat thereof, and to take his portion, and to rejoice in his labour; this @9is@7 the gift of God.
verse	21	5	20	@@For he shall not much remember the days of his life; because God answereth @9him@7 in the joy of his heart.
verse	21	6	1	@@There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, and it @9is@7 common among men:
verse	21	6	2	@@A man to whom God hath given riches, wealth, and honour, so that he wanteth nothing for his soul of all that he desireth, yet God giveth him not power to eat thereof, but a stranger eateth it: this @9is@7 vanity, and it @9is@7 an evil disease.
verse	21	6	3	@@If a man beget an hundred @9children,@7 and live many years, so that the days of his years be many, and his soul be not filled with good, and also @9that@7 he have no burial; I say, @9that@7 an untimely birth @9is@7 better than he.
verse	21	6	4	For he cometh in with vanity, and departeth in darkness, and his name shall be covered with darkness.
verse	21	6	5	@@Moreover he hath not seen the sun, nor known @9any thing:@7 this hath more rest than the other.
verse	21	6	6	@@Yea, though he live a thousand years twice @9told,@7 yet hath he seen no good: do not all go to one place?
verse	21	6	7	@@All the labour of man @9is@7 for his mouth, and yet the appetite is not filled.
verse	21	6	8	For what hath the wise more than the fool? what hath the poor, that knoweth to walk before the living?
verse	21	6	9	@@Better @9is@7 the sight of the eyes than the wandering of the desire: this @9is@7 also vanity and vexation of spirit.
verse	21	6	10	@@That which hath been is named already, and it is known that it @9is@7 man: neither may he contend with him that is mightier than he.
verse	21	6	11	@@Seeing there be many things that increase vanity, what @9is@7 man the better?
verse	21	6	12	@@For who knoweth what @9is@7 good for man in @9this@7 life, all the days of his vain life which he spendeth as a shadow? for who can tell a man what shall be after him under the sun?
verse	21	7	1	@@A good name @9is@7 better than precious ointment; and the day of death than the day of one's birth.
verse	21	7	2	@@@9It is@7 better to go to the house of mourning, than to go to the house of feasting: for that is the end of all men; and the living will lay @9it@7 to his heart.
verse	21	7	3	@@Sorrow @9is@7 better than laughter: for by the sadness of the countenance the heart is made better.
verse	21	7	4	@@The heart of the wise @9is@7 in the house of mourning; but the heart of fools @9is@7 in the house of mirth.
verse	21	7	5	@@@9It is@7 better to hear the rebuke of the wise, than for a man to hear the song of fools.
verse	21	7	6	@@For as the crackling of thorns under a pot, so @9is@7 the laughter of the fool: this also @9is@7 vanity.
verse	21	7	7	Surely oppression maketh a wise man mad; and a gift destroyeth the heart.
verse	21	7	8	@@Better @9is@7 the end of a thing than the beginning thereof: @9and@7 the patient in spirit @9is@7 better than the proud in spirit.
verse	21	7	9	Be not hasty in thy spirit to be angry: for anger resteth in the bosom of fools.
verse	21	7	10	@@Say not thou, What is @9the cause@7 that the former days were better than these? for thou dost not enquire wisely concerning this.
verse	21	7	11	@@Wisdom @9is@7 good with an inheritance: and @9by it there is@7 profit to them that see the sun.
verse	21	7	12	@@For wisdom @9is@7 a defence, @9and@7 money @9is@7 a defence: but the excellency of knowledge @9is, that@7 wisdom giveth life to them that have it.
verse	21	7	13	@@Consider the work of God: for who can make @9that@7 straight, which he hath made crooked?
verse	21	7	14	In the day of prosperity be joyful, but in the day of adversity consider: God also hath set the one over against the other, to the end that man should find nothing after him.
verse	21	7	15	@@All @9things@7 have I seen in the days of my vanity: there is a just @9man@7 that perisheth in his righteousness, and there is a wicked @9man@7 that prolongeth @9his life@7 in his wickedness.
verse	21	7	16	Be not righteous over much; neither make thyself over wise: why shouldest thou destroy thyself?
verse	21	7	17	Be not over much wicked, neither be thou foolish: why shouldest thou die before thy time?
verse	21	7	18	@@@9It is@7 good that thou shouldest take hold of this; yea, also from this withdraw not thine hand: for he that feareth God shall come forth of them all.
verse	21	7	19	@@Wisdom strengtheneth the wise more than ten mighty @9men@7 which are in the city.
verse	21	7	20	@@For @9there is@7 not a just man upon earth, that doeth good, and sinneth not.
verse	21	7	21	Also take no heed unto all words that are spoken; lest thou hear thy servant curse thee:
verse	21	7	22	For oftentimes also thine own heart knoweth that thou thyself likewise hast cursed others.
verse	21	7	23	@@All this have I proved by wisdom: I said, I will be wise; but it @9was@7 far from me.
verse	21	7	24	That which is far off, and exceeding deep, who can find it out?
verse	21	7	25	@@I applied mine heart to know, and to search, and to seek out wisdom, and the reason @9of things,@7 and to know the wickedness of folly, even of foolishness @9and@7 madness:
verse	21	7	26	@@And I find more bitter than death the woman, whose heart @9is@7 snares and nets, @9and@7 her hands @9as@7 bands: whoso pleaseth God shall escape from her; but the sinner shall be taken by her.
verse	21	7	27	@@Behold, this have I found, saith the preacher, @9counting@7 one by one, to find out the account:
verse	21	7	28	Which yet my soul seeketh, but I find not: one man among a thousand have I found; but a woman among all those have I not found.
verse	21	7	29	Lo, this only have I found, that God hath made man upright; but they have sought out many inventions.
verse	21	8	1	@@Who @9is@7 as the wise @9man?@7 and who knoweth the interpretation of a thing? a man's wisdom maketh his face to shine, and the boldness of his face shall be changed.
verse	21	8	2	@@I @9counsel thee@7 to keep the king's commandment, and @9that@7 in regard of the oath of God.
verse	21	8	3	Be not hasty to go out of his sight: stand not in an evil thing; for he doeth whatsoever pleaseth him.
verse	21	8	4	@@Where the word of a king @9is, there is@7 power: and who may say unto him, What doest thou?
verse	21	8	5	Whoso keepeth the commandment shall feel no evil thing: and a wise man's heart discerneth both time and judgment.
verse	21	8	6	@@Because to every purpose there is time and judgment, therefore the misery of man @9is@7 great upon him.
verse	21	8	7	For he knoweth not that which shall be: for who can tell him when it shall be?
verse	21	8	8	@@@9There is@7 no man that hath power over the spirit to retain the spirit; neither @9hath he@7 power in the day of death: and @9there is@7 no discharge in @9that@7 war; neither shall wickedness deliver those that are given to it.
verse	21	8	9	@@All this have I seen, and applied my heart unto every work that is done under the sun: @9there is@7 a time wherein one man ruleth over another to his own hurt.
verse	21	8	10	@@And so I saw the wicked buried, who had come and gone from the place of the holy, and they were forgotten in the city where they had so done: this @9is@7 also vanity.
verse	21	8	11	Because sentence against an evil work is not executed speedily, therefore the heart of the sons of men is fully set in them to do evil.
verse	21	8	12	@@Though a sinner do evil an hundred times, and his @9days@7 be prolonged, yet surely I know that it shall be well with them that fear God, which fear before him:
verse	21	8	13	@@But it shall not be well with the wicked, neither shall he prolong @9his@7 days, @9which are@7 as a shadow; because he feareth not before God.
verse	21	8	14	@@There is a vanity which is done upon the earth; that there be just @9men,@7 unto whom it happeneth according to the work of the wicked; again, there be wicked @9men,@7 to whom it happeneth according to the work of the righteous: I said that this also @9is@7 vanity.
verse	21	8	15	Then I commended mirth, because a man hath no better thing under the sun, than to eat, and to drink, and to be merry: for that shall abide with him of his labour the days of his life, which God giveth him under the sun.
verse	21	8	16	@@When I applied mine heart to know wisdom, and to see the business that is done upon the earth: (for also @9there is that@7 neither day nor night seeth sleep with his eyes:)
verse	21	8	17	@@Then I beheld all the work of God, that a man cannot find out the work that is done under the sun: because though a man labour to seek @9it@7 out, yet he shall not find @9it;@7 yea further; though a wise @9man@7 think to know @9it,@7 yet shall he not be able to find @9it.@7
verse	21	9	1	@@For all this I considered in my heart even to declare all this, that the righteous, and the wise, and their works, are in the hand of God: no man knoweth either love or hatred @9by@7 all @9that is@7 before them.
verse	21	9	2	@@All @9things come@7 alike to all: @9there is@7 one event to the righteous, and to the wicked; to the good and to the clean, and to the unclean; to him that sacrificeth, and to him that sacrificeth not: as @9is@7 the good, so @9is@7 the sinner; @9and@7 he that sweareth, as @9he@7 that feareth an oath.
verse	21	9	3	@@This @9is@7 an evil among all @9things@7 that are done under the sun, that @9there is@7 one event unto all: yea, also the heart of the sons of men is full of evil, and madness is in their heart while they live, and after that @9they go@7 to the dead.
verse	21	9	4	For to him that is joined to all the living there is hope: for a living dog is better than a dead lion.
verse	21	9	5	For the living know that they shall die: but the dead know not any thing, neither have they any more a reward; for the memory of them is forgotten.
verse	21	9	6	@@Also their love, and their hatred, and their envy, is now perished; neither have they any more a portion for ever in any @9thing@7 that is done under the sun.
verse	21	9	7	Go thy way, eat thy bread with joy, and drink thy wine with a merry heart; for God now accepteth thy works.
verse	21	9	8	Let thy garments be always white; and let thy head lack no ointment.
verse	21	9	9	@@Live joyfully with the wife whom thou lovest all the days of the life of thy vanity, which he hath given thee under the sun, all the days of thy vanity: for that @9is@7 thy portion in @9this@7 life, and in thy labour which thou takest under the sun.
verse	21	9	10	@@Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do @9it@7 with thy might; for @9there is@7 no work, nor device, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in the grave, whither thou goest.
verse	21	9	11	@@I returned, and saw under the sun, that the race @9is@7 not to the swift, nor the battle to the strong, neither yet bread to the wise, nor yet riches to men of understanding, nor yet favour to men of skill; but time and chance happeneth to them all.
verse	21	9	12	@@For man also knoweth not his time: as the fishes that are taken in an evil net, and as the birds that are caught in the snare; so @9are@7 the sons of men snared in an evil time, when it falleth suddenly upon them.
verse	21	9	13	@@This wisdom have I seen also under the sun, and it @9seemed@7 great unto me:
verse	21	9	14	@@@9There was@7 a little city, and few men within it; and there came a great king against it, and besieged it, and built great bulwarks against it:
verse	21	9	15	Now there was found in it a poor wise man, and he by his wisdom delivered the city; yet no man remembered that same poor man.
verse	21	9	16	@@Then said I, Wisdom @9is@7 better than strength: nevertheless the poor man's wisdom @9is@7 despised, and his words are not heard.
verse	21	9	17	@@The words of wise @9men are@7 heard in quiet more than the cry of him that ruleth among fools.
verse	21	9	18	@@Wisdom @9is@7 better than weapons of war: but one sinner destroyeth much good.
verse	21	10	1	@@Dead flies cause the ointment of the apothecary to send forth a stinking savour: @9so doth@7 a little folly him that is in reputation for wisdom @9and@7 honour.
verse	21	10	2	@@A wise man's heart @9is@7 at his right hand; but a fool's heart at his left.
verse	21	10	3	@@Yea also, when he that is a fool walketh by the way, his wisdom faileth @9him,@7 and he saith to every one @9that@7 he @9is@7 a fool.
verse	21	10	4	If the spirit of the ruler rise up against thee, leave not thy place; for yielding pacifieth great offences.
verse	21	10	5	@@There is an evil @9which@7 I have seen under the sun, as an error @9which@7 proceedeth from the ruler:
verse	21	10	6	Folly is set in great dignity, and the rich sit in low place.
verse	21	10	7	I have seen servants upon horses, and princes walking as servants upon the earth.
verse	21	10	8	He that diggeth a pit shall fall into it; and whoso breaketh an hedge, a serpent shall bite him.
verse	21	10	9	@@Whoso removeth stones shall be hurt therewith; @9and@7 he that cleaveth wood shall be endangered thereby.
verse	21	10	10	@@If the iron be blunt, and he do not whet the edge, then must he put to more strength: but wisdom @9is@7 profitable to direct.
verse	21	10	11	Surely the serpent will bite without enchantment; and a babbler is no better.
verse	21	10	12	@@The words of a wise man's mouth @9are@7 gracious; but the lips of a fool will swallow up himself.
verse	21	10	13	@@The beginning of the words of his mouth @9is@7 foolishness: and the end of his talk @9is@7 mischievous madness.
verse	21	10	14	A fool also is full of words: a man cannot tell what shall be; and what shall be after him, who can tell him?
verse	21	10	15	The labour of the foolish wearieth every one of them, because he knoweth not how to go to the city.
verse	21	10	16	@@Woe to thee, O land, when thy king @9is@7 a child, and thy princes eat in the morning!
verse	21	10	17	@@Blessed @9art@7 thou, O land, when thy king @9is@7 the son of nobles, and thy princes eat in due season, for strength, and not for drunkenness!
verse	21	10	18	By much slothfulness the building decayeth; and through idleness of the hands the house droppeth through.
verse	21	10	19	@@A feast is made for laughter, and wine maketh merry: but money answereth all @9things.@7
verse	21	10	20	Curse not the king, no not in thy thought; and curse not the rich in thy bedchamber: for a bird of the air shall carry the voice, and that which hath wings shall tell the matter.
verse	21	11	1	Cast thy bread upon the waters: for thou shalt find it after many days.
verse	21	11	2	Give a portion to seven, and also to eight; for thou knowest not what evil shall be upon the earth.
verse	21	11	3	@@If the clouds be full of rain, they empty @9themselves@7 upon the earth: and if the tree fall toward the south, or toward the north, in the place where the tree falleth, there it shall be.
verse	21	11	4	He that observeth the wind shall not sow; and he that regardeth the clouds shall not reap.
verse	21	11	5	@@As thou knowest not what @9is@7 the way of the spirit, @9nor@7 how the bones @9do grow@7 in the womb of her that is with child: even so thou knowest not the works of God who maketh all.
verse	21	11	6	@@In the morning sow thy seed, and in the evening withhold not thine hand: for thou knowest not whether shall prosper, either this or that, or whether they both @9shall be@7 alike good.
verse	21	11	7	@@Truly the light @9is@7 sweet, and a pleasant @9thing it is@7 for the eyes to behold the sun:
verse	21	11	8	@@But if a man live many years, @9and@7 rejoice in them all; yet let him remember the days of darkness; for they shall be many. All that cometh @9is@7 vanity.
verse	21	11	9	@@Rejoice, O young man, in thy youth; and let thy heart cheer thee in the days of thy youth, and walk in the ways of thine heart, and in the sight of thine eyes: but know thou, that for all these @9things@7 God will bring thee into judgment.
verse	21	11	10	@@Therefore remove sorrow from thy heart, and put away evil from thy flesh: for childhood and youth @9are@7 vanity.
verse	21	12	1	Remember now thy Creator in the days of thy youth, while the evil days come not, nor the years draw nigh, when thou shalt say, I have no pleasure in them;
verse	21	12	2	While the sun, or the light, or the moon, or the stars, be not darkened, nor the clouds return after the rain:
verse	21	12	3	In the day when the keepers of the house shall tremble, and the strong men shall bow themselves, and the grinders cease because they are few, and those that look out of the windows be darkened,
verse	21	12	4	And the doors shall be shut in the streets, when the sound of the grinding is low, and he shall rise up at the voice of the bird, and all the daughters of musick shall be brought low;
verse	21	12	5	@@Also @9when@7 they shall be afraid of @9that which is@7 high, and fears @9shall be@7 in the way, and the almond tree shall flourish, and the grasshopper shall be a burden, and desire shall fail: because man goeth to his long home, and the mourners go about the streets:
verse	21	12	6	Or ever the silver cord be loosed, or the golden bowl be broken, or the pitcher be broken at the fountain, or the wheel broken at the cistern.
verse	21	12	7	Then shall the dust return to the earth as it was: and the spirit shall return unto God who gave it.
verse	21	12	8	@@Vanity of vanities, saith the preacher; all @9is@7 vanity.
verse	21	12	9	@@And moreover, because the preacher was wise, he still taught the people knowledge; yea, he gave good heed, and sought out, @9and@7 set in order many proverbs.
verse	21	12	10	@@The preacher sought to find out acceptable words: and @9that which was@7 written @9was@7 upright, @9even@7 words of truth.
verse	21	12	11	@@The words of the wise @9are@7 as goads, and as nails fastened by the masters of assemblies, @9which@7 are given from one shepherd.
verse	21	12	12	@@And further, by these, my son, be admonished: of making many books @9there is@7 no end; and much study @9is@7 a weariness of the flesh.
verse	21	12	13	@@Let us hear the conclusion of the whole matter: Fear God, and keep his commandments: for this @9is@7 the whole @9duty@7 of man.
verse	21	12	14	@@For God shall bring every work into judgment, with every secret thing, whether @9it be@7 good, or whether @9it be@7 evil.
verse	22	1	1	@@The song of songs, which @9is@7 Solomon's.
verse	22	1	2	@@Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth: for thy love @9is@7 better than wine.
verse	22	1	3	@@Because of the savour of thy good ointments thy name @9is as@7 ointment poured forth, therefore do the virgins love thee.
verse	22	1	4	Draw me, we will run after thee: the king hath brought me into his chambers: we will be glad and rejoice in thee, we will remember thy love more than wine: the upright love thee.
verse	22	1	5	@@I @9am@7 black, but comely, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, as the tents of Kedar, as the curtains of Solomon.
verse	22	1	6	@@Look not upon me, because I @9am@7 black, because the sun hath looked upon me: my mother's children were angry with me; they made me the keeper of the vineyards; @9but@7 mine own vineyard have I not kept.
verse	22	1	7	@@Tell me, O thou whom my soul loveth, where thou feedest, where thou makest @9thy flock@7 to rest at noon: for why should I be as one that turneth aside by the flocks of thy companions?
verse	22	1	8	If thou know not, O thou fairest among women, go thy way forth by the footsteps of the flock, and feed thy kids beside the shepherds' tents.
verse	22	1	9	I have compared thee, O my love, to a company of horses in Pharaoh's chariots.
verse	22	1	10	@@Thy cheeks are comely with rows @9of jewels,@7 thy neck with chains @9of gold. @7
verse	22	1	11	We will make thee borders of gold with studs of silver.
verse	22	1	12	@@While the king @9sitteth@7 at his table, my spikenard sendeth forth the smell thereof.
verse	22	1	13	@@A bundle of myrrh @9is@7 my wellbeloved unto me; he shall lie all night betwixt my breasts.
verse	22	1	14	@@My beloved @9is@7 unto me @9as@7 a cluster of camphire in the vineyards of Engedi.
verse	22	1	15	@@Behold, thou @9art@7 fair, my love; behold, thou @9art@7 fair; thou @9hast@7 doves' eyes.
verse	22	1	16	@@Behold, thou @9art@7 fair, my beloved, yea, pleasant: also our bed @9is@7 green.
verse	22	1	17	@@The beams of our house @9are@7 cedar, @9and@7 our rafters of fir.
verse	22	2	1	@@I @9am@7 the rose of Sharon, @9and@7 the lily of the valleys.
verse	22	2	2	@@As the lily among thorns, so @9is@7 my love among the daughters.
verse	22	2	3	@@As the apple tree among the trees of the wood, so @9is@7 my beloved among the sons. I sat down under his shadow with great delight, and his fruit @9was@7 sweet to my taste.
verse	22	2	4	@@He brought me to the banqueting house, and his banner over me @9was@7 love.
verse	22	2	5	@@Stay me with flagons, comfort me with apples: for I @9am@7 sick of love.
verse	22	2	6	@@His left hand @9is@7 under my head, and his right hand doth embrace me.
verse	22	2	7	@@I charge you, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not up, nor awake @9my@7 love, till he please.
verse	22	2	8	The voice of my beloved! behold, he cometh leaping upon the mountains, skipping upon the hills.
verse	22	2	9	My beloved is like a roe or a young hart: behold, he standeth behind our wall, he looketh forth at the windows, shewing himself through the lattice.
verse	22	2	10	My beloved spake, and said unto me, Rise up, my love, my fair one, and come away.
verse	22	2	11	@@For, lo, the winter is past, the rain is over @9and@7 gone;
verse	22	2	12	@@The flowers appear on the earth; the time of the singing @9of birds@7 is come, and the voice of the turtle is heard in our land;
verse	22	2	13	@@The fig tree putteth forth her green figs, and the vines @9with@7 the tender grape give a @9good@7 smell. Arise, my love, my fair one, and come away.
verse	22	2	14	@@O my dove, @9that art@7 in the clefts of the rock, in the secret @9places@7 of the stairs, let me see thy countenance, let me hear thy voice; for sweet @9is@7 thy voice, and thy countenance @9is@7 comely.
verse	22	2	15	@@Take us the foxes, the little foxes, that spoil the vines: for our vines @9have@7 tender grapes.
verse	22	2	16	@@My beloved @9is@7 mine, and I @9am@7 his: he feedeth among the lilies.
verse	22	2	17	Until the day break, and the shadows flee away, turn, my beloved, and be thou like a roe or a young hart upon the mountains of Bether.
verse	22	3	1	By night on my bed I sought him whom my soul loveth: I sought him, but I found him not.
verse	22	3	2	I will rise now, and go about the city in the streets, and in the broad ways I will seek him whom my soul loveth: I sought him, but I found him not.
verse	22	3	3	@@The watchmen that go about the city found me: @9to whom I said,@7 Saw ye him whom my soul loveth?
verse	22	3	4	@@@9It was@7 but a little that I passed from them, but I found him whom my soul loveth: I held him, and would not let him go, until I had brought him into my mother's house, and into the chamber of her that conceived me.
verse	22	3	5	@@I charge you, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not up, nor awake @9my@7 love, till he please.
verse	22	3	6	@@Who @9is@7 this that cometh out of the wilderness like pillars of smoke, perfumed with myrrh and frankincense, with all powders of the merchant?
verse	22	3	7	@@Behold his bed, which @9is@7 Solomon's; threescore valiant men @9are@7 about it, of the valiant of Israel.
verse	22	3	8	@@They all hold swords, @9being@7 expert in war: every man @9hath@7 his sword upon his thigh because of fear in the night.
verse	22	3	9	King Solomon made himself a chariot of the wood of Lebanon.
verse	22	3	10	@@He made the pillars thereof @9of@7 silver, the bottom thereof @9of@7 gold, the covering of it @9of@7 purple, the midst thereof being paved @9with@7 love, for the daughters of Jerusalem.
verse	22	3	11	Go forth, O ye daughters of Zion, and behold king Solomon with the crown wherewith his mother crowned him in the day of his espousals, and in the day of the gladness of his heart.
verse	22	4	1	@@Behold, thou @9art@7 fair, my love; behold, thou @9art@7 fair; thou @9hast@7 doves' eyes within thy locks: thy hair @9is@7 as a flock of goats, that appear from mount Gilead.
verse	22	4	2	@@Thy teeth @9are@7 like a flock @9of sheep that are even@7 shorn, which came up from the washing; whereof every one bear twins, and none @9is@7 barren among them.
verse	22	4	3	@@Thy lips @9are@7 like a thread of scarlet, and thy speech @9is@7 comely: thy temples @9are@7 like a piece of a pomegranate within thy locks.
verse	22	4	4	@@Thy neck @9is@7 like the tower of David builded for an armoury, whereon there hang a thousand bucklers, all shields of mighty men.
verse	22	4	5	@@Thy two breasts @9are@7 like two young roes that are twins, which feed among the lilies.
verse	22	4	6	Until the day break, and the shadows flee away, I will get me to the mountain of myrrh, and to the hill of frankincense.
verse	22	4	7	@@Thou @9art@7 all fair, my love; @9there is@7 no spot in thee.
verse	22	4	8	@@Come with me from Lebanon, @9my@7 spouse, with me from Lebanon: look from the top of Amana, from the top of Shenir and Hermon, from the lions' dens, from the mountains of the leopards.
verse	22	4	9	@@Thou hast ravished my heart, my sister, @9my@7 spouse; thou hast ravished my heart with one of thine eyes, with one chain of thy neck.
verse	22	4	10	@@How fair is thy love, my sister, @9my@7 spouse! how much better is thy love than wine! and the smell of thine ointments than all spices!
verse	22	4	11	@@Thy lips, O @9my@7 spouse, drop @9as@7 the honeycomb: honey and milk @9are@7 under thy tongue; and the smell of thy garments @9is@7 like the smell of Lebanon.
verse	22	4	12	@@A garden inclosed @9is@7 my sister, @9my@7 spouse; a spring shut up, a fountain sealed.
verse	22	4	13	@@Thy plants @9are@7 an orchard of pomegranates, with pleasant fruits; camphire, with spikenard,
verse	22	4	14	Spikenard and saffron; calamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices:
verse	22	4	15	A fountain of gardens, a well of living waters, and streams from Lebanon.
verse	22	4	16	@@Awake, O north wind; and come, thou south; blow upon my garden, @9that@7 the spices thereof may flow out. Let my beloved come into his garden, and eat his pleasant fruits.
verse	22	5	1	@@I am come into my garden, my sister, @9my@7 spouse: I have gathered my myrrh with my spice; I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey; I have drunk my wine with my milk: eat, O friends; drink, yea, drink abundantly, O beloved.
verse	22	5	2	@@I sleep, but my heart waketh: @9it is@7 the voice of my beloved that knocketh, @9saying,@7 Open to me, my sister, my love, my dove, my undefiled: for my head is filled with dew, @9and@7 my locks with the drops of the night.
verse	22	5	3	I have put off my coat; how shall I put it on? I have washed my feet; how shall I defile them?
verse	22	5	4	@@My beloved put in his hand by the hole @9of the door,@7 and my bowels were moved for him.
verse	22	5	5	@@I rose up to open to my beloved; and my hands dropped @9with@7 myrrh, and my fingers @9with@7 sweet smelling myrrh, upon the handles of the lock.
verse	22	5	6	@@I opened to my beloved; but my beloved had withdrawn himself, @9and@7 was gone: my soul failed when he spake: I sought him, but I could not find him; I called him, but he gave me no answer.
verse	22	5	7	The watchmen that went about the city found me, they smote me, they wounded me; the keepers of the walls took away my veil from me.
verse	22	5	8	@@I charge you, O daughters of Jerusalem, if ye find my beloved, that ye tell him, that I @9am@7 sick of love.
verse	22	5	9	@@What @9is@7 thy beloved more than @9another@7 beloved, O thou fairest among women? what @9is@7 thy beloved more than @9another@7 beloved, that thou dost so charge us?
verse	22	5	10	@@My beloved @9is@7 white and ruddy, the chiefest among ten thousand.
verse	22	5	11	@@His head @9is as@7 the most fine gold, his locks @9are@7 bushy, @9and@7 black as a raven.
verse	22	5	12	@@His eyes @9are@7 as @9the eyes@7 of doves by the rivers of waters, washed with milk, @9and@7 fitly set.
verse	22	5	13	@@His cheeks @9are@7 as a bed of spices, @9as@7 sweet flowers: his lips @9like@7 lilies, dropping sweet smelling myrrh.
verse	22	5	14	@@His hands @9are as@7 gold rings set with the beryl: his belly @9is as@7 bright ivory overlaid @9with@7 sapphires.
verse	22	5	15	@@His legs @9are as@7 pillars of marble, set upon sockets of fine gold: his countenance @9is@7 as Lebanon, excellent as the cedars.
verse	22	5	16	@@His mouth @9is@7 most sweet: yea, he @9is@7 altogether lovely. This @9is@7 my beloved, and this @9is@7 my friend, O daughters of Jerusalem.
verse	22	6	1	Whither is thy beloved gone, O thou fairest among women? whither is thy beloved turned aside? that we may seek him with thee.
verse	22	6	2	My beloved is gone down into his garden, to the beds of spices, to feed in the gardens, and to gather lilies.
verse	22	6	3	@@I @9am@7 my beloved's, and my beloved @9is@7 mine: he feedeth among the lilies.
verse	22	6	4	@@Thou @9art@7 beautiful, O my love, as Tirzah, comely as Jerusalem, terrible as @9an army@7 with banners.
verse	22	6	5	@@Turn away thine eyes from me, for they have overcome me: thy hair @9is@7 as a flock of goats that appear from Gilead.
verse	22	6	6	@@Thy teeth @9are@7 as a flock of sheep which go up from the washing, whereof every one beareth twins, and @9there is@7 not one barren among them.
verse	22	6	7	@@As a piece of a pomegranate @9are@7 thy temples within thy locks.
verse	22	6	8	There are threescore queens, and fourscore concubines, and virgins without number.
verse	22	6	9	@@My dove, my undefiled is @9but@7 one; she @9is@7 the @9only@7 one of her mother, she @9is@7 the choice @9one@7 of her that bare her. The daughters saw her, and blessed her; @9yea,@7 the queens and the concubines, and they praised her.
verse	22	6	10	@@Who @9is@7 she @9that@7 looketh forth as the morning, fair as the moon, clear as the sun, @9and@7 terrible as @9an army@7 with banners?
verse	22	6	11	@@I went down into the garden of nuts to see the fruits of the valley, @9and@7 to see whether the vine flourished, @9and@7 the pomegranates budded.
verse	22	6	12	@@Or ever I was aware, my soul made me @9like@7 the chariots of Amminadib.
verse	22	6	13	Return, return, O Shulamite; return, return, that we may look upon thee. What will ye see in the Shulamite? As it were the company of two armies.
verse	22	7	1	@@How beautiful are thy feet with shoes, O prince's daughter! the joints of thy thighs @9are@7 like jewels, the work of the hands of a cunning workman.
verse	22	7	2	@@Thy navel @9is like@7 a round goblet, @9which@7 wanteth not liquor: thy belly @9is like@7 an heap of wheat set about with lilies.
verse	22	7	3	@@Thy two breasts @9are@7 like two young roes @9that are@7 twins.
verse	22	7	4	@@Thy neck @9is@7 as a tower of ivory; thine eyes @9like@7 the fishpools in Heshbon, by the gate of Bath-rabbim: thy nose @9is@7 as the tower of Lebanon which looketh toward Damascus.
verse	22	7	5	@@Thine head upon thee @9is@7 like Carmel, and the hair of thine head like purple; the king @9is@7 held in the galleries.
verse	22	7	6	How fair and how pleasant art thou, O love, for delights!
verse	22	7	7	@@This thy stature is like to a palm tree, and thy breasts to clusters @9of grapes. @7
verse	22	7	8	I said, I will go up to the palm tree, I will take hold of the boughs thereof: now also thy breasts shall be as clusters of the vine, and the smell of thy nose like apples;
verse	22	7	9	@@And the roof of thy mouth like the best wine for my beloved, that goeth @9down@7 sweetly, causing the lips of those that are asleep to speak.
verse	22	7	10	@@I @9am@7 my beloved's, and his desire @9is@7 toward me.
verse	22	7	11	Come, my beloved, let us go forth into the field; let us lodge in the villages.
verse	22	7	12	@@Let us get up early to the vineyards; let us see if the vine flourish, @9whether@7 the tender grape appear, @9and@7 the pomegranates bud forth: there will I give thee my loves.
verse	22	7	13	@@The mandrakes give a smell, and at our gates @9are@7 all manner of pleasant @9fruits,@7 new and old, @9which@7 I have laid up for thee, O my beloved.
verse	22	8	1	@@O that thou @9wert@7 as my brother, that sucked the breasts of my mother! @9when@7 I should find thee without, I would kiss thee; yea, I should not be despised.
verse	22	8	2	@@I would lead thee, @9and@7 bring thee into my mother's house, @9who@7 would instruct me: I would cause thee to drink of spiced wine of the juice of my pomegranate.
verse	22	8	3	@@His left hand @9should be@7 under my head, and his right hand should embrace me.
verse	22	8	4	@@I charge you, O daughters of Jerusalem, that ye stir not up, nor awake @9my@7 love, until he please.
verse	22	8	5	@@Who @9is@7 this that cometh up from the wilderness, leaning upon her beloved? I raised thee up under the apple tree: there thy mother brought thee forth: there she brought thee forth @9that@7 bare thee.
verse	22	8	6	@@Set me as a seal upon thine heart, as a seal upon thine arm: for love @9is@7 strong as death; jealousy @9is@7 cruel as the grave: the coals thereof @9are@7 coals of fire, @9which hath a@7 most vehement flame.
verse	22	8	7	@@Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it: if @9a@7 man would give all the substance of his house for love, it would utterly be contemned.
verse	22	8	8	We have a little sister, and she hath no breasts: what shall we do for our sister in the day when she shall be spoken for?
verse	22	8	9	@@If she @9be@7 a wall, we will build upon her a palace of silver: and if she @9be@7 a door, we will inclose her with boards of cedar.
verse	22	8	10	@@I @9am@7 a wall, and my breasts like towers: then was I in his eyes as one that found favour.
verse	22	8	11	@@Solomon had a vineyard at Baal-hamon; he let out the vineyard unto keepers; every one for the fruit thereof was to bring a thousand @9pieces@7 of silver.
verse	22	8	12	@@My vineyard, which @9is@7 mine, @9is@7 before me: thou, O Solomon, @9must have@7 a thousand, and those that keep the fruit thereof two hundred.
verse	22	8	13	@@Thou that dwellest in the gardens, the companions hearken to thy voice: cause me to hear @9it.@7
verse	22	8	14	Make haste, my beloved, and be thou like to a roe or to a young hart upon the mountains of spices.
verse	23	1	1	@@The vision of Isaiah the son of Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, @9and@7 Hezekiah, kings of Judah.
verse	23	1	2	Hear, O heavens, and give ear, O earth: for the LORD hath spoken, I have nourished and brought up children, and they have rebelled against me.
verse	23	1	3	@@The ox knoweth his owner, and the ass his master's crib: @9but@7 Israel doth not know, my people doth not consider.
verse	23	1	4	Ah sinful nation, a people laden with iniquity, a seed of evildoers, children that are corrupters: they have forsaken the LORD, they have provoked the Holy One of Israel unto anger, they are gone away backward.
verse	23	1	5	Why should ye be stricken any more? ye will revolt more and more: the whole head is sick, and the whole heart faint.
verse	23	1	6	@@From the sole of the foot even unto the head @9there is@7 no soundness in it; @9but@7 wounds, and bruises, and putrifying sores: they have not been closed, neither bound up, neither mollified with ointment.
verse	23	1	7	@@Your country @9is@7 desolate, your cities @9are@7 burned with fire: your land, strangers devour it in your presence, and @9it is@7 desolate, as overthrown by strangers.
verse	23	1	8	And the daughter of Zion is left as a cottage in a vineyard, as a lodge in a garden of cucumbers, as a besieged city.
verse	23	1	9	@@Except the LORD of hosts had left unto us a very small remnant, we should have been as Sodom, @9and@7 we should have been like unto Gomorrah.
verse	23	1	10	Hear the word of the LORD, ye rulers of Sodom; give ear unto the law of our God, ye people of Gomorrah.
verse	23	1	11	@@To what purpose @9is@7 the multitude of your sacrifices unto me? saith the LORD: I am full of the burnt offerings of rams, and the fat of fed beasts; and I delight not in the blood of bullocks, or of lambs, or of he goats.
verse	23	1	12	When ye come to appear before me, who hath required this at your hand, to tread my courts?
verse	23	1	13	@@Bring no more vain oblations; incense is an abomination unto me; the new moons and sabbaths, the calling of assemblies, I cannot away with; @9it is@7 iniquity, even the solemn meeting.
verse	23	1	14	@@Your new moons and your appointed feasts my soul hateth: they are a trouble unto me; I am weary to bear @9them. @7
verse	23	1	15	And when ye spread forth your hands, I will hide mine eyes from you: yea, when ye make many prayers, I will not hear: your hands are full of blood.
verse	23	1	16	Wash you, make you clean; put away the evil of your doings from before mine eyes; cease to do evil;
verse	23	1	17	Learn to do well; seek judgment, relieve the oppressed, judge the fatherless, plead for the widow.
verse	23	1	18	Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.
verse	23	1	19	If ye be willing and obedient, ye shall eat the good of the land:
verse	23	1	20	@@But if ye refuse and rebel, ye shall be devoured with the sword: for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken @9it.@7
verse	23	1	21	How is the faithful city become an harlot! it was full of judgment; righteousness lodged in it; but now murderers.
verse	23	1	22	Thy silver is become dross, thy wine mixed with water:
verse	23	1	23	@@Thy princes @9are@7 rebellious, and companions of thieves: every one loveth gifts, and followeth after rewards: they judge not the fatherless, neither doth the cause of the widow come unto them.
verse	23	1	24	Therefore saith the Lord, the LORD of hosts, the mighty One of Israel, Ah, I will ease me of mine adversaries, and avenge me of mine enemies:
verse	23	1	25	And I will turn my hand upon thee, and purely purge away thy dross, and take away all thy tin:
verse	23	1	26	And I will restore thy judges as at the first, and thy counsellors as at the beginning: afterward thou shalt be called, The city of righteousness, the faithful city.
verse	23	1	27	Zion shall be redeemed with judgment, and her converts with righteousness.
verse	23	1	28	@@And the destruction of the transgressors and of the sinners @9shall be@7 together, and they that forsake the LORD shall be consumed.
verse	23	1	29	For they shall be ashamed of the oaks which ye have desired, and ye shall be confounded for the gardens that ye have chosen.
verse	23	1	30	For ye shall be as an oak whose leaf fadeth, and as a garden that hath no water.
verse	23	1	31	@@And the strong shall be as tow, and the maker of it as a spark, and they shall both burn together, and none shall quench @9them.@7
verse	23	2	1	The word that Isaiah the son of Amoz saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem.
verse	23	2	2	@@And it shall come to pass in the last days, @9that@7 the mountain of the LORD'S house shall be established in the top of the mountains, and shall be exalted above the hills; and all nations shall flow unto it.
verse	23	2	3	And many people shall go and say, Come ye, and let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths: for out of Zion shall go forth the law, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem.
verse	23	2	4	And he shall judge among the nations, and shall rebuke many people: and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruninghooks: nation shall not lift up sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more.
verse	23	2	5	O house of Jacob, come ye, and let us walk in the light of the LORD.
verse	23	2	6	@@Therefore thou hast forsaken thy people the house of Jacob, because they be replenished from the east, and @9are@7 soothsayers like the Philistines, and they please themselves in the children of strangers.
verse	23	2	7	@@Their land also is full of silver and gold, neither @9is there any@7 end of their treasures; their land is also full of horses, neither @9is there any@7 end of their chariots:
verse	23	2	8	Their land also is full of idols; they worship the work of their own hands, that which their own fingers have made:
verse	23	2	9	And the mean man boweth down, and the great man humbleth himself: therefore forgive them not.
verse	23	2	10	Enter into the rock, and hide thee in the dust, for fear of the LORD, and for the glory of his majesty.
verse	23	2	11	The lofty looks of man shall be humbled, and the haughtiness of men shall be bowed down, and the LORD alone shall be exalted in that day.
verse	23	2	12	@@For the day of the LORD of hosts @9shall be@7 upon every @9one that is@7 proud and lofty, and upon every @9one that is@7 lifted up; and he shall be brought low:
verse	23	2	13	@@And upon all the cedars of Lebanon, @9that are@7 high and lifted up, and upon all the oaks of Bashan,
verse	23	2	14	@@And upon all the high mountains, and upon all the hills @9that are@7 lifted up,
verse	23	2	15	And upon every high tower, and upon every fenced wall,
verse	23	2	16	And upon all the ships of Tarshish, and upon all pleasant pictures.
verse	23	2	17	And the loftiness of man shall be bowed down, and the haughtiness of men shall be made low: and the LORD alone shall be exalted in that day.
verse	23	2	18	And the idols he shall utterly abolish.
verse	23	2	19	And they shall go into the holes of the rocks, and into the caves of the earth, for fear of the LORD, and for the glory of his majesty, when he ariseth to shake terribly the earth.
verse	23	2	20	@@In that day a man shall cast his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which they made @9each one@7 for himself to worship, to the moles and to the bats;
verse	23	2	21	To go into the clefts of the rocks, and into the tops of the ragged rocks, for fear of the LORD, and for the glory of his majesty, when he ariseth to shake terribly the earth.
verse	23	2	22	@@Cease ye from man, whose breath @9is@7 in his nostrils: for wherein is he to be accounted of?
verse	23	3	1	For, behold, the Lord, the LORD of hosts, doth take away from Jerusalem and from Judah the stay and the staff, the whole stay of bread, and the whole stay of water,
verse	23	3	2	The mighty man, and the man of war, the judge, and the prophet, and the prudent, and the ancient,
verse	23	3	3	The captain of fifty, and the honourable man, and the counsellor, and the cunning artificer, and the eloquent orator.
verse	23	3	4	@@And I will give children @9to be@7 their princes, and babes shall rule over them.
verse	23	3	5	And the people shall be oppressed, every one by another, and every one by his neighbour: the child shall behave himself proudly against the ancient, and the base against the honourable.
verse	23	3	6	@@When a man shall take hold of his brother of the house of his father, @9saying,@7 Thou hast clothing, be thou our ruler, and @9let@7 this ruin @9be@7 under thy hand:
verse	23	3	7	@@In that day shall he swear, saying, I will not be an healer; for in my house @9is@7 neither bread nor clothing: make me not a ruler of the people.
verse	23	3	8	@@For Jerusalem is ruined, and Judah is fallen: because their tongue and their doings @9are@7 against the LORD, to provoke the eyes of his glory.
verse	23	3	9	@@The shew of their countenance doth witness against them; and they declare their sin as Sodom, they hide @9it@7 not. Woe unto their soul! for they have rewarded evil unto themselves.
verse	23	3	10	@@Say ye to the righteous, that @9it shall be@7 well @9with him:@7 for they shall eat the fruit of their doings.
verse	23	3	11	@@Woe unto the wicked! @9it shall be@7 ill @9with him:@7 for the reward of his hands shall be given him.
verse	23	3	12	@@@9As for@7 my people, children @9are@7 their oppressors, and women rule over them. O my people, they which lead thee cause @9thee@7 to err, and destroy the way of thy paths.
verse	23	3	13	The LORD standeth up to plead, and standeth to judge the people.
verse	23	3	14	@@The LORD will enter into judgment with the ancients of his people, and the princes thereof: for ye have eaten up the vineyard; the spoil of the poor @9is@7 in your houses.
verse	23	3	15	@@What mean ye @9that@7 ye beat my people to pieces, and grind the faces of the poor? saith the LORD GOD of hosts.
verse	23	3	16	@@Moreover the LORD saith, Because the daughters of Zion are haughty, and walk with stretched forth necks and wanton eyes, walking and mincing @9as@7 they go, and making a tinkling with their feet:
verse	23	3	17	Therefore the LORD will smite with a scab the crown of the head of the daughters of Zion, and the LORD will discover their secret parts.
verse	23	3	18	@@In that day the Lord will take away the bravery of @9their@7 tinkling ornaments @9about their feet,@7 and @9their@7 cauls, and @9their@7 round tires like the moon,
verse	23	3	19	The chains, and the bracelets, and the mufflers,
verse	23	3	20	The bonnets, and the ornaments of the legs, and the headbands, and the tablets, and the earrings,
verse	23	3	21	The rings, and nose jewels,
verse	23	3	22	The changeable suits of apparel, and the mantles, and the wimples, and the crisping pins,
verse	23	3	23	The glasses, and the fine linen, and the hoods, and the vails.
verse	23	3	24	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 instead of sweet smell there shall be stink; and instead of a girdle a rent; and instead of well set hair baldness; and instead of a stomacher a girding of sackcloth; @9and@7 burning instead of beauty.
verse	23	3	25	Thy men shall fall by the sword, and thy mighty in the war.
verse	23	3	26	@@And her gates shall lament and mourn; and she @9being@7 desolate shall sit upon the ground.
verse	23	4	1	And in that day seven women shall take hold of one man, saying, We will eat our own bread, and wear our own apparel: only let us be called by thy name, to take away our reproach.
verse	23	4	2	@@In that day shall the branch of the LORD be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the earth @9shall be@7 excellent and comely for them that are escaped of Israel.
verse	23	4	3	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that he that is@7 left in Zion, and @9he that@7 remaineth in Jerusalem, shall be called holy, @9even@7 every one that is written among the living in Jerusalem:
verse	23	4	4	When the Lord shall have washed away the filth of the daughters of Zion, and shall have purged the blood of Jerusalem from the midst thereof by the spirit of judgment, and by the spirit of burning.
verse	23	4	5	@@And the LORD will create upon every dwelling place of mount Zion, and upon her assemblies, a cloud and smoke by day, and the shining of a flaming fire by night: for upon all the glory @9shall be@7 a defence.
verse	23	4	6	And there shall be a tabernacle for a shadow in the daytime from the heat, and for a place of refuge, and for a covert from storm and from rain.
verse	23	5	1	Now will I sing to my wellbeloved a song of my beloved touching his vineyard. My wellbeloved hath a vineyard in a very fruitful hill:
verse	23	5	2	And he fenced it, and gathered out the stones thereof, and planted it with the choicest vine, and built a tower in the midst of it, and also made a winepress therein: and he looked that it should bring forth grapes, and it brought forth wild grapes.
verse	23	5	3	And now, O inhabitants of Jerusalem, and men of Judah, judge, I pray you, betwixt me and my vineyard.
verse	23	5	4	What could have been done more to my vineyard, that I have not done in it? wherefore, when I looked that it should bring forth grapes, brought it forth wild grapes?
verse	23	5	5	@@And now go to; I will tell you what I will do to my vineyard: I will take away the hedge thereof, and it shall be eaten up; @9and@7 break down the wall thereof, and it shall be trodden down:
verse	23	5	6	And I will lay it waste: it shall not be pruned, nor digged; but there shall come up briers and thorns: I will also command the clouds that they rain no rain upon it.
verse	23	5	7	@@For the vineyard of the LORD of hosts @9is@7 the house of Israel, and the men of Judah his pleasant plant: and he looked for judgment, but behold oppression; for righteousness, but behold a cry.
verse	23	5	8	@@Woe unto them that join house to house, @9that@7 lay field to field, till @9there be@7 no place, that they may be placed alone in the midst of the earth!
verse	23	5	9	@@In mine ears @9said@7 the LORD of hosts, Of a truth many houses shall be desolate, @9even@7 great and fair, without inhabitant.
verse	23	5	10	Yea, ten acres of vineyard shall yield one bath, and the seed of an homer shall yield an ephah.
verse	23	5	11	@@Woe unto them that rise up early in the morning, @9that@7 they may follow strong drink; that continue until night, @9till@7 wine inflame them!
verse	23	5	12	And the harp, and the viol, the tabret, and pipe, and wine, are in their feasts: but they regard not the work of the LORD, neither consider the operation of his hands.
verse	23	5	13	@@Therefore my people are gone into captivity, because @9they have@7 no knowledge: and their honourable men @9are@7 famished, and their multitude dried up with thirst.
verse	23	5	14	Therefore hell hath enlarged herself, and opened her mouth without measure: and their glory, and their multitude, and their pomp, and he that rejoiceth, shall descend into it.
verse	23	5	15	And the mean man shall be brought down, and the mighty man shall be humbled, and the eyes of the lofty shall be humbled:
verse	23	5	16	But the LORD of hosts shall be exalted in judgment, and God that is holy shall be sanctified in righteousness.
verse	23	5	17	Then shall the lambs feed after their manner, and the waste places of the fat ones shall strangers eat.
verse	23	5	18	Woe unto them that draw iniquity with cords of vanity, and sin as it were with a cart rope:
verse	23	5	19	@@That say, Let him make speed, @9and@7 hasten his work, that we may see it: and let the counsel of the Holy One of Israel draw nigh and come, that we may know @9it!@7
verse	23	5	20	Woe unto them that call evil good, and good evil; that put darkness for light, and light for darkness; that put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!
verse	23	5	21	@@Woe unto @9them that are@7 wise in their own eyes, and prudent in their own sight!
verse	23	5	22	@@Woe unto @9them that are@7 mighty to drink wine, and men of strength to mingle strong drink:
verse	23	5	23	Which justify the wicked for reward, and take away the righteousness of the righteous from him!
verse	23	5	24	@@Therefore as the fire devoureth the stubble, and the flame consumeth the chaff, @9so@7 their root shall be as rottenness, and their blossom shall go up as dust: because they have cast away the law of the LORD of hosts, and despised the word of the Holy One of Israel.
verse	23	5	25	@@Therefore is the anger of the LORD kindled against his people, and he hath stretched forth his hand against them, and hath smitten them: and the hills did tremble, and their carcases @9were@7 torn in the midst of the streets. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand @9is@7 stretched out still.
verse	23	5	26	And he will lift up an ensign to the nations from far, and will hiss unto them from the end of the earth: and, behold, they shall come with speed swiftly:
verse	23	5	27	None shall be weary nor stumble among them; none shall slumber nor sleep; neither shall the girdle of their loins be loosed, nor the latchet of their shoes be broken:
verse	23	5	28	@@Whose arrows @9are@7 sharp, and all their bows bent, their horses' hoofs shall be counted like flint, and their wheels like a whirlwind:
verse	23	5	29	@@Their roaring @9shall be@7 like a lion, they shall roar like young lions: yea, they shall roar, and lay hold of the prey, and shall carry @9it@7 away safe, and none shall deliver @9it. @7
verse	23	5	30	@@And in that day they shall roar against them like the roaring of the sea: and if @9one@7 look unto the land, behold darkness @9and@7 sorrow, and the light is darkened in the heavens thereof.
verse	23	6	1	In the year that king Uzziah died I saw also the Lord sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple.
verse	23	6	2	Above it stood the seraphims: each one had six wings; with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly.
verse	23	6	3	@@And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, @9is@7 the LORD of hosts: the whole earth @9is@7 full of his glory.
verse	23	6	4	And the posts of the door moved at the voice of him that cried, and the house was filled with smoke.
verse	23	6	5	@@Then said I, Woe @9is@7 me! for I am undone; because I @9am@7 a man of unclean lips, and I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips: for mine eyes have seen the King, the LORD of hosts.
verse	23	6	6	@@Then flew one of the seraphims unto me, having a live coal in his hand, @9which@7 he had taken with the tongs from off the altar:
verse	23	6	7	@@And he laid @9it@7 upon my mouth, and said, Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thine iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged.
verse	23	6	8	@@Also I heard the voice of the Lord, saying, Whom shall I send, and who will go for us? Then said I, Here @9am@7 I; send me.
verse	23	6	9	And he said, Go, and tell this people, Hear ye indeed, but understand not; and see ye indeed, but perceive not.
verse	23	6	10	Make the heart of this people fat, and make their ears heavy, and shut their eyes; lest they see with their eyes, and hear with their ears, and understand with their heart, and convert, and be healed.
verse	23	6	11	Then said I, Lord, how long? And he answered, Until the cities be wasted without inhabitant, and the houses without man, and the land be utterly desolate,
verse	23	6	12	@@And the LORD have removed men far away, and @9there be@7 a great forsaking in the midst of the land.
verse	23	6	13	@@But yet in it @9shall be@7 a tenth, and @9it@7 shall return, and shall be eaten: as a teil tree, and as an oak, whose substance is in them, when they cast @9their leaves: so@7 the holy seed @9shall be@7 the substance thereof.
verse	23	7	1	@@And it came to pass in the days of Ahaz the son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, king of Judah, @9that@7 Rezin the king of Syria, and Pekah the son of Remaliah, king of Israel, went up toward Jerusalem to war against it, but could not prevail against it.
verse	23	7	2	And it was told the house of David, saying, Syria is confederate with Ephraim. And his heart was moved, and the heart of his people, as the trees of the wood are moved with the wind.
verse	23	7	3	Then said the LORD unto Isaiah, Go forth now to meet Ahaz, thou, and Shear-jashub thy son, at the end of the conduit of the upper pool in the highway of the fuller's field;
verse	23	7	4	And say unto him, Take heed, and be quiet; fear not, neither be fainthearted for the two tails of these smoking firebrands, for the fierce anger of Rezin with Syria, and of the son of Remaliah.
verse	23	7	5	Because Syria, Ephraim, and the son of Remaliah, have taken evil counsel against thee, saying,
verse	23	7	6	@@Let us go up against Judah, and vex it, and let us make a breach therein for us, and set a king in the midst of it, @9even@7 the son of Tabeal:
verse	23	7	7	Thus saith the Lord GOD, It shall not stand, neither shall it come to pass.
verse	23	7	8	@@For the head of Syria @9is@7 Damascus, and the head of Damascus @9is@7 Rezin; and within threescore and five years shall Ephraim be broken, that it be not a people.
verse	23	7	9	@@And the head of Ephraim @9is@7 Samaria, and the head of Samaria @9is@7 Remaliah's son. If ye will not believe, surely ye shall not be established.
verse	23	7	10	Moreover the LORD spake again unto Ahaz, saying,
verse	23	7	11	Ask thee a sign of the LORD thy God; ask it either in the depth, or in the height above.
verse	23	7	12	But Ahaz said, I will not ask, neither will I tempt the LORD.
verse	23	7	13	@@And he said, Hear ye now, O house of David; @9Is it@7 a small thing for you to weary men, but will ye weary my God also?
verse	23	7	14	Therefore the Lord himself shall give you a sign; Behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.
verse	23	7	15	Butter and honey shall he eat, that he may know to refuse the evil, and choose the good.
verse	23	7	16	For before the child shall know to refuse the evil, and choose the good, the land that thou abhorrest shall be forsaken of both her kings.
verse	23	7	17	@@The LORD shall bring upon thee, and upon thy people, and upon thy father's house, days that have not come, from the day that Ephraim departed from Judah; @9even@7 the king of Assyria.
verse	23	7	18	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the LORD shall hiss for the fly that @9is@7 in the uttermost part of the rivers of Egypt, and for the bee that @9is@7 in the land of Assyria.
verse	23	7	19	And they shall come, and shall rest all of them in the desolate valleys, and in the holes of the rocks, and upon all thorns, and upon all bushes.
verse	23	7	20	@@In the same day shall the Lord shave with a razor that is hired, @9namely,@7 by them beyond the river, by the king of Assyria, the head, and the hair of the feet: and it shall also consume the beard.
verse	23	7	21	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 a man shall nourish a young cow, and two sheep;
verse	23	7	22	@@And it shall come to pass, for the abundance of milk @9that@7 they shall give he shall eat butter: for butter and honey shall every one eat that is left in the land.
verse	23	7	23	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 every place shall be, where there were a thousand vines at a thousand silverlings, it shall @9even@7 be for briers and thorns.
verse	23	7	24	@@With arrows and with bows shall @9men@7 come thither; because all the land shall become briers and thorns.
verse	23	7	25	@@And @9on@7 all hills that shall be digged with the mattock, there shall not come thither the fear of briers and thorns: but it shall be for the sending forth of oxen, and for the treading of lesser cattle.
verse	23	8	1	Moreover the LORD said unto me, Take thee a great roll, and write in it with a man's pen concerning Maher-shalal-hash-baz.
verse	23	8	2	And I took unto me faithful witnesses to record, Uriah the priest, and Zechariah the son of Jeberechiah.
verse	23	8	3	And I went unto the prophetess; and she conceived, and bare a son. Then said the LORD to me, Call his name Maher-shalal-hash-baz.
verse	23	8	4	For before the child shall have knowledge to cry, My father, and my mother, the riches of Damascus and the spoil of Samaria shall be taken away before the king of Assyria.
verse	23	8	5	The LORD spake also unto me again, saying,
verse	23	8	6	Forasmuch as this people refuseth the waters of Shiloah that go softly, and rejoice in Rezin and Remaliah's son;
verse	23	8	7	@@Now therefore, behold, the Lord bringeth up upon them the waters of the river, strong and many, @9even@7 the king of Assyria, and all his glory: and he shall come up over all his channels, and go over all his banks:
verse	23	8	8	@@And he shall pass through Judah; he shall overflow and go over, he shall reach @9even@7 to the neck; and the stretching out of his wings shall fill the breadth of thy land, O Immanuel.
verse	23	8	9	Associate yourselves, O ye people, and ye shall be broken in pieces; and give ear, all ye of far countries: gird yourselves, and ye shall be broken in pieces; gird yourselves, and ye shall be broken in pieces.
verse	23	8	10	@@Take counsel together, and it shall come to nought; speak the word, and it shall not stand: for God @9is@7 with us.
verse	23	8	11	For the LORD spake thus to me with a strong hand, and instructed me that I should not walk in the way of this people, saying,
verse	23	8	12	@@Say ye not, A confederacy, to all @9them to@7 whom this people shall say, A confederacy; neither fear ye their fear, nor be afraid.
verse	23	8	13	@@Sanctify the LORD of hosts himself; and @9let@7 him @9be@7 your fear, and @9let@7 him @9be@7 your dread.
verse	23	8	14	And he shall be for a sanctuary; but for a stone of stumbling and for a rock of offence to both the houses of Israel, for a gin and for a snare to the inhabitants of Jerusalem.
verse	23	8	15	And many among them shall stumble, and fall, and be broken, and be snared, and be taken.
verse	23	8	16	Bind up the testimony, seal the law among my disciples.
verse	23	8	17	And I will wait upon the LORD, that hideth his face from the house of Jacob, and I will look for him.
verse	23	8	18	@@Behold, I and the children whom the LORD hath given me @9are@7 for signs and for wonders in Israel from the LORD of hosts, which dwelleth in mount Zion.
verse	23	8	19	And when they shall say unto you, Seek unto them that have familiar spirits, and unto wizards that peep, and that mutter: should not a people seek unto their God? for the living to the dead?
verse	23	8	20	@@To the law and to the testimony: if they speak not according to this word, @9it is@7 because @9there is@7 no light in them.
verse	23	8	21	And they shall pass through it, hardly bestead and hungry: and it shall come to pass, that when they shall be hungry, they shall fret themselves, and curse their king and their God, and look upward.
verse	23	8	22	@@And they shall look unto the earth; and behold trouble and darkness, dimness of anguish; and @9they shall be@7 driven to darkness.
verse	23	9	1	@@Nevertheless the dimness @9shall@7 not @9be@7 such as @9was@7 in her vexation, when at the first he lightly afflicted the land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali, and afterward did more grievously afflict @9her by@7 the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, in Galilee of the nations.
verse	23	9	2	The people that walked in darkness have seen a great light: they that dwell in the land of the shadow of death, upon them hath the light shined.
verse	23	9	3	@@Thou hast multiplied the nation, @9and@7 not increased the joy: they joy before thee according to the joy in harvest, @9and@7 as @9men@7 rejoice when they divide the spoil.
verse	23	9	4	For thou hast broken the yoke of his burden, and the staff of his shoulder, the rod of his oppressor, as in the day of Midian.
verse	23	9	5	@@For every battle of the warrior @9is@7 with confused noise, and garments rolled in blood; but @9this@7 shall be with burning @9and@7 fuel of fire.
verse	23	9	6	For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.
verse	23	9	7	@@Of the increase of @9his@7 government and peace @9there shall be@7 no end, upon the throne of David, and upon his kingdom, to order it, and to establish it with judgment and with justice from henceforth even for ever. The zeal of the LORD of hosts will perform this.
verse	23	9	8	The Lord sent a word into Jacob, and it hath lighted upon Israel.
verse	23	9	9	@@And all the people shall know, @9even@7 Ephraim and the inhabitant of Samaria, that say in the pride and stoutness of heart,
verse	23	9	10	@@The bricks are fallen down, but we will build with hewn stones: the sycomores are cut down, but we will change @9them into@7 cedars.
verse	23	9	11	Therefore the LORD shall set up the adversaries of Rezin against him, and join his enemies together;
verse	23	9	12	@@The Syrians before, and the Philistines behind; and they shall devour Israel with open mouth. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand @9is@7 stretched out still.
verse	23	9	13	For the people turneth not unto him that smiteth them, neither do they seek the LORD of hosts.
verse	23	9	14	Therefore the LORD will cut off from Israel head and tail, branch and rush, in one day.
verse	23	9	15	@@The ancient and honourable, he @9is@7 the head; and the prophet that teacheth lies, he @9is@7 the tail.
verse	23	9	16	@@For the leaders of this people cause @9them@7 to err; and @9they that are@7 led of them @9are@7 destroyed.
verse	23	9	17	@@Therefore the Lord shall have no joy in their young men, neither shall have mercy on their fatherless and widows: for every one is an hypocrite and an evildoer, and every mouth speaketh folly. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand @9is@7 stretched out still.
verse	23	9	18	@@For wickedness burneth as the fire: it shall devour the briers and thorns, and shall kindle in the thickets of the forest, and they shall mount up @9like@7 the lifting up of smoke.
verse	23	9	19	Through the wrath of the LORD of hosts is the land darkened, and the people shall be as the fuel of the fire: no man shall spare his brother.
verse	23	9	20	And he shall snatch on the right hand, and be hungry; and he shall eat on the left hand, and they shall not be satisfied: they shall eat every man the flesh of his own arm:
verse	23	9	21	@@Manasseh, Ephraim; and Ephraim, Manasseh: @9and@7 they together @9shall be@7 against Judah. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand @9is@7 stretched out still.
verse	23	10	1	@@Woe unto them that decree unrighteous decrees, and that write grievousness @9which@7 they have prescribed;
verse	23	10	2	@@To turn aside the needy from judgment, and to take away the right from the poor of my people, that widows may be their prey, and @9that@7 they may rob the fatherless!
verse	23	10	3	@@And what will ye do in the day of visitation, and in the desolation @9which@7 shall come from far? to whom will ye flee for help? and where will ye leave your glory?
verse	23	10	4	@@Without me they shall bow down under the prisoners, and they shall fall under the slain. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand @9is@7 stretched out still.
verse	23	10	5	O Assyrian, the rod of mine anger, and the staff in their hand is mine indignation.
verse	23	10	6	I will send him against an hypocritical nation, and against the people of my wrath will I give him a charge, to take the spoil, and to take the prey, and to tread them down like the mire of the streets.
verse	23	10	7	@@Howbeit he meaneth not so, neither doth his heart think so; but @9it is@7 in his heart to destroy and cut off nations not a few.
verse	23	10	8	@@For he saith, @9Are@7 not my princes altogether kings?
verse	23	10	9	@@@9Is@7 not Calno as Carchemish? @9is@7 not Hamath as Arpad? @9is@7 not Samaria as Damascus?
verse	23	10	10	As my hand hath found the kingdoms of the idols, and whose graven images did excel them of Jerusalem and of Samaria;
verse	23	10	11	Shall I not, as I have done unto Samaria and her idols, so do to Jerusalem and her idols?
verse	23	10	12	@@Wherefore it shall come to pass, @9that@7 when the Lord hath performed his whole work upon mount Zion and on Jerusalem, I will punish the fruit of the stout heart of the king of Assyria, and the glory of his high looks.
verse	23	10	13	@@For he saith, By the strength of my hand I have done @9it,@7 and by my wisdom; for I am prudent: and I have removed the bounds of the people, and have robbed their treasures, and I have put down the inhabitants like a valiant @9man: @7
verse	23	10	14	@@And my hand hath found as a nest the riches of the people: and as one gathereth eggs @9that are@7 left, have I gathered all the earth; and there was none that moved the wing, or opened the mouth, or peeped.
verse	23	10	15	@@Shall the axe boast itself against him that heweth therewith? @9or@7 shall the saw magnify itself against him that shaketh it? as if the rod should shake @9itself@7 against them that lift it up, @9or@7 as if the staff should lift up @9itself, as if it were@7 no wood.
verse	23	10	16	Therefore shall the Lord, the Lord of hosts, send among his fat ones leanness; and under his glory he shall kindle a burning like the burning of a fire.
verse	23	10	17	And the light of Israel shall be for a fire, and his Holy One for a flame: and it shall burn and devour his thorns and his briers in one day;
verse	23	10	18	And shall consume the glory of his forest, and of his fruitful field, both soul and body: and they shall be as when a standardbearer fainteth.
verse	23	10	19	And the rest of the trees of his forest shall be few, that a child may write them.
verse	23	10	20	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the remnant of Israel, and such as are escaped of the house of Jacob, shall no more again stay upon him that smote them; but shall stay upon the LORD, the Holy One of Israel, in truth.
verse	23	10	21	@@The remnant shall return, @9even@7 the remnant of Jacob, unto the mighty God.
verse	23	10	22	@@For though thy people Israel be as the sand of the sea, @9yet@7 a remnant of them shall return: the consumption decreed shall overflow with righteousness.
verse	23	10	23	For the Lord GOD of hosts shall make a consumption, even determined, in the midst of all the land.
verse	23	10	24	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts, O my people that dwellest in Zion, be not afraid of the Assyrian: he shall smite thee with a rod, and shall lift up his staff against thee, after the manner of Egypt.
verse	23	10	25	For yet a very little while, and the indignation shall cease, and mine anger in their destruction.
verse	23	10	26	@@And the LORD of hosts shall stir up a scourge for him according to the slaughter of Midian at the rock of Oreb: and @9as@7 his rod @9was@7 upon the sea, so shall he lift it up after the manner of Egypt.
verse	23	10	27	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 his burden shall be taken away from off thy shoulder, and his yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing.
verse	23	10	28	He is come to Aiath, he is passed to Migron; at Michmash he hath laid up his carriages:
verse	23	10	29	They are gone over the passage: they have taken up their lodging at Geba; Ramah is afraid; Gibeah of Saul is fled.
verse	23	10	30	Lift up thy voice, O daughter of Gallim: cause it to be heard unto Laish, O poor Anathoth.
verse	23	10	31	Madmenah is removed; the inhabitants of Gebim gather themselves to flee.
verse	23	10	32	@@As yet shall he remain at Nob that day: he shall shake his hand @9against@7 the mount of the daughter of Zion, the hill of Jerusalem.
verse	23	10	33	@@Behold, the Lord, the LORD of hosts, shall lop the bough with terror: and the high ones of stature @9shall be@7 hewn down, and the haughty shall be humbled.
verse	23	10	34	And he shall cut down the thickets of the forest with iron, and Lebanon shall fall by a mighty one.
verse	23	11	1	And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots:
verse	23	11	2	And the spirit of the LORD shall rest upon him, the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of the LORD;
verse	23	11	3	And shall make him of quick understanding in the fear of the LORD: and he shall not judge after the sight of his eyes, neither reprove after the hearing of his ears:
verse	23	11	4	But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked.
verse	23	11	5	And righteousness shall be the girdle of his loins, and faithfulness the girdle of his reins.
verse	23	11	6	The wolf also shall dwell with the lamb, and the leopard shall lie down with the kid; and the calf and the young lion and the fatling together; and a little child shall lead them.
verse	23	11	7	And the cow and the bear shall feed; their young ones shall lie down together: and the lion shall eat straw like the ox.
verse	23	11	8	And the sucking child shall play on the hole of the asp, and the weaned child shall put his hand on the cockatrice' den.
verse	23	11	9	They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain: for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of the LORD, as the waters cover the sea.
verse	23	11	10	And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek: and his rest shall be glorious.
verse	23	11	11	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the Lord shall set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant of his people, which shall be left, from Assyria, and from Egypt, and from Pathros, and from Cush, and from Elam, and from Shinar, and from Hamath, and from the islands of the sea.
verse	23	11	12	And he shall set up an ensign for the nations, and shall assemble the outcasts of Israel, and gather together the dispersed of Judah from the four corners of the earth.
verse	23	11	13	The envy also of Ephraim shall depart, and the adversaries of Judah shall be cut off: Ephraim shall not envy Judah, and Judah shall not vex Ephraim.
verse	23	11	14	But they shall fly upon the shoulders of the Philistines toward the west; they shall spoil them of the east together: they shall lay their hand upon Edom and Moab; and the children of Ammon shall obey them.
verse	23	11	15	@@And the LORD shall utterly destroy the tongue of the Egyptian sea; and with his mighty wind shall he shake his hand over the river, and shall smite it in the seven streams, and make @9men@7 go over dryshod.
verse	23	11	16	And there shall be an highway for the remnant of his people, which shall be left, from Assyria; like as it was to Israel in the day that he came up out of the land of Egypt.
verse	23	12	1	And in that day thou shalt say, O LORD, I will praise thee: though thou wast angry with me, thine anger is turned away, and thou comfortedst me.
verse	23	12	2	@@Behold, God @9is@7 my salvation; I will trust, and not be afraid: for the LORD JEHOVAH @9is@7 my strength and @9my@7 song; he also is become my salvation.
verse	23	12	3	Therefore with joy shall ye draw water out of the wells of salvation.
verse	23	12	4	And in that day shall ye say, Praise the LORD, call upon his name, declare his doings among the people, make mention that his name is exalted.
verse	23	12	5	@@Sing unto the LORD; for he hath done excellent things: this @9is@7 known in all the earth.
verse	23	12	6	@@Cry out and shout, thou inhabitant of Zion: for great @9is@7 the Holy One of Israel in the midst of thee.
verse	23	13	1	The burden of Babylon, which Isaiah the son of Amoz did see.
verse	23	13	2	Lift ye up a banner upon the high mountain, exalt the voice unto them, shake the hand, that they may go into the gates of the nobles.
verse	23	13	3	@@I have commanded my sanctified ones, I have also called my mighty ones for mine anger, @9even@7 them that rejoice in my highness.
verse	23	13	4	The noise of a multitude in the mountains, like as of a great people; a tumultuous noise of the kingdoms of nations gathered together: the LORD of hosts mustereth the host of the battle.
verse	23	13	5	@@They come from a far country, from the end of heaven, @9even@7 the LORD, and the weapons of his indignation, to destroy the whole land.
verse	23	13	6	@@Howl ye; for the day of the LORD @9is@7 at hand; it shall come as a destruction from the Almighty.
verse	23	13	7	Therefore shall all hands be faint, and every man's heart shall melt:
verse	23	13	8	@@And they shall be afraid: pangs and sorrows shall take hold of them; they shall be in pain as a woman that travaileth: they shall be amazed one at another; their faces @9shall be as@7 flames.
verse	23	13	9	Behold, the day of the LORD cometh, cruel both with wrath and fierce anger, to lay the land desolate: and he shall destroy the sinners thereof out of it.
verse	23	13	10	For the stars of heaven and the constellations thereof shall not give their light: the sun shall be darkened in his going forth, and the moon shall not cause her light to shine.
verse	23	13	11	@@And I will punish the world for @9their@7 evil, and the wicked for their iniquity; and I will cause the arrogancy of the proud to cease, and will lay low the haughtiness of the terrible.
verse	23	13	12	I will make a man more precious than fine gold; even a man than the golden wedge of Ophir.
verse	23	13	13	Therefore I will shake the heavens, and the earth shall remove out of her place, in the wrath of the LORD of hosts, and in the day of his fierce anger.
verse	23	13	14	And it shall be as the chased roe, and as a sheep that no man taketh up: they shall every man turn to his own people, and flee every one into his own land.
verse	23	13	15	@@Every one that is found shall be thrust through; and every one that is joined @9unto them@7 shall fall by the sword.
verse	23	13	16	Their children also shall be dashed to pieces before their eyes; their houses shall be spoiled, and their wives ravished.
verse	23	13	17	@@Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them, which shall not regard silver; and @9as for@7 gold, they shall not delight in it.
verse	23	13	18	@@@9Their@7 bows also shall dash the young men to pieces; and they shall have no pity on the fruit of the womb; their eye shall not spare children.
verse	23	13	19	And Babylon, the glory of kingdoms, the beauty of the Chaldees' excellency, shall be as when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah.
verse	23	13	20	It shall never be inhabited, neither shall it be dwelt in from generation to generation: neither shall the Arabian pitch tent there; neither shall the shepherds make their fold there.
verse	23	13	21	But wild beasts of the desert shall lie there; and their houses shall be full of doleful creatures; and owls shall dwell there, and satyrs shall dance there.
verse	23	13	22	@@And the wild beasts of the islands shall cry in their desolate houses, and dragons in @9their@7 pleasant palaces: and her time @9is@7 near to come, and her days shall not be prolonged.
verse	23	14	1	For the LORD will have mercy on Jacob, and will yet choose Israel, and set them in their own land: and the strangers shall be joined with them, and they shall cleave to the house of Jacob.
verse	23	14	2	And the people shall take them, and bring them to their place: and the house of Israel shall possess them in the land of the LORD for servants and handmaids: and they shall take them captives, whose captives they were; and they shall rule over their oppressors.
verse	23	14	3	And it shall come to pass in the day that the LORD shall give thee rest from thy sorrow, and from thy fear, and from the hard bondage wherein thou wast made to serve,
verse	23	14	4	That thou shalt take up this proverb against the king of Babylon, and say, How hath the oppressor ceased! the golden city ceased!
verse	23	14	5	@@The LORD hath broken the staff of the wicked, @9and@7 the sceptre of the rulers.
verse	23	14	6	@@He who smote the people in wrath with a continual stroke, he that ruled the nations in anger, is persecuted, @9and@7 none hindereth.
verse	23	14	7	@@The whole earth is at rest, @9and@7 is quiet: they break forth into singing.
verse	23	14	8	@@Yea, the fir trees rejoice at thee, @9and@7 the cedars of Lebanon, @9saying,@7 Since thou art laid down, no feller is come up against us.
verse	23	14	9	@@Hell from beneath is moved for thee to meet @9thee@7 at thy coming: it stirreth up the dead for thee, @9even@7 all the chief ones of the earth; it hath raised up from their thrones all the kings of the nations.
verse	23	14	10	All they shall speak and say unto thee, Art thou also become weak as we? art thou become like unto us?
verse	23	14	11	@@Thy pomp is brought down to the grave, @9and@7 the noise of thy viols: the worm is spread under thee, and the worms cover thee.
verse	23	14	12	@@How art thou fallen from heaven, O Lucifer, son of the morning! @9how@7 art thou cut down to the ground, which didst weaken the nations!
verse	23	14	13	For thou hast said in thine heart, I will ascend into heaven, I will exalt my throne above the stars of God: I will sit also upon the mount of the congregation, in the sides of the north:
verse	23	14	14	I will ascend above the heights of the clouds; I will be like the most High.
verse	23	14	15	Yet thou shalt be brought down to hell, to the sides of the pit.
verse	23	14	16	@@They that see thee shall narrowly look upon thee, @9and@7 consider thee, @9saying, Is@7 this the man that made the earth to tremble, that did shake kingdoms;
verse	23	14	17	@@@9That@7 made the world as a wilderness, and destroyed the cities thereof; @9that@7 opened not the house of his prisoners?
verse	23	14	18	@@All the kings of the nations, @9even@7 all of them, lie in glory, every one in his own house.
verse	23	14	19	@@But thou art cast out of thy grave like an abominable branch, @9and as@7 the raiment of those that are slain, thrust through with a sword, that go down to the stones of the pit; as a carcase trodden under feet.
verse	23	14	20	@@Thou shalt not be joined with them in burial, because thou hast destroyed thy land, @9and@7 slain thy people: the seed of evildoers shall never be renowned.
verse	23	14	21	Prepare slaughter for his children for the iniquity of their fathers; that they do not rise, nor possess the land, nor fill the face of the world with cities.
verse	23	14	22	For I will rise up against them, saith the LORD of hosts, and cut off from Babylon the name, and remnant, and son, and nephew, saith the LORD.
verse	23	14	23	I will also make it a possession for the bittern, and pools of water: and I will sweep it with the besom of destruction, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	23	14	24	@@The LORD of hosts hath sworn, saying, Surely as I have thought, so shall it come to pass; and as I have purposed, @9so@7 shall it stand:
verse	23	14	25	That I will break the Assyrian in my land, and upon my mountains tread him under foot: then shall his yoke depart from off them, and his burden depart from off their shoulders.
verse	23	14	26	@@This @9is@7 the purpose that is purposed upon the whole earth: and this @9is@7 the hand that is stretched out upon all the nations.
verse	23	14	27	@@For the LORD of hosts hath purposed, and who shall disannul @9it?@7 and his hand @9is@7 stretched out, and who shall turn it back?
verse	23	14	28	In the year that king Ahaz died was this burden.
verse	23	14	29	@@Rejoice not thou, whole Palestina, because the rod of him that smote thee is broken: for out of the serpent's root shall come forth a cockatrice, and his fruit @9shall be@7 a fiery flying serpent.
verse	23	14	30	And the firstborn of the poor shall feed, and the needy shall lie down in safety: and I will kill thy root with famine, and he shall slay thy remnant.
verse	23	14	31	@@Howl, O gate; cry, O city; thou, whole Palestina, @9art@7 dissolved: for there shall come from the north a smoke, and none @9shall be@7 alone in his appointed times.
verse	23	14	32	@@What shall @9one@7 then answer the messengers of the nation? That the LORD hath founded Zion, and the poor of his people shall trust in it.
verse	23	15	1	@@The burden of Moab. Because in the night Ar of Moab is laid waste, @9and@7 brought to silence; because in the night Kir of Moab is laid waste, @9and@7 brought to silence;
verse	23	15	2	@@He is gone up to Bajith, and to Dibon, the high places, to weep: Moab shall howl over Nebo, and over Medeba: on all their heads @9shall be@7 baldness, @9and@7 every beard cut off.
verse	23	15	3	In their streets they shall gird themselves with sackcloth: on the tops of their houses, and in their streets, every one shall howl, weeping abundantly.
verse	23	15	4	@@And Heshbon shall cry, and Elealeh: their voice shall be heard @9even@7 unto Jahaz: therefore the armed soldiers of Moab shall cry out; his life shall be grievous unto him.
verse	23	15	5	@@My heart shall cry out for Moab; his fugitives @9shall flee@7 unto Zoar, an heifer of three years old: for by the mounting up of Luhith with weeping shall they go it up; for in the way of Horonaim they shall raise up a cry of destruction.
verse	23	15	6	For the waters of Nimrim shall be desolate: for the hay is withered away, the grass faileth, there is no green thing.
verse	23	15	7	Therefore the abundance they have gotten, and that which they have laid up, shall they carry away to the brook of the willows.
verse	23	15	8	For the cry is gone round about the borders of Moab; the howling thereof unto Eglaim, and the howling thereof unto Beer-elim.
verse	23	15	9	For the waters of Dimon shall be full of blood: for I will bring more upon Dimon, lions upon him that escapeth of Moab, and upon the remnant of the land.
verse	23	16	1	Send ye the lamb to the ruler of the land from Sela to the wilderness, unto the mount of the daughter of Zion.
verse	23	16	2	@@For it shall be, @9that,@7 as a wandering bird cast out of the nest, so the daughters of Moab shall be at the fords of Arnon.
verse	23	16	3	Take counsel, execute judgment; make thy shadow as the night in the midst of the noonday; hide the outcasts; bewray not him that wandereth.
verse	23	16	4	Let mine outcasts dwell with thee, Moab; be thou a covert to them from the face of the spoiler: for the extortioner is at an end, the spoiler ceaseth, the oppressors are consumed out of the land.
verse	23	16	5	And in mercy shall the throne be established: and he shall sit upon it in truth in the tabernacle of David, judging, and seeking judgment, and hasting righteousness.
verse	23	16	6	@@We have heard of the pride of Moab; @9he is@7 very proud: @9even@7 of his haughtiness, and his pride, and his wrath: @9but@7 his lies @9shall@7 not @9be@7 so.
verse	23	16	7	@@Therefore shall Moab howl for Moab, every one shall howl: for the foundations of Kir-hareseth shall ye mourn; surely @9they are@7 stricken.
verse	23	16	8	@@For the fields of Heshbon languish, @9and@7 the vine of Sibmah: the lords of the heathen have broken down the principal plants thereof, they are come @9even@7 unto Jazer, they wandered @9through@7 the wilderness: her branches are stretched out, they are gone over the sea.
verse	23	16	9	Therefore I will bewail with the weeping of Jazer the vine of Sibmah: I will water thee with my tears, O Heshbon, and Elealeh: for the shouting for thy summer fruits and for thy harvest is fallen.
verse	23	16	10	@@And gladness is taken away, and joy out of the plentiful field; and in the vineyards there shall be no singing, neither shall there be shouting: the treaders shall tread out no wine in @9their@7 presses; I have made @9their vintage@7 shouting to cease.
verse	23	16	11	Wherefore my bowels shall sound like an harp for Moab, and mine inward parts for Kir-haresh.
verse	23	16	12	And it shall come to pass, when it is seen that Moab is weary on the high place, that he shall come to his sanctuary to pray; but he shall not prevail.
verse	23	16	13	@@This @9is@7 the word that the LORD hath spoken concerning Moab since that time.
verse	23	16	14	@@But now the LORD hath spoken, saying, Within three years, as the years of an hireling, and the glory of Moab shall be contemned, with all that great multitude; and the remnant @9shall be@7 very small @9and@7 feeble.
verse	23	17	1	@@The burden of Damascus. Behold, Damascus is taken away from @9being@7 a city, and it shall be a ruinous heap.
verse	23	17	2	@@The cities of Aroer @9are@7 forsaken: they shall be for flocks, which shall lie down, and none shall make @9them@7 afraid.
verse	23	17	3	The fortress also shall cease from Ephraim, and the kingdom from Damascus, and the remnant of Syria: they shall be as the glory of the children of Israel, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	23	17	4	@@And in that day it shall come to pass, @9that@7 the glory of Jacob shall be made thin, and the fatness of his flesh shall wax lean.
verse	23	17	5	And it shall be as when the harvestman gathereth the corn, and reapeth the ears with his arm; and it shall be as he that gathereth ears in the valley of Rephaim.
verse	23	17	6	@@Yet gleaning grapes shall be left in it, as the shaking of an olive tree, two @9or@7 three berries in the top of the uppermost bough, four @9or@7 five in the outmost fruitful branches thereof, saith the LORD God of Israel.
verse	23	17	7	At that day shall a man look to his Maker, and his eyes shall have respect to the Holy One of Israel.
verse	23	17	8	@@And he shall not look to the altars, the work of his hands, neither shall respect @9that@7 which his fingers have made, either the groves, or the images.
verse	23	17	9	In that day shall his strong cities be as a forsaken bough, and an uppermost branch, which they left because of the children of Israel: and there shall be desolation.
verse	23	17	10	Because thou hast forgotten the God of thy salvation, and hast not been mindful of the rock of thy strength, therefore shalt thou plant pleasant plants, and shalt set it with strange slips:
verse	23	17	11	@@In the day shalt thou make thy plant to grow, and in the morning shalt thou make thy seed to flourish: @9but@7 the harvest @9shall be@7 a heap in the day of grief and of desperate sorrow.
verse	23	17	12	@@Woe to the multitude of many people, @9which@7 make a noise like the noise of the seas; and to the rushing of nations, @9that@7 make a rushing like the rushing of mighty waters!
verse	23	17	13	@@The nations shall rush like the rushing of many waters: but @9God@7 shall rebuke them, and they shall flee far off, and shall be chased as the chaff of the mountains before the wind, and like a rolling thing before the whirlwind.
verse	23	17	14	@@And behold at eveningtide trouble; @9and@7 before the morning he @9is@7 not. This @9is@7 the portion of them that spoil us, and the lot of them that rob us.
verse	23	18	1	@@Woe to the land shadowing with wings, which @9is@7 beyond the rivers of Ethiopia:
verse	23	18	2	@@That sendeth ambassadors by the sea, even in vessels of bulrushes upon the waters, @9saying,@7 Go, ye swift messengers, to a nation scattered and peeled, to a people terrible from their beginning hitherto; a nation meted out and trodden down, whose land the rivers have spoiled!
verse	23	18	3	All ye inhabitants of the world, and dwellers on the earth, see ye, when he lifteth up an ensign on the mountains; and when he bloweth a trumpet, hear ye.
verse	23	18	4	@@For so the LORD said unto me, I will take my rest, and I will consider in my dwelling place like a clear heat upon herbs, @9and@7 like a cloud of dew in the heat of harvest.
verse	23	18	5	@@For afore the harvest, when the bud is perfect, and the sour grape is ripening in the flower, he shall both cut off the sprigs with pruninghooks, and take away @9and@7 cut down the branches.
verse	23	18	6	They shall be left together unto the fowls of the mountains, and to the beasts of the earth: and the fowls shall summer upon them, and all the beasts of the earth shall winter upon them.
verse	23	18	7	In that time shall the present be brought unto the LORD of hosts of a people scattered and peeled, and from a people terrible from their beginning hitherto; a nation meted out and trodden under foot, whose land the rivers have spoiled, to the place of the name of the LORD of hosts, the mount Zion.
verse	23	19	1	The burden of Egypt. Behold, the LORD rideth upon a swift cloud, and shall come into Egypt: and the idols of Egypt shall be moved at his presence, and the heart of Egypt shall melt in the midst of it.
verse	23	19	2	@@And I will set the Egyptians against the Egyptians: and they shall fight every one against his brother, and every one against his neighbour; city against city, @9and@7 kingdom against kingdom.
verse	23	19	3	And the spirit of Egypt shall fail in the midst thereof; and I will destroy the counsel thereof: and they shall seek to the idols, and to the charmers, and to them that have familiar spirits, and to the wizards.
verse	23	19	4	And the Egyptians will I give over into the hand of a cruel lord; and a fierce king shall rule over them, saith the Lord, the LORD of hosts.
verse	23	19	5	And the waters shall fail from the sea, and the river shall be wasted and dried up.
verse	23	19	6	@@And they shall turn the rivers far away; @9and@7 the brooks of defence shall be emptied and dried up: the reeds and flags shall wither.
verse	23	19	7	@@The paper reeds by the brooks, by the mouth of the brooks, and every thing sown by the brooks, shall wither, be driven away, and be no @9more. @7
verse	23	19	8	The fishers also shall mourn, and all they that cast angle into the brooks shall lament, and they that spread nets upon the waters shall languish.
verse	23	19	9	Moreover they that work in fine flax, and they that weave networks, shall be confounded.
verse	23	19	10	@@And they shall be broken in the purposes thereof, all that make sluices @9and@7 ponds for fish.
verse	23	19	11	@@Surely the princes of Zoan @9are@7 fools, the counsel of the wise counsellors of Pharaoh is become brutish: how say ye unto Pharaoh, I @9am@7 the son of the wise, the son of ancient kings?
verse	23	19	12	@@Where @9are@7 they? where @9are@7 thy wise @9men?@7 and let them tell thee now, and let them know what the LORD of hosts hath purposed upon Egypt.
verse	23	19	13	@@The princes of Zoan are become fools, the princes of Noph are deceived; they have also seduced Egypt, @9even they that are@7 the stay of the tribes thereof.
verse	23	19	14	@@The LORD hath mingled a perverse spirit in the midst thereof: and they have caused Egypt to err in every work thereof, as a drunken @9man@7 staggereth in his vomit.
verse	23	19	15	@@Neither shall there be @9any@7 work for Egypt, which the head or tail, branch or rush, may do.
verse	23	19	16	In that day shall Egypt be like unto women: and it shall be afraid and fear because of the shaking of the hand of the LORD of hosts, which he shaketh over it.
verse	23	19	17	And the land of Judah shall be a terror unto Egypt, every one that maketh mention thereof shall be afraid in himself, because of the counsel of the LORD of hosts, which he hath determined against it.
verse	23	19	18	In that day shall five cities in the land of Egypt speak the language of Canaan, and swear to the LORD of hosts; one shall be called, The city of destruction.
verse	23	19	19	In that day shall there be an altar to the LORD in the midst of the land of Egypt, and a pillar at the border thereof to the LORD.
verse	23	19	20	And it shall be for a sign and for a witness unto the LORD of hosts in the land of Egypt: for they shall cry unto the LORD because of the oppressors, and he shall send them a saviour, and a great one, and he shall deliver them.
verse	23	19	21	@@And the LORD shall be known to Egypt, and the Egyptians shall know the LORD in that day, and shall do sacrifice and oblation; yea, they shall vow a vow unto the LORD, and perform @9it. @7
verse	23	19	22	@@And the LORD shall smite Egypt: he shall smite and heal @9it:@7 and they shall return @9even@7 to the LORD, and he shall be intreated of them, and shall heal them.
verse	23	19	23	In that day shall there be a highway out of Egypt to Assyria, and the Assyrian shall come into Egypt, and the Egyptian into Assyria, and the Egyptians shall serve with the Assyrians.
verse	23	19	24	@@In that day shall Israel be the third with Egypt and with Assyria, @9even@7 a blessing in the midst of the land:
verse	23	19	25	@@Whom the LORD of hosts shall bless, saying, Blessed @9be@7 Egypt my people, and Assyria the work of my hands, and Israel mine inheritance.
verse	23	20	1	In the year that Tartan came unto Ashdod, (when Sargon the king of Assyria sent him,) and fought against Ashdod, and took it;
verse	23	20	2	At the same time spake the LORD by Isaiah the son of Amoz, saying, Go and loose the sackcloth from off thy loins, and put off thy shoe from thy foot. And he did so, walking naked and barefoot.
verse	23	20	3	@@And the LORD said, Like as my servant Isaiah hath walked naked and barefoot three years @9for@7 a sign and wonder upon Egypt and upon Ethiopia;
verse	23	20	4	@@So shall the king of Assyria lead away the Egyptians prisoners, and the Ethiopians captives, young and old, naked and barefoot, even with @9their@7 buttocks uncovered, to the shame of Egypt.
verse	23	20	5	And they shall be afraid and ashamed of Ethiopia their expectation, and of Egypt their glory.
verse	23	20	6	@@And the inhabitant of this isle shall say in that day, Behold, such @9is@7 our expectation, whither we flee for help to be delivered from the king of Assyria: and how shall we escape?
verse	23	21	1	@@The burden of the desert of the sea. As whirlwinds in the south pass through; @9so@7 it cometh from the desert, from a terrible land.
verse	23	21	2	A grievous vision is declared unto me; the treacherous dealer dealeth treacherously, and the spoiler spoileth. Go up, O Elam: besiege, O Media; all the sighing thereof have I made to cease.
verse	23	21	3	@@Therefore are my loins filled with pain: pangs have taken hold upon me, as the pangs of a woman that travaileth: I was bowed down at the hearing @9of it;@7 I was dismayed at the seeing @9of it. @7
verse	23	21	4	My heart panted, fearfulness affrighted me: the night of my pleasure hath he turned into fear unto me.
verse	23	21	5	@@Prepare the table, watch in the watchtower, eat, drink: arise, ye princes, @9and@7 anoint the shield.
verse	23	21	6	For thus hath the Lord said unto me, Go, set a watchman, let him declare what he seeth.
verse	23	21	7	@@And he saw a chariot @9with@7 a couple of horsemen, a chariot of asses, @9and@7 a chariot of camels; and he hearkened diligently with much heed:
verse	23	21	8	And he cried, A lion: My lord, I stand continually upon the watchtower in the daytime, and I am set in my ward whole nights:
verse	23	21	9	@@And, behold, here cometh a chariot of men, @9with@7 a couple of horsemen. And he answered and said, Babylon is fallen, is fallen; and all the graven images of her gods he hath broken unto the ground.
verse	23	21	10	O my threshing, and the corn of my floor: that which I have heard of the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, have I declared unto you.
verse	23	21	11	The burden of Dumah. He calleth to me out of Seir, Watchman, what of the night? Watchman, what of the night?
verse	23	21	12	The watchman said, The morning cometh, and also the night: if ye will enquire, enquire ye: return, come.
verse	23	21	13	The burden upon Arabia. In the forest in Arabia shall ye lodge, O ye travelling companies of Dedanim.
verse	23	21	14	The inhabitants of the land of Tema brought water to him that was thirsty, they prevented with their bread him that fled.
verse	23	21	15	For they fled from the swords, from the drawn sword, and from the bent bow, and from the grievousness of war.
verse	23	21	16	For thus hath the Lord said unto me, Within a year, according to the years of an hireling, and all the glory of Kedar shall fail:
verse	23	21	17	@@And the residue of the number of archers, the mighty men of the children of Kedar, shall be diminished: for the LORD God of Israel hath spoken @9it.@7
verse	23	22	1	The burden of the valley of vision. What aileth thee now, that thou art wholly gone up to the housetops?
verse	23	22	2	@@Thou that art full of stirs, a tumultuous city, a joyous city: thy slain @9men are@7 not slain with the sword, nor dead in battle.
verse	23	22	3	@@All thy rulers are fled together, they are bound by the archers: all that are found in thee are bound together, @9which@7 have fled from far.
verse	23	22	4	Therefore said I, Look away from me; I will weep bitterly, labour not to comfort me, because of the spoiling of the daughter of my people.
verse	23	22	5	@@For @9it is@7 a day of trouble, and of treading down, and of perplexity by the Lord GOD of hosts in the valley of vision, breaking down the walls, and of crying to the mountains.
verse	23	22	6	@@And Elam bare the quiver with chariots of men @9and@7 horsemen, and Kir uncovered the shield.
verse	23	22	7	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 thy choicest valleys shall be full of chariots, and the horsemen shall set themselves in array at the gate.
verse	23	22	8	And he discovered the covering of Judah, and thou didst look in that day to the armour of the house of the forest.
verse	23	22	9	Ye have seen also the breaches of the city of David, that they are many: and ye gathered together the waters of the lower pool.
verse	23	22	10	And ye have numbered the houses of Jerusalem, and the houses have ye broken down to fortify the wall.
verse	23	22	11	Ye made also a ditch between the two walls for the water of the old pool: but ye have not looked unto the maker thereof, neither had respect unto him that fashioned it long ago.
verse	23	22	12	And in that day did the Lord GOD of hosts call to weeping, and to mourning, and to baldness, and to girding with sackcloth:
verse	23	22	13	And behold joy and gladness, slaying oxen, and killing sheep, eating flesh, and drinking wine: let us eat and drink; for to morrow we shall die.
verse	23	22	14	And it was revealed in mine ears by the LORD of hosts, Surely this iniquity shall not be purged from you till ye die, saith the Lord GOD of hosts.
verse	23	22	15	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts, Go, get thee unto this treasurer, @9even@7 unto Shebna, which @9is@7 over the house, @9and say, @7
verse	23	22	16	@@What hast thou here? and whom hast thou here, that thou hast hewed thee out a sepulchre here, @9as@7 he that heweth him out a sepulchre on high, @9and@7 that graveth an habitation for himself in a rock?
verse	23	22	17	Behold, the LORD will carry thee away with a mighty captivity, and will surely cover thee.
verse	23	22	18	@@He will surely violently turn and toss thee @9like@7 a ball into a large country: there shalt thou die, and there the chariots of thy glory @9shall be@7 the shame of thy lord's house.
verse	23	22	19	And I will drive thee from thy station, and from thy state shall he pull thee down.
verse	23	22	20	And it shall come to pass in that day, that I will call my servant Eliakim the son of Hilkiah:
verse	23	22	21	And I will clothe him with thy robe, and strengthen him with thy girdle, and I will commit thy government into his hand: and he shall be a father to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and to the house of Judah.
verse	23	22	22	And the key of the house of David will I lay upon his shoulder; so he shall open, and none shall shut; and he shall shut, and none shall open.
verse	23	22	23	And I will fasten him as a nail in a sure place; and he shall be for a glorious throne to his father's house.
verse	23	22	24	And they shall hang upon him all the glory of his father's house, the offspring and the issue, all vessels of small quantity, from the vessels of cups, even to all the vessels of flagons.
verse	23	22	25	@@In that day, saith the LORD of hosts, shall the nail that is fastened in the sure place be removed, and be cut down, and fall; and the burden that @9was@7 upon it shall be cut off: for the LORD hath spoken @9it.@7
verse	23	23	1	The burden of Tyre. Howl, ye ships of Tarshish; for it is laid waste, so that there is no house, no entering in: from the land of Chittim it is revealed to them.
verse	23	23	2	Be still, ye inhabitants of the isle; thou whom the merchants of Zidon, that pass over the sea, have replenished.
verse	23	23	3	@@And by great waters the seed of Sihor, the harvest of the river, @9is@7 her revenue; and she is a mart of nations.
verse	23	23	4	@@Be thou ashamed, O Zidon: for the sea hath spoken, @9even@7 the strength of the sea, saying, I travail not, nor bring forth children, neither do I nourish up young men, @9nor@7 bring up virgins.
verse	23	23	5	@@As at the report concerning Egypt, @9so@7 shall they be sorely pained at the report of Tyre.
verse	23	23	6	Pass ye over to Tarshish; howl, ye inhabitants of the isle.
verse	23	23	7	@@@9Is@7 this your joyous @9city,@7 whose antiquity @9is@7 of ancient days? her own feet shall carry her afar off to sojourn.
verse	23	23	8	@@Who hath taken this counsel against Tyre, the crowning @9city,@7 whose merchants @9are@7 princes, whose traffickers @9are@7 the honourable of the earth?
verse	23	23	9	@@The LORD of hosts hath purposed it, to stain the pride of all glory, @9and@7 to bring into contempt all the honourable of the earth.
verse	23	23	10	@@Pass through thy land as a river, O daughter of Tarshish: @9there is@7 no more strength.
verse	23	23	11	@@He stretched out his hand over the sea, he shook the kingdoms: the LORD hath given a commandment against the merchant @9city,@7 to destroy the strong holds thereof.
verse	23	23	12	And he said, Thou shalt no more rejoice, O thou oppressed virgin, daughter of Zidon: arise, pass over to Chittim; there also shalt thou have no rest.
verse	23	23	13	@@Behold the land of the Chaldeans; this people was not, @9til@7 the Assyrian founded it for them that dwell in the wilderness: they set up the towers thereof, they raised up the palaces thereof; @9and@7 he brought it to ruin.
verse	23	23	14	Howl, ye ships of Tarshish: for your strength is laid waste.
verse	23	23	15	And it shall come to pass in that day, that Tyre shall be forgotten seventy years, according to the days of one king: after the end of seventy years shall Tyre sing as an harlot.
verse	23	23	16	Take an harp, go about the city, thou harlot that hast been forgotten; make sweet melody, sing many songs, that thou mayest be remembered.
verse	23	23	17	And it shall come to pass after the end of seventy years, that the LORD will visit Tyre, and she shall turn to her hire, and shall commit fornication with all the kingdoms of the world upon the face of the earth.
verse	23	23	18	And her merchandise and her hire shall be holiness to the LORD: it shall not be treasured nor laid up; for her merchandise shall be for them that dwell before the LORD, to eat sufficiently, and for durable clothing.
verse	23	24	1	Behold, the LORD maketh the earth empty, and maketh it waste, and turneth it upside down, and scattereth abroad the inhabitants thereof.
verse	23	24	2	And it shall be, as with the people, so with the priest; as with the servant, so with his master; as with the maid, so with her mistress; as with the buyer, so with the seller; as with the lender, so with the borrower; as with the taker of usury, so with the giver of usury to him.
verse	23	24	3	The land shall be utterly emptied, and utterly spoiled: for the LORD hath spoken this word.
verse	23	24	4	@@The earth mourneth @9and@7 fadeth away, the world languisheth @9and@7 fadeth away, the haughty people of the earth do languish.
verse	23	24	5	The earth also is defiled under the inhabitants thereof; because they have transgressed the laws, changed the ordinance, broken the everlasting covenant.
verse	23	24	6	Therefore hath the curse devoured the earth, and they that dwell therein are desolate: therefore the inhabitants of the earth are burned, and few men left.
verse	23	24	7	The new wine mourneth, the vine languisheth, all the merryhearted do sigh.
verse	23	24	8	The mirth of tabrets ceaseth, the noise of them that rejoice endeth, the joy of the harp ceaseth.
verse	23	24	9	They shall not drink wine with a song; strong drink shall be bitter to them that drink it.
verse	23	24	10	The city of confusion is broken down: every house is shut up, that no man may come in.
verse	23	24	11	@@@9There is@7 a crying for wine in the streets; all joy is darkened, the mirth of the land is gone.
verse	23	24	12	In the city is left desolation, and the gate is smitten with destruction.
verse	23	24	13	@@When thus it shall be in the midst of the land among the people, @9there shall be@7 as the shaking of an olive tree, @9and@7 as the gleaning grapes when the vintage is done.
verse	23	24	14	They shall lift up their voice, they shall sing for the majesty of the LORD, they shall cry aloud from the sea.
verse	23	24	15	@@Wherefore glorify ye the LORD in the fires, @9even@7 the name of the LORD God of Israel in the isles of the sea.
verse	23	24	16	@@From the uttermost part of the earth have we heard songs, @9even@7 glory to the righteous. But I said, My leanness, my leanness, woe unto me! the treacherous dealers have dealt treacherously; yea, the treacherous dealers have dealt very treacherously.
verse	23	24	17	@@Fear, and the pit, and the snare, @9are@7 upon thee, O inhabitant of the earth.
verse	23	24	18	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 he who fleeth from the noise of the fear shall fall into the pit; and he that cometh up out of the midst of the pit shall be taken in the snare: for the windows from on high are open, and the foundations of the earth do shake.
verse	23	24	19	The earth is utterly broken down, the earth is clean dissolved, the earth is moved exceedingly.
verse	23	24	20	The earth shall reel to and fro like a drunkard, and shall be removed like a cottage; and the transgression thereof shall be heavy upon it; and it shall fall, and not rise again.
verse	23	24	21	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the LORD shall punish the host of the high ones @9that are@7 on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.
verse	23	24	22	@@And they shall be gathered together, @9as@7 prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.
verse	23	24	23	Then the moon shall be confounded, and the sun ashamed, when the LORD of hosts shall reign in mount Zion, and in Jerusalem, and before his ancients gloriously.
verse	23	25	1	@@O LORD, thou @9art@7 my God; I will exalt thee, I will praise thy name; for thou hast done wonderful @9things; thy@7 counsels of old @9are@7 faithfulness @9and@7 truth.
verse	23	25	2	@@For thou hast made of a city an heap; @9of@7 a defenced city a ruin: a palace of strangers to be no city; it shall never be built.
verse	23	25	3	Therefore shall the strong people glorify thee, the city of the terrible nations shall fear thee.
verse	23	25	4	@@For thou hast been a strength to the poor, a strength to the needy in his distress, a refuge from the storm, a shadow from the heat, when the blast of the terrible ones @9is@7 as a storm @9against@7 the wall.
verse	23	25	5	@@Thou shalt bring down the noise of strangers, as the heat in a dry place; @9even@7 the heat with the shadow of a cloud: the branch of the terrible ones shall be brought low.
verse	23	25	6	And in this mountain shall the LORD of hosts make unto all people a feast of fat things, a feast of wines on the lees, of fat things full of marrow, of wines on the lees well refined.
verse	23	25	7	And he will destroy in this mountain the face of the covering cast over all people, and the vail that is spread over all nations.
verse	23	25	8	@@He will swallow up death in victory; and the Lord GOD will wipe away tears from off all faces; and the rebuke of his people shall he take away from off all the earth: for the LORD hath spoken @9it.@7
verse	23	25	9	@@And it shall be said in that day, Lo, this @9is@7 our God; we have waited for him, and he will save us: this @9is@7 the LORD; we have waited for him, we will be glad and rejoice in his salvation.
verse	23	25	10	For in this mountain shall the hand of the LORD rest, and Moab shall be trodden down under him, even as straw is trodden down for the dunghill.
verse	23	25	11	@@And he shall spread forth his hands in the midst of them, as he that swimmeth spreadeth forth @9his hands@7 to swim: and he shall bring down their pride together with the spoils of their hands.
verse	23	25	12	@@And the fortress of the high fort of thy walls shall he bring down, lay low, @9and@7 bring to the ground, @9even@7 to the dust.
verse	23	26	1	@@In that day shall this song be sung in the land of Judah; We have a strong city; salvation will @9God@7 appoint @9for@7 walls and bulwarks.
verse	23	26	2	Open ye the gates, that the righteous nation which keepeth the truth may enter in.
verse	23	26	3	@@Thou wilt keep @9him@7 in perfect peace, @9whose@7 mind @9is@7 stayed @9on thee:@7 because he trusteth in thee.
verse	23	26	4	@@Trust ye in the LORD for ever: for in the LORD JEHOVAH @9is@7 everlasting strength:
verse	23	26	5	@@For he bringeth down them that dwell on high; the lofty city, he layeth it low; he layeth it low, @9even@7 to the ground; he bringeth it @9even@7 to the dust.
verse	23	26	6	@@The foot shall tread it down, @9even@7 the feet of the poor, @9and@7 the steps of the needy.
verse	23	26	7	@@The way of the just @9is@7 uprightness: thou, most upright, dost weigh the path of the just.
verse	23	26	8	@@Yea, in the way of thy judgments, O LORD, have we waited for thee; the desire of @9our@7 soul @9is@7 to thy name, and to the remembrance of thee.
verse	23	26	9	@@With my soul have I desired thee in the night; yea, with my spirit within me will I seek thee early: for when thy judgments @9are@7 in the earth, the inhabitants of the world will learn righteousness.
verse	23	26	10	@@Let favour be shewed to the wicked, @9yet@7 will he not learn righteousness: in the land of uprightness will he deal unjustly, and will not behold the majesty of the LORD.
verse	23	26	11	@@LORD, @9when@7 thy hand is lifted up, they will not see: @9but@7 they shall see, and be ashamed for @9their@7 envy at the people; yea, the fire of thine enemies shall devour them.
verse	23	26	12	LORD, thou wilt ordain peace for us: for thou also hast wrought all our works in us.
verse	23	26	13	@@O LORD our God, @9other@7 lords besides thee have had dominion over us: @9but@7 by thee only will we make mention of thy name.
verse	23	26	14	@@@9They are@7 dead, they shall not live; @9they are@7 deceased, they shall not rise: therefore hast thou visited and destroyed them, and made all their memory to perish.
verse	23	26	15	@@Thou hast increased the nation, O LORD, thou hast increased the nation: thou art glorified: thou hadst removed @9it@7 far @9unto@7 all the ends of the earth.
verse	23	26	16	@@LORD, in trouble have they visited thee, they poured out a prayer @9when@7 thy chastening @9was@7 upon them.
verse	23	26	17	@@Like as a woman with child, @9that@7 draweth near the time of her delivery, is in pain, @9and@7 crieth out in her pangs; so have we been in thy sight, O LORD.
verse	23	26	18	We have been with child, we have been in pain, we have as it were brought forth wind; we have not wrought any deliverance in the earth; neither have the inhabitants of the world fallen.
verse	23	26	19	@@Thy dead @9men@7 shall live, @9together with@7 my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust: for thy dew @9is as@7 the dew of herbs, and the earth shall cast out the dead.
verse	23	26	20	Come, my people, enter thou into thy chambers, and shut thy doors about thee: hide thyself as it were for a little moment, until the indignation be overpast.
verse	23	26	21	For, behold, the LORD cometh out of his place to punish the inhabitants of the earth for their iniquity: the earth also shall disclose her blood, and shall no more cover her slain.
verse	23	27	1	@@In that day the LORD with his sore and great and strong sword shall punish leviathan the piercing serpent, even leviathan that crooked serpent; and he shall slay the dragon that @9is@7 in the sea.
verse	23	27	2	In that day sing ye unto her, A vineyard of red wine.
verse	23	27	3	@@I the LORD do keep it; I will water it every moment: lest @9any@7 hurt it, I will keep it night and day.
verse	23	27	4	@@Fury @9is@7 not in me: who would set the briers @9and@7 thorns against me in battle? I would go through them, I would burn them together.
verse	23	27	5	@@Or let him take hold of my strength, @9that@7 he may make peace with me; @9and@7 he shall make peace with me.
verse	23	27	6	He shall cause them that come of Jacob to take root: Israel shall blossom and bud, and fill the face of the world with fruit.
verse	23	27	7	@@Hath he smitten him, as he smote those that smote him? @9or@7 is he slain according to the slaughter of them that are slain by him?
verse	23	27	8	In measure, when it shooteth forth, thou wilt debate with it: he stayeth his rough wind in the day of the east wind.
verse	23	27	9	By this therefore shall the iniquity of Jacob be purged; and this is all the fruit to take away his sin; when he maketh all the stones of the altar as chalkstones that are beaten in sunder, the groves and images shall not stand up.
verse	23	27	10	@@Yet the defenced city @9shall be@7 desolate, @9and@7 the habitation forsaken, and left like a wilderness: there shall the calf feed, and there shall he lie down, and consume the branches thereof.
verse	23	27	11	@@When the boughs thereof are withered, they shall be broken off: the women come, @9and@7 set them on fire: for it @9is@7 a people of no understanding: therefore he that made them will not have mercy on them, and he that formed them will shew them no favour.
verse	23	27	12	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the LORD shall beat off from the channel of the river unto the stream of Egypt, and ye shall be gathered one by one, O ye children of Israel.
verse	23	27	13	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the great trumpet shall be blown, and they shall come which were ready to perish in the land of Assyria, and the outcasts in the land of Egypt, and shall worship the LORD in the holy mount at Jerusalem.
verse	23	28	1	@@Woe to the crown of pride, to the drunkards of Ephraim, whose glorious beauty is a fading flower, which @9are@7 on the head of the fat valleys of them that are overcome with wine!
verse	23	28	2	@@Behold, the Lord hath a mighty and strong one, @9which@7 as a tempest of hail @9and@7 a destroying storm, as a flood of mighty waters overflowing, shall cast down to the earth with the hand.
verse	23	28	3	The crown of pride, the drunkards of Ephraim, shall be trodden under feet:
verse	23	28	4	@@And the glorious beauty, which is on the head of the fat valley, shall be a fading flower, @9and@7 as the hasty fruit before the summer; which @9when@7 he that looketh upon it seeth, while it is yet in his hand he eateth it up.
verse	23	28	5	In that day shall the LORD of hosts be for a crown of glory, and for a diadem of beauty, unto the residue of his people,
verse	23	28	6	And for a spirit of judgment to him that sitteth in judgment, and for strength to them that turn the battle to the gate.
verse	23	28	7	@@But they also have erred through wine, and through strong drink are out of the way; the priest and the prophet have erred through strong drink, they are swallowed up of wine, they are out of the way through strong drink; they err in vision, they stumble @9in@7 judgment.
verse	23	28	8	@@For all tables are full of vomit @9and@7 filthiness, @9so that there is@7 no place @9clean.@7
verse	23	28	9	@@Whom shall he teach knowledge? and whom shall he make to understand doctrine? @9them that are@7 weaned from the milk, @9and@7 drawn from the breasts.
verse	23	28	10	@@For precept @9must be@7 upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, @9and@7 there a little:
verse	23	28	11	For with stammering lips and another tongue will he speak to this people.
verse	23	28	12	@@To whom he said, This @9is@7 the rest @9wherewith@7 ye may cause the weary to rest; and this @9is@7 the refreshing: yet they would not hear.
verse	23	28	13	@@But the word of the LORD was unto them precept upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, @9and@7 there a little; that they might go, and fall backward, and be broken, and snared, and taken.
verse	23	28	14	@@Wherefore hear the word of the LORD, ye scornful men, that rule this people which @9is@7 in Jerusalem.
verse	23	28	15	Because ye have said, We have made a covenant with death, and with hell are we at agreement; when the overflowing scourge shall pass through, it shall not come unto us: for we have made lies our refuge, and under falsehood have we hid ourselves:
verse	23	28	16	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD, Behold, I lay in Zion for a foundation a stone, a tried stone, a precious corner @9stone,@7 a sure foundation: he that believeth shall not make haste.
verse	23	28	17	Judgment also will I lay to the line, and righteousness to the plummet: and the hail shall sweep away the refuge of lies, and the waters shall overflow the hiding place.
verse	23	28	18	And your covenant with death shall be disannulled, and your agreement with hell shall not stand; when the overflowing scourge shall pass through, then ye shall be trodden down by it.
verse	23	28	19	From the time that it goeth forth it shall take you: for morning by morning shall it pass over, by day and by night: and it shall be a vexation only to understand the report.
verse	23	28	20	@@For the bed is shorter than that @9a man@7 can stretch himself @9on it:@7 and the covering narrower than that he can wrap himself @9in it. @7
verse	23	28	21	@@For the LORD shall rise up as @9in@7 mount Perazim, he shall be wroth as @9in@7 the valley of Gibeon, that he may do his work, his strange work; and bring to pass his act, his strange act.
verse	23	28	22	Now therefore be ye not mockers, lest your bands be made strong: for I have heard from the Lord GOD of hosts a consumption, even determined upon the whole earth.
verse	23	28	23	Give ye ear, and hear my voice; hearken, and hear my speech.
verse	23	28	24	Doth the plowman plow all day to sow? doth he open and break the clods of his ground?
verse	23	28	25	When he hath made plain the face thereof, doth he not cast abroad the fitches, and scatter the cummin, and cast in the principal wheat and the appointed barley and rie in their place?
verse	23	28	26	@@For his God doth instruct him to discretion, @9and@7 doth teach him.
verse	23	28	27	For the fitches are not threshed with a threshing instrument, neither is a cart wheel turned about upon the cummin; but the fitches are beaten out with a staff, and the cummin with a rod.
verse	23	28	28	@@Bread @9corn@7 is bruised; because he will not ever be threshing it, nor break @9it with@7 the wheel of his cart, nor bruise it @9with@7 his horsemen.
verse	23	28	29	@@This also cometh forth from the LORD of hosts, @9which@7 is wonderful in counsel, @9and@7 excellent in working.
verse	23	29	1	@@Woe to Ariel, to Ariel, the city @9where@7 David dwelt! add ye year to year; let them kill sacrifices.
verse	23	29	2	Yet I will distress Ariel, and there shall be heaviness and sorrow: and it shall be unto me as Ariel.
verse	23	29	3	And I will camp against thee round about, and will lay siege against thee with a mount, and I will raise forts against thee.
verse	23	29	4	@@And thou shalt be brought down, @9and@7 shalt speak out of the ground, and thy speech shall be low out of the dust, and thy voice shall be, as of one that hath a familiar spirit, out of the ground, and thy speech shall whisper out of the dust.
verse	23	29	5	@@Moreover the multitude of thy strangers shall be like small dust, and the multitude of the terrible ones @9shall be@7 as chaff that passeth away: yea, it shall be at an instant suddenly.
verse	23	29	6	Thou shalt be visited of the LORD of hosts with thunder, and with earthquake, and great noise, with storm and tempest, and the flame of devouring fire.
verse	23	29	7	And the multitude of all the nations that fight against Ariel, even all that fight against her and her munition, and that distress her, shall be as a dream of a night vision.
verse	23	29	8	@@It shall even be as when an hungry @9man@7 dreameth, and, behold, he eateth; but he awaketh, and his soul is empty: or as when a thirsty man dreameth, and, behold, he drinketh; but he awaketh, and, behold, @9he is@7 faint, and his soul hath appetite: so shall the multitude of all the nations be, that fight against mount Zion.
verse	23	29	9	Stay yourselves, and wonder; cry ye out, and cry: they are drunken, but not with wine; they stagger, but not with strong drink.
verse	23	29	10	For the LORD hath poured out upon you the spirit of deep sleep, and hath closed your eyes: the prophets and your rulers, the seers hath he covered.
verse	23	29	11	@@And the vision of all is become unto you as the words of a book that is sealed, which @9men@7 deliver to one that is learned, saying, Read this, I pray thee: and he saith, I cannot; for it @9is@7 sealed:
verse	23	29	12	And the book is delivered to him that is not learned, saying, Read this, I pray thee: and he saith, I am not learned.
verse	23	29	13	@@Wherefore the Lord said, Forasmuch as this people draw near @9me@7 with their mouth, and with their lips do honour me, but have removed their heart far from me, and their fear toward me is taught by the precept of men:
verse	23	29	14	@@Therefore, behold, I will proceed to do a marvellous work among this people, @9even@7 a marvellous work and a wonder: for the wisdom of their wise @9men@7 shall perish, and the understanding of their prudent @9men@7 shall be hid.
verse	23	29	15	Woe unto them that seek deep to hide their counsel from the LORD, and their works are in the dark, and they say, Who seeth us? and who knoweth us?
verse	23	29	16	Surely your turning of things upside down shall be esteemed as the potter's clay: for shall the work say of him that made it, He made me not? or shall the thing framed say of him that framed it, He had no understanding?
verse	23	29	17	@@@9Is@7 it not yet a very little while, and Lebanon shall be turned into a fruitful field, and the fruitful field shall be esteemed as a forest?
verse	23	29	18	And in that day shall the deaf hear the words of the book, and the eyes of the blind shall see out of obscurity, and out of darkness.
verse	23	29	19	@@The meek also shall increase @9their@7 joy in the LORD, and the poor among men shall rejoice in the Holy One of Israel.
verse	23	29	20	For the terrible one is brought to nought, and the scorner is consumed, and all that watch for iniquity are cut off:
verse	23	29	21	That make a man an offender for a word, and lay a snare for him that reproveth in the gate, and turn aside the just for a thing of nought.
verse	23	29	22	Therefore thus saith the LORD, who redeemed Abraham, concerning the house of Jacob, Jacob shall not now be ashamed, neither shall his face now wax pale.
verse	23	29	23	But when he seeth his children, the work of mine hands, in the midst of him, they shall sanctify my name, and sanctify the Holy One of Jacob, and shall fear the God of Israel.
verse	23	29	24	They also that erred in spirit shall come to understanding, and they that murmured shall learn doctrine.
verse	23	30	1	Woe to the rebellious children, saith the LORD, that take counsel, but not of me; and that cover with a covering, but not of my spirit, that they may add sin to sin:
verse	23	30	2	That walk to go down into Egypt, and have not asked at my mouth; to strengthen themselves in the strength of Pharaoh, and to trust in the shadow of Egypt!
verse	23	30	3	@@Therefore shall the strength of Pharaoh be your shame, and the trust in the shadow of Egypt @9your@7 confusion.
verse	23	30	4	For his princes were at Zoan, and his ambassadors came to Hanes.
verse	23	30	5	@@They were all ashamed of a people @9that@7 could not profit them, nor be an help nor profit, but a shame, and also a reproach.
verse	23	30	6	@@The burden of the beasts of the south: into the land of trouble and anguish, from whence @9come@7 the young and old lion, the viper and fiery flying serpent, they will carry their riches upon the shoulders of young asses, and their treasures upon the bunches of camels, to a people @9that@7 shall not profit @9them. @7
verse	23	30	7	@@For the Egyptians shall help in vain, and to no purpose: therefore have I cried concerning this, Their strength @9is@7 to sit still.
verse	23	30	8	Now go, write it before them in a table, and note it in a book, that it may be for the time to come for ever and ever:
verse	23	30	9	@@That this @9is@7 a rebellious people, lying children, children @9that@7 will not hear the law of the LORD:
verse	23	30	10	Which say to the seers, See not; and to the prophets, Prophesy not unto us right things, speak unto us smooth things, prophesy deceits:
verse	23	30	11	Get you out of the way, turn aside out of the path, cause the Holy One of Israel to cease from before us.
verse	23	30	12	Wherefore thus saith the Holy One of Israel, Because ye despise this word, and trust in oppression and perverseness, and stay thereon:
verse	23	30	13	Therefore this iniquity shall be to you as a breach ready to fall, swelling out in a high wall, whose breaking cometh suddenly at an instant.
verse	23	30	14	@@And he shall break it as the breaking of the potters' vessel that is broken in pieces; he shall not spare: so that there shall not be found in the bursting of it a sherd to take fire from the hearth, or to take water @9withal@7 out of the pit.
verse	23	30	15	For thus saith the Lord GOD, the Holy One of Israel; In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not.
verse	23	30	16	But ye said, No; for we will flee upon horses; therefore shall ye flee: and, We will ride upon the swift; therefore shall they that pursue you be swift.
verse	23	30	17	@@One thousand @9shall flee@7 at the rebuke of one; at the rebuke of five shall ye flee: till ye be left as a beacon upon the top of a mountain, and as an ensign on an hill.
verse	23	30	18	@@And therefore will the LORD wait, that he may be gracious unto you, and therefore will he be exalted, that he may have mercy upon you: for the LORD @9is@7 a God of judgment: blessed @9are@7 all they that wait for him.
verse	23	30	19	For the people shall dwell in Zion at Jerusalem: thou shalt weep no more: he will be very gracious unto thee at the voice of thy cry; when he shall hear it, he will answer thee.
verse	23	30	20	@@And @9though@7 the Lord give you the bread of adversity, and the water of affliction, yet shall not thy teachers be removed into a corner any more, but thine eyes shall see thy teachers:
verse	23	30	21	@@And thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This @9is@7 the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left.
verse	23	30	22	Ye shall defile also the covering of thy graven images of silver, and the ornament of thy molten images of gold: thou shalt cast them away as a menstruous cloth; thou shalt say unto it, Get thee hence.
verse	23	30	23	Then shall he give the rain of thy seed, that thou shalt sow the ground withal; and bread of the increase of the earth, and it shall be fat and plenteous: in that day shall thy cattle feed in large pastures.
verse	23	30	24	The oxen likewise and the young asses that ear the ground shall eat clean provender, which hath been winnowed with the shovel and with the fan.
verse	23	30	25	@@And there shall be upon every high mountain, and upon every high hill, rivers @9and@7 streams of waters in the day of the great slaughter, when the towers fall.
verse	23	30	26	Moreover the light of the moon shall be as the light of the sun, and the light of the sun shall be sevenfold, as the light of seven days, in the day that the LORD bindeth up the breach of his people, and healeth the stroke of their wound.
verse	23	30	27	@@Behold, the name of the LORD cometh from far, burning @9with@7 his anger, and the burden @9thereof is@7 heavy: his lips are full of indignation, and his tongue as a devouring fire:
verse	23	30	28	@@And his breath, as an overflowing stream, shall reach to the midst of the neck, to sift the nations with the sieve of vanity: and @9there shall be@7 a bridle in the jaws of the people, causing @9them@7 to err.
verse	23	30	29	@@Ye shall have a song, as in the night @9when@7 a holy solemnity is kept; and gladness of heart, as when one goeth with a pipe to come into the mountain of the LORD, to the mighty One of Israel.
verse	23	30	30	@@And the LORD shall cause his glorious voice to be heard, and shall shew the lighting down of his arm, with the indignation of @9his@7 anger, and @9with@7 the flame of a devouring fire, @9with@7 scattering, and tempest, and hailstones.
verse	23	30	31	@@For through the voice of the LORD shall the Assyrian be beaten down, @9which@7 smote with a rod.
verse	23	30	32	@@And @9in@7 every place where the grounded staff shall pass, which the LORD shall lay upon him, @9it@7 shall be with tabrets and harps: and in battles of shaking will he fight with it.
verse	23	30	33	@@For Tophet @9is@7 ordained of old; yea, for the king it is prepared; he hath made @9it@7 deep @9and@7 large: the pile thereof @9is@7 fire and much wood; the breath of the LORD, like a stream of brimstone, doth kindle it.
verse	23	31	1	@@Woe to them that go down to Egypt for help; and stay on horses, and trust in chariots, because @9they are@7 many; and in horsemen, because they are very strong; but they look not unto the Holy One of Israel, neither seek the LORD!
verse	23	31	2	@@Yet he also @9is@7 wise, and will bring evil, and will not call back his words: but will arise against the house of the evildoers, and against the help of them that work iniquity.
verse	23	31	3	@@Now the Egyptians @9are@7 men, and not God; and their horses flesh, and not spirit. When the LORD shall stretch out his hand, both he that helpeth shall fall, and he that is holpen shall fall down, and they all shall fail together.
verse	23	31	4	@@For thus hath the LORD spoken unto me, Like as the lion and the young lion roaring on his prey, when a multitude of shepherds is called forth against him, @9he@7 will not be afraid of their voice, nor abase himself for the noise of them: so shall the LORD of hosts come down to fight for mount Zion, and for the hill thereof.
verse	23	31	5	@@As birds flying, so will the LORD of hosts defend Jerusalem; defending also he will deliver @9it; and@7 passing over he will preserve @9it.@7
verse	23	31	6	@@Turn ye unto @9him from@7 whom the children of Israel have deeply revolted.
verse	23	31	7	@@For in that day every man shall cast away his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which your own hands have made unto you @9for@7 a sin.
verse	23	31	8	Then shall the Assyrian fall with the sword, not of a mighty man; and the sword, not of a mean man, shall devour him: but he shall flee from the sword, and his young men shall be discomfited.
verse	23	31	9	@@And he shall pass over to his strong hold for fear, and his princes shall be afraid of the ensign, saith the LORD, whose fire @9is@7 in Zion, and his furnace in Jerusalem.
verse	23	32	1	Behold, a king shall reign in righteousness, and princes shall rule in judgment.
verse	23	32	2	And a man shall be as an hiding place from the wind, and a covert from the tempest; as rivers of water in a dry place, as the shadow of a great rock in a weary land.
verse	23	32	3	And the eyes of them that see shall not be dim, and the ears of them that hear shall hearken.
verse	23	32	4	The heart also of the rash shall understand knowledge, and the tongue of the stammerers shall be ready to speak plainly.
verse	23	32	5	@@The vile person shall be no more called liberal, nor the churl said @9to be@7 bountiful.
verse	23	32	6	For the vile person will speak villany, and his heart will work iniquity, to practise hypocrisy, and to utter error against the LORD, to make empty the soul of the hungry, and he will cause the drink of the thirsty to fail.
verse	23	32	7	@@The instruments also of the churl @9are@7 evil: he deviseth wicked devices to destroy the poor with lying words, even when the needy speaketh right.
verse	23	32	8	But the liberal deviseth liberal things; and by liberal things shall he stand.
verse	23	32	9	Rise up, ye women that are at ease; hear my voice, ye careless daughters; give ear unto my speech.
verse	23	32	10	Many days and years shall ye be troubled, ye careless women: for the vintage shall fail, the gathering shall not come.
verse	23	32	11	@@Tremble, ye women that are at ease; be troubled, ye careless ones: strip you, and make you bare, and gird @9sackcloth@7 upon @9your@7 loins.
verse	23	32	12	They shall lament for the teats, for the pleasant fields, for the fruitful vine.
verse	23	32	13	@@Upon the land of my people shall come up thorns @9and@7 briers; yea, upon all the houses of joy @9in@7 the joyous city:
verse	23	32	14	Because the palaces shall be forsaken; the multitude of the city shall be left; the forts and towers shall be for dens for ever, a joy of wild asses, a pasture of flocks;
verse	23	32	15	Until the spirit be poured upon us from on high, and the wilderness be a fruitful field, and the fruitful field be counted for a forest.
verse	23	32	16	Then judgment shall dwell in the wilderness, and righteousness remain in the fruitful field.
verse	23	32	17	And the work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of righteousness quietness and assurance for ever.
verse	23	32	18	And my people shall dwell in a peaceable habitation, and in sure dwellings, and in quiet resting places;
verse	23	32	19	When it shall hail, coming down on the forest; and the city shall be low in a low place.
verse	23	32	20	@@Blessed @9are@7 ye that sow beside all waters, that send forth @9thither@7 the feet of the ox and the ass.
verse	23	33	1	@@Woe to thee that spoilest, and thou @9wast@7 not spoiled; and dealest treacherously, and they dealt not treacherously with thee! when thou shalt cease to spoil, thou shalt be spoiled; @9and@7 when thou shalt make an end to deal treacherously, they shall deal treacherously with thee.
verse	23	33	2	O LORD, be gracious unto us; we have waited for thee: be thou their arm every morning, our salvation also in the time of trouble.
verse	23	33	3	At the noise of the tumult the people fled; at the lifting up of thyself the nations were scattered.
verse	23	33	4	@@And your spoil shall be gathered @9like@7 the gathering of the caterpiller: as the running to and fro of locusts shall he run upon them.
verse	23	33	5	The LORD is exalted; for he dwelleth on high: he hath filled Zion with judgment and righteousness.
verse	23	33	6	@@And wisdom and knowledge shall be the stability of thy times, @9and@7 strength of salvation: the fear of the LORD @9is@7 his treasure.
verse	23	33	7	Behold, their valiant ones shall cry without: the ambassadors of peace shall weep bitterly.
verse	23	33	8	The highways lie waste, the wayfaring man ceaseth: he hath broken the covenant, he hath despised the cities, he regardeth no man.
verse	23	33	9	@@The earth mourneth @9and@7 languisheth: Lebanon is ashamed @9and@7 hewn down: Sharon is like a wilderness; and Bashan and Carmel shake off @9their fruits. @7
verse	23	33	10	Now will I rise, saith the LORD; now will I be exalted; now will I lift up myself.
verse	23	33	11	@@Ye shall conceive chaff, ye shall bring forth stubble: your breath, @9as@7 fire, shall devour you.
verse	23	33	12	@@And the people shall be as the burnings of lime: @9as@7 thorns cut up shall they be burned in the fire.
verse	23	33	13	@@Hear, ye @9that are@7 far off, what I have done; and, ye @9that are@7 near, acknowledge my might.
verse	23	33	14	The sinners in Zion are afraid; fearfulness hath surprised the hypocrites. Who among us shall dwell with the devouring fire? who among us shall dwell with everlasting burnings?
verse	23	33	15	He that walketh righteously, and speaketh uprightly; he that despiseth the gain of oppressions, that shaketh his hands from holding of bribes, that stoppeth his ears from hearing of blood, and shutteth his eyes from seeing evil;
verse	23	33	16	@@He shall dwell on high: his place of defence @9shall be@7 the munitions of rocks: bread shall be given him; his waters @9shall be@7 sure.
verse	23	33	17	Thine eyes shall see the king in his beauty: they shall behold the land that is very far off.
verse	23	33	18	@@Thine heart shall meditate terror. Where @9is@7 the scribe? where @9is@7 the receiver? where @9is@7 he that counted the towers?
verse	23	33	19	@@Thou shalt not see a fierce people, a people of a deeper speech than thou canst perceive; of a stammering tongue, @9that thou canst@7 not understand.
verse	23	33	20	@@Look upon Zion, the city of our solemnities: thine eyes shall see Jerusalem a quiet habitation, a tabernacle @9that@7 shall not be taken down; not one of the stakes thereof shall ever be removed, neither shall any of the cords thereof be broken.
verse	23	33	21	@@But there the glorious LORD @9will be@7 unto us a place of broad rivers @9and@7 streams; wherein shall go no galley with oars, neither shall gallant ship pass thereby.
verse	23	33	22	@@For the LORD @9is@7 our judge, the LORD @9is@7 our lawgiver, the LORD @9is@7 our king; he will save us.
verse	23	33	23	Thy tacklings are loosed; they could not well strengthen their mast, they could not spread the sail: then is the prey of a great spoil divided; the lame take the prey.
verse	23	33	24	@@And the inhabitant shall not say, I am sick: the people that dwell therein @9shall be@7 forgiven @9their@7 iniquity.
verse	23	34	1	Come near, ye nations, to hear; and hearken, ye people: let the earth hear, and all that is therein; the world, and all things that come forth of it.
verse	23	34	2	@@For the indignation of the LORD @9is@7 upon all nations, and @9his@7 fury upon all their armies: he hath utterly destroyed them, he hath delivered them to the slaughter.
verse	23	34	3	Their slain also shall be cast out, and their stink shall come up out of their carcases, and the mountains shall be melted with their blood.
verse	23	34	4	@@And all the host of heaven shall be dissolved, and the heavens shall be rolled together as a scroll: and all their host shall fall down, as the leaf falleth off from the vine, and as a falling @9fig@7 from the fig tree.
verse	23	34	5	For my sword shall be bathed in heaven: behold, it shall come down upon Idumea, and upon the people of my curse, to judgment.
verse	23	34	6	@@The sword of the LORD is filled with blood, it is made fat with fatness, @9and@7 with the blood of lambs and goats, with the fat of the kidneys of rams: for the LORD hath a sacrifice in Bozrah, and a great slaughter in the land of Idumea.
verse	23	34	7	And the unicorns shall come down with them, and the bullocks with the bulls; and their land shall be soaked with blood, and their dust made fat with fatness.
verse	23	34	8	@@For @9it is@7 the day of the LORD'S vengeance, @9and@7 the year of recompences for the controversy of Zion.
verse	23	34	9	And the streams thereof shall be turned into pitch, and the dust thereof into brimstone, and the land thereof shall become burning pitch.
verse	23	34	10	It shall not be quenched night nor day; the smoke thereof shall go up for ever: from generation to generation it shall lie waste; none shall pass through it for ever and ever.
verse	23	34	11	But the cormorant and the bittern shall possess it; the owl also and the raven shall dwell in it: and he shall stretch out upon it the line of confusion, and the stones of emptiness.
verse	23	34	12	@@They shall call the nobles thereof to the kingdom, but none @9shall be@7 there, and all her princes shall be nothing.
verse	23	34	13	@@And thorns shall come up in her palaces, nettles and brambles in the fortresses thereof: and it shall be an habitation of dragons, @9and@7 a court for owls.
verse	23	34	14	The wild beasts of the desert shall also meet with the wild beasts of the island, and the satyr shall cry to his fellow; the screech owl also shall rest there, and find for herself a place of rest.
verse	23	34	15	There shall the great owl make her nest, and lay, and hatch, and gather under her shadow: there shall the vultures also be gathered, every one with her mate.
verse	23	34	16	Seek ye out of the book of the LORD, and read: no one of these shall fail, none shall want her mate: for my mouth it hath commanded, and his spirit it hath gathered them.
verse	23	34	17	And he hath cast the lot for them, and his hand hath divided it unto them by line: they shall possess it for ever, from generation to generation shall they dwell therein.
verse	23	35	1	The wilderness and the solitary place shall be glad for them; and the desert shall rejoice, and blossom as the rose.
verse	23	35	2	@@It shall blossom abundantly, and rejoice even with joy and singing: the glory of Lebanon shall be given unto it, the excellency of Carmel and Sharon, they shall see the glory of the LORD, @9and@7 the excellency of our God.
verse	23	35	3	Strengthen ye the weak hands, and confirm the feeble knees.
verse	23	35	4	@@Say to them @9that are@7 of a fearful heart, Be strong, fear not: behold, your God will come @9with@7 vengeance, @9even@7 God @9with@7 a recompence; he will come and save you.
verse	23	35	5	Then the eyes of the blind shall be opened, and the ears of the deaf shall be unstopped.
verse	23	35	6	@@Then shall the lame @9man@7 leap as an hart, and the tongue of the dumb sing: for in the wilderness shall waters break out, and streams in the desert.
verse	23	35	7	@@And the parched ground shall become a pool, and the thirsty land springs of water: in the habitation of dragons, where each lay, @9shall be@7 grass with reeds and rushes.
verse	23	35	8	@@And an highway shall be there, and a way, and it shall be called The way of holiness; the unclean shall not pass over it; but it @9shall be@7 for those: the wayfaring men, though fools, shall not err @9therein. @7
verse	23	35	9	@@No lion shall be there, nor @9any@7 ravenous beast shall go up thereon, it shall not be found there; but the redeemed shall walk @9there: @7
verse	23	35	10	And the ransomed of the LORD shall return, and come to Zion with songs and everlasting joy upon their heads: they shall obtain joy and gladness, and sorrow and sighing shall flee away.
verse	23	36	1	@@Now it came to pass in the fourteenth year of king Hezekiah, @9that@7 Sennacherib king of Assyria came up against all the defenced cities of Judah, and took them.
verse	23	36	2	And the king of Assyria sent Rabshakeh from Lachish to Jerusalem unto king Hezekiah with a great army. And he stood by the conduit of the upper pool in the highway of the fuller's field.
verse	23	36	3	Then came forth unto him Eliakim, Hilkiah's son, which was over the house, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, Asaph's son, the recorder.
verse	23	36	4	And Rabshakeh said unto them, Say ye now to Hezekiah, Thus saith the great king, the king of Assyria, What confidence is this wherein thou trustest?
verse	23	36	5	@@I say, @9sayest thou,@7 (but @9they are but@7 vain words) @9I have@7 counsel and strength for war: now on whom dost thou trust, that thou rebellest against me?
verse	23	36	6	@@Lo, thou trustest in the staff of this broken reed, on Egypt; whereon if a man lean, it will go into his hand, and pierce it: so @9is@7 Pharaoh king of Egypt to all that trust in him.
verse	23	36	7	@@But if thou say to me, We trust in the LORD our God: @9is it@7 not he, whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah hath taken away, and said to Judah and to Jerusalem, Ye shall worship before this altar?
verse	23	36	8	Now therefore give pledges, I pray thee, to my master the king of Assyria, and I will give thee two thousand horses, if thou be able on thy part to set riders upon them.
verse	23	36	9	How then wilt thou turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master's servants, and put thy trust on Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?
verse	23	36	10	And am I now come up without the LORD against this land to destroy it? the LORD said unto me, Go up against this land, and destroy it.
verse	23	36	11	@@Then said Eliakim and Shebna and Joah unto Rabshakeh, Speak, I pray thee, unto thy servants in the Syrian language; for we understand @9it:@7 and speak not to us in the Jews' language, in the ears of the people that @9are@7 on the wall.
verse	23	36	12	@@But Rabshakeh said, Hath my master sent me to thy master and to thee to speak these words? @9hath he@7 not @9sent me@7 to the men that sit upon the wall, that they may eat their own dung, and drink their own piss with you?
verse	23	36	13	Then Rabshakeh stood, and cried with a loud voice in the Jews' language, and said, Hear ye the words of the great king, the king of Assyria.
verse	23	36	14	Thus saith the king, Let not Hezekiah deceive you: for he shall not be able to deliver you.
verse	23	36	15	Neither let Hezekiah make you trust in the LORD, saying, The LORD will surely deliver us: this city shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.
verse	23	36	16	@@Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus saith the king of Assyria, Make @9an agreement@7 with me @9by@7 a present, and come out to me: and eat ye every one of his vine, and every one of his fig tree, and drink ye every one the waters of his own cistern;
verse	23	36	17	Until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of corn and wine, a land of bread and vineyards.
verse	23	36	18	@@@9Beware@7 lest Hezekiah persuade you, saying, The LORD will deliver us. Hath any of the gods of the nations delivered his land out of the hand of the king of Assyria?
verse	23	36	19	@@Where @9are@7 the gods of Hamath and Arphad? where @9are@7 the gods of Sepharvaim? and have they delivered Samaria out of my hand?
verse	23	36	20	@@Who @9are they@7 among all the gods of these lands, that have delivered their land out of my hand, that the LORD should deliver Jerusalem out of my hand?
verse	23	36	21	But they held their peace, and answered him not a word: for the king's commandment was, saying, Answer him not.
verse	23	36	22	@@Then came Eliakim, the son of Hilkiah, that @9was@7 over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, the son of Asaph, the recorder, to Hezekiah with @9their@7 clothes rent, and told him the words of Rabshakeh.
verse	23	37	1	@@And it came to pass, when king Hezekiah heard @9it,@7 that he rent his clothes, and covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the house of the LORD.
verse	23	37	2	@@And he sent Eliakim, who @9was@7 over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests covered with sackcloth, unto Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.
verse	23	37	3	@@And they said unto him, Thus saith Hezekiah, This day @9is@7 a day of trouble, and of rebuke, and of blasphemy: for the children are come to the birth, and @9there is@7 not strength to bring forth.
verse	23	37	4	@@It may be the LORD thy God will hear the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master hath sent to reproach the living God, and will reprove the words which the LORD thy God hath heard: wherefore lift up @9thy@7 prayer for the remnant that is left.
verse	23	37	5	So the servants of king Hezekiah came to Isaiah.
verse	23	37	6	And Isaiah said unto them, Thus shall ye say unto your master, Thus saith the LORD, Be not afraid of the words that thou hast heard, wherewith the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me.
verse	23	37	7	Behold, I will send a blast upon him, and he shall hear a rumour, and return to his own land; and I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.
verse	23	37	8	So Rabshakeh returned, and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah: for he had heard that he was departed from Lachish.
verse	23	37	9	@@And he heard say concerning Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, He is come forth to make war with thee. And when he heard @9it,@7 he sent messengers to Hezekiah, saying,
verse	23	37	10	Thus shall ye speak to Hezekiah king of Judah, saying, Let not thy God, in whom thou trustest, deceive thee, saying, Jerusalem shall not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.
verse	23	37	11	Behold, thou hast heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands by destroying them utterly; and shalt thou be delivered?
verse	23	37	12	@@Have the gods of the nations delivered them which my fathers have destroyed, @9as@7 Gozan, and Haran, and Rezeph, and the children of Eden which @9were@7 in Telassar?
verse	23	37	13	@@Where @9is@7 the king of Hamath, and the king of Arphad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivah?
verse	23	37	14	And Hezekiah received the letter from the hand of the messengers, and read it: and Hezekiah went up unto the house of the LORD, and spread it before the LORD.
verse	23	37	15	And Hezekiah prayed unto the LORD, saying,
verse	23	37	16	@@O LORD of hosts, God of Israel, that dwellest @9between@7 the cherubims, thou @9art@7 the God, @9even@7 thou alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth: thou hast made heaven and earth.
verse	23	37	17	Incline thine ear, O LORD, and hear; open thine eyes, O LORD, and see: and hear all the words of Sennacherib, which hath sent to reproach the living God.
verse	23	37	18	Of a truth, LORD, the kings of Assyria have laid waste all the nations, and their countries,
verse	23	37	19	@@And have cast their gods into the fire: for they @9were@7 no gods, but the work of men's hands, wood and stone: therefore they have destroyed them.
verse	23	37	20	@@Now therefore, O LORD our God, save us from his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that thou @9art@7 the LORD, @9even@7 thou only.
verse	23	37	21	Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent unto Hezekiah, saying, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Whereas thou hast prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria:
verse	23	37	22	@@This @9is@7 the word which the LORD hath spoken concerning him; The virgin, the daughter of Zion, hath despised thee, @9and@7 laughed thee to scorn; the daughter of Jerusalem hath shaken her head at thee.
verse	23	37	23	@@Whom hast thou reproached and blasphemed? and against whom hast thou exalted @9thy@7 voice, and lifted up thine eyes on high? @9even@7 against the Holy One of Israel.
verse	23	37	24	@@By thy servants hast thou reproached the Lord, and hast said, By the multitude of my chariots am I come up to the height of the mountains, to the sides of Lebanon; and I will cut down the tall cedars thereof, @9and@7 the choice fir trees thereof: and I will enter into the height of his border, @9and@7 the forest of his Carmel.
verse	23	37	25	I have digged, and drunk water; and with the sole of my feet have I dried up all the rivers of the besieged places.
verse	23	37	26	@@Hast thou not heard long ago, @9how@7 I have done it; @9and@7 of ancient times, that I have formed it? now have I brought it to pass, that thou shouldest be to lay waste defenced cities @9into@7 ruinous heaps.
verse	23	37	27	@@Therefore their inhabitants @9were@7 of small power, they were dismayed and confounded: they were @9as@7 the grass of the field, and @9as@7 the green herb, @9as@7 the grass on the housetops, and @9as corn@7 blasted before it be grown up.
verse	23	37	28	But I know thy abode, and thy going out, and thy coming in, and thy rage against me.
verse	23	37	29	Because thy rage against me, and thy tumult, is come up into mine ears, therefore will I put my hook in thy nose, and my bridle in thy lips, and I will turn thee back by the way by which thou camest.
verse	23	37	30	@@And this @9shall be@7 a sign unto thee, Ye shall eat @9this@7 year such as groweth of itself; and the second year that which springeth of the same: and in the third year sow ye, and reap, and plant vineyards, and eat the fruit thereof.
verse	23	37	31	And the remnant that is escaped of the house of Judah shall again take root downward, and bear fruit upward:
verse	23	37	32	For out of Jerusalem shall go forth a remnant, and they that escape out of mount Zion: the zeal of the LORD of hosts shall do this.
verse	23	37	33	Therefore thus saith the LORD concerning the king of Assyria, He shall not come into this city, nor shoot an arrow there nor come before it with shields, nor cast a bank against it.
verse	23	37	34	By the way that he came, by the same shall he return, and shall not come into this city, saith the LORD.
verse	23	37	35	For I will defend this city to save it for mine own sake, and for my servant David's sake.
verse	23	37	36	@@Then the angel of the LORD went forth, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians a hundred and fourscore and five thousand: and when they arose early in the morning, behold, they @9were@7 all dead corpses.
verse	23	37	37	So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, and went and returned, and dwelt at Nineveh.
verse	23	37	38	And it came to pass, as he was worshipping in the house of Nisroch his god, that Adrammelech and Sharezer his sons smote him with the sword; and they escaped into the land of Armenia: and Esarhaddon his son reigned in his stead.
verse	23	38	1	In those days was Hezekiah sick unto death. And Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz came unto him, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Set thine house in order: for thou shalt die, and not live.
verse	23	38	2	Then Hezekiah turned his face toward the wall, and prayed unto the LORD,
verse	23	38	3	@@And said, Remember now, O LORD, I beseech thee, how I have walked before thee in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done @9that which is@7 good in thy sight. And Hezekiah wept sore.
verse	23	38	4	Then came the word of the LORD to Isaiah, saying,
verse	23	38	5	Go, and say to Hezekiah, Thus saith the LORD, the God of David thy father, I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears: behold, I will add unto thy days fifteen years.
verse	23	38	6	And I will deliver thee and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria: and I will defend this city.
verse	23	38	7	@@And this @9shall be@7 a sign unto thee from the LORD, that the LORD will do this thing that he hath spoken;
verse	23	38	8	Behold, I will bring again the shadow of the degrees, which is gone down in the sun dial of Ahaz, ten degrees backward. So the sun returned ten degrees, by which degrees it was gone down.
verse	23	38	9	The writing of Hezekiah king of Judah, when he had been sick, and was recovered of his sickness:
verse	23	38	10	I said in the cutting off of my days, I shall go to the gates of the grave: I am deprived of the residue of my years.
verse	23	38	11	@@I said, I shall not see the LORD, @9even@7 the LORD, in the land of the living: I shall behold man no more with the inhabitants of the world.
verse	23	38	12	@@Mine age is departed, and is removed from me as a shepherd's tent: I have cut off like a weaver my life: he will cut me off with pining sickness: from day @9even@7 to night wilt thou make an end of me.
verse	23	38	13	@@I reckoned till morning, @9that,@7 as a lion, so will he break all my bones: from day @9even@7 to night wilt thou make an end of me.
verse	23	38	14	@@Like a crane @9or@7 a swallow, so did I chatter: I did mourn as a dove: mine eyes fail @9with looking@7 upward: O LORD, I am oppressed; undertake for me.
verse	23	38	15	@@What shall I say? he hath both spoken unto me, and himself hath done @9it:@7 I shall go softly all my years in the bitterness of my soul.
verse	23	38	16	@@O Lord, by these @9things men@7 live, and in all these @9things is@7 the life of my spirit: so wilt thou recover me, and make me to live.
verse	23	38	17	@@Behold, for peace I had great bitterness: but thou hast in love to my soul @9delivered it@7 from the pit of corruption: for thou hast cast all my sins behind thy back.
verse	23	38	18	@@For the grave cannot praise thee, death can @9not@7 celebrate thee: they that go down into the pit cannot hope for thy truth.
verse	23	38	19	@@The living, the living, he shall praise thee, as I @9do@7 this day: the father to the children shall make known thy truth.
verse	23	38	20	@@The LORD @9was ready@7 to save me: therefore we will sing my songs to the stringed instruments all the days of our life in the house of the LORD.
verse	23	38	21	@@For Isaiah had said, Let them take a lump of figs, and lay @9it@7 for a plaister upon the boil, and he shall recover.
verse	23	38	22	@@Hezekiah also had said, What @9is@7 the sign that I shall go up to the house of the LORD?
verse	23	39	1	At that time Merodach-baladan, the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present to Hezekiah: for he had heard that he had been sick, and was recovered.
verse	23	39	2	And Hezekiah was glad of them, and shewed them the house of his precious things, the silver, and the gold, and the spices, and the precious ointment, and all the house of his armour, and all that was found in his treasures: there was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them not.
verse	23	39	3	@@Then came Isaiah the prophet unto king Hezekiah, and said unto him, What said these men? and from whence came they unto thee? And Hezekiah said, They are come from a far country unto me, @9even@7 from Babylon.
verse	23	39	4	@@Then said he, What have they seen in thine house? And Hezekiah answered, All that @9is@7 in mine house have they seen: there is nothing among my treasures that I have not shewed them.
verse	23	39	5	Then said Isaiah to Hezekiah, Hear the word of the LORD of hosts:
verse	23	39	6	@@Behold, the days come, that all that @9is@7 in thine house, and @9that@7 which thy fathers have laid up in store until this day, shall be carried to Babylon: nothing shall be left, saith the LORD.
verse	23	39	7	And of thy sons that shall issue from thee, which thou shalt beget, shall they take away; and they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.
verse	23	39	8	@@Then said Hezekiah to Isaiah, Good @9is@7 the word of the LORD which thou hast spoken. He said moreover, For there shall be peace and truth in my days.
verse	23	40	1	Comfort ye, comfort ye my people, saith your God.
verse	23	40	2	Speak ye comfortably to Jerusalem, and cry unto her, that her warfare is accomplished, that her iniquity is pardoned: for she hath received of the LORD'S hand double for all her sins.
verse	23	40	3	The voice of him that crieth in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the LORD, make straight in the desert a highway for our God.
verse	23	40	4	Every valley shall be exalted, and every mountain and hill shall be made low: and the crooked shall be made straight, and the rough places plain:
verse	23	40	5	@@And the glory of the LORD shall be revealed, and all flesh shall see @9it@7 together: for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken @9it. @7
verse	23	40	6	@@The voice said, Cry. And he said, What shall I cry? All flesh @9is@7 grass, and all the goodliness thereof @9is@7 as the flower of the field:
verse	23	40	7	@@The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: because the spirit of the LORD bloweth upon it: surely the people @9is@7 grass.
verse	23	40	8	The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: but the word of our God shall stand for ever.
verse	23	40	9	@@O Zion, that bringest good tidings, get thee up into the high mountain; O Jerusalem, that bringest good tidings, lift up thy voice with strength; lift @9it@7 up, be not afraid; say unto the cities of Judah, Behold your God!
verse	23	40	10	@@Behold, the Lord GOD will come with strong @9hand,@7 and his arm shall rule for him: behold, his reward @9is@7 with him, and his work before him.
verse	23	40	11	@@He shall feed his flock like a shepherd: he shall gather the lambs with his arm, and carry @9them@7 in his bosom, @9and@7 shall gently lead those that are with young.
verse	23	40	12	Who hath measured the waters in the hollow of his hand, and meted out heaven with the span, and comprehended the dust of the earth in a measure, and weighed the mountains in scales, and the hills in a balance?
verse	23	40	13	@@Who hath directed the Spirit of the LORD, or @9being@7 his counsellor hath taught him?
verse	23	40	14	@@With whom took he counsel, and @9who@7 instructed him, and taught him in the path of judgment, and taught him knowledge, and shewed to him the way of understanding?
verse	23	40	15	@@Behold, the nations @9are@7 as a drop of a bucket, and are counted as the small dust of the balance: behold, he taketh up the isles as a very little thing.
verse	23	40	16	@@And Lebanon @9is@7 not sufficient to burn, nor the beasts thereof sufficient for a burnt offering.
verse	23	40	17	@@All nations before him @9are@7 as nothing; and they are counted to him less than nothing, and vanity.
verse	23	40	18	To whom then will ye liken God? or what likeness will ye compare unto him?
verse	23	40	19	The workman melteth a graven image, and the goldsmith spreadeth it over with gold, and casteth silver chains.
verse	23	40	20	@@He that @9is@7 so impoverished that he hath no oblation chooseth a tree @9that@7 will not rot; he seeketh unto him a cunning workman to prepare a graven image, @9that@7 shall not be moved.
verse	23	40	21	Have ye not known? have ye not heard? hath it not been told you from the beginning? have ye not understood from the foundations of the earth?
verse	23	40	22	@@@9It is@7 he that sitteth upon the circle of the earth, and the inhabitants thereof @9are@7 as grasshoppers; that stretcheth out the heavens as a curtain, and spreadeth them out as a tent to dwell in:
verse	23	40	23	That bringeth the princes to nothing; he maketh the judges of the earth as vanity.
verse	23	40	24	Yea, they shall not be planted; yea, they shall not be sown: yea, their stock shall not take root in the earth: and he shall also blow upon them, and they shall wither, and the whirlwind shall take them away as stubble.
verse	23	40	25	To whom then will ye liken me, or shall I be equal? saith the Holy One.
verse	23	40	26	@@Lift up your eyes on high, and behold who hath created these @9things,@7 that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names by the greatness of his might, for that @9he is@7 strong in power; not one faileth.
verse	23	40	27	Why sayest thou, O Jacob, and speakest, O Israel, My way is hid from the LORD, and my judgment is passed over from my God?
verse	23	40	28	@@Hast thou not known? hast thou not heard, @9that@7 the everlasting God, the LORD, the Creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not, neither is weary? @9there is@7 no searching of his understanding.
verse	23	40	29	@@He giveth power to the faint; and to @9them that have@7 no might he increaseth strength.
verse	23	40	30	Even the youths shall faint and be weary, and the young men shall utterly fall:
verse	23	40	31	@@But they that wait upon the LORD shall renew @9their@7 strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; @9and@7 they shall walk, and not faint.
verse	23	41	1	@@Keep silence before me, O islands; and let the people renew @9their@7 strength: let them come near; then let them speak: let us come near together to judgment.
verse	23	41	2	@@Who raised up the righteous @9man@7 from the east, called him to his foot, gave the nations before him, and made @9him@7 rule over kings? he gave @9them@7 as the dust to his sword, @9and@7 as driven stubble to his bow.
verse	23	41	3	@@He pursued them, @9and@7 passed safely; @9even@7 by the way @9that@7 he had not gone with his feet.
verse	23	41	4	@@Who hath wrought and done @9it,@7 calling the generations from the beginning? I the LORD, the first, and with the last; I @9am@7 he.
verse	23	41	5	@@The isles saw @9it,@7 and feared; the ends of the earth were afraid, drew near, and came.
verse	23	41	6	@@They helped every one his neighbour; and @9every one@7 said to his brother, Be of good courage.
verse	23	41	7	@@So the carpenter encouraged the goldsmith, @9and@7 he that smootheth @9with@7 the hammer him that smote the anvil, saying, It is ready for the sodering: and he fastened it with nails, @9that@7 it should not be moved.
verse	23	41	8	@@But thou, Israel, @9art@7 my servant, Jacob whom I have chosen, the seed of Abraham my friend.
verse	23	41	9	@@@9Thou@7 whom I have taken from the ends of the earth, and called thee from the chief men thereof, and said unto thee, Thou @9art@7 my servant; I have chosen thee, and not cast thee away.
verse	23	41	10	@@Fear thou not; for I @9am@7 with thee: be not dismayed; for I @9am@7 thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.
verse	23	41	11	Behold, all they that were incensed against thee shall be ashamed and confounded: they shall be as nothing; and they that strive with thee shall perish.
verse	23	41	12	@@Thou shalt seek them, and shalt not find them, @9even@7 them that contended with thee: they that war against thee shall be as nothing, and as a thing of nought.
verse	23	41	13	For I the LORD thy God will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee.
verse	23	41	14	@@Fear not, thou worm Jacob, @9and@7 ye men of Israel; I will help thee, saith the LORD, and thy redeemer, the Holy One of Israel.
verse	23	41	15	@@Behold, I will make thee a new sharp threshing instrument having teeth: thou shalt thresh the mountains, and beat @9them@7 small, and shalt make the hills as chaff.
verse	23	41	16	@@Thou shalt fan them, and the wind shall carry them away, and the whirlwind shall scatter them: and thou shalt rejoice in the LORD, @9and@7 shalt glory in the Holy One of Israel.
verse	23	41	17	@@@9When@7 the poor and needy seek water, and @9there is@7 none, @9and@7 their tongue faileth for thirst, I the LORD will hear them, @9I@7 the God of Israel will not forsake them.
verse	23	41	18	I will open rivers in high places, and fountains in the midst of the valleys: I will make the wilderness a pool of water, and the dry land springs of water.
verse	23	41	19	@@I will plant in the wilderness the cedar, the shittah tree, and the myrtle, and the oil tree; I will set in the desert the fir tree, @9and@7 the pine, and the box tree together:
verse	23	41	20	That they may see, and know, and consider, and understand together, that the hand of the LORD hath done this, and the Holy One of Israel hath created it.
verse	23	41	21	@@Produce your cause, saith the LORD; bring forth your strong @9reasons,@7 saith the King of Jacob.
verse	23	41	22	@@Let them bring @9them@7 forth, and shew us what shall happen: let them shew the former things, what they @9be,@7 that we may consider them, and know the latter end of them; or declare us things for to come.
verse	23	41	23	@@Shew the things that are to come hereafter, that we may know that ye @9are@7 gods: yea, do good, or do evil, that we may be dismayed, and behold @9it@7 together.
verse	23	41	24	@@Behold, ye @9are@7 of nothing, and your work of nought: an abomination @9is he that@7 chooseth you.
verse	23	41	25	@@I have raised up @9one@7 from the north, and he shall come: from the rising of the sun shall he call upon my name: and he shall come upon princes as @9upon@7 morter, and as the potter treadeth clay.
verse	23	41	26	@@Who hath declared from the beginning, that we may know? and beforetime, that we may say, @9He is@7 righteous? yea, @9there is@7 none that sheweth, yea, @9there is@7 none that declareth, yea, @9there is@7 none that heareth your words.
verse	23	41	27	@@The first @9shall say@7 to Zion, Behold, behold them: and I will give to Jerusalem one that bringeth good tidings.
verse	23	41	28	@@For I beheld, and @9there was@7 no man; even among them, and @9there was@7 no counsellor, that, when I asked of them, could answer a word.
verse	23	41	29	@@Behold, they @9are@7 all vanity; their works @9are@7 nothing: their molten images @9are@7 wind and confusion.
verse	23	42	1	@@Behold my servant, whom I uphold; mine elect, @9in whom@7 my soul delighteth; I have put my spirit upon him: he shall bring forth judgment to the Gentiles.
verse	23	42	2	He shall not cry, nor lift up, nor cause his voice to be heard in the street.
verse	23	42	3	A bruised reed shall he not break, and the smoking flax shall he not quench: he shall bring forth judgment unto truth.
verse	23	42	4	He shall not fail nor be discouraged, till he have set judgment in the earth: and the isles shall wait for his law.
verse	23	42	5	Thus saith God the LORD, he that created the heavens, and stretched them out; he that spread forth the earth, and that which cometh out of it; he that giveth breath unto the people upon it, and spirit to them that walk therein:
verse	23	42	6	I the LORD have called thee in righteousness, and will hold thine hand, and will keep thee, and give thee for a covenant of the people, for a light of the Gentiles;
verse	23	42	7	@@To open the blind eyes, to bring out the prisoners from the prison, @9and@7 them that sit in darkness out of the prison house.
verse	23	42	8	@@I @9am@7 the LORD: that @9is@7 my name: and my glory will I not give to another, neither my praise to graven images.
verse	23	42	9	Behold, the former things are come to pass, and new things do I declare: before they spring forth I tell you of them.
verse	23	42	10	@@Sing unto the LORD a new song, @9and@7 his praise from the end of the earth, ye that go down to the sea, and all that is therein; the isles, and the inhabitants thereof.
verse	23	42	11	@@Let the wilderness and the cities thereof lift up @9their voice,@7 the villages @9that@7 Kedar doth inhabit: let the inhabitants of the rock sing, let them shout from the top of the mountains.
verse	23	42	12	Let them give glory unto the LORD, and declare his praise in the islands.
verse	23	42	13	The LORD shall go forth as a mighty man, he shall stir up jealousy like a man of war: he shall cry, yea, roar; he shall prevail against his enemies.
verse	23	42	14	@@I have long time holden my peace; I have been still, @9and@7 refrained myself: @9now@7 will I cry like a travailing woman; I will destroy and devour at once.
verse	23	42	15	I will make waste mountains and hills, and dry up all their herbs; and I will make the rivers islands, and I will dry up the pools.
verse	23	42	16	@@And I will bring the blind by a way @9that@7 they knew not; I will lead them in paths @9that@7 they have not known: I will make darkness light before them, and crooked things straight. These things will I do unto them, and not forsake them.
verse	23	42	17	@@They shall be turned back, they shall be greatly ashamed, that trust in graven images, that say to the molten images, Ye @9are@7 our gods.
verse	23	42	18	Hear, ye deaf; and look, ye blind, that ye may see.
verse	23	42	19	@@Who @9is@7 blind, but my servant? or deaf, as my messenger @9that@7 I sent? who @9is@7 blind as @9he that is@7 perfect, and blind as the LORD'S servant?
verse	23	42	20	Seeing many things, but thou observest not; opening the ears, but he heareth not.
verse	23	42	21	@@The LORD is well pleased for his righteousness' sake; he will magnify the law, and make @9it@7 honourable.
verse	23	42	22	@@But this @9is@7 a people robbed and spoiled; @9they are@7 all of them snared in holes, and they are hid in prison houses: they are for a prey, and none delivereth; for a spoil, and none saith, Restore.
verse	23	42	23	@@Who among you will give ear to this? @9who@7 will hearken and hear for the time to come?
verse	23	42	24	Who gave Jacob for a spoil, and Israel to the robbers? did not the LORD, he against whom we have sinned? for they would not walk in his ways, neither were they obedient unto his law.
verse	23	42	25	@@Therefore he hath poured upon him the fury of his anger, and the strength of battle: and it hath set him on fire round about, yet he knew not; and it burned him, yet he laid @9it@7 not to heart.
verse	23	43	1	@@But now thus saith the LORD that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called @9thee@7 by thy name; thou @9art@7 mine.
verse	23	43	2	@@When thou passest through the waters, I @9will be@7 with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.
verse	23	43	3	@@For I @9am@7 the LORD thy God, the Holy One of Israel, thy Saviour: I gave Egypt @9for@7 thy ransom, Ethiopia and Seba for thee.
verse	23	43	4	Since thou wast precious in my sight, thou hast been honourable, and I have loved thee: therefore will I give men for thee, and people for thy life.
verse	23	43	5	@@Fear not: for I @9am@7 with thee: I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west;
