verse	23	43	7	@@@9Even@7 every one that is called by my name: for I have created him for my glory, I have formed him; yea, I have made him.
verse	23	43	8	Bring forth the blind people that have eyes, and the deaf that have ears.
verse	23	43	9	@@Let all the nations be gathered together, and let the people be assembled: who among them can declare this, and shew us former things? let them bring forth their witnesses, that they may be justified: or let them hear, and say, @9It is@7 truth.
verse	23	43	10	@@Ye @9are@7 my witnesses, saith the LORD, and my servant whom I have chosen: that ye may know and believe me, and understand that I @9am@7 he: before me there was no God formed, neither shall there be after me.
verse	23	43	11	@@I, @9even@7 I, @9am@7 the LORD; and beside me @9there is@7 no saviour.
verse	23	43	12	@@I have declared, and have saved, and I have shewed, when @9there was@7 no strange @9god@7 among you: therefore ye @9are@7 my witnesses, saith the LORD, that I @9am@7 God.
verse	23	43	13	@@Yea, before the day @9was@7 I @9am@7 he; and @9there is@7 none that can deliver out of my hand: I will work, and who shall let it?
verse	23	43	14	@@Thus saith the LORD, your redeemer, the Holy One of Israel; For your sake I have sent to Babylon, and have brought down all their nobles, and the Chaldeans, whose cry @9is@7 in the ships.
verse	23	43	15	@@I @9am@7 the LORD, your Holy One, the creator of Israel, your King.
verse	23	43	16	Thus saith the LORD, which maketh a way in the sea, and a path in the mighty waters;
verse	23	43	17	Which bringeth forth the chariot and horse, the army and the power; they shall lie down together, they shall not rise: they are extinct, they are quenched as tow.
verse	23	43	18	Remember ye not the former things, neither consider the things of old.
verse	23	43	19	@@Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, @9and@7 rivers in the desert.
verse	23	43	20	@@The beast of the field shall honour me, the dragons and the owls: because I give waters in the wilderness, @9and@7 rivers in the desert, to give drink to my people, my chosen.
verse	23	43	21	This people have I formed for myself; they shall shew forth my praise.
verse	23	43	22	But thou hast not called upon me, O Jacob; but thou hast been weary of me, O Israel.
verse	23	43	23	Thou hast not brought me the small cattle of thy burnt offerings; neither hast thou honoured me with thy sacrifices. I have not caused thee to serve with an offering, nor wearied thee with incense.
verse	23	43	24	Thou hast bought me no sweet cane with money, neither hast thou filled me with the fat of thy sacrifices: but thou hast made me to serve with thy sins, thou hast wearied me with thine iniquities.
verse	23	43	25	@@I, @9even@7 I, @9am@7 he that blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake, and will not remember thy sins.
verse	23	43	26	Put me in remembrance: let us plead together: declare thou, that thou mayest be justified.
verse	23	43	27	Thy first father hath sinned, and thy teachers have transgressed against me.
verse	23	43	28	Therefore I have profaned the princes of the sanctuary, and have given Jacob to the curse, and Israel to reproaches.
verse	23	44	1	Yet now hear, O Jacob my servant; and Israel, whom I have chosen:
verse	23	44	2	@@Thus saith the LORD that made thee, and formed thee from the womb, @9which@7 will help thee; Fear not, O Jacob, my servant; and thou, Jesurun, whom I have chosen.
verse	23	44	3	For I will pour water upon him that is thirsty, and floods upon the dry ground: I will pour my spirit upon thy seed, and my blessing upon thine offspring:
