verse	23	44	5	@@One shall say, I @9am@7 the LORD'S; and another shall call @9himself@7 by the name of Jacob; and another shall subscribe @9with@7 his hand unto the LORD, and surname @9himself@7 by the name of Israel.
verse	23	44	6	@@Thus saith the LORD the King of Israel, and his redeemer the LORD of hosts; I @9am@7 the first, and I @9am@7 the last; and beside me @9there is@7 no God.
verse	23	44	7	And who, as I, shall call, and shall declare it, and set it in order for me, since I appointed the ancient people? and the things that are coming, and shall come, let them shew unto them.
verse	23	44	8	@@Fear ye not, neither be afraid: have not I told thee from that time, and have declared @9it?@7 ye @9are@7 even my witnesses. Is there a God beside me? yea, @9there is@7 no God; I know not @9any.@7
verse	23	44	9	@@They that make a graven image @9are@7 all of them vanity; and their delectable things shall not profit; and they @9are@7 their own witnesses; they see not, nor know; that they may be ashamed.
verse	23	44	10	@@Who hath formed a god, or molten a graven image @9that@7 is profitable for nothing?
verse	23	44	11	@@Behold, all his fellows shall be ashamed: and the workmen, they @9are@7 of men: let them all be gathered together, let them stand up; @9yet@7 they shall fear, @9and@7 they shall be ashamed together.
verse	23	44	12	The smith with the tongs both worketh in the coals, and fashioneth it with hammers, and worketh it with the strength of his arms: yea, he is hungry, and his strength faileth: he drinketh no water, and is faint.
verse	23	44	13	@@The carpenter stretcheth out @9his@7 rule; he marketh it out with a line; he fitteth it with planes, and he marketh it out with the compass, and maketh it after the figure of a man, according to the beauty of a man; that it may remain in the house.
verse	23	44	14	@@He heweth him down cedars, and taketh the cypress and the oak, which he strengtheneth for himself among the trees of the forest: he planteth an ash, and the rain doth nourish @9it. @7
verse	23	44	15	@@Then shall it be for a man to burn: for he will take thereof, and warm himself; yea, he kindleth @9it,@7 and baketh bread; yea, he maketh a god, and worshippeth @9it;@7 he maketh it a graven image, and falleth down thereto.
verse	23	44	16	@@He burneth part thereof in the fire; with part thereof he eateth flesh; he roasteth roast, and is satisfied: yea, he warmeth @9himself,@7 and saith, Aha, I am warm, I have seen the fire:
verse	23	44	17	@@And the residue thereof he maketh a god, @9even@7 his graven image: he falleth down unto it, and worshippeth @9it,@7 and prayeth unto it, and saith, Deliver me; for thou @9art@7 my god.
verse	23	44	18	@@They have not known nor understood: for he hath shut their eyes, that they cannot see; @9and@7 their hearts, that they cannot understand.
verse	23	44	19	@@And none considereth in his heart, neither @9is there@7 knowledge nor understanding to say, I have burned part of it in the fire; yea, also I have baked bread upon the coals thereof; I have roasted flesh, and eaten @9it:@7 and shall I make the residue thereof an abomination? shall I fall down to the stock of a tree?
verse	23	44	20	@@He feedeth on ashes: a deceived heart hath turned him aside, that he cannot deliver his soul, nor say, @9Is there@7 not a lie in my right hand?
verse	23	44	21	@@Remember these, O Jacob and Israel; for thou @9art@7 my servant: I have formed thee; thou @9art@7 my servant: O Israel, thou shalt not be forgotten of me.
verse	23	44	22	I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, thy transgressions, and, as a cloud, thy sins: return unto me; for I have redeemed thee.
verse	23	44	23	@@Sing, O ye heavens; for the LORD hath done @9it:@7 shout, ye lower parts of the earth: break forth into singing, ye mountains, O forest, and every tree therein: for the LORD hath redeemed Jacob, and glorified himself in Israel.
verse	23	44	24	@@Thus saith the LORD, thy redeemer, and he that formed thee from the womb, I @9am@7 the LORD that maketh all @9things;@7 that stretcheth forth the heavens alone; that spreadeth abroad the earth by myself;
