verse	23	45	14	@@Thus saith the LORD, The labour of Egypt, and merchandise of Ethiopia and of the Sabeans, men of stature, shall come over unto thee, and they shall be thine: they shall come after thee; in chains they shall come over, and they shall fall down unto thee, they shall make supplication unto thee, @9saying,@7 Surely God @9is@7 in thee; and @9there is@7 none else, @9there is@7 no God.
verse	23	45	15	@@Verily thou @9art@7 a God that hidest thyself, O God of Israel, the Saviour.
verse	23	45	16	@@They shall be ashamed, and also confounded, all of them: they shall go to confusion together @9that are@7 makers of idols.
verse	23	45	17	@@@9But@7 Israel shall be saved in the LORD with an everlasting salvation: ye shall not be ashamed nor confounded world without end.
verse	23	45	18	@@For thus saith the LORD that created the heavens; God himself that formed the earth and made it; he hath established it, he created it not in vain, he formed it to be inhabited: I @9am@7 the LORD; and @9there is@7 none else.
verse	23	45	19	I have not spoken in secret, in a dark place of the earth: I said not unto the seed of Jacob, Seek ye me in vain: I the LORD speak righteousness, I declare things that are right.
verse	23	45	20	@@Assemble yourselves and come; draw near together, ye @9that are@7 escaped of the nations: they have no knowledge that set up the wood of their graven image, and pray unto a god @9that@7 cannot save.
verse	23	45	21	@@Tell ye, and bring @9them@7 near; yea, let them take counsel together: who hath declared this from ancient time? @9who@7 hath told it from that time? @9have@7 not I the LORD? and @9there is@7 no God else beside me; a just God and a Saviour; @9there is@7 none beside me.
verse	23	45	22	@@Look unto me, and be ye saved, all the ends of the earth: for I @9am@7 God, and @9there is@7 none else.
