verse	23	47	1	@@Come down, and sit in the dust, O virgin daughter of Babylon, sit on the ground: @9there is@7 no throne, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called tender and delicate.
verse	23	47	2	Take the millstones, and grind meal: uncover thy locks, make bare the leg, uncover the thigh, pass over the rivers.
verse	23	47	3	@@Thy nakedness shall be uncovered, yea, thy shame shall be seen: I will take vengeance, and I will not meet @9thee as@7 a man.
verse	23	47	4	@@@9As for@7 our redeemer, the LORD of hosts @9is@7 his name, the Holy One of Israel.
verse	23	47	5	Sit thou silent, and get thee into darkness, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called, The lady of kingdoms.
verse	23	47	6	I was wroth with my people, I have polluted mine inheritance, and given them into thine hand: thou didst shew them no mercy; upon the ancient hast thou very heavily laid thy yoke.
verse	23	47	7	@@And thou saidst, I shall be a lady for ever: @9so@7 that thou didst not lay these @9things@7 to thy heart, neither didst remember the latter end of it.
verse	23	47	8	@@Therefore hear now this, @9thou that art@7 given to pleasures, that dwellest carelessly, that sayest in thine heart, I @9am,@7 and none else beside me; I shall not sit @9as@7 a widow, neither shall I know the loss of children:
verse	23	47	9	@@But these two @9things@7 shall come to thee in a moment in one day, the loss of children, and widowhood: they shall come upon thee in their perfection for the multitude of thy sorceries, @9and@7 for the great abundance of thine enchantments.
verse	23	47	10	@@For thou hast trusted in thy wickedness: thou hast said, None seeth me. Thy wisdom and thy knowledge, it hath perverted thee; and thou hast said in thine heart, I @9am,@7 and none else beside me.
verse	23	47	11	@@Therefore shall evil come upon thee; thou shalt not know from whence it riseth: and mischief shall fall upon thee; thou shalt not be able to put it off: and desolation shall come upon thee suddenly, @9which@7 thou shalt not know.
verse	23	47	12	Stand now with thine enchantments, and with the multitude of thy sorceries, wherein thou hast laboured from thy youth; if so be thou shalt be able to profit, if so be thou mayest prevail.
verse	23	47	13	@@Thou art wearied in the multitude of thy counsels. Let now the astrologers, the stargazers, the monthly prognosticators, stand up, and save thee from @9these things@7 that shall come upon thee.
verse	23	47	14	@@Behold, they shall be as stubble; the fire shall burn them; they shall not deliver themselves from the power of the flame: @9there shall@7 not @9be@7 a coal to warm at, @9nor@7 fire to sit before it.
verse	23	47	15	@@Thus shall they be unto thee with whom thou hast laboured, @9even@7 thy merchants, from thy youth: they shall wander every one to his quarter; none shall save thee.
verse	23	48	1	@@Hear ye this, O house of Jacob, which are called by the name of Israel, and are come forth out of the waters of Judah, which swear by the name of the LORD, and make mention of the God of Israel, @9but@7 not in truth, nor in righteousness.
verse	23	48	2	@@For they call themselves of the holy city, and stay themselves upon the God of Israel; The LORD of hosts @9is@7 his name.
verse	23	48	3	@@I have declared the former things from the beginning; and they went forth out of my mouth, and I shewed them; I did @9them@7 suddenly, and they came to pass.
