verse	23	48	5	@@I have even from the beginning declared @9it@7 to thee; before it came to pass I shewed @9it@7 thee: lest thou shouldest say, Mine idol hath done them, and my graven image, and my molten image, hath commanded them.
verse	23	48	6	@@Thou hast heard, see all this; and will not ye declare @9it?@7 I have shewed thee new things from this time, even hidden things, and thou didst not know them.
verse	23	48	7	They are created now, and not from the beginning; even before the day when thou heardest them not; lest thou shouldest say, Behold, I knew them.
verse	23	48	8	@@Yea, thou heardest not; yea, thou knewest not; yea, from that time @9that@7 thine ear was not opened: for I knew that thou wouldest deal very treacherously, and wast called a transgressor from the womb.
verse	23	48	9	For my name's sake will I defer mine anger, and for my praise will I refrain for thee, that I cut thee not off.
verse	23	48	10	Behold, I have refined thee, but not with silver; I have chosen thee in the furnace of affliction.
verse	23	48	11	@@For mine own sake, @9even@7 for mine own sake, will I do @9it:@7 for how should @9my name@7 be polluted? and I will not give my glory unto another.
verse	23	48	12	@@Hearken unto me, O Jacob and Israel, my called; I @9am@7 he; I @9am@7 the first, I also @9am@7 the last.
verse	23	48	13	@@Mine hand also hath laid the foundation of the earth, and my right hand hath spanned the heavens: @9when@7 I call unto them, they stand up together.
verse	23	48	14	@@All ye, assemble yourselves, and hear; which among them hath declared these @9things?@7 The LORD hath loved him: he will do his pleasure on Babylon, and his arm @9shall be on@7 the Chaldeans.
verse	23	48	15	@@I, @9even@7 I, have spoken; yea, I have called him: I have brought him, and he shall make his way prosperous.
verse	23	48	16	@@Come ye near unto me, hear ye this; I have not spoken in secret from the beginning; from the time that it was, there @9am@7 I: and now the Lord GOD, and his Spirit, hath sent me.
verse	23	48	17	@@Thus saith the LORD, thy Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel; I @9am@7 the LORD thy God which teacheth thee to profit, which leadeth thee by the way @9that@7 thou shouldest go.
verse	23	48	18	O that thou hadst hearkened to my commandments! then had thy peace been as a river, and thy righteousness as the waves of the sea:
verse	23	48	19	Thy seed also had been as the sand, and the offspring of thy bowels like the gravel thereof; his name should not have been cut off nor destroyed from before me.
verse	23	48	20	@@Go ye forth of Babylon, flee ye from the Chaldeans, with a voice of singing declare ye, tell this, utter it @9even@7 to the end of the earth; say ye, The LORD hath redeemed his servant Jacob.
verse	23	48	21	@@And they thirsted not @9when@7 he led them through the deserts: he caused the waters to flow out of the rock for them: he clave the rock also, and the waters gushed out.
verse	23	48	22	@@@9There is@7 no peace, saith the LORD, unto the wicked.
verse	23	49	1	Listen, O isles, unto me; and hearken, ye people, from far; The LORD hath called me from the womb; from the bowels of my mother hath he made mention of my name.
verse	23	49	2	And he hath made my mouth like a sharp sword; in the shadow of his hand hath he hid me, and made me a polished shaft; in his quiver hath he hid me;
verse	23	49	3	@@And said unto me, Thou @9art@7 my servant, O Israel, in whom I will be glorified.
verse	23	49	4	@@Then I said, I have laboured in vain, I have spent my strength for nought, and in vain: @9yet@7 surely my judgment @9is@7 with the LORD, and my work with my God.
verse	23	49	5	@@And now, saith the LORD that formed me from the womb @9to be@7 his servant, to bring Jacob again to him, Though Israel be not gathered, yet shall I be glorious in the eyes of the LORD, and my God shall be my strength.
verse	23	49	6	And he said, It is a light thing that thou shouldest be my servant to raise up the tribes of Jacob, and to restore the preserved of Israel: I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.
verse	23	49	7	@@Thus saith the LORD, the Redeemer of Israel, @9and@7 his Holy One, to him whom man despiseth, to him whom the nation abhorreth, to a servant of rulers, Kings shall see and arise, princes also shall worship, because of the LORD that is faithful, @9and@7 the Holy One of Israel, and he shall choose thee.
verse	23	49	8	Thus saith the LORD, In an acceptable time have I heard thee, and in a day of salvation have I helped thee: and I will preserve thee, and give thee for a covenant of the people, to establish the earth, to cause to inherit the desolate heritages;
verse	23	49	9	@@That thou mayest say to the prisoners, Go forth; to them that @9are@7 in darkness, Shew yourselves. They shall feed in the ways, and their pastures @9shall be@7 in all high places.
verse	23	49	10	They shall not hunger nor thirst; neither shall the heat nor sun smite them: for he that hath mercy on them shall lead them, even by the springs of water shall he guide them.
verse	23	49	11	And I will make all my mountains a way, and my highways shall be exalted.
verse	23	49	12	Behold, these shall come from far: and, lo, these from the north and from the west; and these from the land of Sinim.
verse	23	49	13	Sing, O heavens; and be joyful, O earth; and break forth into singing, O mountains: for the LORD hath comforted his people, and will have mercy upon his afflicted.
verse	23	49	14	But Zion said, The LORD hath forsaken me, and my Lord hath forgotten me.
verse	23	49	15	Can a woman forget her sucking child, that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb? yea, they may forget, yet will I not forget thee.
verse	23	49	16	@@Behold, I have graven thee upon the palms of @9my@7 hands; thy walls @9are@7 continually before me.
verse	23	49	17	Thy children shall make haste; thy destroyers and they that made thee waste shall go forth of thee.
verse	23	49	18	@@Lift up thine eyes round about, and behold: all these gather themselves together, @9and@7 come to thee. @9As@7 I live, saith the LORD, thou shalt surely clothe thee with them all, as with an ornament, and bind them @9on thee,@7 as a bride @9doeth. @7
verse	23	49	19	For thy waste and thy desolate places, and the land of thy destruction, shall even now be too narrow by reason of the inhabitants, and they that swallowed thee up shall be far away.
verse	23	49	20	@@The children which thou shalt have, after thou hast lost the other, shall say again in thine ears, The place @9is@7 too strait for me: give place to me that I may dwell.
verse	23	49	21	@@Then shalt thou say in thine heart, Who hath begotten me these, seeing I have lost my children, and am desolate, a captive, and removing to and fro? and who hath brought up these? Behold, I was left alone; these, where @9had@7 they @9been? @7
verse	23	49	22	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD, Behold, I will lift up mine hand to the Gentiles, and set up my standard to the people: and they shall bring thy sons in @9their@7 arms, and thy daughters shall be carried upon @9their@7 shoulders.
verse	23	49	23	@@And kings shall be thy nursing fathers, and their queens thy nursing mothers: they shall bow down to thee with @9their@7 face toward the earth, and lick up the dust of thy feet; and thou shalt know that I @9am@7 the LORD: for they shall not be ashamed that wait for me.
verse	23	49	24	Shall the prey be taken from the mighty, or the lawful captive delivered?
verse	23	49	25	But thus saith the LORD, Even the captives of the mighty shall be taken away, and the prey of the terrible shall be delivered: for I will contend with him that contendeth with thee, and I will save thy children.
verse	23	49	26	@@And I will feed them that oppress thee with their own flesh; and they shall be drunken with their own blood, as with sweet wine: and all flesh shall know that I the LORD @9am@7 thy Saviour and thy Redeemer, the mighty One of Jacob.
verse	23	50	1	@@Thus saith the LORD, Where @9is@7 the bill of your mother's divorcement, whom I have put away? or which of my creditors @9is it@7 to whom I have sold you? Behold, for your iniquities have ye sold yourselves, and for your transgressions is your mother put away.
verse	23	50	2	@@Wherefore, when I came, @9was there@7 no man? when I called, @9was there@7 none to answer? Is my hand shortened at all, that it cannot redeem? or have I no power to deliver? behold, at my rebuke I dry up the sea, I make the rivers a wilderness: their fish stinketh, because @9there is@7 no water, and dieth for thirst.
verse	23	50	3	I clothe the heavens with blackness, and I make sackcloth their covering.
verse	23	50	4	@@The Lord GOD hath given me the tongue of the learned, that I should know how to speak a word in season to @9him that is@7 weary: he wakeneth morning by morning, he wakeneth mine ear to hear as the learned.
verse	23	50	5	The Lord GOD hath opened mine ear, and I was not rebellious, neither turned away back.
verse	23	50	6	I gave my back to the smiters, and my cheeks to them that plucked off the hair: I hid not my face from shame and spitting.
verse	23	50	7	For the Lord GOD will help me; therefore shall I not be confounded: therefore have I set my face like a flint, and I know that I shall not be ashamed.
verse	23	50	8	@@@9He is@7 near that justifieth me; who will contend with me? let us stand together: who @9is@7 mine adversary? let him come near to me.
verse	23	50	9	@@Behold, the Lord GOD will help me; who @9is@7 he @9that@7 shall condemn me? lo, they all shall wax old as a garment; the moth shall eat them up.
verse	23	50	10	@@Who @9is@7 among you that feareth the LORD, that obeyeth the voice of his servant, that walketh @9in@7 darkness, and hath no light? let him trust in the name of the LORD, and stay upon his God.
verse	23	50	11	@@Behold, all ye that kindle a fire, that compass @9yourselves@7 about with sparks: walk in the light of your fire, and in the sparks @9that@7 ye have kindled. This shall ye have of mine hand; ye shall lie down in sorrow.
verse	23	51	1	@@Hearken to me, ye that follow after righteousness, ye that seek the LORD: look unto the rock @9whence@7 ye are hewn, and to the hole of the pit @9whence@7 ye are digged.
verse	23	51	2	@@Look unto Abraham your father, and unto Sarah @9that@7 bare you: for I called him alone, and blessed him, and increased him.
verse	23	51	3	For the LORD shall comfort Zion: he will comfort all her waste places; and he will make her wilderness like Eden, and her desert like the garden of the LORD; joy and gladness shall be found therein, thanksgiving, and the voice of melody.
verse	23	51	4	Hearken unto me, my people; and give ear unto me, O my nation: for a law shall proceed from me, and I will make my judgment to rest for a light of the people.
verse	23	51	5	@@My righteousness @9is@7 near; my salvation is gone forth, and mine arms shall judge the people; the isles shall wait upon me, and on mine arm shall they trust.
verse	23	51	6	Lift up your eyes to the heavens, and look upon the earth beneath: for the heavens shall vanish away like smoke, and the earth shall wax old like a garment, and they that dwell therein shall die in like manner: but my salvation shall be for ever, and my righteousness shall not be abolished.
verse	23	51	7	@@Hearken unto me, ye that know righteousness, the people in whose heart @9is@7 my law; fear ye not the reproach of men, neither be ye afraid of their revilings.
verse	23	51	8	For the moth shall eat them up like a garment, and the worm shall eat them like wool: but my righteousness shall be for ever, and my salvation from generation to generation.
verse	23	51	9	@@Awake, awake, put on strength, O arm of the LORD; awake, as in the ancient days, in the generations of old. @9Art@7 thou not it that hath cut Rahab, @9and@7 wounded the dragon?
verse	23	51	10	@@@9Art@7 thou not it which hath dried the sea, the waters of the great deep; that hath made the depths of the sea a way for the ransomed to pass over?
verse	23	51	11	@@Therefore the redeemed of the LORD shall return, and come with singing unto Zion; and everlasting joy @9shall be@7 upon their head: they shall obtain gladness and joy; @9and@7 sorrow and mourning shall flee away.
verse	23	51	12	@@I, @9even@7 I, @9am@7 he that comforteth you: who @9art@7 thou, that thou shouldest be afraid of a man @9that@7 shall die, and of the son of man @9which@7 shall be made as grass;
verse	23	51	13	@@And forgettest the LORD thy maker, that hath stretched forth the heavens, and laid the foundations of the earth; and hast feared continually every day because of the fury of the oppressor, as if he were ready to destroy? and where @9is@7 the fury of the oppressor?
verse	23	51	14	The captive exile hasteneth that he may be loosed, and that he should not die in the pit, nor that his bread should fail.
verse	23	51	15	@@But I @9am@7 the LORD thy God, that divided the sea, whose waves roared: The LORD of hosts @9is@7 his name.
verse	23	51	16	@@And I have put my words in thy mouth, and I have covered thee in the shadow of mine hand, that I may plant the heavens, and lay the foundations of the earth, and say unto Zion, Thou @9art@7 my people.
verse	23	51	17	@@Awake, awake, stand up, O Jerusalem, which hast drunk at the hand of the LORD the cup of his fury; thou hast drunken the dregs of the cup of trembling, @9and@7 wrung @9them@7 out.
verse	23	51	18	@@@9There is@7 none to guide her among all the sons @9whom@7 she hath brought forth; neither @9is there any@7 that taketh her by the hand of all the sons @9that@7 she hath brought up.
verse	23	51	19	@@These two @9things@7 are come unto thee; who shall be sorry for thee? desolation, and destruction, and the famine, and the sword: by whom shall I comfort thee?
verse	23	51	20	Thy sons have fainted, they lie at the head of all the streets, as a wild bull in a net: they are full of the fury of the LORD, the rebuke of thy God.
verse	23	51	21	Therefore hear now this, thou afflicted, and drunken, but not with wine:
verse	23	51	22	@@Thus saith thy Lord the LORD, and thy God @9that@7 pleadeth the cause of his people, Behold, I have taken out of thine hand the cup of trembling, @9even@7 the dregs of the cup of my fury; thou shalt no more drink it again:
verse	23	51	23	But I will put it into the hand of them that afflict thee; which have said to thy soul, Bow down, that we may go over: and thou hast laid thy body as the ground, and as the street, to them that went over.
verse	23	52	1	Awake, awake; put on thy strength, O Zion; put on thy beautiful garments, O Jerusalem, the holy city: for henceforth there shall no more come into thee the uncircumcised and the unclean.
verse	23	52	2	@@Shake thyself from the dust; arise, @9and@7 sit down, O Jerusalem: loose thyself from the bands of thy neck, O captive daughter of Zion.
verse	23	52	3	For thus saith the LORD, Ye have sold yourselves for nought; and ye shall be redeemed without money.
verse	23	52	4	For thus saith the Lord GOD, My people went down aforetime into Egypt to sojourn there; and the Assyrian oppressed them without cause.
verse	23	52	5	Now therefore, what have I here, saith the LORD, that my people is taken away for nought? they that rule over them make them to howl, saith the LORD; and my name continually every day is blasphemed.
verse	23	52	6	@@Therefore my people shall know my name: therefore @9they shall know@7 in that day that I @9am@7 he that doth speak: behold, @9it is@7 I.
verse	23	52	7	How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace; that bringeth good tidings of good, that publisheth salvation; that saith unto Zion, Thy God reigneth!
verse	23	52	8	Thy watchmen shall lift up the voice; with the voice together shall they sing: for they shall see eye to eye, when the LORD shall bring again Zion.
verse	23	52	9	Break forth into joy, sing together, ye waste places of Jerusalem: for the LORD hath comforted his people, he hath redeemed Jerusalem.
verse	23	52	10	The LORD hath made bare his holy arm in the eyes of all the nations; and all the ends of the earth shall see the salvation of our God.
verse	23	52	11	@@Depart ye, depart ye, go ye out from thence, touch no unclean @9thing;@7 go ye out of the midst of her; be ye clean, that bear the vessels of the LORD.
verse	23	52	12	@@For ye shall not go out with haste, nor go by flight: for the LORD will go before you; and the God of Israel @9will be@7 your rereward.
verse	23	52	13	Behold, my servant shall deal prudently, he shall be exalted and extolled, and be very high.
verse	23	52	14	As many were astonied at thee; his visage was so marred more than any man, and his form more than the sons of men:
verse	23	52	15	@@So shall he sprinkle many nations; the kings shall shut their mouths at him: for @9that@7 which had not been told them shall they see; and @9that@7 which they had not heard shall they consider.
verse	23	53	1	Who hath believed our report? and to whom is the arm of the LORD revealed?
verse	23	53	2	@@For he shall grow up before him as a tender plant, and as a root out of a dry ground: he hath no form nor comeliness; and when we shall see him, @9there is@7 no beauty that we should desire him.
verse	23	53	3	@@He is despised and rejected of men; a man of sorrows, and acquainted with grief: and we hid as it were @9our@7 faces from him; he was despised, and we esteemed him not.
verse	23	53	4	Surely he hath borne our griefs, and carried our sorrows: yet we did esteem him stricken, smitten of God, and afflicted.
verse	23	53	5	@@But he @9was@7 wounded for our transgressions, @9he was@7 bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace @9was@7 upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.
verse	23	53	6	All we like sheep have gone astray; we have turned every one to his own way; and the LORD hath laid on him the iniquity of us all.
verse	23	53	7	He was oppressed, and he was afflicted, yet he opened not his mouth: he is brought as a lamb to the slaughter, and as a sheep before her shearers is dumb, so he openeth not his mouth.
verse	23	53	8	He was taken from prison and from judgment: and who shall declare his generation? for he was cut off out of the land of the living: for the transgression of my people was he stricken.
verse	23	53	9	@@And he made his grave with the wicked, and with the rich in his death; because he had done no violence, neither @9was any@7 deceit in his mouth.
verse	23	53	10	@@Yet it pleased the LORD to bruise him; he hath put @9him@7 to grief: when thou shalt make his soul an offering for sin, he shall see @9his@7 seed, he shall prolong @9his@7 days, and the pleasure of the LORD shall prosper in his hand.
verse	23	53	11	@@He shall see of the travail of his soul, @9and@7 shall be satisfied: by his knowledge shall my righteous servant justify many; for he shall bear their iniquities.
verse	23	53	12	@@Therefore will I divide him @9a portion@7 with the great, and he shall divide the spoil with the strong; because he hath poured out his soul unto death: and he was numbered with the transgressors; and he bare the sin of many, and made intercession for the transgressors.
verse	23	54	1	@@Sing, O barren, thou @9that@7 didst not bear; break forth into singing, and cry aloud, thou @9that@7 didst not travail with child: for more @9are@7 the children of the desolate than the children of the married wife, saith the LORD.
verse	23	54	2	Enlarge the place of thy tent, and let them stretch forth the curtains of thine habitations: spare not, lengthen thy cords, and strengthen thy stakes;
verse	23	54	3	For thou shalt break forth on the right hand and on the left; and thy seed shall inherit the Gentiles, and make the desolate cities to be inhabited.
verse	23	54	4	Fear not; for thou shalt not be ashamed: neither be thou confounded; for thou shalt not be put to shame: for thou shalt forget the shame of thy youth, and shalt not remember the reproach of thy widowhood any more.
verse	23	54	5	@@For thy Maker @9is@7 thine husband; the LORD of hosts @9is@7 his name; and thy Redeemer the Holy One of Israel; The God of the whole earth shall he be called.
verse	23	54	6	For the LORD hath called thee as a woman forsaken and grieved in spirit, and a wife of youth, when thou wast refused, saith thy God.
verse	23	54	7	For a small moment have I forsaken thee; but with great mercies will I gather thee.
verse	23	54	8	In a little wrath I hid my face from thee for a moment; but with everlasting kindness will I have mercy on thee, saith the LORD thy Redeemer.
verse	23	54	9	@@For this @9is as@7 the waters of Noah unto me: for @9as@7 I have sworn that the waters of Noah should no more go over the earth; so have I sworn that I would not be wroth with thee, nor rebuke thee.
verse	23	54	10	For the mountains shall depart, and the hills be removed; but my kindness shall not depart from thee, neither shall the covenant of my peace be removed, saith the LORD that hath mercy on thee.
verse	23	54	11	@@O thou afflicted, tossed with tempest, @9and@7 not comforted, behold, I will lay thy stones with fair colors, and lay thy foundations with sapphires.
verse	23	54	12	And I will make thy windows of agates, and thy gates of carbuncles, and all thy borders of pleasant stones.
verse	23	54	13	@@And all thy children @9shall be@7 taught of the LORD; and great @9shall be@7 the peace of thy children.
verse	23	54	14	In righteousness shalt thou be established: thou shalt be far from oppression; for thou shalt not fear: and from terror; for it shall not come near thee.
verse	23	54	15	@@Behold, they shall surely gather together, @9but@7 not by me: whosoever shall gather together against thee shall fall for thy sake.
verse	23	54	16	Behold, I have created the smith that bloweth the coals in the fire, and that bringeth forth an instrument for his work; and I have created the waster to destroy.
verse	23	54	17	@@No weapon that is formed against thee shall prosper; and every tongue @9that@7 shall rise against thee in judgment thou shalt condemn. This @9is@7 the heritage of the servants of the LORD, and their righteousness @9is@7 of me, saith the LORD.
verse	23	55	1	Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters, and he that hath no money; come ye, buy, and eat; yea, come, buy wine and milk without money and without price.
verse	23	55	2	@@Wherefore do ye spend money for @9that which is@7 not bread? and your labour for @9that which@7 satisfieth not? hearken diligently unto me, and eat ye @9that which is@7 good, and let your soul delight itself in fatness.
verse	23	55	3	@@Incline your ear, and come unto me: hear, and your soul shall live; and I will make an everlasting covenant with you, @9even@7 the sure mercies of David.
verse	23	55	4	@@Behold, I have given him @9for@7 a witness to the people, a leader and commander to the people.
verse	23	55	5	@@Behold, thou shalt call a nation @9that@7 thou knowest not, and nations @9that@7 knew not thee shall run unto thee because of the LORD thy God, and for the Holy One of Israel; for he hath glorified thee.
verse	23	55	6	Seek ye the LORD while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near:
verse	23	55	7	Let the wicked forsake his way, and the unrighteous man his thoughts: and let him return unto the LORD, and he will have mercy upon him; and to our God, for he will abundantly pardon.
verse	23	55	8	@@For my thoughts @9are@7 not your thoughts, neither @9are@7 your ways my ways, saith the LORD.
verse	23	55	9	@@For @9as@7 the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways, and my thoughts than your thoughts.
verse	23	55	10	For as the rain cometh down, and the snow from heaven, and returneth not thither, but watereth the earth, and maketh it bring forth and bud, that it may give seed to the sower, and bread to the eater:
verse	23	55	11	@@So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please, and it shall prosper @9in the thing@7 whereto I sent it.
verse	23	55	12	@@For ye shall go out with joy, and be led forth with peace: the mountains and the hills shall break forth before you into singing, and all the trees of the field shall clap @9their@7 hands.
verse	23	55	13	@@Instead of the thorn shall come up the fir tree, and instead of the brier shall come up the myrtle tree: and it shall be to the LORD for a name, for an everlasting sign @9that@7 shall not be cut off.
verse	23	56	1	@@Thus saith the LORD, Keep ye judgment, and do justice: for my salvation @9is@7 near to come, and my righteousness to be revealed.
verse	23	56	2	@@Blessed @9is@7 the man @9that@7 doeth this, and the son of man @9that@7 layeth hold on it; that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and keepeth his hand from doing any evil.
verse	23	56	3	@@Neither let the son of the stranger, that hath joined himself to the LORD, speak, saying, The LORD hath utterly separated me from his people: neither let the eunuch say, Behold, I @9am@7 a dry tree.
verse	23	56	4	@@For thus saith the LORD unto the eunuchs that keep my sabbaths, and choose @9the things@7 that please me, and take hold of my covenant;
verse	23	56	5	Even unto them will I give in mine house and within my walls a place and a name better than of sons and of daughters: I will give them an everlasting name, that shall not be cut off.
verse	23	56	6	Also the sons of the stranger, that join themselves to the LORD, to serve him, and to love the name of the LORD, to be his servants, every one that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and taketh hold of my covenant;
verse	23	56	7	@@Even them will I bring to my holy mountain, and make them joyful in my house of prayer: their burnt offerings and their sacrifices @9shall be@7 accepted upon mine altar; for mine house shall be called an house of prayer for all people.
verse	23	56	8	@@The Lord GOD which gathereth the outcasts of Israel saith, Yet will I gather @9others@7 to him, beside those that are gathered unto him.
verse	23	56	9	@@All ye beasts of the field, come to devour, @9yea,@7 all ye beasts in the forest.
verse	23	56	10	@@His watchmen @9are@7 blind: they are all ignorant, they @9are@7 all dumb dogs, they cannot bark; sleeping, lying down, loving to slumber.
verse	23	56	11	@@Yea, @9they are@7 greedy dogs @9which@7 can never have enough, and they @9are@7 shepherds @9that@7 cannot understand: they all look to their own way, every one for his gain, from his quarter.
verse	23	56	12	@@Come ye, @9say they,@7 I will fetch wine, and we will fill ourselves with strong drink; and to morrow shall be as this day, @9and@7 much more abundant.
verse	23	57	1	@@The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth @9it@7 to heart: and merciful men @9are@7 taken away, none considering that the righteous is taken away from the evil @9to come. @7
verse	23	57	2	@@He shall enter into peace: they shall rest in their beds, @9each one@7 walking @9in@7 his uprightness.
verse	23	57	3	But draw near hither, ye sons of the sorceress, the seed of the adulterer and the whore.
verse	23	57	4	@@Against whom do ye sport yourselves? against whom make ye a wide mouth, @9and@7 draw out the tongue? @9are@7 ye not children of transgression, a seed of falsehood,
verse	23	57	5	Enflaming yourselves with idols under every green tree, slaying the children in the valleys under the clifts of the rocks?
verse	23	57	6	@@Among the smooth @9stones@7 of the stream @9is@7 thy portion; they, they @9are@7 thy lot: even to them hast thou poured a drink offering, thou hast offered a meat offering. Should I receive comfort in these?
verse	23	57	7	Upon a lofty and high mountain hast thou set thy bed: even thither wentest thou up to offer sacrifice.
verse	23	57	8	@@Behind the doors also and the posts hast thou set up thy remembrance: for thou hast discovered @9thyself to another@7 than me, and art gone up; thou hast enlarged thy bed, and made thee @9a covenant@7 with them; thou lovedst their bed where thou sawest @9it. @7
verse	23	57	9	@@And thou wentest to the king with ointment, and didst increase thy perfumes, and didst send thy messengers far off, and didst debase @9thyself even@7 unto hell.
verse	23	57	10	@@Thou art wearied in the greatness of thy way; @9yet@7 saidst thou not, There is no hope: thou hast found the life of thine hand; therefore thou wast not grieved.
verse	23	57	11	@@And of whom hast thou been afraid or feared, that thou hast lied, and hast not remembered me, nor laid @9it@7 to thy heart? have not I held my peace even of old, and thou fearest me not?
verse	23	57	12	I will declare thy righteousness, and thy works; for they shall not profit thee.
verse	23	57	13	@@When thou criest, let thy companies deliver thee; but the wind shall carry them all away; vanity shall take @9them:@7 but he that putteth his trust in me shall possess the land, and shall inherit my holy mountain;
verse	23	57	14	And shall say, Cast ye up, cast ye up, prepare the way, take up the stumblingblock out of the way of my people.
verse	23	57	15	@@For thus saith the high and lofty One that inhabiteth eternity, whose name @9is@7 Holy; I dwell in the high and holy @9place,@7 with him also @9that is@7 of a contrite and humble spirit, to revive the spirit of the humble, and to revive the heart of the contrite ones.
verse	23	57	16	@@For I will not contend for ever, neither will I be always wroth: for the spirit should fail before me, and the souls @9which@7 I have made.
verse	23	57	17	For the iniquity of his covetousness was I wroth, and smote him: I hid me, and was wroth, and he went on frowardly in the way of his heart.
verse	23	57	18	I have seen his ways, and will heal him: I will lead him also, and restore comforts unto him and to his mourners.
verse	23	57	19	@@I create the fruit of the lips; Peace, peace to @9him that is@7 far off, and to @9him that is@7 near, saith the LORD; and I will heal him.
verse	23	57	20	@@But the wicked @9are@7 like the troubled sea, when it cannot rest, whose waters cast up mire and dirt.
verse	23	57	21	@@@9There is@7 no peace, saith my God, to the wicked.
verse	23	58	1	Cry aloud, spare not, lift up thy voice like a trumpet, and shew my people their transgression, and the house of Jacob their sins.
verse	23	58	2	Yet they seek me daily, and delight to know my ways, as a nation that did righteousness, and forsook not the ordinance of their God: they ask of me the ordinances of justice; they take delight in approaching to God.
verse	23	58	3	@@Wherefore have we fasted, @9say they,@7 and thou seest not? @9wherefore@7 have we afflicted our soul, and thou takest no knowledge? Behold, in the day of your fast ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours.
verse	23	58	4	@@Behold, ye fast for strife and debate, and to smite with the fist of wickedness: ye shall not fast as @9ye do this@7 day, to make your voice to be heard on high.
verse	23	58	5	@@Is it such a fast that I have chosen? a day for a man to afflict his soul? @9is it@7 to bow down his head as a bulrush, and to spread sackcloth and ashes @9under him?@7 wilt thou call this a fast, and an acceptable day to the LORD?
verse	23	58	6	@@@9Is@7 not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke?
verse	23	58	7	@@@9Is it@7 not to deal thy bread to the hungry, and that thou bring the poor that are cast out to thy house? when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him; and that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh?
verse	23	58	8	Then shall thy light break forth as the morning, and thine health shall spring forth speedily: and thy righteousness shall go before thee; the glory of the LORD shall be thy rereward.
verse	23	58	9	@@Then shalt thou call, and the LORD shall answer; thou shalt cry, and he shall say, Here I @9am.@7 If thou take away from the midst of thee the yoke, the putting forth of the finger, and speaking vanity;
verse	23	58	10	@@And @9if@7 thou draw out thy soul to the hungry, and satisfy the afflicted soul; then shall thy light rise in obscurity, and thy darkness @9be@7 as the noonday:
verse	23	58	11	And the LORD shall guide thee continually, and satisfy thy soul in drought, and make fat thy bones: and thou shalt be like a watered garden, and like a spring of water, whose waters fail not.
verse	23	58	12	@@And @9they that shall be@7 of thee shall build the old waste places: thou shalt raise up the foundations of many generations; and thou shalt be called, The repairer of the breach, The restorer of paths to dwell in.
verse	23	58	13	@@If thou turn away thy foot from the sabbath, @9from@7 doing thy pleasure on my holy day; and call the sabbath a delight, the holy of the LORD, honourable; and shalt honour him, not doing thine own ways, nor finding thine own pleasure, nor speaking @9thine own@7 words:
verse	23	58	14	@@Then shalt thou delight thyself in the LORD; and I will cause thee to ride upon the high places of the earth, and feed thee with the heritage of Jacob thy father: for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken @9it.@7
verse	23	59	1	Behold, the LORD'S hand is not shortened, that it cannot save; neither his ear heavy, that it cannot hear:
verse	23	59	2	@@But your iniquities have separated between you and your God, and your sins have hid @9his@7 face from you, that he will not hear.
verse	23	59	3	For your hands are defiled with blood, and your fingers with iniquity; your lips have spoken lies, your tongue hath muttered perverseness.
verse	23	59	4	@@None calleth for justice, nor @9any@7 pleadeth for truth: they trust in vanity, and speak lies; they conceive mischief, and bring forth iniquity.
verse	23	59	5	They hatch cockatrice' eggs, and weave the spider's web: he that eateth of their eggs dieth, and that which is crushed breaketh out into a viper.
verse	23	59	6	@@Their webs shall not become garments, neither shall they cover themselves with their works: their works @9are@7 works of iniquity, and the act of violence @9is@7 in their hands.
verse	23	59	7	@@Their feet run to evil, and they make haste to shed innocent blood: their thoughts @9are@7 thoughts of iniquity; wasting and destruction @9are@7 in their paths.
verse	23	59	8	@@The way of peace they know not; and @9there is@7 no judgment in their goings: they have made them crooked paths: whosoever goeth therein shall not know peace.
verse	23	59	9	@@Therefore is judgment far from us, neither doth justice overtake us: we wait for light, but behold obscurity; for brightness, @9but@7 we walk in darkness.
verse	23	59	10	@@We grope for the wall like the blind, and we grope as if @9we had@7 no eyes: we stumble at noonday as in the night; @9we are@7 in desolate places as dead @9men. @7
verse	23	59	11	@@We roar all like bears, and mourn sore like doves: we look for judgment, but @9there is@7 none; for salvation, @9but@7 it is far off from us.
verse	23	59	12	@@For our transgressions are multiplied before thee, and our sins testify against us: for our transgressions @9are@7 with us; and @9as for@7 our iniquities, we know them;
verse	23	59	13	In transgressing and lying against the LORD, and departing away from our God, speaking oppression and revolt, conceiving and uttering from the heart words of falsehood.
verse	23	59	14	And judgment is turned away backward, and justice standeth afar off: for truth is fallen in the street, and equity cannot enter.
verse	23	59	15	@@Yea, truth faileth; and he @9that@7 departeth from evil maketh himself a prey: and the LORD saw @9it,@7 and it displeased him that @9there was@7 no judgment.
verse	23	59	16	@@And he saw that @9there was@7 no man, and wondered that @9there was@7 no intercessor: therefore his arm brought salvation unto him; and his righteousness, it sustained him.
verse	23	59	17	@@For he put on righteousness as a breastplate, and an helmet of salvation upon his head; and he put on the garments of vengeance @9for@7 clothing, and was clad with zeal as a cloke.
verse	23	59	18	@@According to @9their@7 deeds, accordingly he will repay, fury to his adversaries, recompence to his enemies; to the islands he will repay recompence.
verse	23	59	19	So shall they fear the name of the LORD from the west, and his glory from the rising of the sun. When the enemy shall come in like a flood, the Spirit of the LORD shall lift up a standard against him.
verse	23	59	20	And the Redeemer shall come to Zion, and unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob, saith the LORD.
verse	23	59	21	@@As for me, this @9is@7 my covenant with them, saith the LORD; My spirit that @9is@7 upon thee, and my words which I have put in thy mouth, shall not depart out of thy mouth, nor out of the mouth of thy seed, nor out of the mouth of thy seed's seed, saith the LORD, from henceforth and for ever.
verse	23	60	1	Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of the LORD is risen upon thee.
verse	23	60	2	For, behold, the darkness shall cover the earth, and gross darkness the people: but the LORD shall arise upon thee, and his glory shall be seen upon thee.
verse	23	60	3	And the Gentiles shall come to thy light, and kings to the brightness of thy rising.
verse	23	60	4	@@Lift up thine eyes round about, and see: all they gather themselves together, they come to thee: thy sons shall come from far, and thy daughters shall be nursed at @9thy@7 side.
verse	23	60	5	Then thou shalt see, and flow together, and thine heart shall fear, and be enlarged; because the abundance of the sea shall be converted unto thee, the forces of the Gentiles shall come unto thee.
verse	23	60	6	The multitude of camels shall cover thee, the dromedaries of Midian and Ephah; all they from Sheba shall come: they shall bring gold and incense; and they shall shew forth the praises of the LORD.
verse	23	60	7	All the flocks of Kedar shall be gathered together unto thee, the rams of Nebaioth shall minister unto thee: they shall come up with acceptance on mine altar, and I will glorify the house of my glory.
verse	23	60	8	@@Who @9are@7 these @9that@7 fly as a cloud, and as the doves to their windows?
verse	23	60	9	Surely the isles shall wait for me, and the ships of Tarshish first, to bring thy sons from far, their silver and their gold with them, unto the name of the LORD thy God, and to the Holy One of Israel, because he hath glorified thee.
verse	23	60	10	And the sons of strangers shall build up thy walls, and their kings shall minister unto thee: for in my wrath I smote thee, but in my favour have I had mercy on thee.
verse	23	60	11	@@Therefore thy gates shall be open continually; they shall not be shut day nor night; that @9men@7 may bring unto thee the forces of the Gentiles, and @9that@7 their kings @9may be@7 brought.
verse	23	60	12	@@For the nation and kingdom that will not serve thee shall perish; yea, @9those@7 nations shall be utterly wasted.
verse	23	60	13	The glory of Lebanon shall come unto thee, the fir tree, the pine tree, and the box together, to beautify the place of my sanctuary; and I will make the place of my feet glorious.
verse	23	60	14	The sons also of them that afflicted thee shall come bending unto thee; and all they that despised thee shall bow themselves down at the soles of thy feet; and they shall call thee, The city of the LORD, The Zion of the Holy One of Israel.
verse	23	60	15	@@Whereas thou hast been forsaken and hated, so that no man went through @9thee,@7 I will make thee an eternal excellency, a joy of many generations.
verse	23	60	16	@@Thou shalt also suck the milk of the Gentiles, and shalt suck the breast of kings: and thou shalt know that I the LORD @9am@7 thy Saviour and thy Redeemer, the mighty One of Jacob.
verse	23	60	17	For brass I will bring gold, and for iron I will bring silver, and for wood brass, and for stones iron: I will also make thy officers peace, and thine exactors righteousness.
verse	23	60	18	Violence shall no more be heard in thy land, wasting nor destruction within thy borders; but thou shalt call thy walls Salvation, and thy gates Praise.
verse	23	60	19	The sun shall be no more thy light by day; neither for brightness shall the moon give light unto thee: but the LORD shall be unto thee an everlasting light, and thy God thy glory.
verse	23	60	20	Thy sun shall no more go down; neither shall thy moon withdraw itself: for the LORD shall be thine everlasting light, and the days of thy mourning shall be ended.
verse	23	60	21	@@Thy people also @9shall be@7 all righteous: they shall inherit the land for ever, the branch of my planting, the work of my hands, that I may be glorified.
verse	23	60	22	A little one shall become a thousand, and a small one a strong nation: I the LORD will hasten it in his time.
verse	23	61	1	@@The Spirit of the Lord GOD @9is@7 upon me; because the LORD hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to @9them that are@7 bound;
verse	23	61	2	To proclaim the acceptable year of the LORD, and the day of vengeance of our God; to comfort all that mourn;
verse	23	61	3	To appoint unto them that mourn in Zion, to give unto them beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness; that they might be called trees of righteousness, the planting of the LORD, that he might be glorified.
verse	23	61	4	And they shall build the old wastes, they shall raise up the former desolations, and they shall repair the waste cities, the desolations of many generations.
verse	23	61	5	@@And strangers shall stand and feed your flocks, and the sons of the alien @9shall be@7 your plowmen and your vinedressers.
verse	23	61	6	@@But ye shall be named the Priests of the LORD: @9men@7 shall call you the Ministers of our God: ye shall eat the riches of the Gentiles, and in their glory shall ye boast yourselves.
verse	23	61	7	@@For your shame @9ye shall have@7 double; and @9for@7 confusion they shall rejoice in their portion: therefore in their land they shall possess the double: everlasting joy shall be unto them.
verse	23	61	8	For I the LORD love judgment, I hate robbery for burnt offering; and I will direct their work in truth, and I will make an everlasting covenant with them.
verse	23	61	9	@@And their seed shall be known among the Gentiles, and their offspring among the people: all that see them shall acknowledge them, that they @9are@7 the seed @9which@7 the LORD hath blessed.
verse	23	61	10	@@I will greatly rejoice in the LORD, my soul shall be joyful in my God; for he hath clothed me with the garments of salvation, he hath covered me with the robe of righteousness, as a bridegroom decketh @9himself@7 with ornaments, and as a bride adorneth @9herself@7 with her jewels.
verse	23	61	11	For as the earth bringeth forth her bud, and as the garden causeth the things that are sown in it to spring forth; so the Lord GOD will cause righteousness and praise to spring forth before all the nations.
verse	23	62	1	@@For Zion's sake will I not hold my peace, and for Jerusalem's sake I will not rest, until the righteousness thereof go forth as brightness, and the salvation thereof as a lamp @9that@7 burneth.
verse	23	62	2	And the Gentiles shall see thy righteousness, and all kings thy glory: and thou shalt be called by a new name, which the mouth of the LORD shall name.
verse	23	62	3	Thou shalt also be a crown of glory in the hand of the LORD, and a royal diadem in the hand of thy God.
verse	23	62	4	Thou shalt no more be termed Forsaken; neither shall thy land any more be termed Desolate: but thou shalt be called Hephzibah, and thy land Beulah: for the LORD delighteth in thee, and thy land shall be married.
verse	23	62	5	@@For @9as@7 a young man marrieth a virgin, @9so@7 shall thy sons marry thee: and @9as@7 the bridegroom rejoiceth over the bride, @9so@7 shall thy God rejoice over thee.
verse	23	62	6	@@I have set watchmen upon thy walls, O Jerusalem, @9which@7 shall never hold their peace day nor night: ye that make mention of the LORD, keep not silence,
verse	23	62	7	And give him no rest, till he establish, and till he make Jerusalem a praise in the earth.
verse	23	62	8	@@The LORD hath sworn by his right hand, and by the arm of his strength, Surely I will no more give thy corn @9to be@7 meat for thine enemies; and the sons of the stranger shall not drink thy wine, for the which thou hast laboured:
verse	23	62	9	But they that have gathered it shall eat it, and praise the LORD; and they that have brought it together shall drink it in the courts of my holiness.
verse	23	62	10	Go through, go through the gates; prepare ye the way of the people; cast up, cast up the highways; gather out the stones; lift up a standard for the people.
verse	23	62	11	@@Behold, the LORD hath proclaimed unto the end of the world, Say ye to the daughter of Zion, Behold, thy salvation cometh; behold, his reward @9is@7 with him, and his work before him.
verse	23	62	12	And they shall call them, The holy people, The redeemed of the LORD: and thou shalt be called, Sought out, A city not forsaken.
verse	23	63	1	@@Who @9is@7 this that cometh from Edom, with dyed garments from Bozrah? this @9that is@7 glorious in his apparel, travelling in the greatness of his strength? I that speak in righteousness, mighty to save.
verse	23	63	2	@@Wherefore @9art thou@7 red in thine apparel, and thy garments like him that treadeth in the winefat?
verse	23	63	3	@@I have trodden the winepress alone; and of the people @9there was@7 none with me: for I will tread them in mine anger, and trample them in my fury; and their blood shall be sprinkled upon my garments, and I will stain all my raiment.
verse	23	63	4	@@For the day of vengeance @9is@7 in mine heart, and the year of my redeemed is come.
verse	23	63	5	@@And I looked, and @9there was@7 none to help; and I wondered that @9there was@7 none to uphold: therefore mine own arm brought salvation unto me; and my fury, it upheld me.
verse	23	63	6	And I will tread down the people in mine anger, and make them drunk in my fury, and I will bring down their strength to the earth.
verse	23	63	7	@@I will mention the lovingkindnesses of the LORD, @9and@7 the praises of the LORD, according to all that the LORD hath bestowed on us, and the great goodness toward the house of Israel, which he hath bestowed on them according to his mercies, and according to the multitude of his lovingkindnesses.
verse	23	63	8	@@For he said, Surely they @9are@7 my people, children @9that@7 will not lie: so he was their Saviour.
verse	23	63	9	In all their affliction he was afflicted, and the angel of his presence saved them: in his love and in his pity he redeemed them; and he bare them, and carried them all the days of old.
verse	23	63	10	@@But they rebelled, and vexed his holy Spirit: therefore he was turned to be their enemy, @9and@7 he fought against them.
verse	23	63	11	@@Then he remembered the days of old, Moses, @9and@7 his people, @9saying,@7 Where @9is@7 he that brought them up out of the sea with the shepherd of his flock? where @9is@7 he that put his holy Spirit within him?
verse	23	63	12	@@That led @9them@7 by the right hand of Moses with his glorious arm, dividing the water before them, to make himself an everlasting name?
verse	23	63	13	@@That led them through the deep, as an horse in the wilderness, @9that@7 they should not stumble?
verse	23	63	14	As a beast goeth down into the valley, the Spirit of the LORD caused him to rest: so didst thou lead thy people, to make thyself a glorious name.
verse	23	63	15	@@Look down from heaven, and behold from the habitation of thy holiness and of thy glory: where @9is@7 thy zeal and thy strength, the sounding of thy bowels and of thy mercies toward me? are they restrained?
verse	23	63	16	@@Doubtless thou @9art@7 our father, though Abraham be ignorant of us, and Israel acknowledge us not: thou, O LORD, @9art@7 our father, our redeemer; thy name @9is@7 from everlasting.
verse	23	63	17	@@O LORD, why hast thou made us to err from thy ways, @9and@7 hardened our heart from thy fear? Return for thy servants' sake, the tribes of thine inheritance.
verse	23	63	18	@@The people of thy holiness have possessed @9it@7 but a little while: our adversaries have trodden down thy sanctuary.
verse	23	63	19	@@We are @9thine:@7 thou never barest rule over them; they were not called by thy name.
verse	23	64	1	Oh that thou wouldest rend the heavens, that thou wouldest come down, that the mountains might flow down at thy presence,
verse	23	64	2	@@As @9when@7 the melting fire burneth, the fire causeth the waters to boil, to make thy name known to thine adversaries, @9that@7 the nations may tremble at thy presence!
verse	23	64	3	@@When thou didst terrible things @9which@7 we looked not for, thou camest down, the mountains flowed down at thy presence.
verse	23	64	4	@@For since the beginning of the world @9men@7 have not heard, nor perceived by the ear, neither hath the eye seen, O God, beside thee, @9what@7 he hath prepared for him that waiteth for him.
verse	23	64	5	@@Thou meetest him that rejoiceth and worketh righteousness, @9those that@7 remember thee in thy ways: behold, thou art wroth; for we have sinned: in those is continuance, and we shall be saved.
verse	23	64	6	@@But we are all as an unclean @9thing,@7 and all our righteousnesses @9are@7 as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.
verse	23	64	7	@@And @9there is@7 none that calleth upon thy name, that stirreth up himself to take hold of thee: for thou hast hid thy face from us, and hast consumed us, because of our iniquities.
verse	23	64	8	@@But now, O LORD, thou @9art@7 our father; we @9are@7 the clay, and thou our potter; and we all @9are@7 the work of thy hand.
verse	23	64	9	@@Be not wroth very sore, O LORD, neither remember iniquity for ever: behold, see, we beseech thee, we @9are@7 all thy people.
verse	23	64	10	Thy holy cities are a wilderness, Zion is a wilderness, Jerusalem a desolation.
verse	23	64	11	Our holy and our beautiful house, where our fathers praised thee, is burned up with fire: and all our pleasant things are laid waste.
verse	23	64	12	@@Wilt thou refrain thyself for these @9things,@7 O LORD? wilt thou hold thy peace, and afflict us very sore?
verse	23	65	1	@@I am sought of @9them that@7 asked not @9for me;@7 I am found of @9them that@7 sought me not: I said, Behold me, behold me, unto a nation @9that@7 was not called by my name.
verse	23	65	2	@@I have spread out my hands all the day unto a rebellious people, which walketh in a way @9that was@7 not good, after their own thoughts;
verse	23	65	3	A people that provoketh me to anger continually to my face; that sacrificeth in gardens, and burneth incense upon altars of brick;
verse	23	65	4	@@Which remain among the graves, and lodge in the monuments, which eat swine's flesh, and broth of abominable @9things is in@7 their vessels;
verse	23	65	5	@@Which say, Stand by thyself, come not near to me; for I am holier than thou. @9These@7 are a smoke in my nose, a fire that burneth all the day.
verse	23	65	6	@@Behold, @9it is@7 written before me: I will not keep silence, but will recompense, even recompense into their bosom,
verse	23	65	7	Your iniquities, and the iniquities of your fathers together, saith the LORD, which have burned incense upon the mountains, and blasphemed me upon the hills: therefore will I measure their former work into their bosom.
verse	23	65	8	@@Thus saith the LORD, As the new wine is found in the cluster, and @9one@7 saith, Destroy it not; for a blessing @9is@7 in it: so will I do for my servants' sakes, that I may not destroy them all.
verse	23	65	9	And I will bring forth a seed out of Jacob, and out of Judah an inheritor of my mountains: and mine elect shall inherit it, and my servants shall dwell there.
verse	23	65	10	And Sharon shall be a fold of flocks, and the valley of Achor a place for the herds to lie down in, for my people that have sought me.
verse	23	65	11	@@But ye @9are@7 they that forsake the LORD, that forget my holy mountain, that prepare a table for that troop, and that furnish the drink offering unto that number.
verse	23	65	12	@@Therefore will I number you to the sword, and ye shall all bow down to the slaughter: because when I called, ye did not answer; when I spake, ye did not hear; but did evil before mine eyes, and did choose @9that@7 wherein I delighted not.
verse	23	65	13	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD, Behold, my servants shall eat, but ye shall be hungry: behold, my servants shall drink, but ye shall be thirsty: behold, my servants shall rejoice, but ye shall be ashamed:
verse	23	65	14	Behold, my servants shall sing for joy of heart, but ye shall cry for sorrow of heart, and shall howl for vexation of spirit.
verse	23	65	15	And ye shall leave your name for a curse unto my chosen: for the Lord GOD shall slay thee, and call his servants by another name:
verse	23	65	16	That he who blesseth himself in the earth shall bless himself in the God of truth; and he that sweareth in the earth shall swear by the God of truth; because the former troubles are forgotten, and because they are hid from mine eyes.
verse	23	65	17	For, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth: and the former shall not be remembered, nor come into mind.
verse	23	65	18	@@But be ye glad and rejoice for ever @9in that@7 which I create: for, behold, I create Jerusalem a rejoicing, and her people a joy.
verse	23	65	19	And I will rejoice in Jerusalem, and joy in my people: and the voice of weeping shall be no more heard in her, nor the voice of crying.
verse	23	65	20	@@There shall be no more thence an infant of days, nor an old man that hath not filled his days: for the child shall die an hundred years old; but the sinner @9being@7 an hundred years old shall be accursed.
verse	23	65	21	@@And they shall build houses, and inhabit @9them;@7 and they shall plant vineyards, and eat the fruit of them.
verse	23	65	22	@@They shall not build, and another inhabit; they shall not plant, and another eat: for as the days of a tree @9are@7 the days of my people, and mine elect shall long enjoy the work of their hands.
verse	23	65	23	@@They shall not labour in vain, nor bring forth for trouble; for they @9are@7 the seed of the blessed of the LORD, and their offspring with them.
verse	23	65	24	And it shall come to pass, that before they call, I will answer; and while they are yet speaking, I will hear.
verse	23	65	25	@@The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like the bullock: and dust @9shall be@7 the serpent's meat. They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain, saith the LORD.
verse	23	66	1	@@Thus saith the LORD, The heaven @9is@7 my throne, and the earth @9is@7 my footstool: where @9is@7 the house that ye build unto me? and where @9is@7 the place of my rest?
verse	23	66	2	@@For all those @9things@7 hath mine hand made, and all those @9things@7 have been, saith the LORD: but to this @9man@7 will I look, @9even@7 to @9him that is@7 poor and of a contrite spirit, and trembleth at my word.
verse	23	66	3	@@He that killeth an ox @9is as if@7 he slew a man; he that sacrificeth a lamb, @9as if@7 he cut off a dog's neck; he that offereth an oblation, @9as if he offered@7 swine's blood; he that burneth incense, @9as if@7 he blessed an idol. Yea, they have chosen their own ways, and their soul delighteth in their abominations.
verse	23	66	4	@@I also will choose their delusions, and will bring their fears upon them; because when I called, none did answer; when I spake, they did not hear: but they did evil before mine eyes, and chose @9that@7 in which I delighted not.
verse	23	66	5	Hear the word of the LORD, ye that tremble at his word; your brethren that hated you, that cast you out for my name's sake, said, Let the LORD be glorified: but he shall appear to your joy, and they shall be ashamed.
verse	23	66	6	A voice of noise from the city, a voice from the temple, a voice of the LORD that rendereth recompence to his enemies.
verse	23	66	7	Before she travailed, she brought forth; before her pain came, she was delivered of a man child.
verse	23	66	8	@@Who hath heard such a thing? who hath seen such things? Shall the earth be made to bring forth in one day? @9or@7 shall a nation be born at once? for as soon as Zion travailed, she brought forth her children.
verse	23	66	9	@@Shall I bring to the birth, and not cause to bring forth? saith the LORD: shall I cause to bring forth, and shut @9the womb?@7 saith thy God.
verse	23	66	10	Rejoice ye with Jerusalem, and be glad with her, all ye that love her: rejoice for joy with her, all ye that mourn for her:
verse	23	66	11	That ye may suck, and be satisfied with the breasts of her consolations; that ye may milk out, and be delighted with the abundance of her glory.
verse	23	66	12	@@For thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will extend peace to her like a river, and the glory of the Gentiles like a flowing stream: then shall ye suck, ye shall be borne upon @9her@7 sides, and be dandled upon @9her@7 knees.
verse	23	66	13	As one whom his mother comforteth, so will I comfort you; and ye shall be comforted in Jerusalem.
verse	23	66	14	@@And when ye see @9this,@7 your heart shall rejoice, and your bones shall flourish like an herb: and the hand of the LORD shall be known toward his servants, and @9his@7 indignation toward his enemies.
verse	23	66	15	For, behold, the LORD will come with fire, and with his chariots like a whirlwind, to render his anger with fury, and his rebuke with flames of fire.
verse	23	66	16	For by fire and by his sword will the LORD plead with all flesh: and the slain of the LORD shall be many.
verse	23	66	17	@@They that sanctify themselves, and purify themselves in the gardens behind one @9tree@7 in the midst, eating swine's flesh, and the abomination, and the mouse, shall be consumed together, saith the LORD.
verse	23	66	18	@@For I @9know@7 their works and their thoughts: it shall come, that I will gather all nations and tongues; and they shall come, and see my glory.
verse	23	66	19	@@And I will set a sign among them, and I will send those that escape of them unto the nations, @9to@7 Tarshish, Pul, and Lud, that draw the bow, @9to@7 Tubal, and Javan, @9to@7 the isles afar off, that have not heard my fame, neither have seen my glory; and they shall declare my glory among the Gentiles.
verse	23	66	20	@@And they shall bring all your brethren @9for@7 an offering unto the LORD out of all nations upon horses, and in chariots, and in litters, and upon mules, and upon swift beasts, to my holy mountain Jerusalem, saith the LORD, as the children of Israel bring an offering in a clean vessel into the house of the LORD.
verse	23	66	21	@@And I will also take of them for priests @9and@7 for Levites, saith the LORD.
verse	23	66	22	For as the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, shall remain before me, saith the LORD, so shall your seed and your name remain.
