verse	24	1	1	@@The words of Jeremiah the son of Hilkiah, of the priests that @9were@7 in Anathoth in the land of Benjamin:
verse	24	1	2	To whom the word of the LORD came in the days of Josiah the son of Amon king of Judah, in the thirteenth year of his reign.
verse	24	1	3	It came also in the days of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, unto the end of the eleventh year of Zedekiah the son of Josiah king of Judah, unto the carrying away of Jerusalem captive in the fifth month.
verse	24	1	4	Then the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	24	1	5	@@Before I formed thee in the belly I knew thee; and before thou camest forth out of the womb I sanctified thee, @9and@7 I ordained thee a prophet unto the nations.
verse	24	1	6	@@Then said I, Ah, Lord GOD! behold, I cannot speak: for I @9am@7 a child.
verse	24	1	7	@@But the LORD said unto me, Say not, I @9am@7 a child: for thou shalt go to all that I shall send thee, and whatsoever I command thee thou shalt speak.
verse	24	1	8	@@Be not afraid of their faces: for I @9am@7 with thee to deliver thee, saith the LORD.
verse	24	1	9	Then the LORD put forth his hand, and touched my mouth. And the LORD said unto me, Behold, I have put my words in thy mouth.
verse	24	1	10	See, I have this day set thee over the nations and over the kingdoms, to root out, and to pull down, and to destroy, and to throw down, to build, and to plant.
verse	24	1	11	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying, Jeremiah, what seest thou? And I said, I see a rod of an almond tree.
verse	24	1	12	Then said the LORD unto me, Thou hast well seen: for I will hasten my word to perform it.
verse	24	1	13	@@And the word of the LORD came unto me the second time, saying, What seest thou? And I said, I see a seething pot; and the face thereof @9is@7 toward the north.
verse	24	1	14	Then the LORD said unto me, Out of the north an evil shall break forth upon all the inhabitants of the land.
verse	24	1	15	For, lo, I will call all the families of the kingdoms of the north, saith the LORD; and they shall come, and they shall set every one his throne at the entering of the gates of Jerusalem, and against all the walls thereof round about, and against all the cities of Judah.
verse	24	1	16	And I will utter my judgments against them touching all their wickedness, who have forsaken me, and have burned incense unto other gods, and worshipped the works of their own hands.
verse	24	1	17	Thou therefore gird up thy loins, and arise, and speak unto them all that I command thee: be not dismayed at their faces, lest I confound thee before them.
verse	24	1	18	For, behold, I have made thee this day a defenced city, and an iron pillar, and brasen walls against the whole land, against the kings of Judah, against the princes thereof, against the priests thereof, and against the people of the land.
verse	24	1	19	@@And they shall fight against thee; but they shall not prevail against thee; for I @9am@7 with thee, saith the LORD, to deliver thee.
verse	24	2	1	Moreover the word of the LORD came to me, saying,
verse	24	2	2	@@Go and cry in the ears of Jerusalem, saying, Thus saith the LORD; I remember thee, the kindness of thy youth, the love of thine espousals, when thou wentest after me in the wilderness, in a land @9that was@7 not sown.
verse	24	2	3	@@Israel @9was@7 holiness unto the LORD, @9and@7 the firstfruits of his increase: all that devour him shall offend; evil shall come upon them, saith the LORD.
verse	24	2	4	Hear ye the word of the LORD, O house of Jacob, and all the families of the house of Israel:
verse	24	2	5	Thus saith the LORD, What iniquity have your fathers found in me, that they are gone far from me, and have walked after vanity, and are become vain?
verse	24	2	6	@@Neither said they, Where @9is@7 the LORD that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, that led us through the wilderness, through a land of deserts and of pits, through a land of drought, and of the shadow of death, through a land that no man passed through, and where no man dwelt?
verse	24	2	7	And I brought you into a plentiful country, to eat the fruit thereof and the goodness thereof; but when ye entered, ye defiled my land, and made mine heritage an abomination.
verse	24	2	8	@@The priests said not, Where @9is@7 the LORD? and they that handle the law knew me not: the pastors also transgressed against me, and the prophets prophesied by Baal, and walked after @9things that@7 do not profit.
verse	24	2	9	Wherefore I will yet plead with you, saith the LORD, and with your children's children will I plead.
verse	24	2	10	For pass over the isles of Chittim, and see; and send unto Kedar, and consider diligently, and see if there be such a thing.
verse	24	2	11	@@Hath a nation changed @9their@7 gods, which @9are@7 yet no gods? but my people have changed their glory for @9that which@7 doth not profit.
verse	24	2	12	Be astonished, O ye heavens, at this, and be horribly afraid, be ye very desolate, saith the LORD.
verse	24	2	13	@@For my people have committed two evils; they have forsaken me the fountain of living waters, @9and@7 hewed them out cisterns, broken cisterns, that can hold no water.
verse	24	2	14	@@@9Is@7 Israel a servant? @9is@7 he a homeborn @9slave?@7 why is he spoiled?
verse	24	2	15	@@The young lions roared upon him, @9and@7 yelled, and they made his land waste: his cities are burned without inhabitant.
verse	24	2	16	Also the children of Noph and Tahapanes have broken the crown of thy head.
verse	24	2	17	Hast thou not procured this unto thyself, in that thou hast forsaken the LORD thy God, when he led thee by the way?
verse	24	2	18	And now what hast thou to do in the way of Egypt, to drink the waters of Sihor? or what hast thou to do in the way of Assyria, to drink the waters of the river?
verse	24	2	19	@@Thine own wickedness shall correct thee, and thy backslidings shall reprove thee: know therefore and see that @9it is@7 an evil @9thing@7 and bitter, that thou hast forsaken the LORD thy God, and that my fear @9is@7 not in thee, saith the Lord GOD of hosts.
verse	24	2	20	@@For of old time I have broken thy yoke, @9and@7 burst thy bands; and thou saidst, I will not transgress; when upon every high hill and under every green tree thou wanderest, playing the harlot.
verse	24	2	21	Yet I had planted thee a noble vine, wholly a right seed: how then art thou turned into the degenerate plant of a strange vine unto me?
verse	24	2	22	@@For though thou wash thee with nitre, and take thee much sope, @9yet@7 thine iniquity is marked before me, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	24	2	23	@@How canst thou say, I am not polluted, I have not gone after Baalim? see thy way in the valley, know what thou hast done: @9thou art@7 a swift dromedary traversing her ways;
verse	24	2	24	@@A wild ass used to the wilderness, @9that@7 snuffeth up the wind at her pleasure; in her occasion who can turn her away? all they that seek her will not weary themselves; in her month they shall find her.
verse	24	2	25	Withhold thy foot from being unshod, and thy throat from thirst: but thou saidst, There is no hope: no; for I have loved strangers, and after them will I go.
verse	24	2	26	As the thief is ashamed when he is found, so is the house of Israel ashamed; they, their kings, their princes, and their priests, and their prophets,
verse	24	2	27	@@Saying to a stock, Thou @9art@7 my father; and to a stone, Thou hast brought me forth: for they have turned @9their@7 back unto me, and not @9their@7 face: but in the time of their trouble they will say, Arise, and save us.
verse	24	2	28	@@But where @9are@7 thy gods that thou hast made thee? let them arise, if they can save thee in the time of thy trouble: for @9according to@7 the number of thy cities are thy gods, O Judah.
verse	24	2	29	Wherefore will ye plead with me? ye all have transgressed against me, saith the LORD.
verse	24	2	30	In vain have I smitten your children; they received no correction: your own sword hath devoured your prophets, like a destroying lion.
verse	24	2	31	O generation, see ye the word of the LORD. Have I been a wilderness unto Israel? a land of darkness? wherefore say my people, We are lords; we will come no more unto thee?
verse	24	2	32	@@Can a maid forget her ornaments, @9or@7 a bride her attire? yet my people have forgotten me days without number.
verse	24	2	33	Why trimmest thou thy way to seek love? therefore hast thou also taught the wicked ones thy ways.
verse	24	2	34	Also in thy skirts is found the blood of the souls of the poor innocents: I have not found it by secret search, but upon all these.
verse	24	2	35	Yet thou sayest, Because I am innocent, surely his anger shall turn from me. Behold, I will plead with thee, because thou sayest, I have not sinned.
verse	24	2	36	Why gaddest thou about so much to change thy way? thou also shalt be ashamed of Egypt, as thou wast ashamed of Assyria.
verse	24	2	37	Yea, thou shalt go forth from him, and thine hands upon thine head: for the LORD hath rejected thy confidences, and thou shalt not prosper in them.
verse	24	3	1	They say, If a man put away his wife, and she go from him, and become another man's, shall he return unto her again? shall not that land be greatly polluted? but thou hast played the harlot with many lovers; yet return again to me, saith the LORD.
verse	24	3	2	Lift up thine eyes unto the high places, and see where thou hast not been lien with. In the ways hast thou sat for them, as the Arabian in the wilderness; and thou hast polluted the land with thy whoredoms and with thy wickedness.
verse	24	3	3	Therefore the showers have been withholden, and there hath been no latter rain; and thou hadst a whore's forehead, thou refusedst to be ashamed.
verse	24	3	4	Wilt thou not from this time cry unto me, My father, thou art the guide of my youth?
verse	24	3	5	@@Will he reserve @9his anger@7 for ever? will he keep @9it@7 to the end? Behold, thou hast spoken and done evil things as thou couldest.
verse	24	3	6	@@The LORD said also unto me in the days of Josiah the king, Hast thou seen @9that@7 which backsliding Israel hath done? she is gone up upon every high mountain and under every green tree, and there hath played the harlot.
verse	24	3	7	@@And I said after she had done all these @9things,@7 Turn thou unto me. But she returned not. And her treacherous sister Judah saw @9it. @7
verse	24	3	8	And I saw, when for all the causes whereby backsliding Israel committed adultery I had put her away, and given her a bill of divorce; yet her treacherous sister Judah feared not, but went and played the harlot also.
verse	24	3	9	And it came to pass through the lightness of her whoredom, that she defiled the land, and committed adultery with stones and with stocks.
verse	24	3	10	And yet for all this her treacherous sister Judah hath not turned unto me with her whole heart, but feignedly, saith the LORD.
verse	24	3	11	And the LORD said unto me, The backsliding Israel hath justified herself more than treacherous Judah.
verse	24	3	12	@@Go and proclaim these words toward the north, and say, Return, thou backsliding Israel, saith the LORD; @9and@7 I will not cause mine anger to fall upon you: for I @9am@7 merciful, saith the LORD, @9and@7 I will not keep @9anger@7 for ever.
verse	24	3	13	Only acknowledge thine iniquity, that thou hast transgressed against the LORD thy God, and hast scattered thy ways to the strangers under every green tree, and ye have not obeyed my voice, saith the LORD.
verse	24	3	14	Turn, O backsliding children, saith the LORD; for I am married unto you: and I will take you one of a city, and two of a family, and I will bring you to Zion:
verse	24	3	15	And I will give you pastors according to mine heart, which shall feed you with knowledge and understanding.
verse	24	3	16	@@And it shall come to pass, when ye be multiplied and increased in the land, in those days, saith the LORD, they shall say no more, The ark of the covenant of the LORD: neither shall it come to mind: neither shall they remember it; neither shall they visit @9it;@7 neither shall @9that@7 be done any more.
verse	24	3	17	At that time they shall call Jerusalem the throne of the LORD; and all the nations shall be gathered unto it, to the name of the LORD, to Jerusalem: neither shall they walk any more after the imagination of their evil heart.
verse	24	3	18	In those days the house of Judah shall walk with the house of Israel, and they shall come together out of the land of the north to the land that I have given for an inheritance unto your fathers.
verse	24	3	19	But I said, How shall I put thee among the children, and give thee a pleasant land, a goodly heritage of the hosts of nations? and I said, Thou shalt call me, My father; and shalt not turn away from me.
verse	24	3	20	@@Surely @9as@7 a wife treacherously departeth from her husband, so have ye dealt treacherously with me, O house of Israel, saith the LORD.
verse	24	3	21	@@A voice was heard upon the high places, weeping @9and@7 supplications of the children of Israel: for they have perverted their way, @9and@7 they have forgotten the LORD their God.
verse	24	3	22	@@Return, ye backsliding children, @9and@7 I will heal your backslidings. Behold, we come unto thee; for thou @9art@7 the LORD our God.
verse	24	3	23	@@Truly in vain @9is salvation hoped for@7 from the hills, @9and from@7 the multitude of mountains: truly in the LORD our God @9is@7 the salvation of Israel.
verse	24	3	24	For shame hath devoured the labour of our fathers from our youth; their flocks and their herds, their sons and their daughters.
verse	24	3	25	We lie down in our shame, and our confusion covereth us: for we have sinned against the LORD our God, we and our fathers, from our youth even unto this day, and have not obeyed the voice of the LORD our God.
verse	24	4	1	If thou wilt return, O Israel, saith the LORD, return unto me: and if thou wilt put away thine abominations out of my sight, then shalt thou not remove.
verse	24	4	2	And thou shalt swear, The LORD liveth, in truth, in judgment, and in righteousness; and the nations shall bless themselves in him, and in him shall they glory.
verse	24	4	3	For thus saith the LORD to the men of Judah and Jerusalem, Break up your fallow ground, and sow not among thorns.
verse	24	4	4	@@Circumcise yourselves to the LORD, and take away the foreskins of your heart, ye men of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem: lest my fury come forth like fire, and burn that none can quench @9it,@7 because of the evil of your doings.
verse	24	4	5	Declare ye in Judah, and publish in Jerusalem; and say, Blow ye the trumpet in the land: cry, gather together, and say, Assemble yourselves, and let us go into the defenced cities.
verse	24	4	6	Set up the standard toward Zion: retire, stay not: for I will bring evil from the north, and a great destruction.
verse	24	4	7	@@The lion is come up from his thicket, and the destroyer of the Gentiles is on his way; he is gone forth from his place to make thy land desolate; @9and@7 thy cities shall be laid waste, without an inhabitant.
verse	24	4	8	For this gird you with sackcloth, lament and howl: for the fierce anger of the LORD is not turned back from us.
