verse	24	4	10	Then said I, Ah, Lord GOD! surely thou hast greatly deceived this people and Jerusalem, saying, Ye shall have peace; whereas the sword reacheth unto the soul.
verse	24	4	11	At that time shall it be said to this people and to Jerusalem, A dry wind of the high places in the wilderness toward the daughter of my people, not to fan, nor to cleanse,
verse	24	4	12	@@@9Even @7a full wind from those @9places @7shall come unto me: now also will I give sentence against them.
verse	24	4	13	@@Behold, he shall come up as clouds, and his chariots @9shall be@7 as a whirlwind: his horses are swifter than eagles. Woe unto us! for we are spoiled.
verse	24	4	14	O Jerusalem, wash thine heart from wickedness, that thou mayest be saved. How long shall thy vain thoughts lodge within thee?
verse	24	4	15	For a voice declareth from Dan, and publisheth affliction from mount Ephraim.
verse	24	4	16	@@Make ye mention to the nations; behold, publish against Jerusalem, @9that@7 watchers come from a far country, and give out their voice against the cities of Judah.
verse	24	4	17	As keepers of a field, are they against her round about; because she hath been rebellious against me, saith the LORD.
verse	24	4	18	@@Thy way and thy doings have procured these @9things@7 unto thee; this @9is@7 thy wickedness, because it is bitter, because it reacheth unto thine heart.
verse	24	4	19	My bowels, my bowels! I am pained at my very heart; my heart maketh a noise in me; I cannot hold my peace, because thou hast heard, O my soul, the sound of the trump, the alarm of war.
verse	24	4	20	@@Destruction upon destruction is cried; for the whole land is spoiled: suddenly are my tents spoiled, @9and@7 my curtains in a moment.
verse	24	4	21	@@How long shall I see the standard, @9and@7 hear the sound of the trumpet?
verse	24	4	22	@@For my people @9is@7 foolish, they have not known me; they @9are@7 sottish children, and they have none understanding: they @9are@7 wise to do evil, but to do good they have no knowledge.
verse	24	4	23	@@I beheld the earth, and, lo, @9it was@7 without form, and void; and the heavens, and they @9had@7 no light.
verse	24	4	24	I beheld the mountains, and, lo, they trembled, and all the hills moved lightly.
verse	24	4	25	@@I beheld, and, lo, @9there was@7 no man, and all the birds of the heavens were fled.
verse	24	4	26	@@I beheld, and, lo, the fruitful place @9was@7 a wilderness, and all the cities thereof were broken down at the presence of the LORD, @9and@7 by his fierce anger.
verse	24	4	27	For thus hath the LORD said, The whole land shall be desolate; yet will I not make a full end.
verse	24	4	28	@@For this shall the earth mourn, and the heavens above be black: because I have spoken @9it,@7 I have purposed @9it,@7 and will not repent, neither will I turn back from it.
verse	24	4	29	@@The whole city shall flee for the noise of the horsemen and bowmen; they shall go into thickets, and climb up upon the rocks: every city @9shall be@7 forsaken, and not a man dwell therein.
verse	24	4	30	@@And @9when@7 thou @9art@7 spoiled, what wilt thou do? Though thou clothest thyself with crimson, though thou deckest thee with ornaments of gold, though thou rentest thy face with painting, in vain shalt thou make thyself fair; @9thy@7 lovers will despise thee, they will seek thy life.
verse	24	4	31	@@For I have heard a voice as of a woman in travail, @9and@7 the anguish as of her that bringeth forth her first child, the voice of the daughter of Zion, @9that@7 bewaileth herself, @9that@7 spreadeth her hands, @9saying,@7 Woe @9is@7 me now! for my soul is wearied because of murderers.
verse	24	5	1	@@Run ye to and fro through the streets of Jerusalem, and see now, and know, and seek in the broad places thereof, if ye can find a man, if there be @9any@7 that executeth judgment, that seeketh the truth; and I will pardon it.
verse	24	5	2	And though they say, The LORD liveth; surely they swear falsely.
verse	24	5	3	@@O LORD, @9are@7 not thine eyes upon the truth? thou hast stricken them, but they have not grieved; thou hast consumed them, @9but@7 they have refused to receive correction: they have made their faces harder than a rock; they have refused to return.
verse	24	5	4	@@Therefore I said, Surely these @9are@7 poor; they are foolish: for they know not the way of the LORD, @9nor@7 the judgment of their God.
verse	24	5	5	@@I will get me unto the great men, and will speak unto them; for they have known the way of the LORD, @9and@7 the judgment of their God: but these have altogether broken the yoke, @9and@7 burst the bonds.
verse	24	5	6	@@Wherefore a lion out of the forest shall slay them, @9and@7 a wolf of the evenings shall spoil them, a leopard shall watch over their cities: every one that goeth out thence shall be torn in pieces: because their transgressions are many, @9and@7 their backslidings are increased.
verse	24	5	7	@@How shall I pardon thee for this? thy children have forsaken me, and sworn by @9them that are@7 no gods: when I had fed them to the full, they then committed adultery, and assembled themselves by troops in the harlots' houses.
verse	24	5	8	@@They were @9as@7 fed horses in the morning: every one neighed after his neighbour's wife.
verse	24	5	9	@@Shall I not visit for these @9things?@7 saith the LORD: and shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?
verse	24	5	10	@@Go ye up upon her walls, and destroy; but make not a full end: take away her battlements; for they @9are@7 not the LORD'S.
verse	24	5	11	For the house of Israel and the house of Judah have dealt very treacherously against me, saith the LORD.
verse	24	5	12	@@They have belied the LORD, and said, @9It is@7 not he; neither shall evil come upon us; neither shall we see sword nor famine:
verse	24	5	13	@@And the prophets shall become wind, and the word @9is@7 not in them: thus shall it be done unto them.
verse	24	5	14	Wherefore thus saith the LORD God of hosts, Because ye speak this word, behold, I will make my words in thy mouth fire, and this people wood, and it shall devour them.
verse	24	5	15	@@Lo, I will bring a nation upon you from far, O house of Israel, saith the LORD: it @9is@7 a mighty nation, it @9is@7 an ancient nation, a nation whose language thou knowest not, neither understandest what they say.
