verse	24	5	26	@@For among my people are found wicked @9men:@7 they lay wait, as he that setteth snares; they set a trap, they catch men.
verse	24	5	27	@@As a cage is full of birds, so @9are@7 their houses full of deceit: therefore they are become great, and waxen rich.
verse	24	5	28	They are waxen fat, they shine: yea, they overpass the deeds of the wicked: they judge not the cause, the cause of the fatherless, yet they prosper; and the right of the needy do they not judge.
verse	24	5	29	@@Shall I not visit for these @9things?@7 saith the LORD: shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?
verse	24	5	30	A wonderful and horrible thing is committed in the land;
verse	24	5	31	@@The prophets prophesy falsely, and the priests bear rule by their means; and my people love @9to have it@7 so: and what will ye do in the end thereof?
verse	24	6	1	O ye children of Benjamin, gather yourselves to flee out of the midst of Jerusalem, and blow the trumpet in Tekoa, and set up a sign of fire in Beth-haccerem: for evil appeareth out of the north, and great destruction.
verse	24	6	2	@@I have likened the daughter of Zion to a comely and delicate @9woman. @7
verse	24	6	3	@@The shepherds with their flocks shall come unto her; they shall pitch @9their@7 tents against her round about; they shall feed every one in his place.
verse	24	6	4	Prepare ye war against her; arise, and let us go up at noon. Woe unto us! for the day goeth away, for the shadows of the evening are stretched out.
