verse	24	6	10	@@To whom shall I speak, and give warning, that they may hear? behold, their ear @9is@7 uncircumcised, and they cannot hearken: behold, the word of the LORD is unto them a reproach; they have no delight in it.
verse	24	6	11	@@Therefore I am full of the fury of the LORD; I am weary with holding in: I will pour it out upon the children abroad, and upon the assembly of young men together: for even the husband with the wife shall be taken, the aged with @9him that is@7 full of days.
verse	24	6	12	@@And their houses shall be turned unto others, @9with their@7 fields and wives together: for I will stretch out my hand upon the inhabitants of the land, saith the LORD.
verse	24	6	13	@@For from the least of them even unto the greatest of them every one @9is@7 given to covetousness; and from the prophet even unto the priest every one dealeth falsely.
verse	24	6	14	@@They have healed also the hurt @9of the daughter@7 of my people slightly, saying, Peace, peace; when @9there is@7 no peace.
verse	24	6	15	@@Were they ashamed when they had committed abomination? nay, they were not at all ashamed, neither could they blush: therefore they shall fall among them that fall: at the time @9that@7 I visit them they shall be cast down, saith the LORD.
verse	24	6	16	@@Thus saith the LORD, Stand ye in the ways, and see, and ask for the old paths, where is the good way, and walk therein, and ye shall find rest for your souls. But they said, We will not walk @9therein. @7
verse	24	6	17	@@Also I set watchmen over you, @9saying,@7 Hearken to the sound of the trumpet. But they said, We will not hearken.
verse	24	6	18	@@Therefore hear, ye nations, and know, O congregation, what @9is@7 among them.
verse	24	6	19	@@Hear, O earth: behold, I will bring evil upon this people, @9even@7 the fruit of their thoughts, because they have not hearkened unto my words, nor to my law, but rejected it.
