verse	24	6	23	@@They shall lay hold on bow and spear; they @9are@7 cruel, and have no mercy; their voice roareth like the sea; and they ride upon horses, set in array as men for war against thee, O daughter of Zion.
verse	24	6	24	@@We have heard the fame thereof: our hands wax feeble: anguish hath taken hold of us, @9and@7 pain, as of a woman in travail.
verse	24	6	25	@@Go not forth into the field, nor walk by the way; for the sword of the enemy @9and@7 fear @9is@7 on every side.
verse	24	6	26	@@O daughter of my people, gird @9thee@7 with sackcloth, and wallow thyself in ashes: make thee mourning, @9as for@7 an only son, most bitter lamentation: for the spoiler shall suddenly come upon us.
