verse	24	7	1	The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,
verse	24	7	2	@@Stand in the gate of the LORD'S house, and proclaim there this word, and say, Hear the word of the LORD, all @9ye of@7 Judah, that enter in at these gates to worship the LORD.
verse	24	7	3	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, Amend your ways and your doings, and I will cause you to dwell in this place.
verse	24	7	4	@@Trust ye not in lying words, saying, The temple of the LORD, The temple of the LORD, The temple of the LORD, @9are@7 these.
verse	24	7	5	For if ye throughly amend your ways and your doings; if ye throughly execute judgment between a man and his neighbour;
verse	24	7	6	@@@9If@7 ye oppress not the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow, and shed not innocent blood in this place, neither walk after other gods to your hurt:
verse	24	7	7	Then will I cause you to dwell in this place, in the land that I gave to your fathers, for ever and ever.
verse	24	7	8	Behold, ye trust in lying words, that cannot profit.
verse	24	7	9	Will ye steal, murder, and commit adultery, and swear falsely, and burn incense unto Baal, and walk after other gods whom ye know not;
verse	24	7	10	And come and stand before me in this house, which is called by my name, and say, We are delivered to do all these abominations?
verse	24	7	11	@@Is this house, which is called by my name, become a den of robbers in your eyes? Behold, even I have seen @9it,@7 saith the LORD.
verse	24	7	12	@@But go ye now unto my place which @9was@7 in Shiloh, where I set my name at the first, and see what I did to it for the wickedness of my people Israel.
verse	24	7	13	And now, because ye have done all these works, saith the LORD, and I spake unto you, rising up early and speaking, but ye heard not; and I called you, but ye answered not;
verse	24	7	14	@@Therefore will I do unto @9this@7 house, which is called by my name, wherein ye trust, and unto the place which I gave to you and to your fathers, as I have done to Shiloh.
verse	24	7	15	@@And I will cast you out of my sight, as I have cast out all your brethren, @9even@7 the whole seed of Ephraim.
verse	24	7	16	Therefore pray not thou for this people, neither lift up cry nor prayer for them, neither make intercession to me: for I will not hear thee.
verse	24	7	17	Seest thou not what they do in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?
verse	24	7	18	@@The children gather wood, and the fathers kindle the fire, and the women knead @9their@7 dough, to make cakes to the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto other gods, that they may provoke me to anger.
verse	24	7	19	@@Do they provoke me to anger? saith the LORD: @9do they@7 not @9provoke@7 themselves to the confusion of their own faces?
verse	24	7	20	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, mine anger and my fury shall be poured out upon this place, upon man, and upon beast, and upon the trees of the field, and upon the fruit of the ground; and it shall burn, and shall not be quenched.
verse	24	7	21	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Put your burnt offerings unto your sacrifices, and eat flesh.
verse	24	7	22	For I spake not unto your fathers, nor commanded them in the day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt, concerning burnt offerings or sacrifices:
verse	24	7	23	But this thing commanded I them, saying, Obey my voice, and I will be your God, and ye shall be my people: and walk ye in all the ways that I have commanded you, that it may be well unto you.
verse	24	7	24	@@But they hearkened not, nor inclined their ear, but walked in the counsels @9and@7 in the imagination of their evil heart, and went backward, and not forward.
