verse	24	11	1	The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,
verse	24	11	2	Hear ye the words of this covenant, and speak unto the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem;
verse	24	11	3	@@And say thou unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel; Cursed @9be@7 the man that obeyeth not the words of this covenant,
verse	24	11	4	@@Which I commanded your fathers in the day @9that@7 I brought them forth out of the land of Egypt, from the iron furnace, saying, Obey my voice, and do them, according to all which I command you: so shall ye be my people, and I will be your God:
verse	24	11	5	@@That I may perform the oath which I have sworn unto your fathers, to give them a land flowing with milk and honey, as @9it is@7 this day. Then answered I, and said, So be it, O LORD.
verse	24	11	6	Then the LORD said unto me, Proclaim all these words in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, saying, Hear ye the words of this covenant, and do them.
verse	24	11	7	@@For I earnestly protested unto your fathers in the day @9that@7 I brought them up out of the land of Egypt, @9even@7 unto this day, rising early and protesting, saying, Obey my voice.
verse	24	11	8	@@Yet they obeyed not, nor inclined their ear, but walked every one in the imagination of their evil heart: therefore I will bring upon them all the words of this covenant, which I commanded @9them@7 to do; but they did @9them@7 not.
verse	24	11	9	And the LORD said unto me, A conspiracy is found among the men of Judah, and among the inhabitants of Jerusalem.
verse	24	11	10	They are turned back to the iniquities of their forefathers, which refused to hear my words; and they went after other gods to serve them: the house of Israel and the house of Judah have broken my covenant which I made with their fathers.
verse	24	11	11	Therefore thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will bring evil upon them, which they shall not be able to escape; and though they shall cry unto me, I will not hearken unto them.
verse	24	11	12	Then shall the cities of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem go, and cry unto the gods unto whom they offer incense: but they shall not save them at all in the time of their trouble.
verse	24	11	13	@@For @9according to@7 the number of thy cities were thy gods, O Judah; and @9according to@7 the number of the streets of Jerusalem have ye set up altars to @9that@7 shameful thing, @9even@7 altars to burn incense unto Baal.
verse	24	11	14	@@Therefore pray not thou for this people, neither lift up a cry or prayer for them: for I will not hear @9them@7 in the time that they cry unto me for their trouble.
verse	24	11	15	@@What hath my beloved to do in mine house, @9seeing@7 she hath wrought lewdness with many, and the holy flesh is passed from thee? when thou doest evil, then thou rejoicest.
