verse	24	11	17	For the LORD of hosts, that planted thee, hath pronounced evil against thee, for the evil of the house of Israel and of the house of Judah, which they have done against themselves to provoke me to anger in offering incense unto Baal.
verse	24	11	18	@@And the LORD hath given me knowledge @9of it,@7 and I know @9it:@7 then thou shewedst me their doings.
verse	24	11	19	@@But I @9was@7 like a lamb @9or@7 an ox @9that@7 is brought to the slaughter; and I knew not that they had devised devices against me, @9saying,@7 Let us destroy the tree with the fruit thereof, and let us cut him off from the land of the living, that his name may be no more remembered.
verse	24	11	20	But, O LORD of hosts, that judgest righteously, that triest the reins and the heart, let me see thy vengeance on them: for unto thee have I revealed my cause.
verse	24	11	21	Therefore thus saith the LORD of the men of Anathoth, that seek thy life, saying, Prophesy not in the name of the LORD, that thou die not by our hand:
