verse	24	12	5	@@If thou hast run with the footmen, and they have wearied thee, then how canst thou contend with horses? and @9if@7 in the land of peace, @9wherein@7 thou trustedst, @9they wearied thee,@7 then how wilt thou do in the swelling of Jordan?
verse	24	12	6	For even thy brethren, and the house of thy father, even they have dealt treacherously with thee; yea, they have called a multitude after thee: believe them not, though they speak fair words unto thee.
