verse	24	19	3	And say, Hear ye the word of the LORD, O kings of Judah, and inhabitants of Jerusalem; Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will bring evil upon this place, the which whosoever heareth, his ears shall tingle.
verse	24	19	4	Because they have forsaken me, and have estranged this place, and have burned incense in it unto other gods, whom neither they nor their fathers have known, nor the kings of Judah, and have filled this place with the blood of innocents;
verse	24	19	5	@@They have built also the high places of Baal, to burn their sons with fire @9for@7 burnt offerings unto Baal, which I commanded not, nor spake @9it,@7 neither came @9it@7 into my mind:
verse	24	19	6	Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that this place shall no more be called Tophet, nor The valley of the son of Hinnom, but The valley of slaughter.
verse	24	19	7	And I will make void the counsel of Judah and Jerusalem in this place; and I will cause them to fall by the sword before their enemies, and by the hands of them that seek their lives: and their carcases will I give to be meat for the fowls of the heaven, and for the beasts of the earth.
verse	24	19	8	And I will make this city desolate, and an hissing; every one that passeth thereby shall be astonished and hiss because of all the plagues thereof.
verse	24	19	9	And I will cause them to eat the flesh of their sons and the flesh of their daughters, and they shall eat every one the flesh of his friend in the siege and straitness, wherewith their enemies, and they that seek their lives, shall straiten them.
verse	24	19	10	Then shalt thou break the bottle in the sight of the men that go with thee,
verse	24	19	11	@@And shalt say unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Even so will I break this people and this city, as @9one@7 breaketh a potter's vessel, that cannot be made whole again: and they shall bury @9them@7 in Tophet, till @9there be@7 no place to bury.
verse	24	19	12	@@Thus will I do unto this place, saith the LORD, and to the inhabitants thereof, and @9even@7 make this city as Tophet:
verse	24	19	13	And the houses of Jerusalem, and the houses of the kings of Judah, shall be defiled as the place of Tophet, because of all the houses upon whose roofs they have burned incense unto all the host of heaven, and have poured out drink offerings unto other gods.
verse	24	19	14	Then came Jeremiah from Tophet, whither the LORD had sent him to prophesy; and he stood in the court of the LORD'S house; and said to all the people,
verse	24	19	15	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will bring upon this city and upon all her towns all the evil that I have pronounced against it, because they have hardened their necks, that they might not hear my words.
verse	24	20	1	@@Now Pashur the son of Immer the priest, who @9was@7 also chief governor in the house of the LORD, heard that Jeremiah prophesied these things.
verse	24	20	2	@@Then Pashur smote Jeremiah the prophet, and put him in the stocks that @9were@7 in the high gate of Benjamin, which @9was@7 by the house of the LORD.
verse	24	20	3	And it came to pass on the morrow, that Pashur brought forth Jeremiah out of the stocks. Then said Jeremiah unto him, The LORD hath not called thy name Pashur, but Magor-missabib.
verse	24	20	4	@@For thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will make thee a terror to thyself, and to all thy friends: and they shall fall by the sword of their enemies, and thine eyes shall behold @9it:@7 and I will give all Judah into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall carry them captive into Babylon, and shall slay them with the sword.
verse	24	20	5	Moreover I will deliver all the strength of this city, and all the labours thereof, and all the precious things thereof, and all the treasures of the kings of Judah will I give into the hand of their enemies, which shall spoil them, and take them, and carry them to Babylon.
verse	24	20	6	And thou, Pashur, and all that dwell in thine house shall go into captivity: and thou shalt come to Babylon, and there thou shalt die, and shalt be buried there, thou, and all thy friends, to whom thou hast prophesied lies.
verse	24	20	7	O LORD, thou hast deceived me, and I was deceived: thou art stronger than I, and hast prevailed: I am in derision daily, every one mocketh me.
verse	24	20	8	For since I spake, I cried out, I cried violence and spoil; because the word of the LORD was made a reproach unto me, and a derision, daily.
verse	24	20	9	@@Then I said, I will not make mention of him, nor speak any more in his name. But @9his word@7 was in mine heart as a burning fire shut up in my bones, and I was weary with forbearing, and I could not @9stay.@7
verse	24	20	10	@@For I heard the defaming of many, fear on every side. Report, @9say they,@7 and we will report it. All my familiars watched for my halting, @9saying,@7 Peradventure he will be enticed, and we shall prevail against him, and we shall take our revenge on him.
verse	24	20	11	@@But the LORD @9is@7 with me as a mighty terrible one: therefore my persecutors shall stumble, and they shall not prevail: they shall be greatly ashamed; for they shall not prosper: @9their@7 everlasting confusion shall never be forgotten.
verse	24	20	12	@@But, O LORD of hosts, that triest the righteous, @9and@7 seest the reins and the heart, let me see thy vengeance on them: for unto thee have I opened my cause.
verse	24	20	13	Sing unto the LORD, praise ye the LORD: for he hath delivered the soul of the poor from the hand of evildoers.
verse	24	20	14	@@Cursed @9be@7 the day wherein I was born: let not the day wherein my mother bare me be blessed.
verse	24	20	15	@@Cursed @9be@7 the man who brought tidings to my father, saying, A man child is born unto thee; making him very glad.
verse	24	20	16	And let that man be as the cities which the LORD overthrew, and repented not: and let him hear the cry in the morning, and the shouting at noontide;
verse	24	20	17	@@Because he slew me not from the womb; or that my mother might have been my grave, and her womb @9to be@7 always great @9with me. @7
verse	24	20	18	Wherefore came I forth out of the womb to see labour and sorrow, that my days should be consumed with shame?
verse	24	21	1	The word which came unto Jeremiah from the LORD, when king Zedekiah sent unto him Pashur the son of Melchiah, and Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah the priest, saying,
verse	24	21	2	Enquire, I pray thee, of the LORD for us; for Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon maketh war against us; if so be that the LORD will deal with us according to all his wondrous works, that he may go up from us.
verse	24	21	3	Then said Jeremiah unto them, Thus shall ye say to Zedekiah:
verse	24	21	4	@@Thus saith the LORD God of Israel; Behold, I will turn back the weapons of war that @9are@7 in your hands, wherewith ye fight @9against@7 the king of Babylon, and against the Chaldeans, which besiege you without the walls, and I will assemble them into the midst of this city.
verse	24	21	5	And I myself will fight against you with an outstretched hand and with a strong arm, even in anger, and in fury, and in great wrath.
verse	24	21	6	And I will smite the inhabitants of this city, both man and beast: they shall die of a great pestilence.
verse	24	21	7	And afterward, saith the LORD, I will deliver Zedekiah king of Judah, and his servants, and the people, and such as are left in this city from the pestilence, from the sword, and from the famine, into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of their enemies, and into the hand of those that seek their life: and he shall smite them with the edge of the sword; he shall not spare them, neither have pity, nor have mercy.
verse	24	21	8	And unto this people thou shalt say, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I set before you the way of life, and the way of death.
verse	24	21	9	He that abideth in this city shall die by the sword, and by the famine, and by the pestilence: but he that goeth out, and falleth to the Chaldeans that besiege you, he shall live, and his life shall be unto him for a prey.
verse	24	21	10	For I have set my face against this city for evil, and not for good, saith the LORD: it shall be given into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall burn it with fire.
verse	24	21	11	And touching the house of the king of Judah, say, Hear ye the word of the LORD;
verse	24	21	12	@@O house of David, thus saith the LORD; Execute judgment in the morning, and deliver @9him that is@7 spoiled out of the hand of the oppressor, lest my fury go out like fire, and burn that none can quench @9it,@7 because of the evil of your doings.
verse	24	21	13	@@Behold, I @9am@7 against thee, O inhabitant of the valley, @9and@7 rock of the plain, saith the LORD; which say, Who shall come down against us? or who shall enter into our habitations?
verse	24	21	14	But I will punish you according to the fruit of your doings, saith the LORD: and I will kindle a fire in the forest thereof, and it shall devour all things round about it.
verse	24	22	1	Thus saith the LORD; Go down to the house of the king of Judah, and speak there this word,
verse	24	22	2	And say, Hear the word of the LORD, O king of Judah, that sittest upon the throne of David, thou, and thy servants, and thy people that enter in by these gates:
verse	24	22	3	Thus saith the LORD; Execute ye judgment and righteousness, and deliver the spoiled out of the hand of the oppressor: and do no wrong, do no violence to the stranger, the fatherless, nor the widow, neither shed innocent blood in this place.
verse	24	22	4	For if ye do this thing indeed, then shall there enter in by the gates of this house kings sitting upon the throne of David, riding in chariots and on horses, he, and his servants, and his people.
verse	24	22	5	But if ye will not hear these words, I swear by myself, saith the LORD, that this house shall become a desolation.
verse	24	22	6	@@For thus saith the LORD unto the king's house of Judah; Thou @9art@7 Gilead unto me, @9and@7 the head of Lebanon: @9yet@7 surely I will make thee a wilderness, @9and@7 cities @9which@7 are not inhabited.
verse	24	22	7	@@And I will prepare destroyers against thee, every one with his weapons: and they shall cut down thy choice cedars, and cast @9them@7 into the fire.
verse	24	22	8	And many nations shall pass by this city, and they shall say every man to his neighbour, Wherefore hath the LORD done thus unto this great city?
verse	24	22	9	Then they shall answer, Because they have forsaken the covenant of the LORD their God, and worshipped other gods, and served them.
verse	24	22	10	@@Weep ye not for the dead, neither bemoan him: @9but@7 weep sore for him that goeth away: for he shall return no more, nor see his native country.
verse	24	22	11	For thus saith the LORD touching Shallum the son of Josiah king of Judah, which reigned instead of Josiah his father, which went forth out of this place; He shall not return thither any more:
verse	24	22	12	But he shall die in the place whither they have led him captive, and shall see this land no more.
verse	24	22	13	@@Woe unto him that buildeth his house by unrighteousness, and his chambers by wrong; @9that@7 useth his neighbour's service without wages, and giveth him not for his work;
verse	24	22	14	@@That saith, I will build me a wide house and large chambers, and cutteth him out windows; and @9it is@7 cieled with cedar, and painted with vermilion.
verse	24	22	15	@@Shalt thou reign, because thou closest @9thyself@7 in cedar? did not thy father eat and drink, and do judgment and justice, @9and@7 then @9it was@7 well with him?
verse	24	22	16	@@He judged the cause of the poor and needy; then @9it was@7 well @9with him: was@7 not this to know me? saith the LORD.
verse	24	22	17	@@But thine eyes and thine heart @9are@7 not but for thy covetousness, and for to shed innocent blood, and for oppression, and for violence, to do @9it. @7
verse	24	22	18	@@Therefore thus saith the LORD concerning Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah; They shall not lament for him, @9saying,@7 Ah my brother! or, Ah sister! they shall not lament for him, @9saying,@7 Ah lord! or, Ah his glory!
verse	24	22	19	He shall be buried with the burial of an ass, drawn and cast forth beyond the gates of Jerusalem.
verse	24	22	20	Go up to Lebanon, and cry; and lift up thy voice in Bashan, and cry from the passages: for all thy lovers are destroyed.
verse	24	22	21	@@I spake unto thee in thy prosperity; @9but@7 thou saidst, I will not hear. This @9hath been@7 thy manner from thy youth, that thou obeyedst not my voice.
verse	24	22	22	The wind shall eat up all thy pastors, and thy lovers shall go into captivity: surely then shalt thou be ashamed and confounded for all thy wickedness.
verse	24	22	23	O inhabitant of Lebanon, that makest thy nest in the cedars, how gracious shalt thou be when pangs come upon thee, the pain as of a woman in travail!
verse	24	22	24	@@@9As@7 I live, saith the LORD, though Coniah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah were the signet upon my right hand, yet would I pluck thee thence;
verse	24	22	25	@@And I will give thee into the hand of them that seek thy life, and into the hand @9of them@7 whose face thou fearest, even into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of the Chaldeans.
verse	24	22	26	And I will cast thee out, and thy mother that bare thee, into another country, where ye were not born; and there shall ye die.
verse	24	22	27	But to the land whereunto they desire to return, thither shall they not return.
verse	24	22	28	@@@9Is@7 this man Coniah a despised broken idol? @9is he@7 a vessel wherein @9is@7 no pleasure? wherefore are they cast out, he and his seed, and are cast into a land which they know not?
verse	24	22	29	O earth, earth, earth, hear the word of the LORD.
verse	24	22	30	@@Thus saith the LORD, Write ye this man childless, a man @9that@7 shall not prosper in his days: for no man of his seed shall prosper, sitting upon the throne of David, and ruling any more in Judah.
verse	24	23	1	Woe be unto the pastors that destroy and scatter the sheep of my pasture! saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	2	Therefore thus saith the LORD God of Israel against the pastors that feed my people; Ye have scattered my flock, and driven them away, and have not visited them: behold, I will visit upon you the evil of your doings, saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	3	And I will gather the remnant of my flock out of all countries whither I have driven them, and will bring them again to their folds; and they shall be fruitful and increase.
verse	24	23	4	And I will set up shepherds over them which shall feed them: and they shall fear no more, nor be dismayed, neither shall they be lacking, saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	5	Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the earth.
verse	24	23	6	@@In his days Judah shall be saved, and Israel shall dwell safely: and this @9is@7 his name whereby he shall be called, THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS.
verse	24	23	7	Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that they shall no more say, The LORD liveth, which brought up the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt;
verse	24	23	8	But, The LORD liveth, which brought up and which led the seed of the house of Israel out of the north country, and from all countries whither I had driven them; and they shall dwell in their own land.
verse	24	23	9	Mine heart within me is broken because of the prophets; all my bones shake; I am like a drunken man, and like a man whom wine hath overcome, because of the LORD, and because of the words of his holiness.
verse	24	23	10	@@For the land is full of adulterers; for because of swearing the land mourneth; the pleasant places of the wilderness are dried up, and their course is evil, and their force @9is@7 not right.
verse	24	23	11	For both prophet and priest are profane; yea, in my house have I found their wickedness, saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	12	@@Wherefore their way shall be unto them as slippery @9ways@7 in the darkness: they shall be driven on, and fall therein: for I will bring evil upon them, @9even@7 the year of their visitation, saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	13	And I have seen folly in the prophets of Samaria; they prophesied in Baal, and caused my people Israel to err.
verse	24	23	14	I have seen also in the prophets of Jerusalem an horrible thing: they commit adultery, and walk in lies: they strengthen also the hands of evildoers, that none doth return from his wickedness: they are all of them unto me as Sodom, and the inhabitants thereof as Gomorrah.
verse	24	23	15	Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts concerning the prophets; Behold, I will feed them with wormwood, and make them drink the water of gall: for from the prophets of Jerusalem is profaneness gone forth into all the land.
verse	24	23	16	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts, Hearken not unto the words of the prophets that prophesy unto you: they make you vain: they speak a vision of their own heart, @9and@7 not out of the mouth of the LORD.
verse	24	23	17	They say still unto them that despise me, The LORD hath said, Ye shall have peace; and they say unto every one that walketh after the imagination of his own heart, No evil shall come upon you.
verse	24	23	18	@@For who hath stood in the counsel of the LORD, and hath perceived and heard his word? who hath marked his word, and heard @9it? @7
verse	24	23	19	Behold, a whirlwind of the LORD is gone forth in fury, even a grievous whirlwind: it shall fall grievously upon the head of the wicked.
verse	24	23	20	The anger of the LORD shall not return, until he have executed, and till he have performed the thoughts of his heart: in the latter days ye shall consider it perfectly.
verse	24	23	21	I have not sent these prophets, yet they ran: I have not spoken to them, yet they prophesied.
verse	24	23	22	But if they had stood in my counsel, and had caused my people to hear my words, then they should have turned them from their evil way, and from the evil of their doings.
verse	24	23	23	@@@9Am@7 I a God at hand, saith the LORD, and not a God afar off?
verse	24	23	24	Can any hide himself in secret places that I shall not see him? saith the LORD. Do not I fill heaven and earth? saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	25	I have heard what the prophets said, that prophesy lies in my name, saying, I have dreamed, I have dreamed.
verse	24	23	26	@@How long shall @9this@7 be in the heart of the prophets that prophesy lies? yea, @9they are@7 prophets of the deceit of their own heart;
verse	24	23	27	Which think to cause my people to forget my name by their dreams which they tell every man to his neighbour, as their fathers have forgotten my name for Baal.
verse	24	23	28	@@The prophet that hath a dream, let him tell a dream; and he that hath my word, let him speak my word faithfully. What @9is@7 the chaff to the wheat? saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	29	@@@9Is@7 not my word like as a fire? saith the LORD; and like a hammer @9that@7 breaketh the rock in pieces?
verse	24	23	30	@@Therefore, behold, I @9am@7 against the prophets, saith the LORD, that steal my words every one from his neighbour.
verse	24	23	31	@@Behold, I @9am@7 against the prophets, saith the LORD, that use their tongues, and say, He saith.
verse	24	23	32	@@Behold, I @9am@7 against them that prophesy false dreams, saith the LORD, and do tell them, and cause my people to err by their lies, and by their lightness; yet I sent them not, nor commanded them: therefore they shall not profit this people at all, saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	33	@@And when this people, or the prophet, or a priest, shall ask thee, saying, What @9is@7 the burden of the LORD? thou shalt then say unto them, What burden? I will even forsake you, saith the LORD.
verse	24	23	34	@@And @9as for@7 the prophet, and the priest, and the people, that shall say, The burden of the LORD, I will even punish that man and his house.
verse	24	23	35	Thus shall ye say every one to his neighbour, and every one to his brother, What hath the LORD answered? and, What hath the LORD spoken?
verse	24	23	36	And the burden of the LORD shall ye mention no more: for every man's word shall be his burden; for ye have perverted the words of the living God, of the LORD of hosts our God.
verse	24	23	37	Thus shalt thou say to the prophet, What hath the LORD answered thee? and, What hath the LORD spoken?
verse	24	23	38	But since ye say, The burden of the LORD; therefore thus saith the LORD; Because ye say this word, The burden of the LORD, and I have sent unto you, saying, Ye shall not say, The burden of the LORD;
verse	24	23	39	@@Therefore, behold, I, even I, will utterly forget you, and I will forsake you, and the city that I gave you and your fathers, @9and cast you@7 out of my presence:
verse	24	23	40	And I will bring an everlasting reproach upon you, and a perpetual shame, which shall not be forgotten.
verse	24	24	1	@@The LORD shewed me, and, behold, two baskets of figs @9were@7 set before the temple of the LORD, after that Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon had carried away captive Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah, and the princes of Judah, with the carpenters and smiths, from Jerusalem, and had brought them to Babylon.
verse	24	24	2	@@One basket @9had@7 very good figs, @9even@7 like the figs @9that are@7 first ripe: and the other basket @9had@7 very naughty figs, which could not be eaten, they were so bad.
verse	24	24	3	Then said the LORD unto me, What seest thou, Jeremiah? And I said, Figs; the good figs, very good; and the evil, very evil, that cannot be eaten, they are so evil.
verse	24	24	4	Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	24	24	5	@@Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel; Like these good figs, so will I acknowledge them that are carried away captive of Judah, whom I have sent out of this place into the land of the Chaldeans for @9their@7 good.
verse	24	24	6	@@For I will set mine eyes upon them for good, and I will bring them again to this land: and I will build them, and not pull @9them@7 down; and I will plant them, and not pluck @9them@7 up.
verse	24	24	7	@@And I will give them an heart to know me, that I @9am@7 the LORD: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God: for they shall return unto me with their whole heart.
verse	24	24	8	And as the evil figs, which cannot be eaten, they are so evil; surely thus saith the LORD, So will I give Zedekiah the king of Judah, and his princes, and the residue of Jerusalem, that remain in this land, and them that dwell in the land of Egypt:
verse	24	24	9	@@And I will deliver them to be removed into all the kingdoms of the earth for @9their@7 hurt, @9to be@7 a reproach and a proverb, a taunt and a curse, in all places whither I shall drive them.
verse	24	24	10	And I will send the sword, the famine, and the pestilence, among them, till they be consumed from off the land that I gave unto them and to their fathers.
verse	24	25	1	@@The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the people of Judah in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, that @9was@7 the first year of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon;
verse	24	25	2	The which Jeremiah the prophet spake unto all the people of Judah, and to all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, saying,
verse	24	25	3	@@From the thirteenth year of Josiah the son of Amon king of Judah, even unto this day, that @9is@7 the three and twentieth year, the word of the LORD hath come unto me, and I have spoken unto you, rising early and speaking; but ye have not hearkened.
verse	24	25	4	@@And the LORD hath sent unto you all his servants the prophets, rising early and sending @9them;@7 but ye have not hearkened, nor inclined your ear to hear.
verse	24	25	5	They said, Turn ye again now every one from his evil way, and from the evil of your doings, and dwell in the land that the LORD hath given unto you and to your fathers for ever and ever:
verse	24	25	6	And go not after other gods to serve them, and to worship them, and provoke me not to anger with the works of your hands; and I will do you no hurt.
verse	24	25	7	Yet ye have not hearkened unto me, saith the LORD; that ye might provoke me to anger with the works of your hands to your own hurt.
verse	24	25	8	Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts; Because ye have not heard my words,
verse	24	25	9	Behold, I will send and take all the families of the north, saith the LORD, and Nebuchadrezzar the king of Babylon, my servant, and will bring them against this land, and against the inhabitants thereof, and against all these nations round about, and will utterly destroy them, and make them an astonishment, and an hissing, and perpetual desolations.
verse	24	25	10	Moreover I will take from them the voice of mirth, and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom, and the voice of the bride, the sound of the millstones, and the light of the candle.
verse	24	25	11	@@And this whole land shall be a desolation, @9and@7 an astonishment; and these nations shall serve the king of Babylon seventy years.
verse	24	25	12	@@And it shall come to pass, when seventy years are accomplished, @9that@7 I will punish the king of Babylon, and that nation, saith the LORD, for their iniquity, and the land of the Chaldeans, and will make it perpetual desolations.
verse	24	25	13	@@And I will bring upon that land all my words which I have pronounced against it, @9even@7 all that is written in this book, which Jeremiah hath prophesied against all the nations.
verse	24	25	14	For many nations and great kings shall serve themselves of them also: and I will recompense them according to their deeds, and according to the works of their own hands.
verse	24	25	15	For thus saith the LORD God of Israel unto me; Take the wine cup of this fury at my hand, and cause all the nations, to whom I send thee, to drink it.
verse	24	25	16	And they shall drink, and be moved, and be mad, because of the sword that I will send among them.
verse	24	25	17	Then took I the cup at the LORD'S hand, and made all the nations to drink, unto whom the LORD had sent me:
verse	24	25	18	@@@9To wit,@7 Jerusalem, and the cities of Judah, and the kings thereof, and the princes thereof, to make them a desolation, an astonishment, an hissing, and a curse; as @9it is@7 this day;
verse	24	25	19	Pharaoh king of Egypt, and his servants, and his princes, and all his people;
verse	24	25	20	And all the mingled people, and all the kings of the land of Uz, and all the kings of the land of the Philistines, and Ashkelon, and Azzah, and Ekron, and the remnant of Ashdod,
verse	24	25	21	Edom, and Moab, and the children of Ammon,
verse	24	25	22	And all the kings of Tyrus, and all the kings of Zidon, and the kings of the isles which are beyond the sea,
verse	24	25	23	@@Dedan, and Tema, and Buz, and all @9that are@7 in the utmost corners,
verse	24	25	24	And all the kings of Arabia, and all the kings of the mingled people that dwell in the desert,
verse	24	25	25	And all the kings of Zimri, and all the kings of Elam, and all the kings of the Medes,
verse	24	25	26	@@And all the kings of the north, far and near, one with another, and all the kingdoms of the world, which @9are@7 upon the face of the earth: and the king of Sheshach shall drink after them.
verse	24	25	27	Therefore thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Drink ye, and be drunken, and spue, and fall, and rise no more, because of the sword which I will send among you.
verse	24	25	28	And it shall be, if they refuse to take the cup at thine hand to drink, then shalt thou say unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Ye shall certainly drink.
verse	24	25	29	For, lo, I begin to bring evil on the city which is called by my name, and should ye be utterly unpunished? Ye shall not be unpunished: for I will call for a sword upon all the inhabitants of the earth, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	24	25	30	@@Therefore prophesy thou against them all these words, and say unto them, The LORD shall roar from on high, and utter his voice from his holy habitation; he shall mightily roar upon his habitation; he shall give a shout, as they that tread @9the grapes,@7 against all the inhabitants of the earth.
verse	24	25	31	@@A noise shall come @9even@7 to the ends of the earth; for the LORD hath a controversy with the nations, he will plead with all flesh; he will give them @9that are@7 wicked to the sword, saith the LORD.
verse	24	25	32	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, Behold, evil shall go forth from nation to nation, and a great whirlwind shall be raised up from the coasts of the earth.
verse	24	25	33	@@And the slain of the LORD shall be at that day from @9one@7 end of the earth even unto the @9other@7 end of the earth: they shall not be lamented, neither gathered, nor buried; they shall be dung upon the ground.
verse	24	25	34	@@Howl, ye shepherds, and cry; and wallow yourselves @9in the ashes,@7 ye principal of the flock: for the days of your slaughter and of your dispersions are accomplished; and ye shall fall like a pleasant vessel.
verse	24	25	35	And the shepherds shall have no way to flee, nor the principal of the flock to escape.
verse	24	25	36	@@A voice of the cry of the shepherds, and an howling of the principal of the flock, @9shall be heard:@7 for the LORD hath spoiled their pasture.
verse	24	25	37	And the peaceable habitations are cut down because of the fierce anger of the LORD.
verse	24	25	38	He hath forsaken his covert, as the lion: for their land is desolate because of the fierceness of the oppressor, and because of his fierce anger.
verse	24	26	1	In the beginning of the reign of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah came this word from the LORD, saying,
verse	24	26	2	Thus saith the LORD; Stand in the court of the LORD'S house, and speak unto all the cities of Judah, which come to worship in the LORD'S house, all the words that I command thee to speak unto them; diminish not a word:
verse	24	26	3	If so be they will hearken, and turn every man from his evil way, that I may repent me of the evil, which I purpose to do unto them because of the evil of their doings.
verse	24	26	4	And thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the LORD; If ye will not hearken to me, to walk in my law, which I have set before you,
verse	24	26	5	@@To hearken to the words of my servants the prophets, whom I sent unto you, both rising up early, and sending @9them,@7 but ye have not hearkened;
verse	24	26	6	Then will I make this house like Shiloh, and will make this city a curse to all the nations of the earth.
verse	24	26	7	So the priests and the prophets and all the people heard Jeremiah speaking these words in the house of the LORD.
verse	24	26	8	@@Now it came to pass, when Jeremiah had made an end of speaking all that the LORD had commanded @9him@7 to speak unto all the people, that the priests and the prophets and all the people took him, saying, Thou shalt surely die.
verse	24	26	9	Why hast thou prophesied in the name of the LORD, saying, This house shall be like Shiloh, and this city shall be desolate without an inhabitant? And all the people were gathered against Jeremiah in the house of the LORD.
verse	24	26	10	@@When the princes of Judah heard these things, then they came up from the king's house unto the house of the LORD, and sat down in the entry of the new gate of the LORD'S @9house. @7
verse	24	26	11	@@Then spake the priests and the prophets unto the princes and to all the people, saying, This man @9is@7 worthy to die; for he hath prophesied against this city, as ye have heard with your ears.
verse	24	26	12	Then spake Jeremiah unto all the princes and to all the people, saying, The LORD sent me to prophesy against this house and against this city all the words that ye have heard.
verse	24	26	13	Therefore now amend your ways and your doings, and obey the voice of the LORD your God; and the LORD will repent him of the evil that he hath pronounced against you.
verse	24	26	14	@@As for me, behold, I @9am@7 in your hand: do with me as seemeth good and meet unto you.
verse	24	26	15	But know ye for certain, that if ye put me to death, ye shall surely bring innocent blood upon yourselves, and upon this city, and upon the inhabitants thereof: for of a truth the LORD hath sent me unto you to speak all these words in your ears.
verse	24	26	16	@@Then said the princes and all the people unto the priests and to the prophets; This man @9is@7 not worthy to die: for he hath spoken to us in the name of the LORD our God.
verse	24	26	17	Then rose up certain of the elders of the land, and spake to all the assembly of the people, saying,
verse	24	26	18	@@Micah the Morasthite prophesied in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah, and spake to all the people of Judah, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Zion shall be plowed @9like@7 a field, and Jerusalem shall become heaps, and the mountain of the house as the high places of a forest.
verse	24	26	19	Did Hezekiah king of Judah and all Judah put him at all to death? did he not fear the LORD, and besought the LORD, and the LORD repented him of the evil which he had pronounced against them? Thus might we procure great evil against our souls.
verse	24	26	20	And there was also a man that prophesied in the name of the LORD, Urijah the son of Shemaiah of Kirjathjearim, who prophesied against this city and against this land according to all the words of Jeremiah:
verse	24	26	21	And when Jehoiakim the king, with all his mighty men, and all the princes, heard his words, the king sought to put him to death: but when Urijah heard it, he was afraid, and fled, and went into Egypt;
verse	24	26	22	@@And Jehoiakim the king sent men into Egypt, @9namely,@7 Elnathan the son of Achbor, and @9certain@7 men with him into Egypt.
verse	24	26	23	And they fetched forth Urijah out of Egypt, and brought him unto Jehoiakim the king; who slew him with the sword, and cast his dead body into the graves of the common people.
verse	24	26	24	Nevertheless the hand of Ahikam the son of Shaphan was with Jeremiah, that they should not give him into the hand of the people to put him to death.
verse	24	27	1	In the beginning of the reign of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah came this word unto Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,
verse	24	27	2	Thus saith the LORD to me; Make thee bonds and yokes, and put them upon thy neck,
verse	24	27	3	And send them to the king of Edom, and to the king of Moab, and to the king of the Ammonites, and to the king of Tyrus, and to the king of Zidon, by the hand of the messengers which come to Jerusalem unto Zedekiah king of Judah;
verse	24	27	4	And command them to say unto their masters, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Thus shall ye say unto your masters;
verse	24	27	5	@@I have made the earth, the man and the beast that @9are@7 upon the ground, by my great power and by my outstretched arm, and have given it unto whom it seemed meet unto me.
verse	24	27	6	And now have I given all these lands into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, my servant; and the beasts of the field have I given him also to serve him.
verse	24	27	7	And all nations shall serve him, and his son, and his son's son, until the very time of his land come: and then many nations and great kings shall serve themselves of him.
verse	24	27	8	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 the nation and kingdom which will not serve the same Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, and that will not put their neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon, that nation will I punish, saith the LORD, with the sword, and with the famine, and with the pestilence, until I have consumed them by his hand.
verse	24	27	9	Therefore hearken not ye to your prophets, nor to your diviners, nor to your dreamers, nor to your enchanters, nor to your sorcerers, which speak unto you, saying, Ye shall not serve the king of Babylon:
verse	24	27	10	For they prophesy a lie unto you, to remove you far from your land; and that I should drive you out, and ye should perish.
verse	24	27	11	But the nations that bring their neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon, and serve him, those will I let remain still in their own land, saith the LORD; and they shall till it, and dwell therein.
verse	24	27	12	I spake also to Zedekiah king of Judah according to all these words, saying, Bring your necks under the yoke of the king of Babylon, and serve him and his people, and live.
verse	24	27	13	Why will ye die, thou and thy people, by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence, as the LORD hath spoken against the nation that will not serve the king of Babylon?
verse	24	27	14	Therefore hearken not unto the words of the prophets that speak unto you, saying, Ye shall not serve the king of Babylon: for they prophesy a lie unto you.
verse	24	27	15	For I have not sent them, saith the LORD, yet they prophesy a lie in my name; that I might drive you out, and that ye might perish, ye, and the prophets that prophesy unto you.
verse	24	27	16	Also I spake to the priests and to all this people, saying, Thus saith the LORD; Hearken not to the words of your prophets that prophesy unto you, saying, Behold, the vessels of the LORD'S house shall now shortly be brought again from Babylon: for they prophesy a lie unto you.
verse	24	27	17	Hearken not unto them; serve the king of Babylon, and live: wherefore should this city be laid waste?
verse	24	27	18	@@But if they @9be@7 prophets, and if the word of the LORD be with them, let them now make intercession to the LORD of hosts, that the vessels which are left in the house of the LORD, and @9in@7 the house of the king of Judah, and at Jerusalem, go not to Babylon.
verse	24	27	19	For thus saith the LORD of hosts concerning the pillars, and concerning the sea, and concerning the bases, and concerning the residue of the vessels that remain in this city,
verse	24	27	20	Which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon took not, when he carried away captive Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah from Jerusalem to Babylon, and all the nobles of Judah and Jerusalem;
verse	24	27	21	@@Yea, thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, concerning the vessels that remain @9in@7 the house of the LORD, and @9in@7 the house of the king of Judah and of Jerusalem;
verse	24	27	22	They shall be carried to Babylon, and there shall they be until the day that I visit them, saith the LORD; then will I bring them up, and restore them to this place.
verse	24	28	1	@@And it came to pass the same year, in the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the fourth year, @9and@7 in the fifth month, @9that@7 Hananiah the son of Azur the prophet, which @9was@7 of Gibeon, spake unto me in the house of the LORD, in the presence of the priests and of all the people, saying,
verse	24	28	2	Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, saying, I have broken the yoke of the king of Babylon.
verse	24	28	3	Within two full years will I bring again into this place all the vessels of the LORD'S house, that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon took away from this place, and carried them to Babylon:
verse	24	28	4	And I will bring again to this place Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah, with all the captives of Judah, that went into Babylon, saith the LORD: for I will break the yoke of the king of Babylon.
verse	24	28	5	Then the prophet Jeremiah said unto the prophet Hananiah in the presence of the priests, and in the presence of all the people that stood in the house of the LORD,
verse	24	28	6	Even the prophet Jeremiah said, Amen: the LORD do so: the LORD perform thy words which thou hast prophesied, to bring again the vessels of the LORD'S house, and all that is carried away captive, from Babylon into this place.
verse	24	28	7	Nevertheless hear thou now this word that I speak in thine ears, and in the ears of all the people;
verse	24	28	8	The prophets that have been before me and before thee of old prophesied both against many countries, and against great kingdoms, of war, and of evil, and of pestilence.
verse	24	28	9	@@The prophet which prophesieth of peace, when the word of the prophet shall come to pass, @9then@7 shall the prophet be known, that the LORD hath truly sent him.
verse	24	28	10	Then Hananiah the prophet took the yoke from off the prophet Jeremiah's neck, and brake it.
verse	24	28	11	And Hananiah spake in the presence of all the people, saying, Thus saith the LORD; Even so will I break the yoke of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon from the neck of all nations within the space of two full years. And the prophet Jeremiah went his way.
verse	24	28	12	@@Then the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah @9the prophet,@7 after that Hananiah the prophet had broken the yoke from off the neck of the prophet Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	28	13	Go and tell Hananiah, saying, Thus saith the LORD; Thou hast broken the yokes of wood; but thou shalt make for them yokes of iron.
verse	24	28	14	For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; I have put a yoke of iron upon the neck of all these nations, that they may serve Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon; and they shall serve him: and I have given him the beasts of the field also.
verse	24	28	15	Then said the prophet Jeremiah unto Hananiah the prophet, Hear now, Hananiah; The LORD hath not sent thee; but thou makest this people to trust in a lie.
verse	24	28	16	Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will cast thee from off the face of the earth: this year thou shalt die, because thou hast taught rebellion against the LORD.
verse	24	28	17	So Hananiah the prophet died the same year in the seventh month.
verse	24	29	1	@@Now these @9are@7 the words of the letter that Jeremiah the prophet sent from Jerusalem unto the residue of the elders which were carried away captives, and to the priests, and to the prophets, and to all the people whom Nebuchadnezzar had carried away captive from Jerusalem to Babylon;
verse	24	29	2	(After that Jeconiah the king, and the queen, and the eunuchs, the princes of Judah and Jerusalem, and the carpenters, and the smiths, were departed from Jerusalem;)
verse	24	29	3	By the hand of Elasah the son of Shaphan, and Gemariah the son of Hilkiah, (whom Zedekiah king of Judah sent unto Babylon to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon) saying,
verse	24	29	4	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, unto all that are carried away captives, whom I have caused to be carried away from Jerusalem unto Babylon;
verse	24	29	5	@@Build ye houses, and dwell @9in them;@7 and plant gardens, and eat the fruit of them;
verse	24	29	6	Take ye wives, and beget sons and daughters; and take wives for your sons, and give your daughters to husbands, that they may bear sons and daughters; that ye may be increased there, and not diminished.
verse	24	29	7	And seek the peace of the city whither I have caused you to be carried away captives, and pray unto the LORD for it: for in the peace thereof shall ye have peace.
verse	24	29	8	@@For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Let not your prophets and your diviners, that @9be@7 in the midst of you, deceive you, neither hearken to your dreams which ye cause to be dreamed.
verse	24	29	9	For they prophesy falsely unto you in my name: I have not sent them, saith the LORD.
verse	24	29	10	For thus saith the LORD, That after seventy years be accomplished at Babylon I will visit you, and perform my good word toward you, in causing you to return to this place.
verse	24	29	11	For I know the thoughts that I think toward you, saith the LORD, thoughts of peace, and not of evil, to give you an expected end.
verse	24	29	12	Then shall ye call upon me, and ye shall go and pray unto me, and I will hearken unto you.
verse	24	29	13	@@And ye shall seek me, and find @9me,@7 when ye shall search for me with all your heart.
verse	24	29	14	And I will be found of you, saith the LORD: and I will turn away your captivity, and I will gather you from all the nations, and from all the places whither I have driven you, saith the LORD; and I will bring you again into the place whence I caused you to be carried away captive.
verse	24	29	15	Because ye have said, The LORD hath raised us up prophets in Babylon;
verse	24	29	16	@@@9Know@7 that thus saith the LORD of the king that sitteth upon the throne of David, and of all the people that dwelleth in this city, @9and@7 of your brethren that are not gone forth with you into captivity;
verse	24	29	17	Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Behold, I will send upon them the sword, the famine, and the pestilence, and will make them like vile figs, that cannot be eaten, they are so evil.
verse	24	29	18	And I will persecute them with the sword, with the famine, and with the pestilence, and will deliver them to be removed to all the kingdoms of the earth, to be a curse, and an astonishment, and an hissing, and a reproach, among all the nations whither I have driven them:
verse	24	29	19	@@Because they have not hearkened to my words, saith the LORD, which I sent unto them by my servants the prophets, rising up early and sending @9them;@7 but ye would not hear, saith the LORD.
verse	24	29	20	Hear ye therefore the word of the LORD, all ye of the captivity, whom I have sent from Jerusalem to Babylon:
verse	24	29	21	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, of Ahab the son of Kolaiah, and of Zedekiah the son of Maaseiah, which prophesy a lie unto you in my name; Behold, I will deliver them into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon; and he shall slay them before your eyes;
verse	24	29	22	@@And of them shall be taken up a curse by all the captivity of Judah which @9are@7 in Babylon, saying, The LORD make thee like Zedekiah and like Ahab, whom the king of Babylon roasted in the fire;
verse	24	29	23	@@Because they have committed villany in Israel, and have committed adultery with their neighbours' wives, and have spoken lying words in my name, which I have not commanded them; even I know, and @9am@7 a witness, saith the LORD.
verse	24	29	24	@@@9Thus@7 shalt thou also speak to Shemaiah the Nehelamite, saying,
verse	24	29	25	@@Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, saying, Because thou hast sent letters in thy name unto all the people that @9are@7 at Jerusalem, and to Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah the priest, and to all the priests, saying,
verse	24	29	26	@@The LORD hath made thee priest in the stead of Jehoiada the priest, that ye should be officers in the house of the LORD, for every man @9that is@7 mad, and maketh himself a prophet, that thou shouldest put him in prison, and in the stocks.
verse	24	29	27	Now therefore why hast thou not reproved Jeremiah of Anathoth, which maketh himself a prophet to you?
verse	24	29	28	@@For therefore he sent unto us @9in@7 Babylon, saying, This @9captivity is@7 long: build ye houses, and dwell @9in them;@7 and plant gardens, and eat the fruit of them.
verse	24	29	29	And Zephaniah the priest read this letter in the ears of Jeremiah the prophet.
verse	24	29	30	Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	29	31	Send to all them of the captivity, saying, Thus saith the LORD concerning Shemaiah the Nehelamite; Because that Shemaiah hath prophesied unto you, and I sent him not, and he caused you to trust in a lie:
verse	24	29	32	Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will punish Shemaiah the Nehelamite, and his seed: he shall not have a man to dwell among this people; neither shall he behold the good that I will do for my people, saith the LORD; because he hath taught rebellion against the LORD.
verse	24	30	1	The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,
verse	24	30	2	Thus speaketh the LORD God of Israel, saying, Write thee all the words that I have spoken unto thee in a book.
verse	24	30	3	For, lo, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will bring again the captivity of my people Israel and Judah, saith the LORD: and I will cause them to return to the land that I gave to their fathers, and they shall possess it.
verse	24	30	4	@@And these @9are@7 the words that the LORD spake concerning Israel and concerning Judah.
verse	24	30	5	For thus saith the LORD; We have heard a voice of trembling, of fear, and not of peace.
verse	24	30	6	Ask ye now, and see whether a man doth travail with child? wherefore do I see every man with his hands on his loins, as a woman in travail, and all faces are turned into paleness?
verse	24	30	7	@@Alas! for that day @9is@7 great, so that none @9is@7 like it: it @9is@7 even the time of Jacob's trouble; but he shall be saved out of it.
verse	24	30	8	@@For it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD of hosts, @9that@7 I will break his yoke from off thy neck, and will burst thy bonds, and strangers shall no more serve themselves of him:
verse	24	30	9	But they shall serve the LORD their God, and David their king, whom I will raise up unto them.
verse	24	30	10	@@Therefore fear thou not, O my servant Jacob, saith the LORD; neither be dismayed, O Israel: for, lo, I will save thee from afar, and thy seed from the land of their captivity; and Jacob shall return, and shall be in rest, and be quiet, and none shall make @9him@7 afraid.
verse	24	30	11	@@For I @9am@7 with thee, saith the LORD, to save thee: though I make a full end of all nations whither I have scattered thee, yet will I not make a full end of thee: but I will correct thee in measure, and will not leave thee altogether unpunished.
verse	24	30	12	@@For thus saith the LORD, Thy bruise @9is@7 incurable, @9and@7 thy wound @9is@7 grievous.
verse	24	30	13	@@@9There is@7 none to plead thy cause, that thou mayest be bound up: thou hast no healing medicines.
verse	24	30	14	@@All thy lovers have forgotten thee; they seek thee not; for I have wounded thee with the wound of an enemy, with the chastisement of a cruel one, for the multitude of thine iniquity; @9because@7 thy sins were increased.
verse	24	30	15	@@Why criest thou for thine affliction? thy sorrow @9is@7 incurable for the multitude of thine iniquity: @9because@7 thy sins were increased, I have done these things unto thee.
verse	24	30	16	Therefore all they that devour thee shall be devoured; and all thine adversaries, every one of them, shall go into captivity; and they that spoil thee shall be a spoil, and all that prey upon thee will I give for a prey.
verse	24	30	17	@@For I will restore health unto thee, and I will heal thee of thy wounds, saith the LORD; because they called thee an Outcast, @9saying,@7 This @9is@7 Zion, whom no man seeketh after.
verse	24	30	18	Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will bring again the captivity of Jacob's tents, and have mercy on his dwellingplaces; and the city shall be builded upon her own heap, and the palace shall remain after the manner thereof.
verse	24	30	19	And out of them shall proceed thanksgiving and the voice of them that make merry: and I will multiply them, and they shall not be few; I will also glorify them, and they shall not be small.
verse	24	30	20	Their children also shall be as aforetime, and their congregation shall be established before me, and I will punish all that oppress them.
verse	24	30	21	@@And their nobles shall be of themselves, and their governor shall proceed from the midst of them; and I will cause him to draw near, and he shall approach unto me: for who @9is@7 this that engaged his heart to approach unto me? saith the LORD.
verse	24	30	22	And ye shall be my people, and I will be your God.
verse	24	30	23	Behold, the whirlwind of the LORD goeth forth with fury, a continuing whirlwind: it shall fall with pain upon the head of the wicked.
verse	24	30	24	@@The fierce anger of the LORD shall not return, until he have done @9it,@7 and until he have performed the intents of his heart: in the latter days ye shall consider it.
verse	24	31	1	At the same time, saith the LORD, will I be the God of all the families of Israel, and they shall be my people.
verse	24	31	2	@@Thus saith the LORD, The people @9which were@7 left of the sword found grace in the wilderness; @9even@7 Israel, when I went to cause him to rest.
verse	24	31	3	@@The LORD hath appeared of old unto me, @9saying,@7 Yea, I have loved thee with an everlasting love: therefore with lovingkindness have I drawn thee.
verse	24	31	4	Again I will build thee, and thou shalt be built, O virgin of Israel: thou shalt again be adorned with thy tabrets, and shalt go forth in the dances of them that make merry.
verse	24	31	5	@@Thou shalt yet plant vines upon the mountains of Samaria: the planters shall plant, and shall eat @9them@7 as common things.
verse	24	31	6	@@For there shall be a day, @9that@7 the watchmen upon the mount Ephraim shall cry, Arise ye, and let us go up to Zion unto the LORD our God.
verse	24	31	7	For thus saith the LORD; Sing with gladness for Jacob, and shout among the chief of the nations: publish ye, praise ye, and say, O LORD, save thy people, the remnant of Israel.
verse	24	31	8	@@Behold, I will bring them from the north country, and gather them from the coasts of the earth, @9and@7 with them the blind and the lame, the woman with child and her that travaileth with child together: a great company shall return thither.
verse	24	31	9	@@They shall come with weeping, and with supplications will I lead them: I will cause them to walk by the rivers of waters in a straight way, wherein they shall not stumble: for I am a father to Israel, and Ephraim @9is@7 my firstborn.
verse	24	31	10	@@Hear the word of the LORD, O ye nations, and declare @9it@7 in the isles afar off, and say, He that scattered Israel will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd @9doth@7 his flock.
verse	24	31	11	@@For the LORD hath redeemed Jacob, and ransomed him from the hand of @9him that was@7 stronger than he.
verse	24	31	12	Therefore they shall come and sing in the height of Zion, and shall flow together to the goodness of the LORD, for wheat, and for wine, and for oil, and for the young of the flock and of the herd: and their soul shall be as a watered garden; and they shall not sorrow any more at all.
verse	24	31	13	Then shall the virgin rejoice in the dance, both young men and old together: for I will turn their mourning into joy, and will comfort them, and make them rejoice from their sorrow.
verse	24	31	14	And I will satiate the soul of the priests with fatness, and my people shall be satisfied with my goodness, saith the LORD.
verse	24	31	15	@@Thus saith the LORD; A voice was heard in Ramah, lamentation, @9and@7 bitter weeping; Rahel weeping for her children refused to be comforted for her children, because they @9were@7 not.
verse	24	31	16	Thus saith the LORD; Refrain thy voice from weeping, and thine eyes from tears: for thy work shall be rewarded, saith the LORD; and they shall come again from the land of the enemy.
verse	24	31	17	And there is hope in thine end, saith the LORD, that thy children shall come again to their own border.
verse	24	31	18	@@I have surely heard Ephraim bemoaning himself @9thus;@7 Thou hast chastised me, and I was chastised, as a bullock unaccustomed @9to the yoke:@7 turn thou me, and I shall be turned; for thou @9art@7 the LORD my God.
verse	24	31	19	@@Surely after that I was turned, I repented; and after that I was instructed, I smote upon @9my@7 thigh: I was ashamed, yea, even confounded, because I did bear the reproach of my youth.
verse	24	31	20	@@@9Is@7 Ephraim my dear son? @9is he@7 a pleasant child? for since I spake against him, I do earnestly remember him still: therefore my bowels are troubled for him; I will surely have mercy upon him, saith the LORD.
verse	24	31	21	@@Set thee up waymarks, make thee high heaps: set thine heart toward the highway, @9even@7 the way @9which@7 thou wentest: turn again, O virgin of Israel, turn again to these thy cities.
verse	24	31	22	How long wilt thou go about, O thou backsliding daughter? for the LORD hath created a new thing in the earth, A woman shall compass a man.
verse	24	31	23	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; As yet they shall use this speech in the land of Judah and in the cities thereof, when I shall bring again their captivity; The LORD bless thee, O habitation of justice, @9and@7 mountain of holiness.
verse	24	31	24	@@And there shall dwell in Judah itself, and in all the cities thereof together, husbandmen, and they @9that@7 go forth with flocks.
verse	24	31	25	For I have satiated the weary soul, and I have replenished every sorrowful soul.
verse	24	31	26	Upon this I awaked, and beheld; and my sleep was sweet unto me.
verse	24	31	27	Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will sow the house of Israel and the house of Judah with the seed of man, and with the seed of beast.
verse	24	31	28	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 like as I have watched over them, to pluck up, and to break down, and to throw down, and to destroy, and to afflict; so will I watch over them, to build, and to plant, saith the LORD.
verse	24	31	29	In those days they shall say no more, The fathers have eaten a sour grape, and the children's teeth are set on edge.
verse	24	31	30	But every one shall die for his own iniquity: every man that eateth the sour grape, his teeth shall be set on edge.
verse	24	31	31	Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel, and with the house of Judah:
verse	24	31	32	@@Not according to the covenant that I made with their fathers in the day @9that@7 I took them by the hand to bring them out of the land of Egypt; which my covenant they brake, although I was an husband unto them, saith the LORD:
verse	24	31	33	@@But this @9shall be@7 the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel; After those days, saith the LORD, I will put my law in their inward parts, and write it in their hearts; and will be their God, and they shall be my people.
verse	24	31	34	And they shall teach no more every man his neighbour, and every man his brother, saying, Know the LORD: for they shall all know me, from the least of them unto the greatest of them, saith the LORD; for I will forgive their iniquity, and I will remember their sin no more.
verse	24	31	35	@@Thus saith the LORD, which giveth the sun for a light by day, @9and@7 the ordinances of the moon and of the stars for a light by night, which divideth the sea when the waves thereof roar; The LORD of hosts @9is@7 his name:
verse	24	31	36	@@If those ordinances depart from before me, saith the LORD, @9then@7 the seed of Israel also shall cease from being a nation before me for ever.
verse	24	31	37	Thus saith the LORD; If heaven above can be measured, and the foundations of the earth searched out beneath, I will also cast off all the seed of Israel for all that they have done, saith the LORD.
verse	24	31	38	Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that the city shall be built to the LORD from the tower of Hananeel unto the gate of the corner.
verse	24	31	39	And the measuring line shall yet go forth over against it upon the hill Gareb, and shall compass about to Goath.
verse	24	31	40	@@And the whole valley of the dead bodies, and of the ashes, and all the fields unto the brook of Kidron, unto the corner of the horse gate toward the east, @9shall be@7 holy unto the LORD; it shall not be plucked up, nor thrown down any more for ever.
verse	24	32	1	@@The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD in the tenth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, which @9was@7 the eighteenth year of Nebuchadrezzar.
verse	24	32	2	@@For then the king of Babylon's army besieged Jerusalem: and Jeremiah the prophet was shut up in the court of the prison, which @9was@7 in the king of Judah's house.
verse	24	32	3	For Zedekiah king of Judah had shut him up, saying, Wherefore dost thou prophesy, and say, Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall take it;
verse	24	32	4	And Zedekiah king of Judah shall not escape out of the hand of the Chaldeans, but shall surely be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon, and shall speak with him mouth to mouth, and his eyes shall behold his eyes;
verse	24	32	5	And he shall lead Zedekiah to Babylon, and there shall he be until I visit him, saith the LORD: though ye fight with the Chaldeans, ye shall not prosper?
verse	24	32	6	And Jeremiah said, The word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	24	32	7	@@Behold, Hanameel the son of Shallum thine uncle shall come unto thee, saying, Buy thee my field that @9is@7 in Anathoth: for the right of redemption @9is@7 thine to buy @9it. @7
verse	24	32	8	@@So Hanameel mine uncle's son came to me in the court of the prison according to the word of the LORD, and said unto me, Buy my field, I pray thee, that @9is@7 in Anathoth, which @9is@7 in the country of Benjamin: for the right of inheritance @9is@7 thine, and the redemption @9is@7 thine; buy @9it@7 for thyself. Then I knew that this @9was@7 the word of the LORD.
verse	24	32	9	@@And I bought the field of Hanameel my uncle's son, that @9was@7 in Anathoth, and weighed him the money, @9even@7 seventeen shekels of silver.
verse	24	32	10	@@And I subscribed the evidence, and sealed @9it,@7 and took witnesses, and weighed @9him@7 the money in the balances.
verse	24	32	11	@@So I took the evidence of the purchase, @9both@7 that which was sealed @9according@7 to the law and custom, and that which was open:
verse	24	32	12	@@And I gave the evidence of the purchase unto Baruch the son of Neriah, the son of Maaseiah, in the sight of Hanameel mine uncle's @9son,@7 and in the presence of the witnesses that subscribed the book of the purchase, before all the Jews that sat in the court of the prison.
verse	24	32	13	And I charged Baruch before them, saying,
verse	24	32	14	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Take these evidences, this evidence of the purchase, both which is sealed, and this evidence which is open; and put them in an earthen vessel, that they may continue many days.
verse	24	32	15	For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Houses and fields and vineyards shall be possessed again in this land.
verse	24	32	16	Now when I had delivered the evidence of the purchase unto Baruch the son of Neriah, I prayed unto the LORD, saying,
verse	24	32	17	@@Ah Lord GOD! behold, thou hast made the heaven and the earth by thy great power and stretched out arm, @9and@7 there is nothing too hard for thee:
verse	24	32	18	@@Thou shewest lovingkindness unto thousands, and recompensest the iniquity of the fathers into the bosom of their children after them: the Great, the Mighty God, the LORD of hosts, @9is@7 his name,
verse	24	32	19	@@Great in counsel, and mighty in work: for thine eyes @9are@7 open upon all the ways of the sons of men: to give every one according to his ways, and according to the fruit of his doings:
verse	24	32	20	@@Which hast set signs and wonders in the land of Egypt, @9even@7 unto this day, and in Israel, and among @9other@7 men; and hast made thee a name, as at this day;
verse	24	32	21	And hast brought forth thy people Israel out of the land of Egypt with signs, and with wonders, and with a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with great terror;
verse	24	32	22	And hast given them this land, which thou didst swear to their fathers to give them, a land flowing with milk and honey;
verse	24	32	23	And they came in, and possessed it; but they obeyed not thy voice, neither walked in thy law; they have done nothing of all that thou commandedst them to do: therefore thou hast caused all this evil to come upon them:
verse	24	32	24	@@Behold the mounts, they are come unto the city to take it; and the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans, that fight against it, because of the sword, and of the famine, and of the pestilence: and what thou hast spoken is come to pass; and, behold, thou seest @9it. @7
verse	24	32	25	And thou hast said unto me, O Lord GOD, Buy thee the field for money, and take witnesses; for the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.
verse	24	32	26	Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	32	27	@@Behold, I @9am@7 the LORD, the God of all flesh: is there any thing too hard for me?
verse	24	32	28	Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the Chaldeans, and into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and he shall take it:
verse	24	32	29	And the Chaldeans, that fight against this city, shall come and set fire on this city, and burn it with the houses, upon whose roofs they have offered incense unto Baal, and poured out drink offerings unto other gods, to provoke me to anger.
verse	24	32	30	For the children of Israel and the children of Judah have only done evil before me from their youth: for the children of Israel have only provoked me to anger with the work of their hands, saith the LORD.
verse	24	32	31	@@For this city hath been to me @9as@7 a provocation of mine anger and of my fury from the day that they built it even unto this day; that I should remove it from before my face,
verse	24	32	32	Because of all the evil of the children of Israel and of the children of Judah, which they have done to provoke me to anger, they, their kings, their princes, their priests, and their prophets, and the men of Judah, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem.
verse	24	32	33	@@And they have turned unto me the back, and not the face: though I taught them, rising up early and teaching @9them,@7 yet they have not hearkened to receive instruction.
verse	24	32	34	But they set their abominations in the house, which is called by my name, to defile it.
verse	24	32	35	@@And they built the high places of Baal, which @9are@7 in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to cause their sons and their daughters to pass through @9the fire@7 unto Molech; which I commanded them not, neither came it into my mind, that they should do this abomination, to cause Judah to sin.
verse	24	32	36	And now therefore thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, concerning this city, whereof ye say, It shall be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon by the sword, and by the famine, and by the pestilence;
verse	24	32	37	Behold, I will gather them out of all countries, whither I have driven them in mine anger, and in my fury, and in great wrath; and I will bring them again unto this place, and I will cause them to dwell safely:
verse	24	32	38	And they shall be my people, and I will be their God:
verse	24	32	39	And I will give them one heart, and one way, that they may fear me for ever, for the good of them, and of their children after them:
verse	24	32	40	And I will make an everlasting covenant with them, that I will not turn away from them, to do them good; but I will put my fear in their hearts, that they shall not depart from me.
verse	24	32	41	Yea, I will rejoice over them to do them good, and I will plant them in this land assuredly with my whole heart and with my whole soul.
verse	24	32	42	For thus saith the LORD; Like as I have brought all this great evil upon this people, so will I bring upon them all the good that I have promised them.
verse	24	32	43	@@And fields shall be bought in this land, whereof ye say, @9It is@7 desolate without man or beast; it is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.
verse	24	32	44	@@Men shall buy fields for money, and subscribe evidences, and seal @9them,@7 and take witnesses in the land of Benjamin, and in the places about Jerusalem, and in the cities of Judah, and in the cities of the mountains, and in the cities of the valley, and in the cities of the south: for I will cause their captivity to return, saith the LORD.
verse	24	33	1	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah the second time, while he was yet shut up in the court of the prison, saying,
verse	24	33	2	@@Thus saith the LORD the maker thereof, the LORD that formed it, to establish it; the LORD @9is@7 his name;
verse	24	33	3	Call unto me, and I will answer thee, and shew thee great and mighty things, which thou knowest not.
verse	24	33	4	For thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, concerning the houses of this city, and concerning the houses of the kings of Judah, which are thrown down by the mounts, and by the sword;
verse	24	33	5	@@They come to fight with the Chaldeans, but @9it is@7 fill them with the dead bodies of men, whom I have slain in mine anger and in my fury, and for all whose wickedness I have hid my face from this city.
verse	24	33	6	Behold, I will bring it health and cure, and I will cure them, and will reveal unto them the abundance of peace and truth.
verse	24	33	7	And I will cause the captivity of Judah and the captivity of Israel to return, and will build them, as at the first.
verse	24	33	8	And I will cleanse them from all their iniquity, whereby they have sinned against me; and I will pardon all their iniquities, whereby they have sinned, and whereby they have transgressed against me.
verse	24	33	9	And it shall be to me a name of joy, a praise and an honour before all the nations of the earth, which shall hear all the good that I do unto them: and they shall fear and tremble for all the goodness and for all the prosperity that I procure unto it.
verse	24	33	10	@@Thus saith the LORD; Again there shall be heard in this place, which ye say @9shall be@7 desolate without man and without beast, @9even@7 in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, that are desolate, without man, and without inhabitant, and without beast,
verse	24	33	11	@@The voice of joy, and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom, and the voice of the bride, the voice of them that shall say, Praise the LORD of hosts: for the LORD @9is@7 good; for his mercy @9endureth@7 for ever: @9and@7 of them that shall bring the sacrifice of praise into the house of the LORD. For I will cause to return the captivity of the land, as at the first, saith the LORD.
verse	24	33	12	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Again in this place, which is desolate without man and without beast, and in all the cities thereof, shall be an habitation of shepherds causing @9their@7 flocks to lie down.
verse	24	33	13	@@In the cities of the mountains, in the cities of the vale, and in the cities of the south, and in the land of Benjamin, and in the places about Jerusalem, and in the cities of Judah, shall the flocks pass again under the hands of him that telleth @9them,@7 saith the LORD.
verse	24	33	14	Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will perform that good thing which I have promised unto the house of Israel and to the house of Judah.
verse	24	33	15	In those days, and at that time, will I cause the Branch of righteousness to grow up unto David; and he shall execute judgment and righteousness in the land.
verse	24	33	16	@@In those days shall Judah be saved, and Jerusalem shall dwell safely: and this @9is the name@7 wherewith she shall be called, The LORD our righteousness.
verse	24	33	17	For thus saith the LORD; David shall never want a man to sit upon the throne of the house of Israel;
verse	24	33	18	Neither shall the priests the Levites want a man before me to offer burnt offerings, and to kindle meat offerings, and to do sacrifice continually.
verse	24	33	19	And the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	33	20	Thus saith the LORD; If ye can break my covenant of the day, and my covenant of the night, and that there should not be day and night in their season;
verse	24	33	21	@@@9Then@7 may also my covenant be broken with David my servant, that he should not have a son to reign upon his throne; and with the Levites the priests, my ministers.
verse	24	33	22	As the host of heaven cannot be numbered, neither the sand of the sea measured: so will I multiply the seed of David my servant, and the Levites that minister unto me.
verse	24	33	23	Moreover the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	33	24	Considerest thou not what this people have spoken, saying, The two families which the LORD hath chosen, he hath even cast them off? thus they have despised my people, that they should be no more a nation before them.
verse	24	33	25	@@Thus saith the LORD; If my covenant be not with day and night, @9and if@7 I have not appointed the ordinances of heaven and earth;
verse	24	33	26	@@Then will I cast away the seed of Jacob, and David my servant, so that I will not take @9any@7 of his seed @9to be@7 rulers over the seed of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob: for I will cause their captivity to return, and have mercy on them.
verse	24	34	1	The word which came unto Jeremiah from the LORD, when Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and all his army, and all the kingdoms of the earth of his dominion, and all the people, fought against Jerusalem, and against all the cities thereof, saying,
verse	24	34	2	Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel; Go and speak to Zedekiah king of Judah, and tell him, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall burn it with fire:
verse	24	34	3	And thou shalt not escape out of his hand, but shalt surely be taken, and delivered into his hand; and thine eyes shall behold the eyes of the king of Babylon, and he shall speak with thee mouth to mouth, and thou shalt go to Babylon.
verse	24	34	4	Yet hear the word of the LORD, O Zedekiah king of Judah; Thus saith the LORD of thee, Thou shalt not die by the sword:
verse	24	34	5	@@@9But@7 thou shalt die in peace: and with the burnings of thy fathers, the former kings which were before thee, so shall they burn @9odours@7 for thee; and they will lament thee, @9saying,@7 Ah lord! for I have pronounced the word, saith the LORD.
verse	24	34	6	Then Jeremiah the prophet spake all these words unto Zedekiah king of Judah in Jerusalem,
verse	24	34	7	When the king of Babylon's army fought against Jerusalem, and against all the cities of Judah that were left, against Lachish, and against Azekah: for these defenced cities remained of the cities of Judah.
verse	24	34	8	@@@9This is@7 the word that came unto Jeremiah from the LORD, after that the king Zedekiah had made a covenant with all the people which @9were@7 at Jerusalem, to proclaim liberty unto them;
verse	24	34	9	@@That every man should let his manservant, and every man his maidservant, @9being@7 an Hebrew or an Hebrewess, go free; that none should serve himself of them, @9to wit,@7 of a Jew his brother.
verse	24	34	10	@@Now when all the princes, and all the people, which had entered into the covenant, heard that every one should let his manservant, and every one his maidservant, go free, that none should serve themselves of them any more, then they obeyed, and let @9them@7 go.
verse	24	34	11	But afterward they turned, and caused the servants and the handmaids, whom they had let go free, to return, and brought them into subjection for servants and for handmaids.
verse	24	34	12	Therefore the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,
verse	24	34	13	Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel; I made a covenant with your fathers in the day that I brought them forth out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondmen, saying,
verse	24	34	14	At the end of seven years let ye go every man his brother an Hebrew, which hath been sold unto thee; and when he hath served thee six years, thou shalt let him go free from thee: but your fathers hearkened not unto me, neither inclined their ear.
verse	24	34	15	And ye were now turned, and had done right in my sight, in proclaiming liberty every man to his neighbour; and ye had made a covenant before me in the house which is called by my name:
verse	24	34	16	But ye turned and polluted my name, and caused every man his servant, and every man his handmaid, whom ye had set at liberty at their pleasure, to return, and brought them into subjection, to be unto you for servants and for handmaids.
verse	24	34	17	Therefore thus saith the LORD; Ye have not hearkened unto me, in proclaiming liberty, every one to his brother, and every man to his neighbour: behold, I proclaim a liberty for you, saith the LORD, to the sword, to the pestilence, and to the famine; and I will make you to be removed into all the kingdoms of the earth.
verse	24	34	18	And I will give the men that have transgressed my covenant, which have not performed the words of the covenant which they had made before me, when they cut the calf in twain, and passed between the parts thereof,
verse	24	34	19	The princes of Judah, and the princes of Jerusalem, the eunuchs, and the priests, and all the people of the land, which passed between the parts of the calf;
verse	24	34	20	I will even give them into the hand of their enemies, and into the hand of them that seek their life: and their dead bodies shall be for meat unto the fowls of the heaven, and to the beasts of the earth.
verse	24	34	21	And Zedekiah king of Judah and his princes will I give into the hand of their enemies, and into the hand of them that seek their life, and into the hand of the king of Babylon's army, which are gone up from you.
verse	24	34	22	Behold, I will command, saith the LORD, and cause them to return to this city; and they shall fight against it, and take it, and burn it with fire: and I will make the cities of Judah a desolation without an inhabitant.
verse	24	35	1	The word which came unto Jeremiah from the LORD in the days of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, saying,
verse	24	35	2	Go unto the house of the Rechabites, and speak unto them, and bring them into the house of the LORD, into one of the chambers, and give them wine to drink.
verse	24	35	3	Then I took Jaazaniah the son of Jeremiah, the son of Habaziniah, and his brethren, and all his sons, and the whole house of the Rechabites;
verse	24	35	4	@@And I brought them into the house of the LORD, into the chamber of the sons of Hanan, the son of Igdaliah, a man of God, which @9was@7 by the chamber of the princes, which @9was@7 above the chamber of Maaseiah the son of Shallum, the keeper of the door:
verse	24	35	5	And I set before the sons of the house of the Rechabites pots full of wine, and cups, and I said unto them, Drink ye wine.
verse	24	35	6	@@But they said, We will drink no wine: for Jonadab the son of Rechab our father commanded us, saying, Ye shall drink no wine, @9neither@7 ye, nor your sons for ever:
verse	24	35	7	@@Neither shall ye build house, nor sow seed, nor plant vineyard, nor have @9any:@7 but all your days ye shall dwell in tents; that ye may live many days in the land where ye @9be@7 strangers.
verse	24	35	8	Thus have we obeyed the voice of Jonadab the son of Rechab our father in all that he hath charged us, to drink no wine all our days, we, our wives, our sons, nor our daughters;
verse	24	35	9	Nor to build houses for us to dwell in: neither have we vineyard, nor field, nor seed:
verse	24	35	10	But we have dwelt in tents, and have obeyed, and done according to all that Jonadab our father commanded us.
verse	24	35	11	But it came to pass, when Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon came up into the land, that we said, Come, and let us go to Jerusalem for fear of the army of the Chaldeans, and for fear of the army of the Syrians: so we dwell at Jerusalem.
verse	24	35	12	Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	35	13	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Go and tell the men of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, Will ye not receive instruction to hearken to my words? saith the LORD.
verse	24	35	14	The words of Jonadab the son of Rechab, that he commanded his sons not to drink wine, are performed; for unto this day they drink none, but obey their father's commandment: notwithstanding I have spoken unto you, rising early and speaking; but ye hearkened not unto me.
verse	24	35	15	@@I have sent also unto you all my servants the prophets, rising up early and sending @9them,@7 saying, Return ye now every man from his evil way, and amend your doings, and go not after other gods to serve them, and ye shall dwell in the land which I have given to you and to your fathers: but ye have not inclined your ear, nor hearkened unto me.
verse	24	35	16	Because the sons of Jonadab the son of Rechab have performed the commandment of their father, which he commanded them; but this people hath not hearkened unto me:
verse	24	35	17	Therefore thus saith the LORD God of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will bring upon Judah and upon all the inhabitants of Jerusalem all the evil that I have pronounced against them: because I have spoken unto them, but they have not heard; and I have called unto them, but they have not answered.
verse	24	35	18	And Jeremiah said unto the house of the Rechabites, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Because ye have obeyed the commandment of Jonadab your father, and kept all his precepts, and done according unto all that he hath commanded you:
verse	24	35	19	Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Jonadab the son of Rechab shall not want a man to stand before me for ever.
verse	24	36	1	@@And it came to pass in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, @9that@7 this word came unto Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,
verse	24	36	2	Take thee a roll of a book, and write therein all the words that I have spoken unto thee against Israel, and against Judah, and against all the nations, from the day I spake unto thee, from the days of Josiah, even into this day.
verse	24	36	3	It may be that the house of Judah will hear all the evil which I purpose to do unto them; that they may return every man from his evil way; that I may forgive their iniquity and their sin.
verse	24	36	4	Then Jeremiah called Baruch the son of Neriah: and Baruch wrote from the mouth of Jeremiah all the words of the LORD, which he had spoken unto him, upon a roll of a book.
verse	24	36	5	@@And Jeremiah commanded Baruch, saying, I @9am@7 shut up; I cannot go into the house of the LORD:
verse	24	36	6	Therefore go thou, and read in the roll, which thou hast written from my mouth, the words of the LORD in the ears of the people in the LORD'S house upon the fasting day: and also thou shalt read them in the ears of all Judah that come out of their cities.
verse	24	36	7	@@It may be they will present their supplication before the LORD, and will return every one from his evil way: for great @9is@7 the anger and the fury that the LORD hath pronounced against this people.
verse	24	36	8	And Baruch the son of Neriah did according to all that Jeremiah the prophet commanded him, reading in the book the words of the LORD in the LORD'S house.
verse	24	36	9	@@And it came to pass in the fifth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, in the ninth month, @9that@7 they proclaimed a fast before the LORD to all the people in Jerusalem, and to all the people that came from the cities of Judah unto Jerusalem.
verse	24	36	10	Then read Baruch in the book the words of Jeremiah in the house of the LORD, in the chamber of Gemariah the son of Shaphan the scribe, in the higher court, at the entry of the new gate of the LORD'S house, in the ears of all the people.
verse	24	36	11	When Michaiah the son of Gemariah, the son of Shaphan, had heard out of the book all the words of the LORD,
verse	24	36	12	@@Then he went down into the king's house, into the scribe's chamber: and, lo, all the princes sat there, @9even@7 Elishama the scribe, and Delaiah the son of Shemaiah, and Elnathan the son of Achbor, and Gemariah the son of Shaphan, and Zedekiah the son of Hananiah, and all the princes.
verse	24	36	13	Then Michaiah declared unto them all the words that he had heard, when Baruch read the book in the ears of the people.
verse	24	36	14	Therefore all the princes sent Jehudi the son of Nethaniah, the son of Shelemiah, the son of Cushi, unto Baruch, saying, Take in thine hand the roll wherein thou hast read in the ears of the people, and come. So Baruch the son of Neriah took the roll in his hand, and came unto them.
verse	24	36	15	@@And they said unto him, Sit down now, and read it in our ears. So Baruch read @9it@7 in their ears.
verse	24	36	16	Now it came to pass, when they had heard all the words, they were afraid both one and other, and said unto Baruch, We will surely tell the king of all these words.
verse	24	36	17	And they asked Baruch, saying, Tell us now, How didst thou write all these words at his mouth?
verse	24	36	18	@@Then Baruch answered them, He pronounced all these words unto me with his mouth, and I wrote @9them@7 with ink in the book.
verse	24	36	19	Then said the princes unto Baruch, Go, hide thee, thou and Jeremiah; and let no man know where ye be.
verse	24	36	20	And they went in to the king into the court, but they laid up the roll in the chamber of Elishama the scribe, and told all the words in the ears of the king.
verse	24	36	21	So the king sent Jehudi to fetch the roll: and he took it out of Elishama the scribe's chamber. And Jehudi read it in the ears of the king, and in the ears of all the princes which stood beside the king.
verse	24	36	22	@@Now the king sat in the winterhouse in the ninth month: and @9there was a fire@7 on the hearth burning before him.
verse	24	36	23	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 when Jehudi had read three or four leaves, he cut it with the penknife, and cast @9it@7 into the fire that @9was@7 on the hearth, until all the roll was consumed in the fire that @9was@7 on the hearth.
verse	24	36	24	@@Yet they were not afraid, nor rent their garments, @9neither@7 the king, nor any of his servants that heard all these words.
verse	24	36	25	Nevertheless Elnathan and Delaiah and Gemariah had made intercession to the king that he would not burn the roll: but he would not hear them.
verse	24	36	26	But the king commanded Jerahmeel the son of Hammelech, and Seraiah the son of Azriel, and Shelemiah the son of Abdeel, to take Baruch the scribe and Jeremiah the prophet: but the LORD hid them.
verse	24	36	27	Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah, after that the king had burned the roll, and the words which Baruch wrote at the mouth of Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	36	28	Take thee again another roll, and write in it all the former words that were in the first roll, which Jehoiakim the king of Judah hath burned.
verse	24	36	29	And thou shalt say to Jehoiakim the king of Judah, Thus saith the LORD; Thou hast burned this roll, saying, Why hast thou written therein, saying, The king of Babylon shall certainly come and destroy this land, and shall cause to cease from thence man and beast?
verse	24	36	30	Therefore thus saith the LORD of Jehoiakim king of Judah; He shall have none to sit upon the throne of David: and his dead body shall be cast out in the day to the heat, and in the night to the frost.
verse	24	36	31	And I will punish him and his seed and his servants for their iniquity; and I will bring upon them, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and upon the men of Judah, all the evil that I have pronounced against them; but they hearkened not.
verse	24	36	32	Then took Jeremiah another roll, and gave it to Baruch the scribe, the son of Neriah; who wrote therein from the mouth of Jeremiah all the words of the book which Jehoiakim king of Judah had burned in the fire: and there were added besides unto them many like words.
verse	24	37	1	And king Zedekiah the son of Josiah reigned instead of Coniah the son of Jehoiakim, whom Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon made king in the land of Judah.
verse	24	37	2	But neither he, nor his servants, nor the people of the land, did hearken unto the words of the LORD, which he spake by the prophet Jeremiah.
verse	24	37	3	And Zedekiah the king sent Jehucal the son of Shelemiah and Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah the priest to the prophet Jeremiah, saying, Pray now unto the LORD our God for us.
verse	24	37	4	Now Jeremiah came in and went out among the people: for they had not put him into prison.
verse	24	37	5	Then Pharaoh's army was come forth out of Egypt: and when the Chaldeans that besieged Jerusalem heard tidings of them, they departed from Jerusalem.
verse	24	37	6	Then came the word of the LORD unto the prophet Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	37	7	Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel; Thus shall ye say to the king of Judah, that sent you unto me to enquire of me; Behold, Pharaoh's army, which is come forth to help you, shall return to Egypt into their own land.
verse	24	37	8	And the Chaldeans shall come again, and fight against this city, and take it, and burn it with fire.
verse	24	37	9	Thus saith the LORD; Deceive not yourselves, saying, The Chaldeans shall surely depart from us: for they shall not depart.
verse	24	37	10	@@For though ye had smitten the whole army of the Chaldeans that fight against you, and there remained @9but@7 wounded men among them, @9yet@7 should they rise up every man in his tent, and burn this city with fire.
verse	24	37	11	And it came to pass, that when the army of the Chaldeans was broken up from Jerusalem for fear of Pharaoh's army,
verse	24	37	12	Then Jeremiah went forth out of Jerusalem to go into the land of Benjamin, to separate himself thence in the midst of the people.
verse	24	37	13	@@And when he was in the gate of Benjamin, a captain of the ward @9was@7 there, whose name @9was@7 Irijah, the son of Shelemiah, the son of Hananiah; and he took Jeremiah the prophet, saying, Thou fallest away to the Chaldeans.
verse	24	37	14	@@Then said Jeremiah, @9It is@7 false; I fall not away to the Chaldeans. But he hearkened not to him: so Irijah took Jeremiah, and brought him to the princes.
verse	24	37	15	Wherefore the princes were wroth with Jeremiah, and smote him, and put him in prison in the house of Jonathan the scribe: for they had made that the prison.
verse	24	37	16	When Jeremiah was entered into the dungeon, and into the cabins, and Jeremiah had remained there many days;
verse	24	37	17	@@Then Zedekiah the king sent, and took him out: and the king asked him secretly in his house, and said, Is there @9any@7 word from the LORD? And Jeremiah said, There is: for, said he, thou shalt be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon.
verse	24	37	18	Moreover Jeremiah said unto king Zedekiah, What have I offended against thee, or against thy servants, or against this people, that ye have put me in prison?
verse	24	37	19	@@Where @9are@7 now your prophets which prophesied unto you, saying, The king of Babylon shall not come against you, nor against this land?
verse	24	37	20	Therefore hear now, I pray thee, O my lord the king: let my supplication, I pray thee, be accepted before thee; that thou cause me not to return to the house of Jonathan the scribe, lest I die there.
verse	24	37	21	Then Zedekiah the king commanded that they should commit Jeremiah into the court of the prison, and that they should give him daily a piece of bread out of the bakers street, until all the bread in the city were spent. Thus Jeremiah remained in the court of the prison.
verse	24	38	1	Then Shephatiah the son of Mattan, and Gedaliah the son of Pashur, and Jucal the son of Shelemiah, and Pashur the son of Malchiah, heard the words that Jeremiah had spoken unto all the people, saying,
verse	24	38	2	Thus saith the LORD, He that remaineth in this city shall die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence: but he that goeth forth to the Chaldeans shall live; for he shall have his life for a prey, and shall live.
verse	24	38	3	Thus saith the LORD, This city shall surely be given into the hand of the king of Babylon's army, which shall take it.
verse	24	38	4	Therefore the princes said unto the king, We beseech thee, let this man be put to death: for thus he weakeneth the hands of the men of war that remain in this city, and the hands of all the people, in speaking such words unto them: for this man seeketh not the welfare of this people, but the hurt.
verse	24	38	5	@@Then Zedekiah the king said, Behold, he is in your hand: for the king @9is@7 not @9he that@7 can do @9any@7 thing against you.
verse	24	38	6	@@Then took they Jeremiah, and cast him into the dungeon of Malchiah the son of Hammelech, that @9was@7 in the court of the prison: and they let down Jeremiah with cords. And in the dungeon @9there was@7 no water, but mire: so Jeremiah sunk in the mire.
verse	24	38	7	Now when Ebed-melech the Ethiopian, one of the eunuchs which was in the king's house, heard that they had put Jeremiah in the dungeon; the king then sitting in the gate of Benjamin;
verse	24	38	8	Ebed-melech went forth out of the king's house, and spake to the king, saying,
verse	24	38	9	@@My lord the king, these men have done evil in all that they have done to Jeremiah the prophet, whom they have cast into the dungeon; and he is like to die for hunger in the place where he is: for @9there is@7 no more bread in the city.
verse	24	38	10	Then the king commanded Ebed-melech the Ethiopian, saying, Take from hence thirty men with thee, and take up Jeremiah the prophet out of the dungeon, before he die.
verse	24	38	11	So Ebed-melech took the men with him, and went into the house of the king under the treasury, and took thence old cast clouts and old rotten rags, and let them down by cords into the dungeon to Jeremiah.
verse	24	38	12	@@And Ebed-melech the Ethiopian said unto Jeremiah, Put now @9these@7 old cast clouts and rotten rags under thine armholes under the cords. And Jeremiah did so.
verse	24	38	13	So they drew up Jeremiah with cords, and took him up out of the dungeon: and Jeremiah remained in the court of the prison.
verse	24	38	14	@@Then Zedekiah the king sent, and took Jeremiah the prophet unto him into the third entry that @9is@7 in the house of the LORD: and the king said unto Jeremiah, I will ask thee a thing; hide nothing from me.
verse	24	38	15	@@Then Jeremiah said unto Zedekiah, If I declare @9it@7 unto thee, wilt thou not surely put me to death? and if I give thee counsel, wilt thou not hearken unto me?
verse	24	38	16	@@So Zedekiah the king sware secretly unto Jeremiah, saying, @9As@7 the LORD liveth, that made us this soul, I will not put thee to death, neither will I give thee into the hand of these men that seek thy life.
verse	24	38	17	Then said Jeremiah unto Zedekiah, Thus saith the LORD, the God of hosts, the God of Israel; If thou wilt assuredly go forth unto the king of Babylon's princes, then thy soul shall live, and this city shall not be burned with fire; and thou shalt live, and thine house:
verse	24	38	18	But if thou wilt not go forth to the king of Babylon's princes, then shall this city be given into the hand of the Chaldeans, and they shall burn it with fire, and thou shalt not escape out of their hand.
verse	24	38	19	And Zedekiah the king said unto Jeremiah, I am afraid of the Jews that are fallen to the Chaldeans, lest they deliver me into their hand, and they mock me.
verse	24	38	20	@@But Jeremiah said, They shall not deliver @9thee.@7 Obey, I beseech thee, the voice of the LORD, which I speak unto thee: so it shall be well unto thee, and thy soul shall live.
verse	24	38	21	@@But if thou refuse to go forth, this @9is@7 the word that the LORD hath shewed me:
verse	24	38	22	@@And, behold, all the women that are left in the king of Judah's house @9shall be@7 brought forth to the king of Babylon's princes, and those @9women@7 shall say, Thy friends have set thee on, and have prevailed against thee: thy feet are sunk in the mire, @9and@7 they are turned away back.
verse	24	38	23	So they shall bring out all thy wives and thy children to the Chaldeans: and thou shalt not escape out of their hand, but shalt be taken by the hand of the king of Babylon: and thou shalt cause this city to be burned with fire.
verse	24	38	24	Then said Zedekiah unto Jeremiah, Let no man know of these words, and thou shalt not die.
verse	24	38	25	But if the princes hear that I have talked with thee, and they come unto thee, and say unto thee, Declare unto us now what thou hast said unto the king, hide it not from us, and we will not put thee to death; also what the king said unto thee:
verse	24	38	26	Then thou shalt say unto them, I presented my supplication before the king, that he would not cause me to return to Jonathan's house, to die there.
verse	24	38	27	Then came all the princes unto Jeremiah, and asked him: and he told them according to all these words that the king had commanded. So they left off speaking with him; for the matter was not perceived.
verse	24	38	28	@@So Jeremiah abode in the court of the prison until the day that Jerusalem was taken: and he was @9there@7 when Jerusalem was taken.
verse	24	39	1	In the ninth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the tenth month, came Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon and all his army against Jerusalem, and they besieged it.
verse	24	39	2	@@@9And@7 in the eleventh year of Zedekiah, in the fourth month, the ninth @9day@7 of the month, the city was broken up.
verse	24	39	3	@@And all the princes of the king of Babylon came in, and sat in the middle gate, @9even@7 Nergal-sharezer, Samgar-nebo, Sarsechim, Rab-saris, Nergal-sharezer, Rabmag, with all the residue of the princes of the king of Babylon.
verse	24	39	4	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 when Zedekiah the king of Judah saw them, and all the men of war, then they fled, and went forth out of the city by night, by the way of the king's garden, by the gate betwixt the two walls: and he went out the way of the plain.
verse	24	39	5	But the Chaldeans' army pursued after them, and overtook Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho: and when they had taken him, they brought him up to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon to Riblah in the land of Hamath, where he gave judgment upon him.
verse	24	39	6	Then the king of Babylon slew the sons of Zedekiah in Riblah before his eyes: also the king of Babylon slew all the nobles of Judah.
verse	24	39	7	Moreover he put out Zedekiah's eyes, and bound him with chains, to carry him to Babylon.
verse	24	39	8	And the Chaldeans burned the king's house, and the houses of the people, with fire, and brake down the walls of Jerusalem.
verse	24	39	9	Then Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive into Babylon the remnant of the people that remained in the city, and those that fell away, that fell to him, with the rest of the people that remained.
verse	24	39	10	But Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard left of the poor of the people, which had nothing, in the land of Judah, and gave them vineyards and fields at the same time.
verse	24	39	11	Now Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon gave charge concerning Jeremiah to Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard, saying,
verse	24	39	12	Take him, and look well to him, and do him no harm; but do unto him even as he shall say unto thee.
verse	24	39	13	So Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard sent, and Nebushasban, Rab-saris, and Nergal-sharezer, Rabmag, and all the king of Babylon's princes;
verse	24	39	14	Even they sent, and took Jeremiah out of the court of the prison, and committed him unto Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan, that he should carry him home: so he dwelt among the people.
verse	24	39	15	Now the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah, while he was shut up in the court of the prison, saying,
verse	24	39	16	@@Go and speak to Ebed-melech the Ethiopian, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will bring my words upon this city for evil, and not for good; and they shall be @9accomplished@7 in that day before thee.
verse	24	39	17	@@But I will deliver thee in that day, saith the LORD: and thou shalt not be given into the hand of the men of whom thou @9art@7 afraid.
verse	24	39	18	For I will surely deliver thee, and thou shalt not fall by the sword, but thy life shall be for a prey unto thee: because thou hast put thy trust in me, saith the LORD.
verse	24	40	1	The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, after that Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had let him go from Ramah, when he had taken him being bound in chains among all that were carried away captive of Jerusalem and Judah, which were carried away captive unto Babylon.
verse	24	40	2	And the captain of the guard took Jeremiah, and said unto him, The LORD thy God hath pronounced this evil upon this place.
verse	24	40	3	@@Now the LORD hath brought @9it,@7 and done according as he hath said: because ye have sinned against the LORD, and have not obeyed his voice, therefore this thing is come upon you.
verse	24	40	4	@@And now, behold, I loose thee this day from the chains which @9were@7 upon thine hand. If it seem good unto thee to come with me into Babylon, come; and I will look well unto thee: but if it seem ill unto thee to come with me into Babylon, forbear: behold, all the land @9is@7 before thee: whither it seemeth good and convenient for thee to go, thither go.
verse	24	40	5	@@Now while he was not yet gone back, @9he said,@7 Go back also to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan, whom the king of Babylon hath made governor over the cities of Judah, and dwell with him among the people: or go wheresoever it seemeth convenient unto thee to go. So the captain of the guard gave him victuals and a reward, and let him go.
verse	24	40	6	Then went Jeremiah unto Gedaliah the son of Ahikam to Mizpah; and dwelt with him among the people that were left in the land.
verse	24	40	7	@@Now when all the captains of the forces which @9were@7 in the fields, @9even@7 they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam governor in the land, and had committed unto him men, and women, and children, and of the poor of the land, of them that were not carried away captive to Babylon;
verse	24	40	8	Then they came to Gedaliah to Mizpah, even Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and Johanan and Jonathan the sons of Kareah, and Seraiah the son of Tanhumeth, and the sons of Ephai the Netophathite, and Jezaniah the son of a Maachathite, they and their men.
verse	24	40	9	And Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan sware unto them and to their men, saying, Fear not to serve the Chaldeans: dwell in the land, and serve the king of Babylon, and it shall be well with you.
verse	24	40	10	@@As for me, behold, I will dwell at Mizpah to serve the Chaldeans, which will come unto us: but ye, gather ye wine, and summer fruits, and oil, and put @9them@7 in your vessels, and dwell in your cities that ye have taken.
verse	24	40	11	@@Likewise when all the Jews that @9were@7 in Moab, and among the Ammonites, and in Edom, and that @9were@7 in all the countries, heard that the king of Babylon had left a remnant of Judah, and that he had set over them Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan;
verse	24	40	12	Even all the Jews returned out of all places whither they were driven, and came to the land of Judah, to Gedaliah, unto Mizpah, and gathered wine and summer fruits very much.
verse	24	40	13	@@Moreover Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces that @9were@7 in the fields, came to Gedaliah to Mizpah,
verse	24	40	14	And said unto him, Dost thou certainly know that Baalis the king of the Ammonites hath sent Ishmael the son of Nethaniah to slay thee? But Gedaliah the son of Ahikam believed them not.
verse	24	40	15	@@Then Johanan the son of Kareah spake to Gedaliah in Mizpah secretly, saying, Let me go, I pray thee, and I will slay Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and no man shall know @9it:@7 wherefore should he slay thee, that all the Jews which are gathered unto thee should be scattered, and the remnant in Judah perish?
verse	24	40	16	But Gedaliah the son of Ahikam said unto Johanan the son of Kareah, Thou shalt not do this thing: for thou speakest falsely of Ishmael.
verse	24	41	1	@@Now it came to pass in the seventh month, @9that@7 Ishmael the son of Nethaniah the son of Elishama, of the seed royal, and the princes of the king, even ten men with him, came unto Gedaliah the son of Ahikam to Mizpah; and there they did eat bread together in Mizpah.
verse	24	41	2	Then arose Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and the ten men that were with him, and smote Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan with the sword, and slew him, whom the king of Babylon had made governor over the land.
verse	24	41	3	@@Ishmael also slew all the Jews that were with him, @9even@7 with Gedaliah, at Mizpah, and the Chaldeans that were found there, @9and@7 the men of war.
verse	24	41	4	@@And it came to pass the second day after he had slain Gedaliah, and no man knew @9it, @7
verse	24	41	5	@@That there came certain from Shechem, from Shiloh, and from Samaria, @9even@7 fourscore men, having their beards shaven, and their clothes rent, and having cut themselves, with offerings and incense in their hand, to bring @9them@7 to the house of the LORD.
verse	24	41	6	And Ishmael the son of Nethaniah went forth from Mizpah to meet them, weeping all along as he went: and it came to pass, as he met them, he said unto them, Come to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam.
verse	24	41	7	@@And it was @9so,@7 when they came into the midst of the city, that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah slew them, @9and cast them@7 into the midst of the pit, he, and the men that @9were@7 with him.
verse	24	41	8	But ten men were found among them that said unto Ishmael, Slay us not: for we have treasures in the field, of wheat, and of barley, and of oil, and of honey. So he forbare, and slew them not among their brethren.
verse	24	41	9	@@Now the pit wherein Ishmael had cast all the dead bodies of the men, whom he had slain because of Gedaliah, @9was@7 it which Asa the king had made for fear of Baasha king of Israel: @9and@7 Ishmael the son of Nethaniah filled it with @9them that were@7 slain.
verse	24	41	10	@@Then Ishmael carried away captive all the residue of the people that @9were@7 in Mizpah, @9even@7 the king's daughters, and all the people that remained in Mizpah, whom Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had committed to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam: and Ishmael the son of Nethaniah carried them away captive, and departed to go over to the Ammonites.
verse	24	41	11	@@But when Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces that @9were@7 with him, heard of all the evil that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah had done,
verse	24	41	12	@@Then they took all the men, and went to fight with Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and found him by the great waters that @9are@7 in Gibeon.
verse	24	41	13	@@Now it came to pass, @9that@7 when all the people which @9were@7 with Ishmael saw Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces that @9were@7 with him, then they were glad.
verse	24	41	14	So all the people that Ishmael had carried away captive from Mizpah cast about and returned, and went unto Johanan the son of Kareah.
verse	24	41	15	But Ishmael the son of Nethaniah escaped from Johanan with eight men, and went to the Ammonites.
verse	24	41	16	@@Then took Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces that @9were@7 with him, all the remnant of the people whom he had recovered from Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, from Mizpah, after @9that@7 he had slain Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, @9even@7 mighty men of war, and the women, and the children, and the eunuchs, whom he had brought again from Gibeon:
verse	24	41	17	And they departed, and dwelt in the habitation of Chimham, which is by Bethlehem, to go to enter into Egypt,
verse	24	41	18	Because of the Chaldeans: for they were afraid of them, because Ishmael the son of Nethaniah had slain Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, whom the king of Babylon made governor in the land.
verse	24	42	1	Then all the captains of the forces, and Johanan the son of Kareah, and Jezaniah the son of Hoshaiah, and all the people from the least even unto the greatest, came near,
verse	24	42	2	@@And said unto Jeremiah the prophet, Let, we beseech thee, our supplication be accepted before thee, and pray for us unto the LORD thy God, @9even@7 for all this remnant; (for we are left @9but@7 a few of many, as thine eyes do behold us:)
verse	24	42	3	That the LORD thy God may shew us the way wherein we may walk, and the thing that we may do.
verse	24	42	4	@@Then Jeremiah the prophet said unto them, I have heard @9you;@7 behold, I will pray unto the LORD your God according to your words; and it shall come to pass, @9that@7 whatsoever thing the LORD shall answer you, I will declare @9it@7 unto you; I will keep nothing back from you.
verse	24	42	5	Then they said to Jeremiah, The LORD be a true and faithful witness between us, if we do not even according to all things for the which the LORD thy God shall send thee to us.
verse	24	42	6	@@Whether @9it be@7 good, or whether @9it be@7 evil, we will obey the voice of the LORD our God, to whom we send thee; that it may be well with us, when we obey the voice of the LORD our God.
verse	24	42	7	And it came to pass after ten days, that the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah.
verse	24	42	8	@@Then called he Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces which @9were@7 with him, and all the people from the least even to the greatest,
verse	24	42	9	And said unto them, Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, unto whom ye sent me to present your supplication before him;
verse	24	42	10	@@If ye will still abide in this land, then will I build you, and not pull @9you@7 down, and I will plant you, and not pluck @9you@7 up: for I repent me of the evil that I have done unto you.
verse	24	42	11	@@Be not afraid of the king of Babylon, of whom ye are afraid; be not afraid of him, saith the LORD: for I @9am@7 with you to save you, and to deliver you from his hand.
verse	24	42	12	And I will shew mercies unto you, that he may have mercy upon you, and cause you to return to your own land.
verse	24	42	13	But if ye say, We will not dwell in this land, neither obey the voice of the LORD your God,
verse	24	42	14	Saying, No; but we will go into the land of Egypt, where we shall see no war, nor hear the sound of the trumpet, nor have hunger of bread; and there will we dwell:
verse	24	42	15	And now therefore hear the word of the LORD, ye remnant of Judah; Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; If ye wholly set your faces to enter into Egypt, and go to sojourn there;
verse	24	42	16	@@Then it shall come to pass, @9that@7 the sword, which ye feared, shall overtake you there in the land of Egypt, and the famine, whereof ye were afraid, shall follow close after you there in Egypt; and there ye shall die.
verse	24	42	17	So shall it be with all the men that set their faces to go into Egypt to sojourn there; they shall die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence: and none of them shall remain or escape from the evil that I will bring upon them.
verse	24	42	18	For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; As mine anger and my fury hath been poured forth upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem; so shall my fury be poured forth upon you, when ye shall enter into Egypt: and ye shall be an execration, and an astonishment, and a curse, and a reproach; and ye shall see this place no more.
verse	24	42	19	The LORD hath said concerning you, O ye remnant of Judah; Go ye not into Egypt: know certainly that I have admonished you this day.
verse	24	42	20	@@For ye dissembled in your hearts, when ye sent me unto the LORD your God, saying, Pray for us unto the LORD our God; and according unto all that the LORD our God shall say, so declare unto us, and we will do @9it. @7
verse	24	42	21	@@And @9now@7 I have this day declared @9it@7 to you; but ye have not obeyed the voice of the LORD your God, nor any @9thing@7 for the which he hath sent me unto you.
verse	24	42	22	@@Now therefore know certainly that ye shall die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence, in the place whither ye desire to go @9and@7 to sojourn.
verse	24	43	1	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 when Jeremiah had made an end of speaking unto all the people all the words of the LORD their God, for which the LORD their God had sent him to them, @9even@7 all these words,
verse	24	43	2	Then spake Azariah the son of Hoshaiah, and Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the proud men, saying unto Jeremiah, Thou speakest falsely: the LORD our God hath not sent thee to say, Go not into Egypt to sojourn there:
verse	24	43	3	But Baruch the son of Neriah setteth thee on against us, for to deliver us into the hand of the Chaldeans, that they might put us to death, and carry us away captives into Babylon.
verse	24	43	4	So Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces, and all the people, obeyed not the voice of the LORD, to dwell in the land of Judah.
verse	24	43	5	But Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces, took all the remnant of Judah, that were returned from all nations, whither they had been driven, to dwell in the land of Judah;
verse	24	43	6	@@@9Even@7 men, and women, and children, and the king's daughters, and every person that Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had left with Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan, and Jeremiah the prophet, and Baruch the son of Neriah.
verse	24	43	7	@@So they came into the land of Egypt: for they obeyed not the voice of the LORD: thus came they @9even@7 to Tahpanhes.
verse	24	43	8	Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah in Tahpanhes, saying,
verse	24	43	9	@@Take great stones in thine hand, and hide them in the clay in the brickkiln, which @9is@7 at the entry of Pharaoh's house in Tahpanhes, in the sight of the men of Judah;
verse	24	43	10	And say unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will send and take Nebuchadrezzar the king of Babylon, my servant, and will set his throne upon these stones that I have hid; and he shall spread his royal pavilion over them.
verse	24	43	11	@@And when he cometh, he shall smite the land of Egypt, @9and deliver@7 such @9as are@7 for death to death; and such @9as are@7 for captivity to captivity; and such @9as are@7 for the sword to the sword.
verse	24	43	12	And I will kindle a fire in the houses of the gods of Egypt; and he shall burn them, and carry them away captives: and he shall array himself with the land of Egypt, as a shepherd putteth on his garment; and he shall go forth from thence in peace.
verse	24	43	13	@@He shall break also the images of Bethshemesh, that @9is@7 in the land of Egypt; and the houses of the gods of the Egyptians shall he burn with fire.
verse	24	44	1	The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the Jews which dwell in the land of Egypt, which dwell at Migdol, and at Tahpanhes, and at Noph, and in the country of Pathros, saying,
verse	24	44	2	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Ye have seen all the evil that I have brought upon Jerusalem, and upon all the cities of Judah; and, behold, this day they @9are@7 a desolation, and no man dwelleth therein,
verse	24	44	3	@@Because of their wickedness which they have committed to provoke me to anger, in that they went to burn incense, @9and@7 to serve other gods, whom they knew not, @9neither@7 they, ye, nor your fathers.
verse	24	44	4	@@Howbeit I sent unto you all my servants the prophets, rising early and sending @9them,@7 saying, Oh, do not this abominable thing that I hate.
verse	24	44	5	But they hearkened not, nor inclined their ear to turn from their wickedness, to burn no incense unto other gods.
verse	24	44	6	@@Wherefore my fury and mine anger was poured forth, and was kindled in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem; and they are wasted @9and@7 desolate, as at this day.
verse	24	44	7	@@Therefore now thus saith the LORD, the God of hosts, the God of Israel; Wherefore commit ye @9this@7 great evil against your souls, to cut off from you man and woman, child and suckling, out of Judah, to leave you none to remain;
verse	24	44	8	In that ye provoke me unto wrath with the works of your hands, burning incense unto other gods in the land of Egypt, whither ye be gone to dwell, that ye might cut yourselves off, and that ye might be a curse and a reproach among all the nations of the earth?
verse	24	44	9	Have ye forgotten the wickedness of your fathers, and the wickedness of the kings of Judah, and the wickedness of their wives, and your own wickedness, and the wickedness of your wives, which they have committed in the land of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem?
verse	24	44	10	@@They are not humbled @9even@7 unto this day, neither have they feared, nor walked in my law, nor in my statutes, that I set before you and before your fathers.
verse	24	44	11	Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will set my face against you for evil, and to cut off all Judah.
verse	24	44	12	@@And I will take the remnant of Judah, that have set their faces to go into the land of Egypt to sojourn there, and they shall all be consumed, @9and@7 fall in the land of Egypt; they shall @9even@7 be consumed by the sword and by the famine: they shall die, from the least even unto the greatest, by the sword @9and@7 by the famine: and they shall be an execration, @9and@7 an astonishment, and a curse, and a reproach.
verse	24	44	13	For I will punish them that dwell in the land of Egypt, as I have punished Jerusalem, by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence:
verse	24	44	14	So that none of the remnant of Judah, which are gone into the land of Egypt to sojourn there, shall escape or remain, that they should return into the land of Judah, to the which they have a desire to return to dwell there: for none shall return but such as shall escape.
verse	24	44	15	Then all the men which knew that their wives had burned incense unto other gods, and all the women that stood by, a great multitude, even all the people that dwelt in the land of Egypt, in Pathros, answered Jeremiah, saying,
verse	24	44	16	@@@9As for@7 the word that thou hast spoken unto us in the name of the LORD, we will not hearken unto thee.
verse	24	44	17	@@But we will certainly do whatsoever thing goeth forth out of our own mouth, to burn incense unto the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto her, as we have done, we, and our fathers, our kings, and our princes, in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem: for @9then@7 had we plenty of victuals, and were well, and saw no evil.
verse	24	44	18	@@But since we left off to burn incense to the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto her, we have wanted all @9things,@7 and have been consumed by the sword and by the famine.
verse	24	44	19	And when we burned incense to the queen of heaven, and poured out drink offerings unto her, did we make her cakes to worship her, and pour out drink offerings unto her, without our men?
verse	24	44	20	@@Then Jeremiah said unto all the people, to the men, and to the women, and to all the people which had given him @9that@7 answer, saying,
verse	24	44	21	@@The incense that ye burned in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, ye, and your fathers, your kings, and your princes, and the people of the land, did not the LORD remember them, and came it @9not@7 into his mind?
verse	24	44	22	@@So that the LORD could no longer bear, because of the evil of your doings, @9and@7 because of the abominations which ye have committed; therefore is your land a desolation, and an astonishment, and a curse, without an inhabitant, as at this day.
verse	24	44	23	Because ye have burned incense, and because ye have sinned against the LORD, and have not obeyed the voice of the LORD, nor walked in his law, nor in his statutes, nor in his testimonies; therefore this evil is happened unto you, as at this day.
verse	24	44	24	@@Moreover Jeremiah said unto all the people, and to all the women, Hear the word of the LORD, all Judah that @9are@7 in the land of Egypt:
verse	24	44	25	Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, saying; Ye and your wives have both spoken with your mouths, and fulfilled with your hand, saying, We will surely perform our vows that we have vowed, to burn incense to the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto her: ye will surely accomplish your vows, and surely perform your vows.
verse	24	44	26	Therefore hear ye the word of the LORD, all Judah that dwell in the land of Egypt; Behold, I have sworn by my great name, saith the LORD, that my name shall no more be named in the mouth of any man of Judah in all the land of Egypt, saying, The Lord GOD liveth.
verse	24	44	27	Behold, I will watch over them for evil, and not for good: and all the men of Judah that are in the land of Egypt shall be consumed by the sword and by the famine, until there be an end of them.
verse	24	44	28	Yet a small number that escape the sword shall return out of the land of Egypt into the land of Judah, and all the remnant of Judah, that are gone into the land of Egypt to sojourn there, shall know whose words shall stand, mine, or theirs.
verse	24	44	29	@@And this @9shall be@7 a sign unto you, saith the LORD, that I will punish you in this place, that ye may know that my words shall surely stand against you for evil:
