verse	24	50	29	Call together the archers against Babylon: all ye that bend the bow, camp against it round about; let none thereof escape: recompense her according to her work; according to all that she hath done, do unto her: for she hath been proud against the LORD, against the Holy One of Israel.
verse	24	50	30	Therefore shall her young men fall in the streets, and all her men of war shall be cut off in that day, saith the LORD.
verse	24	50	31	@@Behold, I @9am@7 against thee, @9O thou@7 most proud, saith the Lord GOD of hosts: for thy day is come, the time @9that@7 I will visit thee.
verse	24	50	32	And the most proud shall stumble and fall, and none shall raise him up: and I will kindle a fire in his cities, and it shall devour all round about him.
verse	24	50	33	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The children of Israel and the children of Judah @9were@7 oppressed together: and all that took them captives held them fast; they refused to let them go.
verse	24	50	34	@@Their Redeemer @9is@7 strong; the LORD of hosts @9is@7 his name: he shall throughly plead their cause, that he may give rest to the land, and disquiet the inhabitants of Babylon.
verse	24	50	35	@@A sword @9is@7 upon the Chaldeans, saith the LORD, and upon the inhabitants of Babylon, and upon her princes, and upon her wise @9men. @7
verse	24	50	36	@@A sword @9is@7 upon the liars; and they shall dote: a sword @9is@7 upon her mighty men; and they shall be dismayed.
verse	24	50	37	@@A sword @9is@7 upon their horses, and upon their chariots, and upon all the mingled people that @9are@7 in the midst of her; and they shall become as women: a sword @9is@7 upon her treasures; and they shall be robbed.
verse	24	50	38	@@A drought @9is@7 upon her waters; and they shall be dried up: for it @9is@7 the land of graven images, and they are mad upon @9their@7 idols.
