verse	24	50	42	@@They shall hold the bow and the lance: they @9are@7 cruel, and will not shew mercy: their voice shall roar like the sea, and they shall ride upon horses, @9every one@7 put in array, like a man to the battle, against thee, O daughter of Babylon.
verse	24	50	43	@@The king of Babylon hath heard the report of them, and his hands waxed feeble: anguish took hold of him, @9and@7 pangs as of a woman in travail.
