verse	24	52	22	@@And a chapiter of brass @9was@7 upon it; and the height of one chapiter @9was@7 five cubits, with network and pomegranates upon the chapiters round about, all of brass. The second pillar also and the pomegranates @9were@7 like unto these.
verse	24	52	23	@@And there were ninety and six pomegranates on a side; @9and@7 all the pomegranates upon the network @9were@7 an hundred round about.
verse	24	52	24	And the captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, and Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the door:
verse	24	52	25	He took also out of the city an eunuch, which had the charge of the men of war; and seven men of them that were near the king's person, which were found in the city; and the principal scribe of the host, who mustered the people of the land; and threescore men of the people of the land, that were found in the midst of the city.
verse	24	52	26	So Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard took them, and brought them to the king of Babylon to Riblah.
verse	24	52	27	And the king of Babylon smote them, and put them to death in Riblah in the land of Hamath. Thus Judah was carried away captive out of his own land.
verse	24	52	28	This is the people whom Nebuchadrezzar carried away captive: in the seventh year three thousand Jews and three and twenty:
verse	24	52	29	In the eighteenth year of Nebuchadrezzar he carried away captive from Jerusalem eight hundred thirty and two persons:
verse	24	52	30	@@In the three and twentieth year of Nebuchadrezzar Nebuzar-adan the captain of the guard carried away captive of the Jews seven hundred forty and five persons: all the persons @9were@7 four thousand and six hundred.
verse	24	52	31	@@And it came to pass in the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, in the five and twentieth @9day@7 of the month, @9that@7 Evilmerodach king of Babylon in the @9first@7 year of his reign lifted up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah, and brought him forth out of prison,
verse	24	52	32	@@And spake kindly unto him, and set his throne above the throne of the kings that @9were@7 with him in Babylon,
verse	24	52	33	And changed his prison garments: and he did continually eat bread before him all the days of his life.
verse	24	52	34	@@And @9for@7 his diet, there was a continual diet given him of the king of Babylon, every day a portion until the day of his death, all the days of his life.
verse	25	1	1	@@How doth the city sit solitary, @9that was@7 full of people @9how@7 is she become as a widow she @9that was@7 great among the nations, @9and@7 princess among the provinces, @9how@7 is she become tributary
verse	25	1	2	@@She weepeth sore in the night, and her tears @9are@7 on her cheeks: among all her lovers she hath none to comfort @9her:@7 all her friends have dealt treacherously with her, they are become her enemies.
verse	25	1	3	Judah is gone into captivity because of affliction, and because of great servitude: she dwelleth among the heathen, she findeth no rest: all her persecutors overtook her between the straits.
verse	25	1	4	@@The ways of Zion do mourn, because none come to the solemn feasts: all her gates are desolate: her priests sigh, her virgins are afflicted, and she @9is@7 in bitterness.
verse	25	1	5	Her adversaries are the chief, her enemies prosper; for the LORD hath afflicted her for the multitude of her transgressions: her children are gone into captivity before the enemy.
verse	25	1	6	@@And from the daughter of Zion all her beauty is departed: her princes are become like harts @9that@7 find no pasture, and they are gone without strength before the pursuer.
verse	25	1	7	@@Jerusalem remembered in the days of her affliction and of her miseries all her pleasant things that she had in the days of old, when her people fell into the hand of the enemy, and none did help her: the adversaries saw her, @9and@7 did mock at her sabbaths.
verse	25	1	8	Jerusalem hath grievously sinned; therefore she is removed: all that honoured her despise her, because they have seen her nakedness: yea, she sigheth, and turneth backward.
verse	25	1	9	@@Her filthiness @9is@7 in her skirts; she remembereth not her last end; therefore she came down wonderfully: she had no comforter. O LORD, behold my affliction: for the enemy hath magnified @9himself. @7
verse	25	1	10	@@The adversary hath spread out his hand upon all her pleasant things: for she hath seen @9that@7 the heathen entered into her sanctuary, whom thou didst command @9that@7 they should not enter into thy congregation.
verse	25	1	11	All her people sigh, they seek bread; they have given their pleasant things for meat to relieve the soul: see, O LORD, and consider; for I am become vile.
verse	25	1	12	@@@9Is it@7 nothing to you, all ye that pass by? behold, and see if there be any sorrow like unto my sorrow, which is done unto me, wherewith the LORD hath afflicted @9me@7 in the day of his fierce anger.
verse	25	1	13	@@From above hath he sent fire into my bones, and it prevaileth against them: he hath spread a net for my feet, he hath turned me back: he hath made me desolate @9and@7 faint all the day.
verse	25	1	14	@@The yoke of my transgressions is bound by his hand: they are wreathed, @9and@7 come up upon my neck: he hath made my strength to fall, the Lord hath delivered me into @9their@7 hands, @9from whom@7 I am not able to rise up.
verse	25	1	15	@@The Lord hath trodden under foot all my mighty @9men@7 in the midst of me: he hath called an assembly against me to crush my young men: the Lord hath trodden the virgin, the daughter of Judah, @9as@7 in a winepress.
verse	25	1	16	@@For these @9things@7 I weep; mine eye, mine eye runneth down with water, because the comforter that should relieve my soul is far from me: my children are desolate, because the enemy prevailed.
verse	25	1	17	@@Zion spreadeth forth her hands, @9and there is@7 none to comfort her: the LORD hath commanded concerning Jacob, @9that@7 his adversaries @9should be@7 round about him: Jerusalem is as a menstruous woman among them.
verse	25	1	18	The LORD is righteous; for I have rebelled against his commandment: hear, I pray you, all people, and behold my sorrow: my virgins and my young men are gone into captivity.
verse	25	1	19	@@I called for my lovers, @9but@7 they deceived me: my priests and mine elders gave up the ghost in the city, while they sought their meat to relieve their souls.
verse	25	1	20	@@Behold, O LORD; for I @9am@7 in distress: my bowels are troubled; mine heart is turned within me; for I have grievously rebelled: abroad the sword bereaveth, at home @9there is@7 as death.
verse	25	1	21	@@They have heard that I sigh: @9there is@7 none to comfort me: all mine enemies have heard of my trouble; they are glad that thou hast done @9it:@7 thou wilt bring the day @9that@7 thou hast called, and they shall be like unto me.
verse	25	1	22	@@Let all their wickedness come before thee; and do unto them, as thou hast done unto me for all my transgressions: for my sighs @9are@7 many, and my heart @9is@7 faint.
verse	25	2	1	@@How hath the Lord covered the daughter of Zion with a cloud in his anger, @9and@7 cast down from heaven unto the earth the beauty of Israel, and remembered not his footstool in the day of his anger!
verse	25	2	2	@@The Lord hath swallowed up all the habitations of Jacob, and hath not pitied: he hath thrown down in his wrath the strong holds of the daughter of Judah; he hath brought @9them@7 down to the ground: he hath polluted the kingdom and the princes thereof.
verse	25	2	3	@@He hath cut off in @9his@7 fierce anger all the horn of Israel: he hath drawn back his right hand from before the enemy, and he burned against Jacob like a flaming fire, @9which@7 devoureth round about.
verse	25	2	4	@@He hath bent his bow like an enemy: he stood with his right hand as an adversary, and slew all @9that were@7 pleasant to the eye in the tabernacle of the daughter of Zion: he poured out his fury like fire.
verse	25	2	5	The Lord was as an enemy: he hath swallowed up Israel, he hath swallowed up all her palaces: he hath destroyed his strong holds, and hath increased in the daughter of Judah mourning and lamentation.
verse	25	2	6	@@And he hath violently taken away his tabernacle, as @9if it were of@7 a garden: he hath destroyed his places of the assembly: the LORD hath caused the solemn feasts and sabbaths to be forgotten in Zion, and hath despised in the indignation of his anger the king and the priest.
verse	25	2	7	The Lord hath cast off his altar, he hath abhorred his sanctuary, he hath given up into the hand of the enemy the walls of her palaces; they have made a noise in the house of the LORD, as in the day of a solemn feast.
verse	25	2	8	The LORD hath purposed to destroy the wall of the daughter of Zion: he hath stretched out a line, he hath not withdrawn his hand from destroying: therefore he made the rampart and the wall to lament; they languished together.
verse	25	2	9	@@Her gates are sunk into the ground; he hath destroyed and broken her bars: her king and her princes @9are@7 among the Gentiles: the law @9is@7 no @9more;@7 her prophets also find no vision from the LORD.
verse	25	2	10	@@The elders of the daughter of Zion sit upon the ground, @9and@7 keep silence: they have cast up dust upon their heads; they have girded themselves with sackcloth: the virgins of Jerusalem hang down their heads to the ground.
verse	25	2	11	Mine eyes do fail with tears, my bowels are troubled, my liver is poured upon the earth, for the destruction of the daughter of my people; because the children and the sucklings swoon in the streets of the city.
verse	25	2	12	@@They say to their mothers, Where @9is@7 corn and wine? when they swooned as the wounded in the streets of the city, when their soul was poured out into their mothers' bosom.
verse	25	2	13	What thing shall I take to witness for thee? what thing shall I liken to thee, O daughter of Jerusalem? what shall I equal to thee, that I may comfort thee, O virgin daughter of Zion? for thy breach is great like the sea: who can heal thee?
verse	25	2	14	Thy prophets have seen vain and foolish things for thee: and they have not discovered thine iniquity, to turn away thy captivity; but have seen for thee false burdens and causes of banishment.
verse	25	2	15	@@All that pass by clap @9their@7 hands at thee; they hiss and wag their head at the daughter of Jerusalem, @9saying, Is@7 this the city that @9men@7 call The perfection of beauty, The joy of the whole earth?
verse	25	2	16	@@All thine enemies have opened their mouth against thee: they hiss and gnash the teeth: they say, We have swallowed @9her@7 up: certainly this @9is@7 the day that we looked for; we have found, we have seen @9it. @7
verse	25	2	17	@@The LORD hath done @9that@7 which he had devised; he hath fulfilled his word that he had commanded in the days of old: he hath thrown down, and hath not pitied: and he hath caused @9thine@7 enemy to rejoice over thee, he hath set up the horn of thine adversaries.
verse	25	2	18	Their heart cried unto the Lord, O wall of the daughter of Zion, let tears run down like a river day and night: give thyself no rest; let not the apple of thine eye cease.
verse	25	2	19	Arise, cry out in the night: in the beginning of the watches pour out thine heart like water before the face of the Lord: lift up thy hands toward him for the life of thy young children, that faint for hunger in the top of every street.
verse	25	2	20	@@Behold, O LORD, and consider to whom thou hast done this. Shall the women eat their fruit, @9and@7 children of a span long? shall the priest and the prophet be slain in the sanctuary of the Lord?
verse	25	2	21	@@The young and the old lie on the ground in the streets: my virgins and my young men are fallen by the sword; thou hast slain @9them@7 in the day of thine anger; thou hast killed, @9and@7 not pitied.
verse	25	2	22	Thou hast called as in a solemn day my terrors round about, so that in the day of the LORD'S anger none escaped nor remained: those that I have swaddled and brought up hath mine enemy consumed.
verse	25	3	1	@@I @9am@7 the man @9that@7 hath seen affliction by the rod of his wrath.
verse	25	3	2	@@He hath led me, and brought @9me into@7 darkness, but not @9into@7 light.
verse	25	3	3	@@Surely against me is he turned; he turneth his hand @9against me@7 all the day.
verse	25	3	4	My flesh and my skin hath he made old; he hath broken my bones.
verse	25	3	5	@@He hath builded against me, and compassed @9me@7 with gall and travail.
verse	25	3	6	@@He hath set me in dark places, as @9they that be@7 dead of old.
verse	25	3	7	He hath hedged me about, that I cannot get out: he hath made my chain heavy.
verse	25	3	8	Also when I cry and shout, he shutteth out my prayer.
verse	25	3	9	He hath inclosed my ways with hewn stone, he hath made my paths crooked.
verse	25	3	10	@@He @9was@7 unto me @9as@7 a bear lying in wait, @9and as@7 a lion in secret places.
verse	25	3	11	He hath turned aside my ways, and pulled me in pieces: he hath made me desolate.
verse	25	3	12	He hath bent his bow, and set me as a mark for the arrow.
verse	25	3	13	He hath caused the arrows of his quiver to enter into my reins.
verse	25	3	14	@@I was a derision to all my people; @9and@7 their song all the day.
verse	25	3	15	He hath filled me with bitterness, he hath made me drunken with wormwood.
verse	25	3	16	He hath also broken my teeth with gravel stones, he hath covered me with ashes.
verse	25	3	17	And thou hast removed my soul far off from peace: I forgat prosperity.
verse	25	3	18	And I said, My strength and my hope is perished from the LORD:
verse	25	3	19	Remembering mine affliction and my misery, the wormwood and the gall.
verse	25	3	20	@@My soul hath @9them@7 still in remembrance, and is humbled in me.
verse	25	3	21	This I recall to my mind, therefore have I hope.
verse	25	3	22	@@@9It is of@7 the LORD'S mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not.
verse	25	3	23	@@@9They are@7 new every morning: great @9is@7 thy faithfulness.
verse	25	3	24	@@The LORD @9is@7 my portion, saith my soul; therefore will I hope in him.
verse	25	3	25	@@The LORD @9is@7 good unto them that wait for him, to the soul @9that@7 seeketh him.
verse	25	3	26	@@@9It is@7 good that @9a man@7 should both hope and quietly wait for the salvation of the LORD.
verse	25	3	27	@@@9It is@7 good for a man that he bear the yoke in his youth.
verse	25	3	28	He sitteth alone and keepeth silence, because he hath borne it upon him.
verse	25	3	29	He putteth his mouth in the dust; if so be there may be hope.
verse	25	3	30	@@He giveth @9his@7 cheek to him that smiteth him: he is filled full with reproach.
verse	25	3	31	For the Lord will not cast off for ever:
verse	25	3	32	But though he cause grief, yet will he have compassion according to the multitude of his mercies.
verse	25	3	33	For he doth not afflict willingly nor grieve the children of men.
verse	25	3	34	To crush under his feet all the prisoners of the earth,
verse	25	3	35	To turn aside the right of a man before the face of the most High,
verse	25	3	36	To subvert a man in his cause, the Lord approveth not.
verse	25	3	37	@@Who @9is@7 he @9that@7 saith, and it cometh to pass, @9when@7 the Lord commandeth @9it@7 not?
verse	25	3	38	Out of the mouth of the most High proceedeth not evil and good?
verse	25	3	39	Wherefore doth a living man complain, a man for the punishment of his sins?
verse	25	3	40	Let us search and try our ways, and turn again to the LORD.
verse	25	3	41	@@Let us lift up our heart with @9our@7 hands unto God in the heavens.
verse	25	3	42	We have transgressed and have rebelled: thou hast not pardoned.
verse	25	3	43	Thou hast covered with anger, and persecuted us: thou hast slain, thou hast not pitied.
verse	25	3	44	@@Thou hast covered thyself with a cloud, that @9our@7 prayer should not pass through.
verse	25	3	45	@@Thou hast made us @9as@7 the offscouring and refuse in the midst of the people.
verse	25	3	46	All our enemies have opened their mouths against us.
verse	25	3	47	Fear and a snare is come upon us, desolation and destruction.
verse	25	3	48	Mine eye runneth down with rivers of water for the destruction of the daughter of my people.
verse	25	3	49	Mine eye trickleth down, and ceaseth not, without any intermission,
verse	25	3	50	Till the LORD look down, and behold from heaven.
verse	25	3	51	Mine eye affecteth mine heart because of all the daughters of my city.
verse	25	3	52	Mine enemies chased me sore, like a bird, without cause.
verse	25	3	53	They have cut off my life in the dungeon, and cast a stone upon me.
verse	25	3	54	@@Waters flowed over mine head; @9then@7 I said, I am cut off.
verse	25	3	55	I called upon thy name, O LORD, out of the low dungeon.
verse	25	3	56	Thou hast heard my voice: hide not thine ear at my breathing, at my cry.
verse	25	3	57	@@Thou drewest near in the day @9that@7 I called upon thee: thou saidst, Fear not.
verse	25	3	58	O Lord, thou hast pleaded the causes of my soul; thou hast redeemed my life.
verse	25	3	59	O LORD, thou hast seen my wrong: judge thou my cause.
verse	25	3	60	@@Thou hast seen all their vengeance @9and@7 all their imaginations against me.
verse	25	3	61	@@Thou hast heard their reproach, O LORD, @9and@7 all their imaginations against me;
verse	25	3	62	The lips of those that rose up against me, and their device against me all the day.
verse	25	3	63	@@Behold their sitting down, and their rising up; I @9am@7 their musick.
verse	25	3	64	Render unto them a recompence, O LORD, according to the work of their hands.
verse	25	3	65	Give them sorrow of heart, thy curse unto them.
verse	25	3	66	Persecute and destroy them in anger from under the heavens of the LORD.
verse	25	4	1	@@How is the gold become dim! @9how@7 is the most fine gold changed! the stones of the sanctuary are poured out in the top of every street.
verse	25	4	2	The precious sons of Zion, comparable to fine gold, how are they esteemed as earthen pitchers, the work of the hands of the potter!
verse	25	4	3	@@Even the sea monsters draw out the breast, they give suck to their young ones: the daughter of my people @9is become@7 cruel, like the ostriches in the wilderness.
verse	25	4	4	@@The tongue of the sucking child cleaveth to the roof of his mouth for thirst: the young children ask bread, @9and@7 no man breaketh @9it@7 unto them.
verse	25	4	5	They that did feed delicately are desolate in the streets: they that were brought up in scarlet embrace dunghills.
verse	25	4	6	For the punishment of the iniquity of the daughter of my people is greater than the punishment of the sin of Sodom, that was overthrown as in a moment, and no hands stayed on her.
verse	25	4	7	@@Her Nazarites were purer than snow, they were whiter than milk, they were more ruddy in body than rubies, their polishing @9was@7 of sapphire:
verse	25	4	8	Their visage is blacker than a coal; they are not known in the streets: their skin cleaveth to their bones; it is withered, it is become like a stick.
verse	25	4	9	@@@9They that be@7 slain with the sword are better than @9they that be@7 slain with hunger: for these pine away, stricken through for @9want of@7 the fruits of the field.
verse	25	4	10	The hands of the pitiful women have sodden their own children: they were their meat in the destruction of the daughter of my people.
verse	25	4	11	The LORD hath accomplished his fury; he hath poured out his fierce anger, and hath kindled a fire in Zion, and it hath devoured the foundations thereof.
verse	25	4	12	The kings of the earth, and all the inhabitants of the world, would not have believed that the adversary and the enemy should have entered into the gates of Jerusalem.
verse	25	4	13	@@For the sins of her prophets, @9and@7 the iniquities of her priests, that have shed the blood of the just in the midst of her,
verse	25	4	14	@@They have wandered @9as@7 blind @9men@7 in the streets, they have polluted themselves with blood, so that men could not touch their garments.
verse	25	4	15	@@They cried unto them, Depart ye; @9it is@7 unclean; depart, depart, touch not: when they fled away and wandered, they said among the heathen, They shall no more sojourn @9there. @7
verse	25	4	16	The anger of the LORD hath divided them; he will no more regard them: they respected not the persons of the priests, they favoured not the elders.
verse	25	4	17	@@As for us, our eyes as yet failed for our vain help: in our watching we have watched for a nation @9that@7 could not save @9us. @7
verse	25	4	18	They hunt our steps, that we cannot go in our streets: our end is near, our days are fulfilled; for our end is come.
verse	25	4	19	Our persecutors are swifter than the eagles of the heaven: they pursued us upon the mountains, they laid wait for us in the wilderness.
verse	25	4	20	The breath of our nostrils, the anointed of the LORD, was taken in their pits, of whom we said, Under his shadow we shall live among the heathen.
verse	25	4	21	Rejoice and be glad, O daughter of Edom, that dwellest in the land of Uz; the cup also shall pass through unto thee: thou shalt be drunken, and shalt make thyself naked.
verse	25	4	22	The punishment of thine iniquity is accomplished, O daughter of Zion; he will no more carry thee away into captivity: he will visit thine iniquity, O daughter of Edom; he will discover thy sins.
verse	25	5	1	Remember, O LORD, what is come upon us: consider, and behold our reproach.
verse	25	5	2	Our inheritance is turned to strangers, our houses to aliens.
verse	25	5	3	@@We are orphans and fatherless, our mothers @9are@7 as widows.
verse	25	5	4	We have drunken our water for money; our wood is sold unto us.
verse	25	5	5	@@Our necks @9are@7 under persecution: we labour, @9and@7 have no rest.
verse	25	5	6	@@We have given the hand @9to@7 the Egyptians, @9and to@7 the Assyrians, to be satisfied with bread.
verse	25	5	7	@@Our fathers have sinned, @9and are@7 not; and we have borne their iniquities.
verse	25	5	8	@@Servants have ruled over us: @9there is@7 none that doth deliver @9us@7 out of their hand.
verse	25	5	9	@@We gat our bread with @9the peril of@7 our lives because of the sword of the wilderness.
verse	25	5	10	Our skin was black like an oven because of the terrible famine.
verse	25	5	11	@@They ravished the women in Zion, @9and@7 the maids in the cities of Judah.
verse	25	5	12	Princes are hanged up by their hand: the faces of elders were not honoured.
verse	25	5	13	They took the young men to grind, and the children fell under the wood.
verse	25	5	14	The elders have ceased from the gate, the young men from their musick.
verse	25	5	15	The joy of our heart is ceased; our dance is turned into mourning.
verse	25	5	16	@@The crown is fallen @9from@7 our head: woe unto us, that we have sinned!
verse	25	5	17	@@For this our heart is faint; for these @9things@7 our eyes are dim.
verse	25	5	18	Because of the mountain of Zion, which is desolate, the foxes walk upon it.
verse	25	5	19	Thou, O LORD, remainest for ever; thy throne from generation to generation.
verse	25	5	20	@@Wherefore dost thou forget us for ever, @9and@7 forsake us so long time?
verse	25	5	21	Turn thou us unto thee, O LORD, and we shall be turned; renew our days as of old.
verse	25	5	22	But thou hast utterly rejected us; thou art very wroth against us.
verse	26	1	1	@@Now it came to pass in the thirtieth year, in the fourth @9month,@7 in the fifth @9day@7 of the month, as I @9was@7 among the captives by the river of Chebar, @9that@7 the heavens were opened, and I saw visions of God.
verse	26	1	2	@@In the fifth @9day@7 of the month, which @9was@7 the fifth year of king Jehoiachin's captivity,
verse	26	1	3	The word of the LORD came expressly unto Ezekiel the priest, the son of Buzi, in the land of the Chaldeans by the river Chebar; and the hand of the LORD was there upon him.
verse	26	1	4	@@And I looked, and, behold, a whirlwind came out of the north, a great cloud, and a fire infolding itself, and a brightness @9was@7 about it, and out of the midst thereof as the colour of amber, out of the midst of the fire.
verse	26	1	5	@@Also out of the midst thereof @9came@7 the likeness of four living creatures. And this @9was@7 their appearance; they had the likeness of a man.
verse	26	1	6	And every one had four faces, and every one had four wings.
verse	26	1	7	@@And their feet @9were@7 straight feet; and the sole of their feet @9was@7 like the sole of a calf's foot: and they sparkled like the colour of burnished brass.
verse	26	1	8	@@And @9they had@7 the hands of a man under their wings on their four sides; and they four had their faces and their wings.
verse	26	1	9	@@Their wings @9were@7 joined one to another; they turned not when they went; they went every one straight forward.
verse	26	1	10	As for the likeness of their faces, they four had the face of a man, and the face of a lion, on the right side: and they four had the face of an ox on the left side; they four also had the face of an eagle.
verse	26	1	11	@@Thus @9were@7 their faces: and their wings @9were@7 stretched upward; two @9wings@7 of every one @9were@7 joined one to another, and two covered their bodies.
verse	26	1	12	@@And they went every one straight forward: whither the spirit was to go, they went; @9and@7 they turned not when they went.
verse	26	1	13	@@As for the likeness of the living creatures, their appearance @9was@7 like burning coals of fire, @9and@7 like the appearance of lamps: it went up and down among the living creatures; and the fire was bright, and out of the fire went forth lightning.
verse	26	1	14	And the living creatures ran and returned as the appearance of a flash of lightning.
verse	26	1	15	Now as I beheld the living creatures, behold one wheel upon the earth by the living creatures, with his four faces.
verse	26	1	16	@@The appearance of the wheels and their work @9was@7 like unto the colour of a beryl: and they four had one likeness: and their appearance and their work was as it were a wheel in the middle of a wheel.
verse	26	1	17	@@When they went, they went upon their four sides: @9and@7 they turned not when they went.
verse	26	1	18	@@As for their rings, they were so high that they were dreadful; and their rings @9were@7 full of eyes round about them four.
verse	26	1	19	And when the living creatures went, the wheels went by them: and when the living creatures were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up.
verse	26	1	20	@@Whithersoever the spirit was to go, they went, thither @9was their@7 spirit to go; and the wheels were lifted up over against them: for the spirit of the living creature @9was@7 in the wheels.
verse	26	1	21	@@When those went, @9these@7 went; and when those stood, @9these@7 stood; and when those were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up over against them: for the spirit of the living creature @9was@7 in the wheels.
verse	26	1	22	@@And the likeness of the firmament upon the heads of the living creature @9was@7 as the colour of the terrible crystal, stretched forth over their heads above.
verse	26	1	23	@@And under the firmament @9were@7 their wings straight, the one toward the other: every one had two, which covered on this side, and every one had two, which covered on that side, their bodies.
verse	26	1	24	And when they went, I heard the noise of their wings, like the noise of great waters, as the voice of the Almighty, the voice of speech, as the noise of an host: when they stood, they let down their wings.
verse	26	1	25	@@And there was a voice from the firmament that @9was@7 over their heads, when they stood, and had let down their wings.
verse	26	1	26	@@And above the firmament that @9was@7 over their heads @9was@7 the likeness of a throne, as the appearance of a sapphire stone: and upon the likeness of the throne @9was@7 the likeness as the appearance of a man above upon it.
verse	26	1	27	And I saw as the colour of amber, as the appearance of fire round about within it, from the appearance of his loins even upward, and from the appearance of his loins even downward, I saw as it were the appearance of fire, and it had brightness round about.
verse	26	1	28	@@As the appearance of the bow that is in the cloud in the day of rain, so @9was@7 the appearance of the brightness round about. This @9was@7 the appearance of the likeness of the glory of the LORD. And when I saw @9it,@7 I fell upon my face, and I heard a voice of one that spake.
verse	26	2	1	And he said unto me, Son of man, stand upon thy feet, and I will speak unto thee.
verse	26	2	2	And the spirit entered into me when he spake unto me, and set me upon my feet, that I heard him that spake unto me.
verse	26	2	3	@@And he said unto me, Son of man, I send thee to the children of Israel, to a rebellious nation that hath rebelled against me: they and their fathers have transgressed against me, @9even@7 unto this very day.
verse	26	2	4	@@For @9they are@7 impudent children and stiffhearted. I do send thee unto them; and thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	2	5	@@And they, whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear, (for they @9are@7 a rebellious house,) yet shall know that there hath been a prophet among them.
verse	26	2	6	@@And thou, son of man, be not afraid of them, neither be afraid of their words, though briers and thorns @9be@7 with thee, and thou dost dwell among scorpions: be not afraid of their words, nor be dismayed at their looks, though they @9be@7 a rebellious house.
verse	26	2	7	@@And thou shalt speak my words unto them, whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear: for they @9are@7 most rebellious.
verse	26	2	8	But thou, son of man, hear what I say unto thee; Be not thou rebellious like that rebellious house: open thy mouth, and eat that I give thee.
verse	26	2	9	@@And when I looked, behold, an hand @9was@7 sent unto me; and, lo, a roll of a book @9was@7 therein;
verse	26	2	10	@@And he spread it before me; and it @9was@7 written within and without: and @9there was@7 written therein lamentations, and mourning, and woe.
verse	26	3	1	Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, eat that thou findest; eat this roll, and go speak unto the house of Israel.
verse	26	3	2	So I opened my mouth, and he caused me to eat that roll.
verse	26	3	3	@@And he said unto me, Son of man, cause thy belly to eat, and fill thy bowels with this roll that I give thee. Then did I eat @9it;@7 and it was in my mouth as honey for sweetness.
verse	26	3	4	And he said unto me, Son of man, go, get thee unto the house of Israel, and speak with my words unto them.
verse	26	3	5	@@For thou @9art@7 not sent to a people of a strange speech and of an hard language, @9but@7 to the house of Israel;
verse	26	3	6	Not to many people of a strange speech and of an hard language, whose words thou canst not understand. Surely, had I sent thee to them, they would have hearkened unto thee.
verse	26	3	7	@@But the house of Israel will not hearken unto thee; for they will not hearken unto me: for all the house of Israel @9are@7 impudent and hardhearted.
verse	26	3	8	Behold, I have made thy face strong against their faces, and thy forehead strong against their foreheads.
verse	26	3	9	@@As an adamant harder than flint have I made thy forehead: fear them not, neither be dismayed at their looks, though they @9be@7 a rebellious house.
verse	26	3	10	Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, all my words that I shall speak unto thee receive in thine heart, and hear with thine ears.
verse	26	3	11	And go, get thee to them of the captivity, unto the children of thy people, and speak unto them, and tell them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear.
verse	26	3	12	@@Then the spirit took me up, and I heard behind me a voice of a great rushing, @9saying,@7 Blessed @9be@7 the glory of the LORD from his place.
verse	26	3	13	@@@9I heard@7 also the noise of the wings of the living creatures that touched one another, and the noise of the wheels over against them, and a noise of a great rushing.
verse	26	3	14	So the spirit lifted me up, and took me away, and I went in bitterness, in the heat of my spirit; but the hand of the LORD was strong upon me.
verse	26	3	15	Then I came to them of the captivity at Tel-abib, that dwelt by the river of Chebar, and I sat where they sat, and remained there astonished among them seven days.
verse	26	3	16	And it came to pass at the end of seven days, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	3	17	Son of man, I have made thee a watchman unto the house of Israel: therefore hear the word at my mouth, and give them warning from me.
verse	26	3	18	@@When I say unto the wicked, Thou shalt surely die; and thou givest him not warning, nor speakest to warn the wicked from his wicked way, to save his life; the same wicked @9man@7 shall die in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at thine hand.
verse	26	3	19	Yet if thou warn the wicked, and he turn not from his wickedness, nor from his wicked way, he shall die in his iniquity; but thou hast delivered thy soul.
verse	26	3	20	@@Again, When a righteous @9man@7 doth turn from his righteousness, and commit iniquity, and I lay a stumblingblock before him, he shall die: because thou hast not given him warning, he shall die in his sin, and his righteousness which he hath done shall not be remembered; but his blood will I require at thine hand.
verse	26	3	21	@@Nevertheless if thou warn the righteous @9man,@7 that the righteous sin not, and he doth not sin, he shall surely live, because he is warned; also thou hast delivered thy soul.
verse	26	3	22	And the hand of the LORD was there upon me; and he said unto me, Arise, go forth into the plain, and I will there talk with thee.
verse	26	3	23	Then I arose, and went forth into the plain: and, behold, the glory of the LORD stood there, as the glory which I saw by the river of Chebar: and I fell on my face.
verse	26	3	24	Then the spirit entered into me, and set me upon my feet, and spake with me, and said unto me, Go, shut thyself within thine house.
verse	26	3	25	But thou, O son of man, behold, they shall put bands upon thee, and shall bind thee with them, and thou shalt not go out among them:
verse	26	3	26	@@And I will make thy tongue cleave to the roof of thy mouth, that thou shalt be dumb, and shalt not be to them a reprover: for they @9are@7 a rebellious house.
verse	26	3	27	@@But when I speak with thee, I will open thy mouth, and thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; He that heareth, let him hear; and he that forbeareth, let him forbear: for they @9are@7 a rebellious house.
verse	26	4	1	@@Thou also, son of man, take thee a tile, and lay it before thee, and pourtray upon it the city, @9even@7 Jerusalem:
verse	26	4	2	@@And lay siege against it, and build a fort against it, and cast a mount against it; set the camp also against it, and set @9battering@7 rams against it round about.
verse	26	4	3	@@Moreover take thou unto thee an iron pan, and set it for a wall of iron between thee and the city: and set thy face against it, and it shall be besieged, and thou shalt lay siege against it. This @9shall be@7 a sign to the house of Israel.
verse	26	4	4	@@Lie thou also upon thy left side, and lay the iniquity of the house of Israel upon it: @9according@7 to the number of the days that thou shalt lie upon it thou shalt bear their iniquity.
verse	26	4	5	For I have laid upon thee the years of their iniquity, according to the number of the days, three hundred and ninety days: so shalt thou bear the iniquity of the house of Israel.
verse	26	4	6	And when thou hast accomplished them, lie again on thy right side, and thou shalt bear the iniquity of the house of Judah forty days: I have appointed thee each day for a year.
verse	26	4	7	@@Therefore thou shalt set thy face toward the siege of Jerusalem, and thine arm @9shall be@7 uncovered, and thou shalt prophesy against it.
verse	26	4	8	And, behold, I will lay bands upon thee, and thou shalt not turn thee from one side to another, till thou hast ended the days of thy siege.
verse	26	4	9	@@Take thou also unto thee wheat, and barley, and beans, and lentiles, and millet, and fitches, and put them in one vessel, and make thee bread thereof, @9according@7 to the number of the days that thou shalt lie upon thy side, three hundred and ninety days shalt thou eat thereof.
verse	26	4	10	@@And thy meat which thou shalt eat @9shall be@7 by weight, twenty shekels a day: from time to time shalt thou eat it.
verse	26	4	11	Thou shalt drink also water by measure, the sixth part of an hin: from time to time shalt thou drink.
verse	26	4	12	@@And thou shalt eat it @9as@7 barley cakes, and thou shalt bake it with dung that cometh out of man, in their sight.
verse	26	4	13	And the LORD said, Even thus shall the children of Israel eat their defiled bread among the Gentiles, whither I will drive them.
verse	26	4	14	Then said I, Ah Lord GOD! behold, my soul hath not been polluted: for from my youth up even till now have I not eaten of that which dieth of itself, or is torn in pieces; neither came there abominable flesh into my mouth.
verse	26	4	15	Then he said unto me, Lo, I have given thee cow's dung for man's dung, and thou shalt prepare thy bread therewith.
verse	26	4	16	Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, behold, I will break the staff of bread in Jerusalem: and they shall eat bread by weight, and with care; and they shall drink water by measure, and with astonishment:
verse	26	4	17	That they may want bread and water, and be astonied one with another, and consume away for their iniquity.
verse	26	5	1	@@And thou, son of man, take thee a sharp knife, take thee a barber's razor, and cause @9it@7 to pass upon thine head and upon thy beard: then take thee balances to weigh, and divide the @9hair. @7
verse	26	5	2	@@Thou shalt burn with fire a third part in the midst of the city, when the days of the siege are fulfilled: and thou shalt take a third part, @9and@7 smite about it with a knife: and a third part thou shalt scatter in the wind; and I will draw out a sword after them.
verse	26	5	3	Thou shalt also take thereof a few in number, and bind them in thy skirts.
verse	26	5	4	@@Then take of them again, and cast them into the midst of the fire, and burn them in the fire; @9for@7 thereof shall a fire come forth into all the house of Israel.
verse	26	5	5	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; This @9is@7 Jerusalem: I have set it in the midst of the nations and countries @9that are@7 round about her.
verse	26	5	6	@@And she hath changed my judgments into wickedness more than the nations, and my statutes more than the countries that @9are@7 round about her: for they have refused my judgments and my statutes, they have not walked in them.
verse	26	5	7	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye multiplied more than the nations that @9are@7 round about you, @9and@7 have not walked in my statutes, neither have kept my judgments, neither have done according to the judgments of the nations that @9are@7 round about you;
verse	26	5	8	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I, even I, @9am@7 against thee, and will execute judgments in the midst of thee in the sight of the nations.
verse	26	5	9	And I will do in thee that which I have not done, and whereunto I will not do any more the like, because of all thine abominations.
verse	26	5	10	Therefore the fathers shall eat the sons in the midst of thee, and the sons shall eat their fathers; and I will execute judgments in thee, and the whole remnant of thee will I scatter into all the winds.
verse	26	5	11	@@Wherefore, @9as@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD; Surely, because thou hast defiled my sanctuary with all thy detestable things, and with all thine abominations, therefore will I also diminish @9thee;@7 neither shall mine eye spare, neither will I have any pity.
verse	26	5	12	A third part of thee shall die with the pestilence, and with famine shall they be consumed in the midst of thee: and a third part shall fall by the sword round about thee and I will scatter a third part into all the winds, and I will draw out a sword after them.
verse	26	5	13	@@Thus shall mine anger be accomplished, and I will cause my fury to rest upon them, and I will be comforted: and they shall know that I the LORD have spoken @9it@7 in my zeal, when I have accomplished my fury in them.
verse	26	5	14	@@Moreover I will make thee waste, and a reproach among the nations that @9are@7 round about thee, in the sight of all that pass by.
verse	26	5	15	@@So it shall be a reproach and a taunt, an instruction and an astonishment unto the nations that @9are@7 round about thee, when I shall execute judgments in thee in anger and in fury and in furious rebukes. I the LORD have spoken @9it. @7
verse	26	5	16	@@When I shall send upon them the evil arrows of famine, which shall be for @9their@7 destruction, @9and@7 which I will send to destroy you: and I will increase the famine upon you, and will break your staff of bread:
verse	26	5	17	@@So will I send upon you famine and evil beasts, and they shall bereave thee; and pestilence and blood shall pass through thee; and I will bring the sword upon thee. I the LORD have spoken @9it.@7
verse	26	6	1	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	6	2	Son of man, set thy face toward the mountains of Israel, and prophesy against them,
verse	26	6	3	@@And say, Ye mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus saith the Lord GOD to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys; Behold, I, @9even@7 I, will bring a sword upon you, and I will destroy your high places.
verse	26	6	4	@@And your altars shall be desolate, and your images shall be broken: and I will cast down your slain @9men@7 before your idols.
verse	26	6	5	And I will lay the dead carcases of the children of Israel before their idols; and I will scatter your bones round about your altars.
verse	26	6	6	In all your dwellingplaces the cities shall be laid waste, and the high places shall be desolate; that your altars may be laid waste and made desolate, and your idols may be broken and cease, and your images may be cut down, and your works may be abolished.
verse	26	6	7	@@And the slain shall fall in the midst of you, and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	6	8	@@Yet will I leave a remnant, that ye may have @9some@7 that shall escape the sword among the nations, when ye shall be scattered through the countries.
verse	26	6	9	And they that escape of you shall remember me among the nations whither they shall be carried captives, because I am broken with their whorish heart, which hath departed from me, and with their eyes, which go a whoring after their idols: and they shall lothe themselves for the evils which they have committed in all their abominations.
verse	26	6	10	@@And they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, @9and that@7 I have not said in vain that I would do this evil unto them.
verse	26	6	11	Thus saith the Lord GOD; Smite with thine hand, and stamp with thy foot, and say, Alas for all the evil abominations of the house of Israel! for they shall fall by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence.
verse	26	6	12	He that is far off shall die of the pestilence; and he that is near shall fall by the sword; and he that remaineth and is besieged shall die by the famine: thus will I accomplish my fury upon them.
verse	26	6	13	@@Then shall ye know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when their slain @9men@7 shall be among their idols round about their altars, upon every high hill, in all the tops of the mountains, and under every green tree, and under every thick oak, the place where they did offer sweet savour to all their idols.
verse	26	6	14	@@So will I stretch out my hand upon them, and make the land desolate, yea, more desolate than the wilderness toward Diblath, in all their habitations: and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	7	1	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	7	2	Also, thou son of man, thus saith the Lord GOD unto the land of Israel; An end, the end is come upon the four corners of the land.
verse	26	7	3	@@Now @9is@7 the end @9come@7 upon thee, and I will send mine anger upon thee, and will judge thee according to thy ways, and will recompense upon thee all thine abominations.
verse	26	7	4	@@And mine eye shall not spare thee, neither will I have pity: but I will recompense thy ways upon thee, and thine abominations shall be in the midst of thee: and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	7	5	Thus saith the Lord GOD; An evil, an only evil, behold, is come.
verse	26	7	6	An end is come, the end is come: it watcheth for thee; behold, it is come.
verse	26	7	7	@@The morning is come unto thee, O thou that dwellest in the land: the time is come, the day of trouble @9is@7 near, and not the sounding again of the mountains.
verse	26	7	8	Now will I shortly pour out my fury upon thee, and accomplish mine anger upon thee: and I will judge thee according to thy ways, and will recompense thee for all thine abominations.
verse	26	7	9	@@And mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: I will recompense thee according to thy ways and thine abominations @9that@7 are in the midst of thee; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD that smiteth.
verse	26	7	10	Behold the day, behold, it is come: the morning is gone forth; the rod hath blossomed, pride hath budded.
verse	26	7	11	@@Violence is risen up into a rod of wickedness: none of them @9shall remain,@7 nor of their multitude, nor of any of theirs: neither @9shall there be@7 wailing for them.
verse	26	7	12	@@The time is come, the day draweth near: let not the buyer rejoice, nor the seller mourn: for wrath @9is@7 upon all the multitude thereof.
verse	26	7	13	@@For the seller shall not return to that which is sold, although they were yet alive: for the vision @9is@7 touching the whole multitude thereof, @9which@7 shall not return; neither shall any strengthen himself in the iniquity of his life.
verse	26	7	14	@@They have blown the trumpet, even to make all ready; but none goeth to the battle: for my wrath @9is@7 upon all the multitude thereof.
verse	26	7	15	@@The sword @9is@7 without, and the pestilence and the famine within: he that @9is@7 in the field shall die with the sword; and he that @9is@7 in the city, famine and pestilence shall devour him.
verse	26	7	16	But they that escape of them shall escape, and shall be on the mountains like doves of the valleys, all of them mourning, every one for his iniquity.
verse	26	7	17	@@All hands shall be feeble, and all knees shall be weak @9as@7 water.
verse	26	7	18	@@They shall also gird @9themselves@7 with sackcloth, and horror shall cover them; and shame @9shall be@7 upon all faces, and baldness upon all their heads.
verse	26	7	19	They shall cast their silver in the streets, and their gold shall be removed: their silver and their gold shall not be able to deliver them in the day of the wrath of the LORD: they shall not satisfy their souls, neither fill their bowels: because it is the stumblingblock of their iniquity.
verse	26	7	20	@@As for the beauty of his ornament, he set it in majesty: but they made the images of their abominations @9and@7 of their detestable things therein: therefore have I set it far from them.
verse	26	7	21	And I will give it into the hands of the strangers for a prey, and to the wicked of the earth for a spoil; and they shall pollute it.
verse	26	7	22	@@My face will I turn also from them, and they shall pollute my secret @9place:@7 for the robbers shall enter into it, and defile it.
verse	26	7	23	Make a chain: for the land is full of bloody crimes, and the city is full of violence.
verse	26	7	24	Wherefore I will bring the worst of the heathen, and they shall possess their houses: I will also make the pomp of the strong to cease; and their holy places shall be defiled.
verse	26	7	25	@@Destruction cometh; and they shall seek peace, and @9there shall be@7 none.
verse	26	7	26	Mischief shall come upon mischief, and rumour shall be upon rumour; then shall they seek a vision of the prophet; but the law shall perish from the priest, and counsel from the ancients.
verse	26	7	27	@@The king shall mourn, and the prince shall be clothed with desolation, and the hands of the people of the land shall be troubled: I will do unto them after their way, and according to their deserts will I judge them; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	8	1	@@And it came to pass in the sixth year, in the sixth @9month,@7 in the fifth @9day@7 of the month, @9as@7 I sat in mine house, and the elders of Judah sat before me, that the hand of the Lord GOD fell there upon me.
verse	26	8	2	Then I beheld, and lo a likeness as the appearance of fire: from the appearance of his loins even downward, fire; and from his loins even upward, as the appearance of brightness, as the colour of amber.
verse	26	8	3	@@And he put forth the form of an hand, and took me by a lock of mine head; and the spirit lifted me up between the earth and the heaven, and brought me in the visions of God to Jerusalem, to the door of the inner gate that looketh toward the north; where @9was@7 the seat of the image of jealousy, which provoketh to jealousy.
verse	26	8	4	@@And, behold, the glory of the God of Israel @9was@7 there, according to the vision that I saw in the plain.
verse	26	8	5	Then said he unto me, Son of man, lift up thine eyes now the way toward the north. So I lifted up mine eyes the way toward the north, and behold northward at the gate of the altar this image of jealousy in the entry.
verse	26	8	6	@@He said furthermore unto me, Son of man, seest thou what they do? @9even@7 the great abominations that the house of Israel committeth here, that I should go far off from my sanctuary? but turn thee yet again, @9and@7 thou shalt see greater abominations.
verse	26	8	7	And he brought me to the door of the court; and when I looked, behold a hole in the wall.
verse	26	8	8	Then said he unto me, Son of man, dig now in the wall: and when I had digged in the wall, behold a door.
verse	26	8	9	And he said unto me, Go in, and behold the wicked abominations that they do here.
verse	26	8	10	So I went in and saw; and behold every form of creeping things, and abominable beasts, and all the idols of the house of Israel, pourtrayed upon the wall round about.
verse	26	8	11	And there stood before them seventy men of the ancients of the house of Israel, and in the midst of them stood Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan, with every man his censer in his hand; and a thick cloud of incense went up.
verse	26	8	12	Then said he unto me, Son of man, hast thou seen what the ancients of the house of Israel do in the dark, every man in the chambers of his imagery? for they say, The LORD seeth us not; the LORD hath forsaken the earth.
verse	26	8	13	@@He said also unto me, Turn thee yet again, @9and@7 thou shalt see greater abominations that they do.
verse	26	8	14	@@Then he brought me to the door of the gate of the LORD'S house which @9was@7 toward the north; and, behold, there sat women weeping for Tammuz.
verse	26	8	15	@@Then said he unto me, Hast thou seen @9this,@7 O son of man? turn thee yet again, @9and@7 thou shalt see greater abominations than these.
verse	26	8	16	@@And he brought me into the inner court of the LORD'S house, and, behold, at the door of the temple of the LORD, between the porch and the altar, @9were@7 about five and twenty men, with their backs toward the temple of the LORD, and their faces toward the east; and they worshipped the sun toward the east.
verse	26	8	17	@@Then he said unto me, Hast thou seen @9this,@7 O son of man? Is it a light thing to the house of Judah that they commit the abominations which they commit here? for they have filled the land with violence, and have returned to provoke me to anger: and, lo, they put the branch to their nose.
verse	26	8	18	@@Therefore will I also deal in fury: mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: and though they cry in mine ears with a loud voice, @9yet@7 will I not hear them.
verse	26	9	1	@@He cried also in mine ears with a loud voice, saying, Cause them that have charge over the city to draw near, even every man @9with@7 his destroying weapon in his hand.
verse	26	9	2	@@And, behold, six men came from the way of the higher gate, which lieth toward the north, and every man a slaughter weapon in his hand; and one man among them @9was@7 clothed with linen, with a writer's inkhorn by his side: and they went in, and stood beside the brasen altar.
verse	26	9	3	@@And the glory of the God of Israel was gone up from the cherub, whereupon he was, to the threshold of the house. And he called to the man clothed with linen, which @9had@7 the writer's inkhorn by his side;
verse	26	9	4	And the LORD said unto him, Go through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem, and set a mark upon the foreheads of the men that sigh and that cry for all the abominations that be done in the midst thereof.
verse	26	9	5	And to the others he said in mine hearing, Go ye after him through the city, and smite: let not your eye spare, neither have ye pity:
verse	26	9	6	@@Slay utterly old @9and@7 young, both maids, and little children, and women: but come not near any man upon whom @9is@7 the mark; and begin at my sanctuary. Then they began at the ancient men which @9were@7 before the house.
verse	26	9	7	And he said unto them, Defile the house, and fill the courts with the slain: go ye forth. And they went forth, and slew in the city.
verse	26	9	8	And it came to pass, while they were slaying them, and I was left, that I fell upon my face, and cried, and said, Ah Lord GOD! wilt thou destroy all the residue of Israel in thy pouring out of thy fury upon Jerusalem?
verse	26	9	9	@@Then said he unto me, The iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah @9is@7 exceeding great, and the land is full of blood, and the city full of perverseness: for they say, The LORD hath forsaken the earth, and the LORD seeth not.
verse	26	9	10	@@And as for me also, mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity, @9but@7 I will recompense their way upon their head.
verse	26	9	11	@@And, behold, the man clothed with linen, which @9had@7 the inkhorn by his side, reported the matter, saying, I have done as thou hast commanded me.
verse	26	10	1	Then I looked, and, behold, in the firmament that was above the head of the cherubims there appeared over them as it were a sapphire stone, as the appearance of the likeness of a throne.
verse	26	10	2	@@And he spake unto the man clothed with linen, and said, Go in between the wheels, @9even@7 under the cherub, and fill thine hand with coals of fire from between the cherubims, and scatter @9them@7 over the city. And he went in in my sight.
verse	26	10	3	Now the cherubims stood on the right side of the house, when the man went in; and the cloud filled the inner court.
verse	26	10	4	@@Then the glory of the LORD went up from the cherub, @9and stood@7 over the threshold of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was full of the brightness of the LORD'S glory.
verse	26	10	5	@@And the sound of the cherubims' wings was heard @9even@7 to the outer court, as the voice of the Almighty God when he speaketh.
verse	26	10	6	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 when he had commanded the man clothed with linen, saying, Take fire from between the wheels, from between the cherubims; then he went in, and stood beside the wheels.
verse	26	10	7	@@And @9one@7 cherub stretched forth his hand from between the cherubims unto the fire that @9was@7 between the cherubims, and took @9thereof,@7 and put @9it@7 into the hands of @9him that was@7 clothed with linen: who took @9it,@7 and went out.
verse	26	10	8	And there appeared in the cherubims the form of a man's hand under their wings.
verse	26	10	9	@@And when I looked, behold the four wheels by the cherubims, one wheel by one cherub, and another wheel by another cherub: and the appearance of the wheels @9was@7 as the colour of a beryl stone.
verse	26	10	10	@@And @9as for@7 their appearances, they four had one likeness, as if a wheel had been in the midst of a wheel.
verse	26	10	11	When they went, they went upon their four sides; they turned not as they went, but to the place whither the head looked they followed it; they turned not as they went.
verse	26	10	12	@@And their whole body, and their backs, and their hands, and their wings, and the wheels, @9were@7 full of eyes round about, @9even@7 the wheels that they four had.
verse	26	10	13	As for the wheels, it was cried unto them in my hearing, O wheel.
verse	26	10	14	@@And every one had four faces: the first face @9was@7 the face of a cherub, and the second face @9was@7 the face of a man, and the third the face of a lion, and the fourth the face of an eagle.
verse	26	10	15	@@And the cherubims were lifted up. This @9is@7 the living creature that I saw by the river of Chebar.
verse	26	10	16	And when the cherubims went, the wheels went by them: and when the cherubims lifted up their wings to mount up from the earth, the same wheels also turned not from beside them.
verse	26	10	17	@@When they stood, @9these@7 stood; and when they were lifted up, @9these@7 lifted up themselves @9also:@7 for the spirit of the living creature @9was@7 in them.
verse	26	10	18	Then the glory of the LORD departed from off the threshold of the house, and stood over the cherubims.
verse	26	10	19	@@And the cherubims lifted up their wings, and mounted up from the earth in my sight: when they went out, the wheels also @9were@7 beside them, and @9every one@7 stood at the door of the east gate of the LORD'S house; and the glory of the God of Israel @9was@7 over them above.
verse	26	10	20	@@This @9is@7 the living creature that I saw under the God of Israel by the river of Chebar; and I knew that they @9were@7 the cherubims.
verse	26	10	21	@@Every one had four faces apiece, and every one four wings; and the likeness of the hands of a man @9was@7 under their wings.
verse	26	10	22	@@And the likeness of their faces @9was@7 the same faces which I saw by the river of Chebar, their appearances and themselves: they went every one straight forward.
verse	26	11	1	Moreover the spirit lifted me up, and brought me unto the east gate of the LORD'S house, which looketh eastward: and behold at the door of the gate five and twenty men; among whom I saw Jaazaniah the son of Azur, and Pelatiah the son of Benaiah, the princes of the people.
verse	26	11	2	@@Then said he unto me, Son of man, these @9are@7 the men that devise mischief, and give wicked counsel in this city:
verse	26	11	3	@@Which say, @9It is@7 not near; let us build houses: this @9city is@7 the caldron, and we @9be@7 the flesh.
verse	26	11	4	Therefore prophesy against them, prophesy, O son of man.
verse	26	11	5	@@And the Spirit of the LORD fell upon me, and said unto me, Speak; Thus saith the LORD; Thus have ye said, O house of Israel: for I know the things that come into your mind, @9every one of@7 them.
verse	26	11	6	Ye have multiplied your slain in this city, and ye have filled the streets thereof with the slain.
verse	26	11	7	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Your slain whom ye have laid in the midst of it, they @9are@7 the flesh, and this @9city is@7 the caldron: but I will bring you forth out of the midst of it.
verse	26	11	8	Ye have feared the sword; and I will bring a sword upon you, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	11	9	And I will bring you out of the midst thereof, and deliver you into the hands of strangers, and will execute judgments among you.
verse	26	11	10	@@Ye shall fall by the sword; I will judge you in the border of Israel; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	11	11	@@This @9city@7 shall not be your caldron, neither shall ye be the flesh in the midst thereof; @9but@7 I will judge you in the border of Israel:
verse	26	11	12	@@And ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD: for ye have not walked in my statutes, neither executed my judgments, but have done after the manners of the heathen that @9are@7 round about you.
verse	26	11	13	And it came to pass, when I prophesied, that Pelatiah the son of Benaiah died. Then fell I down upon my face, and cried with a loud voice, and said, Ah Lord GOD! wilt thou make a full end of the remnant of Israel?
verse	26	11	14	Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	11	15	@@Son of man, thy brethren, @9even@7 thy brethren, the men of thy kindred, and all the house of Israel wholly, @9are@7 they unto whom the inhabitants of Jerusalem have said, Get you far from the LORD: unto us is this land given in possession.
verse	26	11	16	Therefore say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Although I have cast them far off among the heathen, and although I have scattered them among the countries, yet will I be to them as a little sanctuary in the countries where they shall come.
verse	26	11	17	Therefore say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will even gather you from the people, and assemble you out of the countries where ye have been scattered, and I will give you the land of Israel.
verse	26	11	18	And they shall come thither, and they shall take away all the detestable things thereof and all the abominations thereof from thence.
verse	26	11	19	And I will give them one heart, and I will put a new spirit within you; and I will take the stony heart out of their flesh, and will give them an heart of flesh:
verse	26	11	20	That they may walk in my statutes, and keep mine ordinances, and do them: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God.
verse	26	11	21	@@But @9as for them@7 whose heart walketh after the heart of their detestable things and their abominations, I will recompense their way upon their own heads, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	11	22	@@Then did the cherubims lift up their wings, and the wheels beside them; and the glory of the God of Israel @9was@7 over them above.
verse	26	11	23	@@And the glory of the LORD went up from the midst of the city, and stood upon the mountain which @9is@7 on the east side of the city.
verse	26	11	24	Afterwards the spirit took me up, and brought me in a vision by the Spirit of God into Chaldea, to them of the captivity. So the vision that I had seen went up from me.
verse	26	11	25	Then I spake unto them of the captivity all the things that the LORD had shewed me.
verse	26	12	1	The word of the LORD also came unto me, saying,
verse	26	12	2	@@Son of man, thou dwellest in the midst of a rebellious house, which have eyes to see, and see not; they have ears to hear, and hear not: for they @9are@7 a rebellious house.
verse	26	12	3	@@Therefore, thou son of man, prepare thee stuff for removing, and remove by day in their sight; and thou shalt remove from thy place to another place in their sight: it may be they will consider, though they @9be@7 a rebellious house.
verse	26	12	4	Then shalt thou bring forth thy stuff by day in their sight, as stuff for removing: and thou shalt go forth at even in their sight, as they that go forth into captivity.
verse	26	12	5	Dig thou through the wall in their sight, and carry out thereby.
verse	26	12	6	@@In their sight shalt thou bear @9it@7 upon @9thy@7 shoulders, @9and@7 carry @9it@7 forth in the twilight: thou shalt cover thy face, that thou see not the ground: for I have set thee @9for@7 a sign unto the house of Israel.
verse	26	12	7	@@And I did so as I was commanded: I brought forth my stuff by day, as stuff for captivity, and in the even I digged through the wall with mine hand; I brought @9it@7 forth in the twilight, @9and@7 I bare @9it@7 upon @9my@7 shoulder in their sight.
verse	26	12	8	And in the morning came the word of the LORD unto me, saying,
verse	26	12	9	Son of man, hath not the house of Israel, the rebellious house, said unto thee, What doest thou?
verse	26	12	10	@@Say thou unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; This burden @9concerneth@7 the prince in Jerusalem, and all the house of Israel that @9are@7 among them.
verse	26	12	11	@@Say, I @9am@7 your sign: like as I have done, so shall it be done unto them: they shall remove @9and@7 go into captivity.
verse	26	12	12	@@And the prince that @9is@7 among them shall bear upon @9his@7 shoulder in the twilight, and shall go forth: they shall dig through the wall to carry out thereby: he shall cover his face, that he see not the ground with @9his@7 eyes.
verse	26	12	13	@@My net also will I spread upon him, and he shall be taken in my snare: and I will bring him to Babylon @9to@7 the land of the Chaldeans; yet shall he not see it, though he shall die there.
verse	26	12	14	@@And I will scatter toward every wind all that @9are@7 about him to help him, and all his bands; and I will draw out the sword after them.
verse	26	12	15	@@And they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I shall scatter them among the nations, and disperse them in the countries.
verse	26	12	16	@@But I will leave a few men of them from the sword, from the famine, and from the pestilence; that they may declare all their abominations among the heathen whither they come; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	12	17	Moreover the word of the LORD came to me, saying,
verse	26	12	18	Son of man, eat thy bread with quaking, and drink thy water with trembling and with carefulness;
verse	26	12	19	@@And say unto the people of the land, Thus saith the Lord GOD of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, @9and@7 of the land of Israel; They shall eat their bread with carefulness, and drink their water with astonishment, that her land may be desolate from all that is therein, because of the violence of all them that dwell therein.
verse	26	12	20	@@And the cities that are inhabited shall be laid waste, and the land shall be desolate; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	12	21	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	12	22	@@Son of man, what @9is@7 that proverb @9that@7 ye have in the land of Israel, saying, The days are prolonged, and every vision faileth?
verse	26	12	23	Tell them therefore, Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will make this proverb to cease, and they shall no more use it as a proverb in Israel; but say unto them, The days are at hand, and the effect of every vision.
verse	26	12	24	For there shall be no more any vain vision nor flattering divination within the house of Israel.
verse	26	12	25	@@For I @9am@7 the LORD: I will speak, and the word that I shall speak shall come to pass; it shall be no more prolonged: for in your days, O rebellious house, will I say the word, and will perform it, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	12	26	Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,
verse	26	12	27	@@Son of man, behold, @9they of@7 the house of Israel say, The vision that he seeth @9is@7 for many days @9to come,@7 and he prophesieth of the times @9that are@7 far off.
verse	26	12	28	Therefore say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; There shall none of my words be prolonged any more, but the word which I have spoken shall be done, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	13	1	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	13	2	Son of man, prophesy against the prophets of Israel that prophesy, and say thou unto them that prophesy out of their own hearts, Hear ye the word of the LORD;
verse	26	13	3	Thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe unto the foolish prophets, that follow their own spirit, and have seen nothing!
verse	26	13	4	O Israel, thy prophets are like the foxes in the deserts.
verse	26	13	5	Ye have not gone up into the gaps, neither made up the hedge for the house of Israel to stand in the battle in the day of the LORD.
verse	26	13	6	@@They have seen vanity and lying divination, saying, The LORD saith: and the LORD hath not sent them: and they have made @9others@7 to hope that they would confirm the word.
verse	26	13	7	@@Have ye not seen a vain vision, and have ye not spoken a lying divination, whereas ye say, The LORD saith @9it;@7 albeit I have not spoken?
verse	26	13	8	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye have spoken vanity, and seen lies, therefore, behold, I @9am@7 against you, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	13	9	@@And mine hand shall be upon the prophets that see vanity, and that divine lies: they shall not be in the assembly of my people, neither shall they be written in the writing of the house of Israel, neither shall they enter into the land of Israel; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the Lord GOD.
verse	26	13	10	@@Because, even because they have seduced my people, saying, Peace; and @9there was@7 no peace; and one built up a wall, and, lo, others daubed it with untempered @9morter: @7
verse	26	13	11	@@Say unto them which daub it with untempered @9morter,@7 that it shall fall: there shall be an overflowing shower; and ye, O great hailstones, shall fall; and a stormy wind shall rend @9it. @7
verse	26	13	12	@@Lo, when the wall is fallen, shall it not be said unto you, Where @9is@7 the daubing wherewith ye have daubed @9it? @7
verse	26	13	13	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I will even rend @9it@7 with a stormy wind in my fury; and there shall be an overflowing shower in mine anger, and great hailstones in @9my@7 fury to consume @9it. @7
verse	26	13	14	@@So will I break down the wall that ye have daubed with untempered @9morter,@7 and bring it down to the ground, so that the foundation thereof shall be discovered, and it shall fall, and ye shall be consumed in the midst thereof: and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	13	15	@@Thus will I accomplish my wrath upon the wall, and upon them that have daubed it with untempered @9morter,@7 and will say unto you, The wall @9is@7 no @9more,@7 neither they that daubed it;
verse	26	13	16	@@@9To wit,@7 the prophets of Israel which prophesy concerning Jerusalem, and which see visions of peace for her, and @9there is@7 no peace, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	13	17	Likewise, thou son of man, set thy face against the daughters of thy people, which prophesy out of their own heart; and prophesy thou against them,
verse	26	13	18	@@And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe to the @9women@7 that sew pillows to all armholes, and make kerchiefs upon the head of every stature to hunt souls! Will ye hunt the souls of my people, and will ye save the souls alive @9that come@7 unto you?
verse	26	13	19	@@And will ye pollute me among my people for handfuls of barley and for pieces of bread, to slay the souls that should not die, and to save the souls alive that should not live, by your lying to my people that hear @9your@7 lies?
verse	26	13	20	@@Wherefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I @9am@7 against your pillows, wherewith ye there hunt the souls to make @9them@7 fly, and I will tear them from your arms, and will let the souls go, @9even@7 the souls that ye hunt to make @9them@7 fly.
verse	26	13	21	@@Your kerchiefs also will I tear, and deliver my people out of your hand, and they shall be no more in your hand to be hunted; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	13	22	Because with lies ye have made the heart of the righteous sad, whom I have not made sad; and strengthened the hands of the wicked, that he should not return from his wicked way, by promising him life:
verse	26	13	23	@@Therefore ye shall see no more vanity, nor divine divinations: for I will deliver my people out of your hand: and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	14	1	Then came certain of the elders of Israel unto me, and sat before me.
verse	26	14	2	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	14	3	Son of man, these men have set up their idols in their heart, and put the stumblingblock of their iniquity before their face: should I be enquired of at all by them?
verse	26	14	4	Therefore speak unto them, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Every man of the house of Israel that setteth up his idols in his heart, and putteth the stumblingblock of his iniquity before his face, and cometh to the prophet; I the LORD will answer him that cometh according to the multitude of his idols;
verse	26	14	5	That I may take the house of Israel in their own heart, because they are all estranged from me through their idols.
verse	26	14	6	@@Therefore say unto the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Repent, and turn @9yourselves@7 from your idols; and turn away your faces from all your abominations.
verse	26	14	7	For every one of the house of Israel, or of the stranger that sojourneth in Israel, which separateth himself from me, and setteth up his idols in his heart, and putteth the stumblingblock of his iniquity before his face, and cometh to a prophet to enquire of him concerning me; I the LORD will answer him by myself:
verse	26	14	8	@@And I will set my face against that man, and will make him a sign and a proverb, and I will cut him off from the midst of my people; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	14	9	And if the prophet be deceived when he hath spoken a thing, I the LORD have deceived that prophet, and I will stretch out my hand upon him, and will destroy him from the midst of my people Israel.
verse	26	14	10	@@And they shall bear the punishment of their iniquity: the punishment of the prophet shall be even as the punishment of him that seeketh @9unto him; @7
verse	26	14	11	That the house of Israel may go no more astray from me, neither be polluted any more with all their transgressions; but that they may be my people, and I may be their God, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	14	12	The word of the LORD came again to me, saying,
verse	26	14	13	Son of man, when the land sinneth against me by trespassing grievously, then will I stretch out mine hand upon it, and will break the staff of the bread thereof, and will send famine upon it, and will cut off man and beast from it:
verse	26	14	14	@@Though these three men, Noah, Daniel, and Job, were in it, they should deliver @9but@7 their own souls by their righteousness, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	14	15	If I cause noisome beasts to pass through the land, and they spoil it, so that it be desolate, that no man may pass through because of the beasts:
verse	26	14	16	@@@9Though@7 these three men @9were@7 in it, @9as@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither sons nor daughters; they only shall be delivered, but the land shall be desolate.
verse	26	14	17	@@Or @9if@7 I bring a sword upon that land, and say, Sword, go through the land; so that I cut off man and beast from it:
verse	26	14	18	@@Though these three men @9were@7 in it, @9as@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither sons nor daughters, but they only shall be delivered themselves.
verse	26	14	19	@@Or @9if@7 I send a pestilence into that land, and pour out my fury upon it in blood, to cut off from it man and beast:
verse	26	14	20	@@Though Noah, Daniel, and Job, @9were@7 in it, @9as@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither son nor daughter; they shall @9but@7 deliver their own souls by their righteousness.
verse	26	14	21	For thus saith the Lord GOD; How much more when I send my four sore judgments upon Jerusalem, the sword, and the famine, and the noisome beast, and the pestilence, to cut off from it man and beast?
verse	26	14	22	@@Yet, behold, therein shall be left a remnant that shall be brought forth, @9both@7 sons and daughters: behold, they shall come forth unto you, and ye shall see their way and their doings: and ye shall be comforted concerning the evil that I have brought upon Jerusalem, @9even@7 concerning all that I have brought upon it.
verse	26	14	23	And they shall comfort you, when ye see their ways and their doings: and ye shall know that I have not done without cause all that I have done in it, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	15	1	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	15	2	@@Son of man, What is the vine tree more than any tree, @9or than@7 a branch which is among the trees of the forest?
verse	26	15	3	@@Shall wood be taken thereof to do any work? or will @9men@7 take a pin of it to hang any vessel thereon?
verse	26	15	4	@@Behold, it is cast into the fire for fuel; the fire devoureth both the ends of it, and the midst of it is burned. Is it meet for @9any@7 work?
verse	26	15	5	@@Behold, when it was whole, it was meet for no work: how much less shall it be meet yet for @9any@7 work, when the fire hath devoured it, and it is burned?
verse	26	15	6	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; As the vine tree among the trees of the forest, which I have given to the fire for fuel, so will I give the inhabitants of Jerusalem.
verse	26	15	7	@@And I will set my face against them; they shall go out from @9one@7 fire, and @9another@7 fire shall devour them; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I set my face against them.
verse	26	15	8	And I will make the land desolate, because they have committed a trespass, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	16	1	Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	16	2	Son of man, cause Jerusalem to know her abominations,
verse	26	16	3	@@And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD unto Jerusalem; Thy birth and thy nativity @9is@7 of the land of Canaan; thy father @9was@7 an Amorite, and thy mother an Hittite.
verse	26	16	4	@@And @9as for@7 thy nativity, in the day thou wast born thy navel was not cut, neither wast thou washed in water to supple @9thee;@7 thou wast not salted at all, nor swaddled at all.
verse	26	16	5	None eye pitied thee, to do any of these unto thee, to have compassion upon thee; but thou wast cast out in the open field, to the lothing of thy person, in the day that thou wast born.
verse	26	16	6	@@And when I passed by thee, and saw thee polluted in thine own blood, I said unto thee @9when thou wast@7 in thy blood, Live; yea, I said unto thee @9when thou wast@7 in thy blood, Live.
verse	26	16	7	@@I have caused thee to multiply as the bud of the field, and thou hast increased and waxen great, and thou art come to excellent ornaments: @9thy@7 breasts are fashioned, and thine hair is grown, whereas thou @9wast@7 naked and bare.
verse	26	16	8	@@Now when I passed by thee, and looked upon thee, behold, thy time @9was@7 the time of love; and I spread my skirt over thee, and covered thy nakedness: yea, I sware unto thee, and entered into a covenant with thee, saith the Lord GOD, and thou becamest mine.
verse	26	16	9	Then washed I thee with water; yea, I throughly washed away thy blood from thee, and I anointed thee with oil.
verse	26	16	10	I clothed thee also with broidered work, and shod thee with badgers' skin, and I girded thee about with fine linen, and I covered thee with silk.
verse	26	16	11	I decked thee also with ornaments, and I put bracelets upon thy hands, and a chain on thy neck.
verse	26	16	12	And I put a jewel on thy forehead, and earrings in thine ears, and a beautiful crown upon thine head.
verse	26	16	13	@@Thus wast thou decked with gold and silver; and thy raiment @9was of@7 fine linen, and silk, and broidered work; thou didst eat fine flour, and honey, and oil: and thou wast exceeding beautiful, and thou didst prosper into a kingdom.
verse	26	16	14	@@And thy renown went forth among the heathen for thy beauty: for it @9was@7 perfect through my comeliness, which I had put upon thee, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	16	15	But thou didst trust in thine own beauty, and playedst the harlot because of thy renown, and pouredst out thy fornications on every one that passed by; his it was.
verse	26	16	16	@@And of thy garments thou didst take, and deckedst thy high places with divers colours, and playedst the harlot thereupon: @9the like things@7 shall not come, neither shall it be so.
verse	26	16	17	Thou hast also taken thy fair jewels of my gold and of my silver, which I had given thee, and madest to thyself images of men, and didst commit whoredom with them,
verse	26	16	18	And tookest thy broidered garments, and coveredst them: and thou hast set mine oil and mine incense before them.
verse	26	16	19	@@My meat also which I gave thee, fine flour, and oil, and honey, @9wherewith@7 I fed thee, thou hast even set it before them for a sweet savour: and @9thus@7 it was, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	16	20	@@Moreover thou hast taken thy sons and thy daughters, whom thou hast borne unto me, and these hast thou sacrificed unto them to be devoured. @9Is this@7 of thy whoredoms a small matter,
verse	26	16	21	@@That thou hast slain my children, and delivered them to cause them to pass through @9the fire@7 for them?
verse	26	16	22	@@And in all thine abominations and thy whoredoms thou hast not remembered the days of thy youth, when thou wast naked and bare, @9and@7 wast polluted in thy blood.
verse	26	16	23	And it came to pass after all thy wickedness, (woe, woe unto thee! saith the Lord GOD;)
verse	26	16	24	@@@9That@7 thou hast also built unto thee an eminent place, and hast made thee an high place in every street.
verse	26	16	25	Thou hast built thy high place at every head of the way, and hast made thy beauty to be abhorred, and hast opened thy feet to every one that passed by, and multiplied thy whoredoms.
verse	26	16	26	Thou hast also committed fornication with the Egyptians thy neighbours, great of flesh; and hast increased thy whoredoms, to provoke me to anger.
verse	26	16	27	@@Behold, therefore I have stretched out my hand over thee, and have diminished thine ordinary @9food,@7 and delivered thee unto the will of them that hate thee, the daughters of the Philistines, which are ashamed of thy lewd way.
verse	26	16	28	Thou hast played the whore also with the Assyrians, because thou wast unsatiable; yea, thou hast played the harlot with them, and yet couldest not be satisfied.
verse	26	16	29	Thou hast moreover multiplied thy fornication in the land of Canaan unto Chaldea; and yet thou wast not satisfied herewith.
verse	26	16	30	@@How weak is thine heart, saith the Lord GOD, seeing thou doest all these @9things,@7 the work of an imperious whorish woman;
verse	26	16	31	In that thou buildest thine eminent place in the head of every way, and makest thine high place in every street; and hast not been as an harlot, in that thou scornest hire;
verse	26	16	32	@@@9But as@7 a wife that committeth adultery, @9which@7 taketh strangers instead of her husband!
verse	26	16	33	They give gifts to all whores: but thou givest thy gifts to all thy lovers, and hirest them, that they may come unto thee on every side for thy whoredom.
verse	26	16	34	@@And the contrary is in thee from @9other@7 women in thy whoredoms, whereas none followeth thee to commit whoredoms: and in that thou givest a reward, and no reward is given unto thee, therefore thou art contrary.
verse	26	16	35	Wherefore, O harlot, hear the word of the LORD:
verse	26	16	36	Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thy filthiness was poured out, and thy nakedness discovered through thy whoredoms with thy lovers, and with all the idols of thy abominations, and by the blood of thy children, which thou didst give unto them;
verse	26	16	37	@@Behold, therefore I will gather all thy lovers, with whom thou hast taken pleasure, and all @9them@7 that thou hast loved, with all @9them@7 that thou hast hated; I will even gather them round about against thee, and will discover thy nakedness unto them, that they may see all thy nakedness.
verse	26	16	38	And I will judge thee, as women that break wedlock and shed blood are judged; and I will give thee blood in fury and jealousy.
verse	26	16	39	And I will also give thee into their hand, and they shall throw down thine eminent place, and shall break down thy high places: they shall strip thee also of thy clothes, and shall take thy fair jewels, and leave thee naked and bare.
verse	26	16	40	They shall also bring up a company against thee, and they shall stone thee with stones, and thrust thee through with their swords.
verse	26	16	41	And they shall burn thine houses with fire, and execute judgments upon thee in the sight of many women: and I will cause thee to cease from playing the harlot, and thou also shalt give no hire any more.
verse	26	16	42	So will I make my fury toward thee to rest, and my jealousy shall depart from thee, and I will be quiet, and will be no more angry.
verse	26	16	43	@@Because thou hast not remembered the days of thy youth, but hast fretted me in all these @9things;@7 behold, therefore I also will recompense thy way upon @9thine@7 head, saith the Lord GOD: and thou shalt not commit this lewdness above all thine abominations.
verse	26	16	44	@@Behold, every one that useth proverbs shall use @9this@7 proverb against thee, saying, As is the mother, @9so is@7 her daughter.
verse	26	16	45	@@Thou @9art@7 thy mother's daughter, that lotheth her husband and her children; and thou @9art@7 the sister of thy sisters, which lothed their husbands and their children: your mother @9was@7 an Hittite, and your father an Amorite.
verse	26	16	46	@@And thine elder sister @9is@7 Samaria, she and her daughters that dwell at thy left hand: and thy younger sister, that dwelleth at thy right hand, @9is@7 Sodom and her daughters.
verse	26	16	47	@@Yet hast thou not walked after their ways, nor done after their abominations: but, as @9if that were@7 a very little @9thing,@7 thou wast corrupted more than they in all thy ways.
verse	26	16	48	@@@9As@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, Sodom thy sister hath not done, she nor her daughters, as thou hast done, thou and thy daughters.
verse	26	16	49	Behold, this was the iniquity of thy sister Sodom, pride, fulness of bread, and abundance of idleness was in her and in her daughters, neither did she strengthen the hand of the poor and needy.
verse	26	16	50	@@And they were haughty, and committed abomination before me: therefore I took them away as I saw @9good. @7
verse	26	16	51	Neither hath Samaria committed half of thy sins; but thou hast multiplied thine abominations more than they, and hast justified thy sisters in all thine abominations which thou hast done.
verse	26	16	52	Thou also, which hast judged thy sisters, bear thine own shame for thy sins that thou hast committed more abominable than they: they are more righteous than thou: yea, be thou confounded also, and bear thy shame, in that thou hast justified thy sisters.
verse	26	16	53	@@When I shall bring again their captivity, the captivity of Sodom and her daughters, and the captivity of Samaria and her daughters, then @9will I bring again@7 the captivity of thy captives in the midst of them:
verse	26	16	54	That thou mayest bear thine own shame, and mayest be confounded in all that thou hast done, in that thou art a comfort unto them.
verse	26	16	55	When thy sisters, Sodom and her daughters, shall return to their former estate, and Samaria and her daughters shall return to their former estate, then thou and thy daughters shall return to your former estate.
verse	26	16	56	For thy sister Sodom was not mentioned by thy mouth in the day of thy pride,
verse	26	16	57	@@Before thy wickedness was discovered, as at the time of @9thy@7 reproach of the daughters of Syria, and all @9that are@7 round about her, the daughters of the Philistines, which despise thee round about.
verse	26	16	58	Thou hast borne thy lewdness and thine abominations, saith the LORD.
verse	26	16	59	For thus saith the Lord GOD; I will even deal with thee as thou hast done, which hast despised the oath in breaking the covenant.
verse	26	16	60	Nevertheless I will remember my covenant with thee in the days of thy youth, and I will establish unto thee an everlasting covenant.
verse	26	16	61	Then thou shalt remember thy ways, and be ashamed, when thou shalt receive thy sisters, thine elder and thy younger: and I will give them unto thee for daughters, but not by thy covenant.
verse	26	16	62	@@And I will establish my covenant with thee; and thou shalt know that I @9am@7 the LORD:
verse	26	16	63	That thou mayest remember, and be confounded, and never open thy mouth any more because of thy shame, when I am pacified toward thee for all that thou hast done, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	17	1	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	17	2	Son of man, put forth a riddle, and speak a parable unto the house of Israel;
verse	26	17	3	And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; A great eagle with great wings, longwinged, full of feathers, which had divers colours, came unto Lebanon, and took the highest branch of the cedar:
verse	26	17	4	He cropped off the top of his young twigs, and carried it into a land of traffick; he set it in a city of merchants.
verse	26	17	5	@@He took also of the seed of the land, and planted it in a fruitful field; he placed @9it@7 by great waters, @9and@7 set it @9as@7 a willow tree.
verse	26	17	6	And it grew, and became a spreading vine of low stature, whose branches turned toward him, and the roots thereof were under him: so it became a vine, and brought forth branches, and shot forth sprigs.
verse	26	17	7	There was also another great eagle with great wings and many feathers: and, behold, this vine did bend her roots toward him, and shot forth her branches toward him, that he might water it by the furrows of her plantation.
verse	26	17	8	It was planted in a good soil by great waters, that it might bring forth branches, and that it might bear fruit, that it might be a goodly vine.
verse	26	17	9	Say thou, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Shall it prosper? shall he not pull up the roots thereof, and cut off the fruit thereof, that it wither? it shall wither in all the leaves of her spring, even without great power or many people to pluck it up by the roots thereof.
verse	26	17	10	@@Yea, behold, @9being@7 planted, shall it prosper? shall it not utterly wither, when the east wind toucheth it? it shall wither in the furrows where it grew.
verse	26	17	11	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	17	12	@@Say now to the rebellious house, Know ye not what these @9things mean?@7 tell @9them,@7 Behold, the king of Babylon is come to Jerusalem, and hath taken the king thereof, and the princes thereof, and led them with him to Babylon;
verse	26	17	13	And hath taken of the king's seed, and made a covenant with him, and hath taken an oath of him: he hath also taken the mighty of the land:
verse	26	17	14	@@That the kingdom might be base, that it might not lift itself up, @9but@7 that by keeping of his covenant it might stand.
verse	26	17	15	@@But he rebelled against him in sending his ambassadors into Egypt, that they might give him horses and much people. Shall he prosper? shall he escape that doeth such @9things?@7 or shall he break the covenant, and be delivered?
verse	26	17	16	@@As I live, saith the Lord GOD, surely in the place @9where@7 the king @9dwelleth@7 that made him king, whose oath he despised, and whose covenant he brake, @9even@7 with him in the midst of Babylon he shall die.
verse	26	17	17	@@Neither shall Pharaoh with @9his@7 mighty army and great company make for him in the war, by casting up mounts, and building forts, to cut off many persons:
verse	26	17	18	@@Seeing he despised the oath by breaking the covenant, when, lo, he had given his hand, and hath done all these @9things,@7 he shall not escape.
verse	26	17	19	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; @9As@7 I live, surely mine oath that he hath despised, and my covenant that he hath broken, even it will I recompense upon his own head.
verse	26	17	20	And I will spread my net upon him, and he shall be taken in my snare, and I will bring him to Babylon, and will plead with him there for his trespass that he hath trespassed against me.
verse	26	17	21	@@And all his fugitives with all his bands shall fall by the sword, and they that remain shall be scattered toward all winds: and ye shall know that I the LORD have spoken @9it.@7
verse	26	17	22	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will also take of the highest branch of the high cedar, and will set @9it;@7 I will crop off from the top of his young twigs a tender one, and will plant @9it@7 upon an high mountain and eminent:
verse	26	17	23	In the mountain of the height of Israel will I plant it: and it shall bring forth boughs, and bear fruit, and be a goodly cedar: and under it shall dwell all fowl of every wing; in the shadow of the branches thereof shall they dwell.
verse	26	17	24	@@And all the trees of the field shall know that I the LORD have brought down the high tree, have exalted the low tree, have dried up the green tree, and have made the dry tree to flourish: I the LORD have brought down the high tree, have exalted the low tree, have dried up the green tree, and have made the dry tree to flourish: I the LORD have spoken and have done @9it.@7
verse	26	18	1	The word of the LORD came unto me again, saying,
verse	26	18	2	What mean ye, that ye use this proverb concerning the land of Israel, saying, The fathers have eaten sour grapes, and the children's teeth are set on edge?
verse	26	18	3	@@@9As@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, ye shall not have @9occasion@7 any more to use this proverb in Israel.
verse	26	18	4	Behold, all souls are mine; as the soul of the father, so also the soul of the son is mine: the soul that sinneth, it shall die.
verse	26	18	5	But if a man be just, and do that which is lawful and right,
verse	26	18	6	@@@9And@7 hath not eaten upon the mountains, neither hath lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel, neither hath defiled his neighbour's wife, neither hath come near to a menstruous woman,
verse	26	18	7	@@And hath not oppressed any, @9but@7 hath restored to the debtor his pledge, hath spoiled none by violence, hath given his bread to the hungry, and hath covered the naked with a garment;
verse	26	18	8	@@He @9that@7 hath not given forth upon usury, neither hath taken any increase, @9that@7 hath withdrawn his hand from iniquity, hath executed true judgment between man and man,
verse	26	18	9	@@Hath walked in my statutes, and hath kept my judgments, to deal truly; he @9is@7 just, he shall surely live, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	18	10	@@If he beget a son @9that is@7 a robber, a shedder of blood, and @9that@7 doeth the like to @9any@7 one of these @9things, @7
verse	26	18	11	@@And that doeth not any of those @9duties,@7 but even hath eaten upon the mountains, and defiled his neighbour's wife,
verse	26	18	12	Hath oppressed the poor and needy, hath spoiled by violence, hath not restored the pledge, and hath lifted up his eyes to the idols, hath committed abomination,
verse	26	18	13	Hath given forth upon usury, and hath taken increase: shall he then live? he shall not live: he hath done all these abominations; he shall surely die; his blood shall be upon him.
verse	26	18	14	@@Now, lo, @9if@7 he beget a son, that seeth all his father's sins which he hath done, and considereth, and doeth not such like,
verse	26	18	15	@@@9That@7 hath not eaten upon the mountains, neither hath lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel, hath not defiled his neighbour's wife,
verse	26	18	16	@@Neither hath oppressed any, hath not withholden the pledge, neither hath spoiled by violence, @9but@7 hath given his bread to the hungry, and hath covered the naked with a garment,
verse	26	18	17	@@@9That@7 hath taken off his hand from the poor, @9that@7 hath not received usury nor increase, hath executed my judgments, hath walked in my statutes; he shall not die for the iniquity of his father, he shall surely live.
verse	26	18	18	@@@9As for@7 his father, because he cruelly oppressed, spoiled his brother by violence, and did @9that@7 which @9is@7 not good among his people, lo, even he shall die in his iniquity.
verse	26	18	19	@@Yet say ye, Why? doth not the son bear the iniquity of the father? When the son hath done that which is lawful and right, @9and@7 hath kept all my statutes, and hath done them, he shall surely live.
verse	26	18	20	The soul that sinneth, it shall die. The son shall not bear the iniquity of the father, neither shall the father bear the iniquity of the son: the righteousness of the righteous shall be upon him, and the wickedness of the wicked shall be upon him.
verse	26	18	21	But if the wicked will turn from all his sins that he hath committed, and keep all my statutes, and do that which is lawful and right, he shall surely live, he shall not die.
verse	26	18	22	All his transgressions that he hath committed, they shall not be mentioned unto him: in his righteousness that he hath done he shall live.
verse	26	18	23	@@Have I any pleasure at all that the wicked should die? saith the Lord GOD: @9and@7 not that he should return from his ways, and live?
verse	26	18	24	@@But when the righteous turneth away from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity, @9and@7 doeth according to all the abominations that the wicked @9man@7 doeth, shall he live? All his righteousness that he hath done shall not be mentioned: in his trespass that he hath trespassed, and in his sin that he hath sinned, in them shall he die.
verse	26	18	25	Yet ye say, The way of the Lord is not equal. Hear now, O house of Israel; Is not my way equal? are not your ways unequal?
verse	26	18	26	@@When a righteous @9man@7 turneth away from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity, and dieth in them; for his iniquity that he hath done shall he die.
verse	26	18	27	@@Again, when the wicked @9man@7 turneth away from his wickedness that he hath committed, and doeth that which is lawful and right, he shall save his soul alive.
verse	26	18	28	Because he considereth, and turneth away from all his transgressions that he hath committed, he shall surely live, he shall not die.
verse	26	18	29	Yet saith the house of Israel, The way of the Lord is not equal. O house of Israel, are not my ways equal? are not your ways unequal?
verse	26	18	30	@@Therefore I will judge you, O house of Israel, every one according to his ways, saith the Lord GOD. Repent, and turn @9yourselves@7 from all your transgressions; so iniquity shall not be your ruin.
verse	26	18	31	Cast away from you all your transgressions, whereby ye have transgressed; and make you a new heart and a new spirit: for why will ye die, O house of Israel?
verse	26	18	32	@@For I have no pleasure in the death of him that dieth, saith the Lord GOD: wherefore turn @9yourselves,@7 and live ye.
verse	26	19	1	Moreover take thou up a lamentation for the princes of Israel,
verse	26	19	2	@@And say, What @9is@7 thy mother? A lioness: she lay down among lions, she nourished her whelps among young lions.
verse	26	19	3	And she brought up one of her whelps: it became a young lion, and it learned to catch the prey; it devoured men.
verse	26	19	4	The nations also heard of him; he was taken in their pit, and they brought him with chains unto the land of Egypt.
verse	26	19	5	@@Now when she saw that she had waited, @9and@7 her hope was lost, then she took another of her whelps, @9and@7 made him a young lion.
verse	26	19	6	@@And he went up and down among the lions, he became a young lion, and learned to catch the prey, @9and@7 devoured men.
verse	26	19	7	And he knew their desolate palaces, and he laid waste their cities; and the land was desolate, and the fulness thereof, by the noise of his roaring.
verse	26	19	8	Then the nations set against him on every side from the provinces, and spread their net over him: he was taken in their pit.
verse	26	19	9	And they put him in ward in chains, and brought him to the king of Babylon: they brought him into holds, that his voice should no more be heard upon the mountains of Israel.
verse	26	19	10	@@Thy mother @9is@7 like a vine in thy blood, planted by the waters: she was fruitful and full of branches by reason of many waters.
verse	26	19	11	And she had strong rods for the sceptres of them that bare rule, and her stature was exalted among the thick branches, and she appeared in her height with the multitude of her branches.
verse	26	19	12	But she was plucked up in fury, she was cast down to the ground, and the east wind dried up her fruit: her strong rods were broken and withered; the fire consumed them.
verse	26	19	13	@@And now she @9is@7 planted in the wilderness, in a dry and thirsty ground.
verse	26	19	14	@@And fire is gone out of a rod of her branches, @9which@7 hath devoured her fruit, so that she hath no strong rod @9to be@7 a sceptre to rule. This @9is@7 a lamentation, and shall be for a lamentation.
verse	26	20	1	@@And it came to pass in the seventh year, in the fifth @9month,@7 the tenth @9day@7 of the month, @9that@7 certain of the elders of Israel came to enquire of the LORD, and sat before me.
verse	26	20	2	Then came the word of the LORD unto me, saying,
verse	26	20	3	@@Son of man, speak unto the elders of Israel, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Are ye come to enquire of me? @9As@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will not be enquired of by you.
verse	26	20	4	@@Wilt thou judge them, son of man, wilt thou judge @9them?@7 cause them to know the abominations of their fathers:
verse	26	20	5	@@And say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day when I chose Israel, and lifted up mine hand unto the seed of the house of Jacob, and made myself known unto them in the land of Egypt, when I lifted up mine hand unto them, saying, I @9am@7 the LORD your God;
verse	26	20	6	@@In the day @9that@7 I lifted up mine hand unto them, to bring them forth of the land of Egypt into a land that I had espied for them, flowing with milk and honey, which @9is@7 the glory of all lands:
verse	26	20	7	@@Then said I unto them, Cast ye away every man the abominations of his eyes, and defile not yourselves with the idols of Egypt: I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	26	20	8	But they rebelled against me, and would not hearken unto me: they did not every man cast away the abominations of their eyes, neither did they forsake the idols of Egypt: then I said, I will pour out my fury upon them to accomplish my anger against them in the midst of the land of Egypt.
verse	26	20	9	@@But I wrought for my name's sake, that it should not be polluted before the heathen, among whom they @9were,@7 in whose sight I made myself known unto them, in bringing them forth out of the land of Egypt.
verse	26	20	10	Wherefore I caused them to go forth out of the land of Egypt, and brought them into the wilderness.
verse	26	20	11	@@And I gave them my statutes, and shewed them my judgments, which @9if@7 a man do, he shall even live in them.
verse	26	20	12	@@Moreover also I gave them my sabbaths, to be a sign between me and them, that they might know that I @9am@7 the LORD that sanctify them.
verse	26	20	13	@@But the house of Israel rebelled against me in the wilderness: they walked not in my statutes, and they despised my judgments, which @9if@7 a man do, he shall even live in them; and my sabbaths they greatly polluted: then I said, I would pour out my fury upon them in the wilderness, to consume them.
verse	26	20	14	But I wrought for my name's sake, that it should not be polluted before the heathen, in whose sight I brought them out.
verse	26	20	15	@@Yet also I lifted up my hand unto them in the wilderness, that I would not bring them into the land which I had given @9them,@7 flowing with milk and honey, which @9is@7 the glory of all lands;
verse	26	20	16	Because they despised my judgments, and walked not in my statutes, but polluted my sabbaths: for their heart went after their idols.
verse	26	20	17	Nevertheless mine eye spared them from destroying them, neither did I make an end of them in the wilderness.
verse	26	20	18	But I said unto their children in the wilderness, Walk ye not in the statutes of your fathers, neither observe their judgments, nor defile yourselves with their idols:
verse	26	20	19	@@I @9am@7 the LORD your God; walk in my statutes, and keep my judgments, and do them;
verse	26	20	20	@@And hallow my sabbaths; and they shall be a sign between me and you, that ye may know that I @9am@7 the LORD your God.
verse	26	20	21	@@Notwithstanding the children rebelled against me: they walked not in my statutes, neither kept my judgments to do them, which @9if@7 a man do, he shall even live in them; they polluted my sabbaths: then I said, I would pour out my fury upon them, to accomplish my anger against them in the wilderness.
verse	26	20	22	Nevertheless I withdrew mine hand, and wrought for my name's sake, that it should not be polluted in the sight of the heathen, in whose sight I brought them forth.
verse	26	20	23	I lifted up mine hand unto them also in the wilderness, that I would scatter them among the heathen, and disperse them through the countries;
verse	26	20	24	Because they had not executed my judgments, but had despised my statutes, and had polluted my sabbaths, and their eyes were after their fathers' idols.
verse	26	20	25	@@Wherefore I gave them also statutes @9that were@7 not good, and judgments whereby they should not live;
verse	26	20	26	@@And I polluted them in their own gifts, in that they caused to pass through @9the fire@7 all that openeth the womb, that I might make them desolate, to the end that they might know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	20	27	Therefore, son of man, speak unto the house of Israel, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Yet in this your fathers have blasphemed me, in that they have committed a trespass against me.
verse	26	20	28	@@@9For@7 when I had brought them into the land, @9for@7 the which I lifted up mine hand to give it to them, then they saw every high hill, and all the thick trees, and they offered there their sacrifices, and there they presented the provocation of their offering: there also they made their sweet savour, and poured out there their drink offerings.
verse	26	20	29	@@Then I said unto them, What @9is@7 the high place whereunto ye go? And the name thereof is called Bamah unto this day.
verse	26	20	30	Wherefore say unto the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Are ye polluted after the manner of your fathers? and commit ye whoredom after their abominations?
verse	26	20	31	@@For when ye offer your gifts, when ye make your sons to pass through the fire, ye pollute yourselves with all your idols, even unto this day: and shall I be enquired of by you, O house of Israel? @9As@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will not be enquired of by you.
verse	26	20	32	And that which cometh into your mind shall not be at all, that ye say, We will be as the heathen, as the families of the countries, to serve wood and stone.
verse	26	20	33	@@@9As@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, surely with a mighty hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with fury poured out, will I rule over you:
verse	26	20	34	And I will bring you out from the people, and will gather you out of the countries wherein ye are scattered, with a mighty hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with fury poured out.
verse	26	20	35	And I will bring you into the wilderness of the people, and there will I plead with you face to face.
verse	26	20	36	Like as I pleaded with your fathers in the wilderness of the land of Egypt, so will I plead with you, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	20	37	And I will cause you to pass under the rod, and I will bring you into the bond of the covenant:
verse	26	20	38	@@And I will purge out from among you the rebels, and them that transgress against me: I will bring them forth out of the country where they sojourn, and they shall not enter into the land of Israel: and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	20	39	@@As for you, O house of Israel, thus saith the Lord GOD; Go ye, serve ye every one his idols, and hereafter @9also,@7 if ye will not hearken unto me: but pollute ye my holy name no more with your gifts, and with your idols.
verse	26	20	40	For in mine holy mountain, in the mountain of the height of Israel, saith the Lord GOD, there shall all the house of Israel, all of them in the land, serve me: there will I accept them, and there will I require your offerings, and the firstfruits of your oblations, with all your holy things.
verse	26	20	41	I will accept you with your sweet savour, when I bring you out from the people, and gather you out of the countries wherein ye have been scattered; and I will be sanctified in you before the heathen.
verse	26	20	42	@@And ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I shall bring you into the land of Israel, into the country @9for@7 the which I lifted up mine hand to give it to your fathers.
verse	26	20	43	And there shall ye remember your ways, and all your doings, wherein ye have been defiled; and ye shall lothe yourselves in your own sight for all your evils that ye have committed.
verse	26	20	44	@@And ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I have wrought with you for my name's sake, not according to your wicked ways, nor according to your corrupt doings, O ye house of Israel, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	20	45	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	20	46	@@Son of man, set thy face toward the south, and drop @9thy word@7 toward the south, and prophesy against the forest of the south field;
verse	26	20	47	And say to the forest of the south, Hear the word of the LORD; Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will kindle a fire in thee, and it shall devour every green tree in thee, and every dry tree: the flaming flame shall not be quenched, and all faces from the south to the north shall be burned therein.
verse	26	20	48	And all flesh shall see that I the LORD have kindled it: it shall not be quenched.
verse	26	20	49	Then said I, Ah Lord GOD! they say of me, Doth he not speak parables?
verse	26	21	1	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	21	2	@@Son of man, set thy face toward Jerusalem, and drop @9thy word@7 toward the holy places, and prophesy against the land of Israel,
verse	26	21	3	@@And say to the land of Israel, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I @9am@7 against thee, and will draw forth my sword out of his sheath, and will cut off from thee the righteous and the wicked.
verse	26	21	4	Seeing then that I will cut off from thee the righteous and the wicked, therefore shall my sword go forth out of his sheath against all flesh from the south to the north:
verse	26	21	5	That all flesh may know that I the LORD have drawn forth my sword out of his sheath: it shall not return any more.
verse	26	21	6	@@Sigh therefore, thou son of man, with the breaking of @9thy@7 loins; and with bitterness sigh before their eyes.
verse	26	21	7	@@And it shall be, when they say unto thee, Wherefore sighest thou? that thou shalt answer, For the tidings; because it cometh: and every heart shall melt, and all hands shall be feeble, and every spirit shall faint, and all knees shall be weak @9as@7 water: behold, it cometh, and shall be brought to pass, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	21	8	Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
