verse	26	26	8	He shall slay with the sword thy daughters in the field: and he shall make a fort against thee, and cast a mount against thee, and lift up the buckler against thee.
verse	26	26	9	And he shall set engines of war against thy walls, and with his axes he shall break down thy towers.
verse	26	26	10	By reason of the abundance of his horses their dust shall cover thee: thy walls shall shake at the noise of the horsemen, and of the wheels, and of the chariots, when he shall enter into thy gates, as men enter into a city wherein is made a breach.
verse	26	26	11	With the hoofs of his horses shall he tread down all thy streets: he shall slay thy people by the sword, and thy strong garrisons shall go down to the ground.
verse	26	26	12	And they shall make a spoil of thy riches, and make a prey of thy merchandise: and they shall break down thy walls, and destroy thy pleasant houses: and they shall lay thy stones and thy timber and thy dust in the midst of the water.
verse	26	26	13	And I will cause the noise of thy songs to cease; and the sound of thy harps shall be no more heard.
verse	26	26	14	@@And I will make thee like the top of a rock: thou shalt be @9a place@7 to spread nets upon; thou shalt be built no more: for I the LORD have spoken @9it,@7 saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	26	15	Thus saith the Lord GOD to Tyrus; Shall not the isles shake at the sound of thy fall, when the wounded cry, when the slaughter is made in the midst of thee?
verse	26	26	16	@@Then all the princes of the sea shall come down from their thrones, and lay away their robes, and put off their broidered garments: they shall clothe themselves with trembling; they shall sit upon the ground, and shall tremble at @9every@7 moment, and be astonished at thee.
verse	26	26	17	@@And they shall take up a lamentation for thee, and say to thee, How art thou destroyed, @9that wast@7 inhabited of seafaring men, the renowned city, which wast strong in the sea, she and her inhabitants, which cause their terror @9to be@7 on all that haunt it!
verse	26	26	18	@@Now shall the isles tremble in the day of thy fall; yea, the isles that @9are@7 in the sea shall be troubled at thy departure.
verse	26	26	19	For thus saith the Lord GOD; When I shall make thee a desolate city, like the cities that are not inhabited; when I shall bring up the deep upon thee, and great waters shall cover thee;
verse	26	26	20	When I shall bring thee down with them that descend into the pit, with the people of old time, and shall set thee in the low parts of the earth, in places desolate of old, with them that go down to the pit, that thou be not inhabited; and I shall set glory in the land of the living;
verse	26	26	21	@@I will make thee a terror, and thou @9shalt be@7 no @9more:@7 though thou be sought for, yet shalt thou never be found again, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	27	1	The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,
verse	26	27	2	Now, thou son of man, take up a lamentation for Tyrus;
verse	26	27	3	@@And say unto Tyrus, O thou that art situate at the entry of the sea, @9which art@7 a merchant of the people for many isles, Thus saith the Lord GOD; O Tyrus, thou hast said, I @9am@7 of perfect beauty.
verse	26	27	4	@@Thy borders @9are@7 in the midst of the seas, thy builders have perfected thy beauty.
verse	26	27	5	@@They have made all thy @9ship@7 boards of fir trees of Senir: they have taken cedars from Lebanon to make masts for thee.
verse	26	27	6	@@@9Of@7 the oaks of Bashan have they made thine oars; the company of the Ashurites have made thy benches @9of@7 ivory, @9brought@7 out of the isles of Chittim.
verse	26	27	7	Fine linen with broidered work from Egypt was that which thou spreadest forth to be thy sail; blue and purple from the isles of Elishah was that which covered thee.
verse	26	27	8	@@The inhabitants of Zidon and Arvad were thy mariners: thy wise @9men,@7 O Tyrus, @9that@7 were in thee, were thy pilots.
verse	26	27	9	@@The ancients of Gebal and the wise @9men@7 thereof were in thee thy calkers: all the ships of the sea with their mariners were in thee to occupy thy merchandise.
verse	26	27	10	They of Persia and of Lud and of Phut were in thine army, thy men of war: they hanged the shield and helmet in thee; they set forth thy comeliness.
verse	26	27	11	@@The men of Arvad with thine army @9were@7 upon thy walls round about, and the Gammadims were in thy towers: they hanged their shields upon thy walls round about; they have made thy beauty perfect.
verse	26	27	12	@@Tarshish @9was@7 thy merchant by reason of the multitude of all @9kind of@7 riches; with silver, iron, tin, and lead, they traded in thy fairs.
verse	26	27	13	@@Javan, Tubal, and Meshech, they @9were@7 thy merchants: they traded the persons of men and vessels of brass in thy market.
verse	26	27	14	They of the house of Togarmah traded in thy fairs with horses and horsemen and mules.
verse	26	27	15	@@The men of Dedan @9were@7 thy merchants; many isles @9were@7 the merchandise of thine hand: they brought thee @9for@7 a present horns of ivory and ebony.
verse	26	27	16	@@Syria @9was@7 thy merchant by reason of the multitude of the wares of thy making: they occupied in thy fairs with emeralds, purple, and broidered work, and fine linen, and coral, and agate.
verse	26	27	17	@@Judah, and the land of Israel, they @9were@7 thy merchants: they traded in thy market wheat of Minnith, and Pannag, and honey, and oil, and balm.
verse	26	27	18	@@Damascus @9was@7 thy merchant in the multitude of the wares of thy making, for the multitude of all riches; in the wine of Helbon, and white wool.
