verse	26	27	20	@@Dedan @9was@7 thy merchant in precious clothes for chariots.
verse	26	27	21	@@Arabia, and all the princes of Kedar, they occupied with thee in lambs, and rams, and goats: in these @9were they@7 thy merchants.
verse	26	27	22	@@The merchants of Sheba and Raamah, they @9were@7 thy merchants: they occupied in thy fairs with chief of all spices, and with all precious stones, and gold.
verse	26	27	23	@@Haran, and Canneh, and Eden, the merchants of Sheba, Asshur, @9and@7 Chilmad, @9were@7 thy merchants.
verse	26	27	24	@@These @9were@7 thy merchants in all sorts @9of things,@7 in blue clothes, and broidered work, and in chests of rich apparel, bound with cords, and made of cedar, among thy merchandise.
verse	26	27	25	The ships of Tarshish did sing of thee in thy market: and thou wast replenished, and made very glorious in the midst of the seas.
verse	26	27	26	Thy rowers have brought thee into great waters: the east wind hath broken thee in the midst of the seas.
verse	26	27	27	@@Thy riches, and thy fairs, thy merchandise, thy mariners, and thy pilots, thy calkers, and the occupiers of thy merchandise, and all thy men of war, that @9are@7 in thee, and in all thy company which @9is@7 in the midst of thee, shall fall into the midst of the seas in the day of thy ruin.
verse	26	27	28	The suburbs shall shake at the sound of the cry of thy pilots.
verse	26	27	29	@@And all that handle the oar, the mariners, @9and@7 all the pilots of the sea, shall come down from their ships, they shall stand upon the land;
verse	26	27	30	And shall cause their voice to be heard against thee, and shall cry bitterly, and shall cast up dust upon their heads, they shall wallow themselves in the ashes:
verse	26	27	31	@@And they shall make themselves utterly bald for thee, and gird them with sackcloth, and they shall weep for thee with bitterness of heart @9and@7 bitter wailing.
verse	26	27	32	@@And in their wailing they shall take up a lamentation for thee, and lament over thee, @9saying,@7 What @9city is@7 like Tyrus, like the destroyed in the midst of the sea?
verse	26	27	33	When thy wares went forth out of the seas, thou filledst many people; thou didst enrich the kings of the earth with the multitude of thy riches and of thy merchandise.
verse	26	27	34	@@In the time @9when@7 thou shalt be broken by the seas in the depths of the waters thy merchandise and all thy company in the midst of thee shall fall.
verse	26	27	35	@@All the inhabitants of the isles shall be astonished at thee, and their kings shall be sore afraid, they shall be troubled in @9their@7 countenance.
verse	26	27	36	@@The merchants among the people shall hiss at thee; thou @9shalt be@7 a terror, and never shalt be any more.
verse	26	28	1	The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,
verse	26	28	2	@@Son of man, say unto the prince of Tyrus, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thine heart @9is@7 lifted up, and thou hast said, I @9am@7 a God, I sit @9in@7 the seat of God, in the midst of the seas; yet thou @9art@7 a man, and not God, though thou set thine heart as the heart of God:
verse	26	28	3	@@Behold, thou @9art@7 wiser than Daniel; there is no secret that they can hide from thee:
verse	26	28	4	With thy wisdom and with thine understanding thou hast gotten thee riches, and hast gotten gold and silver into thy treasures:
verse	26	28	5	@@By thy great wisdom @9and@7 by thy traffick hast thou increased thy riches, and thine heart is lifted up because of thy riches:
verse	26	28	6	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast set thine heart as the heart of God;
verse	26	28	7	Behold, therefore I will bring strangers upon thee, the terrible of the nations: and they shall draw their swords against the beauty of thy wisdom, and they shall defile thy brightness.
verse	26	28	8	@@They shall bring thee down to the pit, and thou shalt die the deaths of @9them that are@7 slain in the midst of the seas.
verse	26	28	9	@@Wilt thou yet say before him that slayeth thee, I @9am@7 God? but thou @9shalt be@7 a man, and no God, in the hand of him that slayeth thee.
verse	26	28	10	@@Thou shalt die the deaths of the uncircumcised by the hand of strangers: for I have spoken @9it,@7 saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	28	11	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	28	12	Son of man, take up a lamentation upon the king of Tyrus, and say unto him, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Thou sealest up the sum, full of wisdom, and perfect in beauty.
verse	26	28	13	@@Thou hast been in Eden the garden of God; every precious stone @9was@7 thy covering, the sardius, topaz, and the diamond, the beryl, the onyx, and the jasper, the sapphire, the emerald, and the carbuncle, and gold: the workmanship of thy tabrets and of thy pipes was prepared in thee in the day that thou wast created.
verse	26	28	14	@@Thou @9art@7 the anointed cherub that covereth; and I have set thee @9so:@7 thou wast upon the holy mountain of God; thou hast walked up and down in the midst of the stones of fire.
verse	26	28	15	@@Thou @9wast@7 perfect in thy ways from the day that thou wast created, till iniquity was found in thee.
verse	26	28	16	By the multitude of thy merchandise they have filled the midst of thee with violence, and thou hast sinned: therefore I will cast thee as profane out of the mountain of God: and I will destroy thee, O covering cherub, from the midst of the stones of fire.
verse	26	28	17	Thine heart was lifted up because of thy beauty, thou hast corrupted thy wisdom by reason of thy brightness: I will cast thee to the ground, I will lay thee before kings, that they may behold thee.
verse	26	28	18	Thou hast defiled thy sanctuaries by the multitude of thine iniquities, by the iniquity of thy traffick; therefore will I bring forth a fire from the midst of thee, it shall devour thee, and I will bring thee to ashes upon the earth in the sight of all them that behold thee.
verse	26	28	19	@@All they that know thee among the people shall be astonished at thee: thou shalt be a terror, and never @9shalt@7 thou @9be@7 any more.
verse	26	28	20	Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	28	21	Son of man, set thy face against Zidon, and prophesy against it,
verse	26	28	22	@@And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I @9am@7 against thee, O Zidon; and I will be glorified in the midst of thee: and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I shall have executed judgments in her, and shall be sanctified in her.
verse	26	28	23	@@For I will send into her pestilence, and blood into her street; and the wounded shall be judged in the midst of her by the sword upon her on every side; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	28	24	@@And there shall be no more a pricking brier unto the house of Israel, nor @9any@7 grieving thorn of all @9that are@7 round about them, that despised them; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the Lord GOD.
verse	26	28	25	Thus saith the Lord GOD; When I shall have gathered the house of Israel from the people among whom they are scattered, and shall be sanctified in them in the sight of the heathen, then shall they dwell in their land that I have given to my servant Jacob.
verse	26	28	26	@@And they shall dwell safely therein, and shall build houses, and plant vineyards; yea, they shall dwell with confidence, when I have executed judgments upon all those that despise them round about them; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD their God.
verse	26	29	1	@@In the tenth year, in the tenth @9month,@7 in the twelfth @9day@7 of the month, the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	29	2	Son of man, set thy face against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and prophesy against him, and against all Egypt:
verse	26	29	3	@@Speak, and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I @9am@7 against thee, Pharaoh king of Egypt, the great dragon that lieth in the midst of his rivers, which hath said, My river @9is@7 mine own, and I have made @9it@7 for myself.
verse	26	29	4	But I will put hooks in thy jaws, and I will cause the fish of thy rivers to stick unto thy scales, and I will bring thee up out of the midst of thy rivers, and all the fish of thy rivers shall stick unto thy scales.
verse	26	29	5	@@And I will leave thee @9thrown@7 into the wilderness, thee and all the fish of thy rivers: thou shalt fall upon the open fields; thou shalt not be brought together, nor gathered: I have given thee for meat to the beasts of the field and to the fowls of the heaven.
verse	26	29	6	@@And all the inhabitants of Egypt shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, because they have been a staff of reed to the house of Israel.
verse	26	29	7	When they took hold of thee by thy hand, thou didst break, and rend all their shoulder: and when they leaned upon thee, thou brakest, and madest all their loins to be at a stand.
verse	26	29	8	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will bring a sword upon thee, and cut off man and beast out of thee.
verse	26	29	9	@@And the land of Egypt shall be desolate and waste; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD: because he hath said, The river @9is@7 mine, and I have made @9it. @7
verse	26	29	10	@@Behold, therefore I @9am@7 against thee, and against thy rivers, and I will make the land of Egypt utterly waste @9and@7 desolate, from the tower of Syene even unto the border of Ethiopia.
verse	26	29	11	No foot of man shall pass through it, nor foot of beast shall pass through it, neither shall it be inhabited forty years.
verse	26	29	12	@@And I will make the land of Egypt desolate in the midst of the countries @9that are@7 desolate, and her cities among the cities @9that are@7 laid waste shall be desolate forty years: and I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries.
verse	26	29	13	Yet thus saith the Lord GOD; At the end of forty years will I gather the Egyptians from the people whither they were scattered:
verse	26	29	14	@@And I will bring again the captivity of Egypt, and will cause them to return @9into@7 the land of Pathros, into the land of their habitation; and they shall be there a base kingdom.
verse	26	29	15	It shall be the basest of the kingdoms; neither shall it exalt itself any more above the nations: for I will diminish them, that they shall no more rule over the nations.
verse	26	29	16	@@And it shall be no more the confidence of the house of Israel, which bringeth @9their@7 iniquity to remembrance, when they shall look after them: but they shall know that I @9am@7 the Lord GOD.
verse	26	29	17	@@And it came to pass in the seven and twentieth year, in the first @9month,@7 in the first @9day@7 of the month, the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	29	18	@@Son of man, Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon caused his army to serve a great service against Tyrus: every head @9was@7 made bald, and every shoulder @9was@7 peeled: yet had he no wages, nor his army, for Tyrus, for the service that he had served against it:
verse	26	29	19	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will give the land of Egypt unto Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon; and he shall take her multitude, and take her spoil, and take her prey; and it shall be the wages for his army.
verse	26	29	20	@@I have given him the land of Egypt @9for@7 his labour wherewith he served against it, because they wrought for me, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	29	21	@@In that day will I cause the horn of the house of Israel to bud forth, and I will give thee the opening of the mouth in the midst of them; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	30	1	The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,
verse	26	30	2	Son of man, prophesy and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Howl ye, Woe worth the day
verse	26	30	3	@@For the day @9is@7 near, even the day of the LORD @9is@7 near, a cloudy day; it shall be the time of the heathen.
verse	26	30	4	And the sword shall come upon Egypt, and great pain shall be in Ethiopia, when the slain shall fall in Egypt, and they shall take away her multitude, and her foundations shall be broken down.
verse	26	30	5	Ethiopia, and Libya, and Lydia, and all the mingled people, and Chub, and the men of the land that is in league, shall fall with them by the sword.
verse	26	30	6	Thus saith the LORD; They also that uphold Egypt shall fall; and the pride of her power shall come down: from the tower of Syene shall they fall in it by the sword, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	30	7	@@And they shall be desolate in the midst of the countries @9that are@7 desolate, and her cities shall be in the midst of the cities @9that are@7 wasted.
verse	26	30	8	@@And they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I have set a fire in Egypt, and @9when@7 all her helpers shall be destroyed.
verse	26	30	9	In that day shall messengers go forth from me in ships to make the careless Ethiopians afraid, and great pain shall come upon them, as in the day of Egypt: for, lo, it cometh.
verse	26	30	10	Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will also make the multitude of Egypt to cease by the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon.
verse	26	30	11	He and his people with him, the terrible of the nations, shall be brought to destroy the land: and they shall draw their swords against Egypt, and fill the land with the slain.
verse	26	30	12	@@And I will make the rivers dry, and sell the land into the hand of the wicked: and I will make the land waste, and all that is therein, by the hand of strangers: I the LORD have spoken @9it. @7
verse	26	30	13	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will also destroy the idols, and I will cause @9their@7 images to cease out of Noph; and there shall be no more a prince of the land of Egypt: and I will put a fear in the land of Egypt.
verse	26	30	14	And I will make Pathros desolate, and will set fire in Zoan, and will execute judgments in No.
verse	26	30	15	And I will pour my fury upon Sin, the strength of Egypt; and I will cut off the multitude of No.
verse	26	30	16	@@And I will set fire in Egypt: Sin shall have great pain, and No shall be rent asunder, and Noph @9shall have@7 distresses daily.
verse	26	30	17	@@The young men of Aven and of Pi-beseth shall fall by the sword: and these @9cities@7 shall go into captivity.
verse	26	30	18	At Tehaphnehes also the day shall be darkened, when I shall break there the yokes of Egypt: and the pomp of her strength shall cease in her: as for her, a cloud shall cover her, and her daughters shall go into captivity.
verse	26	30	19	@@Thus will I execute judgments in Egypt: and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	30	20	@@And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the first @9month,@7 in the seventh @9day@7 of the month, @9that@7 the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	30	21	Son of man, I have broken the arm of Pharaoh king of Egypt; and, lo, it shall not be bound up to be healed, to put a roller to bind it, to make it strong to hold the sword.
verse	26	30	22	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I @9am@7 against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and will break his arms, the strong, and that which was broken; and I will cause the sword to fall out of his hand.
verse	26	30	23	And I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries.
verse	26	30	24	@@And I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and put my sword in his hand: but I will break Pharaoh's arms, and he shall groan before him with the groanings of a deadly wounded @9man. @7
verse	26	30	25	@@But I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and the arms of Pharaoh shall fall down; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I shall put my sword into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall stretch it out upon the land of Egypt.
verse	26	30	26	@@And I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and disperse them among the countries; and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	31	1	@@And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the third @9month,@7 in the first @9day@7 of the month, @9that@7 the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	31	2	Son of man, speak unto Pharaoh king of Egypt, and to his multitude; Whom art thou like in thy greatness?
verse	26	31	3	@@Behold, the Assyrian @9was@7 a cedar in Lebanon with fair branches, and with a shadowing shroud, and of an high stature; and his top was among the thick boughs.
verse	26	31	4	The waters made him great, the deep set him up on high with her rivers running round about his plants, and sent out her little rivers unto all the trees of the field.
verse	26	31	5	Therefore his height was exalted above all the trees of the field, and his boughs were multiplied, and his branches became long because of the multitude of waters, when he shot forth.
verse	26	31	6	All the fowls of heaven made their nests in his boughs, and under his branches did all the beasts of the field bring forth their young, and under his shadow dwelt all great nations.
verse	26	31	7	Thus was he fair in his greatness, in the length of his branches: for his root was by great waters.
verse	26	31	8	The cedars in the garden of God could not hide him: the fir trees were not like his boughs, and the chesnut trees were not like his branches; nor any tree in the garden of God was like unto him in his beauty.
verse	26	31	9	@@I have made him fair by the multitude of his branches: so that all the trees of Eden, that @9were@7 in the garden of God, envied him.
verse	26	31	10	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast lifted up thyself in height, and he hath shot up his top among the thick boughs, and his heart is lifted up in his height;
verse	26	31	11	I have therefore delivered him into the hand of the mighty one of the heathen; he shall surely deal with him: I have driven him out for his wickedness.
verse	26	31	12	And strangers, the terrible of the nations, have cut him off, and have left him: upon the mountains and in all the valleys his branches are fallen, and his boughs are broken by all the rivers of the land; and all the people of the earth are gone down from his shadow, and have left him.
verse	26	31	13	Upon his ruin shall all the fowls of the heaven remain, and all the beasts of the field shall be upon his branches:
verse	26	31	14	To the end that none of all the trees by the waters exalt themselves for their height, neither shoot up their top among the thick boughs, neither their trees stand up in their height, all that drink water: for they are all delivered unto death, to the nether parts of the earth, in the midst of the children of men, with them that go down to the pit.
verse	26	31	15	Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day when he went down to the grave I caused a mourning: I covered the deep for him, and I restrained the floods thereof, and the great waters were stayed: and I caused Lebanon to mourn for him, and all the trees of the field fainted for him.
verse	26	31	16	I made the nations to shake at the sound of his fall, when I cast him down to hell with them that descend into the pit: and all the trees of Eden, the choice and best of Lebanon, all that drink water, shall be comforted in the nether parts of the earth.
verse	26	31	17	@@They also went down into hell with him unto @9them that be@7 slain with the sword; and @9they that were@7 his arm, @9that@7 dwelt under his shadow in the midst of the heathen.
verse	26	31	18	@@To whom art thou thus like in glory and in greatness among the trees of Eden? yet shalt thou be brought down with the trees of Eden unto the nether parts of the earth: thou shalt lie in the midst of the uncircumcised with @9them that be@7 slain by the sword. This @9is@7 Pharaoh and all his multitude, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	32	1	@@And it came to pass in the twelfth year, in the twelfth month, in the first @9day@7 of the month, @9that@7 the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	32	2	@@Son of man, take up a lamentation for Pharaoh king of Egypt, and say unto him, Thou art like a young lion of the nations, and thou @9art@7 as a whale in the seas: and thou camest forth with thy rivers, and troubledst the waters with thy feet, and fouledst their rivers.
verse	26	32	3	Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will therefore spread out my net over thee with a company of many people; and they shall bring thee up in my net.
verse	26	32	4	Then will I leave thee upon the land, I will cast thee forth upon the open field, and will cause all the fowls of the heaven to remain upon thee, and I will fill the beasts of the whole earth with thee.
verse	26	32	5	And I will lay thy flesh upon the mountains, and fill the valleys with thy height.
verse	26	32	6	@@I will also water with thy blood the land wherein thou swimmest, @9even@7 to the mountains; and the rivers shall be full of thee.
verse	26	32	7	And when I shall put thee out, I will cover the heaven, and make the stars thereof dark; I will cover the sun with a cloud, and the moon shall not give her light.
verse	26	32	8	All the bright lights of heaven will I make dark over thee, and set darkness upon thy land, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	32	9	I will also vex the hearts of many people, when I shall bring thy destruction among the nations, into the countries which thou hast not known.
verse	26	32	10	@@Yea, I will make many people amazed at thee, and their kings shall be horribly afraid for thee, when I shall brandish my sword before them; and they shall tremble at @9every@7 moment, every man for his own life, in the day of thy fall.
verse	26	32	11	For thus saith the Lord GOD; The sword of the king of Babylon shall come upon thee.
verse	26	32	12	By the swords of the mighty will I cause thy multitude to fall, the terrible of the nations, all of them: and they shall spoil the pomp of Egypt, and all the multitude thereof shall be destroyed.
verse	26	32	13	I will destroy also all the beasts thereof from beside the great waters; neither shall the foot of man trouble them any more, nor the hoofs of beasts trouble them.
verse	26	32	14	Then will I make their waters deep, and cause their rivers to run like oil, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	32	15	@@When I shall make the land of Egypt desolate, and the country shall be destitute of that whereof it was full, when I shall smite all them that dwell therein, then shall they know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	32	16	@@This @9is@7 the lamentation wherewith they shall lament her: the daughters of the nations shall lament her: they shall lament for her, @9even@7 for Egypt, and for all her multitude, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	32	17	@@It came to pass also in the twelfth year, in the fifteenth day of the month, @9that@7 the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	32	18	@@Son of man, wail for the multitude of Egypt, and cast them down, @9even@7 her, and the daughters of the famous nations, unto the nether parts of the earth, with them that go down into the pit.
verse	26	32	19	Whom dost thou pass in beauty? go down, and be thou laid with the uncircumcised.
verse	26	32	20	@@They shall fall in the midst of @9them that are@7 slain by the sword: she is delivered to the sword: draw her and all her multitudes.
verse	26	32	21	The strong among the mighty shall speak to him out of the midst of hell with them that help him: they are gone down, they lie uncircumcised, slain by the sword.
verse	26	32	22	@@Asshur @9is@7 there and all her company: his graves @9are@7 about him: all of them slain, fallen by the sword:
verse	26	32	23	Whose graves are set in the sides of the pit, and her company is round about her grave: all of them slain, fallen by the sword, which caused terror in the land of the living.
verse	26	32	24	@@There @9is@7 Elam and all her multitude round about her grave, all of them slain, fallen by the sword, which are gone down uncircumcised into the nether parts of the earth, which caused their terror in the land of the living; yet have they borne their shame with them that go down to the pit.
verse	26	32	25	@@They have set her a bed in the midst of the slain with all her multitude: her graves @9are@7 round about him: all of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword: though their terror was caused in the land of the living, yet have they borne their shame with them that go down to the pit: he is put in the midst of @9them that be@7 slain.
verse	26	32	26	@@There @9is@7 Meshech, Tubal, and all her multitude: her graves @9are@7 round about him: all of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword, though they caused their terror in the land of the living.
verse	26	32	27	@@And they shall not lie with the mighty @9that are@7 fallen of the uncircumcised, which are gone down to hell with their weapons of war: and they have laid their swords under their heads, but their iniquities shall be upon their bones, though @9they were@7 the terror of the mighty in the land of the living.
verse	26	32	28	@@Yea, thou shalt be broken in the midst of the uncircumcised, and shalt lie with @9them that are@7 slain with the sword.
verse	26	32	29	@@There @9is@7 Edom, her kings, and all her princes, which with their might are laid by @9them that were@7 slain by the sword: they shall lie with the uncircumcised, and with them that go down to the pit.
verse	26	32	30	@@There @9be@7 the princes of the north, all of them, and all the Zidonians, which are gone down with the slain; with their terror they are ashamed of their might; and they lie uncircumcised with @9them that be@7 slain by the sword, and bear their shame with them that go down to the pit.
verse	26	32	31	@@Pharaoh shall see them, and shall be comforted over all his multitude, @9even@7 Pharaoh and all his army slain by the sword, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	32	32	@@For I have caused my terror in the land of the living: and he shall be laid in the midst of the uncircumcised with @9them that are@7 slain with the sword, @9even@7 Pharaoh and all his multitude, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	33	1	Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	33	2	Son of man, speak to the children of thy people, and say unto them, When I bring the sword upon a land, if the people of the land take a man of their coasts, and set him for their watchman:
verse	26	33	3	If when he seeth the sword come upon the land, he blow the trumpet, and warn the people;
verse	26	33	4	Then whosoever heareth the sound of the trumpet, and taketh not warning; if the sword come, and take him away, his blood shall be upon his own head.
verse	26	33	5	He heard the sound of the trumpet, and took not warning; his blood shall be upon him. But he that taketh warning shall deliver his soul.
verse	26	33	6	@@But if the watchman see the sword come, and blow not the trumpet, and the people be not warned; if the sword come, and take @9any@7 person from among them, he is taken away in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at the watchman's hand.
verse	26	33	7	So thou, O son of man, I have set thee a watchman unto the house of Israel; therefore thou shalt hear the word at my mouth, and warn them from me.
verse	26	33	8	@@When I say unto the wicked, O wicked @9man,@7 thou shalt surely die; if thou dost not speak to warn the wicked from his way, that wicked @9man@7 shall die in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at thine hand.
verse	26	33	9	Nevertheless, if thou warn the wicked of his way to turn from it; if he do not turn from his way, he shall die in his iniquity; but thou hast delivered thy soul.
verse	26	33	10	@@Therefore, O thou son of man, speak unto the house of Israel; Thus ye speak, saying, If our transgressions and our sins @9be@7 upon us, and we pine away in them, how should we then live?
verse	26	33	11	@@Say unto them, @9As@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, I have no pleasure in the death of the wicked; but that the wicked turn from his way and live: turn ye, turn ye from your evil ways; for why will ye die, O house of Israel?
verse	26	33	12	@@Therefore, thou son of man, say unto the children of thy people, The righteousness of the righteous shall not deliver him in the day of his transgression: as for the wickedness of the wicked, he shall not fall thereby in the day that he turneth from his wickedness; neither shall the righteous be able to live for his @9righteousness@7 in the day that he sinneth.
verse	26	33	13	@@When I shall say to the righteous, @9that@7 he shall surely live; if he trust to his own righteousness, and commit iniquity, all his righteousnesses shall not be remembered; but for his iniquity that he hath committed, he shall die for it.
verse	26	33	14	Again, when I say unto the wicked, Thou shalt surely die; if he turn from his sin, and do that which is lawful and right;
verse	26	33	15	@@@9If@7 the wicked restore the pledge, give again that he had robbed, walk in the statutes of life, without committing iniquity; he shall surely live, he shall not die.
verse	26	33	16	None of his sins that he hath committed shall be mentioned unto him: he hath done that which is lawful and right; he shall surely live.
verse	26	33	17	Yet the children of thy people say, The way of the Lord is not equal: but as for them, their way is not equal.
verse	26	33	18	When the righteous turneth from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity, he shall even die thereby.
verse	26	33	19	But if the wicked turn from his wickedness, and do that which is lawful and right, he shall live thereby.
verse	26	33	20	Yet ye say, The way of the Lord is not equal. O ye house of Israel, I will judge you every one after his ways.
verse	26	33	21	@@And it came to pass in the twelfth year of our captivity, in the tenth @9month,@7 in the fifth @9day@7 of the month, @9that@7 one that had escaped out of Jerusalem came unto me, saying, The city is smitten.
verse	26	33	22	Now the hand of the LORD was upon me in the evening, afore he that was escaped came; and had opened my mouth, until he came to me in the morning; and my mouth was opened, and I was no more dumb.
verse	26	33	23	Then the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	33	24	@@Son of man, they that inhabit those wastes of the land of Israel speak, saying, Abraham was one, and he inherited the land: but we @9are@7 many; the land is given us for inheritance.
verse	26	33	25	Wherefore say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Ye eat with the blood, and lift up your eyes toward your idols, and shed blood: and shall ye possess the land?
verse	26	33	26	Ye stand upon your sword, ye work abomination, and ye defile every one his neighbour's wife: and shall ye possess the land?
verse	26	33	27	@@Say thou thus unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; @9As@7 I live, surely they that @9are@7 in the wastes shall fall by the sword, and him that @9is@7 in the open field will I give to the beasts to be devoured, and they that be in the forts and in the caves shall die of the pestilence.
verse	26	33	28	For I will lay the land most desolate, and the pomp of her strength shall cease; and the mountains of Israel shall be desolate, that none shall pass through.
verse	26	33	29	@@Then shall they know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I have laid the land most desolate because of all their abominations which they have committed.
verse	26	33	30	Also, thou son of man, the children of thy people still are talking against thee by the walls and in the doors of the houses, and speak one to another, every one to his brother, saying, Come, I pray you, and hear what is the word that cometh forth from the LORD.
verse	26	33	31	@@And they come unto thee as the people cometh, and they sit before thee as my people, and they hear thy words, but they will not do them: for with their mouth they shew much love, @9but@7 their heart goeth after their covetousness.
verse	26	33	32	@@And, lo, thou @9art@7 unto them as a very lovely song of one that hath a pleasant voice, and can play well on an instrument: for they hear thy words, but they do them not.
verse	26	33	33	And when this cometh to pass, (lo, it will come,) then shall they know that a prophet hath been among them.
verse	26	34	1	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	34	2	@@Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel, prophesy, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD unto the shepherds; Woe @9be@7 to the shepherds of Israel that do feed themselves! should not the shepherds feed the flocks?
verse	26	34	3	@@Ye eat the fat, and ye clothe you with the wool, ye kill them that are fed: @9but@7 ye feed not the flock.
verse	26	34	4	@@The diseased have ye not strengthened, neither have ye healed that which was sick, neither have ye bound up @9that which was@7 broken, neither have ye brought again that which was driven away, neither have ye sought that which was lost; but with force and with cruelty have ye ruled them.
verse	26	34	5	@@And they were scattered, because @9there is@7 no shepherd: and they became meat to all the beasts of the field, when they were scattered.
verse	26	34	6	@@My sheep wandered through all the mountains, and upon every high hill: yea, my flock was scattered upon all the face of the earth, and none did search or seek @9after them.@7
verse	26	34	7	Therefore, ye shepherds, hear the word of the LORD;
verse	26	34	8	@@@9As@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, surely because my flock became a prey, and my flock became meat to every beast of the field, because @9there was@7 no shepherd, neither did my shepherds search for my flock, but the shepherds fed themselves, and fed not my flock;
verse	26	34	9	Therefore, O ye shepherds, hear the word of the LORD;
verse	26	34	10	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I @9am@7 against the shepherds; and I will require my flock at their hand, and cause them to cease from feeding the flock; neither shall the shepherds feed themselves any more; for I will deliver my flock from their mouth, that they may not be meat for them.
verse	26	34	11	@@For thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I, @9even@7 I, will both search my sheep, and seek them out.
verse	26	34	12	@@As a shepherd seeketh out his flock in the day that he is among his sheep @9that are@7 scattered; so will I seek out my sheep, and will deliver them out of all places where they have been scattered in the cloudy and dark day.
verse	26	34	13	And I will bring them out from the people, and gather them from the countries, and will bring them to their own land, and feed them upon the mountains of Israel by the rivers, and in all the inhabited places of the country.
verse	26	34	14	@@I will feed them in a good pasture, and upon the high mountains of Israel shall their fold be: there shall they lie in a good fold, and @9in@7 a fat pasture shall they feed upon the mountains of Israel.
verse	26	34	15	I will feed my flock, and I will cause them to lie down, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	34	16	@@I will seek that which was lost, and bring again that which was driven away, and will bind up @9that which was@7 broken, and will strengthen that which was sick: but I will destroy the fat and the strong; I will feed them with judgment.
verse	26	34	17	@@And @9as for@7 you, O my flock, thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I judge between cattle and cattle, between the rams and the he goats.
verse	26	34	18	@@@9Seemeth it@7 a small thing unto you to have eaten up the good pasture, but ye must tread down with your feet the residue of your pastures? and to have drunk of the deep waters, but ye must foul the residue with your feet?
verse	26	34	19	@@And @9as for@7 my flock, they eat that which ye have trodden with your feet; and they drink that which ye have fouled with your feet.
verse	26	34	20	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD unto them; Behold, I, @9even@7 I, will judge between the fat cattle and between the lean cattle.
verse	26	34	21	Because ye have thrust with side and with shoulder, and pushed all the diseased with your horns, till ye have scattered them abroad;
verse	26	34	22	Therefore will I save my flock, and they shall no more be a prey; and I will judge between cattle and cattle.
verse	26	34	23	@@And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, @9even@7 my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd.
verse	26	34	24	@@And I the LORD will be their God, and my servant David a prince among them; I the LORD have spoken @9it. @7
verse	26	34	25	And I will make with them a covenant of peace, and will cause the evil beasts to cease out of the land: and they shall dwell safely in the wilderness, and sleep in the woods.
verse	26	34	26	And I will make them and the places round about my hill a blessing; and I will cause the shower to come down in his season; there shall be showers of blessing.
verse	26	34	27	@@And the tree of the field shall yield her fruit, and the earth shall yield her increase, and they shall be safe in their land, and shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I have broken the bands of their yoke, and delivered them out of the hand of those that served themselves of them.
verse	26	34	28	@@And they shall no more be a prey to the heathen, neither shall the beast of the land devour them; but they shall dwell safely, and none shall make @9them@7 afraid.
verse	26	34	29	And I will raise up for them a plant of renown, and they shall be no more consumed with hunger in the land, neither bear the shame of the heathen any more.
verse	26	34	30	@@Thus shall they know that I the LORD their God @9am@7 with them, and @9that@7 they, @9even@7 the house of Israel, @9are@7 my people, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	34	31	@@And ye my flock, the flock of my pasture, @9are@7 men, @9and@7 I @9am@7 your God, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	35	1	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	35	2	Son of man, set thy face against mount Seir, and prophesy against it,
verse	26	35	3	@@And say unto it, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, O mount Seir, I @9am@7 against thee, and I will stretch out mine hand against thee, and I will make thee most desolate.
verse	26	35	4	@@I will lay thy cities waste, and thou shalt be desolate, and thou shalt know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	35	5	@@Because thou hast had a perpetual hatred, and hast shed @9the blood of@7 the children of Israel by the force of the sword in the time of their calamity, in the time @9that their@7 iniquity @9had@7 an end:
verse	26	35	6	@@Therefore, @9as@7 I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will prepare thee unto blood, and blood shall pursue thee: sith thou hast not hated blood, even blood shall pursue thee.
verse	26	35	7	Thus will I make mount Seir most desolate, and cut off from it him that passeth out and him that returneth.
verse	26	35	8	@@And I will fill his mountains with his slain @9men:@7 in thy hills, and in thy valleys, and in all thy rivers, shall they fall that are slain with the sword.
verse	26	35	9	@@I will make thee perpetual desolations, and thy cities shall not return: and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	35	10	Because thou hast said, These two nations and these two countries shall be mine, and we will possess it; whereas the LORD was there:
verse	26	35	11	Therefore, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will even do according to thine anger, and according to thine envy which thou hast used out of thy hatred against them; and I will make myself known among them, when I have judged thee.
verse	26	35	12	@@And thou shalt know that I @9am@7 the LORD, @9and that@7 I have heard all thy blasphemies which thou hast spoken against the mountains of Israel, saying, They are laid desolate, they are given us to consume.
verse	26	35	13	@@Thus with your mouth ye have boasted against me, and have multiplied your words against me: I have heard @9them. @7
verse	26	35	14	Thus saith the Lord GOD; When the whole earth rejoiceth, I will make thee desolate.
verse	26	35	15	@@As thou didst rejoice at the inheritance of the house of Israel, because it was desolate, so will I do unto thee: thou shalt be desolate, O mount Seir, and all Idumea, @9even@7 all of it: and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	36	1	Also, thou son of man, prophesy unto the mountains of Israel, and say, Ye mountains of Israel, hear the word of the LORD:
verse	26	36	2	Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because the enemy hath said against you, Aha, even the ancient high places are ours in possession:
verse	26	36	3	@@Therefore prophesy and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because they have made @9you@7 desolate, and swallowed you up on every side, that ye might be a possession unto the residue of the heathen, and ye are taken up in the lips of talkers, and @9are@7 an infamy of the people:
verse	26	36	4	@@Therefore, ye mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus saith the Lord GOD to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys, to the desolate wastes, and to the cities that are forsaken, which became a prey and derision to the residue of the heathen that @9are@7 round about;
verse	26	36	5	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Surely in the fire of my jealousy have I spoken against the residue of the heathen, and against all Idumea, which have appointed my land into their possession with the joy of all @9their@7 heart, with despiteful minds, to cast it out for a prey.
verse	26	36	6	Prophesy therefore concerning the land of Israel, and say unto the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I have spoken in my jealousy and in my fury, because ye have borne the shame of the heathen:
verse	26	36	7	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I have lifted up mine hand, Surely the heathen that @9are@7 about you, they shall bear their shame.
verse	26	36	8	But ye, O mountains of Israel, ye shall shoot forth your branches, and yield your fruit to my people of Israel; for they are at hand to come.
verse	26	36	9	@@For, behold, I @9am@7 for you, and I will turn unto you, and ye shall be tilled and sown:
verse	26	36	10	@@And I will multiply men upon you, all the house of Israel, @9even@7 all of it: and the cities shall be inhabited, and the wastes shall be builded:
verse	26	36	11	@@And I will multiply upon you man and beast; and they shall increase and bring fruit: and I will settle you after your old estates, and will do better @9unto you@7 than at your beginnings: and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	36	12	@@Yea, I will cause men to walk upon you, @9even@7 my people Israel; and they shall possess thee, and thou shalt be their inheritance, and thou shalt no more henceforth bereave them @9of men. @7
verse	26	36	13	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because they say unto you, Thou @9land@7 devourest up men, and hast bereaved thy nations;
verse	26	36	14	Therefore thou shalt devour men no more, neither bereave thy nations any more, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	36	15	@@Neither will I cause @9men@7 to hear in thee the shame of the heathen any more, neither shalt thou bear the reproach of the people any more, neither shalt thou cause thy nations to fall any more, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	36	16	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	36	17	Son of man, when the house of Israel dwelt in their own land, they defiled it by their own way and by their doings: their way was before me as the uncleanness of a removed woman.
verse	26	36	18	@@Wherefore I poured my fury upon them for the blood that they had shed upon the land, and for their idols @9wherewith@7 they had polluted it:
verse	26	36	19	And I scattered them among the heathen, and they were dispersed through the countries: according to their way and according to their doings I judged them.
verse	26	36	20	@@And when they entered unto the heathen, whither they went, they profaned my holy name, when they said to them, These @9are@7 the people of the LORD, and are gone forth out of his land.
verse	26	36	21	But I had pity for mine holy name, which the house of Israel had profaned among the heathen, whither they went.
verse	26	36	22	@@Therefore say unto the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; I do not @9this@7 for your sakes, O house of Israel, but for mine holy name's sake, which ye have profaned among the heathen, whither ye went.
verse	26	36	23	@@And I will sanctify my great name, which was profaned among the heathen, which ye have profaned in the midst of them; and the heathen shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, saith the Lord GOD, when I shall be sanctified in you before their eyes.
verse	26	36	24	For I will take you from among the heathen, and gather you out of all countries, and will bring you into your own land.
verse	26	36	25	Then will I sprinkle clean water upon you, and ye shall be clean: from all your filthiness, and from all your idols, will I cleanse you.
verse	26	36	26	A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.
verse	26	36	27	@@And I will put my spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do @9them. @7
verse	26	36	28	And ye shall dwell in the land that I gave to your fathers; and ye shall be my people, and I will be your God.
verse	26	36	29	I will also save you from all your uncleannesses: and I will call for the corn, and will increase it, and lay no famine upon you.
verse	26	36	30	And I will multiply the fruit of the tree, and the increase of the field, that ye shall receive no more reproach of famine among the heathen.
verse	26	36	31	@@Then shall ye remember your own evil ways, and your doings that @9were@7 not good, and shall lothe yourselves in your own sight for your iniquities and for your abominations.
verse	26	36	32	@@Not for your sakes do I @9this,@7 saith the Lord GOD, be it known unto you: be ashamed and confounded for your own ways, O house of Israel.
verse	26	36	33	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day that I shall have cleansed you from all your iniquities I will also cause @9you@7 to dwell in the cities, and the wastes shall be builded.
verse	26	36	34	And the desolate land shall be tilled, whereas it lay desolate in the sight of all that passed by.
verse	26	36	35	@@And they shall say, This land that was desolate is become like the garden of Eden; and the waste and desolate and ruined cities @9are become@7 fenced, @9and@7 are inhabited.
verse	26	36	36	@@Then the heathen that are left round about you shall know that I the LORD build the ruined @9places, and@7 plant that that was desolate: I the LORD have spoken @9it,@7 and I will do @9it. @7
verse	26	36	37	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will yet @9for@7 this be enquired of by the house of Israel, to do @9it@7 for them; I will increase them with men like a flock.
verse	26	36	38	@@As the holy flock, as the flock of Jerusalem in her solemn feasts; so shall the waste cities be filled with flocks of men: and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	37	1	@@The hand of the LORD was upon me, and carried me out in the spirit of the LORD, and set me down in the midst of the valley which @9was@7 full of bones,
verse	26	37	2	@@And caused me to pass by them round about: and, behold, @9there were@7 very many in the open valley; and, lo, @9they were@7 very dry.
verse	26	37	3	And he said unto me, Son of man, can these bones live? And I answered, O Lord GOD, thou knowest.
verse	26	37	4	Again he said unto me, Prophesy upon these bones, and say unto them, O ye dry bones, hear the word of the LORD.
verse	26	37	5	Thus saith the Lord GOD unto these bones; Behold, I will cause breath to enter into you, and ye shall live:
verse	26	37	6	@@And I will lay sinews upon you, and will bring up flesh upon you, and cover you with skin, and put breath in you, and ye shall live; and ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	37	7	So I prophesied as I was commanded: and as I prophesied, there was a noise, and behold a shaking, and the bones came together, bone to his bone.
verse	26	37	8	@@And when I beheld, lo, the sinews and the flesh came up upon them, and the skin covered them above: but @9there was @7no breath in them.
verse	26	37	9	Then said he unto me, Prophesy unto the wind, prophesy, son of man, and say to the wind, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Come from the four winds, O breath, and breathe upon these slain, that they may live.
verse	26	37	10	So I prophesied as he commanded me, and the breath came into them, and they lived, and stood up upon their feet, an exceeding great army.
verse	26	37	11	Then he said unto me, Son of man, these bones are the whole house of Israel: behold, they say, Our bones are dried, and our hope is lost: we are cut off for our parts.
verse	26	37	12	Therefore prophesy and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves, and bring you into the land of Israel.
verse	26	37	13	@@And ye shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, when I have opened your graves, O my people, and brought you up out of your graves,
verse	26	37	14	@@And shall put my spirit in you, and ye shall live, and I shall place you in your own land: then shall ye know that I the LORD have spoken @9it,@7 and performed @9it,@7 saith the LORD.
verse	26	37	15	The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,
verse	26	37	16	@@Moreover, thou son of man, take thee one stick, and write upon it, For Judah, and for the children of Israel his companions: then take another stick, and write upon it, For Joseph, the stick of Ephraim, and @9for@7 all the house of Israel his companions:
verse	26	37	17	And join them one to another into one stick; and they shall become one in thine hand.
verse	26	37	18	@@And when the children of thy people shall speak unto thee, saying, Wilt thou not shew us what thou @9meanest@7 by these?
verse	26	37	19	@@Say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which @9is@7 in the hand of Ephraim, and the tribes of Israel his fellows, and will put them with him, @9even@7 with the stick of Judah, and make them one stick, and they shall be one in mine hand.
verse	26	37	20	And the sticks whereon thou writest shall be in thine hand before their eyes.
verse	26	37	21	And say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will take the children of Israel from among the heathen, whither they be gone, and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land:
verse	26	37	22	And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Israel; and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all:
verse	26	37	23	Neither shall they defile themselves any more with their idols, nor with their detestable things, nor with any of their transgressions: but I will save them out of all their dwellingplaces, wherein they have sinned, and will cleanse them: so shall they be my people, and I will be their God.
verse	26	37	24	@@And David my servant @9shall be@7 king over them; and they all shall have one shepherd: they shall also walk in my judgments, and observe my statutes, and do them.
verse	26	37	25	@@And they shall dwell in the land that I have given unto Jacob my servant, wherein your fathers have dwelt; and they shall dwell therein, @9even@7 they, and their children, and their children's children for ever: and my servant David @9shall be@7 their prince for ever.
verse	26	37	26	Moreover I will make a covenant of peace with them; it shall be an everlasting covenant with them: and I will place them, and multiply them, and will set my sanctuary in the midst of them for evermore.
verse	26	37	27	My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their God, and they shall be my people.
verse	26	37	28	And the heathen shall know that I the LORD do sanctify Israel, when my sanctuary shall be in the midst of them for evermore.
verse	26	38	1	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	26	38	2	Son of man, set thy face against Gog, the land of Magog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal, and prophesy against him,
verse	26	38	3	@@And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold I @9am@7 against thee, O Gog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal:
verse	26	38	4	@@And I will turn thee back, and put hooks into thy jaws, and I will bring thee forth, and all thine army, horses and horsemen, all of them clothed with all sorts @9of armour, even@7 a great company @9with@7 bucklers and shields, all of them handling swords:
verse	26	38	5	Persia, Ethiopia, and Libya with them; all of them with shield and helmet:
verse	26	38	6	@@Gomer, and all his bands; the house of Togarmah of the north quarters, and all his bands: @9and@7 many people with thee.
verse	26	38	7	Be thou prepared, and prepare for thyself, thou, and all thy company that are assembled unto thee, and be thou a guard unto them.
verse	26	38	8	@@After many days thou shalt be visited: in the latter years thou shalt come into the land @9that is@7 brought back from the sword, @9and is@7 gathered out of many people, against the mountains of Israel, which have been always waste: but it is brought forth out of the nations, and they shall dwell safely all of them.
verse	26	38	9	Thou shalt ascend and come like a storm, thou shalt be like a cloud to cover the land, thou, and all thy bands, and many people with thee.
verse	26	38	10	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; It shall also come to pass, @9that@7 at the same time shall things come into thy mind, and thou shalt think an evil thought:
verse	26	38	11	And thou shalt say, I will go up to the land of unwalled villages; I will go to them that are at rest, that dwell safely, all of them dwelling without walls, and having neither bars nor gates,
verse	26	38	12	@@To take a spoil, and to take a prey; to turn thine hand upon the desolate places @9that are now@7 inhabited, and upon the people @9that are@7 gathered out of the nations, which have gotten cattle and goods, that dwell in the midst of the land.
verse	26	38	13	Sheba, and Dedan, and the merchants of Tarshish, with all the young lions thereof, shall say unto thee, Art thou come to take a spoil? hast thou gathered thy company to take a prey? to carry away silver and gold, to take away cattle and goods, to take a great spoil?
verse	26	38	14	@@Therefore, son of man, prophesy and say unto Gog, Thus saith the Lord GOD; In that day when my people of Israel dwelleth safely, shalt thou not know @9it? @7
verse	26	38	15	And thou shalt come from thy place out of the north parts, thou, and many people with thee, all of them riding upon horses, a great company, and a mighty army:
verse	26	38	16	And thou shalt come up against my people of Israel, as a cloud to cover the land; it shall be in the latter days, and I will bring thee against my land, that the heathen may know me, when I shall be sanctified in thee, O Gog, before their eyes.
verse	26	38	17	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; @9Art@7 thou he of whom I have spoken in old time by my servants the prophets of Israel, which prophesied in those days @9many@7 years that I would bring thee against them?
verse	26	38	18	@@And it shall come to pass at the same time when Gog shall come against the land of Israel, saith the Lord GOD, @9that@7 my fury shall come up in my face.
verse	26	38	19	@@For in my jealousy @9and@7 in the fire of my wrath have I spoken, Surely in that day there shall be a great shaking in the land of Israel;
verse	26	38	20	@@So that the fishes of the sea, and the fowls of the heaven, and the beasts of the field, and all creeping things that creep upon the earth, and all the men that @9are@7 upon the face of the earth, shall shake at my presence, and the mountains shall be thrown down, and the steep places shall fall, and every wall shall fall to the ground.
verse	26	38	21	And I will call for a sword against him throughout all my mountains, saith the Lord GOD: every man's sword shall be against his brother.
verse	26	38	22	@@And I will plead against him with pestilence and with blood; and I will rain upon him, and upon his bands, and upon the many people that @9are@7 with him, an overflowing rain, and great hailstones, fire, and brimstone.
verse	26	38	23	@@Thus will I magnify myself, and sanctify myself; and I will be known in the eyes of many nations, and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	39	1	@@Therefore, thou son of man, prophesy against Gog, and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I @9am@7 against thee, O Gog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal:
verse	26	39	2	And I will turn thee back, and leave but the sixth part of thee, and will cause thee to come up from the north parts, and will bring thee upon the mountains of Israel:
verse	26	39	3	And I will smite thy bow out of thy left hand, and will cause thine arrows to fall out of thy right hand.
verse	26	39	4	@@Thou shalt fall upon the mountains of Israel, thou, and all thy bands, and the people that @9is@7 with thee: I will give thee unto the ravenous birds of every sort, and @9to@7 the beasts of the field to be devoured.
verse	26	39	5	@@Thou shalt fall upon the open field: for I have spoken @9it,@7 saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	39	6	@@And I will send a fire on Magog, and among them that dwell carelessly in the isles: and they shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD.
verse	26	39	7	@@So will I make my holy name known in the midst of my people Israel; and I will not @9let them@7 pollute my holy name any more: and the heathen shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD, the Holy One in Israel.
verse	26	39	8	@@Behold, it is come, and it is done, saith the Lord GOD; this @9is@7 the day whereof I have spoken.
verse	26	39	9	And they that dwell in the cities of Israel shall go forth, and shall set on fire and burn the weapons, both the shields and the bucklers, the bows and the arrows, and the handstaves, and the spears, and they shall burn them with fire seven years:
verse	26	39	10	@@So that they shall take no wood out of the field, neither cut down @9any@7 out of the forests; for they shall burn the weapons with fire: and they shall spoil those that spoiled them, and rob those that robbed them, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	39	11	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 I will give unto Gog a place there of graves in Israel, the valley of the passengers on the east of the sea: and it shall stop the @9noses@7 of the passengers: and there shall they bury Gog and all his multitude: and they shall call @9it@7 The valley of Hamon-gog.
verse	26	39	12	And seven months shall the house of Israel be burying of them, that they may cleanse the land.
verse	26	39	13	@@Yea, all the people of the land shall bury @9them;@7 and it shall be to them a renown the day that I shall be glorified, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	39	14	And they shall sever out men of continual employment, passing through the land to bury with the passengers those that remain upon the face of the earth, to cleanse it: after the end of seven months shall they search.
verse	26	39	15	@@And the passengers @9that@7 pass through the land, when @9any@7 seeth a man's bone, then shall he set up a sign by it, till the buriers have buried it in the valley of Hamon-gog.
verse	26	39	16	@@And also the name of the city @9shall be@7 Hamonah. Thus shall they cleanse the land.
verse	26	39	17	@@And, thou son of man, thus saith the Lord GOD; Speak unto every feathered fowl, and to every beast of the field, Assemble yourselves, and come; gather yourselves on every side to my sacrifice that I do sacrifice for you, @9even@7 a great sacrifice upon the mountains of Israel, that ye may eat flesh, and drink blood.
verse	26	39	18	Ye shall eat the flesh of the mighty, and drink the blood of the princes of the earth, of rams, of lambs, and of goats, of bullocks, all of them fatlings of Bashan.
verse	26	39	19	And ye shall eat fat till ye be full, and drink blood till ye be drunken, of my sacrifice which I have sacrificed for you.
verse	26	39	20	Thus ye shall be filled at my table with horses and chariots, with mighty men, and with all men of war, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	39	21	And I will set my glory among the heathen, and all the heathen shall see my judgment that I have executed, and my hand that I have laid upon them.
verse	26	39	22	@@So the house of Israel shall know that I @9am@7 the LORD their God from that day and forward.
verse	26	39	23	And the heathen shall know that the house of Israel went into captivity for their iniquity: because they trespassed against me, therefore hid I my face from them, and gave them into the hand of their enemies: so fell they all by the sword.
verse	26	39	24	According to their uncleanness and according to their transgressions have I done unto them, and hid my face from them.
verse	26	39	25	Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Now will I bring again the captivity of Jacob, and have mercy upon the whole house of Israel, and will be jealous for my holy name;
verse	26	39	26	@@After that they have borne their shame, and all their trespasses whereby they have trespassed against me, when they dwelt safely in their land, and none made @9them@7 afraid.
verse	26	39	27	When I have brought them again from the people, and gathered them out of their enemies' lands, and am sanctified in them in the sight of many nations;
verse	26	39	28	@@Then shall they know that I @9am@7 the LORD their God, which caused them to be led into captivity among the heathen: but I have gathered them unto their own land, and have left none of them any more there.
verse	26	39	29	Neither will I hide my face any more from them: for I have poured out my spirit upon the house of Israel, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	40	1	@@In the five and twentieth year of our captivity, in the beginning of the year, in the tenth @9day@7 of the month, in the fourteenth year after that the city was smitten, in the selfsame day the hand of the LORD was upon me, and brought me thither.
verse	26	40	2	@@In the visions of God brought he me into the land of Israel, and set me upon a very high mountain, by which @9was@7 as the frame of a city on the south.
verse	26	40	3	@@And he brought me thither, and, behold, @9there was@7 a man, whose appearance was like the appearance of brass, with a line of flax in his hand, and a measuring reed; and he stood in the gate.
verse	26	40	4	@@And the man said unto me, Son of man, behold with thine eyes, and hear with thine ears, and set thine heart upon all that I shall shew thee; for to the intent that I might shew @9them@7 unto thee @9art@7 thou brought hither: declare all that thou seest to the house of Israel.
verse	26	40	5	@@And behold a wall on the outside of the house round about, and in the man's hand a measuring reed of six cubits @9long@7 by the cubit and an hand breadth: so he measured the breadth of the building, one reed; and the height, one reed.
verse	26	40	6	@@Then came he unto the gate which looketh toward the east, and went up the stairs thereof, and measured the threshold of the gate, @9which was@7 one reed broad; and the other threshold @9of the gate, which was@7 one reed broad.
verse	26	40	7	@@And @9every@7 little chamber @9was@7 one reed long, and one reed broad; and between the little chambers @9were@7 five cubits; and the threshold of the gate by the porch of the gate within @9was@7 one reed.
verse	26	40	8	He measured also the porch of the gate within, one reed.
verse	26	40	9	@@Then measured he the porch of the gate, eight cubits; and the posts thereof, two cubits; and the porch of the gate @9was@7 inward.
verse	26	40	10	@@And the little chambers of the gate eastward @9were@7 three on this side, and three on that side; they three @9were@7 of one measure: and the posts had one measure on this side and on that side.
verse	26	40	11	@@And he measured the breadth of the entry of the gate, ten cubits; @9and@7 the length of the gate, thirteen cubits.
verse	26	40	12	@@The space also before the little chambers @9was@7 one cubit @9on this side,@7 and the space @9was@7 one cubit on that side: and the little chambers @9were@7 six cubits on this side, and six cubits on that side.
verse	26	40	13	@@He measured then the gate from the roof of @9one@7 little chamber to the roof of another: the breadth @9was@7 five and twenty cubits, door against door.
verse	26	40	14	He made also posts of threescore cubits, even unto the post of the court round about the gate.
verse	26	40	15	@@And from the face of the gate of the entrance unto the face of the porch of the inner gate @9were@7 fifty cubits.
verse	26	40	16	@@And @9there were@7 narrow windows to the little chambers, and to their posts within the gate round about, and likewise to the arches: and windows @9were@7 round about inward: and upon @9each@7 post @9were@7 palm trees.
verse	26	40	17	@@Then brought he me into the outward court, and, lo, @9there were@7 chambers, and a pavement made for the court round about: thirty chambers @9were@7 upon the pavement.
verse	26	40	18	@@And the pavement by the side of the gates over against the length of the gates @9was@7 the lower pavement.
verse	26	40	19	Then he measured the breadth from the forefront of the lower gate unto the forefront of the inner court without, an hundred cubits eastward and northward.
verse	26	40	20	And the gate of the outward court that looked toward the north, he measured the length thereof, and the breadth thereof.
verse	26	40	21	@@And the little chambers thereof @9were@7 three on this side and three on that side; and the posts thereof and the arches thereof were after the measure of the first gate: the length thereof @9was@7 fifty cubits, and the breadth five and twenty cubits.
verse	26	40	22	@@And their windows, and their arches, and their palm trees, @9were@7 after the measure of the gate that looketh toward the east; and they went up unto it by seven steps; and the arches thereof @9were@7 before them.
verse	26	40	23	@@And the gate of the inner court @9was@7 over against the gate toward the north, and toward the east; and he measured from gate to gate an hundred cubits.
verse	26	40	24	After that he brought me toward the south, and behold a gate toward the south: and he measured the posts thereof and the arches thereof according to these measures.
verse	26	40	25	@@And @9there were@7 windows in it and in the arches thereof round about, like those windows: the length @9was@7 fifty cubits, and the breadth five and twenty cubits.
verse	26	40	26	@@And @9there were@7 seven steps to go up to it, and the arches thereof @9were@7 before them: and it had palm trees, one on this side, and another on that side, upon the posts thereof.
verse	26	40	27	@@And @9there was@7 a gate in the inner court toward the south: and he measured from gate to gate toward the south an hundred cubits.
verse	26	40	28	And he brought me to the inner court by the south gate: and he measured the south gate according to these measures;
verse	26	40	29	@@And the little chambers thereof, and the posts thereof, and the arches thereof, according to these measures: and @9there were@7 windows in it and in the arches thereof round about: @9it was@7 fifty cubits long, and five and twenty cubits broad.
verse	26	40	30	@@And the arches round about @9were@7 five and twenty cubits long, and five cubits broad.
verse	26	40	31	@@And the arches thereof @9were@7 toward the utter court; and palm trees @9were@7 upon the posts thereof: and the going up to it @9had@7 eight steps.
verse	26	40	32	And he brought me into the inner court toward the east: and he measured the gate according to these measures.
verse	26	40	33	@@And the little chambers thereof, and the posts thereof, and the arches thereof, @9were@7 according to these measures: and @9there were@7 windows therein and in the arches thereof round about: @9it was@7 fifty cubits long, and five and twenty cubits broad.
verse	26	40	34	@@And the arches thereof @9were@7 toward the outward court; and palm trees @9were@7 upon the posts thereof, on this side, and on that side: and the going up to it @9had@7 eight steps.
verse	26	40	35	@@And he brought me to the north gate, and measured @9it@7 according to these measures;
verse	26	40	36	@@The little chambers thereof, the posts thereof, and the arches thereof, and the windows to it round about: the length @9was@7 fifty cubits, and the breadth five and twenty cubits.
verse	26	40	37	@@And the posts thereof @9were@7 toward the utter court; and palm trees @9were@7 upon the posts thereof, on this side, and on that side: and the going up to it @9had@7 eight steps.
verse	26	40	38	@@And the chambers and the entries thereof @9were@7 by the posts of the gates, where they washed the burnt offering.
verse	26	40	39	@@And in the porch of the gate @9were@7 two tables on this side, and two tables on that side, to slay thereon the burnt offering and the sin offering and the trespass offering.
verse	26	40	40	@@And at the side without, as one goeth up to the entry of the north gate, @9were@7 two tables; and on the other side, which @9was@7 at the porch of the gate, @9were@7 two tables.
verse	26	40	41	@@Four tables @9were@7 on this side, and four tables on that side, by the side of the gate; eight tables, whereupon they slew @9their sacrifices. @7
verse	26	40	42	@@And the four tables @9were@7 of hewn stone for the burnt offering, of a cubit and an half long, and a cubit and an half broad, and one cubit high: whereupon also they laid the instruments wherewith they slew the burnt offering and the sacrifice.
verse	26	40	43	@@And within @9were@7 hooks, an hand broad, fastened round about: and upon the tables @9was@7 the flesh of the offering.
verse	26	40	44	@@And without the inner gate @9were@7 the chambers of the singers in the inner court, which @9was@7 at the side of the north gate; and their prospect @9was@7 toward the south: one at the side of the east gate @9having@7 the prospect toward the north.
verse	26	40	45	@@And he said unto me, This chamber, whose prospect @9is@7 toward the south, @9is@7 for the priests, the keepers of the charge of the house.
verse	26	40	46	@@And the chamber whose prospect @9is@7 toward the north @9is@7 for the priests, the keepers of the charge of the altar: these @9are@7 the sons of Zadok among the sons of Levi, which come near to the LORD to minister unto him.
verse	26	40	47	@@So he measured the court, an hundred cubits long, and an hundred cubits broad, foursquare; and the altar @9that was@7 before the house.
verse	26	40	48	@@And he brought me to the porch of the house, and measured @9each@7 post of the porch, five cubits on this side, and five cubits on that side: and the breadth of the gate @9was@7 three cubits on this side, and three cubits on that side.
verse	26	40	49	@@The length of the porch @9was@7 twenty cubits, and the breadth eleven cubits; and @9he brought me@7 by the steps whereby they went up to it: and @9there were@7 pillars by the posts, one on this side, and another on that side.
verse	26	41	1	@@Afterward he brought me to the temple, and measured the posts, six cubits broad on the one side, and six cubits broad on the other side, @9which was@7 the breadth of the tabernacle.
verse	26	41	2	@@And the breadth of the door @9was@7 ten cubits; and the sides of the door @9were@7 five cubits on the one side, and five cubits on the other side: and he measured the length thereof, forty cubits: and the breadth, twenty cubits.
verse	26	41	3	Then went he inward, and measured the post of the door, two cubits; and the door, six cubits; and the breadth of the door, seven cubits.
verse	26	41	4	@@So he measured the length thereof, twenty cubits; and the breadth, twenty cubits, before the temple: and he said unto me, This @9is@7 the most holy @9place. @7
verse	26	41	5	@@After he measured the wall of the house, six cubits; and the breadth of @9every@7 side chamber, four cubits, round about the house on every side.
verse	26	41	6	@@And the side chambers @9were@7 three, one over another, and thirty in order; and they entered into the wall which @9was@7 of the house for the side chambers round about, that they might have hold, but they had not hold in the wall of the house.
verse	26	41	7	@@And @9there was@7 an enlarging, and a winding about still upward to the side chambers: for the winding about of the house went still upward round about the house: therefore the breadth of the house @9was still@7 upward, and so increased @9from@7 the lowest @9chamber@7 to the highest by the midst.
verse	26	41	8	@@I saw also the height of the house round about: the foundations of the side chambers @9were@7 a full reed of six great cubits.
verse	26	41	9	@@The thickness of the wall, which @9was@7 for the side chamber without, @9was@7 five cubits: and @9that@7 which @9was@7 left @9was@7 the place of the side chambers that @9were@7 within.
verse	26	41	10	@@And between the chambers @9was@7 the wideness of twenty cubits round about the house on every side.
verse	26	41	11	@@And the doors of the side chambers @9were@7 toward @9the place that was@7 left, one door toward the north, and another door toward the south: and the breadth of the place that was left @9was@7 five cubits round about.
verse	26	41	12	@@Now the building that @9was@7 before the separate place at the end toward the west @9was@7 seventy cubits broad; and the wall of the building @9was@7 five cubits thick round about, and the length thereof ninety cubits.
verse	26	41	13	So he measured the house, an hundred cubits long; and the separate place, and the building, with the walls thereof, an hundred cubits long;
