verse	26	42	11	@@And the way before them @9was@7 like the appearance of the chambers which @9were@7 toward the north, as long as they, @9and@7 as broad as they: and all their goings out @9were@7 both according to their fashions, and according to their doors.
verse	26	42	12	@@And according to the doors of the chambers that @9were@7 toward the south @9was@7 a door in the head of the way, @9even@7 the way directly before the wall toward the east, as one entereth into them.
verse	26	42	13	@@Then said he unto me, The north chambers @9and@7 the south chambers, which @9are@7 before the separate place, they @9be@7 holy chambers, where the priests that approach unto the LORD shall eat the most holy things: there shall they lay the most holy things, and the meat offering, and the sin offering, and the trespass offering; for the place @9is@7 holy.
verse	26	42	14	@@When the priests enter therein, then shall they not go out of the holy @9place@7 into the utter court, but there they shall lay their garments wherein they minister; for they @9are@7 holy; and shall put on other garments, and shall approach to @9those things@7 which @9are@7 for the people.
verse	26	42	15	@@Now when he had made an end of measuring the inner house, he brought me forth toward the gate whose prospect @9is@7 toward the east, and measured it round about.
verse	26	42	16	He measured the east side with the measuring reed, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed round about.
verse	26	42	17	He measured the north side, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed round about.
verse	26	42	18	He measured the south side, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed.
verse	26	42	19	@@He turned about to the west side, @9and@7 measured five hundred reeds with the measuring reed.
verse	26	42	20	@@He measured it by the four sides: it had a wall round about, five hundred @9reeds@7 long, and five hundred broad, to make a separation between the sanctuary and the profane place.
verse	26	43	1	@@Afterward he brought me to the gate, @9even@7 the gate that looketh toward the east:
verse	26	43	2	@@And, behold, the glory of the God of Israel came from the way of the east: and his voice @9was@7 like a noise of many waters: and the earth shined with his glory.
verse	26	43	3	@@And @9it was@7 according to the appearance of the vision which I saw, @9even@7 according to the vision that I saw when I came to destroy the city: and the visions @9were@7 like the vision that I saw by the river Chebar; and I fell upon my face.
verse	26	43	4	@@And the glory of the LORD came into the house by the way of the gate whose prospect @9is@7 toward the east.
verse	26	43	5	So the spirit took me up, and brought me into the inner court; and, behold, the glory of the LORD filled the house.
verse	26	43	6	@@And I heard @9him@7 speaking unto me out of the house; and the man stood by me.
verse	26	43	7	@@And he said unto me, Son of man, the place of my throne, and the place of the soles of my feet, where I will dwell in the midst of the children of Israel for ever, and my holy name, shall the house of Israel no more defile, @9neither@7 they, nor their kings, by their whoredom, nor by the carcases of their kings in their high places.
verse	26	43	8	In their setting of their threshold by my thresholds, and their post by my posts, and the wall between me and them, they have even defiled my holy name by their abominations that they have committed: wherefore I have consumed them in mine anger.
verse	26	43	9	Now let them put away their whoredom, and the carcases of their kings, far from me, and I will dwell in the midst of them for ever.
verse	26	43	10	Thou son of man, shew the house to the house of Israel, that they may be ashamed of their iniquities: and let them measure the pattern.
verse	26	43	11	@@And if they be ashamed of all that they have done, shew them the form of the house, and the fashion thereof, and the goings out thereof, and the comings in thereof, and all the forms thereof, and all the ordinances thereof, and all the forms thereof, and all the laws thereof: and write @9it@7 in their sight, that they may keep the whole form thereof, and all the ordinances thereof, and do them.
verse	26	43	12	@@This @9is@7 the law of the house; Upon the top of the mountain the whole limit thereof round about @9shall be@7 most holy. Behold, this @9is@7 the law of the house.
verse	26	43	13	@@And these @9are@7 the measures of the altar after the cubits: The cubit @9is@7 a cubit and an hand breadth; even the bottom @9shall be@7 a cubit, and the breadth a cubit, and the border thereof by the edge thereof round about @9shall be@7 a span: and this @9shall be@7 the higher place of the altar.
verse	26	43	14	@@And from the bottom @9upon@7 the ground @9even@7 to the lower settle @9shall be@7 two cubits, and the breadth one cubit; and from the lesser settle @9even@7 to the greater settle @9shall be@7 four cubits, and the breadth @9one@7 cubit.
verse	26	43	15	@@So the altar @9shall be@7 four cubits; and from the altar and upward @9shall be@7 four horns.
verse	26	43	16	@@And the altar @9shall be@7 twelve @9cubits@7 long, twelve broad, square in the four squares thereof.
verse	26	43	17	@@And the settle @9shall be@7 fourteen @9cubits@7 long and fourteen broad in the four squares thereof; and the border about it @9shall be@7 half a cubit; and the bottom thereof @9shall be@7 a cubit about; and his stairs shall look toward the east.
verse	26	43	18	@@And he said unto me, Son of man, thus saith the Lord GOD; These @9are@7 the ordinances of the altar in the day when they shall make it, to offer burnt offerings thereon, and to sprinkle blood thereon.
verse	26	43	19	And thou shalt give to the priests the Levites that be of the seed of Zadok, which approach unto me, to minister unto me, saith the Lord GOD, a young bullock for a sin offering.
verse	26	43	20	@@And thou shalt take of the blood thereof, and put @9it@7 on the four horns of it, and on the four corners of the settle, and upon the border round about: thus shalt thou cleanse and purge it.
verse	26	43	21	Thou shalt take the bullock also of the sin offering, and he shall burn it in the appointed place of the house, without the sanctuary.
verse	26	43	22	@@And on the second day thou shalt offer a kid of the goats without blemish for a sin offering; and they shall cleanse the altar, as they did cleanse @9it@7 with the bullock.
verse	26	43	23	@@When thou hast made an end of cleansing @9it,@7 thou shalt offer a young bullock without blemish, and a ram out of the flock without blemish.
verse	26	43	24	@@And thou shalt offer them before the LORD, and the priests shall cast salt upon them, and they shall offer them up @9for@7 a burnt offering unto the LORD.
verse	26	43	25	@@Seven days shalt thou prepare every day a goat @9for@7 a sin offering: they shall also prepare a young bullock, and a ram out of the flock, without blemish.
verse	26	43	26	Seven days shall they purge the altar and purify it; and they shall consecrate themselves.
verse	26	43	27	@@And when these days are expired, it shall be, @9that@7 upon the eighth day, and @9so@7 forward, the priests shall make your burnt offerings upon the altar, and your peace offerings; and I will accept you, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	44	1	@@Then he brought me back the way of the gate of the outward sanctuary which looketh toward the east; and it @9was@7 shut.
verse	26	44	2	Then said the LORD unto me; This gate shall be shut, it shall not be opened, and no man shall enter in by it; because the LORD, the God of Israel, hath entered in by it, therefore it shall be shut.
verse	26	44	3	@@@9It is@7 for the prince; the prince, he shall sit in it to eat bread before the LORD; he shall enter by the way of the porch of @9that@7 gate, and shall go out by the way of the same.
verse	26	44	4	Then brought he me the way of the north gate before the house: and I looked, and, behold, the glory of the LORD filled the house of the LORD: and I fell upon my face.
verse	26	44	5	And the LORD said unto me, Son of man, mark well, and behold with thine eyes, and hear with thine ears all that I say unto thee concerning all the ordinances of the house of the LORD, and all the laws thereof; and mark well the entering in of the house, with every going forth of the sanctuary.
verse	26	44	6	@@And thou shalt say to the rebellious, @9even@7 to the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; O ye house of Israel, let it suffice you of all your abominations,
verse	26	44	7	@@In that ye have brought @9into my sanctuary@7 strangers, uncircumcised in heart, and uncircumcised in flesh, to be in my sanctuary, to pollute it, @9even@7 my house, when ye offer my bread, the fat and the blood, and they have broken my covenant because of all your abominations.
verse	26	44	8	And ye have not kept the charge of mine holy things: but ye have set keepers of my charge in my sanctuary for yourselves.
verse	26	44	9	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; No stranger, uncircumcised in heart, nor uncircumcised in flesh, shall enter into my sanctuary, of any stranger that @9is@7 among the children of Israel.
verse	26	44	10	And the Levites that are gone away far from me, when Israel went astray, which went astray away from me after their idols; they shall even bear their iniquity.
verse	26	44	11	@@Yet they shall be ministers in my sanctuary, @9having@7 charge at the gates of the house, and ministering to the house: they shall slay the burnt offering and the sacrifice for the people, and they shall stand before them to minister unto them.
verse	26	44	12	Because they ministered unto them before their idols, and caused the house of Israel to fall into iniquity; therefore have I lifted up mine hand against them, saith the Lord GOD, and they shall bear their iniquity.
verse	26	44	13	@@And they shall not come near unto me, to do the office of a priest unto me, nor to come near to any of my holy things, in the most holy @9place:@7 but they shall bear their shame, and their abominations which they have committed.
verse	26	44	14	But I will make them keepers of the charge of the house, for all the service thereof, and for all that shall be done therein.
verse	26	44	15	But the priests the Levites, the sons of Zadok, that kept the charge of my sanctuary when the children of Israel went astray from me, they shall come near to me to minister unto me, and they shall stand before me to offer unto me the fat and the blood, saith the Lord GOD:
verse	26	44	16	They shall enter into my sanctuary, and they shall come near to my table, to minister unto me, and they shall keep my charge.
verse	26	44	17	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 when they enter in at the gates of the inner court, they shall be clothed with linen garments; and no wool shall come upon them, whiles they minister in the gates of the inner court, and within.
verse	26	44	18	@@They shall have linen bonnets upon their heads, and shall have linen breeches upon their loins; they shall not gird @9themselves@7 with any thing that causeth sweat.
verse	26	44	19	@@And when they go forth into the utter court, @9even@7 into the utter court to the people, they shall put off their garments wherein they ministered, and lay them in the holy chambers, and they shall put on other garments; and they shall not sanctify the people with their garments.
verse	26	44	20	Neither shall they shave their heads, nor suffer their locks to grow long; they shall only poll their heads.
verse	26	44	21	Neither shall any priest drink wine, when they enter into the inner court.
verse	26	44	22	Neither shall they take for their wives a widow, nor her that is put away: but they shall take maidens of the seed of the house of Israel, or a widow that had a priest before.
verse	26	44	23	@@And they shall teach my people @9the difference@7 between the holy and profane, and cause them to discern between the unclean and the clean.
verse	26	44	24	@@And in controversy they shall stand in judgment; @9and@7 they shall judge it according to my judgments: and they shall keep my laws and my statutes in all mine assemblies; and they shall hallow my sabbaths.
verse	26	44	25	And they shall come at no dead person to defile themselves: but for father, or for mother, or for son, or for daughter, for brother, or for sister that hath had no husband, they may defile themselves.
verse	26	44	26	And after he is cleansed, they shall reckon unto him seven days.
verse	26	44	27	And in the day that he goeth into the sanctuary, unto the inner court, to minister in the sanctuary, he shall offer his sin offering, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	44	28	@@And it shall be unto them for an inheritance: I @9am@7 their inheritance: and ye shall give them no possession in Israel: I @9am@7 their possession.
verse	26	44	29	They shall eat the meat offering, and the sin offering, and the trespass offering; and every dedicated thing in Israel shall be theirs.
verse	26	44	30	@@And the first of all the firstfruits of all @9things,@7 and every oblation of all, of every @9sort@7 of your oblations, shall be the priest's: ye shall also give unto the priest the first of your dough, that he may cause the blessing to rest in thine house.
verse	26	44	31	The priests shall not eat of any thing that is dead of itself, or torn, whether it be fowl or beast.
verse	26	45	1	@@Moreover, when ye shall divide by lot the land for inheritance, ye shall offer an oblation unto the LORD, an holy portion of the land: the length @9shall be@7 the length of five and twenty thousand @9reeds,@7 and the breadth @9shall be@7 ten thousand. This @9shall be@7 holy in all the borders thereof round about.
verse	26	45	2	@@Of this there shall be for the sanctuary five hundred @9in length,@7 with five hundred @9in breadth,@7 square round about; and fifty cubits round about for the suburbs thereof.
verse	26	45	3	@@And of this measure shalt thou measure the length of five and twenty thousand, and the breadth of ten thousand: and in it shall be the sanctuary @9and@7 the most holy @9place. @7
verse	26	45	4	@@The holy @9portion@7 of the land shall be for the priests the ministers of the sanctuary, which shall come near to minister unto the LORD: and it shall be a place for their houses, and an holy place for the sanctuary.
verse	26	45	5	And the five and twenty thousand of length, and the ten thousand of breadth, shall also the Levites, the ministers of the house, have for themselves, for a possession for twenty chambers.
verse	26	45	6	@@And ye shall appoint the possession of the city five thousand broad, and five and twenty thousand long, over against the oblation of the holy @9portion:@7 it shall be for the whole house of Israel.
verse	26	45	7	@@And @9a portion shall be@7 for the prince on the one side and on the other side of the oblation of the holy @9portion,@7 and of the possession of the city, before the oblation of the holy @9portion,@7 and before the possession of the city, from the west side westward, and from the east side eastward: and the length @9shall be@7 over against one of the portions, from the west border unto the east border.
verse	26	45	8	@@In the land shall be his possession in Israel: and my princes shall no more oppress my people; and @9the rest of@7 the land shall they give to the house of Israel according to their tribes.
verse	26	45	9	Thus saith the Lord GOD; Let it suffice you, O princes of Israel: remove violence and spoil, and execute judgment and justice, take away your exactions from my people, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	45	10	Ye shall have just balances, and a just ephah, and a just bath. I
verse	26	45	11	The ephah and the bath shall be of one measure, that the bath may contain the tenth part of an homer, and the ephah the tenth part of an homer: the measure thereof shall be after the homer.
verse	26	45	12	@@And the shekel @9shall be@7 twenty gerahs: twenty shekels, five and twenty shekels, fifteen shekels, shall be your maneh.
verse	26	45	13	@@This @9is@7 the oblation that ye shall offer; the sixth part of an ephah of an homer of wheat, and ye shall give the sixth part of an ephah of an homer of barley:
verse	26	45	14	@@Concerning the ordinance of oil, the bath of oil, @9ye shall offer@7 the tenth part of a bath out of the cor, @9which is@7 an homer of ten baths; for ten baths @9are@7 an homer:
verse	26	45	15	And one lamb out of the flock, out of two hundred, out of the fat pastures of Israel; for a meat offering, and for a burnt offering, and for peace offerings, to make reconciliation for them, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	45	16	All the people of the land shall give this oblation for the prince in Israel.
verse	26	45	17	@@And it shall be the prince's part @9to give@7 burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and drink offerings, in the feasts, and in the new moons, and in the sabbaths, in all solemnities of the house of Israel: he shall prepare the sin offering, and the meat offering, and the burnt offering, and the peace offerings, to make reconciliation for the house of Israel.
verse	26	45	18	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the first @9month,@7 in the first @9day@7 of the month, thou shalt take a young bullock without blemish, and cleanse the sanctuary:
verse	26	45	19	@@And the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering, and put @9it@7 upon the posts of the house, and upon the four corners of the settle of the altar, and upon the posts of the gate of the inner court.
verse	26	45	20	@@And so thou shalt do the seventh @9day@7 of the month for every one that erreth, and for @9him that is@7 simple: so shall ye reconcile the house.
verse	26	45	21	@@In the first @9month,@7 in the fourteenth day of the month, ye shall have the passover, a feast of seven days; unleavened bread shall be eaten.
verse	26	45	22	@@And upon that day shall the prince prepare for himself and for all the people of the land a bullock @9for@7 a sin offering.
verse	26	45	23	@@And seven days of the feast he shall prepare a burnt offering to the LORD, seven bullocks and seven rams without blemish daily the seven days; and a kid of the goats daily @9for@7 a sin offering.
verse	26	45	24	And he shall prepare a meat offering of an ephah for a bullock, and an ephah for a ram, and an hin of oil for an ephah.
verse	26	45	25	@@In the seventh @9month,@7 in the fifteenth day of the month, shall he do the like in the feast of the seven days, according to the sin offering, according to the burnt offering, and according to the meat offering, and according to the oil.
verse	26	46	1	Thus saith the Lord GOD; The gate of the inner court that looketh toward the east shall be shut the six working days; but on the sabbath it shall be opened, and in the day of the new moon it shall be opened.
verse	26	46	2	@@And the prince shall enter by the way of the porch of @9that@7 gate without, and shall stand by the post of the gate, and the priests shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, and he shall worship at the threshold of the gate: then he shall go forth; but the gate shall not be shut until the evening.
verse	26	46	3	Likewise the people of the land shall worship at the door of this gate before the LORD in the sabbaths and in the new moons.
verse	26	46	4	@@And the burnt offering that the prince shall offer unto the LORD in the sabbath day @9shall be@7 six lambs without blemish, and a ram without blemish.
verse	26	46	5	@@And the meat offering @9shall be@7 an ephah for a ram, and the meat offering for the lambs as he shall be able to give, and an hin of oil to an ephah.
verse	26	46	6	@@And in the day of the new moon @9it shall be@7 a young bullock without blemish, and six lambs, and a ram: they shall be without blemish.
verse	26	46	7	And he shall prepare a meat offering, an ephah for a bullock, and an ephah for a ram, and for the lambs according as his hand shall attain unto, and an hin of oil to an ephah.
verse	26	46	8	@@And when the prince shall enter, he shall go in by the way of the porch of @9that@7 gate, and he shall go forth by the way thereof.
verse	26	46	9	But when the people of the land shall come before the LORD in the solemn feasts, he that entereth in by the way of the north gate to worship shall go out by the way of the south gate; and he that entereth by the way of the south gate shall go forth by the way of the north gate: he shall not return by the way of the gate whereby he came in, but shall go forth over against it.
verse	26	46	10	And the prince in the midst of them, when they go in, shall go in; and when they go forth, shall go forth.
verse	26	46	11	And in the feasts and in the solemnities the meat offering shall be an ephah to a bullock, and ephah to a ram, and to the lambs as he is able to give, and an hin of oil to an ephah.
verse	26	46	12	@@Now when the prince shall prepare a voluntary burnt offering or peace offerings voluntarily unto the LORD, @9one@7 shall then open him the gate that looketh toward the east, and he shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, as he did on the sabbath day: then he shall go forth; and after his going forth @9one@7 shall shut the gate.
verse	26	46	13	@@Thou shalt daily prepare a burnt offering unto the LORD @9of@7 a lamb of the first year without blemish: thou shalt prepare it every morning.
verse	26	46	14	And thou shalt prepare a meat offering for it every morning, the sixth part of an ephah, and the third part of an hin of oil, to temper with the fine flour; a meat offering continually by a perpetual ordinance unto the LORD.
verse	26	46	15	@@Thus shall they prepare the lamb, and the meat offering, and the oil, every morning @9for@7 a continual burnt offering.
verse	26	46	16	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; If the prince give a gift unto any of his sons, the inheritance thereof shall be his sons'; it @9shall be@7 their possession by inheritance.
verse	26	46	17	But if he give a gift of his inheritance to one of his servants, then it shall be his to the year of liberty; after it shall return to the prince: but his inheritance shall be his sons' for them.
verse	26	46	18	@@Moreover the prince shall not take of the people's inheritance by oppression, to thrust them out of their possession; @9but@7 he shall give his sons inheritance out of his own possession: that my people be not scattered every man from his possession.
verse	26	46	19	@@After he brought me through the entry, which @9was@7 at the side of the gate, into the holy chambers of the priests, which looked toward the north: and, behold, there @9was@7 a place on the two sides westward.
verse	26	46	20	@@Then said he unto me, This is the place where the priests shall boil the trespass offering and the sin offering, where they shall bake the meat offering; that they bear @9them@7 not out into the utter court, to sanctify the people.
verse	26	46	21	@@Then he brought me forth into the utter court, and caused me to pass by the four corners of the court; and, behold, in every corner of the court @9there was@7 a court.
verse	26	46	22	@@In the four corners of the court @9there were@7 courts joined of forty @9cubits@7 long and thirty broad: these four corners @9were@7 of one measure.
verse	26	46	23	@@And @9there was@7 a row @9of building@7 round about in them, round about them four, and @9it was@7 made with boiling places under the rows round about.
verse	26	46	24	@@Then said he unto me, These @9are@7 the places of them that boil, where the ministers of the house shall boil the sacrifice of the people.
verse	26	47	1	@@Afterward he brought me again unto the door of the house; and, behold, waters issued out from under the threshold of the house eastward: for the forefront of the house @9stood toward@7 the east, and the waters came down from under from the right side of the house, at the south @9side@7 of the altar.
verse	26	47	2	Then brought he me out of the way of the gate northward, and led me about the way without unto the utter gate by the way that looketh eastward; and, behold, there ran out waters on the right side.
verse	26	47	3	@@And when the man that had the line in his hand went forth eastward, he measured a thousand cubits, and he brought me through the waters; the waters @9were@7 to the ancles.
verse	26	47	4	@@Again he measured a thousand, and brought me through the waters; the waters @9were@7 to the knees. Again he measured a thousand, and brought me through; the waters @9were@7 to the loins.
verse	26	47	5	@@Afterward he measured a thousand; @9and it was@7 a river that I could not pass over: for the waters were risen, waters to swim in, a river that could not be passed over.
verse	26	47	6	@@And he said unto me, Son of man, hast thou seen @9this?@7 Then he brought me, and caused me to return to the brink of the river.
verse	26	47	7	@@Now when I had returned, behold, at the bank of the river @9were@7 very many trees on the one side and on the other.
verse	26	47	8	@@Then said he unto me, These waters issue out toward the east country, and go down into the desert, and go into the sea: @9which being@7 brought forth into the sea, the waters shall be healed.
verse	26	47	9	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 every thing that liveth, which moveth, whithersoever the rivers shall come, shall live: and there shall be a very great multitude of fish, because these waters shall come thither: for they shall be healed; and every thing shall live whither the river cometh.
verse	26	47	10	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 the fishers shall stand upon it from Engedi even unto En-eglaim; they shall be a @9place@7 to spread forth nets; their fish shall be according to their kinds, as the fish of the great sea, exceeding many.
verse	26	47	11	But the miry places thereof and the marishes thereof shall not be healed; they shall be given to salt.
verse	26	47	12	And by the river upon the bank thereof, on this side and on that side, shall grow all trees for meat, whose leaf shall not fade, neither shall the fruit thereof be consumed: it shall bring forth new fruit according to his months, because their waters they issued out of the sanctuary: and the fruit thereof shall be for meat, and the leaf thereof for medicine.
verse	26	47	13	@@Thus saith the Lord GOD; This @9shall be@7 the border, whereby ye shall inherit the land according to the twelve tribes of Israel: Joseph @9shall have two@7 portions.
verse	26	47	14	@@And ye shall inherit it, one as well as another: @9concerning@7 the which I lifted up mine hand to give it unto your fathers: and this land shall fall unto you for inheritance.
verse	26	47	15	@@And this @9shall be@7 the border of the land toward the north side, from the great sea, the way of Hethlon, as men go to Zedad;
verse	26	47	16	@@Hamath, Berothah, Sibraim, which @9is@7 between the border of Damascus and the border of Hamath; Hazar-hatticon, which is by the coast of Hauran.
verse	26	47	17	@@And the border from the sea shall be Hazarenan, the border of Damascus, and the north northward, and the border of Hamath. And @9this is@7 the north side.
verse	26	47	18	@@And the east side ye shall measure from Hauran, and from Damascus, and from Gilead, and from the land of Israel by Jordan, from the border unto the east sea. And @9this is@7 the east side.
verse	26	47	19	@@And the south side southward, from Tamar @9even@7 to the waters of strife @9in@7 Kadesh, the river to the great sea. And @9this is@7 the south side southward.
verse	26	47	20	@@The west side also @9shall be@7 the great sea from the border, till a man come over against Hamath. This @9is@7 the west side.
verse	26	47	21	So shall ye divide this land unto you according to the tribes of Israel.
verse	26	47	22	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 ye shall divide it by lot for an inheritance unto you, and to the strangers that sojourn among you, which shall beget children among you: and they shall be unto you as born in the country among the children of Israel; they shall have inheritance with you among the tribes of Israel.
verse	26	47	23	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 in what tribe the stranger sojourneth, there shall ye give @9him@7 his inheritance, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	48	1	@@Now these @9are@7 the names of the tribes. From the north end to the coast of the way of Hethlon, as one goeth to Hamath, Hazarenan, the border of Damascus northward, to the coast of Hamath; for these are his sides east @9and@7 west; a @9portion for@7 Dan.
verse	26	48	2	@@And by the border of Dan, from the east side unto the west side, a @9portion for@7 Asher.
verse	26	48	3	@@And by the border of Asher, from the east side even unto the west side, a @9portion for@7 Naphtali.
verse	26	48	4	@@And by the border of Naphtali, from the east side unto the west side, a @9portion for@7 Manasseh.
verse	26	48	5	@@And by the border of Manasseh, from the east side unto the west side, a @9portion for@7 Ephraim.
verse	26	48	6	@@And by the border of Ephraim, from the east side even unto the west side, a @9portion for@7 Reuben.
verse	26	48	7	@@And by the border of Reuben, from the east side unto the west side, a @9portion for@7 Judah.
verse	26	48	8	@@And by the border of Judah, from the east side unto the west side, shall be the offering which ye shall offer of five and twenty thousand @9reeds in@7 breadth, and @9in@7 length as one of the @9other@7 parts, from the east side unto the west side: and the sanctuary shall be in the midst of it.
verse	26	48	9	@@The oblation that ye shall offer unto the LORD @9shall be@7 of five and twenty thousand in length, and of ten thousand in breadth.
verse	26	48	10	@@And for them, @9even@7 for the priests, shall be @9this@7 holy oblation; toward the north five and twenty thousand @9in length,@7 and toward the west ten thousand in breadth, and toward the east ten thousand in breadth, and toward the south five and twenty thousand in length: and the sanctuary of the LORD shall be in the midst thereof.
verse	26	48	11	@@@9It shall be@7 for the priests that are sanctified of the sons of Zadok; which have kept my charge, which went not astray when the children of Israel went astray, as the Levites went astray.
verse	26	48	12	@@And @9this@7 oblation of the land that is offered shall be unto them a thing most holy by the border of the Levites.
verse	26	48	13	@@And over against the border of the priests the Levites @9shall have@7 five and twenty thousand in length, and ten thousand in breadth: all the length @9shall be@7 five and twenty thousand, and the breadth ten thousand.
verse	26	48	14	@@And they shall not sell of it, neither exchange, nor alienate the firstfruits of the land: for @9it is@7 holy unto the LORD.
verse	26	48	15	@@And the five thousand, that are left in the breadth over against the five and twenty thousand, shall be a profane @9place@7 for the city, for dwelling, and for suburbs: and the city shall be in the midst thereof.
verse	26	48	16	@@And these @9shall be@7 the measures thereof; the north side four thousand and five hundred, and the south side four thousand and five hundred, and on the east side four thousand and five hundred, and the west side four thousand and five hundred.
verse	26	48	17	And the suburbs of the city shall be toward the north two hundred and fifty, and toward the south two hundred and fifty, and toward the east two hundred and fifty, and toward the west two hundred and fifty.
verse	26	48	18	@@And the residue in length over against the oblation of the holy @9portion shall be@7 ten thousand eastward, and ten thousand westward: and it shall be over against the oblation of the holy @9portion;@7 and the increase thereof shall be for food unto them that serve the city.
verse	26	48	19	And they that serve the city shall serve it out of all the tribes of Israel.
verse	26	48	20	@@All the oblation @9shall be@7 five and twenty thousand by five and twenty thousand: ye shall offer the holy oblation foursquare, with the possession of the city.
verse	26	48	21	@@And the residue @9shall be@7 for the prince, on the one side and on the other of the holy oblation, and of the possession of the city, over against the five and twenty thousand of the oblation toward the east border, and westward over against the five and twenty thousand toward the west border, over against the portions for the prince: and it shall be the holy oblation; and the sanctuary of the house @9shall be@7 in the midst thereof.
verse	26	48	22	@@Moreover from the possession of the Levites, and from the possession of the city, @9being@7 in the midst @9of that@7 which is the prince's, between the border of Judah and the border of Benjamin, shall be for the prince.
verse	26	48	23	@@As for the rest of the tribes, from the east side unto the west side, Benjamin @9shall have@7 a @9portion. @7
verse	26	48	24	@@And by the border of Benjamin, from the east side unto the west side, Simeon @9shall have@7 a @9portion. @7
verse	26	48	25	@@And by the border of Simeon, from the east side unto the west side, Issachar a @9portion. @7
verse	26	48	26	@@And by the border of Issachar, from the east side unto the west side, Zebulun a @9portion. @7
verse	26	48	27	@@And by the border of Zebulun, from the east side unto the west side, Gad a @9portion. @7
verse	26	48	28	@@And by the border of Gad, at the south side southward, the border shall be even from Tamar @9unto@7 the waters of strife @9in@7 Kadesh, @9and@7 to the river toward the great sea.
verse	26	48	29	@@This @9is@7 the land which ye shall divide by lot unto the tribes of Israel for inheritance, and these @9are@7 their portions, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	26	48	30	@@And these @9are@7 the goings out of the city on the north side, four thousand and five hundred measures.
verse	26	48	31	@@And the gates of the city @9shall be@7 after the names of the tribes of Israel: three gates northward; one gate of Reuben, one gate of Judah, one gate of Levi.
verse	26	48	32	And at the east side four thousand and five hundred: and three gates; and one gate of Joseph, one gate of Benjamin, one gate of Dan.
verse	26	48	33	And at the south side four thousand and five hundred measures: and three gates; one gate of Simeon, one gate of Issachar, one gate of Zebulun.
verse	26	48	34	@@At the west side four thousand and five hundred, @9with@7 their three gates; one gate of Gad, one gate of Asher, one gate of Naphtali.
verse	26	48	35	@@@9It was@7 round about eighteen thousand @9measures:@7 and the name of the city from @9that@7 day @9shall be,@7 The LORD @9is@7 there.
verse	27	1	1	In the third year of the reign of Jehoiakim king of Judah came Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon unto Jerusalem, and besieged it.
verse	27	1	2	And the Lord gave Jehoiakim king of Judah into his hand, with part of the vessels of the house of God: which he carried into the land of Shinar to the house of his god; and he brought the vessels into the treasure house of his god.
verse	27	1	3	@@And the king spake unto Ashpenaz the master of his eunuchs, that he should bring @9certain@7 of the children of Israel, and of the king's seed, and of the princes;
verse	27	1	4	@@Children in whom @9was@7 no blemish, but well favoured, and skilful in all wisdom, and cunning in knowledge, and understanding science, and such as @9had@7 ability in them to stand in the king's palace, and whom they might teach the learning and the tongue of the Chaldeans.
verse	27	1	5	And the king appointed them a daily provision of the king's meat, and of the wine which he drank: so nourishing them three years, that at the end thereof they might stand before the king.
verse	27	1	6	Now among these were of the children of Judah, Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah:
verse	27	1	7	@@Unto whom the prince of the eunuchs gave names: for he gave unto Daniel @9the name@7 of Belteshazzar; and to Hananiah, of Shadrach; and to Mishael, of Meshach; and to Azariah, of Abed-nego.
verse	27	1	8	But Daniel purposed in his heart that he would not defile himself with the portion of the king's meat, nor with the wine which he drank: therefore he requested of the prince of the eunuchs that he might not defile himself.
verse	27	1	9	Now God had brought Daniel into favour and tender love with the prince of the eunuchs.
verse	27	1	10	@@And the prince of the eunuchs said unto Daniel, I fear my lord the king, who hath appointed your meat and your drink: for why should he see your faces worse liking than the children which @9are@7 of your sort? then shall ye make @9me@7 endanger my head to the king.
verse	27	1	11	Then said Daniel to Melzar, whom the prince of the eunuchs had set over Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah,
verse	27	1	12	Prove thy servants, I beseech thee, ten days; and let them give us pulse to eat, and water to drink.
verse	27	1	13	Then let our countenances be looked upon before thee, and the countenance of the children that eat of the portion of the king's meat: and as thou seest, deal with thy servants.
verse	27	1	14	So he consented to them in this matter, and proved them ten days.
verse	27	1	15	And at the end of ten days their countenances appeared fairer and fatter in flesh than all the children which did eat the portion of the king's meat.
verse	27	1	16	Thus Melzar took away the portion of their meat, and the wine that they should drink; and gave them pulse.
verse	27	1	17	As for these four children, God gave them knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom: and Daniel had understanding in all visions and dreams.
verse	27	1	18	Now at the end of the days that the king had said he should bring them in, then the prince of the eunuchs brought them in before Nebuchadnezzar.
verse	27	1	19	And the king communed with them; and among them all was found none like Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah: therefore stood they before the king.
verse	27	1	20	@@And in all matters of wisdom @9and@7 understanding, that the king enquired of them, he found them ten times better than all the magicians @9and@7 astrologers that @9were@7 in all his realm.
verse	27	1	21	@@And Daniel continued @9even@7 unto the first year of king Cyrus.
verse	27	2	1	And in the second year of the reign of Nebuchadnezzar Nebuchadnezzar dreamed dreams, wherewith his spirit was troubled, and his sleep brake from him.
verse	27	2	2	Then the king commanded to call the magicians, and the astrologers, and the sorcerers, and the Chaldeans, for to shew the king his dreams. So they came and stood before the king.
verse	27	2	3	And the king said unto them, I have dreamed a dream, and my spirit was troubled to know the dream.
verse	27	2	4	Then spake the Chaldeans to the king in Syriack, O king, live for ever: tell thy servants the dream, and we will shew the interpretation.
verse	27	2	5	The king answered and said to the Chaldeans, The thing is gone from me: if ye will not make known unto me the dream, with the interpretation thereof, ye shall be cut in pieces, and your houses shall be made a dunghill.
verse	27	2	6	But if ye shew the dream, and the interpretation thereof, ye shall receive of me gifts and rewards and great honour: therefore shew me the dream, and the interpretation thereof.
verse	27	2	7	They answered again and said, Let the king tell his servants the dream, and we will shew the interpretation of it.
verse	27	2	8	The king answered and said, I know of certainty that ye would gain the time, because ye see the thing is gone from me.
verse	27	2	9	@@But if ye will not make known unto me the dream, @9there is but@7 one decree for you: for ye have prepared lying and corrupt words to speak before me, till the time be changed: therefore tell me the dream, and I shall know that ye can shew me the interpretation thereof.
verse	27	2	10	@@The Chaldeans answered before the king, and said, There is not a man upon the earth that can shew the king's matter: therefore @9there is@7 no king, lord, nor ruler, @9that@7 asked such things at any magician, or astrologer, or Chaldean.
verse	27	2	11	@@And @9it is@7 a rare thing that the king requireth, and there is none other that can shew it before the king, except the gods, whose dwelling is not with flesh.
verse	27	2	12	@@For this cause the king was angry and very furious, and commanded to destroy all the wise @9men@7 of Babylon.
verse	27	2	13	@@And the decree went forth that the wise @9men@7 should be slain; and they sought Daniel and his fellows to be slain.
verse	27	2	14	@@Then Daniel answered with counsel and wisdom to Arioch the captain of the king's guard, which was gone forth to slay the wise @9men@7 of Babylon:
verse	27	2	15	@@He answered and said to Arioch the king's captain, Why @9is@7 the decree @9so@7 hasty from the king? Then Arioch made the thing known to Daniel.
verse	27	2	16	Then Daniel went in, and desired of the king that he would give him time, and that he would shew the king the interpretation.
verse	27	2	17	Then Daniel went to his house, and made the thing known to Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, his companions:
verse	27	2	18	@@That they would desire mercies of the God of heaven concerning this secret; that Daniel and his fellows should not perish with the rest of the wise @9men@7 of Babylon.
verse	27	2	19	Then was the secret revealed unto Daniel in a night vision. Then Daniel blessed the God of heaven.
verse	27	2	20	Daniel answered and said, Blessed be the name of God for ever and ever: for wisdom and might are his:
verse	27	2	21	And he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom unto the wise, and knowledge to them that know understanding:
verse	27	2	22	@@He revealeth the deep and secret things: he knoweth what @9is@7 in the darkness, and the light dwelleth with him.
verse	27	2	23	@@I thank thee, and praise thee, O thou God of my fathers, who hast given me wisdom and might, and hast made known unto me now what we desired of thee: for thou hast @9now@7 made known unto us the king's matter.
verse	27	2	24	@@Therefore Daniel went in unto Arioch, whom the king had ordained to destroy the wise @9men@7 of Babylon: he went and said thus unto him; Destroy not the wise @9men@7 of Babylon: bring me in before the king, and I will shew unto the king the interpretation.
verse	27	2	25	Then Arioch brought in Daniel before the king in haste and said thus unto him, I have found a man of the captives of Judah, that will make known unto the king the interpretation.
verse	27	2	26	@@The king answered and said to Daniel, whose name @9was@7 Belteshazzar, Art thou able to make known unto me the dream which I have seen, and the interpretation thereof?
verse	27	2	27	@@Daniel answered in the presence of the king, and said, The secret which the king hath demanded cannot the wise @9men,@7 the astrologers, the magicians, the soothsayers, shew unto the king;
verse	27	2	28	But there is a God in heaven that revealeth secrets, and maketh known to the king Nebuchadnezzar what shall be in the latter days. Thy dream, and the visions of thy head upon thy bed, are these;
verse	27	2	29	@@As for thee, O king, thy thoughts came @9into thy mind@7 upon thy bed, what should come to pass hereafter: and he that revealeth secrets maketh known to thee what shall come to pass.
verse	27	2	30	@@But as for me, this secret is not revealed to me for @9any@7 wisdom that I have more than any living, but for @9their@7 sakes that shall make known the interpretation to the king, and that thou mightest know the thoughts of thy heart.
verse	27	2	31	@@Thou, O king, sawest, and behold a great image. This great image, whose brightness was excellent, stood before thee; and the form thereof @9was@7 terrible.
verse	27	2	32	@@This image's head @9was@7 of fine gold, his breast and his arms of silver, his belly and his thighs of brass,
verse	27	2	33	His legs of iron, his feet part of iron and part of clay.
verse	27	2	34	@@Thou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet @9that were@7 of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces.
verse	27	2	35	Then was the iron, the clay, the brass, the silver, and the gold, broken to pieces together, and became like the chaff of the summer threshingfloors; and the wind carried them away, that no place was found for them: and the stone that smote the image became a great mountain, and filled the whole earth.
verse	27	2	36	@@This @9is@7 the dream; and we will tell the interpretation thereof before the king.
verse	27	2	37	@@Thou, O king, @9art@7 a king of kings: for the God of heaven hath given thee a kingdom, power, and strength, and glory.
verse	27	2	38	@@And wheresoever the children of men dwell, the beasts of the field and the fowls of the heaven hath he given into thine hand, and hath made thee ruler over them all. Thou @9art@7 this head of gold.
verse	27	2	39	And after thee shall arise another kingdom inferior to thee, and another third kingdom of brass, which shall bear rule over all the earth.
verse	27	2	40	@@And the fourth kingdom shall be strong as iron: forasmuch as iron breaketh in pieces and subdueth all @9things:@7 and as iron that breaketh all these, shall it break in pieces and bruise.
verse	27	2	41	And whereas thou sawest the feet and toes, part of potters' clay, and part of iron, the kingdom shall be divided; but there shall be in it of the strength of the iron, forasmuch as thou sawest the iron mixed with miry clay.
verse	27	2	42	@@And @9as@7 the toes of the feet @9were@7 part of iron, and part of clay, so the kingdom shall be partly strong, and partly broken.
verse	27	2	43	And whereas thou sawest iron mixed with miry clay, they shall mingle themselves with the seed of men: but they shall not cleave one to another, even as iron is not mixed with clay.
verse	27	2	44	@@And in the days of these kings shall the God of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed: and the kingdom shall not be left to other people, @9but@7 it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever.
verse	27	2	45	Forasmuch as thou sawest that the stone was cut out of the mountain without hands, and that it brake in pieces the iron, the brass, the clay, the silver, and the gold; the great God hath made known to the king what shall come to pass hereafter: and the dream is certain, and the interpretation thereof sure.
verse	27	2	46	Then the king Nebuchadnezzar fell upon his face, and worshipped Daniel, and commanded that they should offer an oblation and sweet odours unto him.
verse	27	2	47	@@The king answered unto Daniel, and said, Of a truth @9it is,@7 that your God is a God of gods, and a Lord of kings, and a revealer of secrets, seeing thou couldst reveal this secret.
verse	27	2	48	@@Then the king made Daniel a great man, and gave him many great gifts, and made him ruler over the whole province of Babylon, and chief of the governors over all the wise @9men@7 of Babylon.
verse	27	2	49	@@Then Daniel requested of the king, and he set Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, over the affairs of the province of Babylon: but Daniel @9sat@7 in the gate of the king.
verse	27	3	1	@@Nebuchadnezzar the king made an image of gold, whose height @9was@7 threescore cubits, @9and@7 the breadth thereof six cubits: he set it up in the plain of Dura, in the province of Babylon.
verse	27	3	2	Then Nebuchadnezzar the king sent to gather together the princes, the governors, and the captains, the judges, the treasurers, the counsellors, the sheriffs, and all the rulers of the provinces, to come to the dedication of the image which Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up.
verse	27	3	3	Then the princes, the governors, and captains, the judges, the treasurers, the counsellors, the sheriffs, and all the rulers of the provinces, were gathered together unto the dedication of the image that Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up; and they stood before the image that Nebuchadnezzar had set up.
verse	27	3	4	Then an herald cried aloud, To you it is commanded, O people, nations, and languages,
verse	27	3	5	@@@9That@7 at what time ye hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, ye fall down and worship the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar the king hath set up:
verse	27	3	6	And whoso falleth not down and worshippeth shall the same hour be cast into the midst of a burning fiery furnace.
verse	27	3	7	@@Therefore at that time, when all the people heard the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and all kinds of musick, all the people, the nations, and the languages, fell down @9and@7 worshipped the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up.
verse	27	3	8	Wherefore at that time certain Chaldeans came near, and accused the Jews.
verse	27	3	9	They spake and said to the king Nebuchadnezzar, O king, live for ever.
verse	27	3	10	Thou, O king, hast made a decree, that every man that shall hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, shall fall down and worship the golden image:
verse	27	3	11	@@And whoso falleth not down and worshippeth, @9that@7 he should be cast into the midst of a burning fiery furnace.
verse	27	3	12	There are certain Jews whom thou hast set over the affairs of the province of Babylon, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego; these men, O king, have not regarded thee: they serve not thy gods, nor worship the golden image which thou hast set up.
verse	27	3	13	@@Then Nebuchadnezzar in @9his@7 rage and fury commanded to bring Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego. Then they brought these men before the king.
verse	27	3	14	@@Nebuchadnezzar spake and said unto them, @9Is it@7 true, O Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, do not ye serve my gods, nor worship the golden image which I have set up?
verse	27	3	15	@@Now if ye be ready that at what time ye hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, ye fall down and worship the image which I have made; @9well:@7 but if ye worship not, ye shall be cast the same hour into the midst of a burning fiery furnace; and who @9is@7 that God that shall deliver you out of my hands?
verse	27	3	16	@@Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, answered and said to the king, O Nebuchadnezzar, we @9are@7 not careful to answer thee in this matter.
verse	27	3	17	@@If it be @9so,@7 our God whom we serve is able to deliver us from the burning fiery furnace, and he will deliver @9us@7 out of thine hand, O king.
verse	27	3	18	But if not, be it known unto thee, O king, that we will not serve thy gods, nor worship the golden image which thou hast set up.
verse	27	3	19	@@Then was Nebuchadnezzar full of fury, and the form of his visage was changed against Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego: @9therefore@7 he spake, and commanded that they should heat the furnace one seven times more than it was wont to be heated.
verse	27	3	20	@@And he commanded the most mighty men that @9were@7 in his army to bind Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, @9and@7 to cast @9them@7 into the burning fiery furnace.
verse	27	3	21	@@Then these men were bound in their coats, their hosen, and their hats, and their @9other@7 garments, and were cast into the midst of the burning fiery furnace.
verse	27	3	22	Therefore because the king's commandment was urgent, and the furnace exceeding hot, the flame of the fire slew those men that took up Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego.
verse	27	3	23	And these three men, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, fell down bound into the midst of the burning fiery furnace.
verse	27	3	24	@@Then Nebuchadnezzar the king was astonied, and rose up in haste, @9and@7 spake, and said unto his counsellors, Did not we cast three men bound into the midst of the fire? They answered and said unto the king, True, O king.
verse	27	3	25	He answered and said, Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of God.
verse	27	3	26	@@Then Nebuchadnezzar came near to the mouth of the burning fiery furnace, @9and@7 spake, and said, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, ye servants of the most high God, come forth, and come @9hither.@7 Then Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, came forth of the midst of the fire.
verse	27	3	27	And the princes, governors, and captains, and the king's counsellors, being gathered together, saw these men, upon whose bodies the fire had no power, nor was an hair of their head singed, neither were their coats changed, nor the smell of fire had passed on them.
verse	27	3	28	@@@9Then@7 Nebuchadnezzar spake, and said, Blessed @9be@7 the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, who hath sent his angel, and delivered his servants that trusted in him, and have changed the king's word, and yielded their bodies, that they might not serve nor worship any god, except their own God.
verse	27	3	29	Therefore I make a decree, That every people, nation, and language, which speak any thing amiss against the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, shall be cut in pieces, and their houses shall be made a dunghill: because there is no other God that can deliver after this sort.
verse	27	3	30	Then the king promoted Shadrach, Meshach, and Abed-nego, in the province of Babylon.
verse	27	4	1	Nebuchadnezzar the king, unto all people, nations, and languages, that dwell in all the earth; Peace be multiplied unto you.
verse	27	4	2	I thought it good to shew the signs and wonders that the high God hath wrought toward me.
verse	27	4	3	@@How great @9are@7 his signs! and how mighty @9are@7 his wonders! his kingdom @9is@7 an everlasting kingdom, and his dominion @9is@7 from generation to generation.
verse	27	4	4	I Nebuchadnezzar was at rest in mine house, and flourishing in my palace:
verse	27	4	5	I saw a dream which made me afraid, and the thoughts upon my bed and the visions of my head troubled me.
verse	27	4	6	@@Therefore made I a decree to bring in all the wise @9men@7 of Babylon before me, that they might make known unto me the interpretation of the dream.
verse	27	4	7	Then came in the magicians, the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers: and I told the dream before them; but they did not make known unto me the interpretation thereof.
verse	27	4	8	@@But at the last Daniel came in before me, whose name @9was@7 Belteshazzar, according to the name of my god, and in whom is the spirit of the holy gods: and before him I told the dream, @9saying, @7
verse	27	4	9	@@O Belteshazzar, master of the magicians, because I know that the spirit of the holy gods @9is@7 in thee, and no secret troubleth thee, tell me the visions of my dream that I have seen, and the interpretation thereof.
verse	27	4	10	@@Thus @9were@7 the visions of mine head in my bed; I saw, and behold a tree in the midst of the earth, and the height thereof @9was@7 great.
verse	27	4	11	The tree grew, and was strong, and the height thereof reached unto heaven, and the sight thereof to the end of all the earth:
verse	27	4	12	@@The leaves thereof @9were@7 fair, and the fruit thereof much, and in it @9was@7 meat for all: the beasts of the field had shadow under it, and the fowls of the heaven dwelt in the boughs thereof, and all flesh was fed of it.
verse	27	4	13	I saw in the visions of my head upon my bed, and, behold, a watcher and an holy one came down from heaven;
verse	27	4	14	He cried aloud, and said thus, Hew down the tree, and cut off his branches, shake off his leaves, and scatter his fruit: let the beasts get away from under it, and the fowls from his branches:
verse	27	4	15	@@Nevertheless leave the stump of his roots in the earth, even with a band of iron and brass, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and @9let@7 his portion @9be@7 with the beasts in the grass of the earth:
verse	27	4	16	Let his heart be changed from man's, and let a beast's heart be given unto him; and let seven times pass over him.
verse	27	4	17	@@This matter @9is@7 by the decree of the watchers, and the demand by the word of the holy ones: to the intent that the living may know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will, and setteth up over it the basest of men.
verse	27	4	18	@@This dream I king Nebuchadnezzar have seen. Now thou, O Belteshazzar, declare the interpretation thereof, forasmuch as all the wise @9men@7 of my kingdom are not able to make known unto me the interpretation: but thou @9art@7 able; for the spirit of the holy gods @9is@7 in thee.
verse	27	4	19	@@Then Daniel, whose name @9was@7 Belteshazzar, was astonied for one hour, and his thoughts troubled him. The king spake, and said, Belteshazzar, let not the dream, or the interpretation thereof, trouble thee. Belteshazzar answered and said, My lord, the dream @9be@7 to them that hate thee, and the interpretation thereof to thine enemies.
verse	27	4	20	The tree that thou sawest, which grew, and was strong, whose height reached unto the heaven, and the sight thereof to all the earth;
verse	27	4	21	@@Whose leaves @9were@7 fair, and the fruit thereof much, and in it @9was@7 meat for all; under which the beasts of the field dwelt, and upon whose branches the fowls of the heaven had their habitation:
verse	27	4	22	@@It @9is@7 thou, O king, that art grown and become strong: for thy greatness is grown, and reacheth unto heaven, and thy dominion to the end of the earth.
verse	27	4	23	@@And whereas the king saw a watcher and an holy one coming down from heaven, and saying, Hew the tree down, and destroy it; yet leave the stump of the roots thereof in the earth, even with a band of iron and brass, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and @9let@7 his portion @9be@7 with the beasts of the field, till seven times pass over him;
verse	27	4	24	@@This @9is@7 the interpretation, O king, and this @9is@7 the decree of the most High, which is come upon my lord the king:
verse	27	4	25	That they shall drive thee from men, and thy dwelling shall be with the beasts of the field, and they shall make thee to eat grass as oxen, and they shall wet thee with the dew of heaven, and seven times shall pass over thee, till thou know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will.
verse	27	4	26	And whereas they commanded to leave the stump of the tree roots; thy kingdom shall be sure unto thee, after that thou shalt have known that the heavens do rule.
verse	27	4	27	Wherefore, O king, let my counsel be acceptable unto thee, and break off thy sins by righteousness, and thine iniquities by shewing mercy to the poor; if it may be a lengthening of thy tranquility.
verse	27	4	28	All this came upon the king Nebuchadnezzar.
verse	27	4	29	At the end of twelve months he walked in the palace of the kingdom of Babylon.
verse	27	4	30	The king spake, and said, Is not this great Babylon, that I have built for the house of the kingdom by the might of my power, and for the honour of my majesty?
verse	27	4	31	@@While the word @9was@7 in the king's mouth, there fell a voice from heaven, @9saying,@7 O king Nebuchadnezzar, to thee it is spoken; The kingdom is departed from thee.
verse	27	4	32	@@And they shall drive thee from men, and thy dwelling @9shall be@7 with the beasts of the field: they shall make thee to eat grass as oxen, and seven times shall pass over thee, until thou know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will.
verse	27	4	33	@@The same hour was the thing fulfilled upon Nebuchadnezzar: and he was driven from men, and did eat grass as oxen, and his body was wet with the dew of heaven, till his hairs were grown like eagles @9feathers,@7 and his nails like birds' @9claws. @7
verse	27	4	34	@@And at the end of the days I Nebuchadnezzar lifted up mine eyes unto heaven, and mine understanding returned unto me, and I blessed the most High, and I praised and honoured him that liveth for ever, whose dominion @9is@7 an everlasting dominion, and his kingdom @9is@7 from generation to generation:
verse	27	4	35	@@And all the inhabitants of the earth @9are@7 reputed as nothing: and he doeth according to his will in the army of heaven, and @9among@7 the inhabitants of the earth: and none can stay his hand, or say unto him, What doest thou?
verse	27	4	36	At the same time my reason returned unto me; and for the glory of my kingdom, mine honour and brightness returned unto me; and my counsellors and my lords sought unto me; and I was established in my kingdom, and excellent majesty was added unto me.
verse	27	4	37	@@Now I Nebuchadnezzar praise and extol and honour the King of heaven, all whose works @9are@7 truth, and his ways judgment: and those that walk in pride he is able to abase.
verse	27	5	1	Belshazzar the king made a great feast to a thousand of his lords, and drank wine before the thousand.
verse	27	5	2	@@Belshazzar, whiles he tasted the wine, commanded to bring the golden and silver vessels which his father Nebuchadnezzar had taken out of the temple which @9was@7 in Jerusalem; that the king, and his princes, his wives, and his concubines, might drink therein.
verse	27	5	3	@@Then they brought the golden vessels that were taken out of the temple of the house of God which @9was@7 at Jerusalem; and the king, and his princes, his wives, and his concubines, drank in them.
verse	27	5	4	They drank wine, and praised the gods of gold, and of silver, of brass, of iron, of wood, and of stone.
verse	27	5	5	In the same hour came forth fingers of a man's hand, and wrote over against the candlestick upon the plaister of the wall of the king's palace: and the king saw the part of the hand that wrote.
verse	27	5	6	Then the king's countenance was changed, and his thoughts troubled him, so that the joints of his loins were loosed, and his knees smote one against another.
verse	27	5	7	@@The king cried aloud to bring in the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers. @9And@7 the king spake, and said to the wise @9men@7 of Babylon, Whosoever shall read this writing, and shew me the interpretation thereof, shall be clothed with scarlet, and @9have@7 a chain of gold about his neck, and shall be the third ruler in the kingdom.
verse	27	5	8	@@Then came in all the king's wise @9men:@7 but they could not read the writing, nor make known to the king the interpretation thereof.
verse	27	5	9	Then was king Belshazzar greatly troubled, and his countenance was changed in him, and his lords were astonied.
verse	27	5	10	@@@9Now@7 the queen, by reason of the words of the king and his lords, came into the banquet house: @9and@7 the queen spake and said, O king, live for ever: let not thy thoughts trouble thee, nor let thy countenance be changed:
verse	27	5	11	@@There is a man in thy kingdom, in whom @9is@7 the spirit of the holy gods; and in the days of thy father light and understanding and wisdom, like the wisdom of the gods, was found in him; whom the king Nebuchadnezzar thy father, the king, @9I say,@7 thy father, made master of the magicians, astrologers, Chaldeans, @9and@7 soothsayers;
verse	27	5	12	Forasmuch as an excellent spirit, and knowledge, and understanding, interpreting of dreams, and shewing of hard sentences, and dissolving of doubts, were found in the same Daniel, whom the king named Belteshazzar: now let Daniel be called, and he will shew the interpretation.
verse	27	5	13	@@Then was Daniel brought in before the king. @9And@7 the king spake and said unto Daniel, @9Art@7 thou that Daniel, which @9art@7 of the children of the captivity of Judah, whom the king my father brought out of Jewry?
verse	27	5	14	@@I have even heard of thee, that the spirit of the gods @9is@7 in thee, and @9that@7 light and understanding and excellent wisdom is found in thee.
verse	27	5	15	@@And now the wise @9men,@7 the astrologers, have been brought in before me, that they should read this writing, and make known unto me the interpretation thereof: but they could not shew the interpretation of the thing:
verse	27	5	16	@@And I have heard of thee, that thou canst make interpretations, and dissolve doubts: now if thou canst read the writing, and make known to me the interpretation thereof, thou shalt be clothed with scarlet, and @9have@7 a chain of gold about thy neck, and shalt be the third ruler in the kingdom.
verse	27	5	17	Then Daniel answered and said before the king, Let thy gifts be to thyself, and give thy rewards to another; yet I will read the writing unto the king, and make known to him the interpretation.
verse	27	5	18	O thou king, the most high God gave Nebuchadnezzar thy father a kingdom, and majesty, and glory, and honour:
verse	27	5	19	And for the majesty that he gave him, all people, nations, and languages, trembled and feared before him: whom he would he slew; and whom he would he kept alive; and whom he would he set up; and whom he would he put down.
verse	27	5	20	But when his heart was lifted up, and his mind hardened in pride, he was deposed from his kingly throne, and they took his glory from him:
verse	27	5	21	@@And he was driven from the sons of men; and his heart was made like the beasts, and his dwelling @9was@7 with the wild asses: they fed him with grass like oxen, and his body was wet with the dew of heaven; till he knew that the most high God ruled in the kingdom of men, and @9that@7 he appointeth over it whomsoever he will.
verse	27	5	22	And thou his son, O Belshazzar, hast not humbled thine heart, though thou knewest all this;
verse	27	5	23	@@But hast lifted up thyself against the Lord of heaven; and they have brought the vessels of his house before thee, and thou, and thy lords, thy wives, and thy concubines, have drunk wine in them; and thou hast praised the gods of silver, and gold, of brass, iron, wood, and stone, which see not, nor hear, nor know: and the God in whose hand thy breath @9is,@7 and whose @9are@7 all thy ways, hast thou not glorified:
verse	27	5	24	Then was the part of the hand sent from him; and this writing was written.
verse	27	5	25	@@And this @9is@7 the writing that was written, MENE, MENE, TEKEL, UPHARSIN.
verse	27	5	26	@@This @9is@7 the interpretation of the thing: MENE; God hath numbered thy kingdom, and finished it.
verse	27	5	27	TEKEL; Thou art weighed in the balances, and art found wanting.
verse	27	5	28	PERES; Thy kingdom is divided, and given to the Medes and Persians.
verse	27	5	29	@@Then commanded Belshazzar, and they clothed Daniel with scarlet, and @9put@7 a chain of gold about his neck, and made a proclamation concerning him, that he should be the third ruler in the kingdom.
verse	27	5	30	In that night was Belshazzar the king of the Chaldeans slain.
verse	27	5	31	@@And Darius the Median took the kingdom, @9being@7 about threescore and two years old.
verse	27	6	1	It pleased Darius to set over the kingdom an hundred and twenty princes, which should be over the whole kingdom;
verse	27	6	2	@@And over these three presidents; of whom Daniel @9was@7 first: that the princes might give accounts unto them, and the king should have no damage.
verse	27	6	3	@@Then this Daniel was preferred above the presidents and princes, because an excellent spirit @9was@7 in him; and the king thought to set him over the whole realm.
verse	27	6	4	@@Then the presidents and princes sought to find occasion against Daniel concerning the kingdom; but they could find none occasion nor fault; forasmuch as he @9was@7 faithful, neither was there any error or fault found in him.
verse	27	6	5	@@Then said these men, We shall not find any occasion against this Daniel, except we find @9it@7 against him concerning the law of his God.
verse	27	6	6	Then these presidents and princes assembled together to the king, and said thus unto him, King Darius, live for ever.
verse	27	6	7	All the presidents of the kingdom, the governors, and the princes, the counsellors, and the captains, have consulted together to establish a royal statute, and to make a firm decree, that whosoever shall ask a petition of any God or man for thirty days, save of thee, O king, he shall be cast into the den of lions.
verse	27	6	8	Now, O king, establish the decree, and sign the writing, that it be not changed, according to the law of the Medes and Persians, which altereth not.
verse	27	6	9	Wherefore king Darius signed the writing and the decree.
verse	27	6	10	Now when Daniel knew that the writing was signed, he went into his house; and his windows being open in his chamber toward Jerusalem, he kneeled upon his knees three times a day, and prayed, and gave thanks before his God, as he did aforetime.
verse	27	6	11	Then these men assembled, and found Daniel praying and making supplication before his God.
verse	27	6	12	@@Then they came near, and spake before the king concerning the king's decree; Hast thou not signed a decree, that every man that shall ask @9a petition@7 of any God or man within thirty days, save of thee, O king, shall be cast into the den of lions? The king answered and said, The thing is true, according to the law of the Medes and Persians, which altereth not.
verse	27	6	13	@@Then answered they and said before the king, That Daniel, which @9is@7 of the children of the captivity of Judah, regardeth not thee, O king, nor the decree that thou hast signed, but maketh his petition three times a day.
verse	27	6	14	@@Then the king, when he heard @9these@7 words, was sore displeased with himself, and set @9his@7 heart on Daniel to deliver him: and he laboured till the going down of the sun to deliver him.
verse	27	6	15	@@Then these men assembled unto the king, and said unto the king, Know, O king, that the law of the Medes and Persians @9is,@7 That no decree nor statute which the king establisheth may be changed.
verse	27	6	16	@@Then the king commanded, and they brought Daniel, and cast @9him@7 into the den of lions. @9Now@7 the king spake and said unto Daniel, Thy God whom thou servest continually, he will deliver thee.
verse	27	6	17	And a stone was brought and laid upon the mouth of the den; and the king sealed it with his own signet, and with the signet of his lords; that the purpose might not be changed concerning Daniel.
verse	27	6	18	Then the king went to his palace, and passed the night fasting: neither were instruments of musick brought before him: and his sleep went from him.
verse	27	6	19	Then the king arose very early in the morning, and went in haste unto the den of lions.
verse	27	6	20	@@And when he came to the den, he cried with a lamentable voice unto Daniel: @9and@7 the king spake and said to Daniel, O Daniel, servant of the living God, is thy God, whom thou servest continually, able to deliver thee from the lions?
verse	27	6	21	Then said Daniel unto the king, O king, live for ever.
verse	27	6	22	My God hath sent his angel, and hath shut the lions mouths, that they have not hurt me: forasmuch as before him innocency was found in me; and also before thee, O king, have I done no hurt.
verse	27	6	23	Then was the king exceeding glad for him, and commanded that they should take Daniel up out of the den. So Daniel was taken up out of the den, and no manner of hurt was found upon him, because he believed in his God.
verse	27	6	24	@@And the king commanded, and they brought those men which had accused Daniel, and they cast @9them@7 into the den of lions, them, their children, and their wives; and the lions had the mastery of them, and brake all their bones in pieces or ever they came at the bottom of the den.
verse	27	6	25	Then king Darius wrote unto all people, nations, and languages, that dwell in all the earth; Peace be multiplied unto you.
verse	27	6	26	@@I make a decree, That in every dominion of my kingdom men tremble and fear before the God of Daniel: for he is the living God, and stedfast for ever, and his kingdom @9that@7 which shall not be destroyed, and his dominion @9shall be even@7 unto the end.
verse	27	6	27	He delivereth and rescueth, and he worketh signs and wonders in heaven and in earth, who hath delivered Daniel from the power of the lions.
verse	27	6	28	So this Daniel prospered in the reign of Darius, and in the reign of Cyrus the Persian.
verse	27	7	1	@@In the first year of Belshazzar king of Babylon Daniel had a dream and visions of his head upon his bed: then he wrote the dream, @9and@7 told the sum of the matters.
verse	27	7	2	Daniel spake and said, I saw in my vision by night, and, behold, the four winds of the heaven strove upon the great sea.
verse	27	7	3	And four great beasts came up from the sea, diverse one from another.
verse	27	7	4	@@The first @9was@7 like a lion, and had eagle's wings: I beheld till the wings thereof were plucked, and it was lifted up from the earth, and made stand upon the feet as a man, and a man's heart was given to it.
verse	27	7	5	@@And behold another beast, a second, like to a bear, and it raised up itself on one side, and @9it had@7 three ribs in the mouth of it between the teeth of it: and they said thus unto it, Arise, devour much flesh.
verse	27	7	6	After this I beheld, and lo another, like a leopard, which had upon the back of it four wings of a fowl; the beast had also four heads; and dominion was given to it.
verse	27	7	7	@@After this I saw in the night visions, and behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly; and it had great iron teeth: it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it @9was@7 diverse from all the beasts that @9were@7 before it; and it had ten horns.
verse	27	7	8	@@I considered the horns, and, behold, there came up among them another little horn, before whom there were three of the first horns plucked up by the roots: and, behold, in this horn @9were@7 eyes like the eyes of man, and a mouth speaking great things.
verse	27	7	9	@@I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment @9was@7 white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne @9was like@7 the fiery flame, @9and@7 his wheels @9as@7 burning fire.
verse	27	7	10	A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.
verse	27	7	11	@@I beheld then because of the voice of the great words which the horn spake: I beheld @9even@7 till the beast was slain, and his body destroyed, and given to the burning flame.
verse	27	7	12	As concerning the rest of the beasts, they had their dominion taken away: yet their lives were prolonged for a season and time.
verse	27	7	13	@@I saw in the night visions, and, behold, @9one@7 like the Son of man came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.
verse	27	7	14	@@And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion @9is@7 an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom @9that@7 which shall not be destroyed.
verse	27	7	15	@@I Daniel was grieved in my spirit in the midst of @9my@7 body, and the visions of my head troubled me.
verse	27	7	16	I came near unto one of them that stood by, and asked him the truth of all this. So he told me, and made me know the interpretation of the things.
verse	27	7	17	@@These great beasts, which are four, @9are@7 four kings, @9which@7 shall arise out of the earth.
verse	27	7	18	But the saints of the most High shall take the kingdom, and possess the kingdom for ever, even for ever and ever.
verse	27	7	19	@@Then I would know the truth of the fourth beast, which was diverse from all the others, exceeding dreadful, whose teeth @9were of@7 iron, and his nails @9of@7 brass; @9which@7 devoured, brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with his feet;
verse	27	7	20	@@And of the ten horns that @9were@7 in his head, and @9of@7 the other which came up, and before whom three fell; even @9of@7 that horn that had eyes, and a mouth that spake very great things, whose look @9was@7 more stout than his fellows.
verse	27	7	21	I beheld, and the same horn made war with the saints, and prevailed against them;
verse	27	7	22	Until the Ancient of days came, and judgment was given to the saints of the most High; and the time came that the saints possessed the kingdom.
verse	27	7	23	Thus he said, The fourth beast shall be the fourth kingdom upon earth, which shall be diverse from all kingdoms, and shall devour the whole earth, and shall tread it down, and break it in pieces.
verse	27	7	24	@@And the ten horns out of this kingdom @9are@7 ten kings @9that@7 shall arise: and another shall rise after them; and he shall be diverse from the first, and he shall subdue three kings.
verse	27	7	25	@@And he shall speak @9great@7 words against the most High, and shall wear out the saints of the most High, and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.
verse	27	7	26	@@But the judgment shall sit, and they shall take away his dominion, to consume and to destroy @9it@7 unto the end.
verse	27	7	27	@@And the kingdom and dominion, and the greatness of the kingdom under the whole heaven, shall be given to the people of the saints of the most High, whose kingdom @9is@7 an everlasting kingdom, and all dominions shall serve and obey him.
verse	27	7	28	@@Hitherto @9is@7 the end of the matter. As for me Daniel, my cogitations much troubled me, and my countenance changed in me: but I kept the matter in my heart.
verse	27	8	1	@@In the third year of the reign of king Belshazzar a vision appeared unto me, @9even unto@7 me Daniel, after that which appeared unto me at the first.
verse	27	8	2	@@And I saw in a vision; and it came to pass, when I saw, that I @9was@7 at Shushan @9in@7 the palace, which @9is@7 in the province of Elam; and I saw in a vision, and I was by the river of Ulai.
verse	27	8	3	@@Then I lifted up mine eyes, and saw, and, behold, there stood before the river a ram which had @9two@7 horns: and the @9two@7 horns @9were@7 high; but one @9was@7 higher than the other, and the higher came up last.
verse	27	8	4	@@I saw the ram pushing westward, and northward, and southward; so that no beasts might stand before him, neither @9was there any@7 that could deliver out of his hand; but he did according to his will, and became great.
verse	27	8	5	@@And as I was considering, behold, an he goat came from the west on the face of the whole earth, and touched not the ground: and the goat @9had@7 a notable horn between his eyes.
verse	27	8	6	@@And he came to the ram that had @9two@7 horns, which I had seen standing before the river, and ran unto him in the fury of his power.
verse	27	8	7	And I saw him come close unto the ram, and he was moved with choler against him, and smote the ram, and brake his two horns: and there was no power in the ram to stand before him, but he cast him down to the ground, and stamped upon him: and there was none that could deliver the ram out of his hand.
verse	27	8	8	Therefore the he goat waxed very great: and when he was strong, the great horn was broken; and for it came up four notable ones toward the four winds of heaven.
verse	27	8	9	@@And out of one of them came forth a little horn, which waxed exceeding great, toward the south, and toward the east, and toward the pleasant @9land. @7
verse	27	8	10	@@And it waxed great, @9even@7 to the host of heaven; and it cast down @9some@7 of the host and of the stars to the ground, and stamped upon them.
verse	27	8	11	@@Yea, he magnified @9himself@7 even to the prince of the host, and by him the daily @9sacrifice@7 was taken away, and the place of his sanctuary was cast down.
verse	27	8	12	@@And an host was given @9him@7 against the daily @9sacrifice@7 by reason of transgression, and it cast down the truth to the ground; and it practised, and prospered.
verse	27	8	13	@@Then I heard one saint speaking, and another saint said unto that certain @9saint@7 which spake, How long @9shall be@7 the vision @9concerning@7 the daily @9sacrifice,@7 and the transgression of desolation, to give both the sanctuary and the host to be trodden under foot?
verse	27	8	14	And he said unto me, Unto two thousand and three hundred days; then shall the sanctuary be cleansed.
verse	27	8	15	@@And it came to pass, when I, @9even@7 I Daniel, had seen the vision, and sought for the meaning, then, behold, there stood before me as the appearance of a man.
verse	27	8	16	@@And I heard a man's voice between @9the banks of@7 Ulai, which called, and said, Gabriel, make this @9man@7 to understand the vision.
verse	27	8	17	@@So he came near where I stood: and when he came, I was afraid, and fell upon my face: but he said unto me, Understand, O son of man: for at the time of the end @9shall be@7 the vision.
verse	27	8	18	Now as he was speaking with me, I was in a deep sleep on my face toward the ground: but he touched me, and set me upright.
verse	27	8	19	@@And he said, Behold, I will make thee know what shall be in the last end of the indignation: for at the time appointed the end @9shall be. @7
verse	27	8	20	@@The ram which thou sawest having @9two@7 horns @9are@7 the kings of Media and Persia.
verse	27	8	21	@@And the rough goat @9is@7 the king of Grecia: and the great horn that @9is@7 between his eyes @9is@7 the first king.
verse	27	8	22	Now that being broken, whereas four stood up for it, four kingdoms shall stand up out of the nation, but not in his power.
verse	27	8	23	And in the latter time of their kingdom, when the transgressors are come to the full, a king of fierce countenance, and understanding dark sentences, shall stand up.
verse	27	8	24	And his power shall be mighty, but not by his own power: and he shall destroy wonderfully, and shall prosper, and practise, and shall destroy the mighty and the holy people.
verse	27	8	25	@@And through his policy also he shall cause craft to prosper in his hand; and he shall magnify @9himself@7 in his heart, and by peace shall destroy many: he shall also stand up against the Prince of princes; but he shall be broken without hand.
verse	27	8	26	@@And the vision of the evening and the morning which was told @9is@7 true: wherefore shut thou up the vision; for it @9shall be@7 for many days.
verse	27	8	27	@@And I Daniel fainted, and was sick @9certain@7 days; afterward I rose up, and did the king's business; and I was astonished at the vision, but none understood @9it.@7
verse	27	9	1	In the first year of Darius the son of Ahasuerus, of the seed of the Medes, which was made king over the realm of the Chaldeans;
verse	27	9	2	In the first year of his reign I Daniel understood by books the number of the years, whereof the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah the prophet, that he would accomplish seventy years in the desolations of Jerusalem.
verse	27	9	3	And I set my face unto the Lord God, to seek by prayer and supplications, with fasting, and sackcloth, and ashes:
verse	27	9	4	And I prayed unto the LORD my God, and made my confession, and said, O Lord, the great and dreadful God, keeping the covenant and mercy to them that love him, and to them that keep his commandments;
verse	27	9	5	We have sinned, and have committed iniquity, and have done wickedly, and have rebelled, even by departing from thy precepts and from thy judgments:
verse	27	9	6	Neither have we hearkened unto thy servants the prophets, which spake in thy name to our kings, our princes, and our fathers, and to all the people of the land.
verse	27	9	7	@@O Lord, righteousness @9belongeth@7 unto thee, but unto us confusion of faces, as at this day; to the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and unto all Israel, @9that are@7 near, and @9that are@7 far off, through all the countries whither thou hast driven them, because of their trespass that they have trespassed against thee.
verse	27	9	8	@@O Lord, to us @9belongeth@7 confusion of face, to our kings, to our princes, and to our fathers, because we have sinned against thee.
verse	27	9	9	@@To the Lord our God @9belong@7 mercies and forgivenesses, though we have rebelled against him;
verse	27	9	10	Neither have we obeyed the voice of the LORD our God, to walk in his laws, which he set before us by his servants the prophets.
verse	27	9	11	@@Yea, all Israel have transgressed thy law, even by departing, that they might not obey thy voice; therefore the curse is poured upon us, and the oath that @9is@7 written in the law of Moses the servant of God, because we have sinned against him.
verse	27	9	12	And he hath confirmed his words, which he spake against us, and against our judges that judged us, by bringing upon us a great evil: for under the whole heaven hath not been done as hath been done upon Jerusalem.
verse	27	9	13	@@As @9it is@7 written in the law of Moses, all this evil is come upon us: yet made we not our prayer before the LORD our God, that we might turn from our iniquities, and understand thy truth.
verse	27	9	14	@@Therefore hath the LORD watched upon the evil, and brought it upon us: for the LORD our God @9is@7 righteous in all his works which he doeth: for we obeyed not his voice.
verse	27	9	15	And now, O Lord our God, that hast brought thy people forth out of the land of Egypt with a mighty hand, and hast gotten thee renown, as at this day; we have sinned, we have done wickedly.
verse	27	9	16	@@O Lord, according to all thy righteousness, I beseech thee, let thine anger and thy fury be turned away from thy city Jerusalem, thy holy mountain: because for our sins, and for the iniquities of our fathers, Jerusalem and thy people @9are become@7 a reproach to all @9that are@7 about us.
verse	27	9	17	Now therefore, O our God, hear the prayer of thy servant, and his supplications, and cause thy face to shine upon thy sanctuary that is desolate, for the Lord's sake.
verse	27	9	18	O my God, incline thine ear, and hear; open thine eyes, and behold our desolations, and the city which is called by thy name: for we do not present our supplications before thee for our righteousnesses, but for thy great mercies.
verse	27	9	19	O Lord, hear; O Lord, forgive; O Lord, hearken and do; defer not, for thine own sake, O my God: for thy city and thy people are called by thy name.
verse	27	9	20	@@And whiles I @9was@7 speaking, and praying, and confessing my sin and the sin of my people Israel, and presenting my supplication before the LORD my God for the holy mountain of my God;
verse	27	9	21	@@Yea, whiles I @9was@7 speaking in prayer, even the man Gabriel, whom I had seen in the vision at the beginning, being caused to fly swiftly, touched me about the time of the evening oblation.
verse	27	9	22	@@And he informed @9me,@7 and talked with me, and said, O Daniel, I am now come forth to give thee skill and understanding.
verse	27	9	23	@@At the beginning of thy supplications the commandment came forth, and I am come to shew @9thee;@7 for thou @9art@7 greatly beloved: therefore understand the matter, and consider the vision.
verse	27	9	24	Seventy weeks are determined upon thy people and upon thy holy city, to finish the transgression, and to make an end of sins, and to make reconciliation for iniquity, and to bring in everlasting righteousness, and to seal up the vision and prophecy, and to anoint the most Holy.
verse	27	9	25	@@Know therefore and understand, @9that@7 from the going forth of the commandment to restore and to build Jerusalem unto the Messiah the Prince @9shall be@7 seven weeks, and threescore and two weeks: the street shall be built again, and the wall, even in troublous times.
verse	27	9	26	@@And after threescore and two weeks shall Messiah be cut off, but not for himself: and the people of the prince that shall come shall destroy the city and the sanctuary; and the end thereof @9shall be@7 with a flood, and unto the end of the war desolations are determined.
verse	27	9	27	@@And he shall confirm the covenant with many for one week: and in the midst of the week he shall cause the sacrifice and the oblation to cease, and for the overspreading of abominations he shall make @9it@7 desolate, even until the consummation, and that determined shall be poured upon the desolate.
verse	27	10	1	@@In the third year of Cyrus king of Persia a thing was revealed unto Daniel, whose name was called Belteshazzar; and the thing @9was@7 true, but the time appointed @9was@7 long: and he understood the thing, and had understanding of the vision.
verse	27	10	2	In those days I Daniel was mourning three full weeks.
