verse	27	10	4	@@And in the four and twentieth day of the first month, as I was by the side of the great river, which @9is@7 Hiddekel;
verse	27	10	5	@@Then I lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and behold a certain man clothed in linen, whose loins @9were@7 girded with fine gold of Uphaz:
verse	27	10	6	@@His body also @9was@7 like the beryl, and his face as the appearance of lightning, and his eyes as lamps of fire, and his arms and his feet like in colour to polished brass, and the voice of his words like the voice of a multitude.
verse	27	10	7	And I Daniel alone saw the vision: for the men that were with me saw not the vision; but a great quaking fell upon them, so that they fled to hide themselves.
verse	27	10	8	Therefore I was left alone, and saw this great vision, and there remained no strength in me: for my comeliness was turned in me into corruption, and I retained no strength.
verse	27	10	9	Yet heard I the voice of his words: and when I heard the voice of his words, then was I in a deep sleep on my face, and my face toward the ground.
verse	27	10	10	@@And, behold, an hand touched me, which set me upon my knees and @9upon@7 the palms of my hands.
verse	27	10	11	And he said unto me, O Daniel, a man greatly beloved, understand the words that I speak unto thee, and stand upright: for unto thee am I now sent. And when he had spoken this word unto me, I stood trembling.
verse	27	10	12	Then said he unto me, Fear not, Daniel: for from the first day that thou didst set thine heart to understand, and to chasten thyself before thy God, thy words were heard, and I am come for thy words.
verse	27	10	13	But the prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me one and twenty days: but, lo, Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me; and I remained there with the kings of Persia.
verse	27	10	14	@@Now I am come to make thee understand what shall befall thy people in the latter days: for yet the vision @9is@7 for @9many@7 days.
verse	27	10	15	And when he had spoken such words unto me, I set my face toward the ground, and I became dumb.
verse	27	10	16	@@And, behold, @9one@7 like the similitude of the sons of men touched my lips: then I opened my mouth, and spake, and said unto him that stood before me, O my lord, by the vision my sorrows are turned upon me, and I have retained no strength.
verse	27	10	17	For how can the servant of this my lord talk with this my lord? for as for me, straightway there remained no strength in me, neither is there breath left in me.
verse	27	10	18	@@Then there came again and touched me @9one@7 like the appearance of a man, and he strengthened me,
verse	27	10	19	@@And said, O man greatly beloved, fear not: peace @9be@7 unto thee, be strong, yea, be strong. And when he had spoken unto me, I was strengthened, and said, Let my lord speak; for thou hast strengthened me.
verse	27	10	20	Then said he, Knowest thou wherefore I come unto thee? and now will I return to fight with the prince of Persia: and when I am gone forth, lo, the prince of Grecia shall come.
verse	27	10	21	@@But I will shew thee that which is noted in the scripture of truth: and @9there is@7 none that holdeth with me in these things, but Michael your prince.
verse	27	11	1	@@Also I in the first year of Darius the Mede, @9even@7 I, stood to confirm and to strengthen him.
verse	27	11	2	@@And now will I shew thee the truth. Behold, there shall stand up yet three kings in Persia; and the fourth shall be far richer than @9they@7 all: and by his strength through his riches he shall stir up all against the realm of Grecia.
verse	27	11	3	And a mighty king shall stand up, that shall rule with great dominion, and do according to his will.
verse	27	11	4	And when he shall stand up, his kingdom shall be broken, and shall be divided toward the four winds of heaven; and not to his posterity, nor according to his dominion which he ruled: for his kingdom shall be plucked up, even for others beside those.
verse	27	11	5	@@And the king of the south shall be strong, and @9one@7 of his princes; and he shall be strong above him, and have dominion; his dominion @9shall be@7 a great dominion.
verse	27	11	6	@@And in the end of years they shall join themselves together; for the king's daughter of the south shall come to the king of the north to make an agreement: but she shall not retain the power of the arm; neither shall he stand, nor his arm: but she shall be given up, and they that brought her, and he that begat her, and he that strengthened her in @9these@7 times.
verse	27	11	7	@@But out of a branch of her roots shall @9one@7 stand up in his estate, which shall come with an army, and shall enter into the fortress of the king of the north, and shall deal against them, and shall prevail:
verse	27	11	8	@@And shall also carry captives into Egypt their gods, with their princes, @9and@7 with their precious vessels of silver and of gold; and he shall continue @9more@7 years than the king of the north.
