verse	28	5	1	@@Hear ye this, O priests; and hearken, ye house of Israel; and give ye ear, O house of the king; for judgment @9is@7 toward you, because ye have been a snare on Mizpah, and a net spread upon Tabor.
verse	28	5	2	@@And the revolters are profound to make slaughter, though I @9have been@7 a rebuker of them all.
verse	28	5	3	@@I know Ephraim, and Israel is not hid from me: for now, O Ephraim, thou committest whoredom, @9and@7 Israel is defiled.
verse	28	5	4	@@They will not frame their doings to turn unto their God: for the spirit of whoredoms @9is@7 in the midst of them, and they have not known the LORD.
verse	28	5	5	And the pride of Israel doth testify to his face: therefore shall Israel and Ephraim fall in their iniquity; Judah also shall fall with them.
verse	28	5	6	@@They shall go with their flocks and with their herds to seek the LORD; but they shall not find @9him;@7 he hath withdrawn himself from them.
verse	28	5	7	They have dealt treacherously against the LORD: for they have begotten strange children: now shall a month devour them with their portions.
verse	28	5	8	@@Blow ye the cornet in Gibeah, @9and@7 the trumpet in Ramah: cry aloud @9at@7 Bethaven, after thee, O Benjamin.
verse	28	5	9	Ephraim shall be desolate in the day of rebuke: among the tribes of Israel have I made known that which shall surely be.
verse	28	5	10	@@The princes of Judah were like them that remove the bound: @9therefore@7 I will pour out my wrath upon them like water.
verse	28	5	11	@@Ephraim @9is@7 oppressed @9and@7 broken in judgment, because he willingly walked after the commandment.
verse	28	5	12	@@Therefore @9will@7 I @9be@7 unto Ephraim as a moth, and to the house of Judah as rottenness.
verse	28	5	13	@@When Ephraim saw his sickness, and Judah @9saw@7 his wound, then went Ephraim to the Assyrian, and sent to king Jareb: yet could he not heal you, nor cure you of your wound.
verse	28	5	14	@@For I will @9be@7 unto Ephraim as a lion, and as a young lion to the house of Judah: I, @9even@7 I, will tear and go away; I will take away, and none shall rescue @9him.@7
verse	28	5	15	@@I will go @9and@7 return to my place, till they acknowledge their offence, and seek my face: in their affliction they will seek me early.
verse	28	6	1	Come, and let us return unto the LORD: for he hath torn, and he will heal us; he hath smitten, and he will bind us up.
verse	28	6	2	After two days will he revive us: in the third day he will raise us up, and we shall live in his sight.
verse	28	6	3	@@Then shall we know, @9if@7 we follow on to know the LORD: his going forth is prepared as the morning; and he shall come unto us as the rain, as the latter @9and@7 former rain unto the earth.
verse	28	6	4	@@O Ephraim, what shall I do unto thee? O Judah, what shall I do unto thee? for your goodness @9is@7 as a morning cloud, and as the early dew it goeth away.
verse	28	6	5	@@Therefore have I hewed @9them@7 by the prophets; I have slain them by the words of my mouth: and thy judgments @9are as@7 the light @9that@7 goeth forth.
verse	28	6	6	For I desired mercy, and not sacrifice; and the knowledge of God more than burnt offerings.
verse	28	6	7	But they like men have transgressed the covenant: there have they dealt treacherously against me.
verse	28	6	8	@@Gilead @9is@7 a city of them that work iniquity, @9and is@7 polluted with blood.
verse	28	6	9	@@And as troops of robbers wait for a man, @9so@7 the company of priests murder in the way by consent: for they commit lewdness.
verse	28	6	10	@@I have seen an horrible thing in the house of Israel: there @9is@7 the whoredom of Ephraim, Israel is defiled.
verse	28	6	11	Also, O Judah, he hath set an harvest for thee, when I returned the captivity of my people.
verse	28	7	1	@@When I would have healed Israel, then the iniquity of Ephraim was discovered, and the wickedness of Samaria: for they commit falsehood; and the thief cometh in, @9and@7 the troop of robbers spoileth without.
verse	28	7	2	@@And they consider not in their hearts @9that@7 I remember all their wickedness: now their own doings have beset them about; they are before my face.
verse	28	7	3	They make the king glad with their wickedness, and the princes with their lies.
verse	28	7	4	@@They @9are@7 all adulterers, as an oven heated by the baker, @9who@7 ceaseth from raising after he hath kneaded the dough, until it be leavened.
verse	28	7	5	@@In the day of our king the princes have made @9him@7 sick with bottles of wine; he stretched out his hand with scorners.
verse	28	7	6	For they have made ready their heart like an oven, whiles they lie in wait: their baker sleepeth all the night; in the morning it burneth as a flaming fire.
verse	28	7	7	@@They are all hot as an oven, and have devoured their judges; all their kings are fallen: @9there is@7 none among them that calleth unto me.
verse	28	7	8	Ephraim, he hath mixed himself among the people; Ephraim is a cake not turned.
verse	28	7	9	@@Strangers have devoured his strength, and he knoweth @9it@7 not: yea, gray hairs are here and there upon him, yet he knoweth not.
verse	28	7	10	And the pride of Israel testifieth to his face: and they do not return to the LORD their God, nor seek him for all this.
verse	28	7	11	Ephraim also is like a silly dove without heart: they call to Egypt, they go to Assyria.
verse	28	7	12	When they shall go, I will spread my net upon them; I will bring them down as the fowls of the heaven; I will chastise them, as their congregation hath heard.
verse	28	7	13	Woe unto them! for they have fled from me: destruction unto them! because they have transgressed against me: though I have redeemed them, yet they have spoken lies against me.
verse	28	7	14	@@And they have not cried unto me with their heart, when they howled upon their beds: they assemble themselves for corn and wine, @9and@7 they rebel against me.
verse	28	7	15	@@Though I have bound @9and@7 strengthened their arms, yet do they imagine mischief against me.
verse	28	7	16	@@They return, @9but@7 not to the most High: they are like a deceitful bow: their princes shall fall by the sword for the rage of their tongue: this @9shall be@7 their derision in the land of Egypt.
verse	28	8	1	@@@9Set@7 the trumpet to thy mouth. @9He shall come@7 as an eagle against the house of the LORD, because they have transgressed my covenant, and trespassed against my law.
verse	28	8	2	Israel shall cry unto me, My God, we know thee.
verse	28	8	3	@@Israel hath cast off @9the thing that is@7 good: the enemy shall pursue him.
verse	28	8	4	@@They have set up kings, but not by me: they have made princes, and I knew @9it@7 not: of their silver and their gold have they made them idols, that they may be cut off.
verse	28	8	5	@@Thy calf, O Samaria, hath cast @9thee@7 off; mine anger is kindled against them: how long @9will it be@7 ere they attain to innocency?
verse	28	8	6	@@For from Israel @9was@7 it also: the workman made it; therefore it @9is@7 not God: but the calf of Samaria shall be broken in pieces.
verse	28	8	7	For they have sown the wind, and they shall reap the whirlwind: it hath no stalk: the bud shall yield no meal: if so be it yield, the strangers shall swallow it up.
verse	28	8	8	@@Israel is swallowed up: now shall they be among the Gentiles as a vessel wherein @9is@7 no pleasure.
verse	28	8	9	For they are gone up to Assyria, a wild ass alone by himself: Ephraim hath hired lovers.
verse	28	8	10	Yea, though they have hired among the nations, now will I gather them, and they shall sorrow a little for the burden of the king of princes.
verse	28	8	11	Because Ephraim hath made many altars to sin, altars shall be unto him to sin.
verse	28	8	12	@@I have written to him the great things of my law, @9but@7 they were counted as a strange thing.
verse	28	8	13	@@They sacrifice flesh @9for@7 the sacrifices of mine offerings, and @9eat it;@7 but the LORD accepteth them not; now will he remember their iniquity, and visit their sins: they shall return to Egypt.
verse	28	8	14	For Israel hath forgotten his Maker, and buildeth temples; and Judah hath multiplied fenced cities: but I will send a fire upon his cities, and it shall devour the palaces thereof.
verse	28	9	1	@@Rejoice not, O Israel, for joy, as @9other@7 people: for thou hast gone a whoring from thy God, thou hast loved a reward upon every cornfloor.
verse	28	9	2	The floor and the winepress shall not feed them, and the new wine shall fail in her.
verse	28	9	3	@@They shall not dwell in the LORD'S land; but Ephraim shall return to Egypt, and they shall eat unclean @9things@7 in Assyria.
verse	28	9	4	@@They shall not offer wine @9offerings@7 to the LORD, neither shall they be pleasing unto him: their sacrifices @9shall be@7 unto them as the bread of mourners; all that eat thereof shall be polluted: for their bread for their soul shall not come into the house of the LORD.
verse	28	9	5	What will ye do in the solemn day, and in the day of the feast of the LORD?
verse	28	9	6	@@For, lo, they are gone because of destruction: Egypt shall gather them up, Memphis shall bury them: the pleasant @9places@7 for their silver, nettles shall possess them: thorns @9shall be@7 in their tabernacles.
verse	28	9	7	@@The days of visitation are come, the days of recompence are come; Israel shall know @9it:@7 the prophet @9is@7 a fool, the spiritual man @9is@7 mad, for the multitude of thine iniquity, and the great hatred.
verse	28	9	8	@@The watchman of Ephraim @9was@7 with my God: @9but@7 the prophet @9is@7 a snare of a fowler in all his ways, @9and@7 hatred in the house of his God.
verse	28	9	9	@@They have deeply corrupted @9themselves,@7 as in the days of Gibeah: @9therefore@7 he will remember their iniquity, he will visit their sins.
verse	28	9	10	@@I found Israel like grapes in the wilderness; I saw your fathers as the firstripe in the fig tree at her first time: @9but@7 they went to Baalpeor, and separated themselves unto @9that@7 shame; and @9their@7 abominations were according as they loved.
verse	28	9	11	@@@9As for@7 Ephraim, their glory shall fly away like a bird, from the birth, and from the womb, and from the conception.
verse	28	9	12	@@Though they bring up their children, yet will I bereave them, @9that there shall@7 not @9be@7 a man @9left:@7 yea, woe also to them when I depart from them!
verse	28	9	13	@@Ephraim, as I saw Tyrus, @9is@7 planted in a pleasant place: but Ephraim shall bring forth his children to the murderer.
verse	28	9	14	Give them, O LORD: what wilt thou give? give them a miscarrying womb and dry breasts.
verse	28	9	15	@@All their wickedness @9is@7 in Gilgal: for there I hated them: for the wickedness of their doings I will drive them out of mine house, I will love them no more: all their princes @9are@7 revolters.
verse	28	9	16	@@Ephraim is smitten, their root is dried up, they shall bear no fruit: yea, though they bring forth, yet will I slay @9even@7 the beloved @9fruit@7 of their womb.
verse	28	9	17	My God will cast them away, because they did not hearken unto him: and they shall be wanderers among the nations.
verse	28	10	1	@@Israel @9is@7 an empty vine, he bringeth forth fruit unto himself: according to the multitude of his fruit he hath increased the altars; according to the goodness of his land they have made goodly images.
verse	28	10	2	Their heart is divided; now shall they be found faulty: he shall break down their altars, he shall spoil their images.
verse	28	10	3	For now they shall say, We have no king, because we feared not the LORD; what then should a king do to us?
verse	28	10	4	They have spoken words, swearing falsely in making a covenant: thus judgment springeth up as hemlock in the furrows of the field.
verse	28	10	5	@@The inhabitants of Samaria shall fear because of the calves of Bethaven: for the people thereof shall mourn over it, and the priests thereof @9that@7 rejoiced on it, for the glory thereof, because it is departed from it.
verse	28	10	6	@@It shall be also carried unto Assyria @9for@7 a present to king Jareb: Ephraim shall receive shame, and Israel shall be ashamed of his own counsel.
verse	28	10	7	@@@9As for@7 Samaria, her king is cut off as the foam upon the water.
verse	28	10	8	The high places also of Aven, the sin of Israel, shall be destroyed: the thorn and the thistle shall come up on their altars; and they shall say to the mountains, Cover us; and to the hills, Fall on us.
verse	28	10	9	O Israel, thou hast sinned from the days of Gibeah: there they stood: the battle in Gibeah against the children of iniquity did not overtake them.
verse	28	10	10	@@@9It is@7 in my desire that I should chastise them; and the people shall be gathered against them, when they shall bind themselves in their two furrows.
verse	28	10	11	@@And Ephraim @9is as@7 an heifer @9that is@7 taught, @9and@7 loveth to tread out @9the corn;@7 but I passed over upon her fair neck: I will make Ephraim to ride; Judah shall plow, @9and@7 Jacob shall break his clods.
verse	28	10	12	@@Sow to yourselves in righteousness, reap in mercy; break up your fallow ground: for @9it is@7 time to seek the LORD, till he come and rain righteousness upon you.
verse	28	10	13	Ye have plowed wickedness, ye have reaped iniquity; ye have eaten the fruit of lies: because thou didst trust in thy way, in the multitude of thy mighty men.
verse	28	10	14	@@Therefore shall a tumult arise among thy people, and all thy fortresses shall be spoiled, as Shalman spoiled Beth-arbel in the day of battle: the mother was dashed in pieces upon @9her@7 children.
verse	28	10	15	So shall Bethel do unto you because of your great wickedness: in a morning shall the king of Israel utterly be cut off.
verse	28	11	1	@@When Israel @9was@7 a child, then I loved him, and called my son out of Egypt.
verse	28	11	2	@@@9As@7 they called them, so they went from them: they sacrificed unto Baalim, and burned incense to graven images.
verse	28	11	3	I taught Ephraim also to go, taking them by their arms; but they knew not that I healed them.
verse	28	11	4	I drew them with cords of a man, with bands of love: and I was to them as they that take off the yoke on their jaws, and I laid meat unto them.
verse	28	11	5	He shall not return into the land of Egypt, but the Assyrian shall be his king, because they refused to return.
verse	28	11	6	@@And the sword shall abide on his cities, and shall consume his branches, and devour @9them,@7 because of their own counsels.
verse	28	11	7	@@And my people are bent to backsliding from me: though they called them to the most High, none at all would exalt @9him. @7
verse	28	11	8	@@How shall I give thee up, Ephraim? @9how@7 shall I deliver thee, Israel? how shall I make thee as Admah? @9how@7 shall I set thee as Zeboim? mine heart is turned within me, my repentings are kindled together.
verse	28	11	9	@@I will not execute the fierceness of mine anger, I will not return to destroy Ephraim: for I @9am@7 God, and not man; the Holy One in the midst of thee: and I will not enter into the city.
verse	28	11	10	They shall walk after the LORD: he shall roar like a lion: when he shall roar, then the children shall tremble from the west.
verse	28	11	11	They shall tremble as a bird out of Egypt, and as a dove out of the land of Assyria: and I will place them in their houses, saith the LORD.
verse	28	11	12	Ephraim compasseth me about with lies, and the house of Israel with deceit: but Judah yet ruleth with God, and is faithful with the saints.
verse	28	12	1	Ephraim feedeth on wind, and followeth after the east wind: he daily increaseth lies and desolation; and they do make a covenant with the Assyrians, and oil is carried into Egypt.
verse	28	12	2	The LORD hath also a controversy with Judah, and will punish Jacob according to his ways; according to his doings will he recompense him.
verse	28	12	3	He took his brother by the heel in the womb, and by his strength he had power with God:
verse	28	12	4	@@Yea, he had power over the angel, and prevailed: he wept, and made supplication unto him: he found him @9in@7 Bethel, and there he spake with us;
verse	28	12	5	@@Even the LORD God of hosts; the LORD @9is@7 his memorial.
verse	28	12	6	Therefore turn thou to thy God: keep mercy and judgment, and wait on thy God continually.
verse	28	12	7	@@@9He is@7 a merchant, the balances of deceit @9are@7 in his hand: he loveth to oppress.
verse	28	12	8	@@And Ephraim said, Yet I am become rich, I have found me out substance: @9in@7 all my labours they shall find none iniquity in me that @9were@7 sin.
verse	28	12	9	@@And I @9that am@7 the LORD thy God from the land of Egypt will yet make thee to dwell in tabernacles, as in the days of the solemn feast.
verse	28	12	10	I have also spoken by the prophets, and I have multiplied visions, and used similitudes, by the ministry of the prophets.
verse	28	12	11	@@@9Is there@7 iniquity @9in@7 Gilead? surely they are vanity: they sacrifice bullocks in Gilgal; yea, their altars @9are@7 as heaps in the furrows of the fields.
verse	28	12	12	@@And Jacob fled into the country of Syria, and Israel served for a wife, and for a wife he kept @9sheep. @7
verse	28	12	13	And by a prophet the LORD brought Israel out of Egypt, and by a prophet was he preserved.
verse	28	12	14	@@Ephraim provoked @9him@7 to anger most bitterly: therefore shall he leave his blood upon him, and his reproach shall his Lord return unto him.
verse	28	13	1	When Ephraim spake trembling, he exalted himself in Israel; but when he offended in Baal, he died.
verse	28	13	2	@@And now they sin more and more, and have made them molten images of their silver, @9and@7 idols according to their own understanding, all of it the work of the craftsmen: they say of them, Let the men that sacrifice kiss the calves.
verse	28	13	3	@@Therefore they shall be as the morning cloud, and as the early dew that passeth away, as the chaff @9that@7 is driven with the whirlwind out of the floor, and as the smoke out of the chimney.
verse	28	13	4	@@Yet I @9am@7 the LORD thy God from the land of Egypt, and thou shalt know no god but me: for @9there is@7 no saviour beside me.
verse	28	13	5	I did know thee in the wilderness, in the land of great drought.
verse	28	13	6	According to their pasture, so were they filled; they were filled, and their heart was exalted; therefore have they forgotten me.
verse	28	13	7	@@Therefore I will be unto them as a lion: as a leopard by the way will I observe @9them: @7
verse	28	13	8	@@I will meet them as a bear @9that is@7 bereaved @9of her whelps,@7 and will rend the caul of their heart, and there will I devour them like a lion: the wild beast shall tear them.
verse	28	13	9	@@O Israel, thou hast destroyed thyself; but in me @9is@7 thine help.
verse	28	13	10	@@I will be thy king: where @9is any other@7 that may save thee in all thy cities? and thy judges of whom thou saidst, Give me a king and princes?
verse	28	13	11	@@I gave thee a king in mine anger, and took @9him@7 away in my wrath.
verse	28	13	12	@@The iniquity of Ephraim @9is@7 bound up; his sin @9is@7 hid.
verse	28	13	13	@@The sorrows of a travailing woman shall come upon him: he @9is@7 an unwise son; for he should not stay long in @9the place of@7 the breaking forth of children.
verse	28	13	14	I will ransom them from the power of the grave; I will redeem them from death: O death, I will be thy plagues; O grave, I will be thy destruction: repentance shall be hid from mine eyes.
verse	28	13	15	@@Though he be fruitful among @9his@7 brethren, an east wind shall come, the wind of the LORD shall come up from the wilderness, and his spring shall become dry, and his fountain shall be dried up: he shall spoil the treasure of all pleasant vessels.
verse	28	13	16	Samaria shall become desolate; for she hath rebelled against her God: they shall fall by the sword: their infants shall be dashed in pieces, and their women with child shall be ripped up.
verse	28	14	1	O Israel, return unto the LORD thy God; for thou hast fallen by thine iniquity.
verse	28	14	2	@@Take with you words, and turn to the LORD: say unto him, Take away all iniquity, and receive @9us@7 graciously: so will we render the calves of our lips.
verse	28	14	3	@@Asshur shall not save us; we will not ride upon horses: neither will we say any more to the work of our hands, @9Ye are@7 our gods: for in thee the fatherless findeth mercy.
verse	28	14	4	I will heal their backsliding, I will love them freely: for mine anger is turned away from him.
verse	28	14	5	I will be as the dew unto Israel: he shall grow as the lily, and cast forth his roots as Lebanon.
verse	28	14	6	His branches shall spread, and his beauty shall be as the olive tree, and his smell as Lebanon.
verse	28	14	7	@@They that dwell under his shadow shall return; they shall revive @9as@7 the corn, and grow as the vine: the scent thereof @9shall be@7 as the wine of Lebanon.
verse	28	14	8	@@Ephraim @9shall say,@7 What have I to do any more with idols? I have heard @9him,@7 and observed him: I @9am@7 like a green fir tree. From me is thy fruit found.
verse	28	14	9	@@Who @9is@7 wise, and he shall understand these @9things?@7 prudent, and he shall know them? for the ways of the LORD @9are@7 right, and the just shall walk in them: but the transgressors shall fall therein.
verse	29	1	1	The word of the LORD that came to Joel the son of Pethuel.
verse	29	1	2	Hear this, ye old men, and give ear, all ye inhabitants of the land. Hath this been in your days, or even in the days of your fathers?
verse	29	1	3	@@Tell ye your children of it, and @9let@7 your children @9tell@7 their children, and their children another generation.
verse	29	1	4	That which the palmerworm hath left hath the locust eaten; and that which the locust hath left hath the cankerworm eaten; and that which the cankerworm hath left hath the caterpiller eaten.
verse	29	1	5	Awake, ye drunkards, and weep; and howl, all ye drinkers of wine, because of the new wine; for it is cut off from your mouth.
verse	29	1	6	@@For a nation is come up upon my land, strong, and without number, whose teeth @9are@7 the teeth of a lion, and he hath the cheek teeth of a great lion.
verse	29	1	7	@@He hath laid my vine waste, and barked my fig tree: he hath made it clean bare, and cast @9it@7 away; the branches thereof are made white.
verse	29	1	8	Lament like a virgin girded with sackcloth for the husband of her youth.
verse	29	1	9	The meat offering and the drink offering is cut off from the house of the LORD; the priests, the LORD'S ministers, mourn.
verse	29	1	10	The field is wasted, the land mourneth; for the corn is wasted: the new wine is dried up, the oil languisheth.
verse	29	1	11	Be ye ashamed, O ye husbandmen; howl, O ye vinedressers, for the wheat and for the barley; because the harvest of the field is perished.
verse	29	1	12	@@The vine is dried up, and the fig tree languisheth; the pomegranate tree, the palm tree also, and the apple tree, @9even@7 all the trees of the field, are withered: because joy is withered away from the sons of men.
verse	29	1	13	Gird yourselves, and lament, ye priests: howl, ye ministers of the altar: come, lie all night in sackcloth, ye ministers of my God: for the meat offering and the drink offering is withholden from the house of your God.
verse	29	1	14	@@Sanctify ye a fast, call a solemn assembly, gather the elders @9and@7 all the inhabitants of the land @9into@7 the house of the LORD your God, and cry unto the LORD,
verse	29	1	15	@@Alas for the day! for the day of the LORD @9is@7 at hand, and as a destruction from the Almighty shall it come.
verse	29	1	16	@@Is not the meat cut off before our eyes, @9yea,@7 joy and gladness from the house of our God?
verse	29	1	17	The seed is rotten under their clods, the garners are laid desolate, the barns are broken down; for the corn is withered.
verse	29	1	18	How do the beasts groan! the herds of cattle are perplexed, because they have no pasture; yea, the flocks of sheep are made desolate.
verse	29	1	19	O LORD, to thee will I cry: for the fire hath devoured the pastures of the wilderness, and the flame hath burned all the trees of the field.
verse	29	1	20	The beasts of the field cry also unto thee: for the rivers of waters are dried up, and the fire hath devoured the pastures of the wilderness.
verse	29	2	1	@@Blow ye the trumpet in Zion, and sound an alarm in my holy mountain: let all the inhabitants of the land tremble: for the day of the LORD cometh, for @9it is@7 nigh at hand;
verse	29	2	2	@@A day of darkness and of gloominess, a day of clouds and of thick darkness, as the morning spread upon the mountains: a great people and a strong; there hath not been ever the like, neither shall be any more after it, @9even@7 to the years of many generations.
verse	29	2	3	@@A fire devoureth before them; and behind them a flame burneth: the land @9is@7 as the garden of Eden before them, and behind them a desolate wilderness; yea, and nothing shall escape them.
verse	29	2	4	@@The appearance of them @9is@7 as the appearance of horses; and as horsemen, so shall they run.
verse	29	2	5	Like the noise of chariots on the tops of mountains shall they leap, like the noise of a flame of fire that devoureth the stubble, as a strong people set in battle array.
verse	29	2	6	Before their face the people shall be much pained: all faces shall gather blackness.
verse	29	2	7	They shall run like mighty men; they shall climb the wall like men of war; and they shall march every one on his ways, and they shall not break their ranks:
verse	29	2	8	@@Neither shall one thrust another; they shall walk every one in his path: and @9when@7 they fall upon the sword, they shall not be wounded.
verse	29	2	9	They shall run to and fro in the city; they shall run upon the wall, they shall climb up upon the houses; they shall enter in at the windows like a thief.
verse	29	2	10	The earth shall quake before them; the heavens shall tremble: the sun and the moon shall be dark, and the stars shall withdraw their shining:
verse	29	2	11	@@And the LORD shall utter his voice before his army: for his camp @9is@7 very great: for @9he is@7 strong that executeth his word: for the day of the LORD @9is@7 great and very terrible; and who can abide it?
verse	29	2	12	@@Therefore also now, saith the LORD, turn ye @9even@7 to me with all your heart, and with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning:
verse	29	2	13	@@And rend your heart, and not your garments, and turn unto the LORD your God: for he @9is@7 gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repenteth him of the evil.
verse	29	2	14	@@Who knoweth @9if@7 he will return and repent, and leave a blessing behind him; @9even@7 a meat offering and a drink offering unto the LORD your God?
verse	29	2	15	Blow the trumpet in Zion, sanctify a fast, call a solemn assembly:
verse	29	2	16	Gather the people, sanctify the congregation, assemble the elders, gather the children, and those that suck the breasts: let the bridegroom go forth of his chamber, and the bride out of her closet.
verse	29	2	17	@@Let the priests, the ministers of the LORD, weep between the porch and the altar, and let them say, Spare thy people, O LORD, and give not thine heritage to reproach, that the heathen should rule over them: wherefore should they say among the people, Where @9is@7 their God?
verse	29	2	18	Then will the LORD be jealous for his land, and pity his people.
verse	29	2	19	Yea, the LORD will answer and say unto his people, Behold, I will send you corn, and wine, and oil, and ye shall be satisfied therewith: and I will no more make you a reproach among the heathen:
verse	29	2	20	@@But I will remove far off from you the northern @9army,@7 and will drive him into a land barren and desolate, with his face toward the east sea, and his hinder part toward the utmost sea, and his stink shall come up, and his ill savour shall come up, because he hath done great things.
verse	29	2	21	Fear not, O land; be glad and rejoice: for the LORD will do great things.
verse	29	2	22	Be not afraid, ye beasts of the field: for the pastures of the wilderness do spring, for the tree beareth her fruit, the fig tree and the vine do yield their strength.
verse	29	2	23	@@Be glad then, ye children of Zion, and rejoice in the LORD your God: for he hath given you the former rain moderately, and he will cause to come down for you the rain, the former rain, and the latter rain in the first @9month. @7
verse	29	2	24	And the floors shall be full of wheat, and the fats shall overflow with wine and oil.
verse	29	2	25	And I will restore to you the years that the locust hath eaten, the cankerworm, and the caterpiller, and the palmerworm, my great army which I sent among you.
verse	29	2	26	And ye shall eat in plenty, and be satisfied, and praise the name of the LORD your God, that hath dealt wondrously with you: and my people shall never be ashamed.
verse	29	2	27	@@And ye shall know that I @9am@7 in the midst of Israel, and @9that@7 I @9am@7 the LORD your God, and none else: and my people shall never be ashamed.
verse	29	2	28	@@And it shall come to pass afterward, @9that@7 I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh; and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, your old men shall dream dreams, your young men shall see visions:
verse	29	2	29	And also upon the servants and upon the handmaids in those days will I pour out my spirit.
verse	29	2	30	And I will shew wonders in the heavens and in the earth, blood, and fire, and pillars of smoke.
verse	29	2	31	The sun shall be turned into darkness, and the moon into blood, before the great and the terrible day of the LORD come.
verse	29	2	32	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 whosoever shall call on the name of the LORD shall be delivered: for in mount Zion and in Jerusalem shall be deliverance, as the LORD hath said, and in the remnant whom the LORD shall call.
verse	29	3	1	For, behold, in those days, and in that time, when I shall bring again the captivity of Judah and Jerusalem,
verse	29	3	2	@@I will also gather all nations, and will bring them down into the valley of Jehoshaphat, and will plead with them there for my people and @9for@7 my heritage Israel, whom they have scattered among the nations, and parted my land.
verse	29	3	3	And they have cast lots for my people; and have given a boy for an harlot, and sold a girl for wine, that they might drink.
verse	29	3	4	@@Yea, and what have ye to do with me, O Tyre, and Zidon, and all the coasts of Palestine? will ye render me a recompence? and if ye recompense me, swiftly @9and@7 speedily will I return your recompence upon your own head;
verse	29	3	5	Because ye have taken my silver and my gold, and have carried into your temples my goodly pleasant things:
verse	29	3	6	The children also of Judah and the children of Jerusalem have ye sold unto the Grecians, that ye might remove them far from their border.
verse	29	3	7	Behold, I will raise them out of the place whither ye have sold them, and will return your recompence upon your own head:
verse	29	3	8	@@And I will sell your sons and your daughters into the hand of the children of Judah, and they shall sell them to the Sabeans, to a people far off: for the LORD hath spoken @9it.@7
verse	29	3	9	Proclaim ye this among the Gentiles; Prepare war, wake up the mighty men, let all the men of war draw near; let them come up:
verse	29	3	10	@@Beat your plowshares into swords, and your pruninghooks into spears: let the weak say, I @9am@7 strong.
verse	29	3	11	Assemble yourselves, and come, all ye heathen, and gather yourselves together round about: thither cause thy mighty ones to come down, O LORD.
verse	29	3	12	Let the heathen be wakened, and come up to the valley of Jehoshaphat: for there will I sit to judge all the heathen round about.
verse	29	3	13	@@Put ye in the sickle, for the harvest is ripe: come, get you down; for the press is full, the fats overflow; for their wickedness @9is@7 great.
verse	29	3	14	@@Multitudes, multitudes in the valley of decision: for the day of the LORD @9is@7 near in the valley of decision.
verse	29	3	15	The sun and the moon shall be darkened, and the stars shall withdraw their shining.
verse	29	3	16	@@The LORD also shall roar out of Zion, and utter his voice from Jerusalem; and the heavens and the earth shall shake: but the LORD @9will be@7 the hope of his people, and the strength of the children of Israel.
verse	29	3	17	@@So shall ye know that I @9am@7 the LORD your God dwelling in Zion, my holy mountain: then shall Jerusalem be holy, and there shall no strangers pass through her any more.
verse	29	3	18	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the mountains shall drop down new wine, and the hills shall flow with milk, and all the rivers of Judah shall flow with waters, and a fountain shall come forth of the house of the LORD, and shall water the valley of Shittim.
verse	29	3	19	@@Egypt shall be a desolation, and Edom shall be a desolate wilderness, for the violence @9against@7 the children of Judah, because they have shed innocent blood in their land.
verse	29	3	20	But Judah shall dwell for ever, and Jerusalem from generation to generation.
verse	29	3	21	@@For I will cleanse their blood @9that@7 I have not cleansed: for the LORD dwelleth in Zion.
verse	30	1	1	The words of Amos, who was among the herdmen of Tekoa, which he saw concerning Israel in the days of Uzziah king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel, two years before the earthquake.
verse	30	1	2	And he said, The LORD will roar from Zion, and utter his voice from Jerusalem; and the habitations of the shepherds shall mourn, and the top of Carmel shall wither.
verse	30	1	3	@@Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Damascus, and for four, I will not turn away @9the punishment@7 thereof; because they have threshed Gilead with threshing instruments of iron:
verse	30	1	4	But I will send a fire into the house of Hazael, which shall devour the palaces of Benhadad.
verse	30	1	5	I will break also the bar of Damascus, and cut off the inhabitant from the plain of Aven, and him that holdeth the sceptre from the house of Eden: and the people of Syria shall go into captivity unto Kir, saith the LORD.
verse	30	1	6	@@Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Gaza, and for four, I will not turn away @9the punishment@7 thereof; because they carried away captive the whole captivity, to deliver @9them@7 up to Edom:
verse	30	1	7	But I will send a fire on the wall of Gaza, which shall devour the palaces thereof:
verse	30	1	8	And I will cut off the inhabitant from Ashdod, and him that holdeth the sceptre from Ashkelon, and I will turn mine hand against Ekron: and the remnant of the Philistines shall perish, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	30	1	9	@@Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Tyrus, and for four, I will not turn away @9the punishment@7 thereof; because they delivered up the whole captivity to Edom, and remembered not the brotherly covenant:
verse	30	1	10	But I will send a fire on the wall of Tyrus, which shall devour the palaces thereof.
verse	30	1	11	@@Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Edom, and for four, I will not turn away @9the punishment@7 thereof; because he did pursue his brother with the sword, and did cast off all pity, and his anger did tear perpetually, and he kept his wrath for ever:
verse	30	1	12	But I will send a fire upon Teman, which shall devour the palaces of Bozrah.
verse	30	1	13	@@Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of the children of Ammon, and for four, I will not turn away @9the punishment@7 thereof; because they have ripped up the women with child of Gilead, that they might enlarge their border:
verse	30	1	14	But I will kindle a fire in the wall of Rabbah, and it shall devour the palaces thereof, with shouting in the day of battle, with a tempest in the day of the whirlwind:
verse	30	1	15	And their king shall go into captivity, he and his princes together, saith the LORD.
verse	30	2	1	@@Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Moab, and for four, I will not turn away @9the punishment@7 thereof; because he burned the bones of the king of Edom into lime:
verse	30	2	2	@@But I will send a fire upon Moab, and it shall devour the palaces of Kirioth: and Moab shall die with tumult, with shouting, @9and@7 with the sound of the trumpet:
verse	30	2	3	And I will cut off the judge from the midst thereof, and will slay all the princes thereof with him, saith the LORD.
verse	30	2	4	@@Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Judah, and for four, I will not turn away @9the punishment@7 thereof; because they have despised the law of the LORD, and have not kept his commandments, and their lies caused them to err, after the which their fathers have walked:
verse	30	2	5	But I will send a fire upon Judah, and it shall devour the palaces of Jerusalem.
verse	30	2	6	@@Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Israel, and for four, I will not turn away @9the punishment@7 thereof; because they sold the righteous for silver, and the poor for a pair of shoes;
verse	30	2	7	@@That pant after the dust of the earth on the head of the poor, and turn aside the way of the meek: and a man and his father will go in unto the @9same@7 maid, to profane my holy name:
verse	30	2	8	@@And they lay @9themselves@7 down upon clothes laid to pledge by every altar, and they drink the wine of the condemned in the house of their god.
verse	30	2	9	@@Yet destroyed I the Amorite before them, whose height @9was@7 like the height of the cedars, and he @9was@7 strong as the oaks; yet I destroyed his fruit from above, and his roots from beneath.
verse	30	2	10	Also I brought you up from the land of Egypt, and led you forty years through the wilderness, to possess the land of the Amorite.
verse	30	2	11	@@And I raised up of your sons for prophets, and of your young men for Nazarites. @9Is it@7 not even thus, O ye children of Israel? saith the LORD.
verse	30	2	12	But ye gave the Nazarites wine to drink; and commanded the prophets, saying, Prophesy not.
verse	30	2	13	@@Behold, I am pressed under you, as a cart is pressed @9that is@7 full of sheaves.
verse	30	2	14	Therefore the flight shall perish from the swift, and the strong shall not strengthen his force, neither shall the mighty deliver himself:
verse	30	2	15	@@Neither shall he stand that handleth the bow; and @9he that is@7 swift of foot shall not deliver @9himself:@7 neither shall he that rideth the horse deliver himself.
verse	30	2	16	@@And @9he that is@7 courageous among the mighty shall flee away naked in that day, saith the LORD.
verse	30	3	1	Hear this word that the LORD hath spoken against you, O children of Israel, against the whole family which I brought up from the land of Egypt, saying,
verse	30	3	2	You only have I known of all the families of the earth: therefore I will punish you for all your iniquities.
verse	30	3	3	Can two walk together, except they be agreed?
verse	30	3	4	Will a lion roar in the forest, when he hath no prey? will a young lion cry out of his den, if he have taken nothing?
verse	30	3	5	@@Can a bird fall in a snare upon the earth, where no gin @9is@7 for him? shall @9one@7 take up a snare from the earth, and have taken nothing at all?
verse	30	3	6	@@Shall a trumpet be blown in the city, and the people not be afraid? shall there be evil in a city, and the LORD hath not done @9it? @7
verse	30	3	7	Surely the Lord GOD will do nothing, but he revealeth his secret unto his servants the prophets.
verse	30	3	8	The lion hath roared, who will not fear? the Lord GOD hath spoken, who can but prophesy?
verse	30	3	9	Publish in the palaces at Ashdod, and in the palaces in the land of Egypt, and say, Assemble yourselves upon the mountains of Samaria, and behold the great tumults in the midst thereof, and the oppressed in the midst thereof.
verse	30	3	10	For they know not to do right, saith the LORD, who store up violence and robbery in their palaces.
verse	30	3	11	@@Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; An adversary @9there shall be@7 even round about the land; and he shall bring down thy strength from thee, and thy palaces shall be spoiled.
verse	30	3	12	@@Thus saith the LORD; As the shepherd taketh out of the mouth of the lion two legs, or a piece of an ear; so shall the children of Israel be taken out that dwell in Samaria in the corner of a bed, and in Damascus @9in@7 a couch.
verse	30	3	13	Hear ye, and testify in the house of Jacob, saith the Lord GOD, the God of hosts,
verse	30	3	14	That in the day that I shall visit the transgressions of Israel upon him I will also visit the altars of Bethel: and the horns of the altar shall be cut off, and fall to the ground.
verse	30	3	15	And I will smite the winter house with the summer house; and the houses of ivory shall perish, and the great houses shall have an end, saith the LORD.
verse	30	4	1	@@Hear this word, ye kine of Bashan, that @9are@7 in the mountain of Samaria, which oppress the poor, which crush the needy, which say to their masters, Bring, and let us drink.
verse	30	4	2	The Lord GOD hath sworn by his holiness, that, lo, the days shall come upon you, that he will take you away with hooks, and your posterity with fishhooks.
verse	30	4	3	@@And ye shall go out at the breaches, every @9cow at that which is@7 before her; and ye shall cast @9them@7 into the palace, saith the LORD.
verse	30	4	4	@@Come to Bethel, and transgress; at Gilgal multiply transgression; and bring your sacrifices every morning, @9and@7 your tithes after three years:
verse	30	4	5	@@And offer a sacrifice of thanksgiving with leaven, and proclaim @9and@7 publish the free offerings: for this liketh you, O ye children of Israel, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	30	4	6	And I also have given you cleanness of teeth in all your cities, and want of bread in all your places: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
verse	30	4	7	@@And also I have withholden the rain from you, when @9there were@7 yet three months to the harvest: and I caused it to rain upon one city, and caused it not to rain upon another city: one piece was rained upon, and the piece whereupon it rained not withered.
verse	30	4	8	@@So two @9or@7 three cities wandered unto one city, to drink water; but they were not satisfied: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
verse	30	4	9	@@I have smitten you with blasting and mildew: when your gardens and your vineyards and your fig trees and your olive trees increased, the palmerworm devoured @9them:@7 yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
verse	30	4	10	I have sent among you the pestilence after the manner of Egypt: your young men have I slain with the sword, and have taken away your horses; and I have made the stink of your camps to come up unto your nostrils: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
verse	30	4	11	@@I have overthrown @9some@7 of you, as God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah, and ye were as a firebrand plucked out of the burning: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.
verse	30	4	12	@@Therefore thus will I do unto thee, O Israel: @9and@7 because I will do this unto thee, prepare to meet thy God, O Israel.
verse	30	4	13	@@For, lo, he that formeth the mountains, and createth the wind, and declareth unto man what @9is@7 his thought, that maketh the morning darkness, and treadeth upon the high places of the earth, The LORD, The God of hosts, @9is@7 his name.
verse	30	5	1	@@Hear ye this word which I take up against you, @9even@7 a lamentation, O house of Israel.
verse	30	5	2	@@The virgin of Israel is fallen; she shall no more rise: she is forsaken upon her land; @9there is@7 none to raise her up.
verse	30	5	3	@@For thus saith the Lord GOD; The city that went out @9by@7 a thousand shall leave an hundred, and that which went forth @9by@7 an hundred shall leave ten, to the house of Israel.
verse	30	5	4	For thus saith the LORD unto the house of Israel, Seek ye me, and ye shall live:
verse	30	5	5	But seek not Bethel, nor enter into Gilgal, and pass not to Beersheba: for Gilgal shall surely go into captivity, and Bethel shall come to nought.
verse	30	5	6	@@Seek the LORD, and ye shall live; lest he break out like fire in the house of Joseph, and devour @9it,@7 and @9there be@7 none to quench @9it@7 in Bethel.
verse	30	5	7	Ye who turn judgment to wormwood, and leave off righteousness in the earth,
verse	30	5	8	@@@9Seek him@7 that maketh the seven stars and Orion, and turneth the shadow of death into the morning, and maketh the day dark with night: that calleth for the waters of the sea, and poureth them out upon the face of the earth: The LORD @9is@7 his name:
verse	30	5	9	That strengtheneth the spoiled against the strong, so that the spoiled shall come against the fortress.
verse	30	5	10	They hate him that rebuketh in the gate, and they abhor him that speaketh uprightly.
verse	30	5	11	@@Forasmuch therefore as your treading @9is@7 upon the poor, and ye take from him burdens of wheat: ye have built houses of hewn stone, but ye shall not dwell in them; ye have planted pleasant vineyards, but ye shall not drink wine of them.
verse	30	5	12	@@For I know your manifold transgressions and your mighty sins: they afflict the just, they take a bribe, and they turn aside the poor in the gate @9from their right. @7
verse	30	5	13	@@Therefore the prudent shall keep silence in that time; for it @9is@7 an evil time.
verse	30	5	14	Seek good, and not evil, that ye may live: and so the LORD, the God of hosts, shall be with you, as ye have spoken.
verse	30	5	15	Hate the evil, and love the good, and establish judgment in the gate: it may be that the LORD God of hosts will be gracious unto the remnant of Joseph.
verse	30	5	16	@@Therefore the LORD, the God of hosts, the Lord, saith thus; Wailing @9shall be@7 in all streets; and they shall say in all the highways, Alas! alas! and they shall call the husbandman to mourning, and such as are skilful of lamentation to wailing.
verse	30	5	17	@@And in all vineyards @9shall be@7 wailing: for I will pass through thee, saith the LORD.
verse	30	5	18	@@Woe unto you that desire the day of the LORD! to what end @9is@7 it for you? the day of the LORD @9is@7 darkness, and not light.
verse	30	5	19	As if a man did flee from a lion, and a bear met him; or went into the house, and leaned his hand on the wall, and a serpent bit him.
verse	30	5	20	@@@9Shall@7 not the day of the LORD @9be@7 darkness, and not light? even very dark, and no brightness in it?
verse	30	5	21	I hate, I despise your feast days, and I will not smell in your solemn assemblies.
verse	30	5	22	@@Though ye offer me burnt offerings and your meat offerings, I will not accept @9them:@7 neither will I regard the peace offerings of your fat beasts.
verse	30	5	23	Take thou away from me the noise of thy songs; for I will not hear the melody of thy viols.
verse	30	5	24	But let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.
verse	30	5	25	Have ye offered unto me sacrifices and offerings in the wilderness forty years, O house of Israel?
verse	30	5	26	But ye have borne the tabernacle of your Moloch and Chiun your images, the star of your god, which ye made to yourselves.
verse	30	5	27	@@Therefore will I cause you to go into captivity beyond Damascus, saith the LORD, whose name @9is@7 The God of hosts.
verse	30	6	1	@@Woe to them @9that are@7 at ease in Zion, and trust in the mountain of Samaria, @9which are@7 named chief of the nations, to whom the house of Israel came!
verse	30	6	2	@@Pass ye unto Calneh, and see; and from thence go ye to Hamath the great: then go down to Gath of the Philistines: @9be they@7 better than these kingdoms? or their border greater than your border?
verse	30	6	3	Ye that put far away the evil day, and cause the seat of violence to come near;
verse	30	6	4	That lie upon beds of ivory, and stretch themselves upon their couches, and eat the lambs out of the flock, and the calves out of the midst of the stall;
verse	30	6	5	@@That chant to the sound of the viol, @9and@7 invent to themselves instruments of musick, like David;
verse	30	6	6	That drink wine in bowls, and anoint themselves with the chief ointments: but they are not grieved for the affliction of Joseph.
verse	30	6	7	Therefore now shall they go captive with the first that go captive, and the banquet of them that stretched themselves shall be removed.
verse	30	6	8	The Lord GOD hath sworn by himself, saith the LORD the God of hosts, I abhor the excellency of Jacob, and hate his palaces: therefore will I deliver up the city with all that is therein.
verse	30	6	9	And it shall come to pass, if there remain ten men in one house, that they shall die.
verse	30	6	10	@@And a man's uncle shall take him up, and he that burneth him, to bring out the bones out of the house, and shall say unto him that @9is@7 by the sides of the house, @9Is there@7 yet @9any@7 with thee? and he shall say, No. Then shall he say, Hold thy tongue: for we may not make mention of the name of the LORD.
verse	30	6	11	For, behold, the LORD commandeth, and he will smite the great house with breaches, and the little house with clefts.
verse	30	6	12	@@Shall horses run upon the rock? will @9one@7 plow @9there@7 with oxen? for ye have turned judgment into gall, and the fruit of righteousness into hemlock:
verse	30	6	13	Ye which rejoice in a thing of nought, which say, Have we not taken to us horns by our own strength?
verse	30	6	14	But, behold, I will raise up against you a nation, O house of Israel, saith the LORD the God of hosts; and they shall afflict you from the entering in of Hemath unto the river of the wilderness.
verse	30	7	1	@@Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto me; and, behold, he formed grasshoppers in the beginning of the shooting up of the latter growth; and, lo, @9it was@7 the latter growth after the king's mowings.
verse	30	7	2	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 when they had made an end of eating the grass of the land, then I said, O Lord GOD, forgive, I beseech thee: by whom shall Jacob arise? for he @9is@7 small.
verse	30	7	3	The LORD repented for this: It shall not be, saith the LORD.
verse	30	7	4	Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto me: and, behold, the Lord GOD called to contend by fire, and it devoured the great deep, and did eat up a part.
verse	30	7	5	@@Then said I, O Lord GOD, cease, I beseech thee: by whom shall Jacob arise? for he @9is@7 small.
verse	30	7	6	The LORD repented for this: This also shall not be, saith the Lord GOD.
verse	30	7	7	@@Thus he shewed me: and, behold, the Lord stood upon a wall @9made@7 by a plumbline, with a plumbline in his hand.
verse	30	7	8	And the LORD said unto me, Amos, what seest thou? And I said, A plumbline. Then said the Lord, Behold, I will set a plumbline in the midst of my people Israel: I will not again pass by them any more:
verse	30	7	9	And the high places of Isaac shall be desolate, and the sanctuaries of Israel shall be laid waste; and I will rise against the house of Jeroboam with the sword.
verse	30	7	10	Then Amaziah the priest of Bethel sent to Jeroboam king of Israel, saying, Amos hath conspired against thee in the midst of the house of Israel: the land is not able to bear all his words.
verse	30	7	11	For thus Amos saith, Jeroboam shall die by the sword, and Israel shall surely be led away captive out of their own land.
verse	30	7	12	Also Amaziah said unto Amos, O thou seer, go, flee thee away into the land of Judah, and there eat bread, and prophesy there:
verse	30	7	13	@@But prophesy not again any more at Bethel: for it @9is@7 the king's chapel, and it @9is@7 the king's court.
verse	30	7	14	@@Then answered Amos, and said to Amaziah, I @9was@7 no prophet, neither @9was@7 I a prophet's son; but I @9was@7 an herdman, and a gatherer of sycomore fruit:
verse	30	7	15	And the LORD took me as I followed the flock, and the LORD said unto me, Go, prophesy unto my people Israel.
verse	30	7	16	@@Now therefore hear thou the word of the LORD: Thou sayest, Prophesy not against Israel, and drop not @9thy word@7 against the house of Isaac.
verse	30	7	17	Therefore thus saith the LORD; Thy wife shall be an harlot in the city, and thy sons and thy daughters shall fall by the sword, and thy land shall be divided by line; and thou shalt die in a polluted land: and Israel shall surely go into captivity forth of his land.
verse	30	8	1	Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto me: and behold a basket of summer fruit.
verse	30	8	2	And he said, Amos, what seest thou? And I said, A basket of summer fruit. Then said the LORD unto me, The end is come upon my people of Israel; I will not again pass by them any more.
verse	30	8	3	@@And the songs of the temple shall be howlings in that day, saith the Lord GOD: @9there shall be@7 many dead bodies in every place; they shall cast @9them@7 forth with silence.
verse	30	8	4	Hear this, O ye that swallow up the needy, even to make the poor of the land to fail,
verse	30	8	5	Saying, When will the new moon be gone, that we may sell corn? and the sabbath, that we may set forth wheat, making the ephah small, and the shekel great, and falsifying the balances by deceit?
verse	30	8	6	@@That we may buy the poor for silver, and the needy for a pair of shoes; @9yea,@7 and sell the refuse of the wheat?
