verse	30	8	8	@@Shall not the land tremble for this, and every one mourn that dwelleth therein? and it shall rise up wholly as a flood; and it shall be cast out and drowned, as @9by@7 the flood of Egypt.
verse	30	8	9	And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the Lord GOD, that I will cause the sun to go down at noon, and I will darken the earth in the clear day:
verse	30	8	10	@@And I will turn your feasts into mourning, and all your songs into lamentation; and I will bring up sackcloth upon all loins, and baldness upon every head; and I will make it as the mourning of an only @9son,@7 and the end thereof as a bitter day.
verse	30	8	11	Behold, the days come, saith the Lord GOD, that I will send a famine in the land, not a famine of bread, nor a thirst for water, but of hearing the words of the LORD:
verse	30	8	12	@@And they shall wander from sea to sea, and from the north even to the east, they shall run to and fro to seek the word of the LORD, and shall not find @9it. @7
verse	30	8	13	In that day shall the fair virgins and young men faint for thirst.
verse	30	8	14	They that swear by the sin of Samaria, and say, Thy god, O Dan, liveth; and, The manner of Beersheba liveth; even they shall fall, and never rise up again.
verse	30	9	1	I saw the LORD standing upon the altar: and he said, Smite the lintel of the door, that the posts may shake: and cut them in the head, all of them; and I will slay the last of them with the sword: he that fleeth of them shall not flee away, and he that escapeth of them shall not be delivered.
verse	30	9	2	Though they dig into hell, thence shall mine hand take them; though they climb up to heaven, thence will I bring them down:
verse	30	9	3	And though they hide themselves in the top of Carmel, I will search and take them out thence; and though they be hid from my sight in the bottom of the sea, thence will I command the serpent, and he shall bite them:
verse	30	9	4	And though they go into captivity before their enemies, thence will I command the sword, and it shall slay them: and I will set mine eyes upon them for evil, and not for good.
verse	30	9	5	@@And the Lord GOD of hosts @9is@7 he that toucheth the land, and it shall melt, and all that dwell therein shall mourn: and it shall rise up wholly like a flood; and shall be drowned, as @9by@7 the flood of Egypt.
verse	30	9	6	@@@9It is@7 he that buildeth his stories in the heaven, and hath founded his troop in the earth; he that calleth for the waters of the sea, and poureth them out upon the face of the earth: The LORD @9is@7 his name.
verse	30	9	7	@@@9Are@7 ye not as children of the Ethiopians unto me, O children of Israel? saith the LORD. Have not I brought up Israel out of the land of Egypt? and the Philistines from Caphtor, and the Syrians from Kir?
verse	30	9	8	@@Behold, the eyes of the Lord GOD @9are@7 upon the sinful kingdom, and I will destroy it from off the face of the earth; saving that I will not utterly destroy the house of Jacob, saith the LORD.
verse	30	9	9	@@For, lo, I will command, and I will sift the house of Israel among all nations, like as @9corn@7 is sifted in a sieve, yet shall not the least grain fall upon the earth.
verse	30	9	10	All the sinners of my people shall die by the sword, which say, The evil shall not overtake nor prevent us.
verse	30	9	11	In that day will I raise up the tabernacle of David that is fallen, and close up the breaches thereof; and I will raise up his ruins, and I will build it as in the days of old:
verse	30	9	12	That they may possess the remnant of Edom, and of all the heathen, which are called by my name, saith the LORD that doeth this.
verse	30	9	13	Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that the plowman shall overtake the reaper, and the treader of grapes him that soweth seed; and the mountains shall drop sweet wine, and all the hills shall melt.
verse	30	9	14	@@And I will bring again the captivity of my people of Israel, and they shall build the waste cities, and inhabit @9them;@7 and they shall plant vineyards, and drink the wine thereof; they shall also make gardens, and eat the fruit of them.
verse	30	9	15	And I will plant them upon their land, and they shall no more be pulled up out of their land which I have given them, saith the LORD thy God.
verse	31	1	1	The vision of Obadiah. Thus saith the Lord GOD concerning Edom; We have heard a rumour from the LORD, and an ambassador is sent among the heathen, Arise ye, and let us rise up against her in battle.
verse	31	1	2	Behold, I have made thee small among the heathen: thou art greatly despised.
verse	31	1	3	@@The pride of thine heart hath deceived thee, thou that dwellest in the clefts of the rock, whose habitation @9is@7 high; that saith in his heart, Who shall bring me down to the ground?
verse	31	1	4	@@Though thou exalt @9thyself@7 as the eagle, and though thou set thy nest among the stars, thence will I bring thee down, saith the LORD.
verse	31	1	5	@@If thieves came to thee, if robbers by night, (how art thou cut off!) would they not have stolen till they had enough? if the grapegatherers came to thee, would they not leave @9some@7 grapes?
verse	31	1	6	@@How are @9the things@7 of Esau searched out! @9how@7 are his hidden things sought up!
verse	31	1	7	@@All the men of thy confederacy have brought thee @9even@7 to the border: the men that were at peace with thee have deceived thee, @9and@7 prevailed against thee; @9they that eat@7 thy bread have laid a wound under thee: @9there is@7 none understanding in him.
verse	31	1	8	@@Shall I not in that day, saith the LORD, even destroy the wise @9men@7 out of Edom, and understanding out of the mount of Esau?
verse	31	1	9	@@And thy mighty @9men,@7 O Teman, shall be dismayed, to the end that every one of the mount of Esau may be cut off by slaughter.
verse	31	1	10	@@For @9thy@7 violence against thy brother Jacob shame shall cover thee, and thou shalt be cut off for ever.
verse	31	1	11	@@In the day that thou stoodest on the other side, in the day that the strangers carried away captive his forces, and foreigners entered into his gates, and cast lots upon Jerusalem, even thou @9wast@7 as one of them.
verse	31	1	12	But thou shouldest not have looked on the day of thy brother in the day that he became a stranger; neither shouldest thou have rejoiced over the children of Judah in the day of their destruction; neither shouldest thou have spoken proudly in the day of distress.
verse	31	1	13	@@Thou shouldest not have entered into the gate of my people in the day of their calamity; yea, thou shouldest not have looked on their affliction in the day of their calamity, nor have laid @9hands@7 on their substance in the day of their calamity;
verse	31	1	14	Neither shouldest thou have stood in the crossway, to cut off those of his that did escape; neither shouldest thou have delivered up those of his that did remain in the day of distress.
verse	31	1	15	@@For the day of the LORD @9is@7 near upon all the heathen: as thou hast done, it shall be done unto thee: thy reward shall return upon thine own head.
verse	31	1	16	@@For as ye have drunk upon my holy mountain, @9so@7 shall all the heathen drink continually, yea, they shall drink, and they shall swallow down, and they shall be as though they had not been.
verse	31	1	17	But upon mount Zion shall be deliverance, and there shall be holiness; and the house of Jacob shall possess their possessions.
verse	31	1	18	@@And the house of Jacob shall be a fire, and the house of Joseph a flame, and the house of Esau for stubble, and they shall kindle in them, and devour them; and there shall not be @9any@7 remaining of the house of Esau; for the LORD hath spoken @9it. @7
verse	31	1	19	@@And @9they of@7 the south shall possess the mount of Esau; and @9they of@7 the plain the Philistines: and they shall possess the fields of Ephraim, and the fields of Samaria: and Benjamin @9shall possess@7 Gilead.
verse	31	1	20	@@And the captivity of this host of the children of Israel @9shall possess@7 that of the Canaanites, @9even@7 unto Zarephath; and the captivity of Jerusalem, which @9is@7 in Sepharad, shall possess the cities of the south.
verse	31	1	21	And saviours shall come up on mount Zion to judge the mount of Esau; and the kingdom shall be the LORD'S.
verse	32	1	1	Now the word of the LORD came unto Jonah the son of Amittai, saying,
verse	32	1	2	Arise, go to Nineveh, that great city, and cry against it; for their wickedness is come up before me.
verse	32	1	3	But Jonah rose up to flee unto Tarshish from the presence of the LORD, and went down to Joppa; and he found a ship going to Tarshish: so he paid the fare thereof, and went down into it, to go with them unto Tarshish from the presence of the LORD.
verse	32	1	4	But the LORD sent out a great wind into the sea, and there was a mighty tempest in the sea, so that the ship was like to be broken.
verse	32	1	5	@@Then the mariners were afraid, and cried every man unto his god, and cast forth the wares that @9were@7 in the ship into the sea, to lighten @9it@7 of them. But Jonah was gone down into the sides of the ship; and he lay, and was fast asleep.
verse	32	1	6	So the shipmaster came to him, and said unto him, What meanest thou, O sleeper? arise, call upon thy God, if so be that God will think upon us, that we perish not.
verse	32	1	7	@@And they said every one to his fellow, Come, and let us cast lots, that we may know for whose cause this evil @9is@7 upon us. So they cast lots, and the lot fell upon Jonah.
verse	32	1	8	@@Then said they unto him, Tell us, we pray thee, for whose cause this evil @9is@7 upon us; What @9is@7 thine occupation? and whence comest thou? what @9is@7 thy country? and of what people @9art@7 thou?
verse	32	1	9	@@And he said unto them, I @9am@7 an Hebrew; and I fear the LORD, the God of heaven, which hath made the sea and the dry @9land. @7
verse	32	1	10	Then were the men exceedingly afraid, and said unto him, Why hast thou done this? For the men knew that he fled from the presence of the LORD, because he had told them.
verse	32	1	11	Then said they unto him, What shall we do unto thee, that the sea may be calm unto us? for the sea wrought, and was tempestuous.
verse	32	1	12	@@And he said unto them, Take me up, and cast me forth into the sea; so shall the sea be calm unto you: for I know that for my sake this great tempest @9is@7 upon you.
verse	32	1	13	@@Nevertheless the men rowed hard to bring @9it@7 to the land; but they could not: for the sea wrought, and was tempestuous against them.
verse	32	1	14	Wherefore they cried unto the LORD, and said, We beseech thee, O LORD, we beseech thee, let us not perish for this man's life, and lay not upon us innocent blood: for thou, O LORD, hast done as it pleased thee.
verse	32	1	15	So they took up Jonah, and cast him forth into the sea: and the sea ceased from her raging.
verse	32	1	16	Then the men feared the LORD exceedingly, and offered a sacrifice unto the LORD, and made vows.
verse	32	1	17	Now the LORD had prepared a great fish to swallow up Jonah. And Jonah was in the belly of the fish three days and three nights.
verse	32	2	1	Then Jonah prayed unto the LORD his God out of the fish's belly,
verse	32	2	2	@@And said, I cried by reason of mine affliction unto the LORD, and he heard me; out of the belly of hell cried I, @9and@7 thou heardest my voice.
verse	32	2	3	For thou hadst cast me into the deep, in the midst of the seas; and the floods compassed me about: all thy billows and thy waves passed over me.
verse	32	2	4	Then I said, I am cast out of thy sight; yet I will look again toward thy holy temple.
verse	32	2	5	@@The waters compassed me about, @9even@7 to the soul: the depth closed me round about, the weeds were wrapped about my head.
verse	32	2	6	@@I went down to the bottoms of the mountains; the earth with her bars @9was@7 about me for ever: yet hast thou brought up my life from corruption, O LORD my God.
verse	32	2	7	When my soul fainted within me I remembered the LORD: and my prayer came in unto thee, into thine holy temple.
verse	32	2	8	They that observe lying vanities forsake their own mercy.
verse	32	2	9	@@But I will sacrifice unto thee with the voice of thanksgiving; I will pay @9that@7 that I have vowed. Salvation @9is@7 of the LORD.
verse	32	2	10	@@And the LORD spake unto the fish, and it vomited out Jonah upon the dry @9land.@7
verse	32	3	1	And the word of the LORD came unto Jonah the second time, saying,
verse	32	3	2	Arise, go unto Nineveh, that great city, and preach unto it the preaching that I bid thee.
verse	32	3	3	So Jonah arose, and went unto Nineveh, according to the word of the LORD. Now Nineveh was an exceeding great city of three days' journey.
verse	32	3	4	And Jonah began to enter into the city a day's journey, and he cried, and said, Yet forty days, and Nineveh shall be overthrown.
verse	32	3	5	So the people of Nineveh believed God, and proclaimed a fast, and put on sackcloth, from the greatest of them even to the least of them.
verse	32	3	6	@@For word came unto the king of Nineveh, and he arose from his throne, and he laid his robe from him, and covered @9him@7 with sackcloth, and sat in ashes.
verse	32	3	7	@@And he caused @9it@7 to be proclaimed and published through Nineveh by the decree of the king and his nobles, saying, Let neither man nor beast, herd nor flock, taste any thing: let them not feed, nor drink water:
verse	32	3	8	@@But let man and beast be covered with sackcloth, and cry mightily unto God: yea, let them turn every one from his evil way, and from the violence that @9is@7 in their hands.
verse	32	3	9	@@Who can tell @9if@7 God will turn and repent, and turn away from his fierce anger, that we perish not?
verse	32	3	10	@@And God saw their works, that they turned from their evil way; and God repented of the evil, that he had said that he would do unto them; and he did @9it@7 not.
verse	32	4	1	But it displeased Jonah exceedingly, and he was very angry.
verse	32	4	2	@@And he prayed unto the LORD, and said, I pray thee, O LORD, @9was@7 not this my saying, when I was yet in my country? Therefore I fled before unto Tarshish: for I knew that thou @9art@7 a gracious God, and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repentest thee of the evil.
verse	32	4	3	@@Therefore now, O LORD, take, I beseech thee, my life from me; for @9it is@7 better for me to die than to live.
verse	32	4	4	Then said the LORD, Doest thou well to be angry?
verse	32	4	5	So Jonah went out of the city, and sat on the east side of the city, and there made him a booth, and sat under it in the shadow, till he might see what would become of the city.
verse	32	4	6	@@And the LORD God prepared a gourd, and made @9it@7 to come up over Jonah, that it might be a shadow over his head, to deliver him from his grief. So Jonah was exceeding glad of the gourd.
verse	32	4	7	But God prepared a worm when the morning rose the next day, and it smote the gourd that it withered.
verse	32	4	8	@@And it came to pass, when the sun did arise, that God prepared a vehement east wind; and the sun beat upon the head of Jonah, that he fainted, and wished in himself to die, and said, @9It is@7 better for me to die than to live.
verse	32	4	9	@@And God said to Jonah, Doest thou well to be angry for the gourd? And he said, I do well to be angry, @9even@7 unto death.
verse	32	4	10	Then said the LORD, Thou hast had pity on the gourd, for the which thou hast not laboured, neither madest it grow; which came up in a night, and perished in a night:
verse	32	4	11	@@And should not I spare Nineveh, that great city, wherein are more than sixscore thousand persons that cannot discern between their right hand and their left hand; and @9also@7 much cattle?
verse	33	1	1	@@The word of the LORD that came to Micah the Morasthite in the days of Jotham, Ahaz, @9and@7 Hezekiah, kings of Judah, which he saw concerning Samaria and Jerusalem.
verse	33	1	2	Hear, all ye people; hearken, O earth, and all that therein is: and let the Lord GOD be witness against you, the Lord from his holy temple.
verse	33	1	3	For, behold, the LORD cometh forth out of his place, and will come down, and tread upon the high places of the earth.
verse	33	1	4	@@And the mountains shall be molten under him, and the valleys shall be cleft, as wax before the fire, @9and@7 as the waters @9that are@7 poured down a steep place.
verse	33	1	5	@@For the transgression of Jacob @9is@7 all this, and for the sins of the house of Israel. What @9is@7 the transgression of Jacob? @9is it@7 not Samaria? and what @9are@7 the high places of Judah? @9are they@7 not Jerusalem?
verse	33	1	6	@@Therefore I will make Samaria as an heap of the field, @9and@7 as plantings of a vineyard: and I will pour down the stones thereof into the valley, and I will discover the foundations thereof.
verse	33	1	7	@@And all the graven images thereof shall be beaten to pieces, and all the hires thereof shall be burned with the fire, and all the idols thereof will I lay desolate: for she gathered @9it@7 of the hire of an harlot, and they shall return to the hire of an harlot.
verse	33	1	8	Therefore I will wail and howl, I will go stripped and naked: I will make a wailing like the dragons, and mourning as the owls.
verse	33	1	9	@@For her wound @9is@7 incurable; for it is come unto Judah; he is come unto the gate of my people, @9even@7 to Jerusalem.
verse	33	1	10	@@Declare ye @9it@7 not at Gath, weep ye not at all: in the house of Aphrah roll thyself in the dust.
verse	33	1	11	Pass ye away, thou inhabitant of Saphir, having thy shame naked: the inhabitant of Zaanan came not forth in the mourning of Beth-ezel; he shall receive of you his standing.
verse	33	1	12	For the inhabitant of Maroth waited carefully for good: but evil came down from the LORD unto the gate of Jerusalem.
verse	33	1	13	@@O thou inhabitant of Lachish, bind the chariot to the swift beast: she @9is@7 the beginning of the sin to the daughter of Zion: for the transgressions of Israel were found in thee.
verse	33	1	14	@@Therefore shalt thou give presents to Moresheth-gath: the houses of Achzib @9shall be@7 a lie to the kings of Israel.
verse	33	1	15	Yet will I bring an heir unto thee, O inhabitant of Mareshah: he shall come unto Adullam the glory of Israel.
verse	33	1	16	Make thee bald, and poll thee for thy delicate children; enlarge thy baldness as the eagle; for they are gone into captivity from thee.
verse	33	2	1	Woe to them that devise iniquity, and work evil upon their beds! when the morning is light, they practise it, because it is in the power of their hand.
verse	33	2	2	@@And they covet fields, and take @9them@7 by violence; and houses, and take @9them@7 away: so they oppress a man and his house, even a man and his heritage.
verse	33	2	3	@@Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, against this family do I devise an evil, from which ye shall not remove your necks; neither shall ye go haughtily: for this time @9is@7 evil.
verse	33	2	4	@@In that day shall @9one@7 take up a parable against you, and lament with a doleful lamentation, @9and@7 say, We be utterly spoiled: he hath changed the portion of my people: how hath he removed @9it@7 from me! turning away he hath divided our fields.
verse	33	2	5	Therefore thou shalt have none that shall cast a cord by lot in the congregation of the LORD.
verse	33	2	6	@@Prophesy ye not, @9say they to them that@7 prophesy: they shall not prophesy to them, @9that@7 they shall not take shame.
verse	33	2	7	@@O @9thou that art@7 named the house of Jacob, is the spirit of the LORD straitened? @9are@7 these his doings? do not my words do good to him that walketh uprightly?
verse	33	2	8	Even of late my people is risen up as an enemy: ye pull off the robe with the garment from them that pass by securely as men averse from war.
verse	33	2	9	The women of my people have ye cast out from their pleasant houses; from their children have ye taken away my glory for ever.
verse	33	2	10	@@Arise ye, and depart; for this @9is@7 not @9your@7 rest: because it is polluted, it shall destroy @9you,@7 even with a sore destruction.
verse	33	2	11	@@If a man walking in the spirit and falsehood do lie, @9saying,@7 I will prophesy unto thee of wine and of strong drink; he shall even be the prophet of this people.
verse	33	2	12	@@I will surely assemble, O Jacob, all of thee; I will surely gather the remnant of Israel; I will put them together as the sheep of Bozrah, as the flock in the midst of their fold: they shall make great noise by reason of @9the multitude of@7 men.
verse	33	2	13	The breaker is come up before them: they have broken up, and have passed through the gate, and are gone out by it: and their king shall pass before them, and the LORD on the head of them.
verse	33	3	1	@@And I said, Hear, I pray you, O heads of Jacob, and ye princes of the house of Israel; @9Is it@7 not for you to know judgment?
verse	33	3	2	Who hate the good, and love the evil; who pluck off their skin from off them, and their flesh from off their bones;
verse	33	3	3	Who also eat the flesh of my people, and flay their skin from off them; and they break their bones, and chop them in pieces, as for the pot, and as flesh within the caldron.
verse	33	3	4	Then shall they cry unto the LORD, but he will not hear them: he will even hide his face from them at that time, as they have behaved themselves ill in their doings.
verse	33	3	5	Thus saith the LORD concerning the prophets that make my people err, that bite with their teeth, and cry, Peace; and he that putteth not into their mouths, they even prepare war against him.
verse	33	3	6	@@Therefore night @9shall be@7 unto you, that ye shall not have a vision; and it shall be dark unto you, that ye shall not divine; and the sun shall go down over the prophets, and the day shall be dark over them.
verse	33	3	7	@@Then shall the seers be ashamed, and the diviners confounded: yea, they shall all cover their lips; for @9there is@7 no answer of God.
verse	33	3	8	But truly I am full of power by the spirit of the LORD, and of judgment, and of might, to declare unto Jacob his transgression, and to Israel his sin.
verse	33	3	9	Hear this, I pray you, ye heads of the house of Jacob, and princes of the house of Israel, that abhor judgment, and pervert all equity.
verse	33	3	10	They build up Zion with blood, and Jerusalem with iniquity.
verse	33	3	11	@@The heads thereof judge for reward, and the priests thereof teach for hire, and the prophets thereof divine for money: yet will they lean upon the LORD, and say, @9Is@7 not the LORD among us? none evil can come upon us.
verse	33	3	12	@@Therefore shall Zion for your sake be plowed @9as@7 a field, and Jerusalem shall become heaps, and the mountain of the house as the high places of the forest.
verse	33	4	1	@@But in the last days it shall come to pass, @9that@7 the mountain of the house of the LORD shall be established in the top of the mountains, and it shall be exalted above the hills; and people shall flow unto it.
verse	33	4	2	And many nations shall come, and say, Come, and let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, and to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths: for the law shall go forth of Zion, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem.
verse	33	4	3	And he shall judge among many people, and rebuke strong nations afar off; and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruninghooks: nation shall not lift up a sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more.
verse	33	4	4	@@But they shall sit every man under his vine and under his fig tree; and none shall make @9them@7 afraid: for the mouth of the LORD of hosts hath spoken @9it. @7
verse	33	4	5	For all people will walk every one in the name of his god, and we will walk in the name of the LORD our God for ever and ever.
verse	33	4	6	In that day, saith the LORD, will I assemble her that halteth, and I will gather her that is driven out, and her that I have afflicted;
verse	33	4	7	And I will make her that halted a remnant, and her that was cast far off a strong nation: and the LORD shall reign over them in mount Zion from henceforth, even for ever.
verse	33	4	8	And thou, O tower of the flock, the strong hold of the daughter of Zion, unto thee shall it come, even the first dominion; the kingdom shall come to the daughter of Jerusalem.
verse	33	4	9	@@Now why dost thou cry out aloud? @9is there@7 no king in thee? is thy counsellor perished? for pangs have taken thee as a woman in travail.
verse	33	4	10	@@Be in pain, and labour to bring forth, O daughter of Zion, like a woman in travail: for now shalt thou go forth out of the city, and thou shalt dwell in the field, and thou shalt go @9even@7 to Babylon; there shalt thou be delivered; there the LORD shall redeem thee from the hand of thine enemies.
verse	33	4	11	Now also many nations are gathered against thee, that say, Let her be defiled, and let our eye look upon Zion.
verse	33	4	12	But they know not the thoughts of the LORD, neither understand they his counsel: for he shall gather them as the sheaves into the floor.
verse	33	4	13	Arise and thresh, O daughter of Zion: for I will make thine horn iron, and I will make thy hoofs brass: and thou shalt beat in pieces many people: and I will consecrate their gain unto the LORD, and their substance unto the Lord of the whole earth.
verse	33	5	1	Now gather thyself in troops, O daughter of troops: he hath laid siege against us: they shall smite the judge of Israel with a rod upon the cheek.
verse	33	5	2	@@But thou, Bethlehem Ephratah, @9though@7 thou be little among the thousands of Judah, @9yet@7 out of thee shall he come forth unto me @9that is@7 to be ruler in Israel; whose goings forth @9have been@7 from of old, from everlasting.
verse	33	5	3	@@Therefore will he give them up, until the time @9that@7 she which travaileth hath brought forth: then the remnant of his brethren shall return unto the children of Israel.
verse	33	5	4	And he shall stand and feed in the strength of the LORD, in the majesty of the name of the LORD his God; and they shall abide: for now shall he be great unto the ends of the earth.
verse	33	5	5	@@And this @9man@7 shall be the peace, when the Assyrian shall come into our land: and when he shall tread in our palaces, then shall we raise against him seven shepherds, and eight principal men.
verse	33	5	6	@@And they shall waste the land of Assyria with the sword, and the land of Nimrod in the entrances thereof: thus shall he deliver @9us@7 from the Assyrian, when he cometh into our land, and when he treadeth within our borders.
verse	33	5	7	And the remnant of Jacob shall be in the midst of many people as a dew from the LORD, as the showers upon the grass, that tarrieth not for man, nor waiteth for the sons of men.
verse	33	5	8	And the remnant of Jacob shall be among the Gentiles in the midst of many people as a lion among the beasts of the forest, as a young lion among the flocks of sheep: who, if he go through, both treadeth down, and teareth in pieces, and none can deliver.
verse	33	5	9	Thine hand shall be lifted up upon thine adversaries, and all thine enemies shall be cut off.
verse	33	5	10	And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD, that I will cut off thy horses out of the midst of thee, and I will destroy thy chariots:
verse	33	5	11	And I will cut off the cities of thy land, and throw down all thy strong holds:
verse	33	5	12	@@And I will cut off witchcrafts out of thine hand; and thou shalt have no @9more@7 soothsayers:
verse	33	5	13	Thy graven images also will I cut off, and thy standing images out of the midst of thee; and thou shalt no more worship the work of thine hands.
verse	33	5	14	And I will pluck up thy groves out of the midst of thee: so will I destroy thy cities.
verse	33	5	15	And I will execute vengeance in anger and fury upon the heathen, such as they have not heard.
verse	33	6	1	Hear ye now what the LORD saith; Arise, contend thou before the mountains, and let the hills hear thy voice.
verse	33	6	2	Hear ye, O mountains, the LORD'S controversy, and ye strong foundations of the earth: for the LORD hath a controversy with his people, and he will plead with Israel.
verse	33	6	3	O my people, what have I done unto thee? and wherein have I wearied thee? testify against me.
verse	33	6	4	For I brought thee up out of the land of Egypt, and redeemed thee out of the house of servants; and I sent before thee Moses, Aaron, and Miriam.
verse	33	6	5	O my people, remember now what Balak king of Moab consulted, and what Balaam the son of Beor answered him from Shittim unto Gilgal; that ye may know the righteousness of the LORD.
verse	33	6	6	@@Wherewith shall I come before the LORD, @9and@7 bow myself before the high God? shall I come before him with burnt offerings, with calves of a year old?
verse	33	6	7	@@Will the LORD be pleased with thousands of rams, @9or@7 with ten thousands of rivers of oil? shall I give my firstborn @9for@7 my transgression, the fruit of my body @9for@7 the sin of my soul?
verse	33	6	8	@@He hath shewed thee, O man, what @9is@7 good; and what doth the LORD require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?
verse	33	6	9	@@The LORD'S voice crieth unto the city, and @9the man of@7 wisdom shall see thy name: hear ye the rod, and who hath appointed it.
verse	33	6	10	@@Are there yet the treasures of wickedness in the house of the wicked, and the scant measure @9that is@7 abominable?
verse	33	6	11	@@Shall I count @9them@7 pure with the wicked balances, and with the bag of deceitful weights?
verse	33	6	12	@@For the rich men thereof are full of violence, and the inhabitants thereof have spoken lies, and their tongue @9is@7 deceitful in their mouth.
verse	33	6	13	@@Therefore also will I make @9thee@7 sick in smiting thee, in making @9thee@7 desolate because of thy sins.
verse	33	6	14	@@Thou shalt eat, but not be satisfied; and thy casting down @9shall be@7 in the midst of thee; and thou shalt take hold, but shalt not deliver; and @9that@7 which thou deliverest will I give up to the sword.
verse	33	6	15	Thou shalt sow, but thou shalt not reap; thou shalt tread the olives, but thou shalt not anoint thee with oil; and sweet wine, but shalt not drink wine.
verse	33	6	16	For the statutes of Omri are kept, and all the works of the house of Ahab, and ye walk in their counsels; that I should make thee a desolation, and the inhabitants thereof an hissing: therefore ye shall bear the reproach of my people.
verse	33	7	1	@@Woe is me! for I am as when they have gathered the summer fruits, as the grapegleanings of the vintage: @9there is@7 no cluster to eat: my soul desired the firstripe fruit.
verse	33	7	2	@@The good @9man@7 is perished out of the earth: and @9there is@7 none upright among men: they all lie in wait for blood; they hunt every man his brother with a net.
verse	33	7	3	@@That they may do evil with both hands earnestly, the prince asketh, and the judge @9asketh@7 for a reward; and the great @9man,@7 he uttereth his mischievous desire: so they wrap it up.
verse	33	7	4	@@The best of them @9is@7 as a brier: the most upright @9is sharper@7 than a thorn hedge: the day of thy watchmen @9and@7 thy visitation cometh; now shall be their perplexity.
verse	33	7	5	Trust ye not in a friend, put ye not confidence in a guide: keep the doors of thy mouth from her that lieth in thy bosom.
verse	33	7	6	@@For the son dishonoureth the father, the daughter riseth up against her mother, the daughter in law against her mother in law; a man's enemies @9are@7 the men of his own house.
verse	33	7	7	Therefore I will look unto the LORD; I will wait for the God of my salvation: my God will hear me.
verse	33	7	8	@@Rejoice not against me, O mine enemy: when I fall, I shall arise; when I sit in darkness, the LORD @9shall be@7 a light unto me.
verse	33	7	9	@@I will bear the indignation of the LORD, because I have sinned against him, until he plead my cause, and execute judgment for me: he will bring me forth to the light, @9and@7 I shall behold his righteousness.
verse	33	7	10	@@Then @9she that is@7 mine enemy shall see @9it,@7 and shame shall cover her which said unto me, Where is the LORD thy God? mine eyes shall behold her: now shall she be trodden down as the mire of the streets.
verse	33	7	11	@@@9In@7 the day that thy walls are to be built, @9in@7 that day shall the decree be far removed.
verse	33	7	12	@@@9In@7 that day @9also@7 he shall come even to thee from Assyria, and @9from@7 the fortified cities, and from the fortress even to the river, and from sea to sea, and @9from@7 mountain to mountain.
verse	33	7	13	Notwithstanding the land shall be desolate because of them that dwell therein, for the fruit of their doings.
verse	33	7	14	@@Feed thy people with thy rod, the flock of thine heritage, which dwell solitarily @9in@7 the wood, in the midst of Carmel: let them feed @9in@7 Bashan and Gilead, as in the days of old.
verse	33	7	15	@@According to the days of thy coming out of the land of Egypt will I shew unto him marvellous @9things.@7
verse	33	7	16	@@The nations shall see and be confounded at all their might: they shall lay @9their@7 hand upon @9their@7 mouth, their ears shall be deaf.
verse	33	7	17	They shall lick the dust like a serpent, they shall move out of their holes like worms of the earth: they shall be afraid of the LORD our God, and shall fear because of thee.
verse	33	7	18	@@Who @9is@7 a God like unto thee, that pardoneth iniquity, and passeth by the transgression of the remnant of his heritage? he retaineth not his anger for ever, because he delighteth @9in@7 mercy.
verse	33	7	19	He will turn again, he will have compassion upon us; he will subdue our iniquities; and thou wilt cast all their sins into the depths of the sea.
verse	33	7	20	@@Thou wilt perform the truth to Jacob, @9and@7 the mercy to Abraham, which thou hast sworn unto our fathers from the days of old.
verse	34	1	1	The burden of Nineveh. The book of the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite.
verse	34	1	2	@@God @9is@7 jealous, and the LORD revengeth; the LORD revengeth, and @9is@7 furious; the LORD will take vengeance on his adversaries, and he reserveth @9wrath@7 for his enemies.
verse	34	1	3	@@The LORD @9is@7 slow to anger, and great in power, and will not at all acquit @9the wicked:@7 the LORD hath his way in the whirlwind and in the storm, and the clouds @9are@7 the dust of his feet.
verse	34	1	4	He rebuketh the sea, and maketh it dry, and drieth up all the rivers: Bashan languisheth, and Carmel, and the flower of Lebanon languisheth.
verse	34	1	5	The mountains quake at him, and the hills melt, and the earth is burned at his presence, yea, the world, and all that dwell therein.
verse	34	1	6	Who can stand before his indignation? and who can abide in the fierceness of his anger? his fury is poured out like fire, and the rocks are thrown down by him.
verse	34	1	7	@@The LORD @9is@7 good, a strong hold in the day of trouble; and he knoweth them that trust in him.
verse	34	1	8	But with an overrunning flood he will make an utter end of the place thereof, and darkness shall pursue his enemies.
verse	34	1	9	What do ye imagine against the LORD? he will make an utter end: affliction shall not rise up the second time.
verse	34	1	10	@@For while @9they be@7 folden together @9as@7 thorns, and while they are drunken @9as@7 drunkards, they shall be devoured as stubble fully dry.
verse	34	1	11	@@There is @9one@7 come out of thee, that imagineth evil against the LORD, a wicked counsellor.
verse	34	1	12	@@Thus saith the LORD: Though @9they be@7 quiet, and likewise many, yet thus shall they be cut down, when he shall pass through. Though I have afflicted thee, I will afflict thee no more.
verse	34	1	13	For now will I break his yoke from off thee, and will burst thy bonds in sunder.
verse	34	1	14	@@And the LORD hath given a commandment concerning thee, @9that@7 no more of thy name be sown: out of the house of thy gods will I cut off the graven image and the molten image: I will make thy grave; for thou art vile.
verse	34	1	15	Behold upon the mountains the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace! O Judah, keep thy solemn feasts, perform thy vows: for the wicked shall no more pass through thee; he is utterly cut off.
verse	34	2	1	@@He that dasheth in pieces is come up before thy face: keep the munition, watch the way, make @9thy@7 loins strong, fortify @9thy@7 power mightily.
verse	34	2	2	For the LORD hath turned away the excellency of Jacob, as the excellency of Israel: for the emptiers have emptied them out, and marred their vine branches.
verse	34	2	3	@@The shield of his mighty men is made red, the valiant men @9are@7 in scarlet: the chariots @9shall be@7 with flaming torches in the day of his preparation, and the fir trees shall be terribly shaken.
verse	34	2	4	The chariots shall rage in the streets, they shall justle one against another in the broad ways: they shall seem like torches, they shall run like the lightnings.
verse	34	2	5	He shall recount his worthies: they shall stumble in their walk; they shall make haste to the wall thereof, and the defence shall be prepared.
verse	34	2	6	The gates of the rivers shall be opened, and the palace shall be dissolved.
verse	34	2	7	@@And Huzzab shall be led away captive, she shall be brought up, and her maids shall lead @9her@7 as with the voice of doves, tabering upon their breasts.
verse	34	2	8	@@But Nineveh is of old like a pool of water: yet they shall flee away. Stand, stand, @9shall they cry;@7 but none shall look back.
verse	34	2	9	@@Take ye the spoil of silver, take the spoil of gold: for @9there is@7 none end of the store @9and@7 glory out of all the pleasant furniture.
verse	34	2	10	@@She is empty, and void, and waste: and the heart melteth, and the knees smite together, and much pain @9is@7 in all loins, and the faces of them all gather blackness.
verse	34	2	11	@@Where @9is@7 the dwelling of the lions, and the feeding place of the young lions, where the lion, @9even@7 the old lion, walked, @9and@7 the lion's whelp, and none made @9them@7 afraid?
verse	34	2	12	The lion did tear in pieces enough for his whelps, and strangled for his lionesses, and filled his holes with prey, and his dens with ravin.
verse	34	2	13	@@Behold, I @9am@7 against thee, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will burn her chariots in the smoke, and the sword shall devour thy young lions: and I will cut off thy prey from the earth, and the voice of thy messengers shall no more be heard.
verse	34	3	1	@@Woe to the bloody city! it is all full of lies @9and@7 robbery; the prey departeth not;
verse	34	3	2	The noise of a whip, and the noise of the rattling of the wheels, and of the pransing horses, and of the jumping chariots.
verse	34	3	3	@@The horseman lifteth up both the bright sword and the glittering spear: and @9there is@7 a multitude of slain, and a great number of carcases; and @9there is@7 none end of @9their@7 corpses; they stumble upon their corpses:
verse	34	3	4	Because of the multitude of the whoredoms of the wellfavoured harlot, the mistress of witchcrafts, that selleth nations through her whoredoms, and families through her witchcrafts.
verse	34	3	5	@@Behold, I @9am@7 against thee, saith the LORD of hosts; and I will discover thy skirts upon thy face, and I will shew the nations thy nakedness, and the kingdoms thy shame.
verse	34	3	6	And I will cast abominable filth upon thee, and make thee vile, and will set thee as a gazingstock.
verse	34	3	7	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 all they that look upon thee shall flee from thee, and say, Nineveh is laid waste: who will bemoan her? whence shall I seek comforters for thee?
verse	34	3	8	@@Art thou better than populous No, that was situate among the rivers, @9that had@7 the waters round about it, whose rampart @9was@7 the sea, @9and@7 her wall @9was@7 from the sea?
verse	34	3	9	@@Ethiopia and Egypt @9were@7 her strength, and @9it was@7 infinite; Put and Lubim were thy helpers.
verse	34	3	10	@@Yet @9was@7 she carried away, she went into captivity: her young children also were dashed in pieces at the top of all the streets: and they cast lots for her honourable men, and all her great men were bound in chains.
verse	34	3	11	Thou also shalt be drunken: thou shalt be hid, thou also shalt seek strength because of the enemy.
verse	34	3	12	@@All thy strong holds @9shall be like@7 fig trees with the firstripe figs: if they be shaken, they shall even fall into the mouth of the eater.
verse	34	3	13	@@Behold, thy people in the midst of thee @9are@7 women: the gates of thy land shall be set wide open unto thine enemies: the fire shall devour thy bars.
verse	34	3	14	Draw thee waters for the siege, fortify thy strong holds: go into clay, and tread the morter, make strong the brickkiln.
verse	34	3	15	There shall the fire devour thee; the sword shall cut thee off, it shall eat thee up like the cankerworm: make thyself many as the cankerworm, make thyself many as the locusts.
verse	34	3	16	Thou hast multiplied thy merchants above the stars of heaven: the cankerworm spoileth, and fleeth away.
verse	34	3	17	@@Thy crowned @9are@7 as the locusts, and thy captains as the great grasshoppers, which camp in the hedges in the cold day, @9but@7 when the sun ariseth they flee away, and their place is not known where they @9are. @7
verse	34	3	18	@@Thy shepherds slumber, O king of Assyria: thy nobles shall dwell @9in the dust:@7 thy people is scattered upon the mountains, and no man gathereth @9them. @7
verse	34	3	19	@@@9There is@7 no healing of thy bruise; thy wound is grievous: all that hear the bruit of thee shall clap the hands over thee: for upon whom hath not thy wickedness passed continually?
verse	35	1	1	The burden which Habakkuk the prophet did see.
verse	35	1	2	@@O LORD, how long shall I cry, and thou wilt not hear! @9even@7 cry out unto thee @9of@7 violence, and thou wilt not save!
verse	35	1	3	@@Why dost thou shew me iniquity, and cause @9me@7 to behold grievance? for spoiling and violence @9are@7 before me: and there are @9that@7 raise up strife and contention.
verse	35	1	4	Therefore the law is slacked, and judgment doth never go forth: for the wicked doth compass about the righteous; therefore wrong judgment proceedeth.
verse	35	1	5	@@Behold ye among the heathen, and regard, and wonder marvellously: for @9I@7 will work a work in your days, @9which@7 ye will not believe, though it be told @9you. @7
verse	35	1	6	@@For, lo, I raise up the Chaldeans, @9that@7 bitter and hasty nation, which shall march through the breadth of the land, to possess the dwellingplaces @9that are@7 not theirs.
verse	35	1	7	@@They @9are@7 terrible and dreadful: their judgment and their dignity shall proceed of themselves.
verse	35	1	8	@@Their horses also are swifter than the leopards, and are more fierce than the evening wolves: and their horsemen shall spread themselves, and their horsemen shall come from far; they shall fly as the eagle @9that@7 hasteth to eat.
verse	35	1	9	@@They shall come all for violence: their faces shall sup up @9as@7 the east wind, and they shall gather the captivity as the sand.
verse	35	1	10	And they shall scoff at the kings, and the princes shall be a scorn unto them: they shall deride every strong hold; for they shall heap dust, and take it.
verse	35	1	11	@@Then shall @9his@7 mind change, and he shall pass over, and offend, @9imputing@7 this his power unto his god.
verse	35	1	12	@@@9Art@7 thou not from everlasting, O LORD my God, mine Holy One? we shall not die. O LORD, thou hast ordained them for judgment; and, O mighty God, thou hast established them for correction.
verse	35	1	13	@@@9Thou art@7 of purer eyes than to behold evil, and canst not look on iniquity: wherefore lookest thou upon them that deal treacherously, @9and@7 holdest thy tongue when the wicked devoureth @9the man that is@7 more righteous than he?
verse	35	1	14	@@And makest men as the fishes of the sea, as the creeping things, @9that have@7 no ruler over them?
verse	35	1	15	They take up all of them with the angle, they catch them in their net, and gather them in their drag: therefore they rejoice and are glad.
verse	35	1	16	@@Therefore they sacrifice unto their net, and burn incense unto their drag; because by them their portion @9is@7 fat, and their meat plenteous.
verse	35	1	17	Shall they therefore empty their net, and not spare continually to slay the nations?
verse	35	2	1	I will stand upon my watch, and set me upon the tower, and will watch to see what he will say unto me, and what I shall answer when I am reproved.
verse	35	2	2	@@And the LORD answered me, and said, Write the vision, and make @9it@7 plain upon tables, that he may run that readeth it.
verse	35	2	3	@@For the vision @9is@7 yet for an appointed time, but at the end it shall speak, and not lie: though it tarry, wait for it; because it will surely come, it will not tarry.
verse	35	2	4	@@Behold, his soul @9which@7 is lifted up is not upright in him: but the just shall live by his faith.
verse	35	2	5	@@Yea also, because he transgresseth by wine, @9he is@7 a proud man, neither keepeth at home, who enlargeth his desire as hell, and @9is@7 as death, and cannot be satisfied, but gathereth unto him all nations, and heapeth unto him all people:
verse	35	2	6	@@Shall not all these take up a parable against him, and a taunting proverb against him, and say, Woe to him that increaseth @9that which is@7 not his! how long? and to him that ladeth himself with thick clay!
verse	35	2	7	Shall they not rise up suddenly that shall bite thee, and awake that shall vex thee, and thou shalt be for booties unto them?
verse	35	2	8	@@Because thou hast spoiled many nations, all the remnant of the people shall spoil thee; because of men's blood, and @9for@7 the violence of the land, of the city, and of all that dwell therein.
verse	35	2	9	Woe to him that coveteth an evil covetousness to his house, that he may set his nest on high, that he may be delivered from the power of evil!
verse	35	2	10	@@Thou hast consulted shame to thy house by cutting off many people, and hast sinned @9against@7 thy soul.
verse	35	2	11	For the stone shall cry out of the wall, and the beam out of the timber shall answer it.
verse	35	2	12	Woe to him that buildeth a town with blood, and stablisheth a city by iniquity!
verse	35	2	13	@@Behold, @9is it@7 not of the LORD of hosts that the people shall labour in the very fire, and the people shall weary themselves for very vanity?
verse	35	2	14	For the earth shall be filled with the knowledge of the glory of the LORD, as the waters cover the sea.
verse	35	2	15	@@Woe unto him that giveth his neighbour drink, that puttest thy bottle to @9him,@7 and makest @9him@7 drunken also, that thou mayest look on their nakedness!
verse	35	2	16	@@Thou art filled with shame for glory: drink thou also, and let thy foreskin be uncovered: the cup of the LORD'S right hand shall be turned unto thee, and shameful spewing @9shall be@7 on thy glory.
verse	35	2	17	@@For the violence of Lebanon shall cover thee, and the spoil of beasts, @9which@7 made them afraid, because of men's blood, and for the violence of the land, of the city, and of all that dwell therein.
verse	35	2	18	What profiteth the graven image that the maker thereof hath graven it; the molten image, and a teacher of lies, that the maker of his work trusteth therein, to make dumb idols?
verse	35	2	19	@@Woe unto him that saith to the wood, Awake; to the dumb stone, Arise, it shall teach! Behold, it @9is@7 laid over with gold and silver, and @9there is@7 no breath at all in the midst of it.
verse	35	2	20	@@But the LORD @9is@7 in his holy temple: let all the earth keep silence before him.
verse	35	3	1	A prayer of Habakkuk the prophet upon Shigionoth.
verse	35	3	2	@@O LORD, I have heard thy speech, @9and@7 was afraid: O LORD, revive thy work in the midst of the years, in the midst of the years make known; in wrath remember mercy.
verse	35	3	3	God came from Teman, and the Holy One from mount Paran. Selah. His glory covered the heavens, and the earth was full of his praise.
verse	35	3	4	@@And @9his@7 brightness was as the light; he had horns @9coming@7 out of his hand: and there @9was@7 the hiding of his power.
verse	35	3	5	Before him went the pestilence, and burning coals went forth at his feet.
verse	35	3	6	@@He stood, and measured the earth: he beheld, and drove asunder the nations; and the everlasting mountains were scattered, the perpetual hills did bow: his ways @9are@7 everlasting.
verse	35	3	7	@@I saw the tents of Cushan in affliction: @9and@7 the curtains of the land of Midian did tremble.
verse	35	3	8	@@Was the LORD displeased against the rivers? @9was@7 thine anger against the rivers? @9was@7 thy wrath against the sea, that thou didst ride upon thine horses @9and@7 thy chariots of salvation?
verse	35	3	9	@@Thy bow was made quite naked, @9according@7 to the oaths of the tribes, @9even thy@7 word. Selah. Thou didst cleave the earth with rivers.
verse	35	3	10	@@The mountains saw thee, @9and@7 they trembled: the overflowing of the water passed by: the deep uttered his voice, @9and@7 lifted up his hands on high.
verse	35	3	11	@@The sun @9and@7 moon stood still in their habitation: at the light of thine arrows they went, @9and@7 at the shining of thy glittering spear.
verse	35	3	12	Thou didst march through the land in indignation, thou didst thresh the heathen in anger.
verse	35	3	13	@@Thou wentest forth for the salvation of thy people, @9even@7 for salvation with thine anointed; thou woundedst the head out of the house of the wicked, by discovering the foundation unto the neck. Selah.
verse	35	3	14	@@Thou didst strike through with his staves the head of his villages: they came out as a whirlwind to scatter me: their rejoicing @9was@7 as to devour the poor secretly.
verse	35	3	15	@@Thou didst walk through the sea with thine horses, @9through@7 the heap of great waters.
verse	35	3	16	When I heard, my belly trembled; my lips quivered at the voice: rottenness entered into my bones, and I trembled in myself, that I might rest in the day of trouble: when he cometh up unto the people, he will invade them with his troops.
verse	35	3	17	@@Although the fig tree shall not blossom, neither @9shall@7 fruit @9be@7 in the vines; the labour of the olive shall fail, and the fields shall yield no meat; the flock shall be cut off from the fold, and @9there shall be@7 no herd in the stalls:
verse	35	3	18	Yet I will rejoice in the LORD, I will joy in the God of my salvation.
verse	35	3	19	@@The LORD God @9is@7 my strength, and he will make my feet like hinds' @9feet,@7 and he will make me to walk upon mine high places. To the chief singer on my stringed instruments.
verse	36	1	1	The word of the LORD which came unto Zephaniah the son of Cushi, the son of Gedaliah, the son of Amariah, the son of Hizkiah, in the days of Josiah the son of Amon, king of Judah.
verse	36	1	2	@@I will utterly consume all @9things@7 from off the land, saith the LORD.
verse	36	1	3	I will consume man and beast; I will consume the fowls of the heaven, and the fishes of the sea, and the stumblingblocks with the wicked; and I will cut off man from off the land, saith the LORD.
verse	36	1	4	@@I will also stretch out mine hand upon Judah, and upon all the inhabitants of Jerusalem; and I will cut off the remnant of Baal from this place, @9and@7 the name of the Chemarims with the priests;
verse	36	1	5	@@And them that worship the host of heaven upon the housetops; and them that worship @9and@7 that swear by the LORD, and that swear by Malcham;
verse	36	1	6	@@And them that are turned back from the LORD; and @9those@7 that have not sought the LORD, nor enquired for him.
verse	36	1	7	@@Hold thy peace at the presence of the Lord GOD: for the day of the LORD @9is@7 at hand: for the LORD hath prepared a sacrifice, he hath bid his guests.
verse	36	1	8	And it shall come to pass in the day of the LORD'S sacrifice, that I will punish the princes, and the king's children, and all such as are clothed with strange apparel.
verse	36	1	9	In the same day also will I punish all those that leap on the threshold, which fill their masters' houses with violence and deceit.
verse	36	1	10	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD, @9that there shall be@7 the noise of a cry from the fish gate, and an howling from the second, and a great crashing from the hills.
verse	36	1	11	Howl, ye inhabitants of Maktesh, for all the merchant people are cut down; all they that bear silver are cut off.
verse	36	1	12	@@And it shall come to pass at that time, @9that@7 I will search Jerusalem with candles, and punish the men that are settled on their lees: that say in their heart, The LORD will not do good, neither will he do evil.
verse	36	1	13	@@Therefore their goods shall become a booty, and their houses a desolation: they shall also build houses, but not inhabit @9them;@7 and they shall plant vineyards, but not drink the wine thereof.
verse	36	1	14	@@The great day of the LORD @9is@7 near, @9it is@7 near, and hasteth greatly, @9even@7 the voice of the day of the LORD: the mighty man shall cry there bitterly.
verse	36	1	15	@@That day @9is@7 a day of wrath, a day of trouble and distress, a day of wasteness and desolation, a day of darkness and gloominess, a day of clouds and thick darkness,
verse	36	1	16	A day of the trumpet and alarm against the fenced cities, and against the high towers.
verse	36	1	17	And I will bring distress upon men, that they shall walk like blind men, because they have sinned against the LORD: and their blood shall be poured out as dust, and their flesh as the dung.
verse	36	1	18	Neither their silver nor their gold shall be able to deliver them in the day of the LORD'S wrath; but the whole land shall be devoured by the fire of his jealousy: for he shall make even a speedy riddance of all them that dwell in the land.
verse	36	2	1	Gather yourselves together, yea, gather together, O nation not desired;
verse	36	2	2	@@Before the decree bring forth, @9before@7 the day pass as the chaff, before the fierce anger of the LORD come upon you, before the day of the LORD'S anger come upon you.
verse	36	2	3	Seek ye the LORD, all ye meek of the earth, which have wrought his judgment; seek righteousness, seek meekness: it may be ye shall be hid in the day of the LORD'S anger.
verse	36	2	4	For Gaza shall be forsaken, and Ashkelon a desolation: they shall drive out Ashdod at the noonday, and Ekron shall be rooted up.
verse	36	2	5	@@Woe unto the inhabitants of the sea coast, the nation of the Cherethites! the word of the LORD @9is@7 against you; O Canaan, the land of the Philistines, I will even destroy thee, that there shall be no inhabitant.
verse	36	2	6	@@And the sea coast shall be dwellings @9and@7 cottages for shepherds, and folds for flocks.
verse	36	2	7	And the coast shall be for the remnant of the house of Judah; they shall feed thereupon: in the houses of Ashkelon shall they lie down in the evening: for the LORD their God shall visit them, and turn away their captivity.
verse	36	2	8	@@I have heard the reproach of Moab, and the revilings of the children of Ammon, whereby they have reproached my people, and magnified @9themselves@7 against their border.
verse	36	2	9	@@Therefore @9as@7 I live, saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, Surely Moab shall be as Sodom, and the children of Ammon as Gomorrah, @9even@7 the breeding of nettles, and saltpits, and a perpetual desolation: the residue of my people shall spoil them, and the remnant of my people shall possess them.
verse	36	2	10	@@This shall they have for their pride, because they have reproached and magnified @9themselves@7 against the people of the LORD of hosts.
verse	36	2	11	@@The LORD @9will be@7 terrible unto them: for he will famish all the gods of the earth; and @9men@7 shall worship him, every one from his place, @9even@7 all the isles of the heathen.
verse	36	2	12	@@Ye Ethiopians also, ye @9shall be@7 slain by my sword.
verse	36	2	13	@@And he will stretch out his hand against the north, and destroy Assyria; and will make Nineveh a desolation, @9and@7 dry like a wilderness.
verse	36	2	14	@@And flocks shall lie down in the midst of her, all the beasts of the nations: both the cormorant and the bittern shall lodge in the upper lintels of it; @9their@7 voice shall sing in the windows; desolation @9shall be@7 in the thresholds: for he shall uncover the cedar work.
verse	36	2	15	@@This @9is@7 the rejoicing city that dwelt carelessly, that said in her heart, I @9am,@7 and @9there is@7 none beside me: how is she become a desolation, a place for beasts to lie down in! every one that passeth by her shall hiss, @9and@7 wag his hand.
verse	36	3	1	Woe to her that is filthy and polluted, to the oppressing city!
verse	36	3	2	She obeyed not the voice; she received not correction; she trusted not in the LORD; she drew not near to her God.
verse	36	3	3	@@Her princes within her @9are@7 roaring lions; her judges @9are@7 evening wolves; they gnaw not the bones till the morrow.
verse	36	3	4	@@Her prophets @9are@7 light @9and@7 treacherous persons: her priests have polluted the sanctuary, they have done violence to the law.
verse	36	3	5	@@The just LORD @9is@7 in the midst thereof; he will not do iniquity: every morning doth he bring his judgment to light, he faileth not; but the unjust knoweth no shame.
verse	36	3	6	I have cut off the nations: their towers are desolate; I made their streets waste, that none passeth by: their cities are destroyed, so that there is no man, that there is none inhabitant.
verse	36	3	7	@@I said, Surely thou wilt fear me, thou wilt receive instruction; so their dwelling should not be cut off, howsoever I punished them: but they rose early, @9and@7 corrupted all their doings.
verse	36	3	8	@@Therefore wait ye upon me, saith the LORD, until the day that I rise up to the prey: for my determination @9is@7 to gather the nations, that I may assemble the kingdoms, to pour upon them mine indignation, @9even@7 all my fierce anger: for all the earth shall be devoured with the fire of my jealousy.
verse	36	3	9	For then will I turn to the people a pure language, that they may all call upon the name of the LORD, to serve him with one consent.
verse	36	3	10	@@From beyond the rivers of Ethiopia my suppliants, @9even@7 the daughter of my dispersed, shall bring mine offering.
verse	36	3	11	In that day shalt thou not be ashamed for all thy doings, wherein thou hast transgressed against me: for then I will take away out of the midst of thee them that rejoice in thy pride, and thou shalt no more be haughty because of my holy mountain.
verse	36	3	12	I will also leave in the midst of thee an afflicted and poor people, and they shall trust in the name of the LORD.
verse	36	3	13	@@The remnant of Israel shall not do iniquity, nor speak lies; neither shall a deceitful tongue be found in their mouth: for they shall feed and lie down, and none shall make @9them@7 afraid.
verse	36	3	14	Sing, O daughter of Zion; shout, O Israel; be glad and rejoice with all the heart, O daughter of Jerusalem.
verse	36	3	15	@@The LORD hath taken away thy judgments, he hath cast out thine enemy: the king of Israel, @9even@7 the LORD, @9is@7 in the midst of thee: thou shalt not see evil any more.
verse	36	3	16	@@In that day it shall be said to Jerusalem, Fear thou not: @9and to@7 Zion, Let not thine hands be slack.
verse	36	3	17	@@The LORD thy God in the midst of thee @9is@7 mighty; he will save, he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love, he will joy over thee with singing.
verse	36	3	18	@@I will gather @9them that are@7 sorrowful for the solemn assembly, @9who@7 are of thee, @9to whom@7 the reproach of it @9was@7 a burden.
verse	36	3	19	Behold, at that time I will undo all that afflict thee: and I will save her that halteth, and gather her that was driven out; and I will get them praise and fame in every land where they have been put to shame.
verse	36	3	20	@@At that time will I bring you @9again,@7 even in the time that I gather you: for I will make you a name and a praise among all people of the earth, when I turn back your captivity before your eyes, saith the LORD.
verse	37	1	1	In the second year of Darius the king, in the sixth month, in the first day of the month, came the word of the LORD by Haggai the prophet unto Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest, saying,
verse	37	1	2	Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, saying, This people say, The time is not come, the time that the LORD'S house should be built.
verse	37	1	3	Then came the word of the LORD by Haggai the prophet, saying,
verse	37	1	4	@@@9Is it@7 time for you, O ye, to dwell in your cieled houses, and this house @9lie@7 waste?
verse	37	1	5	Now therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts; Consider your ways.
verse	37	1	6	@@Ye have sown much, and bring in little; ye eat, but ye have not enough; ye drink, but ye are not filled with drink; ye clothe you, but there is none warm; and he that earneth wages earneth wages @9to put it@7 into a bag with holes.
verse	37	1	7	Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Consider your ways.
verse	37	1	8	Go up to the mountain, and bring wood, and build the house; and I will take pleasure in it, and I will be glorified, saith the LORD.
verse	37	1	9	@@Ye looked for much, and, lo, @9it came@7 to little; and when ye brought @9it@7 home, I did blow upon it. Why? saith the LORD of hosts. Because of mine house that @9is@7 waste, and ye run every man unto his own house.
verse	37	1	10	@@Therefore the heaven over you is stayed from dew, and the earth is stayed @9from@7 her fruit.
verse	37	1	11	@@And I called for a drought upon the land, and upon the mountains, and upon the corn, and upon the new wine, and upon the oil, and upon @9that@7 which the ground bringeth forth, and upon men, and upon cattle, and upon all the labour of the hands.
verse	37	1	12	Then Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest, with all the remnant of the people, obeyed the voice of the LORD their God, and the words of Haggai the prophet, as the LORD their God had sent him, and the people did fear before the LORD.
verse	37	1	13	@@Then spake Haggai the LORD'S messenger in the LORD'S message unto the people, saying, I @9am@7 with you, saith the LORD.
verse	37	1	14	And the LORD stirred up the spirit of Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and the spirit of Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest, and the spirit of all the remnant of the people; and they came and did work in the house of the LORD of hosts, their God,
verse	37	1	15	In the four and twentieth day of the sixth month, in the second year of Darius the king.
verse	37	2	1	@@In the seventh @9month,@7 in the one and twentieth @9day@7 of the month, came the word of the LORD by the prophet Haggai, saying,
verse	37	2	2	Speak now to Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest, and to the residue of the people, saying,
verse	37	2	3	@@Who @9is@7 left among you that saw this house in her first glory? and how do ye see it now? @9is it@7 not in your eyes in comparison of it as nothing?
verse	37	2	4	@@Yet now be strong, O Zerubbabel, saith the LORD; and be strong, O Joshua, son of Josedech, the high priest; and be strong, all ye people of the land, saith the LORD, and work: for @9I am@7 with you, saith the LORD of hosts:
verse	37	2	5	@@@9According to@7 the word that I covenanted with you when ye came out of Egypt, so my spirit remaineth among you: fear ye not.
verse	37	2	6	@@For thus saith the LORD of hosts; Yet once, it @9is@7 a little while, and I will shake the heavens, and the earth, and the sea, and the dry @9land; @7
verse	37	2	7	And I will shake all nations, and the desire of all nations shall come: and I will fill this house with glory, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	37	2	8	@@The silver @9is@7 mine, and the gold @9is@7 mine, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	37	2	9	The glory of this latter house shall be greater than of the former, saith the LORD of hosts: and in this place will I give peace, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	37	2	10	@@In the four and twentieth @9day@7 of the ninth @9month,@7 in the second year of Darius, came the word of the LORD by Haggai the prophet, saying,
verse	37	2	11	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Ask now the priests @9concerning@7 the law, saying,
verse	37	2	12	If one bear holy flesh in the skirt of his garment, and with his skirt do touch bread, or pottage, or wine, or oil, or any meat, shall it be holy? And the priests answered and said, No.
verse	37	2	13	@@Then said Haggai, If @9one that is@7 unclean by a dead body touch any of these, shall it be unclean? And the priests answered and said, It shall be unclean.
verse	37	2	14	@@Then answered Haggai, and said, So @9is@7 this people, and so @9is@7 this nation before me, saith the LORD; and so @9is@7 every work of their hands; and that which they offer there @9is@7 unclean.
verse	37	2	15	And now, I pray you, consider from this day and upward, from before a stone was laid upon a stone in the temple of the LORD:
verse	37	2	16	@@Since those @9days@7 were, when @9one@7 came to an heap of twenty @9measures,@7 there were @9but@7 ten: when @9one@7 came to the pressfat for to draw out fifty @9vessels@7 out of the press, there were @9but@7 twenty.
verse	37	2	17	@@I smote you with blasting and with mildew and with hail in all the labours of your hands; yet ye @9turned@7 not to me, saith the LORD.
verse	37	2	18	@@Consider now from this day and upward, from the four and twentieth day of the ninth @9month, even@7 from the day that the foundation of the LORD'S temple was laid, consider @9it. @7
verse	37	2	19	@@Is the seed yet in the barn? yea, as yet the vine, and the fig tree, and the pomegranate, and the olive tree, hath not brought forth: from this day will I bless @9you.@7
verse	37	2	20	@@And again the word of the LORD came unto Haggai in the four and twentieth @9day@7 of the month, saying,
verse	37	2	21	Speak to Zerubbabel, governor of Judah, saying, I will shake the heavens and the earth;
verse	37	2	22	And I will overthrow the throne of kingdoms, and I will destroy the strength of the kingdoms of the heathen; and I will overthrow the chariots, and those that ride in them; and the horses and their riders shall come down, every one by the sword of his brother.
verse	37	2	23	In that day, saith the LORD of hosts, will I take thee, O Zerubbabel, my servant, the son of Shealtiel, saith the LORD, and will make thee as a signet: for I have chosen thee, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	38	1	1	In the eighth month, in the second year of Darius, came the word of the LORD unto Zechariah, the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo the prophet, saying,
verse	38	1	2	The LORD hath been sore displeased with your fathers.
verse	38	1	3	Therefore say thou unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye unto me, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will turn unto you, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	38	1	4	@@Be ye not as your fathers, unto whom the former prophets have cried, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye now from your evil ways, and @9from@7 your evil doings: but they did not hear, nor hearken unto me, saith the LORD.
verse	38	1	5	@@Your fathers, where @9are@7 they? and the prophets, do they live for ever?
verse	38	1	6	But my words and my statutes, which I commanded my servants the prophets, did they not take hold of your fathers? and they returned and said, Like as the LORD of hosts thought to do unto us, according to our ways, and according to our doings, so hath he dealt with us.
verse	38	1	7	@@Upon the four and twentieth day of the eleventh month, which @9is@7 the month Sebat, in the second year of Darius, came the word of the LORD unto Zechariah, the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo the prophet, saying,
verse	38	1	8	@@I saw by night, and behold a man riding upon a red horse, and he stood among the myrtle trees that @9were@7 in the bottom; and behind him @9were there@7 red horses, speckled, and white.
verse	38	1	9	@@Then said I, O my lord, what @9are@7 these? And the angel that talked with me said unto me, I will shew thee what these @9be. @7
verse	38	1	10	@@And the man that stood among the myrtle trees answered and said, These @9are they@7 whom the LORD hath sent to walk to and fro through the earth.
verse	38	1	11	And they answered the angel of the LORD that stood among the myrtle trees, and said, We have walked to and fro through the earth, and, behold, all the earth sitteth still, and is at rest.
verse	38	1	12	Then the angel of the LORD answered and said, O LORD of hosts, how long wilt thou not have mercy on Jerusalem and on the cities of Judah, against which thou hast had indignation these threescore and ten years?
verse	38	1	13	@@And the LORD answered the angel that talked with me @9with@7 good words @9and@7 comfortable words.
verse	38	1	14	So the angel that communed with me said unto me, Cry thou, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; I am jealous for Jerusalem and for Zion with a great jealousy.
verse	38	1	15	@@And I am very sore displeased with the heathen @9that are@7 at ease: for I was but a little displeased, and they helped forward the affliction.
verse	38	1	16	Therefore thus saith the LORD; I am returned to Jerusalem with mercies: my house shall be built in it, saith the LORD of hosts, and a line shall be stretched forth upon Jerusalem.
verse	38	1	17	Cry yet, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; My cities through prosperity shall yet be spread abroad; and the LORD shall yet comfort Zion, and shall yet choose Jerusalem.
verse	38	1	18	Then lifted I up mine eyes, and saw, and behold four horns.
verse	38	1	19	@@And I said unto the angel that talked with me, What @9be@7 these? And he answered me, These @9are@7 the horns which have scattered Judah, Israel, and Jerusalem.
verse	38	1	20	And the LORD shewed me four carpenters.
verse	38	1	21	@@Then said I, What come these to do? And he spake, saying, These @9are@7 the horns which have scattered Judah, so that no man did lift up his head: but these are come to fray them, to cast out the horns of the Gentiles, which lifted up @9their@7 horn over the land of Judah to scatter it.
verse	38	2	1	I lifted up mine eyes again, and looked, and behold a man with a measuring line in his hand.
verse	38	2	2	@@Then said I, Whither goest thou? And he said unto me, To measure Jerusalem, to see what @9is@7 the breadth thereof, and what @9is@7 the length thereof.
verse	38	2	3	And, behold, the angel that talked with me went forth, and another angel went out to meet him,
verse	38	2	4	@@And said unto him, Run, speak to this young man, saying, Jerusalem shall be inhabited @9as@7 towns without walls for the multitude of men and cattle therein:
verse	38	2	5	For I, saith the LORD, will be unto her a wall of fire round about, and will be the glory in the midst of her.
verse	38	2	6	@@Ho, ho, @9come forth,@7 and flee from the land of the north, saith the LORD: for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the heaven, saith the LORD.
verse	38	2	7	@@Deliver thyself, O Zion, that dwellest @9with@7 the daughter of Babylon.
verse	38	2	8	For thus saith the LORD of hosts; After the glory hath he sent me unto the nations which spoiled you: for he that toucheth you toucheth the apple of his eye.
verse	38	2	9	For, behold, I will shake mine hand upon them, and they shall be a spoil to their servants: and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me.
verse	38	2	10	Sing and rejoice, O daughter of Zion: for, lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee, saith the LORD.
verse	38	2	11	And many nations shall be joined to the LORD in that day, and shall be my people: and I will dwell in the midst of thee, and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto thee.
verse	38	2	12	And the LORD shall inherit Judah his portion in the holy land, and shall choose Jerusalem again.
verse	38	2	13	Be silent, O all flesh, before the LORD: for he is raised up out of his holy habitation.
verse	38	3	1	And he shewed me Joshua the high priest standing before the angel of the LORD, and Satan standing at his right hand to resist him.
verse	38	3	2	@@And the LORD said unto Satan, The LORD rebuke thee, O Satan; even the LORD that hath chosen Jerusalem rebuke thee: @9is@7 not this a brand plucked out of the fire?
verse	38	3	3	Now Joshua was clothed with filthy garments, and stood before the angel.
verse	38	3	4	And he answered and spake unto those that stood before him, saying, Take away the filthy garments from him. And unto him he said, Behold, I have caused thine iniquity to pass from thee, and I will clothe thee with change of raiment.
verse	38	3	5	And I said, Let them set a fair mitre upon his head. So they set a fair mitre upon his head, and clothed him with garments. And the angel of the LORD stood by.
verse	38	3	6	And the angel of the LORD protested unto Joshua, saying,
verse	38	3	7	Thus saith the LORD of hosts; If thou wilt walk in my ways, and if thou wilt keep my charge, then thou shalt also judge my house, and shalt also keep my courts, and I will give thee places to walk among these that stand by.
verse	38	3	8	@@Hear now, O Joshua the high priest, thou, and thy fellows that sit before thee: for they @9are@7 men wondered at: for, behold, I will bring forth my servant the BRANCH.
verse	38	3	9	@@For behold the stone that I have laid before Joshua; upon one stone @9shall be@7 seven eyes: behold, I will engrave the graving thereof, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will remove the iniquity of that land in one day.
verse	38	3	10	In that day, saith the LORD of hosts, shall ye call every man his neighbour under the vine and under the fig tree.
verse	38	4	1	And the angel that talked with me came again, and waked me, as a man that is wakened out of his sleep,
verse	38	4	2	@@And said unto me, What seest thou? And I said, I have looked, and behold a candlestick all @9of@7 gold, with a bowl upon the top of it, and his seven lamps thereon, and seven pipes to the seven lamps, which @9are@7 upon the top thereof:
verse	38	4	3	@@And two olive trees by it, one upon the right @9side@7 of the bowl, and the other upon the left @9side@7 thereof.
verse	38	4	4	@@So I answered and spake to the angel that talked with me, saying, What @9are@7 these, my lord?
verse	38	4	5	Then the angel that talked with me answered and said unto me, Knowest thou not what these be? And I said, No, my lord.
verse	38	4	6	@@Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This @9is@7 the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	38	4	7	@@Who @9art@7 thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel @9thou shalt become@7 a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone @9thereof with@7 shoutings, @9crying,@7 Grace, grace unto it.
verse	38	4	8	Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	38	4	9	The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it; and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you.
verse	38	4	10	@@For who hath despised the day of small things? for they shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbabel @9with@7 those seven; they @9are@7 the eyes of the LORD, which run to and fro through the whole earth.
verse	38	4	11	@@Then answered I, and said unto him, What @9are@7 these two olive trees upon the right @9side@7 of the candlestick and upon the left @9side@7 thereof?
verse	38	4	12	@@And I answered again, and said unto him, What @9be these@7 two olive branches which through the two golden pipes empty the golden @9oil@7 out of themselves?
verse	38	4	13	@@And he answered me and said, Knowest thou not what these @9be?@7 And I said, No, my lord.
verse	38	4	14	@@Then said he, These @9are@7 the two anointed ones, that stand by the LORD of the whole earth.
verse	38	5	1	Then I turned, and lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and behold a flying roll.
verse	38	5	2	@@And he said unto me, What seest thou? And I answered, I see a flying roll; the length thereof @9is@7 twenty cubits, and the breadth thereof ten cubits.
verse	38	5	3	@@Then said he unto me, This @9is@7 the curse that goeth forth over the face of the whole earth: for every one that stealeth shall be cut off @9as@7 on this side according to it; and every one that sweareth shall be cut off @9as@7 on that side according to it.
verse	38	5	4	I will bring it forth, saith the LORD of hosts, and it shall enter into the house of the thief, and into the house of him that sweareth falsely by my name: and it shall remain in the midst of his house, and shall consume it with the timber thereof and the stones thereof.
verse	38	5	5	@@Then the angel that talked with me went forth, and said unto me, Lift up now thine eyes, and see what @9is@7 this that goeth forth.
verse	38	5	6	@@And I said, What @9is@7 it? And he said, This @9is@7 an ephah that goeth forth. He said moreover, This @9is@7 their resemblance through all the earth.
verse	38	5	7	@@And, behold, there was lifted up a talent of lead: and this @9is@7 a woman that sitteth in the midst of the ephah.
verse	38	5	8	@@And he said, This @9is@7 wickedness. And he cast it into the midst of the ephah; and he cast the weight of lead upon the mouth thereof.
verse	38	5	9	@@Then lifted I up mine eyes, and looked, and, behold, there came out two women, and the wind @9was@7 in their wings; for they had wings like the wings of a stork: and they lifted up the ephah between the earth and the heaven.
verse	38	5	10	Then said I to the angel that talked with me, Whither do these bear the ephah?
verse	38	5	11	And he said unto me, To build it an house in the land of Shinar: and it shall be established, and set there upon her own base.
verse	38	6	1	@@And I turned, and lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and, behold, there came four chariots out from between two mountains; and the mountains @9were@7 mountains of brass.
verse	38	6	2	@@In the first chariot @9were@7 red horses; and in the second chariot black horses;
verse	38	6	3	And in the third chariot white horses; and in the fourth chariot grisled and bay horses.
verse	38	6	4	@@Then I answered and said unto the angel that talked with me, What @9are@7 these, my lord?
verse	38	6	5	@@And the angel answered and said unto me, These @9are@7 the four spirits of the heavens, which go forth from standing before the Lord of all the earth.
verse	38	6	6	@@The black horses which @9are@7 therein go forth into the north country; and the white go forth after them; and the grisled go forth toward the south country.
verse	38	6	7	And the bay went forth, and sought to go that they might walk to and fro through the earth: and he said, Get you hence, walk to and fro through the earth. So they walked to and fro through the earth.
verse	38	6	8	Then cried he upon me, and spake unto me, saying, Behold, these that go toward the north country have quieted my spirit in the north country.
verse	38	6	9	And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,
verse	38	6	10	@@Take of @9them of@7 the captivity, @9even@7 of Heldai, of Tobijah, and of Jedaiah, which are come from Babylon, and come thou the same day, and go into the house of Josiah the son of Zephaniah;
verse	38	6	11	@@Then take silver and gold, and make crowns, and set @9them@7 upon the head of Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest;
verse	38	6	12	@@And speak unto him, saying, Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, saying, Behold the man whose name @9is@7 The BRANCH; and he shall grow up out of his place, and he shall build the temple of the LORD:
verse	38	6	13	Even he shall build the temple of the LORD; and he shall bear the glory, and shall sit and rule upon his throne; and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.
verse	38	6	14	And the crowns shall be to Helem, and to Tobijah, and to Jedaiah, and to Hen the son of Zephaniah, for a memorial in the temple of the LORD.
verse	38	6	15	@@And they @9that are@7 far off shall come and build in the temple of the LORD, and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you. And @9this@7 shall come to pass, if ye will diligently obey the voice of the LORD your God.
verse	38	7	1	@@And it came to pass in the fourth year of king Darius, @9that@7 the word of the LORD came unto Zechariah in the fourth @9day@7 of the ninth month, @9even@7 in Chisleu;
verse	38	7	2	When they had sent unto the house of God Sherezer and Regem-melech, and their men, to pray before the LORD,
verse	38	7	3	@@@9And@7 to speak unto the priests which @9were@7 in the house of the LORD of hosts, and to the prophets, saying, Should I weep in the fifth month, separating myself, as I have done these so many years?
verse	38	7	4	Then came the word of the LORD of hosts unto me, saying,
verse	38	7	5	@@Speak unto all the people of the land, and to the priests, saying, When ye fasted and mourned in the fifth and seventh @9month,@7 even those seventy years, did ye at all fast unto me, @9even@7 to me?
verse	38	7	6	@@And when ye did eat, and when ye did drink, did not ye eat @9for yourselves,@7 and drink @9for yourselves? @7
verse	38	7	7	@@@9Should ye@7 not @9hear@7 the words which the LORD hath cried by the former prophets, when Jerusalem was inhabited and in prosperity, and the cities thereof round about her, when @9men@7 inhabited the south and the plain?
verse	38	7	8	And the word of the LORD came unto Zechariah, saying,
verse	38	7	9	Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, saying, Execute true judgment, and shew mercy and compassions every man to his brother:
verse	38	7	10	And oppress not the widow, nor the fatherless, the stranger, nor the poor; and let none of you imagine evil against his brother in your heart.
verse	38	7	11	But they refused to hearken, and pulled away the shoulder, and stopped their ears, that they should not hear.
verse	38	7	12	@@Yea, they made their hearts @9as@7 an adamant stone, lest they should hear the law, and the words which the LORD of hosts hath sent in his spirit by the former prophets: therefore came a great wrath from the LORD of hosts.
verse	38	7	13	@@Therefore it is come to pass, @9that@7 as he cried, and they would not hear; so they cried, and I would not hear, saith the LORD of hosts:
verse	38	7	14	But I scattered them with a whirlwind among all the nations whom they knew not. Thus the land was desolate after them, that no man passed through nor returned: for they laid the pleasant land desolate.
verse	38	8	1	@@Again the word of the LORD of hosts came @9to me,@7 saying,
verse	38	8	2	Thus saith the LORD of hosts; I was jealous for Zion with great jealousy, and I was jealous for her with great fury.
verse	38	8	3	Thus saith the LORD; I am returned unto Zion, and will dwell in the midst of Jerusalem: and Jerusalem shall be called a city of truth; and the mountain of the LORD of hosts the holy mountain.
verse	38	8	4	Thus saith the LORD of hosts; There shall yet old men and old women dwell in the streets of Jerusalem, and every man with his staff in his hand for very age.
verse	38	8	5	And the streets of the city shall be full of boys and girls playing in the streets thereof.
verse	38	8	6	Thus saith the LORD of hosts; If it be marvellous in the eyes of the remnant of this people in these days, should it also be marvellous in mine eyes? saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	38	8	7	Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Behold, I will save my people from the east country, and from the west country;
verse	38	8	8	And I will bring them, and they shall dwell in the midst of Jerusalem: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God, in truth and in righteousness.
verse	38	8	9	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Let your hands be strong, ye that hear in these days these words by the mouth of the prophets, which @9were@7 in the day @9that@7 the foundation of the house of the LORD of hosts was laid, that the temple might be built.
verse	38	8	10	@@For before these days there was no hire for man, nor any hire for beast; neither @9was there any@7 peace to him that went out or came in because of the affliction: for I set all men every one against his neighbour.
verse	38	8	11	@@But now I @9will@7 not @9be@7 unto the residue of this people as in the former days, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	38	8	12	@@For the seed @9shall be@7 prosperous; the vine shall give her fruit, and the ground shall give her increase, and the heavens shall give their dew; and I will cause the remnant of this people to possess all these @9things. @7
verse	38	8	13	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 as ye were a curse among the heathen, O house of Judah, and house of Israel; so will I save you, and ye shall be a blessing: fear not, @9but@7 let your hands be strong.
verse	38	8	14	For thus saith the LORD of hosts; As I thought to punish you, when your fathers provoked me to wrath, saith the LORD of hosts, and I repented not:
verse	38	8	15	So again have I thought in these days to do well unto Jerusalem and to the house of Judah: fear ye not.
verse	38	8	16	@@These @9are@7 the things that ye shall do; Speak ye every man the truth to his neighbour; execute the judgment of truth and peace in your gates:
verse	38	8	17	@@And let none of you imagine evil in your hearts against his neighbour; and love no false oath: for all these @9are things@7 that I hate, saith the LORD.
verse	38	8	18	And the word of the LORD of hosts came unto me, saying,
verse	38	8	19	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The fast of the fourth @9month,@7 and the fast of the fifth, and the fast of the seventh, and the fast of the tenth, shall be to the house of Judah joy and gladness, and cheerful feasts; therefore love the truth and peace.
verse	38	8	20	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts; @9It shall@7 yet @9come to pass,@7 that there shall come people, and the inhabitants of many cities:
verse	38	8	21	@@And the inhabitants of one @9city@7 shall go to another, saying, Let us go speedily to pray before the LORD, and to seek the LORD of hosts: I will go also.
verse	38	8	22	Yea, many people and strong nations shall come to seek the LORD of hosts in Jerusalem, and to pray before the LORD.
verse	38	8	23	@@Thus saith the LORD of hosts; In those days @9it shall come to pass,@7 that ten men shall take hold out of all languages of the nations, even shall take hold of the skirt of him that is a Jew, saying, We will go with you: for we have heard @9that@7 God @9is@7 with you.
verse	38	9	1	@@The burden of the word of the LORD in the land of Hadrach, and Damascus @9shall be@7 the rest thereof: when the eyes of man, as of all the tribes of Israel, @9shall be@7 toward the LORD.
verse	38	9	2	And Hamath also shall border thereby; Tyrus, and Zidon, though it be very wise.
verse	38	9	3	And Tyrus did build herself a strong hold, and heaped up silver as the dust, and fine gold as the mire of the streets.
verse	38	9	4	Behold, the Lord will cast her out, and he will smite her power in the sea; and she shall be devoured with fire.
verse	38	9	5	@@Ashkelon shall see @9it,@7 and fear; Gaza also @9shall see it,@7 and be very sorrowful, and Ekron; for her expectation shall be ashamed; and the king shall perish from Gaza, and Ashkelon shall not be inhabited.
verse	38	9	6	And a bastard shall dwell in Ashdod, and I will cut off the pride of the Philistines.
verse	38	9	7	@@And I will take away his blood out of his mouth, and his abominations from between his teeth: but he that remaineth, even he, @9shall be@7 for our God, and he shall be as a governor in Judah, and Ekron as a Jebusite.
verse	38	9	8	And I will encamp about mine house because of the army, because of him that passeth by, and because of him that returneth: and no oppressor shall pass through them any more: for now have I seen with mine eyes.
verse	38	9	9	@@Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion; shout, O daughter of Jerusalem: behold, thy King cometh unto thee: he @9is@7 just, and having salvation; lowly, and riding upon an ass, and upon a colt the foal of an ass.
verse	38	9	10	@@And I will cut off the chariot from Ephraim, and the horse from Jerusalem, and the battle bow shall be cut off: and he shall speak peace unto the heathen: and his dominion @9shall be@7 from sea @9even@7 to sea, and from river @9even@7 to the ends of the earth.
verse	38	9	11	@@As for thee also, by the blood of thy covenant I have sent forth thy prisoners out of the pit wherein @9is@7 no water.
verse	38	9	12	@@Turn you to the strong hold, ye prisoners of hope: even to day do I declare @9that@7 I will render double unto thee;
verse	38	9	13	When I have bent Judah for me, filled the bow with Ephraim, and raised up thy sons, O Zion, against thy sons, O Greece, and made thee as the sword of a mighty man.
verse	38	9	14	And the LORD shall be seen over them, and his arrow shall go forth as the lightning: and the LORD GOD shall blow the trumpet, and shall go with whirlwinds of the south.
verse	38	9	15	@@The LORD of hosts shall defend them; and they shall devour, and subdue with sling stones; and they shall drink, @9and@7 make a noise as through wine; and they shall be filled like bowls, @9and@7 as the corners of the altar.
verse	38	9	16	@@And the LORD their God shall save them in that day as the flock of his people: for they @9shall be as@7 the stones of a crown, lifted up as an ensign upon his land.
verse	38	9	17	@@For how great @9is@7 his goodness, and how great @9is@7 his beauty! corn shall make the young men cheerful, and new wine the maids.
verse	38	10	1	@@Ask ye of the LORD rain in the time of the latter rain; @9so@7 the LORD shall make bright clouds, and give them showers of rain, to every one grass in the field.
verse	38	10	2	@@For the idols have spoken vanity, and the diviners have seen a lie, and have told false dreams; they comfort in vain: therefore they went their way as a flock, they were troubled, because @9there was@7 no shepherd.
verse	38	10	3	Mine anger was kindled against the shepherds, and I punished the goats: for the LORD of hosts hath visited his flock the house of Judah, and hath made them as his goodly horse in the battle.
verse	38	10	4	Out of him came forth the corner, out of him the nail, out of him the battle bow, out of him every oppressor together.
verse	38	10	5	@@And they shall be as mighty @9men,@7 which tread down @9their enemies@7 in the mire of the streets in the battle: and they shall fight, because the LORD @9is@7 with them, and the riders on horses shall be confounded.
verse	38	10	6	@@And I will strengthen the house of Judah, and I will save the house of Joseph, and I will bring them again to place them; for I have mercy upon them: and they shall be as though I had not cast them off: for I @9am@7 the LORD their God, and will hear them.
verse	38	10	7	@@And @9they of@7 Ephraim shall be like a mighty @9man,@7 and their heart shall rejoice as through wine: yea, their children shall see @9it,@7 and be glad; their heart shall rejoice in the LORD.
verse	38	10	8	I will hiss for them, and gather them; for I have redeemed them: and they shall increase as they have increased.
verse	38	10	9	And I will sow them among the people: and they shall remember me in far countries; and they shall live with their children, and turn again.
verse	38	10	10	@@I will bring them again also out of the land of Egypt, and gather them out of Assyria; and I will bring them into the land of Gilead and Lebanon; and @9place@7 shall not be found for them.
verse	38	10	11	And he shall pass through the sea with affliction, and shall smite the waves in the sea, and all the deeps of the river shall dry up: and the pride of Assyria shall be brought down, and the sceptre of Egypt shall depart away.
verse	38	10	12	And I will strengthen them in the LORD; and they shall walk up and down in his name, saith the LORD.
verse	38	11	1	Open thy doors, O Lebanon, that the fire may devour thy cedars.
verse	38	11	2	Howl, fir tree; for the cedar is fallen; because the mighty are spoiled: howl, O ye oaks of Bashan; for the forest of the vintage is come down.
verse	38	11	3	@@@9There is@7 a voice of the howling of the shepherds; for their glory is spoiled: a voice of the roaring of young lions; for the pride of Jordan is spoiled.
verse	38	11	4	Thus saith the LORD my God; Feed the flock of the slaughter;
verse	38	11	5	@@Whose possessors slay them, and hold themselves not guilty: and they that sell them say, Blessed @9be@7 the LORD; for I am rich: and their own shepherds pity them not.
verse	38	11	6	@@For I will no more pity the inhabitants of the land, saith the LORD: but, lo, I will deliver the men every one into his neighbour's hand, and into the hand of his king: and they shall smite the land, and out of their hand I will not deliver @9them. @7
verse	38	11	7	@@And I will feed the flock of slaughter, @9even@7 you, O poor of the flock. And I took unto me two staves; the one I called Beauty, and the other I called Bands; and I fed the flock.
verse	38	11	8	Three shepherds also I cut off in one month; and my soul lothed them, and their soul also abhorred me.
verse	38	11	9	Then said I, I will not feed you: that that dieth, let it die; and that that is to be cut off, let it be cut off; and let the rest eat every one the flesh of another.
verse	38	11	10	@@And I took my staff, @9even@7 Beauty, and cut it asunder, that I might break my covenant which I had made with all the people.
verse	38	11	11	@@And it was broken in that day: and so the poor of the flock that waited upon me knew that it @9was@7 the word of the LORD.
verse	38	11	12	@@And I said unto them, If ye think good, give @9me@7 my price; and if not, forbear. So they weighed for my price thirty @9pieces@7 of silver.
verse	38	11	13	@@And the LORD said unto me, Cast it unto the potter: a goodly price that I was prised at of them. And I took the thirty @9pieces@7 of silver, and cast them to the potter in the house of the LORD.
verse	38	11	14	@@Then I cut asunder mine other staff, @9even@7 Bands, that I might break the brotherhood between Judah and Israel.
verse	38	11	15	And the LORD said unto me, Take unto thee yet the instruments of a foolish shepherd.
verse	38	11	16	@@For, lo, I will raise up a shepherd in the land, @9which@7 shall not visit those that be cut off, neither shall seek the young one, nor heal that that is broken, nor feed that that standeth still: but he shall eat the flesh of the fat, and tear their claws in pieces.
verse	38	11	17	@@Woe to the idol shepherd that leaveth the flock! the sword @9shall be@7 upon his arm, and upon his right eye: his arm shall be clean dried up, and his right eye shall be utterly darkened.
verse	38	12	1	The burden of the word of the LORD for Israel, saith the LORD, which stretcheth forth the heavens, and layeth the foundation of the earth, and formeth the spirit of man within him.
verse	38	12	2	@@Behold, I will make Jerusalem a cup of trembling unto all the people round about, when they shall be in the siege both against Judah @9and@7 against Jerusalem.
verse	38	12	3	And in that day will I make Jerusalem a burdensome stone for all people: all that burden themselves with it shall be cut in pieces, though all the people of the earth be gathered together against it.
verse	38	12	4	In that day, saith the LORD, I will smite every horse with astonishment, and his rider with madness: and I will open mine eyes upon the house of Judah, and will smite every horse of the people with blindness.
verse	38	12	5	@@And the governors of Judah shall say in their heart, The inhabitants of Jerusalem @9shall be@7 my strength in the LORD of hosts their God.
verse	38	12	6	@@In that day will I make the governors of Judah like an hearth of fire among the wood, and like a torch of fire in a sheaf; and they shall devour all the people round about, on the right hand and on the left: and Jerusalem shall be inhabited again in her own place, @9even@7 in Jerusalem.
verse	38	12	7	@@The LORD also shall save the tents of Judah first, that the glory of the house of David and the glory of the inhabitants of Jerusalem do not magnify @9themselves@7 against Judah.
verse	38	12	8	@@In that day shall the LORD defend the inhabitants of Jerusalem; and he that is feeble among them at that day shall be as David; and the house of David @9shall be@7 as God, as the angel of the LORD before them.
verse	38	12	9	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 I will seek to destroy all the nations that come against Jerusalem.
verse	38	12	10	@@And I will pour upon the house of David, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the spirit of grace and of supplications: and they shall look upon me whom they have pierced, and they shall mourn for him, as one mourneth for @9his@7 only @9son,@7 and shall be in bitterness for him, as one that is in bitterness for @9his@7 firstborn.
verse	38	12	11	In that day shall there be a great mourning in Jerusalem, as the mourning of Hadadrimmon in the valley of Megiddon.
verse	38	12	12	And the land shall mourn, every family apart; the family of the house of David apart, and their wives apart; the family of the house of Nathan apart, and their wives apart;
verse	38	12	13	The family of the house of Levi apart, and their wives apart; the family of Shimei apart, and their wives apart;
verse	38	12	14	All the families that remain, every family apart, and their wives apart.
verse	38	13	1	In that day there shall be a fountain opened to the house of David and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem for sin and for uncleanness.
verse	38	13	2	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD of hosts, @9that@7 I will cut off the names of the idols out of the land, and they shall no more be remembered: and also I will cause the prophets and the unclean spirit to pass out of the land.
verse	38	13	3	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 when any shall yet prophesy, then his father and his mother that begat him shall say unto him, Thou shalt not live; for thou speakest lies in the name of the LORD: and his father and his mother that begat him shall thrust him through when he prophesieth.
verse	38	13	4	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the prophets shall be ashamed every one of his vision, when he hath prophesied; neither shall they wear a rough garment to deceive:
verse	38	13	5	@@But he shall say, I @9am@7 no prophet, I @9am@7 an husbandman; for man taught me to keep cattle from my youth.
verse	38	13	6	@@And @9one@7 shall say unto him, What @9are@7 these wounds in thine hands? Then he shall answer, @9Those@7 with which I was wounded @9in@7 the house of my friends.
verse	38	13	7	@@Awake, O sword, against my shepherd, and against the man @9that is@7 my fellow, saith the LORD of hosts: smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered: and I will turn mine hand upon the little ones.
verse	38	13	8	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 in all the land, saith the LORD, two parts therein shall be cut off @9and@7 die; but the third shall be left therein.
verse	38	13	9	@@And I will bring the third part through the fire, and will refine them as silver is refined, and will try them as gold is tried: they shall call on my name, and I will hear them: I will say, It @9is@7 my people: and they shall say, The LORD @9is@7 my God.
verse	38	14	1	Behold, the day of the LORD cometh, and thy spoil shall be divided in the midst of thee.
verse	38	14	2	For I will gather all nations against Jerusalem to battle; and the city shall be taken, and the houses rifled, and the women ravished; and half of the city shall go forth into captivity, and the residue of the people shall not be cut off from the city.
verse	38	14	3	Then shall the LORD go forth, and fight against those nations, as when he fought in the day of battle.
verse	38	14	4	@@And his feet shall stand in that day upon the mount of Olives, which @9is@7 before Jerusalem on the east, and the mount of Olives shall cleave in the midst thereof toward the east and toward the west, @9and there shall be@7 a very great valley; and half of the mountain shall remove toward the north, and half of it toward the south.
verse	38	14	5	@@And ye shall flee @9to@7 the valley of the mountains; for the valley of the mountains shall reach unto Azal: yea, ye shall flee, like as ye fled from before the earthquake in the days of Uzziah king of Judah: and the LORD my God shall come, @9and@7 all the saints with thee.
verse	38	14	6	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 the light shall not be clear, @9nor@7 dark:
verse	38	14	7	@@But it shall be one day which shall be known to the LORD, not day, nor night: but it shall come to pass, @9that@7 at evening time it shall be light.
verse	38	14	8	@@And it shall be in that day, @9that@7 living waters shall go out from Jerusalem; half of them toward the former sea, and half of them toward the hinder sea: in summer and in winter shall it be.
verse	38	14	9	And the LORD shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one LORD, and his name one.
verse	38	14	10	@@All the land shall be turned as a plain from Geba to Rimmon south of Jerusalem: and it shall be lifted up, and inhabited in her place, from Benjamin's gate unto the place of the first gate, unto the corner gate, and @9from@7 the tower of Hananeel unto the king's winepresses.
verse	38	14	11	@@And @9men@7 shall dwell in it, and there shall be no more utter destruction; but Jerusalem shall be safely inhabited.
verse	38	14	12	And this shall be the plague wherewith the LORD will smite all the people that have fought against Jerusalem; Their flesh shall consume away while they stand upon their feet, and their eyes shall consume away in their holes, and their tongue shall consume away in their mouth.
verse	38	14	13	@@And it shall come to pass in that day, @9that@7 a great tumult from the LORD shall be among them; and they shall lay hold every one on the hand of his neighbour, and his hand shall rise up against the hand of his neighbour.
verse	38	14	14	And Judah also shall fight at Jerusalem; and the wealth of all the heathen round about shall be gathered together, gold, and silver, and apparel, in great abundance.
verse	38	14	15	And so shall be the plague of the horse, of the mule, of the camel, and of the ass, and of all the beasts that shall be in these tents, as this plague.
verse	38	14	16	@@And it shall come to pass, @9that@7 every one that is left of all the nations which came against Jerusalem shall even go up from year to year to worship the King, the LORD of hosts, and to keep the feast of tabernacles.
verse	38	14	17	@@And it shall be, @9that@7 whoso will not come up of @9all@7 the families of the earth unto Jerusalem to worship the King, the LORD of hosts, even upon them shall be no rain.
verse	38	14	18	@@And if the family of Egypt go not up, and come not, that @9have@7 no @9rain;@7 there shall be the plague, wherewith the LORD will smite the heathen that come not up to keep the feast of tabernacles.
verse	38	14	19	This shall be the punishment of Egypt, and the punishment of all nations that come not up to keep the feast of tabernacles.
verse	38	14	20	In that day shall there be upon the bells of the horses, HOLINESS UNTO THE LORD; and the pots in the LORD'S house shall be like the bowls before the altar.
verse	38	14	21	Yea, every pot in Jerusalem and in Judah shall be holiness unto the LORD of hosts: and all they that sacrifice shall come and take of them, and seethe therein: and in that day there shall be no more the Canaanite in the house of the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	1	1	The burden of the word of the LORD to Israel by Malachi.
verse	39	1	2	@@I have loved you, saith the LORD. Yet ye say, Wherein hast thou loved us? @9Was@7 not Esau Jacob's brother? saith the LORD: yet I loved Jacob,
verse	39	1	3	And I hated Esau, and laid his mountains and his heritage waste for the dragons of the wilderness.
verse	39	1	4	Whereas Edom saith, We are impoverished, but we will return and build the desolate places; thus saith the LORD of hosts, They shall build, but I will throw down; and they shall call them, The border of wickedness, and, The people against whom the LORD hath indignation for ever.
verse	39	1	5	And your eyes shall see, and ye shall say, The LORD will be magnified from the border of Israel.
verse	39	1	6	@@A son honoureth @9his@7 father, and a servant his master: if then I @9be@7 a father, where @9is@7 mine honour? and if I @9be@7 a master, where @9is@7 my fear? saith the LORD of hosts unto you, O priests, that despise my name. And ye say, Wherein have we despised thy name?
verse	39	1	7	@@Ye offer polluted bread upon mine altar; and ye say, Wherein have we polluted thee? In that ye say, The table of the LORD @9is@7 contemptible.
verse	39	1	8	@@And if ye offer the blind for sacrifice, @9is it@7 not evil? and if ye offer the lame and sick, @9is it@7 not evil? offer it now unto thy governor; will he be pleased with thee, or accept thy person? saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	1	9	And now, I pray you, beseech God that he will be gracious unto us: this hath been by your means: will he regard your persons? saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	1	10	@@Who @9is there@7 even among you that would shut the doors @9for nought?@7 neither do ye kindle @9fire@7 on mine altar for nought. I have no pleasure in you, saith the LORD of hosts, neither will I accept an offering at your hand.
verse	39	1	11	@@For from the rising of the sun even unto the going down of the same my name @9shall be@7 great among the Gentiles; and in every place incense @9shall be@7 offered unto my name, and a pure offering: for my name @9shall be@7 great among the heathen, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	1	12	@@But ye have profaned it, in that ye say, The table of the LORD @9is@7 polluted; and the fruit thereof, @9even@7 his meat, @9is@7 contemptible.
verse	39	1	13	@@Ye said also, Behold, what a weariness @9is it!@7 and ye have snuffed at it, saith the LORD of hosts; and ye brought @9that which was@7 torn, and the lame, and the sick; thus ye brought an offering: should I accept this of your hand? saith the LORD.
verse	39	1	14	@@But cursed @9be@7 the deceiver, which hath in his flock a male, and voweth, and sacrificeth unto the LORD a corrupt thing: for I @9am@7 a great King, saith the LORD of hosts, and my name @9is@7 dreadful among the heathen.
verse	39	2	1	@@And now, O ye priests, this commandment @9is@7 for you.
verse	39	2	2	@@If ye will not hear, and if ye will not lay @9it@7 to heart, to give glory unto my name, saith the LORD of hosts, I will even send a curse upon you, and I will curse your blessings: yea, I have cursed them already, because ye do not lay @9it@7 to heart.
verse	39	2	3	@@Behold, I will corrupt your seed, and spread dung upon your faces, @9even@7 the dung of your solemn feasts; and @9one@7 shall take you away with it.
verse	39	2	4	And ye shall know that I have sent this commandment unto you, that my covenant might be with Levi, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	2	5	@@My covenant was with him of life and peace; and I gave them to him @9for@7 the fear wherewith he feared me, and was afraid before my name.
verse	39	2	6	The law of truth was in his mouth, and iniquity was not found in his lips: he walked with me in peace and equity, and did turn many away from iniquity.
verse	39	2	7	@@For the priest's lips should keep knowledge, and they should seek the law at his mouth: for he @9is@7 the messenger of the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	2	8	But ye are departed out of the way; ye have caused many to stumble at the law; ye have corrupted the covenant of Levi, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	2	9	Therefore have I also made you contemptible and base before all the people, according as ye have not kept my ways, but have been partial in the law.
verse	39	2	10	Have we not all one father? hath not one God created us? why do we deal treacherously every man against his brother, by profaning the covenant of our fathers?
verse	39	2	11	Judah hath dealt treacherously, and an abomination is committed in Israel and in Jerusalem; for Judah hath profaned the holiness of the LORD which he loved, and hath married the daughter of a strange god.
verse	39	2	12	The LORD will cut off the man that doeth this, the master and the scholar, out of the tabernacles of Jacob, and him that offereth an offering unto the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	2	13	@@And this have ye done again, covering the altar of the LORD with tears, with weeping, and with crying out, insomuch that he regardeth not the offering any more, or receiveth @9it@7 with good will at your hand.
verse	39	2	14	@@Yet ye say, Wherefore? Because the LORD hath been witness between thee and the wife of thy youth, against whom thou hast dealt treacherously: yet @9is@7 she thy companion, and the wife of thy covenant.
verse	39	2	15	And did not he make one? Yet had he the residue of the spirit. And wherefore one? That he might seek a godly seed. Therefore take heed to your spirit, and let none deal treacherously against the wife of his youth.
verse	39	2	16	@@For the LORD, the God of Israel, saith that he hateth putting away: for @9one@7 covereth violence with his garment, saith the LORD of hosts: therefore take heed to your spirit, that ye deal not treacherously.
verse	39	2	17	@@Ye have wearied the LORD with your words. Yet ye say, Wherein have we wearied @9him?@7 When ye say, Every one that doeth evil @9is@7 good in the sight of the LORD, and he delighteth in them; or, Where @9is@7 the God of judgment?
verse	39	3	1	Behold, I will send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me: and the Lord, whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant, whom ye delight in: behold, he shall come, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	3	2	@@But who may abide the day of his coming? and who shall stand when he appeareth? for he @9is@7 like a refiner's fire, and like fullers' sope:
verse	39	3	3	@@And he shall sit @9as@7 a refiner and purifier of silver: and he shall purify the sons of Levi, and purge them as gold and silver, that they may offer unto the LORD an offering in righteousness.
verse	39	3	4	Then shall the offering of Judah and Jerusalem be pleasant unto the LORD, as in the days of old, and as in former years.
verse	39	3	5	@@And I will come near to you to judgment; and I will be a swift witness against the sorcerers, and against the adulterers, and against false swearers, and against those that oppress the hireling in @9his@7 wages, the widow, and the fatherless, and that turn aside the stranger @9from his right,@7 and fear not me, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	3	6	@@For I @9am@7 the LORD, I change not; therefore ye sons of Jacob are not consumed.
verse	39	3	7	@@Even from the days of your fathers ye are gone away from mine ordinances, and have not kept @9them.@7 Return unto me, and I will return unto you, saith the LORD of hosts. But ye said, Wherein shall we return?
verse	39	3	8	Will a man rob God? Yet ye have robbed me. But ye say, Wherein have we robbed thee? In tithes and offerings.
verse	39	3	9	@@Ye @9are@7 cursed with a curse: for ye have robbed me, @9even@7 this whole nation.
verse	39	3	10	@@Bring ye all the tithes into the storehouse, that there may be meat in mine house, and prove me now herewith, saith the LORD of hosts, if I will not open you the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that @9there shall@7 not @9be room@7 enough @9to receive it. @7
verse	39	3	11	And I will rebuke the devourer for your sakes, and he shall not destroy the fruits of your ground; neither shall your vine cast her fruit before the time in the field, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	3	12	And all nations shall call you blessed: for ye shall be a delightsome land, saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	3	13	@@Your words have been stout against me, saith the LORD. Yet ye say, What have we spoken @9so much@7 against thee?
verse	39	3	14	@@Ye have said, It @9is@7 vain to serve God: and what profit @9is it@7 that we have kept his ordinance, and that we have walked mournfully before the LORD of hosts?
verse	39	3	15	@@And now we call the proud happy; yea, they that work wickedness are set up; yea, @9they that@7 tempt God are even delivered.
verse	39	3	16	@@Then they that feared the LORD spake often one to another: and the LORD hearkened, and heard @9it,@7 and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared the LORD, and that thought upon his name.
verse	39	3	17	And they shall be mine, saith the LORD of hosts, in that day when I make up my jewels; and I will spare them, as a man spareth his own son that serveth him.
verse	39	3	18	Then shall ye return, and discern between the righteous and the wicked, between him that serveth God and him that serveth him not.
verse	39	4	1	For, behold, the day cometh, that shall burn as an oven; and all the proud, yea, and all that do wickedly, shall be stubble: and the day that cometh shall burn them up, saith the LORD of hosts, that it shall leave them neither root nor branch.
verse	39	4	2	But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.
verse	39	4	3	@@And ye shall tread down the wicked; for they shall be ashes under the soles of your feet in the day that I shall do @9this,@7 saith the LORD of hosts.
verse	39	4	4	@@Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Israel, @9with@7 the statutes and judgments.
verse	39	4	5	Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet before the coming of the great and dreadful day of the LORD:
verse	39	4	6	And he shall turn the heart of the fathers to the children, and the heart of the children to their fathers, lest I come and smite the earth with a curse.
verse	40	1	1	The book of the generation of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham.
verse	40	1	2	Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob begat Judas and his brethren;
verse	40	1	3	And Judas begat Phares and Zara of Thamar; and Phares begat Esrom; and Esrom begat Aram;
verse	40	1	4	And Aram begat Aminadab; and Aminadab begat Naasson; and Naasson begat Salmon;
verse	40	1	5	And Salmon begat Booz of Rachab; and Booz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed begat Jesse;
verse	40	1	6	@@And Jesse begat David the king; and David the king begat Solomon of her @9that had been the wife@7 of Urias;
verse	40	1	7	And Solomon begat Roboam; and Roboam begat Abia; and Abia begat Asa;
verse	40	1	8	And Asa begat Josaphat; and Josaphat begat Joram; and Joram begat Ozias;
verse	40	1	9	And Ozias begat Joatham; and Joatham begat Achaz; and Achaz begat Ezekias;
verse	40	1	10	And Ezekias begat Manasses; and Manasses begat Amon; and Amon begat Josias;
verse	40	1	11	And Josias begat Jechonias and his brethren, about the time they were carried away to Babylon:
verse	40	1	12	And after they were brought to Babylon, Jechonias begat Salathiel; and Salathiel begat Zorobabel;
verse	40	1	13	And Zorobabel begat Abiud; and Abiud begat Eliakim; and Eliakim begat Azor;
verse	40	1	14	And Azor begat Sadoc; and Sadoc begat Achim; and Achim begat Eliud;
verse	40	1	15	And Eliud begat Eleazar; and Eleazar begat Matthan; and Matthan begat Jacob;
verse	40	1	16	And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ.
verse	40	1	17	@@So all the generations from Abraham to David @9are@7 fourteen generations; and from David until the carrying away into Babylon @9are@7 fourteen generations; and from the carrying away into Babylon unto Christ @9are@7 fourteen generations.
verse	40	1	18	Now the birth of Jesus Christ was on this wise: When as his mother Mary was espoused to Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost.
verse	40	1	19	@@Then Joseph her husband, being a just @9man,@7 and not willing to make her a publick example, was minded to put her away privily.
verse	40	1	20	But while he thought on these things, behold, the angel of the Lord appeared unto him in a dream, saying, Joseph, thou son of David, fear not to take unto thee Mary thy wife: for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Ghost.
verse	40	1	21	And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save his people from their sins.
verse	40	1	22	Now all this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying,
verse	40	1	23	Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us.
verse	40	1	24	Then Joseph being raised from sleep did as the angel of the Lord had bidden him, and took unto him his wife:
verse	40	1	25	And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son: and he called his name JESUS.
verse	40	2	1	Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of Herod the king, behold, there came wise men from the east to Jerusalem,
verse	40	2	2	Saying, Where is he that is born King of the Jews? for we have seen his star in the east, and are come to worship him.
verse	40	2	3	@@When Herod the king had heard @9these things,@7 he was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him.
verse	40	2	4	And when he had gathered all the chief priests and scribes of the people together, he demanded of them where Christ should be born.
verse	40	2	5	And they said unto him, In Bethlehem of Judaea: for thus it is written by the prophet,
verse	40	2	6	And thou Bethlehem, in the land of Juda, art not the least among the princes of Juda: for out of thee shall come a Governor, that shall rule my people Israel.
verse	40	2	7	Then Herod, when he had privily called the wise men, enquired of them diligently what time the star appeared.
verse	40	2	8	@@And he sent them to Bethlehem, and said, Go and search diligently for the young child; and when ye have found @9him,@7 bring me word again, that I may come and worship him also.
verse	40	2	9	When they had heard the king, they departed; and, lo, the star, which they saw in the east, went before them, till it came and stood over where the young child was.
verse	40	2	10	When they saw the star, they rejoiced with exceeding great joy.
verse	40	2	11	And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.
verse	40	2	12	And being warned of God in a dream that they should not return to Herod, they departed into their own country another way.
verse	40	2	13	And when they were departed, behold, the angel of the Lord appeareth to Joseph in a dream, saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and flee into Egypt, and be thou there until I bring thee word: for Herod will seek the young child to destroy him.
verse	40	2	14	When he arose, he took the young child and his mother by night, and departed into Egypt:
verse	40	2	15	And was there until the death of Herod: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying, Out of Egypt have I called my son.
verse	40	2	16	Then Herod, when he saw that he was mocked of the wise men, was exceeding wroth, and sent forth, and slew all the children that were in Bethlehem, and in all the coasts thereof, from two years old and under, according to the time which he had diligently enquired of the wise men.
verse	40	2	17	Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremy the prophet, saying,
verse	40	2	18	@@In Rama was there a voice heard, lamentation, and weeping, and great mourning, Rachel weeping @9for@7 her children, and would not be comforted, because they are not.
verse	40	2	19	But when Herod was dead, behold, an angel of the Lord appeareth in a dream to Joseph in Egypt,
verse	40	2	20	Saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and go into the land of Israel: for they are dead which sought the young child's life.
verse	40	2	21	And he arose, and took the young child and his mother, and came into the land of Israel.
verse	40	2	22	But when he heard that Archelaus did reign in Judaea in the room of his father Herod, he was afraid to go thither: notwithstanding, being warned of God in a dream, he turned aside into the parts of Galilee:
verse	40	2	23	And he came and dwelt in a city called Nazareth: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophets, He shall be called a Nazarene.
verse	40	3	1	In those days came John the Baptist, preaching in the wilderness of Judaea,
verse	40	3	2	And saying, Repent ye: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.
verse	40	3	3	For this is he that was spoken of by the prophet Esaias, saying, The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.
verse	40	3	4	And the same John had his raiment of camel's hair, and a leathern girdle about his loins; and his meat was locusts and wild honey.
verse	40	3	5	Then went out to him Jerusalem, and all Judaea, and all the region round about Jordan,
verse	40	3	6	And were baptized of him in Jordan, confessing their sins.
verse	40	3	7	But when he saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees come to his baptism, he said unto them, O generation of vipers, who hath warned you to flee from the wrath to come?
verse	40	3	8	Bring forth therefore fruits meet for repentance:
verse	40	3	9	@@And think not to say within yourselves, We have Abraham to @9our@7 father: for I say unto you, that God is able of these stones to raise up children unto Abraham.
verse	40	3	10	And now also the axe is laid unto the root of the trees: therefore every tree which bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.
verse	40	3	11	@@I indeed baptize you with water unto repentance: but he that cometh after me is mightier than I, whose shoes I am not worthy to bear: he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost, and @9with@7 fire:
verse	40	3	12	@@Whose fan @9is@7 in his hand, and he will throughly purge his floor, and gather his wheat into the garner; but he will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.
verse	40	3	13	Then cometh Jesus from Galilee to Jordan unto John, to be baptized of him.
verse	40	3	14	But John forbad him, saying, I have need to be baptized of thee, and comest thou to me?
verse	40	3	15	@@And Jesus answering said unto him, @6Suffer @9it to be so@7 now: for thus it becometh us to fulfil all righteousness.@5 Then he suffered him.
verse	40	3	16	And Jesus, when he was baptized, went up straightway out of the water: and, lo, the heavens were opened unto him, and he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove, and lighting upon him:
verse	40	3	17	And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.
verse	40	4	1	Then was Jesus led up of the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted of the devil.
verse	40	4	2	And when he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was afterward an hungred.
verse	40	4	3	And when the tempter came to him, he said, If thou be the Son of God, command that these stones be made bread.
verse	40	4	4	@@But he answered and said, @6It is written, Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God.@5
verse	40	4	5	Then the devil taketh him up into the holy city, and setteth him on a pinnacle of the temple,
verse	40	4	6	@@And saith unto him, If thou be the Son of God, cast thyself down: for it is written, He shall give his angels charge concerning thee: and in @9their@7 hands they shall bear thee up, lest at any time thou dash thy foot against a stone.
verse	40	4	7	@@Jesus said unto him, @6It is written again, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God.@5
verse	40	4	8	Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them;
verse	40	4	9	And saith unto him, All these things will I give thee, if thou wilt fall down and worship me.
verse	40	4	10	@@Then saith Jesus unto him, @6Get thee hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve.@5
verse	40	4	11	Then the devil leaveth him, and, behold, angels came and ministered unto him.
verse	40	4	12	Now when Jesus had heard that John was cast into prison, he departed into Galilee;
verse	40	4	13	And leaving Nazareth, he came and dwelt in Capernaum, which is upon the sea coast, in the borders of Zabulon and Nephthalim:
verse	40	4	14	That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying,
verse	40	4	15	@@The land of Zabulon, and the land of Nephthalim, @9by@7 the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, Galilee of the Gentiles;
verse	40	4	16	The people which sat in darkness saw great light; and to them which sat in the region and shadow of death light is sprung up.
verse	40	4	17	@@From that time Jesus began to preach, and to say, @6Repent: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.@5
verse	40	4	18	And Jesus, walking by the sea of Galilee, saw two brethren, Simon called Peter, and Andrew his brother, casting a net into the sea: for they were fishers.
verse	40	4	19	@@And he saith unto them, @6Follow me, and I will make you fishers of men.@5
verse	40	4	20	@@And they straightway left @9their@7 nets, and followed him.
verse	40	4	21	@@And going on from thence, he saw other two brethren, James @9the son@7 of Zebedee, and John his brother, in a ship with Zebedee their father, mending their nets; and he called them.
verse	40	4	22	And they immediately left the ship and their father, and followed him.
verse	40	4	23	And Jesus went about all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing all manner of sickness and all manner of disease among the people.
verse	40	4	24	And his fame went throughout all Syria: and they brought unto him all sick people that were taken with divers diseases and torments, and those which were possessed with devils, and those which were lunatick, and those that had the palsy; and he healed them.
verse	40	4	25	@@And there followed him great multitudes of people from Galilee, and @9from@7 Decapolis, and @9from@7 Jerusalem, and @9from@7 Judaea, and @9from@7 beyond Jordan.
verse	40	5	1	And seeing the multitudes, he went up into a mountain: and when he was set, his disciples came unto him:
verse	40	5	2	And he opened his mouth, and taught them, saying,
verse	40	5	3	@@@6Blessed @9are@7 the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	5	4	@@@6Blessed @9are@7 they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.@5
verse	40	5	5	@@@6Blessed @9are@7 the meek: for they shall inherit the earth.@5
verse	40	5	6	@@@6Blessed @9are@7 they which do hunger and thirst after righteousness: for they shall be filled.@5
verse	40	5	7	@@@6Blessed @9are@7 the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.@5
verse	40	5	8	@@@6Blessed @9are@7 the pure in heart: for they shall see God.@5
verse	40	5	9	@@@6Blessed @9are@7 the peacemakers: for they shall be called the children of God.@5
verse	40	5	10	@@@6Blessed @9are@7 they which are persecuted for righteousness sake: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	5	11	@@@6Blessed are ye, when @9men@7 shall revile you, and persecute @9you,@7 and shall say all manner of evil against you falsely, for my sake.@5
verse	40	5	12	@@@6Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great @9is@7 your reward in heaven: for so persecuted they the prophets which were before you.@5
verse	40	5	13	@@@6Ye are the salt of the earth: but if the salt have lost his savour, wherewith shall it be salted? it is thenceforth good for nothing, but to be cast out, and to be trodden under foot of men.@5
verse	40	5	14	@@@6Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid.@5
verse	40	5	15	@@@6Neither do men light a candle, and put it under a bushel, but on a candlestick; and it giveth light unto all that are in the house.@5
verse	40	5	16	@@@6Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	5	17	@@@6Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil.@5
verse	40	5	18	@@@6For verily I say unto you, Till heaven and earth pass, one jot or one tittle shall in no wise pass from the law, till all be fulfilled.@5
verse	40	5	19	@@@6Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so, he shall be called the least in the kingdom of heaven: but whosoever shall do and teach @9them,@7 the same shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	5	20	@@@6For I say unto you, That except your righteousness shall exceed @9the righteousness@7 of the scribes and Pharisees, ye shall in no case enter into the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	5	21	@@@6Ye have heard that it was said by them of old time, Thou shalt not kill; and whosoever shall kill shall be in danger of the judgment:@5
verse	40	5	22	@@@6But I say unto you, That whosoever is angry with his brother without a cause shall be in danger of the judgment: and whosoever shall say to his brother, Raca, shall be in danger of the council: but whosoever shall say, Thou fool, shall be in danger of hell fire.@5
verse	40	5	23	@@@6Therefore if thou bring thy gift to the altar, and there rememberest that thy brother hath ought against thee;@5
verse	40	5	24	@@@6Leave there thy gift before the altar, and go thy way; first be reconciled to thy brother, and then come and offer thy gift.@5
verse	40	5	25	@@@6Agree with thine adversary quickly, whiles thou art in the way with him; lest at any time the adversary deliver thee to the judge, and the judge deliver thee to the officer, and thou be cast into prison.@5
verse	40	5	26	@@@6Verily I say unto thee, Thou shalt by no means come out thence, till thou hast paid the uttermost farthing.@5
verse	40	5	27	@@@6Ye have heard that it was said by them of old time, Thou shalt not commit adultery:@5
verse	40	5	28	@@@6But I say unto you, That whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart.@5
verse	40	5	29	@@@6And if thy right eye offend thee, pluck it out, and cast @9it@7 from thee: for it is profitable for thee that one of thy members should perish, and not @9that@7 thy whole body should be cast into hell.@5
verse	40	5	30	@@@6And if thy right hand offend thee, cut if off, and cast it from thee: for it is profitable for thee that one of thy members should perish, and not @9that@7 thy whole body should be cast into hell.@5
verse	40	5	31	@@@6It hath been said, Whosoever shall put away his wife, let him give her a writing of divorcement:@5
verse	40	5	32	@@@6But I say unto you, That whosoever shall put away his wife, saving for the cause of fornication, causeth her to commit adultery: and whosoever shall marry her that is divorced committeth adultery.@5
verse	40	5	33	@@@6Again, ye have heard that it hath been said by them of old time, Thou shalt not forswear thyself, but shalt perform unto the Lord thine oaths:@5
verse	40	5	34	@@@6But I say unto you, Swear not at all; neither by heaven; for it is God's throne:@5
verse	40	5	35	@@@6Nor by the earth; for it is his footstool: neither by Jerusalem; for it is the city of the great King.@5
verse	40	5	36	@@@6Neither shalt thou swear by thy head, because thou canst not make one hair white or black.@5
verse	40	5	37	@@@6But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.@5
verse	40	5	38	@@@6Ye have heard that it hath been said, An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth:@5
verse	40	5	39	@@@6But I say unto you, That ye resist not evil: but whosoever shall smite thee on thy right cheek, turn to him the other also.@5
verse	40	5	40	@@@6And if any man will sue thee at the law, and take away thy coat, let him have @9thy@7 cloke also.@5
verse	40	5	41	@@@6And whosoever shall compel thee to go a mile, go with him twain.@5
verse	40	5	42	@@@6Give to him that asketh thee, and from him that would borrow of thee turn not thou away.@5
verse	40	5	43	@@@6Ye have heard that it hath been said, Thou shalt love thy neighbour, and hate thine enemy.@5
verse	40	5	44	@@@6But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;@5
verse	40	5	45	@@@6That ye may be the children of your Father which is in heaven: for he maketh his sun to rise on the evil and on the good, and sendeth rain on the just and on the unjust.@5
verse	40	5	46	@@@6For if ye love them which love you, what reward have ye? do not even the publicans the same?@5
verse	40	5	47	@@@6And if ye salute your brethren only, what do ye more @9than others?@7 do not even the publicans so?@5
verse	40	5	48	@@@6Be ye therefore perfect, even as your Father which is in heaven is perfect.@5
verse	40	6	1	@@@6Take heed that ye do not your alms before men, to be seen of them: otherwise ye have no reward of your Father which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	6	2	@@@6Therefore when thou doest @9thine@7 alms, do not sound a trumpet before thee, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and in the streets, that they may have glory of men. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.@5
verse	40	6	3	@@@6But when thou doest alms, let not thy left hand know what thy right hand doeth:@5
verse	40	6	4	@@@6That thine alms may be in secret: and thy Father which seeth in secret himself shall reward thee openly.@5
verse	40	6	5	@@@6And when thou prayest, thou shalt not be as the hypocrites @9are:@7 for they love to pray standing in the synagogues and in the corners of the streets, that they may be seen of men. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.@5
verse	40	6	6	@@@6But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret; and thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward thee openly.@5
verse	40	6	7	@@@6But when ye pray, use not vain repetitions, as the heathen @9do:@7 for they think that they shall be heard for their much speaking.@5
verse	40	6	8	@@@6Be not ye therefore like unto them: for your Father knoweth what things ye have need of, before ye ask him.@5
verse	40	6	9	@@@6After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name.@5
verse	40	6	10	@@@6Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done in earth, as @9it is@7 in heaven.@5
verse	40	6	11	@@@6Give us this day our daily bread.@5
verse	40	6	12	@@@6And forgive us our debts, as we forgive our debtors.@5
verse	40	6	13	@@@6And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: For thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, for ever. Amen.@5
verse	40	6	14	@@@6For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you:@5
verse	40	6	15	@@@6But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses.@5
verse	40	6	16	@@@6Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.@5
verse	40	6	17	@@@6But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face;@5
verse	40	6	18	@@@6That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret: and thy Father, which seeth in secret, shall reward thee openly.@5
verse	40	6	19	@@@6Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and where thieves break through and steal:@5
verse	40	6	20	@@@6But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt, and where thieves do not break through nor steal:@5
verse	40	6	21	@@@6For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.@5
verse	40	6	22	@@@6The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light.@5
verse	40	6	23	@@@6But if thine eye be evil, thy whole body shall be full of darkness. If therefore the light that is in thee be darkness, how great @9is@7 that darkness!@5
verse	40	6	24	@@@6No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon.@5
verse	40	6	25	@@@6Therefore I say unto you, Take no thought for your life, what ye shall eat, or what ye shall drink; nor yet for your body, what ye shall put on. Is not the life more than meat, and the body than raiment?@5
verse	40	6	26	@@@6Behold the fowls of the air: for they sow not, neither do they reap, nor gather into barns; yet your heavenly Father feedeth them. Are ye not much better than they?@5
verse	40	6	27	@@@6Which of you by taking thought can add one cubit unto his stature?@5
verse	40	6	28	@@@6And why take ye thought for raiment? Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow; they toil not, neither do they spin:@5
verse	40	6	29	@@@6And yet I say unto you, That even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.@5
verse	40	6	30	@@@6Wherefore, if God so clothe the grass of the field, which to day is, and to morrow is cast into the oven, @9shall he@7 not much more @9clothe@7 you, O ye of little faith?@5
verse	40	6	31	@@@6Therefore take no thought, saying, What shall we eat? or, What shall we drink? or, Wherewithal shall we be clothed?@5
verse	40	6	32	@@@6(For after all these things do the Gentiles seek:) for your heavenly Father knoweth that ye have need of all these things.@5
verse	40	6	33	@@@6But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.@5
verse	40	6	34	@@@6Take therefore no thought for the morrow: for the morrow shall take thought for the things of itself. Sufficient unto the day @9is@7 the evil thereof.@5
verse	40	7	1	@@@6Judge not, that ye be not judged.@5
verse	40	7	2	@@@6For with what judgment ye judge, ye shall be judged: and with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you again.@5
verse	40	7	3	@@@6And why beholdest thou the mote that is in thy brother's eye, but considerest not the beam that is in thine own eye?@5
verse	40	7	4	@@@6Or how wilt thou say to thy brother, Let me pull out the mote out of thine eye; and, behold, a beam @9is@7 in thine own eye?@5
verse	40	7	5	@@@6Thou hypocrite, first cast out the beam out of thine own eye; and then shalt thou see clearly to cast out the mote out of thy brother's eye.@5
verse	40	7	6	@@@6Give not that which is holy unto the dogs, neither cast ye your pearls before swine, lest they trample them under their feet, and turn again and rend you.@5
verse	40	7	7	@@@6Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:@5
verse	40	7	8	@@@6For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened.@5
verse	40	7	9	@@@6Or what man is there of you, whom if his son ask bread, will he give him a stone?@5
verse	40	7	10	@@@6Or if he ask a fish, will he give him a serpent?@5
verse	40	7	11	@@@6If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children, how much more shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him?@5
verse	40	7	12	@@@6Therefore all things whatsoever ye would that men should do to you, do ye even so to them: for this is the law and the prophets.@5
verse	40	7	13	@@@6Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide @9is@7 the gate, and broad @9is@7 the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat:@5
verse	40	7	14	@@@6Because strait @9is@7 the gate, and narrow @9is@7 the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.@5
verse	40	7	15	@@@6Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.@5
verse	40	7	16	@@@6Ye shall know them by their fruits. Do men gather grapes of thorns, or figs of thistles?@5
verse	40	7	17	@@@6Even so every good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree bringeth forth evil fruit.@5
verse	40	7	18	@@@6A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither @9can@7 a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit.@5
verse	40	7	19	@@@6Every tree that bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.@5
verse	40	7	20	@@@6Wherefore by their fruits ye shall know them.@5
verse	40	7	21	@@@6Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	7	22	@@@6Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name? and in thy name have cast out devils? and in thy name done many wonderful works?@5
verse	40	7	23	@@@6And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity.@5
verse	40	7	24	@@@6Therefore whosoever heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them, I will liken him unto a wise man, which built his house upon a rock:@5
verse	40	7	25	@@@6And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell not: for it was founded upon a rock.@5
verse	40	7	26	@@@6And every one that heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them not, shall be likened unto a foolish man, which built his house upon the sand:@5
verse	40	7	27	@@@6And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell: and great was the fall of it.@5
verse	40	7	28	And it came to pass, when Jesus had ended these sayings, the people were astonished at his doctrine:
verse	40	7	29	@@For he taught them as @9one@7 having authority, and not as the scribes.
verse	40	8	1	When he was come down from the mountain, great multitudes followed him.
verse	40	8	2	And, behold, there came a leper and worshipped him, saying, Lord, if thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.
verse	40	8	3	@@And Jesus put forth @9his@7 hand, and touched him, saying, @6I will; be thou clean.@5 And immediately his leprosy was cleansed.
verse	40	8	4	@@And Jesus saith unto him, @6See thou tell no man; but go thy way, shew thyself to the priest, and offer the gift that Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them.@5
verse	40	8	5	And when Jesus was entered into Capernaum, there came unto him a centurion, beseeching him,
verse	40	8	6	And saying, Lord, my servant lieth at home sick of the palsy, grievously tormented.
verse	40	8	7	@@And Jesus saith unto him, @6I will come and heal him.@5
verse	40	8	8	The centurion answered and said, Lord, I am not worthy that thou shouldest come under my roof: but speak the word only, and my servant shall be healed.
verse	40	8	9	@@For I am a man under authority, having soldiers under me: and I say to this @9man,@7 Go, and he goeth; and to another, Come, and he cometh; and to my servant, Do this, and he doeth @9it. @7
verse	40	8	10	@@When Jesus heard @9it,@7 he marvelled, and said to them that followed, @6Verily I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel.@5
verse	40	8	11	@@@6And I say unto you, That many shall come from the east and west, and shall sit down with Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, in the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	8	12	@@@6But the children of the kingdom shall be cast out into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.@5
verse	40	8	13	@@And Jesus said unto the centurion, @6Go thy way; and as thou hast believed, so be it done unto thee. And his servant was healed in the selfsame hour.@5
verse	40	8	14	And when Jesus was come into Peter's house, he saw his wife's mother laid, and sick of a fever.
verse	40	8	15	And he touched her hand, and the fever left her: and she arose, and ministered unto them.
verse	40	8	16	@@When the even was come, they brought unto him many that were possessed with devils: and he cast out the spirits with @9his@7 word, and healed all that were sick:
verse	40	8	17	@@That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying, Himself took our infirmities, and bare @9our@7 sicknesses.
verse	40	8	18	Now when Jesus saw great multitudes about him, he gave commandment to depart unto the other side.
verse	40	8	19	And a certain scribe came, and said unto him, Master, I will follow thee whithersoever thou goest.
verse	40	8	20	@@And Jesus saith unto him, @6The foxes have holes, and the birds of the air @9have@7 nests; but the Son of man hath not where to lay @9his@7 head.@5
verse	40	8	21	And another of his disciples said unto him, Lord, suffer me first to go and bury my father.
verse	40	8	22	@@But Jesus said unto him, @6Follow me; and let the dead bury their dead.@5
verse	40	8	23	And when he was entered into a ship, his disciples followed him.
verse	40	8	24	And, behold, there arose a great tempest in the sea, insomuch that the ship was covered with the waves: but he was asleep.
verse	40	8	25	@@And his disciples came to @9him,@7 and awoke him, saying, Lord, save us: we perish.
verse	40	8	26	@@And he saith unto them, @6Why are ye fearful, O ye of little faith? Then he arose, and rebuked the winds and the sea; and there was a great calm.@5
verse	40	8	27	But the men marvelled, saying, What manner of man is this, that even the winds and the sea obey him!
verse	40	8	28	And when he was come to the other side into the country of the Gergesenes, there met him two possessed with devils, coming out of the tombs, exceeding fierce, so that no man might pass by that way.
verse	40	8	29	And, behold, they cried out, saying, What have we to do with thee, Jesus, thou Son of God? art thou come hither to torment us before the time?
verse	40	8	30	And there was a good way off from them an herd of many swine feeding.
verse	40	8	31	So the devils besought him, saying, If thou cast us out, suffer us to go away into the herd of swine.
verse	40	8	32	@@And he said unto them, @6Go.@5 And when they were come out, they went into the herd of swine: and, behold, the whole herd of swine ran violently down a steep place into the sea, and perished in the waters.
verse	40	8	33	And they that kept them fled, and went their ways into the city, and told every thing, and what was befallen to the possessed of the devils.
verse	40	8	34	@@And, behold, the whole city came out to meet Jesus: and when they saw him, they besought @9him@7 that he would depart out of their coasts.
verse	40	9	1	And he entered into a ship, and passed over, and came into his own city.
verse	40	9	2	@@And, behold, they brought to him a man sick of the palsy, lying on a bed: and Jesus seeing their faith said unto the sick of the palsy; @6Son, be of good cheer; thy sins be forgiven thee.@5
verse	40	9	3	@@And, behold, certain of the scribes said within themselves, This @9man@7 blasphemeth.
verse	40	9	4	@@And Jesus knowing their thoughts said, @6Wherefore think ye evil in your hearts?@5
verse	40	9	5	@@@6For whether is easier, to say, @9Thy@7 sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Arise, and walk?@5
verse	40	9	6	@@@6But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins,@5 (then saith he to the sick of the palsy,) @6Arise, take up thy bed, and go unto thine house.@5
verse	40	9	7	And he arose, and departed to his house.
verse	40	9	8	@@But when the multitudes saw @9it,@7 they marvelled, and glorified God, which had given such power unto men.
verse	40	9	9	@@And as Jesus passed forth from thence, he saw a man, named Matthew, sitting at the receipt of custom: and he saith unto him, @6Follow me.@5 And he arose, and followed him.
verse	40	9	10	And it came to pass, as Jesus sat at meat in the house, behold, many publicans and sinners came and sat down with him and his disciples.
verse	40	9	11	@@And when the Pharisees saw @9it,@7 they said unto his disciples, Why eateth your Master with publicans and sinners?
verse	40	9	12	@@But when Jesus heard @9that,@7 he said unto them, @6They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick.@5
verse	40	9	13	@@@6But go ye and learn what @9that@7 meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice: for I am not come to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.@5
verse	40	9	14	Then came to him the disciples of John, saying, Why do we and the Pharisees fast oft, but thy disciples fast not?
verse	40	9	15	@@And Jesus said unto them, @6Can the children of the bridechamber mourn, as long as the bridegroom is with them? but the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken from them, and then shall they fast.@5
verse	40	9	16	@@@6No man putteth a piece of new cloth unto an old garment, for that which is put in to fill it up taketh from the garment, and the rent is made worse.@5
verse	40	9	17	@@@6Neither do men put new wine into old bottles: else the bottles break, and the wine runneth out, and the bottles perish: but they put new wine into new bottles, and both are preserved.@5
verse	40	9	18	While he spake these things unto them, behold, there came a certain ruler, and worshipped him, saying, My daughter is even now dead: but come and lay thy hand upon her, and she shall live.
verse	40	9	19	@@And Jesus arose, and followed him, and @9so did@7 his disciples.
verse	40	9	20	@@And, behold, a woman, which was diseased with an issue of blood twelve years, came behind @9him,@7 and touched the hem of his garment:
verse	40	9	21	For she said within herself, If I may but touch his garment, I shall be whole.
verse	40	9	22	@@But Jesus turned him about, and when he saw her, he said, @6Daughter, be of good comfort; thy faith hath made thee whole.@5 And the woman was made whole from that hour.
verse	40	9	23	And when Jesus came into the ruler's house, and saw the minstrels and the people making a noise,
verse	40	9	24	@@He said unto them, @6Give place: for the maid is not dead, but sleepeth.@5 And they laughed him to scorn.
verse	40	9	25	But when the people were put forth, he went in, and took her by the hand, and the maid arose.
verse	40	9	26	And the fame hereof went abroad into all that land.
verse	40	9	27	@@And when Jesus departed thence, two blind men followed him, crying, and saying, @9Thou@7 Son of David, have mercy on us.
verse	40	9	28	@@And when he was come into the house, the blind men came to him: and Jesus saith unto them, @6Believe ye that I am able to do this?@5 They said unto him, Yea, Lord.
verse	40	9	29	@@Then touched he their eyes, saying, @6According to your faith be it unto you.@5
verse	40	9	30	@@And their eyes were opened; and Jesus straitly charged them, saying, @6See @9that@7 no man know @9it. @7@5
verse	40	9	31	But they, when they were departed, spread abroad his fame in all that country.
verse	40	9	32	As they went out, behold, they brought to him a dumb man possessed with a devil.
verse	40	9	33	And when the devil was cast out, the dumb spake: and the multitudes marvelled, saying, It was never so seen in Israel.
verse	40	9	34	But the Pharisees said, He casteth out devils through the prince of the devils.
verse	40	9	35	And Jesus went about all the cities and villages, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every sickness and every disease among the people.
verse	40	9	36	But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.
verse	40	9	37	@@Then saith he unto his disciples, @6The harvest truly @9is@7 plenteous, but the labourers @9are@7 few;@5
verse	40	9	38	@@@6Pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest.@5
verse	40	10	1	@@And when he had called unto @9him@7 his twelve disciples, he gave them power @9against@7 unclean spirits, to cast them out, and to heal all manner of sickness and all manner of disease.
verse	40	10	2	@@Now the names of the twelve apostles are these; The first, Simon, who is called Peter, and Andrew his brother; James @9the son@7 of Zebedee, and John his brother;
verse	40	10	3	@@Philip, and Bartholomew; Thomas, and Matthew the publican; James @9the son@7 of Alphaeus, and Lebbaeus, whose surname was Thaddaeus;
verse	40	10	4	Simon the Canaanite, and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed him.
verse	40	10	5	@@These twelve Jesus sent forth, and commanded them, saying, @6Go not into the way of the Gentiles, and into @9any@7 city of the Samaritans enter ye not:@5
verse	40	10	6	@@@6But go rather to the lost sheep of the house of Israel.@5
verse	40	10	7	@@@6And as ye go, preach, saying, The kingdom of heaven is at hand.@5
verse	40	10	8	@@@6Heal the sick, cleanse the lepers, raise the dead, cast out devils: freely ye have received, freely give.@5
verse	40	10	9	@@@6Provide neither gold, nor silver, nor brass in your purses,@5
verse	40	10	10	@@@6Nor scrip for @9your@7 journey, neither two coats, neither shoes, nor yet staves: for the workman is worthy of his meat.@5
verse	40	10	11	@@@6And into whatsoever city or town ye shall enter, enquire who in it is worthy; and there abide till ye go thence.@5
verse	40	10	12	@@@6And when ye come into an house, salute it.@5
verse	40	10	13	@@@6And if the house be worthy, let your peace come upon it: but if it be not worthy, let your peace return to you.@5
verse	40	10	14	@@@6And whosoever shall not receive you, nor hear your words, when ye depart out of that house or city, shake off the dust of your feet.@5
verse	40	10	15	@@@6Verily I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom and Gomorrha in the day of judgment, than for that city.@5
verse	40	10	16	@@@6Behold, I send you forth as sheep in the midst of wolves: be ye therefore wise as serpents, and harmless as doves.@5
verse	40	10	17	@@@6But beware of men: for they will deliver you up to the councils, and they will scourge you in their synagogues;@5
verse	40	10	18	@@@6And ye shall be brought before governors and kings for my sake, for a testimony against them and the Gentiles.@5
verse	40	10	19	@@@6But when they deliver you up, take no thought how or what ye shall speak: for it shall be given you in that same hour what ye shall speak.@5
verse	40	10	20	@@@6For it is not ye that speak, but the Spirit of your Father which speaketh in you.@5
verse	40	10	21	@@@6And the brother shall deliver up the brother to death, and the father the child: and the children shall rise up against @9their@7 parents, and cause them to be put to death.@5
verse	40	10	22	@@@6And ye shall be hated of all @9men@7 for my name's sake: but he that endureth to the end shall be saved.@5
verse	40	10	23	@@@6But when they persecute you in this city, flee ye into another: for verily I say unto you, Ye shall not have gone over the cities of Israel, till the Son of man be come.@5
verse	40	10	24	@@@6The disciple is not above @9his@7 master, nor the servant above his lord.@5
verse	40	10	25	@@@6It is enough for the disciple that he be as his master, and the servant as his lord. If they have called the master of the house Beelzebub, how much more @9shall they call@7 them of his household?@5
verse	40	10	26	@@@6Fear them not therefore: for there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed; and hid, that shall not be known.@5
verse	40	10	27	@@@6What I tell you in darkness, @9that@7 speak ye in light: and what ye hear in the ear, @9that@7 preach ye upon the housetops.@5
verse	40	10	28	@@@6And fear not them which kill the body, but are not able to kill the soul: but rather fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.@5
verse	40	10	29	@@@6Are not two sparrows sold for a farthing? and one of them shall not fall on the ground without your Father.@5
verse	40	10	30	@@@6But the very hairs of your head are all numbered.@5
verse	40	10	31	@@@6Fear ye not therefore, ye are of more value than many sparrows.@5
verse	40	10	32	@@@6Whosoever therefore shall confess me before men, him will I confess also before my Father which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	10	33	@@@6But whosoever shall deny me before men, him will I also deny before my Father which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	10	34	@@@6Think not that I am come to send peace on earth: I came not to send peace, but a sword.@5
verse	40	10	35	@@@6For I am come to set a man at variance against his father, and the daughter against her mother, and the daughter in law against her mother in law.@5
verse	40	10	36	@@@6And a man's foes @9shall be@7 they of his own household.@5
verse	40	10	37	@@@6He that loveth father or mother more than me is not worthy of me: and he that loveth son or daughter more than me is not worthy of me.@5
verse	40	10	38	@@@6And he that taketh not his cross, and followeth after me, is not worthy of me.@5
verse	40	10	39	@@@6He that findeth his life shall lose it: and he that loseth his life for my sake shall find it.@5
verse	40	10	40	@@@6He that receiveth you receiveth me, and he that receiveth me receiveth him that sent me.@5
verse	40	10	41	@@@6He that receiveth a prophet in the name of a prophet shall receive a prophet's reward; and he that receiveth a righteous man in the name of a righteous man shall receive a righteous man's reward.@5
verse	40	10	42	@@@6And whosoever shall give to drink unto one of these little ones a cup of cold @9water@7 only in the name of a disciple, verily I say unto you, he shall in no wise lose his reward.@5
verse	40	11	1	And it came to pass, when Jesus had made an end of commanding his twelve disciples, he departed thence to teach and to preach in their cities.
verse	40	11	2	Now when John had heard in the prison the works of Christ, he sent two of his disciples,
verse	40	11	3	And said unto him, Art thou he that should come, or do we look for another?
verse	40	11	4	@@Jesus answered and said unto them, @6Go and shew John again those things which ye do hear and see:@5
verse	40	11	5	@@@6The blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, the dead are raised up, and the poor have the gospel preached to them.@5
verse	40	11	6	@@@6And blessed is @9he,@7 whosoever shall not be offended in me.@5
verse	40	11	7	@@And as they departed, Jesus began to say unto the multitudes concerning John, @6What went ye out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken with the wind?@5
verse	40	11	8	@@@6But what went ye out for to see? A man clothed in soft raiment? behold, they that wear soft @9clothing@7 are in kings' houses.@5
verse	40	11	9	@@@6But what went ye out for to see? A prophet? yea, I say unto you, and more than a prophet.@5
verse	40	11	10	@@@6For this is @9he,@7 of whom it is written, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, which shall prepare thy way before thee.@5
verse	40	11	11	@@@6Verily I say unto you, Among them that are born of women there hath not risen a greater than John the Baptist: notwithstanding he that is least in the kingdom of heaven is greater than he.@5
verse	40	11	12	@@@6And from the days of John the Baptist until now the kingdom of heaven suffereth violence, and the violent take it by force.@5
verse	40	11	13	@@@6For all the prophets and the law prophesied until John.@5
verse	40	11	14	@@@6And if ye will receive @9it,@7 this is Elias, which was for to come.@5
verse	40	11	15	@@@6He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.@5
verse	40	11	16	@@@6But whereunto shall I liken this generation? It is like unto children sitting in the markets, and calling unto their fellows,@5
verse	40	11	17	@@@6And saying, We have piped unto you, and ye have not danced; we have mourned unto you, and ye have not lamented.@5
verse	40	11	18	@@@6For John came neither eating nor drinking, and they say, He hath a devil.@5
verse	40	11	19	@@@6The Son of man came eating and drinking, and they say, Behold a man gluttonous, and a winebibber, a friend of publicans and sinners. But wisdom is justified of her children.@5
verse	40	11	20	Then began he to upbraid the cities wherein most of his mighty works were done, because they repented not:
verse	40	11	21	@@@6Woe unto thee, Chorazin! woe unto thee, Bethsaida! for if the mighty works, which were done in you, had been done in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes.@5
verse	40	11	22	@@@6But I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon at the day of judgment, than for you.@5
verse	40	11	23	@@@6And thou, Capernaum, which art exalted unto heaven, shalt be brought down to hell: for if the mighty works, which have been done in thee, had been done in Sodom, it would have remained until this day.@5
verse	40	11	24	@@@6But I say unto you, That it shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom in the day of judgment, than for thee.@5
verse	40	11	25	@@At that time Jesus answered and said, @6I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes.@5
verse	40	11	26	@@@6Even so, Father: for so it seemed good in thy sight.@5
verse	40	11	27	@@@6All things are delivered unto me of my Father: and no man knoweth the Son, but the Father; neither knoweth any man the Father, save the Son, and @9he@7 to whomsoever the Son will reveal @9him.@7@5
verse	40	11	28	@@@6Come unto me, all @9ye@7 that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.@5
verse	40	11	29	@@@6Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.@5
verse	40	11	30	@@@6For my yoke @9is@7 easy, and my burden is light.@5
verse	40	12	1	At that time Jesus went on the sabbath day through the corn; and his disciples were an hungred, and began to pluck the ears of corn, and to eat.
verse	40	12	2	@@But when the Pharisees saw @9it,@7 they said unto him, Behold, thy disciples do that which is not lawful to do upon the sabbath day.
verse	40	12	3	@@But he said unto them, @6Have ye not read what David did, when he was an hungred, and they that were with him;@5
verse	40	12	4	@@@6How he entered into the house of God, and did eat the shewbread, which was not lawful for him to eat, neither for them which were with him, but only for the priests?@5
verse	40	12	5	@@@6Or have ye not read in the law, how that on the sabbath days the priests in the temple profane the sabbath, and are blameless?@5
verse	40	12	6	@@@6But I say unto you, That in this place is @9one@7 greater than the temple.@5
verse	40	12	7	@@@6But if ye had known what @9this@7 meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice, ye would not have condemned the guiltless.@5
verse	40	12	8	@@@6For the Son of man is Lord even of the sabbath day.@5
verse	40	12	9	And when he was departed thence, he went into their synagogue:
verse	40	12	10	@@And, behold, there was a man which had @9his@7 hand withered. And they asked him, saying, Is it lawful to heal on the sabbath days? that they might accuse him.
verse	40	12	11	@@And he said unto them, @6What man shall there be among you, that shall have one sheep, and if it fall into a pit on the sabbath day, will he not lay hold on it, and lift @9it@7 out?@5
verse	40	12	12	@@@6How much then is a man better than a sheep? Wherefore it is lawful to do well on the sabbath days.@5
verse	40	12	13	@@Then saith he to the man, @6Stretch forth thine hand.@5 And he stretched @9it@7 forth; and it was restored whole, like as the other.
verse	40	12	14	Then the Pharisees went out, and held a council against him, how they might destroy him.
verse	40	12	15	@@But when Jesus knew @9it,@7 he withdrew himself from thence: and great multitudes followed him, and he healed them all;
verse	40	12	16	And charged them that they should not make him known:
verse	40	12	17	That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying,
verse	40	12	18	Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him, and he shall shew judgment to the Gentiles.
verse	40	12	19	He shall not strive, nor cry; neither shall any man hear his voice in the streets.
verse	40	12	20	A bruised reed shall he not break, and smoking flax shall he not quench, till he send forth judgment unto victory.
verse	40	12	21	And in his name shall the Gentiles trust.
verse	40	12	22	Then was brought unto him one possessed with a devil, blind, and dumb: and he healed him, insomuch that the blind and dumb both spake and saw.
verse	40	12	23	And all the people were amazed, and said, Is not this the son of David?
verse	40	12	24	@@But when the Pharisees heard @9it,@7 they said, This @9fellow@7 doth not cast out devils, but by Beelzebub the prince of the devils.
verse	40	12	25	@@And Jesus knew their thoughts, and said unto them, @6Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation; and every city or house divided against itself shall not stand:@5
verse	40	12	26	@@@6And if Satan cast out Satan, he is divided against himself; how shall then his kingdom stand?@5
verse	40	12	27	@@@6And if I by Beelzebub cast out devils, by whom do your children cast @9them@7 out? therefore they shall be your judges.@5
verse	40	12	28	@@@6But if I cast out devils by the Spirit of God, then the kingdom of God is come unto you.@5
verse	40	12	29	@@@6Or else how can one enter into a strong man's house, and spoil his goods, except he first bind the strong man? and then he will spoil his house.@5
verse	40	12	30	@@@6He that is not with me is against me; and he that gathereth not with me scattereth abroad.@5
verse	40	12	31	@@@6Wherefore I say unto you, All manner of sin and blasphemy shall be forgiven unto men: but the blasphemy @9against@7 the @9Holy@7 Ghost shall not be forgiven unto men.@5
verse	40	12	32	@@@6And whosoever speaketh a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him: but whosoever speaketh against the Holy Ghost, it shall not be forgiven him, neither in this world, neither in the @9world@7 to come.@5
verse	40	12	33	@@@6Either make the tree good, and his fruit good; or else make the tree corrupt, and his fruit corrupt: for the tree is known by @9his@7 fruit.@5
verse	40	12	34	@@@6O generation of vipers, how can ye, being evil, speak good things? for out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.@5
verse	40	12	35	@@@6A good man out of the good treasure of the heart bringeth forth good things: and an evil man out of the evil treasure bringeth forth evil things.@5
verse	40	12	36	@@@6But I say unto you, That every idle word that men shall speak, they shall give account thereof in the day of judgment.@5
verse	40	12	37	@@@6For by thy words thou shalt be justified, and by thy words thou shalt be condemned.@5
verse	40	12	38	Then certain of the scribes and of the Pharisees answered, saying, Master, we would see a sign from thee.
verse	40	12	39	@@But he answered and said unto them, @6An evil and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given to it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas:@5
verse	40	12	40	@@@6For as Jonas was three days and three nights in the whale's belly; so shall the Son of man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.@5
verse	40	12	41	@@@6The men of Nineveh shall rise in judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: because they repented at the preaching of Jonas; and, behold, a greater than Jonas @9is@7 here.@5
verse	40	12	42	@@@6The queen of the south shall rise up in the judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: for she came from the uttermost parts of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and, behold, a greater than Solomon @9is@7 here.@5
verse	40	12	43	@@@6When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking rest, and findeth none.@5
verse	40	12	44	@@@6Then he saith, I will return into my house from whence I came out; and when he is come, he findeth @9it@7 empty, swept, and garnished.@5
verse	40	12	45	@@@6Then goeth he, and taketh with himself seven other spirits more wicked than himself, and they enter in and dwell there: and the last @9state@7 of that man is worse than the first. Even so shall it be also unto this wicked generation.@5
verse	40	12	46	@@While he yet talked to the people, behold, @9his@7 mother and his brethren stood without, desiring to speak with him.
verse	40	12	47	Then one said unto him, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren stand without, desiring to speak with thee.
verse	40	12	48	@@But he answered and said unto him that told him, @6Who is my mother? and who are my brethren?@5
verse	40	12	49	@@And he stretched forth his hand toward his disciples, and said, @6Behold my mother and my brethren!@5
verse	40	12	50	@@@6For whosoever shall do the will of my Father which is in heaven, the same is my brother, and sister, and mother.@5
verse	40	13	1	The same day went Jesus out of the house, and sat by the sea side.
verse	40	13	2	And great multitudes were gathered together unto him, so that he went into a ship, and sat; and the whole multitude stood on the shore.
verse	40	13	3	@@And he spake many things unto them in parables, saying, @6Behold, a sower went forth to sow;@5
verse	40	13	4	@@@6And when he sowed, some @9seeds@7 fell by the way side, and the fowls came and devoured them up:@5
verse	40	13	5	@@@6Some fell upon stony places, where they had not much earth: and forthwith they sprung up, because they had no deepness of earth:@5
verse	40	13	6	@@@6And when the sun was up, they were scorched; and because they had no root, they withered away.@5
verse	40	13	7	@@@6And some fell among thorns; and the thorns sprung up, and choked them:@5
verse	40	13	8	@@@6But other fell into good ground, and brought forth fruit, some an hundredfold, some sixtyfold, some thirtyfold.@5
verse	40	13	9	@@@6Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.@5
verse	40	13	10	And the disciples came, and said unto him, Why speakest thou unto them in parables?
verse	40	13	11	@@He answered and said unto them, @6Because it is given unto you to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to them it is not given.@5
verse	40	13	12	@@@6For whosoever hath, to him shall be given, and he shall have more abundance: but whosoever hath not, from him shall be taken away even that he hath.@5
verse	40	13	13	@@@6Therefore speak I to them in parables: because they seeing see not; and hearing they hear not, neither do they understand.@5
verse	40	13	14	@@@6And in them is fulfilled the prophecy of Esaias, which saith, By hearing ye shall hear, and shall not understand; and seeing ye shall see, and shall not perceive:@5
verse	40	13	15	@@@6For this people's heart is waxed gross, and @9their@7 ears are dull of hearing, and their eyes they have closed; lest at any time they should see with @9their@7 eyes, and hear with @9their@7 ears, and should understand with @9their@7 heart, and should be converted, and I should heal them.@5
verse	40	13	16	@@@6But blessed @9are@7 your eyes, for they see: and your ears, for they hear.@5
verse	40	13	17	@@@6For verily I say unto you, That many prophets and righteous @9men@7 have desired to see @9those things@7 which ye see, and have not seen @9them;@7 and to hear @9those things@7 which ye hear, and have not heard @9them.@7@5
verse	40	13	18	@@@6Hear ye therefore the parable of the sower.@5
verse	40	13	19	@@@6When any one heareth the word of the kingdom, and understandeth @9it@7 not, then cometh the wicked @9one,@7 and catcheth away that which was sown in his heart. This is he which received seed by the way side.@5
verse	40	13	20	@@@6But he that received the seed into stony places, the same is he that heareth the word, and anon with joy receiveth it;@5
verse	40	13	21	@@@6Yet hath he not root in himself, but dureth for a while: for when tribulation or persecution ariseth because of the word, by and by he is offended.@5
verse	40	13	22	@@@6He also that received seed among the thorns is he that heareth the word; and the care of this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, choke the word, and he becometh unfruitful.@5
verse	40	13	23	@@@6But he that received seed into the good ground is he that heareth the word, and understandeth @9it;@7 which also beareth fruit, and bringeth forth, some an hundredfold, some sixty, some thirty.@5
verse	40	13	24	@@Another parable put he forth unto them, saying, @6The kingdom of heaven is likened unto a man which sowed good seed in his field:@5
verse	40	13	25	@@@6But while men slept, his enemy came and sowed tares among the wheat, and went his way.@5
verse	40	13	26	@@@6But when the blade was sprung up, and brought forth fruit, then appeared the tares also.@5
verse	40	13	27	@@@6So the servants of the householder came and said unto him, Sir, didst not thou sow good seed in thy field? from whence then hath it tares?@5
verse	40	13	28	@@@6He said unto them, An enemy hath done this. The servants said unto him, Wilt thou then that we go and gather them up?@5
verse	40	13	29	@@@6But he said, Nay; lest while ye gather up the tares, ye root up also the wheat with them.@5
verse	40	13	30	@@@6Let both grow together until the harvest: and in the time of harvest I will say to the reapers, Gather ye together first the tares, and bind them in bundles to burn them: but gather the wheat into my barn.@5
verse	40	13	31	@@Another parable put he forth unto them, saying, @6The kingdom of heaven is like to a grain of mustard seed, which a man took, and sowed in his field:@5
verse	40	13	32	@@@6Which indeed is the least of all seeds: but when it is grown, it is the greatest among herbs, and becometh a tree, so that the birds of the air come and lodge in the branches thereof.@5
verse	40	13	33	@@Another parable spake he unto them; @6The kingdom of heaven is like unto leaven, which a woman took, and hid in three measures of meal, till the whole was leavened.@5
verse	40	13	34	All these things spake Jesus unto the multitude in parables; and without a parable spake he not unto them:
verse	40	13	35	That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying, I will open my mouth in parables; I will utter things which have been kept secret from the foundation of the world.
verse	40	13	36	Then Jesus sent the multitude away, and went into the house: and his disciples came unto him, saying, Declare unto us the parable of the tares of the field.
verse	40	13	37	@@He answered and said unto them, @6He that soweth the good seed is the Son of man;@5
verse	40	13	38	@@@6The field is the world; the good seed are the children of the kingdom; but the tares are the children of the wicked @9one; @7@5
verse	40	13	39	@@@6The enemy that sowed them is the devil; the harvest is the end of the world; and the reapers are the angels.@5
verse	40	13	40	@@@6As therefore the tares are gathered and burned in the fire; so shall it be in the end of this world.@5
verse	40	13	41	@@@6The Son of man shall send forth his angels, and they shall gather out of his kingdom all things that offend, and them which do iniquity;@5
verse	40	13	42	@@@6And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.@5
verse	40	13	43	@@@6Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.@5
verse	40	13	44	@@@6Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto treasure hid in a field; the which when a man hath found, he hideth, and for joy thereof goeth and selleth all that he hath, and buyeth that field.@5
verse	40	13	45	@@@6Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto a merchant man, seeking goodly pearls:@5
verse	40	13	46	@@@6Who, when he had found one pearl of great price, went and sold all that he had, and bought it.@5
verse	40	13	47	@@@6Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto a net, that was cast into the sea, and gathered of every kind:@5
verse	40	13	48	@@@6Which, when it was full, they drew to shore, and sat down, and gathered the good into vessels, but cast the bad away.@5
verse	40	13	49	@@@6So shall it be at the end of the world: the angels shall come forth, and sever the wicked from among the just,@5
verse	40	13	50	@@@6And shall cast them into the furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.@5
verse	40	13	51	@@Jesus saith unto them, @6Have ye understood all these things?@5 They say unto him, Yea, Lord.
verse	40	13	52	@@Then said he unto them, @6Therefore every scribe @9which is@7 instructed unto the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man @9that is@7 an householder, which bringeth forth out of his treasure @9things@7 new and old.@5
verse	40	13	53	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 when Jesus had finished these parables, he departed thence.
verse	40	13	54	@@And when he was come into his own country, he taught them in their synagogue, insomuch that they were astonished, and said, Whence hath this @9man@7 this wisdom, and @9these@7 mighty works?
verse	40	13	55	Is not this the carpenter's son? is not his mother called Mary? and his brethren, James, and Joses, and Simon, and Judas?
verse	40	13	56	@@And his sisters, are they not all with us? Whence then hath this @9man@7 all these things?
verse	40	13	57	@@And they were offended in him. But Jesus said unto them, @6A prophet is not without honour, save in his own country, and in his own house.@5
verse	40	13	58	And he did not many mighty works there because of their unbelief.
verse	40	14	1	At that time Herod the tetrarch heard of the fame of Jesus,
verse	40	14	2	And said unto his servants, This is John the Baptist; he is risen from the dead; and therefore mighty works do shew forth themselves in him.
verse	40	14	3	@@For Herod had laid hold on John, and bound him, and put @9him@7 in prison for Herodias' sake, his brother Philip's wife.
verse	40	14	4	For John said unto him, It is not lawful for thee to have her.
verse	40	14	5	And when he would have put him to death, he feared the multitude, because they counted him as a prophet.
verse	40	14	6	But when Herod's birthday was kept, the daughter of Herodias danced before them, and pleased Herod.
verse	40	14	7	Whereupon he promised with an oath to give her whatsoever she would ask.
verse	40	14	8	And she, being before instructed of her mother, said, Give me here John Baptist's head in a charger.
verse	40	14	9	@@And the king was sorry: nevertheless for the oath's sake, and them which sat with him at meat, he commanded @9it@7 to be given @9her. @7
verse	40	14	10	And he sent, and beheaded John in the prison.
verse	40	14	11	@@And his head was brought in a charger, and given to the damsel: and she brought @9it@7 to her mother.
verse	40	14	12	And his disciples came, and took up the body, and buried it, and went and told Jesus.
verse	40	14	13	@@When Jesus heard @9of it,@7 he departed thence by ship into a desert place apart: and when the people had heard @9thereof,@7 they followed him on foot out of the cities.
verse	40	14	14	And Jesus went forth, and saw a great multitude, and was moved with compassion toward them, and he healed their sick.
verse	40	14	15	And when it was evening, his disciples came to him, saying, This is a desert place, and the time is now past; send the multitude away, that they may go into the villages, and buy themselves victuals.
verse	40	14	16	@@But Jesus said unto them, @6They need not depart; give ye them to eat.@5
verse	40	14	17	And they say unto him, We have here but five loaves, and two fishes.
verse	40	14	18	@@He said, @6Bring them hither to me.@5
verse	40	14	19	@@And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the grass, and took the five loaves, and the two fishes, and looking up to heaven, he blessed, and brake, and gave the loaves to @9his@7 disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.
verse	40	14	20	And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the fragments that remained twelve baskets full.
verse	40	14	21	And they that had eaten were about five thousand men, beside women and children.
verse	40	14	22	And straightway Jesus constrained his disciples to get into a ship, and to go before him unto the other side, while he sent the multitudes away.
verse	40	14	23	And when he had sent the multitudes away, he went up into a mountain apart to pray: and when the evening was come, he was there alone.
verse	40	14	24	But the ship was now in the midst of the sea, tossed with waves: for the wind was contrary.
verse	40	14	25	And in the fourth watch of the night Jesus went unto them, walking on the sea.
verse	40	14	26	And when the disciples saw him walking on the sea, they were troubled, saying, It is a spirit; and they cried out for fear.
verse	40	14	27	@@But straightway Jesus spake unto them, saying, @6Be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid.@5
verse	40	14	28	And Peter answered him and said, Lord, if it be thou, bid me come unto thee on the water.
verse	40	14	29	@@And he said, @6Come.@5 And when Peter was come down out of the ship, he walked on the water, to go to Jesus.
verse	40	14	30	But when he saw the wind boisterous, he was afraid; and beginning to sink, he cried, saying, Lord, save me.
verse	40	14	31	@@And immediately Jesus stretched forth @9his@7 hand, and caught him, and said unto him, @6O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?@5
verse	40	14	32	And when they were come into the ship, the wind ceased.
verse	40	14	33	Then they that were in the ship came and worshipped him, saying, Of a truth thou art the Son of God.
verse	40	14	34	And when they were gone over, they came into the land of Gennesaret.
verse	40	14	35	And when the men of that place had knowledge of him, they sent out into all that country round about, and brought unto him all that were diseased;
verse	40	14	36	And besought him that they might only touch the hem of his garment: and as many as touched were made perfectly whole.
verse	40	15	1	Then came to Jesus scribes and Pharisees, which were of Jerusalem, saying,
verse	40	15	2	Why do thy disciples transgress the tradition of the elders? for they wash not their hands when they eat bread.
verse	40	15	3	@@But he answered and said unto them, @6Why do ye also transgress the commandment of God by your tradition?@5
verse	40	15	4	@@@6For God commanded, saying, Honour thy father and mother: and, He that curseth father or mother, let him die the death.@5
verse	40	15	5	@@@6But ye say, Whosoever shall say to @9his@7 father or @9his@7 mother, @9It is@7 a gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be profited by me;@5
verse	40	15	6	@@@6And honour not his father or his mother, @9he shall be free.@7 Thus have ye made the commandment of God of none effect by your tradition.@5
verse	40	15	7	@@@6@9Ye@7 hypocrites, well did Esaias prophesy of you, saying,@5
verse	40	15	8	@@@6This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with @9their@7 lips; but their heart is far from me.@5
verse	40	15	9	@@@6But in vain they do worship me, teaching @9for@7 doctrines the commandments of men.@5
verse	40	15	10	@@And he called the multitude, and said unto them, @6Hear, and understand:@5
verse	40	15	11	@@@6Not that which goeth into the mouth defileth a man; but that which cometh out of the mouth, this defileth a man.@5
verse	40	15	12	Then came his disciples, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the Pharisees were offended, after they heard this saying?
verse	40	15	13	@@But he answered and said, @6Every plant, which my heavenly Father hath not planted, shall be rooted up.@5
verse	40	15	14	@@@6Let them alone: they be blind leaders of the blind. And if the blind lead the blind, both shall fall into the ditch.@5
verse	40	15	15	Then answered Peter and said unto him, Declare unto us this parable.
verse	40	15	16	@@And Jesus said, @6Are ye also yet without understanding?@5
verse	40	15	17	@@@6Do not ye yet understand, that whatsoever entereth in at the mouth goeth into the belly, and is cast out into the draught?@5
verse	40	15	18	@@@6But those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart; and they defile the man.@5
verse	40	15	19	@@@6For out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts, false witness, blasphemies:@5
verse	40	15	20	@@@6These are @9the things@7 which defile a man: but to eat with unwashen hands defileth not a man.@5
verse	40	15	21	Then Jesus went thence, and departed into the coasts of Tyre and Sidon.
verse	40	15	22	@@And, behold, a woman of Canaan came out of the same coasts, and cried unto him, saying, Have mercy on me, O Lord, @9thou@7 Son of David; my daughter is grievously vexed with a devil.
verse	40	15	23	But he answered her not a word. And his disciples came and besought him, saying, Send her away; for she crieth after us.
verse	40	15	24	@@But he answered and said, @6I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel.@5
verse	40	15	25	Then came she and worshipped him, saying, Lord, help me.
verse	40	15	26	@@But he answered and said, @6It is not meet to take the children's bread, and to cast @9it@7 to dogs.@5
verse	40	15	27	And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the dogs eat of the crumbs which fall from their masters' table.
verse	40	15	28	@@Then Jesus answered and said unto her, @6O woman, great @9is@7 thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt. And her daughter was made whole from that very hour.@5
verse	40	15	29	And Jesus departed from thence, and came nigh unto the sea of Galilee; and went up into a mountain, and sat down there.
verse	40	15	30	@@And great multitudes came unto him, having with them @9those that were@7 lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many others, and cast them down at Jesus' feet; and he healed them:
verse	40	15	31	Insomuch that the multitude wondered, when they saw the dumb to speak, the maimed to be whole, the lame to walk, and the blind to see: and they glorified the God of Israel.
verse	40	15	32	@@Then Jesus called his disciples @9unto him,@7 and said, @6I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way.@5
verse	40	15	33	And his disciples say unto him, Whence should we have so much bread in the wilderness, as to fill so great a multitude?
verse	40	15	34	@@And Jesus saith unto them, @6How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes.@5
verse	40	15	35	And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground.
verse	40	15	36	@@And he took the seven loaves and the fishes, and gave thanks, and brake @9them,@7 and gave to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.
verse	40	15	37	@@And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken @9meat@7 that was left seven baskets full.
verse	40	15	38	And they that did eat were four thousand men, beside women and children.
verse	40	15	39	And he sent away the multitude, and took ship, and came into the coasts of Magdala.
verse	40	16	1	The Pharisees also with the Sadducees came, and tempting desired him that he would shew them a sign from heaven.
verse	40	16	2	@@He answered and said unto them, @6When it is evening, ye say, @9It will be@7 fair weather: for the sky is red.@5
verse	40	16	3	@@@6And in the morning, @9It will be@7 foul weather to day: for the sky is red and lowring. O @9ye@7 hypocrites, ye can discern the face of the sky; but can ye not @9discern@7 the signs of the times?@5
verse	40	16	4	@@@6A wicked and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given unto it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas.@5 And he left them, and departed.
verse	40	16	5	And when his disciples were come to the other side, they had forgotten to take bread.
verse	40	16	6	@@Then Jesus said unto them, @6Take heed and beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees.@5
verse	40	16	7	@@And they reasoned among themselves, saying, @9It is@7 because we have taken no bread.
verse	40	16	8	@@@9Which@7 when Jesus perceived, he said unto them, @6O ye of little faith, why reason ye among yourselves, because ye have brought no bread?@5
verse	40	16	9	@@@6Do ye not yet understand, neither remember the five loaves of the five thousand, and how many baskets ye took up?@5
verse	40	16	10	@@@6Neither the seven loaves of the four thousand, and how many baskets ye took up?@5
verse	40	16	11	@@@6How is it that ye do not understand that I spake @9it@7 not to you concerning bread, that ye should beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees?@5
verse	40	16	12	@@Then understood they how that he bade @9them@7 not beware of the leaven of bread, but of the doctrine of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees.
verse	40	16	13	@@When Jesus came into the coasts of Caesarea Philippi, he asked his disciples, saying, @6Whom do men say that I the Son of man am?@5
verse	40	16	14	@@And they said, Some @9say that thou art@7 John the Baptist: some, Elias; and others, Jeremias, or one of the prophets.
verse	40	16	15	@@He saith unto them, @6But whom say ye that I am?@5
verse	40	16	16	And Simon Peter answered and said, Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God.
verse	40	16	17	@@And Jesus answered and said unto him, @6Blessed art thou, Simon Barjona: for flesh and blood hath not revealed @9it@7 unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	16	18	@@@6And I say also unto thee, That thou art Peter, and upon this rock I will build my church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.@5
verse	40	16	19	@@@6And I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.@5
verse	40	16	20	Then charged he his disciples that they should tell no man that he was Jesus the Christ.
verse	40	16	21	From that time forth began Jesus to shew unto his disciples, how that he must go unto Jerusalem, and suffer many things of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be killed, and be raised again the third day.
verse	40	16	22	Then Peter took him, and began to rebuke him, saying, Be it far from thee, Lord: this shall not be unto thee.
verse	40	16	23	@@But he turned, and said unto Peter, @6Get thee behind me, Satan: thou art an offence unto me: for thou savourest not the things that be of God, but those that be of men.@5
verse	40	16	24	@@Then said Jesus unto his disciples, @6If any @9man@7 will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.@5
verse	40	16	25	@@@6For whosoever will save his life shall lose it: and whosoever will lose his life for my sake shall find it.@5
verse	40	16	26	@@@6For what is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul? or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?@5
verse	40	16	27	@@@6For the Son of man shall come in the glory of his Father with his angels; and then he shall reward every man according to his works.@5
verse	40	16	28	@@@6Verily I say unto you, There be some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the Son of man coming in his kingdom.@5
verse	40	17	1	And after six days Jesus taketh Peter, James, and John his brother, and bringeth them up into an high mountain apart,
verse	40	17	2	And was transfigured before them: and his face did shine as the sun, and his raiment was white as the light.
verse	40	17	3	And, behold, there appeared unto them Moses and Elias talking with him.
verse	40	17	4	Then answered Peter, and said unto Jesus, Lord, it is good for us to be here: if thou wilt, let us make here three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias.
verse	40	17	5	While he yet spake, behold, a bright cloud overshadowed them: and behold a voice out of the cloud, which said, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; hear ye him.
verse	40	17	6	@@And when the disciples heard @9it,@7 they fell on their face, and were sore afraid.
verse	40	17	7	@@And Jesus came and touched them, and said, @6Arise, and be not afraid.@5
verse	40	17	8	And when they had lifted up their eyes, they saw no man, save Jesus only.
verse	40	17	9	@@And as they came down from the mountain, Jesus charged them, saying, @6Tell the vision to no man, until the Son of man be risen again from the dead.@5
verse	40	17	10	And his disciples asked him, saying, Why then say the scribes that Elias must first come?
verse	40	17	11	@@And Jesus answered and said unto them, @6Elias truly shall first come, and restore all things.@5
verse	40	17	12	@@@6But I say unto you, That Elias is come already, and they knew him not, but have done unto him whatsoever they listed. Likewise shall also the Son of man suffer of them.@5
verse	40	17	13	Then the disciples understood that he spake unto them of John the Baptist.
verse	40	17	14	@@And when they were come to the multitude, there came to him a @9certain@7 man, kneeling down to him, and saying,
verse	40	17	15	Lord, have mercy on my son: for he is lunatick, and sore vexed: for ofttimes he falleth into the fire, and oft into the water.
verse	40	17	16	And I brought him to thy disciples, and they could not cure him.
verse	40	17	17	@@Then Jesus answered and said, @6O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you? how long shall I suffer you? bring him hither to me.@5
verse	40	17	18	And Jesus rebuked the devil; and he departed out of him: and the child was cured from that very hour.
verse	40	17	19	Then came the disciples to Jesus apart, and said, Why could not we cast him out?
verse	40	17	20	@@And Jesus said unto them, @6Because of your unbelief: for verily I say unto you, If ye have faith as a grain of mustard seed, ye shall say unto this mountain, Remove hence to yonder place; and it shall remove; and nothing shall be impossible unto you.@5
verse	40	17	21	@@@6Howbeit this kind goeth not out but by prayer and fasting.@5
verse	40	17	22	@@And while they abode in Galilee, Jesus said unto them, @6The Son of man shall be betrayed into the hands of men:@5
verse	40	17	23	@@And they shall kill him, and the third day he shall be raised again. @6And they were exceeding sorry.@5
verse	40	17	24	@@And when they were come to Capernaum, they that received tribute @9money@7 came to Peter, and said, Doth not your master pay tribute?
verse	40	17	25	@@He saith, Yes. And when he was come into the house, Jesus prevented him, saying, @6What thinkest thou, Simon? of whom do the kings of the earth take custom or tribute? of their own children, or of strangers?@5
verse	40	17	26	@@Peter saith unto him, Of strangers. Jesus saith unto him, @6Then are the children free.@5
verse	40	17	27	@@@6Notwithstanding, lest we should offend them, go thou to the sea, and cast an hook, and take up the fish that first cometh up; and when thou hast opened his mouth, thou shalt find a piece of money: that take, and give unto them for me and thee.@5
verse	40	18	1	At the same time came the disciples unto Jesus, saying, Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?
verse	40	18	2	And Jesus called a little child unto him, and set him in the midst of them,
verse	40	18	3	@@And said, @6Verily I say unto you, Except ye be converted, and become as little children, ye shall not enter into the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	18	4	@@@6Whosoever therefore shall humble himself as this little child, the same is greatest in the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	18	5	@@@6And whoso shall receive one such little child in my name receiveth me.@5
verse	40	18	6	@@@6But whoso shall offend one of these little ones which believe in me, it were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and @9that@7 he were drowned in the depth of the sea.@5
verse	40	18	7	@@@6Woe unto the world because of offences! for it must needs be that offences come; but woe to that man by whom the offence cometh!@5
verse	40	18	8	@@@6Wherefore if thy hand or thy foot offend thee, cut them off, and cast @9them@7 from thee: it is better for thee to enter into life halt or maimed, rather than having two hands or two feet to be cast into everlasting fire.@5
verse	40	18	9	@@@6And if thine eye offend thee, pluck it out, and cast @9it@7 from thee: it is better for thee to enter into life with one eye, rather than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire.@5
verse	40	18	10	@@@6Take heed that ye despise not one of these little ones; for I say unto you, That in heaven their angels do always behold the face of my Father which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	18	11	@@@6For the Son of man is come to save that which was lost.@5
verse	40	18	12	@@@6How think ye? if a man have an hundred sheep, and one of them be gone astray, doth he not leave the ninety and nine, and goeth into the mountains, and seeketh that which is gone astray?@5
verse	40	18	13	@@@6And if so be that he find it, verily I say unto you, he rejoiceth more of that @9sheep,@7 than of the ninety and nine which went not astray.@5
verse	40	18	14	@@@6Even so it is not the will of your Father which is in heaven, that one of these little ones should perish.@5
verse	40	18	15	@@@6Moreover if thy brother shall trespass against thee, go and tell him his fault between thee and him alone: if he shall hear thee, thou hast gained thy brother.@5
verse	40	18	16	@@@6But if he will not hear @9thee, then@7 take with thee one or two more, that in the mouth of two or three witnesses every word may be established.@5
verse	40	18	17	@@@6And if he shall neglect to hear them, tell @9it@7 unto the church: but if he neglect to hear the church, let him be unto thee as an heathen man and a publican.@5
verse	40	18	18	@@@6Verily I say unto you, Whatsoever ye shall bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever ye shall loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.@5
verse	40	18	19	@@@6Again I say unto you, That if two of you shall agree on earth as touching any thing that they shall ask, it shall be done for them of my Father which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	18	20	@@@6For where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them.@5
verse	40	18	21	Then came Peter to him, and said, Lord, how oft shall my brother sin against me, and I forgive him? till seven times?
verse	40	18	22	@@Jesus saith unto him, @6I say not unto thee, Until seven times: but, Until seventy times seven.@5
verse	40	18	23	@@@6Therefore is the kingdom of heaven likened unto a certain king, which would take account of his servants.@5
verse	40	18	24	@@@6And when he had begun to reckon, one was brought unto him, which owed him ten thousand talents.@5
verse	40	18	25	@@@6But forasmuch as he had not to pay, his lord commanded him to be sold, and his wife, and children, and all that he had, and payment to be made.@5
verse	40	18	26	@@@6The servant therefore fell down, and worshipped him, saying, Lord, have patience with me, and I will pay thee all.@5
verse	40	18	27	@@@6Then the lord of that servant was moved with compassion, and loosed him, and forgave him the debt.@5
verse	40	18	28	@@@6But the same servant went out, and found one of his fellowservants, which owed him an hundred pence: and he laid hands on him, and took @9him@7 by the throat, saying, Pay me that thou owest.@5
verse	40	18	29	@@@6And his fellowservant fell down at his feet, and besought him, saying, Have patience with me, and I will pay thee all.@5
verse	40	18	30	@@@6And he would not: but went and cast him into prison, till he should pay the debt.@5
verse	40	18	31	@@@6So when his fellowservants saw what was done, they were very sorry, and came and told unto their lord all that was done.@5
verse	40	18	32	@@@6Then his lord, after that he had called him, said unto him, O thou wicked servant, I forgave thee all that debt, because thou desiredst me:@5
verse	40	18	33	@@@6Shouldest not thou also have had compassion on thy fellowservant, even as I had pity on thee?@5
verse	40	18	34	@@@6And his lord was wroth, and delivered him to the tormentors, till he should pay all that was due unto him.@5
verse	40	18	35	@@@6So likewise shall my heavenly Father do also unto you, if ye from your hearts forgive not every one his brother their trespasses.@5
verse	40	19	1	@@And it came to pass, @9that@7 when Jesus had finished these sayings, he departed from Galilee, and came into the coasts of Judaea beyond Jordan;
verse	40	19	2	And great multitudes followed him; and he healed them there.
verse	40	19	3	The Pharisees also came unto him, tempting him, and saying unto him, Is it lawful for a man to put away his wife for every cause?
verse	40	19	4	@@And he answered and said unto them, @6Have ye not read, that he which made @9them@7 at the beginning made them male and female,@5
verse	40	19	5	@@@6And said, For this cause shall a man leave father and mother, and shall cleave to his wife: and they twain shall be one flesh?@5
verse	40	19	6	@@@6Wherefore they are no more twain, but one flesh. What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder.@5
verse	40	19	7	They say unto him, Why did Moses then command to give a writing of divorcement, and to put her away?
verse	40	19	8	@@He saith unto them, @6Moses because of the hardness of your hearts suffered you to put away your wives: but from the beginning it was not so.@5
verse	40	19	9	@@@6And I say unto you, Whosoever shall put away his wife, except @9it be@7 for fornication, and shall marry another, committeth adultery: and whoso marrieth her which is put away doth commit adultery.@5
verse	40	19	10	@@His disciples say unto him, If the case of the man be so with @9his@7 wife, it is not good to marry.
verse	40	19	11	@@But he said unto them, @6All @9men@7 cannot receive this saying, save @9they@7 to whom it is given.@5
verse	40	19	12	@@@6For there are some eunuchs, which were so born from @9their@7 mother's womb: and there are some eunuchs, which were made eunuchs of men: and there be eunuchs, which have made themselves eunuchs for the kingdom of heaven's sake. He that is able to receive @9it,@7 let him receive @9it.@7@5
verse	40	19	13	@@Then were there brought unto him little children, that he should put @9his@7 hands on them, and pray: and the disciples rebuked them.
verse	40	19	14	@@But Jesus said, @6Suffer little children, and forbid them not, to come unto me: for of such is the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	19	15	@@And he laid @9his@7 hands on them, and departed thence.
verse	40	19	16	And, behold, one came and said unto him, Good Master, what good thing shall I do, that I may have eternal life?
verse	40	19	17	@@And he said unto him, @6Why callest thou me good? @9there is@7 none good but one, @9that is,@7 God: but if thou wilt enter into life, keep the commandments.@5
verse	40	19	18	@@He saith unto him, Which? Jesus said, @6Thou shalt do no murder, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt not bear false witness,@5
verse	40	19	19	@@@6Honour thy father and @9thy@7 mother: and, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.@5
verse	40	19	20	The young man saith unto him, All these things have I kept from my youth up: what lack I yet?
verse	40	19	21	@@Jesus said unto him, @6If thou wilt be perfect, go @9and@7 sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come @9and@7 follow me.@5
verse	40	19	22	But when the young man heard that saying, he went away sorrowful: for he had great possessions.
verse	40	19	23	@@Then said Jesus unto his disciples, @6Verily I say unto you, That a rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven.@5
verse	40	19	24	@@@6And again I say unto you, It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.@5
verse	40	19	25	@@When his disciples heard @9it,@7 they were exceedingly amazed, saying, Who then can be saved?
verse	40	19	26	@@But Jesus beheld @9them,@7 and said unto them, @6With men this is impossible; but with God all things are possible.@5
verse	40	19	27	Then answered Peter and said unto him, Behold, we have forsaken all, and followed thee; what shall we have therefore?
verse	40	19	28	@@And Jesus said unto them, @6Verily I say unto you, That ye which have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son of man shall sit in the throne of his glory, ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.@5
verse	40	19	29	@@@6And every one that hath forsaken houses, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or lands, for my name's sake, shall receive an hundredfold, and shall inherit everlasting life.@5
verse	40	19	30	@@@6But many @9that are@7 first shall be last; and the last @9shall be@7 first.@5
verse	40	20	1	@@@6For the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man @9that is@7 an householder, which went out early in the morning to hire labourers into his vineyard.@5
verse	40	20	2	@@@6And when he had agreed with the labourers for a penny a day, he sent them into his vineyard.@5
verse	40	20	3	@@@6And he went out about the third hour, and saw others standing idle in the marketplace,@5
verse	40	20	4	@@@6And said unto them; Go ye also into the vineyard, and whatsoever is right I will give you. And they went their way.@5
verse	40	20	5	@@@6Again he went out about the sixth and ninth hour, and did likewise.@5
verse	40	20	6	@@@6And about the eleventh hour he went out, and found others standing idle, and saith unto them, Why stand ye here all the day idle?@5
verse	40	20	7	@@@6They say unto him, Because no man hath hired us. He saith unto them, Go ye also into the vineyard; and whatsoever is right, @9that@7 shall ye receive.@5
verse	40	20	8	@@@6So when even was come, the lord of the vineyard saith unto his steward, Call the labourers, and give them @9their@7 hire, beginning from the last unto the first.@5
verse	40	20	9	@@@6And when they came that @9were hired@7 about the eleventh hour, they received every man a penny.@5
verse	40	20	10	@@@6But when the first came, they supposed that they should have received more; and they likewise received every man a penny.@5
verse	40	20	11	@@@6And when they had received it, they murmured against the goodman of the house,@5
verse	40	20	12	@@@6Saying, These last have wrought @9but@7 one hour, and thou hast made them equal unto us, which have borne the burden and heat of the day.@5
verse	40	20	13	@@@6But he answered one of them, and said, Friend, I do thee no wrong: didst not thou agree with me for a penny?@5
verse	40	20	14	@@@6Take @9that@7 thine @9is,@7 and go thy way: I will give unto this last, even as unto thee.@5
verse	40	20	15	@@@6Is it not lawful for me to do what I will with mine own? Is thine eye evil, because I am good?@5
verse	40	20	16	@@@6So the last shall be first, and the first last: for many be called, but few chosen.@5
verse	40	20	17	And Jesus going up to Jerusalem took the twelve disciples apart in the way, and said unto them,
verse	40	20	18	@@@6Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man shall be betrayed unto the chief priests and unto the scribes, and they shall condemn him to death,@5
verse	40	20	19	@@@6And shall deliver him to the Gentiles to mock, and to scourge, and to crucify @9him:@7 and the third day he shall rise again.@5
verse	40	20	20	@@Then came to him the mother of Zebedee's children with her sons, worshipping @9him,@7 and desiring a certain thing of him.
verse	40	20	21	@@And he said unto her, @6What wilt thou?@5 She saith unto him, Grant that these my two sons may sit, the one on thy right hand, and the other on the left, in thy kingdom.
verse	40	20	22	@@But Jesus answered and said, @6Ye know not what ye ask. Are ye able to drink of the cup that I shall drink of, and to be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?@5 They say unto him, We are able.
verse	40	20	23	@@And he saith unto them, @6Ye shall drink indeed of my cup, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with: but to sit on my right hand, and on my left, is not mine to give, but @9it shall be given to them@7 for whom it is prepared of my Father.@5
verse	40	20	24	@@And when the ten heard @9it,@7 they were moved with indignation against the two brethren.
verse	40	20	25	@@But Jesus called them @9unto him,@7 and said, @6Ye know that the princes of the Gentiles exercise dominion over them, and they that are great exercise authority upon them.@5
verse	40	20	26	@@@6But it shall not be so among you: but whosoever will be great among you, let him be your minister;@5
verse	40	20	27	@@@6And whosoever will be chief among you, let him be your servant:@5
verse	40	20	28	@@@6Even as the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.@5
verse	40	20	29	And as they departed from Jericho, a great multitude followed him.
verse	40	20	30	@@And, behold, two blind men sitting by the way side, when they heard that Jesus passed by, cried out, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, @9thou@7 Son of David.
verse	40	20	31	@@And the multitude rebuked them, because they should hold their peace: but they cried the more, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, @9thou@7 Son of David.
verse	40	20	32	@@And Jesus stood still, and called them, and said, @6What will ye that I shall do unto you?@5
verse	40	20	33	They say unto him, Lord, that our eyes may be opened.
verse	40	20	34	@@So Jesus had compassion @9on them,@7 and touched their eyes: and immediately their eyes received sight, and they followed him.
verse	40	21	1	And when they drew nigh unto Jerusalem, and were come to Bethphage, unto the mount of Olives, then sent Jesus two disciples,
verse	40	21	2	@@Saying unto them, @6Go into the village over against you, and straightway ye shall find an ass tied, and a colt with her: loose @9them,@7 and bring @9them@7 unto me.@5
verse	40	21	3	@@@6And if any @9man@7 say ought unto you, ye shall say, The Lord hath need of them; and straightway he will send them.@5
verse	40	21	4	All this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying,
verse	40	21	5	Tell ye the daughter of Sion, Behold, thy King cometh unto thee, meek, and sitting upon an ass, and a colt the foal of an ass.
verse	40	21	6	And the disciples went, and did as Jesus commanded them,
verse	40	21	7	@@And brought the ass, and the colt, and put on them their clothes, and they set @9him@7 thereon.
verse	40	21	8	@@And a very great multitude spread their garments in the way; others cut down branches from the trees, and strawed @9them@7 in the way.
verse	40	21	9	@@And the multitudes that went before, and that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna to the Son of David: Blessed @9is@7 he that cometh in the name of the Lord; Hosanna in the highest.
verse	40	21	10	And when he was come into Jerusalem, all the city was moved, saying, Who is this?
verse	40	21	11	And the multitude said, This is Jesus the prophet of Nazareth of Galilee.
verse	40	21	12	And Jesus went into the temple of God, and cast out all them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves,
verse	40	21	13	@@And said unto them, @6It is written, My house shall be called the house of prayer; but ye have made it a den of thieves.@5
verse	40	21	14	And the blind and the lame came to him in the temple; and he healed them.
verse	40	21	15	And when the chief priests and scribes saw the wonderful things that he did, and the children crying in the temple, and saying, Hosanna to the Son of David; they were sore displeased,
verse	40	21	16	@@And said unto him, Hearest thou what these say? And Jesus saith unto them, @6Yea; have ye never read, Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings thou hast perfected praise?@5
verse	40	21	17	And he left them, and went out of the city into Bethany; and he lodged there.
verse	40	21	18	Now in the morning as he returned into the city, he hungered.
verse	40	21	19	@@And when he saw a fig tree in the way, he came to it, and found nothing thereon, but leaves only, and said unto it, @6Let no fruit grow on thee henceforward for ever.@5 And presently the fig tree withered away.
verse	40	21	20	@@And when the disciples saw @9it,@7 they marvelled, saying, How soon is the fig tree withered away!
verse	40	21	21	@@Jesus answered and said unto them, @6Verily I say unto you, If ye have faith, and doubt not, ye shall not only do this @9which is done@7 to the fig tree, but also if ye shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea; it shall be done.@5
verse	40	21	22	@@@6And all things, whatsoever ye shall ask in prayer, believing, ye shall receive.@5
verse	40	21	23	And when he was come into the temple, the chief priests and the elders of the people came unto him as he was teaching, and said, By what authority doest thou these things? and who gave thee this authority?
verse	40	21	24	@@And Jesus answered and said unto them, @6I also will ask you one thing, which if ye tell me, I in like wise will tell you by what authority I do these things.@5
verse	40	21	25	@@@6The baptism of John, whence was it? from heaven, or of men? And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say unto us, Why did ye not then believe him?@5
verse	40	21	26	But if we shall say, Of men; we fear the people; for all hold John as a prophet.
verse	40	21	27	@@And they answered Jesus, and said, We cannot tell. And he said unto them, @6Neither tell I you by what authority I do these things.@5
verse	40	21	28	@@@6But what think ye? A @9certain@7 man had two sons; and he came to the first, and said, Son, go work to day in my vineyard.@5
verse	40	21	29	@@@6He answered and said, I will not: but afterward he repented, and went.@5
verse	40	21	30	@@@6And he came to the second, and said likewise. And he answered and said, I @9go,@7 sir: and went not.@5
verse	40	21	31	@@@6Whether of them twain did the will of @9his@7 father?@5 They say unto him, The first. Jesus saith unto them, @6Verily I say unto you, That the publicans and the harlots go into the kingdom of God before you.@5
verse	40	21	32	@@@6For John came unto you in the way of righteousness, and ye believed him not: but the publicans and the harlots believed him: and ye, when ye had seen @9it,@7 repented not afterward, that ye might believe him.@5
verse	40	21	33	@@@6Hear another parable: There was a certain householder, which planted a vineyard, and hedged it round about, and digged a winepress in it, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into a far country:@5
verse	40	21	34	@@@6And when the time of the fruit drew near, he sent his servants to the husbandmen, that they might receive the fruits of it.@5
verse	40	21	35	@@@6And the husbandmen took his servants, and beat one, and killed another, and stoned another.@5
verse	40	21	36	@@@6Again, he sent other servants more than the first: and they did unto them likewise.@5
verse	40	21	37	@@@6But last of all he sent unto them his son, saying, They will reverence my son.@5
verse	40	21	38	@@@6But when the husbandmen saw the son, they said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and let us seize on his inheritance.@5
verse	40	21	39	@@@6And they caught him, and cast @9him@7 out of the vineyard, and slew @9him. @7@5
verse	40	21	40	@@@6When the lord therefore of the vineyard cometh, what will he do unto those husbandmen?@5
verse	40	21	41	@@They say unto him, He will miserably destroy those wicked men, and will let out @9his@7 vineyard unto other husbandmen, which shall render him the fruits in their seasons.
verse	40	21	42	@@Jesus saith unto them, @6Did ye never read in the scriptures, The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner: this is the Lord's doing, and it is marvellous in our eyes?@5
verse	40	21	43	@@@6Therefore say I unto you, The kingdom of God shall be taken from you, and given to a nation bringing forth the fruits thereof.@5
verse	40	21	44	@@@6And whosoever shall fall on this stone shall be broken: but on whomsoever it shall fall, it will grind him to powder.@5
verse	40	21	45	And when the chief priests and Pharisees had heard his parables, they perceived that he spake of them.
verse	40	21	46	But when they sought to lay hands on him, they feared the multitude, because they took him for a prophet.
verse	40	22	1	And Jesus answered and spake unto them again by parables, and said,
verse	40	22	2	@@@6The kingdom of heaven is like unto a certain king, which made a marriage for his son,@5
verse	40	22	3	@@@6And sent forth his servants to call them that were bidden to the wedding: and they would not come.@5
verse	40	22	4	@@@6Again, he sent forth other servants, saying, Tell them which are bidden, Behold, I have prepared my dinner: my oxen and @9my@7 fatlings @9are@7 killed, and all things @9are@7 ready: come unto the marriage.@5
verse	40	22	5	@@@6But they made light of @9it,@7 and went their ways, one to his farm, another to his merchandise:@5
verse	40	22	6	@@@6And the remnant took his servants, and entreated @9them@7 spitefully, and slew @9them. @7@5
verse	40	22	7	@@@6But when the king heard @9thereof,@7 he was wroth: and he sent forth his armies, and destroyed those murderers, and burned up their city.@5
verse	40	22	8	@@@6Then saith he to his servants, The wedding is ready, but they which were bidden were not worthy.@5
verse	40	22	9	@@@6Go ye therefore into the highways, and as many as ye shall find, bid to the marriage.@5
verse	40	22	10	@@@6So those servants went out into the highways, and gathered together all as many as they found, both bad and good: and the wedding was furnished with guests.@5
verse	40	22	11	@@@6And when the king came in to see the guests, he saw there a man which had not on a wedding garment:@5
verse	40	22	12	@@@6And he saith unto him, Friend, how camest thou in hither not having a wedding garment? And he was speechless.@5
verse	40	22	13	@@@6Then said the king to the servants, Bind him hand and foot, and take him away, and cast @9him@7 into outer darkness; there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.@5
verse	40	22	14	@@@6For many are called, but few @9are@7 chosen.@5
verse	40	22	15	@@Then went the Pharisees, and took counsel how they might entangle him in @9his@7 talk.
verse	40	22	16	@@And they sent out unto him their disciples with the Herodians, saying, Master, we know that thou art true, and teachest the way of God in truth, neither carest thou for any @9man:@7 for thou regardest not the person of men.
verse	40	22	17	Tell us therefore, What thinkest thou? Is it lawful to give tribute unto Caesar, or not?
verse	40	22	18	@@But Jesus perceived their wickedness, and said, @6Why tempt ye me, @9ye@7 hypocrites?@5
verse	40	22	19	@@@6Shew me the tribute money.@5 And they brought unto him a penny.
verse	40	22	20	@@And he saith unto them, @6Whose @9is@7 this image and superscription?@5
verse	40	22	21	@@They say unto him, Caesar's. Then saith he unto them, @6Render therefore unto Caesar the things which are Caesar's; and unto God the things that are God's.@5
verse	40	22	22	@@When they had heard @9these words,@7 they marvelled, and left him, and went their way.
verse	40	22	23	The same day came to him the Sadducees, which say that there is no resurrection, and asked him,
verse	40	22	24	Saying, Master, Moses said, If a man die, having no children, his brother shall marry his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.
verse	40	22	25	Now there were with us seven brethren: and the first, when he had married a wife, deceased, and, having no issue, left his wife unto his brother:
verse	40	22	26	Likewise the second also, and the third, unto the seventh.
verse	40	22	27	And last of all the woman died also.
verse	40	22	28	Therefore in the resurrection whose wife shall she be of the seven? for they all had her.
verse	40	22	29	@@Jesus answered and said unto them, @6Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God.@5
verse	40	22	30	@@@6For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of God in heaven.@5
verse	40	22	31	@@@6But as touching the resurrection of the dead, have ye not read that which was spoken unto you by God, saying,@5
verse	40	22	32	@@@6I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob? God is not the God of the dead, but of the living.@5
verse	40	22	33	@@And when the multitude heard @9this,@7 they were astonished at his doctrine.
verse	40	22	34	But when the Pharisees had heard that he had put the Sadducees to silence, they were gathered together.
verse	40	22	35	@@Then one of them, @9which was@7 a lawyer, asked @9him a question, @7tempting him, and saying,
verse	40	22	36	@@Master, which @9is@7 the great commandment in the law?
verse	40	22	37	@@Jesus said unto him, @6Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.@5
verse	40	22	38	@@@6This is the first and great commandment.@5
verse	40	22	39	@@@6And the second @9is@7 like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.@5
verse	40	22	40	@@@6On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets.@5
verse	40	22	41	While the Pharisees were gathered together, Jesus asked them,
verse	40	22	42	@@Saying, @6What think ye of Christ? whose son is he? They say unto him, @9The Son@7 of David.@5
verse	40	22	43	@@He saith unto them, @6How then doth David in spirit call him Lord, saying,@5
verse	40	22	44	@@@6The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool?@5
verse	40	22	45	@@@6If David then call him Lord, how is he his son?@5
verse	40	22	46	@@And no man was able to answer him a word, neither durst any @9man@7 from that day forth ask him any more @9questions.@7
verse	40	23	1	Then spake Jesus to the multitude, and to his disciples,
verse	40	23	2	@@Saying, @6The scribes and the Pharisees sit in Moses' seat:@5
verse	40	23	3	@@@6All therefore whatsoever they bid you observe, @9that@7 observe and do; but do not ye after their works: for they say, and do not.@5
verse	40	23	4	@@@6For they bind heavy burdens and grievous to be borne, and lay @9them@7 on men's shoulders; but they @9themselves@7 will not move them with one of their fingers.@5
verse	40	23	5	@@@6But all their works they do for to be seen of men: they make broad their phylacteries, and enlarge the borders of their garments,@5
verse	40	23	6	@@@6And love the uppermost rooms at feasts, and the chief seats in the synagogues,@5
verse	40	23	7	@@@6And greetings in the markets, and to be called of men, Rabbi, Rabbi.@5
verse	40	23	8	@@@6But be not ye called Rabbi: for one is your Master, @9even@7 Christ; and all ye are brethren.@5
verse	40	23	9	@@@6And call no @9man@7 your father upon the earth: for one is your Father, which is in heaven.@5
verse	40	23	10	@@@6Neither be ye called masters: for one is your Master, @9even@7 Christ.@5
verse	40	23	11	@@@6But he that is greatest among you shall be your servant.@5
verse	40	23	12	@@@6And whosoever shall exalt himself shall be abased; and he that shall humble himself shall be exalted.@5
verse	40	23	13	@@@6But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut up the kingdom of heaven against men: for ye neither go in @9yourselves,@7 neither suffer ye them that are entering to go in.@5
verse	40	23	14	@@@6Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye devour widows' houses, and for a pretence make long prayer: therefore ye shall receive the greater damnation.@5
verse	40	23	15	@@@6Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than yourselves.@5
verse	40	23	16	@@@6Woe unto you, @9ye@7 blind guides, which say, Whosoever shall swear by the temple, it is nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gold of the temple, he is a debtor!@5
verse	40	23	17	@@@6@9Ye@7 fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gold, or the temple that sanctifieth the gold?@5
verse	40	23	18	@@@6And, Whosoever shall swear by the altar, it is nothing; but whosoever sweareth by the gift that is upon it, he is guilty.@5
verse	40	23	19	@@@6@9Ye@7 fools and blind: for whether @9is@7 greater, the gift, or the altar that sanctifieth the gift?@5
verse	40	23	20	@@@6Whoso therefore shall swear by the altar, sweareth by it, and by all things thereon.@5
verse	40	23	21	@@@6And whoso shall swear by the temple, sweareth by it, and by him that dwelleth therein.@5
verse	40	23	22	@@@6And he that shall swear by heaven, sweareth by the throne of God, and by him that sitteth thereon.@5
verse	40	23	23	@@@6Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint and anise and cummin, and have omitted the weightier @9matters@7 of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith: these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone.@5
verse	40	23	24	@@@6@9Ye@7 blind guides, which strain at a gnat, and swallow a camel.@5
verse	40	23	25	@@@6Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye make clean the outside of the cup and of the platter, but within they are full of extortion and excess.@5
verse	40	23	26	@@@6@9Thou@7 blind Pharisee, cleanse first that @9which is@7 within the cup and platter, that the outside of them may be clean also.@5
verse	40	23	27	@@@6Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead @9men's@7 bones, and of all uncleanness.@5
verse	40	23	28	@@@6Even so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but within ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity.@5
verse	40	23	29	@@@6Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! because ye build the tombs of the prophets, and garnish the sepulchres of the righteous,@5
verse	40	23	30	@@@6And say, If we had been in the days of our fathers, we would not have been partakers with them in the blood of the prophets.@5
verse	40	23	31	@@@6Wherefore ye be witnesses unto yourselves, that ye are the children of them which killed the prophets.@5
verse	40	23	32	@@@6Fill ye up then the measure of your fathers.@5
verse	40	23	33	@@@6@9Ye@7 serpents, @9ye@7 generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of hell?@5
verse	40	23	34	@@@6Wherefore, behold, I send unto you prophets, and wise men, and scribes: and @9some@7 of them ye shall kill and crucify; and @9some@7 of them shall ye scourge in your synagogues, and persecute @9them@7 from city to city:@5
verse	40	23	35	@@@6That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Abel unto the blood of Zacharias son of Barachias, whom ye slew between the temple and the altar.@5
verse	40	23	36	@@@6Verily I say unto you, All these things shall come upon this generation.@5
verse	40	23	37	@@@6O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, @9thou@7 that killest the prophets, and stonest them which are sent unto thee, how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen gathereth her chickens under @9her@7 wings, and ye would not!@5
verse	40	23	38	@@@6Behold, your house is left unto you desolate.@5
verse	40	23	39	@@@6For I say unto you, Ye shall not see me henceforth, till ye shall say, Blessed @9is@7 he that cometh in the name of the Lord.@5
verse	40	24	1	@@And Jesus went out, and departed from the temple: and his disciples came to @9him@7 for to shew him the buildings of the temple.
verse	40	24	2	@@And Jesus said unto them, @6See ye not all these things? verily I say unto you, There shall not be left here one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down.@5
verse	40	24	3	@@And as he sat upon the mount of Olives, the disciples came unto him privately, saying, Tell us, when shall these things be? and what @9shall be@7 the sign of thy coming, and of the end of the world?
verse	40	24	4	@@And Jesus answered and said unto them, @6Take heed that no man deceive you.@5
verse	40	24	5	@@@6For many shall come in my name, saying, I am Christ; and shall deceive many.@5
verse	40	24	6	@@@6And ye shall hear of wars and rumours of wars: see that ye be not troubled: for all @9these things@7 must come to pass, but the end is not yet.@5
verse	40	24	7	@@@6For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be famines, and pestilences, and earthquakes, in divers places.@5
verse	40	24	8	@@@6All these @9are@7 the beginning of sorrows.@5
verse	40	24	9	@@@6Then shall they deliver you up to be afflicted, and shall kill you: and ye shall be hated of all nations for my name's sake.@5
verse	40	24	10	@@@6And then shall many be offended, and shall betray one another, and shall hate one another.@5
verse	40	24	11	@@@6And many false prophets shall rise, and shall deceive many.@5
verse	40	24	12	@@@6And because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold.@5
verse	40	24	13	@@@6But he that shall endure unto the end, the same shall be saved.@5
verse	40	24	14	@@@6And this gospel of the kingdom shall be preached in all the world for a witness unto all nations; and then shall the end come.@5
verse	40	24	15	@@@6When ye therefore shall see the abomination of desolation, spoken of by Daniel the prophet, stand in the holy place,@5 (whoso readeth, let him understand:)
verse	40	24	16	@@@6Then let them which be in Judaea flee into the mountains:@5
verse	40	24	17	@@@6Let him which is on the housetop not come down to take any thing out of his house:@5
verse	40	24	18	@@@6Neither let him which is in the field return back to take his clothes.@5
verse	40	24	19	@@@6And woe unto them that are with child, and to them that give suck in those days!@5
verse	40	24	20	@@@6But pray ye that your flight be not in the winter, neither on the sabbath day:@5
verse	40	24	21	@@@6For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to this time, no, nor ever shall be.@5
verse	40	24	22	@@@6And except those days should be shortened, there should no flesh be saved: but for the elect's sake those days shall be shortened.@5
verse	40	24	23	@@@6Then if any man shall say unto you, Lo, here @9is@7 Christ, or there; believe @9it@7 not.@5
verse	40	24	24	@@@6For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and wonders; insomuch that, if @9it were@7 possible, they shall deceive the very elect.@5
verse	40	24	25	@@@6Behold, I have told you before.@5
verse	40	24	26	@@@6Wherefore if they shall say unto you, Behold, @9he is@7 in the desert; go not forth: behold, he is in the secret chambers; believe @9it@7 not.@5
verse	40	24	27	@@@6For as the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.@5
verse	40	24	28	@@@6For wheresoever the carcase is, there will the eagles be gathered together.@5
verse	40	24	29	@@@6Immediately after the tribulation of those days shall the sun be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light, and the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of the heavens shall be shaken:@5
verse	40	24	30	@@@6And then shall appear the sign of the Son of man in heaven: and then shall all the tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of man coming in the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.@5
verse	40	24	31	@@@6And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.@5
verse	40	24	32	@@@6Now learn a parable of the fig tree; When his branch is yet tender, and putteth forth leaves, ye know that summer is nigh:@5
verse	40	24	33	@@@6So likewise ye, when ye shall see all these things, know that it is near, @9even@7 at the doors.@5
verse	40	24	34	@@@6Verily I say unto you, This generation shall not pass, till all these things be fulfilled.@5
verse	40	24	35	@@@6Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.@5
verse	40	24	36	@@@6But of that day and hour knoweth no @9man,@7 no, not the angels of heaven, but my Father only.@5
verse	40	24	37	@@@6But as the days of Noe @9were,@7 so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.@5
verse	40	24	38	@@@6For as in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noe entered into the ark,@5
verse	40	24	39	@@@6And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.@5
verse	40	24	40	@@@6Then shall two be in the field; the one shall be taken, and the other left.@5
verse	40	24	41	@@@6Two @9women shall be@7 grinding at the mill; the one shall be taken, and the other left.@5
verse	40	24	42	@@@6Watch therefore: for ye know not what hour your Lord doth come.@5
verse	40	24	43	@@@6But know this, that if the goodman of the house had known in what watch the thief would come, he would have watched, and would not have suffered his house to be broken up.@5
verse	40	24	44	@@@6Therefore be ye also ready: for in such an hour as ye think not the Son of man cometh.@5
verse	40	24	45	@@@6Who then is a faithful and wise servant, whom his lord hath made ruler over his household, to give them meat in due season?@5
verse	40	24	46	@@@6Blessed @9is@7 that servant, whom his lord when he cometh shall find so doing.@5
verse	40	24	47	@@@6Verily I say unto you, That he shall make him ruler over all his goods.@5
verse	40	24	48	@@@6But and if that evil servant shall say in his heart, My lord delayeth his coming;@5
verse	40	24	49	@@@6And shall begin to smite @9his@7 fellowservants, and to eat and drink with the drunken;@5
verse	40	24	50	@@@6The lord of that servant shall come in a day when he looketh not for @9him,@7 and in an hour that he is not aware of,@5
verse	40	24	51	@@@6And shall cut him asunder, and appoint @9him@7 his portion with the hypocrites: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.@5
verse	40	25	1	@@@6Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened unto ten virgins, which took their lamps, and went forth to meet the bridegroom.@5
verse	40	25	2	@@@6And five of them were wise, and five @9were@7 foolish.@5
verse	40	25	3	@@@6They that @9were@7 foolish took their lamps, and took no oil with them:@5
verse	40	25	4	@@@6But the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps.@5
verse	40	25	5	@@@6While the bridegroom tarried, they all slumbered and slept.@5
verse	40	25	6	@@@6And at midnight there was a cry made, Behold, the bridegroom cometh; go ye out to meet him.@5
verse	40	25	7	@@@6Then all those virgins arose, and trimmed their lamps.@5
verse	40	25	8	@@@6And the foolish said unto the wise, Give us of your oil; for our lamps are gone out.@5
verse	40	25	9	@@@6But the wise answered, saying, @9Not so;@7 lest there be not enough for us and you: but go ye rather to them that sell, and buy for yourselves.@5
verse	40	25	10	@@@6And while they went to buy, the bridegroom came; and they that were ready went in with him to the marriage: and the door was shut.@5
verse	40	25	11	@@@6Afterward came also the other virgins, saying, Lord, Lord, open to us.@5
verse	40	25	12	@@@6But he answered and said, Verily I say unto you, I know you not.@5
verse	40	25	13	@@@6Watch therefore, for ye know neither the day nor the hour wherein the Son of man cometh.@5
verse	40	25	14	@@@6For @9the kingdom of heaven is@7 as a man travelling into a far country, @9who@7 called his own servants, and delivered unto them his goods.@5
verse	40	25	15	@@@6And unto one he gave five talents, to another two, and to another one; to every man according to his several ability; and straightway took his journey.@5
verse	40	25	16	@@@6Then he that had received the five talents went and traded with the same, and made @9them@7 other five talents.@5
verse	40	25	17	@@@6And likewise he that @9had received@7 two, he also gained other two.@5
verse	40	25	18	@@@6But he that had received one went and digged in the earth, and hid his lord's money.@5
verse	40	25	19	@@@6After a long time the lord of those servants cometh, and reckoneth with them.@5
verse	40	25	20	@@@6And so he that had received five talents came and brought other five talents, saying, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me five talents: behold, I have gained beside them five talents more.@5
verse	40	25	21	@@@6His lord said unto him, Well done, @9thou@7 good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.@5
verse	40	25	22	@@@6He also that had received two talents came and said, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me two talents: behold, I have gained two other talents beside them.@5
verse	40	25	23	@@@6His lord said unto him, Well done, good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.@5
verse	40	25	24	@@@6Then he which had received the one talent came and said, Lord, I knew thee that thou art an hard man, reaping where thou hast not sown, and gathering where thou hast not strawed:@5
verse	40	25	25	@@@6And I was afraid, and went and hid thy talent in the earth: lo, @9there@7 thou hast @9that is@7 thine.@5
verse	40	25	26	@@@6His lord answered and said unto him, @9Thou@7 wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that I reap where I sowed not, and gather where I have not strawed:@5
verse	40	25	27	@@@6Thou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the exchangers, and @9then@7 at my coming I should have received mine own with usury.@5
verse	40	25	28	@@@6Take therefore the talent from him, and give @9it@7 unto him which hath ten talents.@5
verse	40	25	29	@@@6For unto every one that hath shall be given, and he shall have abundance: but from him that hath not shall be taken away even that which he hath.@5
verse	40	25	30	@@@6And cast ye the unprofitable servant into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.@5
verse	40	25	31	@@@6When the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory:@5
verse	40	25	32	@@@6And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth @9his@7 sheep from the goats:@5
verse	40	25	33	@@@6And he shall set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left.@5
verse	40	25	34	@@@6Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:@5
verse	40	25	35	@@@6For I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in:@5
verse	40	25	36	@@@6Naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came unto me.@5
verse	40	25	37	@@@6Then shall the righteous answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, and fed @9thee?@7 or thirsty, and gave @9thee@7 drink?@5
verse	40	25	38	@@@6When saw we thee a stranger, and took @9thee@7 in? or naked, and clothed @9thee? @7@5
verse	40	25	39	@@@6Or when saw we thee sick, or in prison, and came unto thee?@5
verse	40	25	40	@@@6And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done @9it@7 unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done @9it@7 unto me.@5
verse	40	25	41	@@@6Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels:@5
verse	40	25	42	@@@6For I was an hungred, and ye gave me no meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me no drink:@5
verse	40	25	43	@@@6I was a stranger, and ye took me not in: naked, and ye clothed me not: sick, and in prison, and ye visited me not.@5
verse	40	25	44	@@@6Then shall they also answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, or athirst, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and did not minister unto thee?@5
verse	40	25	45	@@@6Then shall he answer them, saying, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye did @9it@7 not to one of the least of these, ye did @9it@7 not to me.@5
verse	40	25	46	@@@6And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal.@5
verse	40	26	1	And it came to pass, when Jesus had finished all these sayings, he said unto his disciples,
verse	40	26	2	@@@6Ye know that after two days is @9the feast of@7 the passover, and the Son of man is betrayed to be crucified.@5
verse	40	26	3	Then assembled together the chief priests, and the scribes, and the elders of the people, unto the palace of the high priest, who was called Caiaphas,
verse	40	26	4	@@And consulted that they might take Jesus by subtilty, and kill @9him. @7
verse	40	26	5	@@But they said, Not on the feast @9day,@7 lest there be an uproar among the people.
verse	40	26	6	Now when Jesus was in Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper,
verse	40	26	7	@@There came unto him a woman having an alabaster box of very precious ointment, and poured it on his head, as he sat @9at meat. @7
verse	40	26	8	@@But when his disciples saw @9it,@7 they had indignation, saying, To what purpose @9is@7 this waste?
verse	40	26	9	For this ointment might have been sold for much, and given to the poor.
verse	40	26	10	@@When Jesus understood @9it,@7 he said unto them, @6Why trouble ye the woman? for she hath wrought a good work upon me.@5
verse	40	26	11	@@@6For ye have the poor always with you; but me ye have not always.@5
verse	40	26	12	@@@6For in that she hath poured this ointment on my body, she did @9it@7 for my burial.@5
verse	40	26	13	@@@6Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever this gospel shall be preached in the whole world, @9there@7 shall also this, that this woman hath done, be told for a memorial of her.@5
verse	40	26	14	Then one of the twelve, called Judas Iscariot, went unto the chief priests,
verse	40	26	15	@@And said @9unto them,@7 What will ye give me, and I will deliver him unto you? And they covenanted with him for thirty pieces of silver.
verse	40	26	16	And from that time he sought opportunity to betray him.
verse	40	26	17	@@Now the first @9day@7 of the @9feast of@7 unleavened bread the disciples came to Jesus, saying unto him, Where wilt thou that we prepare for thee to eat the passover?
verse	40	26	18	@@And he said, @6Go into the city to such a man, and say unto him, The Master saith, My time is at hand; I will keep the passover at thy house with my disciples.@5
verse	40	26	19	And the disciples did as Jesus had appointed them; and they made ready the passover.
verse	40	26	20	Now when the even was come, he sat down with the twelve.
verse	40	26	21	@@And as they did eat, he said, @6Verily I say unto you, that one of you shall betray me.@5
verse	40	26	22	And they were exceeding sorrowful, and began every one of them to say unto him, Lord, is it I?
verse	40	26	23	@@And he answered and said, @6He that dippeth @9his@7 hand with me in the dish, the same shall betray me.@5
verse	40	26	24	@@@6The Son of man goeth as it is written of him: but woe unto that man by whom the Son of man is betrayed! it had been good for that man if he had not been born.@5
verse	40	26	25	@@Then Judas, which betrayed him, answered and said, Master, is it I? He said unto him, @6Thou hast said.@5
verse	40	26	26	@@And as they were eating, Jesus took bread, and blessed @9it,@7 and brake @9it,@7 and gave @9it@7 to the disciples, and said, @6Take, eat; this is my body.@5
verse	40	26	27	@@And he took the cup, and gave thanks, and gave @9it@7 to them, saying, @6Drink ye all of it;@5
verse	40	26	28	@@@6For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins.@5
verse	40	26	29	@@@6But I say unto you, I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that day when I drink it new with you in my Father's kingdom.@5
verse	40	26	30	And when they had sung an hymn, they went out into the mount of Olives.
verse	40	26	31	@@Then saith Jesus unto them, @6All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad.@5
verse	40	26	32	@@@6But after I am risen again, I will go before you into Galilee.@5
verse	40	26	33	@@Peter answered and said unto him, Though all @9men@7 shall be offended because of thee, @9yet@7 will I never be offended.
verse	40	26	34	@@Jesus said unto him, @6Verily I say unto thee, That this night, before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.@5
verse	40	26	35	Peter said unto him, Though I should die with thee, yet will I not deny thee. Likewise also said all the disciples.
verse	40	26	36	@@Then cometh Jesus with them unto a place called Gethsemane, and saith unto the disciples, @6Sit ye here, while I go and pray yonder.@5
verse	40	26	37	And he took with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, and began to be sorrowful and very heavy.
verse	40	26	38	@@Then saith he unto them, @6My soul is exceeding sorrowful, even unto death: tarry ye here, and watch with me.@5
verse	40	26	39	@@And he went a little farther, and fell on his face, and prayed, saying, @6O my Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me: nevertheless not as I will, but as thou @9wilt. @7@5
verse	40	26	40	@@And he cometh unto the disciples, and findeth them asleep, and saith unto Peter, @6What, could ye not watch with me one hour?@5
verse	40	26	41	@@@6Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed @9is@7 willing, but the flesh @9is@7 weak.@5
verse	40	26	42	@@He went away again the second time, and prayed, saying, @6O my Father, if this cup may not pass away from me, except I drink it, thy will be done.@5
verse	40	26	43	And he came and found them asleep again: for their eyes were heavy.
verse	40	26	44	And he left them, and went away again, and prayed the third time, saying the same words.
verse	40	26	45	@@Then cometh he to his disciples, and saith unto them, @6Sleep on now, and take @9your@7 rest: behold, the hour is at hand, and the Son of man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.@5
verse	40	26	46	@@@6Rise, let us be going: behold, he is at hand that doth betray me.@5
verse	40	26	47	And while he yet spake, lo, Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and elders of the people.
verse	40	26	48	Now he that betrayed him gave them a sign, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is he: hold him fast.
verse	40	26	49	And forthwith he came to Jesus, and said, Hail, master; and kissed him.
verse	40	26	50	@@And Jesus said unto him, @6Friend, wherefore art thou come?@5 Then came they, and laid hands on Jesus, and took him.
verse	40	26	51	@@And, behold, one of them which were with Jesus stretched out @9his@7 hand, and drew his sword, and struck a servant of the high priest's, and smote off his ear.
verse	40	26	52	@@Then said Jesus unto him, @6Put up again thy sword into his place: for all they that take the sword shall perish with the sword.@5
verse	40	26	53	@@@6Thinkest thou that I cannot now pray to my Father, and he shall presently give me more than twelve legions of angels?@5
verse	40	26	54	@@@6But how then shall the scriptures be fulfilled, that thus it must be?@5
verse	40	26	55	@@In that same hour said Jesus to the multitudes, @6Are ye come out as against a thief with swords and staves for to take me? I sat daily with you teaching in the temple, and ye laid no hold on me.@5
verse	40	26	56	@@@6But all this was done, that the scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled. @5Then all the disciples forsook him, and fled.
verse	40	26	57	@@And they that had laid hold on Jesus led @9him@7 away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were assembled.
verse	40	26	58	But Peter followed him afar off unto the high priest's palace, and went in, and sat with the servants, to see the end.
verse	40	26	59	Now the chief priests, and elders, and all the council, sought false witness against Jesus, to put him to death;
verse	40	26	60	@@But found none: yea, though many false witnesses came, @9yet@7 found they none. At the last came two false witnesses,
verse	40	26	61	@@And said, This @9fellow@7 said, I am able to destroy the temple of God, and to build it in three days.
verse	40	26	62	@@And the high priest arose, and said unto him, Answerest thou nothing? what @9is it which@7 these witness against thee?
verse	40	26	63	But Jesus held his peace. And the high priest answered and said unto him, I adjure thee by the living God, that thou tell us whether thou be the Christ, the Son of God.
verse	40	26	64	@@Jesus saith unto him, @6Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.@5
verse	40	26	65	Then the high priest rent his clothes, saying, He hath spoken blasphemy; what further need have we of witnesses? behold, now ye have heard his blasphemy.
verse	40	26	66	What think ye? They answered and said, He is guilty of death.
verse	40	26	67	@@Then did they spit in his face, and buffeted him; and others smote @9him@7 with the palms of their hands,
verse	40	26	68	Saying, Prophesy unto us, thou Christ, Who is he that smote thee?
verse	40	26	69	Now Peter sat without in the palace: and a damsel came unto him, saying, Thou also wast with Jesus of Galilee.
verse	40	26	70	@@But he denied before @9them@7 all, saying, I know not what thou sayest.
verse	40	26	71	@@And when he was gone out into the porch, another @9maid@7 saw him, and said unto them that were there, This @9fellow@7 was also with Jesus of Nazareth.
verse	40	26	72	And again he denied with an oath, I do not know the man.
verse	40	26	73	@@And after a while came unto @9him@7 they that stood by, and said to Peter, Surely thou also art @9one@7 of them; for thy speech bewrayeth thee.
verse	40	26	74	@@Then began he to curse and to swear, @9saying,@7 I know not the man. And immediately the cock crew.
verse	40	26	75	@@And Peter remembered the word of Jesus, which said unto him, @6Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.@5 And he went out, and wept bitterly.
verse	40	27	1	When the morning was come, all the chief priests and elders of the people took counsel against Jesus to put him to death:
verse	40	27	2	@@And when they had bound him, they led @9him@7 away, and delivered him to Pontius Pilate the governor.
verse	40	27	3	Then Judas, which had betrayeth him, when he saw that he was condemned, repented himself, and brought again the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders,
verse	40	27	4	@@Saying, I have sinned in that I have betrayed the innocent blood. And they said, What @9is that@7 to us? see thou @9to that. @7
verse	40	27	5	And he cast down the pieces of silver in the temple, and departed, and went and hanged himself.
verse	40	27	6	And the chief priests took the silver pieces, and said, It is not lawful for to put them into the treasury, because it is the price of blood.
verse	40	27	7	And they took counsel, and bought with them the potter's field, to bury strangers in.
verse	40	27	8	Wherefore that field was called, The field of blood, unto this day.
verse	40	27	9	Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremy the prophet, saying, And they took the thirty pieces of silver, the price of him that was valued, whom they of the children of Israel did value;
verse	40	27	10	And gave them for the potter's field, as the Lord appointed me.
verse	40	27	11	@@And Jesus stood before the governor: and the governor asked him, saying, Art thou the King of the Jews? And Jesus said unto him, @6Thou sayest.@5
verse	40	27	12	And when he was accused of the chief priests and elders, he answered nothing.
verse	40	27	13	Then said Pilate unto him, Hearest thou not how many things they witness against thee?
verse	40	27	14	And he answered him to never a word; insomuch that the governor marvelled greatly.
verse	40	27	15	@@Now at @9that@7 feast the governor was wont to release unto the people a prisoner, whom they would.
verse	40	27	16	And they had then a notable prisoner, called Barabbas.
verse	40	27	17	Therefore when they were gathered together, Pilate said unto them, Whom will ye that I release unto you? Barabbas, or Jesus which is called Christ?
verse	40	27	18	For he knew that for envy they had delivered him.
verse	40	27	19	When he was set down on the judgment seat, his wife sent unto him, saying, Have thou nothing to do with that just man: for I have suffered many things this day in a dream because of him.
verse	40	27	20	But the chief priests and elders persuaded the multitude that they should ask Barabbas, and destroy Jesus.
verse	40	27	21	The governor answered and said unto them, Whether of the twain will ye that I release unto you? They said, Barabbas.
verse	40	27	22	@@Pilate saith unto them, What shall I do then with Jesus which is called Christ? @9They@7 all say unto him, Let him be crucified.
verse	40	27	23	And the governor said, Why, what evil hath he done? But they cried out the more, saying, Let him be crucified.
verse	40	27	24	@@When Pilate saw that he could prevail nothing, but @9that@7 rather a tumult was made, he took water, and washed @9his@7 hands before the multitude, saying, I am innocent of the blood of this just person: see ye @9to it. @7
verse	40	27	25	@@Then answered all the people, and said, His blood @9be@7 on us, and on our children.
verse	40	27	26	@@Then released he Barabbas unto them: and when he had scourged Jesus, he delivered @9him@7 to be crucified.
verse	40	27	27	@@Then the soldiers of the governor took Jesus into the common hall, and gathered unto him the whole band @9of soldiers. @7
verse	40	27	28	And they stripped him, and put on him a scarlet robe.
verse	40	27	29	@@And when they had platted a crown of thorns, they put @9it@7 upon his head, and a reed in his right hand: and they bowed the knee before him, and mocked him, saying, Hail, King of the Jews!
verse	40	27	30	And they spit upon him, and took the reed, and smote him on the head.
verse	40	27	31	@@And after that they had mocked him, they took the robe off from him, and put his own raiment on him, and led him away to crucify @9him. @7
verse	40	27	32	And as they came out, they found a man of Cyrene, Simon by name: him they compelled to bear his cross.
verse	40	27	33	And when they were come unto a place called Golgotha, that is to say, a place of a skull,
verse	40	27	34	@@They gave him vinegar to drink mingled with gall: and when he had tasted @9thereof,@7 he would not drink.
verse	40	27	35	And they crucified him, and parted his garments, casting lots: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, They parted my garments among them, and upon my vesture did they cast lots.
verse	40	27	36	And sitting down they watched him there;
verse	40	27	37	And set up over his head his accusation written, THIS IS JESUS THE KING OF THE JEWS.
verse	40	27	38	Then were there two thieves crucified with him, one on the right hand, and another on the left.
verse	40	27	39	And they that passed by reviled him, wagging their heads,
verse	40	27	40	@@And saying, Thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest @9it@7 in three days, save thyself. If thou be the Son of God, come down from the cross.
verse	40	27	41	@@Likewise also the chief priests mocking @9him,@7 with the scribes and elders, said,
verse	40	27	42	He saved others; himself he cannot save. If he be the King of Israel, let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him.
verse	40	27	43	He trusted in God; let him deliver him now, if he will have him: for he said, I am the Son of God.
verse	40	27	44	The thieves also, which were crucified with him, cast the same in his teeth.
verse	40	27	45	Now from the sixth hour there was darkness over all the land unto the ninth hour.
verse	40	27	46	@@And about the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, @6Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani?@5 that is to say, @6My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?@5
verse	40	27	47	@@Some of them that stood there, when they heard @9that,@7 said, This @9man@7 calleth for Elias.
verse	40	27	48	@@And straightway one of them ran, and took a spunge, and filled @9it@7 with vinegar, and put @9it@7 on a reed, and gave him to drink.
verse	40	27	49	The rest said, Let be, let us see whether Elias will come to save him.
verse	40	27	50	Jesus, when he had cried again with a loud voice, yielded up the ghost.
verse	40	27	51	And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks rent;
verse	40	27	52	And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose,
verse	40	27	53	And came out of the graves after his resurrection, and went into the holy city, and appeared unto many.
verse	40	27	54	Now when the centurion, and they that were with him, watching Jesus, saw the earthquake, and those things that were done, they feared greatly, saying, Truly this was the Son of God.
verse	40	27	55	And many women were there beholding afar off, which followed Jesus from Galilee, ministering unto him:
verse	40	27	56	Among which was Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James and Joses, and the mother of Zebedee's children.
verse	40	27	57	When the even was come, there came a rich man of Arimathaea, named Joseph, who also himself was Jesus' disciple:
verse	40	27	58	He went to Pilate, and begged the body of Jesus. Then Pilate commanded the body to be delivered.
verse	40	27	59	And when Joseph had taken the body, he wrapped it in a clean linen cloth,
verse	40	27	60	And laid it in his own new tomb, which he had hewn out in the rock: and he rolled a great stone to the door of the sepulchre, and departed.
verse	40	27	61	And there was Mary Magdalene, and the other Mary, sitting over against the sepulchre.
verse	40	27	62	Now the next day, that followed the day of the preparation, the chief priests and Pharisees came together unto Pilate,
verse	40	27	63	@@Saying, Sir, we remember that that deceiver said, while he was yet alive, @6After three days I will rise again.@5
verse	40	27	64	Command therefore that the sepulchre be made sure until the third day, lest his disciples come by night, and steal him away, and say unto the people, He is risen from the dead: so the last error shall be worse than the first.
verse	40	27	65	@@Pilate said unto them, Ye have a watch: go your way, make @9it@7 as sure as ye can.
verse	40	27	66	So they went, and made the sepulchre sure, sealing the stone, and setting a watch.
verse	40	28	1	@@In the end of the sabbath, as it began to dawn toward the first @9day@7 of the week, came Mary Magdalene and the other Mary to see the sepulchre.
verse	40	28	2	And, behold, there was a great earthquake: for the angel of the Lord descended from heaven, and came and rolled back the stone from the door, and sat upon it.
verse	40	28	3	His countenance was like lightning, and his raiment white as snow:
verse	40	28	4	@@And for fear of him the keepers did shake, and became as dead @9men. @7
verse	40	28	5	And the angel answered and said unto the women, Fear not ye: for I know that ye seek Jesus, which was crucified.
verse	40	28	6	He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where the Lord lay.
verse	40	28	7	And go quickly, and tell his disciples that he is risen from the dead; and, behold, he goeth before you into Galilee; there shall ye see him: lo, I have told you.
verse	40	28	8	And they departed quickly from the sepulchre with fear and great joy; and did run to bring his disciples word.
verse	40	28	9	@@And as they went to tell his disciples, behold, Jesus met them, saying, @6All hail.@5 And they came and held him by the feet, and worshipped him.
verse	40	28	10	@@Then said Jesus unto them, @6Be not afraid: go tell my brethren that they go into Galilee, and there shall they see me.@5
verse	40	28	11	Now when they were going, behold, some of the watch came into the city, and shewed unto the chief priests all the things that were done.
verse	40	28	12	And when they were assembled with the elders, and had taken counsel, they gave large money unto the soldiers,
verse	40	28	13	@@Saying, Say ye, His disciples came by night, and stole him @9away@7 while we slept.
verse	40	28	14	And if this come to the governor's ears, we will persuade him, and secure you.
verse	40	28	15	So they took the money, and did as they were taught: and this saying is commonly reported among the Jews until this day.
verse	40	28	16	Then the eleven disciples went away into Galilee, into a mountain where Jesus had appointed them.
verse	40	28	17	And when they saw him, they worshipped him: but some doubted.
verse	40	28	18	@@And Jesus came and spake unto them, saying, @6All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth.@5
verse	40	28	19	@@@6Go ye therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost:@5
verse	40	28	20	@@@6Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with you alway, @9even@7 unto the end of the world. Amen.@5
verse	41	1	1	The beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, the Son of God;
verse	41	1	2	As it is written in the prophets, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, which shall prepare thy way before thee.
verse	41	1	3	The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.
verse	41	1	4	John did baptize in the wilderness, and preach the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins.
verse	41	1	5	And there went out unto him all the land of Judaea, and they of Jerusalem, and were all baptized of him in the river of Jordan, confessing their sins.
verse	41	1	6	And John was clothed with camel's hair, and with a girdle of a skin about his loins; and he did eat locusts and wild honey;
verse	41	1	7	And preached, saying, There cometh one mightier than I after me, the latchet of whose shoes I am not worthy to stoop down and unloose.
verse	41	1	8	I indeed have baptized you with water: but he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost.
verse	41	1	9	And it came to pass in those days, that Jesus came from Nazareth of Galilee, and was baptized of John in Jordan.
verse	41	1	10	And straightway coming up out of the water, he saw the heavens opened, and the Spirit like a dove descending upon him:
verse	41	1	11	@@And there came a voice from heaven, @9saying,@7 Thou art my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.
verse	41	1	12	And immediately the Spirit driveth him into the wilderness.
verse	41	1	13	And he was there in the wilderness forty days, tempted of Satan; and was with the wild beasts; and the angels ministered unto him.
verse	41	1	14	Now after that John was put in prison, Jesus came into Galilee, preaching the gospel of the kingdom of God,
verse	41	1	15	@@And saying, @6The time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand: repent ye, and believe the gospel.@5
verse	41	1	16	Now as he walked by the sea of Galilee, he saw Simon and Andrew his brother casting a net into the sea: for they were fishers.
verse	41	1	17	@@And Jesus said unto them, @6Come ye after me, and I will make you to become fishers of men.@5
verse	41	1	18	And straightway they forsook their nets, and followed him.
verse	41	1	19	@@And when he had gone a little farther thence, he saw James the @9son@7 of Zebedee, and John his brother, who also were in the ship mending their nets.
verse	41	1	20	And straightway he called them: and they left their father Zebedee in the ship with the hired servants, and went after him.
verse	41	1	21	And they went into Capernaum; and straightway on the sabbath day he entered into the synagogue, and taught.
verse	41	1	22	And they were astonished at his doctrine: for he taught them as one that had authority, and not as the scribes.
verse	41	1	23	And there was in their synagogue a man with an unclean spirit; and he cried out,
verse	41	1	24	@@Saying, Let @9us@7 alone; what have we to do with thee, thou Jesus of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art, the Holy One of God.
verse	41	1	25	@@And Jesus rebuked him, saying, @6Hold thy peace, and come out of him.@5
verse	41	1	26	And when the unclean spirit had torn him, and cried with a loud voice, he came out of him.
verse	41	1	27	@@And they were all amazed, insomuch that they questioned among themselves, saying, What thing is this? what new doctrine @9is@7 this? for with authority commandeth he even the unclean spirits, and they do obey him.
verse	41	1	28	And immediately his fame spread abroad throughout all the region round about Galilee.
verse	41	1	29	And forthwith, when they were come out of the synagogue, they entered into the house of Simon and Andrew, with James and John.
verse	41	1	30	But Simon's wife's mother lay sick of a fever, and anon they tell him of her.
verse	41	1	31	And he came and took her by the hand, and lifted her up; and immediately the fever left her, and she ministered unto them.
verse	41	1	32	And at even, when the sun did set, they brought unto him all that were diseased, and them that were possessed with devils.
verse	41	1	33	And all the city was gathered together at the door.
verse	41	1	34	And he healed many that were sick of divers diseases, and cast out many devils; and suffered not the devils to speak, because they knew him.
verse	41	1	35	And in the morning, rising up a great while before day, he went out, and departed into a solitary place, and there prayed.
verse	41	1	36	And Simon and they that were with him followed after him.
verse	41	1	37	@@And when they had found him, they said unto him, All @9men@7 seek for thee.
verse	41	1	38	@@And he said unto them, @6Let us go into the next towns, that I may preach there also: for therefore came I forth.@5
verse	41	1	39	And he preached in their synagogues throughout all Galilee, and cast out devils.
verse	41	1	40	And there came a leper to him, beseeching him, and kneeling down to him, and saying unto him, If thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.
verse	41	1	41	@@And Jesus, moved with compassion, put forth @9his@7 hand, and touched him, and saith unto him, @6I will; be thou clean.@5
verse	41	1	42	And as soon as he had spoken, immediately the leprosy departed from him, and he was cleansed.
verse	41	1	43	And he straitly charged him, and forthwith sent him away;
verse	41	1	44	@@And saith unto him, @6See thou say nothing to any man: but go thy way, shew thyself to the priest, and offer for thy cleansing those things which Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them.@5
verse	41	1	45	@@But he went out, and began to publish @9it@7 much, and to blaze abroad the matter, insomuch that Jesus could no more openly enter into the city, but was without in desert places: and they came to him from every quarter.
verse	41	2	1	@@And again he entered into Capernaum, after @9some@7 days; and it was noised that he was in the house.
verse	41	2	2	@@And straightway many were gathered together, insomuch that there was no room to receive @9them,@7 no, not so much as about the door: and he preached the word unto them.
verse	41	2	3	And they come unto him, bringing one sick of the palsy, which was borne of four.
verse	41	2	4	@@And when they could not come nigh unto him for the press, they uncovered the roof where he was: and when they had broken @9it@7 up, they let down the bed wherein the sick of the palsy lay.
verse	41	2	5	@@When Jesus saw their faith, he said unto the sick of the palsy, @6Son, thy sins be forgiven thee.@5
verse	41	2	6	But there were certain of the scribes sitting there, and reasoning in their hearts,
verse	41	2	7	@@Why doth this @9man@7 thus speak blasphemies? who can forgive sins but God only?
verse	41	2	8	@@And immediately when Jesus perceived in his spirit that they so reasoned within themselves, he said unto them, @6Why reason ye these things in your hearts?@5
verse	41	2	9	@@@6Whether is it easier to say to the sick of the palsy, @9Thy@7 sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Arise, and take up thy bed, and walk?@5
verse	41	2	10	@@@6But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins,@5 (he saith to the sick of the palsy,)
verse	41	2	11	@@@6I say unto thee, Arise, and take up thy bed, and go thy way into thine house.@5
verse	41	2	12	And immediately he arose, took up the bed, and went forth before them all; insomuch that they were all amazed, and glorified God, saying, We never saw it on this fashion.
verse	41	2	13	And he went forth again by the sea side; and all the multitude resorted unto him, and he taught them.
verse	41	2	14	@@And as he passed by, he saw Levi the @9son@7 of Alphaeus sitting at the receipt of custom, and said unto him, @6Follow me.@5 And he arose and followed him.
verse	41	2	15	And it came to pass, that, as Jesus sat at meat in his house, many publicans and sinners sat also together with Jesus and his disciples: for there were many, and they followed him.
verse	41	2	16	And when the scribes and Pharisees saw him eat with publicans and sinners, they said unto his disciples, How is it that he eateth and drinketh with publicans and sinners?
verse	41	2	17	@@When Jesus heard @9it,@7 he saith unto them, @6They that are whole have no need of the physician, but they that are sick: I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.@5
verse	41	2	18	And the disciples of John and of the Pharisees used to fast: and they come and say unto him, Why do the disciples of John and of the Pharisees fast, but thy disciples fast not?
verse	41	2	19	@@And Jesus said unto them, @6Can the children of the bridechamber fast, while the bridegroom is with them? as long as they have the bridegroom with them, they cannot fast.@5
verse	41	2	20	@@@6But the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken away from them, and then shall they fast in those days.@5
verse	41	2	21	@@@6No man also seweth a piece of new cloth on an old garment: else the new piece that filled it up taketh away from the old, and the rent is made worse.@5
verse	41	2	22	@@@6And no man putteth new wine into old bottles: else the new wine doth burst the bottles, and the wine is spilled, and the bottles will be marred: but new wine must be put into new bottles.@5
verse	41	2	23	And it came to pass, that he went through the corn fields on the sabbath day; and his disciples began, as they went, to pluck the ears of corn.
verse	41	2	24	And the Pharisees said unto him, Behold, why do they on the sabbath day that which is not lawful?
verse	41	2	25	@@And he said unto them, @6Have ye never read what David did, when he had need, and was an hungred, he, and they that were with him?@5
verse	41	2	26	@@@6How he went into the house of God in the days of Abiathar the high priest, and did eat the shewbread, which is not lawful to eat but for the priests, and gave also to them which were with him?@5
verse	41	2	27	@@And he said unto them, @6The sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath:@5
verse	41	2	28	@@@6Therefore the Son of man is Lord also of the sabbath.@5
verse	41	3	1	And he entered again into the synagogue; and there was a man there which had a withered hand.
verse	41	3	2	And they watched him, whether he would heal him on the sabbath day; that they might accuse him.
verse	41	3	3	@@And he saith unto the man which had the withered hand, @6Stand forth.@5
verse	41	3	4	@@And he saith unto them, @6Is it lawful to do good on the sabbath days, or to do evil? to save life, or to kill?@5 But they held their peace.
verse	41	3	5	@@And when he had looked round about on them with anger, being grieved for the hardness of their hearts, he saith unto the man, @6Stretch forth thine hand.@5 And he stretched @9it@7 out: and his hand was restored whole as the other.
verse	41	3	6	And the Pharisees went forth, and straightway took counsel with the Herodians against him, how they might destroy him.
verse	41	3	7	But Jesus withdrew himself with his disciples to the sea: and a great multitude from Galilee followed him, and from Judaea,
verse	41	3	8	@@And from Jerusalem, and from Idumaea, and @9from@7 beyond Jordan; and they about Tyre and Sidon, a great multitude, when they had heard what great things he did, came unto him.
verse	41	3	9	And he spake to his disciples, that a small ship should wait on him because of the multitude, lest they should throng him.
verse	41	3	10	For he had healed many; insomuch that they pressed upon him for to touch him, as many as had plagues.
verse	41	3	11	And unclean spirits, when they saw him, fell down before him, and cried, saying, Thou art the Son of God.
verse	41	3	12	And he straitly charged them that they should not make him known.
verse	41	3	13	@@And he goeth up into a mountain, and calleth @9unto him@7 whom he would: and they came unto him.
verse	41	3	14	And he ordained twelve, that they should be with him, and that he might send them forth to preach,
verse	41	3	15	And to have power to heal sicknesses, and to cast out devils:
verse	41	3	16	And Simon he surnamed Peter;
verse	41	3	17	@@And James the @9son@7 of Zebedee, and John the brother of James; and he surnamed them Boanerges, which is, The sons of thunder:
verse	41	3	18	@@And Andrew, and Philip, and Bartholomew, and Matthew, and Thomas, and James the @9son@7 of Alphaeus, and Thaddaeus, and Simon the Canaanite,
verse	41	3	19	And Judas Iscariot, which also betrayed him: and they went into an house.
verse	41	3	20	And the multitude cometh together again, so that they could not so much as eat bread.
verse	41	3	21	@@And when his friends heard @9of it,@7 they went out to lay hold on him: for they said, He is beside himself.
verse	41	3	22	And the scribes which came down from Jerusalem said, He hath Beelzebub, and by the prince of the devils casteth he out devils.
verse	41	3	23	@@And he called them @9unto him,@7 and said unto them in parables, @6How can Satan cast out Satan?@5
verse	41	3	24	@@@6And if a kingdom be divided against itself, that kingdom cannot stand.@5
verse	41	3	25	@@@6And if a house be divided against itself, that house cannot stand.@5
verse	41	3	26	@@@6And if Satan rise up against himself, and be divided, he cannot stand, but hath an end.@5
verse	41	3	27	@@@6No man can enter into a strong man's house, and spoil his goods, except he will first bind the strong man; and then he will spoil his house.@5
verse	41	3	28	@@@6Verily I say unto you, All sins shall be forgiven unto the sons of men, and blasphemies wherewith soever they shall blaspheme:@5
verse	41	3	29	@@@6But he that shall blaspheme against the Holy Ghost hath never forgiveness, but is in danger of eternal damnation:@5
verse	41	3	30	Because they said, He hath an unclean spirit.
verse	41	3	31	There came then his brethren and his mother, and, standing without, sent unto him, calling him.
verse	41	3	32	And the multitude sat about him, and they said unto him, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren without seek for thee.
verse	41	3	33	@@And he answered them, saying, @6Who is my mother, or my brethren?@5
verse	41	3	34	@@And he looked round about on them which sat about him, and said, @6Behold my mother and my brethren!@5
verse	41	3	35	@@@6For whosoever shall do the will of God, the same is my brother, and my sister, and mother.@5
verse	41	4	1	And he began again to teach by the sea side: and there was gathered unto him a great multitude, so that he entered into a ship, and sat in the sea; and the whole multitude was by the sea on the land.
verse	41	4	2	And he taught them many things by parables, and said unto them in his doctrine,
verse	41	4	3	@@@6Hearken; Behold, there went out a sower to sow:@5
verse	41	4	4	@@@6And it came to pass, as he sowed, some fell by the way side, and the fowls of the air came and devoured it up.@5
verse	41	4	5	@@@6And some fell on stony ground, where it had not much earth; and immediately it sprang up, because it had no depth of earth:@5
verse	41	4	6	@@@6But when the sun was up, it was scorched; and because it had no root, it withered away.@5
verse	41	4	7	@@@6And some fell among thorns, and the thorns grew up, and choked it, and it yielded no fruit.@5
verse	41	4	8	@@@6And other fell on good ground, and did yield fruit that sprang up and increased; and brought forth, some thirty, and some sixty, and some an hundred.@5
verse	41	4	9	@@And he said unto them, @6He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.@5
verse	41	4	10	And when he was alone, they that were about him with the twelve asked of him the parable.
verse	41	4	11	@@And he said unto them, @6Unto you it is given to know the mystery of the kingdom of God: but unto them that are without, all these @9things@7 are done in parables:@5
verse	41	4	12	@@@6That seeing they may see, and not perceive; and hearing they may hear, and not understand; lest at any time they should be converted, and @9their@7 sins should be forgiven them.@5
verse	41	4	13	@@And he said unto them, @6Know ye not this parable? and how then will ye know all parables?@5
verse	41	4	14	@@@6The sower soweth the word.@5
verse	41	4	15	@@@6And these are they by the way side, where the word is sown; but when they have heard, Satan cometh immediately, and taketh away the word that was sown in their hearts.@5
verse	41	4	16	@@@6And these are they likewise which are sown on stony ground; who, when they have heard the word, immediately receive it with gladness;@5
verse	41	4	17	@@@6And have no root in themselves, and so endure but for a time: afterward, when affliction or persecution ariseth for the word's sake, immediately they are offended.@5
verse	41	4	18	@@@6And these are they which are sown among thorns; such as hear the word,@5
verse	41	4	19	@@@6And the cares of this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, and the lusts of other things entering in, choke the word, and it becometh unfruitful.@5
verse	41	4	20	@@@6And these are they which are sown on good ground; such as hear the word, and receive @9it,@7 and bring forth fruit, some thirtyfold, some sixty, and some an hundred.@5
verse	41	4	21	@@And he said unto them, @6Is a candle brought to be put under a bushel, or under a bed? and not to be set on a candlestick?@5
verse	41	4	22	@@@6For there is nothing hid, which shall not be manifested; neither was any thing kept secret, but that it should come abroad.@5
verse	41	4	23	@@@6If any man have ears to hear, let him hear.@5
verse	41	4	24	@@And he said unto them, @6Take heed what ye hear: with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you: and unto you that hear shall more be given.@5
verse	41	4	25	@@@6For he that hath, to him shall be given: and he that hath not, from him shall be taken even that which he hath.@5
verse	41	4	26	@@And he said, @6So is the kingdom of God, as if a man should cast seed into the ground;@5
verse	41	4	27	@@@6And should sleep, and rise night and day, and the seed should spring and grow up, he knoweth not how.@5
verse	41	4	28	@@@6For the earth bringeth forth fruit of herself; first the blade, then the ear, after that the full corn in the ear.@5
verse	41	4	29	@@@6But when the fruit is brought forth, immediately he putteth in the sickle, because the harvest is come.@5
verse	41	4	30	@@And he said, @6Whereunto shall we liken the kingdom of God? or with what comparison shall we compare it?@5
verse	41	4	31	@@@6@9It is@7 like a grain of mustard seed, which, when it is sown in the earth, is less than all the seeds that be in the earth:@5
verse	41	4	32	@@@6But when it is sown, it groweth up, and becometh greater than all herbs, and shooteth out great branches; so that the fowls of the air may lodge under the shadow of it.@5
verse	41	4	33	@@And with many such parables spake he the word unto them, as they were able to hear @9it. @7
verse	41	4	34	But without a parable spake he not unto them: and when they were alone, he expounded all things to his disciples.
verse	41	4	35	@@And the same day, when the even was come, he saith unto them, @6Let us pass over unto the other side.@5
verse	41	4	36	And when they had sent away the multitude, they took him even as he was in the ship. And there were also with him other little ships.
verse	41	4	37	And there arose a great storm of wind, and the waves beat into the ship, so that it was now full.
verse	41	4	38	And he was in the hinder part of the ship, asleep on a pillow: and they awake him, and say unto him, Master, carest thou not that we perish?
verse	41	4	39	@@And he arose, and rebuked the wind, and said unto the sea, @6Peace, be still.@5 And the wind ceased, and there was a great calm.
verse	41	4	40	@@And he said unto them, @6Why are ye so fearful? how is it that ye have no faith?@5
verse	41	4	41	And they feared exceedingly, and said one to another, What manner of man is this, that even the wind and the sea obey him?
verse	41	5	1	And they came over unto the other side of the sea, into the country of the Gadarenes.
verse	41	5	2	And when he was come out of the ship, immediately there met him out of the tombs a man with an unclean spirit,
verse	41	5	3	@@Who had @9his@7 dwelling among the tombs; and no man could bind him, no, not with chains:
verse	41	5	4	@@Because that he had been often bound with fetters and chains, and the chains had been plucked asunder by him, and the fetters broken in pieces: neither could any @9man@7 tame him.
verse	41	5	5	And always, night and day, he was in the mountains, and in the tombs, crying, and cutting himself with stones.
verse	41	5	6	But when he saw Jesus afar off, he ran and worshipped him,
verse	41	5	7	@@And cried with a loud voice, and said, What have I to do with thee, Jesus, @9thou@7 Son of the most high God? I adjure thee by God, that thou torment me not.
verse	41	5	8	@@For he said unto him, @6Come out of the man, @9thou@7 unclean spirit.@5
verse	41	5	9	@@And he asked him, @6What @9is@7 thy name?@5 And he answered, saying, My name @9is@7 Legion: for we are many.
verse	41	5	10	And he besought him much that he would not send them away out of the country.
verse	41	5	11	Now there was there nigh unto the mountains a great herd of swine feeding.
verse	41	5	12	And all the devils besought him, saying, Send us into the swine, that we may enter into them.
verse	41	5	13	And forthwith Jesus gave them leave. And the unclean spirits went out, and entered into the swine: and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the sea, (they were about two thousand;) and were choked in the sea.
verse	41	5	14	@@And they that fed the swine fled, and told @9it@7 in the city, and in the country. And they went out to see what it was that was done.
verse	41	5	15	And they come to Jesus, and see him that was possessed with the devil, and had the legion, sitting, and clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid.
verse	41	5	16	@@And they that saw @9it@7 told them how it befell to him that was possessed with the devil, and @9also@7 concerning the swine.
verse	41	5	17	And they began to pray him to depart out of their coasts.
verse	41	5	18	And when he was come into the ship, he that had been possessed with the devil prayed him that he might be with him.
verse	41	5	19	@@Howbeit Jesus suffered him not, but saith unto him, @6Go home to thy friends, and tell them how great things the Lord hath done for thee, and hath had compassion on thee.@5
verse	41	5	20	@@And he departed, and began to publish in Decapolis how great things Jesus had done for him: and all @9men@7 did marvel.
verse	41	5	21	And when Jesus was passed over again by ship unto the other side, much people gathered unto him: and he was nigh unto the sea.
verse	41	5	22	And, behold, there cometh one of the rulers of the synagogue, Jairus by name; and when he saw him, he fell at his feet,
verse	41	5	23	@@And besought him greatly, saying, My little daughter lieth at the point of death: @9I pray thee,@7 come and lay thy hands on her, that she may be healed; and she shall live.
verse	41	5	24	@@And @9Jesus@7 went with him; and much people followed him, and thronged him.
verse	41	5	25	And a certain woman, which had an issue of blood twelve years,
verse	41	5	26	And had suffered many things of many physicians, and had spent all that she had, and was nothing bettered, but rather grew worse,
verse	41	5	27	When she had heard of Jesus, came in the press behind, and touched his garment.
verse	41	5	28	For she said, If I may touch but his clothes, I shall be whole.
verse	41	5	29	@@And straightway the fountain of her blood was dried up; and she felt in @9her@7 body that she was healed of that plague.
verse	41	5	30	@@And Jesus, immediately knowing in himself that virtue had gone out of him, turned him about in the press, and said, @6Who touched my clothes?@5
verse	41	5	31	@@And his disciples said unto him, Thou seest the multitude thronging thee, and sayest thou, @6Who touched me?@5
verse	41	5	32	And he looked round about to see her that had done this thing.
verse	41	5	33	But the woman fearing and trembling, knowing what was done in her, came and fell down before him, and told him all the truth.
verse	41	5	34	@@And he said unto her, @6Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole; go in peace, and be whole of thy plague.@5
verse	41	5	35	@@While he yet spake, there came from the ruler of the synagogue's @9house certain@7 which said, Thy daughter is dead: why troublest thou the Master any further?
verse	41	5	36	@@As soon as Jesus heard the word that was spoken, he saith unto the ruler of the synagogue, @6Be not afraid, only believe.@5
verse	41	5	37	And he suffered no man to follow him, save Peter, and James, and John the brother of James.
verse	41	5	38	And he cometh to the house of the ruler of the synagogue, and seeth the tumult, and them that wept and wailed greatly.
verse	41	5	39	@@And when he was come in, he saith unto them, @6Why make ye this ado, and weep? the damsel is not dead, but sleepeth.@5
verse	41	5	40	And they laughed him to scorn. But when he had put them all out, he taketh the father and the mother of the damsel, and them that were with him, and entereth in where the damsel was lying.
verse	41	5	41	@@And he took the damsel by the hand, and said unto her, @6Talitha cumi;@5 which is, being interpreted, @6Damsel,@5 I say unto thee, @6arise.@5
verse	41	5	42	@@And straightway the damsel arose, and walked; for she was @9of the age@7 of twelve years. And they were astonished with a great astonishment.
verse	41	5	43	And he charged them straitly that no man should know it; and commanded that something should be given her to eat.
verse	41	6	1	And he went out from thence, and came into his own country; and his disciples follow him.
verse	41	6	2	@@And when the sabbath day was come, he began to teach in the synagogue: and many hearing @9him@7 were astonished, saying, From whence hath this @9man@7 these things? and what wisdom @9is@7 this which is given unto him, that even such mighty works are wrought by his hands?
verse	41	6	3	Is not this the carpenter, the son of Mary, the brother of James, and Joses, and of Juda, and Simon? and are not his sisters here with us? And they were offended at him.
verse	41	6	4	@@But Jesus said unto them, @6A prophet is not without honour, but in his own country, and among his own kin, and in his own house.@5
verse	41	6	5	@@And he could there do no mighty work, save that he laid his hands upon a few sick folk, and healed @9them. @7
verse	41	6	6	And he marvelled because of their unbelief. And he went round about the villages, teaching.
verse	41	6	7	@@And he called @9unto him@7 the twelve, and began to send them forth by two and two; and gave them power over unclean spirits;
verse	41	6	8	@@And commanded them that they should take nothing for @9their@7 journey, save a staff only; no scrip, no bread, no money in @9their@7 purse:
verse	41	6	9	@@But @9be@7 shod with sandals; and not put on two coats.
verse	41	6	10	@@And he said unto them, @6In what place soever ye enter into an house, there abide till ye depart from that place.@5
verse	41	6	11	@@@6And whosoever shall not receive you, nor hear you, when ye depart thence, shake off the dust under your feet for a testimony against them. Verily I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for Sodom and Gomorrha in the day of judgment, than for that city.@5
verse	41	6	12	And they went out, and preached that men should repent.
verse	41	6	13	@@And they cast out many devils, and anointed with oil many that were sick, and healed @9them. @7
verse	41	6	14	@@And king Herod heard @9of him;@7 (for his name was spread abroad:) and he said, That John the Baptist was risen from the dead, and therefore mighty works do shew forth themselves in him.
verse	41	6	15	Others said, That it is Elias. And others said, That it is a prophet, or as one of the prophets.
verse	41	6	16	@@But when Herod heard @9thereof,@7 he said, It is John, whom I beheaded: he is risen from the dead.
verse	41	6	17	For Herod himself had sent forth and laid hold upon John, and bound him in prison for Herodias' sake, his brother Philip's wife: for he had married her.
verse	41	6	18	For John had said unto Herod, It is not lawful for thee to have thy brother's wife.
verse	41	6	19	Therefore Herodias had a quarrel against him, and would have killed him; but she could not:
verse	41	6	20	For Herod feared John, knowing that he was a just man and an holy, and observed him; and when he heard him, he did many things, and heard him gladly.
verse	41	6	21	@@And when a convenient day was come, that Herod on his birthday made a supper to his lords, high captains, and chief @9estates@7 of Galilee;
verse	41	6	22	@@And when the daughter of the said Herodias came in, and danced, and pleased Herod and them that sat with him, the king said unto the damsel, Ask of me whatsoever thou wilt, and I will give @9it@7 thee.
verse	41	6	23	@@And he sware unto her, Whatsoever thou shalt ask of me, I will give @9it@7 thee, unto the half of my kingdom.
verse	41	6	24	And she went forth, and said unto her mother, What shall I ask? And she said, The head of John the Baptist.
verse	41	6	25	And she came in straightway with haste unto the king, and asked, saying, I will that thou give me by and by in a charger the head of John the Baptist.
verse	41	6	26	@@And the king was exceeding sorry; @9yet@7 for his oath's sake, and for their sakes which sat with him, he would not reject her.
verse	41	6	27	And immediately the king sent an executioner, and commanded his head to be brought: and he went and beheaded him in the prison,
verse	41	6	28	And brought his head in a charger, and gave it to the damsel: and the damsel gave it to her mother.
verse	41	6	29	@@And when his disciples heard @9of it,@7 they came and took up his corpse, and laid it in a tomb.
verse	41	6	30	And the apostles gathered themselves together unto Jesus, and told him all things, both what they had done, and what they had taught.
verse	41	6	31	@@And he said unto them, @6Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while:@5 for there were many coming and going, and they had no leisure so much as to eat.
verse	41	6	32	And they departed into a desert place by ship privately.
verse	41	6	33	And the people saw them departing, and many knew him, and ran afoot thither out of all cities, and outwent them, and came together unto him.
verse	41	6	34	And Jesus, when he came out, saw much people, and was moved with compassion toward them, because they were as sheep not having a shepherd: and he began to teach them many things.
verse	41	6	35	@@And when the day was now far spent, his disciples came unto him, and said, This is a desert place, and now the time @9is@7 far passed:
verse	41	6	36	Send them away, that they may go into the country round about, and into the villages, and buy themselves bread: for they have nothing to eat.
verse	41	6	37	@@He answered and said unto them, @6Give ye them to eat.@5 And they say unto him, Shall we go and buy two hundred pennyworth of bread, and give them to eat?
verse	41	6	38	@@He saith unto them, @6How many loaves have ye? go and see.@5 And when they knew, they say, Five, and two fishes.
verse	41	6	39	And he commanded them to make all sit down by companies upon the green grass.
verse	41	6	40	And they sat down in ranks, by hundreds, and by fifties.
verse	41	6	41	@@And when he had taken the five loaves and the two fishes, he looked up to heaven, and blessed, and brake the loaves, and gave @9them@7 to his disciples to set before them; and the two fishes divided he among them all.
verse	41	6	42	And they did all eat, and were filled.
verse	41	6	43	And they took up twelve baskets full of the fragments, and of the fishes.
verse	41	6	44	And they that did eat of the loaves were about five thousand men.
verse	41	6	45	And straightway he constrained his disciples to get into the ship, and to go to the other side before unto Bethsaida, while he sent away the people.
verse	41	6	46	And when he had sent them away, he departed into a mountain to pray.
verse	41	6	47	And when even was come, the ship was in the midst of the sea, and he alone on the land.
verse	41	6	48	And he saw them toiling in rowing; for the wind was contrary unto them: and about the fourth watch of the night he cometh unto them, walking upon the sea, and would have passed by them.
verse	41	6	49	But when they saw him walking upon the sea, they supposed it had been a spirit, and cried out:
verse	41	6	50	@@For they all saw him, and were troubled. And immediately he talked with them, and saith unto them, @6Be of good cheer: it is I; be not afraid.@5
verse	41	6	51	And he went up unto them into the ship; and the wind ceased: and they were sore amazed in themselves beyond measure, and wondered.
verse	41	6	52	@@For they considered not @9the miracle@7 of the loaves: for their heart was hardened.
verse	41	6	53	And when they had passed over, they came into the land of Gennesaret, and drew to the shore.
verse	41	6	54	And when they were come out of the ship, straightway they knew him,
verse	41	6	55	And ran through that whole region round about, and began to carry about in beds those that were sick, where they heard he was.
verse	41	6	56	And whithersoever he entered, into villages, or cities, or country, they laid the sick in the streets, and besought him that they might touch if it were but the border of his garment: and as many as touched him were made whole.
verse	41	7	1	Then came together unto him the Pharisees, and certain of the scribes, which came from Jerusalem.
verse	41	7	2	And when they saw some of his disciples eat bread with defiled, that is to say, with unwashen, hands, they found fault.
verse	41	7	3	@@For the Pharisees, and all the Jews, except they wash @9their@7 hands oft, eat not, holding the tradition of the elders.
verse	41	7	4	@@And @9when they come@7 from the market, except they wash, they eat not. And many other things there be, which they have received to hold, @9as@7 the washing of cups, and pots, brasen vessels, and of tables.
verse	41	7	5	Then the Pharisees and scribes asked him, Why walk not thy disciples according to the tradition of the elders, but eat bread with unwashen hands?
verse	41	7	6	@@He answered and said unto them, @6Well hath Esaias prophesied of you hypocrites, as it is written, This people honoureth me with @9their@7 lips, but their heart is far from me.@5
verse	41	7	7	@@@6Howbeit in vain do they worship me, teaching @9for@7 doctrines the commandments of men.@5
verse	41	7	8	@@@6For laying aside the commandment of God, ye hold the tradition of men, @9as@7 the washing of pots and cups: and many other such like things ye do.@5
verse	41	7	9	@@And he said unto them, @6Full well ye reject the commandment of God, that ye may keep your own tradition.@5
verse	41	7	10	@@@6For Moses said, Honour thy father and thy mother; and, Whoso curseth father or mother, let him die the death:@5
verse	41	7	11	@@@6But ye say, If a man shall say to his father or mother, @9It is@7 Corban, that is to say, a gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be profited by me; @9he shall be free. @7@5
verse	41	7	12	@@@6And ye suffer him no more to do ought for his father or his mother;@5
verse	41	7	13	@@@6Making the word of God of none effect through your tradition, which ye have delivered: and many such like things do ye.@5
verse	41	7	14	@@And when he had called all the people @9unto him,@7 he said unto them, @6Hearken unto me every one @9of you,@7 and understand:@5
verse	41	7	15	@@@6There is nothing from without a man, that entering into him can defile him: but the things which come out of him, those are they that defile the man.@5
verse	41	7	16	@@@6If any man have ears to hear, let him hear.@5
verse	41	7	17	And when he was entered into the house from the people, his disciples asked him concerning the parable.
verse	41	7	18	@@And he saith unto them, @6Are ye so without understanding also? Do ye not perceive, that whatsoever thing from without entereth into the man, @9it@7 cannot defile him;@5
verse	41	7	19	@@@6Because it entereth not into his heart, but into the belly, and goeth out into the draught, purging all meats?@5
verse	41	7	20	@@And he said, @6That which cometh out of the man, that defileth the man.@5
verse	41	7	21	@@@6For from within, out of the heart of men, proceed evil thoughts, adulteries, fornications, murders,@5
verse	41	7	22	@@@6Thefts, covetousness, wickedness, deceit, lasciviousness, an evil eye, blasphemy, pride, foolishness:@5
verse	41	7	23	@@@6All these evil things come from within, and defile the man.@5
verse	41	7	24	@@And from thence he arose, and went into the borders of Tyre and Sidon, and entered into an house, and would have no man know @9it:@7 but he could not be hid.
verse	41	7	25	@@For a @9certain@7 woman, whose young daughter had an unclean spirit, heard of him, and came and fell at his feet:
verse	41	7	26	The woman was a Greek, a Syrophenician by nation; and she besought him that he would cast forth the devil out of her daughter.
verse	41	7	27	@@But Jesus said unto her, @6Let the children first be filled: for it is not meet to take the children's bread, and to cast @9it@7 unto the dogs.@5
verse	41	7	28	And she answered and said unto him, Yes, Lord: yet the dogs under the table eat of the children's crumbs.
verse	41	7	29	@@And he said unto her, @6For this saying go thy way; the devil is gone out of thy daughter.@5
verse	41	7	30	And when she was come to her house, she found the devil gone out, and her daughter laid upon the bed.
verse	41	7	31	And again, departing from the coasts of Tyre and Sidon, he came unto the sea of Galilee, through the midst of the coasts of Decapolis.
verse	41	7	32	And they bring unto him one that was deaf, and had an impediment in his speech; and they beseech him to put his hand upon him.
verse	41	7	33	And he took him aside from the multitude, and put his fingers into his ears, and he spit, and touched his tongue;
verse	41	7	34	@@And looking up to heaven, he sighed, and saith unto him, @6Ephphatha,@5 that is, @6Be opened.@5
verse	41	7	35	And straightway his ears were opened, and the string of his tongue was loosed, and he spake plain.
verse	41	7	36	@@And he charged them that they should tell no man: but the more he charged them, so much the more a great deal they published @9it; @7
verse	41	7	37	And were beyond measure astonished, saying, He hath done all things well: he maketh both the deaf to hear, and the dumb to speak.
verse	41	8	1	@@In those days the multitude being very great, and having nothing to eat, Jesus called his disciples @9unto him,@7 and saith unto them,
verse	41	8	2	@@@6I have compassion on the multitude, because they have now been with me three days, and have nothing to eat:@5
verse	41	8	3	@@@6And if I send them away fasting to their own houses, they will faint by the way: for divers of them came from far.@5
verse	41	8	4	@@And his disciples answered him, From whence can a man satisfy these @9men@7 with bread here in the wilderness?
verse	41	8	5	@@And he asked them, @6How many loaves have ye?@5 And they said, Seven.
verse	41	8	6	@@And he commanded the people to sit down on the ground: and he took the seven loaves, and gave thanks, and brake, and gave to his disciples to set before @9them;@7 and they did set @9them@7 before the people.
verse	41	8	7	@@And they had a few small fishes: and he blessed, and commanded to set them also before @9them. @7
verse	41	8	8	@@So they did eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken @9meat@7 that was left seven baskets.
verse	41	8	9	And they that had eaten were about four thousand: and he sent them away.
verse	41	8	10	And straightway he entered into a ship with his disciples, and came into the parts of Dalmanutha.
verse	41	8	11	And the Pharisees came forth, and began to question with him, seeking of him a sign from heaven, tempting him.
verse	41	8	12	@@And he sighed deeply in his spirit, and saith, @6Why doth this generation seek after a sign? verily I say unto you, There shall no sign be given unto this generation.@5
verse	41	8	13	And he left them, and entering into the ship again departed to the other side.
verse	41	8	14	@@Now @9the disciples@7 had forgotten to take bread, neither had they in the ship with them more than one loaf.
verse	41	8	15	@@And he charged them, saying, @6Take heed, beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, and @9of@7 the leaven of Herod.@5
verse	41	8	16	@@And they reasoned among themselves, saying, @9It is@7 because we have no bread.
verse	41	8	17	@@And when Jesus knew @9it,@7 he saith unto them, @6Why reason ye, because ye have no bread? perceive ye not yet, neither understand? have ye your heart yet hardened?@5
verse	41	8	18	@@@6Having eyes, see ye not? and having ears, hear ye not? and do ye not remember?@5
verse	41	8	19	@@@6When I brake the five loaves among five thousand, how many baskets full of fragments took ye up?@5 They say unto him, Twelve.
verse	41	8	20	@@@6And when the seven among four thousand, how many baskets full of fragments took ye up?@5 And they said, Seven.
verse	41	8	21	@@And he said unto them, @6How is it that ye do not understand?@5
verse	41	8	22	And he cometh to Bethsaida; and they bring a blind man unto him, and besought him to touch him.
verse	41	8	23	And he took the blind man by the hand, and led him out of the town; and when he had spit on his eyes, and put his hands upon him, he asked him if he saw ought.
verse	41	8	24	And he looked up, and said, I see men as trees, walking.
verse	41	8	25	@@After that he put @9his@7 hands again upon his eyes, and made him look up: and he was restored, and saw every man clearly.
verse	41	8	26	@@And he sent him away to his house, saying, @6Neither go into the town, nor tell @9it@7 to any in the town.@5
verse	41	8	27	@@And Jesus went out, and his disciples, into the towns of Caesarea Philippi: and by the way he asked his disciples, saying unto them, @6Whom do men say that I am?@5
verse	41	8	28	@@And they answered, John the Baptist: but some @9say,@7 Elias; and others, One of the prophets.
verse	41	8	29	@@And he saith unto them, @6But whom say ye that I am?@5 And Peter answereth and saith unto him, Thou art the Christ.
verse	41	8	30	And he charged them that they should tell no man of him.
verse	41	8	31	@@And he began to teach them, that the Son of man must suffer many things, and be rejected of the elders, and @9of@7 the chief priests, and scribes, and be killed, and after three days rise again.
verse	41	8	32	And he spake that saying openly. And Peter took him, and began to rebuke him.
verse	41	8	33	@@But when he had turned about and looked on his disciples, he rebuked Peter, saying, @6Get thee behind me, Satan: for thou savourest not the things that be of God, but the things that be of men.@5
verse	41	8	34	@@And when he had called the people @9unto him@7 with his disciples also, he said unto them, @6Whosoever will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.@5
verse	41	8	35	@@@6For whosoever will save his life shall lose it; but whosoever shall lose his life for my sake and the gospel's, the same shall save it.@5
verse	41	8	36	@@@6For what shall it profit a man, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul?@5
verse	41	8	37	@@@6Or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?@5
verse	41	8	38	@@@6Whosoever therefore shall be ashamed of me and of my words in this adulterous and sinful generation; of him also shall the Son of man be ashamed, when he cometh in the glory of his Father with the holy angels.@5
verse	41	9	1	@@And he said unto them, @6Verily I say unto you, That there be some of them that stand here, which shall not taste of death, till they have seen the kingdom of God come with power.@5
verse	41	9	2	@@And after six days Jesus taketh @9with him@7 Peter, and James, and John, and leadeth them up into an high mountain apart by themselves: and he was transfigured before them.
verse	41	9	3	And his raiment became shining, exceeding white as snow; so as no fuller on earth can white them.
verse	41	9	4	And there appeared unto them Elias with Moses: and they were talking with Jesus.
verse	41	9	5	And Peter answered and said to Jesus, Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias.
verse	41	9	6	For he wist not what to say; for they were sore afraid.
verse	41	9	7	And there was a cloud that overshadowed them: and a voice came out of the cloud, saying, This is my beloved Son: hear him.
verse	41	9	8	And suddenly, when they had looked round about, they saw no man any more, save Jesus only with themselves.
verse	41	9	9	And as they came down from the mountain, he charged them that they should tell no man what things they had seen, till the Son of man were risen from the dead.
verse	41	9	10	And they kept that saying with themselves, questioning one with another what the rising from the dead should mean.
verse	41	9	11	And they asked him, saying, Why say the scribes that Elias must first come?
verse	41	9	12	@@And he answered and told them, @6Elias verily cometh first, and restoreth all things; and how it is written of the Son of man, that he must suffer many things, and be set at nought.@5
verse	41	9	13	@@@6But I say unto you, That Elias is indeed come, and they have done unto him whatsoever they listed, as it is written of him.@5
verse	41	9	14	@@And when he came to @9his@7 disciples, he saw a great multitude about them, and the scribes questioning with them.
verse	41	9	15	@@And straightway all the people, when they beheld him, were greatly amazed, and running to @9him@7 saluted him.
verse	41	9	16	@@And he asked the scribes, @6What question ye with them?@5
verse	41	9	17	And one of the multitude answered and said, Master, I have brought unto thee my son, which hath a dumb spirit;
verse	41	9	18	And wheresoever he taketh him, he teareth him: and he foameth, and gnasheth with his teeth, and pineth away: and I spake to thy disciples that they should cast him out; and they could not.
verse	41	9	19	@@He answereth him, and saith, @6O faithless generation, how long shall I be with you? how long shall I suffer you? bring him unto me.@5
verse	41	9	20	And they brought him unto him: and when he saw him, straightway the spirit tare him; and he fell on the ground, and wallowed foaming.
verse	41	9	21	@@And he asked his father, @6How long is it ago since this came unto him?@5 And he said, Of a child.
verse	41	9	22	And ofttimes it hath cast him into the fire, and into the waters, to destroy him: but if thou canst do any thing, have compassion on us, and help us.
verse	41	9	23	@@Jesus said unto him, @6If thou canst believe, all things @9are@7 possible to him that believeth.@5
verse	41	9	24	And straightway the father of the child cried out, and said with tears, Lord, I believe; help thou mine unbelief.
verse	41	9	25	@@When Jesus saw that the people came running together, he rebuked the foul spirit, saying unto him, @6@9Thou@7 dumb and deaf spirit, I charge thee, come out of him, and enter no more into him.@5
verse	41	9	26	@@And @9the spirit@7 cried, and rent him sore, and came out of him: and he was as one dead; insomuch that many said, He is dead.
verse	41	9	27	But Jesus took him by the hand, and lifted him up; and he arose.
verse	41	9	28	And when he was come into the house, his disciples asked him privately, Why could not we cast him out?
verse	41	9	29	@@And he said unto them, @6This kind can come forth by nothing, but by prayer and fasting.@5
verse	41	9	30	@@And they departed thence, and passed through Galilee; and he would not that any man should know @9it. @7
verse	41	9	31	@@For he taught his disciples, and said unto them, @6The Son of man is delivered into the hands of men, and they shall kill him; and after that he is killed, he shall rise the third day.@5
verse	41	9	32	But they understood not that saying, and were afraid to ask him.
verse	41	9	33	@@And he came to Capernaum: and being in the house he asked them, @6What was it that ye disputed among yourselves by the way?@5
verse	41	9	34	@@But they held their peace: for by the way they had disputed among themselves, who @9should be@7 the greatest.
verse	41	9	35	@@And he sat down, and called the twelve, and saith unto them, @6If any man desire to be first, @9the same@7 shall be last of all, and servant of all.@5
verse	41	9	36	And he took a child, and set him in the midst of them: and when he had taken him in his arms, he said unto them,
verse	41	9	37	@@@6Whosoever shall receive one of such children in my name, receiveth me: and whosoever shall receive me, receiveth not me, but him that sent me.@5
verse	41	9	38	And John answered him, saying, Master, we saw one casting out devils in thy name, and he followeth not us: and we forbad him, because he followeth not us.
verse	41	9	39	@@But Jesus said, @6Forbid him not: for there is no man which shall do a miracle in my name, that can lightly speak evil of me.@5
verse	41	9	40	@@@6For he that is not against us is on our part.@5
verse	41	9	41	@@@6For whosoever shall give you a cup of water to drink in my name, because ye belong to Christ, verily I say unto you, he shall not lose his reward.@5
verse	41	9	42	@@@6And whosoever shall offend one of @9these@7 little ones that believe in me, it is better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and he were cast into the sea.@5
verse	41	9	43	@@@6And if thy hand offend thee, cut it off: it is better for thee to enter into life maimed, than having two hands to go into hell, into the fire that never shall be quenched:@5
verse	41	9	44	@@@6Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched.@5
verse	41	9	45	@@@6And if thy foot offend thee, cut it off: it is better for thee to enter halt into life, than having two feet to be cast into hell, into the fire that never shall be quenched:@5
verse	41	9	46	@@@6Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched.@5
verse	41	9	47	@@@6And if thine eye offend thee, pluck it out: it is better for thee to enter into the kingdom of God with one eye, than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire:@5
verse	41	9	48	@@@6Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched.@5
verse	41	9	49	@@@6For every one shall be salted with fire, and every sacrifice shall be salted with salt.@5
verse	41	9	50	@@@6Salt @9is@7 good: but if the salt have lost his saltness, wherewith will ye season it? Have salt in yourselves, and have peace one with another.@5
verse	41	10	1	And he arose from thence, and cometh into the coasts of Judaea by the farther side of Jordan: and the people resort unto him again; and, as he was wont, he taught them again.
verse	41	10	2	@@And the Pharisees came to him, and asked him, Is it lawful for a man to put away @9his@7 wife? tempting him.
verse	41	10	3	@@And he answered and said unto them, @6What did Moses command you?@5
verse	41	10	4	@@And they said, Moses suffered to write a bill of divorcement, and to put @9her@7 away.
verse	41	10	5	@@And Jesus answered and said unto them, @6For the hardness of your heart he wrote you this precept.@5
verse	41	10	6	@@@6But from the beginning of the creation God made them male and female.@5
verse	41	10	7	@@@6For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and cleave to his wife;@5
verse	41	10	8	@@@6And they twain shall be one flesh: so then they are no more twain, but one flesh.@5
verse	41	10	9	@@@6What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder.@5
verse	41	10	10	@@And in the house his disciples asked him again of the same @9matter. @7
verse	41	10	11	@@And he saith unto them, @6Whosoever shall put away his wife, and marry another, committeth adultery against her.@5
verse	41	10	12	@@@6And if a woman shall put away her husband, and be married to another, she committeth adultery.@5
verse	41	10	13	@@And they brought young children to him, that he should touch them: and @9his@7 disciples rebuked those that brought @9them. @7
verse	41	10	14	@@But when Jesus saw @9it,@7 he was much displeased, and said unto them, @6Suffer the little children to come unto me, and forbid them not: for of such is the kingdom of God.@5
verse	41	10	15	@@@6Verily I say unto you, Whosoever shall not receive the kingdom of God as a little child, he shall not enter therein.@5
verse	41	10	16	@@And he took them up in his arms, put @9his@7 hands upon them, and blessed them.
verse	41	10	17	And when he was gone forth into the way, there came one running, and kneeled to him, and asked him, Good Master, what shall I do that I may inherit eternal life?
verse	41	10	18	@@And Jesus said unto him, @6Why callest thou me good? @9there is@7 none good but one, @9that is,@7 God.@5
verse	41	10	19	@@@6Thou knowest the commandments, Do not commit adultery, Do not kill, Do not steal, Do not bear false witness, Defraud not, Honour thy father and mother.@5
verse	41	10	20	And he answered and said unto him, Master, all these have I observed from my youth.
verse	41	10	21	@@Then Jesus beholding him loved him, and said unto him, @6One thing thou lackest: go thy way, sell whatsoever thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, take up the cross, and follow me.@5
verse	41	10	22	And he was sad at that saying, and went away grieved: for he had great possessions.
verse	41	10	23	@@And Jesus looked round about, and saith unto his disciples, @6How hardly shall they that have riches enter into the kingdom of God!@5
verse	41	10	24	@@And the disciples were astonished at his words. But Jesus answereth again, and saith unto them, @6Children, how hard is it for them that trust in riches to enter into the kingdom of God!@5
verse	41	10	25	@@@6It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.@5
verse	41	10	26	And they were astonished out of measure, saying among themselves, Who then can be saved?
verse	41	10	27	@@And Jesus looking upon them saith, @6With men @9it is@7 impossible, but not with God: for with God all things are possible.@5
verse	41	10	28	Then Peter began to say unto him, Lo, we have left all, and have followed thee.
verse	41	10	29	@@And Jesus answered and said, @6Verily I say unto you, There is no man that hath left house, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or lands, for my sake, and the gospel's,@5
verse	41	10	30	@@@6But he shall receive an hundredfold now in this time, houses, and brethren, and sisters, and mothers, and children, and lands, with persecutions; and in the world to come eternal life.@5
verse	41	10	31	@@@6But many @9that are@7 first shall be last; and the last first.@5
verse	41	10	32	And they were in the way going up to Jerusalem; and Jesus went before them: and they were amazed; and as they followed, they were afraid. And he took again the twelve, and began to tell them what things should happen unto him,
verse	41	10	33	@@@9Saying,@7 @6Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man shall be delivered unto the chief priests, and unto the scribes; and they shall condemn him to death, and shall deliver him to the Gentiles:@5
verse	41	10	34	@@@6And they shall mock him, and shall scourge him, and shall spit upon him, and shall kill him: and the third day he shall rise again.@5
verse	41	10	35	And James and John, the sons of Zebedee, come unto him, saying, Master, we would that thou shouldest do for us whatsoever we shall desire.
verse	41	10	36	@@And he said unto them, @6What would ye that I should do for you?@5
verse	41	10	37	They said unto him, Grant unto us that we may sit, one on thy right hand, and the other on thy left hand, in thy glory.
verse	41	10	38	@@But Jesus said unto them, @6Ye know not what ye ask: can ye drink of the cup that I drink of? and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?@5
verse	41	10	39	@@And they said unto him, We can. And Jesus said unto them, @6Ye shall indeed drink of the cup that I drink of; and with the baptism that I am baptized withal shall ye be baptized:@5
verse	41	10	40	@@@6But to sit on my right hand and on my left hand is not mine to give; but @9it shall be given to them@7 for whom it is prepared.@5
verse	41	10	41	@@And when the ten heard @9it,@7 they began to be much displeased with James and John.
verse	41	10	42	@@But Jesus called them @9to him,@7 and saith unto them, @6Ye know that they which are accounted to rule over the Gentiles exercise lordship over them; and their great ones exercise authority upon them.@5
verse	41	10	43	@@@6But so shall it not be among you: but whosoever will be great among you, shall be your minister:@5
verse	41	10	44	@@@6And whosoever of you will be the chiefest, shall be servant of all.@5
verse	41	10	45	@@@6For even the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.@5
verse	41	10	46	And they came to Jericho: and as he went out of Jericho with his disciples and a great number of people, blind Bartimaeus, the son of Timaeus, sat by the highway side begging.
verse	41	10	47	@@And when he heard that it was Jesus of Nazareth, he began to cry out, and say, Jesus, @9thou@7 Son of David, have mercy on me.
verse	41	10	48	@@And many charged him that he should hold his peace: but he cried the more a great deal, @9Thou@7 Son of David, have mercy on me.
verse	41	10	49	And Jesus stood still, and commanded him to be called. And they call the blind man, saying unto him, Be of good comfort, rise; he calleth thee.
verse	41	10	50	And he, casting away his garment, rose, and came to Jesus.
verse	41	10	51	@@And Jesus answered and said unto him, @6What wilt thou that I should do unto thee?@5 The blind man said unto him, Lord, that I might receive my sight.
verse	41	10	52	@@And Jesus said unto him, @6Go thy way; thy faith hath made thee whole.@5 And immediately he received his sight, and followed Jesus in the way.
verse	41	11	1	And when they came nigh to Jerusalem, unto Bethphage and Bethany, at the mount of Olives, he sendeth forth two of his disciples,
verse	41	11	2	@@And saith unto them, @6Go your way into the village over against you: and as soon as ye be entered into it, ye shall find a colt tied, whereon never man sat; loose him, and bring @9him. @7@5
verse	41	11	3	@@@6And if any man say unto you, Why do ye this? say ye that the Lord hath need of him; and straightway he will send him hither.@5
verse	41	11	4	And they went their way, and found the colt tied by the door without in a place where two ways met; and they loose him.
verse	41	11	5	And certain of them that stood there said unto them, What do ye, loosing the colt?
verse	41	11	6	And they said unto them even as Jesus had commanded: and they let them go.
verse	41	11	7	And they brought the colt to Jesus, and cast their garments on him; and he sat upon him.
verse	41	11	8	@@And many spread their garments in the way: and others cut down branches off the trees, and strawed @9them@7 in the way.
verse	41	11	9	@@And they that went before, and they that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna; Blessed @9is@7 he that cometh in the name of the Lord:
verse	41	11	10	@@Blessed @9be@7 the kingdom of our father David, that cometh in the name of the Lord: Hosanna in the highest.
verse	41	11	11	And Jesus entered into Jerusalem, and into the temple: and when he had looked round about upon all things, and now the eventide was come, he went out unto Bethany with the twelve.
verse	41	11	12	And on the morrow, when they were come from Bethany, he was hungry:
verse	41	11	13	@@And seeing a fig tree afar off having leaves, he came, if haply he might find any thing thereon: and when he came to it, he found nothing but leaves; for the time of figs was not @9yet. @7
verse	41	11	14	@@And Jesus answered and said unto it, @6No man eat fruit of thee hereafter for ever.@5 And his disciples heard @9it.@7
verse	41	11	15	And they come to Jerusalem: and Jesus went into the temple, and began to cast out them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves;
verse	41	11	16	@@And would not suffer that any man should carry @9any@7 vessel through the temple.
verse	41	11	17	@@And he taught, saying unto them, @6Is it not written, My house shall be called of all nations the house of prayer? but ye have made it a den of thieves.@5
verse	41	11	18	@@And the scribes and chief priests heard @9it,@7 and sought how they might destroy him: for they feared him, because all the people was astonished at his doctrine.
verse	41	11	19	And when even was come, he went out of the city.
verse	41	11	20	And in the morning, as they passed by, they saw the fig tree dried up from the roots.
verse	41	11	21	And Peter calling to remembrance saith unto him, Master, behold, the fig tree which thou cursedst is withered away.
verse	41	11	22	@@And Jesus answering saith unto them, @6Have faith in God.@5
verse	41	11	23	@@@6For verily I say unto you, That whosoever shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea; and shall not doubt in his heart, but shall believe that those things which he saith shall come to pass; he shall have whatsoever he saith.@5
verse	41	11	24	@@@6Therefore I say unto you, What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive @9them,@7 and ye shall have @9them. @7@5
verse	41	11	25	@@@6And when ye stand praying, forgive, if ye have ought against any: that your Father also which is in heaven may forgive you your trespasses.@5
verse	41	11	26	@@@6But if ye do not forgive, neither will your Father which is in heaven forgive your trespasses.@5
verse	41	11	27	And they come again to Jerusalem: and as he was walking in the temple, there come to him the chief priests, and the scribes, and the elders,
verse	41	11	28	And say unto him, By what authority doest thou these things? and who gave thee this authority to do these things?
verse	41	11	29	@@And Jesus answered and said unto them, @6I will also ask of you one question, and answer me, and I will tell you by what authority I do these things.@5
verse	41	11	30	@@@6The baptism of John, was @9it@7 from heaven, or of men? answer me.@5
verse	41	11	31	And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say, Why then did ye not believe him?
verse	41	11	32	@@But if we shall say, Of men; they feared the people: for all @9men@7 counted John, that he was a prophet indeed.
verse	41	11	33	@@And they answered and said unto Jesus, We cannot tell. And Jesus answering saith unto them, @6Neither do I tell you by what authority I do these things.@5
verse	41	12	1	@@And he began to speak unto them by parables. @6A @9certain@7 man planted a vineyard, and set an hedge about @9it,@7 and digged @9a place for@7 the winefat, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into a far country.@5
verse	41	12	2	@@@6And at the season he sent to the husbandmen a servant, that he might receive from the husbandmen of the fruit of the vineyard.@5
verse	41	12	3	@@@6And they caught @9him,@7 and beat him, and sent @9him@7 away empty.@5
verse	41	12	4	@@@6And again he sent unto them another servant; and at him they cast stones, and wounded @9him@7 in the head, and sent @9him@7 away shamefully handled.@5
verse	41	12	5	@@@6And again he sent another; and him they killed, and many others; beating some, and killing some.@5
verse	41	12	6	@@@6Having yet therefore one son, his wellbeloved, he sent him also last unto them, saying, They will reverence my son.@5
verse	41	12	7	@@@6But those husbandmen said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and the inheritance shall be ours.@5
verse	41	12	8	@@@6And they took him, and killed @9him,@7 and cast @9him@7 out of the vineyard.@5
verse	41	12	9	@@@6What shall therefore the lord of the vineyard do? he will come and destroy the husbandmen, and will give the vineyard unto others.@5
verse	41	12	10	@@@6And have ye not read this scripture; The stone which the builders rejected is become the head of the corner:@5
verse	41	12	11	@@@6This was the Lord's doing, and it is marvellous in our eyes?@5
verse	41	12	12	And they sought to lay hold on him, but feared the people: for they knew that he had spoken the parable against them: and they left him, and went their way.
verse	41	12	13	@@And they send unto him certain of the Pharisees and of the Herodians, to catch him in @9his@7 words.
verse	41	12	14	And when they were come, they say unto him, Master, we know that thou art true, and carest for no man: for thou regardest not the person of men, but teachest the way of God in truth: Is it lawful to give tribute to Caesar, or not?
verse	41	12	15	@@Shall we give, or shall we not give? But he, knowing their hypocrisy, said unto them, @6Why tempt ye me? bring me a penny, that I may see @9it. @7@5
verse	41	12	16	@@And they brought @9it.@7 And he saith unto them, @6Whose @9is@7 this image and superscription?@5 And they said unto him, Caesar's.
verse	41	12	17	@@And Jesus answering said unto them, @6Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar's, and to God the things that are God's.@5 And they marvelled at him.
verse	41	12	18	Then come unto him the Sadducees, which say there is no resurrection; and they asked him, saying,
verse	41	12	19	@@Master, Moses wrote unto us, If a man's brother die, and leave @9his@7 wife @9behind him,@7 and leave no children, that his brother should take his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.
verse	41	12	20	Now there were seven brethren: and the first took a wife, and dying left no seed.
verse	41	12	21	And the second took her, and died, neither left he any seed: and the third likewise.
verse	41	12	22	And the seven had her, and left no seed: last of all the woman died also.
verse	41	12	23	In the resurrection therefore, when they shall rise, whose wife shall she be of them? for the seven had her to wife.
verse	41	12	24	@@And Jesus answering said unto them, @6Do ye not therefore err, because ye know not the scriptures, neither the power of God?@5
verse	41	12	25	@@@6For when they shall rise from the dead, they neither marry, nor are given in marriage; but are as the angels which are in heaven.@5
verse	41	12	26	@@@6And as touching the dead, that they rise: have ye not read in the book of Moses, how in the bush God spake unto him, saying, I @9am@7 the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob?@5
verse	41	12	27	@@@6He is not the God of the dead, but the God of the living: ye therefore do greatly err.@5
verse	41	12	28	And one of the scribes came, and having heard them reasoning together, and perceiving that he had answered them well, asked him, Which is the first commandment of all?
verse	41	12	29	@@And Jesus answered him, @6The first of all the commandments @9is,@7 Hear, O Israel; The Lord our God is one Lord:@5
verse	41	12	30	@@@6And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment.@5
verse	41	12	31	@@@6And the second @9is@7 like, @9namely@7 this, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself. There is none other commandment greater than these.@5
verse	41	12	32	And the scribe said unto him, Well, Master, thou hast said the truth: for there is one God; and there is none other but he:
verse	41	12	33	@@And to love him with all the heart, and with all the understanding, and with all the soul, and with all the strength, and to love @9his@7 neighbour as himself, is more than all whole burnt offerings and sacrifices.
verse	41	12	34	@@And when Jesus saw that he answered discreetly, he said unto him, @6Thou art not far from the kingdom of God.@5 And no man after that durst ask him @9any question.@7
verse	41	12	35	@@And Jesus answered and said, while he taught in the temple, @6How say the scribes that Christ is the Son of David?@5
verse	41	12	36	@@@6For David himself said by the Holy Ghost, The Lord said to my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool.@5
verse	41	12	37	@@@6David therefore himself calleth him Lord; and whence is he @9then@7 his son? And the common people heard him gladly.@5
verse	41	12	38	@@And he said unto them in his doctrine, @6Beware of the scribes, which love to go in long clothing, and @9love@7 salutations in the marketplaces,@5
verse	41	12	39	@@@6And the chief seats in the synagogues, and the uppermost rooms at feasts:@5
verse	41	12	40	@@@6Which devour widows' houses, and for a pretence make long prayers: these shall receive greater damnation.@5
verse	41	12	41	And Jesus sat over against the treasury, and beheld how the people cast money into the treasury: and many that were rich cast in much.
verse	41	12	42	And there came a certain poor widow, and she threw in two mites, which make a farthing.
verse	41	12	43	@@And he called @9unto him@7 his disciples, and saith unto them, @6Verily I say unto you, That this poor widow hath cast more in, than all they which have cast into the treasury:@5
verse	41	12	44	@@@6For all @9they@7 did cast in of their abundance; but she of her want did cast in all that she had, @9even@7 all her living.@5
verse	41	13	1	@@And as he went out of the temple, one of his disciples saith unto him, Master, see what manner of stones and what buildings @9are here! @7
verse	41	13	2	@@And Jesus answering said unto him, @6Seest thou these great buildings? there shall not be left one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down.@5
verse	41	13	3	And as he sat upon the mount of Olives over against the temple, Peter and James and John and Andrew asked him privately,
verse	41	13	4	@@Tell us, when shall these things be? and what @9shall be@7 the sign when all these things shall be fulfilled?
verse	41	13	5	@@And Jesus answering them began to say, @6Take heed lest any @9man@7 deceive you:@5
verse	41	13	6	@@@6For many shall come in my name, saying, I am @9Christ;@7 and shall deceive many.@5
verse	41	13	7	@@@6And when ye shall hear of wars and rumours of wars, be ye not troubled: for @9such things@7 must needs be; but the end @9shall@7 not @9be@7 yet.@5
verse	41	13	8	@@@6For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be earthquakes in divers places, and there shall be famines and troubles: these @9are@7 the beginnings of sorrows.@5
verse	41	13	9	@@@6But take heed to yourselves: for they shall deliver you up to councils; and in the synagogues ye shall be beaten: and ye shall be brought before rulers and kings for my sake, for a testimony against them.@5
verse	41	13	10	@@@6And the gospel must first be published among all nations.@5
verse	41	13	11	@@@6But when they shall lead @9you,@7 and deliver you up, take no thought beforehand what ye shall speak, neither do ye premeditate: but whatsoever shall be given you in that hour, that speak ye: for it is not ye that speak, but the Holy Ghost.@5
verse	41	13	12	@@@6Now the brother shall betray the brother to death, and the father the son; and children shall rise up against @9their@7 parents, and shall cause them to be put to death.@5
verse	41	13	13	@@@6And ye shall be hated of all @9men@7 for my name's sake: but he that shall endure unto the end, the same shall be saved.@5
verse	41	13	14	@@@6But when ye shall see the abomination of desolation, spoken of by Daniel the prophet, standing where it ought not,@5 (let him that readeth understand,) @6then let them that be in Judaea flee to the mountains:@5
verse	41	13	15	@@@6And let him that is on the housetop not go down into the house, neither enter @9therein,@7 to take any thing out of his house:@5
verse	41	13	16	@@@6And let him that is in the field not turn back again for to take up his garment.@5
verse	41	13	17	@@@6But woe to them that are with child, and to them that give suck in those days!@5
verse	41	13	18	@@@6And pray ye that your flight be not in the winter.@5
verse	41	13	19	@@@6For @9in@7 those days shall be affliction, such as was not from the beginning of the creation which God created unto this time, neither shall be.@5
verse	41	13	20	@@@6And except that the Lord had shortened those days, no flesh should be saved: but for the elect's sake, whom he hath chosen, he hath shortened the days.@5
verse	41	13	21	@@@6And then if any man shall say to you, Lo, here @9is@7 Christ; or, lo, @9he is@7 there; believe @9him@7 not:@5
verse	41	13	22	@@@6For false Christs and false prophets shall rise, and shall shew signs and wonders, to seduce, if @9it were@7 possible, even the elect.@5
verse	41	13	23	@@@6But take ye heed: behold, I have foretold you all things.@5
verse	41	13	24	@@@6But in those days, after that tribulation, the sun shall be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light,@5
verse	41	13	25	@@@6And the stars of heaven shall fall, and the powers that are in heaven shall be shaken.@5
verse	41	13	26	@@@6And then shall they see the Son of man coming in the clouds with great power and glory.@5
verse	41	13	27	@@@6And then shall he send his angels, and shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from the uttermost part of the earth to the uttermost part of heaven.@5
verse	41	13	28	@@@6Now learn a parable of the fig tree; When her branch is yet tender, and putteth forth leaves, ye know that summer is near:@5
verse	41	13	29	@@@6So ye in like manner, when ye shall see these things come to pass, know that it is nigh, @9even@7 at the doors.@5
verse	41	13	30	@@@6Verily I say unto you, that this generation shall not pass, till all these things be done.@5
verse	41	13	31	@@@6Heaven and earth shall pass away: but my words shall not pass away.@5
verse	41	13	32	@@@6But of that day and @9that@7 hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels which are in heaven, neither the Son, but the Father.@5
verse	41	13	33	@@@6Take ye heed, watch and pray: for ye know not when the time is.@5
verse	41	13	34	@@@6@9For the Son of man is@7 as a man taking a far journey, who left his house, and gave authority to his servants, and to every man his work, and commanded the porter to watch.@5
verse	41	13	35	@@@6Watch ye therefore: for ye know not when the master of the house cometh, at even, or at midnight, or at the cockcrowing, or in the morning:@5
verse	41	13	36	@@@6Lest coming suddenly he find you sleeping.@5
verse	41	13	37	@@@6And what I say unto you I say unto all, Watch.@5
verse	41	14	1	@@After two days was @9the feast of@7 the passover, and of unleavened bread: and the chief priests and the scribes sought how they might take him by craft, and put @9him@7 to death.
verse	41	14	2	@@But they said, Not on the feast @9day,@7 lest there be an uproar of the people.
verse	41	14	3	@@And being in Bethany in the house of Simon the leper, as he sat at meat, there came a woman having an alabaster box of ointment of spikenard very precious; and she brake the box, and poured @9it@7 on his head.
verse	41	14	4	And there were some that had indignation within themselves, and said, Why was this waste of the ointment made?
verse	41	14	5	For it might have been sold for more than three hundred pence, and have been given to the poor. And they murmured against her.
verse	41	14	6	@@And Jesus said, @6Let her alone; why trouble ye her? she hath wrought a good work on me.@5
verse	41	14	7	@@@6For ye have the poor with you always, and whensoever ye will ye may do them good: but me ye have not always.@5
verse	41	14	8	@@@6She hath done what she could: she is come aforehand to anoint my body to the burying.@5
verse	41	14	9	@@@6Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever this gospel shall be preached throughout the whole world, @9this@7 also that she hath done shall be spoken of for a memorial of her.@5
verse	41	14	10	And Judas Iscariot, one of the twelve, went unto the chief priests, to betray him unto them.
verse	41	14	11	@@And when they heard @9it,@7 they were glad, and promised to give him money. And he sought how he might conveniently betray him.
verse	41	14	12	And the first day of unleavened bread, when they killed the passover, his disciples said unto him, Where wilt thou that we go and prepare that thou mayest eat the passover?
verse	41	14	13	@@And he sendeth forth two of his disciples, and saith unto them, @6Go ye into the city, and there shall meet you a man bearing a pitcher of water: follow him.@5
verse	41	14	14	@@@6And wheresoever he shall go in, say ye to the goodman of the house, The Master saith, Where is the guestchamber, where I shall eat the passover with my disciples?@5
verse	41	14	15	@@@6And he will shew you a large upper room furnished @9and@7 prepared: there make ready for us.@5
verse	41	14	16	And his disciples went forth, and came into the city, and found as he had said unto them: and they made ready the passover.
verse	41	14	17	And in the evening he cometh with the twelve.
verse	41	14	18	@@And as they sat and did eat, Jesus said, @6Verily I say unto you, One of you which eateth with me shall betray me.@5
verse	41	14	19	@@And they began to be sorrowful, and to say unto him one by one, @9Is@7 it I? and another @9said, Is@7 it I?
verse	41	14	20	@@And he answered and said unto them, @6@9It is@7 one of the twelve, that dippeth with me in the dish.@5
verse	41	14	21	@@@6The Son of man indeed goeth, as it is written of him: but woe to that man by whom the Son of man is betrayed! good were it for that man if he had never been born.@5
verse	41	14	22	@@And as they did eat, Jesus took bread, and blessed, and brake @9it,@7 and gave to them, and said, @6Take, eat: this is my body.@5
verse	41	14	23	@@And he took the cup, and when he had given thanks, he gave @9it@7 to them: and they all drank of it.
verse	41	14	24	@@And he said unto them, @6This is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many.@5
verse	41	14	25	@@@6Verily I say unto you, I will drink no more of the fruit of the vine, until that day that I drink it new in the kingdom of God.@5
verse	41	14	26	And when they had sung an hymn, they went out into the mount of Olives.
verse	41	14	27	@@And Jesus saith unto them, @6All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered.@5
verse	41	14	28	@@@6But after that I am risen, I will go before you into Galilee.@5
verse	41	14	29	@@But Peter said unto him, Although all shall be offended, yet @9will@7 not I.
verse	41	14	30	@@And Jesus saith unto him, @6Verily I say unto thee, That this day, @9even@7 in this night, before the cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me thrice.@5
verse	41	14	31	But he spake the more vehemently, If I should die with thee, I will not deny thee in any wise. Likewise also said they all.
verse	41	14	32	@@And they came to a place which was named Gethsemane: and he saith to his disciples, @6Sit ye here, while I shall pray.@5
verse	41	14	33	And he taketh with him Peter and James and John, and began to be sore amazed, and to be very heavy;
verse	41	14	34	@@And saith unto them, @6My soul is exceeding sorrowful unto death: tarry ye here, and watch.@5
verse	41	14	35	And he went forward a little, and fell on the ground, and prayed that, if it were possible, the hour might pass from him.
verse	41	14	36	@@And he said, @6Abba, Father, all things @9are@7 possible unto thee; take away this cup from me: nevertheless not what I will, but what thou wilt.@5
verse	41	14	37	@@And he cometh, and findeth them sleeping, and saith unto Peter, @6Simon, sleepest thou? couldest not thou watch one hour?@5
verse	41	14	38	@@@6Watch ye and pray, lest ye enter into temptation. The spirit truly @9is@7 ready, but the flesh @9is@7 weak.@5
verse	41	14	39	And again he went away, and prayed, and spake the same words.
verse	41	14	40	And when he returned, he found them asleep again, (for their eyes were heavy,) neither wist they what to answer him.
verse	41	14	41	@@And he cometh the third time, and saith unto them, @6Sleep on now, and take @9your@7 rest: it is enough, the hour is come; behold, the Son of man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.@5
verse	41	14	42	@@@6Rise up, let us go; lo, he that betrayeth me is at hand.@5
verse	41	14	43	And immediately, while he yet spake, cometh Judas, one of the twelve, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priest and the scribes and the elders.
verse	41	14	44	@@And he that betrayed him had given them a token, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is he; take him, and lead @9him@7 away safely.
verse	41	14	45	And as soon as he was come, he goeth straightway to him, and saith, Master, master; and kissed him.
verse	41	14	46	And they laid their hands on him, and took him.
verse	41	14	47	And one of them that stood by drew a sword, and smote a servant of the high priest, and cut off his ear.
verse	41	14	48	@@And Jesus answered and said unto them, @6Are ye come out, as against a thief, with swords and @9with@7 staves to take me?@5
verse	41	14	49	@@@6I was daily with you in the temple teaching, and ye took me not: but the scriptures must be fulfilled.@5
verse	41	14	50	And they all forsook him, and fled.
verse	41	14	51	@@And there followed him a certain young man, having a linen cloth cast about @9his@7 naked @9body;@7 and the young men laid hold on him:
verse	41	14	52	And he left the linen cloth, and fled from them naked.
verse	41	14	53	And they led Jesus away to the high priest: and with him were assembled all the chief priests and the elders and the scribes.
verse	41	14	54	And Peter followed him afar off, even into the palace of the high priest: and he sat with the servants, and warmed himself at the fire.
verse	41	14	55	And the chief priests and all the council sought for witness against Jesus to put him to death; and found none.
verse	41	14	56	For many bare false witness against him, but their witness agreed not together.
verse	41	14	57	And there arose certain, and bare false witness against him, saying,
verse	41	14	58	We heard him say, I will destroy this temple that is made with hands, and within three days I will build another made without hands.
verse	41	14	59	But neither so did their witness agree together.
verse	41	14	60	@@And the high priest stood up in the midst, and asked Jesus, saying, Answerest thou nothing? what @9is it which@7 these witness against thee?
verse	41	14	61	But he held his peace, and answered nothing. Again the high priest asked him, and said unto him, Art thou the Christ, the Son of the Blessed?
verse	41	14	62	@@And Jesus said, @6I am: and ye shall see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.@5
verse	41	14	63	Then the high priest rent his clothes, and saith, What need we any further witnesses?
verse	41	14	64	Ye have heard the blasphemy: what think ye? And they all condemned him to be guilty of death.
verse	41	14	65	And some began to spit on him, and to cover his face, and to buffet him, and to say unto him, Prophesy: and the servants did strike him with the palms of their hands.
verse	41	14	66	And as Peter was beneath in the palace, there cometh one of the maids of the high priest:
verse	41	14	67	And when she saw Peter warming himself, she looked upon him, and said, And thou also wast with Jesus of Nazareth.
verse	41	14	68	But he denied, saying, I know not, neither understand I what thou sayest. And he went out into the porch; and the cock crew.
verse	41	14	69	@@And a maid saw him again, and began to say to them that stood by, This is @9one@7 of them.
verse	41	14	70	@@And he denied it again. And a little after, they that stood by said again to Peter, Surely thou art @9one@7 of them: for thou art a Galilaean, and thy speech agreeth @9thereto. @7
verse	41	14	71	@@But he began to curse and to swear, @9saying,@7 I know not this man of whom ye speak.
verse	41	14	72	@@And the second time the cock crew. And Peter called to mind the word that Jesus said unto him, @6Before the cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me thrice.@5 And when he thought thereon, he wept.
verse	41	15	1	@@And straightway in the morning the chief priests held a consultation with the elders and scribes and the whole council, and bound Jesus, and carried @9him@7 away, and delivered @9him@7 to Pilate.
verse	41	15	2	@@And Pilate asked him, Art thou the King of the Jews? And he answering said unto him, @6Thou sayest @9it. @7@5
verse	41	15	3	And the chief priests accused him of many things: but he answered nothing.
verse	41	15	4	And Pilate asked him again, saying, Answerest thou nothing? behold how many things they witness against thee.
verse	41	15	5	But Jesus yet answered nothing; so that Pilate marvelled.
verse	41	15	6	@@Now at @9that@7 feast he released unto them one prisoner, whomsoever they desired.
verse	41	15	7	@@And there was @9one@7 named Barabbas, @9which lay@7 bound with them that had made insurrection with him, who had committed murder in the insurrection.
verse	41	15	8	@@And the multitude crying aloud began to desire @9him to do@7 as he had ever done unto them.
verse	41	15	9	But Pilate answered them, saying, Will ye that I release unto you the King of the Jews?
verse	41	15	10	For he knew that the chief priests had delivered him for envy.
verse	41	15	11	But the chief priests moved the people, that he should rather release Barabbas unto them.
verse	41	15	12	@@And Pilate answered and said again unto them, What will ye then that I shall do @9unto him@7 whom ye call the King of the Jews?
verse	41	15	13	And they cried out again, Crucify him.
verse	41	15	14	Then Pilate said unto them, Why, what evil hath he done? And they cried out the more exceedingly, Crucify him.
verse	41	15	15	@@And @9so@7 Pilate, willing to content the people, released Barabbas unto them, and delivered Jesus, when he had scourged @9him,@7 to be crucified.
verse	41	15	16	And the soldiers led him away into the hall, called Praetorium; and they call together the whole band.
verse	41	15	17	@@And they clothed him with purple, and platted a crown of thorns, and put it about his @9head, @7
verse	41	15	18	And began to salute him, Hail, King of the Jews!
verse	41	15	19	@@And they smote him on the head with a reed, and did spit upon him, and bowing @9their@7 knees worshipped him.
verse	41	15	20	And when they had mocked him, they took off the purple from him, and put his own clothes on him, and led him out to crucify him.
verse	41	15	21	And they compel one Simon a Cyrenian, who passed by, coming out of the country, the father of Alexander and Rufus, to bear his cross.
verse	41	15	22	And they bring him unto the place Golgotha, which is, being interpreted, The place of a skull.
verse	41	15	23	@@And they gave him to drink wine mingled with myrrh: but he received @9it@7 not.
verse	41	15	24	And when they had crucified him, they parted his garments, casting lots upon them, what every man should take.
verse	41	15	25	And it was the third hour, and they crucified him.
verse	41	15	26	And the superscription of his accusation was written over, THE KING OF THE JEWS.
verse	41	15	27	And with him they crucify two thieves; the one on his right hand, and the other on his left.
verse	41	15	28	And the scripture was fulfilled, which saith, And he was numbered with the transgressors.
verse	41	15	29	@@And they that passed by railed on him, wagging their heads, and saying, Ah, thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest @9it@7 in three days,
verse	41	15	30	Save thyself, and come down from the cross.
verse	41	15	31	Likewise also the chief priests mocking said among themselves with the scribes, He saved others; himself he cannot save.
verse	41	15	32	Let Christ the King of Israel descend now from the cross, that we may see and believe. And they that were crucified with him reviled him.
verse	41	15	33	And when the sixth hour was come, there was darkness over the whole land until the ninth hour.
verse	41	15	34	@@And at the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, @6Eloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani?@5 which is, being interpreted, @6My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?@5
verse	41	15	35	@@And some of them that stood by, when they heard @9it,@7 said, Behold, he calleth Elias.
verse	41	15	36	@@And one ran and filled a spunge full of vinegar, and put @9it@7 on a reed, and gave him to drink, saying, Let alone; let us see whether Elias will come to take him down.
verse	41	15	37	And Jesus cried with a loud voice, and gave up the ghost.
verse	41	15	38	And the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom.
verse	41	15	39	And when the centurion, which stood over against him, saw that he so cried out, and gave up the ghost, he said, Truly this man was the Son of God.
verse	41	15	40	There were also women looking on afar off: among whom was Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James the less and of Joses, and Salome;
verse	41	15	41	(Who also, when he was in Galilee, followed him, and ministered unto him;) and many other women which came up with him unto Jerusalem.
verse	41	15	42	And now when the even was come, because it was the preparation, that is, the day before the sabbath,
verse	41	15	43	Joseph of Arimathaea, an honourable counsellor, which also waited for the kingdom of God, came, and went in boldly unto Pilate, and craved the body of Jesus.
verse	41	15	44	@@And Pilate marvelled if he were already dead: and calling @9unto him@7 the centurion, he asked him whether he had been any while dead.
verse	41	15	45	@@And when he knew @9it@7 of the centurion, he gave the body to Joseph.
verse	41	15	46	And he bought fine linen, and took him down, and wrapped him in the linen, and laid him in a sepulchre which was hewn out of a rock, and rolled a stone unto the door of the sepulchre.
verse	41	15	47	@@And Mary Magdalene and Mary @9the mother@7 of Joses beheld where he was laid.
verse	41	16	1	@@And when the sabbath was past, Mary Magdalene, and Mary the @9mother@7 of James, and Salome, had bought sweet spices, that they might come and anoint him.
verse	41	16	2	@@And very early in the morning the first @9day@7 of the week, they came unto the sepulchre at the rising of the sun.
verse	41	16	3	And they said among themselves, Who shall roll us away the stone from the door of the sepulchre?
verse	41	16	4	And when they looked, they saw that the stone was rolled away: for it was very great.
verse	41	16	5	And entering into the sepulchre, they saw a young man sitting on the right side, clothed in a long white garment; and they were affrighted.
verse	41	16	6	And he saith unto them, Be not affrighted: Ye seek Jesus of Nazareth, which was crucified: he is risen; he is not here: behold the place where they laid him.
verse	41	16	7	But go your way, tell his disciples and Peter that he goeth before you into Galilee: there shall ye see him, as he said unto you.
verse	41	16	8	@@And they went out quickly, and fled from the sepulchre; for they trembled and were amazed: neither said they any thing to any @9man;@7 for they were afraid.
verse	41	16	9	@@Now when @9Jesus@7 was risen early the first @9day@7 of the week, he appeared first to Mary Magdalene, out of whom he had cast seven devils.
verse	41	16	10	@@@9And@7 she went and told them that had been with him, as they mourned and wept.
verse	41	16	11	And they, when they had heard that he was alive, and had been seen of her, believed not.
